Initially God created the heavens and the earth
The earth is void and chaotic . The depths are dark . The Spirit of God is on the waters .
God said , &quot; If there is light , there is light
God sees the light as good , and separates the darkness
God calls the day light , and the night darkness ; and there is night and morning , and it is the first day
God said , &quot; There will be air in all the waters , and water will flow up and down
And God created the air , and opened the waters beneath the air , and the waters above the air ; and so it was .
God calls the air heaven . There is night , and there is morning , and it is the second day .
And God said , &quot; The waters of the earth shall be gathered together , and the dry land shall be exposed ; and this is how it was done .
God calls the land dry , and the dwelling place of water sea . God sees good
And it shall come to pass , that there shall be on the earth grasses , and herbs and herbs that bear fruit , and trees that bear fruit , every one of its kind ; and the fruit of them shall be wrapped in nuts ; and it shall be so .
And there was formed on the earth grass , and herbs and herbs of every kind , and trees of every kind , bearing fruit , bearing nuclei ; and God looked well .
There is night , and there is morning , and it is the third day
&quot; There shall be light in the heavens , &quot; God said , &quot; that it may divide day and night , and that it may be a sign , and that it may set times , and days , and years .
And it shall be lighted in the heavens , and it shall shine upon the earth ; and it shall be so .
Then God created two great lights , a great channel for the day , and a small channel for the night , and created the stars .
And set them up in the sky , and shine upon the earth .
Manage day and night , and do not divide darkness . God &apos;s eyes are good .
There is night , and there is morning , and it is the fourth day
God said , &quot; Water will give birth to life , and birds will fly above the earth and in the sky .
And He created the great fish , and all the living creatures that were born in the water , of their kinds , and all the birds that fly , of their kinds ; and God looked well .
&quot; And God blessed them all , and said , &apos; They will multiply and fill the waters of the sea , and the birds will multiply on the earth .
There is night , and there is morning , and it is the fifth day
&quot; And God said , &apos; The earth will bring forth living creatures of all kinds , beasts , insects , and beasts of all kinds ; and this is how it will be
Then God created beasts of all kinds , beasts of all kinds , and insects of all kinds on the earth , and God looked upon them as good
&quot; And God said , &apos; We will build men according to our likeness , according to our likeness , that they may rule over the fish of the sea , and over the birds of the air , and over the beasts of the earth , and over all the earth , and over all the creeping things that creep on the earth .
God made man in his own image , and made a man a woman in his image .
Then God blessed them , and said to them , &quot; You shall raise up many people on the whole earth , and rule over the land , and over the fish of the sea , and over the birds of the air , and over all that moves on the earth . &quot;
And God said , &quot; Behold , I will give you all the vegetables and herbs that have seeds on the earth , and all the nuts that are on all the trees , as food
&quot; As for the beasts of the earth , and the birds of the air , and all that creep on the earth , I will give them grass for food , and it shall be so .
God sees all that he has created , and it is the sixth day , the night and the morning .
All things in heaven and earth are made together
And it came to pass on the seventh day , when the work of God was finished , that on the seventh day he rested from all his work .
Blessed be the seventh day , which is set as a holy day , because on that day God rests from all that He has created
&quot; This is the history of the creation of the heavens and the days of the creation of the heavens in the Lord God
&quot; The wilderness has not yet grown , neither have the herbs and herbs of the field grown ; for the Lord God has not yet rained on the earth , neither have men cultivated the land
But there is a mist pouring out of the earth , and filling the earth
&quot; The LORD God who created man in the dust of the earth will pour anger into his nostrils , and he will become a living man of the Spirit , named Adam .
&quot; The Lord God has set up a garden in Eden in the east , and has placed in it the man who made it
&quot; The Lord God has made all kinds of trees grow out of the earth to please the eyes of men , and the fruit thereof is good for food ; and in the garden there are trees of life and trees of good and evil .
A river flows out of Eden to nourish the garden , and from there it is divided into four paths .
And the first way was called Bison , and it was round about all the land of Haphirah , and there was gold there
And the gold therein is good , and therein are pearls and scarlet pearls
&quot; The second river is called Guidance , which is round about the ancient land .
And the third river was called the Hittite , and it was on the east side of Assyria ; and the fourth river was called the Beersheba
&quot; The Lord God will place him in the garden of Eden , and he will repair and keep watch
And the Lord God commanded him , saying , &quot; You may eat of the fruit of every tree of the garden
&quot; You shall not eat of the fruit of the tree of good and evil , for the days you eat shall surely die .
&quot; It is not good for him to live alone , &quot; says the Lord God ; &quot; I will make him a spouse to help him
And the LORD God brought unto him all the beasts of the field , and all the birds of the air , which the earth hath created , to see what he hath called : and the name of every living thing that he hath called is his .
And he made a name to all cattle , and to the birds of the air , and to the beasts of the field ; but he found not a partner to help him
And the LORD God made him sleep , and he fell asleep ; and he took a rib from him , and put it together
Then the Lord God made a woman out of the ribs of that man , and brought him before him
And he said , This is the bone in my bones , the flesh in my flesh ; that she may be called a woman , because she is taken out of a man
Therefore , one must leave one &apos;s parents , join oneself with one &apos;s wife , and become one
At that time , the couple were not ashamed to be naked
&quot; But the serpent , the work of the Lord God , is more cunning than all the creatures of the field ; and he said to the woman , &quot; Is it not true that God says , &apos; You shall not eat the fruit of all the trees of the garden ? &apos;
&quot; The woman said to the serpent , &quot; We can eat the fruit of the trees of the garden
&quot; But as for the fruit of the tree in the garden , God said , &apos; You shall neither eat nor touch , lest you die
The serpent said to the woman , &quot; You do not have to die
For God knows that the days you eat will be bright in your eyes , and you will know good and evil as God knows .
And when the woman saw that the fruit of the tree was good for food , and pleasing to the eyes of men , and beloved , and wise , she took it and ate it , and gave it to her husband , and his husband ate it
Their eyes were bright , and they knew that they were naked , and they took leaves of a tree without fruit , and made a skirt for themselves
And it came to pass , when the wind was cool , that the Lord God walked in the garden ; and when he and his wife heard the voice of God , they hid themselves in the trees of the garden , and hid themselves from the face of the Lord God .
&quot; The Lord God called the man and said to him , &quot; Here you are
He said , &quot; When I heard your voice in the garden , I was afraid , for I was naked , and hid myself .
&quot; Who told you to be naked , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; Have you eaten the fruit of the tree which I commanded you not to eat ?
&quot; The man said , &quot; You gave me a woman who lives with me , and he gave me the fruit of the tree , and I ate it
And the LORD God said unto the woman , What have ye done ? And the woman said , The serpent hath seduced me , and I have eaten it
&quot; The Lord God said to the serpent , &quot; You will be cursed for what you have done , and you will be more than all the beasts and beasts of the field , and you will walk with your bellies and eat the earth for life
And I will call you and the woman to one another , and your seed and the seed of the woman to one another ; and the seed of the woman shall hurt your head , and you shall hurt his feet .
And said to the woman , &quot; I will add to the pains of your wombs , and the pains of your offspring ; and you will love your husband , and your husband will rule over you .
And he said unto Adam , If thou hast eaten the fruit of the tree which I commanded thee not to eat , and thou hast obeyed the voice of thy wife , the land shall be cursed for thy sake , and thou shalt labour for ever , and eat of it
&quot; The earth will give you thorns and plums , and you will eat the herbs and vegetables of the field
&quot; You will be filled with sweat , and you will be confused , until you return to the earth , because you came forth from the earth . You were dust , and you will still be dust .
And Adam named his wife Sheva , because she was the mother of all the living
&quot; The Lord God clothed Adam and his wife with leather , and gave them to wear
&quot; This man , &quot; says the Lord God , &quot; has been like us , and knows good and evil ; and now I fear that he will reach out and pick up the fruit of the tree of life , and live for ever and ever .
Then the Lord God sent him out of the garden of Eden , and he reaped the land that he had taken
Then they drove him out , and set up a reinforcement on the east side of the garden of Eden , and a sword of fire on all sides , to guard the way of the tree of life .
And it came to pass on one day , when he was in the house with his wife , and she conceived , and gave birth to Shechem , that he said , The Lord hath given me a man
And he gave birth unto the brother of Cain , whose sheep were shepherds , and whose land he planted .
And it shall come to pass on a day , that the fruit of the land of Shemnah shall be a sacrifice unto the LORD
And he offered the firstborn of his flock , and the fat of the sheep ; and the LORD saw the offering of Abel and of him .
But he did not see Cain and his offerings ; and Cain was greatly wroth , and turned his face .
Then the Lord said to Cain , &quot; Why are you angry , and why have you changed your face
&quot; If you do well , will you not be pleased ? If you do not well , sin will lie before your door ; He will love you , and you will surrender to Him
Then Cain spoke to his brother Abel ; and when they were in the field , Cain came up and struck his brother Abel , and slew him
Then the Lord said to Cain , &quot; Behold , your brother Abel is in it . &quot; He said , &quot; I do not know ; am I a watchman over my brothers ?
&quot; What have you done , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; Your brother &apos;s blood cries out to me from the earth
&quot; The land has opened its mouth and accepted the blood of your brothers from your hand ; and now you will be cursed from this land .
&quot; And the land which you have planted will no longer be of use to you , and you will be scattered on the earth .
Then Cain said to the Lord , &quot; My punishment is too heavy for me ,
&quot; Now you have driven me out of the land , that I may not see your face ; and I will float away on the earth , and everyone who meets me will kill me .
And the LORD said unto him , Whosoever slayeth Cain shall be recompensed sevenfold : and the LORD made a sign unto Cain , lest any man meet him and slay him
So Cain departed from the presence of the LORD , and dwelt in the land of Moab east of Eden
