And he cast out a dove again , to see if the water had withdrawn from the earth
But there was water all over the earth , and the dove sought a place where she could not fall , and returned to Noah in the ark ; and Noah reached out and took the dove into the ark
And he waited seven days , and cast out the dove from the ark
And it came to pass in the evening , that the dove returned to him with a newly twisted olive leaf in his mouth , and Noah knew that the waters of the earth had receded .
And he waited seven days , and let go the dove , and the dove did not come again
And it came to pass , when Noah was six hundred and one years old , on the first day of the new moon , that the waters of the earth were dried up ; and Noah removed from the ark , and looked , and behold , they were dried up on the earth .
And it came to pass on the twenty-seventh day of February , that the land was finished
God said to Noah
&quot; You and your wives , your sons , your daughters , shall go out of the ark
