When the water of the sack was exhausted , the captain left the child under the small tree
And he went a long way , and sat down opposite him , and said , &quot; I cannot bear a child to die , &quot; and sat down opposite him , and cried with a loud voice .
God heard the voice of the child ; and the angel of God called out from heaven to Shatak , saying , &quot; Why do you do this , Shatak ? Don &apos;t be afraid ; God has heard the voice of the child .
&quot; Arise , hold the child in your arms , and I will make his seed a great nation .
And God made his eyes bright , and when he saw a well , he filled the sack with water and gave it to the child to drink .
Blessed be the child , and he shall grow in stature , and dwell in the wilderness , and become bowmen and arrowmen
He lived in the wilderness of Balaam , and his mother took him a wife out of Egypt
Then Abimelech said to Abraham , &quot; There is God &apos;s blessing in all that you do ,
&quot; I pray that you will swear by God to me here today that you will not deceive me and my sons and my sons , and how I have been kind to you , and how you will be kind to me , and to the people of the land where you dwell
Then Abraham said , &quot; I will swear by myself
And Abraham blamed Abimelech for this , because the servants of Abimelech had taken over a well
Then Abimelech said , &quot; I do not know who did this ; neither did you tell me ; but today I have heard it
And Abraham gave the sheep and the oxen to Abimelech ; and they made a covenant with one another
And Abraham put the seven lambs in one place
