And when they were come to Bethlehem , Joabmiel rose up , and went back to Philistine with Phinehas his captain .
Abraham planted in Beth-bath a palm tree , and in it he prayed for the name of the Lord , the God of everlasting life
Abraham lived many days in the land of the Philistines
And after these things , when God had tried Abraham , He called and said unto him , Abraham , and said , Here am I
&quot; And God said , &apos; Take your son , your only son , Isaac , whom you have loved , and go to the land of Moriah , and offer him for a burnt offering on the mountain which I command you
And Abraham arose early in the morning , and put on his donkey , and took two of his servants , and Isaac his son , and broke the wood of the burnt offering , and went up to the place which God had commanded him .
And it came to pass on the third day , that Abraham lifted up his eyes and saw the place afar off
Abraham said to his servants , &quot; Wait here , you and the donkey ; I will go there with the child , and I will come back to you
And Abraham laid the wood of the burnt offering upon Isaac his son , and he had in his hand a fire and a sword : and the two went with him
He said to Abraham his father , &quot; Father , &quot; and Abraham said , &quot; My son , I am here . &quot; He said , &quot; Look , there is fire and wood , but there is a lamb for a burnt offering .
Then Abraham said , &quot; My son , God will prepare for himself a lamb for a burnt offering , &quot; and the two went with him
And when they were come to the place which God had commanded , Abraham built there an altar , and set up the wood , and bound Isaac his son , and laid it upon the wood of the altar .
Then Abraham stretched out his hand and took the sword to kill his son
Then the angel of the Lord called from heaven , saying , Abraham , Abraham , he said , Here am I
And the angel said unto him , Thou shalt not smite the child , neither shalt thou hurt him : now I know that thou art a God-fearing , because thou hast not left thy son , thy only-begotten son , unto me
And Abraham lifted up his eyes and looked , and behold , there was a goat with two horns in a thick tree , and Abraham took the goat , and offered it for a burnt offering , to replace his son
And Abraham called the name of the place El , the Lord ; and to this day the people said , There will be provision on the mountain of the Lord .
The second time the angel of the Lord called Abraham from heaven , saying ,
&quot; I have sworn by myself , saying , &apos; You have done this , and will not leave your son , your only son ,
&quot; For blessing , I will give you great blessing . For children , I will multiply your children as the stars of heaven and the sand of the sea . Your children will have the gates of their enemies
Blessed are all the nations of the earth for your seed , because you have obeyed my word
Then Abraham returned to his servants , and they rose up together to Beer-sheba , and Abraham lived there
And it came to pass after this , that it was told Abraham , saying , Micah hath given birth unto Nahor thy brother
