And the two children grew and grew , and became hunter-gatherers , and dwelt in the fields ; and Jacob was quiet , and dwelled in tents
And Esau loved Esau , because he often ate of his venison ; and Rebekah loved Jacob .
One day Jacob was exhausted from the field to finish his meal
And Esau said unto Jacob , Behold , I am weary : give me this red soup , that I may drink it ; and Esau called it Edom .
And Jacob said , Sell me today the name of the eldest son
And Esau said , &quot; I am about to die . What good is the name of this elder son to me
And Jacob said , You have sworn to me this day ; and Esau sworn to him , and he sold the name of the eldest son to Jacob .
And Jacob gave Esau the cake and the bean soup . And Esau ate and drank , and went forth : and it was the name of his eldest son that was given to him lightly .
