And Esau said unto his father , Father , hast thou only one blessing to be blessed , and bless me , O my father ? And he cried out and wept .
And his father Isaac said , &quot; The fertile land of the earth shall be your dwelling place , and the sweetness of the heavens shall be your gain .
&quot; You will rely on the sword for days , and you will serve your brother , and when you are strong , you will remove his yoke from your neck .
And Esau hated Jacob because of the blessing of his father , and said in his heart , The days of my father &apos;s death are near , and I will kill my brother Jacob
Then there came a man , who told him the words of Esau the son of Rechab ; and he sent messengers , and called Jacob his younger son , and said to him , &quot; Your brother Esau wants to kill you , and to revenge on you .
Now , my son , listen to me , and rise up , and flee to Haran , to Laban my brother
Live with him for a few days , and wait for your brother &apos;s wrath to cease
&quot; When your brother was angry with you and forgot what you had done to him , I sent messengers to bring you back from there . Why do you two die one day ?
Then Rebekah said to Esau , &quot; I am tired of the women of this house , and I am tired of my life . What good is it for me to be alive , if Jacob also marries the women of this house , like these ?
And Isaac called Jacob , and blessed him , and commanded him , saying , Thou shalt not take the women of Canaan for wife
&quot; Go up to Padania , and marry a woman among the daughters of your father-in-law , Laban , in the house of your father-in-law , Pedur .
Blessed be the Almighty God , that He may make you multiply in number and multiply in number
&quot; The blessing of Abraham will be given to you , and to your descendants , that you may possess the land in which you dwell , the land which God gave to Abraham
And Esau sent Jacob away , and went to Padan-aram , unto Laban the son of Pedur the Aryan , Jacob &apos;s uncle to Esau .
And it came to pass , when Esau saw that Isaac had received the blessing of Jacob , and had sent him to Padan-aram , where he was to take wives , and when he had seen the blessing , he charged him not to take the women of Canaan as wives
And Jacob heard the words of his parents , and went to Padanaram
And it came to pass at that time , that Esau his father saw not the women of Canaan
And he went to Ishmael , and took to wife , besides his two wives , Mahara , the daughter of Ishmael the son of Abraham , the sister of Nebaiah .
And Jacob went out , and went to Haran without Baal
And he came to a place , and lodged there , because it was too sunny ; and he picked up a stone thereof , and lay down under his head , and slept there .
&quot; He dreamed of a ladder standing on the ground , and the head of the ladder was over the sky ; and the angel of God was on the ladder , going up and down
And the Lord stood above the ladder , and said , &quot; I am the Lord God of your father Abraham , and God of Isaac , and I will give you and your descendants the place where you are lying down
And thy seed shall be multiplied as the dust of the earth , to the east and to the south and to the north ; and all the nations of the earth shall be blessed because of thee and thy seed .
&quot; I am with you , and wherever you go , I will bless you , and bring you back to this land , and I will not forsake you , until I have fulfilled what I have promised you .
And Jacob awoke , and said , The Lord is indeed here , and I do not know
Then they feared and said , &quot; What a dreadful place this is ! This is not another , but the house of God , and the gate of heaven
And Jacob arose early in the morning , and set up the stone upon which he had put his pillow as a pillar , and poured oil on it
And he called the place Bethlehem ; but the name of the place was first called Luz
And Jacob swore , saying , &quot; If God is with me , He will bless me in the way I walk , and will give me food and clothing
&quot; And I will return to my father &apos;s house in peace , and I will be my God in the Lord
&quot; And the stone that I have set as pillars will be the house of God ; and I will give you one tenth of all that you have given me
And Jacob arose , and came to the land of the people of the east
&quot; Behold , there was a well in the field , and there were three groups of sheep lying by the well : for the water of the well was for the sheep , and the stone of the well was great .
The sheep were often gathered there , and the shepherd turned the stone away from the well to drink the sheep , and then put it in the place of the well .
And Jacob said unto the priests , brethren , ye are of that place ; and they said , We are of Haran
He said to them , &quot; Do you know Laban the son of Nahor ? &quot; They said , &quot; We do .
And Jacob said , Is he at ease ? And they said , Peace : behold , his daughters are come with sheep
And Jacob said , &quot; It is a high day , and it is not the time for the sheep to gather together , but rather you should drink the sheep and let them go .
They said , &quot; We will not be able to drink the sheep until the sheep are gathered together and the stone is turned away from the well
And it came to pass , when Jacob was speaking with them , that Lachun came with the sheep of his father , because he had shepherded them
And Jacob saw Lachun the daughter of Laban his uncle , and the flock of Laban his uncle , and turned the stone from the mouth of the well , and drank of the flock of Laban his uncle
And Jacob fell on his lips with Laah , and wept with a loud voice
And Jacob told Lachun that he was the nephew of his father , and the son of Rebekah . And Lachun ran and told his father
When Laban heard the news of Jacob &apos;s nephew , he ran and greeted him , and held him and kissed him , and brought him to his own house . Jacob brought all his feelings to Laban
And Laban said unto him , Thou art indeed my flesh : and Jacob dwelt with him a month .
And Laban said unto Jacob , If thou art my flesh , and serve me white and white , tell me what thou wilt for a wage
And Laban had two daughters : the great one was called Elijah , and the younger was called Rahab .
Leah &apos;s eyes were unspirited , but Rachel was beautiful and handsome
Jacob loved Lachun , and said , &quot; I would serve you seven years for your little daughter Lachun .
&quot; I have given him to you , &quot; said Laban , &quot; like other men ; so stay with me
And Jacob served Lachun seven years , and he saw them as days , because he loved Lachun
And Jacob said unto Laban , The day is fulfilled ; give me my wife , that I may dwell with him
And Laban made a feast , and gathered together all the people of the place
And it came to pass in the evening , that Laban brought the daughter to Jacob , and Jacob was with him in his room .
And Laban made Shepha the maid &apos;s maid to be an ambassador to Hilaria
And it came to pass in the morning , when Jacob saw that it was Elijah , that he said to Laban , &quot; What have you done to me , that I obey you , and not for Lachun , and that you deceive me ?
And Laban said , There is no law in this place where we have not given the little ones , but give the great ones first
&quot; You will have seven days for this , and I will give you the same ; and you will serve me seven more days for him .
And Jacob did so ; and it came to pass , that at the end of the seven days of Leah , Laban took the daughters and gave them to Jacob for wife .
And Laban made her a maidservant , and made her a messenger to the daughters of Laban
And Jacob dwelled with Lachun ; and Lachun was victorious like Elijah ; and he served Laban seven years .
When the Lord saw that Elijah was not well-pleased , He gave birth to him , but Lachun did not .
And when she conceived , she named him Reuben , which means to have a son ; and she said , The Lord sees my affliction , and now my husband will love me .
And he conceived again , and said , The LORD hath given me this son again , because he hath despised me to hear ; and he called his name Simeon .
And he conceived a son , and called his name Levi ; and he said , I have given my husband three sons , and he shall be with me .
And he conceived again , and said , &quot; This time I will praise the Lord , and I will give him the name of Judah , &quot; and it ceased .
And when he saw that he had not given Jacob a son , he envied his sister , and said unto Jacob , Give me my son , or I shall die
Jacob was angry with Lacan , and said to him , &quot; Can I take his place as Lord , if God is the one that makes you barren ? &quot;
And Lachun said , Behold , here is my envoy Bilhah , and thou shalt dwell with her , and she shall bear a son under my knees ; and I will have a son for her .
And Lachun took his wife Beer-sheba for a concubine unto his husband ; and Jacob was with him in the house .
And she conceived , and bare Jacob a son
And he said , God hath stretched out my righteousness , and hath heard my voice , and hath given me a son , and hath therefore named him Dan .
And the daughter of Rachel conceived again , and bare Jacob a second son
And Lachun said , I contended greatly with my sister , and I won ; and I called him Naphtali .
And when Elijah saw that he had ceased to bear , he gave Jacob the concubine of Shephas the daughter of Shephas
And Zedekiah the daughter of Leah bare Jacob a son
Then Elijah said , &quot; Blessed is he , &quot; and named him Gad .
And Zephah the daughter of Leah bare Jacob a second son
And she said , Blessed am I , O LORD ; and all the women shall call me Blessed : and she named him Asheem .
And it came to pass , when he had harvested the wheat , that the stream went into the field to seek the cigar , and brought it to his mother Elijah ; and Lachun said unto him , Give me the cigar of thy son
And she said , Is it any small thing that thou hast taken my husband , or that thou wilt take my son &apos;s cigar ? And Lachun said , For thy son &apos;s cigar , that he may sleep with thee this night
And it came to pass in the evening , when Jacob was come out of the field , that Elijah came out to meet him , and said unto him , Thou shalt sleep with me ; for I have hired thee with my son &apos;s cigar ; and Jacob slept with him that night
And God answered and she conceived , and gave birth to Jacob a fifth son
And she said , God hath given me value , because he hath given my husband a wife for me ; and she called him Isaac .
And she conceived again , and bare Jacob a sixth son .
And she said , God hath blessed me , and my husband shall dwell with me , because I have given him six sons ; and I called his name Zebulun .
Then he gave birth to another daughter , and named her Danna
God cared for Lachun , and gave him permission , that he might bear
&quot; And she conceived and gave birth , saying , &apos; God has removed my shame .
Then she named him Joseph , and said , &quot; May the Lord add me another son . &quot;
Then Jacob said to Laban , &quot; Please send me away , that I may return to my homeland
Give me the wives and children that you have , and let me go ; for you know how I obey you .
Then Laban said to him , &quot; If I have mercy in your sight , please stay with me , for I have calculated that the Lord has blessed me for your sake
&quot; And I will give you your wages , if you will .
Jacob said to him , &quot; You know how I obey you , and how your cattle are in my hand .
&quot; You were few before I came , but now you are many . The Lord blesses you with my steps . When will I wait to build my house ?
And he said , What shall I give thee ? And Jacob said , Whatsoever thou wilt not give me , it is only one thing : if thou wilt accept it , I will keep thy flock .
&quot; Today I will go through your flock , and I will choose out of the sheep all that is spotted , and all that is black , and all that is spotted , and all that is spotted , and all that is small , even the price of my labour .
Then you shall look at my wages ; and every sheep that is not spotted in my hand , nor black in my hand , shall be my thief ; and it shall be a testimony of my righteousness .
And Laban said , Good is it , O LORD , that I may do according to thy word
And on that day Laban brought forth the lambs of the goats , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the goats , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones , and the lambs of the little ones
And he separated himself from Jacob for three days , and Jacob reared the rest of Laban &apos;s sheep .
And Jacob took the young branches of the fig tree , and the almond tree , and the maple tree , and stripped the skin of it with white stripes , and made the branches white .
And the branches of the skin shall be cut off , and the sheep shall be placed in the wells where the sheep are to drink , and in the tanks where the sheep are to drink .
And when the sheep were in harmony with the branches , they brought forth a mark , a little , and a spot .
And Jacob divided the lambs , and set the Lamb of Laban against the sheep that had stripes and black , and put his own sheep in another place , lest he should be confused with the Lamb of Laban .
And it came to pass , when the flock was well fed , that Jacob put the branches in the ditch , and the sheep were well fed with the branches .
&quot; But when the sheep are weak , they will not plant branches ; and the weak will belong to Laban , and the strong to Jacob .
And Jacob waxed exceedingly great , and took many sheep , and servants , and camels , and donkeys
And Jacob heard the words of the sons of Laban , saying , Jacob has taken away all that was in our father &apos;s hand , and has borrowed all that was in our father &apos;s hand , and has obtained all this glory .
Jacob saw that Laban &apos;s spirit was less toward him than before
Then the Lord said to Jacob , &quot; You shall return to the land of your fathers and your fathers , to your relatives , and I will be with you
And Jacob sent and called Rachel and Leah to the sheep of the field
And he said unto them , I see that the spirit of your father is unto me as never before ; but the God of my father is with me
&quot; You also know that I have served your father with all my might .
&quot; Your father deceived me , and changed my wages ten times ; yet God did not allow him to harm me .
&quot; If he says , &apos; A little is your wage , and a little of the flock is born , &apos; and if he says , &apos; The one who has a mark is your wage , and the one who has a mark is your wage
&quot; So God has taken away the livestock of your father and given it to me
When the sheep were in harmony , I lifted up my eyes in my dream , and saw the goats of the flock jumping , all of them with markings , a little bit , and with spots .
And the angel of God called me in that dream , saying , Jacob ; and I said , Here am I
Then he said , &quot; Look , and all the goats that jump from the lambs are striped , a little bit , and have spots ; and I have seen all that Laban has done to you
&quot; I am the God of Bethlehem , and you have poured out the pillars therein with oil , and you have made a vow to me . Now arise and leave the land , and go back to your place .
And they answered Jacob , and said , Is there a portion in our father &apos;s house , or in our inheritance ?
Have we not been treated as strangers by Him , because He has sold us and swallowed up our worth
&quot; All that God took out of our father was for us and for our children ; and now do what God has commanded you , and do it only .
And Jacob arose , and put his sons and his wives on camels
And he brought with him all the livestock and all the goods that he had gained in the land of Dan , and went to Canaan , to his father Isaac
At that time Laban went to cut the wool , and Laban stole the image of God from his father &apos;s house
And Jacob stole Laban the son of Aram , and didn &apos;t bring charges against him
And he fled with all that he had , and rose up , and passed over the great river , and went toward Mount Gilead .
And it came to pass on the third day , that Laban was accused , and Jacob fled .
And Laban pursued after his brethren seven days , and pursued them in mount Gilead .
Then God came to Laban the son of Aram at night , and said to him in a dream , &quot; Be careful that you do not speak good or evil to Jacob
And Laban pursued Jacob , and Jacob pitched in the mountain , and Laban and all his brethren pitched in the mountain of Gilead
And Laban said unto Jacob , What hast thou done , that thou hast stolen after me , and hast taken away my daughters as with a sword ?
Why hast thou fled in darkness , and stolen away , and told me not that I might rejoice , and sing , and play the harp , and play the harp , and bring thee back
And do not allow me to kiss my grandchildren and my daughters ; for what you do is foolishness .
&quot; I had the power to harm you in my hand , but the God of your father said to me last night , &apos; Be careful not to speak good or evil to Jacob
Why did you steal my image , even though you had to go to your father &apos;s house now ?
And Jacob answered and said unto Laban , I am afraid that thou hast taken away thy daughters from me , therefore I fled
And whosoever thou seekest of thy idols , he shall not bear him alive ; and when thou hast confessed unto our brethren , whatsoever belongeth unto thee of the east and west of my house , take it away ; for Jacob knew not that Rahab had stolen them .
And Laban entered into the tents of Jacob , and of Elijah , and into the tents of the two envoys ; and he did not search them : but he came out of the tents of Elijah , and entered into the tents of Rachel .
And when he had put the image of God in the camel &apos;s basket , he sat upon his head , and Laban touched the tent , and touched it not
And Laban said unto his father , It is an inconvenience unto me that I cannot stand before thee , and I pray my Lord be not angry . And Laban searched for God &apos;s image , and there was none .
Then Jacob rebuked Laban in anger , and said , What have I done wrong , and what have I done evil , and why hast thou pursued me at such a speed
&quot; You have searched all my furniture , and what have you found ? You shall put it before my brothers and me , that they may distinguish between you and me .
&quot; For twenty years I have been in your house , and your sheep and your goats have not given birth ; and I have not eaten the goats of your flock .
&quot; I have not brought it to you , which was torn by the beasts ; it is my own recompense , whether it be day or night , which was stolen , and you have asked me .
My day is full of dry heat , and my night is full of cold frost , and I do not sleep with one eye , as I often do
&quot; I have been in your house for twenty years ; I have served your two daughters for fourteen years ; I have served your flock for six years ; and you have changed my wages ten times .
&quot; If not the God of my father Isaac , the God of Abraham , who feared me , were with me , you would certainly send me away empty-handed . God saw my affliction and my labour , and rebuked you last night .
And Laban answered Jacob , and said , This is my daughter , and these are my children , and these are my sheep ; and all that is before thee is mine ; and what can I do to them today , my daughter , and the children that they have born ?
&quot; Come , and you and I will make a covenant as evidence between you and me
And Jacob took a stone head , and set it as a pillar
Then he said to the brethren , &quot; You are gathering stones , &quot; and they gathered them together , and they ate and drank by the side
And Laban called it Isar-sahadath , and Jacob called it Gad .
And Laban said , This is the stone which is in the midst of thee and of me this day : therefore is the name of the place called Gerdec .
&quot; The Lord will judge between you and me after we have separated from one another .
&quot; If you suffer my daughters , and marry another woman than my daughters , God will testify between you and me , though no man knows
And Laban said , &quot; Look at the pile of stones and the pillars which I have placed between you and me .
&quot; This is a proof , and this is a pillar of proof ; I will not pass over this stone to harm you , nor will you pass over this stone and this pillar to harm me
But let the God of Abraham and the God of the Crane judge between you and me , the God of their father . And Jacob swore by the God that his father Isaac feared .
And they sacrificed on the mountain , and invited all the brethren to eat ; and when they had eaten , they lodged on the mountain
And Laban arose early in the morning , and kissed his sons and his daughters , and blessed them , and returned to his place .
Jacob was still walking , and the angels of God met him
And when Jacob saw them , he said , This is the army of God : and he called the name of the place Mahan .
And Jacob sent and went to the land of Zair , which is Edom , to meet his brother Esau
And he said unto them , Say unto my lord Esau , Thus saith your servant Jacob , I dwell in Laban unto this day
&quot; I have cattle , donkeys , flocks of sheep , and servants ; and I am sending messengers to report to my Lord , that I may have mercy before You
Then the messenger returned to Jacob and said , &quot; We have come to your brother Esau , and he is coming to you with forty men
Then Jacob was very afraid and troubled , and divided the people who were with him into two groups : sheep , cattle , and camels .
He said , &quot; To slay them with Saul , and the remnant will escape . &quot;
Jacob said , &quot; Lord , God of my father Abraham , God of my father Isaac , you have said to me , &apos; Go back to your people , and I will have mercy on you
&quot; I am not worthy of all the kindness and truth that you have shown to your servants . I used to carry my staff over the Jordan , but now I am in two groups .
Save me from the hand of my brother Esau ; for I fear that he will kill me , and that he will kill my wife and my children with her .
&quot; You said , &apos; I will be merciful to you , and I will make your descendants as the sand of the sea .
And Jacob lodged there that night , and took a present out of all that he had , and gave it to his brother Esau
Two hundred lambs , twenty lambs , two hundred lambs , twenty lambs
Thirty camels bearing calves , forty cattle , ten oxen , twenty donkeys , and ten donkeys
Then he divided them into groups , and gave them into the hands of the servants , and said to them , &quot; You shall pass before me , and separate the groups from the resting place
&quot; When my brother Esau met you , he said to you , &apos; Who are you in that house , that you should go to ?
Then saidst thou , It is Jacob thy servant &apos;s , the gift of my lord Esau ; and he himself is behind us
And he commanded the second , and the third , and all the men that had driven away the herds , saying , &quot; Thus shall you say to him when you meet Esau
And you shall say , &quot; Your servant Jacob is behind us , because in Jacob &apos;s heart he said , &apos; I have borrowed the gift that went before me to relieve his anger , and to see him again , or he will accept me
Then the gift passed away . Jacob lodged in the company that night
And he arose in the night , and passed over Jabbok with his two wives , and his two messengers , and his eleven sons
First send them over the river , then send them all over
And there remained only one Jacob : and a man came and wrestled with him , and he came to the dawn .
And when the man saw that he was superior to him , he touched his hammock , and the hammock of Jacob twisted while he wrestled .
And he said , The sun is risen , let me go ; and Jacob said , If thou blessest me not , I will not
And he said , What is thy name ? And he said , My name is Jacob
He said , &quot; Your name shall no longer be Jacob , but Israel ; for you have been victorious over God and over men
Then Jacob said to him , &quot; Tell me your name , &quot; and he said , &quot; Why will you ask my name ? &quot; Then he blessed Jacob there
And Jacob named the place Binuel , which is the face of God , saying , I have seen God face to face , and my life is preserved
And it came to pass , when the day was come , that Jacob passed by Binuel , and his legs were lame
Therefore the children of Israel did not eat the bones of the bark until this day , because he touched the bones of the bark of Jacob
And Jacob lifted up his eyes , and saw Esau come , and after him were forty men : and he gave the children unto Elijah , and to Rachel , and to the two envoys
And he commanded the two daughters of the envoys , and their sons , to be at the forefront , and to be at the rear , and to be at the end of the rear , and to be at the end of the rear , and to be at the end of the rear ,
And he himself passed before them , and fell down seven times in succession , and came near to his brother
And they ran and greeted him , and held him , and wrapped their necks around his neck , and kissed him ; and they wept .
And Esau lifted up his eyes , and looked at the children of the woman , and said , Who are these that go with thee ? And Jacob said , These are the servants of God unto thee
And the two sent before the women and their children
And Elijah and his sons came and worshipped ; and Joseph and Rachel came and worshipped
And Esau said , What is the meaning of these beasts that I have found ? And Jacob said , They are to be blessed before my Lord
And Esau said , My brother , my things have passed away , and yours are still with you
Jacob said , &quot; No , if I have mercy in your sight , I ask you to take this gift out of my hand , for I have seen your face , as I have seen the face of God , and you have accepted me
&quot; Bring down the gift which I have brought to you , for God has given me abundance , and Jacob asked again and again , and he brought it down .
Then said Esau , &quot; Let us get up and go , and I will go before you
And Jacob said unto him , My Lord knoweth that the children are young and tender , and that the sheep and goats are breastfeeding ; and if one day they should be driven away , all the beasts would die .
&quot; My Lord , walk before my servant , and I will measure the strength of the flock and of the children before me , and I will go straight to my Lord in Siir .
And Esau said , Let me keep a few of those who are with me here with you . And Jacob said , What shall I do if I have mercy before my Lord ?
And it came to pass on the day that Esau went up , that he returned to Siir
And Jacob went to the field , and built in it houses for himself , and tents for cattle ; and the name of the place was the field .
And it came to pass , when Jacob returned from Padanaram , that he went in peace to Shechem in the land of Canaan , and pitched tents in the east part of the city
And he bought the land of the tent of tents with an hundred pieces of silver to the sons of Hamath the father of Shechem .
And in it he built an altar , and called it Eli Eli-iro-i Israel ; that is , God , the God of Israel
And Elijah took the daughter of Jacob &apos;s son , Deah , and went out to see the women of the land
And when the Lord of the land , Shechem the son of Hamath , the Hivite , saw him , he drew him , and committed adultery with him , and defiled him
The heart of Shechem was in love with the daughter of Jacob , Deana ; he loved her , and comforted him with sweet words and sweet words .
Then said Shechem to Hamor his father , &quot; Please hire this woman for me as a wife
And when Jacob heard that the sword had defiled his daughter Deana , and that his sons were in the field with the cattle , he kept his mouth shut , and waited until they returned
Hamor , the father of Shechem , came out to Jacob , and talked with him
And when the sons of Jacob heard this , they returned from the field , and were filled with wrath and great indignation , because Shechem had done abominations in the house of Israel , and had committed adultery with the daughters of Jacob , which was not lawful .
And Hamath consulted with them , and said , &quot; My son Shechem hath a love for this woman , and give him my son as wife .
&quot; You may marry one another with us ; you may give us daughters , and you may marry our daughters .
&quot; You shall dwell with us , and this land shall be before you , and you shall dwell therein , and you shall do business therein , and you shall possess it
And he said unto the fathers and to the brethren of his daughter , May I have mercy in your sight ; and whatsoever ye ask of me , I will give unto you
Give me many hiring and gifts , and I will give them as you have said , as long as you give me a wife of a woman
And the sons of Jacob answered Shechem with deceitful words , and Hamath his father , because he had defiled their sister Deana for Shechem
They said to them , &quot; We cannot give our sisters as wives to those who have not been circumcised , for that is our shame .
Only one will be acceptable , if all your males are circumcised , just as we are
&quot; And we will give you daughters , and we will take your daughters , and we will dwell with you two generations
If you do not obey our circumcision , we will go with our sisters
Hamor and Shechem his son rejoiced at this
The young man did it without delay , for he loved Jacob &apos;s daughter , and he was most respected in his father &apos;s house .
And Hamath and Shechem his son came to the gate of the city , and said unto the men of the city ,
Rather than allow them to dwell and trade in this land , which is wide and sufficient for them , that we may take their daughters as wives , and give them our daughters as wives ,
Only one thing we must do , that they may obey , and dwell with us , and become one people : that all the males among us may be circumcised , as they are
&quot; Will not their cattle , their goods , and all their livestock belong to Us , and they will dwell with us as long as they obey them
And all that came out of the gate heard the words of Hamath and of Shechem his son ; and every male that came out of the gate was circumcised
And it came to pass on the third day , while all the people were in pain , that the two sons of Jacob , Simon and Levi , the brothers of Dean , came into the city with swords , and slew all the men of the city , when all the people did not know .
Then he struck Hamath with the sword , and Shechem his son , and took him out of the house of Shechem , and went away .
And the sons of Jacob came to the slain , and took the city captive , because their sisters were defiled
And they took their flocks , and their herds , and their donkeys , and all that was in the city and in the fields ,
And they took away all their goods , and their children , and their women , and all that was in the houses
And Jacob said to Simeon and to Levi , &quot; Because you have burdened me , you have made me a detestable name among the inhabitants of the land , among the Canaanites and among the Philistines ; and because my people are few , they will gather themselves together to kill me , and I and all my family will be destroyed .
They said , &quot; Will he treat our sisters as prostitutes ?
And God said unto Jacob , Arise , go up to Bethlehem , and dwell therein , and build therein an altar unto God , that which appeared unto thee when thou fledst from thy brother Esau
And Jacob said unto the men of his house , and unto all that were with him , Take away the foreign gods from among you , and purify yourselves , and change your garments
&quot; We will rise up and go up to Bethlehem , where I will build an altar for God , the one who will answer my prayers in the days of my trouble , and will bless me in the way I go .
And they gave the image of the gods of the Gentiles , and the rings of their ears , to Jacob ; and he hid them under the oak tree of the sword .
Then they departed , and God made all the cities that surrounded them afraid , so that they pursued not the children of Jacob .
And Jacob , and all that were with him , came to Luz , which is Bethlehem , in the land of Canaan .
And he built therein an altar , and named the place Elbertori , which is the name of the God of Elbertori , because God appeared unto him therein , when he fled from his brother .
And when Deborah the milkmaid of Libkah was dead , she was buried under the oak tree that was under Bethlehem , whose name was Arambago
Then Jacob returned from Padanaram , and God appeared again to him and blessed him
Then he said to him , &quot; Your name was Jacob , and from now on you shall no more call your name Jacob , but Israel ; and he will call your name Israel . &quot;
Then God said to him , &quot; I am the Almighty God . You will raise up many people , and there will be a nation from you , and a people from many countries , and a king from you
&quot; I will give you the land which I gave to Abraham and to Isaac , and to your seed
God went up from the place where he spoke to Jacob
And Jacob set a stone pillar in it , and poured wine on it , and poured oil on it .
And Jacob called the name of the place Bethlehem
And they went up from Bethlehem , and from Ephesus he had another way , and it was hard for them to draw near .
When it was hard , the mother said to him , &quot; Don &apos;t be afraid ; you will have another child
&quot; When he was near to die , and his soul was about to go , he named his son Benoni ; and his father named him Benjamite
And Lachun died , and was buried by the way of Ephraim : and Ephraim was Bethlehem .
And Jacob set up in his tomb a memorial , the memorial of Rachel , which is to this day .
And Israel went forth , and pitched tents on the side of Edom .
And it came to pass , when Israel was in the land , that Ehud went to sleep with Beer-sheba , his father &apos;s concubine ; and Israel heard ; and Jacob had twelve sons
The firstborn of Jacob was Reuben , and Simeon , and Levi , and Judah , and Issachar , and Zebulun ,
The son of Lachun was Joseph , Benjamin ,
And the son of Dan , Naphtali , the daughter of Beer-sheba of Lacan ,
And the son of Gad , and the son of Asheah , the son of Shephas , the daughter of Leah , the son of Jacob , who was born in Padanaram ,
And Jacob came to his father Isaac , and to Manly of Gilead , where Abraham and Isaac dwelt ; and Gilead was Hebron .
Isaac lived a hundred and eighty years
And it came to pass in old age , when the days were fulfilled , that he died in despair , that he was returned to his fathers , and they buried him , and his two sons , Jacob and Issachar .
And Esau was Edom , his seed , as follows :
And Esau took the wife of the daughters of Canaan , Adah the daughter of Elon the Hittite , and the daughter of Baal-ben the Hivite , and the daughter of Anah , Aholibamah .
And he took the daughter of Ishmael , Bath-shema the sister of Nebaioth ,
And Adam gave to Esau Eliphah ; and Bath-sheba gave to Reuel
And Aholibamah begat Jeush , and Jaram , and Pelah , the sons of Esau , which were born in Canaan
And Esau departed from his brother Jacob , and took with him his wife , and his children , and all the people that were in his house , and his cattle , and his livestock , and all the goods that he had gained in the land of Canaan ,
&quot; Because of the multitude of beasts and livestock that belong to the two , they cannot live together in the place where they are lodged
And Esau dwelt in mount Seir ; and Esau was to the east
And Esau was the father of the Edomites in mount Seir , and his seed is written as follows :
The names of the sons of Esau were as follows : Eliphah the son of Adah , Esau &apos;s wife ; and Bathim the son of Reuel , Esau &apos;s wife .
And the sons of Eliphah were Timan , and Amah , and Shebo , and Gatan , and Kenaz .
Tenah was the concubine of Eliphah , the son of Esau ; and he gave him Amalek , the son of Adah , Esau &apos;s wife
And the sons of Reuer were Nahath , and Shelah , and Shammah , and Misah : and these are the sons of Esau , the wife of Bath-shema
And Esau &apos;s wife , Aholibamah , the daughter of Anah , the daughter of Baal-ben , gave birth to Esau , and to Jeush , and to Jaram , and to Korah
Of the sons of Esau , the chief of the sons of Eliphah , the chief of the tribe of Timan , the chief of the tribe of Amah , the chief of the tribe of Ziboh , the chief of the tribe of Kenaz ,
And the chief of the tribe of Kohath , and the chief of the tribe of Gath , and the chief of the tribe of Amariel : these are the chiefs of the tribe of the children of Adah , which came out of Eliphah in the land of Edom
Of the sons of Reuer , the sons of Esau , were the chiefs of Nahath , and the chiefs of Shelah , and the chiefs of Shammah , and the chiefs of Misah : these are the chiefs of Reuer in the land of Edom , the sons of Bath-shema , Esau &apos;s wife .
Of the sons of Aholi-bamah , the wife of Esau , the chief of the tribe of Jeush , the chief of the tribe of Jaram , the chief of the tribe of Korah : these are the chiefs of the sons of Aholi-bamah , the daughter of Anah , the wife of Esau ,
And these were the sons of Esau ; and Esau was Edom .
Below are the names of the inhabitants of the land , the children of the Horites , and the sons of Seir , which dwelt therein : Reuben , Shuba , Beth-Bin , and Ana
These are the chiefs of the sons of Tyre , of the Horites of the land of Edom , Dishon , Issah , and Deshan .
And the sons of Reuben were Hori , and Shiman , and the sisters of Reuben were Tenah .
And the sons of Shuba were Elvin , and Manasseh , and Ibaroth , and Shibo , and Anah .
And the son of Reuben was Anah ; and this was Anah , who laid the donkey of Reuben his father in the wilderness under the hot spring
And the son of Anah was Deshon ; and the daughter of Anah was Ahlibamah .
And the sons of Deshon were Shindan , and Iel-ban , and Islan , and Kiran .
And the sons of Issah were Bilhah , and Zaban , and Achan .
And the sons of Deshaim were Uz , and Aram .
Below are the names of the elders of the Horites : the elders of Reuben , the elders of Shuba , the elders of Palin , and the elders of Ana
The chief of the tribe of Deshon , and the chief of the tribe of Issachar , and the chief of the tribe of Deshan : these are the chiefs of the tribe of the Philistines in the land of Tyre , according to their families .
&quot; For there was no king over Edom among the children of Israel before he began to reign over the land of Edom .
And Beer-sheba the son of Beer-sheba reigned in Edom ; and his city was called Tiib-habah .
And when Bela was dead , Joab the son of Shelah the Persian reigned in his stead .
And Joab died , and Hushan the man of the land of Timan reigned in his stead
And Hushan died , and Hadad the son of Bida reigned in his stead : and Hadad was the one that slew the Midianites in Moab ; and his city was called Abied in the city of the kingdom of Egypt .
And Hadad died , and Sanlah the Maghreb reigned in his stead .
And it came to pass , when Sarah was dead , that Saul the Count of the River , which was by the river , reigned in his stead
And Saul died , and Balakanah the son of Ahab reigned in his stead
And the son of Agim was dead , and Hadad reigned in his stead ; and the name of his city was Baugh , and his wife &apos;s name was Mizpah , the daughter of Mizhail , the daughter of Matreel .
Below are the names of the chiefs of the tribe of Esau , according to their families , and their dwellings , and their names : the chiefs of Timnah , the chiefs of Eleazar , and the chiefs of Jethro
chief of the tribe of Aholi , chief of the tribe of Bamah , chief of the tribe of Elah , chief of the tribe of Benon
The chiefs of Kinas , Timan , and Mibias
The chiefs of the Makites , and the chiefs of the Ephrates , were all the chiefs of the Ephrates , according to their dwelling places , in the land which the Ephrates possessed ; and they were the fathers of the Ephrates , and the sons of Esau
Jacob lived in the land of Canaan , where his father dwelt
Joseph was seventeen years old and shepherd sheep with his brothers ; he was a child , and he was a concubine of his father , and the sons of Hilazephah were with him ; and he recounted the evil deeds of his brothers to their father
&quot; For Israel loved Joseph more than all the children of Israel who loved him , because he was born old to him , and made him a garment
And when the brothers of Joseph saw that his father loved him more than he loved them , they hated him , and did not speak to him peaceably
Joseph dreamed and told his brothers , and the more they hated him ,
Joseph said to them , &quot; Listen to my dream
&quot; Behold , we bound the wheat in the field , and my bundles stand , and your bundles surround my bundles .
Then his brothers answered , &quot; Will you really be our king , or will you really rule over us ? &quot; And the more they hated him for his dreams and his words , the more they despised him .
Then he dreamed again , and told his brothers , saying , &quot; Behold , I dreamed again , and I dreamed that the sun , the moon , and the eleven stars were worshipping me .
Joseph told this dream to his father and to his brothers , and his father reproached him , saying , &quot; What is this dream that you have made , that I and your mother and your brothers should come down and worship you ?
His brothers were jealous of him , but his father had the word in his heart
And the brothers of Joseph went to Shechem , and laid the sheep of their father
And Israel said unto Joseph , Are not your brethren shepherds in Shechem ? come thou , and I will send thee unto them : and he said , Here am I
And Israel said , &quot; Go and see the peace of your brothers , and the peace of the flock , and the peace of the flock ; and come back and write to me . &quot; And they sent him out of the valley of Hebron , and he went to Shechem
Then a man found him lost in the field , and asked him , &quot; What are you looking for
He said , &quot; I am looking for my brothers . Tell me where they lay their sheep
Then he said , &quot; They have passed away . I heard them say , &apos; Go down to the valley of Dorah . &apos; &quot; Then Joseph went after his brothers and met them at the valley of Dorah
And when they saw him afar off , and had not come before him , they plotted to kill him
They said to each other , &quot; Look , the dreamer has come
&quot; Come , and we will kill him , and throw him into a pit , and say , &apos; The evil beast has eaten him ; and we will see what his dreams will be
And when the flood heard that they were to deliver him out of their hand , they said , We cannot harm his life .
&quot; You shall not shed his blood , nor cast him into the pits of the wilderness , nor slay him ; but to shed his blood is to deliver him out of their hands , and to return him to his father .
When Joseph came to his brothers , they stripped off his coat , which he had worn ,
&quot; And cast him into a pit , which is empty and without water .
And they sat down to eat , and lifted up their eyes , and saw a company of the Ephraimites of Midian coming from Gilead , carrying with them in their camel spices , and milk , and no medicine , to bring them down to Egypt
And Judah said unto his brethren , What good is it that we kill our brethren , and hide his blood ?
Rather than that we should sell him to the Edomites , we should not slay him : for he is our brother , our bone , and all the brethren have obeyed him .
Then some of the merchants of Midian passed by , and the brothers brought Joseph up out of the pit , and gave him twenty shekels of silver , and sold him to the Edomites , and they brought him to Egypt
Then the stream returned to the side of the pit , and saw that Joseph was not in the pit , and he rent his clothes .
&quot; Return to the brothers and say , &apos; The boy is gone . I &apos;d better go there
They slaughtered a goat , and dyed the coat of Joseph with blood
And they sent messengers to their father , saying , &quot; We have found this , and please acknowledge it ; it is not your son &apos;s coat
When he recognized it , he said , &quot; This is my son &apos;s coat ; and the evil beast has eaten him ; and Joseph has been torn , torn
And Jacob rent his clothes , and wrapped his loins in linen , and mourned for his son many days
And his daughters rose up to comfort him , but he could not : and he said , &quot; I will come down to my son in the shadow , and I will mourn ; and Joseph &apos;s father will weep for him .
Then the Midianites brought Joseph to Egypt , and sold him to Potiphar , the captain of the guard , the servant of Pharaoh
Then Judah departed from his brethren , and went to the house of Hila of Adullam
And when Judah saw there a Canaanite named Shuah &apos;s daughter , he took her as wife , and dwelt with her
And he conceived and bore a son , and Judah called his name Er
And he conceived and bore a son ; and his mother named him Amen .
And he gave birth again to a son , and called his name Shelah : and Judah was in Gibeah when he gave birth to Shelah .
And Judah took a wife for the eldest son , whose name was Herma
And the eldest son of Judah saw evil in the eyes of the LORD , and the LORD called him to death
And Judah said unto him , When thou art in the house of thy brother &apos;s wife , thou shalt give him thy brother &apos;s portion , and stand for thy brother &apos;s son
&quot; And he knew that he would not return to his own son ; so when he was in the same house , he lay on the ground , lest he be left to his brother .
&quot; They did that which was evil in the eyes of the Lord , and the Lord caused him to die
And Judah said in his heart , I fear that Shelah shall also die , as his two brothers did ; and he said unto his daughter Herma , Go and be a widow in thy father &apos;s house , till Shelah my son grow up ; and Herma returned and dwelt in her father &apos;s house
And it came to pass after a long time , when the daughter of Sheba , the wife of Judah , was dead , and Judah was comforted , that he took her with his friend Hila the Adullamite into the tent , unto the man that shewed his wool
Someone told him , saying , &quot; Your prince went upstairs to cut wool
And when he saw that Shelah had grown old , and had not yet taken him for a wife , he took off his widow &apos;s garment , and covered his face with a cloak , and covered his body , and sat at the gate of the city of Enaim in the way of Tiennah .
Judah saw him as a prostitute , because he was veiled
And Judah turned to him , and said , Come , let me sleep with thee ; for he knew not that she was his daughter . And he said , What wilt thou give me , that thou mayest sleep with me ?
And Judah said , &quot; I have sent to you from among the sheep a lamb of the mountain , &quot; and he said , &quot; Will you give me a head before I send it ? &quot;
And he said , What shall I give thee ? And he said , Thy seal , and thy belt , and the staff of thy hand : and Judah gave him , and slept with him , and he conceived from Judah
And he arose , and went away , and took off his sackcloth , and put on his widow &apos;s garment
And Judah sent to his friend Adullam a lamb to take it back from the hand of the woman , but he found it not
And he said unto the men of the place , There are no prostitutes here , neither are there prostitutes by the way of Ennah .
And he returned to Judah , and said , I have not found him ; and the men of the place said , There is no prostitute here
And Judah said , &quot; I have sent this lamb , and you have not found it ; take it from him , lest we be ashamed
And it came to pass about three months afterward , that they were accused of Judah , saying , &quot; Your daughter Mary was a prostitute , and she conceived by her prostitution ; and Judah said , &apos; Bring him out , and burn him
And it came to pass , when he was taken away , that he sent messengers to his prince , and said unto him , Whose are these things , and from whom am I begotten ? Recognise thou , O LORD , whose are these seals , and the bands , and the staffs
And Judah confessed that he was more righteous than I , because I had not given him Shelah my son , and Judah slept with him no more .
He will be born without expecting a twin in his belly
And it came to pass at the time of birth , that a child stretched forth a hand , and the mother of the child held the red line in his hand , and said , This is the firstborn
Then the child took his hand back , and his brother was born ; and the mother said to him , &quot; Why hast thou taken it ? &quot; So he called his name Pharaoh
And when the red line was in his brother &apos;s hand , and he was born , they named him Shelah .
Joseph was taken to Egypt , and an Egyptian , a servant of Pharaoh , captain of the guard , Potiphar , bought him from the Edomites who brought him .
Joseph lived in the house of his master , the Egyptian , and the Lord was with him , and he prospered
&quot; And his master saw the Lord with him , and the Lord doing all that he had done in his hand
And Joseph was gracious before his master , and served his master , and the master sent him to do the household , and gave all things into his hand
Blessed is the house of the Egyptians , because of whom the Lord blessed Joseph , who was sent from his master to do the household , and all that was with him , and all that was in the house and in the field
And all that Potiphar had given into Joseph &apos;s hand , he had no knowledge of anything but what he had eaten . Joseph had come to Sheba Shunam
And it came to pass after this , that the wife of Joseph &apos;s master , Elijah &apos;s wife , sent to Joseph with love , saying , Sleep with me
And Joseph said unto his master &apos;s wife , Behold , my master knew not all the household , and he gave it all into my hand
&quot; There is no greater than I in this house , and he has not left me a thing that he will not give to me , but you . How can I do this great evil and sin against God , because I am his wife for you ?
Then he said to Joseph every day , &quot; But Joseph did not obey him , nor slept with him , nor was he with him
One day Joseph went into the house to do business , and there was none in the house
And the woman took his garment , and said , Sleep with me ; and Joseph cast it into the woman &apos;s hand , and ran out
And when the woman saw that Joseph had cast away his garment in his hand , she ran away
Then he called the men of his house , and said to them , &quot; Look , he has brought a Hebrew into our house to play with us . He has come to me to sleep with me , and I cried out with a loud voice
When he heard me crying out , he threw away his clothes from me , and ran out
And the woman put Joseph &apos;s garment in her , and waited for her master to come home
and said to him , &quot; The Hebrew servant whom you have brought to us here , come in to make fun of me
&quot; I cried out , and he threw away his clothes and ran away from me
When the master of Joseph heard what his wife had said to him , he was angry , saying , &quot; Your servant has treated me so and so
And he put Joseph in prison , where the king &apos;s prisoners were kept : and Joseph sat there in prison
&quot; But the Lord was with Joseph , and He blessed him , and He blessed him in the sight of the prison
And the prison gave all the prisoners into Joseph &apos;s hand , and all that they did therein was by his hand .
For the LORD is with Joseph ; and the LORD hath done all that he did smoothly
Then the king of Egypt , his lord the king of Egypt , was guilty of this , because of the wine and the food of the king of Egypt .
Then Pharaoh was angry with the governor of the wine and with the captain of the host
and put them in the prison of the chief guard , which is the place where Joseph was imprisoned
And the captain of the guard gave them to Joseph , and he served them ; and they were in prison some days
And the king of Egypt , the governor of the wine and the captain of the hosts , who was imprisoned , dreamed a dream at the same night , and each dream was explained .
And it came to pass in the morning , that Joseph came to them , and saw their sadness
Then he asked Pharaoh &apos;s two servants , who were with him in his master &apos;s house , &quot; Why are they sad today ?
And they said unto him , We have dreamed a dream , and none of us can make it come true . And Joseph said , Is it not from God that ye should make it known unto me
Then the governor reported his dream to Joseph , saying , &quot; I dreamed that there was a vine in front of me
There were three branches in the tree , as if they had sprouted , and had bloomed , and the grapes on their heads were ripe
&quot; The cup of Pharaoh is in my hand , and I will squeeze the grapes into Pharaoh &apos;s cup , and I will give it to him
Joseph said to him , &quot; This is the interpretation of his dream ; three branches are three days
&quot; In three days , Pharaoh will bring you out of prison and restore you to your office ; and you will still present the cup in Pharaoh &apos;s hand , as he did with his winepress .
&quot; But when you have gained , remember me , and show mercy to me , and speak to Pharaoh , saying , &apos; Save me from this prison . &apos; 
&quot; I was indeed taken from the land of the Hebrews ; and what have I done here that they may put me in prison ?
When the captain of the host saw the dream well , he said to Joseph , &quot; I saw in my dream three baskets of white bread over my head
And in the baskets of the high places were all kinds of food for Pharaoh to roast ; and in the baskets of my head were birds to eat
Joseph said , &quot; This is the interpretation of your dream ; three baskets are three days
&quot; In three days Pharaoh will cut off your head , and hang you on a tree , and birds will eat the flesh of your body .
And it came to pass on the third day , which was Pharaoh &apos;s birthday , that he set up a feast for the servants of the people , and brought in the governor of the wine and the governor of the feast
He restored the drunken governor , who still had the cup in Pharaoh &apos;s hand
But hang up the table , as Joseph explained to them .
But the winepress has forgotten Joseph , and forgotten him
For two years Pharaoh dreamed . He dreamed of standing by the river
And there came up out of the river seven oxen , beautiful and fat , and did eat of the grass in the groves
Then came up from the river seven other oxen , ugly and lean , standing by the river with the seven oxen
And Pharaoh awoke , when the seven ugly and lean cows had eaten up the seven beautiful and fat cows .
And he fell asleep again , and dreamed a second time , and dreamed that a wheat had seven ears , and that it was fat and beautiful
And thereafter seven ears were grown , and weak , and burned by the east wind
And the weak ear swallowed up the seven fat and full ears ; and Pharaoh awoke , and it was a dream .
And it came to pass in the morning , when Pharaoh was troubled in his heart , that he sent messengers to all the scribes and doctors of Egypt , and he told them the dreams which he had made , but none could give Pharaoh an answer .
Then said the drunkard to Pharaoh , &quot; Today I remember my sin
&quot; For Pharaoh was angry with his servants , and put me and the captain of the host in the custody of the captain of the guard
We two dreamed one dream at night , and each dream was explained .
And there was in it a young man of Hebrews with us , a servant of the captain of guard ; and we told him that he had fulfilled our dreams , according to the dreams of every man .
Afterwards it was as if he had given us a settlement . My office was restored , and the chief of the dining room was hanged up
Then Pharaoh sent messengers to call Joseph ; and they hurried to bring him out of the prison ; and he shaved his head , shaved his face , and changed his clothes , and came into Pharaoh &apos;s presence
Pharaoh said to Joseph , &quot; I dreamed a dream that no man could explain , and I heard people say , &apos; You will understand it when you hear it . &apos; 
Joseph answered Pharaoh , &quot; It is not for me ; God will answer Pharaoh with the word of peace
Pharaoh said to Joseph , &quot; I dreamed that I was standing by the river
And there came up out of the river seven oxen , fat and beautiful , and they ate grass in the groves
Then came up seven other cows , weak and ugly and lean , which I have not seen in all the land of Egypt
&quot; This lean and ugly cow has eaten up the seven fat cows that were before
And when I had eaten it , it did not appear to have been eaten ; and the ugly appearance was as it was before ; and I awoke
And I dreamed again of a wheat , and seven ears were grown , full and beautiful
Then seven more ears were grown , weak and dry , and burned by the east wind
These weak ears swallowed up the seven beautiful ears . I told this dream to the wizards , but no man could explain it to me
Joseph said to Pharaoh , &quot; The dream of Pharaoh is a dream , and God has instructed Pharaoh what to do .
The seven good cows are seven years , and the seven good ears are seven years .
And the seven cows that came after them , dry and lean and ugly , were seven years ; and the seven ears of empty space , which were scorched by the east wind , were seven years , seven years of waste
&quot; I said to Pharaoh , &apos; God has made clear to Pharaoh what he has to do .
There will come seven great years of abundance throughout Egypt
Then there will come seven years of famine , and the land of Egypt will forget its first harvest , and the whole land will be destroyed by famine .
For the famine that followed was great , and he did not feel that he had received much of what was before him .
As for Pharaoh , he dreamed twice , because of God &apos;s commandment , and soon it would be accomplished
So Pharaoh chose a wise and wise man , and sent him to rule over the land of Egypt
And Pharaoh did so , and sent officers over the land ; and he took one fifth of the land of Egypt in the seven years of abundance .
Let them gather together all the food of the years of abundance , and store up five valleys , and store up in the cities for food , and be under Pharaoh &apos;s hand .
The food that is stored up will guard the land of Egypt against the seven years of famine that will come , lest it be destroyed by famine
Pharaoh and all his servants were wont by this
Pharaoh said to his servants , &quot; How can we find such a man with the Spirit of God in his head ?
And Pharaoh said unto Joseph , God hath instructed thee of all these things : behold , there is none that is wise and wise like thee
&quot; You will be in charge of my house , and all my people will listen to your words ; but I am greater than you in the throne .
Then Pharaoh said to Joseph , &quot; I have sent you to rule over all the land of Egypt
Then Pharaoh took the printed ring out of his hand , and put it on Joseph &apos;s hand ; and he put on him a fine linen garment , and put gold on his neck .
And Joseph was taken in his carriage , and the drunken cried out before him , and said , &quot; Kneel down ; &quot; and Pharaoh sent him to rule over all Egypt
Pharaoh said to Joseph , &quot; I am Pharaoh , and in all the land of Egypt no man shall do anything without your command .
Pharaoh named Joseph Zephaniah , and gave him Asina the daughter of Potiphar the priest of An ; and Joseph went out to travel in the land of Egypt .
Joseph was thirty years old when he saw Pharaoh king of Egypt , and went out before Pharaoh throughout all Egypt
In the seven years of abundance , the fruit of the land was abundant and abundant .
Joseph gathered together all the flourishing of the land of Egypt in the seven years of abundance , and stored up the food in the cities , and the food around the fields was stored up in this city
Joseph stored up five great valleys , like sand on the seashore , which could not be counted , for the number of the valleys could not be counted
And it came to pass before the year of famine , that Assyne the daughter of Potiphah the priest of Anshi gave birth to Joseph with two sons
Joseph named his eldest son Manasseh , for he said , &quot; God has forgotten all my affliction and my father &apos;s family
And he named his son Ephraim : for he said , God hath made me to prosper in the land of my affliction .
The seven years of prosperity in Egypt are over
Then came seven years of famine , as Joseph said , and there was famine throughout all the land ; and there was no food in all Egypt
And there was famine all over Egypt ; and the people cried to Pharaoh for food ; and Pharaoh said to them , Go to Joseph , and do all that he has said .
And there was a great famine in the land of Egypt , and Joseph opened the storehouses and gathered the food for the Egyptians .
And all the people went to Egypt , and sought food in Joseph &apos;s land , because of the great famine which was on the earth
When Jacob saw that there was food in Egypt , he said to the children , &quot; Why do you see him ?
&quot; I have heard that there is food in Egypt , and you can go down and pour out of it for us , that we may live and not die .
So all the ten brothers of Joseph went down to eat of the corn of Egypt
But Benjamin , Joseph &apos;s brother , did not send Jacob to go with his brothers , because he said , &quot; I am afraid he will be put to death
And among those who came to gather food were the sons of Israel : for there was famine in Canaan .
And Joseph reigned in the land of Egypt at that time ; and he fed the people therein : and Joseph &apos;s brethren came , and bowed themselves before the land , and worshipped him
And when Joseph saw his brothers , he recognized them , and dressed himself as a living man , and spoke to them harsh words , and said to them , &quot; You are from there , &quot; and they said , &quot; We have come from Canaan to gather grain
Joseph recognized his brothers , but they did not recognize him
And Joseph remembered the dreams which he had dreamed , and said unto them , Ye are wicked , and come to spy on the falsehood of the land
They said to him , &quot; My Lord , it is not so ; the servants have come for food
&quot; We are all the sons of one man ; we are honest , and our servants are not wicked .
&quot; No , &quot; said Joseph , &quot; you will come to spy on the truth of the land
They said , &quot; The servants were twelve brothers , the sons of one of the Canaanites , the smallest of whom is no more among our fathers .
Joseph said , &quot; I said that you were adulterers , and it is true
&quot; I swear by the life of Pharaoh that if your little brothers were not here , you would not have come to this place , and from now on you would have been testified
&quot; You shall send a man among you , and bring your brothers , and you shall be imprisoned here , to testify that what you say is not true . If it is not true , I swear by the life of Pharaoh , that you are adulterers .
So Joseph put them all in prison for three days
And it came to pass on the third day , that Joseph said unto them , I fear God ; and ye shall live according to my word
&quot; If you are truthful , you may keep a prisoner among you in prison , but you may bring back food , and save the famine in your houses .
Bring your little brothers here to me , and there will be evidence of your words , and you will not die ; and so they will do .
They said to one another , &quot; We are indeed guilty in our brothers . When he cried to us , we saw his sorrow in our hearts , but we did not listen .
He said , &quot; Did I not say to you , &apos; You cannot harm the child , &apos; but you do not listen to me , and so I ask you for the sins of his blood ?
They did not know that Joseph had heard it , for he had spoken among them by word of mouth
Then Joseph turned and wept once , and spoke to them again , and drew Sammon out of among them , and bound him in their sight .
And Joseph commanded the people to fill their vessels with food , and to put their silver back into their pockets , and to give them food for their journeys ; and they did as he had said .
And they carried the food on the donkey , and departed from there
And it came to pass at the place where they were lodged , that one of them opened his sack for the donkey , and saw that his silver was still in his sack
And he said unto his brethren , My silver is returned ; behold , it is still in my pocket ; and they were afraid , and they said unto one another , What is this that God hath done unto us ?
And they came to Canaan , to Jacob their father , and told him all that they had seen , saying ,
&quot; The Lord of the land has spoken against us severely , and has taken us for spies in the land .
&quot; We said to him , &quot; We are true men , and not adulterers .
&quot; We were twelve brothers , the sons of one father , and one that is no more , the smallest , who is now with our father in Canaan .
Then said the Lord of the land unto us , If I know that ye are true men , let a man of yours remain with me , and ye shall bring back bread , and save the famine in your houses .
Bring your little brothers here to me , and I will know that you are not deceitful , but righteous ; and I will give your brothers to you , and you will be able to trade there
Then they threw down their pockets , and they did not expect the silver bag of every man to be in their pockets , and they and their father were afraid when they saw it
Jacob , their father , said to them , &quot; You have caused me to lose my son , and Joseph , and Simeon , and you have taken Benjamin away ; all these things are upon me .
Then said Reuben to his father , &quot; If I don &apos;t bring him back to you , you can kill my two sons and hand him over to me , and I will bring him back and hand him over to you
And Jacob said , My son shall not go down with you ; for his brother is dead , and there is only he ; and if he be slain in the way that you do , then you shall make me white , and I shall go down into a pity and a pity .
The famine in the land was great
And when they had eaten up all that they had brought forth out of Egypt , their father said unto them , Go ye again , and feed me
And Judah said unto him , The man spake unto us , saying , If your brothers come not with you , ye shall not see my face
&quot; If you send our brothers with us , we will go down and feed you
&quot; If you do not send him , we will not go down ; for he said to us , &apos; If your brothers do not come with you , you will not see my face .
Then said Israel , &quot; Why do you do this to me ? Tell him that you have brothers
They answered , &quot; The man asked us and our relatives in detail , saying , &apos; Is your father still , and do you have any brothers ? &apos; Then we told him according to what he had asked , knowing that he was going to say , &apos; You must bring your brothers down . &apos; 
And Judah said unto his father Israel , Send the child with me , and let us rise up , that we may live , you and us , and our women &apos;s children , and not die
&quot; I am his shield , and you can seek him out of my hand ; and if I do not bring him back and betray him before you , I will be guilty forever .
If we had not delayed , we would have returned for the second time
And their father Israel said , If it be so , you shall do so , and take the best of the inheritance of the land , the honey , the spices , the unfermented things , the plums , and the almonds , and bring them down into the vessels , and present them to that man
&quot; And you shall take doubled silver in your hand , and you shall return the silver that is in your pockets , and you shall keep it in your hand ; or it is wrong
Take your brothers with you , and rise up to meet him
May the Almighty God have mercy on you in the sight of that man , and release your brother and Benjamin ; and if I lose my son , I shall die .
And they took the present , and doubled the silver in their hands , and took Benjamin , and went down to Egypt , and stood before Joseph
And when Joseph saw Benjamin and them come with him , he said unto his household , Take these men into the house , that they may slaughter the livestock , and prepare a feast , because they eat with me at noon
And the priests went according to Joseph &apos;s commandment , and brought them into Joseph &apos;s house
Fearing that they had been brought into Joseph &apos;s house , they said , &quot; When you bring us here , it will be because you have returned the silver in your pockets for the first time , because you have found your faults , because you have slaughtered us , because you have made us slaves , because you have robbed our donkeys
And they entered into Joseph &apos;s house , and spoke to him at the door of the house
&quot; Then they said , &quot; Lord , our first coming is to gather food
And when we came to the place of our lodging , we opened our pockets , and we did not expect the sum of the silver of each man &apos;s pockets to be full , but it was still in each man &apos;s pockets , and now it is in our hands that we brought it back .
&quot; And they brought down silver for food , and they did not know who put it in our pockets before .
Then said the governor , &quot; Be assured , and fear not ; for he is your God , and the God of your father , who has given you your treasures in your pockets ; and I have taken your silver early ; and he brought forth Simeon , and gave it to them .
And the slayer brought them into Joseph &apos;s house , and gave them water to wash their feet , and grass to graze their donkeys
And they prepared the present , and waited for Joseph to come at noon ; for they heard that they were to eat therein
And when Joseph was come into the house , they brought the presents of their hands into the house to him , and fell down and worshipped him
Joseph said to them , &quot; Is it safe with your father , the old man whom you have spoken of , and is he still ? &quot;
And they answered and said , Peace be unto our father , thy servant ; he is still : and they bowed down their heads
Then Joseph lifted up his eyes and saw Benjamin his brother , his mother &apos;s brother , and said to him , &quot; Is this the youngest brother whom you have spoken to me ? &quot; And he said , &quot; My child , may God bless you
When Joseph &apos;s love for his brother had begun , he hurried to find a place to cry , and entered into his own house , and wept
&quot; And he washed his face , and with patience commanded the people to cook
And they set a table for Joseph alone , and a table for those who were with him , and another table for the Egyptians who were eating with him ; for the Egyptians could not eat with the Hebrews ; that was the abomination of the Egyptians .
Joseph appointed all the brethren to sit before him in the order of the old and the young , and all the brethren marveled at one another
And Joseph gave them the food that was before him ; but Benjamin had five times more than any man ; and they drank wine and had a feast with Joseph
And Joseph commanded the priests , saying , Fill the people &apos;s pockets with food , as much as their donkeys can carry , and put the silver of the people in their pockets
And he put my silver cup and the silver of the young man &apos;s meat in his pocket , and the householder did as Joseph had said .
The first day of the morning he sent those who carried donkeys away
And when they were come out of the city , Joseph said unto his father-in-law , Arise , pursue the men ; and when they were come up , he said unto them , Why do ye reward good with evil ?
&quot; Isn &apos;t this the cup of my master &apos;s wine ? Isn &apos;t it his divination ? You do evil in this way
&quot; The chieftain pursued them , and spoke these words to them
They answered , &quot; Why does my Lord say this ? Your servant refuses to do it
&quot; Behold , how can we steal from your master &apos;s house the silver that we have seen in our pockets , and brought it back to you from Canaan ?
&quot; Whoever you find among your servants , kill him , and we will be servants to my Lord .
&quot; Now do as you say , and whoever is taken out of it will be my servant ; and the rest will not be guilty .
So they all hurried to unload their pockets on the ground , and opened their pockets
And the father-in-law searched , and found the cup in Benjamin &apos;s pocket from the old to the young .
Then they rent their clothes , and each one carried his load on his donkey , and went back to the city
And Judah and his brethren came to the house of Joseph ; and Joseph was there , and they fell down before him on the ground .
Joseph said to them , &quot; What do you do ? Do you not know that a man like me will
And Judah said , What shall we say unto my Lord ? and what shall we say ? how can we make ourselves known ? for God hath proved the iniquity of his servant , and we are the servants of my Lord , even as he that hath gathered the cup out of his hand .
Joseph said , &quot; I refuse to do this ; whoever takes the cup out of his hand will be my servant , and you will go in peace with your father
And Judah came near and said unto him , My Lord , let thy servant speak a word unto my Lord , and be not angry with thy servant ; for thou art as Pharaoh
&quot; My Lord asked the servants , &quot; Do you have fathers or brothers ?
&quot; We said to our Lord , &apos; We have a father who has grown old , and a child who has grown old , and his brother has died , and his mother has left him alone , and his father has loved him
&quot; You said to your servant , &quot; Bring him to me , and let me see him with my own eyes
&quot; We said to our Lord , &apos; A child cannot leave his father ; if he leaves , his father will die .
&quot; You said to your servants , &apos; If your little brothers do not come down with you , you will never see me again .
&quot; And we went up to thy servant , and told him the word of my Lord in our father &apos;s house .
And our father said , Go ye again , and feed me
Then we said , &quot; We can &apos;t go down ; if our little brothers go with us , we can go down ; for if they don &apos;t go with us , we won &apos;t see the face of that man
&quot; You servants , my father said to us , &apos; You know that my wife gave me two sons
&quot; A man who has left me has gone out , &quot; I said , &quot; and he will be torn apart , and I have not seen him until now .
Now you will take this away from me again ; and if he be harmed , it will be that you have put me in a dark , bleak and miserable place .
&quot; The life of my father is joined to the life of this child ; and now I will return to your servant in my father &apos;s house , if there is no child with us .
&quot; When our father sees no child , he will die . This is the place where we have made your servant , our father , to grow white , and to fall into the darkness of sorrow .
&quot; Because he was a servant to my father for the child , and said , &apos; If I do not bring him back and give it to my father , I will bear my sins before my father forever
&quot; Behold , I ask you to let my servant live , and to make him a servant of my Lord , and to bring him up with his brothers
&quot; If the child does not go with me , how can I go up to see my father ? I am afraid that I will see evil come upon my father
And Joseph stood before the people who stood on his left and on his right , and commanded with a loud voice , saying , &quot; Let everyone go out of me ; for there was not a man standing before him at the time when Joseph and his brethren recognized each other .
Then he cried with a loud voice , and all the Egyptians and the house of Pharaoh heard
And Joseph said unto his brethren , Am I Joseph , and is my father still ? And his brethren could not answer , for they were afraid before him
And Joseph said unto his brethren , Come near , and they will come near ; and he said unto them , I am your brother Joseph , whom ye have sold unto Egypt
&quot; Now do not grieve and despise because you have sold me here ; for it is God who sent me before you to preserve your lives
The famine in the land has been for two years , and for five years it has not been possible to cultivate or harvest
&quot; God has sent me before you to save you and to preserve your lives , to give you the remnant of the world
&quot; Behold , it is not you who sent me here , but God , who made me the father of Pharaoh , the lord of all his house , and the governor of all Egypt
&quot; Come quickly to my father , and say to him , &apos; Thus says your son Joseph , &apos; God has made me the Lord of all Egypt . Come down to me , and do not delay .
&quot; You and your sons and your sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons and your sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons &apos; sons
&quot; I will feed you there , because the famine of five years has defeated you and your family , and all who are with you .
&quot; Your eyes , and the eyes of Benjamin my brother , see that I speak to you with my mouth .
&quot; You shall also tell my father all the glory of Egypt , and all that you have seen , and bring my father to me quickly .
Then Joseph fell down on the neck of Benjamin his brother , and Benjamin also on his neck
Then he kissed the brethren , and wept with them , and his brethren spoke to him .
And it came to pass in Pharaoh &apos;s palace , saying , The brethren of Joseph are come , and Pharaoh and his servants love them .
Pharaoh said to Joseph , &quot; You have commanded your brothers , saying , &apos; This is how you shall do ; carry your loads on your cattle and go up to Canaan
&quot; I will bring your father and your family to me , and I will give you the good things of the land of Egypt , and you will eat the fruit of the land .
&quot; Behold , I have commanded you to do this , and to go out of Egypt in a carriage , and to bring your children and your wives and your fathers
&quot; Do not despise your furniture in your eyes , for all the beauty of Egypt is yours .
Thus did the sons of Israel ; and Joseph gave them the carriages and the food of the way , as Pharaoh commanded them
And one set of clothing for each one of them , and three hundred pieces of silver for Benjamin , and five sets of clothing
And he gave his father ten donkeys , bearing the good things of Egypt , and his mother ten donkeys , bearing food , and bread , and meat , for his father &apos;s way
Then Joseph sent his brothers back and said to them , &quot; You shall not fight on the way
And they went up from Egypt , and came to Canaan , to Jacob their father
And they told him that Joseph was still there , and that he was the governor of all the land of Egypt ; and Jacob was cold in his heart because he did not believe them
And they told him all that Joseph had said to them ; and when their father Jacob saw that Joseph sent forth to receive his car , his heart was awakened .
&quot; Then Israel said , &quot; Yes , yes , my son Joseph is still here , and before I die , I will go to see him
And Israel came up with all that he had , and came to Beer-sheba , and sacrificed unto the God of his father Esau
And God said unto Israel in the vision of the night , Jacob , Jacob ; and he said , Here am I
&quot; I am God , the God of your father , &quot; God said , &quot; and go down from Egypt , and fear not ; for I will make you a great nation there
I will go down to Egypt with you , and I will bring you up ; and Joseph will bring you to an end .
And Jacob arose from Beer-sheba ; and the sons of Israel put Jacob their father , and their wives , and their children , in the chariot that Pharaoh brought forth for Jacob
And they came to Egypt with the cattle and the spoil of the land of Canaan ; and Jacob came with all his sons .
And Jacob brought his sons , and his sons &apos; sons , and his daughters , and his daughters &apos; sons , and his sons &apos; sons , and his sons &apos; sons , and his sons &apos; sons , into Egypt
The name of the Israelites who came to Egypt is written below : Jacob and his sons ; and the eldest son of Jacob was Reuben .
And the sons of Reuben were Hanoah , and Pharaoh , and Hezron , and Gami .
And the sons of Simeon were Jemoriah , and Jamin , and Ahaz , and Jachin , and Zochar , and Saul , the son of the daughters of Canaan
And the sons of Levi were Gershon , and Goshen , and Mirali .
And the sons of Judah were Er , and Ozan , and Shelah , and Pharaoh , and Shelah : but Er and Ozan died in the land of Canaan ; and the sons of Pharaoh were Hezron , and Hammor .
And the sons of Issachar ; Dara , and Puah , and Joab , and Shinron .
And the sons of Zebulun were Zeri , and Elon , and Jael .
And these are the sons of Jacob , and the daughters of Denah , which were born to him in the land of Dan , threescore and thirty :
And the sons of Gad ; Shephib , and Hachi , and Shuni , and Esben , and Eli , and Arrod , and Aaleel .
And the sons of Asheah were Zinnah , and Sheva , and Sheva , and Beer-sheba , and their sister Shelah : and the sons of Beer-sheba were Shib , and Mark .
These are the sons of Jacob , Shephah the maid of Laban , his daughter-in-law , sixteen :
And the sons of Rachel Jacob &apos;s wife were Joseph and Benjamin
Joseph gave birth in Egypt to Manasseh and Ephraim , the daughter of Potiphar , the priest of An , to Joseph .
And the sons of Benjamin were Beer-sheba , and Beer-sheba , and Asheba , and Gira , and Naaman , and Ehi , and Rosh , and Maphiah , and Shuphiah , and Aaleah .
These are the sons of Lachun , who were born to Jacob : fourteen in all .
But his son is Shushin
And the sons of Naphtali : Jasheh , and Tuni , and Jezre , and Shelah .
These are the seven sons of Jacob , of Bilhah the maidservant of Laban , his daughter Rachel :
All that came to Egypt with Jacob , except for his daughters , were sixty-six , all that were born of him .
And two sons of Joseph , who were born in Egypt : and the house of Jacob came to Egypt seventy .
And Jacob sent Judah to meet Joseph , and commanded men to lead him to Goshen ; and they came to the land of Goshen
And Joseph went in his chariot to Goshen to meet his father Israel ; and when he saw his face , he fell on his father &apos;s neck , and wept for a long time
And Israel said unto Joseph , I will see thy face , and know that thou art still , and that I will die ;
Joseph said to his brothers and to all his father &apos;s household , &quot; I am going to go up and speak to Pharaoh , &quot; and said to him , &quot; My brothers and all my father &apos;s household have come to me from the land of Canaan to this day
They are shepherds who feed their livestock , and they keep their flock , their herd , and all that is therein
&quot; When the Pharaoh calls you , he will ask you , &apos; What are you doing ? &apos;
&quot; You shall say , &apos; Your servants have been raising cattle from their youth to this day , and so have our fathers ; and you shall dwell in the land of Gaza ; for all the shepherds are hated by the Egyptians .
Joseph went in and told Pharaoh , saying , &quot; My father and my brothers have come from Canaan , with sheep , and oxen , and all that is therein , and are now in Goshen
And Joseph took five men out of his brethren , and led them to Pharaoh
Then Pharaoh said to Joseph &apos;s brothers , &quot; You are servants in good works . &quot; They said to Pharaoh , &quot; Your servants are shepherds , and our fathers are shepherds
Then they said to Pharaoh , &quot; The famine is great in Canaan , and the sheep of the servants have no grass to eat ; therefore we have come to settle here . Now let your servants dwell in Goshen
Pharaoh said to Joseph , &quot; Your father and your brother have come to you
And the land of Egypt is before thee , to keep thy father and thy brethren in the best of the land , that they may dwell in the land of Uzzah ; and if thou knowest what man is in them , send them over my cattle
Joseph led Jacob his father into Pharaoh &apos;s presence , and Jacob blessed Pharaoh
Pharaoh said to Jacob , &quot; How long have you lived
And Jacob said unto Pharaoh , The year in which I dwell in the world is one hundred and thirty years , and the year in which I live is less and less , and more and more painful than the year in which my fathers dwelled .
And Jacob blessed Pharaoh again , and went out from before Pharaoh
Joseph , according to the commandment of Pharaoh , gave his father and his brothers to dwell in the best of the land of Egypt , the land of Lance , as an inheritance
Joseph fed his father , and his brothers , and all the family of his father , according to the number of the families
The famine was great , and all the land was consumed ; and even the people of Egypt and of Canaan fainted for the cause of the famine
Then Joseph gathered together all the silver of the land of Egypt and of the land of Canaan , which was the food of the people , and brought it into the house of Pharaoh
The silver of the land of Egypt and of the land of Canaan was spent ; and all the people of Egypt came to Joseph , and said , &quot; Our silver is spent , and please feed us ; why do we die before you ? &quot;
Joseph said , &quot; If the silver is consumed , give me your cattle , and I will feed your cattle for you
Then they brought the cattle into Joseph &apos;s house , and he took their cattle , and their sheep , and their donkeys , and their horses for food ; and in that year he fed them for all their cattle
Then came they to Joseph in the second year , and said , &quot; We will not hide from my Lord , for all our silver has been spent , and all the cattle have returned to my Lord , and there is nothing left for us in the sight of my Lord except our bodies and the land
&quot; Why do you see our dead land as desolate ? Buy us our land with food , that we may serve Pharaoh with our land ; and give us our seed , that we may live , and not die , and the earth not be desolate .
So Joseph bought all the land of Egypt for Pharaoh ; and the Egyptians sold all their fields because of the famine , and the land returned to Pharaoh .
As for the people , Joseph commanded them to go straight from the side of Egypt to the side of Egypt , and to return to their cities
Joseph did not buy the land of the priests , because they had the regular wages of Pharaoh , and they ate the regular wages of Pharaoh , and they did not sell their land
Joseph said to the people , &quot; Today I have bought you and your land for Pharaoh . Behold , here is a seed for you , and you can plant it
&quot; When it comes to the food , you shall give Pharaoh one fifth of it ; and fourth of it shall be to you as seed in the land , and as food for you and for your children at home .
They said , &quot; You have saved our lives . May we have mercy in the sight of our Lord , and we will be an old servant
So Joseph set the ordinance for the land of Egypt to this day : Pharaoh shall receive one fifth of the land , and the land of the priests shall not belong to Pharaoh
And the children of Israel dwelled in the land of Canaan in Egypt ; and they had in it their inheritance , and they had much fruit
Jacob lived seventeen years in the land of Egypt , and his days were an hundred and forty-seven years
And it came to pass , when the time of Israel &apos;s death was near , that he called his son Joseph , saying , If I have mercy before thee , lay thy hand under my thigh , and be merciful unto me , and be faithful unto me , and bury me not in Egypt
&quot; When I have slept with my father and my grandfather , you shall bring me out of Egypt , and bury me in the place where they bury me , &quot; Joseph said , &quot; I will do according to your commandment .
Jacob said , &quot; You will swear to me , &quot; and Joseph swore to him . So Israel worshipped God on the bedside
And it came to pass after this , that Joseph was accused , saying , Thy father is sick ; and he took with him the two sons Manasseh and Ephraim
Then there was a man who complained to Jacob , saying , &quot; Behold , your son Joseph has come to you ; and Israel sat down on the bed with reluctance
And Jacob said unto Joseph , The Almighty God hath appeared unto me in the land of Canaan , and hath blessed me
&quot; I will raise up many people for you , and make you many people , and I will give this land to your descendants for ever .
&quot; Behold , these two sons , Ephraim and Manasseh , whom you have born in the land of Egypt before I came to see you in Egypt , are mine , just as Reuben and Simeon were mine
&quot; Then they shall inherit their inheritance in the name of their brethren , as you have been born after them .
&quot; As for me , when I came from Babylon , Lachun died before me in the way of Canaan , and there was another way from Ephesus , and I buried him in the way of Ephesus , which is Bethlehem
When Israel saw the two sons of Joseph , they said , &quot; Who are these
And Joseph said unto his father , This is the son that God hath given me here : and Israel said , Bring them unto me , and I will bless them
Then Joseph brought them before him , and he kissed them , and held them
And Israel said unto Joseph , I desire not to see thee , but God hath made me see thy son again
And Joseph took the two sons out of the knees of Israel , and bowed himself to the ground
Then Joseph took their two sons , Ephraim in his right hand , to the left hand of Israel , and Manasseh in his left hand , to the right hand of Israel , and brought them before Israel .
And Israel stretched out his right hand , and laid it upon the head of Ephraim , the second , and cut off his left hand , and laid it upon the head of Manasseh , the firstborn of Manasseh
Then he blessed Joseph , saying , &quot; May the God of my father Abraham and the God of my father Isaac be the God who raised me up from the dead to this day . &quot;
Blessed be He who redeemed me from all trouble , and blessed the two children , that they may be in My name , and in the name of my father Abraham , and of my father Isaac , and that they may be multiplied in the world
And when Joseph saw that his father laid his right hand on the head of Ephraim , he was not pleased , and lifted up his father &apos;s hand , and went from the head of Ephraim to the head of Manasseh
Joseph said to his father , &quot; My father is not like this ; this is the eldest son . Put your right hand on his head
&quot; But his father refused , saying , &apos; I know , my son , I know , that he will also be one family , and that he will prosper ; but his brothers will be greater than he , and his brothers &apos; descendants will be many .
And he blessed them that day , saying , The children of Israel shall say by your blessing , May God make you like Ephraim and Manasseh : and Ephraim stood above Manasseh
Then Israel said to Joseph , &quot; I am going to die , but God will be with you and bring you back to the land of your fathers
&quot; And I have given you the land which I took from the children of Ammon with the bow and with the sword , that you may be one more than the brethren
And Jacob called his sons , and said unto them , Gather yourselves together , that I may declare unto you that which shall befall you in the days to come
&quot; You sons of Jacob , gather yourselves together , and listen to the words of your father Israel ,
O River , thou art my eldest son , and my strength , and my glory , and my power ;
&quot; But you will not be in the first place , because you have put your father &apos;s bed on , and you have polluted my bed , and you have let your desire boil like water .
Simon and Levi are brothers , and their swords are a cruel instrument
&quot; Do not associate with them , O my Spirit ; do not communicate with them , O my heart ; for in their rage they have cut off the thighs of cattle , and slaughtered their lives .
Cursed be their rage , and cursed be their wrath , and I will make them to dwell in the house of Jacob , and to dwell in the land of Israel
&quot; Your brethren will praise you , O Judah ; Your hands will pin the neck of your enemy ; Your father &apos;s sons will worship you
Judah is a little lion , and you , my son , when you have grasped your food , go up ; and you bow down , and lie down as a lion , and as a mother lion ; who dare to provoke you ?
&quot; He will not leave Judah , nor his staff between his feet ; he will wait for the coming of Sheol , the Giver of peace ; and all the people will be obedient .
Judah tied the donkey to a grape tree , and the donkey &apos;s coat to a good grape tree ; and he washed his clothes in wine , and his coat in grape juice
His eyes shall be red with wine , and his teeth white with milk .
And Shebron shall dwell at the mouth of the sea , and shall be a port for ships ; and his border shall be stretched out to Sidon .
Isaac was a strong donkey , lying in the flock
He is good in quietness , and good in fertility ; and he is humble , and he is a servant of suffering .
But He will cut off His people from among the tribes of Israel .
But he shall be a snake in the way , and a snake in the way , and he shall bite the hoofs of horses , and the riders shall fall afterwards .
&quot; I have been waiting for Your salvation , O Lord .
And Gad shall be pursued by the enemy , and he shall pursue their footsteps
The land of Assyria will bring forth fat food , and delicious food for kings .
Naphtali was the released deer , and he spoke the words of Cameroon
Joseph was a tree of fruitful branches , a fruitful branch by the fountain , and his branches were found outside the wall .
And the archers torment him , and shoot at him , and oppress him
But his bow is still strong , and his hands are strong and sharp : for he is the shepherd of Israel , and the rock of Israel , and the mighty man of Jacob
&quot; The God of your father will help you , and the Almighty will give you all the blessings of the heavens , the blessings hidden in the earth , and the blessings of breast-feeding .
The blessings of your father are greater than the blessings of my fathers , like the everlasting mountains and the limits of the abyss . These blessings will be on Joseph &apos;s head and on the head of Reuben , who is different from his brothers .
Benjamin was a wolf that was torn apart ; he would eat what he had taken in the morning , and he would divide what he had taken in the evening .
All these are the twelve tribes of Israel ; and this is the blessing which their father spoke to them , and the blessing which he blessed for them , according to the blessing of every man ;
And he commanded them , saying , &quot; I will return to my fathers , and you will bury me in the cave in the field of Ephraim , in the land of the Hittites , with my father and my father .
And this is the cave of the field of Mephirah before the mantle of Canaan , which Abraham bought of Ephraim the Hittite for an inheritance , and for a tomb .
And there they buried Abraham , and Sarah his wife , and there they buried Isaac , and Rebekah his wife , and there I buried Elias .
The fields and the holes in the fields were bought to the Hittites .
And Jacob commanded the children , and when he had finished , he laid his feet on the bed , and died in despair , and returned to his fathers
Joseph fell down on his father &apos;s face , and wept , and kissed him
Joseph commanded his doctor to anoint his father with incense , and the doctor anointed Israel with incense
&quot; Forty days , the days were full , and the Egyptians mourned for him seventy days .
And it came to pass , when the days of his weeping were over , that Joseph said to the men of Pharaoh &apos;s house , If I have mercy in your sight , tell Pharaoh ,
&quot; When my father dies , make me swear , saying , &apos; You will bury me in the land of Canaan , in the tomb that I have dug for myself ; now let me go up and bury my father , and I will come back
Pharaoh said , &quot; You can go up and bury him , as your father swore you would .
Then Joseph went up to bury his father , and with him the servants of Pharaoh , and the elders of the house of Pharaoh , and the elders of the land of Egypt
And all the house of Joseph , and his brethren , and his father &apos;s household , and their wives , and their children , and their flocks , and their cattle , remained in the land of Canaan
There were also vehicles and horsemen who went up with him , and there were many of them
And when they were come to the field of the fields of Adah , which is beyond Jordan , there was in it a great weeping , and Joseph wept for his father seven days
And when the inhabitants of Canaan saw the mourning in the field of Adah , they said , This is the great mourning of the Egyptians : therefore the name of the place is Abimelech , which is on the east side of Jordan
And the sons of Jacob did as his father commanded them
And he brought him into the land of Canaan , and buried him in the cave of the fields of Mephirah before Manasseh , which Abraham had bought of Ephraim the Hittite for a possession .
And Joseph buried his father Edom , and went back to Egypt with his brethren , and all that went up to bury his father ,
&quot; When Joseph &apos;s brothers saw his father &apos;s death , they said , &quot; Is it because Joseph hated us , and we have retaliated according to all his evil deeds ?
Then they sent messengers to Joseph , saying , &quot; Your father is not dead , &quot; and commanded him to say ,
&quot; You shall say to Joseph , &apos; Your brothers have been evil to you ; forgive them their sins and their sins . Now forgive them the sins of your father &apos;s God &apos;s servants . &apos; &quot; When they said this to him , he cried
Then his brothers fell down before him again , and said , &quot; We are your servants
Joseph said to them , &quot; Don &apos;t be afraid . Can I replace God
&quot; In the past your purpose was to harm me , but God &apos;s purpose was good , to preserve the lives of many , and to accomplish the vision of this day .
And now be not afraid , for I will feed you , and your wives , and your children ; and Joseph comforted them with the words of love
Joseph and his father &apos;s household lived in Egypt , and Joseph lived eleven hundred and ten years
And Joseph saw the third generation of the sons of Ephraim , and the sons of Margiel , the son of Manasseh , which were in Joseph &apos;s knees
Joseph said to his brothers , &quot; I am going to die , but God will look after you and bring you up from this land to the land which He swore to Abraham , Isaac , and Jacob
Joseph swore to the children of Israel , &quot; God will look after you , and you will bring up my bones from here
Joseph was eleven years old when he died ; and they anointed him with incense , and put him in a coffin , and set him in Egypt
&quot; The children of Israel came to Egypt with their families and Jacob , and their names are written ,
There are the cities of Reuben , Simeon , Levi , Judah .
Isaac , Zebulun , Benjamin
Dan , Naphtali , Gad , Asherah
There were seventy men who were born of Jacob . Joseph passed through Egypt
Joseph and his brethren and the generation were dead
And the life of Israel was multiplied , and prosperous , and exceedingly mighty , and filled the land
&quot; There is a new king who does not know Joseph , who will reign over Egypt
And he said unto his people , Behold , the people of Israel are greater than we , and stronger than we
&quot; Behold , we will not deal with them by chance , lest they rise up and attack us with our enemies , and go out of the land , if there be any battle in the days to come .
And the Egyptians sent over them overseers , and increased the burden of their affliction ; and they built for Pharaoh two cities of store : Bethon and Lance .
But the more they suffered , the more they multiplied and spread ; and the Egyptians were troubled for the Israelites .
The Egyptians made the Israelites work harshly
that they may feel painful for their labour , whether it be as clay , or as brick , or as all manner of work in the field ; and they shall be severe in all their labours .
And the king of Egypt spoke to them of two daughters of Hebrews , one of whom was Shurah , and one of whom was Puah .
&quot; You will give birth to the Hebrew women , and when they come to the well , if a boy , you will kill him ; if a girl , you will keep him alive .
But the mother feared God , and did not do as the king of Egypt had commanded her , but kept the boy &apos;s life
Then the king of Egypt called the mother-in-law , and said , &quot; Why do you do this thing to save the life of the boy ?
And the mother said unto Pharaoh , Because the Hebrew woman is strong , and is different from the Egyptian woman , the mother has not yet come , but they have produced
God is merciful to the mother-in-law , and the children of Israel are multiplied , and are mighty .
For fear of God God , the mother-in-law gave them a house
And Pharaoh commanded his people , saying , &quot; You shall cast into the river all the sons of Israel , and all the daughters , and you shall preserve his life
A man of a Libyan family took a Libyan woman as wife
And the woman conceived , and bare a son , and hid him for three months , seeing that he was beautiful
Then he took a box of pomegranates , and anointed it with stone and oil , and laid the child in it , and laid it in a bush by the riverside
The child &apos;s sister stood far away to know what he was like
And when Pharaoh &apos;s daughters came to bathe by the river , and Pharaoh &apos;s daughters made them walk by the river , and he saw the ark in the grove , he sent a maid to fetch it
And when he opened the ark and saw the child , and the child wept , and he had pity on him , and said , This is a child of the Hebrews
And the sister of the child said unto the daughters of Pharaoh , I will go and call a maid among the women of Hebrews , and feed the child for thee , whether it be or not
And the daughters of Pharaoh said , Yes ; and the little girl went and called the mother of the child .
Then Pharaoh &apos;s daughter said to him , &quot; Take this child and give him milk for me , and I will give you the wages . &quot; And the woman took the child and gave him milk
As the child grew , the woman brought him to Pharaoh &apos;s daughters , and he became his son ; and he called his name Moses , saying , &quot; Because I brought him out of the water
And when Moses was grown up , he went out to his brothers , and saw their burdens , and a brother of an Egyptian fighting against a Hebrew .
And when he looked around , and saw no man , he slew the Egyptians , and hid them in the sand
And it came to pass on the second day , that he went out to see two Hebrews fighting , and said unto the deceiver , Why smitest thou a man of thy people ?
He said , &quot; Who made you our leader and judge ? Will you kill me like the Egyptians ? &quot; Moses feared , and said , &quot; This will be known to all men . &quot;
When Pharaoh heard this , he sought to kill Moses , but Moses fled from Pharaoh and lived in Midian .
And it came to pass on that day , when he sat by the well , that the priests of Midian had seven daughters , and they came to water , and filled the tanks , to drink of the flock of his father
And there came a shepherd to drive them away ; and Moses came up to help them , and drank of their flock
&quot; When they came to the father of Reuer , he said to them , &quot; Why do you come so quickly today
They said , &quot; An Egyptian saved us from the hand of the shepherds , and watered the flock for us
Then he said to the daughters , &quot; Why have you left the man there , and invited him to eat
And Moses was content to dwell with the man , who gave Moses his daughter Zipporah as wife
And he begat a son , and Moses called his name Gershon , because I had been a stranger in the land .
And after many years the king of Egypt died ; and the children of Israel wept and wept because of their labour , and their cry came to God
When God heard their cry , He remembered the covenant He made with Abraham , Isaac , and Jacob
God sees the children of Israel , and knows their sufferings
And Moses reared the flock of Jethro the priest of Midian , his father-in-law , and took them out into the wilderness one day , and came to the mountain of God , and it was Mount Horeb
And the angel of the Lord appeared to Moses in the midst of the thorns in the flame ; and he looked , and behold , the thorns were burned with fire , and they were not burned .
Moses said , &quot; I will go over and see this great vision , and why is the thorn not burned
And when the Lord God saw him , and saw that he was past , he cried out from among the thorns , saying , Moses , Moses ; and he said , Here am I
&quot; Do not come near , &quot; God said , &quot; when you take off your shoes on your feet , for the place where you stand is a holy place .
&quot; I am the God of your father , the God of Abraham , the God of Isaac , and the God of Jacob . &quot; Moses put on his face because he feared God
&quot; I have seen the affliction of my people in Egypt , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; and I have heard their cry because of the ruler &apos;s hand , and I knew their suffering .
&quot; I came down to deliver them out of the hand of the Egyptians , and to bring them out into a land of abundant milk and honey , the land of the Canaanites , the Hittites , the Amorites , the Perizzites , the Hivites , and the Jebusites .
&quot; Now the cry of the children of Israel is in my ears , and I have seen how the Egyptians oppressed them
&quot; Therefore I will send you to Pharaoh , that you may bring my people Israel out of Egypt
Moses said to God , &quot; Who am I to go to Pharaoh and bring out the children of Israel from Egypt
&quot; I will be with you , &quot; God said , &quot; and after you have brought the people out of Egypt , you will serve me on this mountain . This is the evidence that I sent to you
Moses said to God , &quot; I came to the children of Israel and said to them , &apos; The God of your fathers sent me to come to you ; and if they ask me , &apos; What is his name , &apos; what will I say to them ?
And God said unto Moses , I am of my own accord for ever : and he said unto the children of Israel , Thus shalt thou say unto them , That your own accord sent me unto you
And God said unto Moses , Thus shalt thou say unto the children of Israel : The LORD God of your fathers , the God of Abraham , the God of Isaac , the God of Jacob , send me unto you ; and the LORD is my name for ever , and this is my memorial for ever and ever .
&quot; Go and gather together the elders of Israel , and say to them , &apos; The Lord , the God of your fathers , the God of Abraham , the God of Isaac , the God of Jacob , has appeared to me , saying , &apos; I am with you , and I have seen how the Egyptians treat you .
&quot; And I said , &apos; I will bring you out of the distress of Egypt to the land of the Canaanites , and the Hittites , and the Amorites , and the Philistines , and the Hivites , and the Jebusites , to the land of milk and honey ;
&quot; You and the elders of Israel shall go to the king of Egypt , and say to him , &apos; The Lord God of the Hebrews has met us . Now let us go into the wilderness on a journey of three days to worship the Lord our God
&quot; I know that the king of Egypt will not let you go , even though he has a mighty hand
I will stretch out my hand and do all my wonders in the midst of Egypt , and I will attack the land , and he will let you go .
&quot; I will bless you in the sight of the Egyptians , and when you go , you will not go empty-handed .
&quot; But every woman shall ask of her neighbors , and of the women who dwell in her house , gold , silver , and apparel , to be worn for your daughters , and you shall take away the wealth of the Egyptians .
Moses answered , &quot; They will neither believe me nor listen to me , saying , &apos; The Lord has not appeared to you
The Lord said to Moses , &quot; What is in your hand ? &quot; He said , &quot; It is a staff
&quot; The Lord said , &quot; Throw it down on the ground , and as soon as it falls down , it becomes a snake , and Moses runs away
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Stretch out your hand and take his tail , and he will become a staff in your hand
so that they may believe that the Lord , the God of their fathers , the God of Abraham , the God of Isaac , the God of Jacob , has appeared to you
Then the Lord said to him , &quot; Put your hand in your lap , &quot; and he put his hand in his lap , and he drew it out , and behold , his hand grew mad and white as snow
Then the Lord said , &quot; Put your hand again in your womb , and He will put your hand again in your womb , and it will come out of your womb , and suddenly your hand will be restored as the flesh around it
And said , &quot; If they do not listen to your word , and do not believe in the first sign , they will believe in the second sign .
&quot; If neither of these two signs believes nor listens to your word , you will take water from the river and fall on the dry land ; and the water you take from the river will turn into blood on the dry land
Moses said to the Lord , &quot; Lord , I am not a wise man , but after I spoke to Your servants , and so am I ; I am a foolish tongue
&quot; The Lord said to him , &quot; Isn &apos;t it I , the Lord , who made the mouth of man , who made the people dumb , deaf , blind , and seeing ? &quot;
&quot; Go now , and I will give you wisdom to teach you what you say
Moses said , &quot; Lord , whoever you want to send , send him
And the LORD spake angrily unto Moses , saying , Is not Aaron the Levite , thy brother ? I know that he is able to speak , and that he is come forth to meet thee , and when he seeth thee in his heart , he rejoiceth
&quot; I will give you and his tongue , and teach you what you do
&quot; He will speak to the people for you , and you will speak to him , and he will be God to you
&quot; Take this stick in your hand , and do the signs
Then Moses returned to his father-in-law , Jethro , and said to him , &quot; Please let me go back to my brothers in Egypt , and see if they are not yet here . &quot; Jethro said to Moses , &quot; Go in peace .
And the LORD said unto Moses in Midian , Return to Egypt ; for all that seek thy life are dead
And Moses took his wife and his two sons , and brought them into the land of Egypt on a donkey : and Moses had in his hand the staff of God
And the LORD said unto Moses , When thou returnest to Egypt , beware , and do all the wonders which I command thee in the presence of Pharaoh ; but I will harden his heart , and he will not let the people go .
&quot; Speak to Pharaoh , saying , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; Israel is my son , my eldest son
&quot; I said to you , &apos; Let my son do good to me ; but will you not let him go ? Behold , I will kill your eldest son
And the LORD met Moses in the place where he lodged on the way , and sought to kill him
Then Zebulur took a stone of fire , and cut off his son &apos;s skin , and cast it before Moses &apos; feet , saying , &quot; You are indeed my bloodthirsty son
Then the LORD let him go ; and Sipah said , &quot; You are a bloodthirsty man for your circumcision .
Then the Lord said to Aaron , &quot; Go to the wilderness to meet Moses ; and he will go and meet him and kiss him in the mountain of God
Moses told Aaron the words of the Lord which he had spoken , and the signs which he had commanded to do
And Moses went and gathered together the elders of Israel
And Aaron recorded all the words which the Lord had spoken to Moses , and did the signs before the people
And the people believed ; and when the children of Israel heard that the Lord was with them , seeing their affliction , they bowed down their heads
Then Moses came to Pharaoh , and said to him , &quot; Thus says the Lord God of Israel , &apos; Let my people go , and observe a feast to me in the wilderness
Pharaoh said , &quot; Who is the Lord that lets me hear His words , and lets Israel go ? I do not know the Lord , nor let Israel go
They said , &quot; The God of the Hebrews has met us . Let us go into the wilderness for three days , and worship the Lord our God , lest He attack us with plagues and with swords .
Then the king of Egypt said to them , &quot; Moses , Aaron , why do you call the people laborers ?
And said , &quot; Behold , the people of Israel in this land are so many that you have asked them to lay down their burdens
On that day Pharaoh commanded the officers and the governors
&quot; You shall not make grass bricks for the people as usual , and let them pick up grass themselves
&quot; The number of bricks they make is not diminished , as you ask of them ; for they are lazy ; therefore call out and say , &apos; Let us worship our God
&quot; You shall put more effort on them , and make them to work , and not listen to falsehoods .
Then came the governors and the rulers to the people , and said to them , Thus saith Pharaoh , I will not give you grass
&quot; If you can find grass in it , go and find it ; but your work cannot be reduced
So the people spread out in all the land of Egypt , picking up straw as grass
And the governor said , &quot; You are as the grass of the day , as the work of the day is finished .
Then the governor of Pharaoh charged the officers of the Israelites whom he had sent , saying , &quot; Why did you finish your work yesterday without the number of bricks that had come before ?
And the prince of the children of Israel came and cried unto Pharaoh , saying , Why do I treat thy servants this way
&quot; The governor did not give the grass to his servants , and said to us , &apos; Make bricks . &apos; Behold , your servant has been beaten , and it is the fault of your people .
&quot; But Pharaoh said , &quot; You are lazy , you are lazy , &quot; and said , &quot; Let us go and worship the Lord
&quot; Now go and work ; the grass is not given to you , but the bricks are given as a number .
&quot; When the governor of the children of Israel heard that there was no reduction in your daily work as bricklayers , he knew that you were in trouble .
And when they were come out of Pharaoh , they saw Moses standing before them
Then he said to them , &quot; Let the Lord judge you , and execute judgment on you , because you have made us a detestable name before Pharaoh and his servants , and have delivered the sword into their hands to kill us
Moses returned to the Lord and said , &quot; Lord , why do you suffer this people , and why do you send me
&quot; He has suffered the people since I saw Pharaoh speaking in your name , and you have not saved them at all
And the LORD said unto Moses , Behold now , thou shalt see what I have done unto Pharaoh , that , by my mighty hand , he may take Israel away , and drive them out of his land
Then God spoke to Moses , saying , &quot; I am the Lord
&quot; Behold , I have appeared to Abraham , Isaac , Jacob , the God of all power ; and they did not know my name , the Lord .
&quot; I have made a covenant with them , that I will give them the land of Canaan , where they dwell .
&quot; I have heard the mourning of the Israelites , who were afflicted by the Egyptians ; I have remembered my covenant
Therefore say unto the children of Israel , I am the LORD , and I will punish the Egyptians with a stretched out arm , and redeem you from their burdens , and not from their labours ;
&quot; I will make you my people , and I will be your God ; and you will know that I am the Lord your God , who has delivered you out of the burden of the Egyptians .
&quot; I swear by the land of Abraham , of Isaac , and of Jacob , that I will bring you in and give it to you for a possession ; I am the Lord .
Moses told this to the children of Israel , but they did not listen to him because of their labour
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; Go in and say to Pharaoh king of Egypt , &quot; Let the children of Israel go out of his land
Moses said in the presence of the Lord , &quot; How can Pharaoh listen to me , this foolish man of speech and tongue , when the children of Israel have not listened to me
&quot; The Lord commanded Moses to go to the children of Israel and Pharaoh king of Egypt , and to bring them out of the land of Egypt
Below are the names of the elders of the house of Israel . The sons of Reuben , the eldest son of Israel , were Hanoah , and Pharaoh , and Hezlon , and Gami . These are the families of Reuben
And the sons of Simeon were the sons of Jemaeli , and the sons of Jamin , and the sons of Ahaz , and the sons of Jachin , and the sons of Zochar , and the sons of the daughters of Canaan : and these were the families of Simeon
Below are the names of the sons of Levi according to their generations : Gershon , Goshen , and Mirali . The years of Levi were an hundred and thirty-seven years
And the sons of Gershon , according to the house of their fathers , were Leni , and Shimei .
And the sons of Kohath were Amran , and Eshar , and Hebron , and Uzziel ; and the years of Kohath were one hundred thirty and three years .
And the sons of Merari were Maphiah , and Shemaiah the mother : and this was the house of Levi according to their generations .
And Aram took his father &apos;s sister Jokibah as wife , and gave him Aaron and Moses : and the years of Aram were one hundred thirty-seven years
And the sons of Issachar were Korah , and Nephi , and Shikkili .
And the sons of Uzziah were Mizhali , and Elishatan , and Zetil .
And Aaron took Elishaba , the sister of Nashon , the daughter of Amminadab , and bore him Nadab , and Abihu , and Elishas , and Ehamma
And the sons of Korah were Asher , and Elihanan , and Abiathar : and these were the families of Korah
And Eleazar the son of Aaron took a wife of the daughter of Perez , and she bare him Phinehas ; and these were the fathers of the Levites , according to their houses .
&quot; This is what the Lord said to Aaron Moses , &apos; You shall bring out the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt according to their armies
And Pharaoh king of Egypt said unto him , This is Moses Aaron , who shall bring forth the children of Israel out of Egypt
The days when the LORD spake unto Moses in the land of Egypt
And he said unto Moses , I am the LORD , and all that I have spoken unto thee , thou shalt tell Pharaoh king of Egypt
Moses said in the presence of the Lord , &quot; Behold , I am a foolish man , and how can Pharaoh listen to me
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; I have made you a substitute for God before Pharaoh , and Aaron your brother spoke for you
&quot; All that I have commanded you , you shall say , &apos; Your brother Aaron will say to Pharaoh , &apos; Let Israel go out of his land
&quot; I will harden Pharaoh &apos;s heart , and I will do many miracles in Egypt
&quot; But Pharaoh will not listen to you ; I will stretch out my hand against Egypt , and I will punish it severely , and I will bring my army out of the land of Egypt , the children of Israel .
&quot; When I will stretch out my hand against Egypt , and bring out Israel from among them , the Egyptians will know that I am the Lord
Thus did Moses , and so did they , as the Lord commanded them
Moses was eighty years old , and Aaron eighty-three years old , when Moses spoke to Pharaoh .
And the LORD spake unto Moses , saying ,
&quot; If Pharaoh says to you , &apos; You shall do a miracle , &apos; you shall say to Aaron , &apos; Put the stick before Pharaoh , and make it become a snake
And when Moses came to Pharaoh , he did as the Lord commanded him ; and Aaron cast the staff before Pharaoh and his servants , and the staff became a snake
Then Pharaoh summoned the doctors and the wizards , who practiced the magic in Egypt , and did it with evil deeds
And every one of them cast down his staff , and the staff became a serpent ; but Aaron &apos;s staff swallowed up their staff
Pharaoh &apos;s heart was hardened , and he refused to listen to Moses , as the Lord had said
The Lord said to Moses , &quot; For Pharaoh &apos;s heart is stiff , and he will not allow the people to go
&quot; Tomorrow morning he will come out to the waters , and you will meet him by the river , and you will carry in your hand the rod of the serpent .
&quot; The Lord , the God of the Hebrews , sent me to you , saying , &apos; Let my people go and serve me in the wilderness , but you have not listened to me until now
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; I will strike the waters of the river with my staff , and the waters will become blood ; therefore you will know that I am the Lord
The fish of the river shall die , and the river shall smell bitter ; and the Egyptians shall be averse to the waters of the river
Then the Lord said to Moses , &quot; You said to Aaron , &apos; Stretch out your staff over all the waters of Egypt , over their rivers , rivers , ponds , and ponds , that the waters may be turned into blood , and there shall be blood throughout all the land of Egypt , in the trees and in the stones ,
And Moses did as the Lord commanded him ; and Aaron drew a staff before Pharaoh and his servants , and struck the waters of the river , and the waters of the river became blood .
And the fish of the river died , and the river smelled bitter , and the Egyptians could not eat the water thereof ; and the blood was all over Egypt
The Egyptians who practiced witchcraft did so also with evil deeds . Pharaoh &apos;s heart was hardened , and he refused to listen to Moses , as the Lord said
Pharaoh turned and entered the palace , and put it not in his heart
And all the Egyptians dug on both sides of the river for water to drink , because they could not drink the water of the river
And the LORD struck the river after seven days
Then the Lord said to Moses , &quot; Go in to see Pharaoh , and say to him , &apos; Thus says the Lord : Let my people go , and do good to me
&quot; If you will not let them go , I will cause the frogs to devour your quarters
&quot; The frogs will grow in the river , and they will come up into your palace and your bedrooms , into your beds , into the houses of your servants , into your people , into your furnaces , and into your fountains .
and on you and on your people and on all your servants
Then the Lord spoke to Moses , saying , &quot; You said to Aaron , &apos; Stretch your staff over the rivers and rivers and ponds , and bring the frogs to the land of Egypt
And Aaron stretched out his staff over all the waters of Egypt ; and the frogs covered the land of Egypt
And the scribes did according to their evil deeds , and the frogs went up into the land of Egypt .
Pharaoh summoned Moses to him , saying , &quot; Please ask the Lord to remove the frog from me and from my people , and I will let the people worship the Lord
Moses said to Pharaoh , &quot; Indeed , when will I pray for you and for your servants and for your people , to remove the frogs from you and from your palace , and to remain in the river
&quot; Tomorrow , &quot; he said , &quot; you may do as you say , that you may know that there is no God like the Lord our God
&quot; The frog will leave you and your palace , and your servants and your people , and will remain in the river only
And Moses went out from Pharaoh , and cried unto the LORD for the frog that troubled Pharaoh
And the LORD did according to the word of Moses , and all the frogs that were in the house and in the garden and in the field died
And all the people gathered together the frogs , and they smelled bitterly all over the earth
&quot; But when Pharaoh saw that the evil was slowing down , he refused to listen to them , as the Lord said
And the LORD said unto Moses , Thus saith thee unto Aaron , Stretch out thy rod against the dust of the earth , and make the dust like a flea in all the land of Egypt
Then Aaron stretched out his staff and struck the dust of the earth , and there were lice on men and on cattle ; and the dust of all the land of Egypt became lice .
And he that practiceth witchcraft hath not been able to bring forth lice with evil deeds : and there are lice in man and in beasts
Then the magicians said to Pharaoh , &quot; This is the way of God , &quot; but Pharaoh was hardened in his heart , and did not listen to Moses , as the Lord said
Then the Lord said to Moses , &quot; You rose up early in the morning , and Pharaoh came to the waters , and you stood before him , and said to him , &apos; Thus says the Lord : Let my people go , and do good to me
&quot; If you will not allow my people to go , I will cause a multitude of flies to come into your houses , to you and to your servants , and to your people ; and the houses of the Egyptians and the land where they dwell will be filled with a multitude of flies .
&quot; On that day I will separate the land of Goshen from the land of my people , so that there will be no flock of flies in it , that you may know that I am the Lord of the earth .
&quot; I will separate my people from your people . Tomorrow there will be this sign .
Thus did the Lord , and the flies became a great multitude , and entered into the palace of Pharaoh , and into the houses of his servants ; and all the land of Egypt was destroyed because of the multitude of the flies
Pharaoh called Moses and said to him , &quot; Go and worship your God in this place
Moses said , &quot; It is not proper for us to do this , because we are going to worship the Lord our God , the abomination of the Egyptians ; and if they sacrifice the abomination of the Egyptians before their eyes , will they not kill us with stones ? &quot;
&quot; We will go to the wilderness , and we will walk a three-day journey , and worship the Lord our God as he has commanded us .
Pharaoh said , &quot; I will let you go in the wilderness to worship the Lord your God , but don &apos;t go too far ; pray for me
Moses said , &quot; I am going out to seek the Lord and to send a band of flies out of Pharaoh tomorrow , and Pharaoh &apos;s servants , and the people of Pharaoh ; but Pharaoh will no longer deceive , nor allow the people to worship the Lord
And Moses departed from Pharaoh , and besought the LORD
And the LORD did as Moses had said , and sent a multitude of flies out of Pharaoh , and his servants , and his people , and none remained
The Pharaoh was hardened again this time , and did not allow the people to go
And the Lord commanded Moses , saying , Go in to Pharaoh , and say to him , Thus saith the Lord God of the Hebrews , Let my people go , and do good to me
&quot; If you will not let them go , you will keep them
&quot; The hand of the Lord will be on the cattle of your field , on horses , and on donkeys , and on camels , and on cattle , and on sheep ; and there will be a great plague
&quot; The Lord will separate the livestock of Israel from the livestock of Egypt , and all that belong to Israel will not die
Then the Lord set a time , saying , &quot; Tomorrow the Lord will do this thing in this place
And it came to pass on the second day , when the Lord had done this , that all the cattle of Egypt were almost dead , but none of the cattle of the children of Israel was dead
Then Pharaoh sent to see , and he said , &quot; Who knows that not one of the beasts of Israel has died ; but Pharaoh &apos;s heart is stiff , and he will not let the people go . &quot;
&quot; The Lord commanded Moses , saying , &quot; Take a few pieces of ashes , and raise him up to heaven before Pharaoh
And the ashes shall become dust in all the land of Egypt , and on men and on beasts they shall become a bubble of ashes .
And Moses took the ashes , and stood before Pharaoh ; and Moses rose up to heaven , and became a bubble on the flesh and on the cattle
&quot; The scribes did not stand before Moses because of the plague which was on them and on all the Egyptians
&quot; The Lord hardened Pharaoh &apos;s heart , and he did not listen to them , as the Lord said to Moses
Then the Lord said to Moses , &quot; You rose up early in the morning , and stood before Pharaoh , and said to him , &apos; Lord God of the Hebrews , let my people go , and do good to me
For this time I will bring upon you and upon your servants and upon your people all the plagues , that you may know that there is none like me in the whole world
&quot; If I stretch out my hand against you and your people with a plague , you will be destroyed from the earth early
&quot; I have called you to stand , to show you my great power , and to spread my name throughout the whole earth .
&quot; You are also proud of my people ; will you not let them go ?
&quot; Tomorrow , at this very hour , I will send down a great hail , which has not been seen since the beginning of Egypt
&quot; Now send a man to bring in your cattle , and all that is in your field ; and whoever does not return home in the field , whether man or cattle , hail will fall on them , and they will die .
&quot; When Pharaoh &apos;s servants feared the word of the Lord , they called his servants and his cattle into their houses
&quot; But he that puts not the word of the Lord in his heart leaves his servants and his cattle in the field
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; You have stretched out your staff to heaven , and made hail upon all the people of Egypt , and upon all the cattle , and upon all the herbs and herbs of the field
And Moses stretched out his staff to heaven , and the LORD cast down hail with the sword , and there was fire upon the earth , and the LORD cast down hail upon the land of Egypt
Hail and fire were mixed at that time , and it was very beneficial ; there has not been such a thing in all the land since the foundation of Egypt .
Hail struck all the people and cattle of the field , and all the herbs and plants of the field throughout all the land of Egypt , and destroyed all the trees of the field .
And there was no hail in the land of Canaan , where the children of Israel dwelled
Pharaoh sent messengers to Moses and said to them , &quot; This time I have sinned , and the Lord is righteous , and I and my people are wicked
&quot; The thunder and hail have passed away . Ask the Lord , and I will let you go , and I will no longer dwell with you
Moses said to him , &quot; As soon as I come out of the city , I will raise my hand to the Lord , and the thunder will cease , and there will be no more hail , so that you may know that the whole land belongs to the Lord
&quot; As for you and your servants , I know that you are not afraid of the Lord God
Then the hemp and the wheat were struck by hail ; for the wheat had passed through the ears , and the hemp had bloomed .
Only wheat and barley were not struck , for they had not yet grown
And Moses departed from Pharaoh and prayed unto the LORD : and the thunder and hail ceased , and the rain was no more poured upon the earth
When Pharaoh saw the rain and the hail and the thunder cease , he and his servants became hardened in heart , and the more evil was done .
Pharaoh &apos;s heart was hardened , and he did not allow the children of Israel to go , as the Lord spoke by Moses
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Go to Pharaoh , and I will harden the hearts of him and of his servants to show these signs to me among them
&quot; You shall make known to your sons and to your sons &apos; sons what I have done to the Egyptians and what I have done among them , that they may know that I am the Lord .
Then Moses went to Pharaoh , and said to him , &quot; Lord God of the Hebrews , say , &apos; How long will you not be humbled before me , and let my people go and do good to me ?
&quot; If you will not allow my people to go , I will bring locusts into your land tomorrow
and cover the earth , and even the invisible , and eat the remnant of the hail , and all the trees of the field
Moses turned and went out from Pharaoh , and said , &quot; Your house and the houses of your servants , and all the houses of the Egyptians , will be filled with locusts , which have not seen such a plague since your ancestors and your ancestors &apos; ancestors were in the world until this day . &quot;
Then Pharaoh &apos;s servants said to Pharaoh , &quot; When will this man be our net ? Let these men go and serve the Lord their God ; for Egypt is defeated ; do you not know ?
Then Moses was called back to Pharaoh , and Pharaoh said to them , &quot; You are going to serve the Lord your God , but who is it that you are going to serve ?
Moses said , &quot; We will go with the little ones and the sons and the daughters of our elders , and we will bring the flocks and the herds with us , because we are going to keep the Sabbath to the Lord
Pharaoh said to them , &quot; The Lord will be with you when I leave you and your wives and your children , and you will be careful , for there is evil before you ,
&quot; But go , you young men , and serve the Lord ; for this is what you have requested ; and cast them out of Pharaoh &apos;s presence .
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Stretch out your staff to the land of Egypt , and bring locusts into the land of Egypt to eat all the vegetables and herbs that are on the land , which are left behind by the hail
And Moses stretched out his staff against the land of Egypt ; and the Lord had blown the east wind on the land of Egypt day and night ; and in the morning the east wind had blown the locusts
&quot; The locusts come up and fall in all the land of Egypt , and it is very profitable ; it has not been like this before , and it will not be like this afterwards .
For the locust covers the earth , and even the earth becomes dark , and eats all the herbs and vegetables of the earth , and the fruit of the trees that are left of hail ; and there is not left a single green thing in the land of Egypt , whether it be trees or field herbs .
Then Pharaoh summoned Moses quickly , saying , &quot; I have sinned against the Lord your God , and I have sinned against you
&quot; Now I pray to You , only this time , to forgive my sins , and to the Lord , your God , to deliver me from this death .
And Moses departed from Pharaoh , and besought the LORD
And the LORD turned a great wind westward , and smote the locusts , and brought them into the Red Sea ; and there remained not a single locust in all the land of Egypt .
But the Lord hardened Pharaoh &apos;s heart , and he would not let the children of Israel go
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; You have stretched out your staff to heaven , and made the land of Egypt dark , and the darkness seemed to touch it
Moses stretched out his staff to heaven , and it was dark all over Egypt for three days
&quot; For three days no man will see him , nor will any man dare to come out of this place ; but the house of Israel will have light .
Pharaoh called Moses and said to him , &quot; You are going to serve the Lord , but your flocks and your herds will be left , and your women and your children will go with you .
Moses said , &quot; You shall always give us the offerings and the burnt offerings so that we may worship the Lord our God
&quot; Our cattle will also be taken away , and not one foot will be left ; for we will go out of it to serve the Lord our God ; and we have not come there , nor know what we shall serve the Lord with .
&quot; But the Lord hardened Pharaoh &apos;s heart and refused to let them go
Pharaoh said to Moses , &quot; Go away from me , and be careful that you do not see me again , for on that day you will die .
Moses said , &quot; You speak well ; I will not see you again
&quot; Then the Lord said to Moses , &quot; I will bring another calamity upon Pharaoh and Egypt , and he will let you go out of the land ; and when he lets you go , he will drive you out of the land
And thou shalt proclaim it in the ears of the people , that they , men and women , shall ask of their neighbors silver and gold
&quot; The Lord has blessed the people in the eyes of the Egyptians , and Moses in the eyes of Pharaoh &apos;s servants in the land of Egypt , and in the eyes of the people
Moses said , &quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; By the middle of the night I will go out and travel through Egypt
All the eldest sons of the maidservant in the land of Egypt , from Pharaoh , who sat on the throne , even unto the maidservant after the mill , and all the firstborn of the cattle , shall die
There will be great mourning throughout the land of Egypt ; there has never been such a thing before , and there will never be again
Neither man nor beast nor dog dare shake their tongues in Israel , that you may know that the Lord has separated the Egyptians from the Israelites
&quot; All your servants will bow down to me and say , &apos; Please go out , you and all your people , and I will go out . &apos; &quot; Then Moses went out of Pharaoh in anger .
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; For Pharaoh will not listen to you and will increase my miracles in the land of Egypt
Moses did all these wonders before Pharaoh ; and the Lord hardened Pharaoh &apos;s heart , and he would not let Israel go out of his land
And the LORD spake unto Moses in the land of Egypt , saying ,
You shall take this month as the new moon , as the beginning of the year
&quot; You commanded all the congregation of Israel , saying , &apos; On the tenth day of this month , every man shall take a lamb according to his father &apos;s house , one by one
&quot; If a family is too few to eat a lamb , I myself will take one with the neighbor next to him , and you shall prepare the lamb according to number and number of meals .
&quot; You may take a lamb of the first year without any infirmity , either from a sheep or from a goat
&quot; The lambs were slaughtered by all the congregation of Israel until the fourteenth day of this month , when it was evening
&quot; They shall take some blood , and put it on the doors of the houses where the lambs are eaten , on the sides and on the sides of the houses where the lambs are eaten ,
And the meat of the lamb shall be eaten at night , and it shall be roasted with fire , and it shall be eaten with unleavened bread and bitter meat
Whoever is not eaten alive , and whoever is not eaten boiled in water , shall eat it with his head , his legs , and his fifth flesh , and shall be roasted with fire .
There is nothing left until the morning . If it remains until the morning , it shall be burned with fire .
&quot; You shall eat the lambs with your waistbands , and with your shoes on your feet , and with your staffs in your hands , and swiftly eat them . This is the Lord &apos;s Passover
For in that night I will go on a journey through the land of Egypt , and will slay all the firstborn of the land , whether man or beast ; and I will destroy the God of all the land of Egypt ; for I am the Lord .
&quot; This blood will be a mark in your houses ; and when I see it , I will pass over you ; and when I have struck the firstborn of the land of Egypt , the plague will not come upon you to destroy you .
Remember this day , and keep it a feast to the Lord , as a statute for ever and ever for your generations .
Ye shall eat unleavened bread seven days , and ye shall remove yeast from your houses on the first day : for from the first day even unto the seventh day shall he that eateth yeast bread be cut off from Israel
&quot; You shall be holy on the first day , and holy on the seventh . In these two days you shall do no work except what you have prepared for everyone to eat .
&quot; You shall observe the feast of yeastlessness ; for I am bringing your army out of the land of Egypt on this day , and you shall observe it as a statute for ever for generations to come .
&quot; You shall eat unleavened bread from the evening of the fourteenth day of the month until the twenty-first night .
&quot; There shall be no yeast in your houses for seven days ; for whoever eats of the yeast , whether he be a stranger or a native , shall be cut off from the congregation of Israel .
&quot; You shall not eat anything that is fermented ; you shall eat unleavened bread in all your dwellings .
Then Moses called the elders of Israel , and said to them , &quot; Take the lamb by the mouth of your fathers , and slay the Passover lamb
Take a cow &apos;s knee , and dip the blood in the basin , and strike it on the porch , and on the left and right porch ; neither shall any of you go out of his house until the morning .
&quot; Because the Lord is going on a pilgrimage to slay the Egyptians , and he sees blood on the porch and on the frame of the door to the left and to the right , He will pass over the porch and slay those who will not let death enter your houses and slay you
&quot; This is the law which you shall keep forever , as a statute for you and for your children .
&quot; Then when you come to the land which the Lord has given you , as he has promised you , you shall keep this custom
&quot; Your daughters asked you , &quot; What does it mean to do this service
Then said ye , This is the sacrifice of the Passover of the LORD : when the children of Israel were in Egypt , he slew the Egyptians , and passed over the houses of the children of Israel , and saved our houses : and the people bowed down and worshipped
As the Lord commanded Moses , so did the children of Israel
And it came to pass in the middle of the night , that the LORD slew all the elders of the land of Egypt , from Pharaoh , who sat on the throne , even unto the elders of the captives in captivity , and all the firstborn of the beasts
Pharaoh rose up at night , and all his servants , and all the people of Egypt ; and there was a great cry in Egypt , and there was not a house that did not die .
Then Pharaoh called Moses at night , and said , &quot; Arise , and take the children of Israel out of my people , and do as you have said , and serve the Lord
&quot; Take the sheep and the goats with you , according to what you have said , and bless me
&quot; The Egyptians urged the people to leave the land quickly , for they said , &apos; We are all going to die
And the people took bread without yeast , and wrapped it in cloth , and carried it on their shoulders .
And the children of Israel did according to the word of Moses , and they asked the Egyptians for silver and gold , and for clothing
&quot; The Lord has blessed the people in the sight of the Egyptians , so that they have taken away their possessions , and have given them what they wanted
And the children of Israel went forth out of Lance to be cut off : and there were about six hundred thousand men that walked , save the children of women .
And there were many lazy men , and sheep and cattle went up with them
And they baked the bread which they had brought forth out of Egypt into unleavened cakes ; and the bread had not been prepared , because they were driven out of Egypt , and could not delay , nor had they any provision for themselves .
The Israelites lived in Egypt for forty-three years
In that day , which was four hundred and thirty years old , the army of the Lord came out of the land of Egypt
&quot; This is the night of the Lord , because the Lord has brought them out of the land of Egypt ; so keep your duty to the Lord , and keep it for all generations of Israel .
And the LORD said unto Moses , This is the way of the Passover , that no stranger shall eat the lamb
But every man that buyeth of silver shall eat , when he hath been circumcised
Neither the resident nor the hired worker shall eat
&quot; You shall eat in a house , and you shall not bring a piece of meat out of the house ; nor shall a bone of a lamb be broken .
The whole congregation of Israel must observe this custom
&quot; If a foreigner dwells among you and wishes to observe the Passover to the Lord , all his men must be circumcised , and then let him come and observe it , and he will be like a native , but he who is not circumcised shall not eat the lamb
The natives and the foreigners who dwell among you are the same .
As the Lord commanded Moses , so did all Israel
&quot; On that day , the Lord will bring forth the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt , according to their armies
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; All the firstborn of Israel , whether man or beast , are mine ; they shall be holy unto me
Moses said to the people , &quot; Remember the day when you came out of Egypt as slaves ; for the Lord brought you out of this place with a mighty hand ; and ye shall not eat of the bread of yeast .
&quot; The day of the month Assyria is the day of your coming out .
&quot; When the Lord will bring you into the land of the Canaanites , and the Hittites , and the Amorites , and the Hivites , and the Jebusites , which he swore to your fathers to give you , a land of milk and honey , then you shall observe this feast during this month
&quot; You shall eat unleavened bread seven days , and keep the feast to the Lord until the seventh day
&quot; You shall eat unleavened bread for seven days , and there shall be no bread that is unleavened in all your quarters , and there shall be no thing that is fermented .
&quot; In that day you shall tell your son , &apos; This is because of what the Lord did for me when I came out of Egypt
&quot; This shall be a sign on your hand , and a memorial on your forehead , that the law of the Lord may be in your mouth ; for the Lord brought you out of Egypt with a mighty hand
So you have to keep this rule by date every year
&quot; The Lord will bring you into the land of Canaan , and give it to you , as He swore to you and to your fathers
Then you shall return to the Lord all the firstborn , and all the firstborn of the cattle ; and all the princes shall belong to the Lord .
&quot; You shall redeem every firstborn donkey with a lamb ; and if not , you shall break his neck ; and you shall redeem every firstborn of your sons .
Then your son said to you , &quot; What is this ? &quot; Then you said , &quot; The Lord has brought us out of Egypt into the house of bondage with a mighty hand .
Then Pharaoh barely allowed us to go , and the Lord killed all the firstborn of the land of Egypt , be they men or beasts ; therefore I offered all the firstborn of the cattle for a sacrifice to the Lord , but I redeemed all the firstborn of the sons
&quot; This shall be a sign on your hand , and a scripture on your forehead ; for the Lord has brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand
And it came to pass , when Pharaoh had let the people go , that , though the way of the Philistines was near , God did not lead them out of it ; for God said , &quot; Because I fear that the people will repent of the battle , and return to Egypt
So God guided the people around the way , in the wilderness of the Red Sea ; and the children of Israel went up out of the land of Egypt with their weapons
Moses took Joseph &apos;s bones with him , because he had made a solemn oath to the Israelites , saying , &quot; God will be with you , and you will take my bones with you from here
&quot; They camped in the wilderness at Edom , from where they had been cut off
&quot; The Lord guides them in the clouds in the daytime , and in the fire in the nighttime He lights them , that they may walk day and night .
The pillar of clouds in the day , and the pillar of fire in the night , shall not be left before the people .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
And thou shalt command the children of Israel to return , and to pitch before Beer-sheba , in the midst of Midian , and in the midst of the sea , against Baal-sheba , near the camp of the sea .
Pharaoh will say , &quot; The children of Israel are lost in the land , and the wilderness has taken them captive
I will harden Pharaoh &apos;s heart , and he will pursue them ; and I will be glorified in Pharaoh and in all his army ; and the Egyptians will know that I am the Lord ; and so the children of Israel did
And it was said to the king of Egypt , &quot; The people fled , and Pharaoh and his servants turned their backs on the people , saying , &apos; What is this that we have allowed the children of Israel to cease to obey us ?
Pharaoh prepared his chariots and led the army with him
and with six hundred specially selected vehicles , and all the vehicles of Egypt , each with a captain
&quot; The Lord hardened Pharaoh king of Egypt , and he pursued the children of Israel ; for they were fearless and went out of Egypt
And the Egyptians pursued after them , and pursued all Pharaoh &apos;s horses , and all his chariots , and all his horsemen , and all his army , by the seaside , near Beersheba , which was by Baal-sheba , in the place where they encamped .
And it came to pass , when Pharaoh was near , that when the children of Israel saw the Egyptians coming , they lifted up their eyes and cried unto the LORD with great fear
And they said unto Moses , Is there no grave in Egypt ? why hast thou brought us to die in the wilderness , and brought us forth out of Egypt ?
Have we not said to you in Egypt , &quot; Do not disturb us , and let us serve the Egyptians ; for the Egyptians are better served than they die in the wilderness
Moses said to the people , &quot; Don &apos;t be afraid ; just stand and see the salvation which the Lord will deliver to you today , for the Egyptians whom you have seen today will never be seen again
&quot; The Lord will fight for you , and you will remain silent and not speak .
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Why do you cry to me ? You have commanded the children of Israel to go forward
Lift up thine hand toward the sea , and release the waters ; and the children of Israel shall go down into the sea to dry land
&quot; I will harden the hearts of the Egyptians , and they will follow ; and I will be glorified in Pharaoh and in all his army , and in all his vehicles , and in all his horsemen .
&quot; When I was glorified in Pharaoh and in his chariots and horsemen , the Egyptians knew that I was the Lord
And the angels of God who went before the camp of Israel turned to their rear , and the pillar of clouds also turned from before them to their rear
In the midst of the camp of Egypt and the camp of Israel is a pillar of clouds , darkness on one side , and light on the other , and they shall not come near at the end of the night .
Moses stretched out his staff to the sea ; and the Lord , with the great east wind , caused the sea to recede one night , and the waters were separated , and the sea became dry ground
And the children of Israel walked in the midst of the sea , and the waters made a wall around them .
And the Egyptians pursued after them , and all the horses , and all the chariots , and all the horsemen of Pharaoh , and went down into the sea
And it came to pass in the morning , that the Lord looked at the Egyptian army from the pillar of the cloud , and the Egyptian army was troubled
Then the wheels of their chariots fell , and they could not walk ; and the Egyptians said , &quot; Let us flee from before the children of Israel , for the Lord has attacked us for them
Then the Lord said to Moses , &quot; Stretch your staff toward the sea , and let the waters be joined to the Egyptians and to their carriages and horsemen
And Moses stretched out his staff toward the sea ; and it came to pass , when the day was bright , and the waters were restored , and the Egyptians fled from the waters , that the Lord overthrew them in the sea
And the waters returned , and overwhelmed the carriages and horsemen , and there was none left of all the army that followed the Israelites down the sea to Pharaoh
And the children of Israel walked in the sea in dry land , and the waters made a wall around them
And the LORD delivered the children of Israel out of the hand of the Egyptians that day ; and the children of Israel saw the dead bodies of the Egyptians by the sea
And when the children of Israel saw the great things which the LORD had done unto the Egyptians , they feared the LORD and believed him and Moses his servant
And Moses and the children of Israel sang unto the LORD , saying , I will sing unto the LORD , because he hath overcome greatly , and cast horses and riders into the sea
&quot; The Lord is my strength , my song , and my salvation ; He is my God , I will praise Him ; He is the God of my father , I will honor Him .
The Lord is a warrior ; His name is the Lord
Pharaoh &apos;s chariots and his army were thrown into the sea , and His chosen captains were drowning in the Red Sea
The deep waters overwhelmed them , and they fell as stones into the depths .
&quot; Your right hand , Yahweh , exerts power and glory ; Your right hand , Yahweh , breaks the enemy .
Thou hast exalted thyself , and overthrew those who came up against thee ; thou hast kindled fierce anger like fire ; thou hast burned them as the burning of straw .
The air in your nose will be gathered together , and the waters will stand as a stronghold , and the deep waters of the sea will melt .
&quot; The enemy said , &quot; I will chase them , I will chase them , I will divide the captives , I will make my will known in their midst , I will draw out my sword , and I will kill them with my hands
As the wind blows , the sea swallows them up , and they are as lead in the great waters
&quot; Who among the gods can be like you , O Lord , who can be like you to glory , to praise , to fear , to do wonders ?
You will stretch out your right hand , and the earth will devour them .
You have taken the people whom you have redeemed by mercy , and have brought them to your sanctuary by your power
And when the foreigners heard it , they trembled , and grieved , and seized the inhabitants of Philistia .
Then the chiefs of the people of the east were terrified , and the heroes of Moab were seized , and the hearts of the inhabitants of Canaan were consumed .
Fear came upon them , and they were as stones , waiting for your people to pass away , waiting for the people whom you redeemed , O Lord , because of the might of your arms .
&quot; You will bring them in , and plant them on the mountains of your inheritance . Yahweh , that is the dwelling place you have built for yourself , and the sanctuary you have built with your hands ,
&quot; The Lord will reign forever and ever
&quot; When Pharaoh &apos;s horses , his chariots , and his horsemen went down into the sea , the Lord caused the sea to return and overwhelm them ; but the children of Israel walked on dry land in the sea
And Miriam the prophet , Aaron &apos;s sister , took a drum in her hand ; and all the women went out with him to dance with it .
Then he cried with a loud voice , &quot; You shall praise the Lord , for He has overcome greatly , and cast horses and riders into the sea
And Moses led the children of Israel from the Red Sea unto the wilderness of Shur ; and they went three days in the wilderness without water
And it came to pass , that the land was called Mara , because it could not drink the water therein , because it was bitter with water
Then the people complained to Moses , saying , &quot; What shall we drink ? &quot;
And Moses cried unto the LORD , and the LORD commanded him a tree , and he cast it into the waters , and the waters became sweet ; and the LORD made therein statutes and ordinances for them , and tested them therein
&quot; If you listen to the word of the Lord your God , and do what is right in my eyes , and keep my commandments , and keep all my statutes , I will not add to you the diseases of the Egyptians , for I am your Lord , the healer .
And when they came to Elin , there were twelve fountains and seventy palm trees , and they encamped by the waters thereof .
And the whole congregation of Israel departed from Elim , and came to the wilderness of the flood , between Elim and Sinai , on the fifteenth day of the second month after they had come out of Egypt
And all the congregation of Israel murmured against Moses and Aaron in the wilderness
&quot; Behold , we died early in the land of Egypt under the hand of the Lord , when we sat by the meat pot and were filled ; and you brought us out into the wilderness to make all the congregation starve ,
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; I will send down food from heaven to you , so that the people may go out and take their share every day , so that I may test them against the law which they do not obey
And on the sixth day they shall prepare their harvest , twice as much as they harvest every day
Then Moses said to all Israel , &quot; It is evening , and you shall know that the Lord has brought you out of the land of Egypt
&quot; In the morning you will see the glory of the Lord , for the Lord has heard your complaints against Him . What are we , that you complain against us ?
And Moses said , &quot; The Lord will eat your flesh in the evening , and will give you food in the morning ; for he has heard your complaints to the Lord , and what are we to do ? Your complaints are not against us , but against the Lord
Moses said to Aaron , &quot; Tell all the congregation of Israel , &apos; You are near to the Lord , for he has heard your complaints
When Aaron spoke to all the congregation of Israel , they looked to the wilderness , and behold , the glory of the Lord appeared in the clouds
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
I have heard the reproach of the children of Israel , and thou hast said unto them , Ye shall eat meat by the evening , and there shall be food in the morning , and ye shall know that I am the LORD your God
In the evening quails came and covered the camp ; and in the morning there was dew on the ground around the camp .
Suddenly , after the dew had risen , there were small circles on the field like white frost
And when the children of Israel saw it , and knew not what it was , they asked one another , saying , What is this ? And Moses said unto them , This is the food which the LORD hath given you
&quot; This is what the Lord has commanded you , that you shall take up every man according to his meat , according to the number of the people in the tent , and every man shall take an omer
Thus did the Israelites , how much they received , and how little they received
And there is no more to be harvested than that which is harvested , and there is no shortage of that which is harvested ; and every man shall receive according to his own meat .
And Moses said unto them , Let no man keep what he hath received until the morning
But when they did not hear Moses &apos; words , and there remained of them until the morning , the beasts became odorless , and Moses was angry with them .
And every morning they take their food according to the number of the people , and they digest it as soon as the day heats up .
And it came to pass on the sixth day , that they received twice as much food , and two princes of the congregation came to Moses , one for each man .
Moses said to them , &quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; Tomorrow is the Sabbath , the Sabbath to the Lord , and what you want to bake will be baked , and what you want to boil will be boiled , and all that remains will be left until morning
And they stayed until the morning , as Moses commanded them , without smell , and without worms in their heads
Moses said , &quot; Eat this day , for it is a Sabbath to the Lord , and you will not find it in the fields
Six days shall be reckoned , and the seventh day shall be a Sabbath , and that day shall not be .
On the seventh day a man of the people went out to collect , and found nothing .
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; When will it be that you will not keep my commandments and my laws
&quot; Behold , the Lord has given you the Sabbath , and on the sixth day He has given you two days of food ; and on the seventh day everyone shall dwell in his own place , and no man shall go out .
Then the people rested on the seventh day
&quot; What is the name of this food , the house of Israel ? It looks like a coriander , and its colour is white , and its taste is like a thin cake mixed with honey
Moses said , &quot; This is what the Lord has commanded : &apos; Will you leave a land full of Omer for generations to come , so that they may see what I will bring you out of the land of Egypt on that day , and what I will feed you in the wilderness ?
Moses said to Aaron , &quot; Have you taken a can full of ore , and been present before the Lord for generations to come ?
&quot; How did the Lord command Moses , and how did Aaron do , and put it in front of the ark
And it came to pass forty years , that the children of Israel went straight into the land of Canaan , wherein dwelled men :
And all the congregation of Israel walked according to the commandment of the LORD from the wilderness of the flood , and pitched in Rephi , and the people had no water to drink
So they argued with Moses , saying , &quot; Drink our water . &quot; Moses said to them , &quot; Why do you argue with me , and why do you seek the Lord
And the people there were thirsty to drink water , and complained to Moses , saying , &quot; Why have you brought us out of Egypt , and made us and our children and our livestock thirsty to death ?
And Moses cried unto the LORD , saying , What shall I do unto this people ? They shall almost stone me with stones
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Take your rod in your hand , which you used to throw at the waters of the river , and lead the elders of Israel past the people
And I will stand before thee in the rock of fire , and thou shalt smite the rock , and water shall come forth out of the rock , that the people may drink : and Moses did so before the elders of Israel .
And he called the name of the place Massah , and the name of the place Milla , because of the strife of the children of Israel , and because of their strife against the LORD , saying , The LORD is not among us
Then came the Amalekites to battle with the children of Israel at Libnah
Moses said to Joshua , &quot; You have chosen a man for us to go out and fight against the Amalekites ; and tomorrow I will stand on the top of the mountain with the stick of God in my hand
So Joshua did as Moses had said to him , and fought with the Amalekites : and Moses , Aaron , and Hur went up to the top of the mountain
When Moses raises his hand , the children of Israel shall be victorious ; and when he hangs his hand , the children of Amalek shall be victorious
And Moses &apos; hands sank , and they brought up the stone , and laid it under him , and he sat on it ; and Aaron and Hur held his hands one by one , and one by one , and his hands were steady , until the day fell .
Joshua struck king Amaziah and his people with the sword
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; I will blot out Amalek &apos;s name from all the earth , and you will write it on a book as a memorial , and you will recite it to Joshua
And Moses built an altar , and called it the name of the Lord , which is the meaning of the LORD my banner
&quot; The Lord has sworn that generations and generations will fight against the Amalekites
And Jethro , the priest of Midian , Moses &apos; father-in-law , heard all that God had done for Moses and for the people of God in Israel , that the Lord had brought forth Israel out of Egypt
And he took Siphrah , Moses &apos; wife , whom he had sent back .
and with him two sons of Zipporah , one named Gershon , because he said to Moses , &quot; I have been a stranger in the land
A man named Eliezer , because he said , &quot; The God of my father helped me , and saved me from the sword of Pharaoh
And Jethro , Moses &apos; father-in-law , came with his wife and two sons to the mountain of God , where Moses encamped in the wilderness
He said to Moses , &quot; I am Jethro , your father-in-law , who came to you with your wife and two sons
And Moses received his father-in-law , and worshipped him , and kissed him , and greeted one another , and entered into the tent
Moses told his father-in-law all the things that the Lord had done to Pharaoh and to the Egyptians for the sake of Israel , and all the difficulties that they had encountered on the way , and how the Lord had saved them
And Jethro rejoiced because of all the goodness of the LORD unto Israel , that he might deliver them out of the hand of the Egyptians
And Jethro said , Blessed is the Lord , who has delivered you out of the hand of the Egyptians and Pharaoh , and has delivered this people out of the hand of the Egyptians
&quot; Now I know that the LORD is greater than all the gods in the pride of the Egyptians against this people
And Jethro , Moses &apos; father-in-law , offered burnt offerings and sacrifices of peace unto God ; and Aaron and the elders of Israel came and ate with Moses &apos; father-in-law before God
On the second day Moses sat and judged the people , and the people stood on his right hand and on his left from morning until evening
When Moses &apos; father-in-law saw all that he had done to the people , he said , &quot; What have you done to the people ? Why do you sit alone , and the people stand on your side from morning until evening ?
Moses said to his father-in-law , &quot; This is because the people came to me to ask God
&quot; When they come to Me in the time of their affairs , I will judge between the two generations , and I will make known to them the law and the law of God
And Moses &apos; father-in-law said , It is not good for you to do this
&quot; You and these people will be exhausted , for it is too heavy for you to deal with it alone .
&quot; Behold , I have a plan for you , that you may hear my words , and that God may be with you , and that you may come before God for the people , and bring the case before God .
And to teach them the law and the law , and to show them the way to do and the things to do
&quot; And he will choose from among the people those who are wise , those who fear God , those who are faithful and without hypocrisy , and those who hate unrighteousness , and he will make them thousand captains , hundred captains , fifty captains , ten captains , and he will rule over the people
&quot; Let them judge the people at all times , and bring to you all the great things , and let them judge the small things themselves ; and then you will be lighter , and they will be with you in this office .
&quot; If you do so , as God has commanded you , you will be able to live , and the people will return to their dwellings in peace .
Then Moses listened to the words of his father-in-law , and walked according to what he had said
Moses chose from among the children of Israel wise men to be captains of the people , thousand captains , hundred captains , fifty captains , ten captains
&quot; They judge the people at all times , and they bring to Moses matters that are difficult to resolve , but they judge every little thing by themselves .
Then Moses let his father-in-law go , and he went to his place
And it came to pass in that day , after the children of Israel had come out of the land of Egypt , after three months , that they came into the wilderness of Sinai
And they departed from Libnah , and came to the wilderness of Sinai , and encamped under the mountains thereof .
Then Moses came to God , and the Lord called him from the mountain , saying , &quot; Thus shall you speak to the house of Jacob and to the children of Israel , saying ,
&quot; You have seen what I did to the Egyptians , and you have seen me as an eagle bringing you back to me on your wings
&quot; Now , if you will listen to me and keep my covenant , you will be my children among all the people , for the whole earth is mine .
&quot; You shall be to me a priest &apos;s land , a holy nation , and you shall speak these words to the children of Israel
Then Moses called the elders of the people , and made known to them all the words which the Lord had commanded him
And all the people answered one voice , and said , All that the LORD hath spoken we shall do . And Moses answered the LORD with the words of the people
And the LORD said unto Moses , I will come unto thee in the clouds , that the people may hear when I speak unto thee , and that they may believe thee for ever : and Moses recorded the words of the people unto the LORD
Then the Lord said to Moses , &quot; Go to the people , and make them cleanse themselves today and tomorrow , and wash their clothes
Prepare for the third day , for on the third day the Lord will come before all the people on Mount Sinai
&quot; You shall set the borders around the mountains for the people , saying , &apos; Be careful that you do not go up the mountains , nor touch the borders of the mountains . Whoever touches the mountains must be put to death .
They shall not touch him with their hands ; they shall kill him with stones or with arrows ; neither man nor beast shall they live : they shall not come to the mountain until the sound of the trumpet is prolonged .
And Moses went down to the people , and sanctified them , and they washed their clothes
He said to the people , &quot; You must prepare yourselves for the third day , and you shall not be near to a woman
And it came to pass on the third day in the morning , that there were thunders , lightning , and clouds in the mountains ; and there was a great noise , and all the people in the camp trembled
Moses led the people out of the camp to meet God , and they stood under the mountain
And all the mountains were filled with smoke , because the LORD was come down on the mountains in the fire , and the smoke of the mountains was as the burning of brass ; and there was a great trembling all over the mountains .
Then Moses spoke , and God answered him with a loud voice
And the LORD came down upon the top of mount Sinai , and the LORD called Moses to the top of the mount , and he went up
Then the Lord said to Moses , &quot; Go down and command the people , that they do not come and look at me , lest many of them die
&quot; And sanctify the priests who are near to me , lest I suddenly come and slay them
Moses said to the Lord , &quot; The people will not be able to go up to Mount Sinai , because you have commanded us to set the borders around it , to sanctify it
Then the Lord said to him , &quot; Go down , and come up with Aaron ; for the priests and the people cannot come up to me , lest I come out and slay them suddenly
Then Moses went down to the people and told them
And God commanded all these words , saying ,
&quot; I am Yahweh , your God , who brought you out of the land of Egypt as a house of bondage
&quot; There is no god for you except Me
&quot; You shall not carve an idol for yourselves , nor make any figure for yourself , as if it were in heaven , or in the earth , or in the earth , or in the waters .
&quot; You shall not kneel before the likes , nor serve them ; for I , the Lord , your God , am the God of evil , the one who hates me , and I will pursue his sins from his father and son for three or four generations .
For those who love me and keep My commandments , I will be merciful to them for a thousand generations
&quot; Do not mock the name of the Lord your God ; for whoever mocks the name of the Lord , the Lord will not make him innocent
Remember the Sabbath , and keep it a holy day
Six days to do all your work
&quot; But the seventh day shall be a sabbath to the Lord your God ; and it shall not be done to you , nor to your sons , nor to your maids , nor to your cattle , nor to any stranger that dwells in your city ,
&quot; For in the six days that the Lord created the heavens , the earth , the sea , and all that is in them , the seventh day rests ; therefore the Lord has blessed it and made it a holy day
When you respect your parents , that your days may be prolonged in the land which the Lord your God has given you
Do Not Kill
Non-violence
Don &apos;t steal
No false witness shall be given to a victim
&quot; You shall not love a man &apos;s house , nor his wife , nor his maidservant , nor his cattle , nor his donkey , nor all that he has
And when all the people saw the thunder , and the lightning , and the sound of the horns , and the smoke of the mountains , they trembled , and stood afar off
Then he said to Moses , &quot; Speak to us , and we will hear ; God will not speak to us , lest we die
And Moses said unto the people , Fear not : for the coming of God is to test you , that ye may fear him continually , and not sin
And the people stood afar off , and Moses came near unto God in the darkness
And the LORD said unto Moses , Thus shalt thou say unto the children of Israel : Ye have seen me speak with you from heaven
&quot; Why can &apos;t you make a god like me ? Why can &apos;t you make a god of silver and gold for yourself ?
&quot; You shall build an altar for me , and on it you shall offer a burnt offering of rams and sheep , a peace offering ; and I will bless you in all the places where My name is written .
&quot; If you build a stone altar for me , and it is not a stone that can be pierced , because you have moved the furniture on the top , you will defile the altar
&quot; You shall not go up to my altar with steps , lest your lower body be exposed .
&quot; This is the law which you shall set before the people .
&quot; If you buy a Hebrew as a servant , he will serve you six years and seven years , and he will go out free and free
If he comes alone , he can go alone ; and if he has a wife , his wife can go out with him .
If his master gives his wife , and the wife gives him a son , or daughters , wives , and children , he shall return to his master , and he shall go out alone
&quot; If the servant says , &apos; I love my master and my wife and my children , and I will not go out free
And his master shall bring him to the judge , and he shall bring him to the door , and to the frame of the door , and shall pierce his ears with a cone ; and he shall serve his master for ever .
&quot; If a man sells his daughter for a maidservant , she shall not go out as a manservant
&quot; If the master chooses him to be his own , and does not rejoice in him , let him redeem himself ; and he has no power to sell him to the Gentiles , because he has deceived him
&quot; If the master chooses a son for himself , he shall treat him as a daughter
If she marries another , her food , her clothing , and her manner of life shall not be reduced .
&quot; If he doesn &apos;t do these three things to him , he can go forth white and white without redemption
If a man is beaten to death , he must be put to death .
&quot; If a man is not buried to kill , but God is in his hand , then I will set a place where he can flee .
&quot; If a man kills his neighbour by deceit , and flees to my altar , then he is caught and put to death .
He who beats his parents must be put to death
It is necessary to put him to death by kidnapping the people , or by selling them , or by keeping them in his hands
He who curses his parents must be put to death
&quot; If a man fights with one another , and strikes him with a stone or a fist , he shall not die , nor lie down in bed .
&quot; If he is able to get up and out with a staff , it is not sin to strike him , but to compensate for his delay with money , and to heal him completely .
If a man strikes a slave or a maid with a stick and stands and dies under his hand , he shall be punished .
If you die a day or two later , you will not be punished , because you bought it with money
If a man fights with one another , and hurts a pregnant woman , or even falls , and thereafter does no harm , then the harm done to him shall be according to the punishment of the wife &apos;s husband , according to the judgment of the judge .
If there is no harm , it shall be repaid by death .
eye for eye , tooth for tooth , hand for hand , foot for foot
Bounded Against Wounded Against Wounded Against Wounded
&quot; If a man breaks an eye of his servant or of his maid , let him go free because of his eyes .
&quot; If he strikes a tooth of his servant or of his maidservant , let him go free because of his tooth
If a cow touches a man or a woman , he shall smite the cow with a stone , but he shall not eat his flesh ; and the owner of the cow shall be counted innocent .
&quot; If a man reports to the lord of the cattle that it has touched a man , and he does not bind the cattle to touch a man or a woman , then he will kill the cattle with a stone , and the lord of the cattle will die .
&quot; If he punishes with the price of his life , he shall redeem his life according to what he has punished .
&quot; This shall be the case whether the bull touches a man &apos;s son or his daughter .
&quot; If a cow touches a servant or a maid , he will offer thirty pieces of silver to his master , and he will kill the cow with stones .
When a man opens the mouth of a well , or digs it without covering , a cow or a donkey falls in it
The well mainly takes the money back to its owner . The dead animals are to be returned to themselves .
&quot; If the cow of this man hurts the cow of that man to death , they shall sell the live cow for the same price as the dead cow .
&quot; If a man knows that the cow has touched a man , but the master does not bind the cow , he must return the cow , and the dead cow shall return to himself .
&quot; If a man steals a cow , or a sheep , whether it is slaughtered or sold , he shall repay one for a cow , and four for a sheep
&quot; If a man meets a thief and digs a hole , and beats him to death , he will not be guilty of bloodshed .
If the sun is gone , it is bloody for him ; and if the thief is taken , he shall be repaid ; and if he has nothing , he shall be sold , and he shall be overcome with that which he has stolen .
&quot; If the cattle , or the donkey , or the sheep , which he has stolen , are still alive in his hand , he shall repay twice as much
&quot; If a man lays his livestock in the field , or in the vineyard , and lets it eat in the field of another man , he shall repay himself the good in the field , and the good in the vineyard .
&quot; If a fire burns the thorns , so that the bundles of wheat that others have gathered , or the standing grain , or the fields , are consumed , then the need of the fire shall be repaid .
&quot; If a man delivers silver money or furniture to his neighbour &apos;s guardian , and it is stolen from his house , and if he finds the thief , he shall repay it twice as much
&quot; If he does not find the thief , then the master shall come near to the judge to see whether he has taken away the property of his master
&quot; The case of two men , whether it be for the crime , or for the cattle , or for the donkey , or for the sheep , or for the garments , or for the things that were lost , one said , &apos; This is mine ; I will make it known to the judges , and the judges will determine who is guilty , and who will double the recompense .
If a man delivers a donkey , or a cow , or a sheep , or any other beast , to his neighbour &apos;s guardian , beast or dead , or injured , or driven away , no one shall see him
&quot; As the watchman swears by the Lord , &quot; The Lord will cease from taking in his hand what he has not taken in his neighbour &apos;s hand , and the watchman will not repay it .
&quot; If a beast is stolen from the watchman , he shall repay his Lord
If it is torn by a beast , the guardian shall bring it as evidence , and it shall not be repaid
&quot; If a man borrows from his neighbour , or borrows , or is injured , or dies , the Lord is not with him , and he who borrows shall repay .
If the Lord is in one place , he shall have no recompense ; and if he is hired , he shall have no recompense ; for he is hired for the price of his hire
If a man seduces a virgin who has no hired servant , and commits adultery with her , he shall offer her a bribe to marry her .
If the father of a woman refuses to give her to him , he shall pay her according to the manner of the woman .
A woman who practices evil will not allow him to live
&quot; He who is in love with the beast will surely be put to death
&quot; He who worships another god , and not only the Lord , must be destroyed .
&quot; You shall not blame the one who has settled , nor oppress him ; for you have settled in the land of Egypt .
Do not suffer widows and orphans
&quot; If I suffer them a little , they will cry to me , and I will hear their cry .
&quot; He will be angry and slay you with the sword , and make your wives widows , and your children orphans .
&quot; There is a poor man among my people who dwells with you . If you lend him money , you shall not profit him as if you lend a debt .
&quot; You shall return your neighbor &apos;s garments to him before the sunset .
&quot; For if he had no covering , what would he sleep with ? For he cried to me , and I answered him , for I was gracious .
&quot; Do not slander God , nor slander the ruler of your people
&quot; You shall not delay to bring forth the wine that is poured out of the fields of your crops , and the wine that is poured out of the winepress ; and you shall return to me the firstborn son .
&quot; This is what you shall do to the head of your cattle and your sheep ; seven days you shall be with your mother , and eight days you shall return to me .
&quot; You shall be holy before me , and you shall not eat the flesh of the beasts , which are torn in the fields by the beasts ; but you shall give it to the dogs .
&quot; You shall not spread rumours with your companions , nor make a false witness with the wicked .
&quot; You shall not do evil in the midst of the people ; you shall not prejudice the people in matters of dispute , nor testify against their integrity .
Neither can the poor be favoured in disputes
&quot; If you meet a cow or a donkey of your enemy who has lost his way , bring it back and give it to him
&quot; If you see a donkey that hates your people lying under a heavy burden , and you cannot go away , you must carry it with the owner of the donkey
There shall be no disregard for the integrity of the poor in matters of dispute
Stay away from falsehood . Do not kill the innocent and righteous ; for I will not do justice to the wicked .
No one shall be bribed , for bribery makes the blind blind , and turns away the righteous .
Do not oppress the dwellers ; for you have dwelled in the land of Egypt , and know the hearts of those who dwell there .
For six years you will cultivate fields and collect crops
&quot; But in the seventh year you shall cause the land to cease from cultivating and from planting , so that the poor among your people may eat of what remains of them , and the beasts of the field , and your vineyards and your olive groves .
&quot; You shall do your work on the sixth day , and rest on the seventh day , so that the cattle and the donkeys may rest , and so that the sons of your maidservant and the dwellers may rest
&quot; You shall keep all that I say to you , and you shall not speak the name of any other god , nor shall you speak it in your mouths .
&quot; Three and three times a year , you shall keep the Sabbath to me
&quot; You shall observe the feast of yeast , and eat unleavened bread seven days , as I have commanded you , on the appointed day in the month of Assyria ; and no man shall come unto me empty-handed , for you have come out of Egypt this month .
And keep the feast of harvest , that which is harvested of the first ripening of your labour in the field ; and keep the feast of collecting at the end of the year .
&quot; Every male shall come to the Lord three times a year
&quot; You shall not offer the blood of my sacrifice together with the bread of yeast , nor leave the fat of my sacrifice in the morning
&quot; The first fruits of the ground shall be brought to the house of the Lord your God.You shall not boil the lambs with the milk of the mother of the lamb
&quot; Behold , I have sent messengers before you to protect you on the way and to bring you to the place which I have prepared for you
&quot; He has come in my name . Be careful before him , and listen to his words , and do not provoke him ; for he will not forgive your transgressions .
&quot; If you listen to his words , and walk in all that I say , I will be an enemy to your enemies , and an enemy to your enemies
&quot; My messenger will go before you and bring you to the children of Ammon , and to the children of Hesh , and to the children of Belize , and to the children of Canaan , and to the children of Hivite , and to the children of Jebus , and I will cut them off .
Thou shalt not kneel before their God , neither shalt thou serve him , neither shalt thou obey their deeds ; but shalt destroy the likeness of God to the end , and break down their pillars .
&quot; You shall serve the Lord your God ; He will bless you with your food and with your water , and he will remove disease from among you
&quot; In your land shall there be none to give birth , none to bear fruit ; and I will fill you with the number of your years .
&quot; In every place where you have come , I will make the people there fear and disturb before you , and I will turn away all your enemies .
&quot; I will send the bee flying before you , and I will drive out the Hebrews , the Canaanites , and the Hittites
&quot; I will not drive them out from before you in one year , lest the beasts of the wilderness become a desolation and beasts of the field come to harm you
&quot; I will gradually drive them out from before you , until more of your people take up the land for their occupation .
I will set your borders from the Red Sea to the Sea of Philistine , and from the wilderness to the great river ; and I will deliver the inhabitants of that land into your hand , and you will drive them out from before you .
Do not make a covenant with them and with their God
&quot; They shall not dwell in your land , lest they sin you against me ; and if you serve their God , it will be a snare for you .
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; You and Aaron , and Nathan , and Abihu , and seventy of the elders of Israel , will come to me to worship from afar
Only thou shalt be near unto the LORD , and they shall not be near , neither shall the people come up with thee
Then Moses went down and spoke to the people all the commandments and the statutes of the Lord , and all the people said with a loud voice , &quot; We will all do as the Lord has commanded us
&quot; Moses wrote all the commandments of the Lord , saying , &apos; From the morning you shall build an altar under the mountain , and set up twelve pillars according to the twelve tribes of Israel
and sent the young men among the children of Israel to offer burnt offerings , and to the Lord to sacrifice cattle for a sacrifice of peace
Moses poured half of the blood into the basin , and half of it on the altar .
Then he recited the Book to the people , and they said , &quot; We will all do as the Lord has commanded us
And Moses sprinkled the blood upon the people , and said , &quot; Behold , this is the blood of the covenant which the Lord made with you according to all these words
Moses , Aaron , Nathan , Abihu , and seventy of the elders of Israel went up to the mountain
And they saw the God of Israel , and under his feet was like a plain stone , like the brightness of the sky .
His hands did not harm the holy ones of Israel ; they looked on God , and they ate and drank
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Come up to me on the mountain and dwell here , and I will give you the stone tablets and the law and the commandments which I have written , so that you may teach the people
Moses and Joshua , his companions , arose , and went up to the mountain of God
Moses said to the old man , &quot; Wait here until we come back . Aaron and Hur are with you . Anyone who has a dispute will come near them
Moses went up the mountain , and the clouds covered the mountain .
And the glory of the LORD was upon mount Sinai , and the cloud covered it six days : and on the seventh day he called Moses out of the clouds
The glory of the LORD is on the top of the mountain , and in the sight of the children of Israel , as a flame of fire
Moses went up into the clouds forty days and forty nights
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; Tell the children of Israel , &apos; When you bring a present to me , you will bring it back to me , if you will .
&quot; The gift that is to be received is gold , silver , and copper
Blue , purple , red , silk , sheep &apos;s hair
Red sheep skins , sea dog skins , soap pods
And oil for the light , and oil for the anointing and for the fragrance .
And a scarlet marble , and other stones , that may be set on the ephod and on the breastplate ;
And made holy places for me , that I might dwell among them
&quot; Make the tent and all the instruments therein according to the pattern which I have commanded you
&quot; You shall make a cupboard of acacia trees , two cubits long , one cubit wide , and one cubit high
The outer envelope shall be of fine gold , and the sides of it shall be of gold .
And four gold rings shall be cast on the four feet of the ark , two on this side , and two on that side .
&quot; You shall make two bars out of sapwood , and wrap them in gold
Put the bars in the circle next to the cupboard to lift the cupboard
The bar shall always be in the circle of the cupboard ; it shall not be drawn out
&quot; And I will put the law which I have given you in the ark
&quot; You shall make the altar of mercy out of pure gold , two cubits and a half in length , and one cubit and a half in breadth
&quot; You shall hammer out two reins with gold , and you shall be on the two heads of the seat of grace .
And the head shall be a reinforcement , and the head a reinforcement , and the two reinforcements shall be joined together as one of the two heads in the throne of grace .
He will raise up his wings , and cover the throne of grace ; and he will face to face toward the throne of grace .
&quot; You shall lay the seat of grace on the top of the ark , and put in the ark the law which I have given you
&quot; I will meet with you there , and I will come from the altar of grace in the middle of the valley , and you will tell me all that I have commanded you to do to the children of Israel
A table shall be made of acacia trees , two cubits long , one cubit wide , and one and a half cubits high
&quot; You shall wrap it in fine gold , and put it on the edges of your teeth .
And the four corners of the table were beside a broad beam , and on the beam were golden teeth .
And four golden rings shall be on the four corners of the table , the four corners on the four feet of the table .
The place of the ring should be near the side beam , and the table should be carried by bars
&quot; You shall make two bars out of saplings , and wrap them in gold to lift up the table .
And the plates that were on the table , and the spoons , and the cups of wine , and the bottles , shall be made of pure gold
&quot; And on the tables , before me , they shall set up their cakes ,
&quot; You shall make a lampstand out of pure gold , and the seats of the lampstand , and the dry ones , and the cups , and the balls , and the flowers , shall be hammered together .
&quot; You shall cut out six branches on both sides of the lampstand , three on this side and three on that side
And on every branch there were three cups of the shape of an almond , and a ball , and a flower ; and on every branch there were three cups of the shape of an almond , and a ball , and a flower ; and so were the six branches that came out of the top of the lampstand .
There were four cups on the lampstand , shaped like almonds , with balls and flowers
Below each of the two branches of the lampstand is a sphere joined together with the branches ; so are the six branches of the lampstand
And the ball and the branches shall be joined together by a hammer of pure gold .
&quot; The priest shall light this lamp , and make the lamp to be a lampstand for seven lamps .
The candlesticks of the lampstand , and the candlesticks of the candlesticks , are also precious .
and all the lampstands and all the instruments shall be joined together with pure gold
Be careful to make these things , according to the patterns which are appointed to you on the mountains
And thou shalt make ten curtains for the tabernacle : and they shall be made of fine linen of shittim , and of blue purple , and red , and of fine embroidery .
And the length of the mantle shall be twenty-eight cubits , and the breadth four cubits ; and the mantle shall be of the same measure .
The five curtains shall be joined together widely , and the five curtains shall be joined widely
And it shall be a blue button on the end of the curtain that is joined together , and it shall be likewise on the end of the curtain that is joined together .
And there shall be fifty buttons on the mantle that is joined together , and fifty buttons on the mantle that is joined together , two and two ;
And fifty hooks of gold to join together the mantle ; and this is the tabernacle .
And thou shalt weave eleven curtains of sheep &apos;s hair for a covering over the tabernacle .
The length of each curtain shall be thirty cubits , and the breadth four cubits ; and the eleven curtains shall be of the same measure .
And thou shalt fold up five curtains into one , and six curtains into one ; and the sixth curtain shalt thou fold up before the tabernacle .
And there shall be fifty buttons on the end of the curtain that is joined thereto , and fifty buttons on the end of the curtain that is joined thereto .
And fifty copper hooks shall be made , and the hooks shall be in the buttons , and the sheath shall be joined together .
And the rest of the curtains of the tent , the half curtains that hang down , shall hang on the back of the tent .
And the remainder of the curtains of the tent shall be an elbow on the one side , and an elbow on the other side , to hang over the two sides of the tent , to cover the tent .
The covering of the shelter shall be made of red sheep &apos;s fur , and the top of the shelter shall be made of sea dog &apos;s fur .
And thou shalt make a pillar for the tent of sackcloth
10 cubits long and one and a half cubits wide for each piece
&quot; There shall be two pins for each piece ; so shall all the boards of the tent be .
And twenty boards shall be made for the south side of the tabernacle .
And under the twenty boards there shall be forty silver seats , bearing sockets ; two sockets for the board , and two sockets for the board .
And on the second side of the tabernacle , on the north side , twenty boards ;
And forty silver stars with them , two under the board , and two under the board .
Behind the tabernacle , on the west side , six boards ;
And the corner of the tabernacle behind it shall be two boards
The lower half of the board shall be doubled , and the upper half whole ; and the top of the board shall be straight to the first ring ; and the two pieces shall be two corners .
And there shall be eight boards , and sixteen silver pillars with hooks under them , and two hooks under them , and two hooks under them .
And thou shalt make bars of sapphire , and five bars for the board of the tabernacle :
And five bars for the board on the side of the tabernacle , and five bars for the board behind the tabernacle ;
the middle bar between the boards and the waist , from one end to the other ;
The boards shall be wrapped in gold , and the bars on the boards shall be made of gold rings , and the bars shall be wrapped in gold
&quot; You shall set up the tent according to the pattern which He has shown you in the mountains .
And thou shalt make a mantle of blue , purple , and scarlet , and fine linen ; and thou shalt embroider it with the hand of a skillful embroiderer .
And thou shalt hang the mantle upon four pillars of soap , which are of gold ; and upon the pillars shall be hooks of gold ; and the pillars shall be on four silver pillars with hooks .
&quot; You shall put the mantle under the hook , and bring the ark of the law into the mantle , and the mantle shall separate the sanctuary from the sanctuary .
And the seat of grace shall be set upon the ark of the law in the sanctuary
And thou shalt set the table on the north side of the tabernacle outside the mantle , and the lampstands on the south side of the tabernacle against one another .
And thou shalt take blue , purple , and scarlet , and fine linen , and embroidered curtains for the tents :
And five pillars shall be made of sapphire for curtains , and they shall be wrapped with gold ; and on the pillars shall be hooks of gold ; and five posts shall be made of brass for the pillars .
&quot; You shall make an altar of acacia trees , five cubits long , five cubits wide , and three cubits high .
And four corners shall be made on the four corners of the altar , and a piece shall be joined to the altar , and the altar shall be wrapped with brass .
&quot; You shall make a basin , and take the ashes of the altar , and the shovels , and the plates , and the fillets of flesh , and the spears , and all the vessels of the altar , of brass .
&quot; You shall make for the altar a net of copper , and on the four corners of the net four rings of copper .
And thou shalt lay the net under the girdle of the altar on all its sides , and it shall come down to the half waist of the altar .
&quot; The bars of the altar shall be made of sapwood , and they shall be wrapped in copper .
&quot; The bar shall be worn in the ring on either side of the altar to lift up the altar
&quot; You shall make the altar with boards , and the altar shall be empty , according to the pattern which you have commanded on the mountains
And thou shalt make the court of the tabernacle ; and on the south side of the court shalt thou make a curtain of fine linen , an hundred cubits long .
And the pillars of the curtain shall be twenty , and twenty copper seats with hooks ; and the hooks and the rods of the pillars shall be of silver .
And on the north side shall be a curtain an hundred cubits long , and twenty pillars of the curtain , and twenty sockets of brass ; and the hooks and the rods of the pillars shall be of silver .
And on the west side of the court shall be a curtain , fifty cubits wide , and ten pillars of the curtain , and ten seats with hooks .
And the east side of the court shall be fifty cubits wide .
And the curtain on the side of the gate shall be fifteen cubits , and three pillars of the curtain , and three seats with hooks .
And the curtain over against the gate shall be fifteen cubits , and three pillars of the curtain , and three sockets .
And for the doors of the house shall be curtains twenty cubits long ; and they shall be of blue , purple , and scarlet , and fine linen , woven by hand with embroidery , and four pillars , and four seats with hooks .
And all the pillars that are round about the court shall be joined by a rod of silver ; and the hooks of the pillars shall be of silver ; and the posts of brass shall be of brass .
The length of the court shall be one hundred cubits , and the breadth fifty cubits , and the height five cubits ; and the curtains shall be of fine linen , and the seats of brass ;
And all the vessels of the tabernacle , and all the bars of the tabernacle , and all the bars of the court , shall be of brass .
&quot; You shall command the children of Israel to bring to you the pure olive oil which they have mixed for the lamp , and to make the lamp light continually
And Aaron and his sons shall keep the lamp before the LORD from evening till morning , outside the curtain of the tabernacle of the congregation before the ark of the LORD , for a statute for ever and ever for the generations of Israel .
And thou shalt bring Aaron thy brother , and Nadab his son , and Abihu his son , and Eleazar his son , and Ehamma his son , from among the children of Israel near unto thee , to minister unto me as priests
&quot; You shall make Aaron your brother a holy garment for glory and beauty
And to command all that have wisdom in their hearts , that I , filled with the Spirit of wisdom , may clothe Aaron , and sanctify him , that he may minister unto me as a priest
And it shall be a breastplate , and an ephod , and an outer garment , and a mixed inner garment , and a crown , and a girdle , that Aaron your brother and his son may wear it , that they may minister to me as priests .
To be made with gold and blue purple and red lines , and fine linen
And they shall take gold , and blue , and purple , and scarlet , and fine linen , and work it with a skillful hand .
And Ephraim had two shoulder girdles , and two heads were joined to him ,
And the cords thereof shall be made of gold , and of blue , and purple , and scarlet , and fine linen , in a manner like unto the work of Ephraim ; and they shall be joined together in a bundle of ephraim .
&quot; You shall take two pieces of red marble , and engrave on them the name of the son of Israel .
Six names were on this stone , and six names on that stone , according to the order of their birth
And they shall engrave the two stones with the hand of the stone , as if they were engraved books , in the name of the son of Israel , and they shall be set in a gold pot .
And Aaron shall bear their names on their shoulders before the LORD , and they shall be a memorial for the children of Israel on the two shoulders of Ephrath .
To use gold for two tanks
And he took the purple gold , and made it two chains with a twister like a rope , and put it in two jars ,
You shall make a decisive breastplate with the hand of a skilled craftsman . You shall make it with the work of Ephraim , with gold and blue purple and red and fine linen .
The breastplate shall be on four sides , and it shall be overlaid in two layers , one for the mouth and one for the mouth .
And four rows of stones shall be placed on it , the first row of which shall be red stones , and the second row of which shall be red pearls , and the third row of which shall be red jade
The second line is green gemstone , blue gemstone , gold and steel
The third line is purple , white and purple crystals
And the fourth row shall be blue jewels , and red marble , and blue jewels ; and they shall be set in a golden vessel
These stones shall bear the names of the twelve sons of Israel , as if they were a book , and the names of the twelve tribes .
And thou shalt make a chain like a rope upon the breastplate of pure gold .
And two gold rings shall be made on the breastplate , on the two heads of the breastplate .
And thou shalt put the two chains of gold , which thou hast twisted , through the rings of the two heads of the breastplate .
And the two heads of the chains shall be bound in two cords , and they shall be on the shoulders of Ephraim before him .
And two gold rings shall be on the two heads of the breastplate , on the sides of Ephraim .
And two gold rings shall be made , on the bottom of the two shoulder bands that were before Ephraim , and on the sides that were near to them , above the bands that Ephraim had weaved .
And thou shalt bind the rings of the breastplate with the rings of the ephod with blue bands , and thou shalt not sew the ephod with the rings of the ephod &apos;s skillful weaving .
&quot; When Aaron enters the sanctuary , the breastplate , which bears the name of the son of Israel , shall be cut off , and it shall be put on his chest for a continual memorial before the Lord
And they shall put the Urals and the Tombs in the seal of judgment ; and Aaron shall bring the seal of judgment of the children of Israel before the LORD at the time that he enters into the presence of the LORD .
And thou shalt make the robe of Ephraim , and it shall be of blue .
And thou shalt have a porch for the head of the robe , and thou shalt weave the porch around it , as if it were a porch of armor , lest it be broken .
On the bottom of the robe round about shall be pomegranates of blue , purple , and red , and in the middle of the pomegranates around the robe shall be bells of gold .
A golden bell , a pomegranate , a golden bell , a pomegranate , on the bottom around the robe
&quot; And Aaron shall be clothed in this robe at the time of his ministry ; and the voice of the robe shall be heard when he enters into the sanctuary before the Lord , and when he comes out , lest he die
&quot; You shall make a board of pure gold , and you shall engrave it according to the law of the book , and it shall be holy to the Lord .
&quot; Take a blue ribbon , and put it in front of the crown .
And it shall be on Aaron &apos;s forehead , that he may bear the iniquity of the law of the holy things , which the children of Israel have holy in all their holy gifts ; and it shall be on his forehead continually , that they may be pleasing before the Lord
And a cloak of fine linen shall be woven , and a crown of fine linen , and a waistband of embroidered work .
And thou shalt make for the son of Aaron an inner garment , and a girdle , and a veil , for glory , and for beauty ;
&quot; You shall put them on Aaron your brother and on his sons , and anoint them , and sanctify them , that you may give me the priest &apos;s office
And thou shalt give them fine linen trousers to cover their underparts , from their waist to their thighs .
And Aaron and his son shall enter into the tabernacle of the congregation , or near the altar , and they shall put on them in the time of their service in the holy place , lest they die of sin ; and this shall be a statute forever for Aaron and his seed .
&quot; You have sanctified Aaron and his sons , and you have given me the priest &apos;s office . Take a bull , and two lambs without blemish ,
Unleavened bread , and unleavened bread with oil , and unleavened bread with oil : these shall be made of fine flour
&quot; You shall place the cake in a basket , and bring the basket with you , and bring the bull and the two rams
&quot; You shall bring Aaron and his son to the door of the Tent of Meeting to wash themselves with water
And Aaron shall be clothed in an inner robe , and in an outer robe of Ephraim , and in Ephraim ; and he shall have a breastplate , and a girdle of fine ephraim .
He will put the crown on his head , and the holy crown on his crown .
Then pour the oil over his head , and anoint him
&quot; Let his sons come , and put on their robes
And Aaron and his sons shall be bound in girdles and in scarves ; and they shall be appointed priests by an everlasting statute , and they shall sanctify Aaron and his sons
And thou shalt bring the bull before the tabernacle of the congregation ; and Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands on the head of the bull
&quot; You shall slaughter the bull before the Lord , at the door of the Tent of Meeting ,
&quot; You shall take some of the blood of the bull , and sprinkle it on the four corners of the altar with your fingers , and put it in the foot of the altar .
And you shall burn on the altar all the fat that is covered with filth , and the nets that are on the liver , and the two waist , and the fat that is on the waist .
Only the skin , the flesh , and the dung of the bull shall be burned with fire outside the camp , for a sin offering .
&quot; You shall bring a ram , and Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands on the head of the ram
&quot; You shall kill the sheep , and sprinkle the blood around the altar
And thou shalt cut the sheep in pieces , and wash them of their five filths , and put them in one place with the legs , and with the bands of their heads .
&quot; You shall burn the whole sheep on the altar , as a burnt offering to the Lord , and as a sweet savour to the Lord
And thou shalt bring the ram , and Aaron and his son , and lay thy hand on the head of the ram ;
And thou shalt kill the sheep , and take some blood , and sprinkle it upon the right ear of Aaron , and upon the right ear of his son , and upon the thumb of his right hand , and upon the thumb of his right foot , and sprinkle it upon the borders of the altar .
&quot; You shall take some of the oil and the blood of the altar , and sprinkle it on Aaron and on his garments , and on his sons and on his sons &apos; garments , and they and their garments , and become holy together .
And thou shalt take the fat of the sheep , and the fat of the tail , and cover it with the filthy fat , and the nets of the liver , and the two waist , and the fat of the waist , and the right leg .
Then take a cake , an oiled cake , and a thin cake out of the basket of unleavened cakes before the Lord
And they laid them in the hand of Aaron , and in the hand of his son , as a wave offering before the LORD .
&quot; They shall take it out of their hands , and burn it on the altar before the Lord , as a burnt offering to the Lord , a sweet aroma
&quot; You shall take Aaron &apos;s breast , which he has consecrated for the holy service , as a wave offering , and wave it before the Lord , and it shall be your portion .
The breast of the sacrifice , and the legs of the sacrifice , are the hands of Aaron and his sons , that they may be holy .
&quot; This is the portion that Aaron and his sons shall receive from the children of Israel for ever and ever , because it is an offering made in the midst of the peace offerings of the children of Israel , as an offering made to the Lord
And Aaron &apos;s holy garment shall be reserved for his sons , that they may be anointed , and that they may bear the holy office .
And his seed shall bear seven days of his priesthood , when he entereth into the tabernacle of the congregation , when he ministereth in the holy place
And the meat of the goats of the sanctuary , which thou hast offered , thou shalt boil in the holy place .
And Aaron and his sons shall eat the flesh of the sheep , and the bread in the basket , at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation
And they eat of the things of redemption , that they may receive the holy office , and become saints : but none of them shall eat them , because they are holy
&quot; If any meat or cake of the consecration remains until the morning , it shall be burned with fire ; it shall not be eaten , for it is holy .
&quot; You shall do so seven days , according to all that I have commanded you , to Aaron and to his sons , to take the holy charge
&quot; You shall offer a bull every day for a sin offering ; and when you have cleansed the altar , it shall be cleansed ; and you shall anoint it , and sanctify it .
&quot; You shall cleanse the altar seven days , and make it holy , and the altar shall be holy ; and whoever is next to it shall be holy
&quot; You shall offer on the altar every day two lambs of the first year .
Give this in the morning , and give that in the evening .
and one tenth of an ephah of fine flour mixed with one tenth of a hin of mixed oil , and one tenth of a hin of wine for a drink offering ,
&quot; The lamb shall be offered in the evening , according to the ordinance of the morning offering , and according to the ordinance of the drink offering , as a burnt offering to the Lord , sweet incense
&quot; This shall be a burnt offering before the Lord at the door of the Tent of Meeting for your generations to come ; and I will meet with you there and speak with you
&quot; In it I will meet with the children of Israel ; and the tabernacle will be holy for my glory .
&quot; I will sanctify the tabernacle of the congregation and the altar , and I will sanctify Aaron and his sons , and give me the office of priest
&quot; I will dwell among the children of Israel as their God
And they shall know that I am the LORD their God , which brought them forth out of the land of Egypt to dwell among them ; I am the LORD their God
And thou shalt make an altar of incense out of saplings
&quot; The altar shall be on its four sides , one elbow long , one elbow wide , and two elbows high ; and the four corners of the altar shall be joined together .
And he shall cover the top of the altar with fine gold , and the four corners of the altar , and the four corners of the altar with fine gold ; and he shall set the corners of the altar with gold .
And two golden rings shall be made under the corners of the teeth , on the sides of the altar , and on the two sides of the altar , to be for the bars to bear the altar .
For bars to be made of sapwood , and for gold to be wrapped
&quot; You shall place the altar outside the mantle before the ark , and on the altar of grace , where I will meet with you .
And Aaron burned on the altar the incense of sweet incense ; and he burned it every morning , when he had set up the lamp
&quot; He shall burn this in the presence of the Lord in the evening , when the lamps are set , as the incense of the generations to come
No strange incense shall be offered on this altar , nor any burnt offering , nor any sacrifice of flesh , nor any drink offering
And Aaron shall make atonement at the corner of the altar year by year , and he shall make atonement at the altar year by year with the blood of the sin offering , as a statute for generations to come , and it shall be holy before the Lord
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You shall count the number of the children of Israel according to their number , and when you have numbered them , every one of them shall offer his life for a ransom to the Lord , and there shall be a plague among them when they shall be exempted from the number .
&quot; Everyone who goes to those who are numbered shall receive half a shekel of silver in the holy place , as a gift to the Lord , and one shekel twenty shekels
&quot; Everyone who goes to the numbered , from twenty years old and upward , shall offer this gift to the Lord
&quot; They shall offer their offerings to the Lord for a ransom of their lives ; the rich shall not be multiplied , neither shall the poor be diminished ; each man shall give half a shekel .
&quot; You shall take this money of redemption from the children of Israel , and use it for the tabernacle of the congregation , to make a memorial to the children of Israel before the Lord , and to redeem their lives
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
And thou shalt make a basin of copper for the washing , and a basin for the washing ; and thou shalt place the basin between the tabernacle of the congregation and the altar , and pour water in it .
And Aaron and his sons shall wash their hands and their feet in this basin
&quot; When they enter the Tent of Meeting , or when they serve near the altar , to offer a burnt offering to the Lord , they shall wash themselves with water , lest they die
And they shall wash their hands and their feet , lest they die ; and this shall be a statute for Aaron and for his seed for ever and ever .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You shall take five hundred shekels of the best spices , five hundred shekels of unclean fluids , half a hin of cinnamon , two hundred and fifty shekels , and two hundred and fifty shekels of irises .
and five hundred shekels of oil , according to the shekel of the sanctuary ;
To make the ointment according to the manner of incense , and to season it , and to make the oil
&quot; This oil shall be applied to the tabernacle and to the chamber .
and the table , and all the vessels thereof , and the lampstand , and all the vessels thereof , and the altar
the altar of burnt offering , and all the vessels thereof , and the washing basin , and the basin seat ,
to make them holy , that they may be holy ; and every one that is near shall be holy .
&quot; You shall anoint Aaron and his sons , and make them holy , that they may serve me as priests
&quot; You shall say to the children of Israel , &apos; I will anoint this oil for generations to come
&quot; You shall not fall on others , nor be like them in this manner . This oil is holy , and you shall be holy .
&quot; He who mixes something similar to it , or puts it on someone else &apos;s body , shall be cut off from the people .
And the Lord commanded Moses , saying , &quot; Take a sweet incense , Naphthah , and Shechem , and Gibeah , and a large measure of the sweet incense and of the pure milk ,
Then you shall add salt to them , and make a pure and holy incense according to the manner of incense .
&quot; Take a little of it , and put it in front of the chamber of the congregation , where I will meet you , and you shall make it holy .
&quot; You shall not incense yourselves according to this manner , but you shall be holy in the Lord .
&quot; Whoever makes a fragrance like this , and smells it , he shall be cut off from the people .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
Behold , I have called him by his name , the son of Hur , the son of Uri , of the tribe of Judah ,
&quot; I also filled him with my spirit , that he might be wise , wise , wise , and able to do all kinds of work .
A craftsman who can make all things out of gold and silver and copper
And they can carve stones , and they can engrave , and they can carve wood , and they can do all kinds of work .
&quot; I have appointed among the tribes of Dan Aholiab , the son of Asaph , to work with him . He has wisdom in every heart , and I have made him more wise , and he can do all that I have commanded him .
And the tabernacle of the congregation , and the ark of the law , and the seat of grace upon it , and all the vessels of the tabernacle of the congregation ;
And the table , and all the vessels of the table , and the lampstand of gold , and all the vessels of the lampstand , and the altar of incense
And the altar of burnt offering , and all the vessels thereof , and the washbasin , and the basin seat ,
and Aaron the priest , and his sons , in the holy garments for the priest &apos;s office ;
&quot; They shall do according to all that I have commanded them , to anoint themselves with oil , and to anoint the saints with sweet incense .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
And thou shalt say unto the children of Israel , Keep my sabbaths , for it is a sign between me and thee for generations to come , that thou mayest know that my Lord hath sanctified thee
&quot; Therefore keep the Sabbath as a holy day ; and whoever commits any sin on it shall surely be put to death ; and whoever does any work on it shall be cut off from among the people .
&quot; The sixth day shall be a work , but the seventh day is a Sabbath , a holy day to the Lord ; and he who works on the Sabbath shall be put to death .
Therefore the children of Israel shall keep the Sabbath for ever and ever for generations
&quot; This is the proof for ever between me and the children of Israel ; for in six days the Lord created the heavens and the earth ; and on the seventh day he rested and was well rested .
And when the LORD had finished speaking in mount Sinai and in Moses , he gave him two tablets of the law , which were written with the fingers of God
And when the people saw that Moses had not yet come down , they gathered themselves together to Aaron , and said unto him , Arise , and be a god unto us , that he may guide us before us ; for we know not what was done to Moses , who brought us out of the land of Egypt .
Then Aaron said to them , &quot; Go and take the golden ring from the ears of your wives and children , and bring it to me
And all the people took away the golden ring from their ears , and brought it to Aaron
And Aaron took it from their hand , and cast a calf , and made it with carvings ; and they said , &quot; This is the God who brought you out of the land of Egypt , O Israel
When Aaron saw it , he built an altar in front of the calf , and proclaimed , &quot; Tomorrow you will observe the feast to the Lord
And the people rose up early the next day to offer burnt offerings and peace offerings , and sat down to eat and drink , and rose up to play
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Go down ; for your people , whom you brought out of the land of Egypt , have perished
Soon they turned away from the way I had commanded them , and cast a calf for themselves , and worshipped him , and said , &quot; This is the God who brought you out of the land of Egypt , O Israel
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; I see that this people is a people with hard necks
&quot; You and I will be angry with them , and will destroy them , and make your descendants a great nation .
Moses pleaded with the Lord his God , saying , &quot; Lord , why are you angry with your people , whom you brought out of the land of Egypt with a mighty and mighty hand
Why did he cause the Egyptians to argue , saying , &quot; He has brought them out to bring evil upon them , to kill them in the mountains , and to destroy them from the earth ? Turn away from your wrath and repentance , and do not bring evil upon your people
Remember your servant Abraham , Isaac , and Israel , when you swore to yourself , &quot; I will make your descendants as many as the stars of heaven , and I will give to your descendants all the land which I have promised them , and they will inherit it forever .
Then the Lord repented , and did not bring the evil that he had spoken to his people
And Moses turned and went down the mountain , and took in his hand two copies of the law , which were written on both sides , both of which contained words
It is the work of God , and the words are written by God , and engraved on the pages .
And when Joshua heard the voice of the people , he said unto Moses , There is a voice of war in the camp
Moses said , &quot; This is not the voice of men who fight , nor is it the voice of men who fight ; but what I have heard is the voice of men who sing .
And when Moses came near to the camp , he saw the calf , and the people dancing , and he was very wroth , and he threw the two pieces down the mountain , and broke them
And they burned the calves that they had cast with fire , and grinded them to pieces , and poured them upon the waters , and gave them to the children of Israel to drink
Moses said to Aaron , &quot; What have these people done to you , that you have put them in great sin
Then Aaron said , &quot; My Lord , do not be angry , for you know that this people are devoted to evil
And they said unto me , Thou art a god unto us , that thou mayest guide us before us : for we know not what he hath done unto Moses , who brought us out of the land of Egypt .
And I said unto them , Whosoever hath a ring of gold , let him take it down ; and they gave it unto me ; and I cast it into the fire , and the calf came forth .
When Moses saw the people &apos;s indulgence , Aaron tolerated them , and reproached them in the midst of their enemies ,
Then he stood in the gate of the camp , and said , &quot; All who belong to the Lord will come to me ; &quot; and the sons of Levi assembled themselves there
And he said unto them , Thus saith the Lord , the God of Israel ; Every one of you shall spread his sword between his loins , and come into the camp , from one door to another , and slay his brothers , and his companions , and his neighbors
And the children of Levi did according to the word of Moses : and there were about three thousand slain in that day among the people .
Moses said , &quot; Today you will be purified and sanctified before the Lord , and you will fight against his son and his brothers , so that the Lord may bless you
And it came to pass on the second day , that Moses said to the people , &quot; You have committed a great sin , and I will go to the Lord now , or I can redeem you for your sins
Moses returned to the Lord and said , &quot; Woe to this people ! They have committed a great sin , and they have made themselves a golden image
If thou wilt forgive their sins , or blot out my name from the book that thou hast written
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Whoever sins on me , I will blot out his name from my book
&quot; Now , when you go to take this people to the place where I have told you , My messengers will guide them before you ; but in the days that I will pursue , I will pursue their sins .
For the LORD slew the people because they had made calves with Aaron
And the LORD said unto Moses , I have sworn unto Abraham , and unto Isaac , and unto Jacob , that I would give the land of Canaan unto thy seed ; and now go thou from here unto that land , and the people that thou hast brought forth out of the land of Egypt
&quot; I will send messengers before you to drive out the Canaanites , the Amorites , the Hittites , the Perizzites , the Hivites , the Jebustes
Take you to the land of milk and honey , and I will go up against you , for you are a people with hard necks ; for I will destroy you on the way
The people mourned when they heard this evil letter , and no man was clothed in it .
And the Lord said to Moses , &quot; Tell the children of Israel , &apos; Tell the Lord , &apos; You are a people who have hard necks , and if I come to you in a moment , I will destroy you , and take away all your adornment from you , that I may know how you are treated .
And the children of Israel cleansed their garments after they had dwelt in Mount Horeb .
Moses used to set the tents outside the camp , and when he was far from the camp , he called it the Tent of Meeting . He who asked the Lord went into the Tent of Meeting outside the camp
And it came to pass , when Moses had come out of the camp to the Tent of Meeting , that all the people rose up , and stood at the door of their tents , looking at Moses , until he had entered into the Tent of Meeting
&quot; When Moses entered the Tent of Meeting , the cloud came down and stood before the door of the Tent of Meeting , and the Lord spoke to Moses
And when all the people saw the pillar of the cloud standing before the door of the tabernacle of the congregation , they rose up and worshipped at the door of their tents
And the LORD spoke to Moses as to a man and to a friend : and Moses went into the camp , but Joshua the son of Nun , a young man of his helpers , did not leave the tabernacle of the congregation
Moses said to the Lord , &quot; You said to me , &apos; Take this people up , &apos; but you did not tell me who you would send with me , saying , &apos; I know you by your name , and you have been gracious before my eyes
&quot; If I now have mercy in your sight , show me your ways , that I may know you , and may have mercy in your sight , and think that these people are your people
&quot; I will go with you personally , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; that you may rest
Moses said , &quot; If you do not go with me personally , you will not bring us up from here
Is it not because you have gone with us that you have made me and your people and all the people of the earth separate from you , that they may know that I and your people have been blessed before you ?
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; I will do what you ask of me , because you have been gracious before my eyes , and I know you in your name
Moses said , &quot; Please show me your glory
&quot; I will show all my mercy , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will pass through before you , and declare my name ; and whoever I will have mercy , he will have mercy ; and whoever I will have mercy , he will have mercy
&quot; You will not see my face , &quot; he said , &quot; because no man can survive seeing my face .
&quot; Behold , there is a place in my presence , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; and you shall stand on a rock
&quot; When My glory has passed , I will place you in a rocky pit , and cover you with My hands , until I pass by .
Then I will take my hand back , and you will see my back , but you will not see my face .
And the LORD commanded Moses , saying , &quot; You shall cut out two pieces of stone , like the one which you broke before , and I will write on it the words which are on it
&quot; Be ready tomorrow morning , and stand before me on the top of Mount Sinai
&quot; No man shall go up with you ; no man shall be in the mountains , and no sheep and cattle shall feed on the roots of the mountains .
And Moses dug out two pieces of stone , and the like of the former ; and he arose early in the morning , and went up to Mount Sinai , as the Lord had commanded him , and took in his hand two pieces of stone
&quot; The Lord came down into the clouds , and stood there with Moses , proclaiming the name of the Lord
And the Lord proclaimed before him , saying , &quot; The Lord , the Lord , is a God of mercy and grace , not easily angry , and full of mercy and truth
&quot; For a multitude of millions He will have mercy and forgiveness for iniquity , transgression , and sin . He who is not guilty will not be made innocent , but will seek for his sins from his father and son , even to the third and fourth generation .
