&quot; If I have mercy in Your sight , O Lord , please accompany us among us , for these are a people with hard necks ; and forgive our iniquity and our sins , and forgive us our inheritance for You
&quot; I will make a covenant , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will do wonderful things in the sight of the people , which have not been done in all the nations ; and the foreigners around you will see the work of the Lord , because what I have done to you is a terrible thing .
&quot; Be obedient to what I command you today , and I will drive out from before you the Amorites , the Canaanites , the Hittites , the Perizzites , the Hivites , and the Jebustes
Be careful , and do not make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land wherein you have gone , lest they become a snare among you .
&quot; But they will destroy their altars , and break down their pillars , and cut down their figurines .
&quot; You shall not worship any other god , for the Lord is a god who is wicked , and is called a wicked man .
&quot; Because you have made a covenant with the inhabitants of the land , and the people have committed adultery with their gods , and worshipped their gods ; and someone has called you , and you have eaten his offerings .
&quot; Take their daughters as wives for your sons , and their daughters commit adultery with their God ; and your sons commit adultery with their God .
Don &apos;t cast idols for yourself
&quot; You shall keep the feast of yeast , and eat unleavened bread seven days in the month of Assyria , as I have commanded you ; for you have come out of Egypt in the month of Assyria for you .
&quot; All the firstborn are mine , and all the firstborn of cattle , whether cattle or sheep , all the princes are mine .
&quot; The firstborn donkey shall be redeemed with a lamb ; and if he is not redeemed , then his neck shall be broken ; and all the firstborn sons shall be redeemed ; and no man shall come to me empty-handed .
&quot; You shall work on the sixth day , and rest on the seventh day ; and you shall rest when you sow and harvest
Seventy-seven festivals shall be observed at the time of harvesting the first ripe wheat , and at the end of the year a festival of collection .
&quot; You all men , come three times a year to the Lord Yahweh God of Israel
&quot; I will drive out the foreigners from before you , and I will expand your borders ; and no man will lust for your land , when you go up to the Lord your God three times a year
&quot; You shall not offer with me the blood of my offering , and the bread of yeast ; nor shall you keep the Passover offering until the morning
&quot; The first things that are ripe in the land shall be brought to the house of the Lord your God.You shall not boil the lambs with the milk of the mother of lambs
