and the garments of the priests , which Aaron and his sons used in the sanctuary for the priest &apos;s office
&quot; All these things were done by the children of Israel , as the Lord commanded Moses
As the Lord commanded , so they did ; and when Moses saw all the work that was done , he blessed them
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; On the first day of the new month , you shall set up the tent of account
Put the ark of the law in it , and cover it with a mantle
Move the table , and place the things above it . Move the lampstand , and light the lamps on it
And he hanged the golden altar of incense before the ark of the law , and the curtains of the tent .
&quot; You shall place the burnt offering before the door of the Tent of Meeting
And thou shalt pour the washbasin in the midst of the tabernacle of the congregation and the altar ,
And the curtains of the house were round about , and the curtains of the house were hanged
And he anointed the tabernacle with oil , and all that was therein , and sanctified the tabernacle , and all the vessels thereof ; and they were sanctified
&quot; And you shall anoint the burnt offering and all the instruments that make it holy , and it shall be holy
&quot; You shall wash the washbasin and the basin seat , and make it holy .
&quot; You shall bring Aaron and his son to the door of the Tent of Meeting to wash themselves with water
&quot; You shall put on Aaron the holy garment , and anoint him , and make him holy , that he may give me the priestly office
&quot; And he will bring his son , and put on his robe for them
&quot; As their fathers were anointed , so shall I also anoint them , that they may serve me as priests ; and whoever is anointed in their generations shall long be priests .
&quot; Moses did all these things , as the Lord commanded him
On the first day of the first month of the second year , the tent of account stood up
&quot; Moses set up the tent , and set up the seats for the tent , and the boards , and put on the bars , and set up the pillars ,
&quot; He shall set up a tent above the tent , and cover the top of the tent , and cover it , as the Lord commanded him
And he put the book of the law in the ark , and put the bars on the sides of the ark , and laid the altar on the ark .
&quot; Take the ark up into the tent , and hang the curtain of the covering of the ark , and cover the ark , as the Lord commanded him
And the table shall be set in the tabernacle of the congregation , on the north side of the tabernacle , and outside the mantle
And set the bread before the LORD upon the table , as the LORD commanded him
And the lampstand shall be set in the tent of meeting , on the south side of the tent of meeting , against the table
light a lamp before the Lord , as the Lord commanded him
And set the altar before the curtain of the tabernacle of the congregation
And he burned on the altar sweet incense , as the Lord had commanded him
And the curtains of the tent ,
&quot; You shall set up the burnt offering before the door of the Tent of Meeting , and offer the burnt offering and the meal offering on it , as the Lord has commanded him
And lay the washbasin in the middle of the tabernacle and the altar , and pour water into it , that it may be washed
And Moses and Aaron and the sons of Aaron washed their hands and their feet in the basin
&quot; When they enter the tabernacle of the congregation , or when they approach the altar , they wash , as the Lord commanded him
And he set up the curtains of the tent and the altar round about , and hanged up the curtains of the house : and Moses finished the work .
Then the clouds covered the tents , and the glory of the Lord filled the tents
Moses could not enter the Tent of Meeting because the clouds stood on it and the glory of the Lord filled the Tent of Meeting
Whenever the clouds came up from the tent of meeting , the children of Israel set out to go
And if the clouds do not come up , they will not depart , until the clouds come up
The clouds of the Lord in the day are above the tent , and fire in the clouds in the night before all the house of Israel , and in the way that they walk .
&quot; The Lord called Moses from the Tent of Meeting and spoke to him
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , and say to them , &apos; If any man among you offers a sacrifice to the Lord , let him offer a sacrifice of cattle and of sheep
&quot; If his offering is a burnt offering for a bull , then he shall offer it at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation , a bull without blemish , to be acceptable to the Lord
&quot; He will lay his hand on the head of the burnt offering , and the burnt offering will be acceptable , and he will be redeemed for his sin .
&quot; He shall slaughter bulls before the Lord , and the sons of Aaron the priest , and he shall offer blood , and sprinkle it around the altar at the door of the Tent of Meeting
&quot; Then he shall take off the skin of the burnt offering , and cut it into pieces
&quot; The sons of Aaron the priest shall put the fire on the altar , and put the wood on the fire
And the sons of Aaron the priest shall place the meat , and the head , and the fat thereof , on a wood of fire upon the altar
&quot; But the flesh and the legs of the burnt offering shall be washed with water , and the priest shall burn them all on the altar as a burnt offering , and offer it to the Lord for a sweet savour
&quot; If a man &apos;s offering is a sheep or a goat for a burnt offering , then he shall offer an unimpaired lamb
&quot; You shall slaughter the sheep on the north side of the altar before the Lord ; and you shall sprinkle the blood of the sheep around the altar for the priests of the sons of Aaron
&quot; The priest shall cut the burnt offering into pieces , with the head and the fat , and place it on a wood of fire on the altar .
&quot; Their intestines and their legs shall be washed with water , and the priest shall burn them all on the altar ; it is a burnt offering , an offering made by fire to the Lord for a sweet savour
&quot; When a man offers his offering to the Lord , if he burns a bird for a burnt offering , he shall offer a dove or a young pigeon
&quot; The priest shall take the bird before the altar , and he shall take off his head , and burn it on the altar ; and the blood of the bird shall flow by the altar .
And thou shalt take away the wings of the birds , and the filth , and cast it into the ashes of the east side of the altar .
&quot; You shall take the two wings of the bird and tear it apart , but you shall not tear it apart ; and the priest shall burn it on the altar on firewood ; it is a burnt offering , a sweet aroma to the Lord
&quot; If any man offers an offering to the Lord , he shall pour oil on it with fine flour , and add lard to it
&quot; The priest shall take a tray out of the fine flour , and take some oil , and all the scent of milk , and burn it on the altar for a memorial to the Lord , for a burnt offering of sweet incense .
&quot; The rest of the priest &apos;s offerings shall be returned to Aaron and to his sons , for a most holy offering to the Lord in the feast of fire
If it is baked in a furnace for an offering , it shall be a baked unleavened bread with oil , or a baked unleavened bread with oil
If it is made of iron , it shall be made of fine unleavened flour mingled with oil .
&quot; And he divided them into pieces , and poured on them oil ; and this is the offering of the firstfruits .
&quot; If it is for a sin offering made on a platter , it shall be made with oil and fine flour
&quot; They shall bring the firstfruits of these things before the Lord , and bring them before the altar to the priests
&quot; The priest shall take it out of the meal offering for a memorial , and burn it on the altar , as a burnt offering to the Lord for a sweet savour
The remnant of the firstfruits shall be given to Aaron and to his sons , which is holy in the burnt offering with the Lord .
&quot; None of the grain offerings you offer to the Lord shall have any yeast ; for you shall not burn any yeast nor any honey for a burnt offering to the Lord
&quot; They shall be offered to the Lord as a firstfruit offering , but they shall not be offered on the altar for a sweet savour
&quot; Every offering made for the sacrifice of the passover shall be prepared with salt , and there shall be no shortage of the salt of the covenant of your God ; and every offering shall be prepared with salt .
&quot; If you offer the firstfruits to the Lord as an offering , you shall offer the newly baked ears of the firstfruits , the newly rolled ears of the firstfruits
&quot; They shall pour oil on it , and add lard to it ; this is the offering of the firstfruits .
And the priest shall burn thereof for a memorial some of the ears of the wheat rolled , and some of the oil , and all the frankincense , as a burnt offering unto the LORD .
&quot; When a man offers a sacrifice for a sacrifice of peace , whether it be from the flock , whether it be a public offering , or a mother &apos;s offering , it shall be offered before the Lord without any infirmity .
&quot; He shall lay his hand on the head of the offering , and kill it at the door of the Tent of Meeting ; and the sons of Aaron the priest shall sprinkle blood around the altar
&quot; You shall offer the burnt offering to the Lord from the feast of peace , and you shall cover the filthy fat , and all the filthy fat ,
And the two waistbands , and the fat on the waistbands , the fat on the sides of the waistbands , and the nets on the liver , and the waistbands ,
&quot; The sons of Aaron shall burn them on the burnt offering of the altar , on the wood of fire , for a sweet aroma to the Lord
&quot; A man who offers a sacrifice to the Lord for a sacrifice of peace , whether it be from a flock of sheep , whether it be a public offering , or a mother &apos;s offering , shall do so without any infirmity
&quot; If you offer a lamb for a sacrifice , you shall offer it before the Lord
And they shall lay their hands on the head of the offering , and slay it before the Tent of Meeting ; and the blood of the sons of Aaron shall be sprinkled around the altar .
&quot; You shall offer a burnt offering to the Lord on the feast of peace , and the fat thereof , and the whole fat tail , shall be taken down from near the spine , and the fat that is dirty shall be covered , and all the fat that is dirty shall be covered .
The two waistbands , and the fat on the waistbands , the fat on the sides of the waistbands , and the nets on the liver , and the waistband ,
&quot; The priest shall burn it on the altar , as a burnt offering for food to the Lord
&quot; If a man &apos;s offering is a sheep , he shall offer it before the Lord
&quot; You shall lay your hands on the head of the sheep , and slaughter them before the Tent of Meeting ; and you shall sprinkle the blood of the sons of Aaron around the altar .
And he shall take the fat that is covered with filth , and all the fat that is on the filth , the two waistbands , and the fat that is on the waistbands , the fat that is on the sides of the waistbands , and the net that is on the liver , and the waistbands , and offer them unto the LORD for a burnt offering
