&quot; The priest shall burn it on the altar for a sweet savour offering , and the fat shall be the Lord &apos;s
&quot; You shall not eat fat or blood in all your dwellings . This shall be a statute for your generations forever .
And the Lord said unto Moses
Speak unto the children of Israel , saying , If a man committeth a sin in that which the LORD hath commanded him not to do ,
Or if the anointed priest commits a sin , and puts the people in sin , then he shall offer the calf without any infirmity for a sin offering to the Lord for atonement for his sins .
And he shall bring the bull to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD , and shall lay his hand on the head of the bull , and slay it before the LORD
&quot; The anointed priest shall take some of the blood of the bull and bring it to the Tent of Meeting
And you shall dip your fingers in the blood , and sprinkle seven times blood on the mantle of the sanctuary before the Lord
And you shall sprinkle some of the blood on the four corners of the altar of burnt offering before the Lord in the tabernacle of the congregation , and all the blood of the bulls shall you put on the foot of the altar of burnt offering at the door of the congregation .
&quot; You shall offer the fat of all the bulls for a sin offering : it is the fat that covers the filth , and the fat that covers all the filth .
And the two waistbands , and the fat on the waistbands , the fat on the sides of the waistbands , and the nets on the liver , and the waistbands ,
&quot; The priest shall burn them on the altar of the burnt offering
the skins of bulls , and all flesh , and their heads , and their legs , and their intestines , and their bowels , and their dung
&quot; All the bulls shall be brought to a clean place outside the camp , a place of ashes , and burned with fire on wood .
&quot; If all the congregation of Israel commits a sin which the Lord has commanded them not to do , it is hidden and not seen , and the congregation is not seen .
&quot; When all the congregation has known their sins , they shall offer a calf for a sin offering , and bring it before the Tent of Meeting
&quot; The elders of the congregation shall lay their hands on the head of the bull before the Lord , and they shall kill it before the Lord
&quot; The anointed priest shall take some of the blood of the bull and bring it to the tabernacle of the congregation
And you shall dip your fingers in the blood , and sprinkle seven times blood on the mantle before the Lord
&quot; And you shall sprinkle some of the blood in the Tent of Meeting on the four corners of the altar before the Lord , and you shall place all the blood at the foot of the burnt offering altar at the door of the Tent of Meeting .
Take all the fat of the cow , and burn it on the altar
&quot; Take away the cow , just as the cow for a sin offering ; and the priest will redeem them , and they will be forgiven .
&quot; He will bring the cow to the camp and burn it like the head of a cow . It is a sin offering for the congregation .
&quot; If a ruler does that which the Lord his God has commanded him not to do , he has sinned .
And when he had known his sins , he took for a sacrifice a goat without any infirmity
&quot; You shall lay your hands on the head of the sheep , and slaughter them before the Lord , in the place where you slaughter the burnt offering , for a sin offering
&quot; The priest shall dip the blood of the sin offering with his fingers , and sprinkle it on the four corners of the burnt offering , and put it on the foot of the burnt offering
&quot; The priest shall burn all the fat on the altar , as the fat of the sacrifice of peace ; and the priest shall redeem him for his sins , and he shall be forgiven
&quot; If any man among the people does that which the Lord has commanded him not to do , he is guilty of sin .
&quot; When he has known his sins , he will take a lamb without any infirmity for his sins .
And he laid his hand on the head of the sin offering , and slew it in the place where the burnt offering was slain
&quot; The priest shall dip some of the blood of the sheep with his finger , and sprinkle it on the four corners of the altar of burnt offering ; and all the blood shall fall on the feet of the altar
&quot; And he shall take all the fat of the sheep , as the fat of the sacrifice of peace , and he shall burn it on the altar before the Lord as a sweet savour , and he shall be forgiven for his sins ;
&quot; If a man takes a lamb for a sin offering , he must take a lamb without a disability
And he laid his hand on the head of the sin offering , and slaughtered it in the place where the burnt offering was slaughtered , for a sin offering
&quot; The priest shall dip some of the blood of the sin offering with his finger on the four corners of the altar of burnt offering ; and all the blood shall fall on the feet of the altar
And he shall take away all the fat , as the fat of the lamb of peace ; and he shall burn it on the altar , according to the ordinance of the burnt offering of the Lord ; and he shall be forgiven for his sins , and he shall be forgiven .
&quot; If a man hears the voice of the oath , he is a witness , but does not speak what he sees , and what he knows , saying , &apos; This is sin ; &apos; and he will bear his iniquity .
Or if a man touches an unclean thing , whether it be an unclean beast , or an unclean beast , or an unclean worm , and he does not know it , and becomes unclean , he is guilty .
&quot; Or if he touches another man &apos;s filth , or whatever filth he has stained , he does not know it ; but when he knows it , he is guilty .
Or if a man swears in his mouth to do evil , or to do good , and he swears in any thing , but he does not know it ; and when he knows it , he is guilty of it .
When he has sinned , let him confess his sins
And he shall bring his offering for his sins , the lamb of the flock , or a lamb , or a goat , for a sin offering before the LORD ; and the priest shall redeem him for his sins .
&quot; If his strength fails to offer a lamb , he shall bring two turtledoves , or two young pigeons , for a sin offering before the Lord , one for a sin offering , and one for a burnt offering ,
&quot; The priest shall bring them into the priest &apos;s house , and he shall first offer the sin offering , and take his head off the neck of the bird , but he shall not tear it apart .
And he shall sprinkle some of the blood of the sin offering beside the altar ; and the rest of the blood shall flow at the feet of the altar : this is the sin offering .
&quot; He shall offer a second burnt offering according to the pattern , and the priest shall redeem him for his sins , and he shall be forgiven
If his strength fails to offer two turtledoves , or two young pigeons , he shall bring a offering for his sins , one tenth of an ephah of fine flour , for a sin offering , neither oil nor frankincense , for a sin offering
And he shall bring the offering to the priest , and the priest shall take out his handkerchief for a memorial , and burn it on the altar , according to the ordinance of the burnt offering of the LORD : it is a sin offering .
&quot; The priest shall redeem him for his sins which he committed in these things , and he shall be forgiven ; and the rest of his face shall be as the priest &apos;s and as the priest &apos;s .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; If a man commits a sin in the holy things of the Lord , and has committed a sin , then he shall take the silver of the sanctuary , according to your estimation , and offer it for a ransom , a sheep without blemish from the flock , and bring it before the Lord for a ransom .
And he shall be recompensed for his sins in the holy things , and an additional fifth shall be given to the priest ; and the priest shall redeem him for his sins with the sheep of the sacrifice of rams , and he shall be forgiven .
&quot; If a man commits a sin , and does that which the Lord has commanded him not to do , even though he does not know it , yet he is guilty , he shall bear his iniquity .
&quot; You shall also bring a ram from the flock , without any infirmity , for a ransom to the priest , according to the price that you have estimated ; and the priest shall redeem him for his sins , and he shall be forgiven for his errors .
&quot; This is the sacrifice of the redemption , because he has sinned before the Lord
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; If a man commits a sin , and commits an offence against the Lord , and deceives his neighbour in the things which he delivers to him , or in the transactions , or robs a man &apos;s property , or oppresses his neighbour ,
Or what sin have you committed in taking away lost things , in lying , in swearing , in all these things ?
He who commits a sin , and has committed it , shall return what he has taken , or what he has gained by oppression , or what he has been delivered , or what he has lost .
&quot; If he swears by any thing , he shall return it to the Lord as a number , plus one fifth , in the day when he is found guilty .
&quot; You shall also bring to the Lord the ransom offering of the lamb , which is one of the sheep of the flock , without any infirmity , for the price which you have estimated , and give it to the priest for a ransom offering
&quot; The priest shall make atonement for him in the sight of the Lord , and he shall be forgiven for his sins , whatever he does
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
And thou shalt say unto Aaron and to his sons , Thus shall be the ordinance of the burnt offering : The burnt offering shall be put on the wood of the altar , and the fire of the altar shall be burned continually from the evening even unto the morning ;
&quot; The priest shall put on a linen garment , and put on linen trousers , and take up the ashes of the burnt offering on the altar , and lay them beside it
Then take off this garment , put on another garment , and bring the ashes to the place where the camp is cleansed
&quot; The fire of the altar shall be on it continually , and it shall not be quenched ; and the priest shall burn wood on it every morning ; and he shall place the burnt offering on the altar , and burn on it the fat of the peace offerings
There will be on the altar a continually burning fire that cannot be extinguished .
&quot; This is the ordinance of the priesthood : The sons of Aaron shall offer it before the altar before the Lord
&quot; The priest shall take out of it a handful of oil , and of all the milk of the offering , which is on the fine surface of the altar , and burn it on the altar for a memorial to the Lord for a sweet altar .
&quot; All that remains shall be eaten by Aaron and his sons ; they shall eat it in the holy place without yeast , and in the courts of the tabernacle of the congregation
&quot; When it is roasted , it shall not be mixed with yeast . This is the most holy of the offerings of the burnt offerings which he has offered to me , as a sin offering and as a ransom offering
&quot; Every male among the sons of Aaron , who sacrifices a burnt offering to the Lord , shall eat of that portion , and it shall be a portion for them for ever , for generations to come ; and whoever touches it shall become holy .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; In the days of Aaron &apos;s anointing , he and his sons shall offer to the Lord one tenth of an ephah of fine flour for a continual offering , half in the morning and half in the evening ,
&quot; You shall mix it with oil and mix it in a mixture , and you shall bring it in , and bake it well , and break it into pieces , and offer it to the Lord as a sweet savour
&quot; From among the sons of Aaron , they shall be his anointed priests , and they shall offer the offering of this oil , and burn it all to the Lord , for a statute for ever .
&quot; You shall burn the priest &apos;s meat offerings , but you shall not eat them
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You said to Aaron and to his sons , &apos; This is the ordinance of the sin offering , to sacrifice the sin offering in the place of the burnt offering before the Lord ; it is holy .
&quot; The priests who offer this sacrifice for sin shall eat it in the sanctuary , in the court of the Tent of Meeting
&quot; Whoever touches the flesh of the sacrifice shall be holy ; and the blood of the sacrifice , if it is cast into any garment , shall be cleansed in the sanctuary .
&quot; But the vessel of the offering that is boiled shall be broken ; and if it is boiled in a copper vessel , it shall be polished and rinsed in water .
&quot; Every male among the priests shall eat it ; it is holy .
&quot; If any man who offers a sin offering brings blood into the Tent of Meeting at the sanctuary for a sin offering , it shall not be eaten , but it shall be burned with fire
&quot; This is the ordinance of the sacrifice of the redemption offering , which is holy
A man shall slaughter therein his burnt offering , and therein his offering for ransom ; and the priest shall sprinkle his blood around the altar .
&quot; The fat tail and the dirty fat shall be covered
The two waistbands , and the fat on the waistbands , the fat on the sides of the waistbands , and the nets on the liver , and the waistband ,
&quot; The priest shall burn it on the altar for a burnt offering to the Lord for a ransom offering
&quot; It is holy for every male among the priests to eat of it in the holy place .
How is the offering for sins , and how is the offering for ransom ? The two offerings are one ordinance ; and the priest who offers the ransom for sins shall receive it
&quot; The priest who offers a burnt offering , whoever it is , shall receive the skin of the burnt offering he has offered for himself .
All that is baked in a furnace , and that is made in a pan , and that is made on iron , shall be to the priest who offers it .
And the offering of all flesh , whether it be oiled or dried , shall be given to the sons of Aaron , and they shall be divided .
&quot; This is the ordinance of the sacrifice of peace offerings to the Lord
And if he offer it in thanksgiving , he shall offer it together with the sacrifice of thanksgiving , unleavened cakes anointed with oil , and unleavened cakes anointed with oil , and cakes of fine flour mixed with oil .
And they shall offer it with the bread of yeast , and with the sacrifice of peace for thanksgiving ;
&quot; From every offering he shall offer a cake to the Lord for an offering , to be returned to the priest who sprinkles the blood of the sacrifice of peace
And the meat of the sacrifice of peace shall be eaten in the day of the offering , and one hour shall not be left until the morning
&quot; If it is offered willingly or willingly , it shall be eaten on the day of the sacrifice , and the second day that remains shall be eaten .
&quot; But the meat that remains shall be burned with fire on the third day .
&quot; On the third day , if he eats the flesh of the sacrifice of peace , it will not be acceptable to him ; neither will anything given by any man be counted as a sacrifice ; but if he eats the flesh of it , he will bear his iniquity .
&quot; The meat of uncleanness shall not be eaten , but it shall be burned with fire ; and the meat of the sacrifice of peace shall be eaten by every clean man .
&quot; It is the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings to the Lord ; and if a man eats it uncleanly , he shall be cut off from among the people .
&quot; When a man touches something unclean , or something unclean of a man , or something unclean of a beast , or something unclean that is hateful , and eats the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings to the Lord , he shall be cut off from among the people
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; You shall not eat the fat of the cows , the fat of the sheep , the fat of the goats
&quot; The fat of the dead and of the torn by the beasts will be for another use , but you shall not eat it .
&quot; Whoever eats the fat of the cattle sacrificed to the Lord for a burnt offering , he shall be cut off from among the people
&quot; You shall not eat in all your dwellings the blood of birds , the blood of beasts ,
&quot; Whoever eats blood will be cut off from the people
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; Whoever offers a sacrifice of peace to the Lord , let him take some of it and give it to the Lord
&quot; He shall bring the burnt offering of the Lord by hand , fat and breasts , that he may shake them before the Lord , and shake them one by one .
&quot; The priest shall burn the fat on the altar , but the breasts shall be to Aaron and to his sons
&quot; You shall raise up your right leg from the sacrifice of peace , and offer it to the priest .
&quot; The right leg shall be divided among the sons of Aaron for the blood and for the fat of the sacrifice of peace offerings .
&quot; For I have taken the breast and the raised leg out of the sacrifice of the peace of the children of Israel for Aaron the priest and for his sons , as an everlasting portion from among the children of Israel .
&quot; This is the anointing of Aaron and his sons from the Lord &apos;s burnt offering , in the days when Moses called them to minister to the Lord
&quot; This is what the Lord commanded the children of Israel to do in the days of Moses , when he anointed them ; and this is their portion for ever throughout their generations .
&quot; This is the ordinance of the burnt offering , and of the sacrifice of the firstfruits , and of the sin offering , and of the ransom offering , and of the peace offering , and of the consecration of the holy office
And all that the LORD commanded Moses in Mount Sinai , and that he commanded the children of Israel in the wilderness of Sinai to offer unto the LORD in the day of the LORD
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
And thou shalt bring Aaron and his son with him , and bring the holy garments , and the anointing oil , and a bullock for a sin offering , and two rams , and a basket of unleavened bread
And invite the congregation to the door of the tabernacle
And Moses did as the Lord commanded : and the congregation gathered themselves together at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation
And Moses cried unto the congregation , saying , This is the thing which the Lord commanded to be done
And Moses brought Aaron and his sons , and washed them with water
And Aaron put on his inner robe , and on his waistcoat , and on his outer robe , and on him Ephrath , and a cord of fine weaving , and he fastened Ephrath upon him .
And they gave him a breastplate , and put Urling and Thumming in it .
And he put the crown on his head , and he nailed gold before the crown , which is the holy crown , according to all that the Lord commanded Moses
Moses anointed the tabernacle with oil , and all that was in it , and sanctified him
And he sprinkled on the altar seven times with oil , and anointed the altar , and all the vessels thereof , and washed the basin , and the basin seat , and sanctified him
Then he poured the oil upon Aaron &apos;s head , and anointed him , and sanctified him
And Moses brought Aaron &apos;s sons , and put on their robes , and on their waistbands , and on their headscarves , as the Lord commanded Moses
And he took the ox for a sin offering , and Aaron and his sons laid their hands on the head of the ox for a sin offering
And Moses dipped the blood with his fingers , and sprinkled it around the four corners of the altar , and cleansed it , and poured the blood on the feet of the altar , and sanctified it , and the altar was cleansed
And he took all the fat that was dirty , and the nets that were on the liver , and the two waistbands , and the fat that was on the waistbands , and burned them on the altar .
&quot; But the bulls , and their meat , and their dung , were burned with fire outside the camp , as the Lord commanded Moses
And Aaron and his sons laid their hands on the head of the ram ,
And Moses sprinkled the blood around the altar
And he cut the sheep into pieces , and burned the head and the flesh , and the fat thereof ,
And he washed the intestines and the legs with water , and burned the whole sheep on the altar for a sweet burnt offering , a burnt offering to the Lord , according to all that the Lord commanded Moses
And he offered the second ram , the sheep of the holy service , Aaron and his sons , and laid their hands on the head of the sheep .
Moses sprinkled some blood on Aaron &apos;s right ear , and on his thumb on his right hand , and on his right foot
And he brought Aaron &apos;s son , and sprinkled some of the blood upon their right ears , and upon their right thumb , and upon their right foot , and sprinkled it around the altar .
Take the fat , and the fat tail , and all the fat that is filthy , and the nets of the liver , and the two waist , and the fat that is on the waist , and the right leg ;
And he took out of the basket of unleavened bread before the Lord a cake of unleavened bread , and an oil cake , and a thin cake , and put them on the fat and on the right leg
&quot; Put all this in Aaron &apos;s hand , and in the hand of his son , as an offering , and shake it before the Lord
Moses took it out of their hands , and burned it on the altar for a burnt offering , a sweet aroma to the Lord for the taking of the holy charge
And Moses took the breast of the sheep for a wave offering , and waved it before the Lord , as a gift to Moses for the holy service , according to all that the Lord commanded Moses .
And Moses took some of the oil and the blood of the altar , and sprinkled it on Aaron and on his garments , and on the garments of his sons and of his sons , and sanctified him and their garments together
And Moses said unto Aaron and to his sons , Boil the flesh at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation , and eat therein , and eat the cakes of the basket of the holy office , as I have commanded you : this is what Aaron and his sons shall eat
&quot; You shall burn the rest of the meat and the cakes with fire .
&quot; You shall not go out of the door of the Tent of Meeting for seven days , until the days of your consecration are fulfilled , because you have been consecrated to the Lord for seven days
&quot; All that is done today is according to the commandment of the Lord , to redeem your sins
&quot; For seven days you shall dwell at the door of the Tent of Meeting , day and night , and keep the commandment of the Lord , lest you die ; for this is what I have commanded you
And Aaron and his son did all that the LORD commanded Moses
And it came to pass on the eighth day , that Moses called Aaron and his sons , and the elders of Israel
And he said to Aaron , &quot; Take a bull out of the flock for a sin offering , and a ram for a burnt offering , and offer them before the Lord without any infirmity
&quot; You shall also say to the children of Israel , &apos; Take a goat for a sin offering , and a calf and a lamb for a burnt offering , without blemish for one year
&quot; Take also a bull and a ram for a sacrifice of peace before the Lord , and a meat offering with oil , for the Lord is to be revealed to you today
So they took what Moses had commanded , and brought it before the tabernacle of the congregation ; and the whole congregation came near , and stood before the Lord
Moses said , &quot; This is what the Lord has commanded you to do ; and the glory of the Lord will appear to you
And Moses said unto Aaron , Come near unto the altar , and offer thy sin offering and thy burnt offering for thyself and for the people , and offer offerings of a hundred families for their sins , as the Lord hath commanded
And Aaron came near the altar , and slew the calf for his sin offering
And Aaron &apos;s son offered him blood , and he dipped his finger in the blood , and sprinkled it on the four corners of the altar , and put the blood in the foot of the altar
&quot; But the fat of the sin offering , and the waist , and the nets of the liver , shall be burned on the altar , as the Lord commanded Moses
And the flesh and the skin were burned with fire outside the camp
And when Aaron had slain the burnt offering , his son gave him the blood , and he sprinkled it around the altar
&quot; Then he who offered a burnt offering , one by one , handed it over to him with his head , and he burned it on the altar .
And he washed his intestines and his legs , and burned them on the burnt offering on the altar
And he offered the offering of the people , and slaughtered the goats of the people for a sin offering , and offered them for sin , and as a first offering
and offer burnt offerings according to the pattern
And he offered an offering of raisin , and took a basket full of it , and burned it on the altar , beside the morning burnt offering
And Aaron slaughtered the bull and the ram for a peace offering to the people ; and his son gave him the blood , and he sprinkled it around the altar
And he gave him the fat of the bull and the sheep , and the fat of the tail , and the fat of the filthy , and the waist , and the nets of the liver ,
He put the fat on his chest , and he burned it on the altar
And Aaron , his chest and his right legs , were to be waved before the Lord as a wave offering , as Moses commanded
And Aaron lifted up his hand to the people , and blessed them ; and he offered the sin offering , and the burnt offering , and the sacrifice of peace , and came down
Then Moses entered into the Tent of Meeting , and blessed the people , and the glory of the Lord appeared to the people
Then a fire came out from before the Lord , and consumed the burnt offering and the fat on the altar ; and when the people saw it , they rejoiced , and fell down on the ground
And Nathan the son of Aaron , and Abihu , took their own fireplaces , and set them on fire , and put incense , and offered all the fire before the Lord ; for the Lord had not commanded them
Then a fire came out from before the Lord , and consumed them , and they died before the Lord
And Moses said unto Aaron , Thus saith the Lord ; I will be holy among the people that are near to me , and I will be glorified in the sight of all the people ; and Aaron said nothing .
Then Moses called Elisha , the son of Mizhali , the son of Uzziah , the uncle of Aaron , and said to them , &quot; Come up and bring your relatives out of the sanctuary
Then the two men went up and brought them out of the camp in their robes , as Moses had commanded them .
Moses said to Aaron , and to Eleazar his son , and to Ishmael , &quot; Do not spread your heads , nor tear your clothes , lest you die , lest the Lord be angry with the congregation , as long as all your brethren Israel mourn for the fire of the Lord
&quot; You shall not enter the doors of the Tent of Meeting , lest you die , for the anointing of the Lord is on you ; and they will do as Moses said .
The Lord spoke to Aaron , saying ,
&quot; When you and your son enter the tabernacle of the congregation , you shall not drink wine or strong drink , lest you die , and this shall be a statute for ever for your generations .
so that you may separate the holy , the profane , the clean , and the unclean
and that you may teach the children of Israel all the statutes of the Lord through Moses
Moses said to Aaron and to Eleazar the son of Aaron , and to Ishmael , the remnant of him , &quot; You shall eat by the altar the remainder of the meat offering of the Lord &apos;s burnt offering without yeast , for it is holy
&quot; You shall eat in the holy place , for this is your portion and your son &apos;s portion in the burnt offering to the Lord ; and this is the law which I have commanded you .
&quot; You shall eat the breasts that are shaken and the legs that are lifted up in a clean place ; you and your children shall eat it together ; for it is your portion and your son &apos;s portion from the sacrifice of peace among the children of Israel .
&quot; They shall bring the legs that they have lifted up , and the breasts that they have shaken , with the fat of the burnt offering , and shake it before the Lord as a wave offering , and it shall be yours and your sons &apos;s inheritance for ever , as the Lord has commanded them .
Now Moses , looking for the goat for a sin offering , when he knew that it had been burned , was angry with Eleazar the son of Aaron , the remnant , and with Ehamma , saying ,
&quot; This is a holy sin offering , which the Lord has given to you for your sins against the congregation , and for their sins before the Lord . Why do you not eat of the holy things ?
&quot; Behold , the blood of this sacrifice has not been brought into the sanctuary ; but you have eaten it in the sanctuary , as I have commanded you
And Aaron said to Moses , &quot; Today they offer the sin offering and the burnt offering before the Lord ; and I have seen such a disaster again ; can the Lord see it beautiful if they have eaten the sin offering this day
When Moses heard this , he was pleased
And the LORD said unto Moses ,
&quot; You spoke to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; These are the foods of all the beasts of the earth
&quot; You shall eat every beast whose hoofs are divided into two halves .
&quot; But the camel that cannot be chewed or divided in its feet is unclean to you because it does not divide its feet .
&quot; Shaban , you are unclean with you because you do not break your feet to chew .
Rabbits are not clean with you , because they do not separate their feet from each other .
&quot; The pigs are not clean with you , because their feet are divided into two halves , and they do not chew .
&quot; The flesh of these beasts you shall not eat , and the dead you shall not touch ; they are not clean with you .
These are the things that can be eaten in the waters ; and they that have wings and scales in the waters , and in the sea , and in the rivers , can eat
&quot; You shall detest all that moves in the sea , and in the river , and in all the waters , without wings and without scales .
Those without wings and without scales are abominable ; you shall not eat his flesh ; and those who die are abominable .
&quot; You who have no wings and no scales in the waters shall be hated .
&quot; In the birds of prey you are carved carvings , carvings of dogs , carvings of red heads , which you hate and which you cannot eat .
Eagle , small eagle , and its kind
Crows , and their kinds
Ostriches , night eagle , fish eagle , eagle , and their kinds
Owls , owls , owls
Horned lizard , pelican , bald eagle
Snakes , Snakes , and their kinds . Snakes , and Bats
&quot; Everything that has wings and crawls on its four feet , you shall hate .
&quot; But among the things that crawl with wings and four feet , and have feet and legs , and jump on the ground , you shall eat .
And among them are locusts , grasshoppers , crickets , and their kinds , and grasshoppers , and their kinds , which you may eat
&quot; But there are reptiles with wings and four feet , and you shall be despised .
&quot; These things will make you unclean . He who touches the dead will not be clean until the night .
&quot; He who takes the dead will not be clean until the evening , and will wash his clothes .
&quot; Whoever walks and does not divide his feet into two , nor chews , is unclean with you ; and whoever touches is unclean .
Every beast that walks on all fours with his hands is unclean with you ; and he that touches his body shall be unclean until the night .
&quot; He who takes his body will be unclean until evening , and he will wash his clothes ; these are unclean to you .
These are the creeping things of the earth that are unclean to you : the locusts , the locusts , the lizards , and their kinds .
Wall tiger , dragon , house guard , snake doctor , dragonfly
&quot; These reptiles are unclean to you . Whoever touches them after their death will be unclean until the night .
&quot; Whatever falls on the east and west of the dead shall not be clean on the east and west , whether it be wooden vessels , clothes , skins , pockets , or utensils for any work ; it shall be placed in water , and it shall not be clean until the night , until the night .
&quot; If a man dies and falls into a pot , and there is nothing in it , he is not clean ; you shall break the pot .
And all that is eaten therein shall be unclean , and all that is drinked therein shall be unclean .
&quot; If any of them die , and there is a spot on any thing , it will be unclean , whether it be a furnace or a boiler , it will be broken , it will be unclean , and it will be unclean with you .
But the fountain , or the fountain of water , shall be clean ; but he that is slain shall not be clean .
And if he die , there shall be a drop on the seed to be planted , and the seed shall be clean .
&quot; If the water has been poured on a grain , and there is a drop on the head of the dead , it will not be clean with you .
&quot; If the beast you eat dies , and someone touches it , it will not be clean until the evening
A man shall eat the dead beast , and shall not be clean until the night , and shall wash his clothes ; and he that takes the dead beast , and shall not be clean until the night , and shall wash his clothes
&quot; You shall not eat any creeping thing that is abominable on the earth .
&quot; You shall not eat any that walks with his belly , or walks on four feet , or on many feet ; for it is abominable .
&quot; You shall not make yourselves abominable because of creeping things , nor purify yourselves because of them , that you may be defiled .
&quot; I am the Lord your God , therefore you shall be holy , for I am holy ; and you shall not defile yourselves with the creeping things of the earth
&quot; I am the Lord who brought you out of the land of Egypt to be your God ; therefore be holy , for I am holy
These are the ordinances of the beasts , of the birds , and of the living creatures that move in the water , and of the creeping things on the earth
&quot; You shall separate the clean from the unclean , and the edible from the un edible ;
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; If a woman conceives a boy , she shall not be clean seven days , as in the days of the moon , when it is unclean .
On the eighth day to circumcise the infant
A woman shall dwell in her house thirty-three days in the midst of uncleanness , and her days of purity shall not be fulfilled , neither shall she touch the holy things , nor enter the sanctuary .
&quot; If he bears a girl , he shall not cleanse her for two and seven days , as in the time of uncleanness ; and he shall be in her house for sixty-six days in the midst of uncleanness .
&quot; When the days are full of cleanness , whether for a boy or for a girl , he shall bring a lamb of the first year for a burnt offering , or a dove , or a turtledove for a sin offering , to the door of the Tent of Meeting , and give it to the priest .
&quot; The priest shall offer it before the Lord for atonement for him , and his blood shall be cleansed . This is for a woman to be born , male or female ,
&quot; If his strength fails to offer a lamb , he shall take two turtledoves , or two young pigeons , one for a burnt offering , and one for a sin offering ; and the priest shall redeem him , and he shall be clean .
And the LORD spake unto Moses , saying ,
&quot; If there is a leprosy on a man &apos;s flesh , or if there is a plague on his flesh , or if there is a plague of madness on his flesh , then he shall be brought to Aaron the priest , or to a son of Aaron the priest .
&quot; The priest shall look at the plague on the skin of the flesh . If the hair of the plague has become white , and the plague is deeper than the skin of the flesh , it is the plague of madness , and the priest shall look at him and determine that he is unclean
&quot; If the plague is white on his flesh , and the phenomenon is not deeper than the skin , and the hair on it has not become white , then the priest shall shut up the afflicted for seven days .
&quot; On the seventh day the priest shall examine him , and if the plague ceases , and does not spread on the skin , then the priest shall seal him up seven days
&quot; On the seventh day the priest shall look again at him , and if the plague is dark , and it has not spread on the skin , then the priest shall cleanse him , and he shall wash his clothes , and he shall be clean
&quot; But after he has examined the body to be clean , if the psoriasis has spread on the skin , then he shall examine the body again to the priest
&quot; The priest shall look , and if the plague spreads on the skin , he shall be deemed unclean , and a great madman .
&quot; When a man has a great plague of madness , he shall be brought before the priest
Then the priest shall look , and , behold , if there be white spots on the skin , and the hair be white , and there be red stains in the spots of the white spots
&quot; This is an old madman on the flesh . The priest will not lock him up for uncleanness , because he is unclean
And if the great leprosy be spread out from the four corners of the skin , and be filled with the skin of the afflicted , it shall not be found from head to foot , as the priest saw it
&quot; The priest shall look , and if the whole flesh is full of madness , he shall cleanse the afflicted , and his whole body shall become white , and he is clean .
But when the red flesh appeared on him , it was not clean .
The priest , when he saw the red meat , determined that it was unclean ; and the red meat was unclean , and it was madness .
&quot; If the red flesh is restored and become white , he shall come to the priest
&quot; The priest shall look , and if the place of the plague becomes white , the priest shall declare the plague clean , and he is clean
If a man has a sore on the flesh , he is healed
Then the priest shall see if there is a spot of white on the sore , or a spot of red in the white .
And if the phenomenon is low in the skin , and the hair thereof becomes white , then he shall be deemed unclean , and the plague of the great leprosy shall be in the wound .
&quot; If the priest sees that there is no white hair on him , nor any decay in his skin , but that he is dark , then he will be locked up seven days
&quot; If it spreads on the skin , the priest shall declare him unclean , a plague
&quot; If the spot remains where it was , and does not spread , it is the mark of a plague , and the priest shall cleanse it .
If a poisonous , poisonous stain is on the skin of a man , it becomes a spot of fire , or red in white , or completely white
And the priest shall look , and if the hair of the spot of fire be white , and the phenomenon be deeper than the skin , and it be the plague of madness in the poison of fire , then he shall be deemed unclean , and it shall be the plague of madness .
But the priest saw that if there was no white hair in the spot , nor any low spot in the skin , but darkness , then he would be locked up seven days .
&quot; On the seventh day the priest shall examine him , and if the plague is spread out on his skin , he shall declare him unclean , a plague of the great plague of madness .
&quot; If the spot remains where it was , and there is no spreading on the skin , it is darkness , and a flame of poison ; and the priest shall make him clean , and there shall be no trace of it .
Whether male or female , if there is a plague on the head , or a plague on the man &apos;s beard
Then the priest shall look , and if the plague be deeper than the skin , and there be fine yellow hair in it , then he shall declare it unclean : it is the scalp , it is on the head , or it is the great scalp of the beard
&quot; If the priest sees the plague of the head lice , and the phenomenon is not deeper than the skin , and there is no black hair in it , he shall seal the plague of the head lice seven days .
&quot; On the seventh day the priest shall observe the plague ; if the scalp is not spread , and there is no yellow hair in it , and the scalp is not deeper than the skin
&quot; Then he shall shave off his beard , but he shall not shave in the place where he has shaved his head ; and the priest shall shut it up for seven days
&quot; On the seventh day the priest shall examine the head lice , and if the head lice have not spread out on the skin , and the phenomenon is not deeper than the skin , then he shall make him clean , and he shall wash his clothes , and he shall be clean
&quot; But afterwards he must be cleansed , so that if the plague spreads on the skin ,
&quot; The priest will look at him ; and if the scalp is spread out on the skin , he will not find the yellow hair , for he is unclean .
&quot; If the priest sees that the head lice have stopped , and black hair has grown in them , and the head lice are healed , and the man is clean , then he shall be cleansed
Whether male or female , if there is a spot on the skin , it is a white spot
And the priest shall look , and if the spots of their flesh be black in white , it is the white plague which is on their skin ; then he is clean .
&quot; When a man &apos;s hair is cut off , he is neither bald nor clean
&quot; If his hair is cut off before his head , he is neither bald nor clean
&quot; If there is a plague of white and red , it is the great madness , spreading on his head , or on his gates ,
And the priest shall look , and see that the plague which he hath caused , if it be on the head , or on the top of the door , and there be a phenomenon of madness on the skin of the flesh , as if it were red in white ;
&quot; This is he who has grown mad and unclean , and the priests will judge him unclean , and his plague is on his head
&quot; A man who has grown up with a disease of madness , and his clothes are torn , and his head is spread out , and his lips are covered , and he cries out , &apos; Not clean ! Not clean !
&quot; In the days when the plague is on him , he is unclean , and he is unclean , and he will dwell alone in camps
Clothes infected with the disease , whether wool or cloth
whether it be on a scale , or on a ladder , or of linen , or of wool , or of leather , or of any thing made of leather
&quot; If the plague is green or red , or if it is a plague of the great plague of madness , it shall be seen to the priest , on the garment , on the skin , on the veil , on the lace , or on any thing made of the skin .
&quot; The priest shall observe the plague , and seal up the plague-infected things for seven days .
&quot; On the seventh day he shall examine the plague , whether it be on the garment , or on the waist , or on the lace , or on the skin , whether it be spread , or what kind of skin it is for , and whether it be unclean , the plague is a great madness of the silkworm .
&quot; He who has stained the garment of the plague , or the veil , or the lace , or the wool , or the linen , or anything made of leather , shall burn it ; for he is a mad man who eats silk , and will burn it in the fire .
&quot; The priest shall see if the plague has not spread on any of the garments , or on any of the stripes , or on any of the laces , or on any of the skins .
And the priest said unto them , Wash the plague-stricken things , and shut them up seven days
And after he has washed it , the priest shall look : and if it is not discolored , and if the plague is not spread , and if it is not clean , and if it is a severe plague , it shall be burned in the fire , on the one hand and on the other .
And after he has washed him , the priest shall look : and if he see the plague darkened , he shall tear it from the garment , and from the skin , and from the veil , and from the lace ,
&quot; If it is still on a garment , or on a piece of cloth , or on a lace , or on a piece of leather , it will be a new plague , and the plague will be burned with fire .
And if the plague be gone , and the garments that are washed , or the veils , or the laces , or the skins , be washed again , they shall be clean .
&quot; This is the ordinance of the plague of leprosy , whether it be on woolen garments , or on linen garments , or on lace , or on lace , or on things made of leather , whether it be clean or not .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; This is the case in the days when he grows up mad and becomes clean , and brings him to the priest
&quot; The priest shall go out into the camp to see ; and if he see that his great frog is healed ,
And he shall command that for him that seeketh cleanness , he shall take two clean birds , and cedar trees , and scarlet threads , and oxen &apos;s knees ,
&quot; The priest shall command to pour the living water into the pot , and to kill a bird over it
And the priest shall dip the living bird in the blood of the bird that is slain in the living water , with the acacia trees , with the red line , and with the oxen &apos;s knees
and sprinkle seven times on the man who has grown mad and seeks to be clean , and make him clean , and lay the living birds in the field
And those who seek purity shall be purified when they wash their clothes , shave their hair , and bathe themselves in water ; then they shall enter into the camp , but to dwell outside their tents for seven days .
Then on the seventh day you shall shave all your hair on your head , and your beard , and your eyebrows , and all your hair ; and you shall wash your clothes , and wash yourselves with water , and you shall be clean .
&quot; On the eighth day he shall take two lambs without blemish , and a lamb of the first year without blemish ; and he shall take three tenths of an ephah of fine flour mingled with oil for a supper offering , and a raisin of oil ,
&quot; The priest who performs the cleansing service shall place the cleansing man and all these things before the Lord at the door of the Tent of Meeting
&quot; The priest shall take a lamb for a ransom offering , and the raisin oil , and shake it together before the Lord
&quot; The lambs shall be slaughtered in the holy place , the place of the sin offering and the burnt offering ; and the offering of the offering shall be to the priest , as the offering of the sin offering is holy
&quot; The priest shall take the blood of the offering of the young bull , and sprinkle it on the right ear of the cleanser , and on the thumb of the right hand , and on the thumb of the right foot ,
&quot; The priest shall take some of the oil of the locust , and put it in his left hand
&quot; You shall dip one finger of your right hand in the oil of your left hand , and smite it seven times with your finger before the Lord
And he shall sprinkle the rest of the oil of his hand upon the right ear of the cleansing man , and upon the thumb of his right hand , and upon the thumb of his right foot , and upon the blood of the sacrifice of the young bullock .
&quot; The rest of the oil that remains in the priest &apos;s hand shall be poured on the head of the cleansing man , and he shall make atonement for it before the Lord
&quot; The priest shall offer a sin offering , for the sin of the unclean one who seeks to be clean , and he shall kill the burnt offering
&quot; And he made atonement for him on the altar with the burnt offering and the meat offering , and he was cleansed
&quot; If the poor cannot prepare the number of rams , then he shall take a lamb for the offering of rams , which he may shake for his sins ; and he shall bring with him one tenth of an ephah of fine oil for an offering of rams , and one logar of oil for atonement .
And he took , by his power , two turtledoves , or two young pigeons , one for a sin offering , and one for a burnt offering
&quot; Then on the eighth day you shall bring it for atonement to the door of the Tent of Meeting , before the Lord , and give it to the priest
&quot; The priest shall shake the lamb for a ransom offering with the oil of the locust , and shake it before the Lord
And he shall kill the lamb for a ransom offering , and take some of the blood of the ransom offering , and sprinkle it on the right ear of the cleansing man , and on the thumb of his right hand , and on the thumb of his right foot ,
&quot; The priest shall pour some oil into his left hand
And thou shalt smite the oil of the left hand seven times before the LORD with one finger of the right hand
And the oil of your hand shall be sprinkled on the right ear of the cleansing man , and on the thumb of his right hand , and on the thumb of his right foot , which is the place of the blood of the offering of the heifer .
&quot; The rest of the oil that remains in the priest &apos;s hand shall be poured on the head of the cleansing man , and he shall make atonement for it before the Lord
And he shall offer a dove , or a young pigeon , according to his power
&quot; The priest shall offer one for a sin offering , one for a burnt offering , and one for a meal offering , and the priest shall make atonement for him before the Lord
&quot; This is the law of the man who has a great plague of leprosy , and can &apos;t prepare the number of leprosy for clean things .
And the LORD spake unto Moses , saying ,
&quot; You have come to the land of Canaan , which I have given you for a possession ; and if I cause you to enter into the houses of the land for a possession , there will be a great plague of madness .
Then the lord of the house went to complain to the priest , saying , &quot; It seems to me that there is a plague in the house
Before the priest enters to inspect the plague , he shall command the people to empty the house , lest all things in it become unclean . Then the priest shall enter and inspect the house
He shall observe the plague , if there are green or red spots on the walls of the house , and if the plague is low on the walls
&quot; The priest shall go out to the door of the house , and seal the house for seven days
&quot; On the seventh day the priest shall make another inspection . If the plague spreads on the walls of the house ,
And he shall command a man to dig out the stone of the plague , and to cast it out of the city into unclean places
And they shall shave the enclosures of the houses , and the ashes which they have shaved shall be cast into the unclean places outside the city .
And another stone shall be taken for the stone that was dug out , and a house of clay shall be added
He dug out a stone , and shaved the house , and when he was bowed , the plague was found in the house
&quot; The priest shall go in and look ; and if the plague be spread in the house , it is a great madman , which eats silk in the house , and is unclean
And he will destroy the houses , and he will bring the stones , and the wood , and the clay , to a place that is not clean outside the city
&quot; When the house is locked up , those who enter it shall not be clean until the evening .
&quot; Those who lie in the house shall wash their clothes , and those who eat in the house shall wash their clothes .
&quot; When the house has been torn down , and the priest has entered in and seen that the plague has not spread in the house , then he shall cleanse the house , for the plague has been eradicated .
Take for a clean house two birds , and acacia trees , and scarlet threads , and oxen &apos;s knees ,
Pour live water into the pot , and slaughter a bird over it
And you shall sprinkle the house seven times with the firewood , and with the barley , and with the red line , and with the living bird , in the blood of the slain bird , and in the living water .
&quot; You shall cleanse the house with the blood of birds , and with the water of living birds , and with acacia trees , and with oxen &apos;s knees , and with red lines .
&quot; But put the living birds in the fields outside the city , and the house will be cleansed , and the house will be cleansed .
This is for all kinds of plague diseases , and head lice .
And clothes , and the house of the great madman
as well as the Ordinance on the Prevention and Punishment of Sclerosis , Tinnitus and Spotted Spots
When it is clean , and when it is unclean , this is the ordinance of the great madman
And the LORD said unto Moses ,
&quot; You have spoken to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; If a man has leprosy , he will not be clean because of it
He has leprosy , whether it be downstream , whether it be stopped , whether it be unclean
His bed was unclean , and his seat was unclean .
&quot; He who touches the bed shall not be clean until the evening , and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water .
&quot; He who sits with leprosy shall not be clean until evening , and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water .
&quot; He who touches the flesh of a leper shall not be clean until evening , and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water .
&quot; If a leper spits on a clean person , he shall not be clean until evening , and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water
And the saddle which the leper rides is unclean .
&quot; He who touches anything underneath him shall not be clean until the night ; and he who takes it shall not be clean until the night ; and he shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water .
&quot; He who has leprosy shall have no water to wash his hands , and whoever touches him shall not be clean until the evening , and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water .
And the vessels that the leper toucheth shall be broken , and all the wooden vessels that he toucheth shall be washed with water .
&quot; When a man who has leprosy is healed , he shall reckon seven days to cleanse himself , and he shall wash his clothes , and wash himself with living water , and he shall be clean .
&quot; On the eighth day you shall take two turtledoves , or two young pigeons , and bring them to the door of the Tent of Meeting before the Lord , and give them to the priest
&quot; The priest shall offer one for a sin offering , and one for a burnt offering ; and the priest shall make atonement for him before the Lord for the leprosy of the man
&quot; If a man dreams , he will not be clean until the evening , and he will wash his whole body with water
&quot; Whether it is a garment or leather , dyed with purity , it shall not be clean until the evening , and it shall be washed with water .
If a man and woman have sex , they shall not be clean until the evening . They shall bathe themselves in water
A woman who practices will be unclean for seven days ; and whoever touches him will not be clean until the evening .
A woman is unclean in the filth ; all that she lays down is unclean ; and all that she sits down is unclean .
&quot; He who touches his bed shall not be clean until the evening , and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water .
&quot; He who touches the things in which he sits shall not be clean until evening , and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water .
&quot; If a man touches anything on the woman &apos;s bed or on her seat , he will not be clean until the night .
&quot; If a man touches his filth in his room with the woman , he shall be unclean seven days , and the bed on which he lies shall be unclean .
If a woman has a leak of blood for many days , or a leak of blood for too long , outside of menstruation , he shall be unclean because of it , as he was unclean during menstruation .
The bed wherein he lay and the things wherein he sat in the days of leprosy shall be defiled , as it was in the days of his menstruation .
&quot; Whoever touches these things shall be unclean , and shall not be clean until the evening , and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water .
If the woman &apos;s leakage is good , seven days shall be counted , and then cleansed
&quot; On the eighth day you shall take two turtledoves , or two young pigeons , and bring them to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation to the priest
&quot; The priest shall offer one for a sin offering and one for a burnt offering , and the priest shall make atonement for him before the Lord for the uncleanness of his blood
&quot; You shall separate the children of Israel from their filth , lest they defile My tabernacle , and die for their own filth
It &apos;s leakage , and it &apos;s unclean dreaming .
There are also regulations for men and women with menstrual diseases and leprosy , and for men and women who are unclean .
And the two sons of Aaron came near to die before the LORD : and after they had died the LORD spake unto Moses , saying ,
&quot; Thus I tell you , Aaron your brother , that you shall not enter the mantle of the sanctuary at any time before the altar on the ark , lest he die ; for I will appear in the altar from the clouds
And Aaron went into the holy place , and brought a calf for a sin offering , and a ram for a burnt offering
He shall put on a saintly robe of fine linen , and put on fine linen trousers , a belt of fine linen , and a crown of fine linen on his head . These are his holy garments . He shall wash himself with water , and then put on his garments
&quot; You shall take from the congregation of Israel two rams for a sin offering , and one ram for a burnt offering
And Aaron shall offer up the bull for a sin offering , and for himself and for his house
&quot; And you shall place the two goats before the Lord at the door of the Tent of Meeting
&quot; For the two sheep , one goat is to the Lord , and one goat is to Azariah
&quot; And Aaron shall return the lot to the Lord for a sin offering
&quot; But the sheep that went to Azariah shall be kept alive in the presence of the Lord for a ransom , and shall be sent to the wilderness to Azariah
And Aaron shall bring the bull for a sin offering , and slaughter it for himself , and for his house :
&quot; Take a fireplace full of charcoal from the altar before the Lord , and take a spoon of fine incense , and bring it into the mantle
&quot; Put the incense on the fire before the Lord , and let the smoke of the incense cover the altar of the law , lest he die
&quot; You shall also take some blood of bulls , and smite them with your fingers on the east side of the altar , and on the front side of the altar seven times .
&quot; Then he shall kill the goat for a sin offering for the people , and bring the blood of the goat into the mantle , and shoot it on the altar , and on the forehead , as the blood of a bull .
&quot; For all the filthiness of the children of Israel , and for all their sins , he has transgressed , and has performed the service of redemption in the sanctuary , and has done so in the filthiness of the tabernacle of the congregation
When he entered into the sanctuary of redemption , there was no one in the tabernacle of the congregation until he had redeemed himself and his house , and all the congregation of Israel .
&quot; And he shall come out to the altar before the Lord , and make atonement on the altar , and take the blood of the bulls and the blood of the goats , and sprinkle it around the four corners of the altar
&quot; You shall sprinkle on the altar seven times with your fingers , and you shall cleanse it , and remove from it all the filth of the children of Israel , and make it holy
And when Aaron had finished offering the sin offering for the sanctuary , and for the tabernacle , and for the altar , he would offer up the only live goat
And they laid their hands on the head of the sheep , and confessed all the iniquities of the children of Israel , their transgressions , and all their sins ; and they laid them on the head of the sheep , and carried them into the wilderness by the hand of the One who had sent them .
And he shall lay the sheep in the wilderness , and he shall bear all their iniquity , and bring them into the land of no man .
And Aaron shall enter into the tabernacle of the congregation , and take off his fine linen garments which he was clothed in when he entered into the sanctuary , and put them therein
&quot; And he shall wash himself with water in the sanctuary , and put on his clothes , and come forth , and offer his burnt offering , and the burnt offering of the people , to forgive himself and the people
&quot; The fat of the sin offering shall be burned on the altar
&quot; The sheep were brought to the men of Azariah to wash their clothes , and to wash themselves with water , and to enter into the camp .
&quot; The bull for a sin offering , and the blood of the goat for a sin offering , which is brought into the sanctuary for a sin offering , shall be carried out of the camp , and his skin , and his flesh , and his dung , shall be burned with fire
The burners had to wash their clothes , wash themselves with water , and then enter the camp
&quot; On the tenth day of the first month of July , you shall do no work for yourselves , whether you are a native or a foreigner who dwells among you ; it shall be a statute for ever .
&quot; For on that day I will redeem you for your sins , and make you clean , and you will be clean before the Lord , and you will be cleansed from all your sins
&quot; You shall observe this day as a holy Sabbath , and suffer yourselves ; it is a statute for ever .
&quot; The anointed priest , who is in charge of the holy office of his father , shall put on a fine linen garment for a sin offering
&quot; He will make atonement in the sanctuary , and in the tabernacle of the congregation , and in the altar ; and he will make atonement for the priests , and for the people of the congregation
And Aaron did as the LORD commanded Moses , saying , This shall be a statute for ever for you , that you may redeem yourselves for all the sins of the children of Israel year after year
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to Aaron and to his sons and to all Israel , saying , &apos; This is what the Lord has commanded
&quot; Every man of the house of Israel that slays a bull , or a lamb , or a goat , shall not be slaughtered in the camp outside the camp
&quot; If he has not been brought to the door of the Tent of Meeting , to the front of the Tent of the Lord , to offer it as a sacrifice to the Lord , then the sin of blood will be on him , and he will be cut off from among the people ,
&quot; This is to bring the offerings of the children of Israel which they have offered in the field to the door of the Tent of Meeting before the Lord , and to give them to the priests for a sacrifice of peace with the Lord
&quot; The priest shall sprinkle the blood on the altar of the Lord at the door of the Tent of Meeting , and burn the fat for an offering made sweet to the Lord
They shall no more offer sacrifices to the devils whom they have followed in their wickedness ; this shall be a statute for ever for their generations .
And thou shalt say unto them , Every man of the house of Israel , and every stranger that dwelleth among them , shall offer a burnt offering or a sacrifice of peace
&quot; If he does not bring it to the door of the Tent of Meeting and offer it to the Lord , he will be cut off from among the people
&quot; If any man of the house of Israel , or any stranger who dwells among them , eats any blood , I will turn his face to him who eats it , and cut him off from among the people .
&quot; For the life of the living is in the blood , which I have given to you , that you may make atonement for your life on the altar ; and because there is life in the blood , that you may make atonement
Therefore I said to the children of Israel , &quot; You shall not eat blood , neither shall the foreigner who dwells among you eat blood
&quot; If any of the children of Israel , or any foreigner who dwells among them , hunts any beast that can be eaten , he shall bring forth his blood and cover it with soil
&quot; Therefore I said to the children of Israel , &apos; You shall not eat the blood of any living creature , for the blood of all living creatures is his life ; and whoever eats the blood will be cut off
&quot; Whoever eats from the dead , or is torn by beasts , and is a native or a stranger , shall not be clean until the night , but shall wash his clothes and wash himself with water , and it shall be clean until the night .
&quot; But if he does not wash his clothes , nor does he wash himself , he will bear his iniquity .
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; I am the Lord your God
&quot; In the land of Egypt , where you used to dwell , there is no law for you to do ; and in Canaan , where I will bring you , there is no law for you to do , nor for you to do according to their wickedness .
&quot; You shall keep My statutes and My ordinances , and do them ; I am the Lord your God
Therefore keep my statutes and my ordinances ; and if any man do them , he shall live according to them ; and I am the Lord .
&quot; You shall not reveal the flesh of the flesh , nor come near to them ; I am the Lord .
Thou shalt not reveal thy mother &apos;s belly ; thou shalt disgrace thy father ; he is thy mother ; thou shalt not reveal his belly
&quot; You shall not reveal the body of your mother-in-law ; it is the body of your father
&quot; Your sisters , who are foreign mothers and fathers and fathers and mothers , and who are born at home and who are born abroad , shall not reveal their bodies
&quot; You shall not reveal your granddaughters or your great-granddaughters &apos; bodies , but you shall reveal their bodies , and you shall reveal your own bodies .
&quot; You shall not reveal the body of your mother &apos;s daughter , your father &apos;s daughter , your sister .
&quot; You shall not reveal the body of your aunt ; she is the kinsman of your father &apos;s flesh .
&quot; You shall not reveal the body of your aunt ; he is the kinsman of your mother &apos;s flesh .
&quot; You shall not approach your uncle &apos;s wife , nor humiliate your uncle , for he is your uncle &apos;s mother
&quot; You shall not reveal the body of your daughter ; she is your son &apos;s wife ; you shall not reveal his body
&quot; You shall not reveal the body of your brother &apos;s wife ; this is the body of your brother
&quot; You shall not reveal the bodies of a woman , nor the bodies of his daughter , nor marry his granddaughters , or his great-granddaughters , to reveal their bodies ; for they are the kinsmen of the flesh ; that is evil .
&quot; Your wife shall not marry his sister as her husband , while she is still alive , and reveal her body to him .
&quot; When a woman is unclean , she shall not reveal her lower body to him , nor be near to him .
Thou shalt not commit adultery with thy neighbor &apos;s wife , nor defile thyself
&quot; You shall not cause your children to pass through the fire to return to Moses , nor shall you profane the name of your God ; I am the Lord .
&quot; Do not be like a man , like a woman ; that is abominable .
&quot; You shall not be obedient to the beast and defile yourselves ; nor shall a woman stand before the beast and be obedient to him ; that is an abomination .
&quot; You shall not defile yourselves in all these things ; for in all these things you have defiled yourselves , the nations which I have driven out before you .
&quot; Because the land is defiled , I will pursue the iniquity of the land , and the land will expel its inhabitants
&quot; Therefore keep My statutes and My ordinances , and all these abominations , whether they be of the natives or of strangers who dwell among you , shall not be done .
The land is defiled because of all these abominations which you have done to those who dwell therein first .
&quot; Beware that when you defile the land , the land will spit out you , as it spit out the nations before you .
&quot; Whoever does an abomination of it shall be cut off from among the people .
&quot; Therefore keep what I have commanded you , lest you follow the abominable customs of your fathers , and defile yourselves ; for I am the Lord your God .
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to all the congregation of Israel , saying , &apos; You must be holy , for I , the Lord , your God , am holy
Each one of you shall respect his parents , and keep my sabbaths : I am the LORD your God .
&quot; You shall not turn your backs on the God of nothingness , nor cast for yourselves idols . I am the Lord your God .
&quot; When you offer the sacrifice of peace to the Lord , it shall be a pleasant offering
&quot; This offering shall be eaten on the day it is offered , and on the second day ; and if there remains until the third day , it shall be burnt with fire .
&quot; If you eat again on the third day , it will be unpleasant for the wicked .
&quot; He who eats will bear his iniquity , for he has profaned the holy things of the Lord , and he will be cut off from among the people
&quot; You shall not harvest in your land , nor cut off the corners of the field , nor take away what is lost .
&quot; You shall not take away the fruit of the vineyard , nor take away the fruit of the vineyard that is lost , and leave it to the poor and to the dwellers ; I am the Lord your God .
&quot; You shall not steal , nor deceive , nor lie to one another
&quot; You shall not swear by my name , nor profane the name of your God ; I am the Lord .
Thou shalt not oppress thy neighbour , neither shalt thou take away his goods ; and thou shalt not hire a man for his wages , and he shall not dwell therein till the morning .
Thou shalt not curse the deaf , neither shalt thou lay a stumbling block before the blind : but thou shalt fear thy God : I am the LORD .
Thou shalt not judge , nor do evil , nor prejudice the poor , nor overlook the mighty ; but judge thy neighbours according to righteousness .
&quot; You shall not move yourselves among the people , neither shall you be an enemy to your neighbours , and put them to death ; I am the Lord .
Do not hate your brethren in your heart , but point out to your neighbour , lest he should be guilty .
&quot; You shall not retaliate , nor reproach your children in your land , but love them as yourself ; I am the Lord
&quot; You shall keep my statutes , and your cattle shall not be mixed with other kinds ; neither shall two mixed varieties be used for your land , nor shall two mixed materials be used for clothing , nor shall they be worn on your bodies .
&quot; The maid has given her husband , and he has not yet been redeemed . If a man commits adultery with him , two of them will be punished , but he will not put them to death , for he has not yet had freedom for the maid .
&quot; Then he shall bring the offering of the ram , a ram , to the door of the Tent of Meeting before the Lord
&quot; The priest shall redeem his sins before the Lord , and his sins shall be forgiven .
&quot; When you come to the land of Canaan and plant trees of all kinds , you shall eat of the fruit of the tree that is cut down , uncircumcised ; and for three years you shall eat of it , uncircumcised .
But the fruit of the fourth year shall be sanctified , to praise the Lord
&quot; In the fifth year you shall eat the fruit of the tree , that the tree may bear more fruit for you ; I am the Lord your God
&quot; You shall not eat bloody things ; neither shall you use witchcraft nor signs .
No shaving shall be done around the head , nor shall the beard be damaged around it .
Thou shalt not cut the dead with the sword , neither shalt thou put a veil upon them : for I am the LORD .
Thou shalt not insult thy daughter , and make her a prostitute : for the earth is full of wickedness , and the land is full of wickedness .
&quot; You shall keep My Sabbaths , My sanctuary ; I am the Lord .
Thou shalt not turn aside from them that deceive and do witchcraft , nor ask of them that thou mayest be defiled by them : I am the LORD your God
&quot; Stand up before the white-haired , and respect the elderly , and fear your God ; I am the Lord .
&quot; If a stranger dwells with you in your land , you shall not deceive him
&quot; You shall see him as a native , and love him as yourself , for you have dwelled in the land of Egypt , and I am the Lord your God .
Thou shalt not do unjustly in judgment , nor in scales , nor in scales , nor in heights , nor in battles .
&quot; I am Yahweh your God who brought you out of the land of Egypt , and you shall walk in the right way , and in the right way , and in the right way , and in the right way , and in the right way , and in the right way ;
&quot; You shall keep all my statutes and my ordinances ; I am the Lord .
And the Lord said unto Moses
And thou shalt say unto the children of Israel , Whosoever of the children of Israel , or of any stranger that dwelleth in Israel , giveth his sons and his daughters unto Moses , he shall surely be put to death ; and the inhabitants of the land shall slay him with stones .
&quot; I will also turn my face to that man , and cut him off from among the people , because he has dedicated his sons and daughters to Moses , and has defiled my sanctuary and my holy name .
&quot; He has given his sons and daughters to Moses ; but if the natives pretend to be absent , they will not put him to death .
&quot; I will turn my face to this man and to his house , and I will cut him off from among the people , and all those who commit wickedness with him and with Moab .
&quot; I will turn my face to him , and cut him off from among the people , because he who has turned to devils and practices sorcery has committed adultery with them .
&quot; Therefore sanctify yourselves , for I am the Lord your God
&quot; You shall keep my statutes , and I am the Lord that sanctifies you .
&quot; He who curses his parents will be put to death , and he who curses his parents will have his sins returned to him .
Whoever commits adultery with his neighbor &apos;s wife , and whoever commits adultery with his husband , and whoever commits adultery with his wife , shall be put to death .
Whoever commits adultery with his mother-in-law , and is ashamed of his father , he shall surely put both of them to death , and the sin shall be upon them .
&quot; He who dwells with his daughters shall surely put both of them to death ; for they have done evil , and their sins shall return to them .
&quot; If a man walks with a man as a woman , and two of them commit abominations , they shall surely be put to death , and their sins shall be returned to them .
&quot; If a man marries a wife and marries his mother , it is evil ; so burn them with fire , that evil may not be done among you .
&quot; If a man commits adultery with a beast , he will surely punish him and kill the beast .
&quot; If a woman is close to a beast and has sexual intercourse with him , you will kill the woman and the beast , and you will surely kill them , and the sin will be on them .
&quot; If a man marries his sisters , whether mother and father , or father and mother , and they see each other &apos;s bodies , it is a shameful thing ; they will be cut off before the eyes of the people ; and he who reveals the bodies of his sisters will bear his iniquity .
&quot; When a woman has menstruation , if she is in her room with him , and she reveals her underparts , she reveals her blood source , and she reveals her own blood source , two will be cut off from the people .
&quot; You shall not expose your aunt or her aunt &apos;s body ; it is the body of the relatives of the bones ; they shall be responsible for their sins .
&quot; If a man stays with his uncle &apos;s wife , he is ashamed of his uncle ; and if two men bear their own sins , they shall die without children .
&quot; If a man marries his brother &apos;s wife , it is an unclean thing , and humiliates his brothers , and two will have no children .
&quot; Therefore keep all my statutes and my ordinances , lest I expel you from the land where I have brought you to dwell
&quot; You , the people whom I have driven out before you , do not follow their customs ; for they have done all these things , and I hate them .
&quot; But I said to you , &apos; You shall inherit their land , and I will give you a land of milk and honey for a possession . I am the Lord your God , and I will separate you from all the people .
Therefore you shall separate the clean from the unclean , and you shall not make yourselves abominable because I have divided you into unclean beasts , or the living creatures of the earth .
&quot; You shall be holy to me , because my Lord is holy , and separate you from all the people , and make you my people
&quot; Whether they be male or female , they who are possessed by demons or who practise sorcery , they shall be put to death , and they shall be put to death with stones , and their sins shall return to them .
And the LORD said unto Moses , Thus saith the LORD unto the priests of the sons of Aaron , The priest shall not wash himself of the dead among the people
Unless the parents , children , brothers and sisters of his bones
and sisters who have not married as virgins , so that they may wash themselves
&quot; The priest who is first among the people shall not contaminate himself with secularity
&quot; You shall not shave your head , nor shave your beard , nor cut your body with a knife .
&quot; You shall be holy to God , and you shall not profane the name of God ; for the Lord &apos;s burnt offering is the food of God , which they have offered , so that they may be holy
&quot; You shall not marry a prostitute or a woman who has been corrupted , nor a woman who is restless , for the priest is holy to God .
Thou shalt therefore sanctify him , because he hath consecrated the food of thy God ; and thou shalt sanctify him , because the Lord , whom I sanctify of you , is holy .
&quot; If the daughter of the priest defiles herself , and defiles her father , she shall burn him with fire
&quot; He who is a great priest among his brethren , and pours oil on his head , and takes the holy office , and is clothed in holy garments , shall not spread his head , nor tear his clothes .
You must not approach the dead , nor contaminate yourself for your parents
&quot; You shall not go out of the sanctuary , nor blaspheme the sanctuary of God ; for God &apos;s crown of oil is on his head ; for I am the Lord .
He wants to marry a woman
A widow , or a woman who is restless , or a woman who is defiled as a prostitute , shall not be married ; only a virgin among the people shall be married .
&quot; You shall not insult his sons and his daughters among the people ; for I am the Lord who sanctifies him
And the Lord said unto Moses
And thou saidst unto Aaron , The remnant of thy generations shall not come near to offer the food of his God unto them that are handicapped
For whoever has a disability , whether blind , lame , nose-broken , and limb-deprived ,
of the legs of the hands
A camel , a dwarf , an eye diseased , a scab , a dwarf , or a kidney damaged shall not come near
&quot; The descendants of Aaron the priest , whoever has a disability , shall not come near to offer a burnt offering to the Lord , nor shall he come near to offer the food of God who has a disability
He can eat the food of God , whatever it is holy and most holy .
&quot; But you shall not enter before the mantle , nor be near the altar ; for he is disabled , so that he may not profane My holy place ; I am the Lord who sanctifies him .
Then Moses spoke to Aaron , and to the sons of Aaron , and to all Israel
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; You have commanded Aaron and his sons , saying , &apos; Stay away from the holy things which the children of Israel have dedicated to me , lest they profane my holy name ; I am the Lord
&quot; You shall say to them , &apos; Your descendants from generation to generation will be cut off before me from all that is filthy in their bodies , from the holy things of the nearest of Israel , which are holy to the Lord ; I am the Lord .
&quot; The descendants of Aaron , who have grown up to be mad , or who have leprosy , shall not eat of the holy things until they are cleansed , and whoever touches the unclean thing of the dead body , or whoever touches the defiled person , or whoever touches the defiled person ,
or touch the creeping thing that makes him unclean , or touch the man that makes him unclean , whether he is unclean or not ,
&quot; He who touches them will not be clean until the evening , and will not eat the holy things unless he washes himself with water .
&quot; When the sun sets , he is cleansed , and can eat the holy things , for these are his foods .
&quot; He who dies , or is torn by the beasts , cannot eat , and therefore defiles himself : I am the Lord .
So that they may keep what I have commanded them , lest they neglect , and die in sin ; I am the Lord who sanctifies them
&quot; No foreigner shall eat of the holy things , neither shall he who dwells in the priest &apos;s house , nor shall he who employs workers eat of the holy things
&quot; If the priest buys a man for his money , he may eat the holy things , and he who is born in his house may eat them .
&quot; If the daughter of the priest marries a stranger , she shall not eat the holy things of the sacrifice
But if the daughter of the priest be a widow , or a destitute woman , and have no child , and return to her father &apos;s house , and be as his youth , she shall eat the bread of her father ; but no stranger shall eat it .
&quot; If a man eats the holy things wrongly , then he shall give it to the priest , according to the number of the holy things , and one fifth of the number thereof .
The priest shall not profane the holy things which the children of Israel have offered to the Lord
For I am the LORD that sanctifieth them , lest they take their iniquity on the holy things .
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to Aaron and to his sons , and to all Israel , saying , &apos; All the people of the house of Israel , and all the inhabitants of Israel , whoever offers anything , whatever it is that is promised , it is offered willingly , and it is offered for a burnt offering to the Lord
&quot; This is how you will be pleased if you offer a bull , or a sheep , or a goat without any infirmity .
&quot; You shall not offer to anyone with a disability , for it is not pleasing
&quot; Whoever offers a sacrifice of peace to the Lord from the cattle or from the sheep , for a vow of redemption , or as a sweet offering , will be acceptable to him , and he who offers it will be without blemish
&quot; The blind , the wounded , the lame , the leprosy , the leprosy , the leprosy , the leprosy , the leprosy , shall not be offered to the Lord , nor shall they be offered on the altar for a burnt offering to the Lord
&quot; Whether it be a bull or a lamb , if there be more or less of the flesh , it shall be for a freewill offering , for a recompense , but it shall not be acceptable
&quot; A kidney that is broken , or crushed , or broken , or pierced , shall not be offered to the Lord on your land ; neither shall it be done to you
Neither is it acceptable for you to offer such things from the hands of strangers as your God &apos;s food ; for they are corrupt , handicapped , and unpleasant .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
A newborn bull , or a sheep , or a goat , shall be with his mother seven days , and after the eighth day shall be a pleasant offering , a burnt offering to the Lord .
&quot; You shall not slaughter a mother or a child on the same day , be it a cow or a sheep
&quot; You offer thanksgiving to the Lord for a pleasant offering
&quot; You shall not eat that day until the morning ; I am the Lord .
&quot; You shall keep My commandments , and I am the Lord .
&quot; You shall not profane My holy name ; I am holy among the children of Israel ; I am the Lord that sanctifies you
&quot; I will bring you out of the land of Egypt as your God ; I am the Lord .
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; The Lord &apos;s Sabbath , you shall proclaim as the Sabbath of the congregation
&quot; You shall do your work on the sixth day ; and on the seventh day is the Sabbath ; you shall do no work when there is a holy convocation ; it is the Sabbath to the Lord in all your dwellings .
These are the feasts of the Lord , the days when you shall proclaim the feast .
&quot; It is the Lord &apos;s Passover on the fourteenth day of the month at twilight .
&quot; The fifteenth day of this month is the feast of unleavened bread , which you shall keep before the Lord : seven days ye shall eat unleavened bread
On the first day , when there is a holy feast , no labour shall be done
&quot; You shall offer a burnt offering to the Lord seven days . The seventh day is a solemn feast , and no labour shall be done .
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , and say to them , &apos; You have come to harvest your land , which I have given you , and to bring a bundle of the first ripe crops to the priests
&quot; And he will shake it before the Lord , that you may be pleased ; and the priest will shake it on the next day of the Sabbath
&quot; You shall offer to the Lord for a burnt offering a lamb of the first year without blemish ,
&quot; The first offering of it shall be two tenths of an ephah of fine flour mingled with oil , a burnt offering of sweet savour to the Lord ; and the second offering of it shall be one-fourth of a hin of wine
&quot; You shall not eat any cake , nor any baked grain , nor any new ear , until the day when you bring the offering of God , which is in all your dwellings , as a statute for ever and ever for generations .
&quot; You shall count the seven days of the Sabbath from the next day of the offering of the flock for a wave offering .
&quot; On the seventh day of the Sabbath , fifty days in total , you shall offer the offering of figs to the Lord
&quot; You shall take two tenths of an ephah of fine flour from your dwelling places , and ferment it , and bake it into two cakes for a wave offering , and offer it to the Lord as a firstfruit
And seven lambs a year old without blemish , and one bull , and two rams , with cakes , and their meat offerings , and their drink offerings , shall be for a burnt offering to the Lord , a sweet burnt offering to the Lord ;
&quot; You shall offer one lamb for a sin offering , and two lambs of the first year for a sacrifice of peace .
&quot; The priest shall wave these offerings together with the cakes of the first ripe wheat , and wave them before the Lord ; this is the offering of the holy things to the priest to the Lord
On that day you shall proclaim the holy convocation , and no labour shall be done ; it shall be a statute for ever in all your dwellings , for generations to come .
&quot; You shall not harvest your crops in your land , nor cut off the corners of your fields , nor take away the remnant that is left , but leave it to the poor and to the dwellers ; I am the Lord your God .
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; In the first month of July , you shall observe the Sabbath , and blow a trumpet in remembrance , when there is a holy feast
&quot; No hard work can be done , but to offer a burnt offering to the Lord .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; The first tenth of July is the day of redemption , and you shall keep it as a holy feast , and you shall make your hearts bitter , and you shall offer a burnt offering to the Lord
&quot; You shall not do any work on this day , because it is a day of redemption , to make atonement before the Lord your God .
On that day , He who does not grieve will be cut off from the people .
&quot; I will cut him off from among the people , whoever does any work that day
Nothing of yours shall be done ; it shall be a statute for ever in all your dwellings , for generations to come
&quot; You shall keep this day as a holy Sabbath , and suffer yourselves ; and from the ninth night of the first month until the next night you shall keep it as a Sabbath .
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; The fifteenth day of July is the Sabbath of tents , and you shall observe it before the Lord seven days
On the first day there shall be a holy feast . No hard work shall be done
&quot; In seven days you shall offer a burnt offering to the Lord , and on the eighth day you shall offer a burnt offering to the Lord at the holy feast ; it is a solemn feast , and no hard work shall be done .
&quot; This is the feast of the Lord , the feast you shall proclaim for the holy assembly , and you shall offer burnt offerings , and burnt offerings , and sacrifices , and drink offerings , to the Lord on every day .
&quot; This is outside the Sabbath of the Lord , and outside your offerings and your vows and your willing offerings to the Lord
&quot; From the fifteenth day of July you shall keep the seventh day of the feast of the Lord , which is the Sabbath of the first day and the Sabbath of the eighth day .
&quot; In the first day you shall rejoice in the Lord your God with the fruit of the good trees , and with the branches of the palm trees , and with the branches of the bushes , and with the branches of the reeds by the river .
&quot; You shall observe seven days of the Sabbath before the Lord in the month of July every year , for a statute forever for your generations to come .
Ye shall dwell in the tent seven days ; and all the house of Israel shall dwell in the tent
&quot; That your generations may know that I brought Israel out of the land of Egypt and made them dwell in tents ; and I am the Lord your God
Then Moses gave the Passover of the Lord to the children of Israel
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; And command the children of Israel to bring to you the pure olive oil which they have mixed for the lamp , and to make the lamps light continually
And Aaron shall keep the lamp before the LORD from evening till morning , outside the mantle of the ark of the congregation ; and it shall be a statute for ever for your generations .
And he shall keep the lamps of gold before the LORD
&quot; You shall take fine flour and bake it into twelve cakes , two tenths of an ephah of flour for each cake .
And you shall place the cakes in two rows , six rows each , on a table of gold before the Lord ,
And you shall put pure milk on every cake for a memorial , for a burnt offering to the Lord
Every Sabbath shall be before the LORD for ever , an everlasting covenant for Israel .
&quot; This cake shall be for Aaron and his sons , and they shall eat it in the holy place , for a statute for ever : for it is holy in the sacrifice of the fire to the Lord
And there was a son of an Israelite woman whose father was an Egyptian , who roamed among the Israelites one day , and the son of the Israelite woman fought with an Israelite in the camp
And it came to pass , when the son of the woman of Israel had profaned the holy name , and had cursed , that a man sent him to Moses , whose mother &apos;s name was Shelomith , the daughter of Deborah of Dan .
&quot; Then they took him into prison , to receive the word of the Lord
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
Then he brought out the man who had cursed the name of the LORD from the camp , and all that heard laid their hands on his head , and the whole congregation struck him with the head of stone .
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; Whoever curses God will bear his sins
&quot; He who blasphemes the name of the Lord will be put to death , and the whole congregation will stone him , and he who is a resident and a native will be put to death when he blasphemes the name of the Lord .
Whoever strikes a man shall be put to death .
He that smiteth the livestock shall recompense the livestock , and life shall be recompensed for life .
&quot; If a man has a disability in the body of his neighbour , the same shall be done to him in all his ways .
&quot; He who gives injury to injury , He who gives eyes to eyes , He who gives teeth to teeth , He who makes a man &apos;s body handicapped , so shall he do to him
He that smiteth the livestock shall recompense the livestock ; and he that smiteth man shall be put to death .
&quot; Behold , I am the Lord your God , even to the inhabitants of the land , even to the nations .
And Moses spake unto the children of Israel , and they brought the man that cursed the name out of the camp , and slew him with stones ; and the children of Israel did as the LORD commanded Moses .
And the LORD spake unto Moses in mount Sinai
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; When you have come to the land which I have given you , the land shall rest before the Lord
Six years to cultivate the fields , and also to repair the vineyards , and to collect the produce of the land
&quot; In the seventh year the land shall keep a holy sabbath , a sabbath to the Lord ; no field shall be planted , nor vineyards repaired .
&quot; In this year shall the land keep the Sabbath , the crops which have been lost , which cannot be harvested , and the vines which have not been repaired , and the grapes which cannot be harvested .
&quot; The land that comes out of the Sabbath year shall be for food for you and for your servants , and for your maids , and for your workers , and for the foreigners that dwell therein
And the inheritance of this year shall be for your cattle , and for your beasts of the earth , to eat .
If you calculate seven years of rest , it will be seventy-seven years ; and this will be seven years of rest for you , for forty-nine years in all
&quot; On the tenth day of the first month of July you shall make a loud noise ; it will be a day of redemption , and you shall make a loud noise all over the earth .
The fiftieth year shall be a holy year for you , and a proclamation of liberty for all the inhabitants of the earth ; and it shall be the jubilee of you , and every man shall return to his inheritance , and every man to his house .
The fiftieth year shall be your jubilee ; it shall not be sown , nor grown in the land , nor harvested ; neither shall the vines be repaired , nor shall the grapes be harvested .
For this is the Jubilee , and ye shall be holy , and eat of the inheritance of the land .
&quot; In this jubilee , you shall all return to your own land ,
&quot; If you sell something to your neighbor , or buy something from his hand , you shall not lose one another
&quot; You shall buy it to your neighbour in the year after the Jubilee , and he shall sell it to you in the year of its harvest .
If you are old enough , add to it ; and if you are younger , reduce to it ; for he has sold you the number of the harvests
&quot; You shall not lose one another , but fear your God ; for I am the Lord your God
&quot; You shall observe My statutes , and observe My ordinances , and in that land you shall dwell safely .
&quot; The land will come forth , and you will be filled , and you will dwell in it safely .
&quot; What shall we eat in the seventh year , if you say , &apos; We will neither sow nor gather the earth
&quot; In the sixth year I will give you the blessing of my life , and the land will be a three-year inheritance .
&quot; In the eighth year you will sow and you will eat fat , and in the ninth year you will eat fat
&quot; The land shall never be sold , for it belongs to me . You are travellers and dwellers before me
&quot; You shall redeem the whole land that you have gained for yourselves .
&quot; Your brothers , if he becomes poor and sells a portion of the land , his nearest relatives shall come and redeem what they have sold him .
If there is no redemption for him , he will become rich and redeem himself
Then he shall reckon the years of the sale of the land , and the value of the remaining years , and the buyer shall return to his own land .
If he cannot return what he has sold for himself , he will still be in the hands of the buyer until the jubilee . When the jubilee comes , the land will return to the buyer , and he will return to his land .
A man who sells his house in the city shall be redeemed within a year after it has been sold , and he shall have the right to redeem it for an entire year .
&quot; If there is no redemption of the houses in the city for a whole year , it shall be given to the buyer for an everlasting possession for generations to come , and there shall be no buyer at the jubilee .
&quot; But houses in villages without walls shall be redeemed as the land of the countryside ; and at the jubilee they shall give their hands to the buyer .
&quot; But in the cities where the Levites gained possession , their houses shall be redeemed at any time
&quot; If a Levite does not redeem the house that he has sold , and it is in the city that he has gained for his possession , until the jubilee of the year , then he shall give out the hand of the buyer ; for the houses of the cities of the Levites are their possession among the children of Israel .
&quot; Their suburbs will not be sold , for they are their inheritance forever .
&quot; If your brother becomes poor in your midst and is lacking in your hand , you will help him and make him dwell with you as a stranger and a dweller .
&quot; Do not profit him , nor do you ask him much ; but fear your God , and let your brothers dwell with you
&quot; You shall not borrow money from him , nor profit from him ; nor shall you borrow food from him , nor increase it from him
&quot; I am the LORD your God , who brought you out of the land of Egypt to give you the land of Canaan , to be your God
&quot; If your brother becomes poor in your midst and sells himself to you , let him not serve you as a slave
&quot; He will be in you as a worker and as a dwelling place , and will serve you until the Jubilee .
&quot; In the year of jubilee , he and his daughters will leave you , and go out together to their homes , to the land of their fathers ,
&quot; For they are my servants , whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt , and they shall not be sold as slaves .
Thou shalt not judge him severely , save thou fear thy God
&quot; Your servants and your maids shall be bought out of the countries around you
And you shall buy from it all that is born in your land of strangers who dwell among you and their families , and they shall be your inheritance .
&quot; You shall leave them to your sons as your inheritance , and you shall appoint servants from among them for ever , but your brethren Israel , whose authority is not strict .
&quot; When a foreigner or a stranger who lives with you becomes rich , your brothers become poor , and sell themselves to the foreigner or the stranger or the foreigner &apos;s tribe
&quot; After he has sold , he may be redeemed , whether it be his brother or his brother .
or the uncle , or the son of the uncle , or the kinsman of our house , may redeem him ; and he may redeem himself , when he becomes rich
He shall reckon with the buyer from the year of his sale to the jubilee , and the value of the sale shall be according to the number of years , as the price of the labourer &apos;s labour every year .
If there is more than one year missing , the redemption shall be paid from the purchase according to the year .
If there are few years left until the jubilee , the redemption shall be paid to the buyer according to the number of years , and the buyer shall be reckoned
and he shall dwell with the buyer , as a worker hired every year ; and the buyer shall not be severe in his judgment .
&quot; If he is not so redeemed , then when the jubilee is come , let him go out with his daughters
For all Israel are my servants , whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt ; and I am the Lord your God
&quot; You shall not make any idol , or any statue , or any pillar , or any stone on your earth , to worship Him ; for I am the Lord your God
&quot; You shall keep My Sabbaths , My sanctuary ; I am the Lord .
&quot; If you obey My statutes , and keep My commandments ,
And when it raineth on you , I will cause the earth to bear fruit , and the trees of the field to bear fruit .
&quot; When you gather your food , you will gather your grapes , when you will plant them , and when you will be filled , you will dwell safely in your land .
&quot; I will give you peace in your land , and you will lie down , and no one will be afraid . I will cause the evil beasts to perish from your land , and the sword will not pass through your land .
&quot; You will pursue your enemies , and they will fall under your sword .
Five of you will chase after a hundred , and a hundred will chase after a thousand ; and the enemy will fall under your sword .
&quot; I will be with you , and multiply you , and I will establish my covenant with you
&quot; You will eat the old food , and for the new you will take away the old food
&quot; I will set my tent among you , and my heart will not despise you .
I will walk among you , and I will be your God , and you will be my children .
&quot; I am the Lord , your God , who brought you out of the land of Egypt , that you should not be servants to the Egyptians ; and I have broken your yoke , that you may walk upright .
&quot; If you do not obey Me , do not obey My commandments
For they have despised My statutes , they have despised My ordinances , they have not kept all My commandments , they have despised My covenant
&quot; This is what I will do to you ; I will command terror , and the disease of the eyes , and the disease of the spirit , and the disease of the fever , to govern you ; and you will sow white and white , because your enemies will eat what you sow .
&quot; I will turn my face to you , and you will be defeated in the sight of your enemies ; and your hatred will be in your hands ; and no one will pursue you , but you will flee .
&quot; If you do not obey me for these things , I will double your sins sevenfold
I will cut off the pride of your power , and I will cover your heavens like iron , and carry your land like brass .
&quot; You shall labor in vain , for your land does not yield fruit , and the trees on it do not bear fruit .
&quot; If you rebel against me and do not obey me , I will double your sins seven times , and bring disaster upon you .
And I will send among you the beasts of the field , and I will devour your sons and your daughters , and I will devour your cattle , and I will make your people fewer , and the roads shall be desolate .
&quot; If you do not correct me for these things , then you will act against me .
I will act against you seven times , because of your sins .
&quot; And I will bring the sword upon you in recompense for your enmity , and gather you together in the cities , and I will send a plague among you , and I will deliver you into the hands of your enemies .
&quot; I will cut off your staff and your food , and there will be ten women baking cakes for you in a furnace and weighing them by weight , and you will eat , and you will not be satisfied .
&quot; For all these things , if you do not obey me , you will act against me .
I will be angry against you , and I will act against you , and I will punish you seven times for your sins .
And you shall eat the flesh of your sons , and the flesh of your daughters
&quot; I will also destroy your high places , and cut down your statues , and throw your dead bodies on your idols ; and my heart will hate you .
&quot; I will make your cities desolate , and your holy places desolate ; and I will not smell your fragrances .
Therefore I was astonished that I should make the land a wilderness , and that the enemy that dwelled therein should dwell therein .
&quot; I will scatter you among the nations , and I will pursue you with swords ; and your land will be a desolation , and your cities a desolation .
&quot; When you dwell in the land of your enemies , rest in the wilderness of your land , and rest in the land of those who dwell therein .
&quot; If the land is a wilderness , it will rest for a long time ; and such rest will not be possible for you in the Sabbath year on which you dwell .
&quot; As for the remnant of you , I will make them afraid in the land of the enemy , and chase them with the sound of the leaves blown by the wind , and they will flee like men fleeing the sword , and no one will chase them , but they will fall .
No one will be pursued ; they will collide with one another like before the sword ; and you will not stand before the enemy .
You shall perish in the nations , and the land of the enemy shall devour you .
&quot; The remnant of you will be destroyed in the land of the enemy for their iniquity and for the iniquity of their fathers .
&quot; If they confess their sins and the sins of their fathers , they are guilty of my sins , and they confess that they are acting against me
Therefore I acted against them , and brought them into the land of their enemies ; and if they had not been circumcised , if they had been humble , they would have served the punishment of iniquity
I will remember the covenant I made with Jacob , the covenant I made with Isaac , and the covenant I made with Abraham , and the land
&quot; They will leave the land , and they will have rest when it is desolate , and they will serve the punishment of iniquity ; for they have despised My statutes , and in their hearts they have despised My law .
Nevertheless , they are in the land of their enemies , and I will not despise them , neither will I hate them , neither will I destroy them , neither will I forsake my covenant with them , for I am the Lord their God
I will remember for their sakes the covenant I made with their fathers , whose fathers I brought forth out of the land of Egypt before the heathen , to be their God , and I am the Lord .
These are the statutes and the ordinances and the ordinances which the Lord and the children of Israel borrowed from Moses in mount Sinai
And the Lord said unto Moses
And thou shalt say unto the children of Israel , Whatsoever man hath promised , and whatsoever man hath been promised , let him return unto the LORD according to thy estimation .
And the man that thou estimatest , from twenty years old to sixty years old , shall be worth fifty shekels of silver , according to the shekel of the sanctuary .
&quot; If you are a woman , you shall estimate thirty shekels
&quot; If you are five to twenty years old , you shall estimate twenty shekels for a man , and ten shekels for a woman
&quot; If you are five years old from January until the age of five , you shall estimate five shekels for a man , and three shekels for a woman
If a man is over sixty years of age , you shall give him fifteen shekels , and a woman ten shekels
&quot; If a poor man can &apos;t afford the price that you have set him , then bring him before the priest , and the priest will set his price according to the power of the promised man .
&quot; If it is a promised animal , it is the offering of man to the Lord ; and all that is offered to the Lord shall be holy .
A man cannot be changed , nor can he be changed any more , nor can a good one be changed by a bad one , nor can a bad one be changed by a good one . If a man is changed by an animal , then what is promised and what is exchanged shall become holy .
&quot; If the beast is not clean , and it cannot be offered to the Lord for a sacrifice , then you shall place it before the priest
The priest shall estimate the value , and the cattle for good and for evil ; and how shall the priest estimate , and how shall he be
&quot; If he is sure to redeem himself , he shall add one fifth to the value you have estimated
&quot; When a man sanctifies the houses , and gives them to the Lord , the priest will judge between good and evil ; and how will the priest judge between good and evil ?
&quot; If the man who sanctifies the house redeems the house , then it shall still be to him , besides the value which you have estimated , plus one fifth .
&quot; If a man shall give to the Lord the portion of the land which he shall possess , which is holy , how much of it shall he sow according to its value ? If he sows one hundred shekels of wheat , how much shall he sow according to its value ?
&quot; If he sanctifies himself from the year of jubilee , he shall be judged according to your estimate
If he sanctifies himself after the Jubilee , the priest shall reckon the value according to the number of years remaining until the Jubilee , and shall deduct it from your estimate .
&quot; If a man who has consecrated the land is determined to redeem it , he shall give it to him in addition to one fifth of the value you have estimated .
&quot; If he does not redeem the land , or sell it to another , he will not redeem it
&quot; But in the year of jubilee , when the land shall come out of the hands of the buyer , it shall be to the Lord as a holy and ever-offering land , and to the priest as a possession
&quot; If he buys a piece of land which he has not taken for a possession , it shall be holy to the Lord
And the priest shall give him the estimate of thy estimate unto the jubilee , and he shall give it unto the LORD for holy in the price of thy estimate
&quot; In the year of jubilee , the land shall be sold to the Lord , the original Lord , who bears the inheritance .
&quot; You shall give all that you have estimated at the price of the sanctuary : twenty shekels for a shekel .
&quot; None but the firstborn of the beast , be it a cow or a sheep , shall be holy to the Lord ; for it is the Lord &apos;s
&quot; If the beast is unclean , it shall be sold according to your estimation , plus one fifth ; if it is not , it shall be sold according to your estimation .
But all that is ever given to the Lord is ever given by man from all that he has given to the Lord , whether man or beast , the land which he has taken for a possession , it shall not be sold or redeemed ; and all that is ever given to the Lord is holy
&quot; Whoever is destroyed from among men shall not be redeemed , but shall be put to death .
&quot; Everything that is on the earth , whether it is a seed or a fruit in a tree , one tenth is the Lord &apos;s , and it is holy to the Lord
&quot; If a man redeems one tenth of it , he shall add one fifth to it .
&quot; Every tenth of every flock of oxen and sheep that passes under the rod shall be holy to the Lord .
There is no question whether it is good or bad , nor can it be changed any more ; and if it is to be changed any more , then all that is changed shall be holy and not be redeemed .
This is the commandment which the LORD commanded Moses for the children of Israel in mount Sinai
And it came to pass in the second year , on the first day of February , after the children of Israel had come out of the land of Egypt , that the LORD spake unto Moses in the tabernacle of the congregation in the wilderness of Sinai
And thou shalt number all the males according to the number of the houses , and the families , and the names of all the congregation of Israel :
&quot; You and Aaron shall count the number of the children of Israel , from twenty years old and upward , according to the number of their armies
&quot; In every tribe there shall be a chief of your tribe to help you
And their name was Reuben : Elizur the son of Shedeur .
and Shiloh , the son of Suli-saddai , of the sons of Simeon ,
Of Judah , Nashon the son of Amminadab .
Of Issachar , Nethaniah the son of Zoab .
And of the tribe of the children of Zebulun , Eliab the son of Hilan .
The sons of Joseph were of Ephraim : Elishama the son of Amoz ; Gamaliel the son of Azzur , of Manasseh .
Of Benjamin : Abiathar the son of Gideoni .
And of Dan was Ahiezer the son of Amishaddai
And of the tribe of Assyria , Palin the son of Oran .
of Gad , Eleazar the son of Doer ;
And of Naphtali , Ahira the son of the south ,
These are the chiefs of their tribes , appointed by the congregation , and the commanders of the army of Israel .
Then Moses brought with him these men by their names :
And when they had gathered all the congregation on the first day of February , they told their genealogy by their households , by their families , by the number of names , from twenty years old and upward
As the Lord commanded Moses , so he numbered them in the wilderness of Sinai
The sons of Israel , the sons of Reuben , according to their families , according to their fathers &apos; houses , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , were forty-six thousand five hundred males , who could go out to war .
See Up
Of the sons of Simeon , according to their families , according to their fathers &apos; houses , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were numbered to go out to war were fifty-nine thousand and three hundred .
See Up
Of the sons of Gad , according to their families , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war were forty-five thousand six hundred fifty .
See Up
Of the children of Judah , according to their families , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war were seventy-four thousand six hundred .
See Up
Of the sons of Issachar , according to their families , according to their families , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war , were fifty-four thousand and four hundred .
See Up
Of the sons of Zebulun , according to their families , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , all that were able to go out to war , from twenty years old and upward , were fifty-seven thousand and four hundred .
See Up
Of the sons of Joseph , the sons of Ephraim , according to their families , according to their fathers &apos; houses , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war were forty-five thousand five hundred .
See Up
Of the sons of Manasseh , according to their families , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war were thirty-two thousand and two hundred .
See Up
Of the sons of Benjamin , according to their families , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war were thirty-five thousand and four hundred .
See Up
And the children of Israel , according to their families , according to their fathers &apos; houses , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war , were sixty-two thousand and seven hundred .
See Up
Of the sons of Assyria , according to their families , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war were forty-one thousand and five hundred .
See Up
Of the sons of Naphtali , according to their families , according to their families , according to the number of the names of the people , from twenty years old and upward , all that were able to go out to war , were fifty-three thousand and four hundred .
See Up
These are they that were numbered , which were numbered by Moses and by the twelve princes of Israel , who were representatives of the tribes .
And all that were numbered of the children of Israel , according to their families , from twenty years old and upward , that could go out to war , were six hundred twenty-three thousand five hundred fifty .
See Up
The Levites , however , did not have a number of tribes among them
For the Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
Neither can you count the number of the sons of Israel , nor count their number among the sons of Israel
As long as the Levites are in charge of the tabernacle of the law , and of the vessels thereof , and belong to the tabernacle , they shall carry the tabernacle , and the vessels thereof , and handle the affairs thereof .
When the tabernacle shall be removed , and when it shall be laid up , and when it shall be raised up , the Levites shall be removed ; and the strangers that came near shall be put to death .
&quot; The children of Israel shall set up tents , according to the number of their armies , in their camps and in their barracks
But the Levites shall camp around the tabernacle of the LORD , that the wrath may not come upon the congregation of Israel ; and the Levites shall guard the tabernacle of the LORD
Thus did the children of Israel ; and they did all that the Lord commanded Moses
And the LORD spake unto Moses , saying ,
&quot; The children of Israel shall camp under their tents , under the banner of their fathers &apos; houses , around the tabernacle of the congregation .
And on the east side was the camp of the camp of Judah , which was toward the sunrise : and Nashon the son of Amminadab was captain of the Jews .
The number of his army was seventy-four thousand six hundred
And beside him was the tribe of Issachar : and Nathaniel the son of Zoab was chief over the Issacharites .
His army was numbered , a total of 54,400
And of the tribe of the children of Zebulun , Eliab the son of Hilan , captain of the children of Zebulun .
His army was numbered , a total of 57,400
All the camps of Judah , according to the number of their armies , were an hundred and eighty-six thousand and four hundred ; and the first company went forward .
And on the south side was the camp of the Reubenites , according to their armies : and Elishar the son of Shedeur was captain of the Reubenites .
His army numbered forty-six thousand five hundred
