&quot; On the eighth day he shall bring two turtledoves or two young pigeons to the door of the Tent of Meeting and give them to the priest
&quot; The priest shall offer one for a sin offering , one for a burnt offering , to redeem him for the sins of the dead body , and to sanctify his head that day
&quot; He will choose the days of his separation from the secular world to the Lord , and he will take a lamb of the first year for a ransom offering ; but the days of his separation will come to nothing , for he has been defiled in the midst of the secular world .
&quot; This is the ordinance of the day when the ears of the deaf shall be full of the wicked , and they shall bring him to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation
