The weight of a table was one hundred thirty shekels , and the weight of a bowl seventy shekels , and the silver of all the vessels , according to the shekel of the sanctuary , twenty and four hundred shekels .
And the twelve spoons of gold were full of frankincense , ten shekels for each spoon , according to the measure of the sanctuary ; and all the gold was one hundred twenty shekels .
and for a burnt offering twelve bulls , twelve rams , twelve lambs of the first year , and twelve male goats for a sin offering with their meat offerings
&quot; For the sacrifice of peace were twenty-four bulls , sixty sheep , sixty goats , and sixty lambs of the first year : these were the offerings after the anointing of the altar for the service of the altar .
&quot; When Moses entered the Tent of Meeting to speak to the Lord , he heard a voice speaking to him above the altar of the Law , in the midst of the two curtains , that the Lord was speaking to him
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
And thou saidst unto Aaron , At the time of the light , seven lamps shall shine before the lampstand
And Aaron did so ; and he lit the lamp that was on the lampstand , and the lamp went forward , according to the commandment of the Lord to Moses
&quot; The work of the lampstand was hammered out of gold , and the seat and the flower were hammered out ; and Moses made the lampstand according to the pattern of the Lord .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You have chosen the Levites from among the children of Israel , and you have cleansed them
and purify them according to this manner , and sprinkle them with the waters of iniquity ; and they shall shave their whole body with a razor , and wash their clothes , and purify themselves .
Then you shall take a calf , and the meat offering with it shall be fine flour mingled with oil ; and you shall take another calf for a sin offering .
And he brought the Levites before the tabernacle of the congregation , and gathered all the congregation of Israel together
&quot; The children of Israel shall lay their hands on their heads , and they shall bring the Levites before the Lord
And Aaron presented them before the LORD as an offering for the children of Israel , that they might do the work of the LORD
&quot; The Levites shall lay their hands on the heads of the two oxen , and you shall offer one for a sin offering , and one for a burnt offering , to the Lord , to make atonement for the Levites
&quot; You shall also make the Levites stand before Aaron and his sons , and offer them as an offering to the Lord
&quot; So you will separate the Levites from among the children of Israel , and the Levites will return to Me
&quot; Then the Levites shall enter into the service of the tabernacle of the congregation , and you shall purify them , and offer them as an offering .
&quot; For they have been given to me from all the children of Israel , and I have chosen them for me , to replace all the firstborn of Israel
&quot; All the firstborn among the children of Israel , men and beasts , are mine ; they shall be sanctified unto me on the day that I slew them in the land of Egypt
&quot; I have chosen the Levites to replace all the firstborn of Israel
&quot; I have rewarded the Levites among the children of Israel for the work of Aaron and his sons in the synagogue , for the work of the children of Israel , and for the sins of the children of Israel , lest all the plagues of the holy things come near to them
Thus did Moses , Aaron , and all the congregation of Israel to the Levites ; and the children of Israel did to them according to all that the Lord commanded Moses by the Levites
Then the Levites cleansed themselves , and washed their clothes , except for sin ; and Aaron offered them as a wave offering before the LORD , and cleansed them for their sins
Then the Levites went in , and did their business before Aaron and his sons in the synagogue , as the LORD commanded Moses , and as the children of Israel did to them
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
That is the way of the Levites : from twenty-five years old and upward they shall come to minister and do the business of the tabernacle of the congregation
When you are fifty years old , you have to stop working and quit your job
&quot; You shall no longer do anything in the tabernacle of the congregation , except that you serve with your brothers and keep what you have been commanded . Thus you shall do to the Levites what they have been commanded
And it came to pass in the second year , in the first month , after the children of Israel were come out of the land of Egypt , that the LORD commanded Moses in the wilderness of Sinai , saying ,
&quot; The Israelites shall observe the Passover on the appointed day
&quot; On the fourteenth day of this month , at the evening , you shall observe the Sabbath on the appointed day , and observe it in accordance with the law of the Sabbath .
And Moses commanded the children of Israel to keep the Passover
And they kept the Passover in the wilderness of Sinai at the even of the fourteenth day of the month : and all Israel did according to all that the Lord commanded Moses
And there were a few that could not keep the Passover that day , because they were unclean from the dead : and they came to Moses that day
&quot; Why were we not prevented from offering the Lord &apos;s offerings to the Israelites on the appointed day , even though we were not clean because of the dead ?
Moses said to them , &quot; Wait , I can go and hear what the Lord has commanded you
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , and say to them , &apos; If anyone among you and your descendants is unclean from the dead , or walks far off , let him keep the Passover to the Lord
&quot; They shall observe the Passover on the fourteenth day of February at twilight , and they shall eat it with unleavened bread and bitterness , and with the Passover lambs
Neither shall a bone of a lamb be broken until the morning ; but they shall keep all the statutes of the Passover .
&quot; Whoever is clean and does not walk , and refuses to observe the Passover , he shall be cut off from among the people , because he has not offered the offering of the Lord on the appointed day , he shall bear his sin .
&quot; If a foreigner who lives among you wishes to observe the Passover to the Lord , he shall do it according to the ordinance of the Passover , whether he be a resident or a native .
On the day when the tent is set up , there will be clouds covering the tent , the tent of the tabernacle of the law , from evening to morning , and the clouds on it will be like fire .
It is often like this : the clouds cover the tents , and the shape of the night is like fire
When the clouds came up from the tent , and when the children of Israel went forth , where the clouds stood , and where the children of Israel encamped
&quot; The children of Israel did as the Lord commanded them , and camped as the Lord commanded them ; and when the clouds stopped on the tent of meeting , they camped
&quot; The clouds stayed in the tent for many days , and the children of Israel did not do as the Lord had commanded them .
And it came to pass , when the cloud was over the tabernacle for a few days , that they encamped as the Lord commanded them , and they did as the Lord commanded them
From the evening to the morning , the clouds were on the tent ; and when the clouds came up in the morning , they departed ; and when the clouds stood on the tent day and night , they departed when they came up .
&quot; The clouds stayed on the tent for two days , a month , or a year ; and the Israelites did not camp , but the clouds came up and they departed .
And they camped according to the commandment of the Lord , and did according to the commandment of the Lord : and they kept the commandment of the Lord according to the commandment of the Lord of Moses
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You shall make two branches of silver , which you shall hammer out , to gather the congregation together , and to cause the camps to rise up
&quot; When the trumpet is blown , the whole congregation will come to you at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation .
&quot; If a single branch is blown , the heads of the hosts of the army of Israel will be gathered to you
In the time of a loud blast , the camps of the east side shall rise up .
In the second blast , the camps of the south shall rise up , and they shall rise up , and they shall rise up , and they shall rise up .
&quot; But when you gather the assembly , you shout , but not loudly .
&quot; The sons of Aaron , who are priests , shall blow this , and it shall be a statute for ever for your generations .
&quot; You shall fight in your own land against your enemies who oppress you , and you shall be remembered in the sight of the Lord your God , and you shall be saved from your enemies by a loud cry .
And in the days of your joy , and in the seasons , and in the months , and in the feasts of burnt offerings , and in the feasts of peace , ye shall make a proclamation before your God : I am the LORD your God .
On the twentyth day of February the second year , clouds came up from the ark of the law
And the children of Israel went forward , and departed from the wilderness of Sinai ; and the clouds stopped in the wilderness of Balaam
&quot; This is the first of the things that they did , as the Lord commanded Moses
And the first to go forward by the army was Nahshon the son of Amminadab , the captain of the army of the camp of Judah ,
And over the army of the tribe of Issachar was Nathaniel the son of Zoab .
And the captain of the army of the tribe of the children of Zerubbabel was Eliab the son of Hilan .
And they removed the tent , and the sons of Gershon , and the sons of Merari , lifted up the tent , and went forward .
And by the way of the army was Elishar the son of Shedeur , the captain of the army , of the camp of the stream .
Shiloh the son of Sulisaddai , who commanded the army of the tribe of Simeon ,
And the captain of the army of the tribe of Gad was Eleazar the son of Tyre .
And the Chaldeans went forward with the holy things ; and those who had not brought up the ark before , they had set it up .
And by the way of the host was Elishama the son of Amoz , the captain of the host , the son of the camp of Ephraim .
And the captain of the army of the tribe of Manasseh was Gamaliel the son of Beazzur .
And over the army of the tribe of Benjamin was Abiathar the son of Gideoni .
And at the end of the camp was the son of Dan , and the son of Ahiezer , the son of Amishaddai , the captain of the army , going forward by the army .
And the captain of the army of the tribe of Assyria was Pagan the son of Oran .
And over the army of the tribe of Naphtali was Ahira the son of the south .
And the children of Israel went forth with their armies , as it were
Moses said to Joab the son of Reuer the Midianite , his father-in-law , saying , &quot; We will go to the land which the Lord has promised ; for he said , &apos; I will give it to you , and I ask you to come with me , and we will be kind to you ; for the Lord has promised good to Israel
He answered , &quot; I will not go ; I will return to my native people
Moses said , &quot; Please do not leave us , for you know that we will camp in the wilderness , and you can be our eyes
&quot; If you go with us , and the Lord will do good to us in the future , and we will do good to you
And the children of Israel departed from the mountain of the LORD for three days , and the ark of the LORD went forth before them for three days , to seek the place of Asherah for them
&quot; The clouds of the Lord are above them in the day when they go forth from their camps
And it came to pass , as the ark was going forward , that Moses said , &quot; Lord , rise up , and let your enemies scatter , and let those who hate you flee from before you .
And it came to pass , when the ark was shut , that he said , &quot; Lord , return to the ten million of Israel
Then the people complained , and their evil words came to the Lord &apos;s ear ; and when the Lord heard it , he was angry , and he burned the fire among them , and it burned straight to the border of the camp .
The people cried to Moses , and Moses prayed to the Lord , and the fire was extinguished
And the place was called Beer-sheba , because the fire of the Lord burned among them
Then cried the children of Israel again , and said , Who shall eat our flesh
We remember that in Egypt we ate fish without spending money , and we remember that there were cucumbers , sesame seeds , almonds , vinegar , garlic
Now our heart and blood are exhausted , and there is nothing but this before our eyes
As a coriander , and as a pearl
&quot; When the people walk around , who will take it , or grind it , or grind it , and boil it in a pot , and make cakes , the taste of which is like new oil
It rains in the camp at night , and everywhere it rains
And Moses heard the voice of the people crying at the doors of the tents of their houses : and the wrath of the LORD was kindled , and Moses was not pleased
Moses said to the Lord , &quot; Why do you suffer as a servant , and why do I not have mercy in your sight , and add to me this burden of the people ? &quot;
&quot; Are these people the wombs of my wombs , or am I born ? &quot; &quot; You said to me , &apos; Take them into your wombs , like the breasts of a father , and go straight to the land you swore to their fathers . &apos; &quot;
Then they cried out to me , saying , &quot; Give us our meat
The responsibilities of managing this people are too heavy , and I cannot bear them alone
&quot; If you do this to me , if I have mercy in your sight , kill me when you stand up , and do not let me see my own suffering
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; You have gathered seventy elders from among the elders of Israel , the elders and princes of the people whom you know to be , to come to me , and bring them to the Tent of Meeting , and make them stand with you
&quot; I will come and speak to you there , and I will give them the Spirit that is upon you , and they will be with you in the charge of the people , and you will not be responsible for them alone .
&quot; And say to the people , &apos; You shall be clean , and prepare yourselves to eat meat tomorrow , because you cried out , &apos; Who will eat my meat ? We are good in Egypt ; &apos; and the voice came into the ears of the Lord , and he will eat your meat
You eat not more than one day , two days , five days , ten days , twenty days
&quot; Eat for a whole month , and the flesh will come out of your nostrils , and you will be ashamed , because you will be ashamed of the Lord who lives among you , and you will cry before Him , saying , &apos; Why have we come out of Egypt ? &apos;
Moses said to the Lord , &quot; These are six million men who walk with me , and you said , &apos; I will give them meat , that they may eat for a whole month
&quot; Have they slain their flocks and their herds , or gathered together all the fish of the sea , and eat them ?
And the LORD said unto Moses , Is not the arm of the LORD shortened ? see now what I say unto thee , and see it not .
And Moses went out , and told the people the word of the LORD , and gathered together seventy of the elders of the people , and stood around the tabernacle of the congregation
And the Lord came down into the cloud , and spoke to Moses , and gave him the Spirit of healing and of healing upon him to the seventy elders ; and when the Spirit was resting on them , they were moved to speak , and there was no more to say .
But there were still two men in the camp , one named Elijah , and one named Midian ; and they were among those who were recorded , but they did not go into the Tent of Meeting ; and the Spirit was upon them , and they prophesied in the camp
Then a young man ran and told Moses , saying , &quot; Iida and Mida spoke a prophecy in the camp
And Joshua the son of Nun , Moses &apos; helper , one of his chosen men , said , My Lord Moses , forbid them
Moses said to him , &quot; Are you jealous for my sake ? Let the people of the Lord speak , and let the Lord bring down His Spirit upon them
So Moses and the elders of Israel returned to the camp
And the wind came from the Lord , and struck the quails from the sea , and they flew round about the camp , and round about the camp , about a day &apos;s journey on this side , and about a day &apos;s journey on that side , and about two cubits off the ground .
And the people arose , day and night , and the next day and the whole day , and took quails , and at least ten heifers , and set themselves round about the camp .
The Lord &apos;s anger was kindled against them , and he struck them with the most severe punishment , while the flesh was still among their teeth .
And the place was called Kibor Hathwa , because in it they buried the lustful .
And the people went up from Gibeon , and dwelt in Hazareth
And Moses took a woman of old age as his wife ; and they blasphemed him because of the woman of old age whom he had taken
He said , &quot; Isn &apos;t the Lord speaking to Moses alone , and not to us ? The Lord has heard it
For Moses excelled all the people of the world in humility
Then the Lord said to Moses , to Aaron , and to Miles in secret , &quot; Three of you have come out to the Tent of Meeting , and they have come out
And the Lord came down in the clouds , and stood at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation , and called Aaron and Miriam , and they came out
&quot; Listen to me , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; if there is a prophet among you , My Lord will appear to him in visions and speak to him in dreams
&quot; This is not my servant Moses , who is faithful in all my house
&quot; I will speak to him face to face with a clear word , without riddles , and he will see my image . Why do you not fear to blaspheme my servant Moses ?
Then the Lord went out to them in anger
Then the clouds moved away from the tent of meeting , and , behold , Milly grew dark and mad .
And when Aaron saw that Milly was grown dark and mad , he said to Moses , &quot; Lord , do not add this sin to us for our foolishness ,
&quot; Do not make him like the dead child that comes out of the womb , whose flesh is half rotten
And Moses cried unto the LORD , saying , God , cure him
And the LORD said unto Moses , If his father spit on his face , shall he not be ashamed seven days , when he is to be shut up outside the camp seven days , and then he shall be brought in
Then he was locked up outside the camp seven days , and the people had no way , until they had brought him in .
And the people of Edom departed from Hazareth , and encamped in the wilderness of Balaam
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You shall send men to spy on the land of Canaan , which I have given to the children of Israel ; and you shall send one man to be captain of every tribe of them .
Moses sent them out of the wilderness of Balaam , as the Lord commanded them , and they were the chief of the children of Israel
And their names were , of the tribe of Reuben , Shemaiah the son of Zechariah .
of the tribe of Simeon , Shaphah the son of Holi ;
Of the tribe of Judah , Caleb the son of Jephunneh
Of the tribe of Issachar , Icah the son of Josiah .
Of the tribe of Ephraim , Hoshea the son of Nun .
And of the tribe of Benjamin , Patti the son of Lapho ,
And of the tribe of the children of Zebulun ; Cappad the son of Zode .
And of the sons of Joseph , of the tribe of Manasseh , Gad the son of Suzieh ,
And of the tribe of Dan , Ammiel the son of Kimari .
And of the tribe of Asheah , Zechariah the son of Micah .
Of the tribe of Naphtali , Nabi the son of Zabdith .
Of the tribe of Gad , Shuli the son of Machi .
And Moses called Hoshea the son of Nun Jehoshaphat , the name of the men that spyed on the land .
Moses sent them to spy out the land of Canaan , saying , &quot; Go up from the land of Canaan to the mountains
Behold , the people of that land are strong and weak , and few and many .
The land where they dwell is good and evil , and the camp where they dwell is strong .
Behold , the land is fertile and barren , and there are no trees in it . Be courageous , and bring forth the fruit thereof ; for it is the time of the first ripening of the grapes .
And they went up and searched the land , from the wilderness of the search unto Lyab , and straight unto the mouth of Ham .
And they went up from the south , and came to Hebron ; and there were in Hebron the Assyrians , and the Ahimnites , and the Shinites , and the Tarmites ; and the city of Hebron was built seven years before the city of Lockan in Egypt .
And they came to the valleys of Ephraim , and cut down from there a branch of a vine , and a vine hanging on its head ; and two men lifted up bars , and brought with them pomegranates and unfruitful things
&quot; For the vineyards from which the Israelites cut down , the place is called Ephraim
After forty days , they searched the land and came back
And he came to Gad in the wilderness of Baal , and saw Moses , and Aaron , and all the congregation of Israel ; and he returned Moses , and Aaron , and all the congregation , and showed them the fruit of the land
And he said unto Moses , We have come to the land which thou hast sent unto us , and it is indeed a land of milk and honey , and it is the fruit thereof
&quot; But the inhabitants of the land are strong , and the cities are strong and broad , and we have seen in them the sons of Anak
And the Amalekites dwelt in the south , and the Hittites , and the Jebusites , and the Amorites , and in the mountains , and the Canaanites by the sea , and by the Jordan
Then Gaal comforted the people before Moses , saying , &quot; Let us go up to that place immediately , and we will be victorious
But those who went with him said , &quot; We cannot go up and attack the people , for they are stronger than we are
And there was a man among the spies , who spoke of the land which they had sought , and testified against the children of Israel , saying , &quot; The land which we have sought is the land which swallows up the inhabitants , and the people which we have seen therein are many and great .
&quot; Behold , there we see the Assyrians , and they are great , and they are the descendants of great , and we see ourselves as grasshoppers , and we are as grasshoppers in their eyes .
The whole congregation cried out , and the people cried out that night .
And all the congregation complained unto Moses , saying unto them , Shall we die in the land of Egypt , or in the wilderness ?
&quot; Why has the Lord brought us into the land , and put us under the sword ? Our wives and our children will be taken away ; will it not be good for us to return to Egypt ?
Then they said to one another , &quot; Let us go back to Egypt , rather than appoint a leader
And Moses bowed himself before all the congregation of Israel
And among the men that peered into the land , Joshua the son of Nun , and Caleb the son of Jephunneh , tore their clothes
And he said unto all the congregation of Israel , The land which we have peered through is a beautiful land
&quot; If the Lord pleases us , He will bring us into the land , and give it to us , a land of milk and honey
&quot; But you shall not betray the Lord , nor fear the inhabitants of the land ; for they are our food , and their shadow has departed from them ; and the Lord is with us , and you shall not fear them .
And all the congregation said , Take a stone and slay the two of them ; and the glory of the LORD appeared unto all Israel in the tabernacle of the congregation
And the Lord said to Moses , &quot; How long will this people despise me , and how long will they not believe that I have done all these signs among them
&quot; I will smite them with a plague , and they will not be able to bear the land ; and I will make your descendants great , and will prevail over them .
Moses said to the Lord , &quot; The Egyptians will hear this , because you have done great things to bring this people up from among them
&quot; The Egyptians will tell the inhabitants of the land of Canaan that they have heard that your Lord is among them ; for you are seen in front of them , and your clouds are above them , and you walk before them in the clouds day and night , and in the fire .
&quot; Now if you kill this people , as you kill a man , the nations that hear your name will speak
&quot; The LORD slew them in the wilderness because he could not bring them into the land which he swore to them
Now in the great power of the Lord , as you have said ,
&quot; The Lord is not easily angry , and has abundant mercy , and forgives iniquity and transgression ; and he will not make the guilty innocent , but will pursue his sins from his father and from his son for three or four generations .
Forgive the iniquity of this people , according to your great mercy , as you have always forgiven them from Egypt to this day
&quot; I have forgiven them according to your word , &quot; said the Lord
&quot; But I swear by my eternal life that My glory shall be filled in all the earth
&quot; They have seen my glory , and the signs that I have done in Egypt and the wilderness , but have not listened to me these ten times
They refuse to see the land which I swore to their fathers ; and none who despises me will see it .
&quot; I will bring him into the land where he has gone , and his descendants will inherit it , because of my servant Caleb , who has another heart and follows me .
&quot; The Amalekites and the Canaanites dwell in the valley ; and tomorrow you shall turn from the way of the Red Sea into the wilderness
And the LORD said unto Moses ,
&quot; The wicked multitude has complained to me , and I have heard all the complaints of the children of Israel against me
&quot; You have told them , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; I have sworn by my eternal life that I will be with you according to what you have spoken to me .
&quot; Your bodies will be laid down in the wilderness , and every one of you who has been counted among you who has complained to me from the age of twenty ,
&quot; You shall not enter into the land which I have sworn to you to inhabit , except Caleb the son of Jephunneh and Joshua the son of Nun .
&quot; But your daughters and your daughters , whom you said were to be taken captive , I will bring them in , and they will know the land which you have despised .
&quot; As for you , your bodies will fall in the wilderness
&quot; Your children will float forty years in the wilderness , bearing the sins of your prostitution , until your dead bodies are consumed in the wilderness .
&quot; You shall know that I have strayed from you for forty years of your iniquity , according to the forty days of your spying on the land , from year to year .
&quot; This is what I , the Lord , have said , &apos; I will do to all these evil assemblies that gather against me , and they will be destroyed in the wilderness , and they will die there .
Then Moses returned , and told the people who had spyed on the land the evil of the land , and the whole congregation complained to Moses
&quot; All those who reject the faith will die before the Lord in the plague
Only Joshua the son of Nun and Caleb the son of Jephunneh remained alive
Moses told all Israel these words , and they were grieved
And he rose up early in the morning , and went up to the top of the mountain , and said , &quot; Here we are , for we have sinned , and will go to the place which the Lord has promised us .
Moses said , &quot; Why do you disobey the commandment of the Lord ? It will not go well
&quot; Do not go up , for the Lord is not among you , lest you be defeated by your enemies
&quot; Behold , the Amalekites and the Canaanites are before you , and you will fall under the sword , because you have turned away from following the Lord , and he will not be with you
But they ventured to the top of the mountain , but the ark of the Lord and Moses did not go out
Then came down the Amalekites , and the Canaanites that dwelt on that mountain , and struck them , and slew them , and returned to Hormah
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; You have come to the land which I have given you to dwell in
&quot; If any of the bulls or of the flock is willing to offer a burnt offering to the Lord as a burnt offering , a peace offering , for a vow of redemption , or as a sweet offering , or as an offering at your feasts , then you shall offer it to the Lord as a sweet savour
&quot; Then he who offers shall offer to the Lord one tenth of an ephah of fine flour , and one quarter of a hin of oil , mixed with spices ,
&quot; Whether it be a burnt offering or a sacrifice of peace , you shall prepare for each lamb a fourth of a hin of the wine of the drink offering
&quot; You shall prepare for the ram two tenths of an ephah of fine flour , and one third of a hin of oil , and mix it for a supper
And one third of a hin of wine as a drink offering for a sweet aroma to the Lord
&quot; You shall prepare the bulls for a burnt offering , or for a sacrifice of peace offerings , for a vow of redemption , or for a sacrifice of peace offerings , to the Lord
&quot; You shall offer three tenths of an ephah of fine flour , and half a hin of oil , mixed with spices , and for a preliminary offering , with the bulls
and half a hin of wine for a drink offering , and a burnt offering to the Lord of sweet aromas
&quot; This shall be the case for the bulls , the rams , the lambs , and the goats , each of them
&quot; This shall be done according to the number which you have prepared , according to the number of the people .
&quot; This is how it shall be done to all the inhabitants of the land , when they offer a sweet fire offering to the Lord
&quot; If a stranger lives with you , or there are generations who live among you , and wish to offer a sweet fire offering to the Lord , how shall you deal with it ?
&quot; As for the congregation , you and the strangers with whom you dwell shall be set before the Lord as a statute for ever , for generations to come , and for those who dwell therein .
When there is a law , and a statute , for you , and for the stranger that dwells with you ,
And the Lord said unto Moses
&quot; Speak to the children of Israel , saying , &apos; You have come to the place where I have brought you in
&quot; Eat the food of the land , and offer an offering to the Lord
&quot; You shall offer the first ripe wheat for a cake , and you shall raise it up like the raising of a field of wheat .
&quot; For your generations to come you shall grind your faces with the first ripe wheat for an offering to the Lord .
&quot; When you are in error , you do not keep all the commandments which the Lord has spoken to Moses
&quot; This is all that the Lord has commanded you through Moses from that day until your generations .
And if there be any mischief , which the congregation does not know , then the whole congregation shall burn a bull for a burnt offering , and offer the meal offering and the drink offering together as a sweet savour unto the LORD according to the ordinance , and a ram for a sin offering
&quot; The priest shall make atonement for all the congregation of Israel , and they shall be forgiven for their sins ; and they shall offer their offerings , the burnt offerings and the sin offerings , before the Lord , for their own sins
&quot; The whole congregation of Israel , and all the strangers who dwell among them , will be forgiven , for this is a sin which the people have committed
&quot; If a man sins in error , he shall offer a ram of one year &apos;s age for a sin offering
&quot; The priest shall make atonement for the transgressor in the sight of the Lord in the time of his sin , and he shall be forgiven
&quot; When the inhabitants of Israel and the foreigners who dwell among them commit any misdeeds , there shall be a statute like it .
&quot; But he who is bold in his deeds will be cut off from among the people , whether he be a native or a stranger , for he has profaned the Lord
For he hath despised the word of the LORD , and hath rebelled against the commandment of the LORD ; he shall be cut off , and his iniquity shall be upon him .
When the children of Israel were in the wilderness , they found a man picking wood on the Sabbath day
And when he found the man who took the wood , he brought him to Moses , and to Aaron , and to all the congregation ,
&quot; He will be put in prison , for it has not been revealed to him how he will do it .
And the LORD commanded Moses , saying , The man shall surely be put to death ; and all the congregation shall stone him outside the camp
Then the whole congregation brought him out of the camp , and struck him with the head of stone , as the Lord commanded Moses
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You have commanded the children of Israel , that for their generations they should make a ribbon on the side of their garments , and a blue band on the bottom of the ribbon ,
&quot; Behold , you are wearing this yoke , so that you may see , and remember to keep all the commandments of the Lord , and not to follow your own hearts , nor your own eyes , nor to commit adultery , as you do .
Remember to keep all my commandments , to be holy , and to belong to your God
I am the LORD your God , who brought you forth out of the land of Egypt to be your God ; I am the LORD your God
the sons of Levi , the sons of Kohath , Korah the son of Issachar , and the sons of Reuben , the son of Eliab , and Abiram , the son of Beer-sheba ,
And the two hundred and fifty captains of the congregation of Israel , the men that were well known to be of the congregation , rose up together before Moses
Then they gathered themselves together to attack Moses and Aaron , and said , &quot; Why do you exalt yourself above the congregation of the Lord , when you have authority and the whole congregation is holy , and the Lord is among them ?
When Moses heard this , he bowed himself to the ground
And he said unto him and to his party , It shall come to pass in the morning , that the Lord will tell him who belongeth to Him , and who is holy , and will bring him near , and whosoever He hath chosen will bring him near
&quot; This is what you shall do ; you and your party shall bring a fireplace
&quot; Tomorrow put the fire in the oven before the Lord , and put the incense on it . Whoever the Lord chooses will be holy , and your sons of Levi are in authority .
And Moses said unto Korah , Sons of Levi , hearken unto me
&quot; The God of Israel has separated you from the congregation of Israel , and has brought you near to him to do the work of the tabernacle of the Lord , and has stood before the congregation to minister to them
&quot; Is it a small thing that the Lord has made you and all your brothers , the sons of Levi , come near to Him , and you ask for the priest &apos;s office ?
&quot; What is it that you and your party gather together to attack the Lord , Aaron ? Why do you complain to him ?
And Moses sent messengers to Abiram , the son of Eliab , to whom David said , We will not go up
&quot; Have you brought us up out of the land of milk and honey , and slaughtered us in the wilderness ? Is it a small thing , and have you become king over us ?
And thou hast not brought us into the land of milk and honey , nor hast thou given us the fields and the vineyards for an occupation : wilt thou then cut off the eyes of these men , and we shall not go up ?
Then Moses was very angry , and said to the Lord , &quot; Please do not enjoy their offerings , for I have not taken a donkey from them , nor harmed one of them
Moses said to Coran , &quot; Tomorrow you and all your company and Aaron will stand before the Lord
&quot; You shall take one fireplace , two hundred and fifty , and put incense on it before the Lord ; and you and Aaron shall take your own fireplace
And they took a fire , and set it on fire , and anointed it , and stood before the door of the Tent of Meeting with Moses and Aaron
Then Korah gathered all the congregation together to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation to attack Moses ; and the glory of the Lord Aaron appeared to all the congregation
And the LORD spake unto Moses , saying ,
&quot; If you leave this congregation , I will destroy them in the midst of my eyes
Then Moses and Aaron fell on their faces , and said , &quot; God , God of the spirits of all the people , will you be angry with the whole congregation , for you have sinned ?
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You commanded the congregation , saying , &apos; You shall leave the enclosures of the tabernacle of Korah , the great collapse , and Abiram
And Moses arose , and went to the great collapse , to Abiram ; and the elders of Israel went with him
And he commanded the congregation , saying , &quot; Get out of the tent of the wicked , and do not touch their property , lest you fall into their sins and be destroyed with them .
And they departed from the border of the tabernacle of Korah the Great , and Abiram : and Abiram the Great stood at the door of his tent , with his wife , and his children , and his little ones
&quot; Moses said , &quot; All these things I have done have not been done by my own will ; but the Lord has inspired me to do them , and there will be evidence to show it to you
&quot; If they die like the world , or what they have suffered is the same as the world , then the Lord has not sent me
&quot; If the Lord creates a new thing , and opens the earth , and swallows them up , and all that belong to them , and causes them to fall into the shadow of their living , then you will know that they have despised the Lord
When Moses had finished all these words , he opened his mouth at their feet
And they swallowed them up , and their families , and all that belonged to the tribe of Korah , and all their possessions .
Thus they and all that belong to them will fall into the shadows alive , and the mouth will be shut over them as it was before , and they will perish from the congregation .
&quot; When all Israel around them heard their cry , they fled , saying , &apos; I am afraid they will swallow us up
Then a fire came out of the Lord , and consumed the two hundred and fifty who offered the incense .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You commanded Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest , to pick up the stoves out of the fire , and to spread them elsewhere , because they are holy to them
&quot; Take the fireplaces of those who commit sins , and kill themselves , and hammer them into pieces , and use them as an altar ; for they are holy , because they have offered them before the Lord , and they are a sign to the children of Israel .
Then Eleazar the priest took the bronze burner offered by the burner , and the man hammered it out for an altar
&quot; As a memorial to the children of Israel , let no man come near to burn incense in the presence of the Lord other than the sons of Aaron , lest he be struck by the hand of Coran and his party , as the Lord commanded Moses .
On the second day all the congregation of Israel complained to Moses , saying , &quot; You have killed the people of the Lord
And it came to pass , when the congregation was gathered together to fight against Moses , that they looked at the tabernacle of the congregation , and behold , the glory of the Lord appeared , and the clouds were covered .
And Moses and Aaron came to the door of the congregation
And the LORD commanded Moses , saying ,
&quot; Behold , you have left the congregation , and I will destroy them in the midst of the turning of my eyes , and the two of them will fall to the ground .
Moses said to Aaron , &quot; Take your fireplace , and put the fire of the altar in it , and anoint it , and bring it quickly to the congregation for atonement for them ; for the wrath of the Lord has come out , and the plague has spread .
Then Aaron ran to the congregation in the way that Moses had spoken , and behold , the plague was spread among the people ; and he added incense to make atonement for the people
He stood between the living and the dead , and the plague ceased
A total of forty-four thousand and seven hundred were slain by the plague , except for those who died of the plague of Coran
And Aaron returned to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation , and came to Moses , and the plague was stopped
And the Lord said unto Moses
And thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel , saying , Take a staff out of their hand , one for every tribe , and twelve for all their princes , according to the tribe ; and write their names on the staffs of them .
And the name of Aaron shall be written on the staff of Levi : for there shall be a staff among the elders of the tribes .
&quot; You shall put these sticks in front of the ark of the congregation , where I will meet you .
&quot; Then the rod of the one whom I have chosen will sprout , and I will stop the reproach of the children of Israel against you from reaching me .
And Moses spake unto the children of Israel , and their princes gave him the staffs , twelve staffs , according to the tribes , one for each prince ; and Aaron &apos;s staff was in them .
And Moses put the staff before the Lord in the tent of the ark
And it came to pass on the second day , that Moses went into the ark of the law , and said , &quot; Who knoweth that the rod of Aaron the Levite hath sprouted , and hath sprouted , and hath bloomed , and hath harvested almonds ?
And Moses took all the staffs out of the presence of the Lord , and showed them to the children of Israel ; and when they saw it , the princes took their staffs away
And the Lord commanded Moses , saying , &quot; Put Aaron &apos;s staff again before the ark of the law , and mark it for these children of treacherousness , that you may put an end to their complaint against me , lest they die
Thus did Moses ; and as the Lord commanded him , so did he
And the children of Israel said unto Moses , We are dead , and we perish , and we perish all
&quot; Are we to die , all those who come near to the tabernacle of the Lord ?
And the LORD said unto Aaron , Thou and thy son , and thy father &apos;s house , and all the people that are with thee , shall be guilty together of the iniquity of the sanctuary , and thou and thy son shall be guilty together of the iniquity of the priest &apos;s office
&quot; You shall bring your brothers , the Levites , before the tribes of your fathers , that they may serve you with you ; but you and your sons shall serve together before the ark of the ark of the LORD .
&quot; They shall keep what you have commanded them , and keep all the tents , but they shall not approach the instruments of the sanctuary and the altar , lest they and you die .
&quot; They will be united with you , and they will guard the tent of meeting , and handle all the affairs of the tent of meeting ; but strangers will not come near to you
&quot; You shall guard the sanctuary and the altar , lest the wrath come upon the children of Israel again
&quot; I have chosen your brothers , the Levites , from among the children of Israel , to the Lord , as a reward for you , for the work of the tabernacle of the congregation
&quot; You and your sons shall serve as priests together for all that belongs to the altar and the mantle ; and so shall you serve ; and I will give you the priest &apos;s office as a reward , and you shall serve Me ; and every stranger who is near shall be put to death
&quot; The Lord said to Aaron , &quot; I have given to you the offerings which are to me , all the holy things of the children of Israel , for you have been anointed , and I will give them to you and to your sons for an everlasting portion
&quot; The most holy offering which the children of Israel have given me , all the firstfruits , the sin offerings , and the sacrifices of rams , and all that remains without fire , are holy to you and to your sons
&quot; Take these things , and eat them as holy things ; they are holy for every man to eat ;
&quot; All the offerings of the children of Israel , the raising and shaking of the offerings , are yours ; I have given them to you and to your children as a reward for ever , and they shall be eaten by all the clean in your house .
&quot; I will give you the best of all the oil , and the new wine , and the fifth wine , which the children of Israel have offered to the Lord , the first ripened
&quot; Everything that they bring forth from their land to the Lord , the first of its seasons , shall be returned to you ; and the clean ones of your house shall eat it .
And all that is ever given in Israel shall return to thee
&quot; Everything that they have dedicated to the Lord , whether man or beast , will be returned to you . Only the firstborn of man will be redeemed , and the firstborn of unclean beasts will be redeemed
And all that is redeemed outside the month of January shall be redeemed by five shekels of silver , according to the shekel of the sanctuary , according to the price which you have estimated : one shekel is twenty shekels .
Only the firstborn of the bull , or the firstborn of the sheep , and the firstborn of the goats , shall not be redeemed ; they are holy ; he shall sprinkle his blood on the altar , and burn his fat , and offer it to the Lord as a sweet burnt offering .
And his flesh shall be to thee as the chest that is shaken , and as the right leg that is lifted up .
&quot; I will give to you and to your sons and daughters all the sacrifices of the holy things which the children of Israel have offered to the Lord as an everlasting portion for you and for your seed , as a covenant of salt before the Lord for ever .
And the LORD said unto Aaron , Thou shalt have no inheritance among the children of Israel , neither shalt thou have a share among them : I am thy share , and thy inheritance .
&quot; I have given to the sons of Levi one tenth of all the children of Israel as their inheritance , because they did the work of the tabernacle of the congregation , and I have given to them as a reward for their labour
&quot; From now on , the children of Israel shall not come near the Tent of Meeting , lest they die on account of their sins
&quot; But the Levites shall do the business of the Tent of Meeting , and bear the iniquity ; and this shall be a statute for ever for your generations ; and they shall have no inheritance among the children of Israel .
&quot; For I have given the Levites an inheritance for one tenth of the children of Israel , which they sacrificed to the Lord for an offering ; therefore I said to them , There is no inheritance among the children of Israel
And the LORD commanded Moses , saying ,
&quot; Speak to the Levites , and say , &apos; You shall take one tenth of the tenth of the children of Israel , which I have given you for a possession , and one tenth of the tenth of that tenth you shall offer for an offering to the Lord
&quot; This sacrifice shall be for your field as wine full of wine ,
&quot; You shall offer up one tenth of the children of Israel as a sacrifice to the Lord , and from one tenth you shall give Aaron the priest your offering to the Lord
&quot; You shall offer all your gifts to the Lord for a sacrifice , from which the best of them shall be holy .
&quot; Therefore say to the Levites , &apos; The best thing you will raise up out of it will be food for your fields , and wine for your vineyards .
&quot; This is your reward , and the reward of your labour in the synagogue , that you and your families may eat wherever you go .
&quot; You will not take the best of it , and you will not be guilty of it ; and you will not profane the holy things of Israel , lest you die .
Then the Lord spoke to Moses , and Aaron said ,
&quot; This is the law which the Lord commanded in the law , saying , &apos; You shall command the children of Israel to bring to you a pure red ox without blemish and without yoke
&quot; And it shall be given to Eleazar the priest , and he shall be taken out of the camp , and the bulls shall be slaughtered before him
Then Eliezer the priest shall sprinkle the blood of the cow with his fingers seven times before the Tent of Meeting
&quot; The man shall burn the cow in his sight , and the skin , the flesh , the blood , and the dung of the cow shall be burned
And the priest shall cast the acacia trees , and the oxen &apos;s knees , and the red threads , into the fire of the cow
&quot; The priest shall not be clean until the evening . He shall wash his clothes and wash himself with water , and then he shall enter the camp .
And he that burneth the cow shall not be clean until the evening , nor shall he wash his clothes , nor wash himself with water .
&quot; A clean man shall take the ashes of the cow , and there shall be a clean place outside the camp , and make it a clean water for the congregation of Israel , and it shall be cleansed from sin .
He who takes the ashes of the cow will not be clean until the evening , and he will wash his clothes . This will be a statute forever for Israel and for the foreigners who dwell among them .
&quot; He who touches a dead body will not be clean seven days
&quot; On the third day he shall purify himself with the water that is purified , and on the seventh day he shall be purified ; and if he does not purify himself on the third day , he will not be purified on the seventh day .
&quot; Whoever touches a dead body and does not cleanse himself will defile the tabernacle of the Lord , and he will be cut off from Israel ; for the water of cleansing has not poured out on him , and he will be unclean , and the uncleanness will be on him
&quot; This is the ordinance of death in the tent : whoever enters the tent , and whoever is in the tent , shall be unclean seven days
Every open vessel is uncovered and unclean .
&quot; Whoever touches the slain in the field , or the body , or the bone of a man , or the tomb , shall not be clean seven days
&quot; Take some of the ashes burned for the unclean , and put them in a vessel , and pour on it living water .
And it shall come to pass , that there shall be a clean man , and he shall dip in the water of the oxen &apos;s knees , and sprinkle it upon the tent , and upon all the vessels , and upon all the people in the tent , and upon the bones , and upon the slain , and upon the dead , and upon the tomb ;
And on the third day and on the seventh day the clean man shall sprinkle water on the unclean man , and on the seventh day he shall be clean , and he shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water , and he shall be clean at night .
&quot; But he who is unclean and does not cleanse himself , let him be cut off from the congregation , because he has defiled the sanctuary of the Lord ; and there is no water to wash away from him ; he is unclean
&quot; This shall be a statute for you for ever ; and he who pours out the filthy water shall wash his clothes ; and he who touches the filthy water shall not be clean until the evening .
Everything he touches that is unclean is unclean ; and he that touches it will not be clean until the night .
And in the first month all the congregation of Israel came unto the wilderness which they sought ; and they dwelt in Gathmosh ; and in it Micah died , and was buried .
And when the congregation had no water to drink , they gathered themselves together to attack Moses and Aaron
And the people argued with Moses , saying , &quot; Our brethren have died before the Lord , and we hate to die with them
&quot; Why do you bring the congregation of the Lord into the wilderness , and cause us and our cattle to die here ?
Why have you driven us out of Egypt , and brought us into this evil place , where there is no good sowing , no fruit trees , no vines , no pomegranates , and no water to drink
Moses and Aaron went out of the congregation to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation , and fell on the ground , and the glory of the Lord appeared to them .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; Take your staff and gather the congregation together with Aaron your brother , and command the rock to send out water before them , and it shall flow out of the rock for the congregation and for their cattle to drink
And Moses took a staff from before the Lord , as the Lord had commanded him
And Moses and Aaron gathered together the congregation before the rock ; and Moses said , &quot; Listen to me , you treacherous people ; have I sent water out of the rock for you
And Moses lifted up his hand , and struck the rock with a staff ; and much water came forth , and the congregation and their cattle drank .
&quot; The Lord said to Moses and Aaron , &quot; Because you do not believe in me , and do not consider me holy in the eyes of the children of Israel , you shall not bring the congregation into the land which I have given them
And the name of the water was called Milibah , because the children of Israel contended with the LORD , and the LORD was sanctified before them
Then Moses sent messengers from Gath , to the king of Edom , saying , Thus saith thy brethren Israel , All the hardships which we have suffered
&quot; It is our ancestors who came down to Egypt , and we have lived in Egypt for a long time ; and the Egyptians have done evil to our ancestors and to us
&quot; When we cried to the Lord , He heard our voice ; and you knew that the messengers had brought us out of Egypt ; and now we are in Gath , the city on your border .
&quot; Let us pass through your land , and we will not walk in the fields and vineyards , nor drink the waters of the wells , but on the highway , and not on the left or on the right , until we have passed through your borders .
&quot; The king of Edom said , &quot; You shall not pass through my land , lest I go out with a sword and attack you
And the children of Israel said , &quot; We will go up the way , and if we and the cattle drink of your water , it will be of value to you ; but you will not ask anything else , but let us pass by on foot .
Then said the king of Edom , &quot; You shall not pass through ; but lead many men out , and strike the children of Israel with a mighty hand .
So the king of the East refused to let the children of Israel pass by from his border , and they turned away from him
And all the congregation of Israel went up from Gadesh unto mount Hor
&quot; The Lord spoke to Moses on Mount Hor near the east border , saying ,
&quot; And Aaron shall return to his fathers , and shall not enter into the land which I have given to the children of Israel ; for you have rebelled against my life in the waters of Mirib
And thou shalt bring Aaron and Eleazar his son up to mount Hor
Take off Aaron &apos;s holy garment , and put it on Eleazar his son ; and Aaron shall die therein in the place of his fathers .
And Moses did as the Lord commanded : and the three went up to Mount Hor before the congregation .
And Moses took off Aaron &apos;s holy garment , and put it on Eleazar his son ; and Aaron died there on the top of the mountain . And Moses and Eleazar went down the mountain
And when all the congregation , and all the house of Israel , saw that Aaron was dead , they wept for Aaron thirty days
When king Arad of Canaan in the south heard that the Israelites had come from the way of Ahiram , he fought with them , and took away several of them
And the children of Israel cried unto the LORD , saying , If thou wilt deliver this people into my hand , I will destroy their cities to the end
And the LORD did hearken unto the children of Israel , and delivered the Canaanites unto them , and they did destroy the Canaanites , and the cities of the Canaanites ; and the name of that place was called Hormah .
And they went up from Mount Hor to the way of the Red Sea , and passed through the land of Edom ; and the people were troubled in their hearts because of the way
Then they complained to God and to Moses , saying , &quot; Why do you bring us out of Egypt and cause us to die in the wilderness , where there is no food and no water , and our hearts hate this light food ?
Then the Lord brought the serpent of fire into the midst of the people , and the serpent bit them , and many of the children of Israel died
Then the people came to Moses , and said , &quot; We have sinned against the Lord and against you . Pray to the Lord that these snakes may leave us . &quot; And Moses prayed for the people
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; You have made a serpent of fire hanging on a rod . Anyone who is bitten will live when he sees the serpent
And Moses made a serpent of brass hanging on a rod ; and whosoever is bitten by the serpent shall live when he looks at it .
And the children of Israel arose , and encamped in Ab
And they went up from Ab , and encamped in the wilderness of Eer , and in Abilene , which is before Moab , in the land of the rising sun .
&quot; From there , and camp in the valley of Zareth
And they arose from there , and encamped over against the river , which came out of the wilderness from the border of the Amorites ; and the river was the border of Moab in the place where the border was between Moab and the Amorites .
Thus says the Lord in the book of war , &quot; Wahab of Shuphah and the valley of the river Anin
And to the valley of the children of Ar , which is near the border of Moab .
And the children of Israel departed from there , and came to Beer ; and the Lord said unto Moses before , Gather the people together , that I may give them water ; and he said , This is the well
At that time the children of Israel sang , saying , &quot; Water is pouring in , O well , and you will sing to it .
And the children of Israel took it from the wilderness unto the land of Manasseh , and dug it with a rod , and with a rod , and dug it with a rod , and dug it with a rod , and dug it with a rod , and dug it with a rod , and dug it with a rod , and dug it with a rod , and dug it with a rod ,
From Ma he came to Nahor , and from Nahor to Baal
from Baalmah to the valley of Moab , and to the top of Bishah in the wilderness ,
And the children of Israel sent an apostle unto Sihon king of the Amorites , saying ,
&quot; Let us pass through your land , and we will not enter into the fields and vineyards , nor drink the waters of the wells ; let us walk by the way , and come straight to your borders .
&quot; When Sihon refused to let the children of Israel pass through his border , he gathered his people together into the wilderness to attack the children of Israel ; and he came to Jahaz , and fought with the children of Israel
And the children of Israel slew him with the sword , and took his land , from the river Arnon even unto the river Jabbok , even unto the border of the children of Ammon ; for the border of the children of Ammon was fortified
And the children of Israel took all these cities , and the cities of the Amorites , which were in Sheshbon and all the villages of Sheshbon
This is the capital of Sihon king of Amoly , who fought with the fathers of Moab , and took all the land out of his hand , even to the river Arnon
&quot; Therefore those who write poetry say , &apos; Come to Sheshbon , and let the city of Sihon be built and established .
For there was a fire from Heshbon , and a flame came out of the city of Sihon , and consumed the high places of Aor in Moab and the high places of the river Aun .
Woe to you , O Moab ! You are destroyed , O people of Gibeah ! The men of Gibeah fled , and the women were taken captive , and delivered to Sihon king of Amoly .
We shot at them , and destroyed them from Heshbon even to Debon ; and we turned the land into a wilderness even to Noah , and Noah stretched out to Midian .
So the children of Israel lived in the land of the Amorites
And Moses sent men to spy on Jahaz ; and the children of Israel took the towns of Jahaz , and drove out the Amorites thereof
And the children of Israel turned their backs , and went to Bashan ; and the night of the king of Bashan came , and all his people came out to fight with them at Edom
And the LORD said unto Moses , Fear him not : for I have given him into thine hand , and his people , and his land ; and thou shalt be with him as with Sihon king of the Amorites that dwelt in Shechembon .
Then they slew him and his sons and his people , and they took his land without leaving a remnant
And the children of Israel arose , and encamped against the camp of Jericho in the plains of Moab east of the Jordan
And all that the children of Israel did unto the children of Ammon was seen by Balak the son of Ziph .
And the children of Moab were greatly afraid , and were troubled in their hearts , because of the multitude of Israel
And he said unto the elders of Midian , Behold , all that is round about us in this people shall be cut down as the grass of the field of cattle ; and Balak the son of Zadok shall be king over Moab .
And he sent an apostle unto Bethany by the river , unto Balaam the son of Beer , and called unto him , saying , A people have come out of Egypt to dwell with me , covering the earth
&quot; Behold , these people are stronger than I ! Now come and curse them for me , or I will prevail against them , and attack them , and drive them out of the land ; for I know who you bless , and whoever is blessed , and whoever you curse , and whoever is cursed
And the elders of Moab and of Midian came to Balaam , and told him all the words of Balak , with the money in their hand .
And Balaam said , &quot; Stay here tonight , and I will return to you , as the Lord has spoken to me ; and the servants of Moab will dwell there .
Then God came to Balaam and said to him , &quot; Who are all those who are here with you
Then Balaam answered and said , Balak the son of Zippoel king of Moab sent to me , saying ,
&quot; Behold , the people who came out of Egypt were covered in the ground . You came to curse them for me , or I could fight them and drive them out
And God said unto Balaam , Thou shalt not go with them , neither shalt thou curse the people , for they are blessed
And Balaam arose in the morning , and said unto the messengers of Balak , Return to the land ; for the LORD will not allow me to go with you
And the servants of Moab rose up , and went to Balak , and said , Balak will not come with us
And Balak sent messengers , more and more precious than before
And when they were come to Balaam , they said unto him , Thus saith Balak the son of Zippoel , Will thou not forbid me that thou come not unto me ?
For I will give thee great honour : whatsoever thou askest of me , I will give thee ; and come and curse this people for me .
Then Balaam answered and said to his servants , &quot; Behold , Balak has given me the silver and gold of his house , and I will do no greater thing than the life of the Lord my God
&quot; Now I ask you to stay here tonight , until I know what the Lord will say to me
Then God came to Balaam that night and said , &quot; If these people call you , then you will rise up and go with them , and do as I have spoken to you .
And Balaam arose in the morning , and set up the donkey , and went with the servants of Moab
And the anger of God was kindled for him : and the enemies of the LORD stood on the way against him , and he rode on a donkey , and two of his servants followed him .
And when the donkey saw the messenger of the Lord standing in the way , with a sword drawn out of his hand , he crossed the way into the field ; and Balaam struck the donkey to make him return to the way
And the angel of the Lord stood on the narrow way of the vineyard , and there was a wall on this side , and a wall on that side
When the donkey saw the angel of the Lord , he leaned against the wall , and crushed Balaam &apos;s foot , and struck him again .
And the messenger of the Lord went forward again , and stood in a narrow place , where there was no turning on either side
And when the donkey saw the angel of the Lord , he lay down under Balaam ; and Balaam was wroth , and struck the donkey with a staff
And the LORD called the donkey , and said unto Balaam , What have I done unto thee ? why hast thou smitten me these three times
Then Balaam said to the donkey , &quot; Because you have played a trick on me , I hate that I cannot have a sword in my hand , and have killed you
And the donkey said unto Balaam , Am I not the donkey that thou hast ridden from the hour even unto this day , and have I done this unto thee ? And Balaam said , No
Then the LORD made the eyes of Balaam bright , and he saw the angel of the LORD standing in the way with a sword drawn out of his hand , and Balaam bowed down on his face to the ground .
And the angel of the LORD said unto him , Why hast thou smitten thy donkey these three times ? for I am come out against thee , and for that which thou hast done , thou art far from me
&quot; When the donkey saw me , he turned away from me three times ; and if he hadn &apos;t turned away , I would have killed you early and kept him alive
And Balaam said unto the messenger of the LORD , I am guilty , and I know not that thou standest in the way to hinder me ; and if thou wilt not rejoice in me , I will turn again
And the angel of the LORD said unto Balaam , Go with these men , and speak as I speak unto thee : and Balaam went with the servants of Balak
And when Balak heard that Balaam was come , he went to meet him in the city of Moab , which is on the border , by the river Arnon
And Balak said unto Balaam , Am I not anxious to send a messenger unto thee to call thee ? why art thou not come unto me , and can I not honour thee ?
Then said Balaam , &quot; I have come to you , and can I speak with authority here ? Whatever God has spoken to me , I will speak
And Balaam and Balak accompanied him , and came to Gilead-huzo .
And he slaughtered cattle and sheep , and gave them to Balaam and to his companions
And it came to pass in the morning , that Balak led Balaam to the height of Balak , and he looked from there at the border of the camp of Israel .
Then Balaam said to Balak , &quot; You have made seven altars for me here , and prepared for me seven bulls and seven rams
And Balak did according to the words of Balaam ; and they offered on every altar a bull and a ram
And Balaam said unto Balak , Stand by thy burnt offering , and I will go before thee ; or the LORD shall come to meet me , and I will tell thee what he hath commanded me ; and there shall be a high place on Balaam in clear light .
Then God came to Balaam , and he said , &quot; I have prepared seven altars , and on each of them I have offered a bull and a ram
Then the Lord spoke to Balaam , saying , &quot; Return to Balak , and say thus and thus ,
And he returned to Balak , and behold , he stood by the burnt offering with the servants of Moab
Then Balak began to sing , &quot; Ball has brought me out of Aram , and the king of Moab has brought me out of the mountains of the east , saying , Come , curse Jacob for me , and come , curse Israel in anger
For God has no curse , and I can &apos;t curse ; For the Lord has no wrath , and I can &apos;t wrath
&quot; I have looked at him from the top of the mountain , and from the bottom of the mountain . He is a solitary people , and not among the multitude
Who can count the dust of Jacob , Who can count the fourth part of Israel ? I wish to die as a righteous man , I wish to die as a righteous man
Then Balak said to Balaam , &quot; What have you done to me ? I brought you to curse my enemies , and you did not expect to bless them
Then he answered , &quot; What the Lord has spoken to me , can I not speak with caution ?
Then said Balak , &quot; Go with me to another place where you can see them ; you cannot see them all , but only those who are on their borders ; and curse them there for me .
And he took Balaam to Zophr , and went up to the top of Bisha , and built seven altars , and on each altar he offered a bull and a ram
Then Balaam said to Balak , &quot; Stand by the burnt offering , and wait for me to come to meet the Lord
Then the Lord came to Balaam and spoke to him , saying , &quot; Return to Balaam , and say thus and thus ,
Then he returned to Balak , and saw him standing by the burnt offering , and the servants of Moab with him ; and Balak said to him , &quot; What has the Lord said
And Balak said in a psalm , Arise , Balak , and hear ; and hear me , thou son of Zebulun .
God is not a man , He will not lie , He is not a son , He will not repent ; Will He not speak according to his deeds , Will He not speak to be accomplished ?
Blessed be I , and blessed be God , and I cannot turn back
He saw no iniquity in Jacob , and no wickedness in Israel : and the LORD his God was with him , and there was a voice among them that rejoiced at the king
God brought them out of Egypt , and they seemed to have the power of a cattle .
For there is no magic that can harm Jacob , nor is there any divination that can harm Israel ; and now there will be a man to speak to Jacob , and to speak to Israel , saying , What great things God has done for him
&quot; The people arise as a mother lion , and stand up as a lion ; they have not eaten the food of the field , they have not drank the blood of the injured , and they will never lie down .
And Balak said unto Balaam , Thou shalt not curse them , nor bless them
Then Balaam answered Balak , &quot; Did I not tell you that I would obey all that the Lord has spoken ?
Then Balak said to Balaam , &quot; Come , I will take you to another place , or God will like you to curse them for me there
And Balak took Balaam , and brought him to the top of Mount Beer in the wilderness ,
Then Balaam said to Balak , &quot; You have built seven altars for me here , and prepared for me here seven bulls and seven rams
And Balak did according to the word of Balaam , and he offered on every altar a bull and a ram
&quot; When Balaam saw the joy and blessing of the Lord with Israel , he went not to seek the law as he had done two times before , but to the wilderness
And when Balaam lifted up his eyes , and saw that the children of Israel dwell in the midst of the tribes , the Spirit of God came upon him
And he composed a psalm , saying , Thus saith Balaam the son of Beer , The man that shut his eyes , or openeth them ,
He who hears the word of God , and sees the vision of the Almighty , and opens his eyes and falls down ,
How beautiful is thy tent , O Jacob ; how beautiful is thy tent , O Israel !
As the valleys joined together , as the gardens by the rivers , as the trees of the LORD , as the cypresses by the waters ,
Water shall flow out of his barrel , and seeds shall be planted in the midst of abundant water ; and his king shall overtake Amah ; and his land shall be revived .
God brought him out of Egypt , and he appeared to be strong like a cattle , and he would devour the enemy , and break their bones , and shoot through them with arrows .
Blessed be he that blesseth thee , and blessed be he that curseth thee , and blessed be he that curseth thee
And when Balak was angry with Balaam , he lifted up his hand , and said unto Balaam , I have called thee to curse my enemies ; behold , thou hast blessed them three times
Now therefore return quickly to your land ; for I desired to give you great glory , and the Lord has not hindered you from it .
And Balaam said unto Balak , Am I not the messenger that thou hast sent unto me ?
&quot; Behold , Balak has given me the silver and gold of his house , and I will not go beyond the life of the Lord , to do good and evil in my own heart , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will speak .
&quot; Now I am returning to my people ; and you have come , and I will tell you how to deal with your people in the days to come .
And he composed a psalm , saying , Thus saith Balaam the son of Beer ; The man that shut his eyes , or openeth them ,
He who hears the word of God , and understands the will of the Most High , and sees the vision of the Almighty , and opens his eyes and falls down ,
&quot; I see him not in the present , and I see him not in the near future . A star will come forth from Jacob , and a staff will rise up for Israel , and it will break the corners of Moab , and it will destroy the children of distress .
He will be able to build an inheritance in the east , and an inheritance in the land of the enemy , Seir ; and Israel will be brave .
&quot; There is a man from Jacob who will take power , and he will destroy the remnant of the city .
And when Balaam saw Amalek , he began to sing a song , saying , Amalek was the head of the nations , but he shall surely perish
And Balaam looked at the Kenites , and said in a psalm , &quot; Your dwelling place is strong , and your nest is in a rocky pit .
&quot; But Keni will be weakened , and will take you captive to Assyria
Then Balaam recited another psalm , saying , &quot; Woe to you ! Who can live if God does this thing
And a man shall come by ship from the border of Kiti , and shall suffer Assyria , and Hebrews ; and he shall fall .
Then Balaam returned to his place ; and Balaam also returned .
And the children of Israel dwelled in Sheth ; and the people did prostitution with the daughters of Moab .
&quot; For they brought the people together to offer sacrifices to their God for this woman , and the people ate their offerings and kneeled before their God
And the children of Israel were joined to Baal-bir ; and the wrath of the LORD was kindled against the children of Israel
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; Put all the elders of the people on their heads before me , that my wrath against the children of Israel may be quenched
Moses commanded the judges of Israel , saying , &quot; Every one of your people who is associated with Baal-bir , kill him
&quot; When Moses and all the congregation of Israel were weeping before the door of the Tent of Meeting , a man of Israel came to his brother with a Midianite woman in front of them
And Phinehas the son of Eleazar , the son of Aaron the priest , when he saw it , rose up out of the congregation , and had a gun in his hand
&quot; Then he went with the Israelites into the tent , and pierced the Israelites and the woman through their bellies ; and the plague ceased among the Israelites .
At that time there were twenty and four thousand that died of the plague .
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
For Phinehas , the son of Aaron the priest , the son of Eleazar , hath put away my wrath from the children of Israel , because he hath been among them , and hath taken my iniquity for his heart , and hath not destroyed them in their iniquity
Therefore say , &quot; I have given him my covenant of peace
&quot; This is the covenant that shall be given to him and to his seed as a long-lasting priesthood for the redemption of the children of Israel , because of his wicked heart toward God .
And the name of the Israelite that was slain with the Midianite woman was Shinli , the son of Zareel , the head of the tribe of Simeon
The woman of Midian who was slain , whose name was Gosbee , was the daughter of Suor , the head of the tribe of Midian
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
Thou shalt disturb the Midianites , and slay them
For they have deceived you with this deceit in the matter of Beer , and in the matter of Gosbee , the daughter of their sister , the prince of Midian ; and Gosbee was slain in the days of the plague .
After the plague the Lord spoke to Moses and to Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest , saying ,
&quot; You shall number all the congregation of Israel according to their tribes , from twenty years old and upward , whoever is able to go out to fight
And Moses and Eleazar the priest said unto the children of Israel by the Jordan , which is in the plain of Moab , which is by Jericho
&quot; The total number of you from twenty years old and upward shall be numbered according to the word of Moses and the children of Israel who came out of the land of Egypt , as the Lord commanded them
