Nadab the son of Aaron , Abihu , Eleazar , Ehamma
And Nadab and Abihu died when they offered all the fire before the Lord
There were twenty-three thousand males among the Levites that were numbered every month , and they were not numbered among the children of Israel , because there was no portion among the children of Israel in their inheritance .
These are they that Moses and Eleazar the priest numbered in the plains of Moab , by the Jordan , which is before Jericho , of the children of Israel .
But none of the men that were numbered was of the children of Israel , whom Moses and Aaron the priest had numbered in the wilderness of Sinai
&quot; Because the Lord said to them , &apos; They must die in the wilderness . &apos; So there was not a man left , except Galilee the son of Jephunneh and Joshua the son of Nun
And of the sons of Manasseh , the sons of Joseph , the sons of Manasseh , the sons of Maghi , the sons of Gilead , the daughter of Zerubbabel the son of Heph , named Marah , Noah , and Zorah , and Micah , and Datzah ; and they came
And he stood at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before Moses , and before Eleazar the priest , and before all the elders of the congregation ,
&quot; Our father died in the wilderness , and he did not gather together with the company of the Philistines to attack the Lord ; he died in his own sin , and he had no son .
&quot; Why do you take away his name from his people , because our father has no sons ? Divide your inheritance among the brothers of our father .
Then Moses presented their case before the Lord
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
And thou shalt divide the land among the brethren of their father , and give unto them the inheritance of their father ; and thou shalt give unto them the inheritance of their father .
And thou shalt say unto the children of Israel , If a man die without a son , give his inheritance unto his daughter
&quot; If he has no daughter , he will give his inheritance to his brothers
&quot; If he has no brother , he shall give his inheritance to his father &apos;s brothers
&quot; If his father has no brothers , he shall give his inheritance to his nearest relatives , and they shall be his inheritance . This is the law and the statute of the children of Israel , as the Lord commanded Moses
And the LORD said unto Moses , Go up to mount Abal , and see the land which I have given unto the children of Israel
&quot; When you have seen it , you will also return to your fathers , as Aaron your brother did .
For in the wilderness which you seek you have contravened my life , when the congregation was in dispute , and have not sanctified me in the sight of the congregation in the land of the flood , which is the wilderness which you seek , and the waters of Smiliba .
And Moses said unto the LORD
&quot; Let the Lord , the God of the spirit of all the people , set up a man to rule over the congregation
He may go in and out before them , and guide them , lest the congregation of the Lord be like a flock of sheep without a shepherd
&quot; The Lord said to Moses , &quot; You will bring Joshua the son of Nun , who has the Spirit in his heart , and you will lay your hand on his head
And he stood before Eleazar the priest , and before the whole congregation , and commanded him
and give him your glory , that all the congregation of Israel may hearken to him
And he shall stand before Eleazar the priest , and he shall inquire of him before the LORD by the judgment of the tomb , and he and all the congregation of Israel shall go in and out according to the commandment of Eleazar .
And Moses brought Joshua , as the Lord commanded him , and made him stand before Eleazar the priest and before the whole congregation
Put your hand on his head , and command him , as the Lord has spoken through Moses
The Lord spoke to Moses , saying ,
&quot; You shall say to the children of Israel , &apos; You shall give me your offering , which is a sweet savour offering for me , and you shall give it to me on a date
&quot; And you shall say to them , &apos; You shall offer the burnt offering to the Lord as a continual burnt offering , two lambs a day without blemish a year old
One in the morning , one in the evening
and one tenth of an iphah of fine flour , and one-fourth of a hin of oil mixed with it , and mixed therewith for a sin offering
&quot; This is the continual burnt offering , as appointed by Mount Sinai , a burnt offering to the Lord , a sweet savour
&quot; You shall offer for the lamb a fourth of a hin of the wine of the offering , and you shall offer it to the Lord for a drink in the sanctuary .
&quot; In the evening , you shall offer the lamb to the Lord as a sweet burnt offering , like the firstfruits of the morning , and as a drink offering with them .
&quot; On the Sabbath day you shall offer two lambs a year old without blemish , and two tenths of an ephah of fine flour mingled with oil , and you shall offer the same drink offering
This is the burnt offering on the Sabbath day , and the continual burnt offering , and the drink offering that is with it
&quot; In the first month of the month you shall offer two bulls , one ram , and seven lambs of the first year without blemish for a burnt offering to the Lord
&quot; A bull shall be given three tenths of an ephah of fine flour mingled with oil for a sin offering ; and the sheep two tenths of an ephah of fine flour mingled with oil for a sin offering .
and one tenth of an ephah of fine flour mingled with oil for a burnt offering of oil and sweet savour , for a burnt offering to the Lord ,
A bull shall drink half a hin , and a sheep a third of a hin , and a lamb a quarter of a hin : this is the burnt offering of every month , for months and months throughout the year .
&quot; A male goat for a sin offering shall be offered to the Lord , except for the continual burnt offering and the same drink offering
&quot; The 14th of January is the Lord &apos;s Passover
&quot; The fifteenth day of this month is the feast , seven days of unleavened bread
On the first day , when there is a holy feast , no labour shall be done
&quot; When you offer to the Lord for a burnt offering two bulls , one ram , and seven lambs a year old without any blemish ,
And the meat offering of the same shall be fine flour mingled with oil , three tenths of an ephah for a bullock , and two tenths of an ephah for a ram .
One tenth of an ephah for each of the seven lambs ;
&quot; And you shall offer a goat for a sin offering for your sins
&quot; You shall offer it except for the usual burnt offering in the morning .
&quot; The food of the sweet burnt offering shall be offered to the Lord in this manner seven days in a row , every day , except for the continual burnt offering and the same drink offering
On the seventh day , when there is a holy feast , no labour shall be done
&quot; When the harvest is ripe , you offer a new sacrifice to the Lord in the days of holiness , and no hard work can be done
&quot; You shall offer to the Lord two bulls , one ram , and seven lambs of the first year , for a burnt offering of sweet incense
And three tenths of an ephah for a bullock , and two tenths of an ephah for a ram , of fine flour mingled with oil , for the meat offering with it ;
One tenth of an ephah for each of the seven lambs ;
&quot; And you shall offer a goat for your sins
&quot; You shall offer these without any disability , except the burnt offering , and the meat offering , and the drink offering , which you have always offered
On the first day of July you shall have a holy feast , and no labour shall be done ; it is the day that you shall keep it as a trumpet .
&quot; You shall offer to the Lord a bull , and a ram , and seven lambs of the first year without blemish , for a sweet burnt offering
And the meat offering of the same shall be fine flour mingled with oil , three tenths of an ephah for a bullock , and two tenths of an ephah for a ram .
One tenth of an ephah for each of the seven lambs ;
&quot; And you shall offer a goat for a sin offering for your sins
These are the burnt offerings of the moon , and the sacrifices made together , and the continual burnt offerings , and the sacrifices made together , and the drink offerings made together , besides the like offerings ; these are offered unto the LORD as a sweet burnt offering .
&quot; On the tenth day of the first month of July , when you have a holy feast , you shall not do any work to grieve yourselves .
&quot; You shall offer to the Lord a burnt offering of sweet incense , one calf , one ram , seven lambs of the first year without blemish
And for the meat offering with it , three tenths of an ephah for a bullock , and two tenths of an ephah for a ram , of fine flour mingled with oil
One tenth of Iphah shall be given to each of the seven lambs .
And one goat for a sin offering , beside the sin offering , and the continual burnt offering , and the same meat offering , and the same drink offering
&quot; On the fifteenth day of July , when you have a holy feast , you shall not do any hard work ; but you shall keep the Sabbath to the Lord seven days
And thirteen bulls , two rams , and fourteen lambs of the first year , without any infirmity , shall they offer for a burnt offering to the Lord with fire , a sweet savour
And three-tenths of an ephah for each of the thirteen bullocks , and two-tenths of an ephah for each of the two rams ;
One tenth of an ephah for each of the fourteen lambs
