&quot; When the Lord heard these words of you , He swore in anger ,
&quot; None of this wicked generation shall see the beauty of the land which I swore to give to your fathers
&quot; But the son of Jephunneh , Caleb , will see , and I will give him the land which he has trodden , and his sons , because he is determined to follow me .
&quot; For the sake of you , the Lord is angry with me , saying , &apos; You shall not enter into the land
&quot; Serve Joshua your son , the son of Nun ; he will enter the land , and you will encourage him , because he will make the children of Israel possess it for a possession .
&quot; And your wives and your children , whom you say will be taken captive , and the children of evil and good who do not know this day , will enter into the land , and I will give it to them , and they will be given for a possession .
As for you , turn back from the way of the Red Sea to the wilderness
Then you answered me , &quot; We have sinned against the Lord , and would like to go up and fight according to the commandment of the Lord our God , &quot; and each one of you went up to the mountains with his weapons .
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; Tell them , &apos; Do not go up or fight , for I am not among you , lest you be defeated by your enemies
&quot; I told you that you did not obey the commandment of the Lord and went up into the mountains without permission
&quot; The Amorites who lived in the mountains came out and attacked you , chasing you like a flock , and slaughtered you in Siir , even to Hormah .
&quot; You will come back and cry before the Lord , but the Lord will not listen to your voice , nor listen to your ears
So you lived in Gallows for many days
&quot; After that , we returned from the way of the Red Sea to the wilderness , as the Lord had commanded me , and we went about Mount Siir many days
The Lord said to me
&quot; The days of your journey around the mountain are over , and you turn northward .
&quot; You commanded the people , saying , &apos; Your brothers , the sons of Esau , will live in Siir , and you will pass through their borders ; and they will be afraid of you , so be careful of yourselves
&quot; Do not fight with them , and I will not give you their land , where you can walk with your feet , for I have given Mount Seir to Esau for a possession
&quot; You will buy food for them with money , and water for them with money
&quot; For the Lord , your God , has blessed you in all that you do in your hand ; and he knows that you walk in the wilderness ; and the Lord , your God , has been with you forty years ; therefore you have no shortage
Then we departed from Siir , where our brethren the sons of Esau dwelt , from the way of Arabah , and passed through Elah , and through Ishangai , and turned to the way of the wilderness of Moab .
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; You shall neither disturb the Moabites nor fight with them , and I will not give their land to you for a possession , because I have given it to the sons of Aaron for a possession
And there lived in it before the Edomites , a great multitude , and a great body , as the Assyrians
The children of Edom were like the children of Achan ; and they were called the children of Libion ; and the Moabites called them Edom
The Philistines lived in Siir before , but the sons of Esau destroyed them , and took their land , and dwelt therein , just as Israel did in the land which the Lord gave him for a possession .
Now arise and pass through the brook ; and we pass through the brook
&quot; For thirty-eight years , from the time that they left Galilee to the time that they came to the brook Sarai , all the men of that generation were consumed from their camps , as the Lord swore to them .
And the hand of the LORD came upon them , and destroyed them from the camp , even to the end .
After the soldiers killed all of the people
&quot; The Lord commanded me , saying ,
&quot; Today you shall pass through Aor from the border of Moab
&quot; You shall not approach the land of the children of Ammon , nor disturb them , nor fight with them ; I will not give you the land of the children of Ammon for a possession , for I have given it to the sons of Lot for a possession .
&quot; And the land shall be called the land of the Lebanese ; there lived the Lebanese before ; and the children of Ammon called them a people to waste .
&quot; The people were as tall as the Assyrians , but the Lord destroyed them from before the children of Ammon , and the children of Ammon took their land and lived there
&quot; Just as the Lord destroyed the Philistines from before them for the sons of Esau , who lived in Siir , and they took the land of the Philistines , and dwelt therein , even to this day
The Canaanites who came out of the land of Gath shall be destroyed , and they shall dwell thereafter , even as the children of Ahab had dwelt in the country , and shall return to Gaza .
&quot; Arise , and go over the valley of Arnon ; I have delivered into your hand Sihon king of Heshbon the Amorite , and his land ; and you shall fight against him and take his land for a possession .
From this day onward I will make all the people of the earth tremble , and fear , and mourn for your name
&quot; I sent messengers from the wilderness of Gideon to Sihon king of Hesh , saying in a word of peace
&quot; Let me pass through your land , and walk only on the road , and not on the left or on the right
&quot; You can sell me food to eat , and you can sell me water to drink , as long as you allow me to walk
&quot; Just as the sons of Esau in Siir and Moab in Aor treated me , when I passed over the Jordan to enter the land which the Lord our God has given to us
&quot; But Sihon the king of Heshbon did not allow us to pass through him , because the Lord your God made his heart stiff , and his heart stiff , to deliver him into your hand , as it is today
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; From now on I will give you Sihon and his land , and you will receive his land for a possession
Then Sihon and all his people came out against us , and fought against us at Jahaz
&quot; The Lord , our God , has given him to us , and we have struck him and his son and all his people
&quot; We have taken all his cities , and destroyed all the cities that smoke , women and children , and there is not one left .
Only the cattle and the cities which they have taken , and the wealth thereof , take for their own prey .
&quot; The Lord , our God , has given us from Aroer on the bank of the valley , and from the city in the valley , even to Gilead ; and there is not a city that is so high that we cannot take it .
&quot; But the land of the children of Ammon , and all that is near the river Jabbok , and the cities of the mountains , have not come near to the place where the Lord our God has forbidden us to go
Then we returned to Bashan ; and the night of Bashan and all his people came out to fight with us at Edom
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; Don &apos;t fear him , for I have given him and his people and his land into your hand , and you will treat him as Sihon king of Amoly , who lived in Heshbon .
&quot; Then the Lord , our God , will deliver the nightmare of the king of Bashan and his people into our hands , and we will kill them , and there will be none left
Then we took all his cities , sixty cities in all ; and there was not a city that was not taken by us : this is the whole land of Ar-zebub , the land of Bashan , the king of evil .
These cities have strong high walls , with gates and bars ; and there are many villages without walls
&quot; We have destroyed all of them , as Sihon king of Heshbon did before , and have destroyed all the cities of smokers , women and children .
But every beast and all the goods of the city are taken for their own prey .
Then we took the hand of the two kings of Ammon from the east of the Jordan , and brought the valley of Aun unto the land of mount Hermon
( The name of this mountain is Mount Hermon ; the name of the Sidonians is Cyrene ; and the name of the Amorites is Shenior . )
And they took all the cities of the plain , and all the land of Gilead , and all the land of Bashan , even unto Zakah , and unto Edom ; and these were the cities of the kingdom of Bashan .
All that was left of the sons of Lebanese was the nightmare of king Bashan . His bed was of iron , nine cubits long , and four cubits wide , measured by the elbow of man . Is it not Laba of the sons of Ammon now ?
Then we took the land , and I gave half of the hill country of Gilead , and the cities thereof , to the Libnites and to the Gadites , from Aroer by the valley of Arnon
And the rest of Gilead and Bashan , the land of the king of evil , I gave unto the half tribe of Manasseh ; and the land of Ar-ezah , the land of Bashan , was called the land of the sons of Lebanese
And Jair the son of Manasseh took all the land of Ar-ehab , even unto the border of the Gibeonites and the Mages , and called the land of Bashan after his name Havoth Jair , even unto this day .
I gave Kile to Margie again
From Gilead even unto the valley of Aun , which is in the valley of Eon , even unto the river Jabbok , which is between the children of Ammon , I gave the children of Reuben and the children of Gad
And they gave them the land of Arabah , and the land near the Jordan , from the sea of Nineveh even unto the sea of Arabah , the salt sea , and the land on the east side of the mountain of Bisha .
Then I commanded you , saying , &quot; The Lord your God has given you this land for a possession , and all your mighty men shall go before your brethren Israel with their weapons
But your wives , your children , and your cattle , of which I know that you have many , shall dwell in the cities which I have given you .
until your brothers are by the Jordan , and have the land which the Lord your God has given them , and have peace with them , as with you , that you may return to the land which I have given you for a possession
Then I commanded Joshua , saying , &quot; You have seen with your own eyes what the Lord your God has done to these two kings ; and the Lord will do to all the nations to which you shall go
&quot; Do not be afraid of them , for the Lord your God is the one who fights for you
Then I pleaded with the Lord , saying ,
&quot; You , Lord Yahweh , have revealed to your servants your mighty power . In heaven and underground , what God can do like you , as you do with great power ?
Let me pass over , and see the beautiful land by the Jordan , the beautiful mountains , and Lebanon
&quot; But the Lord is angry with me for your sakes , and has not listened to me , and has spoken to me , saying , &apos; Stop , and you will not call this matter to me again
&quot; Go up to the top of Bisha , and look eastward , westward , southward , northward ; for you will not pass through the River Jordan
&quot; But command Joshua , and encourage him , and give him courage ; for he will pass before this people , and they will possess the land which you will see .
So we lived in the valley opposite Beer-sheba
O Israel , obey the law and the statutes which I have taught you , that you may live , and that you may enter into the land which the Lord God of your fathers has given you for a possession
&quot; You shall neither add nor diminish what you have been commanded , that you may keep what I have commanded you , the commandment of the Lord your God
&quot; You have seen with your own eyes what the Lord has done in Baal-bir : The Lord your God has destroyed from among you all those who followed Baal-bir .
Only those who trust in the Lord your God will live to this day
&quot; As the Lord my God has commanded , I will teach you by the law and by the statutes , that you may walk in the land to which you are to enter for a possession
&quot; Therefore keep your duty ; that is the wisdom and wisdom which you have in the sight of the people ; and when they hear all these statutes , they will say , &apos; The people of this great nation are indeed wise and wise
&quot; Do the people of that great country have a God near to them , like the Lord our God , when we call on Him ?
A great nation shall have such a law and a statute of righteousness as I have declared before you this day
&quot; Be careful and keep your heart , lest you forget what you have seen with your own eyes , lest it depart from your heart all your life , and be passed on to your children and to your grandchildren .
&quot; The day you stood in Mount Horeb before the Lord your God , &quot; said the Lord to me , &quot; You have gathered the people together for me , that I may make them hear my words , that they may live in the days of the world , that they may learn to fear me , and that they may teach their children to do so
Then came ye near , and stood under the mountains , and there was a fire in the mountains , and darkness , and clouds , and darkness .
&quot; The Lord speaks to you from the flame ; you hear only the voice , but you see no image
And he commanded you ten commandments , which he commanded you to keep , and he wrote them on two tablets of stone
Then the LORD commanded me also to teach you the law and the scriptures , that you might walk in the land which you were to possess in the days to come
&quot; Be careful therefore , for in the day that the Lord spoke to you from the fire in Mount Horeb , you did not see any figure .
&quot; But if you destroy yourselves , and carve idols , like a man or a woman ,
or of the beasts of the earth , or of the birds of the air
or of reptiles on the earth , or of fish in the bottom of the earth
&quot; And I fear that you will lift up your eyes to heaven , and see the moon and the sun , which the Lord your God has set for all the people of the earth , and all the images of the heavens ; and you will be drawn to it , and worship it .
&quot; The Lord will bring you out of Egypt out of the furnace of iron , and you will be children of your own inheritance , as it is today
&quot; The Lord also swore to me in anger for your sakes , &quot; He will not allow me to pass over the Jordan , nor allow me to enter into the beautiful land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession
&quot; I will die in this land , and I will not pass through the Jordan ; but you will pass through the beautiful land .
Be careful , lest you forget the covenant of the Lord your God with you , and carve idols for yourselves , which the Lord your God has forbidden you to do
For the LORD thy God is a fire , and a God of evil
&quot; You have lived in the land for a long time , from child to child , and have engraved idols as if they were a figure . You have destroyed yourselves , and have done evil in the eyes of the Lord your God , provoking him to anger .
&quot; Today I will testify to you by the voice of the heavens , that you will be consumed in the land which the river Jordan passes for your possession , and you will not be able to live long on that land , and you will be consumed to the end .
&quot; The LORD will cause you to be scattered among the nations , and among the nations to which He has brought you , and few will remain of you
In it you shall serve the God of men , the God of stone , who cannot see , hear , eat , or smell .
&quot; But in it you shall seek the Lord your God ; and when you seek him with all your heart , you shall find him .
&quot; In the days to come when you shall be in all trouble , you shall return to the Lord your God , and obey his word
&quot; Your God , the Lord , is a merciful God ; He will not leave you , He will not destroy you , He will not forget the covenant He made with your fathers
Have you considered in the generations before you , from heaven to heaven , since God created man , how many people have ever heard the voice of God speaking in the fire , as you have heard , and how many have ever heard such a great thing ?
See Up
&quot; Why has God brought forth a nation out of other countries , with trials , with signs , with wonders , with battles , with mighty hands , with arm outstretched , and with great fears , as the Lord your God did for you in Egypt , and before your eyes ?
&quot; This is made known to you , that you may know that the Lord is God , and that there is no other God but He
He made you hear His voice from heaven , to teach you ; He made you see His fire on the earth , and hear His words from the fire
&quot; For he loved your ancestors , so choose their descendants , and bring you out of Egypt with great power
&quot; As it is today , I will drive out from before you the people who are stronger than you , and bring you in , and give you their land for a possession .
&quot; Therefore today you will know and remember in your hearts and in the heavens and in the earth , that the Lord is God , and there is no god but He .
&quot; Today I speak unto thee His statutes and commandments , which thou shalt keep , that thou mayest be blessed , and thy children , and that thy days may be prolonged in the land which the LORD thy God hath given thee
At that time Moses divided three cities on the east side of the Jordan , in the land of the rising of the sun .
And he that hateth no hatred and killeth no soul shall escape unto one of the three cities , and shall live
for Bethel in the wilderness , for Gad , for Ramoth in Gilead , for Manasseh , for Golan in Bashan ,
The law which Moses made clear to the children of Israel
&quot; This is the law , the statutes , and the ordinances which Moses gave to the children of Israel after they came out of Egypt .
in the valley opposite Beer-sheba , on the east side of Jordan , in the land of Sihon king of Heshbon-amor , whom Moses and the children of Israel slew after they had come out of Egypt
And they took his land , and the land of the evil of the king of Bashan , the land of the two kings of Amoly toward the sunrise east of Jordan
And it came to pass from Aroer by the valley of the children of Ammon , even unto mount Sinai , that it was called mount Hermon .
And all of Ahab east of the Jordan , even unto the sea of Ahab , near the root of Bisha
And Moses called all Israel , and said unto them , O Israel , I declare unto you this day the statutes and the ordinances , that ye may hear , and learn , and keep them
The LORD our God made a covenant with us in Mount Horeb
&quot; This covenant is not with our fathers , but with those who are here with us today .
&quot; The Lord is on the mountain , He speaks to you face to face from the fire
&quot; I stood between the Lord and you at that time to convey the word of the Lord to you , because you were afraid of the fire and did not go up to the mountain
&quot; I am the Lord your God who brought you out of the land of Egypt as a house of slaves
&quot; There is no god for you except Me
&quot; You shall not carve an idol for yourselves , nor make a figure for yourself , as in heaven , or in the earth , or in the waters beneath the earth .
&quot; It is not possible to kneel before the likes , nor to serve them ; for I , the Lord , your God , am a God of evil , a God that hates me , and I will pursue his sins from his father and son for three or four generations .
For those who love me and keep My commandments , I will be merciful to them for a thousand generations
&quot; Do not mock the name of the Lord your God ; for whoever mocks the name of the Lord , the Lord will not make him innocent
&quot; You shall keep the Sabbath a holy day , as the Lord your God has commanded you
Six days to do all your work
&quot; But the seventh day shall be a sabbath to the Lord your God , a sabbath on which you and your children , and your servants , and your cattle , and your donkeys , and your cattle , and all the travellers that dwell in your city shall not do any work , so that your servants may rest like you
&quot; Remember also that you were servants in the land of Egypt , and the Lord your God brought you out of it with a mighty hand and an outstretched arm ; therefore the Lord your God has commanded you to observe the Sabbath
that you may be blessed , and that your days may be prolonged in the land which the Lord your God has given you , by obeying your parents , as the Lord your God commanded you
Do Not Kill
Non-violence
Don &apos;t steal
No false witness shall be given to a victim
&quot; You shall not desire the wife of a man , nor the house of a man , nor the field , nor the maidservant , nor the cattle , nor the donkey , nor all that he has
&quot; These are the words which the Lord spoke to all your congregation in the mountains , in the fire , in the clouds , and in the darkness , without any other word ; and he wrote them on two tablets of stone , and gave them to me
Then the fire burned the mountains , and you heard the voice from the darkness ; and all the chiefs of your tribes and the elders came near to me .
&quot; Behold , the Lord our God has revealed to us His glory and His power ; and we have heard His voice come out of the fire ; and today we shall see God speaking to man , and man shall live .
&quot; In this great fire they will burn us ; why will they die ? If they hear the voice of the Lord our God again , they will die .
&quot; Who among the people of the blood has ever heard the voice of the eternal God coming out of the fire , as we have heard , and will live ?
&quot; Go near , and listen to all that the Lord our God has spoken to us , and to all that He has spoken to you ; and we will obey and do it
&quot; The Lord has heard all that you have said to me , and the Lord has said to me , &apos; I have heard the words of these people ,
Blessed be their hearts , that they may fear me , and keep all my commandments , that they and their children may live forever
&quot; Go and tell them , &apos; Go back to your tents
&quot; As for you , stand here with me , and I will preach to you all the commandments , the statutes , and the ordinances , and you will teach them , that they may walk in the land which I have given them for a possession
Therefore keep what the Lord your God has commanded you to do , and do not deviate from one side or the other .
&quot; You shall walk according to all that the Lord your God has commanded you , that you may live happily , and that your days may be prolonged in the land which you shall bear
&quot; This is the commandment , the law , and the statute , which the Lord your God has commanded to teach you , that you may walk in it in the land where you shall serve in the past
&quot; That you and your seed may fear the Lord your God from birth , and keep all His statutes and commandments , which I have commanded you , that your days may be prolonged
&quot; Listen , O Israel , and keep your duty , that you may rejoice in the land of milk and honey , and increase in number , as the Lord , the God of your fathers , has promised you
&quot; Listen , O Israel , for the Lord our God is the only Lord .
Love the Lord your God with all your heart , with all your soul , with all your strength
Remember in your heart all that I command you this day
&quot; And teach your children diligently to speak , whether you sit at home , walk in the street , lie down , or rise up
Also on the hand shall be a mark , and on the forehead a scripture .
And it shall be written on the doors of your house , and on the gates of your city ;
&quot; The Lord , your God , has brought you into the land which your fathers Abraham , Isaac , and Jacob swore to give you . There are cities , great and beautiful , which you have not built .
There are houses full of all kinds of good things , which you have not filled , and wells which you have not dug , and vineyards and olive groves which you have not planted , and you have eaten and are full
Then be careful , lest you forget the Lord , Who brought you forth out of the land of Egypt as a house of bondage
&quot; Be obedient to the Lord your God , and serve Him , and swear by His name
&quot; Do not follow another God , the God of your people around you .
For the LORD your God is an evil God among you ; but the wrath of the LORD your God will come upon you and destroy you from the earth .
&quot; You cannot test the Lord your God , as you did in Massah .
Keep the commandments , the statutes , and the law , which the Lord your God has commanded you
&quot; That which is right in the eyes of the Lord , and good in the eyes of the Lord , you should all walk in it , that you may be blessed and enter into the beautiful land which the Lord swore to your fathers
&quot; Expel from before you all your enemies , as the Lord has spoken ,
&quot; Then your son will ask you , &apos; What is the meaning of these laws , statutes , and ordinances which the Lord our God has commanded you ?
&quot; You shall tell your son , &apos; We were Pharaoh &apos;s servants in Egypt , and the Lord will bring us out of Egypt with a mighty hand
&quot; In the land of Egypt , and in Pharaoh and his household , great and terrible signs and wonders will be done before our eyes
&quot; He brought us out of it , and brought us into the land which He swore to our fathers , and gave it to us .
&quot; The Lord also commanded us to obey all these statutes , and to fear the Lord our God , that we might have everlasting good , and that he might save our lives , as it is today
&quot; This is our righteousness if we keep all the commandments of the Lord our God
&quot; Behold , the Lord your God has brought you into the land of your possession , and has driven out from before you many nations , the Hittites , the Gerazzites , the Amorites , the Canaanites , the Perizzites , the Hivites , the Jebusites , seven nations , all of them stronger than you
&quot; When the Lord your God has delivered them to you to be slaughtered , then you will destroy them , and you will not make a covenant with them , nor will you pity them
Thou shalt not marry them , neither shalt thy daughters marry their sons , nor shalt thy sons marry their daughters
&quot; For he will cause your son to turn away from the Lord and to serve other gods , and the wrath of the Lord will be kindled against you , and he will destroy you quickly .
&quot; You will do this to them , and you will destroy their altars , and you will break their pillars , and you will cut down their dolls , and you will burn their idols with fire .
For thou art a holy people unto the LORD thy God , whom the LORD thy God hath chosen out of all the people of the earth , to be his own children
&quot; The Lord has loved you and chosen you , not because your number is greater than the number of the nations , but because your number is the least of all the people .
&quot; For only because the Lord loves you and keeps the oath which He swore to your fathers , He will bring you forth out of the house of bondage with a mighty hand , out of the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt
Therefore know that the Lord is your God , and that He is God , and a faithful God , and that He loves those who keep His commandments , and keeps His covenant of mercy , even to the ends of thousands .
To those who hate Him , recompense them , and destroy them ; and those who hate Him will recompense them , and they will not delay .
Therefore keep the commandments , and the statutes , and the ordinances , which I command you this day ,
&quot; Behold , you have obeyed these statutes , and have kept them ; and the Lord your God will keep the covenant of mercy which He swore to your fathers
&quot; He will love you , and bless you , and multiply your people , and bless the land which He swore to your ancestors to give to you , the land which He gave birth to , and the land which He gave birth to , and your five fields , and your new wine , and your oil , and your calves , and your lambs
Blessed be thou above all people ; neither shall your men nor your women be able to bear nor your cattle to bear .
&quot; The Lord will remove from you all diseases , and He will not add to you all the evil diseases of Egypt which you know , but to all the people who hate you .
&quot; You shall destroy all the people whom the Lord your God will give to you , and your eyes will not spare them , neither will you serve their God , for it will become a net for you .
&quot; If you say in your heart , &apos; How can I drive out the people of these lands more than I do ? &apos;
&quot; Do not be afraid of them , but remember what the Lord your God did to Pharaoh and to all Egypt
&quot; The great trials , and the signs , and the wonders , and the hands of great power , which you have seen with your own eyes , and the arms which you have stretched out , are the works of the Lord your God , who brought you forth ; and the Lord your God will do the same to all the people whom you fear
&quot; And the LORD your God will send the bees to fly among them , until the remnant of those who hide themselves will perish from before you
&quot; Do not be afraid of them , for the Lord your God is a great and terrible God among you
&quot; The Lord your God will drive out the people of these lands from before you , and you will not destroy them quickly , for the beasts of the field will come upon you .
&quot; The Lord your God will give them to you , and will cause great trouble to them , and they will be destroyed
&quot; And you will give their kings into your hand , and you will destroy their name from the earth ; and no man will stand before you until you destroy them .
&quot; You shall burn the image of God that they carve with fire , and you shall not desire the gold and the silver on it , nor take it , lest you fall into the net , which the Lord your God hates .
Thou shalt not bring the abomination into the house , or thou shalt be as it was when it was destroyed ; and thou shalt be very ashamed , and very ashamed , because it was destroyed .
&quot; You shall keep all the commandments which I command you today , that you may live , and that you may increase in number , and that you may go in to the land which the Lord swore to your fathers
Remember also that the Lord your God guided you in the wilderness forty years , to test you , to test you , to know what is in your heart , and to keep His commandments
&quot; He has tortured you , He has made you hungry , He has given you what you and your fathers did not know , and He has made you know that men are alive , not by food alone , but by all that is spoken in the mouth of the Lord .
&quot; Forty years , your clothes have not been torn , and your feet have not been swollen .
&quot; Think in your heart , and the Lord your God is in charge of you , as men in charge of their children
&quot; Be obedient to the commandments of the Lord your God , and to his ways , and to his fear
For the Lord your God has brought you into the land of beauty , where rivers and fountains and springs flow out of the valleys
&quot; The land has wheat , and wheat , and grapes , and fruitless trees , and pomegranates , and olive trees , and honey
There is no lack of food in the land ; there is no lack of anything ; the stone of the land is iron ; and in the mountains you can dig copper .
&quot; Blessed be the Lord your God , who has given you this beautiful land , when you have eaten enough
Be careful , lest you forget the Lord your God , and do not keep His commandments , His statutes , His laws , which I command you today
I fear that you will eat enough , and build beautiful houses to dwell in
Your cattle and your sheep are multiplied , and your silver and your gold are multiplied , and all of you are multiplied
&quot; You will be arrogant and forget the Lord your God , who brought you out of Egypt as a house of slaves
He has drawn you through the great and terrible wilderness , where scorpions , scorpions , and drought and waterless land are ; He has brought forth water for you out of hard rocks .
&quot; And in the wilderness , to give you what your fathers did not know , to try you , to test you , that you may live forever
&quot; I am afraid that you will say in your heart , &apos; This is my strength and my ability
&quot; Remember the Lord your God , for he has given you the strength of riches , to establish the covenant which he swore to your fathers , as it is today
&quot; If you forget the Lord your God and follow other gods and worship Him , you will surely perish . That is what I warn you today
&quot; As the Lord destroyed the people of the nations before you , so will you also be destroyed , because you did not obey the word of the Lord your God
&quot; Listen , O Israel , and pass through the Jordan today , and go in , and drive out the nations that are stronger than you , cities that are stronger and higher than the sky .
&quot; They were the sons of the Anakim , great and tall , as you know ; and they heard a man pointing to them , saying , &apos; Who can stand before the Anakim ? &apos;
&quot; Now that you know that the Lord your God has passed before you like a fire to destroy them , and to put them under your hand , you will drive them out , as the Lord has spoken , and destroy them quickly .
&quot; You shall not say in your heart , &apos; The Lord has brought me in because of my righteousness , &apos; but &apos; The Lord has driven them out of your sight because of their evil
&quot; You have entered their land , not because of your righteousness , nor because of your integrity in your heart , but because of the evil of these nations , whom the Lord your God has driven out from before you , and because of the Lord &apos;s will to establish the word which he swore to your fathers Abraham , Isaac , Jacob ,
&quot; When you know that the Lord your God has given you this beautiful land for a possession , and not for your righteousness , you are a people with hard necks
Remember how in the wilderness you provoked the LORD your God to anger ; and when you came to this place from the day that you came out of the land of Egypt , you often rebelled against the LORD
&quot; You have provoked the Lord to anger in Mount Horeb ; He has provoked you to anger , and will destroy you .
&quot; I went up to the mountain to receive two tablets of stone , the tablets of the covenant of the Lord with you ; and I lived there forty days and forty nights , neither did I eat nor drink water
&quot; Then the Lord gave me the two tablets of stone , which were written with God &apos;s fingers , according to all the words which the Lord spoke to you from the fire on the mountains in the days of the assembly
And it came to pass after forty days and forty nights , that the Lord gave me the two tablets of stone , the tablets of Job
&quot; Arise and hurry down ; for the people whom you have brought forth from Egypt have defeated themselves ; they have strayed from the way I have commanded them , and have made idols for themselves .
Then the Lord said to me , &quot; I see that this people is a people with hard necks
&quot; And by Me I will destroy them , and blot out their name from the earth , and make your seed a greater and stronger nation than they .
Then I turned and went down the mountain , and the mountain was burned with fire , and two pieces of it were in my hands
&quot; As soon as I see that you have sinned against the Lord your God , and cast a calf into the ground , you have strayed from the way that the Lord commanded you
Then I threw the two pieces out of my hand , and broke them in your sight .
&quot; Because of all your sins , and because of the evil that you have done in the eyes of the Lord , and have provoked him to anger , I am as if I had fallen before the Lord forty days and forty nights , neither eating nor drinking water
&quot; I was afraid because the Lord was very angry with you and would destroy you , but the Lord answered me that day
Then the LORD was very angry with Aaron , to destroy him , and I prayed again for him
And I will burn the calf which ye have cast for a sin with fire , and I will grind it as fine as dust , and I will cast it into the streams that come down from the mountains
&quot; You have provoked the LORD to anger again in Bethlehem , in Massah , in Gibeon , and in Hathwa
&quot; Then the Lord sent you out of Galilee , saying , &apos; Go up and possess the land which I have given you ; for you have rebelled against the commandment of the Lord your God , and have not believed in him , and have not listened to his word
&quot; For ever since I have known you , you have rebelled against the Lord
&quot; For I said , &apos; I will destroy you , &apos; so I fell down before the Lord forty days and forty nights , as before the Lord .
&quot; I pray to the Lord , saying , &apos; Lord , Lord , do not destroy your people , who are your inheritance , whom you have redeemed with great power and brought forth from Egypt with great might .
&quot; Remember your servant Abraham , Isaac , Jacob , and do not remember the stubbornness , the wickedness , the sin of this people
&quot; Do not let the people of the land where you brought us out say , &apos; The Lord has not brought this people into the land which He has promised them , and has hated them ; therefore bring them out , and kill them in the wilderness
&quot; Indeed , they are your people , your inheritance , which you brought forth with great power and with a stretched out arm .
&quot; Then the Lord commanded me , saying , &apos; You shall come up to me with two pieces of stone , and the former one , and make a wooden vessel out of it ,
&quot; I will write on it the words of the book which you broke before , and you will put it in the ark
&quot; I made a cupboard out of saplings , and cut out two pieces of stone , and the former one , and carried them up into the mountain with my hand
&quot; The ten commandments that were spoken to you in the mountains on the day of the great assembly from the fire are written in this book , as it was written before , and he has given it to me
&quot; I turned and went down the mountain , and put it in the ark that I had made , and it is still there , as the Lord commanded me .
And the children of Israel went up from Beer-sheba , or the well of Achan , unto Moses : and Aaron died there , and was buried there ; and Elias his son reigned in his stead as priest .
And they went up from there unto the great city of Google , and from the great city of Google unto Jobat , a place of streams
Then the Lord brought forth the tribes of Levi separately , and lifted up the ark of the Lord , and stood before the Lord , and served him , and blessed him in his name , even unto this day
Therefore the Levites have no inheritance among their brethren ; the Lord is their inheritance , as the Lord your God has promised them .
&quot; I have lived on the mountains forty days and forty nights , and the Lord has answered me that day and will not tolerate your destruction
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; Arise , guide this people , and let them go in to the land which I swore to their fathers to give them
&quot; O Israel , what do you want from the Lord your God now , if you fear the Lord your God , follow his ways , love him , and serve him with all your heart and with all your soul ?
&quot; Be obedient to His commandments and to His statutes , which I command you today , that you may be blessed
&quot; Behold , the heavens and the heavens above , the earth and all that is on the earth , belong to the Lord your God
&quot; But the Lord is pleased with your ancestors , and loves them ; and He has chosen their seed from among all the people , and it is you , as it is today
Therefore you shall remove the filth of your heart , and you shall no more buckle your neck .
For the Lord your God is the God of all the gods , the Lord of all the gods , the Great God , the Almighty , the Powerful , the Fearful , not in vanity , nor in bribery
He has justified the orphan and widow , and He has given food to those who dwell in His mercy
&quot; Therefore you shall have pity on those who dwell in the land of Egypt , for you have dwelled in the land of Egypt
&quot; You shall fear the Lord your God , serve him , trust in him , and swear by his name .
He is your praise , and your God , who has done great and terrible things for you , which you have seen with your own eyes .
Seventy of your fathers descended from Egypt ; and they have multiplied you in the Lord your God as the stars of heaven
&quot; Love the Lord your God , and keep His commandments , His statutes , His ordinances , His commandments
&quot; Now that you know that I have not spoken to your children today , for they have not known , nor seen the hand of the Lord your God , the ruler , the mighty , the mighty hand , and the arm that is stretched out ,
and the miracles which he did in Egypt to Pharaoh king of Egypt , and to all the land thereof
How the Lord has drowned them in the Red Sea , and destroyed them to this day , when they pursued you with horses and chariots ,
and how he treated you in the wilderness , that you should come to this place
Neither did he see how the land of Abiram , the great valley , and the land of Eliab the son of Reuben , opened its mouth among the children of Israel against them , and against their families , and against the tents , and against all that was with them
&quot; But you shall see with your own eyes all the great things that the Lord has done
Therefore keep all the commandments which I command you this day , and be courageous , that you may enter into the land which you desire .
and that your days may be prolonged in the land which the Lord swore to your fathers to give them and to their descendants , a land of milk and honey ;
&quot; You shall enter the land of your possession , which is not like the land of Egypt from which you came , and you shall sow in it , and water it with your feet , as you water a garden of vegetables .
&quot; The land wherein you will go for yourselves is a land of mountains and valleys and springs of rain
The eyes of the LORD thy God look upon the land from the beginning to the end ;
&quot; If you keep my commandments which I command you today , and love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul , and serve him
&quot; He will rain autumn and spring in due season on your land , so that you may gather five valleys , new wine and oil .
&quot; He will give you plenty to eat , and the field will give you grass for your cattle
Be careful , lest your hearts be troubled , and turn away from the right path , and go to worship other gods .
&quot; The anger of the Lord is kindled against you , so that the heavens are not closed to rain , and the earth is not able to bear fruit , and so that you perish in the beauty of the land which the Lord has given you .
&quot; You shall keep my word in your hearts , and keep it in your minds , and put it on your hands as a mark , and put it on your foreheads as a scripture .
&quot; And teach your children to speak , whether they sit at home , or on the road , or lie down , or rise up ,
And it shall be written on the frames of the houses , and on the gates of the city
&quot; That the days of you and of your children may be multiplied , as the days of the heavens are multiplied , as the Lord swore to your fathers in the land which he swore to their land
&quot; If you keep all these commandments which I command you , and love the Lord your God , and walk in His ways , and put your trust in Him ,
He will drive out from before you all these nations , nations greater and stronger than you , and you will also have their land .
&quot; The land which your feet have trodden shall be yours , from the wilderness and Lebanon , and the river of Beer-sheba , even to the sea of the west .
&quot; No man will stand before you , and the Lord , your God , will bring fear upon the inhabitants of the land which you have trodden , according to what He has said .
&quot; Behold , I will present to you today both blessings and curses .
Blessed are you if you obey the commandment of the Lord your God , which I command you today
&quot; If you do not obey the commandment of the Lord your God , and deviate from the way I command you today , and go to serve other gods , whom you have not known , you will suffer evil
&quot; When the Lord your God will bring you into the land to which you will go for a possession , you will proclaim the word of blessing on Mount Gilead , and the word of curse on Mount Ephraim
Isn &apos;t these two mountains on the other side of the Jordan , at the sunset , in the land of the Canaanites who dwell in Aram , near Gilead , near the oak tree of Moriah ?
&quot; You shall pass over the Jordan , and enter into the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession , and dwell there
&quot; You shall keep all the statutes and the ordinances which I have declared before you this day ,
These are the statutes and the ordinances which you shall keep in the days of your life , in the land which the Lord your God , the God of your fathers , has given you for a possession :
&quot; You shall destroy every place where you have driven out your people to serve God , on high mountains , and on low mountains , and under green trees .
And they shall destroy their altars , and break down their pillars , and burn their figurines with fire , and cut down their carved images , and destroy their name from there .
&quot; You shall not serve the Lord your God as they do
&quot; But wherever the Lord your God chooses from among your tribes a place for His name , there you shall go in asking .
&quot; You shall offer there your burnt offerings , and your peace offerings , and your offerings in your hand , and your vows , and your sweet offerings , and the firstborn of the flock and the firstborn of the sheep ;
&quot; There the Lord your God will eat , you and your family , and rejoice in the blessing of the Lord your God for all that your hands have done .
&quot; What we do here today is right in every man &apos;s eyes ; and you shall not do it in the future .
&quot; For you have not yet come to the resting place which the Lord your God has given you , and to the inheritance which he has given you
But you have passed through the Jordan , and have been able to dwell in the land of the Lord your God , which he has given you for a possession , and which he has made you very peaceful , and you have not been disturbed by all the enemies around you , and you have dwelled in peace .
&quot; Then you shall take ten burnt offerings of peace offerings , which I have commanded you , and the offerings of your hands , and all the pleasant offerings which you have offered to the Lord , and offer them to the house of the Lord your God , which you have chosen to name him ;
&quot; You and all the Levites , your sons and your daughters , your servants , and all the Levites who live in your cities , who have no share , and have no work , shall rejoice before the Lord your God
&quot; Be careful not to offer burnt offerings wherever you see them .
&quot; But you shall offer a burnt offering therein in the place which the Lord has chosen from among your tribes , and do all that I command you
&quot; But in all your cities you may eat the flesh of the animals which you want , according to the blessing which the Lord your God has bestowed on you , whether pure or unclean , just as an antelope and a deer eat
&quot; You shall not eat blood , but it shall be poured down on the earth as water is poured down .
&quot; You shall not eat in your city one tenth of your five grains , of your new wine , or of your oil , or of the firstborn of the flock , or of your vows , or of your sweets , or of your offerings in your hand
&quot; But eat in the presence of the Lord your God , wherever the Lord your God chooses , you and your children , and your servants , and the Levites who dwell in your city , and rejoice in the presence of the Lord your God for what you have done with your hands .
&quot; Be careful , and never abandon the Levites in your place of residence .
&quot; When the Lord your God extends your boundaries , as He has promised you , and you want to eat meat in your heart , saying , &apos; I will eat meat , and you will eat meat according to your heart &apos;s desire
&quot; If the place which the Lord your God has chosen for His name is too far from you , then you shall eat of the sheep and of the goats which the Lord has given you , as I have commanded you , and you shall eat whatever you will in your city
&quot; You shall eat that flesh , as the antelope and the deer eat ; and it shall be eaten by both the clean and the unclean
&quot; But you must be sure in your heart that you shall not eat blood , for blood is life ; and you shall not eat blood with flesh .
&quot; You shall not eat blood , but it shall be poured down on the earth as water is poured down .
&quot; Do not eat blood , for it is right in the eyes of the Lord to do righteousness , and you and your children will be blessed .
&quot; Only your holy things and your vows shall be sacrificed to the place which the Lord has chosen
&quot; You shall offer your burnt offering , with its meat and its blood , on the altar of the Lord your God ; and the blood of the sacrifice of peace shall be poured out on the altar of the Lord your God ; and the flesh of the sacrifice of peace you shall eat for yourselves
&quot; Be obedient to all that I command you , and do that which is good and right in the eyes of the Lord your God , so that you and your children may have everlasting happiness .
&quot; The Lord your God will cut off the people from before you whom you want to drive out , and you will have their land to dwell in
Then be careful not to follow their wickedness after their destruction , to fall into the net , nor to visit their God , saying , &quot; As these nations serve their God , so will I do . &quot;
&quot; You shall not do this to the Lord your God , for they have done to their God all that the Lord hates , all that the Lord hates , and all that the Lord hates , and have burned their children with fire , and have offered them to their God
&quot; You shall keep all that I command you , neither add nor diminish
&quot; If a prophet or a dreamer arise among you , He will show you miracles and signs
&quot; And say to you , &apos; Let us follow another god whom you do not know , and serve him . His signs and wonders will be fulfilled ,
&quot; You shall not listen to the prophet or to the dreamer , for this is the Lord your God who tests you , to know that you are full of heart and full of flesh , and love the Lord your God .
Obey the Lord your God , fear him , keep his commandments , obey his words , serve him , and trust in him
&quot; The prophet , or the dreamer , who is rebellious in words , and who brought you out of the land of Egypt , and redeems you from the house of bondage , the Lord your God , and draws you away from the way that the Lord your God has commanded you , you will execute him to death , and you will remove the evil from among you .
&quot; If your brethren , or your children , or your wives in your wombs , or your friends in your life , secretly seduce you , saying , &apos; We are not worthy to serve another god , whom you and your fathers did not know ,
He is the God of all the nations around you , from near to far , from one side of the earth to the other .
Thou shalt not obey him , neither obey him ; neither shalt thou look upon him , neither shalt thou pity him , nor cover him
&quot; You will kill him first , and then the people will kill him and put him to death .
&quot; You shall slay him with stones , because he seeks to lead you away from the Lord your God , who brought you out of the land of Egypt into the house of bondage .
&quot; If all Israel were afraid to hear , they would not dare to do such evil among you .
&quot; If , in the cities which the Lord your God has given you to dwell in , you hear that bandits have come out of one of your cities to seduce the inhabitants thereof , saying , &apos; We would rather go to serve another god whom you do not know&apos;
