&quot; You shall not eat anything that has wings , which is unclean with you .
&quot; You shall eat every clean bird .
&quot; You shall not eat that which has died of itself , nor give it to those who dwell in your city , nor sell it to strangers ; for you are a holy people to the Lord your God ; and you shall not boil the lambs with the milk of the Lamb &apos;s mother
&quot; You shall bring forth one tenth of a tenth of what you sow , that is , what your field produces every year .
&quot; You shall eat of your five grains , of your new wine , and of your tenth of your oil , and of the firstborn of the flock , in the presence of the Lord your God , the place which He has chosen for His name ; so that you may fear the Lord your God when you learn
&quot; When the Lord your God blesses you , and the place which the Lord your God chooses to stand in His name is too far from you , and the way too long , so that you cannot bring it into it
Then you shall exchange it for silver , and you shall wrap it up , and take it in your hand , and go to the place which the Lord your God chooses
&quot; You shall buy with this money whatever you will , whether it be cattle or sheep , or wine , or spirits , whatever you will ; and you and your families shall eat and drink in the presence of the Lord your God .
&quot; You shall not forsake the Levites who dwell in your city , for they have no share among you .
&quot; In the last year of three years you shall take one tenth of the inheritance of this year and store it in your city .
&quot; The Levites , who have no share in your city , and the inhabitants of your city , and the orphans and widows , will come and eat enough ; and the Lord your God will bless you in all that you do in your hand
Every year at the end of seven years , you will be exempted
Thus is the dispensation of exemption ; and whosoever is exempted by the debts of his neighbour , he shall not seek vengeance on his neighbour and on his brethren , for the year of the Lord &apos;s exemption has been proclaimed .
&quot; If you lend to a foreigner , you may pursue him ; but if you lend to your brothers , whatever it may be , you shall be exempt .
&quot; If you listen to the word of the Lord your God , and keep all the commandments which I command you today , there will be no poor among you ; and the Lord will bless you greatly in the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession .
