For the Lord , your God , will bless you according to the blessing which He has promised you ; and you will lend to many nations , but not to them ; and you will rule over many nations , but they will not rule over you .
If there be a poor man among your brethren in any of the cities which the Lord your God has given you , you shall not bear with patience , nor shake your hand , nor help your poor brethren
Let your hands be loose from him , and lend him what he lacks , and fill him with what he lacks .
Be careful , lest your heart sink , saying , &quot; The seventh year of your exemption is near , and you will look upon your poor brother with evil eyes , and you will not give him anything , so that his sin will be on you , because you have asked the Lord . &quot;
&quot; You shall not grieve for him , nor grieve for his time ; for the Lord your God will bless you in all that you do and in all that you do in your hand .
&quot; I have commanded you , saying , &apos; Let your brothers in your land , who are poor and needy , give up their hands , for the poor who were born on the earth will perish forever .
&quot; If there is a Hebrew man among your brethren , or a Hebrew woman sold to you , and serves you six years , let him go forth free until the seventh year .
When you give him liberty , you cannot leave him empty of hands .
&quot; As the Lord your God has blessed you , so you shall bless him also from among your flocks , from among your fields , from among your winepresses
Remember that you were servants in the land of Egypt , and that the Lord your God will redeem you ; therefore I command you this thing today
&quot; If he says to you , &apos; I will not leave you , because he loves you and your house , and because he is good in you
&quot; Take a cone , and pierce his ears through the door ; and he will be your servant for ever ; and so will you do as a maidservant .
&quot; When you give him liberty , there shall be no hardship for him ; for he has served you six years twice as much as a hired servant ; and the Lord your God will bless you in all that you do .
&quot; The firstborn of your flock and the firstborn of your sheep shall be holy to the Lord your God , and the firstborn of the flock shall not sow in his land , and the firstborn of the sheep shall not shave .
&quot; You and your household shall eat of the firstborn every year in the place of your choice before the Lord your God .
&quot; If a man is born with any infirmity , he shall not give it to the Lord your God , as a lame man or a blind man , with any evil infirmity
&quot; You shall eat in your city , and the clean and the unclean shall eat , as the antelope and as the deer eat
&quot; You shall not eat his blood , but it shall be poured down on the earth as water .
Take heed to the month of Assyria , and observe the Passover to the Lord your God ; for the Lord your God brought you out of Egypt in the night of Assyria .
&quot; You shall offer the Passover sacrifice to the Lord your God from among the flocks and the sheep , in the place which the Lord has chosen for His name
&quot; You shall not eat of this sacrifice any bread that is unleavened ; but in seven days you shall eat of the unleavened bread , the bitter bread , that you may remember for a lifetime the days when you came out of Egypt
Ye shall not meet yeast in your four quarters for seven days ; neither shall the meat offered in the first night remain until the morning .
&quot; You shall not offer the Passover in the cities which the Lord your God has given you
&quot; Only when the Lord your God chooses to set up his house in his name , at night and at day , when you come out of Egypt , to offer the Passover ,
&quot; When you have roasted the meat in the place which the Lord your God has chosen , you shall return to your tent in the morning .
&quot; You shall eat unleavened bread six days , and on the seventh day you shall keep a solemn meeting with the Lord your God , and you shall not do any work .
&quot; You shall count seven and seven days from the time you laid the sickle and harvested the grain , seven and seven days in all .
&quot; You shall keep seven and seven festivals of sweetness in your hands , according to the blessing which the Lord your God has given you , and offer them before the Lord your God
&quot; You and your children , and your maids , and the Levites who dwell in your city , and those who dwell among you , and the orphans and widows , shall rejoice in the name of the Lord your God , which he has chosen , in the presence of the Lord your God .
Remember also that thou wast a servant in Egypt , and that thou shouldest keep these statutes
&quot; You shall keep the Sabbath seven days , after you have stored up the fields and the wine of the vineyard .
&quot; You and your children and your maids and the Levites who dwell in your city , and those who dwell therein , and the orphans and widows , shall rejoice at the time of the Sabbath
&quot; You shall fast seven days before the Lord your God in the place which the Lord has chosen ; for the Lord your God will bless you in all your inheritance and in all that your hands do , and you will rejoice greatly .
&quot; You , all your sons , shall come to him three times a year , on the feast of yeast , on the seventy-seventh day , and on the sabbath of tents , in the place which the Lord your God has chosen ; but you shall not come to him empty-handed
Every man shall offer a gift according to his own strength , according to the blessing of the Lord your God
In the cities which the Lord your God has given you , you shall set up judges and magistrates , according to the tribes , and they shall judge the people according to righteousness .
Thou shalt not disregard integrity , neither shalt thou see the appearance of men , neither shalt thou be bribed : for bribery blindeth the eyes of the wise , and turneth away the words of the righteous .
&quot; You shall seek righteousness and righteousness , that you may live , and bear the land which the Lord your God has given you
&quot; You shall build an altar for the Lord your God ; and no tree shall be planted by the altar as a doll
&quot; You shall not set up a pillar for yourselves ; that is the wickedness of the Lord your God
&quot; You shall not give to the Lord your God any cattle or sheep with any infirmity or any disease , for that is the abomination of the Lord your God
&quot; In all the cities which the Lord your God has given you among you , whether men or women , do evil in the sight of the Lord your God , contrary to His covenant ,
&quot; It is not the Lord &apos;s commandment that you should go to other gods , or to the sun , or to the moon , or to the image of the sky
&quot; Someone has said to you , &apos; You have heard , and you will listen carefully ; indeed it is true , that this abomination will be done in Israel .
&quot; You shall bring the man or woman who has done this evil to the gates of the city , and slay him with a stone .
&quot; You shall testify by the mouth of two or three people , and he who is dead shall be put to death ; you cannot testify by the mouth of one person , and he shall be put to death .
&quot; The witness will first strike , and then the people will strike , and he will be put to death . Then you will remove the evil from among you .
&quot; When there is a dispute in your city , or bloodshed , or strife , or beatings , which you cannot break , you shall rise up to the place which the Lord your God has chosen
&quot; Go to the priests of the Levites and to the judges at that time , and ask them , and they will tell you what to say .
&quot; In the place which the Lord has chosen , where they teach you , you shall do according to all that they teach you , and keep your duty .
&quot; Act according to the law which they command you , and according to the judgments which they command you , and do not deviate from the right or the left .
&quot; If any man dare not obey the priest who stands before the Lord your God , or the judge , he will surely die , and he will remove the evil from Israel .
And all the people will hear fear , and will no longer dare to act
&quot; When you have received the land which the Lord your God has given you for your inheritance , if you say , &apos; I will reign over me like the kingdoms around me
&quot; You shall reign over whomever the Lord your God has chosen , and you shall reign over one of your brethren , and you shall not reign over anyone other than your brethren
&quot; But the king cannot add horses to himself , nor let the people go back to Egypt to add horses to him ; for the Lord has commanded you , saying , &apos; You shall not go back in that way . &apos; 
Neither shall he set up more wives for himself , for fear of his wickedness , nor shall he accumulate more money for himself
&quot; When he has risen to the throne , he will make a copy of it for himself before the priests of the Levites
to live there , to read and to learn to fear the Lord his God , and to keep all the words of this law and these statutes ,
so that he and his sons may dwell in the throne of Israel for ever and ever
&quot; The Levites , the priests , and all the tribes of the Levites , shall have no share in Israel , neither shall they eat anything that is profitable , but the burnt offering to the Lord , and all that they have given
&quot; They shall have no inheritance among their brethren ; the Lord is their inheritance , as the Lord promised them
&quot; This is the priest &apos;s portion from among the people . Whoever offers a cattle or a sheep for a sacrifice shall give the priest the fore legs and the cheeks and the spleen
&quot; The first five grains , new wine , and oil , and the first sheep &apos;s hair , shall be given to him .
&quot; For the Lord , your God , has chosen him out of your tribes , that he may serve him and his sons forever in the name of the Lord .
&quot; The Levites , whoever dwells in the city of Israel , whoever comes out of it , will go to the place which the Lord has chosen
