&quot; There is no man among you who causes his children to be burned with fire , nor is there any who does divination , vision , magic , and evil deeds .
who uses magic , who betrays demons , who practices sorcery , who transgresses the law of evil ,
&quot; Everyone who does these things is an abomination to the Lord ; therefore the Lord , your God , will drive them out from before you because of the abominations of the people
Thou shalt be perfect before the LORD thy God
&quot; Because all the nations that you are about to drive out listen to signs and to divination , and the Lord your God has never permitted you to do this
&quot; The Lord your God will raise up to you a prophet like me from among your brethren , and you will obey him
&quot; As in the days of your assembly in Mount Horeb , pray to the Lord your God , that you will no longer make me hear the voice of the Lord my God , nor see the great fire , lest I die
Then the Lord said to me , &quot; This is what they said
&quot; In the midst of their brethren I will raise up to them a prophet like yours , and I will convey to him what I have spoken , and he will convey to them all that I have commanded .
&quot; Whoever does not listen to what he says in my name , I will punish him
&quot; If a prophet trusts in my name , and says what I have not commanded him to say , or speaks in the name of another god , he will surely die .
&quot; How can we know what the Lord has not commanded , if you say in your heart ?
&quot; The prophet speaks in the name of the Lord , and if what he says does not come to fruition , neither will it come to fruition . This is not what the Lord has commanded , but what the prophet himself said , &quot; Do not fear him
&quot; When the LORD your God will cut off the people of the nations , the LORD your God will give you their land , and you will dwell in their cities and in their houses
&quot; You shall divide three cities in the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession
&quot; You shall divide the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession into three parts ; and you shall prepare a way for those who mislead people to flee into it .
&quot; The man who kills a wrongdoer escapes to a place where he can live , for that is the law ; and he who kills a man without hatred and without heart ,
&quot; It is as if a man and his neighbour went into the forest to cut down trees with one hand , and took an axe , and wished to cut down the trees ; and when he did not expect it , he took off his axe , and fled into the neighbourhood to die ; and he escaped to a city of those cities , and lived .
&quot; He who is not vengeful of blood will be pursued by fire in his heart , and he will be pursued by a far way to kill him ; for he should not die , for he hates not the slain .
&quot; Therefore I commanded you , saying , &apos; Separate three cities
&quot; If the Lord , your God , extends your borders , as He swore to your ancestors , He will give you all the land which He promised to your ancestors
&quot; If you will keep all the commandments which I command you today , and love the Lord your God , and keep his ways , then you will add three more cities outside of these three cities
&quot; Do not let the blood of the innocent flow in the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession ; for the sins of blood will be on you .
&quot; If a man hates his neighbour , and bury himself , and rise and slay him , and die , he shall flee to a city of these cities
&quot; The elders of this city will send a man and bring him out from there , and will put him to death in the hand of the vengeful .
Thou shalt not despise him , but remove the sin of innocent blood from Israel , that thou mayest be blessed
&quot; You shall not move the borders of your neighbours in the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession , as the ancients commanded you .
No man can testify by the mouth of one man , or by the mouth of two or three men , for whatsoever sin he has committed , or for whatsoever evil he has done , that he may judge .
