And you shall treat him as his brethren whom he desires to serve ; and thereby shall the evil be removed from among you .
&quot; They will be afraid when they hear it , and will not dare to do such evil among you again .
&quot; Your eyes will not spare , but you will pay for your life , eye for eye , tooth for tooth , hand for hand , foot for foot .
&quot; When you go out to fight with your enemies , you will see horses and carriages , and there will be more people than you . Do not be afraid of them , for the Lord your God who brought you out of the land of Egypt is with you .
&quot; When you stand up , the priest will proclaim it before the people .
He said , &quot; Listen , O Israel , for today you will fight against your enemies , without fear , without fear , without fear , and without fear because of them .
&quot; For the Lord your God is with you to fight for you against your enemies and to save you
&quot; The governor shall also proclaim to the people , &apos; Whoever builds houses and has not yet offered them , he may go home , for fear of his death , and others will go and offer them .
&quot; He who plants vineyards and does not use the fruit that he has harvested , he may go home , for he is afraid of death , and others will use him .
&quot; He who has appointed a wife , and has not yet married her , may go home , for fear that he will perish , and others may marry him
&quot; The governor will also proclaim to the people , &quot; Whoever is afraid and fears , he can go home , for fear that his brother &apos;s heart will digest , just as he did
