&quot; If a man has a son who is obstinate and rebellious , and does not obey his parents , even though they punish him , he does not obey
&quot; They will seize him , and bring him to the gate of the city , to the elders of the city .
&quot; They said to the elders , &quot; Our children are stubborn and rebellious , they do not listen to our words , they are addicted to good wine .
And all the people of this city shall slay him with stones ; and the evil shall be removed from among you ; and all Israel shall hear fear .
&quot; If a man commits a sin that is worthy of death and is put to death , you shall hang him on a tree
&quot; You shall not leave his body on the wood for the night , nor bury him on the day when it is necessary , lest you defile the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession ; for he who is hanged is cursed before God .
&quot; If you see your brother &apos;s cattle or sheep lost in their way , do not pretend to be blind , but bring them back to your brothers .
&quot; If your brother is far from you , or you do not know him , take him to your house , and stay there with you ; and when your brother comes to seek him , give him back .
&quot; If you meet any of your brothers , whether lost , or donkey , or clothed , do so , and do not pretend to be absent
&quot; If you see a brother &apos;s cattle or donkey falling on the road , do not pretend to be blind , but help him to pull it up
