You will never seek their peace and their benefit in your lifetime
Thou shalt not hate the Edomites , because they are thy brethren ; and the Egyptians , because thou didst dwell in their land
And their third generation shall enter into the congregation of the LORD
Thou shalt go forth against the enemy , and avoid evil from afar .
&quot; If there is a man among you who dreams unclean at night , he shall go out of the camp , and he shall not enter the camp .
He had to bathe himself in water by the evening and entered the camp until sunset
You should also set up a place for your convenience outside the camp
When you have prepared a shovel in your instruments , when you have gone out of the camp and drowned , use it to shovel the earth and turn around and cover yourself .
&quot; Because the Lord , your God , walks in your camps to save you and to hand over your enemies to you , so that your camps are holy , and he will not see the filth therein , and will leave you
&quot; If a servant takes away his master &apos;s hand and flees to you , you shall not deliver him to his master
&quot; He will dwell with you in it , and in your cities he will choose a pleasant place to dwell in ; and you shall not deceive him .
No prostitute shall be among the women of Israel , and no child shall be among the men of Israel .
&quot; You shall not bring into the house of the Lord your God the money of a prostitute or the price of a dog , for both of these are evil from the Lord your God .
&quot; You shall not profit from what you lend to your brothers , or from money , or from food , or from anything profitable
&quot; You can borrow to foreigners , but you cannot borrow to your brothers . Thus the Lord your God will bless you in the land which you will possess and in all that you will do in your hand .
&quot; You shall not delay in repaying what you have pledged to the Lord your God ; for the Lord your God will seek you , and you will be guilty if you do not repay .
If you do not , you are innocent .
&quot; Whatever comes out of your mouth is what you have promised , and what you have given willingly , that you may keep it , as you have promised the Lord your God .
&quot; When you enter the vineyards of your neighbours , you may eat the grapes at will , but you shall not put them in the dishes
&quot; When you enter the grass that stands in your neighbourhood , you may pick it with your hand , but you must not cut it with a sickle .
&quot; If a man , after he has married his wife , finds that something unreasonable is with him , and does not please him , he may write a letter in his hand , and send him away from his husband &apos;s house .
When a woman leaves her husband &apos;s house , she can marry another
&quot; If a widow hates him , and writes a decree in his hand , and sends him away from his husband &apos;s house , or marries him as a wife , he dies .
&quot; The former husband who sent him shall not marry him again after the woman has defiled him ; for that is the abomination of the Lord ; and the land which the Lord your God has given you shall not be defiled
A newly married man shall not go forth out of the army , nor trust in any public affairs , but he shall rest at home for a year , that his wife may rejoice .
&quot; You shall not take the whole stone of a man , or the stone above him , for it is the life of a man .
&quot; If a man meets a brother of Israel who has been kidnapped , and he has been slaved or sold , he will be put to death , and he will remove the evil from among you .
&quot; Be careful in the plague of the great leprosy , and keep all that the priests of the Levites have commanded you , and do it ; how have I commanded them , and how have you done it ?
&quot; Remember what the Lord your God did in the way to Miley , after he had remembered Egypt
&quot; Whatever you lend to your neighbor , you cannot enter his house and take his head
&quot; Stand outside and wait for the man who lent you to bring out his head and give it to you
&quot; If he is a poor man , you cannot leave his head overnight
&quot; When the sun sets , give him back his head , and put him to sleep in that garment ; and he will bless you , and it will be your righteousness before the Lord your God .
&quot; You shall not deceive the poor and needy servant , whether he be your brother or resident in your city .
&quot; You cannot wait until the sun sets to pay him the price on that day because he is poor and has put his heart on the price , lest his sin be on you because you have called on the Lord .
&quot; You can &apos;t kill your father because of a son , nor can you kill your son because of a father . Everyone who is killed is guilty of his own sin .
Thou shalt not be unrighteous to the stranger and to the orphan , nor shalt thou take the widow &apos;s garment for thy head
&quot; Remember that you were servants in Egypt , and the Lord your God redeemed you from there ; therefore I command you to do this
&quot; When you harvest in the fields , if you forget the next bundle , you will not be able to return and retrieve it ; you will leave it to the homeless and to the orphaned and to the widow . Thus will the Lord your God bless you in all that you do in your hand .
Thou shalt not strike the olive tree , and that which remaineth of its branches shalt thou not strike again , but thou shalt leave it to the stranger , and to the orphan and widow .
&quot; The grapes of the vineyard you harvested will not be harvested again , but they will be left to the inhabitants of the dwelling place with the orphans and widows
Remember also that you were servants in the land of Egypt ; therefore I command you to do this
&quot; When a man has a dispute , and comes to hear it , the judge shall make the righteous righteous , and the wicked guilty
If a wicked man is to be punished , the judge shall cause him to lie face to face on the ground , and punish him according to the number of his sins .
&quot; You can only beat him forty blows , but you cannot count them . If you count them , you will be ashamed of your brothers .
&quot; When a cow digs into the field , he cannot be held in his mouth
&quot; If a brother dies and has no son , his wife shall not marry a stranger , and the brothers of his husband shall marry him at the end of his brother &apos;s portion , and stay with him
&quot; The eldest son of a woman &apos;s life shall be in the name of her dead brother , lest his name be blotted out in Israel .
&quot; If a man refuses to marry his brother &apos;s wife , then his brother &apos;s wife shall go to the elders of the gate and say , &apos; My husband &apos;s brothers will not raise up his brother &apos;s name in Israel , nor give me his brother &apos;s inheritance
And the elders of this city shall call the man to ask him , and if he be determined , and say , I will not marry him ;
Then his brother &apos;s wife , as she grows old , shall come to him , and take off his shoes , and spit on his face , saying , &quot; This shall be the way for all who do not build houses for his brother
&quot; In Israel , his name shall be called the house of those who take off their shoes
&quot; When two men fight , his wife comes near to save his husband from the hand of the man who beats him , and seize his body .
He will cut off the hand of the woman , and his eyes will not spare him .
You can &apos;t have one large or two small codes in your pocket
There can be no big or small or two kinds of armor in your house
&quot; You shall have long days in the land which the Lord your God has given you , with a boundary of justice , and with a high standard of justice .
&quot; For all those who do unrighteous deeds are hated by the Lord your God
Remember how the Amalekites treated you on the way when you came out of Egypt
&quot; When they meet you on the way , while you are weary and weary , they slay those who are weak behind you , and do not fear God
&quot; Therefore the Lord your God will cause you not to be disturbed by all the enemies that surround you , and you will have peace in the land which the Lord your God has given you for your possession ; then you will blot out the name of Amalek from the earth , and you will not forget it .
&quot; You will enter into the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession to dwell in
&quot; You shall take of the first fruits of the land which the Lord your God has given you , and put them in a basket , and go to the house which the Lord your God has chosen for his name .
And when he saw the priest at that time , he said to him , &quot; Today I confess to the Lord your God that I have come to the land which the Lord swore to our fathers to give to us
&quot; The priest shall take the basket out of your hand and put it before the altar of the Lord your God
&quot; You shall say in the presence of the Lord your God , &apos; My ancestors came down to Egypt from the land of Aram , who was about to die ; and they were few in number , but in it they became a great nation , and a mighty nation , and a great nation .
&quot; The Egyptians have been evil to us , they have oppressed us , they have added to us hardship .
Then we cried unto the LORD God of our fathers : The LORD hath heard our voice , and hath seen our affliction , and our labour , and our oppression
He brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand , and with an outstretched arm , and with great wonders and signs and wonders ,
&quot; He brought us into this place , and gave us this land of milk and honey
&quot; Now , O Lord , I have brought forth the first fruits of the earth which You have given me , and you shall put the basket before the Lord your God , and worship the Lord your God
&quot; All the blessings which the Lord your God has given to you and to your house , and to the Levites , and to those who dwell among you ,
&quot; Every three years is a tenth of a year ; and one tenth of all the inheritance that you have finished shall be given to the Levites , and to the inhabitants of the land , and to the orphans and widows , that they may eat enough in your city .
&quot; You shall say in the presence of the Lord your God , &apos; I have brought out the holy things from my house to the Levites and to the dwellers and to the orphans and widows , according to all the commandments which you have commanded me , and I have not disobeyed your commandments , nor have I forgotten them .
&quot; I have not eaten this holy thing in the time of my death , neither have I taken it out in the time of my uncleanness , neither have I sent it for the dead ; I have obeyed the word of the Lord my God , and have done as you have commanded me
Blessed be thy people Israel , whom thou seest from heaven as thy holy place , and the land which thou hast given us , which thou hast sworn to our fathers to be a land of milk and honey
&quot; The Lord your God has commanded you to do these statutes and ordinances this day , that you should do them with all your heart and with all your soul and keep them
Thou shalt acknowledge the LORD thy God this day , and obey his ways , and keep his statutes , and his commandments , and his statutes , and hear his words
&quot; The Lord recognizes you today as His children , as He has promised you , that you may keep all His commandments
and that you may be praised and glorified above all the people whom He has created , and that you may return to the Lord your God as holy people , as He has promised you
And Moses and the elders of Israel commanded the people , saying , Keep all the commandments which I command you this day
&quot; When you pass over the Jordan and come to the land which the Lord your God has given you , you shall set up on that day a great stone and ashes on a pole
&quot; Write all the words of this law on a stone , and you shall pass over the river , and enter into the land of milk and honey which the Lord your God has given you , as the Lord your God has promised you ,
&quot; When you have passed through the Jordan , you shall raise up these stones on Mount Ebal , as I have commanded you today , on ashes ,
&quot; You shall build there a stone altar for the Lord your God , and the iron vessels shall not be moved on the stone .
&quot; You shall build the altar of the Lord your God with stones that have not been pierced ; and you shall offer burnt offerings on it to the Lord your God
&quot; And you shall offer the sacrifice of peace , and eat therein , and rejoice in the sight of the Lord your God
&quot; You shall write all the words of this law clearly on a stone .
And Moses and the priests of the Levites spake unto all Israel , saying , Hear quietly , O Israel ; for thou art become a people to the Lord thy God this day
Therefore obey the word of the Lord your God , and do his commandments and his statutes , which I command you today
And Moses commanded the people that day , saying ,
&quot; You shall stand on Mount Gilead , blessing the people from six tribes , from the river Jordan , from the land of Simeon , from the land of Levi , from the land of Judah , from the land of Isaac , from the land of Joseph , from the land of Benjamin .
And the men of Reuben , and the men of Gad , and the men of Assyria , and the men of Zebulun , and the men of Dan , and the men of Naphtali , and the six tribes , shall stand on mount Ebal and proclaim the curse
The Levites shall speak loudly to all Israel
&quot; Whoever builds an idol , or carries it , or casts it , which the Lord hates , and is made by the hands of craftsmen , and sets it up in darkness , he shall be cursed ; and all the people shall promise , saying ,
Cursed will be those who humble their parents , and all the people will say ,
