&quot; But the little lion jumped out of Bashan , &quot; said Dan
Then he said , &quot; O Naphtali , you have been blessed , and have filled yourselves with the blessing of the Lord , so that you may possess the west and the south
And he said , Let him enjoy the joy of many children , and the joy of his brethren , that he may dip his feet in oil
Your bars are of copper and iron . How will your days be , and how will your strength be ?
There is none like God , O Jerusalem , who rides in the heavens to help you , and shows His glory , and rides through the heavens
&quot; The God of everlasting life is your dwelling place . His everlasting arm is under you . He is before you , driving out your enemies , saying , &apos; Destroy !
&quot; He dwells in peace ; he is the father of Jacob ; he lives alone in five valleys ; he drinks new wine ; his days are full of sweet pomegranates .
Blessed are you , O Israel ! Who is like you , the people whom the Lord has saved ? He is your shield and your helper , and your mighty sword . Your enemies will surrender to you , and you will walk on their high places .
And Moses went up from the plain of Moab , unto Mount Nebo , unto the top of Bisha , which is toward Jericho : and the LORD brought all the land of Gilead unto Dan
And all Naphtali , and all Ephraim , and all Manasseh , and all Judah , to the sea westward .
&quot; The land of the south , and the plains of Jericho , the city of palm trees , straight to Zoar , pointed out to him
And the Lord said unto him , This is the land which I swore unto Abraham , and unto Isaac , and unto Jacob , saying , I will give it unto thy seed ; and now I have made thy eyes see , and thou shalt not go therein
So Moses the servant of the Lord died in the land of Moab , as the Lord said
&quot; The Lord buried him in the valley of Moab , opposite Beersheba ; but to this day no man knew his grave
Moses was 120 years old when he died , and his eyes were not dim , and his spirit was not decayed .
thirty days the children of Israel mourned for Moses in the plain of Moab ; and the days of mourning for Moses were fulfilled
Joshua the son of Nun was filled with the Spirit of Wisdom because he had laid his hand on Moses &apos; head , and the children of Israel listened to him , and did as the Lord commanded Moses .
There was no prophet like Moses in Israel after Edom , whom the Lord knew face to face .
&quot; The Lord sent him in the land of Egypt to Pharaoh and all his servants , and to all his land , to do miracles and wonders
And in the sight of all Israel a mighty hand did all great and terrible things
After the death of Moses the servant of the Lord , the Lord spoke to Joshua the son of Nun , Moses &apos; helper , saying ,
&quot; Now rise , and pass over the Jordan with all the people , to the land which I will give to the children of Israel
&quot; I have given you all the land which you have walked with your feet , according to the word which I swore to Moses
From the wilderness , and from the land of Tyre , even to the river Beer-sheba , and to all the land of the Hittites , and to the sunset of the sea , shall be your border .
&quot; No man will stand before you in the days of your life , and I will be with you just as I was with Moses ; I will not forsake you , nor forsake you
&quot; Be strong and courageous , for you will make this people possess the land , which I swore to their fathers to give them .
As long as you are strong and courageous , and keep all the laws which Moses my servant commanded you , and do not deviate from one side or the other , so that you may go therein with ease
&quot; This law shall not go out of your mouth . Think day and night , that you may keep all that is written in it , so that your way may prosper , and all things may be well .
&quot; Have I not commanded you , when you are yet strong , not to fear , nor to be afraid ; for wherever you go , the Lord your God will be with you
Then Joshua commanded the officers of the people , saying ,
&quot; You shall go through the camps , and command the people , saying , &apos; When you have prepared your food , for in three days you shall pass over the River Jordan and enter into the land which the Lord your God has given you for a possession .
Joshua spoke to the tribe of the Reubenites , the Gadites , and the half tribe of Manasseh , saying ,
&quot; Remember what Moses your servant , the Lord &apos;s servant , commanded you , saying , &apos; The Lord your God will give you this land for your peace
&quot; Your wives , your children , and your livestock shall remain in the land which Moses gave you on the east side of Jordan ; but all the mighty men among you shall go before your brothers with their weapons and help them .
&quot; When the Lord will make your brethren as well as you in peace , and in the land which the Lord your God has given them for a possession , then you will be able to return to the land which you received , and to possess it , which Moses , the servant of the Lord , gave you in the land of the sunrise east of the Jordan ,
They answered Joshua , &quot; What you have commanded us to do , we will do ; and what you have sent us to do , we will do
&quot; As we used to obey Moses in all things , so will we now obey you . May the Lord your God be with you as he was with Moses
Whoever contravenes your commandments , and does not obey all that you have commanded him , he will surely be put to death ; but you must be strong and courageous .
Then Joshua the son of Nun secretly sent two men out of Shethrib to spy on the land and on Jericho , and they went and came to the house of a prostitute named Lalai , and lay there
Some told the king of Jericho , saying , &quot; Tonight Israel has come here to spy on this place
Then the king of Jericho sent to meet Laad , and said , &quot; The men who have come to you and entered into your house will be delivered , for they are spies in all the land
Then the woman hid the two men , and said , &quot; The man has come to me , and I do not know who they are .
&quot; When it is dark and the gates are shut , they go out , and I do not know where to go ; and as soon as you pursue , you will pursue .
And the woman took two men up to the roof , and hid them in the straw that was set therein .
And they pursued after them at the mouth of the Jordan ; and as soon as they had gone out , the gates of the city were shut .
And when the two had not yet laid down , the woman went up to them
And he said unto them , I know that the LORD hath given the land unto you , and that for your sakes we are troubled , and all the inhabitants of the land are consumed before you .
For we have heard how the Lord dried up the waters of the Red Sea before you when you came out of Egypt , and how you dealt with the two kings of the Amorites , Sihon and Badr , on the east side of the Jordan , and destroyed them to the end .
&quot; As soon as we heard these things , our hearts were filled with bitterness ; for your sakes there was no man of any boldness ; and the Lord your God is the God of heaven and earth .
&quot; Behold , I am gracious to you , and you swear by the Lord to me , that you will also be gracious to my father &apos;s house , and that you will give me a true proof
Save my parents , my brethren , my sisters , and all that belong to them , and save our life without death
And they said unto him , If thou wilt not reveal this thing unto us , we will surely die for thee , when the LORD hath given thee this land unto us , and we will be merciful unto thee in truth
And the woman cast the two men down from the window with a rope ; for his house was by the wall , and he also dwelled by the wall
And he said unto them , Go up into the mountains , lest the pursuers meet you ; and hide there three days , until the pursuers return , and then you may go your way .
And they said unto him , Thus wilt thou do ; or that which thou hast sworn unto us shall not be done unto us .
&quot; When we come to this place , you shall tie this red line to the window under which we go down , and gather your parents , your brothers , and all your father &apos;s household to your house .
&quot; Whoever comes out of your house to the streets , his sin shall be on his own head , and he shall have no part with us ; and whoever is in your house and is slain and blooded , his sin shall be on our head .
&quot; If you disclose this thing to us , you will do nothing to us , as you swore to us .
And the woman said , Do as ye say ; and sent them away , and bound the rope of the red line over the window
And they went up to the mountain , and dwelt there three days , waiting for the pursuers to return ; and the pursuers sought them , but they found them not .
And they came down from the mountain , and passed over the river , and came to Joshua the son of Nun , and told him all that had happened
And he said unto Joshua , Verily the LORD hath delivered the whole land into our hands , and all the inhabitants thereof have digested their hearts before us
And Joshua arose early in the morning , and all Israel departed from Shittim , and came to the Jordan , and dwelt there , waiting to pass over the Jordan
After three days , the chief went through the camp
And he commanded the people , saying , &quot; When you see the ark of the Lord your God , and see the Levites carrying it , then go away from your dwellings and follow the ark
Thou shalt measure two thousand cubits from the ark ; and thou shalt not come near the ark that thou mayest know the way that thou hast walked : for this way was not passed by thee .
Joshua commanded the people , saying , &quot; Be clean , for tomorrow the Lord will do miracles among you
And Joshua said unto the priest , Lift up the ark , and pass before the people ; and they lifted up the ark , and passed before the people
And the Lord said to Joshua , From this day onward I will make thee great in the sight of all Israel , that they may know how I am with Moses , and how I will be with thee
&quot; You shall command the priest who carries the ark of the covenant , saying , &apos; When you have come to the waters of the Jordan , stand in the waters of the Jordan
And Joshua said unto the children of Israel , Come near , and hear the word of the LORD your God
Joshua said , &quot; Behold , the ark of the Lord of all the earth will pass before you into the Jordan , so that you will know that there is a God who lives among you , and that he will drive out before you the Canaanites , the Hebrews , the Hebrews , the Philistines , the Gerazzites , the Amorites , and the Jebustes
See Up
&quot; You shall now choose twelve men from among the tribes of Israel , one for each tribe .
&quot; When the priest who lifts up the ark of the Lord Yahweh , the Lord of all the earth , stands in the waters of the Jordan , the waters of the Jordan , the waters that flow from top to bottom , will be cut off , and they will stand as a barrier
&quot; When the people leave the tent , and pass over the Jordan , the priest who lifts up the ark of the covenant is before the people
And when they came to the Jordan , they entered into the waters , and the waters of the Jordan rose above the two banks in the day of harvest
And the waters that went up and down stopped in the far country , in the city of Adan by Sarath ; and the waters that went up and down to the sea of Ahab were cut off , the salt waters that went down ; and the people passed over against Jericho .
And the priests that lifted up the ark of the LORD stood on the dry land in the Jordan , and all Israel passed over from the dry land even unto all the people , and passed over the Jordan
And all the people passed over the Jordan , and the Lord said to Joshua ,
Thou shalt choose twelve men from among the people , one from every tribe .
&quot; And he said to them , &apos; Take twelve stones from here , from the place where the priest stands in the Jordan , and place them in the place where you will lodge tonight
Then Joshua called out the twelve men whom he had prepared of the children of Israel , one from every tribe
And he said unto them , Go down into the Jordan , and pass over to the front of the ark of the LORD your God , according to the number of the twelve tribes of Israel , and carry a stone upon your shoulders
&quot; These stones will be a proof among you , and in the days to come your children will ask you , &apos; What do these stones mean
And ye said unto them , This is because the waters of the Jordan were cut off before the ark of the LORD ; and the waters of the Jordan were cut off when the ark passed over the Jordan ; and these stones shall be a memorial unto Israel for ever .
And the children of Israel took twelve stones out of the Jordan , according to the number of the tribes of Israel , according to the commandment of Joshua , according to the commandment of the LORD of hosts ; and they took them , and brought them to the place where they were lodged , and laid them therein
And Joshua set up twelve stones in the river Jordan , in the place where the priests who carried the ark stood , even to this day ,
And the priests that bore the ark of the covenant stood in the Jordan , until the word of the LORD which Moses commanded Joshua was fulfilled , and the people passed by quickly .
And all the people passed over the river , and the ark of the LORD and the priest passed before the people
And the children of Reuben , and the children of Gad , and the half tribe of Manasseh , passed before the children of Israel with their weapons , as Moses commanded them
And about forty thousand were ready to fight , and passed before the Lord , and waited on the plain of Jericho
In that day the Lord made Joshua great in the sight of all Israel , and in his days the people feared him as they had feared Moses before
Then the Lord spoke to Joshua , saying ,
&quot; You commanded the priests who carried the ark of the law to come up from the river Jordan
Then Joshua commanded the priest , saying , &quot; Come up out of the Jordan
And the priests that lifted up the ark of the LORD came up out of the Jordan , and the waters of the Jordan flowed to the place where it was , and were still rising on the two banks
On the tenth day of the first month the people came up from the Jordan , and encamped at Gideon , on the east side of Jericho
And Joshua stood at Gideon , the twelve stones which they had taken out of the Jordan
And he said unto the children of Israel , In the days to come your children shall ask their fathers , saying , What mean these stones ?
Then you told them , saying , &quot; The children of Israel passed through the Jordan in dry land
For the Lord your God has dried up the waters of the Jordan before you , waiting for you ; just as the Lord your God dried up the Red Sea before us , waiting for us
that all the people of the earth may know the hand of the Lord , the mighty hand , and that you may fear the Lord your God for ever
&quot; When the kings of the Amorites of the West Jordan and the kings of the Canaanites heard that the LORD dried up the waters of the Jordan before the children of Israel , until we passed by , their hearts were consumed for the sake of the children of Israel , and they were no longer afraid
Then the Lord commanded Joshua , saying , &quot; Make a sword of fire , and make a second circumcision for the children of Israel
And Joshua made the sword of fire , and he made the circumcision of the children of Israel in the mount Pekah
For the people who came out of Egypt , all the men of war , after they came out of Egypt , died in the way of the wilderness
For all the people that came out were circumcised ; but all the people that came out of Egypt in the wilderness were not circumcised .
And the children of Israel went forty years in the wilderness , until the people , the soldiers that came out of Egypt , were destroyed , because they had not obeyed the word of the LORD ; and the LORD swore unto them , saying , He will not let them see the land which the LORD swore unto their fathers to give us , a land of milk and honey .
Their seed , which the Lord raised up to be their seed , was not circumcised ; for it was not on the way that they were circumcised , which Joshua did to them
All the people were circumcised , and lived in their camps until they were healed .
And the LORD said unto Joshua , I have rolled away the shame of Egypt from among you this day ; therefore the name of the place is called Gideon even unto this day .
And the children of Israel encamped at Gilead . And on the evening of the fourteenth day of the month they kept the Passover in the plains of Jericho
And on the day of the Passover they ate the fruit of the land ; and on that day they ate unleavened bread and baked grain
And they ate of the fruit of the land ; and on the second day they ceased , and the children of Israel were no more ; and in that year they ate of the fruit of Canaan
And it came to pass , when Joshua was come near to Jericho , that he lifted up his eyes and looked , and , behold , a man stood before him with a sword drawn out of his hand ; and Joshua came to him , and said unto him , Art thou to help us , and to help our enemies ?
He answered , &quot; No , I am coming to be the captain of the army of the Lord . &quot; Joshua fell down and worshipped underground , and said , &quot; What has my Lord commanded my servants
And the captain of the army of the LORD said unto Joshua , Take off thy shoes that are upon thy feet , for the place where thou standest is holy . And Joshua did so .
&quot; The gates of the city of Jericho were sealed up for Israel , and no man went in or out
Then the Lord spoke to Joshua , saying , &quot; Behold , I have delivered into your hand Jericho , and the king of Jericho , and all the mighty men of war
All your soldiers shall surround this city one day and one time , six days in a row .
&quot; The seven priests shall take seven sheep &apos;s horns and walk before the ark of the covenant ; and on the seventh day you shall go around the city seven times , and the priests shall blow the horns
&quot; The sound of their trumpets will be prolonged , and you will hear the sound of their trumpets ; and the people will cry out , and the walls will fall , and everyone will go straight ahead .
And Joshua the son of Nun called the priests , and said unto them , Lift up the ark , and let seven priests walk before the ark of the LORD with seven horns of sheep
Then he said to the people , &quot; Go around the city before you , and those who are armed shall go before the ark of the Lord
When Joshua had finished speaking to the people , the seven priests took seven horns of sheep and blew them before the Lord , and the ark of the Lord followed them
And before the priest who was carrying the armor , who was walking at the blowing horn , the latter company followed the ark , and the priest went and blew one at a time .
And Joshua said unto the people , Ye shall not cry , neither shall ye speak , neither shall a word come out of your mouth , until the day that I command you to cry , when ye shall be able to cry
So he made the ark of the Lord go round about the city , and he went round about it once ; and they returned to the camp , and lodged in the camp
And Joshua arose early in the morning , and the priest lifted up the ark of the LORD
And the seven priests took seven horns of sheep , and went up and down before the ark of the LORD to blow , and the armed men went before them , and the latter company followed the ark of the LORD , and they blew one after another ,
And on the second day , when they had circumvented the city once , they returned to the camp ; and so it was on six days
And on the seventh day , at the beginning of the morning , they arose , and went around the city seven times in the same manner ; but this day they went around the city seven times .
And it came to pass on the seventh day , when the priest had blown the trumpet , that Joshua commanded the people , saying , Cry , for the LORD hath given the city unto you
&quot; This city and all that is in it will be destroyed before the Lord . Only the prostitute Lalai and all that are in his house will survive , for he has hidden the messengers that we sent .
Be careful that you do not take that which is destroyed ; for if you take that which is destroyed , you will bring on the whole camp of Israel , and curse it .
&quot; But all the vessels of gold , silver , and brass , and iron , shall be holy to the Lord , and shall enter into the Lord &apos;s treasure
Then the people cried , and the priests blew a trumpet ; and when the people heard the sound of the trumpet , they cried with a loud voice , and the walls fell down , and the people went up into the city , and they went up straight forward , and took the city .
And they slew all that were in the city with the sword , men and women , old and young , cattle and sheep , and donkeys ,
And Joshua commanded the two spies , saying , &quot; Go into the house of the prostitute , and bring out the woman and all that is with her , as you swore to her ,
And when the two young men of the son of Nun were come in , they brought forth Laad , and his parents , and his brethren , and all that he had , and all his household , and set them in camps outside Israel .
And they burned the city with fire , and all that was therein ; but all the vessels of gold , silver , and brass and iron were in the treasure of the house of the Lord .
And Joshua saved the prostitute , and his father &apos;s house , and all that he had , because he hid the messengers that Joshua sent to spy on Jericho ; and he dwelt in Israel until this day
Then Joshua made a vow to all the people , saying , &quot; When the people of the city of Jericho are cursed before the Lord , they will be destroyed in the time of their foundation , and in the time of Enum , they will be destroyed in the time of their children
The Lord is with Joshua . The name of Joshua is spread throughout all the earth
And the children of Israel sinned against the things that were destroyed , because they had taken the things that were destroyed for the tribe of Judah , for the sons of Shelah , and for the sons of Zedekiah , and for Achan the son of Hami ; and the wrath of the LORD was kindled against the children of Israel
Now Joshua sent messengers from Jericho to Ai , which is near Beer-sheba , to the east side of Bethlehem , and said to them , Go up and spy on that place ; and they went up and spy on Ai
And they returned to Joshua , and said unto him , The people shall not go up , but thirty-two thousand shall go up , that they may take Ai ; neither shall the people go up , because there are few in number
And about three thousand of the people went up there , and fled before the men of Ai
And the men of Ai slew thirty-six of them , and chased them from before the gates of the city , and slew them down the slope , even to Shebarin ; and the hearts of the people were as waters .
And Joshua rent his clothes , and he and the elders of Israel laid ashes upon his head , and fell on the ground before the ark of the LORD until the evening
Then Joshua said , &quot; Woe to you , Lord Yahweh ! Why do you take this people across the Jordan , and give us into the hands of the Amorites , and cause us to perish , rather than to dwell on the side of the Jordan ?
&quot; What have I to say , O Lord , that the children of Israel have turned their backs and fled before their enemies ?
&quot; When the Canaanites and all the inhabitants of the land have heard it , they will besiege us , and destroy our name from the earth . What then will you do for your great name ?
&quot; The Lord said to Joshua , &quot; Arise , and why do you so bow down in the land
&quot; The children of Israel have sinned , and have transgressed my covenant with them , and have taken the things that were destroyed , and have stolen , and have deceived , and have put the things that were destroyed in their furniture
Therefore the children of Israel will not stand up in the face of their enemies , nor will they flee in the face of their enemies ; for they have been cursed ; and if you do not remove the things that were destroyed from among you , I will not be with you any more .
&quot; Arise , make the people clean , and say to them , &apos; You shall prepare for yourselves for tomorrow , because the Lord , the God of Israel , says , &apos; O Israel , there is a desolation among you , and if you do not remove it , you will not stand before your enemies and you will not live .
In the morning , you shall come near by tribes ; the tribes of the Lord shall come near by tribes ; the tribes of the Lord shall come near by houses ; and the houses of the Lord shall come near by houses , one by one .
&quot; He who is taken will be destroyed there , and he and all that is with him will be burned with fire , because he has contravened the covenant of the Lord , and because he has done foolishness in Israel .
Then Joshua arose early in the morning , and brought forth the children of Israel according to the tribes that were before him ; and they were of the tribe of Judah .
And the tribes of Judah came near , and took the tribe of Shelah ; and the tribe of Shelah came near by the house of Dan , one by one land ; and the one that came out was Zedekiah .
And the house of Zedekiah came near by the hand of the sons of Hintin , one by one , and took out of the tribe of Judah the grandson of Shelah , the son of Zedekiah , and Achan the son of Gamim ,
Then Joshua said to Achan , &quot; My son , I urge you to restore glory to the Lord God of Israel , and to confess before Him , and to report to me what you have done , and not to hide it from me .
And Achan answered Joshua , and said , I have indeed sinned against the LORD God of Israel , according to all that I have done
&quot; When I saw in the treasures that I had taken a beautiful garment , two hundred shekels of silver , and a piece of gold weighing fifty shekels , I loved them and took them ; and now they are hidden in the land of my tent , underneath the garments .
Then Joshua sent and ran into the tent of Achan ; and the garment was hidden in his tent , and the silver underneath
Then they took them out of the tent , and brought them to Joshua and to all Israel , and laid them before the Lord
And Joshua and all Israel took Achan the son of Shelah , and the silver , and the garment , and the gold , and the children of Achan , and the cattle , and the donkeys , and the sheep , and the tents , and all that he had , and brought them into the valley of Ahaz
Then Joshua said , Why are you weary of us , and the Lord will make you weary today ? And all Israel slew him with stones , and threw stones upon him , and burned him all with fire .
Then the Lord turned , and did not provoke him to anger ; and the name of the place was called Ashdod , even to this day .
And the LORD said unto Joshua , Fear not , neither be afraid : rise up , and lead all the host , and go up to Ai ; for I have delivered into thy hand the king of Ai , and his people , and his city , and his land
As thou art with Jericho , and as thou art with the king of Jericho , so art thou with Ai , and as thou art with the king of Ai : but all that thou hast taken in the city , and all the cattle , thou shalt take for thine own prey ; and thou shalt set foot after the city
So Joshua arose , and all the host , to go up to Ai ; and Joshua chose thirty thousand mighty men , and sent them at night to go up to Ai .
And he commanded them , saying , &quot; You shall bury yourselves in the city ; and you shall not leave the city too far , but prepare yourselves
&quot; I will go to the city with the people that I have led , and we will flee before them , as the men of the city did when they first came to attack us .
&quot; They will come out to chase us , and they will come straight to us , and we will drive them out of the city ; for they will say , &apos; These men have fled before us for the first time ; therefore we will flee before them . &apos; 
&quot; You shall rise up from the place where you were buried and take it ; for the Lord your God will give it to you .
&quot; When you have taken the city of Ephesus , you will set it on fire , and do according to the word of the Lord , which I command you
And Joshua sent them , and they went up to the place where they were buried , and dwelt in the midst of Bethlehem and Ai , on the west side of Ai ; and Joshua lodged in the people that night .
And Joshua arose early in the morning , and gathered the people together , and he and the elders of Israel went up to Ai before the people
And all the people , and the men of war that were with him , went up , and went straight forward , and came before the city , and encamped on the north side of Ai : and there was a valley between Joshua and Ai .
And he took about five thousand men , and buried them in the midst of Bethlehem and Ai , on the west side of Ai .
And Joshua entered into the valley that night , and the people , the whole army that was in the north of the city , and the foot soldiers that were in the west of the city ,
And when the king of Ai saw this , he hurried early in the morning with all the people of the city , and went out at the appointed time unto battle with the children of Israel before Ahab , but he knew not that there was an army behind the city .
Joshua and all Israel defeated before them , and fled to the way of the wilderness
And all the people of the city were gathered together and pursued them ; and when the men of Ai were pursued , they were driven away from the city .
No man left the open gates of Ai and Bethlehem to pursue the children of Israel
And the LORD said unto Joshua , Stretch out thy hand against Ai , for I will give the city into thine hand ; and Joshua stretched out his hand against the city
Then he stretched out his hand , and the foot soldiers hurried from the place where they were buried , and took the city , and ran into the city , and set it on fire
Then the men of Ai looked back , and behold , smoke was blowing in the city , and they could not turn left or right ; and the people who had fled into the wilderness turned and attacked those who pursued them .
And when Joshua and all Israel saw that the foot soldiers had taken the city , and the smoke had gone out of the city , they turned and struck the men of Ai
And the foot soldiers went out to meet the men of Ai , and they were caught in the midst of the children of Israel , both before and after ; and the children of Israel slew them , and there was none left , nor escaped .
He took the king of Ai , and delivered him to Joshua ,
And the children of Israel smote all the inhabitants of Ai in the fields and in the wilderness , and they fell down under the sword , and were consumed : and the children of Israel returned to Ai , and slew with the sword those who were in the city
All the men that were slain that day , male and female , were twelve thousand , all the men of Ai .
Joshua did not take back the pistol he had drawn , and went straight to destroy all the inhabitants of Ai .
Only the livestock and the treasures of the city were taken by the Israelites for their own prey , as the Lord commanded Joshua
Joshua burned Ai , and made it to this day a great pile and a desolation
And he hanged the king of Ai upon the tree until the evening ; and it came to pass , when the sun was set , that Joshua commanded the people to take the body out of the tree , and to cast it into the gates of the city , and to pile it up in a great pile of stones , to this day .
Then Joshua built an altar for the LORD God of Israel on mount Ephraim
And it was made of whole stones without iron rods , according to all that Moses the servant of the Lord commanded the children of Israel , as it is written in the book of the law of Moses ; and they offered burnt offerings and peace offerings to the Lord on this altar
Then Joshua stood there before the children of Israel , and wrote the law which Moses had written on a stone
And all Israel , the inhabitants of the land , and the elders , and the princes , and the judges , stood by the sides of the ark before the Levites , the priests who lifted up the ark of the LORD , half to Mount Gilead , and half to Mount Ephraim , to bless the people of Israel , as Moses the servant of the LORD had commanded before
Then Joshua read again the words of the curse which were blessed in the law , according to all that was written in the law
&quot; There was not a single word that Joshua did not proclaim before all the congregation of Israel , and the women , and the children , and the strangers who dwell among them , of all the words which Moses commanded
And the kings of the mountains and the plains west of Jordan , and the kings of the hills and the plains that are by the sea , the Hittites , the Amorites , the Canaanites , the Perizzites , the Hivites , and the Jebusites , heard this
And they gathered themselves together , and agreed with one accord , to fight against Joshua and against the children of Israel
The inhabitants of Gibeon heard what Joshua had done to Jericho and Ai
&quot; They will take old sacks and old leather sacks , which have been torn and sewn , and they will lay them on donkeys .
They will put their old shoes on their feet , and their old clothes on their bodies ; and all the cakes they bring are dried , and they are long and rotten .
Then they came to Joshua to the camp of Gilead , and said to him and to the children of Israel , &quot; We have come from a far place . Now make a covenant with us
And the children of Israel said unto the Hebrews , Fear ye not that ye dwell among us : how then shall ye make a covenant with you ?
And they said unto Joshua , We are thy servants : and he said unto them , Who are ye , and from where come ye ?
They answered and said , &quot; The servant has come from far away , because he has heard the name of the Lord your God and all that he has done in Egypt
and all that he did to the two kings of the Amorites east of Jordan , Sihon king of Heshbon , and to the night of Bashan king of Asheroth ,
&quot; The elders of our people and all the inhabitants of our land said to us , &apos; Take with you the food of the way to meet the children of Israel , and say to them , &apos; We are your servants ; now make a covenant with us
The bread which we brought out of our house was hot , and behold , it is dried up , and it is longed up .
This sack of wine is new when we poured out our wine ; behold , it is broken ; and our clothes and our shoes are old , because the way is far off .
&quot; The children of Israel received some of their food , and they asked not the Lord
Then Joshua spoke to them , and made a covenant with them , and kept them alive ; and the prince of the congregation swore to them
And it came to pass after three days , when the children of Israel had made a covenant with them , that they heard that they were neighbours , and that they dwelt among the children of Israel
And the children of Israel arose , and came to their cities on the third day , which were Gibeon , and Gibeah , and Beeroth , and Gilead ;
because the Lord , the God of Israel , has sworn to them concerning the leaders of the congregation , so that the children of Israel will not slay them , and the whole congregation will complain to the leaders
And the princes said unto the whole congregation , We have sworn unto them by the LORD God of Israel , that we shall not hurt them now
Thus shall we deal with them , and keep them alive , lest there be wrath upon us because of the oath which we have taken .
And he said unto the assembly , Let them live ; and they made for the whole assembly a man to cut wood and water , as the chief said unto them .
Then Joshua called them , and said to them , &quot; Why do you deceive us by saying , &apos; How far are we from you ?
&quot; Now you are cursed , and those who are among you will refuse to be slaves , to be the house of my God , and to cut down wood and water .
They answered Joshua , &quot; Because there is a man who tells your servant , &apos; The Lord your God has commanded Moses his servant , to give you the whole land , and to destroy all the inhabitants of the land before you , &apos; we have done it for your sake , for fear of death .
&quot; Now that we are in your hand , how will you treat us for good and for right ?
So Joshua did to them , and saved them from the hand of the Israelites , and the Israelites did not kill them
On that day Joshua sent them to the place which the Lord had chosen for the assembly and for the altar of the Lord , to cut wood and water , even unto this day
And the king of Jerusalem , Adonijah , heard that Joshua had taken Ai , and had destroyed it , as he had done to the kings of Jericho and Jericho , and that the inhabitants of Gibeon made a covenant with the children of Israel , and dwelt among them
And they were afraid , for Gibeon was a great city , as the city of Tub , greater than Ai , and all that were in it were mighty men .
So Adonijah the king of Jerusalem sent messengers to Hoham the king of Hebron , and to Bilan the king of Jezreel , and to Japhia the king of Lachish , and to Dephix the king of Ilelon , saying ,
&quot; Come up and help me , that we may attack Gibeon ; for they have made a covenant with Joshua and with the children of Israel
Then the five kings of Amorah , the king of Jerusalem , the king of Hebron , the king of Jeshua , the king of Lachish , and the king of Elekron , all gathered themselves together , and led up their armies , and encamped against Gibeon , and struck it
Then sent the men to Joshua to the camp of Gideon , and said to him , &quot; Do not turn away your servants , and come quickly and save us , and help us ; for the kings of the Amorites are gathered together against us in the mountains .
So Joshua and all his host , and the mighty men of war , went up from Gilead
&quot; The Lord said to Joshua , &quot; Do not be afraid of them , for I have given them into your hand , and none of them can stand before you
And Joshua went up from Gilead at the end of the night , and came suddenly to them
And the LORD spoiled them before the children of Israel ; and Joshua slew them at Gibeon greatly , and chased them down on the hills of Bethlehem , and slew them even unto Assyria , and unto Makkah
And it came to pass , when they fled before the children of Israel , and were coming down from Bethlehem , that the LORD sent a great hail from heaven upon them , and struck them in Assyria , and struck them ; and they were slain by the hail more than the children of Israel were slain by the sword .
And Joshua prayed unto the LORD before the children of Israel in the day that the LORD delivered the children of Ammon unto the children of Israel , saying , Thou head of the day , thou shalt be in Gibeon ; and the moon , thou shalt be in the valley of Ajar
&quot; The sun will stand still , and the moon will stand still , waiting for the people to avenge their enemies . Isn &apos;t this written in the book of Jahaz ? The sun will stand still in the sky , and it will not fall suddenly , for about a day
&quot; Before this day , and after this day , the Lord heard the prayer of men , and there was no prayer like this day , because the Lord fought for Israel
Joshua and all Israel returned to the camp of Gideon
The five kings fled , and hid themselves in the cave of Machi
Then someone told Joshua , saying , &quot; The five kings have been found , and they are all hidden in the cave of Makkah
Then Joshua said , &quot; You roll some of the great stones into the mouth of the cave , and send watchmen
But you shall not delay , but pursue your enemies , and slay those who are behind them , and let them not go into your own cities ; for the Lord your God has delivered them into your hands
And Joshua and the children of Israel slew them greatly , and destroyed them , and all that remained of them entered into a strong city
And all the people returned safely to the camp of Makkah to Joshua : and none dared to spare the tongue of the children of Israel
Then Joshua said , &quot; Open the mouth of the cave , and bring the five kings out of the cave , and bring them before me
And all the people did so , and brought out the five kings , the king of Jerusalem , the king of Hebron , the king of Jeshua , the king of Lachish , and the king of Elekron , out of the cave , and brought them before Joshua
And it came to pass , when he had brought the five kings before Joshua , that Joshua called all Israel , and said to the captains of the army that were with him , Come near , and put your feet on the necks of these kings ; and they came near , and put their feet on the necks of these kings
And Joshua said unto them , Fear not , neither be afraid , but be strong : for thus shall the LORD deal with all your enemies whom ye shall smite
Then Joshua killed the five kings , and hanged them on five trees , and they hanged on them until the evening .
And it came to pass at the time of the sun &apos;s departing , that Joshua commanded , &quot; They shall take the dead bodies out of the trees , and cast them into the cave where they hid them , and they shall lay some great stones in the mouth of the cave , and they shall remain there until this day . &quot;
Then Joshua took him that day , and struck the men of the city and the king with the sword ; and he slew all the people thereof with the edge of the sword ; and there remained none left , but he served king Mark as he had served king Jericho .
Joshua and all Israel went from Makkah to Reuna , and fought against Reuna
&quot; And the Lord will deliver Reuben and the king of Reuben into the hand of the children of Israel . Joshua struck the city with the sword , and struck all the inhabitants thereof with the sword , and there remained none left ; and he was king over Reuben , as he was king over Jericho
Joshua and all Israel went from Reuben to Lagen , and fought against the camp of Lagen , and besieged the city
And the LORD delivered him into the hand of the children of Israel ; and it came to pass on the second day , that Joshua took him , and slew all the inhabitants of the city with the edge of the sword , as he had done to Reuben .
Then king Cyrus came to the Netherlands to help Lachish , and Joshua slew him and all his people , leaving none .
Joshua and all Israel went from Lachish to Elekron , and fought against the camp of Elekron , and struck the city
And Joshua took the city that day , and struck the men therein with the sword ; and Joshua slew all the people therein that day , according to all that he did unto Lachish .
Joshua and all Israel went up from Gilead to Hebron , and struck the city
And he took Hebron , and all the cities that belonged to Hebron , and struck them with the sword , and the king , and the people of those cities , and slew them , and left none ; as he did to Elisha , and slew all the people of the city .
And Joshua and all Israel returned to Dephaim , and struck the city
And he took the city and the cities that belonged to the city , and the king of the city , and struck them with the edge of the sword , and slew them with the edge of the sword , and there remained none ; and he served the king of the city and the king of the city as he had served Hebron before , and Reuben and Reuben .
Then Joshua slew all the people of the land , the people of the mountains , and the people of the south , and the people of the high places , and the people of the hills , and the kings of the land , and left not one , but he slew every one that breathed , as the LORD God of Israel commanded .
And Joshua struck from Galilee to Gaza , and struck all the land of Uzzah , even to Gibeon .
Joshua once slew these kings , and took their land ; for the LORD God of Israel fought against Israel
So Joshua and all Israel returned to the camp of Gideon
When Jebin king of Shazzar heard of this , he sent messengers to Joab king of Matton , king of Shinlon , and king of Absalom
and the kings of the north , and of the mountains , and of the plains of Arabah on the south side of Nineveh , and of the hills of Dor on the west side ;
And to the Canaanites of the east and of the west , and to the Amorites of the mountains , and to the Hittites , and to the Beershebaites , and to the Jebusites , and to the Hebrews of the hills of Shechem in Mizpah
And these kings and their armies came forth , and the number of them was as the sand of the sea , and many horsemen and chariots
&quot; The kings gathered together and came to the waters of Meren , and camped together against the children of Israel
Then the Lord said to Joshua , &quot; Do not be afraid of them ; I will deliver them up to the children of Israel tomorrow , and you will cut off the hoofs of their horses , and burn their carriages with fire
Then Joshua , with all the men of war , came suddenly to the waters of Meren , and struck them
And the LORD delivered them into the hand of the children of Israel , and they slew them , and chased them to the city of Sidon , and to Mesopotamia , and to the plains of Mizpah to the east , and slew them , and there remained none
Then Joshua went as the Lord commanded him , and cut off the hoofs of their horses , and burned their carriages with fire
Then Joshua returned , and took Shathiah , and struck him with the sword ; and Shathiah was the first of these nations
And the children of Israel smote the people of the city with the sword , and slew them with all their might ; and there remained none of them that breathed : and Joshua burned Shazor with fire
Joshua took all the cities of these kings , and captured the kings thereof , and struck them with the sword , and slew them with the edge of the sword , as Moses the servant of the Lord commanded
As for the cities that were built on the hills , the children of Israel did not burn them , save Shazoah ; and Joshua burned Shazoah only
And all the wealth of the cities , and all the livestock , the children of Israel took for their own prey ; and all the people struck with the sword until they were consumed ; and there remained none of them that breathed .
As the Lord commanded Moses his servant , so Moses commanded Joshua , and so Joshua did ; and there was not one of the things that the Lord commanded Moses that Joshua did not fail .
And Joshua took all the land , the mountains , and the south , and the whole land of Gaza , and the high places , and the mountains of Israel , and the high places beneath the mountains ,
And they took the kings of the land , and slew them , from mount Harah in upper Tyre , even unto Balakgad in the plain of Lebanon , under mount Hemen .
Joshua and the kings fought for many years
And there was not a city that spoke with the Israelites , save the Hebrews of Gibeon , which the Israelites had taken in battle
&quot; For the Lord &apos;s purpose is to make their hearts harden , and to fight against the children of Israel , that they may be destroyed , and not have mercy , as the Lord commanded Moses
Then Joshua came , and cut off all the Assyrians that dwelled in the mountains , and in Hebron , and in Dephaim , and in Anak , and in the mountains of Judah , and in the mountains of Israel , and destroyed them and all their cities .
And there was not left in the land of the children of Israel a remnant of the Assyrians , save in Gaza , and in Gath , and in Ashdod
So Joshua took all the land , according to all that the Lord had commanded Moses , and divided it among the tribes of Israel for their possession ; and there was no war in the land .
And the children of Israel slew the two kings outside the Jordan in the land of the sunrise ; and their land was from the valley of the children of Ammon even unto mount Hermon , and all the land of Ahab by the east .
The two kings were Sihon king of the Amorites of Heshbon ; and his dominion was from Aroer by the Jordan , and the city in the valley , and half Gilead , even unto the border of the children of Ammon , the river Jabbok .
And it came to pass at Arabah , on the east side of the Jordan , that the salt sea , and the way to the end of Timber , and the mountains of Bisha , were toward the sea of Arabah ;
Then came the night of Bashan , the remnant of the Libeans , who dwelled in Asheroth and Edom
And his dominion was mount Hermon , and Zakah , and all Bashan , even unto the border of the Geshurites and the Magians , and half of the Geshurites , even unto the border of Sihon king of Hesh .
The two kings were slain by Moses the servant of the LORD , and by the children of Israel : and Moses the servant of the LORD gave their land for an inheritance to the children of Reuben , and to the children of Gad , and to the half tribe of Manasseh
And Joshua and the children of Israel slew the kings on the west side of the Jordan ; and their land was from Balakgad in the plain of Lebanon even unto mount Harah in Upper Tyre ; and Joshua divided the land among them according to the tribes of Israel .
and the Hittites , and the Amorites , and the Canaanites , and the Perizzites , and the Hivites , and the mountains of the Jebusites , and the high places of the plains , and the hills , and the wilderness , and the land of the south ,
The king of theirs , the king of Jericho , and the king of Ai near Bethlehem ,
One is the king of Jerusalem , and one is the king of Hebron
One is the king of Judah , and the other is the king of Lach .
One is the king of Isle , and the other is the king of Keilah .
One is the king of Dephaim , and the other is the king of Kid
One is king of Hormah , and one is king of Arad
One is the king of Lebanon , and one is the king of Adullam
One is King Machi , and the other is King Bethlehem
One is the king of Puah , and the other is the king of Heph .
One is king of Aphr , and one is king of Lacharon .
One is the king of Matton , and one is the king of Shazo
One is the king of Shinron , and the other is the king of Absalom .
One is the king of Hena , and the other is the king of Mightydo
One was king of Gibeah , and the other was king of Jonah , which was near to Hami .
and the king of Dor in the hills of Dor , and the king of Goin in Gilead ,
One was the king of Damascus , a total of thirty-one kings .
Then the Lord said to Joshua in his old age , &quot; You are old , and there are many lands which you have not gained
that is , the whole land of the Philistines , and the whole land of the Hebrews
northward from the river Sidon before Egypt , even to the border of Ephraim , even to the land of the Canaanites : the land of the Canaanites , which was ruled by the five princes of the Philistines , the land of the Canaanites , the land of the Ashdodites , the land of the Ashkenites , the land of the Gadites , the land of the Ephraimites , and the land of the south of the children of David ,
And all the land of the Canaanites , and Miara of the Sidonites , to Aph , even unto the border of the Amorites ;
And the land of the Canaanites , and all Lebanon toward the sunrise , from Baal-Khadad at the foot of the Mount of Shechem , even unto Hamath .
&quot; I will drive out all the inhabitants of the mountains , from Lebanon even to Mizlim-Mason , and all the Sidonians , before the children of Israel ; and you shall do as I have commanded you , and divide the land for an inheritance to the children of Israel by lot .
&quot; Now you shall divide the land into nine tribes , and half of the tribe of Manasseh .
The half tribe of Manasseh and the two tribes of Reuben and Gad were in possession of the inheritance which Moses , the servant of the Lord , gave them on the east side of the Jordan .
And it came to pass from Aroer by the Jordan , and from the city in the valley , and from the whole plain of Midian even unto Debon .
and all the cities of Sheshbon king of Amoly king of Sihon , even to the border of the children of Ammon
And the land of Gilead , and the land of the Gibeonites , and the land of the Magians , and all the hills of Hebron , and all the land of Bashan , even unto Zaccha
And the land of Bashan , the land of the night , where he came to reign in Asheroth and Edom ; and all that remained of the sons of Lebanese was he ; and all the people of the land were driven away by Moses .
But the children of Israel had not driven out the Gibeonites and the Magians , who lived in Israel until this day
&quot; But Moses , the tribe of the Levites , did not divide their inheritance among them ; but their inheritance was a burnt offering to the Lord God of Israel , as the Lord had promised them
And Moses divided their inheritance among the tribes of the Benites according to their families .
And their border was Aaron by the valley of the children of Ammon , and the city that was in the valley , and the whole plain of Midian .
The cities of Heshbon , and of the plains of Heshbon , Dibon , Bathum-Bali , Ber-Bali-min
Jahaz , Kidim , Miphaab
the provinces of Gilead , Sibmah , and Sheilah , in the valley of the mountains ;
Bebir , the hills of Bisha , and Beth-jessaud .
And all the cities of the plain , and all the land of Sihon king of Amor , who reigned in Heshbon , Moses slew him , and the princes of Midian , Ebed , and Libin , and Suir , and Hur , and Libah ; and these were the princes of the land that belonged to Sihon .
And the children of Israel also slew among the slain with the sword Balaam the son of Beer the scribe
And the border of the River Jordan was with the land that was near the River Jordan ; and these are the cities and the villages of the River Jordan according to their families
And Moses divided their inheritance according to the tribe of Gad
And their border was the cities of Jasheh and Gilead , and half the land of the children of Ammon , even unto Aroer before Rabbah .
From Heshbon , to Ramah-mizba , and to Bidon , and from Mahan , to the end of the perfect boundary .
And the rest of the kingdom of Shechem in the midst of the valley was Beer-alah , and Beninrah , and Shephath , and Zabmah , in the midst of the valley ; and the river Jordan , and the land that is near the river Jordan , even unto the end of the sea of Kenire , to the east of the river Jordan
These are the cities of the Gadites according to their tribes , and their villages
Moses divided the inheritance among the half tribe of Manasseh according to the tribe of the half tribe of Manasseh .
Their borders were from the land of Manasseh , the whole land of Bashan , the land of the night of the king of Bashan , and all the cities of Bashan and Jair , sixty cities .
And the half of Gilead , and Ashtaroth , and Ed , were two cities of the kingdom of Bashan , the half of the sons of Machi , the son of Manasseh , according to their families .
And these are the inheritance which Moses gave them in the plain of Moab , which is toward Jericho , on the east side of the Jordan
Only the tribe of the Levites , and Moses , had not divided their inheritance among them ; but the Lord God of Israel was their inheritance , as the Lord had promised them
Behold , the inheritance of the children of Israel in the land of Canaan , which Elisha the priest and Joshua the son of Nun , and the princes of the tribes of Israel , divided among them , is as follows :
&quot; As the Lord commanded Moses , he divided the inheritance by lot into nine and a half tribes
Moses had divided his inheritance to the two half tribes on the east side of Jordan , but there was no inheritance among them to the Levites
&quot; Because there were two tribes among the sons of Joseph , Manasseh and Ephraim , and they did not give the land to the Levites , but to dwell in their cities , and in their suburbs , to feed their cattle , and to house their possessions
&quot; As the Lord commanded Moses , so did the children of Israel , and they divided the land
Then came the Jews to Gideon , and saw Joshua , and said to Joshua , &quot; You know that the Lord is in Galilee concerning what I said to Moses the God-man with you .
Moses , the servant of the Lord , sent me from Galilee to spy on the land ; and I was forty years old , and I returned to him according to my heart
&quot; But the brethren who went up with me dispersed the hearts of the people ; but I kept my devotion to the Lord my God
Moses swore on that day , &quot; The land which your feet have trodden will be yours and yours &apos;s for ever and ever , because you have been obedient to the Lord my God
&quot; The Lord has given me life for forty-five years from the time that the Lord spoke these words to Moses , as He had promised me ; and the children of Israel walked in the wilderness , and behold , I am eighty-five years old
I am still strong , as Moses sent me on that day : how was my strength then , and how is it now , whether in battle or out of battle
&quot; You shall give me the mountains which the Lord has promised me that day , where the Assyrians are , and a large and strong city , which you have heard ; or the Lord will be with me as He has promised me , and I will drive them out
Then Joshua blessed Caleb the son of Jephunneh , and gave him Hebron for a possession
So Hebron became the inheritance of Caleb the son of Jephunneh of the tribe of Gibeah , even to this day , because he was obedient to the LORD God of Israel
The name of Hebron was Cyril-Aba . Aba was the most noble of the Assyrians , and there was no war in the land .
And the land of the tribes of Judah according to the lot of their families was at the southern end of the border to the east , and straight southward to the wilderness of the desire .
Their south border is from the end of the salt sea , and from the sea of the south .
And it came to pass on the south side of Acrebenpoh , and on the south side of Gath-shebanya , and over Hezlon , and on Adar , and round about Mecca ,
And it was joined unto the children of Assyria , and it was joined unto the little river of Egypt , and it was joined unto the sea , and it was their southern border .
The east border is from Salt Hainan to the mouth of the Jordan , and the north border is from the mouth of the Jordan to the sea .
And they went up to Beer-sheba , and to the north side of Beer-sheba , and to the rock of Pohan the son of Reuben ,
From the valley of Ahab northward , upward unto the valley of Dephaim , and straight unto Geth , which is on the south side of the valley of Adom in Henan ; and it is joined unto the fountain of the wheat , and straight unto the brook of the wheat .
And they went up to the valley of Hinnom , near the south border of Jebus , which is Jerusalem ; and they went up to the top of the valley of Hinnom , which is on the northern border of the valley of Lyman .
And it went up from the top of the mountain unto the waters of Nephdoa , unto the cities of Mount Ephraim , and unto Barah , which is Gilead ;
And they went from Barah westward unto mount Seir , which is on the north side of mount Jeron , which is Caesarea , and came down unto Beersheba , and passed over the valley of Timnah .
And it came to the north side of Egron , and to Shekelon , and to mount Bala , and to Jabin , and straight to the sea ;
And the border of the west was the sea , and the land that was near to the sea ; and the border was round about the land of Judah according to the tribe &apos;s possessions .
And Joshua divided a portion of the land of Judah , which was Gilead , according to the commandment of the Lord , to Caleb the son of Jephunneh , the father of the tribe of Achan , who was Hebron
Then Caleb cast out from there three of the chiefs of the tribe of the sons of Ahiman , Sheshai , and Ahimen , and Tekoai
And he went up from there , and attacked the inhabitants of Dephaim , whose name was before Cyrus .
And Caleb said , Whosoever shall take the city from Gilead , I will give him my daughter Absalom as wife
And Odoniel the son of Kenaz the brother of Kareah took the city , and Kareah gave Absalom his daughter as wife .
And it came to pass , when Absalom had passed the door , that he persuaded his husband to ask his father for a field , and to cast out a donkey . And Caleb asked him , &quot; What do you want ? &quot;
&quot; Bless me , &quot; he said , &quot; and give me a spring , even as you have set me in the land of the south ; and his father gave him a spring from the top to the bottom
The following are the inheritance of the tribes of Judah according to their families
And the cities of the tribe of Judah that were to the south , which were near to the border of the east , were Geshel , Ed , and Jagur
Kinah , Demonah , Adadah
Gideus , Shazo , Etynus
Sift , refined , bio-green
Hadadeh Shazo , Galilee , which is Shazo
Amman , Shema , Morada
Hazagad , Shechemmon , Beer-Pale
Hassachuah , Be not Baa , Beer-sheba ,
Bara , Ein , Esson
Eldora , Keilah , Hormah
Zechariah , and Manasseh , and Sansaniah
and Libnah , and Shinin , and Ain , and Rimmon , nineteen cities , and the villages that belonged to them
And in the plains were Ishmael , Zorah , and Ashennah .
and Zanoah , and Zimkinin , and Hephah , and Enun ,
Jerusalem , Adullam , Sophoth , Assyria
Saran , Adian , Kedra , Kedroth , fourteen cities , and their villages
and Shenan , and Hazar , and Medehad ,
Trinity , Mizpah , Joter
Lagos , Bosnia and Herzegovina , Illinois
Gabon , Raman , Kitil
Kelow , Berdon , Naamah , Machidah , sixteen cities , and villages belonging to them ;
And Rena , and Ether , and Asaph ,
Ephraim , and Ashennah , and Nisheth
Kiir , Aghiz , and Malissa , nine cities , and their villages
There are also villages in the township of Egron and in the township of Egron .
From Ephraim even unto the sea , all the villages that were near the land of Assyria , and that belonged thereto ,
and the towns of Assyria and the towns of Assyria and the towns of Gaza . To the small river of Egypt , and to the sea , and to the land near the sea
And in the mountains were Shamim , and Jatir , and Shogo .
Daana , Gilesana ( The Gilesana is the perfect )
Anah , Ephraim , Tim , and Ain ,
Kazan , Horen , Kiro , eleven cities , and their villages .
And Arrah , and Demah , and Issahan ,
Janon , Beth-Pah , Aphega
Harut , and Kirjath-eba ( the name of Kirjath-eba is Hebron ) , and Zeru , nine cities , and their villages .
And Manasseh , and Gamim , and Siph , and Siddith ,
Jezreel , Jordan , and Zanoah
The cities of Cain , Gibeah , Tiennah , ten cities , and villages belonging thereto
And Hahud , and Beth Shu , and Ketun .
There were six cities , and towns belonging to the city , Mara , Berano , and Ileti ,
There were also two cities , and the villages that belonged to the city , which were called Gilebalin and Raba .
And in the wilderness were Beer-Laba , and Midian , and Sicaiah .
Ananias , Salt City , Hidden City , six cities , and villages belonging thereto
&quot; As for the Jews who lived in Jerusalem , the Jews could not drive them out , but they lived with the Jews in Jerusalem to this day
And the land of the children of Joseph was from the Jordan near Jericho , and the waters of the east side of Jericho , from Jericho upward through the wilderness of the mountains to Bethlehem
And from Bethlehem unto Luz , and unto the border of the children of Ahi , and unto the green land of Ahi .
And from the west unto the border of the children of Assyria , unto the border of Bethlehem , even unto Keilah , even unto the sea .
And Manasseh the son of Joseph , Ephraim , received their inheritance
The border of the children of Ephraim according to the families of the children of Ephraim is as follows : The east border of their possession is from Ahithophel Adah unto Sheb-ar-lon
And it came to pass from the west unto Mimeth on the north side , and from the east unto his Nazareth , and from the east unto the land of Noah .
From Noah even unto Ahath Green , and unto Narah , to Jericho , and unto the Jordan
And from Poah westward unto the river of Canaan , even unto the sea : and this was the inheritance of the tribe of Ephraim according to their families .
And in the land of the Canaanites were cities , and villages in their cities , which were given to the sons of Ephraim .
And they had not driven out the Canaanites that dwelled in Gibeah , the Canaanites , but dwelled among the Ephrates , and were servants to this day in labour .
Now concerning Manasseh , the eldest of Joseph &apos;s sons , and the land which his tribes received by lot , behold , Marge , the father of Gilead , the eldest of Manasseh , was given to Gilead and Bashan , because he was a mighty man
And the rest of the sons of Manasseh , according to their families , were the sons of Abiezer , the sons of Helah , the sons of Assyria , the sons of Shechem , the sons of Heph , the sons of Shimei : and these were the sons of Manasseh the son of Joseph , according to their families .
The firstborn of Manasseh , the firstborn of Margiel , the son of Gilead , the son of Heph , Zerophiah , had no sons , but daughters : and his daughters were named Marah , Noah , and Churah , and Micah , and Datzah
Then they came to Eleazar the priest , and to Joshua the son of Nun , and to the princes , and said , &quot; The Lord commanded Moses to divide our inheritance among our brethren ; and Joshua divided it among his brethren , as the Lord commanded
In addition to Gilead east of Jordan , and Bashan , there were ten inhabitants of Manasseh
For the daughters of Manasseh had inheritance among the sons of Manasseh ; and Gilead was the rest of the sons of Manasseh .
the border of Manasseh , from Ashead unto Mimeth before Shechem , northward unto the inhabitants of the inhabitants of Shephath-Pah
And he went to Manasseh in the land of Pekah , and to the sons of Ephraim in the city of Pekah , which was on the border of Manasseh
And the border of the land of Manasseh shall be from the south side of the river Canaan , even unto the sea , from the north even unto the east , even unto the land of Ephraim ; and the cities of Manasseh shall be among the cities of Manasseh .
to Ephraim in the south , to Manasseh in the north , to the sea in the north , to Assyria in the north , and to Isaac in the east ;
And in the land of Manasseh , in Issachar and in Assyria , were Bethen and the towns of Bethen , and Ephraim and the towns of Ephraim , the inhabitants of Dor , and the towns of Dor ; and there were three mountains , the towns of Endor , and the towns of Endor , the inhabitants of Hena , and the towns of Hena , the inhabitants of Midian , and the towns of Midian .
Only the sons of Manasseh could not drive out the inhabitants of these cities ; and the Canaanites preferred to dwell there
And it came to pass , when the children of Israel were strong , that they made the Canaanites to labour , and did not drive them out at all
And the sons of Joseph said unto Joshua , Why hast thou given us a portion of the land for an inheritance , when the LORD hath blessed us to this day , and we have grown great among the heathen ?
Then Joshua said , &quot; If there are many of you who do not like the narrowness of the land of Ephraim , you may go up to the land of the Baals , the sons of Lebanese , and cut down trees in the woods
&quot; The sons of Joseph said , &quot; The mountains will not accommodate us , and the Canaanites of the plains , the towns of Beth Shen and the towns of Beth Shen , and the people of the plains of Jezreel , have railcars
And Joshua said unto the house of Joseph , the children of Ephraim and the children of Manasseh , Thou art a great and mighty people , and hast not a single land
&quot; And the mountains will be yours , and the forests you can cut down ; and the near places will be yours ; and the Canaanites , even though they had railroads and mighty men , you can drive them out
And all the congregation of Israel gathered themselves together at Shiloh , and set up the tabernacle therein ; and the land was subdued by them .
The remaining seven tribes of the Israelites have not yet been given their land
Joshua said to the children of Israel , &quot; How long will it be until the Lord , the God of your fathers , gives you your land
&quot; In each of your tribes I will send three elected men , and they will walk through the land according to the land that is given to them , and come back to me .
And they shall divide the land into seven parts : Judah shall dwell in the south in his land ; and the house of Joseph in the north in his land .
&quot; It is written that you shall divide the land into seven parts , and bring it here to me ; and I will cast lots for you before the Lord my God
&quot; The Levites have no share among you , because their inheritance is to serve as priests to the Lord . The tribe of Gad , the tribe of Reuben , and the half tribe of Manasseh have acquired the land east of Jordan , which Moses the servant of the Lord gave them
And it came to pass , when the men who drew the line were risen up , that Joshua commanded them , saying , Go and draw the line throughout the land , and come again to me , and I will lay lots for you before the Lord here at Shiloh
And they went and went through the land , and divided the cities sevenfold according to the book , and came again into the camp of Zeruiah to see Joshua .
Then Joshua cast lots for them in the presence of the Lord in Shiloh ; and Joshua divided the land among them according to the tribes of Israel
The tribe of Benjamin , according to the number of the tribes , was among the sons of Joseph in Judah
And their north border was from the Jordan upward toward the north side of Jericho , and westward through the mountains , even unto the wilderness of Beer-sheba .
And from there they went southward unto Luz , near Luz , which is Bertie , and down unto the mountains of Athar , which are on the south side of Sheb and Lon .
From there to the west , and to the south , from the mountain that is on the south side of Bethlehem , to the city of the Jews , which is Gilead ; that is the border of the west .
The southern border is from the end of Gilead to the waters of Nephdoa to the west .
And it came to pass at the end of the valley of Hinnom , which is on the north side of the valley of Lebanon , on the other side of the mountain ; and it came to pass at the valley of Hinnom , which is near Jebus , and at the end of the valley of Enron ,
And northward they went to Shemshima , and to Gilead , which is on the other side of the valley of Adullam , and down to the rock of Pohan the son of Reuben .
And it was joined to the side of Arabah , and went down northward to Arabah .
And it was joined to the north side of Bethlehem , and to the north side of the Salt Sea , which is the south end of the Jordan , which is the south border .
And the border of the east is the Jordan ; and it is the land which the children of Benjamin inherit , according to their families , according to the border round about them
And the cities of the tribe of Benjamin according to their families were Jericho , Bethlehem , and Imelech ,
