For the land of the children of Dan went beyond the land which they had obtained ; for the men of Dan went up to take Reuben , and slew with the sword those who were in the city ; and they possessed the city , and dwelt therein , and called Reuben after their fathers , Dan .
These cities , and their villages , are the inheritance of the tribe of Dan according to their families .
And when the children of Israel had finished the inheritance according to the border , they gave it to Joshua the son of Nun among them for an inheritance
&quot; This is the city which the Lord commanded Joshua to build , and to dwell in it , which he gave him , the city of Nazareth , which is in the hill country of Ephraim , which he sought .
This is the portion of the land which Eleazar the priest , and Joshua the son of Nun , and the princes of the tribes of Israel divided in lots before the LORD at the door of the tabernacle of Zeruiah , and they divided it .
Then the Lord spoke to Joshua , saying ,
&quot; You commanded the children of Israel , saying , &apos; You shall set up for yourselves cities of refuge , as I have spoken to you through Moses
And let those who kill without heart flee there ; and these cities shall be for you to flee for the blood of your enemies .
&quot; The murderer shall flee to one of these cities , and stand at the gate of the city , and tell the elders of the city what he has done ; and they shall bring him into the city , and give him a place , and he shall dwell among them .
&quot; If the bloodthirsty pursues him , the elders will not place him in the hands of the bloodthirsty , for he is a wicked man , and he has slain no soul .
And he shall dwell in that city , and stand before the congregation to hear judgment ; and it shall come to pass , when the high priest at that time is dead , that he that killeth shall be able to return to his own house , to the city from which he fled .
And the children of Israel divided Gibeah in Galilee , and Shechem in Ephraim , and Kirjath-eba in Judah , which is Hebron
and from the tribe of Reuben in the plains of the wilderness , east of Jericho beyond the Jordan ; and from the tribe of Gad , Ramoth of Gilead ; and from the tribe of Manasseh , Golan of Bashan ;
&quot; These are the cities which have been determined for the people of Israel , and for the foreigners who dwell among them , so that the manslayer may flee there , and not die in the hand of the bloody enemy , until he stands before the congregation to hear judgment .
Then came the elders of the Levites to Eleazar the priest , and to Joshua the son of Nun , and to the elders of the tribes of Israel
And Zeruiah in the land of Canaan said unto them , The LORD hath borrowed the cities which Moses commanded to dwell in , and the suburbs of the cities , to feed our cattle
And the children of Israel gave the Levites out of their possessions , as the LORD had commanded them , the cities and the suburbs of the cities , as they were written :
And for the tribe of Kohath , and for the sons of Aaron the priest of the Levites , thirteen cities were given by lot out of the land of the tribe of Judah , of the tribe of Simeon , and of the tribe of Benjamin ,
Of the tribe of Ephraim , and of the tribe of Dan , and of the tribe of Manasseh , and of the half tribe of the sons of Kohath , were ten cities according to their divisions :
And the children of Gershon had thirteen cities according to the tribe of Issachar , and the tribe of Asheah , and the tribe of Naphtali , and the half tribe of Manasseh in Bashan .
And the sons of Merari had twelve cities according to their families , according to the tribe of Reuben , and according to the tribe of Gad , and according to the tribe of Zebulun .
&quot; The children of Israel divided these cities and their suburbs among the Levites by lot , as the Lord commanded Moses
And out of the land of the tribe of Judah and of the tribe of Simeon he gave the sons of Aaron of the tribe of Kohath the Levite the following cities , because he had given them the first lobster :
