All these cities are surrounded by suburbs belonging to the city , and so are all the cities
&quot; Then the Lord will give to the children of Israel the whole land which he swore to their fathers before , and they will have an inheritance and will dwell therein
And the LORD hath given them peace in all their land , according to all that he hath sworn unto their fathers , and none of their enemies standeth in their sight ; and the LORD hath given them all their enemies into his hand
&quot; The word of the Lord , which He has blessed the house of Israel , has been fulfilled
Then Joshua called the Reubenites , the Gadites , and the half tribe of Manasseh
And he said unto them , Ye have obeyed all that the Lord &apos;s servant Moses commanded you , and ye have obeyed all that I commanded you
&quot; For many days you have not left your brethren to this day , and have kept what the Lord your God has commanded you to do .
&quot; Now the Lord your God , as He has promised , will make your brethren in peace , and will return to your tents , to the land which Moses the servant of the Lord gave you for a possession on the east side of the Jordan
&quot; As long as you keep the commandments and the law of Moses your servant , the Lord your God , with care , and love the Lord your God , and walk in all His ways , and keep His commandments , and lean on Him , and serve Him with all your heart and all your soul
Then Joshua blessed them , and sent them away , and they returned to their tents
The half-tribe of Manasseh , which Moses had given to them in Bashan , and the half-tribe of Joshua in the west of Jordan among his brethren , blessed them when he sent them back to the tents
&quot; And they said to them , &apos; Go back to your tents with your promised possessions , and with your promised livestock , and with your promised gold , and silver , and copper , and iron , and with your promised clothing , that you may share with all your brethren what you have taken from the enemy .
And the children of Reuben , and the children of Gad , and the half tribe of Manasseh , departed from Shiloh in the land of Canaan from the children of Israel , and returned to the land of Gilead , which they should possess , as the LORD commanded Moses
And the children of Reuben , and the children of Gad , and the half tribe of Manasseh , came unto the land of Canaan , which is by the Jordan , and built an altar by the Jordan , and behold , the altar was high
When the children of Israel heard that the tribe of the Reubenites , the Gadites , and the half-tribe of Manasseh had set up an altar near the Jordan , on the side of the children of Israel in the land of Canaan
And when all the congregation heard it , they gathered themselves together at Shiloh to go up and smite them
And the children of Israel sent Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest to Gilead to meet the tribe of the Reubenites , the Gadites , and the half tribe of Manasseh
And ten captains were sent with Phinehas , captains of every tribe of Israel , captains of the army of Israel .
And when they were come to Gilead , they saw the children of Reuben , and the children of Gad , and the half tribe of Manasseh , and said unto them ,
&quot; Thus says the Lord to all the congregation , &apos; What sin have you committed today , that you have turned away from following the Lord , and have sinned against the God of Israel , and have built an altar for yourselves against the Lord ?
&quot; How little is the iniquity of Baabir before ! Even though the plague has come to the congregation of the Lord , we have not yet cleansed this sin
&quot; Have you turned away from the Lord today , and rebelled against the Lord today ? Tomorrow He will be angry with all the congregation of Israel
&quot; If you do not want to be unclean , you can go to the land of the Lord , where the Tent of Meeting of the Lord lives . You will earn a possession among us , but you will not be rebellious against the Lord , nor sin against us , but you will build an altar for yourselves outside the altar of the Lord our God .
&quot; Isn &apos;t there wrath on all the congregation of Israel because of the sins of Zerah &apos;s son-in-law Achan , who has sinned in that which was destroyed ? Not one of them died in his sins
Then the Reubenites , and the Gadites , and the half-tribe of Manasseh , answered the captains of the army of Israel ,
&quot; Lord , the Almighty , the Almighty , He knows , and the children of Israel will know ; and if we are rebellious , or do evil to the Lord , may Thou not protect us today
&quot; If you build an altar for yourselves , and turn away from following the Lord , or if you offer burnt offerings , and fat offerings , and peace offerings on the altar , let the Lord himself repay our sins
&quot; It is not for nothing that we have done this thing ; it is for our own sakes ; for I fear that in the days to come your children will say to our children , &apos; What do you have to do with the Lord God of Israel ?
For the LORD hath made the Jordan a border between us and the river of the Gadites , and ye are separate from the LORD ; so shall your seed make our seed no more to fear the LORD ;
&quot; Therefore we said , &apos; It is better for us to build an altar for ourselves , neither for a burnt offering nor for any other sacrifice
&quot; It is a sign between you and me , and between you and my descendants , that we may offer burnt offerings , sacrifices of peace offerings , and other sacrifices before the Lord , lest your descendants say to our descendants in the future , &apos; You are of no part with the Lord
Then we said , &quot; In the days to come you will say to us , or to our descendants , &apos; You see the altar that our fathers built , the likeness of the altar of the Lord ; it is not for a burnt offering , nor for any other sacrifice , but for a sign between you and me .
&quot; We have set up another altar outside the altar of the Lord , in front of the Tent of Our God , to offer burnt offerings , and sacrifices of oil , and other sacrifices , and have rebelled against the Lord , and have turned away from following Him today , and we do not understand it
&quot; The chief priest of the congregation , Phinehas , the chief of the army of Israel , who came with him , heard the words of the Reubenites , the Gadites , and the Manassehites , and they were all beautiful
Then said Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest , of the children of Gad , and of the children of Manasseh , and of the children of Reuben , and of the children of Gad , &quot; Today we know that the LORD is among us , because you have not committed this sin against him ; and now you have delivered Israel out of the hand of the LORD .
Then Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest departed from the children of Ephraim and the children of Gad , and returned from Gilead unto Canaan , and came unto the children of Israel , and did this in return to them
And the children of Israel glorified it , and praised God , and went up no more , and struck the children of Ephraim , and the children of Gad , and destroyed the land in which they dwelt .
&quot; The Men of Reuben and the Men of Gad called the altar the Testimony , saying , &apos; This is the testimony between us that the Lord is God
&quot; It has been a long time since the LORD made Israel to be quiet , and they did not fight against all their enemies around them
Then he called the elders of all Israel , and the chief of the tribes , and the judges , and the chief of the officers , and said unto them , I am old and old
&quot; You have seen with your own eyes all that the Lord your God has done to the nations for your sakes ; for it is the Lord your God who fought for you .
&quot; I have divided the land which I have cut off , and the land that remains , from the river Jordan to the sunset , in lots for your tribes .
&quot; The Lord your God will drive them out from before you , and make them leave you ; and you will receive their land for a possession , as the Lord your God has promised you .
Therefore be ye greatly courageous , and keep all that is written in the book of the law of Moses : ye shall not turn aside or turn aside .
&quot; Do not mix with the remnant of your people , whose God you do not name , nor swear by , nor serve , nor worship .
&quot; Rely on the Lord your God , as you have done to this day
For the LORD hath driven out from before you a nation great and mighty ; and to this day there is not a man standing before you
One of you will chase away thousands , because the Lord your God fights for you as He has promised
&quot; Be careful , and love the Lord your God .
If you turn a little , you will communicate with those nations that remain among you , and you will be close to one another , and you will come to one another .
&quot; You shall know that the Lord your God will no longer drive them out of your sight , but they will become your nets , your rods , your whips , and your eyes &apos; stings , until you perish in the beautiful land which the Lord your God has given you .
&quot; Behold , I am come to walk in the way that the world will walk ; and you know with all your heart that the blessing which the Lord your God has promised to you will be fulfilled in you .
&quot; As all the blessings which the Lord your God has promised come upon you , so the Lord will bring on you all evil until he destroys you from the beautiful land which the Lord your God has given you .
&quot; If you break the covenant which the Lord your God commanded you to keep , and go to serve another God and worship him , the wrath of the Lord will come upon you , and you will perish in the beautiful land which He has given you .
Then Joshua gathered all the tribes of Israel together at Shechem , and called the elders of Israel , and the chief of the tribes , and the judges , and the chief of the officers , and they stood before God
And Joshua said unto the people , Thus saith the LORD God of Israel ; Behold , your fathers in the days of old , Abraham and Eleazar the father of Nahor , dwelled by the side of the river , and served other gods
&quot; I have brought Abraham your father from the river , and I have carried him throughout all the land of Canaan , and I have multiplied his seed , and I have given him Isaac
And he gave Jacob and Esau unto Esau , and the mountain of Tyre unto Esau for an inheritance : and Jacob and his sons went down to Egypt
&quot; I sent Moses and Aaron , and brought you out of Egypt according to the plagues which I caused in Egypt .
And I brought your fathers out of Egypt , and they came to the Red Sea ; and the Egyptians followed them to the Red Sea with chariots and horsemen .
&quot; Your fathers cried to the Lord , and He made darkness between you and the Egyptians , and waters overwhelmed the Egyptians . You saw with your own eyes what I did in Egypt , and you lived in the wilderness for many years .
&quot; I will bring you to the land of the Amorites on the east of the Jordan , where they fought with you ; I will give them into your hands , and you will possess their land ; and I will destroy them before you ,
Then Balak the son of Zippoel king of Moab arose against the children of Israel , and sent Balaam the son of Beer to curse you
&quot; I did not listen to the words of Balaam ; therefore he blessed you , and I saved you from the hand of Balaam .
And ye passed over the Jordan , and came unto Jericho , and the Jericho , and the Amorites , and the Beershebaites , and the Canaanites , and the Hittites , and the Gerazzites , and the Hivites , and the Jebusites , all fought against you ; and I gave them into your hand
&quot; Behold , I have made the bees fly before you , and I have driven out the two kings of the Amorites from before you , neither with your sword nor with your bow
&quot; I have given you the land which you did not possess , and cities which you did not build , and in which you will dwell , and grapes and olive trees which you did not plant , and fruit of which you will eat .
&quot; Now therefore fear the Lord and serve Him with all your heart and with all your soul , and remove the gods of your fathers who served on the banks of the River and in Egypt , and go to serve the Lord
&quot; If you do not do well in the Lord &apos;s service , you will choose today to serve the God of your ancestors on the banks of the river , the God of the Amorites in the land where you live ; and I and my family shall serve the Lord
And the people answered and said , We will not forsake the Lord to serve other gods
&quot; For the Lord , our God , who brought us and our fathers out of the house of bondage in the land of Egypt , has done great signs before us , and has protected us in the ways that we have walked , and in all the lands that have passed by ,
&quot; The Lord has driven out all the Amorites who dwell in this land from before us ; therefore we shall serve the Lord , for he is our God
And Joshua said unto the people , Ye cannot serve the LORD : for he is the Holy God , the God of iniquity , and he will not forgive your sins
&quot; If you turn away from the Lord and serve the gods of the nations , after the Lord has blessed you , He will turn and bring evil upon you and destroy you
Then the people answered Joshua , &quot; No , we will serve the Lord
Then Joshua said to the people , &quot; You have chosen to serve the Lord by yourselves , &quot; and they said , &quot; We are willing to bear witness
Then Joshua said , &quot; You are now about to remove the foreign gods from among you , and you are about to return to the Lord God of Israel
Then the people answered Joshua , and said , &quot; We will serve the Lord our God and obey his word
On that day Joshua made a covenant with the people , and laid down the law for them in Shechem
And Joshua wrote these words in the book of the law of God , and set a great stone under an oak beside the sanctuary of the Lord
And Joshua said unto the people , Behold , this stone shall testify unto us : for having heard all that the Lord hath commanded us , if ye turn away from the God of yours , this stone shall testify unto you , whether it be clouds or clouds , that ye may not turn away from the Lord your God
Then Joshua sent out the people , and gave them all their possessions
And it came to pass after these things , that Joshua the son of Nun , the servant of the Lord , died at the age of eleventeen .
And the children of Israel buried him in the land of his possession , in the pavilion of the mount Ephraim , in the north side of mount Gath , at Naziah .
When Joshua lived and when Joshua died , the elders who knew all the things that the Lord did for Israel served the Lord
And the bones of Joseph , which the children of Israel brought out of Egypt , were buried in Shechem , in the land which Jacob had bought of the sons of Hamath the father of Shechem with an hundred pieces of silver , and which was the inheritance of the sons of Joseph .
And Eleazar the son of Aaron died , and he buried him in the mount of his son Phinehas-ephraim .
And when Joshua was dead , the children of Israel asked the Lord , saying , &quot; Who among us will go up first and fight against the Canaanites
And the LORD said , Judah shall go up first ; and I will give the land into his hand
And Judah said unto Simeon his brother , Go with me to the land of the spoil , that I may fight against the Canaanites : and I will go with thee to the land of the spoil , and Simeon shall go with him
And Judah went up , and the LORD delivered into their hands the Canaanites and the Beer-shebaites ; and they slew ten thousand men at Beer-sheba .
And there they met Adoni-Besah , and fought with him , and slew the Canaanites and the Beer-shebaites
And Adoni-Behar fled , and they pursued him , and took him , and cut off the fingers of his feet
