Then came down the Jews , and fought against the Canaanites that dwelt in the mountains , in the south , and in the high places
And the Jews went up against the Canaanites that dwelled in Hebron , and slew Shechem , and Ahimen , and Zadok ; and the name of Hebron was before Gilead
They went from there to attack the inhabitants of the wall of the bottom . The name of the bottom was formerly Gilesif .
And Caleb said , Whosoever shall attack Gilead , and take the city , I will give him my daughter Absalom as wife
And Odoniel the son of Kenaz the brother of Kareah took the city ; and Kareah gave him Absalom his wife .
And it came to pass at the time of Absalom &apos;s entry , that he persuaded his husband to ask his father for a field ; and he cast out a donkey ; and Caleb said unto him , What wilt thou ?
Then he said , &quot; Bless me , and give me a spring , for you have set me in the land of the south , and give him a spring from the top to the bottom .
And Moses &apos; father-in-law was a Kenite , and his sons went out with the Jews out of the city of the palm trees to the wilderness of Judah south of Arad , and dwelt among the people .
And Judah and Simeon his brother went with him , and slew the Canaanites that dwelt in Shebaph , and destroyed the city to the end : and the name of the city was Hormah
And Judah took Gaza , and the four borders of Gaza , and the four borders of Assyria , and the four borders of Assyria , and the four borders of Ekron , and the four borders of Ekron
