And the children of Israel gave Hebron unto Caleb , as Moses had said ; and Caleb cast out from there the three princes of the tribe of Achan
And there was no Jebus out of Jerusalem among the children of Benjamin ; and the Jebus dwelled with the children of Benjamin in Jerusalem to this day
And the house of Joseph went up against Bethlehem ; and the Lord was with them
And the house of Joseph sent men to spy on Bethlehem ; and the name of the city was called Luz
And when the spy saw a man coming out of the city , he said to him , &quot; Please show us the way into the city , for we will be merciful to you
&quot; They struck the inhabitants of the city with the sword , and left him and his family
&quot; He went to the land of the Hittites and built a city called Luz , which is called to this day .
And Manasseh had not driven out the inhabitants of Bethany and Bethany , nor the inhabitants of Hena and Hena , nor the inhabitants of Dor and Dor , nor the inhabitants of Ephraim and Ephraim , nor the inhabitants of Midian and Midian ; but the Canaanites were determined to dwell therein .
And it came to pass , when Israel was strong , that he made the Canaanites to labour , and did not drive them out at all
And it came to pass , when Ephraim had not driven out the Canaanites that dwelt in Gibeah , that the Canaanites dwelt in Gibeah in the midst of Ephraim
And it came to pass , when the inhabitants of Hebron had not driven out the inhabitants of Kirun , nor the inhabitants of Nahara , that the Canaanites dwelt in the midst of Hebron , and became a people of bondage
None of the inhabitants of Assyria cast out the inhabitants of Achor and Sidon , nor the inhabitants of Ahira and Aghiz , nor the inhabitants of Heba , Afra and Eliab
And Esau dwelt among them , because they had not driven out the Canaanites from the land
And Naphtali did not drive out the inhabitants of Beersheba and Beer-Anah ; so Naphtali dwelt among the Canaanites of the land ; but the inhabitants of Beer-Anah and Beer-Anah became subjects to bondage .
The children of Ammon forced the men of Dan to dwell in the mountains , and they did not let them go down to the plain
And the children of Ammon were determined to dwell in the mountains of Tyre , and in the plains of Aram , and in the plains of Shabbin ; but the house of Joseph overcame them , and made them subjects
And the border of the Amorites was from Aqabanpoh , and from Shelah
And the angel of the LORD came up from Gilead unto Pokin , and said unto the children of Israel , I will bring you up out of Egypt , and will bring you into the land which I swore unto your fathers , and I will not forsake the covenant which I made with you
Neither can you make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land , to destroy their altars ; for you have not listened to me . Why do you do this ?
&quot; Therefore I say again , &apos; I will not drive them out from before you ; they will become thorns under your ribs , and their God will be your net .
&quot; When the messenger of the Lord spoke these words to all Israel , the people cried out and wept
And the name of the place was called Pokin : and there they offered sacrifices unto the LORD .
&quot; When Joshua sent the people of Israel , they all returned to their possessions , and took possession of the land
And all the people served the LORD in the days of Joshua , and in the days after Joshua &apos;s death , when the elders who saw the great things which the LORD did for the children of Israel
Joshua the son of Nun , the servant of the Lord , died at the age of eleventeen
And the children of Israel buried him in the land of his possession , in the pavilion of Nahir in the land of Ephraim , on the north side of mount Gath .
Then came another generation , which knew not the LORD , nor what the LORD had done unto Israel ,
&quot; The children of Israel did evil in the sight of the Lord , and went to serve the Philistines
They have forsaken the Lord , the God of their fathers , who brought them out of the land of Egypt , and worshipped other gods , the God of the nations around them , provoking the Lord to anger
&quot; And they turned away from the Lord , and went to serve Baal and Asheroth
And the anger of the LORD was kindled against the children of Israel , and the LORD delivered them into the hand of those who had taken them , and into the hand of the enemies that were round about them , and they could not stand before them any more
Wherever they go , the Lord will strike them with a plague , as the Lord has spoken and as the Lord has sworn to them , and they will suffer greatly .
&quot; The Lord raised up the disciples , and the disciples saved them from the hand of the robbers
&quot; But they have not obeyed the scribes , nor worshipped other gods ; they have committed adultery , and have strayed far from the way of their fathers , lest they should obey the commandment of the Lord .
&quot; The Lord will raise up the disciples for them , and He will be with the disciples for all the days of the world . The Lord will deliver them out of the hand of their enemies , and they will mourn and weep because of their oppression , and they will repent after the Lord .
And after the death of the scribes , they turned to evil deeds , more than their fathers , and worshipped other gods , and persisted in their wickedness .
Then the anger of the LORD was kindled against the children of Israel , and he said , &quot; Because they have rebelled against the covenant which I commanded their fathers to keep , and have not listened to my word
&quot; Therefore I will not drive out the remnant of the tribes that remained when Joshua died from before them .
to test the children of Israel in this way , and to see whether they will walk in my ways , as their fathers walked
Thus the Lord left the tribes , and did not drive them out quickly , nor delivered into the hand of Joshua
&quot; The Lord left these tribes to test the children of Israel , who knew not the battle against Canaan
For the generations of Israel shall know and learn wars which they did not know .
And all the Canaanites , and the Sidonians , and the Hebrews that dwell in mount Lebanon , from mount Balakhel even unto Hamath , were left .
&quot; Then leave these tribes to test the children of Israel , knowing that they will not obey the commandment of the Lord , which Moses commanded their fathers
And the children of Israel dwelt among the Canaanites , and among the Hittites , and among the Amorites , and among the Perizzites , and among the Hivites , and among the Jebusites
Take their daughters as wives , and give their daughters to their sons , and serve their God
&quot; The children of Israel did evil in the sight of the Lord , and forgot the Lord their God , and went to serve Baal and Asher
Therefore the anger of the LORD was kindled against the children of Israel , and he delivered them into the hand of Goshen-li-sada , king of Mizbo-daim ; and the children of Israel served in Goshen-li-sada eight years .
And it came to pass , when the children of Israel cried unto the LORD , that the LORD raised up for them a savior , and delivered them ; and he was the son of Odon , the brother of Kareah , the son of Kenaz
And the Spirit of the LORD came upon him , and he became an army of Israel , and went out to fight ; and the LORD gave him the land of Goshen-lesar , king of Mizbo-daim , and he overcame Goshen-lesar
So the kingdom was restrained forty years : and the son of Kenaz , Odoniel , died .
And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD ; and the LORD strengthened Elisha king of Moab against the children of Israel
And Elekron gathered together the Ammonites and the Amalekites , to attack the children of Israel , and to possess the city of the palm trees
And the children of Israel served Eliel king of Moab eighteen years
And it came to pass , when the children of Israel cried unto the LORD , that the LORD raised up unto them a savior , Esau the son of Kira the Benjamite , a helper of the left hand ; and they gave him a present unto Elekron king of Moab
And he struck a sword with two edges , an elbow long , and put it in the garment on his right leg
And he gave the gift to Elisha king of Moab ; for Elisha was very fat
And when he had finished the present , he sent away the man who carried it
Then he returned from the place of the stone , and said , &quot; Lord , I have a secret message for you . &quot; He said , &quot; Get away from me . &quot; So all those who waited on the left and on the right turned away .
And Esau came unto the king , and the king sat alone in the cool house : and he said , I tell thee a thing by the commandment of God : and the king rose up from his seat
And Ehud stretched out his left hand , and drew out his sword from his right leg , and struck the king &apos;s belly
And the sword pierced them , and the sword was fastened with fat flesh , and he had not taken it out of the king &apos;s belly , and had not passed through his back
And he went out into the gallery , and shut the doors of the buildings to the ends .
And it came to pass , when Esau was come out , that the servant of the king came and saw the doors of the house locked , and said , He will be great in the house
When they were tired , and saw that they had not opened the door , they opened the keys , and behold , their master was dead , and fell on the ground .
And it came to pass , when they had delayed , that Esau fled , and passed through the rocky land , and fled to Siir .
And when he was come , he blew a trumpet in the mountains of Ephraim ; and the children of Israel went down with him into the mountains ; and he guided them in the forefront .
And they said unto them , Come with me , for the LORD hath delivered into your hands the Moabites , your enemies : and they went down after him , and guarded the gate of the Jordan , and let not a man pass by .
And there struck the Moabites about ten thousand men , all mighty men of valour ; and none escaped
So Moab was surrounded by the children of Israel ; and there was peace in the land for eighty years .
And after him was Sancah the son of Anah , who slew six hundred Philistines with the rod of the bull , and he saved the children of Israel
After the death of Esau , the children of Israel did again evil in the sight of the Lord
And the LORD delivered them into the hand of Jebin king of Canaan , who reigned in Shazzar : and his captain was Shezrah , and Sharosheth of the Gentiles .
And the king of Jabin had nine hundred chariots ; and he had greatly oppressed the children of Israel for twenty years ; and the children of Israel cried unto the LORD
And there was a woman a prophet , whose name was Deborah , the wife of Rabiddo , who was an officer in Israel at that time
And he dwelt in the middle of Ramah and Bethlehem in the mountains of Ephraim under the palm trees of Deborah ; and all the children of Israel went up to him to hear judgment
Then he sent a messenger from Kedesh of Naphtali , and called Balak the son of Abi-Noah , and said to him , &quot; The Lord God of Israel has commanded you , saying , &apos; Take the ten thousand men of Naphtali and the children of Zebulun , and go up to him to the mountain of Peshawar
And I will send Zechariah the captain of Jabin , with his chariots and all his army , to the brook Kishon , and I will deliver him into your hand
And Balak said , If thou goest with me , I will go ; and if thou differest from me , I will not go
And Deborah said , I will go with thee , but thou shalt not be glorified in the way that thou hast walked : for the LORD hath given Shechem in the hand of a woman . And Deborah arose , and went with Balak unto Gibeah .
And Balak gathered together the Chaldeans and the Naphtalites to Gibeah ; and there went up with him ten thousand , and Deborah went up with him .
The sons of Gibeah , the sons of Hiber the Kenite , the father of Moses , went out of the Kenites , and pitched tents by the oak trees near Gibeah--
And it came to pass , when a certain man was brought against Seisera , that Balak the son of Abi-Noah had passed over the mountain of Pekah before him
Then Zechariah gathered together all the railroad cars , nine hundred , and all the army that followed him , from Sharo the foreigner , and came to the river Kishon .
Then Deborah said to Balak , &quot; Arise , for today is the day when the Lord will hand over Shechem to you ; will not the Lord go before you ? &quot; And Balak went down to the mountain , and a thousand men followed him .
And the LORD caused Sisira and all his chariots to perish , and all his army , and they were slain by the sword before Balak ; and Sisira went down by foot , and fled
And Bala chased away the carriages and the army , and went straight to Sharosheth the foreigner ; and all the army of Sisira fell under the sword , and there was none left .
And it came to pass , when Sishira had fled by foot , that he came to the tent of Jabal the wife of Hezekiah the Kenite , for the good of Jebin king of Shazor and the house of Hezekiah the Kenite
And Jacob came out to meet Zedekiah , and said unto him , My Lord , come in , fear not : and Zedekiah entered into his tent , and Jacob covered him with a covering
She said to Jacob , &quot; I am thirsty . Give me some water , &quot; and Jacob opened his sack , and gave him milk , and kept covering him .
Then Zechariah said to Jacob , &quot; Stand at the door of the tent , and if any man asks you , saying , &apos; There is no one here , &apos; you will say , &apos; No
Then Jacob the wife of Hezekiah took the ox of the tent , and came quietly to him with a hammer in his hand , and nailed it from his neck to the ground , and Sisira died .
And it came to pass , when Balak pursued Shezra , that Jabal came out to meet him , and said , Come , I will show thee the man whom thou seest : and he entered into the tent , and behold Shezra was dead , and fallen upon the earth , and the young pigeon was in his forehead
Thus God put Jebin king of Canaan under the hand of the children of Israel
From that time onward the hand of the children of Israel was stronger and stronger , and they overcame Jabin king of Canaan , and destroyed him
Then Balak the son of Deborah and Abi Noah sang , saying ,
&quot; For there are captains in Israel , and the people are willing to sacrifice themselves , and you should praise the Lord
Listen , O king , and listen , O prince ; I will sing unto the LORD , and I will praise the LORD God of Israel
