And the mountain trembled when it saw the face of the Lord ; and the mountain of Sinai saw the face of the Lord , the God of Israel
In the days of Zancah the son of Anah , and in the days of Jabal , no man walked in the streets , but they were all bypassed .
The chief of the officers of Israel shall cease to be , and shall rise up to me at Deborah , until I rise up as the mother of Israel
Then came the battle of the choice of the new God to the gates of the city ; and could not the firing sword be seen among the 40,000 men of Israel ?
&quot; My heart is on the heads of Israel , who have sacrificed themselves in the midst of the people . You should praise the Lord
&quot; You who ride on white donkeys , and you who sit on embroidered carpets , and you who walk , all of you shall be proclaimers .
And it shall come to pass , when the people of the LORD were come to the gates of the city , that they shall speak of the righteousness of the LORD , the righteousness of his dominion over Israel , far from the sound of the bow and the sound of the arrow ,
Rise up , Rise up , Rise up , and sing ; Rise up , Rise up , and sing ; and plunder your enemies , Baraah the son of Abi-Noah
Then came down the remnant of the nobles with the people ; and the Lord came down to fight against the mighty for me
from Ephraim , from the land of the Amalekites : Benjamin followed thee among the people ; from Magi , the ruler ; and from Zebulun , the number of the people , who searched with a staff .
And the princes of Issachar came with Deborah ; and as for Issachar , so did Balak ; and all the people followed Balak , and went down to the plain : and there was a man with a great heart by the stream that flowed .
Why do you sit in the flock , and hear the sound of the whistling of the multitude ? There is a plan in your heart by the running stream .
And the children of Gilead dwelled by the Jordan : but why were they in ships ? And the children of Assyria sat still at the mouth of the sea , and dwelled in the port .
The people of Sibron had fought hard to die , and so did the Naphtalites in the high places of the fields .
Then the kings of Canaan fought at Hena by the waters of Mighty , but they had not to plunder silver
The stars fought from the sky and attacked Sicily from its orbit
&quot; Strike down the enemy by the river Kishon , O my spirit , and strive to go forth .
At that time the horses were running , kicking and jumping , and running
And the angels of the Lord said , Curse Milos , and curse the inhabitants thereof greatly , for they are not to help the Lord , nor to help the Lord to fight against the mighty
Blessed be Jacob , the wife of Shepherd the Kenites , more than all the women , and more than the women of the tents
She asked for water , and Yahweh gave her milk , and gave her butter on a precious platter .
And Jacob &apos;s left hand had the hammer of the tent , and his right hand had the hammer of the craftsman , and he struck Shezreel , and struck his head , and broke through his neck .
And Sishua fell down before his feet , and he fell down before his feet , and he fell down therein , and died therein .
And the mother of Shezreel looked out of the window , and cried out of the window , saying , Why is his chariot not delayed , and why is his wheel slowed ?
And the wise maid comforted him , and he said his own words .
And he brought forth a garment for the captivity , and a garment of embroidery for the captivity , which was embroidered on both sides , and was on the neck of the captive .
&quot; Lord , let your enemies perish like this , and let your people who love you appear like the sun , bright and fierce ; for forty years shall be in peace in the land
And the children of Israel did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD : and the LORD gave them seven years in the hand of Midian
The Midianites oppressed the Israelites , and the Israelites dug holes in the mountains , and dug holes , and built camps for the Midianites
And every time the children of Israel sowed , the Midianites , the Amalekites , and all the people of the east came up against them
And they camped against them , and destroyed their inheritance , and went straight to Gaza , and left no food for the children of Israel , neither did the cattle nor the donkeys .
For there are as many as locusts for those who bring tents of cattle , and as many as come into the land and destroy the whole land , and as many as come into the land as locusts , and as many as come into the land as locusts
And the children of Israel cried unto the LORD because of the Midianites , because of their poverty
The children of Israel cried to the LORD for the cause of the Midianites
Then the Lord sent the prophets to the children of Israel , and said to them , &quot; Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel , &apos; I have brought you up out of Egypt into the house of slaves
Save you from the hand of the Egyptians , and from all the hands of your oppressors , and drive them out from before you , and give you their land .
And said unto them , I am the LORD your God ; and ye dwell in the land of the Amorites , and fear not their God ; but ye hearken not unto my word
And the angel of the LORD came to Oprah , and sat under the oak tree of Joash the Abiezite ; and Gideon the son of Joash was wrestling wheat in the winepress , to prepare the Midianites
Then the angel of the Lord appeared to Gideon , and said to him , &quot; The Lord is with you , you mighty warrior
Then said Gideon , &quot; Lord , if the Lord were with us , how would we come to all these things ? Didn &apos;t our fathers say to us , &apos; Has the Lord brought us up from Egypt , and in it has he performed such a marvelous thing ? &apos; And now he has abandoned us , and has given us into the hands of the Midianites
Then the Lord looked at Gideon , and said , &quot; Have I not sent you to deliver the children of Israel out of the hand of the Midianites by your power ?
Then said Gideon , &quot; Lord , what can I do to save the children of Israel ? My family is poor in the tribe of Manasseh , and I am small in my father &apos;s house .
Then the Lord said to him , &quot; I am with you , and you will strike the Midianites like a man
Then said Gideon , If I have mercy in thy sight , give me a proof , that I may know that it is the Lord that speaketh unto me
&quot; Don &apos;t leave here until I come back and bring the gifts before you , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; and I will wait until you come back
&quot; And Gideon went and prepared a lamb , and made an unleavened cake of fine flour , and put the meat in a basket , and put the soup in a pot , and brought it under an oak tree , and presented it to the messengers
Then the angel of God said to Gideon , &quot; Put meat and unleavened bread on this rock , and pour out the soup , &quot; and he did so .
And the angel of the Lord stretched out his staff out of his hand , and touched the head of the staff with the flesh and the unleavened bread ; and fire came out of the rock , and consumed the flesh and the unleavened bread ; and the angel of the Lord saw not .
When Gideon saw that he was the messenger of the Lord , he said , &quot; Woe to me , Lord Yahweh , for I have seen the messenger of the Lord
Then the Lord said to him , &quot; Relieve , do not be afraid ; you will not die
And Gideon built there an altar unto the LORD , and called it the name of the LORD , Sharon : and the altar was in Ophrah of Abiezer , even unto this day .
And it came to pass that night , that the Lord said to Gideon , &quot; Take your father &apos;s ox , the second ox of the seven years old , and destroy the altar that your father built for Baal , and cut down the figurines by the altar
&quot; You shall set up an altar for the Lord your God on this rock , and you shall offer a second bull for a burnt offering , and you shall make wood out of the wood which you have cut down
Then Gideon took ten men out of his servants , and did as the Lord commanded him ; and he did it by night , for he feared the house of his father and the people of his city , and would not do it by day
And the men of the city arose early in the morning , and saw that the altar of Balak had been destroyed , and that the dolls beside it had been cut down , and that the second bull had been offered on the new altar .
And they said unto one another , Who did this thing ? And when they had examined it , they said , This is done by Gideon the son of Joash .
Then the men of the city said to Joash , &quot; Bring out your son , that you may put him to death , for he has destroyed the altar of Baal , and has cut down the dolls by it
Then Joash answered and said to all the people who stood and attacked him , &quot; Are you arguing for Balak , and are you going to save him ? Who is to argue for him , and who is to rule over him before he dies ? If Balak is God , let him argue for himself , and let someone destroy his altar
So the people named Gideon Jerusalem Balak that day , saying , &quot; He has destroyed the altar of Balak , and he has given Balak to contend with him
And the Midianites , and the Amalekites , and the children of the east , were gathered together over the river , and encamped in the plains of Jezreel
And the Spirit of the LORD came upon Gideon , and he blew a trumpet ; and all the house of Abiezer assembled themselves with him .
And he sent throughout Manasseh , and the Manasseh gathered themselves together with him ; and he sent forth to meet the Assyrians , and the Sibronites , and the Naphtalites , and they came out to meet with them
Then said Gideon unto God , If thou wilt save the children of Israel by my hand according to that which thou hast said
&quot; I will lay a bundle of wool on the field , and if there is water on it , and the rest is dry , I know that you will save the children of Israel by my hand , according to what you have said .
And the next morning Gideon arose , and saw that it was so : and he took the wool , and rolled it out of the wool , and poured it into a pot full of water .
Then said Gideon to God , &quot; Do not be angry with me , for I have said it again , and let me try the wool again , and let it be dried , and let there be water in other places
And so did God that night : the wool alone was dry , and there was dew everywhere .
And Jeroboam the Gideonite , and all that were with him , arose early in the morning , and encamped by the fountain of Harut , and pitched in the plains to their north , near the city of Mordecai .
&quot; The Lord said to Gideon , &apos; I cannot give the Midianites into their hands , for there are too many of them who follow you , lest the children of Israel exclaim to me , saying , &apos; It is our own hands that have saved us
&quot; Now you shall proclaim to these men , &apos; Whoever fears and fears , let him return from mount Gilead ; and there will be twenty and two thousand , and there will be the next ten thousand .
&quot; The Lord said to Gideon , &apos; The people are too many ; take them down to the waters , and I will try them for you there . &apos; I said to him , &apos; The man can go with you , and he can go with you . &apos; I said to him , &apos; The man cannot go with you , and he cannot go with you
Then Gideon took them down to the waters , and the Lord said to Gideon , &quot; Whoever pours water with his tongue like a dog , let him stand alone ; and whoever kneels and drinks water , let him stand alone
Then three hundred of them who had offered water with their hands fell on their knees to drink .
And the LORD said unto Gideon , I will save you with this water three hundred men , and I will give the Midianites into your hand ; and the rest shall go to their places
And the rest of the children of Israel sent to the camps of Gideon their tents , and the three hundred men that remained were left in the plains beside him .
And it came to pass that night , that the Lord said unto Gideon , Arise , and go down to the camp of Midian ; for I have delivered them into thine hand
&quot; If you are afraid to go down , take your servant Prah into the camp
&quot; You will hear what they say , and you will have the courage to go down and fight . Then Gideon went down to the camp with his servant Prah
And the Midianites , and the Amalekites , and all the people of the east , were scattered in the plains like locusts ; and their camels were countless , as the sand of the sea .
And when Gideon came , he heard a man report a dream to his companion , saying , &quot; I had a dream , and I dreamed that a loaf of wheat rolled into the camp of Midian , and I came to the tent , and I knocked the tent down , and the tent was rolled back and rolled up .
The companion said , &quot; This is not another sword , but the sword of Gideon the son of Joash the Israelite , whom God has given into his hand , Midian and all his army
When Gideon heard the dream and the interpretation of the dream , he worshipped God and returned to the camp of Israel , saying , &quot; Arise , for the Lord has given Midian &apos;s army into your hands
Then Gideon divided the three hundred men into three armies , and gave the horns and the empty bottles into the hands of each one , and hid in them a staff of fire
And he said unto them , See what I shall do , and what ye shall do , when I come to the camp
&quot; When I blow with all those who follow me , you will also blow around the camp , and cry out , &apos; The sword of the Lord and of Gideon !
&quot; When Gideon and the hundred who followed him came to the camp at the beginning of the third month , and it was time to change , he blew a trumpet and broke the bottle in his hand .
And all the three bands blew their trumpets , and broke the bottles , and with their left hand they took the staff , and with their right hand they took the horns , and cried out , saying , The sword of the Lord and of Gideon
And they stood in all the quarters of the camp , and the whole camp fled : and three hundred cried out , and they fled .
And the LORD caused all the men of the camp to smite one another with the edge of the sword , and fled to Beer-sheba in Sheilah , and straight to Abimelech near to Beer-sheba ,
And the children of Israel gathered themselves together from Naphtali , and from Assyria , and from Manasseh , to pursue the Midianites
Then Gideon sent messengers throughout the mountains of Ephraim , saying , &quot; Come down and attack the Midianites , and fight against them before you reach the mouth of the Jordan straight to Beer-bala . &quot; Then all the people of Ephraim assembled , and fought against them before you reach the mouth of the Jordan straight to Beer-bala
And they took two of the chiefs of the Midianites , one an Olyth , and one a Sieb , and slew them on the rock of Olyth , and slew them at the winepress of Sieb ; and they pursued the Midianites , and they took Olyth and the chiefs of Sieb by the Jordan into the land of Gideon
Then the men of Ephraim said to Gideon , &quot; Why do you go to fight with the Midianites , and there is no one to invite us with you ? Why do you treat us this way ? Then they quarrelled with Gideon a great deal
Then said Gideon unto them , Can what I have done be better than what ye have done ? Is not Ephraim the harvester of the residue of the grapes stronger than the harvester of Abiezer ?
&quot; God has delivered into your hands the two princes of Midian , Olyth and Sieb ; and what I have done is better than what you have done . &quot; Then Gideon said , &quot; The wrath of the Ephraim is gone away . &quot;
And Gideon and the thirty men that were with him passed over the Jordan , and pursued them , though they were weary .
Then said Gideon to the harvesters , &quot; Take bread and eat it for my people ; for they are weary , and we have pursued the two kings of the Midianites , Sheba and Samunah
Then the chiefs of the people answered , &quot; Have Siba and Samuna passed through your hand , and have you given us bread for your soldiers ?
Then said Gideon , After the Lord has delivered Sheba and Samuna into my hand , I will strike you with thorns and thorns in the wilderness
Then Gideon went up from there to Binuil , and said to the people there , and the people of Binuil answered him as the people of the field answered him .
He said to the sons of Binuel , &quot; When I come back safe and sound , I will destroy this building
And Siba and Samunah , and all the army with them , were left in Gath , about fifteen thousand men : and all the army of the east was left , and about twenty thousand swords were slain .
And Gideon went up from the way of the tenants of the tents to the east of Noah and Joab , and slew the children of Midian , because they had no fear .
And Ziba and Samuna fled ; and Gideon pursued them , and took the two kings of Midian , Ziba and Samuna ; and they scattered all the army .
And Gideon the son of Joash came up out of the camp from the land of Gilead .
And he took a young man who had been cut off , and asked him , &quot; Who is the chief of the seventy-seven who have been cut off ? &quot; And he wrote the names of the chiefs of the seventy-seven
And it came to pass , when Gideon was at the harvest , that he said to the people there , &quot; You used to mock me , saying , &apos; Seba and Samuna have passed through your hand ; have you given us bread to the weak who are with you ? Now here are Seba and Samuna
And they took the elders of the city , and struck them with thorns and thorns in the wilderness , and cut them off .
And they have demolished the buildings of Binuel , and they have struck the men of the city .
Then said Gideon unto Sheba and to Samunah , What manner of men were ye that slew in the mountain of Pekah ? And they answered , They are like thee , every one having a prince .
&quot; They are my brothers and my mother &apos;s brothers , &quot; said Gideon , &quot; and I have sworn by the LORD of hosts , &apos; If you had saved their lives before , I would not kill you now .
And he said unto his eldest son , Arise , and slay them : but he feared , and was afraid of the sword , because he was a child .
And Ziba and Samuna said , Arise , and slay us ; for as men are , so is power : and Gideon arose , and slew Ziba and Samuna , and took the rings of the moon which they had put on their camels &apos; knees .
&quot; The children of Israel said to Gideon , &quot; May you and your sons rule over us , because you have delivered us out of the hand of the Midianites
Then said Gideon , &quot; I will not rule over you , neither will my son rule over you ; only the Lord will rule over you
Then said Gideon unto them , I have a request unto you , that every one of you give me the earrings which he hath taken : for the enemy was the Ishmaelites , and they were all of gold .
Then they said , &quot; We wish to give you a coat , and they will put on it the earrings which they have taken . &quot;
And the golden earrings that were to come out of Gideon , one thousand seven hundred shekels of gold ; and the moon rings that the king of Midian had worn , and the earrings , and the purple garments that he had worn , and the gold chains of camels &apos; knees ,
So Gideon built an Ephrath in his own city , in Ophrah : and the children of Israel committed adultery in the name of that Ephrath , and this was the net of Gideon and his household
Thus the Midianites were subdued by the Israelites , and did not dare to rise again ; and Gideon was still in the land of the days forty years in peace .
And Jeroboam the son of Joash returned , and dwelt in his own house
And Gideon had seventy sons born unto him , because he had many wives
And his concubine dwelled in Shechem ; and she gave him a son : and Gideon called with him Abimelech .
And Gideon the son of Joash died of old age , and was buried in the sepulchre of Joash his father in Ophrah of Abiezer .
And after the death of Gideon , the children of Israel went again to commit adultery with the children of Baal , and called the land of Baal Bile their God
&quot; The children of Israel do not remember the Lord , their God , who saved them from the hand of the enemy that surrounded them
And not according to Balak , but according to the favour of Gideon , and according to the kindness of his house ,
Then Abimelech the son of Jerubbaal came to Shechem to his uncles and uncles , and said to them , and to all the house of his fathers ,
Ask the people of Shechem , saying , &quot; Is it the seventy sons of Jeroboam who are in charge of you , or is it one who is in charge of you ? Remember that I am your bones
Then his fathers and his mothers heard all these words of him to the Shechemites , and the heart of the Shechemites returned to Abimelech , and they said , &quot; He was our brother
And he took seventy shekels of silver out of the temple of the land of Babylon , and gave it to Abimelech ; and Abimelech hired bandits to follow him
And he went to Ophrah unto his father &apos;s house , and slew seventy of the sons of Jeroboam his brother on a rock ; and the remnant of Jeroboam &apos;s son Jonathan was left , because he hid himself
And the men of Shechem and the men of Miro assembled themselves together , and went to the pillars by the oak of Shechem , and reigned over them .
Then there came a man to Jotham , and he stood on the top of the mountain in the heart of Gilead , and cried out to the people , saying , &quot; O men of Shechem , listen to me , and God will listen to you
&quot; When a tree was anointed as king and ruled over it , he went to the olive tree and said to it , &apos; Please make you our king
And the olive tree answered and said , Shall I cease to serve ? And the oil of God and of men is upon all the trees .
&quot; The tree said to the flowerless tree , &quot; Come and be our king
And the fruitless tree answered and said , Shall I cease to dwell , and let the sweet fruit of the house float upon all the trees
&quot; The tree said to the vine , &quot; Please be our king
Then the vine answered , &quot; Shall I stop the messenger , when the new wine of God and of men is floating on all the trees ?
&quot; The trees said to the thorns , &quot; Please make you our king
And the thorn answered and said , If ye anoint me truly as king , then cast you into my shade ; or let fire come out of the thorns and burn the acacia trees of Lebanon
&quot; Now you shall reign over Abimelech ; and it shall be his reward if you do good to Jerusalem and to all her household in truth and in integrity .
&quot; My father died before , and fought for you , and delivered you out of the hand of the Midianites
&quot; Arise now , and attack my father &apos;s house , and kill seventy of his sons on a rock , and make Abimelech , the son of his maidservant , king over the Shechemites , who were your brothers
&quot; If you now treat Jerusalem and her house honestly and uprightly , you will rejoice in Abimelech , and he will rejoice in you
&quot; If not , let fire come out of Abimelech , and burn the people of Shechem and all the people of Miro , and let fire come out of the people of Shechem and all the people of Miro , and burn Abimelech
And Jotham fled from his brother Abimelech , and came to Beer-sheba , and lived there
Abby Miller Three Years in Israel
God sent the devil down between Abimelech and the Shechemites , and the Shechemites treated Abimelech in deceit
&quot; This is the evil done to the seventy children of Jerubbaal , to Abimelech , their brother , and to the Shechemites , who helped him kill his brothers .
And the men of Shechem lay on the top of the mountain , and waited for Abimelech ; and whosoever passed by from them took it ; and there was a man who brought it to Abimelech
And Caleb the son of Ebed came to Shechem with his brethren ; and all the men of Shechem trusted in him .
And the men of Shechem went out of the city into the fields , and took grapes , and smote wine , and made a feast , and entered into the temple of their God to eat and drink , and cursed Abimelech
And Caleb the son of Ebe said , Who is Abimelech , and who is Shechem , that we should serve him ? Isn &apos;t he the son of Jerubbaal , and isn &apos;t his helper Zebul , that you should serve the seed of Hamath , the father of Shechem ? Why should we serve Abimelech ?
&quot; If only this people were in My hands , I would have removed Abimelech . Then Gaal said to Abimelech , &apos; Add up your army
And when Jezebel heard the words of Caleb the son of Ebed , he was wroth .
Then he sent a messenger to Abimelech , saying , &quot; The sons of Ebed , Caleb and his brothers , have come to Shechem , and the people of the city , who are incensing , have attacked you .
Arise this night , and lie down in the fields with those who are with you .
And it came to pass in the morning , as soon as the sun was risen , that thou arosest and broke through the city ; and when the Chaldeans and those who were with them came out to attack thee , thou didst so in the sight of them
And Abimelech rose up at night , and all that were with him , in four groups , and lay on their faces , waiting for the men of Shechem .
And Gaal the son of Ebed went out , and stood at the gate of the city : and Abimelech and all that were with him rose up from the place of the burial .
And when he saw them , he said unto Zebulun , Behold , there is a man come down from the top of the mountain ; and Zebulun said unto him , Thou seest the shadow of the mountain as a man
Then he said , &quot; Look , there are people coming down from high , and there is a company coming from the way of the oak tree of Mephiron
Then Zebulun said to him , &quot; You said , &apos; Who is Abimelech , that we should serve him ? Is it not the people whom you despise ? Now go out and fight with them
Then Gaal went out with the men of Shechem , and fought against Abimelech
And Abimelech pursued him , and he fled before him ; and many of the wounded fell down to the gates of the city
And Abimelech dwelt in Aruma , and Zebulur drove out Caleb and his brethren , and they were not allowed to dwell in Shechem
The next day the people went out into the fields . Some complained to Abimelech
And he divided his people into three armies , and lay in the fields : and when he saw the men of Shechem coming out of the city , he arose and slew them
And Abimelech and his company went forward , and stood at the gate of the city ; and they went straight into the field , and slew all the people
And Abimelech struck the city all the day , and took it , and slew its inhabitants , and destroyed it , and poured out salt upon it
And when the men of the house of Shechem heard it , they hid themselves in the guard of the temple of the soil of Babylon .
And there was a man who accused Abimelech , saying , All the men of the house of Shechem are gathered together in one place
And Abimelech went up to mount Sammon , and all that were with him ; and Abimelech took an axe in his hand , and cut down a branch of the tree , and carried it on his shoulders , and said unto those that were with him , See what I have done , and do it quickly .
And all the people cut down one branch after another , and followed Abimelech , and set the branches upon the walls of the tabernacle , and burned it with fire : and all the men of the house of Shechem died , about a thousand men and women .
And Abimelech went to Timan , and besieged the city , to the camp of Timan .
&quot; There is a strong building in the city ; and all the people of the city , men and women , fled into the building , and shut the doors , and went up to the top
And Abimelech came to the door of the house , and struck it , and burned it with fire .
A woman threw a stone on Abimelech &apos;s head and broke his brainbone
Then he cried out to the young man who had taken his weapons , and said to him , &quot; Take out your sword , and kill me ; lest anyone argue against me , saying , &apos; He killed a woman . &apos; &quot; And the young man pierced him , and he died .
And when the children of Israel saw that Abimelech was dead , they went every man to his own place
Thus God rewarded Abimelech for the evil that he had done to his father , that he had killed seventy of his brothers .
All the evil of the people of Shechem shall God recompense on their heads ; and the curse of Jotham the son of Jerubbaal shall be upon them .
And after Abimelech , the son of Dodo the Issacharite , and the son of Puah , rose up and saved the children of Israel , and dwelt in Shami in the mountains of Ephraim
And he died , and was buried in Shami , thirty-three years after that he was a disciple of Israel .
And after him was Jair of the Philistines , who was captain of Israel twenty-two years .
And he had thirty sons riding upon thirty donkeys ; and they had thirty cities , which were called Havoth Jair , even unto this day in the land of Gilead
And when Jair was dead , he was buried in Gath .
And the children of Israel did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD , and served Baal and Asheroth and the God of Aram , the God of Sidon , the God of Moab , the God of the Ammonites , and the God of the Philistines , and forsook the LORD , and served him not
And the anger of the LORD was kindled against Israel , and he delivered them into the hand of the Philistines and the Ammonites
From that year onward they harassed and oppressed the children of Israel in the land of Gilead , which belonged to the Amorites by the Jordan , for eighteen years .
And the children of Ammon passed over the Jordan , and struck Judah , and Benjamin , and the children of Ephraim ; and the children of Israel were troubled
And the children of Israel cried unto the LORD , saying , We have sinned against thee , because we have forsaken our God , and have gone to serve the Philistines
&quot; The Lord said to the children of Israel , &quot; Did I not save you from the Egyptians , the Amorites , the Ammonites , and the Philistines
And the Sidonians , and the Amalekites , and the Maunites oppressed you ; and you cried to Me , and I delivered you out of their hand
&quot; Because you have forsaken me and served other gods , I will not save you any more .
Go to the God of your choice , and let him save you in the hour of distress .
And the children of Israel said unto the LORD , We have sinned ; so do thou to us according to thy will ; save us only this day
And the children of Israel removed the foreign gods from among them , and served the Lord ; and the Lord was troubled in their hearts because of the affliction of the children of Israel
And the children of Ammon were gathered together , and encamped in Gilead ; and the children of Israel were gathered together , and encamped in Mizpah
Then the people and the princes of Gilead consulted among themselves , saying , &quot; Who can first attack the children of Ammon and be the leader of all the inhabitants of Gilead
And Jephthah the Philistine was a mighty warrior , the son of a prostitute ; and Jephthah the Philistine was born
And when the wife of Gilead had given birth to several sons , and the sons that his wife had given birth to were grown old , they cast out Jephthah , and said unto him , Thou shalt not inherit the inheritance of our father &apos;s house , for thou art the son of a prostitute for thy sake
And Jephthah fled from his brothers , and lived in the land of Tobdi ; and there gathered to him bandits , and went in and out with him
A few days later the Ammonites attacked Israel
And it came to pass , when the sons of Ammon had struck Israel , that the elders of Gilead went to Tabekah to call Jephthah back
He said to Jephthah , &quot; Please be our commander , that we may fight against the children of Ammon
Then answered Jephthah the elder of Gilead , &quot; Have you not hated me before , and driven me out of my father &apos;s house ? Why do you come to me in this hour of great distress
Then the elders of Gilead answered Jephthah , and said , &quot; Behold , we come to you , that you may go with us to fight against the children of Ammon ; and you may be the leader of all the inhabitants of Gilead .
And Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead , &quot; You have brought me back to fight against the children of Ammon ; the Lord has given him to me ; can I be your leader ? &quot;
Then the elders of Gilead answered Jephthah , saying , &quot; The Lord has witnessed among you and among me , and we shall do according to your word
Then Jephthah returned with the elders of Gilead , and the people made Jephthah their leader and their captain ; and Jephthah made all his words known in Mizpah before the Lord
And Jephthah sent messengers to the king of the children of Ammon , saying , What have you to do with me that you come to attack me in my land
And the king of the children of Ammon answered the messenger of Jephthah , and said , For the children of Israel have possessed my land from the time that they came up out of Egypt , from the river Arnon even unto the river Jabbok , even unto the river Jordan ; and now return it to you in good manner .
And Jephthah sent messengers to the king of the children of Ammon
And he said unto him , Thus saith Jephthah ; The children of Israel have not possessed the land of Moab , nor the land of the children of Ammon
&quot; The children of Israel came up from Egypt through the wilderness to the Red Sea , and came to Gath
Then they sent messengers to king Edom , saying , &quot; Please let me pass through your land , &quot; but Edom refused ; and they sent messengers to king Moab , and he refused ; and the children of Israel lived in Gath
And they passed through the wilderness , and round about Edom and the land of Moab , and came from the east side of the land of Moab , and encamped on the banks of the river Arnon , and they entered not into the land of Moab ; for the river Arnon was the border of Moab .
And the children of Israel sent messengers to Sihon king of Amoly , king of Heshbon , and said unto him , Let us pass through thy land unto our own place
&quot; But Sihon did not believe the children of Israel , nor allowed them to pass through his borders , but gathered his people together to battle against the children of Israel in the camp of Jabesh .
&quot; The Lord , the God of Israel , has given Sihon and all his people into the hands of Israel , and they have struck them , and they have taken all the land of the Amorites
From the river of Arnon to the river of Jabbok , from the wilderness even to the river of Jordan
&quot; You , the Lord God of Israel , have driven out the Amorites before His people Israel , and have obtained their land
Will you not use the land which your God Gideon has given you for a possession ? The Lord , our God , will give us his land for those whom he has driven out before us
Are you stronger than Balak the son of Zebulun king of Moab , who fought against the children of Israel , or against them ?
For thirty years have the children of Israel dwelled in Sheshbon , and in the villages of Sheshbon , and in the villages of Aroer , and in the villages of Aroer , and in all the cities that are by the river Arnon ; and why have you not taken them back in those thirty years ?
&quot; Behold , I am not guilty of you , but you have attacked me , and you have done me evil . May the Lord who judges judge between the children of Israel and the children of Ammon today
But the king of the children of Ammon would not listen to the words of Jephthah , which he had sent to them
The Spirit of the Lord descended on Jephthah , and he passed through Gilead and Manasseh , and came to Mizpah of Gilead , and from Mizpah to the children of Ammon
Then Jephthah made a vow to the Lord , saying , &quot; If you give the children of Ammon into my hand
&quot; When I come back from the children of Ammon in peace and quiet , whoever comes out of my house first to meet me will return to you , and I will offer him for a burnt offering
Then Jephthah went to the children of Ammon , and fought with them ; and the Lord delivered them into his hand
And he slew them greatly , and took twenty cities from Aroer unto Mian , and straight unto Aben-lech-ramin ; and the children of Ammon were subdued by the children of Israel
And Jephthah returned to Mizpah to his own house ; and behold , his daughters came out to him with drums and danced , and they were his only children ; and he had no sons nor daughters
And when Jephthah saw him , he rent his clothes , and said , &quot; Woe to me , my daughter ! You have grieved me greatly , and made me grieve ; for I have made a vow to the Lord , and I will not be saved .
And his daughter answered and said , Father , when thou hast opened thy mouth unto the LORD , do unto me as thou hast said in thine mouth : for the LORD hath avenged thee on the children of Ammon his enemy
Then he said to his father , &quot; Please allow me to go for two months with my companions on the mountains , and to weep that I may become a virgin
And Jephthah said , Go , and let him go for two months ; and he went with his companions , and mourned for him in the mountains .
When the two months had come to an end , he returned to his father , and the father did as he had promised him ; and the daughters had no near man
There was a statute in Israel after this : Every year the daughters of Israel went to mourn for Jephthah the daughter of the Philistines for four days
Then the men of Ephraim gathered themselves together , and came to the north , and said to Jephthah , &quot; Why have you not invited us to fight with the children of Ammon ? We will burn you and your house with fire
And Jephthah said unto them , I and my people have fought a great battle with the children of Ammon ; and I have called you , and ye have not come to save me from their hand
&quot; When I saw that you did not come to rescue me , I fought hard against the children of Ammon , and the Lord delivered them into my hand . Why do you come up against me today ?
And Jephthah gathered together the Philistines , and fought against the Philistines ; and the Philistines slew the Philistines , because they said , &quot; You Philistines are not among the men of Manasseh in the midst of Ephraim , nor among those who fled from Ephraim
And the Philistines kept the gates of the Jordan , and would not let the Ephraim pass by ; and if the man that fled said , Let me pass by , then the Philistines would say unto him , Thou art the Ephraim ; and if he said , Thou art not ,
And he said unto him , Thou sayest , Shepherd . And the Philistines said , Shepherd . And the Philistines took him , and slew him at the mouth of the Jordan : and there were slain the Philistines forty and two thousand .
And Jephthah the Gileadite died , and was buried in a city of Gilead , and he was a captain of Israel for six years
And after Jephthah there was Ebi Zan of Bethlehem , a captain of Israel
And he had thirty sons , and thirty daughters , and all the daughters were married : and he took thirty wives for the children of Israel out of the country : and he was a centurion in Israel seven years .
And Abiezer died , and was buried in Bethlehem .
And after him was Elon of the children of Zebulun ten years as a captain over Israel .
And the sons of Eron died , and were buried in Aarlon in the land of Eron .
And after Enron was Absalom the son of Hilel the Beerothite , a captain of Israel .
And he had forty sons , and thirty sons-in-law , and he rode on seventy donkeys . And Absalom was an officer of Israel eight years .
And Absalom the son of Hillel the Beerothite died , and was buried in Beeroth in the land of Ephraim , in the mountains of the Amalekites .
And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD , and the LORD gave them forty years in the hand of the Philistines
And there was a Zorah of Dan , named Manoah ; and his wife was not conceived , nor bare .
Then the angel of the Lord appeared to the woman , and said to her , &quot; You have not been pregnant , nor have you given birth ; now you will be pregnant and have a son
Therefore be careful , and drink no pure wine , nor eat anything unclean .
And thou shalt conceive a son , and thou shalt not shave his head with a razor : for he hath given birth unto him , and he shall be a man of the ears : and he shall be the first to deliver Israel out of the hand of the Philistines .
And the woman returned and said unto her husband , A man of God hath come unto me , and his appearance is as the appearance of an angel of God : he is a dreadful man ; I have not asked him where he came from , nor hath he declared his name unto me
&quot; But he said to me , &apos; If you are to conceive a son , you shall not drink strong wine , nor eat anything unclean , for God will take care of this child from birth to death .
And Manoah prayed unto the LORD , saying , Lord , send the man of God again unto us , that he may teach us how to deal with the child that shall be born
And it came to pass , when the woman was sitting in the field , that the angel of God came to him , and his husband Manoah was not with him
Then the woman ran quickly and told her husband , &quot; The man who came to me that day has appeared again to me
And Manoah arose , and came with his wife to the man , and said unto him , Art thou the one that speaketh unto this woman ? And he said , I am
And Manoah said , Let thy words be fulfilled : how shall we deal with this child , and how shall he be afterwards ?
And the angel of the Lord said unto Manoah , All that I report unto the woman , she shall do with caution
&quot; You shall not eat of the fruit of the vine , nor of the wine of pure wine , nor of anything unclean ; and he shall keep all that I command him .
And Manoah said to the messenger of the Lord , &quot; Please let us keep you , and prepare for you a lamb
And the angel of the LORD said unto Manoah , Though thou hast kept me , yet will I not eat of thy food ; and if thou preparest a burnt offering , give it unto the LORD : for Manoah knew not that he was the angel of the LORD
And Manoah said to the messenger of the Lord , &quot; Tell me your name , and we will respect you when your words are fulfilled
And the angel of the Lord said unto him , Why wilt thou ask my name ? My name is marvellous
And Manoah offered a lamb and a sacrifice of fat on a rock unto the LORD . And the angel did a marvelous thing , and Manoah and his wife looked .
And it came to pass , when the flame was lifted up from the altar , that the angel of the Lord was lifted up in the flame of the altar ; and when Manoah and his wife saw it , they fell down on the ground
And the angel of the LORD was no more manifest unto Manoah and to his wife , until Manoah knew that he was the angel of the LORD
And Manoah said unto his wife , We must die because we have seen God
&quot; But his wife said to him , &quot; If the Lord kills us , he will not take the burnt offering and the sacrifice of the flesh out of our hands , nor will he tell us all these things , nor will he tell us these things today
Then the woman gave birth to a son , and named him Samson ; and when he was grown up , the Lord blessed him
The Spirit of the Lord touched him in the midst of Zorah and Ishmael in Manasseh
And he went down to Timnath , and behold a woman in Timnath , the daughter of the Philistines .
And he came and told his parents , and said , &quot; I have seen in the pavilion a woman , the daughter of the Philistines , whom you shall give me as a wife
And his parents said unto him , Is there not a woman among the daughters of thy brother , or among the people of the land , that thou shouldest go and marry among the uncircumcised of the Philistines ? And he said unto his father , Let me marry her , that I may please him
&quot; But his parents did not know that it was the Lord &apos;s doing , because he had found an opportunity to attack the Philistines ; and at that time the Philistines ruled over Israel
And he went down to the vineyard with his parents , and came to the vineyard , and there a young lion cried out to him
&quot; The Spirit of the Lord moved him greatly , and he tear the lion as a lamb , even though he had no instruments in his hand ; and he did it without telling his parents
And he went down and spoke to the woman , and rejoiced in him .
&quot; A few days later he went down to marry the woman , and turned to the road to see the dead lion , and saw a bee and honey in the dead lion .
Then he took the honey with his hand , and ate it , and went away ; and came to his parents , and gave it to his parents , and they ate it ; but he did not tell them that it was from the dead lion .
And his father went down to see the woman , and there he made a feast , because it was the custom of the young men
When they saw him , they invited thirty men to accompany him
And he said to them , &quot; I have given you a riddle , and if you in the seven days of the feast can guess what you intend to say to me , I will give you thirty linen garments and thirty robes
&quot; If you can &apos;t guess what it is you are accusing me of , then give me thirty garments and thirty robes , &quot; they said , &quot; and tell us the riddles .
And he said unto them , Out of the eater cometh that which eats , and out of the stronger cometh that which is sweet ; and for three days they could not discern the meaning of the riddle .
And it came to pass on the seventh day , that they said unto the wife of Samson , Havest thou persuaded thy husband to tell us the interpretation of the riddle , lest we burn thee and thy father &apos;s house with fire , and have thou invited us to take all of us ?
And his wife cried in the presence of his husband , saying , Thou hast hated me , and not loved me ; thou hast devised a riddle for the people of my land , and hast not spoken it to me . And he answered , I have not spoken it to you , neither have my parents spoken it to you
During the seventh day of the feast , he cried before his husband , and on the seventh day he pressed him , and he told his wife the meaning of the riddle , and she told the people of her land .
And it came to pass on the seventh day , before the sun had set , that the men of the city said unto him , What is sweeter than honey , and what is stronger than a lion ? And he said unto them , If ye have not sown the land of my calf , ye shall not understand my riddle .
And the Spirit of the LORD was greatly moved on him , and he went down to Assyria , and slew thirty men , and took their garments , and gave them unto the man that had guessed a riddle : and he was wroth , and went up to his father &apos;s house .
Then his wife returned to him as his companion , and became his friend .
&quot; A few days later , when it was time to harvest the wheat , he took a lamb with him to see his wife , and said , &quot; I will go in to see my wife ; but his father-in-law will not allow him in .
And said , &quot; I have estimated that you hated him exceedingly , so I have given him to be your companion . Is not his sister more beautiful than he , and you can marry him instead ? &quot;
&quot; This time I did not sin against the Philistines , &quot; said he
So he took three hundred foxes , and bound their tails in pairs , and bound the fire between the two tails .
Then he lighted a torch , and put the fox in the grass of the Philistines , and he burned the bundles of grass he had gathered , and the untreated grass , and the olive grove .
Then the Philistines said , &quot; Who did this ? &quot; Some said , &quot; The son-in-law of Timnath , because his father-in-law gave his wife to be with him . &quot; So the Philistines went up and burned the woman and his father with fire .
Then said he to the Philistines , &quot; Because you have done this , I will avenge you , and I will cease from speaking to you
And he struck them with a great slaughter , and cut off their legs and their loins ; and he went down to dwell in the cave of Iman .
And the Philistines went up , and encamped in Judah , and spread out themselves in Lich
Then said the Jews , &quot; Why have you come to attack us ? &quot; They said , &quot; We have come to bind the sons of Samson . How will he do to us , and how will we do to him ? &quot;
Then came three thousand of the Jews down to the cave of Iman , and said unto him , Knowest thou not what the Philistines do unto us ? And he answered , How shall they do unto me , and how shall I do unto them
And the Jews said unto him , We are come down to bind thee , and to deliver thee into the hand of the Philistines . And he said , Swear unto me , that thou shalt not kill me
And they said , We will not kill thee , but bind thee to the hand of the Philistines . And they bound him with two new ropes , and carried him up from the rock Ethan
And it came to pass , when he was come to Lich , and the Philistines were screaming with him , that the Spirit of the Lord stirred him greatly , and the cords of his arms were as the linen of a burning fire , and his cords were taken away from his hand .
And when he saw a moustache of a donkey that had not been cut off , he stretched out his hand and picked it up , and slew a thousand men
&quot; I have scattered the slain with the moustache of the donkey , and I have slain with the moustache of the donkey a thousand people
And when he had said this , he cast out the breastbone out of his hand ; and the name of the place was called Lamech .
And when he was thirsty , he cried unto the LORD , saying , Shall I die thirsty in the hands of the uncircumcised , because thou hast delivered me with the hand of thy servant ?
And God split the valley of Lech , and water came forth out of it , and he drank of the Spirit of Resurrection : and the name of that spring was Imhakali , and it is in Lech to this day .
And it came to pass , when the Philistines ruled over the children of Israel , that he was captain over Israel twenty years
And when he came to Gaza , he saw a prostitute there , and came near unto him
And there was a man who said unto the people of Gath , Thus saith the LORD ; Behold , Samson is come unto this place , and they have surrounded his company , and they have hid themselves at the gates of the city all night , saying , We shall kill him until the morning
And it came to pass at midnight , when he was asleep , that he arose , and took down the doors of the city , and the windows , and the frames , and the bars , and carried them on his shoulders , and carried them on the top of the mountain before Hebron
And it came to pass , when he was in the valley of Shure , that he loved a woman named Delilah
Then the prince of the Philistines went up to the woman , and said to her , &quot; Give him counsel , and find out why he is so strong , and how can we prevail against him , and bind him , and give you one hundred shekels of silver per person
Then she said to him , &quot; Tell me , why do you have such great power , and how do you bound yourself ? &quot;
And he said , If a man bound me with seven unthorned blue ropes , I would be as weak as any man .
Then the prince of the Philistines took seven uncut blue ropes , and gave them to the woman ; and he bound the sons of Israel with them
And it came to pass , as soon as he was buried in the woman &apos;s house , that the woman said , Son of Samson , the Philistines have brought thee : and he broke the rope , as a thread that passeth through the fire , and the root of his power was not known .
And she said unto him , Thou hast deceived me , and hast lied unto me : now therefore tell me how to bind thee
And he answered and said , If a man bound me with a new cord which he had not made , I would be as weak as any man
Then Elisha bound him with a new rope , and said to him , &quot; Son of Samson , the Philistines have brought you ; and there is a man who has prepared to be buried in the inner chamber , and he has broken the rope on his arm as if he had broken a line
And she said unto him , Thou hast deceived me to this day , and hast spoken a lie unto me : tell me , and how shall I bind thee ? And he said unto him , If thou wilt weave the seven horns of my head with lace ,
Then she weaved his hair with the lashes , and nailed him with the lashes , and said unto him , Son of Samson , the Philistines have brought thee : and when he was awake from his sleep , he drew out the lashes and the lashes of the machine together .
And Delilah said unto him , Why lovest thou me , when thou hast not been with me , and hast deceived me three times , and hast not told me why thou hast so great power ?
Delilah pressed him every day with words , and even he was anxious to die
And when he had told him all that was hidden in his heart , he said unto him , No man has ever shaved my head with a razor ; for I have come from my mother unto God as a thin ear ; and if I have shaved my hair , my strength shall be gone from me , and I shall be weak as the rest of men .
And when David saw that he had told him all that was hidden in his heart , he sent messengers to the princes of the Philistines , and said unto them , He hath told me all that is hidden in his heart : come again , I pray you . And the princes of the Philistines went up to the woman with silver in their hand .
And he put him to sleep on his knees , and called a man to shave the seven hairs of his head : and he brake him , and his strength departed from him .
And Elisha said , Son of Samson , the Philistines have brought thee ; and when he was awakened from his sleep , he said in his heart , I will go out as I went out before , but he knew not that the Lord had passed away from him
And the Philistines took him , and cut off his eyes , and brought him down to Gaza , and besieged him with brass , and he was grinding in prison .
However , after his hair had been shaved , it grew again
And the princes of the Philistines gathered themselves together , and offered a great sacrifice to their God , and rejoiced , because they said , &quot; Our God has delivered our enemies into our hands .
And when they saw him , they praised their God , saying , &quot; Our God will destroy our land , and kill many of our enemies , and give them into our hands .
And it came to pass , as they were having a feast , that they said , &quot; Call forth Samson , and play with him before us ; &quot; and he brought him up from the prison , and he played with him before the people ; and they made him stand between the two pillars .
And he said unto the child that took him by the hand , Let me touch the pillars of the tabernacle , and I will lean upon one .
The room was full of men and women , and the chiefs of the Philistines were in it ; and there were about 3,000 men and women on the roof of the room to watch the play of the sunrise .
And he cried unto the LORD , saying , O Lord GOD , remember me , and give me this strength , O God , that I may bear the vengeance of the Philistines , which hath cast out my eyes
And he took hold of the two pillars of the tabernacle , one by his left hand , and one by his right hand .
&quot; I wish I had died with the Philistines , and I would have done my utmost to surrender , and the houses would have collapsed , and the princes and all the people in the houses would have been crushed . Thus more people were killed when he died than when he was alive .
And his brothers went down , and all his father &apos;s household , and took his body , and brought it up , and buried it in the tomb of Manoah his father , in the midst of Zorah and Eshtaol . And he was an officer in Israel twenty years
There was a man named Micah in the mountains of Ephraim
Then he said to his mother , &quot; Your one hundred shekels of silver were taken away by men , and you cursed them , and said to me , &apos; Behold , the silver is here with me , and I have taken it . &apos; &quot; His mother said , &quot; Blessed be the Lord with you , my son
Then Micah returned the one hundred shekels of silver to his mother , and his mother said , &quot; I have divided them for you to give to the Lord , and I will carve a statue , and cast a statue , and I will give it to you
Then Micah gave the silver to his mother , and his mother gave two hundred shekels of silver to the silversmith , and he carved an image , and cast an image , and placed it in Micah &apos;s house
And Micah had a sanctuary , and made Ephraim , and the image of God in the house , and gave him a son to be priest .
There was no king in Israel at that time , and every man did his own thing .
And there was a young man in Bethlehem of Judah , a Levite of the Jews , who dwelled there
And he departed from Bethlehem of Judah to seek a dwelling place ; and it came to pass at the time of the journey , that he came to the house of Micah in the mountains of Ephraim
Then Micah said to him , &quot; Where are you from ? &quot; He answered , &quot; From Bethlehem in Judah , I am a Levite , seeking a place to dwell
And Micah said , Thou shalt dwell here with me ; I have made thee a priest as thy father ; and I have given thee ten shekels of silver a year , and a garment , and daily bread : and the Levites entered into his house
And the Levites desired to dwell with him ; and he saw the young man as his own son
And Micah appointed the young man a Levite priest , and he lived in Micah &apos;s house
Then Micah said , &quot; Now I know that the Lord will bless me , because I have a Levite as a priest
And there was no king in Israel at that time ; but the tribes dwelled in search of land ; for in that day they had not earned any work in the tribes of Israel .
Then they sent out five of the men of Zorah and Ephraim to spy out the land , and said to them , &quot; Go spy out the land ; and when they have come to the mountains of Ephraim , and have entered the house of Micah , they will lodge there
And when they came to the house of Micah , and heard the voice of the young Levite , they entered in and asked him , Who brought you here , and what have you done here , and what have you gained here
Then answered he , Thus and thus has Micah treated me , and asked me to be a priest
And they said unto him , Ask thou God , that we may know the way in which we are going , not one way or another .
And the priest said unto them , Go ye in peace : for the way that ye walk is before the LORD
And when the five went , they came to Laburon , and saw the people there dwelling without fear , as the Sidonians dwelled : and there was no man in the land to disturb them ; and they were far from the Sidonians , and they had not come to any man .
And the five returned to Zorah and Ephraim , and saw their brethren ; and they asked them , saying , What say ye ?
They answered , &quot; Arise , and we will go up and attack them . We have peered into the land , and it is good to see it . Why do you not sit still , and do not delay to get to the land quickly for your business ?
And when ye are therein , ye shall see a people dwelling without fear ; and the land shall be extensive ; and God hath given it into your hands , and the land shall be full and full .
Then six hundred men of the tribe of Dan went up from Zorah and Ishmael , every man with his weapon .
And they came up to Gilead , which is in Judah , and pitched behind Gilead ; and the name of the place was called Mahanidan , even to this day .
From there they went to the mountains of Ephraim , and came to the house of Micah .
Then said the five men who had been spying in the hundreds of thousands of lands , to their brothers , &quot; You know that there is in this house Ephraim , and the images of God in the house , and the images of carvings , and the images of castings ; and now you will think how to do it .
And they entered into the house of Micah , and came into the house of the young Levite , and asked him :
And the six hundred men stood at the door , every man with his weapon
And the five men that were in the field went in , and took the carved images , and the images of Ephraim , and the images of the house of God , and the images that were cast : and the priest stood at the door with the six hundred men that were armed
And when the five men entered into the house of Micah , they took out a carved image , an image of Ephraim , the God of the house , and cast it ; and the priest said unto them , What do ye do ?
They answered , &quot; Don &apos;t speak out loud . Go with us , and we will make you a father and a priest . Are you good as a priest for a family , or as a priest for a tribe of Israel ? &quot;
And the priest was glad in his heart , and took the image of God which was in Ephraim and in the house , and carved it , and entered into the midst of them
Then they turned and left , and their wives , and their children , and their cattle , and their possessions , were before them
And the dwellings of Micah were far off , and all the neighbours of Micah were gathered together , and pursued Dan .
Then they called for Dan , and the Dan turned to Micah , and said , What have you done with all these multitudes ?
Then Micah said , &quot; Have you taken away the image of God and the priests that I have made , and what do I have left ? &quot; Then he asked me , &quot; What do you do ? &quot;
But they said to Micah , &quot; You will not make our ears hear your voice , lest a violent man attack you , and you and all your family die .
And Micah turned and went home , seeing that their power was stronger than his own .
But when they had brought Micah &apos;s image of God and his priests to Rehoboam , they struck him with the sword , and burned the city with fire , when they saw that there was no refuge for the people .
And there was no rescuer , because they were far from Sidon , and they had no contact with any other people ; and the city was in the plain , and the plain was near Bethlehem ; and they dwelt therein
And they called the name of the city after the name of Dan , the son of Israel , their father : and the name of the city was Lamoth
And they set up for themselves the statue of Jonah the son of Moses , the son of Gershon , and his sons , priests of the tribe of Dan , until the days of the captivity thereof .
How many days were the days of the house of God in Shiloh , and how many days were the days of the statue of Micah , which men carved for themselves
A Levite who lived on the side of the mountains of Ephraim took a daughter of Bethlehem , a Jew , as a concubine in the days of no king in Israel
The concubine went away from her husband , and returned to Bethlehem , Judah , to her father &apos;s house , and lived there four months .
And he arose , and took a servant , and two donkeys , and went to him , and counseled him with good words : and the woman led him into his father &apos;s house ; and when he saw him , he greeted him with joy .
And the father of that man , the father of the woman , left him for three days ; and they ate and drank , and lodged together
And it came to pass on the fourth day , when the Levites arose early in the morning to go , that the father of the woman said unto her son-in-law , Let thee eat bread , and add strength , and let thee walk
Then they sat down to eat and drink . And the father of the woman said unto him , Rejoice in thy heart for one more night
&quot; The man arose to go , and his father-in-law forbade him , and he stayed for a while
And it came to pass on the fifth day , when he was risen early in the morning to go , that the father of the woman said unto him , Eat and strengthen yourselves , until the day cometh , and go west again ; and they ate together
And he arose , and went with his concubines and his servants : and his father , the father of the woman , said unto him , Behold , the day is far from the west , and I pray thee to dwell one more night ; and the day is late , and thou shalt be able to lodge here in peace with thine heart : and I will go home early and early tomorrow
&quot; But the man refused to stay one more night , and took up the two donkeys , and went away with his concubine , and came to Jebus , which is Jerusalem
&quot; When the day was coming near for Jebus , the servant said to his master , &quot; Why don &apos;t we stay in the city of the Jebusites
&quot; The master answered , &quot; We cannot enter into a foreign city , which is not the home of the Israelites , but rather go to Gibeah
Then he said to his servants , &quot; We may go to a place , or live in Gibeah , or in Ramah
And they went forth , and came to Gibeah in Benjamin ; and the day had come to pass .
And when they entered into Gibeah to lodge therein , they sat in the streets of the city ; for no man received them to lodge in their houses .
And at night there came an old man from the field to work : and he was of the land of Ephraim , and he lived in Gibeah ; and the men of the land were of Benjamin .
Then the old man lifted up his eyes and saw a stranger sitting in the streets of the city , and asked him , &quot; Where are you coming from ?
And he answered and said , We are come from Bethlehem of Judah , to the side of mount Ephraim , where I was ; and I have come over to Bethlehem of Judah , and I am going into the house of the Lord ; and there shall no man receive me into his house
&quot; I have grapes to feed the donkeys . I have bread and wine with my concubines and my servants .
The elders said , &quot; Peace be to you ; I have given you all that you need , but you cannot spend the night in the streets
And he brought them into the house , and fed them with donkeys , and they washed their feet and drank .
And when they were rejoicing , the bandits of the city surrounded the house , and knocked on the doors , and said unto the old master of the house , Bring forth the man that is come into thy house , and we will make a league with him
Then the lord of the house came out and said to them , &quot; Brothers , do not do this evil ; for this man has entered into my house , so do not do this ugly thing .
&quot; I have a daughter , and a virgin , and a concubine of this man ; and I have brought them forth to defile them , because of you ; but you shall not do such abominations to this man
But they did not listen to him , and he took out his concubine , and gave her to them ; and they became partners with him , and abused him at night , and left him until the morning .
And it came to pass in the morning , when the woman returned to the door of her master &apos;s house , that she fell down to the ground , and was brought to the light .
&quot; In the morning , his master came up and opened the door , and went out on his way ; and he did not expect the woman &apos;s servant to fall before the door , and to lay his hands on the threshold
And he said unto the woman , Arise , let us go ; but the woman answered not : and he carried him on the donkey , and rose up , and went to his place
And when he was come into the house , he cut the body of his concubine in twelve pieces with the sword , and brought them into the four quarters of Israel
All those who saw said , &quot; Nothing like this has been done from the time of the Israelites to this day , from the time they came out of the land of Egypt to this day , neither have they seen it .
And all Israel , from Dan even unto Beersheba , and all the inhabitants of Gilead , came out as one , and gathered themselves together before the LORD of Mizpah
The captains of the children of Israel , and the captains of the armies of the tribes , stood in the congregation of the people of God . There were forty thousand footmen with swords .
And when the men of Israel had heard it from Mizpah to Benjamin , they said , Explain unto us this evil thing ,
The Levite , the husband of the woman who was slain , answered , &quot; I and my concubine have come to stay in Gibeah of Benjamin .
&quot; The Gibeonites rose up at night , and surrounded my house , and tried to kill me , and raped and killed my concubine
&quot; I have cut off the body of my concubine into pieces , and they shall carry it with them into all the land of Israel for a possession , because of the abominations and the abominations which they have committed against the Gibeonites in Israel .
All of you , Israel , plan and negotiate
And the people rose up as one , and said , We will not return to our tents , nor to our houses , not one of us
&quot; This is how we shall do to the Gibeonites , and we shall sign against them according to the bounds .
And we shall take out of the tribes of Israel a hundred for ten , and a thousand for a hundred , and a thousand for a thousand for food for the people : and when the great assembly come to Gibeah of Benjamin , they shall conquer them according to the abominations of the Gibeahites in Israel .
Then all Israel gathered themselves together as one man , and struck the city
Then sent all the tribes of Israel , and asked the families of the tribe of Benjamin , saying , How have you done such evil among you ?
&quot; Now you shall deliver out the bandits of Gibeah , that we may put them to death and remove this evil from Israel ; but the children of Benjamin will not listen to the words of their brothers Israel
And the children of Benjamin came out of their cities , and gathered themselves together to Gibeah to fight against the children of Israel
At that time there were twenty and six thousand of the children of Benjamin that drew swords out of the cities ; and the children of Gibeah drew seven hundred men of war .
There were seven hundred chosen soldiers in the army , all of them of the left hand , able to throw stones at men with the string of a machine , and not less than a millimeter
Out of the children of Benjamin , there were forty thousand men , all men of Israel with swords , who were warriors
Then the children of Israel arose , and went to Bethlehem , and asked God , saying , &quot; Who among us will go up first to fight with the children of Benjamin ? &quot; And the Lord said , &quot; Juda goes up first .
And the children of Israel arose in the morning , and encamped against Gibeah
&quot; Then the children of Israel came out to fight against Benjamin , and pitched before Gibeah
And the children of Benjamin came out of Gibeah , and slew the children of Israel that day twenty and two thousand
And the children of Israel fought with one another , and fought again in the first day
And the children of Israel went up before the battle , and cried before the LORD until the evening , and asked the LORD , saying , &quot; Shall we go again to battle with our brethren Benjamin , or shall we not ? &quot; And the LORD said , &quot; Shall we go up and smite them
And on the second day the children of Israel went up and struck the children of Benjamin
And the children of Benjamin came out of Gibeah that day against the children of Israel , and slew them with the edge of the sword , and slew them eighteen thousand
And all Israel went up to Bethlehem , and sat down before the LORD crying , and fasted until the evening that day , and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before the LORD
Then the ark of God was there ; and Phinehas the son of Eleazar , Aaron &apos;s son , stood in front of the ark ; and the children of Israel said to the Lord , &quot; Shall we go out again and fight with our brethren against the children of Ammon , or shall we fight with them ? &quot; The Lord said , &quot; Go up , for tomorrow I will deliver them into your hands
See you soon .
And the children of Israel pitched against Gibeah in all its quarters
And it came to pass on the third day , that the children of Israel went up again , and struck the children of Benjamin , and pitched before Gibeah , as they had done the first two days
And the children of Benjamin came out to meet the enemy , and were driven out of the city : and they slew about thirty Israelites on the two roads of the fields , one by Bethlehem and one by Gibeah , as they had slew the first two times .
Then said the children of Benjamin , &quot; They are still defeated before us ; but the children of Israel said , &quot; Let us flee , and lead them away from the city to the way
And all Israel arose , and pitched in Baal-i-Maah ; and the swordmen of Israel went up from the place where the sword was laid , from the place where the sword was laid .
And there were ten thousand men of valour among the children of Israel that came to fight before Gibeah ; and the mighty men were very mighty ; but the Benjaminites knew not that the plague was near .
And the LORD slew the children of Israel with the sword ; and in that day slew the children of Benjamin with the sword twenty and five thousand and one
Then the children of Benjamin knew that they were defeated : first the children of Israel had defeated the children of Benjamin because of the troops that they had set up before Gibeah
The foot soldiers hurried into Gibeah and struck the whole city with the sword
And the children of Israel made a covenant with the foot soldiers , that they would set fire in the city , and that they would make a sound of smoke
And it came to pass , when the children of Israel were come back , that the men of Benjamin began to slay the children of Israel , about thirty men , and said , They are still defeated as before
And it came to pass , when the smoke was poured out of the city like a pillar , that the men of Benjamin turned their faces , and saw the smoke of the whole city blowing in the sky .
And the children of Israel turned again , and behold , the children of Benjamin were terrified , because they saw that the evil was come upon them
And they fled before the children of Israel , and turned to the wilderness ; and the children of Israel pursued after them ; and those who came out of the cities struck them with the edge of the sword .
And the children of Israel went around Benjamin , and chased them , and trampled them upon Gibeah , who was in the land of the rising of the sun , where they lay their feet
And the sons of Benjamin died , and there were eighteen thousand , all of them mighty men .
And the rest turned and fled into the wilderness , and came to the rock of the gate : and the children of Israel slew five thousand of them on the way , as a picking of leaves ; and they pursued to Kedon , and slew two thousand of them .
