And the people went into the forest , and saw honey on it
When they entered the forest , they saw honey flowing down , but none dared to take it in by hand , for they feared the oath .
&quot; But Jonah did not hear his father swear to the people , so he dipped the stick in his hand into the beehive , and turned his hand into his mouth , and the eyes were bright
Then one of the people said to him , &quot; Your father made a solemn oath to the people , saying , &apos; What you eat today will be cursed ; so the people are weary .
Then Jonah said , &quot; My father is tired of you , and you see , when I have tasted the honey , my eyes are bright
&quot; What more will the people today eat of that which they have taken from their enemies , and of the Philistines that they have struck ?
And it came to pass on that day , that the children of Israel slew the Philistines from Mizpah even unto Aal-arun ; and the people were very weary
