Then Saul said to the people , &quot; Your men have brought cattle and sheep here to me to be slaughtered ; it is a sin for you , Yahweh , that you do not eat the flesh of blood , &quot; and the people brought the cattle and sheep there to be slaughtered that night
And Saul built an altar unto the LORD ; and this was the first altar he built unto the LORD
Saul said , &quot; It is better for us to go down in the night to pursue the Philistines and to plunder them , and not to leave them alone until the dawn . &quot; The people said , &quot; Go as you please , &quot; and the priest said , &quot; First let us be close to God
And Saul said unto God , I will go down to pursue the Philistines , and you will not deliver them into the hand of the children of Israel ; and God answered him not that day
And Saul said , Come , all the elders of your people , and find out who has sinned this day
&quot; I swear by the Lord , who will save Israel forever , that my son Jonathan will die for his sins ; but none of the people answered him
