And Saul prayed unto the LORD God of Israel , saying , Show me the truth ; and he cast out Saul and Jonathan , and all the people were well
Then Saul said , &quot; Set your fingers again , and see that I am Jonathan my son ; and bring out Jonathan
Then Saul said to Jonathan , &quot; Tell me what you have done . &quot; Jonathan said , &quot; I am in my hand with a staff , and I have dipped a little honey in the head of the staff , and I have tasted it ; will I then die ? &quot;
And Saul said , O Jonathan , if thou wilt not die , let God bring upon me a great punishment
And the people said unto Saul , Shall Jonathan save so great a thing among the children of Israel that he should die ? for we have sworn by the LORD of hosts that not a hair of his should fall , because he doeth this day the same thing with God . And the people saved Jonathan from death
And Saul returned , and pursued not the Philistines ; and the Philistines returned to Ben .
Saul ruled over the kingdom of Israel , and he often attacked all the enemies around him , the Moabites , the Ammonites , the Edomites , the kings of Zobah , and the Philistines ; and wherever he went , he defeated them
