&quot; But the people have taken the best sheep and goats of the slaughter , and they will offer them to the Lord your God in Gideon .
Then Samuel said , &quot; Is the Lord pleased with the burnt offering and with the sacrifice of peace like a happy man who listens to His word ? Hear life is better than sacrifice , and obey is better than the fat of the goat
The sin of disobedience is like the sin of evil deeds , and the sin of obstinacy is like the sin of worshipping false gods and idols ; and you reject the commandment of the Lord , and the Lord rejects you as kings
Saul said to Samuel , &quot; I have sinned , because I feared that the people would listen to their words , and I have contravened the commandment of the Lord and your words
&quot; Behold , I ask forgiveness of my sins , and return with me , that I may worship the Lord
Then Samuel said to Saul , &quot; I am different from you when you go back , because you reject the commandment of the Lord , and the Lord rejects you as king over Israel
Then Samuel turned to go , and took away the collar of his robe , and the collar of his robe was torn
