And Saul himself went to Ramah , and came to the great well of Zadok , and said unto the people , Where are Samuel and David ? And they said , Nahor in Ramah .
And he went to Nahor in Ramah , and the Spirit of God moved him , and he went and spoke to Nahor in Ramah .
Then he took off his clothes , and began to speak in the ears of Sarah , and lay on his face day and night ; and it came to pass , saying , Is Saul also among the prophets ?
And David fled from Nahor in Ramah , and came to Jonathan , and said unto him , What have I done , and what iniquity have I committed before thy father , that he seek my life ?
Then Jonah answered , &quot; No , you will not die . My father has done nothing to make me know what he has done , no matter how great it is . How can he hide it from me alone ? It will never be so .
Then David took another oath , saying , &quot; Your father knows that I have been blessed before you , &quot; and he said in his heart , &quot; It would be better not to let Jonathan know , lest he be troubled . I have sworn before you by the Lord of everlasting life , and I am a step away from death
Then Jonathan said to David , &quot; I will do for you what you have asked of me
Then David said to Jonathan , &quot; Tomorrow is the first day , and I will be with the king , and you will allow me to hide myself in the field until the third night
&quot; If your father sees me not in his seat , you shall say , &apos; Please let David go back to his own city , to Bethlehem ; for there his whole family sacrifices annually
&quot; If your father says good , the servant is at ease ; and if he is angry , you will know that he is determined to do me harm
&quot; Be merciful to your servants , for you have made a covenant with them before the Lord . If I should be guilty , why would you hand me over to your father if you killed me yourself ?
&quot; But Jonah said , &quot; Do not say this . If I knew that my father was determined to do you harm , would I not tell you ?
Then David said to Jonathan , &quot; Who will tell me if your father answers you with a sharp tongue ?
Then Jonathan said to David , &quot; You and I go to the field . Then the two went to the field
Then Jonathan said to David , &quot; Let the Lord , the God of Israel , be the witness ; for tomorrow , at this time , or on the third day , I will seek out the words of my father ; will I not send a message to you , if you will do me good ? &quot;
&quot; If my father intends to harm you , I will not tell you to walk in peace . May the Lord be with me in great retribution , and may the Lord be with you as he was with my father before
&quot; Be merciful to me in the Lord &apos;s mercy , and spare me not from death while I am alive .
&quot; When the Lord will cut off your enemies from the earth after my death , you will never give up your favor to my house
Then Jonathan made an alliance with the house of David , saying , &quot; May the Lord redeem the sins of the LORD through the enemy of David
Jonathan took another oath from David , because he loved his own life as he loved his own
Then Jonah said to him , &quot; Tomorrow is the first day . Your seat will be empty , and people will consider you if you are not in it
&quot; Wait three days , and go down quickly , and wait in the rock of Ephraim , where you hid yourselves from the evil that you committed before .
&quot; I will shoot three arrows at the side of the rock , like the arrow of a target
&quot; I will send the child , saying , &apos; Go and find the arrow ; &apos; and if I say to the child , &apos; The arrow is behind you , take it , and you will return ; &apos; I swear by the Lord , the Everlasting One , &apos; You will be safe and sound .
&quot; If I say to the child , &apos; The arrow is in front of you , &apos; you will go ; for the Lord has sent you
&quot; As for the words which you and I have spoken today , the Lord is witness between you and me for ever and ever
And David hid himself in the field : and it came to pass on the first day , that the king sat down to eat
