But Saul had nothing to say that day ; he thought that David was unclean by chance , and that he must be unclean .
Then Saul said to Jonathan his son , &quot; Why did the son of Jesse not come to eat bread yesterday and to this day ? &quot;
Then Jonathan answered Saul , and said , David ask me to let him go to Bethlehem
And he said , Let me go , for there is a sacrifice in my house in the city , which my elder brother commanded me to do ; and if I now have mercy in your sight , let me go to my brethren ; and David shall have no place in the king &apos;s seat .
Saul was angry with Jonathan , and said to him , &quot; Did I not know that you , a woman who is stubborn and rebellious , were born to please the son of Jesse , and to be ashamed of yourself until your mother appeared to be ashamed ?
&quot; If the son of Jesse is alive in the world , you and your throne will not stand . Now send a messenger to me , and take him and hand him over to me ; he is to die .
Then Jonathan said to Saul his father , Why should he die , and what has he done ?
Saul struck Jonathan with a gun , and Jonathan knew that his father was determined to kill David
So Jonah rose up from his seat , and did not eat on the first two days of his reign ; and when he saw David &apos;s father &apos;s shame , he was troubled
And the next morning Jonathan went out into the field , according to the time that David had been appointed , and a child followed him .
And Jonathan said unto the child , Run , and find the arrow that I have cast : and when the child ran , Jonathan cast the arrow before him .
And the child came to the place where Jonathan fell upon the arrow ; and Jonathan called and said unto him , Is not the arrow before thee ?
Then Jonah called the child again , and said , &quot; Go quickly , and do not delay ; &quot; and he picked up the arrow , and returned to his master .
But the child did not know what it meant ; only Jonathan and David knew
