But David took the shield of Zion , the city of David .
David said on that day , &quot; Whoever attacks the Jebusites when he attacks the lame and blind man in the ditch , whom I hate in my heart , &quot; and it has been said since then , &quot; There is a lame and blind man in it , and he cannot enter the house
&quot; He lived in the city of David , and called it the city of David ; and he built walls around it from Miroel
For the Lord God of hosts is with David
Then Hilan king of Tyre brought the acacia trees to David , and sent messengers and carpenters and stonemasons to build him a palace
And David knew that the LORD had established him king over Israel , and that his kingdom had prospered for his people Israel
And after David had departed from Hebron , he became a wife in Jerusalem , and bore children
The sons of Shemaiah , Sheothaim , Nathan , and Solomon , who were born in Jerusalem ,
Ephraim , and Elisha , and Nephim , and Japhim ,
Elishama , Elijah , Eliphael ,
And when the Philistines heard that they anointed David king of Israel , all the Philistines went up to seek David : and when David heard it , he went down to the garrison
And the Philistines came , and spread themselves out in the valley of Lymeon
David asked the Lord , &quot; Can I go up and fight against the Philistines ? Will you hand them over to me ? &quot; The Lord said , &quot; You can go up , and I will hand the Philistines over to you
Then David came to Balak-Bhalibah , and struck the Philistines therein , and said , &quot; The Lord has struck the enemy before me as the waters struck ; so the place shall be called Balak-Bhalibah
The Philistines left the idols there , and David and those who were with him took them away .
And the Philistines came up again , and spread out in the valley of Lymeon
And David asked the Lord , and the Lord said , &quot; Do not go up , and turn after them , and attack them from the side of Samaria
&quot; When you hear the sound of the footsteps on the tops of the palm trees , go quickly forth ; for at that time the Lord had come before you to smite the army of the Philistines
And David went according to the commandment of the LORD , and struck the Philistines from Capernaum even unto Gibeah
And David gathered together all the chosen men of Israel , thirty thousand
And David rose up , and led all the people that were with him , and brought forth the ark of God , which was brought forth out of Judah , which was the name of the Lord of hosts , who sat on the two reins .
And they lifted up the ark of God out of the house of Abinadab in Gog , and put it in a new cart ; and Uzzah and Ahijah the sons of Abinadab drove it .
And it came to pass , when they had brought forth the ark of God out of the house of Abi-Nadab in Gog , that Ahijah walked before the ark .
And David and all the house of Israel danced before the LORD with instruments of pine , and with harps , and psalteries , and harps , and psalteries , and psalteries ,
&quot; When he came to the field of grapes in Burgundy , because the cattle had lost their hoofs , he stretched out his hand to hold the ark of God
And the LORD God was angry with him , and he slew him for his error , and he died by the ark of God
And David was troubled because of the LORD &apos;s smite of Uzzah , and called the place Blessed Uzzah to this day
David feared the Lord that day and said , &quot; How can the ark of the Lord come to me
So David refused to bring the ark of the LORD into the city of David , but brought it into the house of the children of Gad east of Obed
The ark of the LORD was in the house of Obedeon the Gadites three months : and the LORD blessed Obedeon and his household
Then there came a man to the king , saying , &quot; The Lord has blessed the house of Obed-edom and all that belongs to them for the ark ; and David went and brought the ark of God , the cheerful bringer , up from the house of Obed-edom into the city of David
And the man who carried the ark of the LORD went six steps , and David offered the bullocks and the fat lambs for a sacrifice
And David danced in the presence of the LORD , even Ephraim in fine linen
So David and the whole house of Israel lifted up the ark of the Lord with a loud voice
When the ark of the LORD came into the city of David , Micah the daughter of Saul looked out of the window , and saw King David dancing before the LORD , and she despised him in her heart
And they brought in the ark of the LORD , and laid it in the place which he had prepared , in the tent which David had set up ; and David offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before the LORD
And when David had finished the burnt offering and the sacrifice of peace , he blessed the people in the name of the Lord of hosts
And he gave unto all Israel , both men and women , a cake , and a meat cake , and a grape cake : and they went every man to his house .
Then came Micah , Saul &apos;s daughter , out to meet him , and said to him , &quot; Glory be to the king of Israel , that he may appear before his servant &apos;s maids today , as a humble and shameless man .
And David said unto Micah , This is before the LORD ; for the LORD hath chosen me , and hath cut off thy father and all thy father &apos;s house , and hath made me king over Israel the people of the LORD ; therefore I will dance before the LORD
&quot; I will also be more humble and humble to myself ; and the maids whom you have spoken of will respect me .
And Micah , Saul &apos;s daughter , bare no sons until the day of her death .
&quot; The king dwells in his own house ; the Lord has made him rest , and he is not disturbed by the enemies around him
Then the king said to Nathan the prophet , &quot; Behold , I live in the palace of acacia , and the ark of God is in the mantle
Then Nathan said to the king , &quot; You can do as you wish , for the Lord is with you
And the word of the LORD came to Nathan in the night , saying ,
&quot; Go and tell my servant David , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; Will you build a house for me to dwell in ?
&quot; I have not lived in the temple , nor walked in the tents of meeting , nor in the tents of tents , from whence I brought the children of Israel out of Egypt to this day
&quot; Wherever I went with the children of Israel , I said to the centurions of the tribe of Israel , and to the shepherds of my people Israel , &apos; Why don &apos;t you build me a palace of cedars ?
&quot; Now tell my servant David , &apos; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; I have called you out of the flock , that you may no longer be with the flock , and that you may be king over my people Israel
Wherever you go , I will always be with you ; I will cut off all your enemies , and I will make you a great name , as a great man in the world .
&quot; I will choose a place for my people Israel , and I will cultivate them , and I will make them dwell in their own place , and they will not move ; and the sons of the wicked will not disturb them as before .
&quot; I will make you to rest , and not be disturbed by all your enemies ; and I will set up houses for you , as my Lord has promised you ,
&quot; When your days are fulfilled , when you sleep with your ancestors , I will make your descendants succeed you , and I will establish his country .
He will build houses in My name , and I will establish His throne forever .
&quot; I will be his father , and he will be my son ; and if he sins , I will punish him with the rod of men , and with the whip of men .
But my loving kindness is not departed from him , as from Saul , who was rejected before thee .
Thy house and thy land shall stand firm before Me for ever , and thy throne shall stand firm for ever .
&quot; Take the book and tell David according to all these words , and according to this commandment ,
Then king David went in , and sat before the Lord , and said , &quot; Lord Yahweh , who am I , and what is my house , that you have brought me to this place
&quot; Is this , O Lord Yahweh , a small thing in your sight , and a promise to the house of your servants for a long time , O Lord Yahweh , a thing that is common to man ?
&quot; What more can I say to you , Lord Yahweh , because you know your servants
&quot; You have done this great thing to make known to your servants , because of your promises , and because of your heart
&quot; Lord Yahweh , you are great ; there is none like you in our ears , and there is no god except you .
&quot; There is no nation in the world like your people Israel . You have redeemed them from Egypt as your own children , and you have done great and terrible things in front of the people whom you have redeemed . You have driven out the nations and their gods , and you have made known your great name .
&quot; You have strengthened your people , Israel , as your children for ever , and you , Yahweh , have made them their God
&quot; Your word , O Lord God , which you have promised to your servants and to their families , be firm for ever , and do as you have spoken .
&quot; Let people honor your name forever , and say , &apos; The Lord of hosts is the God of Israel ; &apos; and the house of your servant David will stand before you
O Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , for you have revealed to your servants , saying , &quot; I will build a house for you , &quot; so they boldly pray to you
&quot; But you , Lord Yahweh , are God , and your words are true ; and you shall give this blessing to your servants
Blessed be the house of your servants , O Lord GOD , which you have promised them , that they may live forever in your presence ; bless the house of your servants forever
Then David struck the Philistines , and conquered them , and took the kingdom of Beijing from their hands .
And they struck the Moabites , and laid them down on the ground , and slew them with one rope , and two rope , and one rope for the remnant ; and the Moabites delivered them into the hand of David , and gave him a hire
And Hadadezer the son of Eliab king of Zobah went to the River to take back his kingdom ; and David struck him
He took away one thousand seven hundred horsemen and twenty thousand footmen , and cut off the horses of the chariots , and left behind the horses of the hundred chariots
And the children of Aram of Damascus came to help Hadadezer king of Zobah ; and David slew the children of Aram twenty and two thousand
Then David set up a camp in the land of Aram , in Damascus ; and the children of Aram gave him inheritance for a hire ; and David went there without saying , and the Lord overcame him
And he took the gold shield which the servant of Hadadezer had taken , and brought it to Jerusalem
And king David took much of the copper from Beeroth of Hadadezer , and from the city of Beeroth ,
And king Darius of Hama heard that David had defeated all the army of Hadadezer
And he sent Joram his son to king David , and asked him for an安 , and blessed him , because he had defeated Hadadezer , for he had often fought with Hadadezer : and Joram brought with him vessels of silver and gold
&quot; All these vessels , and all the silver and gold that David had brought in the kingdoms , he consecrated to the Lord
that came from Aram , Moab , Ammon , Philistines , and Amalek , and that was plundered from Hadadezer the son of Reuel king of Zobah ,
And when David had slain Aaron in the valley of salt , and had returned eighteen thousand men , he was glorified
And they set up camps in all the land of Edom ; and all the men of Edom surrendered unto David ; and David went not into it , but the LORD overcame him
David was king over all Israel , and he did righteousness to all the people
And Joab the son of Zeruiah was captain , and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahithophel historian .
And Zadok the son of Ahithophel , and Ahimiel the son of Abijah , were over the priests , and Silaj the scribe .
Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the tribe of the Philistines , and over the tribe of the Philistines , and over all the children of David
Then David said , &quot; The rest of the house of Saul are gone , and there is no man left : for Jonathan &apos;s sake I will give him a favour
And there was a servant of Saul , whose name was Sheba ; and they called him to David . And the king said unto him , Art thou Sheba ? And he answered , The servant is Sheba
And the king said , There is no man in the house of Saul , but I will have mercy on him in the sight of God . And Sheba said unto the king , There is also a lame son of Jonathan
And the king said , There he is . And Baal said unto the king , He is in the house of Margiel the son of Baramiel of Rhode
So king David sent and called him from the house of Machi , the son of Bar-amili the Rodethite
Then came Miphibosheth the son of Jonathan , Saul &apos;s son , to David ; and he bowed himself to David , and said , Miphibosheth ; and Miphibosheth said , Here is my servant
And David said , Fear not : for the sake of Jonathan thy father will I give thee all the land of Saul thy father , and thou shalt eat with me continually .
Then Miphibosheth bowed again , and said , &quot; What is it that a servant is not as a dead dog , but receives the king &apos;s affection
Then the king called to Saul &apos;s servant Baal , and said to him , &quot; I have given to your master the sons of Saul and all the inheritance of his house
&quot; You and all your servants shall sow the fields for Midian the son of your master , and bring to him what he has produced for his sustenance ; and he shall eat with me continually .
And Sheba said unto the king , All that my lord my king hath commanded his servants , they shall do ; and the king said , Mephibosheth shall eat with me , as the king &apos;s sons do
And Miphibosheth had a little son , whose name was Micah : and all that dwelt in the house of Sheba were servants unto Miphibosheth .
And Miphibosheth lived in Jerusalem , and ate with the king continually : and his legs were lame
Then the king of the children of Ammon died , and Hanun his son reigned in his stead
Then David sent his servants to comfort him for his father &apos;s death , and his servants came to the land of the children of Ammon
But the princes of the children of Ammon said to their lord Hanun , &quot; Do you think that David has sent a man to comfort you , to respect your father , and that he has sent his servants to spy on this city , and to overthrow it ?
And Hanun shaved the beard of the servants of David in half , and cut off their garments in half , and exposed them , and sent them back
Then there was a man who accused David , and sent a messenger to meet them , because they were ashamed , and told them , &quot; You can stay in Jericho until your beard grows and you come back
And when the children of Ammon knew that David hated them , they sent messengers to recruit the children of Aram of Belize , and the children of Aram of Zobah , twenty thousand footmen , and a thousand men with king Magah , and a thousand and two thousand of the children of Doab .
And when David heard it , he sent forth Joab with all his mighty army
And the children of Ammon went out , and pitched before the gate of the city ; and the children of Zobah , and the children of Aram , and the children of Dober , and the children of Manasseh , and the children of Reuim , pitched in the fields
And when Joab saw that the enemy stood before him and behind him , he chose men of valour out of the army of Israel , and set them before the children of Aram
And the rest of the army joined themselves with his brother Abijah , and pitched against the children of Ammon .
And Joab said to Abishai , If the children of Aram oppress me , you will help me ; and if the children of Ammon oppress you , I will help you
&quot; Let us be strong , and cities for the people of our land , and for the cities of God ; and let the Lord do according to his will .
So Joab and those who were with him went forward to attack the children of Aram ; and the children of Aram fled before Joab .
And when the children of Ammon saw that the children of Aram fled , they fled before Abishai , and entered into the city ; and Joab departed from the children of Ammon , and returned to Jerusalem
When the children of Aram saw that they were defeated by the children of Israel , they gathered themselves together again
And Hadadezer sent messengers , and brought the children of Aram by the river : and they came to Shelah , and Shaopha the general of Hadadezer led them .
And there came a man against David , and he gathered all Israel together , and came over the Jordan unto the land of Syria ; and the children of Aram stood before David , and fought against him
And the children of Aram fled before the children of Israel ; and David slew the men of the seven hundred chariots of Aram , and the 40,000 horsemen , and Shaopha the general of Aram
And when the kings of Hadadezer saw that they were defeated by the children of Israel , they returned to them in peace with the children of Israel ; and the children of Aram refused to help the children of Ammon any more
And it came to pass after a year , when the kings were at war , that David sent Joab and his servants and all Israel to war , and they defeated the children of Ammon and besieged Rabbah ; and David lived in Jerusalem
And it came to pass on the day that David rose up from his bed , and walked on the top of the palace , and saw a woman bathing , and her appearance was beautiful .
And David sent messengers to hear who was the woman : and they said , She is Bathsheba the daughter of Ephraim , the wife of Uriah the Hittite .
And David sent and took the woman , and it was at that time that his menstruation was cleansed ; and when he came , David was with him , and he went home
Then he conceived , and sent messengers to tell David , &quot; I have conceived
And David sent to Joab , and said , Send Uriah the Hittite unto me ; and he sent Uriah to meet David .
Then came Uriah , and David asked Joab , and the soldiers , and what was the matter of the battle
Then David said to Uriah , &quot; Go home and wash your feet . Then Uriah went out of the king &apos;s house , and the king gave him a portion of food
But Uriah slept outside the door of the house with his master &apos;s servants , and went not home
And there was a man who accused David , saying , There was no way for Uriah to go home . And David said to Uriah , Why didst thou not go home from a far way
And Uriah said unto David , The ark and Israel and the army of Judah dwell in the tents ; and my lord Joab and my lord &apos;s servants camp in the field : shall I go home to eat and drink , and sleep with my wife , and swear before the king that I will not do this thing ?
And David said unto Uriah , Thou shalt dwell here this day , and I will send thee to morrow : and Uriah dwelled in Jerusalem that day and the next day
And David called Uriah , and commanded him to eat and drink before him , and to be drunk : and it came to pass in the evening , that Uriah went out , and lodged with his Lord &apos;s servants , until he had returned to his house .
The next morning David wrote a letter to Joab and took it with him to Uriah
&quot; It is written in the letter , &apos; You shall send Uriah to the most dangerous place , and you shall turn back and kill him .
And it came to pass , when Joab had besieged the city , that when he knew that there were mighty men in the enemy , he sent Uriah there
And the men of the city went out to fight with Joab ; and of the servants of David were slain a few ; and Uriah the Hittite died .
So Joab sent messengers to tell David about all the matters concerning the battle
And he charged the messenger , saying , &quot; You have spoken to the king all the matters concerning the battle
&quot; If the king is angry , and asks you , &apos; Why do you fight against the walls of the city ? Do you not know that the enemy will shoot at the city ?
&quot; Who was the man who killed Abimelech the son of Jerubim before ? Was it not a woman who threw a stone out of the city , and struck him , and he died at Teman ? Why did you come near the wall ? Then you said , &apos; The servant of the king , Hur , was also dead .
&quot; The angel rose up to meet David , and spoke to him according to the word of Joab ,
And the angel said unto David , The enemy hath overcome us , and come out into the country to fight with us , and we shall pursue them , and come straight unto the gate of the city
And the arrowmen shot the king &apos;s servants out of the city , and struck several , and Uriah the Hittite died .
And the king said to the messengers , &quot; Tell Job , &apos; Do not grieve over this matter , neither sword nor slay this man , nor slay that man , but you will do your utmost to destroy the city and to overthrow it .
When the wife of Uriah heard that Uriah &apos;s husband was dead , she wept for him
And it came to pass , when the days of mourning were past , that David sent him into the house , and she became his wife , and gave him a son : but the Lord was not pleased with all that David did .
And the LORD sent Nathan to David ; and when he was come to David , he said unto him , There are two men in a city , one rich and one poor
Rich families , many cattle and sheep
&quot; The poor has nothing but a little lamb , which he has bought for his livelihood ; and the lamb grows up in his house with his daughters , eating what he eats , drinking what he drinks , sleeping in his womb , and looking upon him as a woman
&quot; There came a guest to the house of the rich , and the rich man could not take a lamb of his flock for his guests , but he took the lamb of the poor man for his guests .
Then David was very angry with the man , and said to Nathan , &quot; I have sworn by the LORD of hosts that whoever does this shall die .
&quot; He will repay the lamb fourfold , because he has done this without a heart of mercy
Then Nathan said to David , &quot; Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel , &apos; I anointed you king of Israel , and I saved you from the hand of Saul
&quot; I will give you your master &apos;s household , and your master &apos;s wife will be in your arms , and I will give you Israel and Judah ; and if you are not enough , I will multiply it for you beforehand .
Why do you despise the commandment of the LORD , and do evil in his sight ? Why have you lent the sword of the children of Ammon , and killed Uriah the Hittite , and married his wife
&quot; Because you have despised me and taken the wife of Uriah the Hittite as your wife , the sword will never leave your house
Thus saith the Lord ; Behold , I will bring evil upon thee from thy house , and I will give thy concubines unto others before thee , and he shall sleep with them under the sun
&quot; But I will recompense you in the sight of all Israel under the sun , when you do it in the darkness
And David said unto Nathan , I have sinned against the LORD ; and Nathan said , The LORD hath blotted out thy sin , and thou shalt not die
&quot; It is only because you have done this thing that the enemy of the Lord will have a great opportunity to blaspheme ; therefore your children will surely die .
Then Nathan went home , and the LORD struck the child of David , which was born to the wife of Uriah , and made him very sick
So David begged God for the child , and fasted , and went into the inner room , and lay on the ground all night
&quot; The elders of his house came to him to lift him up from the earth ; but he refused to rise and did not eat with them
And it came to pass on the seventh day , that the child was dead ; and the servants of David dared not tell him that the child was dead ; for they said , &quot; We counseled him when the child was still alive , and yet he refused to listen to us . Would it not be more grievous if we told him that the child was dead ? &quot;
When David saw the servants speaking to one another with low voices , he knew that the child was dead . He asked the servants , &quot; Is the child dead ? &quot; They said , &quot; He is dead
And David arose from the earth , and bathed himself , and anointed himself , and changed his garments , and went into the house of the Lord to worship , and came again into the house ; and he commanded the people to cook , and he ate
Then the servant asked him , &quot; What do you mean ? When the child is alive , you fast and weep . When the child is dead , you fall down to eat
David said , &quot; The child is still alive , and I fast and weep , because I do not know whether the Lord will have mercy on me , or whether the child will not die .
&quot; The child is dead ; why should I fast ? Can I bring him back ? I will go to him , but he will not come back to me
And David comforted Bathsheba his wife , and slept with him ; and he gave birth to a son , and called his name Solomon ; and the Lord loved him
and by the prophet gave him a name , Jedeiah , because the Lord loved him
And Joab took Rabbah , the city of the sons of Ammon ,
And Joab sent messengers to David , saying , I will attack Rabbah , and take its water city
&quot; Now gather the rest of the army together in your midst , and besiege the city ; for I am afraid that I have taken it , and it will be called by my name
Then David gathered his army together , and went to Laba to attack the city , and took it
And he took the crown of gold that the king of the children of Ammon had worn , and the gold that was on it , and he joined it again , and embedded it with stones ; and they put it on David &apos;s head ; and David took much of the treasures of the city .
Thus did David do to the inhabitants of the cities of the children of Ammon , when he brought forth the men of the city under saws , or under bars , or under axes , or through bricks ; and David and his army returned to Jerusalem .
And Absalom the son of David had a beautiful sister , whose name was Ma : and Amnon the son of David loved him .
And Amon was troubled for his sister , whose mother was ill , and whose mother was a virgin ; and Amon dealt hard with him
And there was a friend of Amnon , named Jonathan , the son of Shemiah , the brother of David , a man of great cunning
And he said unto him , Son of the king , why is a day weaker than a day ? tell me , I pray thee . And he answered , I love the sister of my brother Absalom , Herma
Then Jonah said to him , &quot; Do not lie in bed , and your father comes to see you , and says to him , &apos; Father , call my sister Herma , and prepare for me food before my eyes , and give it to me , that I may see it , and take it from his hand
Then the king came to him and said to the king , &quot; Father , let my sister Hama come and make for me two cakes in my sight , that I may take them from his hand
Then David sent messengers into the house , and said to him , &quot; Go to your brother &apos;s dark house , and prepare food for him
And he went into the house of his brother , which was lying in darkness ; and he baked bread before his eyes , and it was baked
Then he threw the bread out of the pot before him , but he refused to eat ; and he said , &quot; Leave me alone ; and all the people will leave him alone
And he said unto her , Take the bread into the bedroom , and I will take it out of your hand to eat ; and she took the bread that she had made , and brought it into the bedroom , and went into the room of his brother Amnon
And he took the cake and gave it to him ; and he drew his hand and said , My sister , come and sleep with me
He said , &quot; My brother , do not defile me ; do not do this among the children of Israel ; do not do this ugly thing .
&quot; Why do I hide my shame , when you have defiled me ? You have also become a fool in Israel . You can ask the king , and he will not forbid me to come to you .
But he refused to listen to his words ; for he defiled him with greater power than he , and slept with him .
Then he hated him exceedingly , and his heart hated him more than it had loved him before . He said to him , &quot; Come and go .
He said , &quot; No , it is worse than what you have done , that you have driven me out of the land ; &quot; but Amon refused to listen to him .
Then he called his servant , and said to him , &quot; Bring the woman out ; and when she comes out , you will buckle the door .
And he was clothed in sackcloth ; for the princess that had not been married was clothed in sackcloth . And the servant of the darkness drove him out , and shut the door with bars .
And he laid the dust upon his head , and torn the garment that he had worn ; and he held his head with his hands , and went on one side , and cried on the other .
And his brother Absalom said unto him , Is not thine brother Amon near with thee ? my sister , let no one speak for a while ; he is thy brother , and let no one put this thing in his heart : and he dwelt alone in his brother Absalom &apos;s house
When King David heard this , he was very angry
And Absalom did not speak good or evil to his brother Amon ; for Absalom hated Amon because he had defiled his sister Hama
And it came to pass after two years , that there was a shepherd for Absalom in Balakshazzar , which was near Ephraim , and Absalom asked the king &apos;s sons to go with him
Then Absalom came to the king , and said , &quot; There is a shepherd for the servants , and he asks the king and his servants to go with him
And the king said unto Absalom , My son , we shall not go together , lest it be too much for thee . And Absalom asked the king again , and the king refused to go , but blessed him
And Absalom said , If the king will not go , ask the king to let my brother Amen go with him ; and the king said , Why will he go
And Absalom cried again to the king , and the king promised Amnon and all the king &apos;s children to go with him
And Absalom said unto his servants , Behold , the time when the wine of the young men is poured out , and I said unto you , Kill the young men , and ye shall kill him , and fear not : is it not that I commanded you , that ye should be strong and mighty ?
And the servants of Absalom went to Amnon , as Absalom had commanded them : and all the king &apos;s sons arose , and rode on horses , and fled .
And while they were yet on the way , there came a voice unto David , saying , Absalom hath killed all the king &apos;s sons , and hath left none
And the king arose , and rent his clothes , and lay on the ground ; and all his servants rent their clothes , and stood by him
Then Jehonadab the son of Shemiah , David &apos;s elder brother , said , &quot; Lord , I will not kill all the sons and the young men of the king . Only one Amon has died , and Amon has been determined to kill Amon since the day Amon defiled his sister Hama , Absalom &apos;s daughter .
&quot; Do not put this thing in your heart , O Lord my king , for all the sons of the king have died ; only one of the sons of Ammon has died .
And Absalom fled , and the watchman lifted up his eyes , and saw many coming from the way of the hillside .
Then Jonathan said to the king , &quot; Behold , all the king &apos;s sons have come , and they are in accord with what your servant has said
And it came to pass at the end of the word , that all the king &apos;s sons came and cried with a loud voice , and the king and his servants wept with great mourning
And Absalom fled to Damascus , the son of Amish , king of Gibeah : and David mourned daily for his son
And Absalom fled to Geshur , and lived there three years .
After the death of Amnon , King David was comforted ; and he remembered Absalom in his heart
And Joab the son of Reuah knew that the king thought of Absalom
Then he sent a messenger to Tikoah , and from there a wise woman called to him , saying , &quot; Please dress yourself as a deceased woman , and not as a dying woman , but as a woman who has mourned for a long time .
And he entered into the king &apos;s house , and said unto the king , Thus and thus : and Joseph taught the woman according to all that he had said
And the women of Tikoah came to the king , and worshipped the LORD , and said , O king , save me
And the king said unto him , What hast thou to do ? And he answered , The maid is indeed a widow ; my husband is dead
&quot; I have two sons , and one day they fought in the field , and there was no one to persuade , and he slew the one .
Then all the people of the house arose and attacked the maidservant , saying , &quot; Bring out the man who killed his brother , that we may put him to death , and that we may repay him for the death of his brother , and that they may destroy those who are in charge of the household ; and they will destroy the coal fire that remains of me , and they will not remain in the world after I have left a name with my husband . &quot;
&quot; The king said to the woman , &quot; Go home , and I will command you
And the woman of Tiko said unto the king , My lord my king , let this sin be upon me , and upon my father &apos;s house , and upon the king and upon the king &apos;s office
&quot; The king said , &quot; Whoever is troubled for you , bring him to me , and he will not disturb you any more
&quot; The woman said , &quot; Let the king remember the Lord your God , and let those who do not pay blood-for-death do so , lest they destroy my son , &quot; and the king said , &quot; I swear by the Lord for ever , &quot; Your son , not a hair will fall to the ground
&quot; The woman said , &quot; My Lord , my king , allow the maid to say another word , &quot; and the king said , &quot; You say it
The woman said , &quot; Why does the king intend to harm the people of God ? The king does not bring back those who fled , but he speaks falsely .
&quot; We shall all die as water that pours out on the earth , and shall not be recovered . God does not take away the life of man , but He makes the fleeing not to return .
&quot; I have come to tell my Lord , my king , because of the fear of the people , and the maid-servant thinks that it is better to tell the king , or that the king will do what the maid-servant asks
&quot; They will destroy me and my son from the land of God , and the king will promise to deliver me from his hand
And the maid thought that the words of my lord my king would comfort me ; for my lord my king is able to discern right and wrong , as the messenger of God ; but the Lord your God be with you
And the king said unto the woman , I will ask thee a word , and thou shalt not hide me a moment : and the woman said , Let my lord my king say
The king said , &quot; Isn &apos;t this the will of Joseph ? &quot; And the woman said , &quot; I swear by my Lord , my king , that his words are true , and that he is not a partisan , and that he is my servant , and that he has taught me
Thus did Joab , the servant of the king , that the wisdom of my Lord might be restored , and that he might know all things in the world , as the wisdom of the angels of God .
Then the king said to Joab , &quot; I have given you my word : go and bring the young man Absalom back
Then Joab fell on his face and worshipped the king , and thanked him , and said , &quot; The king has done what he asked of his servants , and they know today that they have been blessed in the sight of my Lord my king
So Joab went up to Gibeah , and brought Absalom back to Jerusalem
Then the king said , &quot; Let him go back to his own house , and he will not see me ; but Absalom will go back to his own house , and he will not see the king . &quot;
No man in all the land of Israel is as beautiful as Absalom , and is praised , from the bottom to the top , without defect .
And his hair was heavy , and he shaved it at the end of the year : and he that was shaved was two hundred shekels , according to the king &apos;s measure .
And Absalom begat three sons , and a daughter , whose name was Naamah , a beautiful woman .
And Absalom lived in Jerusalem two years , and saw not the face of the king .
And Absalom sent for Joab to see the king , and he refused ; and the second time he sent for him , and he refused
Then Absalom said to his servants , &quot; Behold , there is a field in Joab , which is near to my field , and in it is wheat ; and you shall set it on fire ; and Absalom &apos;s servants shall set it on fire
Then Joab arose , and came to the house of Absalom , and said to him , &quot; Why have your servants set fire to my field ?
And Absalom answered and said unto Joab , I have sent messengers to ask thee , that thou mayest come unto the king , and speak unto me , saying , Why am I come again from the book of Genesis , rather than to remain there ? now let me see the king &apos;s face , and if I have sinned , let the king kill me .
So Joab went to the king , and told the king . And the king called Absalom , and Absalom came to the king , and he fell down before the king , and the king kissed Absalom
Then Absalom prepared for himself chariots and horses , and sent fifty men to run before him .
And Absalom rose up in the morning by the way of the gate , and he called him , and said unto him , Art thou of that city ? And he answered , The servant is of a tribe of Israel
And Absalom said unto him , Thy cause is right ; but the king hath not appointed any to hear thy plea
Then said Absalom , &quot; Do not despise me as a warrior in the land ; and whoever has a dispute and seeks judgment , come to me , and I will judge with justice .
&quot; If any man comes near to worship Absalom , he will stretch out his hand against him , and kiss him
Thus did Absalom deal with all the people of Israel , who went to the king to judge them ; and thus did Absalom gain the heart of the people of Israel in the darkness
And it came to pass at the end of forty years , four years , that Absalom said unto the king , Grant me to go to Hebron , and give me the promise which I have made unto the LORD
&quot; Because he had made a vow for the servants who lived in the land of Gilead , saying , &apos; If the Lord sends me back to Jerusalem , I will serve Him
And the king said , Go in peace ; and Absalom arose , and went to Hebron .
And Absalom sent spies throughout all the tribes of Israel , saying , When you heard the sound of the trumpet , you said , Absalom is king in Hebron
And Absalom invited two hundred men to go with him to Jerusalem ; and they went with him in truth , and knew not the truth thereof
And it came to pass at the time of the offering of Absalom , that he sent messengers from his own city , to summon the counsellor of David , Ahithophel the Cyrene : and the rebellion was great , for the people that followed Absalom grew and grew
And it was told David , saying , &quot; The hearts of the children of Israel are returned to Absalom
Then David said to the servants of Jerusalem who were with him , &quot; We must rise up and flee , or we will not be able to escape Absalom ; and we must go quickly , lest he suddenly come and smite us and slay all the people of the city with the sword .
&quot; The king &apos;s servants said to the king , &quot; All my servants will do as my lord my king has commanded
So the king went out with all his household , and left ten concubines to guard the palace
And the king went out , and all the people followed him , and came to Beer-sheba , and abode there
And all the servants of the king passed by before him ; and the Philistines and the Philistines , six hundred men that followed the king from Gath , passed by before him
Then the king said to Edom the Gadites , &quot; Why are you fleeing from the land of the nations , and going with us ? Go back and live with the new king , or go back to your own land
&quot; How can I make you float with us today , when your days are few , and there is no place for you to dwell ? Take your brothers back , and the Lord will be with you in mercy and truth .
And he said unto the king , I swear by the Lord of everlasting life , and I swear before the king that wheresoever the king is , and wheresoever his servant is , he shall be there
And David said unto Edom , Go over the river before thee : and Edom the Gadite passed over , and all the women and children that were with him , and all the women and children that were with him
The people of the land cried with a loud voice , and the people passed away ; and the king passed through the rivers , and the people went into the wilderness .
And Zadok and the Levites who carried the ark of God came together , and laid down the ark of God ; and Abijah came up , and waited for the people to come forth out of the city .
&quot; The king said to the governor , &quot; You will bring the ark of God back to the city , and if I am blessed in the sight of the Lord , He will bring me back and see the ark and His house
&quot; If he says , &apos; I am not pleased with you ; &apos; behold , I am here ; let him serve me by his own will
Then the king said to the priest , &quot; Are you not the first , that you may return safely to the city , and that your son Ahimes and Abijah and Jonathan his son may go with you
I am at the gate of the wilderness waiting for your letter to be sent to me
So Zadok and Abijah brought the ark of God back to Jerusalem , and they lived there
And David went up to Mount Olives with his feet bare , and wept on one side and on the other ; and all those who were with him went up with their heads bare , and wept
And it was said to David , &quot; Ahithophel was also among the rebels , and he followed Absalom . &quot; And David prayed , &quot; Lord , make the scheme of Ahithophel foolish
And David came to the top of the mountain , to the place where he worshipped God , and saw the house of the Assyrians come to him with their clothes torn and their heads covered with dust
Then David said to him , &quot; If you go with me , you will be a burden to me
&quot; If you go back to the city , and say to Absalom , &apos; Lord , I want to be your servant ; I was your father &apos;s servant , and now I am your servant , so that you may destroy the scheme of Ahidor for me
&quot; Will not the priest Zadok and Abiathar be in it ? Whatever you hear in the king &apos;s house , report it to the priest Zadok and Abiathar .
&quot; Ahimas the son of Zadok , and Jonah the son of Abijah , were in it ; and whatever you have heard , let them report to me .
So the house of David &apos;s friends went into the city , and Absalom went into Jerusalem
And it came to pass as soon as David had passed over the top of the mountain , that the servants of Miphibosheth came to meet him , washing Barah with two well-prepared donkeys , bearing on them two hundred loaves , and a hundred cakes of grapes , and a hundred summer fruits , and a sack of wine
The king said to Sheba , &quot; What do you mean by this ? &quot; Sheba said , &quot; The donkey is for the king &apos;s household to ride , the bread , and the summer fruit for the young men , and the wine for the weary in the wilderness .
The king said , &quot; Is your master &apos;s son in it ? &quot; Sheba answered the king , &quot; He is still in Jerusalem , because he said , &apos; Today the children of Israel will return my father &apos;s land to me
And the king said unto Sheba , It belongeth unto thee all that are of Miphibosheth ; and Sheba said , I pray unto my lord my king , that I may be gracious before thee
And when king David came to Baruch , he saw a man come out , the son of Kiriah of the children of Saul , whose name was Shimei , walking and cursing
And he took stones and cut down the king of David and his servants ; and all the people and all the mighty men were on the king &apos;s side .
Every man cursed him , saying , &quot; Go away , you bloodthirsty evil man !
&quot; You have shed the blood of all the house of Saul , and you have succeeded him as king ; and the Lord has laid this sin upon you , and has given the land to your son Absalom ; and now you have taken your own iniquity , because you have shed the blood of men for yourselves
And Abishai the son of Zeruiah said unto the king , Shall this dead dog curse my lord my king ? Let me pass by , and cut off his head
Then the king said , &quot; What have I to do with you , the son of Zeruiah , that he curses you , because the Lord said to him , &apos; You shall curse David , &apos; and who can say why you do this ?
And David said unto Abishai and to all his servants , This is the son of my father , and he seeketh my life ; and this is the son of Benjamin : curse him , for this is what the Lord hath commanded him
&quot; Or if the Lord sees my affliction , and is cursed for me this day , then He will give mercy to me
Then David and those who were with him went forth , and Zechariah went forth against David on the hillside , and cursed him on one side , and struck him with stones , and exalted him in the ground
Then the king and all those who were with him came to a place where they were weary , and there they rested
And Absalom and all Israel came to Jerusalem , and Ahidor came with him
And the friend of David , Hushai of the children of Ahi , went to Absalom , and said unto him , Long live the king , long live the king
Then Absalom said to Hushai , &quot; Is this your kindness to your friends , and why do you not go with your friends ?
Then Hushai said to Absalom , &quot; No , I will be obedient to the Lord , and to this people , and to all the chosen ones of Israel , and I will dwell with him
&quot; And who am I to obey ? Am I not the son of the former king ? As I obey your father , so will I obey you
Then Absalom said to Ahithophel , &quot; You have a plan , how shall we do ?
And he said unto Absalom , Thou shalt be near to the wives that thy father left to guard the palace , and the children of Israel shall hear that thy father hated thee , and he that is in the hand of thy people shall be stronger
So they set up tents for Absalom on the top of the palace , and Absalom was near to his father &apos;s concubines before all Israel
Then the counsel of Ahidor was as a question of God , as the counsel of David , and as the counsel of Absalom , which he gave to David to this day .
Then he said to Absalom , &quot; Please let me choose twelve thousand men , and I will rise up to pursue David tonight
&quot; When his hands were weak and weak , suddenly I pursued him , and terrified him ; and all his people fled with him , and I killed only one king .
&quot; And let all the people be subject to You ; and as the people have been subject to You since the dead of the man whom You have sought , so shall all the people be in peace
Both Absalom and the elders of Israel were pleased with this saying
Then Absalom said , &quot; You shall call Hushai the Archite , and we shall listen to what he says .
And Hushai came to Absalom , and Absalom said unto him , Thus saith Ahithophel , We will do according to his word , whether it be not , or whether it be not , say thou :
And Hushai said unto Absalom , The scheme of Ahithophel this time is evil
Then Hushai said , &quot; You know that your father and those who are with him were warriors ; and now they are wroth in their hearts like a bear that loses its young in the field ; and your father is a warrior , and he will not dwell with the people
He is now either hidden in a pit , or somewhere else ; and if any man is killed first , he who hears will say , The people who followed Absalom were killed .
&quot; Whoever is as brave as a lion , his heart will digest him ; for all Israel know that your father is a hero , and all those who follow him are warriors .
&quot; It is better for me to gather all Israel together unto thee from Dan even unto Beer-sheba , as the sand of the sea ; and thou hast also led them to battle
&quot; So wherever we meet him , we will go down to him as under a dew on the ground , and not one of his companions will remain .
&quot; If he enters into that city , all Israel will take a rope and drag it into the river , and there will not be left a single stone
And Absalom and all the people of Israel said , The plot of Hushai the Achite is better than the plot of Ahithophel ; for the LORD hath purposed to destroy the good plot of Ahithophel , to bring evil upon Absalom
And Hushai said unto Zadok the priest , and unto Abijah , Thus is the plan of Ahidor for Absalom , and for the elders of Israel ; Thus is my plan
&quot; Now send quickly and tell David , &apos; You shall not live at the gate of the wilderness this night , except you pass over the river , lest the king and all those who are with him be destroyed
Then Jonah and Ahimes waited in Hebron , fearing not to enter into the city , lest they should be seen : and there came out a woman , and she told them this , and they sent a letter to king David
But when a boy saw them , he went to plead with Sharon , and they hurried to the house of one of Bahu &apos;lin , where there was a well , and they went down into it .
&quot; The woman covered the well with a covering , and laid wheat on her head , and there was no leakage
And the servants of Absalom came unto the house , and said unto the woman , Behold , Ahimes and Jonathan are there ; and the woman said , They have passed over the river ; and when they sought them , and found them not , they returned unto Jerusalem .
And when they were gone , the two men came up out of the well , and told the king of David , saying , Thus and thus hath Ahithophel plotted against thee : get up , and pass over the river quickly
So David and those who were with him came up over the Jordan ; and when it was morning , there was none that passed over the Jordan
And when Ahithophel saw that he did not obey his counsel , he put on his donkey , and returned to his own city , and came to his house , and left a testament , and hanged himself , and was buried in the tomb of his father
And David came to Mahan , and to Absalom , and to all Israel that were with him , and passed over the Jordan
And Absalom made Amaziah captain over Joab , the son of Ephraim the Ishmaelite , the son of Abijah the Nethinim , the son of Abijah the Nethinim , the daughter of Nathanael , the sister of Abijah and of Joab &apos;s mother , Reuiah the Baptizer ,
And Absalom and the children of Israel encamped in Gilead
And David came to Mahanneh , Shubi the son of Nasser the Rabathite of the children of Ammon , and Maghi the son of Ammiel of Rodeba , and Basil the Rokite of Gilead ,
carrying blankets , beds , pots , bowls , tiles , wheat , barley , flour , fried corn , beans , red beans , fried beans
And honey and butter and sheep and cakes were given to David and to those who were with him ; and they said , &quot; In the wilderness the people will be hungry and needy
And David numbered the men that followed him , and they were numbered by thousands and by hundreds .
And David divided the army into three armies , one under Joab , one under Abisiah the brother of Joab the son of Zeruiah , and one under Edom the Gadite , and David said unto the army , I will fight with you
But the soldiers said , &quot; You cannot fight ; if we flee , the enemy will not mind ; and half of us will die , and the enemy will not mind ; for you are as strong as all our people , and you are better prepared to help us in the city
And the king said unto them , How shall I do that which ye think good ? And the king stood by the gate of the city , and went forth with hundreds and thousands of men
And the king commanded Joab , and Abishai , and Edom , saying , For my sake you shall have mercy on the young man Absalom ; and all the soldiers heard the word which the king commanded the princes for Absalom .
And the soldiers went out into the field to meet the children of Israel , and fought in the forest of Ephraim
And the children of Israel were defeated before the servants of David ; and there were 20,000 men that fell that day .
For there is war on all sides ; and he that dies in the forest is more than he that dies in the sword .
And Absalom came by chance to meet David &apos;s servant ; and Absalom rode on a horse , and passed under the thick branches of a great oak , and his hair was wrapped around the branches of the oak , and he hung up , and the horse departed from him .
And when a man saw it , he pleaded with Absalom , saying , I see Absalom hanging upon an oak tree
And Joab said unto the messengers , Why shalt thou not kill him , when thou hast seen him , and lay him on the ground ? and if thou shalt kill him , I will give thee ten shekels of silver , and a cord
And he said unto Joab , I will give thee a thousand shekels of silver , and I will not stretch out my hand against the king &apos;s son : for we have heard the king say unto thee and to Abijah and to Edom , Be careful , lest thou shalt smite the young man Absalom
&quot; If I try to harm his life , you yourself will be an enemy to me ; for the king knows nothing of anything
And he said , I will not be with thee : and his hand took three trumpets , and it pierced his heart while Absalom was still alive in the oak tree .
&quot; The ten young men who had taken the weapons from Joab surrounded Absalom and killed him
And Joab blew his trumpet , and stopped all the people ; and they returned , and pursued not the children of Israel any more
And they cast Absalom into a great pit in the forest , and set up a great pile of stones upon his head ; and all Israel fled , and returned to their homes .
When Absalom was alive , he set up a pillar in the valley of the king ; for he said , &quot; I have no son to name me ; so he called that pillar in his own name , Absalom &apos;s pillar , even to this day
Then Ahimes the son of Zadok said , &quot; Let me go and tell the king the word of the Lord concerning the king &apos;s vengeance against his enemies
And Joab said unto him , Thou shalt not be able to report this day , but to report the day : for the king &apos;s son is dead this day , and thou shalt not report
And he said unto him , Go and tell the king what thou hast seen ; and he bowed down before him , and ran away .
Then Ahimes the son of Zadok said to Joab , &quot; In any case , let me go with you , and let the Philistines run away . &quot; He said , &quot; My son , if you have given this message , you will not be rewarded . Why would you run away ? &quot;
And he said , I will run anyhow . And Joab said , Run . And Ahimes ran from the plain , and passed over the Philistines .
And David was sitting in the barn ; and the watchman went up to the top of the gate , and looked , and behold a man running by himself .
Then the watchman cried out to the king , and the king said , &quot; If he comes alone , he will be a messenger , and he will come nearer and nearer .
And when the watchman saw a man running again , he said unto the watchman of the gate , There is another running by himself ; and the king said , This shall also be a letter
And the watchman said , I see the way of the former ruler as the way of Ahimes the son of Zadok ; and the king said , He is a good man , and he will give good news .
And he cried unto the king , saying , Peace ; and he bowed himself before the king , and worshipped , and said , Blessed be the LORD thy God , for he hath delivered unto the king the man that lifted up his hand against my lord my king
Then the king said , &quot; Peace be upon the young man Absalom , and peace be upon him ! &quot; And Ahimes answered , &quot; Joab sent his servant , and when he heard the noise of the people , he did not know what was going on
Then the king said , &quot; Go back and stand by ; &quot; and he went back and stood by
And the ancients came and said , &quot; Tell me , my lord , my king , that the Lord has avenged you today against all those who rise up against you .
And the king said unto him , Peace be unto Absalom the young man ; and he answered , Let the enemy of my lord , my king , and all that arise to slay thee be as the young man
Then the king went up to the gates of the city in mourning , and went out on one side , and said , &quot; My son , O Sharon , my son , my son , O Sharon , I hate not to die for you , O Sharon , my son , my son
And there was a man who complained to Joab , saying , The king wept and mourned for Absalom
And when the people heard that the king mourned for his son , the joy of their victory turned into mourning
On that day the people shall enter the city in darkness , as a people who are ashamed fleeing from the battle .
And the king lifted up his face , and cried with a loud voice , and said , My son Absalom , Absalom , my son , my son
And Joab went to the king , and said , &quot; You have made all your servants ashamed today , and they have saved your life today , and the life of your daughters and your wives and your concubines .
Thou lovest those who hate thee , and those who hate those who love thee ; and thou hast manifestly not remembered the handsome servant this day ; and I have seen this day that if Absalom were alive , and we were all dead , thou wouldest be glad
&quot; Now , when you go out , comfort the hearts of your servants ; for I swear by the Lord , if you do not go out , there will be no one with you tonight ; and the plague will be greater than that which you suffered from your youth to this day .
And the king arose , and sat at the gate : and when all the people heard that the king sat at the gate , they came to the king : and the children of Israel fled , and went every man to his house .
And all the tribes of Israel reasoned , saying , The king has delivered us from the hand of the enemy , and he has delivered us from the hand of the Philistines ; and now he is fled from Absalom .
And we anointed Absalom , and he ruled over us ; and he was gone out of battle ; and why did we not ask the king to come again ?
Then king David sent to the priests Zadok and Abijah , and said to them , &quot; Speak to the elders of Judah , saying , &apos; Why are you behind them , when all Israel have spoken to the king to return to the house ?
&quot; You are my brothers and my bones . Why do you ask the king to come back after men ?
And thou shalt say unto Amaziah , Art thou not my flesh ? if I have not made thee captain over Joab for ever , let God give me a mighty recompense
Then they restored the hearts of the people of Judah , as of a man : and they sent messengers to the king , saying , &quot; Please bring back the king and all his servants . &quot;
Then the king returned to the Jordan , and the Jews came to Gilead to meet the king , and asked him to pass over the Jordan
And Zedekiah the son of Gilead , the Benjamite of Bahuni , went down with the Jews , and greeted king David
And of Shechem were a thousand Benjaminites , and Sheba the servant of the house of Saul , and his fifteen sons and twenty servants ; and they passed over the river Jordan to meet the king
Then Shimei the son of Kira fell down before the king , when the king was about to pass over the Jordan ,
And he said unto the king , My lord , my king , when he came out of Jerusalem , let not my lord sin against the servants , nor remember them , nor put them in your hearts
&quot; The servant knew that he was guilty , and I came to meet my lord and my king this day first among all the house of Joseph
Then said Abijah the son of Zeruiah , Should not the anointed curse the Lord , and be put to death ?
And David said , Son of Zeruiah , what have I to do with you that you should be against me this day ? Shall the dead be judged in Israel this day ? Shall I not know that I am king in Israel this day ?
Then said the king unto Shechem , Thou shalt not die : and the king swore unto him
And Miphibosheth the son of Saul went down to meet the king ; and he came back to the king in peace from the days that he was gone , neither repaired his feet , nor shaved his beard , nor washed his clothes
And it came to pass , when he was come to Jerusalem to meet the king , that the king said unto him , Micah of Persia , why art thou not with me
Then he answered , &quot; My lord , my king , my servant is lame ; and on that day I wanted to ride a donkey and go with the king ; but my servants deceived me
and destroyed me before my Lord my King ; but my Lord my King is like the angel of God ; how well you see , how well do you !
&quot; For all my fathers and all my family are dead before my lord my king , and the king has made his servants eat with him in his seat .
And the king said unto him , Why willst thou call again thy cause ? And I said , Thou hast divided the land with Sheba .
Then Miphibosheth said to the king , &quot; My lord , my king , he has taken Baal for himself , even as he has returned to the house in peace
And Brazilel the Cyrene came down from Rogelin to send the king over the Jordan , and passed over the Jordan with the king
When he was eighty years old , he brought food for the king when he lived in Maha-min , and he was a very rich man
Then the king said to Balak , &quot; Go with me , and I will raise up your old man in Jerusalem
And he said unto the king , How many years shall I have in the world , that I may go up to Jerusalem with the king
The servant is now eighty years old ; can he taste the taste of his food , discern good and evil , and hear the voice of men and women singing ? Why should my lord and my king be burdened
&quot; If only the servants had sent the king over the Jordan , why would the king give me such a favor ?
&quot; Please allow me to return , and die in my own city , and be buried by the tomb of my parents . Here is King &apos;s servant Jinnah , and let him go with my lord , my king , and he may be with him at will .
&quot; The king said , &quot; Kingham can go with me ; I will serve him according to your will ; and whatever you ask of me , I will do for you
And the people passed over the Jordan , and the king passed over ; and the king bowed himself to Brezhnev , and blessed him ; and Brezhnev returned to his place
And the king went over to Gilead , and Kinham went over with him ; and all the people of Judah and half the people of Israel sent the king over
Then all Israel came to the king and said to him , &quot; Why do our brothers , Jews , secretly send the king and his family and his people over the Jordan
And all the children of Judah answered and said unto the children of Israel , Why are ye wroth with this thing , because the king is a kinsman with us ? what have we eaten of the king , and what hath the king rewarded us ?
And the children of Israel answered and said unto the Jews , We have much affection with the king according to the tribes , and we have more affection for David than for you : why do you despise us , and ask the king to come back before you negotiate with us ? But the words of the Jews were harder than the words of the children of Israel
And it came to pass in the midst thereof , that a bandit named Sheba , the son of Gilead , a Benjamite , blew a trumpet , saying , &quot; We have no part with David , nor with the son of Jesse . Go , O Israel , to your houses ,
So all Israel departed from David , and followed Sheba the son of Bichri ; and the men of Judah followed their king from the Jordan even unto Jerusalem
And when king David came to Jerusalem , and entered into the palace , he shut up the ten concubines that had been in the palace , and kept them in the cold house , feeding them , and not close to them ; and they were shut up as widows , to the day of death .
And the king said to Amaziah , &quot; In three days you shall gather the Jews together , and you shall come again to this place
Then Amaziah went to gather the Jews together , but he delayed the king &apos;s appointed time
And David said unto Abisheba , Behold , I am afraid that Sheba the son of Gilead will do more harm unto us than Absalom ; and thou shalt lead thy lord &apos;s servants to chase him , lest he gain a strong city , and escape from us
And the men of Joab , and the Philistines , and the Philistines , and all the mighty men of war , went out of Jerusalem after Abishai , and pursued Sheba the son of Bichri
And it came to pass , when they were come to the great rock of Gibeon , that Amaziah came to meet them , and Joab was clothed in war vestments , and girded with swords , and the sword was in the sheath , and the sword that went before Joab fell out of the sheath
And he took up the sword with his left hand , and said unto him , My brother , be good , and take hold of his beard with your right hand , and kiss him
And Amaziah had no defense against the sword that was in Joab &apos;s hand ; and Joab struck his belly with the sword , and his intestines were poured out on the earth ; and he died , and he struck him no more : and Joab and Abishai his brother pursued after Sheba the son of Bedekiah .
A young man of Joab stood by the body of Amaziah , and said to all the people , &quot; Whoever is pleased with Joab , and whoever is obedient to David , follow him .
And when he saw that all the people passed by stood still , he removed the body of Amaziah out of the way into the field , and covered it with cloth .
And it came to pass , when the body had departed from the way , that all the people followed Joab , and pursued after Sheba the son of Bedekiah .
And he went through all the tribes of Israel , even unto Abirah in Beth-maachah , and unto all the land of the Philistines ; and the men of the land gathered themselves together with him
And it came to pass , when Joab and those who were with him came to Abirah in Bermah , and besieged Sheba , that they built a fort against the city , and the people that were with Joab struck the city with hammers , that they might cause it to fall
A wise woman cried out from the city , saying , &quot; Listen , listen , please come to Joab , that I may speak to him
And Joseph came near , and the woman said unto him , Art thou Joseph ? And he said , I am . And the woman said , Hear thou the words of the maidservant . And he said , I hear
The woman said , &quot; It was said in ancient times , &apos; When you ask in Abirah , then things are settled .
&quot; The people of this city are peaceful and faithful among the children of Israel . Why do you destroy the great city of Israel and destroy the inheritance of the Lord ?
And Joab answered and said , I will not swallow up nor destroy
&quot; Because there was a man in the mountains of Ephraim , Shiba the son of Gilead , who raised his hand against king David ; and if you should deliver him out of the city , I would go away from the city . &quot; And the woman said to Joab , &quot; The prince of that man will be thrown out of the wall of the city to you
And the woman counseled the people in his wisdom , and they cast down the firstborn of Sheba the son of Gilead , and gave it to Joab ; and he blew a trumpet , and all the people departed from the city , and went every man to his own house : and he returned to Jerusalem to the king
And Joab was captain over all the host of Israel : and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the tribe of the Philistines and the Philistines .
And Adoram was in charge of the people who suffered ; and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahithophel was the scribe .
Zephaniah was the secretary , and Zadok and Abijah the priest .
Elah the Jairite , the governor of David
Then David asked the Lord , saying , &quot; This famine is because of Saul and his bloody house , and because of the killing of the Gibeonites
And the men of Gibeon were not of Israel , but of the remnant of the children of Ammon , whom the children of Israel had sworn not to slay ; but Saul was jealous of the children of Israel and of the Jews , and desired to slay them ; and king David called them
Then said he unto them , What shall I do for you , that I may redeem this sin , and bless you for the inheritance of the Lord ?
And the men of Gibeon answered and said unto David , Whatsoever ye say , whatsoever I shall do for you , it shall not be for us , neither shall it be for Saul nor for his house , neither shall ye slay an Israelite for our sakes .
And they said unto the king , He that hath murdered us , and hath destroyed us , that we may no more dwell in Israel
&quot; Now , if he will give us seven of his sons , let us stand before the Lord and hang them in Gibeah , which the Lord has chosen for Saul , &quot; said the king , &quot; I will give them to you
because he had made a covenant with Jonah the son of Saul by the word of the LORD , and he loved the son of Saul , Micah the son of Jonah , and gave him not out
And Elisha the daughter of Aijah gave to the sons of Saul two sons , Amnon , and Miphibosheth , and Micah the sister of Saul &apos;s daughter , five sons , the sons of Adeleh , the son of Brazil of Mihorah .
And it came to pass , when they were delivered into the hand of the Gibeonites , that the Gibeonites hanged them up in the mountain before the LORD , and they died together ; and it was the day of the harvest , and the day of the wheat harvest , that they were slain .
And Lisha the daughter of Aijah laid a tent on a rock with linen , from the time of the harvesting of hands , even unto the day when it rained on the body , that the birds of the air should not fall upon it in the daytime , and that the beasts of the field should not be trampled upon at night .
And it came to pass , that there was a man that brought this thing against David , concerning the work of Lyspah , the daughter of Aijah , Saul &apos;s concubine
And David went and carried away the bones of Saul and of Jonathan his son out of the tribe of the Gileadites : for the Philistines had slain Saul in Gilead before , and had hanged him in the city of Beer-sheba , and the tribe of the Gileadites had stolen him
And David removed the bones of Saul and Jonathan his son from there , and gathered together the bones of the seven hanged
And they buried the bones of Saul and Jonathan his son in the tomb of Kish Saul &apos;s father in Shelah Benjamin : and all the people did as the king commanded ; and God listened to the voice of the people .
The Philistines fought against the Israelites ; and David led his servants down , and fought against the Philistines ; and David was weary
One of the mighty men &apos;s sons , Ishmael , was about to kill David , and he had three hundred shekels of brass with his new sword .
Then Abijah the son of Zeruiah helped David , and fought against the Philistines , and slew him ; and the men who were with him swore to David that day , saying , &quot; You shall not fight with us any more , lest the lamps of Israel be put out
Then the children of Israel fought against the Philistines at Gibeah , and the Hussites killed the son of a mighty man , Saph
Again he fought against the Philistines at Gibeah ; and Eleazar the son of Jaroerkin the Bethlehemite slew Galilee the Hittite ; and his sword was as the axes of a weaving cloth .
And there was a man of great stature in Gath , whose feet were six fingers , and his head twenty-four ; and he was the son of a mighty man .
Then Jonathan the son of Shemiah , David &apos;s brother , slew him , and cursed the children of Israel .
And these four were the sons of Gad ; and they died under the hand of David and his servants
When the LORD delivered David from all his enemies and from the hand of Saul , he remembered this verse to the LORD
&quot; The Lord is my rock , my shelter , my salvation ,
&quot; My God , my rock , which I have leaned upon ; He is my shield ; He saves my corner ; He is my high place ; He is my refuge ; You , my Savior , have delivered me from the violence .
&quot; In this way I will be delivered from the hand of the enemy , and I will call on the Lord who is praised .
I was surrounded by the waves of death , and I was terrified by the rush of bandits .
The rope of the shadow encircles me , and the net of death approaches me .
I cried unto the LORD in affliction ; I cried unto my God ; and he heard my voice from the house , and my cry came into his ears .
Then the earth trembled because of his wrath , and the foundations of heaven trembled .
From his nostrils smoke was poured out , and fire burned from his mouth , and coal was burned .
And He brought down the heavens , and came down in person ; and under His feet were black clouds .
He sat on the wings of the wind , and appeared
He built the palace around Him in darkness , and in the waters that gathered together , and in the clouds of the sky .
For all the coals of light before him are shattered
The Lord sends thunder from heaven , and the Most High makes a voice .
He casts out his arrows , so that the enemies are scattered ; He sends out lightning , so that they are disturbed .
The Lord &apos;s rebuke shall come forth , and the breath of the nostrils shall come forth , and the bottom of the sea shall appear , and the roots of the earth shall be revealed
He stretched out his hand from heaven and seized me , and pulled me up from the great water .
He has delivered me from my enemies , and from those who hate me ; for they are stronger than I.
&quot; In the days of my calamity they will come against me ; but the Lord is my trust .
He has also brought me to a wide place ; He has lifted me up , because He is pleased with me .
&quot; The Lord answers me according to my righteousness ; He rewards me according to the cleanness of my hand
For I have obeyed the way of the Lord , and have not departed from my God with evil
All His statutes are before Me , and I have not forsaken His statutes .
I have been perfect before him , and I have kept myself from my iniquity
Therefore the Lord will reward me according to my righteousness , according to my cleanness before Him
Thou art the merciful , and Thou art the perfect , and Thou art the perfect
A clean man , Thou hast treated him with cleanness ; and a perverse man , Thou hast treated him with bend .
&quot; You will save the people who are in distress , but Your eyes will make the proud man humble .
O LORD , thou art my lamp ; and the LORD shall light my darkness .
I have jumped into the enemy with you , I have jumped through the walls with my God
As for God , His way is perfect , and the word of the Lord is pure ; and whoever leans on Him , He will be their shield .
&quot; Who is God except the Lord ? Who is the rock except our God ?
God is my firm shield ; He guides all men in His way
He has made my feet as the feet of a deer , and I am secure in high places .
He taught my hands to fight , and even my arms to open bronze bows .
You have given me your salvation as a shield . Your gentleness has made me great
Thou hast made the foot of my feet wide , and my feet have not slipped .
I have pursued My enemies , and have destroyed them ; I have no return before them .
And I have destroyed them , and I have wounded them , and they are not able to rise up ; and they are all fallen at my feet .
For thou hast bound my loins with strength , that I might fight ; and thou hast subjected under me those who have come to attack me .
Thou hast also made my enemies to flee before me , that I might cut off those who hate me .
They look up , and no one saves them ; they call upon the Lord , and He does not answer them .
I will crush them like dust on the earth , and I will trample them on the earth like the mud of the streets .
Thou hast delivered me from the strife of my people ; Thou hast protected me as the head of the nations ; and the people whom I know not shall serve me .
&quot; The foreigners will surrender to Me , and they will obey Me when they hear My name .
The foreigners shall be weakened , and shall go out of their camps in fear of war .
Blessed be my rock , O LORD , the living God ; and honoured be the rock of my salvation ,
&quot; This is the God who justified me , and made all the people to serve under me .
Thou hast delivered me from the enemy , and lifted me up above them that arose against me ; Thou hast delivered me from the wicked .
Therefore , O LORD , I will give thanks unto thee in the land of the nations , and I will sing praises unto thy name
&quot; The Lord has given great salvation to the king whom He has appointed , and to the anointed whom He has given mercy , to David and to his seed forever and ever
And David the son of Jesse , which was anointed by the God of Jacob , was made high , and he was the singer of Israel , saying ,
&quot; The Spirit of the Lord has borrowed me to speak His words in my mouth
&quot; The God of Israel , the rock of Israel , has spoken to me , saying , &apos; He who governs the people in righteousness fears God and is in power
He will be like the dawn of the sun , like the morning without clouds , like the sunshine after the rain , so that the earth grows green .
My house is not like that in the sight of God ; but God has made an everlasting covenant with me . Is not this covenant firm in all my salvation , and in all my desires , that He will accomplish for me ?
But the bandits will be thrown away like thorns , and no man will dare to take him by the hand
&quot; He who takes him will carry iron rods and spears , and he will be burned in the fire for ever .
Behold , the name of the mighty man David , Joseph of the sons of the Ammonites , and Adonijah of the Isnites , commander of the captains of the hosts , slew at one time eight hundred men .
Then came Eleazar the son of Dodo of the Assyrians ; and the Philistines were gathered together to fight ; and the children of Israel rose up , and three mighty men with David scolded the Philistines , and Eleazar was one of them
And he arose , and struck the Philistines , and bowed down to his arms , and pressed his hand against the sword ; and the LORD overcame the people of Israel that day , and the people took possession of their possessions after Eleazar
Then came Shama the son of Ahi the Haranite ; and the Philistines gathered themselves together one day in a field full of red beans , and the people fled before the Philistines .
And Samaria stood in the field , and slew the Philistines , and saved the field ; and the LORD made the people of Israel to prevail
And it came to pass at the time of the harvest , that three of the thirty mighty men went down to David to the cave of Adullam ; and the Philistines encamped in the valley of Lyman .
At that time David was in the camp , and the camp of the Philistines was in Bethlehem .
And David was thirsty , and said , Would that a man had poured water into the well by the gate of Bethlehem for me to drink
And the three mighty men went through the camp of the Philistines , and poured water out of the well by the gate of Bethlehem , and brought it for David , but he refused to drink , and laid it before the Lord
They said , &quot; Lord , these three men have taken their lives to drink water , like their blood , and I refuse to drink it ; so David refused to drink it ; and this is what the three mighty men did
And Abijah the brother of Joab , the son of Zeruiah , was the captain of the three mighty men ; and he slew three hundred men with the firing of his hand ; and he was called in the name of the three mighty men
He is the most noble of the three warriors ; therefore he shall be their leader ; but he shall be short of the first three warriors .
And there was a mighty thing done by Benaiah , the son of Jehiedai , the mighty man of Shechem , who slew the two sons of Eliel the Moabites , and went down into the pit in the snow , and slew a lion
And he slew a mighty Egyptian with a sword in his hand ; and Benaiah went down with only a stick , and took the sword out of his hand , and slew him with it .
&quot; This is what Jehoiada the son of Neriah did ; and he received a name among the three mighty men .
He was no more precious than the thirty warriors , but less than the first three ; and David made him captain of the guard
Of the thirty mighty men , Asahel the brother of Joab , and Elhanan the son of Dodo the Bethlehemite ,
Shama the Harite , Elijah the Harite
Elah the son of Giles the Palthite , and of the Mighty of Tikoa ,
Abiezer the Anathonite , and Miboniah the Hushaite ,
The Assyrians , Samaritans , and the Nethites ,
and Hiliel the son of Barnabas , and Ethai the son of Libai the Gibeonite of Benjamin ,
And of the children of Ladon , and of the children of Naiah , and of the children of Sheth ,
Abiaben the Beer-Labanite , Absmaph the Baruchite
Eliahab , Jonathan the son of Jasen ,
Shamah the Harathite , Ahikam the son of Sharah the Harathite
Eliphael the son of Ahab the Magahite , Irena the son of Ahidor the Cyrene ,
Shisle of Cameroon , Pale of Aban
And the sons of Natan the Zobahite , Bani the Gadite ,
Now the sons of Ammon , Zeruiah the son of Zeruiah , and Nahaliah the Beershebaite , were of the armor of Joab the son of Zeruiah .
the Edomites of Ella , the Edomites of Galilee
There were thirty-seven people in the city of Uriah , a Hebrew .
Then the LORD was angry with the children of Israel , and stirred up David , and commanded them to number the children of Israel and the children of Judah
And David commanded Joab the captain of the host , who was with him , saying , &quot; Go and go through the tribes of Israel from Dan even unto Beer-sheba , and number the people , that I may know the number of them
And Joab said unto the king , Let the LORD thy God multiply the number of the people a hundredfold , that my lord my king may see it with his own eyes ; and how shall my lord my king be glad to do it
But the commandment of the king was greater than that of Joab and all the captains of the army ; and they went out before the king , and numbered the people of Israel
And they passed over the Jordan , and encamped at Aaron &apos;s camp on the right side of the city in the midst of the valley of Gad , against Jasheh .
Then it came to pass that Gilead and he stopped at Sheth ; and it came to pass that Dan was round about Sidon
And they came to the cities of Tyre , and to the cities of the Hebrews and the Canaanites , and to Beer-sheba in the south of Judah .
They traveled all over the land , and returned to Jerusalem nine months and twenty days
And Joab recounted unto the king the number of the people : and of the men of Israel that drew swords were eighty thousand , and of Judah fifty thousand .
Then David counted the number of the people , and in his heart he prayed to the Lord , saying , &quot; I have sinned greatly in doing this ; O Lord , remove from me the iniquity of my servant , for what I have done is foolishness .
And David arose in the morning , and the word of the LORD came unto Gad the prophet , which was David &apos;s forefather , saying ,
&quot; Go and testify against David , saying , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I have three plagues , and I have chosen one with you , and I am well with you
And Gad came to David , and said unto him , Wouldst thou have seven years of famine in thy land , and three months of persecution before thine enemies , and three days of plague in thy land ? now therefore think thou , and I will answer the one that sent me
David said to Gad , &quot; I am in great distress . I want to fall into the hand of the Lord , for he has abundant mercy , and I do not want to fall into the hand of men
And the LORD struck the plague with the children of Israel from the morning until the appointed time ; and from Dan even unto Beer-sheba 70,000 men died .
And it came to pass , when the Lord repented , and stretched out his hand against Jerusalem to destroy it , that the angel of the destroyers said to it , Hold your hand , and let it fall ; and the angels of the Lord were at the field of wheat of Aaron the Jebusite
And when David saw the angel that destroyed the people , he prayed unto the LORD , saying , I have sinned and done evil ; but what have these sheep done ? May thy hand be upon me and upon my father &apos;s house
Then Gad came to David that day and said to him , &quot; Go up and build an altar for the Lord on the field of wheat of Aaron the Jebusite
And David went up , as Gad had said in the name of the Lord ,
And when Aaron looked , and saw the king and his servants coming , he received them , and went out , and bowed himself to the ground , and worshipped the king
And David said , I will buy thee this field , and I will build an altar unto the LORD , that the plague of the people may cease
Then Aaron said to David , &quot; My lord , my king , whatever you like to use , take it and offer it ; behold , there is a cow for a burnt offering , a feeding vessel , and a yoke for a ram &apos;s sleeve , which you can burn with fire
&quot; All this I , Aaron , have dedicated to you , O king ; and I said to the king , &apos; May the Lord your God please you
And the king said unto Aaron , Nay ; but I must buy it unto thee at a price , and I will not burn it for a burnt offering with that which is of white unto the LORD my God . And David bought the field and the oxen with fifty shekels of silver
And David built therein an altar unto the LORD for a burnt offering and a sacrifice of peace : and the plague ceased in the midst of Israel , because the LORD had heard the voice of the people
King David is old , and he is not warm , though he is covered
Then his servant said to him , &quot; Wouldn &apos;t it be better for my lord my king to seek a maidservant , to serve the king , to be his caregiver , and to sleep in the king &apos;s arms , so that my lord my king may be warm
And he brought unto the king Abigail , a daughter of the book , whom he sought in all the land of Israel for a beautiful daughter
The little girl was very beautiful , and she served the king and served the king , but the king was not close to her
At that time Adonijah the son of Hachijah said to himself , &quot; I will be king , and I will prepare for myself chariots and horsemen , and I will send fifty men running before him
And his father had nothing to make him sorrowful , but said , &quot; What are you doing ? He is very handsome , born after Absalom
And Adonijah consulted with Joab the son of Zeruiah , and with Abijah the priest ; and they obeyed him , and helped him
But Zechariah the priest , Benaiah the son of Jehoiada the prophet , and Nathan the prophet , and Shechem , and Elijah , and the mighty men of David , did not obey Adonijah
And it came to pass on that day , when Adonijah had slain cattle , and lambs , and calves , at the rock of Zohiel by Hebron , he asked his brethren , the children of the king , and all the Jews that were servants to the king
Only the prophet Nathanael , and Benaiah , and the mighty men , and Solomon his brother , did not ask
Then Nathan said to Bathsheba , Solomon &apos;s mother , &quot; Have you not heard that Adonijah the son of Hachim is king ? David our lord does not know
&quot; Now I am able to give you an idea to save your life and that of Solomon your son
&quot; You entered into the presence of King David , and said to him , &apos; My Lord , my king , have you not sworn to the maidservant , saying , &apos; Will Solomon your son succeed me as king , and sit in my throne ? &apos;
&quot; When you spoke to the king , I went in and confirmed your words .
And Bathsheba entered into the king &apos;s house , and behold , the king was very old , and Abijah , the daughter of the scribes , was waiting for the king .
Then Bath-sheba bowed down to the king , and the king said , &quot; What do you want
He said , &quot; Lord , you swore to the maidservant , by the Lord your God , &apos; Your son Solomon will succeed me as king and sit in my throne
&quot; Now he is king in Adonijah ; but my lord and my king do not know
He slaughtered many bulls and lambs , and invited the king &apos;s sons , and Abiathar the priest , and the captain of the guard , Joab , and Solomon the king &apos;s servant , whom he did not invite
&quot; My lord my king , the eyes of all Israel are on you , until you tell them who will sit in your throne after my lord my king
&quot; If not , I and Solomon my son will be counted sinners after my Lord my king and my fathers have slept with Edom .
And it came to pass , while he was yet speaking to the king , that Nathan the prophet came in
Then a certain man told the king , saying , &quot; The prophet has brought the scroll , and he has entered into the king &apos;s presence , and is lying on the ground
Then Nathan said , &quot; My lord , my king , has indeed spoken to Adonijah , saying , &apos; Will you sit in my throne to succeed me as king
&quot; Today he went down , and slaughtered many bulls and lambs , and called the king &apos;s sons and his captains , and Abijah the priest , who were eating and drinking in the presence of Adonijah , saying , &apos; May the king of Adonijah live for ever .
&quot; Only I am your servant , and the priest Zadok , Benaiah the son of Jehoiada , and Solomon the king &apos;s servant , who did not ask
&quot; But the king did not tell his servants who would sit in your place after my lord my king
And the king commanded , saying , &quot; Bring him in , and he shall come in and stand before the king
&quot; I swear by the Lord , the Everlasting Lord , that he will deliver my life from all hardship
&quot; Now that I have sworn to you by the Lord God of Israel , saying , &apos; Your son Solomon will succeed me as king , and he will sit on my throne , and I will do so today
Then Bath-sheba bowed down to the ground , and worshipped the king , and said , &quot; May my lord , King David , live forever
And the king commanded , saying , &quot; Bring the priests , and the governors , and Nathan the prophet , and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada , and they shall come before the king
&quot; The king said to them , &quot; Take your lord &apos;s servant , and send Solomon my son down to Guidance , riding on my donkey
&quot; The priests , the governors and the prophet Nathanael , will anoint him there , and make him king over Israel ; and you will blow a trumpet , saying , &apos; May King Solomon live forever
Then I will come with him , and he will sit in my throne , and he will succeed me as king ; and I have made him king over Israel and over Judah .
And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada said unto the king , Thus saith the LORD God of my lord my king
&quot; How is it that the Lord is with my lord my king , and that He is with Solomon , and that His kingdom is greater than that of David my lord
Then went down Zechariah the priest , and Nathan the prophet , and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada , and the Philistines , the Philistines , and brought Solomon on horseback the son of David king of Israel , and brought him to Gibeah
Then Zechariah the priest took a horn of oil from the Tent of Meeting , and anointed Solomon with it ; and they blew the horn , and all the people said , &quot; May the king of Solomon live forever
And the people came up with him , and whistled , and shouted with a loud voice ,
And it came to pass at the end of the feast , when Adonijah heard the voice , and all the guests whom he had invited , that when Joab heard the sound of the horn , he said , Why is there a voice in the city ?
While he was speaking , the priest came to Abijah , Jonah his son ; and Adonijah said to him , &quot; Come in , for you are a faithful man , and you will give good news .
Then Jonathan said to Adonijah , &quot; Truly Solomon is king , our Lord , King David
And the king sent Zadok the priest , and Nathan the prophet , and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada , and the Philistines , the Philistines , to make Solomon ride upon the bow of the king
&quot; The priest Zechariah and the prophet Nathanael anointed him king in the book of Revelation , and from it all the people came out with joy , and a voice shook the city , and this is the voice that you heard .
And Solomon ascended to the throne
The servants of the king came and blessed David our Lord , saying , &quot; May the God of the king magnify the name of Solomon more than the name of the king , and make his kingdom greater than the king &apos;s kingdom ; and the king fell down on his bed and worshipped
And the king said , Blessed is the LORD God of Israel , for he hath given me a man to sit upon my throne this day , whom I have seen with my own eyes
And when all the people of Adonijah heard this , they were astonished , and went about .
And Adonijah feared Solomon , and arose , and seized the horn of the altar
And it was told Solomon , saying , Behold , Adonijah was afraid of the king of Solomon , and he seized the horn of the altar , and said , If the king of Solomon had sworn to me this day , that he would not kill his servants with the sword
Solomon said , &quot; If he is a righteous man , not a hair will fall on the earth ; but if he does evil , he must die . &quot;
Then king Solomon sent messengers , and Adonijah came down from the altar to worship king Solomon , and Solomon said to him , &quot; Go home
And it came to pass , when the days of David &apos;s death were near , that he charged Solomon his son , saying ,
&quot; Behold , I am about to go in the way that the world will go ; therefore be thou a mighty husband
&quot; Be obedient to the commandment of the Lord your God , and to the way of the Lord , which is written in the law of Moses , and to his statutes , and to his commandments , and to his statutes , and to his ordinances ; and whatever you do , wherever you go , do it with all diligence .
&quot; The word which the Lord has spoken to me will be fulfilled , saying , &apos; If your sons will be prudent in their deeds , and will do their utmost in truth before me , they will not forsake the throne of Israel
Knowest thou what Joab the son of Reuiah did unto me , when he slew the two captains of Israel , Abner the son of Ner , and Amaziah the son of Mesheth , when he poured out their blood in the days of Tyre , as he did in the days of the battle , and dyed the bands of the waist and the shoes of the feet
Therefore do according to your wisdom , and let him not rest in the darkness with his white head .
&quot; You have been kind to the children of Brazil , the children of Gilead , and have made them sit with you at mealtimes ; for they brought me food when I fled from your brother Absalom .
&quot; Behold , here is Shechem the son of Kira , Benjamin of Bahu &apos;lin ; and on the day that I went to Mahan , he cursed me with an evil word , and came down to meet me in the Jordan , and I swore to him by the Lord , saying , &apos; I will not kill you with a sword
&quot; Now you will not accuse him of sin , for you are a wise man , and you will know how to deal with him , so that he will be slain with his head white , and blood will flow down to the womb
And David slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David
David reigned forty years in Israel , seven years in Hebron , and thirty and three years in Jerusalem
Solomon sat in the throne of David his father ; and his kingdom was strong
Then Adonijah the son of Hachijah came to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon , and said to him , &quot; Are you coming for peace ? &quot; And he answered , &quot; For peace
And he said , &quot; I have a word to say to you , &quot; and said to Bath-sheba , &quot; Tell me
Then said Adonijah , &quot; You know that the kingdom belonged to me , and that all Israel looked to me as king ; but the kingdom returned to my brothers , because it was from the Lord that he received the kingdom
&quot; Now I have a request to you , that you do not deny it . Then said Bath-sheba , &quot; Tell me
He said , &quot; Please ask the king of Solomon to give me Abijah , the woman who reads the book , as a wife , for he will not deny you
Then said Bath-sheba , &quot; Well , I will speak to the king for you
Then Bath-sheba went to the king of Solomon , and said to Adonijah , &quot; Arise , welcome the king , and worship him ; and sit on the throne , and make a seat for your mother , &quot; and he sat on the right hand of the king
Then said Bath-sheba , &quot; I have a small request for you , that you do not deny it ; &quot; and the king said , &quot; Please tell your mother , I will not deny it
Then said Bath-sheba , &quot; Please give your brother Adonijah the wife of Abijah , the woman who reads the book .
Then king Solomon said to his mother , &quot; Why do you seek Abishai , the daughter of the scribes , for him , and also for his kingdom ? He is my brother , and he has Abiathar the priest , and Joab the son of Zeruiah , as his assistant
Then the king of Solomon swore by the Lord , saying , &quot; This is the word of Adonijah , that he has delivered himself to life ; or else God will bring upon me a great penalty
&quot; The Lord has strengthened me , and has made me sit in the throne of David my father , and has set up the house for me according to the word which he has promised me ; and he has sworn in me by the Lord who lives forever , &apos; Today Adonijah will be put to death
So king Solomon sent Benaiah the son of Jehoiada to kill Adonijah
Then the king said to Abijah the priest , &quot; Go back to your own land in Anathoth ; you should have died ; but I will not kill you today because you lifted up the ark of the Lord Yahweh before my father David , and suffered all the torment with my father .
Then Solomon removed Abijah , and he was not permitted to be a priest to the Lord ; so that he might testify to the words of the Lord concerning the house of Eli in Shiloh
And when Joab had not returned to Absalom , he returned to Adonijah ; and when he heard the sound of the wind , he fled to the tabernacle of the LORD , and seized the horns of the altar
And it was told the king of Solomon , saying , Joab fled unto the tabernacle of the Lord , and is now by the altar ; and Solomon sent to Benaiah the son of Jehoiada , saying , Go and kill him
Then Benaiah came to the ark of the Lord , and said to Joab , &quot; The king said , &apos; Go out . &apos; He said , &apos; I will not go out ; I will die here . &apos; Then Benaiah returned to the king , and said , &apos; This is how Joab answered me
&quot; The king said , &quot; You can do according to his word , kill him , and bury him , so that Joseph will not return to me and to my father &apos;s house for the blood of innocent people .
&quot; The Lord will put the sin of Joab on his head , because he struck with the sword two men more righteous and good than he , Abner the son of Ner , the commander of Israel , and Amaziah the son of Mesheth , the commander of Judah ; but my father David did not know
Therefore the sins of the blood of the two men will be upon the heads of Joab and his seed for ever ; but David and his seed , and his house and his country , will be in peace with the Lord for ever .
Then Benaiah the son of Jehoiada went up , and slew Joab , and buried him in his own grave in the wilderness .
And the king appointed Benaiah the son of Jehoiada captain over Joab , and Zadok the priest over Abiathar
Then the king &apos;s messenger called to him , and said to him , &quot; You shall build houses in Jerusalem , and you shall not go out to any other place
&quot; When you know what day you have come and gone through the flood , you will die , and your sins will be on your heads .
Then Zebedee said to the king , &quot; This is a good saying , and as my lord , my king , has said , and as my servants shall do , so Zebedee lived in Jerusalem many days
Then after three years two of Shemei &apos;s servants fled to Aginar the son of Magah king of Gath ; and it was reported to Shemei , saying , &quot; Your servants are in Gath
Then Zechariah arose , and set up his donkeys , and went to Gath to Agin , to seek his servants , and brought them back from Gath
And it was told Solomon , saying , Zebedee went out of Jerusalem to Gath , and came back
Then the king sent messengers , and every one of them who was called to him said to him , &quot; Did I not make you swear by the Lord , and warn you , saying , &apos; When you know that you will come out to another place on that day , you will die ? &apos; And you said to me , &apos; This is good ; I will obey
&quot; Now why do you not keep the oath which you swore by the Lord , and the commandment which I commanded you
Then the king said to Shechem , &quot; You know in your heart all the evil things that you have done to my father David ; therefore the Lord will put your sins on your head
Blessed is the king of Solomon , and the throne of David shall stand firm before the Lord for ever
Then the king commanded Benaiah the son of Jehoiada to go and kill Shechem ; and he established the kingdom of Solomon
And Solomon married Pharaoh king of Egypt , and took Pharaoh &apos;s daughter as wife , and brought him into the city of David , until he had finished the building of his house , and the house of the Lord , and the walls around Jerusalem
In those days the people sacrificed in the altar , because there was not a house built for the name of the Lord
Solomon loved the Lord , and did according to the law of David his father , but he offered sacrifices and burnt incense in the high places
And king Solomon went up and offered , because there was a great altar , and he offered a thousand burnt offerings on that altar
And the Lord appeared to Solomon in the night dream of Keilah , and said unto him , What wilt thou that I give thee , thou shalt ask
And Solomon said , &quot; Your servant David my father , when he walks before you in truth , and in righteousness , and in an upright heart , you will give him great grace , and you will keep great grace for him , and give him a son to sit on his throne , as it is today
&quot; Now , O Lord , my God , you have made my servant king over David my father ; but I was a child , and I did not know how to go in and out
&quot; The servant dwells among the people whom you have chosen , and they are countless .
Therefore give me wisdom , that I may judge your people , and discern right and wrong ; or who will judge the multitude of them ?
Solomon rejoiced in the Lord for his request
God said to him , &quot; Because you ask for this , you do not ask for yourselves to live , nor for riches , nor for the destruction of your enemy &apos;s life , but for wisdom to hear judgment
&quot; I will give you wisdom according to what you have asked , and I will give you wisdom , which has not been like you before you , nor after you
&quot; And I have given you what you did not ask , riches and honour , that in the days of your life there may be no king like you among the kings .
&quot; If you obey your father David , and follow My ways , and keep My statutes , and My commandments , I will make you live long
And Solomon awoke , and behold , it was a dream ; and he returned to Jerusalem , and stood before the ark of the Lord , and offered burnt offerings and sacrifices of peace offerings , and prepared a feast for all his servants
On one day two prostitutes came and stood before the king
One said , &quot; Lord , I lived in the same house with this woman , and when she was in the house , I gave birth to a boy
On the third day after my birth , this woman also gave birth to a child , and we lived together , and there was no one else in the house except two of us
When the woman slept in the night , she put her child to death
He arose in the middle of the night , while I slept , and took my child by my side , and laid him in his arms , and laid his dead child in my arms
&quot; In the day when the sun will rise , I will rise and give my child milk , and it will not come to pass that the child will die ; and when the sun will rise , my eyes will be dim , and they will not be the children I was born with .
And the woman said , No , the living child is mine , and the dead child is thy ; and the woman said , No , the dead child is thine , and the living child is mine ; and so they argued before the king
The king said , &quot; The woman said , &apos; The living child is mine , and the dead child is yours . &apos; &quot; The woman said , &quot; No , the dead child is yours , and the living child is mine
Then he said , &quot; Take the sword , and the people will take the sword
&quot; The king said , &quot; Separate the living child into two halves , one for the woman , and one for this woman
Then the mother of the living child , grieving for her own child , said , &quot; My Lord , give the living child to the woman , lest she kill him . &quot; The woman said , &quot; This child is not mine , neither is it yours ; cut him down
&quot; The king said , &quot; You shall give this woman a living child , and you shall not kill her ; she is indeed his mother
When all Israel heard the judgment of the king , they feared him , because they saw that God &apos;s wisdom was in his heart , and that he was able to judge
Solomon king over all Israel
Below are his servants : And Azariah the son of Zadok was a priest .
And the two sons of Shesha , Elihor , and Ahijah , were scribes ; and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahirim was scribe .
And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was captain over them ; and Zadok and Abijah were priests .
And Azariah the son of Nebuchadnezzar was over all the people ; and Zab the son of Nebuchadnezzar , the friend of the king , was over all the people .
Adonilan , the son of Abigail , the writer of Ahishah , ruled over the people who suffered .
And Solomon set up twelve officers throughout all Israel , and they fed the king and the king &apos;s household , each man for a month each year
Behold , their names are written : In the mountains of Ephraim was Penhuir .
And at Magaz , and at Shabbin , and at Beth-shemesh , and at Eneb-hanan , and at Ben-dehmah ,
And in Arupha he had Ben-chizillai , and he administered all the land of Sogo and Hephr .
And in the hills of Tyre was Benaib Nadab , and he took the daughter of Solomon his wife .
And in Hebron , and in Migdo , and near Sarathnah , in the whole land of Beersheba , which is under Jezreel , from Beersheba even unto Abimelech even unto Jotham , was Barnabas the son of Ahithophel .
And in Latham in Gilead was Ben-Kibe , who oversaw the cities of Jair the son of Manasseh in Gilead , and sixty great cities in the land of Aor in Bashan , with walls and bars of brass ;
And in the land of Mahanneh was Ahaziah the son of Iddo .
And Ahimes was in Naphtali ; and he took Bath-sheba , Solomon &apos;s daughter , to wife
And in Asheah and in Aaron was Barnabas the son of Hushai .
And in Issachar was Jehoshaphat the son of Pariah
And in Benjamin was Shimei the son of Elah .
And the land of Gilead was from Sihon king of Amorah , and from Bashan king of Bashan : and Kib the son of Uri was over it .
And the children of Judah and the children of Israel rejoiced as in the sand of the sea , eating and drinking
Solomon ruled over all the kingdoms , from the great river to the land of Assyria , even to the border of Egypt ; and in the days of Solomon &apos;s life all the kingdoms were subject to him
The food which Solomon used daily was thirty shekels of fine flour , and sixty shekels of fine flour .
Ten fattened cattle , twenty fattened cattle in the field , and a hundred sheep , and deer , antelopes , oxen , and fattened poultry
Solomon ruled over the kings on the west side of the river , and over all the land from Tiphras even unto Gaza ; and there was peace in all the land
In the days of Solomon , from Dan even to Beersheba , the Jews and the children of Israel dwelt safely under their vineyards and under the trees without fruit
Solomon had forty thousand horses with chariots , and twelve thousand horsemen
The twelve officers provided the king of Solomon , and all the food of those who were with him , according to the months .
And all the people shall be divided according to their divisions , and the wheat and the herbs of the horses and of the horses , and they shall be brought to the officers
God gave Solomon great wisdom and wisdom , and a great heart , as the sand of the sea cannot be measured
Solomon &apos;s wisdom exceeded all the wisdom of the Orientals and of the Egyptians
His wisdom is greater than all the people , and greater than the wisdom of Edom the Ephrathite , and of Heman the son of Manasseh , and of Korah , and of Dadab ; and his fame is spread in all the nations round about .
He made three thousand proverbs , and fifteen thousand poems .
He spoke of the grasses , of the acacia trees of Lebanon , of the oxen &apos;s knees , which grow up straight to the wall , and of the birds , of the beasts , and of the insects , and of the water creatures
When all the kings of the earth heard the wisdom of Solomon , they sent men to hear his words
Herod the king of Tyre loved David ; and when he heard that the children of Israel had anointed Solomon and succeeded him as king , he sent his servants to meet him
And Solomon sent men to Shelan , saying ,
&quot; You know that my father David was unable to build a house for the name of the Lord , his God , because of the battle that was raging around him , until the Lord made all his enemies submit to His feet
&quot; Behold , in the Lord , my God , He has given me peace all around , and no enemy , and no evil
&quot; I will build a house for the name of the Lord my God , as the Lord promised David my father , saying , &apos; I will make your son succeed you in your stead , and he will build a house for my name
&quot; So command your servants to cut down cedar trees for me in Lebanon , and my servants will help them ; and I will give your servants their wages according to what you have ordained ; for you know that there is no one among us who is good at cutting trees like the Sidonians .
Then when Herod heard the words of Solomon , he rejoiced , and said , &quot; Today let us praise the Lord , for he has given David a wise son to rule over many people
He sent messengers to Solomon , saying , &quot; I have heard all that you have spoken to me concerning the palm trees and pine trees , and I will do according to your will .
&quot; My servant will bring the timber out of Lebanon into the sea , and bound it in rafts , and bring it to the sea , to the place which You have appointed for me , and you will take it ; and you will give me food in my house , according to all my will .
And Hilan gave him cedars and pine trees , according to the desire of Solomon ;
And Solomon gave unto the sons of Hilan twenty thousand shekels , and twenty shekels of oil for food for his house : and so Solomon gave to Hilan every year
&quot; The Lord has given Solomon wisdom according to his promise . He and Solomon have made good covenants
Of the children of Israel , thirty thousand were chosen by the king of Solomon for service
And he sent them round about , ten thousand men a month to Lebanon , a month in Lebanon , and two months at home ; and Adonijah was over them .
Solomon carried 70,000 , and stoned 80,000 in the mountains .
Moreover , Solomon employs thirty-three hundred supervisory and supervisory workers
&quot; Then the king commanded , and they dug out a great and precious stone for the foundation of the house
And the craftsmen of Solomon , and the craftsmen of Hilan , and the craftsmen of the Canaanites , cut stone well , and prepared wood and stones for the house
In the fourth year of Solomon king of Israel , in the four hundred and eighty years after the children of Israel came out of the land of Egypt , in the moon Shiv , which is February , he began to build the house of the Lord
The house which the king of Solomon built for the Lord was sixty cubits long , twenty cubits wide , and thirty cubits high
And the porch in front of the house was twenty cubits , as the breadth of the house , ten cubits wide .
And made for the palace a curtain firm ,
And by the walls of the temple , and by the inner temple of the outer temple , and by the side chambers of three floors ,
the lower level shall be five cubits , the middle six cubits , and the upper seven cubits ; and the beams of the courtyard of the house shall be laid upon the tent of the walls , lest they enter the walls .
The building of the temple was made of stones cut in the mountains , and the sound of the hammer , the axe , and all the iron instruments was not heard at the time of the construction
On the right side of the palace there are doors to the side chambers in the middle , and stairs with spirals in the doors , from the second to the third floor .
And Solomon built the house , and set up the beams of acacia wood , and covered it with acacia boards .
And they laid on the side chambers of the house , which were made of cedar , five cubits high on each floor , on the camp of the walls of the house .
The word of the Lord came to Solomon , saying ,
&quot; For this house which you have built , if you will keep my statutes and my ordinances and all my commandments , I will prove to you what I promised your father David
&quot; I will dwell among the children of Israel , and I will not forsake my people Israel
The Temple of Solomon
And the walls of the house were covered with boards of cedar , and the roofs of the house were covered with boards of wood , and the floors of the house were covered with boards of pine
The inner house , which is to the sanctuary , is twenty cubits long , and covers the roof of the tent from the ground with cedar boards .
the outer court of the inner court , forty cubits long ,
No stone was revealed in the temple , but it was covered with acacia trees , and on it were engraved cucumbers and early flowers .
&quot; In the house there is prepared the inner house , to set up the ark of the Lord
And the length of the house was twenty cubits , and the breadth twenty cubits , and the height twenty cubits , and the walls were covered with gold , and the altar was made of acacia wood , and it was wrapped with gold
And Solomon put gold on the walls of the house , and hanged a chain of gold upon the doors of the house before it , and wrapped it with gold
And the whole house was plastered with gold , until it was finished ; and the altar before the inner house was plastered with gold .
And he made two reins of olive trees , ten cubits high each , and sat in the inner court
And the one had two wings , five cubits in length , ten cubits from the top of the wings to the top of the wings .
And the two wings of the one that draws the reins were ten cubits ; and the size and the form of the two reins were one .
This is ten cubits high , and so is that which is high .
And he placed two wings in the inner temple ; and the wings of the one were open , and the one was toward the wall , and the other toward the wall ; and the two wings were joined together in the midst of the temple .
And with gold wrappings , the two attracted each other
On the walls around the inner and outer courts were engraved reindeer , palm trees , and early flowers .
And the floors of the inner and the outer courts were covered with gold
And one fifth of the walls of the doors of the inner house shall be made of olive trees , and of cedars , and of frames ,
And on the two doors of the olive tree gold was engraved , and on the two doors of the olive tree gold was engraved , and on the two doors of the olive tree gold was engraved , and on the two doors of the olive tree gold was engraved .
And of olive trees he made the frame of the gates of the tabernacle , and a quarter of the walls of the gates .
&quot; For two doors of pine trees , this one is folded , and that one is folded
And there were engraved on it reindeer , and palm trees , and first blossoms ; and they were engraved with gold .
And he made three layers of stone , and one layer of cedar , and the inner court of the building .
In the fourth year , in the month of Zephaniah , Solomon laid the foundation of the house of the Lord
In the eleventh year , in the month of Pleasant , that is , in the month of August , the temple and all that belongs to it , were made according to the pattern . It took him seven years to build the temple
Solomon built the palace for himself in thirteen years
And he built the house of the forest of Lebanon , an hundred cubits long , fifty cubits wide , and thirty cubits high , with three pillars of acacia trees , and beams of acacia trees on the pillars .
and covered it with acacia trees ; fifteen pillars in each row , forty-five in all .
There are three levels of windows , windows and windows relative
All the doors were of thick wood , with three storeys of windows , and the windows were proportional to the windows
And a porch with pillars , fifty cubits long and thirty cubits wide , and a porch before it , and pillars and steps outside it ;
And a porch was built in which the seats of judgment were set up ; and the porch was covered with cedar from the ground to the top .
And in the courtyard there was a palace in which Solomon dwelled , and he built a palace for the daughter of Pharaoh , whom he had married , as in the courtyard
&quot; All the stones for the construction of these things are precious ; they are carved according to the measure , and they are cut out with a saw : from the foundation they are straight to the eaves , and from the outside they are straight to the court .
The foundation is a precious stone , ten cubits long , and eight cubits long
On it were cedar trees , and precious stones cut down by measure .
And around the house were three layers of stones , and one layer of cedars , of cut stone , like the inner court of the house of the Lord , and like the porch of the house of the Lord .
And king Solomon sent men to Tyre , and called Huran
&quot; He was the son of a widow of the tribe of Naphtali , and his father was of Tyre , a coppersmith ; and Huramun was wise , and wise , and skillful , and skillful in all kinds of copper ; and he came to the king of Solomon to do all that he should do
And he made two pillars of brass , eighteen cubits high , and twelve cubits round about .
And two pillars of brass were cast on the pillars , five cubits high each .
And on the tops of the pillars were nets of adornment , and chains of twisted work , seven on each head .
There were two rows of pomegranate around the net , covering the pillars , both of them
The pillars of the porch shall be four cubits in diameter , engraved with hyacinth .
And on the belly of the pillars were two rows of pomegranates round about , and two hundred rows were round about .
And he set up two pillars in front of the porch , one on the right , to be called Jachin , and one on the left , to be called Boaz
And on the top of the pillars were engraved almonds ; and the work of building the pillars was finished .
And he made a copper sea round , five cubits high , ten cubits in diameter , and thirty cubits round .
Underneath the sea were the cucumbers of the field round about , ten cucumbers per elbow , in two rows , cast at the time of the casting of the sea .
There were twelve copper cows carrying the sea , three to the north , three to the west , three to the south , three to the east ; and the sea was upon the cow , and the tail was inward .
A palm of the sea is thick , like a cup , and like a hundred petals ; it can contain two thousand talents .
He made ten bastions of brass , four cubits long , four cubits wide , and three cubits high .
&quot; This is the way the seat was made : on all sides were hearts , and hearts were in the midst of hearts .
And on the heart were lions and cattle , and on the sides were mounts , and under them were lions and cattle , and on the sides were mounts .
There were four bronze wheels and a bronze axle for each basin ; and under the basin , on the four corners of the basin , was a molten basin-shape , and on its sides was a basin-shape .
A small throne is an elbow high , and its mouth is round , as if it were a seat ; and it is one and a half cubits in diameter , and there is a carpenter on its mouth ; and its heart is square , and not round .
The four wheels shall be under the heart , and the axes of the wheels shall be joined to the seats , one cubit and a half high for each wheel .
The form of the wheel is like a wheel of a car . Axes , rods , iron rods , hubs , are all cast
And on every square of the seat there shall be a basin , and it shall be cast in the same place .
And on the seat there was a circle , and a half elbow high ; and on the seat there was a fountain and a heart , which were cast with the seat .
There were engraved on the fountain and on the heart of the lion , and on the palm tree , and around it was the fountain .
The ten basin seats are the same , the same casting method , the same size , the same pattern
And he made ten bowls of brass , forty cubits in each bowl , four cubits in diameter ; and on the ten bowls he placed one bowl for each bowl .
And five sat on the right side of the gate , and five on the left side of the gate , and the sea on the right side of the gate , that is , on the south side ;
And Huran made a basin , and a shovel , and a dish ; and he finished all the work of the house of the Lord for king Solomon
And two pillars were made , and on the pillars two like the tops of the balls , and two nets over the pillars .
And four hundred pomegranates on two nets , two rows for each net , covered with two pillars , like the top of a ball .
Ten seats , and ten bowls above them ,
The twelve oxen of the sea and under the sea
The pots , and the shovels , and the dishes , were all of the brass that Huran made for the house of the Lord , of bright copper for king Solomon .
It was cast out of clay in the plains of Jordan , and in the trenches , and in the midst of Sarath according to the king &apos;s commandment .
All these things Solomon did not weigh , for many things , and the weight of brass was not discernible .
And Solomon made an altar of gold in the house of the Lord , and a golden table for cakes
and the lampstands of gold before the inner court , five on the right , five on the left , and the gold flowers , lamps , and waxenware on them ;
and the cups of gold , and the bowls , and the spoons , and the spoons , and the spoons of fire , and the gates of the sanctuary , and the gates of the inner house , and the gates of the outer house ,
And when king Solomon had finished all the work of the house of the LORD , he divided the silver and the gold of his father David , and the vessels , and brought them into the ark of the house of the LORD
Then Solomon gathered the elders of Israel , and the heads of the tribes , and the heads of the tribes of Israel , to Jerusalem , to bring up the ark of the LORD from David to Zion
And all Israel gathered themselves unto the king of Solomon before the Sabbath , in the month of Edom , the month of July
And when the elders of Israel came , the priest lifted up the ark of the covenant
And the priests and the Levites brought up the ark of the Lord , and brought up the tabernacle and all the holy vessels of the tabernacle of the congregation
And king Solomon , and all the congregation of Israel that was gathered to him , sacrificed bulls and lambs before the ark , as many as were numbered
And the priest brought up the ark of the Lord into the inner house , which is the sanctuary , and laid it under two winged wings
And he stretched out his wings above the ark , and covered the ark , and the bars of the ark .
The bars were long , and the bars could be seen in the sanctuary in front of the inner temple , and they could not be seen outside the temple ; and they are still there to this day .
There were only two stone tablets in the ark , which Moses laid in Mount Horeb , after the children of Israel had come out of the land of Egypt , in the time of the covenant of the Lord with them , and nothing else
When the priests came out of the sanctuary , there were clouds filling the house of the Lord
Even the priests could not stand up to serve , for the glory of the Lord filled the temple
Then Solomon said , &quot; The Lord said , &apos; He will dwell in the darkness
I have built the house for you as your dwelling place , and as your dwelling place for ever .
The king turned his face to bless the congregation of Israel , and all the congregation of Israel stood up
Solomon said , &quot; Blessed is the Lord , the God of Israel , for he has fulfilled with his hands what he promised my father David with his mouth
He said , &quot; Since I brought my people Israel out of Egypt , I have not chosen a city from among the tribes of Israel , nor built houses for my name , but chose David to rule over my people Israel .
Solomon said , &quot; My father David made a vow to build a house for the name of the Lord , the God of Israel
&quot; But the Lord said to David my father , &quot; It is good that you intend to build a house for my name
&quot; But you will not build a house , but your son who is born will build a house in my name
&quot; Now the word of the Lord has been fulfilled , that I may succeed David my father in the throne of Israel , and build a house in the name of the Lord , the God of Israel
&quot; And I have prepared in it for the ark of the covenant , which is the covenant of the Lord with our fathers when He brought them out of the land of Egypt .
And Solomon stood before the altar of the Lord in the midst of the congregation of Israel , and lifted up his hand to heaven
&quot; Lord , God of Israel , there is no God in heaven or on earth that can be compared to you , and you will keep the covenant of mercy to the servants who are before you with all your heart .
&quot; The word which you swore to your servant David my father , has now been fulfilled ; and as it is today , your word has been fulfilled , and your hand has been fulfilled
&quot; Now therefore , O Lord , God of Israel , confirm what you have promised to your servant David my father , saying , &apos; If your sons will be prudent in their conduct , and act before me as you did , they will not forsake the kingdom of Israel .
O God of Israel , fulfill the word which David my father swore to thy servant
&quot; Doth God dwell on the earth ? Behold , the heavens and the heavens above are not enough for you to dwell in , and this house which I have built ?
&quot; But the Lord , my God , listen to the prayers of his servants , and listen to the prayers of his servants , which are before you today
&quot; Look at this house , which you have promised to set up for your name , day and night ; and listen to the prayers of your servants to this place .
&quot; When your servants and your people Israel pray here , hearken to your abode in heaven , and hearken , and forgive ;
&quot; If a man sins against his neighbor , and he is called to swear , he shall come to this house and swear before your altar
&quot; Hear thou in heaven , and judge thy servants , and make the wicked to be guilty , and recompense him according to what he hath done ; and make him righteous , and give him according to his righteousness
&quot; If your people Israel have sinned against you , and have fallen before their enemies , they will return to you , and acknowledge your name , and pray and pray in this house
Listen in heaven , and forgive the sins of your people Israel , that they may return to the land which you gave to their fathers
Your people have sinned against you , and you have punished them , and the heavens have not been shut up to rain ; and if they pray to this place , and confess your name , then leave their sins .
&quot; Hear in heaven , and forgive the sins of your servants , the children of Israel , and teach them the righteous way of doing ; and rain on your land , which you have given to your people for a possession ;
If there be famine , plague , drought , mold , locusts , grasshoppers in the land , or enemy enemies encircle the cities , whatever plague or disease there may be
&quot; Your people Israel , or all of them , or one of them , shall lift up their hands to this house , whatever they pray , whatever they pray
Forgive , O Lord , your dwelling place in heaven ; for you know the hearts , and do to them as men do ; but you know the hearts of the world .
that they may fear thee in the land which thou hast given to our fathers for a lifetime
&quot; The foreigners , who are not of your people Israel , came for your name from afar
And they prayed unto this house , when they heard the words of thy great name , and of thy mighty hand , and of thy stretched out arm
Listen to your dwelling place in heaven , and do according to the prayers of the Gentiles ; that all the people of the earth may know your name , and fear you as your people Israel fear you , and that they may know that the house which I have built is called under your name
&quot; If your people are sent to fight against your enemies , wherever they may go , pray to the city which the Lord has chosen , and to the house which I have built in your name .
Listen to their prayers and supplications in heaven , that they may be victorious
&quot; If your people sin against you , and there is no one who does not sin , then you will be angry with them , and you will take them away from their enemies to their enemy &apos;s land , either far or near
&quot; If they remember sin in the land of captivity , and turn their hearts , and ask You , saying , &apos; We have sinned , we have rebelled , we have done evil ,
&quot; If they turn to you in all their hearts in the land of captivity , and turn to their own land , which you have given to their fathers , and to the city which you have chosen , and to the house which I have built in your name ,
&quot; Listen to their prayers and supplications in your dwelling place in heaven , and do justice to them .
Forgive your people for their sins , and forgive all their transgressions , that they may have mercy on the captives of their people .
&quot; For they are your children , your inheritance , which you brought out of Egypt from the furnace of iron .
&quot; Let your eyes be on your servants , and hear the prayers of your people Israel , that they may pray to you at any time , and that you may listen
&quot; You , Lord Yahweh , have separated them from the people of the earth for your inheritance , as you promised them by your servant Moses , when you brought our fathers out of Egypt .
Then Solomon knelt down before the altar of the Lord , and lifted up his hand to heaven , and when the prayer and the supplication had been finished before the Lord , he arose
And he stood and blessed the whole congregation of Israel with a loud voice ,
Blessed is the Lord , for in all that He has promised , He has given peace to His people Israel , and not one word of the blessings promised by His servant Moses has failed
&quot; May the Lord , our God , be with us as with our fathers , and not forsake us , nor forsake us
Let our hearts return to Him , and walk in His ways , and keep the commandments , the statutes , and the ordinances of our fathers .
May the Lord , our God , remember these words that I have prayed before the Lord day and night , and do justice to His servants and to His people Israel every day
that all the people of the earth may know that the Lord is God , and that there is no other God
&quot; Therefore keep your hearts to the Lord our God , and keep his statutes , and keep his commandments , even as it is today
The king and all the people of Israel sacrificed together before the Lord
Solomon offered a sacrifice of peace offerings to the Lord , twenty and two thousand oxen and twelve thousand sheep , as a sacrifice for the house of the Lord , the king and all the people of Israel
On that day , because the bronze altar in front of the house of the Lord was too small for the fat of the burnt offering , the fat of the sacrifice , and the fat of the peace offering , the king sanctified it in the court of the house of the Lord , and offered therein the fat of the burnt offering , the fat of the sacrifice , and the peace offering
And it came to pass at that time , when Solomon and all Israel were gathered together from the mouth of Hamath even unto the little river of Egypt , all Israel were gathered together for assembly , to keep the Sabbath before the Lord our God seven days and seven days and fourteen days
And on the eighth day the king sent away all the people , and they blessed the king : and they were glad in their hearts , and went every man to his house , seeing all the favour which the LORD had bestowed upon David his servant , and upon all Israel his people
The house of the Lord and the kingdom , which Solomon built , and all that he desired to build , were finished
Then the Lord appeared to Solomon twice , as he had appeared to him at Gibeon
And he said unto him , I have answered all that thou hast prayed unto me ; and I have sanctified the house which thou hast built , and my name shall be there for ever , and my eyes and my heart shall be there for ever .
&quot; If you obey your father David , and walk before me with a heart of truth and integrity , and do all that I have commanded you , and keep my statutes and my ordinances
&quot; I will establish your kingdom in Israel for ever and ever , just as I promised your father David , &quot; Your sons will sit in the kingdom of Israel forever and ever .
&quot; If you and your children turn away from following me and from obeying my commandments and my statutes and from worshipping other gods
&quot; And I will cut off the children of Israel from My land which I have given them ; and I will forsake the sanctuary which I have sanctified for My name ; and I will make the children of Israel a mockery and a derision among the people .
&quot; Wherefore does the Lord do this to this land and to this house , even though it is so high ? Those who pass by shall be amazed and laugh ,
And they shall say , It is because the people of the land have forsaken the LORD their God , who brought their fathers out of the land of Egypt , and have come near unto other gods , and have worshipped him , that the LORD hath brought all this evil upon them
&quot; For twenty years Solomon built the house of the Lord and the king &apos;s house
And the king of Solomon gave to Hilan the twenty cities of Galilee , which Hilan king of Tyre had given to Solomon , according to all that he had desired , with acacia trees , pine trees , and gold
He went out of Tyre , and looked at the cities which Solomon had given him , and was not pleased
&quot; And he said , &apos; My brother , what cities have you given me ? &apos; And he named the land of these cities Capernaum to this day
And Hilan gave Solomon an hundred and twenty pieces of gold
&quot; The king of Solomon chose the people who suffered to build the house of the Lord , his own house , Mirro , the wall of Jerusalem , Shazo , Midian , and Kedesh
Pharaoh the king of Egypt , who had come before , took Kizrah , and burned it with fire , and killed the Canaanites who dwelled in it , and gave it to Solomon &apos;s wife , his daughter , as a spoil
And Solomon built Kizr , and Bethlehem ,
Damo in the wilderness of Bala and the confederates
and all the cities of the storehouses , and the cities of the chariots , and the cities of the horsemen , which they shall build , as they will in Jerusalem , and in Lebanon , and in all the kingdoms which they shall rule ;
And concerning the remnant of the children of Ammon , and the children of Hesh , and the children of Bile , and the children of Shimei , and the children of Jebus , which were not of the children of Israel ,
&quot; For Solomon chose his seed as a slave to his affliction , even to this day , which the children of Israel could not consume
Only the children of Israel did Solomon not make them slaves ; but they were his soldiers , his servants , his commanders , his captains , his chariots , his horsemen
Solomon has five hundred and fifty inspectors and supervisory workers
And the daughters of Pharaoh moved from David unto the house which Solomon had built for him ; and it was at that time that Solomon built Miro
And it came to pass three times a year , that Solomon offered burnt offerings and peace offerings on the altar which he had built for the LORD , and burnt incense on the altar before the LORD ; and the work of building the house was finished .
And king Solomon built ships in the land of Edom , by the Red Sea , at Ezun-gabat , which is near Ephraim
He sent his servants as sailors who were acquainted with the sea , and they sailed with Solomon &apos;s servants .
And when they were come to Ophir , they took from it four hundred and twenty pieces of gold , and brought it to the king of Solomon
And when Sheba heard the fame of Solomon in the name of the Lord , she came to test Solomon with words that could not be understood
And there came with him to Jerusalem a great multitude , and camels carrying incense , and precious stones , and much gold ; and when he came to the king of Solomon , he spoke to Solomon all that was in his heart .
And king Solomon answered all that he had asked , and there was not a word that was not understood or answerable
And the queen of Sheba saw Solomon wise , and the palace which he had built
And it came to pass , when they saw the delicacies of the seats , and the people sitting in rows , and the servants sitting by their sides , and the adornment of their garments , and the adornment of the wine-dressing apparel , and when they saw him go up on the steps of the house of the LORD , as a burnt offering in the house of the LORD , that God was astonished .
He said to the king , &quot; What I have heard in my country concerning your affairs and your wisdom is true .
&quot; I did not believe those words until I saw them with my own eyes , and I knew not half of what they had told me . Your wisdom and your blessings are greater than the winds I have heard .
Blessed are thy servants , thy servants , who stand before thee continually , and hear the words of thy wisdom
Blessed be the LORD thy God , who hath pleased thee , and made thee sit in the throne of Israel : for he hath loved Israel for ever , and hath made thee king , and hath made thee righteous
Then the queen of Sheba gave him a hundred and twenty pieces of gold , and stones , and a great multitude of spices , to the king of Solomon , and he gave the king &apos;s spices , and there was no more of them .
And the ships of the Syrians brought gold from Ophir , and from Ophir a great number of sandalwoods and jewels
The king made of it a bar for the house of the Lord and the king &apos;s palace , and a harp for the singers ; and there was no more of it in the land , and no man saw it , until this day .
And all that the queen of Sheba sought , the king of Solomon gave him , and in his own goodness , and the queen and her servants returned to their own land
And of the gold that Solomon received every year were six hundred sixty and sixty and six .
And there were merchants , and kings of the tribe , and governors of the land , and gold which they brought in .
And the king of Solomon made two hundred faces of gold with hammers , and six hundred shekels of gold for each face .
And three hundred shields of gold , hammered out , were laid in the house of the forest of Lebanon , with three measures of gold on each side .
The king made a throne out of ivory , and wrapped it in gold .
The throne has six steps . The back of the throne is round . There are arms on either side . Two lion stand near the arms .
There stood twelve lions on the six steps , two on each floor , one on the left and one on the right . This was not done in all the nations .
All the drinking vessels of the king of Solomon were of gold ; and all the vessels of the house of Lebanon were of pure gold ; and silver was no measure in Solomon &apos;s years
For he has given the king a ship to sail with the ships of the Philistines , three years at a time , carrying gold and silver , and ivory , and monkeys and monkeys , and birds of prey .
The riches and wisdom of king Solomon are greater than all the kings of the earth
All the kings of the earth seek Solomon , to hear the words of God , which have given him wisdom
And they brought gifts of gold , and silver , and clothing , and weapons , and spices , and horses ; and there was an ordinance every year .
And Solomon gathered together chariots and horsemen , and there were a thousand and four hundred chariots , and twelve thousand horsemen , and set them in the cities of Tun-shaw , and Jerusalem was with the king
And the king made silver as stones in Jerusalem , and cedars as firs in the high places .
The horses of Solomon were brought from Egypt , and they were bought by the king &apos;s merchants , one by one , according to the price .
The cars which the kings of Hesh and of Aram bought from Egypt were six hundred shekels of silver for each car , and one hundred fifty shekels for each horse ; and the horses which the kings of Hesh and of Aram bought were also by their hand
besides the daughters of Pharaoh , king Solomon also loved the daughters of many lands : the daughters of Moab , the daughters of Ammon , the daughters of Edom , the daughters of Sidon , the daughters of Hesh
And concerning the people of these lands , the Lord said to the children of Israel , &quot; You shall not come in company with them , for they will tempt your hearts to follow their God ; but Solomon loves these women
Solomon had seven hundred wives , all of them princesses , and three hundred concubines , which seduced his heart
When Solomon was old , his concubines tempted his heart to follow other gods , not following David his father , but obeying the Lord his God in truth and truth .
For Solomon followed the goddess of the Sidonians , Asheroth , and the goddess of the Ammonites , Milcah .
Solomon did that which was evil in the sight of the Lord , and did not obey David his father , but was obedient to the Lord
Solomon built an altar on the mountain opposite Jerusalem for Gibeah , the God of Moab , and for Moab , the God of the Ammonites ,
Thus did he for the foreign women , the wives whom he had married , who offered sacrifices to his God
And the LORD was angry with Solomon , because his heart was turned away from the LORD God of Israel , who appeared to him twice
The Lord commanded him not to obey other gods , but he did not keep what the Lord commanded him
Then the Lord said to him , &quot; You have done this , and you have not kept the covenant and the law which I have commanded you to keep , and I will take back your land and give it to your servants
&quot; But for the sake of your father David , I will not do this in your lifetime , and I will take away the kingdom from your son &apos;s hand .
&quot; But I will not take the whole nation back , but leave a tribe to thy son for David my servant and for Jerusalem which I have chosen
And the LORD raised up Hadad the Edomite , the enemy of Solomon , which was the seed of the king of Edom
And David struck Edom before , and Joseph the commander went up to bury the slain , and slew all the men of Edom .
And Joab and all Israel dwelt in Edom six months , until they had cut off all the men of Edom .
Hadad was still a child at that time , and he and his father &apos;s servants fled to Egypt , and several Edomites .
And they went up from Midian unto Balaam ; and they came to Egypt from Balaam with a few men , and saw Pharaoh king of Egypt , who had provided him with food , and had given him a house and a field
And Hadad was gracious before Pharaoh , and Pharaoh gave him the wife of the queen &apos;s sister , whom he had given to Annan
And the sister of Reuben bore Hadad a son , whose name was Cunuphar ; and Reuben gave him suckling in the house of Pharaoh ; and Cunuphar lived in the house of Pharaoh with all the children of Pharaoh
And when Hadad heard that David slept with his fathers in Egypt , and that Joseph the captain of the host was dead , he said unto Pharaoh , Permit me , O king , to return to my country
And Pharaoh said unto him , What lackest thou in me , that thou shouldest return to thy own land ? And he answered , I have nothing but to ask the king to let me return .
God also raised up Lyson the son of Elijah , an enemy to Solomon , who had fled from Hadadezer king of Zobah , his master
And it came to pass , when David had struck the Zobahites , that he gathered a people together , and made himself their head , and dwelt in Damascus , and reigned therein
When Solomon was alive , Elisha was an enemy to Israel , besides Hadad , who hated Israel , and made him king over the children of Aram
And Jeroboam the son of Nethan , Solomon &apos;s servant , lifted up his hand against the king ; and he was of the Chaldeans of the tribe of Ephraim ; and his mother was a widow , whose name was Zeruiah .
For he lifted up his hand against the king , because he had built Miro in the days of Solomon , and repaired the breaches of David his father
And when Solomon saw the young man &apos;s diligence , he sent him over all the work of the house of Joseph
And it came to pass on a day , when Jeroboam went out of Jerusalem , that Ahijah the prophet of the children of Tyre met him on the way ; and he was clothed in a new garment ; and there was no one else among them in the field .
Ahijah tore the new garment which he had worn into twelve pieces
Then he said to Jeroboam , &quot; You may take ten pieces , &quot; as the Lord God of Israel said , &quot; and I will take the kingdom out of the hand of Solomon , and give you ten tribes
&quot; For the sake of David my servant , and for the sake of Jerusalem , which I have chosen among the tribes of Israel , I have left a tribe to Solomon
For he has forsaken me , and has not obeyed my ways , nor done righteousness in my sight , nor kept my statutes , as David his father did , to worship the goddess of the Sidonians , Asheroth , the God of Moab , and the God of the Ammonites ,
&quot; But I will not take away the whole land from his hand , and make him king for ever , but because my chosen servant David kept my commandments and my statutes
&quot; I will take back the kingdom from his son &apos;s hand , and give it to you in ten tribes
&quot; And he left a branch to his son , that David my servant might have a lamp in front of me in the city of Jerusalem , which I chose for my name
&quot; I will choose thee , and make thee king over Israel according to all that is in thy heart
&quot; If you will obey all that I command you , and follow my ways , and do righteousness in my sight , and keep the commandments of my law , as my servant David did , I will be with you , and I will build you a strong house , as I did for David , and I will give you the children of Israel
I will cause the seed of David to suffer because of what Solomon did , but not for ever
So Solomon sought to kill Jeroboam ; and Jeroboam fled to Egypt , and came to the king of Egypt , Zechariah , and lived in Egypt , until Solomon died .
The rest of the acts of Solomon , and all that he did , and his wisdom , are written in the book of Solomon .
Solomon reigned forty years in Jerusalem as king over all Israel
And Solomon slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David his father : and his son Rehoboam reigned in his stead
And he went to Shechem : for all the children of Israel came to Shechem to make him king
And Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar fled before the king of Solomon to Egypt , and lived there .
And the men of Israel sent to him , and asked him to come ; and he came to him , and all the congregation of Israel , and spoke to him
&quot; Your father has burdened us with a heavy yoke and made us suffer . Now , please , lighten the burden and the heavy yoke that we have suffered , and we will serve you
And he said unto them , Go ye for a while , and come again unto me on the third day : and the people went away .
And in the days of Solomon the father of Rehoboam , king Rehoboam and the elders who were before him consulted with them , saying , What counsel have you given me , that I may return to this people ?
And the elders said unto him , If the people now be servants unto the king , and answer them with good words , they shall be servants unto the king for ever
But the king did not use the counsel of the elders , but he consulted with the young men who stood before him and grew up with him .
&quot; The people said to me , &apos; Your father has put us on a heavy yoke , and please make it easier for us . What idea have you given me , and I will respond to them
Then he said to the young men who had grown up with him , &quot; They said to the king , &apos; Your father has put us in a heavy yoke , and please make us lighter . &apos; Thus will the king say to them , &apos; My thumb is thicker than my father &apos;s waist
&quot; My father has yoked you with a heavy yoke , and I will yoke you with a more heavy yoke . My father will scourge you with a whip , and I will scourge you with a scorpion .
&quot; Then Jeroboam and all the people followed the words of the king of Jeroboam , saying , &quot; You will come to me on the third day , and they will come on the third day
And the king answered the people with a severe word , and it was not necessary for the elders to give him the counsel
He said to the people , &quot; My father has yoked you with a heavy yoke , and I will yoke you with a greater yoke ; and my father will whip you with a whip , and I will whip you with a scorpion .
&quot; But the king refused to obey the people , because it was the Lord &apos;s will to testify to the words which He spoke to Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar by Ahijah the Shelonite
And when the people of Israel saw that the king did not obey them , they said unto the king , What portion have we with David , that we have nothing to do with the sons of Jesse ? go ye , O Israel , every man to his own house , O house of David , concern yourselves : and all the people returned to their own houses
Only the children of Israel , who dwell in the cities of Judah , did Rehoboam reign over them
And king Rehoboam sent Adonijah , the ruler of the people , to the children of Israel , and they slew him with stones ; and he hurried in his car , and fled to Jerusalem .
Thus have Israel rebelled against the house of David , even to this day
And when all Israel heard that Jeroboam was come again , they sent messengers to invite him before the congregation , and to make him king over all Israel ; and they obeyed not the house of David , save the tribe of Judah
And he came to Jerusalem , and gathered together all the house of Judah and the tribe of Benjamin , an hundred and eighty thousand men , chosen to fight against the house of Israel , to take the kingdom , and to return to the sons of Solomon ,
But the word of God came to Shemaiah the man of God , saying ,
&quot; Go and tell the sons of Solomon , and to Rehoboam king of Judah , and to Judah , and to the house of Benjamin , and to the rest of the people ,
Thus says the Lord : &quot; You shall not go up and fight with your brethren Israel ; but go to your houses , for it is for me to do it ; and they will all return according to the word of the Lord , according to the commandment of the Lord . &quot;
And Jeroboam built Shechem in the mountains of Ephraim , and lived therein ; and he went out of Shechem , and built Binuel
Then Jeroboam said , &quot; I fear that the land will still belong to the house of David
&quot; If these people go up to Jerusalem and offer sacrifices in the house of the Lord , their heart shall return to their lord , the king of Judah , and he will kill me , and he will return to the king of Judah ,
Then the king of Jeroboam prepared and cast two calves of gold , and said to the people , &quot; O Israel , it is hard for you to go up to Jerusalem , and this is the God who brought you out of the land of Egypt
And he laid a calf in Bethlehem , and a calf in Dan
&quot; This puts the people in sin , because they go to Dan and worship the calf
And Jeroboam built a house in the high place , and made all the people that were not of the Levites priests
And Jeroboam made the fifteenth day of August a feast for himself , as in the feast of Judah ; and he offered the calf that he had cast in Bethlehem , and set up the priests of the high altar in Bethlehem
On the fifteenth day of August , which is the month which he ordained for the children of Israel , he burned incense on the altar at Bethlehem
Then came a man of God from Judah to Bethlehem , according to the word of the Lord : and Jeroboam stood by the altar to burn incense
And the man of God called to the altar by the commandment of the Lord , saying , &quot; O altar , O altar , Thus says the Lord : &apos; A son shall be born in the house of David , named Josiah , who shall burn the priests of the high altar on you , and kill them on you , and the bones of men on you .
&quot; In the day when the man of God will make a sign , saying , &apos; The altar will break , and the ashes of the altar will be poured out ; &apos; This is the sign that the Lord has spoken
And when the king of Jeroboam heard that the man of God had called to the altar of Bethlehem , he stretched out his hand from the altar , and said , Take him ; and the hand that the man of God had stretched out was dried up , and he could not turn .
And the altar was broken , and the ashes of the altar were poured out , as the men of God did according to the commandment of the Lord .
And the king said unto the gods , Pray for me , and seek the grace of the Lord thy God , that he may restore my hands : and the gods prayed unto the Lord , and the king &apos;s hand was restored , and it was restored as usual
Then the king said to the men of God , &quot; Go back to eat with me , and add to your heart , and I will give you a reward
And the man of God said unto the king , Thou hast given me half of thy house , and I am not the same as thee : neither eatest thou nor drinkest therein
&quot; For the word of the Lord has commanded me , saying , &apos; You shall neither eat nor drink water in Bethlehem , nor return from the way to which you went .
Then returned the God of men from another way , and from the original way that came from Bethlehem
There was an old prophet who lived in Bethlehem , and his sons came and told his father all the things that the man of God had done in Bethlehem that day , and what he had said to the king
And the father said unto them , What way did the gods go ? And the sons told him : for they saw the way of the gods that came from Judah
Then the old prophet commanded his sons , saying , &quot; You have prepared a donkey for me ; and they have prepared a good donkey , and he rides on it
Then they pursued him , and found him sitting under the oak tree , and said to him , &quot; Are you a god from Judah ? &quot; He said , &quot; Yes .
The old prophet said to him , &quot; Please come home with me for dinner
&quot; I will not go back with you , nor enter your house , nor eat and drink with you here , &quot; said the man of God .
&quot; For the word of the Lord commanded me , saying , &apos; You shall not eat therein , nor drink therein , nor return from the way you went .
And the old prophet said unto him , I am also a prophet , as thou art ; and an angel , according to the commandment of the Lord , said unto me , Go and bring him into thine house , that he may eat and drink water ; and it was the old prophet that tempted him
Then the man of God went back with the old prophet , and ate and drank in his house
&quot; The word of the Lord came to the prophet who brought back the angels when they sat down .
And he said unto the God of Judah , Thus saith the Lord ; Ye have rebelled against the word of the Lord , and have not kept the commandment of the Lord your God
&quot; Return and eat and drink in the place where the Lord has forbidden you to eat and drink water ; so your bodies shall not enter into the grave of your fathers .
And when the old prophet had eaten and drunk , he prepared an ass for the prophet that he brought back
Then he went , and a lion met him on the way , and slew him , and the body fell on the way , and the donkey stood by the body , and the lion also stood by the body
Then came a man from there , and saw the body lying on the way , and the lion standing by it , and he came to the city where the old prophet lived , and spoke of it
And when the prophet that brought the man of God back heard it , he said , &quot; This is the man of God who has rebelled against the commandment of the Lord ; therefore the Lord has delivered him into the hand of a lion , and the lion has struck him and has bitten him to death , to prove what the Lord has said to him
Then the old prophet commanded his sons , saying , &quot; You have prepared an ass for me , and they have prepared an ass
And he went and saw the body of the Godman lying on the way , and the donkey and the lion stood by the body , and the lion ate it not , nor touched the donkey
&quot; The old prophet carried the body of the man of God on a donkey , and brought him back to his own city , to mourn him and to bury him
Then he buried his body in his own tomb , and wept at him , saying , &quot; Woe , my brother !
After he had been buried , the old prophet said to his sons , &quot; I am dead . You will bury me in the tomb of the gods , and make my bones near to his bones
For the word which he spoke by the commandment of the Lord concerning the altar of Bethlehem , and concerning the high places in the cities of Samaria , shall surely be fulfilled
And it came to pass after this , that Jeroboam did not depart from his wicked way , but made all the people priests of the high places ; and whosoever would , he was sanctified , and made them priests of the high places .
&quot; This caused the house of Jeroboam to sin , and even his house to perish from the earth .
And Abijah the son of Jeroboam was sick at that time
Then Jeroboam said to his wife , &quot; Go to Sheol , where the prophet Ahijah said to me , &apos; You will be king over this people , and you will change your clothes , so that people will not know that you are Jeroboam &apos;s wife .
&quot; Now you shall bring ten cakes with a few slices and a bottle of honey to meet him , and he will tell your son what will happen
So the wife of Jeroboam arose , and went to Sheroth , and came to the house of Ahijah ; for he was old , and had straight eyes , and could not see .
&quot; The Lord spoke to Ahijah first , saying , &quot; The wife of Jeroboam will come to ask you because his son is sick , and you will tell him so and so ; and when he comes in , you will be dressed as other women
As soon as he entered the door , Ahijah heard the sound of his steps , and said , &quot; Woman of Jeroboam , come in ; why do you dress as another woman , and I am sent to tell you of the crime
&quot; Go back and tell Jeroboam , &apos; Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel , &apos; I have raised you up from among the people , and made you king over my people Israel
&quot; You have taken the kingdom from the house of David and given it to you , but you have not done the will of my servant David , and have not kept My commandments , and have not obeyed Me , and have not done what is right in My eyes
Thou hast done evil more than that which was before thee ; Thou hast set up other gods for thyself , and cast down idols , and provoked me to anger , and cast me behind thy backs .
&quot; Therefore I will bring evil upon the house of Jeroboam , and I will cut off from Israel the males of Jeroboam , whoever is in captivity , free , and I will cut off the house of Jeroboam , as men cut off the dung .
&quot; Everyone who dies in the city of Jeroboam will be eaten by the dogs , and every one who dies in the field will be eaten by the birds of the air , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; So get up and go home ; and as soon as your foot enters the city , your son will die .
And all Israel shall mourn for him , and bury him ; and all the people of Jeroboam shall enter into the tomb ; for in the house of Jeroboam only he has done good to the Lord God of Israel .
And the LORD shall set up another king over Israel ; and the day shall come , and he shall cut off the house of Jeroboam ; and the day shall come
&quot; The Lord will strike the children of Israel , and shake them like a reed in the water , and bring them out of the beautiful land which the Lord has given to their fathers , and spread them out by the banks of the river , because they are puppets , provoking the Lord to anger .
&quot; The Lord will deliver Israel into the hand of his enemies because of the sins of Jeroboam and because of the sins of the children of Israel
And the wife of Jeroboam arose and returned , and came to Deza , and when she had come to the threshold , the son died .
&quot; The people of Israel will bury him and weep for him , just as the Lord spoke by His servant Ahijah the prophet
The rest of the acts of Jeroboam , how he fought , and how he became king , are written in the book of the kings of Israel
And Jeroboam reigned twenty-two years , and slept with his fathers : and Nadab his son reigned in his stead .
And Rehoboam the son of Solomon reigned in Judah forty-one years at the time of his ascension ; and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem , the city which the LORD had chosen of the tribes of Israel to name him . And his mother &apos;s name was Naamah , an Ammonite
The Jews did that which was evil in the sight of the Lord , and the sins provoked him to anger more than their fathers
For they have set up altars and statues and puppets in the high places and under the green trees .
And the children of Judah did all abominations , according to all that the Lord had driven out of the land before the children of Israel
In the fifth year of king Rehoboam , Zechariah king of Egypt came to take Jerusalem
They took away all the treasures of the house of the Lord and the king &apos;s house , and took away the gold shields of Solomon
And the king of Rehoboam made a bronze shield in place of the gold shield , and gave it to the captain of the guard that guarded the gates of the king &apos;s house
&quot; Whenever the king enters the house of the Lord , the guard takes the shield , and brings it back to the house of the guard .
The rest of the acts of Rehoboam , and all that he did , were written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah .
Romans and Jeroboam at times
And he slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David , in the sepulchre of his fathers : and his mother &apos;s name was Naamah the Ammonite ; and Abijah his son reigned in his stead .
In the eighteenth year of king Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar began Abijah to reign over Judah
And he reigned three years in Jerusalem : and his mother &apos;s name was Machah , the daughter of Absalom .
He did all the evil that his father had done before him , and his heart was not as the heart of David his father , who obeyed the LORD his God in truth and truth .
Yet the Lord , his God , gave him light in Jerusalem for David &apos;s sake , that his son might succeed him as king , and strengthen Jerusalem
&quot; Besides that which happened to Uriah the Hittite , there was nothing in David &apos;s life that was contrary to all that the Lord had commanded , but that he did what was right in the eyes of the Lord
In the days of the life of Rehoboam there was often a battle with Jeroboam
The rest of Abijah &apos;s deeds and all that he did were written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah . Abijah fought often with Jeroboam
And Abijah slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David ; and Asa his son reigned in his stead
Twenty years was the reign of Jeroboam king of Israel , and Asa king of Judah .
And he reigned in Jerusalem forty and one years ; and his mother &apos;s name was Machah , the daughter of Absalom .
And Asa did according to the righteousness of David his father in the sight of the Lord
Remove from the land the frog , and all the idols of his fathers ,
And he hath degraded the throne of his grandmother , the daughter of Magdalene ; for he hath made an abominable idol , and Asa hath cut down his idol , and burned it by the river that floweth down .
&quot; But the high places have not yet been destroyed ; but Asa the son of Jesse had a faithful heart to the Lord
And Asa presented all that his father had sanctified , and all the silver and the gold and the vessels that he had sanctified , to the house of the Lord
In the days of Asa and Bashar king of Israel there was often war
&quot; Behold , the king of Israel comes up against Judah , and builds Ramah , and forbids any man to come out of Asanah king of Judah
And Asa delivered into the hand of his servants all that remained of the house of the LORD , and of the king &apos;s house , and of the treasures of the king &apos;s house , and sent them to the sons of Sheshan king of Aram , and to Benhadan the son of his Berites , king of Damascus .
&quot; Your father made a covenant with my father , and I will also make a covenant with you ; and now I will give you gold and silver as a gift ; and please forsake your covenant with the king of Israel , and let him go from me
Then Benhadad listened to the words of king Asa , and sent the captains of the army to attack the cities of Israel , and they struck Eun , Dan , and Jabbar , and Magah , and all the land of Kenirah , and all the land of Naphtali
And it came to pass , when he heard it , that he ceased to work , and did not build Ramah , but lived in Desha .
Then king Asa proclaimed unto all Judah , without a word , and commanded them to send forth the stones and the woods of Bashan to build the house of Ramah , and to build Gibeah and Mizpah in Benjamin
The rest of the acts of Asa , and all that he did , and his might , and the cities that he built , were written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah . When Asa was old , he had a sick foot
And Asa slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David his fathers , in the sepulchre of his fathers : and Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his stead
In the second year of Asa king of Judah , Nadab the son of Jeroboam reigned two years in Israel .
&quot; Behold , you have done evil in the eyes of the Lord , and have done that which his father did , and have committed the sin of his father , that he caused Israel to sin
And Bath-sheba the son of Ahijah the Issacharite rebelled against Nathan , and slew him at Gibeon in the Philistines : and when he and all Israel were besieged at Gibeon ,
In the third year of Asa king of Judah , Baasha killed him , and took his throne
And it came to pass , when Bath-sheba was king , that he slew all the house of Jeroboam ; and all that breathed , and left none , were consumed , as the LORD had spoken by his servant Ahijah the Shilonite
&quot; This is because of the sins of Jeroboam , which made Israel to sin , and provoked the wrath of the LORD God of Israel
And all the rest of that which he did was written in the book of the kings of Israel .
In the days of Asa and Bashar king of Israel there was often war
In the third year of Asa king of Judah , Bashan the son of Ahijah reigned twenty-four years in the land of Dan , king over all Israel .
He did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD , and walked in the way of Jeroboam , and committed the sin which he committed , that he caused the children of Israel to sin
The word of the Lord came to Jehu the son of Hanani , and he reproached Bashan , saying ,
&quot; I have lifted you up out of the dust , and have made you king over my people Israel ; and you have walked in the ways of Jeroboam , and have caused my people Israel to sin , and have provoked me to anger
&quot; I will cut off you and your house , and make your house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nethan
&quot; Whoever dies in the city of Bashan shall be eaten by the dogs ; and whoever dies in the field shall be eaten by the birds of the air .
The rest of the acts of Bashar , and all that he did , and his might , are written in the book of the kings of Israel
And Bath-sheba slept with his fathers , and was buried at Dezath ; and Elah his son reigned in his stead .
And the word of the LORD came unto the son of Hanani , the prophet Jehu , to reproach Bath-sheba and his house for all the evil that he did in the sight of the LORD , and to provoke the LORD to anger with that which he did in his hand , as the house of Jeroboam did , and because he slew the house of Jeroboam .
In the thirty-sixth year of Asa king of Judah , Elah the son of Bath-sheba reigned two years in Damascus as king of Israel
The servants who ruled half his chariot betrayed him , when he was drunk at the slaughter of the house of Asa
Then Zechariah went in and killed him , and overthrew his throne : and it was so in the year 27 of Asa king of Judah
When he sat on the throne , he killed the whole family of Bashar , and there remained not a single male among his relatives or friends .
&quot; He destroyed all the house of Bashar , just as the Lord reproached Bashar by the word of the prophet Jehu
&quot; This is because of all the sins of Baasha and of Elah his son , and because of the sins which they have committed against the children of Israel , and because of the wrath of the LORD God of Israel in the presence of an empty God .
And all the rest of the acts of Elah , and all that he did , were written in the book of the kings of Israel
And it came to pass , in the seventeenth year of Asa king of Judah , that Shinnery reigned seven days in Desha ; and the people encamped against Gibeon of the Philistines
&quot; When the people heard in the camp that he had betrayed the king and killed him , all the people of Israel made him king in the camp that day
And he went up from Gibeon , and besieged all Israel
&quot; When his heart saw that the city was destroyed , he entered into the guard of the king &apos;s house , and set fire to the palace , and burned himself to death
This is because he sinned , and did that which was evil in the eyes of the LORD , and did that which was done by Jeroboam , and did that which was committed by him , that he put the children of Israel in sin
&quot; The rest of the acts of Zechariah and his rebellion are written in the book of the kings of Israel .
And the children of Israel were divided in two : the one half was to Tibni the son of Kenai , to make him king , and the other half to Amri .
But the people who followed him were better than the people of Tiberius , the son of Kenai ; and when Tiberius died , he became king .
And Asa king of Judah reigned thirty and one years , and Amri king of Israel reigned twelve years ; and he reigned six years in Desh .
And he bought the mountain of Samaria with two pieces of silver ; and he built a city on the mountain , and called the name of the city which he had built it Samaria , after the name of the LORD of the mountain , Samaria .
And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD , more evil than all the kings before him
For he did that which was done by Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar , to provoke the anger of the LORD God of Israel in an empty God , because he had committed the sin which made Israel to sin
And all the rest of the acts of Enoch , and all the might that he showed , were written in the book of the kings of Israel .
And he slept with his fathers , and was buried in Samaria : and Ahasuerus his son reigned in his stead .
And Asa king of Judah reigned thirty-eight years , and Ahab the son of Amri reigned twenty-two years in Samaria .
&quot; Ahab the son of Amri did more evil in the sight of the Lord than the kings before him
And he took the wife of Jezebel the daughter of Balak king of Sidon , and went to worship Balak , because he was light in heart , for the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nethan
to build the temple of Balak in Samaria , and to build the altar for Balak in the temple
And Ahab also became Asherrah , and more than all the kings of Israel before him , in the wrath of the LORD God of Israel , because of what he did
&quot; In the days of Ahab , Shiel the Berthite rebuilt the city of Jericho ; in the days of the foundation , he destroyed Abiram the eldest son ; in the days of Enam he destroyed Zechariah the youngest son ; as the Lord said by Joshua the son of Nun
Elijah the Tisbite , who lived in Gilead , said to Ahab , &quot; I swear by the works of the Lord , the God of Israel , who lives forever , that if I do not pray these years , neither will it rain nor rain
And the word of the LORD came to Elijah , saying ,
And when thou hast left this place , go eastward , and hide thyself by the brook Gilead on the east side of the Jordan
&quot; You shall drink the water of that stream ; and I have commanded the crows to feed you therein
So Elijah went , according to the word of the LORD , to dwell by the brook Gilead east of Jordan
And the crows brought him bread and meat morning and evening , and he drank the water of the stream
After a few days , the stream dried up , for there was no rain on the ground
&quot; The word of the Lord came to him , saying ,
And thou shalt arise , and go to Saleh of Sidon , and dwell therein : and I have commanded a widow therein to be thy shepherd .
And Elijah arose , and went to Saleh , and came to the gate of the city , and behold a widow picking wood in it ; and Elijah called unto him , and said unto him , Take me some water out of the vessel , and drink it for me
And it came to pass , when he was come to fetch water , that Elijah called him again , saying , Bring me also a cake
&quot; I swear by the Lord your God , the Everlasting One , &apos; I have no bread , and there is only one face in the altar , and there is only one drop of oil in the bottle . Now I have found two woods , and I will go home and make bread for me and my son ; and when we have eaten , we will die , and when we die , we will die .
Then Elijah said to him , &quot; Don &apos;t be afraid ; do as you have said : first make me a little cake , and bring it to me , and then make it for you and your son
&quot; For thus says the Lord , the God of Israel : &apos; The face of the altar will not be diminished , nor the oil of the bottle shortened , until the day when the Lord rains on the earth
And the woman did according to the word of Elijah ; and he ate many days with the men of his house , and with Elijah .
&quot; The fruit of the altar will not be shortened , neither will the oil of the bottle be shortened , as the Lord said through Elijah
And it came to pass after this , that the wife of the mother-in-law of the house was sick , and his son was very sick , and he was breathless .
And the woman said unto Elijah , What have I done with thee , O man of God , that thou art come unto me , that God may remember my sins , and that my son may die ?
And Elijah said unto him , Give me thy son : and he took the child from the woman &apos;s womb , and took him into the house where he dwelled , and laid him in his bed .
Then they said to the Lord , &quot; Lord , my God , have you cursed him and killed his son , because I dwell in the house of this widow ?
And Elijah fell upon the child three times , and besought the Lord , saying , &quot; Lord , my God , let the soul of this child remain in his body .
&quot; When the Lord has listened to Elijah , the soul of the child is still in his body , and he lives
Then Elijah lifted up his son from the loft , and brought him into the house , and gave him to his mother , saying , &quot; Behold , your son is alive
The woman said to Elijah , &quot; Now I know that you are a man of God , and that the word of the Lord is true through your mouth .
And it came to pass in the third year , that the word of the Lord came to Elijah , saying , &quot; Go , let Ahab see you , and I will rain on the earth
And Elijah went to make Ahab see him : and there was a great famine in Samaria .
And Ahasuerus called Obed , who had slain his house ; and Obed feared the LORD exceedingly
&quot; When Yahweh did not kill the prophets of the Lord , Obadiah hid one hundred prophets , fifty of them in a cave , and took bread and water to feed them
And Ahaziah said to Obadiah , &quot; We have walked through the land to every spring , and to every stream , and we have found grass , that we may save the horses , and that we may save the livestock .
So the two men marched in a separate way ; Ahab alone , and Obed only , all the way
And it came to pass on the way , when he met Elijah , that he recognized him , and bowed himself to the ground , and said , Art thou not Elijah my lord ?
And he answered , Yea , go and tell thy master , saying , Here is Elijah
And Obadiah said , What is the sin of the servant , that thou hast delivered me into the hand of Ahab , and he slew me ?
&quot; I swear by the Lord your God , the Everlasting Lord , that my Lord will send men to seek you in every nation and in every country ; and if you are not there , I will make the people of that nation swear by you , saying , &apos; You are not there . &apos; 
&quot; Now you say , &apos; I am going to tell your master that Elijah is here
&quot; Behold , I am afraid that as soon as I leave you , the Spirit of the Lord , I will take you to a place I do not know . Then I will go and tell Ahab , &apos; If he does not seek you , he will kill me ; but the servant has feared the Lord from his youth
&quot; When Yahweh does not kill the prophets of the Lord , I will hide one hundred of the Lord &apos;s prophets , fifty of them in a cave , and take bread and water for their sustenance . Will no man tell my Lord ?
&quot; Now you say , &apos; I am going to tell your master , &apos; Behold , Elijah is here and he will kill me
Elijah said , &quot; I have sworn by the Lord of hosts to do all things for ever , that I will make Ahab see me today
Then went Obed to meet Ahab , and told him ; and Ahab went to meet Elijah
When Ahab saw Elijah , he said , &quot; Are you the one who caused Israel to perish ?
Elijah said , &quot; It is not I that caused Israel to perish , but you and your fathers , because you have forsaken the commandment of the Lord , and have followed Baal
&quot; Now therefore , when you have sent , gather all Israel together , and the four hundred and fifty prophets who ministered to Baal , and the four hundred prophets who ministered to Asherrah , whom Jezebel fed , and let them all go up to me to Mount Carmel
Then Ahab sent messengers to gather all Israel together , and the prophets , to mount Carmel
Then Elijah came and said to the people , &quot; How long will it be before you have two thoughts ? If the Lord is God , then obey the Lord ; and if Balak is God , then obey Balak ; and the people did not answer . &quot;
Then Elijah said to the people , &quot; I am the only one that remains as the Lord &apos;s prophet , and the prophet of Balak is forty-five
&quot; When he gives us two calves , the prophet of Baal may choose one , and cut it into pieces , and put it on a wood , and let it not burn ; and I have prepared a calf , and put it on a wood , and let it not burn
&quot; You call on the name of your God , and I call on the name of the Lord ; and the God who sends out the fire is God . &quot; And the people answered and said , &quot; This is good
Then Elijah said to the prophet of Balak , &quot; Because you are many , when you have chosen a calf , and are ready , call on the name of your God , but do not set fire
And they prepared the calf that they had received from morning until noon , and they called upon the name of Balak , saying , &quot; O Balak , hear us ; but there was no voice , and there was no listening ; and they danced around the altar that they had built
And it came to pass at noon , that Elijah laughed at them , and said , &quot; Call on him with a loud voice , for he is God , and you shall wake him when he is silent , or when he comes to one side , or when he walks , or when he sleeps .
They cried out , and broke themselves with the sword , and stabbed themselves , according to their statutes , until their bodies were bleeding .
From noon until the time of the offering of the evening , they cried out , but there was no voice , no obedience , and no understanding .
And Elijah said unto the people , Come ye unto me : and the people came unto him , and he repaired the altar of the LORD , which was destroyed .
Elijah took twelve stones according to the number of the tribes of Jacob , according to the word of the Lord which came to Jacob , saying , &quot; Your name shall be called Israel
And with these stones shall he build an altar in the name of the Lord ; and he shall make a ditch in the four corners thereof for the corn of the two sons of Zephaniah
Then he set the wood on the altar , and cut the calf into pieces , and laid it on the wood , and said to the people , &quot; Put four buckets full of water on the burnt offering and on the wood
Again , a second time . Again , a second time . Again , a third time . Again , a third
The waters were filled around the altar , and the ditches
And it came to pass at the time of the offering of the passover , that the prophet Elijah came near , and said , &quot; Abraham , Isaac , God of Israel , Lord , make known to this day that you are the God of Israel , and that I am your servant , and that I do all these things by your commandment
&quot; Listen to me , O Lord , and listen to me , that they may know that your Lord is God , and that you have turned their hearts
Then the Lord sent down fire , and burnt the burnt offering , and the wood , and the stones , and the dust , and the waters of the dry ditch
And when the people saw it , they bowed down and said , The Lord is God , and the Lord is God
And Elijah said unto them , Take the prophet of Balak , and let no man escape : and they took them , and he brought them unto the brook Kishon , and slew them therein .
Elijah said to Ahab , &quot; You are now able to go up and eat and drink because of the noise of the rain .
And he went up to eat and drink : and Elijah went up to the top of mount Carmel , and bowed himself to the ground , and put his face on his knees .
And he said unto his servant , Go up and see the sea ; and he went up and saw it , and said , There is nothing : and he said , Go again and see it seven times .
Then the seventh said , &quot; I have seen a cloud come up from the sea that is not as great as a man &apos;s hand . &quot; Elijah said , &quot; Go up and tell Ahab that you will not be hindered by the rain while you are riding down
And it came to pass at once , when the cloud was darkened , and it rained heavily , that Ahasuerus took the car , and went to Jezreel
And the Spirit of the Lord descended upon Elijah , and he bowed himself , and ran before Ahab , and came to the gate of Jezreel
And all that Ahab did to Elijah , and that he slew the prophets with the edge of the sword , he brought it to Jezebel
Then Jezebel sent messengers to Elijah , and said to him , &quot; If I do not make your life like the life of those men tomorrow at this hour , God will punish me with a great penalty .
And when Elijah saw the vision , he fled , and came to Beer-sheba of Judah , and left his servant there
And he went a day &apos;s journey in the wilderness , and came under a lotus tree ; and he sat down there to die , and said , O Lord , take my life , for I am not greater than my fathers .
And he lay down under the lotus tree , and fell asleep ; and an angel took him by the hand , and said , Arise , eat
And he looked , and behold , beside his head was a bottle of water , and a cake burned with charcoal ; and he ate and drank , and lay still
Then the second time the angel of the Lord came and beat him , saying , &quot; Arise and eat , for you are far off in the way
And he arose , and ate and drank , and went forty days and forty nights , and came to the mountain of God , and it was Mount Horeb .
Then he entered into a cave , and lived in it ; and the word of the Lord came to him , saying , &quot; What are you doing here , Elijah
&quot; Because the children of Israel have rejected your covenant , destroyed your altar , and struck your prophets with the sword , I am one of them , and they seek my life , &quot; he said .
And the Lord said , &quot; Go out and stand on the mountain before me , &quot; and the Lord passed by , and there was a great wind before Him , and the mountains and the rocks were broken down , and the Lord was not in the wind , and the earthquake after the wind , and the Lord was not in it
There is fire after the earthquake , and the Lord is not in the fire ; and there is a small voice after the fire .
And when Elijah heard it , he put on his coat , and stood in the cave , and a voice said unto him , Elijah , what art thou doing here ?
&quot; Because the children of Israel have rejected your covenant , destroyed your altar , and struck your prophets with the sword , I am one of them , and they seek my life , &quot; he said .
Then the Lord said to him , &quot; Go back from the wilderness to Damascus ; and when you have entered there , anoint Hazael king of Aram
and anointed Jehu the son of Nineveh king of Israel ; and anointed Elisha the son of Shaphah of Abimelech prophet in your stead
&quot; Whoever will escape the sword of Hashish in the future , he will be killed by Yahweh ; and whoever will escape the sword of Yahweh , he will be killed by Elisha .
&quot; But I have left for myself among the children of Israel seven thousand , who have not kneaded themselves to Balak , nor kissed him .
Then Elijah departed from there , and met Elisha the son of Shaphah , who was in the field ; and there were twelve cows before him , and he pursued the twelve ; and Elijah came to him , and put on his coat
Then Elisha departed from the cattle , and ran to Elijah , and said , &quot; Please let me kiss my parents first , and then I will follow you . &quot; Elijah said to him , &quot; Go back , what have I done to you ? &quot;
Then Elisha departed from him , and went back , and slaughtered a cow , and boiled the people with the meat of the cow &apos;s loins , and rose up , and ministered unto him .
Then Benhadad king of Aram gathered together all his army , and led them with thirty-two kings , and besieged Samaria in chariots
Then he sent messengers into the city to Ahab king of Israel , and said to him , &quot; This is what Benhadad said
Your silver and your gold shall be mine ; and the most beautiful of your wives and your children shall be mine .
And the king of Israel answered and said , My lord and my king , according to thy word shall I and all that I have belong to thee
Then said Benhadad , &quot; I have sent a messenger to see you , asking you to give me all your silver and your gold wives and your children .
&quot; But at this time tomorrow , I will send my servants to you , to search your house and the house of your servants , and to take away all that you love in your sight .
Then the king of Israel called the elders of the land , and said to them , &quot; Look , how this man has murdered me ; and he has sent men to me first to ask my wives , and my children , and my silver and my gold ; and I have no objection to him
&quot; The elders and the people said to the king , &quot; Do not listen to him , nor obey him
Then said the king of Israel to the messenger of Benhadad , &quot; Thus says my lord my king , &apos; When the king sends a messenger to his servant , all the servants obey him ; but this time I cannot obey him . &apos; &quot; Then the messenger returned to Benhadad
Then Benhadad sent messengers to Ahab , saying , &quot; If the dust of Samaria and every one of my people give one offering , God will give me a great recompense
Then said the king of Israel , &quot; Tell him that he who puts on his helmet and covers his armor should be as if he had taken his helmet and uncovered it
And when Benhadad and the kings were drinking in the tabernacle , when they heard this , they said unto his servants , Stand up , and they shall stand up against the city
And there came a prophet unto Ahab king of Israel , saying , Thus saith the Lord ; Havest thou seen this great multitude , whom I will deliver into thine hand this day , and thou shalt know that I am the Lord
And he answered , The Lord said , With the young men of the governors . And he said , Who shall lead ? And he said , You alone shall lead .
And Ahab numbered with the young men of the governor two hundred and thirty-two ; and the children of Israel numbered seven thousand .
And at midday they went out of the city ; and Benhadad and the thirty-two kings who were with him were drinking bitterly in the tabernacle .
And when they had come out of the city with the young men of the governor , Hadad sent men to seek them , and they reported , saying , There is a man come out of Samaria
He said , &quot; If they speak and come out , capture them alive ; and if they come out to fight , capture them alive .
And they went out with the young men of the governor , and the soldiers followed them
And when they saw the enemy , they slew him ; and the children of Aram fled , and the children of Israel pursued after them ; and Benhadad king of Aram fled on horseback , and with the horsemen
And the king of Israel went out of the city , and struck the chariots , and slew the children of Aram greatly .
Then the prophet came to the king of Israel and said to him , &quot; Be strong , and be careful , for at this time next year King Aram will come and attack you
And the servants of the king of Aram said unto the king of Aram , The God of Israel is the God of the mountains ; therefore they have overcome us ; but if ye fight against them in the plain , we shall surely prevail .
&quot; The king will do this , and he will send the kings away , and the captains of the army will replace them .
Then , according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king &apos;s soldiers that he had lost , and according to the number of the king&apos;
And it came to pass in the next year , that Benhadad sent the children of Zion up to Afar to fight against the children of Israel
And the children of Israel gathered together all their armies , and prepared food , and went out to meet the children of Aram , and pitched against them like two small groups of lambs ; and the land was full of the children of Aram
Then a man of God came to the king of Israel , and said , &quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; Because the children of Aram said , &apos; My Lord is the God of the mountains , and not the God of the plains , &apos; I will deliver all these people into your hands , and you will know that I am the Lord
On the seventh day the Israelites fought with the Aramites against the camp ; and on the seventh day the two armies fought ; and on that day the Israelites slew the Aramites with a hundred thousand footmen
And the rest fled into the city of Afar ; and the walls fell , and the remnant of the twenty-seven thousand were put to death ; and Benhadad fled into the city , and hid himself in tents .
And his servants said unto him , We have heard that the king of Israel is a merciful king ; and now it is better for us to go out and surrender to the king of Israel , clothed in linen and cords , or to save the life of the king
Then they put on their loins linen and cords , and went to the king of Israel , and said , &quot; The king &apos;s servant Benhadad said to him , &apos; Please save my life . &apos; And Ahab said , &apos; Is he still alive ? He is my brother
Then the men looked diligently at his speech , and hurried to record it , and said , Benhadad is the brother of the king ; and the king said , Go and invite him ; and Benhadad came out to meet the king , and the king invited him to the chariot
And Benhadad said unto the king , I will return the cities which my father took from thy father , and thou shalt stand in the streets of Damascus , as my father stood in Samaria . And Ahab said , I have made a covenant with thee , and I will let thee go , and thou shalt make a covenant with him , and I will let him go
A prophet &apos;s disciple , by the command of the Lord , said to his companions , &quot; Strike me , for he will not strike him . &quot;
Then he said to the man , &quot; You have not listened to the word of the Lord , and as soon as you leave me , a lion will bite you ; and as soon as the man leaves him , he meets the lion and kills him .
Then the disciples of the prophet met another man , and said to him , &quot; Strike me , &quot; and he struck him , and hurt him .
Then he went and covered his eyes with a scarf , and changed his face , and waited for the king by the way
Then the king passed by , and called to the king , saying , &quot; When the servant was in the battle , a man brought a man . He said to me , &apos; You will watch over this man , and if you lose him , your life will replace his life , or you will give him a man with silver .
And the king of Israel said unto him , Thou hast done well , and I will judge thee according to the manner , as the servant was in the midst of trouble ; and the man saw not .
And the king of Israel recognized that he was a prophet , and immediately removed the veil of his eyes .
And he said unto the king , Thus saith the LORD ; Because thou hast sent away him whom I set to destroy , thy life shall replace his life , and thy people shall replace his people
Then the king of Israel returned to Samaria , and entered into his palace ,
And it came to pass after this , that there was a vineyard in Jezreel by the house of Nabal the Jezreelite , near the house of Ahaziah king of Samaria
And Ahab said unto Nabal , Thou hast given me thy vineyard as a garden for me : for it is near to my house , and I will give thee a better vineyard ; or if thou wilt have silver , I will give it unto thee according to the price
And he said unto Ahab , I fear the LORD , and will not give thee the inheritance that my fathers left
Then Nabal the Ahieneesite said , &quot; If I dare not give you the inheritance of my fathers , I will go back to the palace , and lie on my bed , and turn my face inward , and I will not eat
&quot; Don &apos;t ask her why you are so sad and don &apos;t eat
He answered , &quot; Because I said to the Jews , &apos; You will give me your vineyard , and I will give you money , or else I will give you another vineyard , &apos; but he said , &apos; I will not give you my vineyard
Then Jezebel the king said to Ahab , &quot; You are not ruling the land of Israel , but you are ruling it ; eat with your heart and with your soul , and I will give you the vineyard of Nabal the Jezreelite
And the letter of Toah was written on the seal of the king , to the elders of the city , and to the nobles that dwelled with him
And it was written in it , saying , &quot; When you declare a fast , let Nebuchadnezzar sit on the throne of the people
Then two of the bandits sat opposite him and testified to him , saying , &quot; You have blasphemed God and the king . &quot; Then they drew him out and struck him with stones
And it came to pass , when the letters of Jezebel were received by the elders and the nobles who dwelled with Naboth in the city , that they did so
proclaimed a fast , and commanded that Nebuchadnezzar should sit on the throne of the people
Then two bandits came , and sat opposite him , and testified to the people , saying , &quot; Naboth has blasphemed God and the king , &quot; and they brought him out of the city , and slew him with stones .
Then they sent to see Jezebel , saying , &quot; Don &apos;t say , &apos; Naboth was stoned to death
And he said unto Ahab , Arise , that the Jews may not give thee the vineyard for a price : for now he is dead
And when Ahab heard that Naboth was dead , he rose up and went down , and sought the vineyard of Naboth the Jews
And the word of the LORD came unto Elijah the Tisbite , saying ,
&quot; Arise , and see Ahasuerus king of Israel , who dwells in Samaria ; and he shall go down to the vineyard of Nabal , where he is now .
&quot; You shall say to him , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; Have you killed a man and gained his inheritance ? &apos; And you shall say to him , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; Where does the dog swallow up the blood of Nabal , and where does your blood swallow up your blood ? &apos;
And Ahab said unto Elijah , Hast thou found me , my enemy ? And he answered , I have found thee , because thou hast sold thyself , and hast done evil in the sight of the LORD
&quot; I will bring evil upon you , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will cut off from Israel all the males who belong to you , both captives and free ,
&quot; I will make your house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar , and like the house of Bath-sheba the son of Ahijah ; for you have provoked me to anger , and have caused the children of Israel to sin
And concerning Jezebel , the Lord said , &quot; The dogs shall eat the flesh of Jezebel in the outskirts of Jezreel
&quot; He who dies in the city shall be eaten by the dogs ; and he who dies in the field shall be eaten by the birds of the air .
&quot; There is no man like Ahab , because he sold himself , and did evil in the eyes of the Lord , and was shaken by the wrath of Jezebel the Queen
And they believed in idols , according to the abominations of the Amorites , whom the Lord had driven out before the children of Israel .
When Ahab heard this , he tore his clothes , fasted , clothed himself in linen , and slept in linen , and walked slowly
And the word of the LORD came unto Elijah the Tisbite , saying ,
&quot; Have you seen that Ahasuerus was so humble before me ? For when he was humble before me , while he was still alive , I did not bring this evil upon him ; but when his son was born , I will bring this evil upon his house
There was no war between the kingdoms of Aram and Israel for three years
And it came to pass in the third year , that Jehoshaphat king of Judah went down to meet the king of Israel
&quot; The king of Israel said to his servants , &quot; Do you not know that Ramoth of Gilead belongs to us ? Shall we sit still , and not take it back from the hand of the king of Aram ?
Then Ahab said to Jehoshaphat , &quot; Will you go with me to take Ramoth of Gilead ? &quot; And Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel , &quot; You and I are not divided ; my people are like your people , and my horses like your horses
And Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel , Ask the Lord first
Then the king of Israel gathered together the prophets , about forty men , and said to them , &quot; Shall I go up and take Ramoth of Gilead , or shall I not ? &quot; They said , &quot; Shall I go up , for the Lord will deliver it into the hand of the king
And Jehoshaphat said , Is there not here a prophet of the Lord , that we may ask him
Then the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat , &quot; There is another man , Micaiah the son of Nunrah , whom we can call upon the Lord ; but I hate him , because he speaks no good words , but only evil words , concerning the prophecy which I have spoken . &quot; And Jehoshaphat said , &quot; The king will not say this
Then the king of Israel called a captain of the guard , and said to him , &quot; Go quickly , and call Micaiah the son of Nunrah
And the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah sat upon a seat in array in the open field before the gate of Samaria ; and all the prophets prophesied before them
And the house of Zedekiah the son of Kenanah made two horns of iron , saying , Thus saith the Lord ; Thou shalt strike the children of Aram with this horn , even to the point of their destruction
For thus prophesied all the prophets , saying , &quot; If you go up to Ramoth of Gilead , you will surely prevail ; for the Lord will deliver the city into the hand of the king
Then the messengers of Micaiah who came to him said to Micaiah , &quot; All the prophets have spoken to the king with the same voice , and it is better for you to speak a similar word to them and speak a good word
And Micaiah said , &quot; I swear by the Lord of everlasting life , and what the Lord says to me , I will say
And Micaiah came to the king , and the king said unto him , Micaiah , may we go up and take Ramoth of Gilead , or may we not ? And he answered and said , Go up , and ye shall surely be victorious ; and the LORD shall deliver the city into the king &apos;s hand .
&quot; The king said to him , &quot; I have commanded you several times , but you have not spoken to me the truth in the name of the Lord
Then Micaiah said , &quot; I have seen the people of Israel scattered in the mountains like sheep without shepherds , &quot; and the Lord said , &quot; These people have no master , and they will go home in peace to their families .
Then the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat , &quot; Have I not told you that this man speaks no good words , nor speaks any evil words , concerning the prophecy I have spoken ?
Then Micaiah said , &quot; Listen to the word of the Lord . I saw the Lord sitting on the throne , and all the hosts of heaven standing around him
&quot; This is what the Lord says , and this is what the Lord says , &apos; Who will persuade Latham of Gilead to flee from Ahab ? &apos;
Then a spirit came out , and stood before the Lord , saying , &quot; I will seduce him
Then the Lord said to him , &quot; What law do you use ? &quot; He said , &quot; I am going to make a spirit lying in the mouths of his prophets , &quot; and the Lord said , &quot; You will be able to attract him , and you will do so .
&quot; Now the Spirit of lies has entered into the mouths of your prophets in the Lord , and the Lord has ordained evil for you
And the house of Zedekiah the son of Kenanah came , and smote Micaiah &apos;s face , and said , Where is the Spirit of the Lord from speaking to thee ?
And Micaiah said , &quot; In the day when you enter the houses of refuge , you will see
Then the king of Israel said , &quot; Take Micaiah and give him back to Uzziah , and to Joash the son of the king ,
&quot; Then the king said , &quot; Put this man in prison , and make him suffer , and eat and drink not enough , and wait until I come back in peace and quiet
Then Micaiah said , &quot; If you come back in peace , the Lord has not spoken this word through me , &quot; and said , &quot; Listen , all you people
And Jehoshaphat king of Israel and king of Judah went up to Ramoth of Gilead
And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat , I will prepare myself for the battle ; and thou shalt still wear the king &apos;s garment ; and the king of Israel shall prepare himself for the battle
Then the king of Aram commanded his thirty-two captains of the chariots , saying , &quot; You shall not fight with their captains , whether they be great or small , but with the king of Israel
And when the captain of the chariot saw Jehoshaphat , he said , This is the king of Israel ; and he turned and fought with him ; and Jehoshaphat cried out
And when they saw that he was not the king of Israel , they turned and did not pursue him
Then there came a man with a bow , and he shot at the king of Israel in the armor ; and the king said to him who drove , &quot; I am severely wounded ; turn your car around , and take me out of the way .
The battle was fierce that day ; and there stood up a man to support the king in the car , and to resist the Aramites ; and by night the king died , and blood flowed from the wounds in the car .
&quot; When the sun was set , a command was given to all the armies , saying , &apos; Return to your own city , and to your own land .
And when the king was dead , they sent him to Samaria , and buried him there
And there was a man who washed his car by the pool of Samaria , and the prostitute washed in it , and the dogs poured out his blood , as the Lord said
The rest of the acts of Ahab , and all that he did , and the palace of the ivory that he built , and all the cities that he built , are written in the book of the kings of Israel
And Ahab slept with his fathers , and Ahaziah his son reigned in his stead .
In the fourth year of king Ahaziah king of Israel began Jehoshaphat the son of Asa to reign over Judah
Jehoshaphat was thirty-five years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned twenty-five years in Jerusalem . His mother &apos;s name was Azubah , the daughter of Hezekiah .
Joseph walked in the way of his father Asa , and did not deviate from the right and the left , but did right in the sight of the Lord : but the altar was not desolate , and the people offered in it burnt offerings
Blessed be Jehoshaphat , king of Israel ,
The rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat , and his might , and how he fought , were written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah .
And Jehoshaphat removed from the land all that remained of his father Asa the son of Hinnom from the earth
There was no king in Edom at that time , and no governor ruled .
And Jehoshaphat built a ship for him to go to Ophir , and brought gold ; but he did not go , because the ship had destroyed Esun-gaib
And Ahaziah the son of Ahab said unto Jehoshaphat , Let my servant and thy servant go with you in the ship : but Jehoshaphat refused .
And Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers , and was buried in the sepulchre of his fathers in David : and Jehoram his son reigned in his stead .
In the seventeenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah , Ahaziah the son of Ahab reigned two years in Samaria .
He did that which was evil in the eyes of the Lord , and did that which was right in the eyes of his parents , and did that which was right in the eyes of Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar , which caused Israel to sin
And he did all that his father had done , and worshipped Baal , and provoked the wrath of the Lord God of Israel
After Ahab &apos;s death , Moab betrayed Israel .
And it came to pass one day , when Ahaziah fell down from the pillar of Samaria , and was sick , that the messengers said unto him , Go and inquire of Baal-zeb the God of Ephraim , whether I am well or ill
And the angel of the Lord said unto Elijah the Tisbite , Arise , and go to meet the messengers of king Samaria , and say unto them , Go and ask Balashib the God of Ephraim , saying , Is there no God in Israel ?
Therefore thus saith the Lord ; Thou shalt not lay down the bed wherein thou hast laid down , but shalt surely die ; and Elijah went away .
Then the messenger came back to the king , and the king asked them , &quot; Why did you come back
Then the angel answered , &quot; A man came to us , and said to us , &apos; Go back to see the king who has sent you , &apos; and said to him , &apos; Thus says the Lord : &apos; Have you sent you to ask Balaksed , the God of Ephraim , because there is no God in Israel ? Therefore you will not be able to enter your bed , and you will surely die .
&quot; The king said to them , &quot; Who is it that came to you to tell you these things
Then the king said , &quot; This is Elijah the Tisbite , and he is clothed in a coat and girded with a girdle . &quot;
And the king sent forth fifty captains , and brought fifty men unto Elijah ; and he went up to Elijah , and he sat on the top of the mountain . And the captains said unto him , O man of God , the king hath commanded thee to come down
Then Elijah answered , &quot; If I were a man of God , a fire would come down from heaven to destroy you and your fifty , and a fire would come down from heaven to destroy the fifty captains and his fifty
The second time the king sent a captain of fifty , and he led fifty men to Elijah ; and the captain of fifty said to Elijah , &quot; O man of God , the king commanded you to come down quickly
And Elijah answered , If I were a man of God , the fire of God would come down from heaven , and consume thee and the fifty that are with thee , and the fire of God would come down from heaven , and consume the fifty captains and the fifty that are with him
And the king sent forth for the third time a captain of fifty , and he led fifty men : and the captain of fifty went up , and kneeled on his knees before Elijah , and besought him , saying , O man of God , let my life be precious in thy sight , and that of thy fifty servants .
&quot; I have come down from heaven through fire , and I have burned down the fifty elders of the first two generations , and the fifty men whom they brought with them , and now let my life be precious in your sight .
And the angel of the LORD said unto Elijah , Go down with him , and fear him not : and Elijah arose , and went down with him unto the king
Then he said to the king , &quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; Have you sent a man to ask Balaksed , the God of Ephraim , because there is no God in Israel ? Therefore you will not enter the bed where you have been , but you will die .
And Ahaziah died , as the LORD spake by Elijah ; for he had no son , and his brother Joram reigned in his stead in the second year of Jehoshaphat the son of Judah .
The rest of the acts of Ahaziah were written in the book of the kings of Israel
And it came to pass , when the LORD had taken Elijah by the swift wind , when the heavens were lifted up , that Elijah and Elisha departed from Gilead
And Elijah said unto Elisha , The LORD hath sent me unto Bethlehem , and thou shalt await there : and Elisha said , I am the LORD of hosts , and I swear before thee , I will not depart from thee : and they came down to Bethlehem
And the disciples of the prophets that were in Bethlehem came to Elisha , and said unto him , The LORD will take thy master from thee this day , and thou knowest it or not ; and he said , I know it ; and ye shall not speak .
And Elijah said unto Elisha , The LORD hath sent me unto Jerusalem , and thou shalt await there : and Elisha said , I am the LORD of hosts , and I swear before thee , I will not leave thee : and the two came unto Jerusalem
The disciples of the prophets who lived in Jericho came near to Elisha , and said to him , &quot; The Lord will take away from you today your master , you know it or not , &quot; and he said , &quot; I know it , and do not raise your voice .
And Elijah said unto Elisha , The LORD hath sent me unto the river Jordan , where thou shalt await : and Elisha said , By the LORD of hosts I swear before thee , I will not depart from thee : and they went together .
And there went forth fifty of the prophets , and stood afar off before them , and stood by the river Jordan .
And Elijah rolled up his garments , and poured water on them ; and the water was divided from one side and the other , and the two men passed through the dry land .
Then Elijah said to Elisha , &quot; I have not been taken away from you ; ask me only what you want me to do for you . &quot; Elisha said , &quot; Bring me as much as your spirit has touched me .
Elijah said , &quot; It is hard for you to do what you ask , but when I am taken away from you , if you see me , you will receive it ; otherwise , you will not receive it .
And as they were walking and speaking , a train came and brake the two men apart , and Elijah went up in the wind .
And when Elisha saw it , he cried out , and said , My father , my father , O horsemen of Israel ; and he saw him no more ; and he rent his clothes in two .
And he took up the garments that had fallen upon Elijah , and went back and stood by the Jordan
And he poured out water with the garment that had fallen upon Elijah , and said , &quot; Lord , there is the God of Elijah in it . &quot; And after he had poured out water , the waters were divided , and Elisha came .
And when the prophets of Jericho saw him from the other side , they said , The Spirit of Elijah touched Elisha ; and they came to meet him , and fell down before him on the ground
And he said unto him , My servants , behold , there are fifty mighty men here : let them seek your master , or the Spirit of the Lord will raise him up , and cast him into a mountain or into a valley . And Elisha said unto him , Thou shalt not send any man
And they urged him again , and he could not deny it , and said , Send forth , and they sent forth fifty men ; and they sought three days , and found none .
Elisha was still in Jericho , waiting for them to return to him . He said to them , &quot; Did I not tell you that you would not go ?
And the men of Jericho said unto Elisha , My Lord hath seen that the land of this city is good : but the waters are evil , and the land is barren
Then Elisha said , &quot; Take a new bottle of salt for me , and they will bring it to him
&quot; And he went out to the spring , and poured salt into the water , saying , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I have healed this water , and I will no more cause man to die , neither will I cause the earth to grow again .
And the water was healed , even unto this day , as Elisha saith
And Elisha went up from there to Bethlehem ; and as he was going up , some of the children came out of the city , and laughed at him , saying , Go up bald , go up bald .
Then he turned and saw them , and cursed them in the name of the Lord : and two bears came out of the forest , and tear through the midst of them forty-two children .
And Elisha went up from Bethlehem unto mount Carmel , and returned from mount Carmel unto Samaria
In the eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah , Joram the son of Ahab reigned twelve years in Damascus
He did evil in the sight of the Lord , but not as his parents did , because he removed the pillar of Baal which his father had built
Nevertheless he was close to Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar , and he would not leave the sins of the children of Israel
And Mizpah king of Moab reared many sheep ; and he offered the king of Israel ten thousand lambs and ten thousand rams each year
After Ahab &apos;s death , the king of Moab betrayed the king of Israel .
Then king Jehoram came out of Samaria , and numbered all Israel
Then they sent messengers to Jehoshaphat king of Judah in the days before , saying , &quot; The king of Moab has betrayed me . Will you go up against Moab with me ? &quot; He said , &quot; I will go up , and you and I will not be divided ; my people will be like your people , and my horse will be like your horse . &quot;
Then said Joram , From that way shall we go up ? And he answered , From the way of the wilderness of Edom
So the king of Israel , and the king of Judah , and the king of the east , went together round about the seven days of the journey ; and the army and the cattle that were with them had no water to drink
Then the king of Israel said , &quot; Woe to you ! The Lord has gathered us together to give these three kings into the hand of Moab
And Jehoshaphat said , Is there not here a prophet of the LORD , that we may ask the LORD ? And one of the servants of the king of Israel answered , Here is Elisha the son of Shaphah , who had served Elijah before .
Then went down the king of Israel , and Jehoshaphat , and the king of Edom , to see him , saying , The word of the LORD shall come upon him .
And Elisha said unto the king of Israel , What shall I do with thee ? go and ask the prophets of thy father and the prophets of thy mother ; and the king of Israel said unto him , Say not thus : The LORD hath gathered us together three kings , but he shall deliver them into the hand of the Moabites
Then Elisha said , &quot; I swear by the Lord , the Lord of hosts for ever and ever , &apos; If I do not see the face of Jehoshaphat king of Judah , I will not listen to you , nor look at you
Now therefore seek ye me a harp : and the Spirit of the LORD shall come upon Elisha at the time of the harp .
Then he said , Thus says the Lord : &quot; You shall dig holes in the valley
&quot; For thus says the Lord : &apos; While you do not see the wind , nor the rain , the valley will be filled with water , to drink water with you and with the cattle
&quot; This is a small thing in the sight of the Lord , and he will deliver the Moabites into your hands
Thou shalt smite every strong city , and shalt cut down every good tree , and shalt shut up every fountain , and shalt trample every field with stones .
And it came to pass in the morning , at the time of the sacrifice , that water came from the east , and the whole earth was filled with water
And all the people of Moab heard that the three kings were coming up to fight with them , and all that were able to carry their helmets and their armor , old and young , were gathered together , and stood on the border
And it came to pass in the morning , when the sun was shining on the waters , that the Moabites arose , and saw the waters red as blood before them
Then he said , &quot; This is blood , and the three kings will slay each other , and all will perish . Now , O Moab , we are going to plunder property
And when the children of Moab were come into the camp of Israel , the children of Israel rose up and fought against them , and fled before the children of Israel ; and they pursued the children of Moab , and slew them in the land of Moab .
And all the fields were filled with stones , and all the fountains were shut up , and all the good trees were cut down ; and there remained only the stone walls of Gilead ; and the men of the stone struck the city round about .
And when king Moab saw that the battle was great and mighty , he commanded seven hundred men with swords to go over against him , but he could not
And he offered in the city for a burnt offering the eldest son that should succeed him as king : and the anger of the LORD was kindled against the children of Israel : and the three kings departed from the king of Moab , and went every one to his own country
Then the wife of the prophet &apos;s disciples cried to Elisha , saying , &quot; Your servant , my husband , is dead ; he fears the Lord , as you know ; and now a creditor has come to take my two sons as servants
And Elisha said unto him , What can I do for thee ? tell me , and what is in thy house ? And he said , There is nothing in the house of the maidservant save a bottle of oil
Then Elisha said , &quot; Go and lend empty vessels to your neighbours , and do not lend less .
&quot; Return to your house , and shut the door , and be in it with your son , and pour the oil into all the vessels , and place the full on one side
Then the woman departed from Elisha , and shut the door , and she and her son were in it ; and the son took the vessel , and he poured out the oil
And when the vessels were full , he said unto the son , Bring me again the vessels ; and the son said , There is no more vessels , and the oil is gone
&quot; The woman went and told the man of God , saying , &apos; Go and sell the oil and pay the debt , and you and your son will be able to rely on the rest of the days
And it came to pass on a day , when Elisha was come to the book , that a woman of the house of Elisha forbade him to eat ; and Elisha went in to eat from there every time he passed by .
And the woman said unto her husband , I have seen that he that passeth by from among us is a holy God
And we shall build for him a little house on the wall , wherein shall be beds , tables , chairs , and lampstands ; and when he cometh unto us , he shall dwell therein
And it came to pass one day , when Elisha was come there , that he entered into the room , and lay down
And Elisha commanded Gehazi his servant , saying , Bring this book to the woman ; and he brought it , and the woman stood before Elisha
And Elisha said unto his servant , What can be done for thee , since thou hast labored so much for us ? And thou hast not asked the king or the captain of the host . And he answered and said , I dwell in my own country .
And Elisha said unto his servant , What shall be done for him ? And Gehazi said , He hath no son , and his husband is old .
And Elisha said , Call him again . And when he had called him , he stood at the door
And Elisha said , Unto this time of the year thou shalt bear a son . And he said , O man of God , my Lord , let not such a woman be deceived
And it came to pass , when the woman was conceived , that she bore a son , as Elisha had said
The child grew up , and one day he came to his father and to the harvester
And he said unto his father , O my head , O my head ; and his father said unto the servant , Take him into his mother &apos;s house
And the servant took him and gave him to his mother , and the child sat on her knees , and died at midday .
And his mother took him up the stairs , and laid him on the bed of the God-man , and shut the door forth
And he called to his husband , and said , &quot; You have called a servant to bring me a donkey , and I will return to the man of God very soon
And he said , This day is not the moon , neither is it a sabbath : why wilt thou go to him ? And the woman said , Peace be upon thee .
Then he set up his donkey and said to his servant , &quot; Go quickly , and if I do not command you , you will not be late
And the woman went up to mount Carmel to meet the man of God : and when the man of God saw him afar off , he said unto Kihashi his servant , Behold , a woman of the book is come
Then you ran to meet him , and asked him , &quot; Are you safe ? Are your husband safe ? Are your children safe ? &quot; He said , &quot; Are you safe ?
And the woman went up to the mountain , and to the man of God , and took hold of his feet ; and Gehazi came to push him away , and the man of God said , &quot; Behold , it is he who is grieving in his heart ; and the Lord has hidden it from me , and has not instructed me
The woman said , &quot; Why have I asked my Lord for a child ? Have I not said , &apos; Will you not deceive me ? &apos;
And Elisha commanded Gehazi , saying , Take my staff before thee , and put it upon thy loins ; and if thou meet a man , ask him no peace ; and if a man ask thee no peace , ask him no peace ; and put my staff upon the face of the child
And the mother of the child said , I have sworn before thee by the Lord of everlasting life , I will not leave thee . And Elisha rose up , and went with him
Then Gehazi went and laid his staff on the child &apos;s face , and there was no voice , and no movement . Then Gehazi returned to Elisha , and told him , &quot; The child has not yet awakened
And Elisha came , and entered into the house , and saw the child dead , and laid him in his bed
Then he shut the door , and he prayed to the Lord , only himself and his children
Being on the bed , face to face , eye to eye , hand to hand . Being on the bed , the child &apos;s body gradually warms up
Then he came down , went in and out of the house , and went up again , and lay down on the child , and when the child had given seven sneezes , he opened his eyes
Then Elisha called Kihashi , and said to him , &quot; Bring this book to the woman , &quot; and called him , and said , &quot; Take up your son
And the woman came in , and bowed herself to the ground before Elisha &apos;s feet , and took up his son , and went out
Then Elisha came again to Geth , where there was famine ; and the disciples of the prophets sat before him , and he said to his servants , &quot; Put the pot on fire , and bake the soup for the disciples
A man went into the fields , and gathered up a field , and met a field cucumber , and picked up a field cucumber , and cut it back , and laid it in a pot to boil the soup , because they did not know what it was
And it came to pass , when they had eaten it , that they cried out , saying , O man of God , there is a poison in the pot , and the people cannot eat it .
And Elisha said , Take bread , and spread it in a pot , and say , Draw it out , and eat it for the people ; and there shall be no poison in the pot .
And there came a man from Balak-shali-sha , and took twenty cakes of the first ripe wheat , and new ears , and put them in his pockets , and gave them unto the gods , saying , Eat these things unto all the people
And the servant said , Shall this be given to a hundred men to eat ? And Elisha said , Thou shalt eat it only for the people : for thus saith the Lord , All the people shall eat , and there remaineth nothing
Then the servant stood before the people , and they ate , and there was indeed left , as the Lord said
And Naaman , the captain of the king of Aram , was great in the sight of his master , because the LORD had made the people of Aram prevail through him ; and he was a mighty warrior , but he was a great madman .
And the children of Aram went out in a multitude , and took away a little woman out of the land of Israel , and she served Naaman &apos;s wife
He said to his mother , &quot; My lord will not go to the prophet of Samaria , but he will cure his great madness .
And Naaman went in and told his master , saying , Thus saith the daughter of Israel , Thus saith the daughter of Israel
Then said the king of Aram , &quot; You can go ; I also have confidence in the king of Israel . &quot; And Naaman went , and took ten pieces of silver , six thousand shekels of gold , and ten linen garments ,
And he brought a letter to the king of Israel , saying , &quot; I have sent Naaman my servant to see you , and when you have received this letter , you will cure his great madness
When the king of Israel saw the letter , he tore his clothes , and said , &quot; Am I God , that I can make a man die and a man live ? This man has sent me to heal his great madness , and you have seen why he has sought a way to attack me
And when Elisha the man of God heard that the king of Israel had torn his clothes , he sent messengers to the king , saying , &quot; Why have you torn your clothes ? Then let him come to me , and he will know that there is a prophet in Israel
Then Naaman came to Elisha &apos;s house in a chariot , and stood before the door
Then Elisha sent an angel and said to Naaman , &quot; Go and bathe in the Jordan seven times , and your flesh will be restored and purified
Then Naaman went away in anger , and said , &quot; I think he must come out to see me , and stand and pray in the name of the Lord his God , and shake his hand over the afflictions , and heal the great devil .
Is not the river of Damascus , and the waters of Athan , and the waters of Pharaoh , better than all the waters of Israel , wherein I shall not bathe myself clean ? Then he turned away in anger .
And his servant came and said unto him , My father , if the prophet had commanded thee to do a great thing , wouldst thou not have done it ? and if he had commanded thee to bathe and be clean , wouldst thou not have been clean ?
Then Naaman went down , according to the word of the man of God ; and he washed himself seven times in the Jordan , and his flesh was restored as the flesh of a child , and he was cleansed .
Then Naaman returned to the man of God , and stood before him , and said , &quot; Now I know that there is no God in all the earth except Israel , and now I ask you to receive the gift of a servant
Then Elisha said , &quot; I swear by the Lord , who lives forever , that I will not suffer ; but Naaman has asked him three times , and he has not suffered
Then Naaman said , &quot; If you do not accept it , give to your servants the soil of two rams , and from now on they will no longer offer burnt offerings or sacrifices of peace offerings to other gods , but to the Lord
&quot; There is one thing , Lord , forgive your servant : When my master came to the temple to worship , I laid his hand on him , and I bowed down , and the Lord forgive me for that I bowed down at the temple .
And Elisha said unto him , Return in peace : and Naaman departed from him , and went not far .
Then said the servant of Elisha , the man of God , in the heart of Gehazi , &quot; My lord will not receive the gift which he brought from Naaman the son of Aram ; I have sworn by the Lord of everlasting life , I will run after him and ask of him
Then Gehazi pursued Naaman ; and Naaman saw that they were chasing him , and hurried down to meet him , saying , Is it safe ?
&quot; And my master sent to me , saying , &apos; There are two young men , a prophet &apos;s disciple , who have come to see me from the land of Ephraim . Give them one silver and two robes
Then Naaman said , &quot; Take him , and he will be bound . Then , when he receives the third one , he will bound him with silver in two pockets , and give two sets of clothes to two of his servants , and they will go up in front of Kihashi .
And it came to pass , when he was come to the mountains , that Gehazi took them from their hands , and laid them in the house , and sent them back
Then Gehazi went in , and stood before his master ; and Elisha said unto him , Where comeest thou , Gehazi ? And he answered , There is no servant to go in
And Elisha said unto him , Is not my heart gone when he cometh down to meet thee , and receiveth silver , and raiment , and buyeth an olive grove , and a vineyard , and a sheep , and a servant ?
Therefore the madness of Naaman shall touch thee and thy seed for ever and ever : and when Gehazi went forth from before Elisha , he was as white as snow .
And the disciples said unto Elisha , Behold , we are too narrow a place to dwell with thee
&quot; Let us go to the river Jordan , and every man take a piece of wood from it , and build a house for his dwelling ; &quot; and he said , &quot; Go .
And one said , Go with thy servant . And he answered , I can go
Then Elisha went with them , and came to the river Jordan , and cut down trees
When a man cut down a tree , and his axe fell into the water , he cried out , &quot; Woe to you , Lord ! This axe has been borrowed
Then the man of God said , &quot; Behold , you are fallen into it . &quot; And he pointed to it to Elisha ; and he cut down a tree , and cast it into the water , and the axe came floating .
And Elisha said , Take it up ; and the man took it up .
Then king Aram fought with the children of Israel , and said to his servants and to his merchants , &quot; I will camp somewhere
And the man of God sent messengers to the king of Israel , saying , &quot; Be careful , and do not pass through any place , for the children of Aram came down from there
&quot; When the king of Israel sent to spy on the place where the man of God had told him that he had been warned , he did so more than once or twice , so that he would not be harmed
Then the king of Aram , being amazed at this , called his servants and said to them , &quot; Who is here to help the king of Israel ?
Then said one of his servants , &quot; My lord , my king , there is no one to help him , except Elisha the prophet of Israel , who told the king what he said in his bedroom
Then said the king , Go and look for him there , and I will send messengers to seize him ; and some told the king , saying , He is fallen
And the king sent chariots and horses and a great army to go there , and came in the night , and besieged the city
And the servant of God came out early in the morning , and saw that the army of chariots and horsemen had besieged the city ; and he said unto the servant of God , Woe unto me , O Lord ! how shall we do ?
&quot; Do not be afraid , &quot; said the man of God , &quot; for he is with us more than he is with them .
And Elisha prayed , and said , Lord , open the eyes of this young man , that he may see ; and when the Lord opened his eyes , he saw that there was a fire upon the mountain , and chariots and horses round about Elisha
Then the enemy came down to Elisha , and Elisha prayed to the Lord , saying , &quot; Please make the eyes of these men go astray ; and the Lord will make their eyes go astray according to the word of Elisha . &quot;
And Elisha said unto them , This is not the way , neither is the city : go ye with me , and I will bring you unto the man whom ye seek : and he brought them unto Samaria
And when they were come into Samaria , Elisha prayed , saying , Lord , open the eyes of these men , that they may see ; and the Lord opened their eyes , and they saw ; and behold , they were in the city of Samaria
When the king of Israel saw them , he said to Elisha , &quot; Father , can I kill them ?
And he said , Thou shalt not slay them ; shalt thou slay them whom thou hast taken captive with the sword and with the bow , when thou hast prepared food before them , that they may eat and drink , and return unto their master ?
And the king prepared for them much food ; and when they had eaten and drunk , he sent them back to their master ; and the army of Aram committed no more sins in the land of Israel .
Then Benhadad king of Aram gathered together all his army , and came and besieged Samaria
Then was Samaria besieged , and there was famine , and even one donkey was worth eighty shekels of silver , and the pigeon &apos;s dung was worth five shekels of silver
One day , as the king of Israel passed through the city , a woman cried out to him , saying , &quot; Lord , my king , please help me
&quot; The king said , &quot; The Lord does not help you ; where am I to help you , from the field or from the winepress
And the king said unto the woman , What is thy affliction ? And she said unto me , Take thy son , that we may eat this day , and eat my son tomorrow
Then we boiled my son and ate it ; and the next day I said unto him , Take thy son , and we shall eat ; and he hid his son .
And when the king heard the words of the woman , he rent his clothes ; and when the people saw him clothed in linen , he passed through the city .
And the king said , If I bear this day Elisha the son of Shaphah &apos;s head on his knees , let God give me a great recompense .
And Elisha was sitting in the house , and the elder was sitting with him . And the king sent a servant to him , and when he had not come , Elisha said unto the elder , Behold , ye see the son of the murderer , and send him to cut off my head : and when ye saw the angel come , shut the door , and let him go out with the door ; and behold , there was no sound of his master &apos;s footsteps behind him .
And it came to pass at the time when he was speaking , that the angel came , and the king came , saying , &quot; The evil is from the Lord ; why shall I turn to the Lord again ?
&quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , &quot; said Elisha , &quot; as the Lord has spoken , &quot; at the gates of Samaria you shall sell one shekel of silver for a shekel of fine flour , and one shekel of wheat for a shekel of fine flour
Then said one of the captains of the king &apos;s army to the men of God , &quot; It will not happen , even if the Lord opens the heavens , &quot; and Elisha said , &quot; You will see with your own eyes , but you will not eat
At the gate of the city there were four great madmen , and they said to one another , &quot; Why are we sitting here waiting to die ?
&quot; If we say , &apos; Come into the city ; there will be famine in the city , and you will die there ; and if you sit here and do not move , you will die there ; come , let us surrender the army of the children of Aram , and they will live , and if they kill us , they will die .
And it came to pass in the twilight , that they arose , and went to the camp of the children of Aram ; and when they came to the camp , they found none there
And they said unto one another , This is the king of Israel , the kings of the Hittites , and the kings of the Egyptians , who have bribed the LORD to come against us , because the army of the children of Aram heard the voice of the chariots , and the voice of the mighty army
So they rose up in the twilight , and fled ; and left the tents , and the horses , and the donkeys , and the camps as they were , to flee for their lives .
And they that were grown mad came to the camp , and entered into the tent , and ate , and drank , and took out of it silver and gold , and clothes , and went to collect them ; and when they came back , they entered another tent , and took out of it treasures , and went to collect them .
Then said they unto one another , What we have done is evil ; and this day is a day of good tidings , and we have not spoken ; and if the day come , sin shall come upon us ; come , and we shall send letters unto the kingdom .
Then they went to call the guards of the gates , and told them , &quot; We have come to the camp of the children of Aram , and there is no man there , and no voice ; only the horses and the donkeys are tied , and the tents are old .
&quot; The guards of the gates called all the guards of the gates , and they entered and wrote to the king &apos;s house
Then the king arose in the night , and said to his servants , &quot; I tell you how the children of Aram should deal with us ; for they know that we are hungry , so they left the camp and lay in the fields , saying , &apos; When the children of Israel come out of the city , we will catch them alive and enter the city
Then one of the servants said to the king , &quot; Why don &apos;t we send forth five horses out of the rest of the city , which are the same as the rest of Israel , and are about to be destroyed ? &quot;
Then he took two cars and two horses , and sent messengers to seek out the army of the children of Aram , saying , &quot; Look , look , look
And when they were come to the Jordan , they saw that all the garments which the children of Aram had thrown away as they ran , were full of garments ; and the angel returned and told the king .
Then all the people went out , and took away the camp of the children of Aram ; and they sold one shekel of silver for one shekel of the face of Assyria , and one shekel of silver for one shekel of the wheat of Dishon , as the Lord had said
Then the king sent the captain of the army , who was with him , and shot at the gates of the city , and they trampled on him there , and he died , as the angels said when they came to him under the king
The man of God said to the king , &quot; Tomorrow , about this time , at the gate of the city of Samaria , one shekel of the wheat of Dishoniah will be sold , and one shekel of the grain of Dishoniah will be sold .
And the captain said unto the man of God , Even if the Lord had opened the heavens , it would not have happened ; and the man of God said , Thou shalt see with thine own eyes , and shalt not eat
And it shall surely come to pass in him , that he died , because he was trampled upon at the gate of the city for a multitude
And Elisha said unto the woman that saved the child , Arise , thou and all thy household , and dwell in the place where thou canst dwell : for the LORD hath smitten the famine in the land seven years
And the woman arose , and went to the land of Philistine with all her household , according to the word of God , and lived there seven years .
And it came to pass , when the seven years had ended , that the woman returned from the land of Assyria , and went out to mourn the king for her house and for her field .
Then said the king to Kihasi the servant of the gods , &quot; Please tell me all the things that Elisha has done
And Gehazi told the king how he had brought the dead to life : and the woman , whom Elisha had saved his son , came to the king to mourn for her house , and for her field ; and Gehazi said , My lord , my king , this is the woman , and this is his son , and this is the woman that Elisha had saved
Then the king asked the woman , and she brought the matter to the king ; and the king sent for him a magistrate , saying , &quot; All that belongs to the woman shall be returned to him , from the time that he left the land to this day , from the birth of his field
Then Elisha came to Damascus , and Benhadad king of Aram was sick ; and a man told the king , saying , Here is the man of God
Then the king said to Hazer , &quot; Take your presents to the man of God , and ask him of the Lord , whether my disease is good or bad
And Hazael came to Elisha with forty camels , and with all the good things of the horses , and stood before him , and said , Benhadad thy son king of Aram , send me to meet thee ; and he said , Is my disease well , or is it not well
Then Elisha said to Hazer , &quot; Go back and testify to him , saying , &apos; This disease will be cured ; but the Lord has instructed me that he should die
And the man of God looked at Hazer , and was so ashamed of him that he cried
He said , &quot; Why does my Lord weep ? &quot; He answered , &quot; Because I know that you will torment the children of Israel , and burn their shields with fire , and slay their spears with the sword , and slay their infants , and cut off their pregnant women
And he said , What is thy servant but a dog , that he may do this great thing ? And Elisha answered , The LORD hath commanded me , Thou shalt be king over Aram
Then Hazer departed from Elisha , and returned to his master . The master asked him , &quot; What did Elisha say to you ? &quot; He answered , &quot; He told me that you would be well
The next day Hezekiah was buried , and was immersed in the water , and covered the king &apos;s face ; and the king died ; and Hezekiah took his throne
In the fifth year of Jehoram the son of Ahab king of Israel , when Jehoshaphat king of Judah was yet in power , Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah reigned in his stead
And Joram was thirty-two years old when he ascended , and reigned eight years in Jerusalem .
And he did that which the kings of Israel did , as the house of Ahab did : for he took the daughter of Ahab as wife , and did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD
&quot; But the Lord will not destroy Judah for the sake of His servant David , and will give him and his sons eternal light , as He promised him
In the days of Joram , the Edomites rebelled against Judah , and became kings of their own accord .
And Joram took all the chariots , and went to Zaim ; and he rose up at night , and struck the Edomites and the captains of the chariots that were besieged him ; and the Jews fled , and went every man to his own house .
Thus the children of Edom rebelled against Judah , and departed from his authority , even to this day ; and the children of Reuben also rebelled .
The rest of the acts of Joram , and all that he did , were written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah .
And Joram slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David , in the sepulchre of his fathers : and Ahaziah his son reigned in his stead
the twelve years of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel , the son of Ahaziah king of Judah ,
He was twenty-two years old when he ascended , and reigned one year in Jerusalem . His mother &apos;s name was Ahaziah , the daughter of Amri king of Israel
And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD , as the house of Ahab did , because he was the son of Ahab &apos;s wife
And he fought with Joram the son of Ahab , and with Latham of Gilead , king of Aram : and the children of Aram wounded Joram .
And the king of Jordan returned to Jerusalem , and healed himself of the wounds which he had suffered in the battle between Latham and Hazer the king of Jordan : and Ahaziah the son of Jordan king of Judah went down to see him because of the sickness of Jordan the son of Ahab .
Then Elisha called a prophet &apos;s disciple , and said to him , &quot; Take this bottle of oil , and put it on your loins , and go to Latham in Gilead
And they came there to seek Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat , the son of Nineveh , the son of Nineveh ; and he rose up from among his brethren , and brought him into the house of the guard .
Then he poured the oil of the bottle upon his head , and said , Thus saith the Lord ; I will anoint thee king of Israel ; and when it is finished , open the door and flee , and do not delay
Then the young man went to Latham of Gilead , the prophet
And when he was there , he saw all the captains of the host sitting , and said , &quot; General , I have a word for you . &quot; And Jehu said , &quot; Are you going to speak to one of us ? &quot; And he answered , &quot; General , I am going to speak to you
And Jehu arose , and went into the house , and the young man poured oil upon his head , and said to him , Thus saith the Lord God of Israel , I have anointed thee king over the people of the Lord , Israel
&quot; You shall slay the house of your master Ahasuerus , and I will stretch out the blood of my servants and of the prophets and of all the servants of the Lord on Jezebel
And all the house of Ahab shall perish ; and I will cut off from Israel all the males of Ahab , whether they be captives or free
And the house of Ahab was like the house of Jeroboam the son of Ner , and like the house of Bath-sheba the son of Ahijah .
&quot; You shall not be eaten by dogs in the field of Jezreel , nor be buried by any man ; and when it was finished , the young man opened the door and fled .
Then came Jehu and returned to his master &apos;s servants . One of them asked him , &quot; Peace ? What is the matter with you that this mad man comes to see you ? &quot; He answered , &quot; You recognize him and know what he is saying .
And they said , This is falsehood , which thou hast told us in truth . And he answered , Thus saith he unto me , Thus saith the Lord , I anointed thee king over Israel
So they hurried , and put their clothes on the upper steps , and Jehu sat on them ; and they blew a trumpet , saying , &quot; Jehu is king .
Thus Jehu the son of Nershish , the son of Jehoshaphat , betrayed Joram , and Joram , and all Israel , because of Hazer king of Aram , kept Lamoth of Gilead
Then the king of Jordan returned to Jerusalem , and healed him of the wounds that he had suffered in the battle with Hazer king of Aram ; and Jehu said , &quot; If it is your will , let no man flee from the city to report to Jerusalem
And Jehu took his chariot , and went to Jezreel , because Joram was sick there : and Ahaziah king of Judah went down and looked on him .
And there stood a watchman in the house of Israel , and when he saw that Jehu had come with a multitude , he said , I have seen a multitude . And he said , Send a horseman to meet them , and say , Peace is not peace .
Then the riders came and greeted Jehu , and said , &quot; The king said , &apos; Peace is not peace . &apos; He said , &apos; Peace is not peace . &apos; What is the matter with you ? Turn behind me . &apos; And the watchmen said , &apos; The messenger has come to them , but he has not come back
And the king sent another horseman , and he came to them , and said , The king said , Peace is not peace ; and Jehu said , Peace is not peace ; what is the matter with thee ? turn thou after me
Then said the watchman , &quot; He has come to them and will not come back . The cars have driven like the drive of Jehu the son of Nineveh .
And Joram the king of Israel and Ahaziah the king of Judah went out in their own cars to meet Jehu in the field of Naab the Jezreelite , and they met him
And when Joram saw Jehu , he said , &quot; Peace , O Jehu ? &quot; And Jehu said , &quot; Why is it that your mother washed away so many evil deeds ?
Then Joram turned and fled , and said to Ahaziah , Ahaziah , he turned away .
And Jehu filled the bow , and shot at Joram &apos;s back , and the arrows came out of his heart &apos;s chamber , and Joram fell on the cart
And Jehu said to his captain , Behold , thou hast cast him into the land of Nabal the Jew , and thou hast remembered the prophecy of the LORD concerning Ahab his father , when thou and I were with him in the carriage
&quot; I saw the blood of Naboth yesterday , and the blood of all his children , and I will recompense you in the field , &quot; said the Lord ; &quot; and now , according to the word of the Lord , cast him into the field
And when Ahaziah king of Judah saw the vision , he fled from the way of the garden ; and Jehu pursued him , and said , Slay him also in the chariot ; and he came near the hill of Ephraim , and struck him ; and he fled to Midian , and died there
And his servants brought his body in a car to Jerusalem , and buried it in the city of David , in his own tomb , with his ancestors
The eleventh year of Jehoram the son of Ahab was Ahaziah king of Judah .
&quot; When Jehu came to Jezreel , and Jezebel did not listen , he wiped the powder , and combed his head , and looked out of the window
&quot; When Jehu entered the door , &quot; Do not say , &apos; Peace be upon the heart of the man who kills his master ,
And Jehu lifted up his head , and looked at the window , and said , Who is he that obeyeth me ? And there were two or three overseers looking out the window at him
Then Jehu said , &quot; Throw him down , &quot; and they threw him down ; and his blood splashed on the wall , and immediately , and they trampled him .
And Jehu went in , and ate and drank , and said , &quot; You have buried this cursed woman , because she is the daughter of the king
And they went to bury him , and found only his head , and his feet , and his hands .
Then they returned and told Jehu , saying , &quot; This is what the Lord has spoken by his servant Elijah the Tisbite , saying , &apos; In the fields of Jezreel , the dogs will eat the flesh of the Lord &apos;s washing
&quot; The dead bodies of Jezebel will be as dung in the midst of the land of Israel , and no man will say , &apos; This is Jezebel
And there were seventy sons of Ahab in Samaria ; and Jehu wrote to them , and sent them to Samaria , and told the princes of Jezreel , the elders , and the fathers of the children of Ahab , saying ,
&quot; Behold , among you are the children of your masters , and chariots , and instruments , and a strong city .
&quot; When you have received this letter , you may choose among the children of your master a righteous man who will sit in the place of his father , and you may fight for your master &apos;s house .
But they were afraid , and said to one another , &quot; How can we stand when the two kings are still standing before him ?
Then the fathers , the fathers , and the elders , and the fathers &apos; fathers , and the fathers &apos; fathers , sent messengers to Yahweh , saying , &quot; We are your servants , and you will do all that you have commanded us ; we do not appoint any king ; how well you see , how well you do
Then Jehu wrote to them , saying , &quot; If you will obey me and listen to my voice , then tomorrow at this time you will bring to me the heads of your masters &apos; sons to Jerusalem ; and there lived seventy of the king &apos;s sons among the nobles who raised them in the city .
And when it came to pass , they killed the seventy sons of the king , and put the firstborn in a basket , and brought them to the house of Jezreel
Then there came an angel to tell Jehu , saying , &quot; They have sent the heads of the king &apos;s sons , &quot; and he said , &quot; Set the heads of the king &apos;s sons in two piles at the gate of the city until tomorrow
And it came to pass the next morning , that Jehu stood up and said unto the people , Ye are all righteous : I have betrayed my master , and have slew him ; and who is it that slew them ?
&quot; Therefore the word of the LORD concerning the house of Ahab has not vanished ; for the word of the LORD has been fulfilled through Elijah his servant
And all the remnant of the house of Ahab that remained in Jezreel , and all his ministers , and his friends , and his priests , Jehu killed , and there remained none .
And Jehu arose , and went to Samaria ; and on the way the shepherd cut off the sheep &apos;s wool
&quot; When he met the brothers of Ahaziah king of Judah , he said to them , &quot; Who are you ? &quot; They said , &quot; We are the brothers of Ahaziah . Now go down and ask the king and the daughters of the queen
And he said , Take them alive ; and those who obeyed them took them alive , and slew them by the edge of the pit where the sheep were cut : and there were forty-two men , and none remained .
And Jehu went up from there , and came to meet Jonathan the son of Rechab ; and Jehu asked him , &quot; Are you kind to me , as I am kind to you ? &quot; And Jonathan answered , &quot; Yes . &quot; And he said , &quot; If it were so , you would stretch out your hand to me , &quot; and he stretched it out , and Jehu took him to the chariot
And Jehu said , Go with me , and see how I am enthusiastic for the Lord . And he asked him to sit in the car
And when he was come to Samaria , he slew all the remnant of the house of Samaria , even to the end , as the Lord said to Elijah
Then Jehu gathered the people together , and said to them , &quot; Ahab &apos;s service to Balak was cold , but Jehu was more enthusiastic
&quot; Behold , I am present to offer a great sacrifice to Baal ; and let all the prophets of Baal , and all the people who worship Baal , and all the priests of Baal , come to me without one ; and whoever does not come shall not live ; for this is a deceit to destroy the people who worship Baal .
And Jehu said , A solemn assembly shall be proclaimed for Balak ; and he proclaimed
And Jehu sent throughout all the land of Israel ; and all the worshippers of Balak were gathered together , and none came not : and they entered into the temple of Balak ; and the temple of Balak was full of people , from the first to the second
And Jehu commanded the man who was over the garments , saying , Bring out the garments , and put them on all the men of Baal ; and he brought out the garments , and gave them to them
Then Jonah the son of Jehu and Rekah entered into the temple of Baal , and said to the people who worshipped Baal , &quot; Look , look , there is no servant of the Lord among you , but only the people who worship Baal .
And Jehu and Jonathan went in , and offered peace offerings and burnt offerings ; and Jehu set forth eighty men outside the temple , and commanded them , saying , &quot; I will deliver these men into your hands ; and if any man escapes , he who escapes will be requited .
And when Jehu had finished the burnt offering , he came out and commanded the guard and the captains of the host , saying , Come in , and slay them ; and let no man come out : and they slew them with the sword , and cast them out , and went into the city of the temple of Balak .
And he took out the pillars of the Temple of Baal , and burned them .
destroyed the pillar of Baal , destroyed the temple of Baal , as a toilet , to this day
Thus Jehu destroyed Balak in Israel
&quot; But Jehu did not leave Jeroboam the son of Nethan , for the sin which he committed against the children of Israel , which was the golden calf of Bethlehem and Dan
&quot; The Lord said to Jehu , &apos; Because you have done righteousness in my sight , and have treated the house of Ahab according to my heart , your sons will continue to sit in the throne of Israel for four generations
&quot; But Jehu did not keep the law of the Lord , the God of Israel , and did not depart from Jeroboam for the sins which he committed against Israel
In those days the Lord broke up the land of Israel , and Hazer attacked the borders of Israel
This is the whole land of Gilead , east of the Jordan , from Aroer near the valley of Arnon , the land of Gad of Gilead and Bashan , the land of the Reubenites and the Manassehs .
The rest of the acts of Jehu , and all that he did , and his might , were written in the book of the kings of Israel
And Jehu slept with his fathers , and was buried in Samaria ; and Jehoash his son reigned in his stead
And Jehu reigned twenty-eight years in Samaria king of Israel
