Joash and his mother hid themselves in the house of the Lord six years : and Artaiah took the throne .
And it came to pass in the seventh year , that Jehoiada sent forth the elders of the Chaldeans and the captains of the guard , and brought them into the house of the LORD , and made a covenant with them , that they might swear in the house of the LORD , and showed them the king &apos;s son
And he commanded them , saying , &quot; You shall do this : One third of all the people who go into the sabbath class shall watch over the king &apos;s house
A third part shall be at the gate of Shur , and a third part at the rear of the house of the guard , to keep the king &apos;s house , and to keep the wicked .
&quot; Two-thirds of all you who go out on the Sabbath day shall guard the king in the house of the Lord
Every man shall take his armor , and guard the king four times ; and whoever enters into your ranks shall die ; and when the king comes in , you shall follow him .
And all the captains of hundreds went according to all that the priest Jehoiada had commanded them : and they came to the priest Jehoiada , every man in his division , who was over the Sabbath day .
And the priest gave to the captains of hundreds the guns and the shields which David had hidden in the house of the Lord
And they took every man his weapon in his hand , from the altar and from the house straight to the house to the left , and stood round about the prince .
Then the priest brought out the prince , and put on his crown , and gave him the book of the law , and anointed him king ; and all the people clapped their hands , and said , &quot; May the king live forever
And when Athaliah heard the voice of the guard and of the people , he came to the people , and entered into the house of the Lord
And it came to pass , as the king stood by the pillars , that the captains of hundreds and the trumpeters were standing beside the king , and the people of the land shouted with joy : and he rent his clothes , and cried out , saying , Again , Again ,
And the priest Jehoiada commanded the captains of hundreds of the army to drive him out of the camp , and to kill him with the sword , because he said unto the priest , Thou shalt not kill him in the house of the Lord
And the multitude fled , and let him go ; and he went from the king &apos;s house by the way , and there he was slain
The king and the people made a covenant with the Lord , as the people of the Lord , and the king made a covenant with the people
