&quot; You shall repair all the ruins of the house , as you have received from a man whom you know .
And it came to pass in the thirty-three years of king Jehoash , that the priests had not repaired the ruins of the temple
So king Jehoash called the high priest Jehiediah and all the priests , and said to them , &quot; How can you not repair the ruins of the house ? From now on you will not take any more silver from anyone you know , nor will you return what you have received , to repair the ruins of the house
&quot; The priests shall no longer take the silver of the people , nor repair the ruins of the temple
And Jehoiada the priest took a cupboard , and made a hole in the lid of the cupboard , and put it by the altar , on the right side of the house of the LORD ; and all the silver that was offered to the house of the LORD was put into the cupboard by the priest who guarded the gate .
And when they saw that the silver in the ark was exceeding , they called the king &apos;s scribe and the high priest , and took up the sum of the silver in the house of the Lord
&quot; The men who handed over the silver to the stewards , the men who did the work in the house of the Lord , handed it over to the carpenters and workers who repaired the house of the Lord .
and the carpenters , and the stonemasons , and the buyers of wood and of stones , and the repairers of the destruction of the house of the LORD , and of all the repairers of the house of the LORD ;
&quot; But the silver that is given to the house of the Lord shall not be used for silver cups , for waxenware , for bowls , for musical instruments , or for any other silver and gold vessels in the house of the Lord
&quot; He will give it to the man who will repair the house of the Lord .
and give the money to those who do the work , and give it to those who do the work , and do not reckon with them , for they do it honestly .
