And Jehoash king of Israel came down to see Elisha , and lay down on his face , and wept , and said , My father , my father , the horsemen of Israel
And Elisha said unto him , Take the bow ; and the king took the bow
Then he said to the king of Israel , &quot; Take the bow with your hand , and the king will take the bow with his hand . And Elisha laid his hand on the king &apos;s hand
&quot; You open the window to the east , &quot; said Elisha , &quot; and he opens it . &quot; He said , &quot; Shoot , and he will shoot . &quot; He said , &quot; This is the arrow of the Lord , the arrow of victory over the children of Aram ; for you will strike the children of Aram in Afar , and you will destroy them
Then said Elisha , Take some arrows , and he took them ; and he said , Smite the ground ; and he struck three times , and was still .
Then the man of God was angry with him , and said , &quot; You should have struck them fifty-six times , and you would have struck the children of Aram , and they would have been destroyed ; and now you can only defeat them three times .
And Elisha died , and they buried him : and the New Year came , and there was a band of Moabites in prison
And when a man was buried , he saw a multitude , and cast them into the tomb of Elisha ; and as soon as he touched the bone of Elisha , he was raised again .
