&quot; This is because of the sins of the children of Israel , which led them out of the land of Egypt , and out of the Lord their God , the King of Egypt , the old law , to fear other gods
according to the custom of the Lord , who has driven out the Gentiles before them , and according to the statutes of the kings of Israel
&quot; The children of Israel have done wickedly in secret , and have rebelled against the Lord their God , in all their cities , from the tower to the strong city , and have built high places
On the high hills , under the green trees , statues and puppets ;
They burned incense in the high places , and did evil deeds , as the Lord had done to the foreigners whom he had driven out before them , and provoked the anger of the Lord
&quot; The Lord warns them against idolatry .
&quot; But the Lord , through the prophets , first and foremost , has warned the children of Israel and the children of Judah , saying , &apos; Be obedient to the law of my commandments , and to the law which I have commanded your fathers , and to the law which I have sent down to you through the prophets of my servants
&quot; But they have not obeyed , and they have put their necks on their necks , and they have obeyed their fathers , and they have not believed in the Lord their God
&quot; If they despise his statutes , and the covenant that he made with their fathers , and persuade their words , and follow the gods of nothing , and deceive themselves , and act like strangers around them , it is because the Lord has commanded them not to act ;
He has forsaken all the commandments of the Lord their God , and cast for himself two calves , and set up Asherrah , and worshiped all the images of heaven , and served Baal .
And their sons and their daughters have been burned with fire , and they have sold themselves for evil in the sight of the Lord , and have provoked him to anger
Therefore the LORD was very angry with the children of Israel , and cast them out from before Him , and there remained only one tribe of Judah
Neither did the Jews keep the commandments of the Lord their God , and the statutes of the children of Israel
Then the LORD hated all the people of Israel , and made them suffer , and delivered them into the hand of those who had taken them , that they might be driven out of his sight
And they took the kingdom of Israel out of the house of David , and made Jeroboam the son of Nethaniah king ; and Jeroboam drew the children of Israel away from the LORD , and they were in great sin
&quot; The children of Israel will not leave for all the sins of Jeroboam
And the LORD delivered them out of his sight , as he had spoken by the prophets of his servants ; and the children of Israel were carried away from the land to Assyria , even unto this day
And the king of Assyria removed from Babylon , and from Goghur , and from Awa , and from Hama , and from Zephaniah , and settled them in the cities of Samaria in place of the children of Israel ; and they received Samaria , and dwelt therein
&quot; They did not fear the Lord when they lived there ; therefore the Lord sent the lion into the midst of them , and slew some of them
Then there was a man who complained to the king of Assyria , saying , &quot; The people of the cities of Samaria , whom you have moved , know not the law of the God of the land ; therefore the God of the land sent the lion into their midst , and slew them
Then the king of Assyria commanded , saying , &quot; Let one of the priests of the captivity return , and let him dwell there , and teach the people the statutes of the God of the land
Then came a priest from the captivity of Samaria , and lived in Bethlehem , and taught them how to fear the Lord
But every tribe made an image of God for itself in the city in which they lived , and placed it in the palace which the Samaritans had built with an altar .
The Babylonians made the likeness of Beersheba ; the ancients made the likeness of Azim ; the Hamathians made the likeness of Azim ;
And the sons of Avah made Annah , and like him ; and the sons of Shepha &apos;an burned their daughters with fire , and gave them to Admiel the God of Shepha &apos;an , and Anamiel
&quot; They feared the Lord , and from among themselves the priests of the high places offered sacrifices for them in the temple of the high places .
And they feared the Lord , and served their God ; and they migrated from which land , and followed the customs of which land
And they have walked in the customs of the days of old , and have not feared the LORD with all their heart , neither have they kept their statutes and their ordinances , nor have they obeyed the law and the commandment which the LORD commanded the seed of Jacob , whom the LORD had called Israel before
&quot; The Lord made a covenant with them , and commanded them , saying , &apos; You shall not fear any other god , nor kneel before him , nor offer sacrifices to him
&quot; But fear the Lord who brought you out of the land of Egypt with a mighty arm and a stretched out arm , and kneel before Him and offer His sacrifices
&quot; The laws , the statutes , the laws , and the commandments which He has written for you , you shall keep them for ever , and you shall not fear any other God
&quot; You shall not forget the covenant which I , the Lord , have made with you , nor shall you fear any other god .
&quot; But fear the Lord your God , who will deliver you from the hand of all your enemies
&quot; But they did not obey , but followed the customs of old
Thus these people feared the Lord , and served their idols , and so did their sons and their daughters , and so did their fathers , even to this day .
the third year of Hoshea the son of Elah king of Israel , and the third year of Hezekiah the son of Ahaz king of Judah ,
At the time of his ascension he was twenty-five years old , and reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem : and his mother &apos;s name was Abi , the daughter of Zacariah .
Hezekiah did righteousness in the sight of the Lord , according to all that David his father did
&quot; He has destroyed the high places , he has destroyed the pillars , he has cut down the statues , he has destroyed the serpent of brass that Moses had made ; for at that time the children of Israel still burned incense to the serpent of brass ; and the house of Hezekiah called the serpent of brass a piece of brass .
Hezekiah trusted in the LORD God of Israel , and there was not one of the kings of Judah before him and after him
&quot; For he trusts in the Lord , and never leaves , and keeps the commandment of the Lord which he commanded Moses
&quot; The Lord is with him ; wherever he goes , he will prosper ; he has rebelled and refused to serve the king of Assyria
And Hezekiah attacked the Philistines , and went straight to Gaza , and all the borders of Gaza , from the watchtower to the strong city .
In the fourth year of king Hezekiah , in the seventh year of Hoshea the son of Elah king of Israel , Saman Ezer king of Assyria came and besieged Samaria .
In the sixth year of Hezekiah , in the ninth year of Hoshea king of Israel , Samaria was taken
And the king of Assyria took the children of Israel captive to Assyria , and set them in Harah , and by the river Habo , which is by the river of Geth , and in the cities of the Medes
For they have not obeyed the word of the Lord their God , and have not kept his covenant , which Moses , the servant of the Lord , commanded them
In the fourteenth year of king Hezekiah , the king of Assyria came up against Sinai , and struck all the strong cities of Judah , and took them .
Then sent Hezekiah king of Judah to Lachish , and said to the king of Assyria , &quot; I have sinned ; leave me , and I will bear whatever you punish me for . &quot; So the king of Assyria punished Hezekiah king of Judah with three hundred pieces of silver and thirty pieces of gold
And Hezekiah gave him all the silver of the house of the Lord , and of the treasures of the king &apos;s house
Then Hezekiah king of Judah shattered all the gold that was on the door of the house of Yahweh , and all the gold that he had wrapped on the pillars , and gave it to the king of Assyria
And the king of Assyria sent from Lachish unto Jerusalem , with the captains of the army of Ur , Rabshakeh , and Rabshakeh , to the king of the house of Hezekiah ; and when they were come to Jerusalem , they stood by the fountain of the upper pond , in the great way of the wasteland
And it came to pass , when they had called to the king , that the house of Eliakim , the son of the house of Helah , and Sheban the scribe , and Joash the son of Asa , the scribe , came out to meet them .
Then Rabshakeh said , Go and tell the house of Hezekiah , Thus saith the king of Assyria , What is it upon which ye trust ?
You say , &quot; I do not think that there is any plan or ability to fight , and who do you rely on to betray me ? &quot;
&quot; Behold , the land of Egypt upon which you have relied is the reed rod that is crushed ; and if a man leans on it , it will pierce his hand ; and so Pharaoh the king of Egypt leaned on all his people
&quot; If you said to me , &apos; We are trusting in the Lord our God , &apos; wouldn &apos;t the house of Hezekiah have destroyed the high places and the altars of God , and said to the people of Judah and Jerusalem , &apos; Will you worship before this altar in Jerusalem ?
&quot; Behold , I have given thee two thousand horses , when thou hast given them to my lord , King Assyria ; and behold , there is a man riding on this side of thee
&quot; If not , how can you defeat the least of my lord &apos;s servants ? Why do you rely on the horsemen of Egypt ?
&quot; Isn &apos;t it the Lord &apos;s will that you come up against me to destroy the land ? &quot; And the Lord said to me , &quot; Go up and destroy the land .
Then Elijah the son of Hilkiah , and Shebanah , and Joah , said to Rabshakeh , &quot; Speak in the language of Aram , and in the language of the servants , for we know ; and do not speak in the language of Judah , nor in the language of us , to the ears of the hundreds of the people of the city .
Then Rabshakeh said , &quot; Is it nothing that my Lord has sent me to speak to you and to your Lord alone , or to those who sit in the city and eat their own dung and drink their own urine with you ?
Then Rabshakeh stood and cried with a loud voice in the language of Judah , saying , &quot; Listen to the words of the king of Assyria
&quot; You shall not be deceived by the house of Hezekiah , &quot; said the king , &quot; for he cannot deliver you out of my hand .
&quot; Do not listen to the house of Hezekiah , saying , &apos; The Lord must save us , and this city will not be given to the king of Assyria
&quot; Do not listen to the words of the house of Hezekiah ; for thus said the king of Assyria , &apos; Go out with me , and surrender to me ; and every man shall eat of his own grape tree , and of the fruit of his own fruitless tree , and of the water of his own well ;
&quot; When I bring you to a place like your own land , a land of five vineyards and new wines , a land of food and vineyards , a land of olive trees and honey , that you may live and not die , &quot; the house of Hezekiah counseled you , saying , &quot; The Lord will save us , and you will not listen to His word
&quot; Is there a God of the nations who has delivered his country out of the hand of Assyrians ?
And in it was the God of Harmaiah and Arbor ; and in it was the God of Zephaniah and Nebaiah ; and have they delivered Samaria out of my hand ?
Who , the God of these nations , has saved his own country from my hand ? Can the Lord save Jerusalem from my hand ?
And the people did not speak , nor answer a word ; for he had commanded the king , saying , &quot; You shall not answer him
Now the house of the sons of Hezekiah , the slayer of Elijah , and Shebna the scribe , and Joah the son of Asa the scribe , torn their clothes , and came to the house of Hezekiah , and told him the words of Rabshakeh .
And when the king of Hezekiah heard it , he rent his clothes and put on linen , and entered into the house of the Lord
And Elijah the governor of the house , and Shebanah the scribe , and the elders of the priests , were clothed in linen , to see Isaiah the prophet , the son of Amos
And he said unto him , Thus saith the house of Hezekiah : This day is a day of severe punishment for transgression ; as a woman shall bear a child , but shall not be able to bear .
Or the LORD thy God heareth all the words of Rabshakeh , which his master the king of Assyria hath sent unto him , to blaspheme the God of everlasting life ; and the LORD thy God heareth it , and blasphemeth it ; therefore pray thou for the remnant , and pray with a loud voice :
And the servants of king Hezekiah went to meet Isaiah
Then Isaiah said to them , &quot; Tell your master , Thus says the Lord : &apos; When you have heard the servants of king Assyria blaspheme me , do not be afraid
I will shake his heart , and he will hear the wind , and he will return to his place , and I will cause him to fall under the sword in it .
Then Rabshakeh returned , and found king Assyria fighting against Rena : for he had heard earlier that king Assyria had withdrawn from Ragi
And when the king of Assyria heard that they had spoken of Tephah king of the ancients , he said , He is come out to fight with you . And he sent messengers again to the house of Hezekiah , and commanded them , saying ,
&quot; You have said to Hezekiah king of Judah , &apos; Don &apos;t listen to the God on whom you rely to deceive you , saying , &apos; Jerusalem will not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria
&quot; You have heard that all the kings of Assyria have done to the nations : they have done to the ends of the earth . Can you save them ?
&quot; Who saved the nations that my fathers destroyed , Goshen , Haran , and Lich , and the children of Eden of Tyre , the God of these nations ?
And the king of Hama , and the king of Arbor , and the king of the city of Siphah-wan , and the king of Shenah , and the king of Ivah , were in it .
And when Hezekiah had received the letter from the messenger , and had finished it , he went up into the house of the Lord , and opened it before the Lord
And Hezekiah prayed unto the LORD , and said , Sit thou on the throne of the LORD God of Israel , Thou art the God of all the kingdoms of the earth , and hast created the heavens and the earth .
&quot; Listen , O Lord , and open your eyes , O Lord , and hear the words of Sinai , when he sent an apostle to blaspheme the God of everlasting life
Indeed , O Lord , the kings of Assyria have made the nations and the land of the nations desolate
&quot; He has cast the images of the gods of the nations into the fire ; for he is not God , but a man made of wood and stone ; therefore destroy him .
&quot; Lord , our God , behold , I ask you to deliver us from the hand of the king of Assyria , so that all the nations of the earth may know that only your Lord is God .
Then Isaiah the son of Amos sent messengers to the house of Hezekiah , saying , &quot; Thus says the Lord God of Israel , &apos; Because you have asked me to attack Sinai king of Assyria , I have heard
Thus saith the Lord concerning him ; The virgins of Zion have despised thee , they have despised thee ; and the women of Jerusalem shake their heads at thee
&quot; Who do you blaspheme ? Who do you blaspheme ? Who do you raise up your voice ? Who do you lift up your eyes to attack ?
&quot; You have insulted the Lord with your angels , saying , &apos; I have commanded many chariots to the tops of the mountains to the depths of Lebanon , and I will cut down the tall cedar trees and the beautiful pine trees thereof ; and I will go up to the heights and into the forests of the fields .
I have dug wells to drink water in foreign lands ; and I will sow all the rivers of Egypt with my feet .
&quot; What I have done in the ancient days , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; is that I have made the strong city desolate and desolate through You ? Have you not heard it ?
Therefore the inhabitants thereof are weak and ashamed , and they are as the grass of the field , and as the green herbs , and as the grass of the roof of the house , and as the wheat that is not grown and dried up
&quot; You sit down , You go out , You come in , You are angry with me , I know it
&quot; Because of your wrath on me , and because of your arrogance in my ears , I will hook your nose with hooks , and put a chewing ring in your mouth , and turn you back from your way .
O Israel , I have given you a proof : this year you shall eat of your own flesh , and next year you shall eat of your own fruit ; and in the years to come you shall sow and reap and plant vineyards and eat of their fruit
The remnant of Judah , who escaped , will still be rooted downwards , and will come upwards .
And the remnant of the people shall come forth from Jerusalem , and the escaped from mount Zion ; and the wrath of the Lord shall accomplish it .
Therefore thus says the Lord concerning the king of Assyria , &quot; He shall not come to this city , nor shoot at it , nor take a shield before it , nor build a stronghold against it
&quot; He will come from that way , and he will return from that way , and he will not come to this city , &quot; says the Lord
For my own sake , and for the sake of my servant David , I will save this city
And the angel of the Lord went out that night , and slew in the camp of Assyria eighteen thousand and five thousand ; and when a man arose early in the morning , he saw that they were all dead
Then Nebuchadnezzar king of Assyria took up his camp , and lived in Nineveh
And it came to pass on a day , when he worshipped in the temple of his God , which was in Nisloh , that his sons Admiel and Saliszar slew him with the edge of the sword , and fled into the land of Ararat ; and his son Isaac reigned in his stead .
Then the house of Hezekiah was sick to death ; and Isaiah the prophet , the son of Amos , came to meet him , and said to him , Thus saith the Lord ; Save thy life with thy house , for thou shalt die , and shalt not live
Then Hezekiah turned his face to the wall , and prayed to the Lord , saying ,
Remember , O LORD , how I have kept my whole heart before thee , and have walked in truth , and have done that which is good in thy sight : and the house of Hezekiah wept bitterly .
And Esau came out , and the word of the LORD came unto him , when he had not yet come into the inner court , saying ,
&quot; Go back and tell Hezekiah the king of my people , saying , &apos; Lord , the God of your father David , I have heard your prayers , I have seen your tears , and I will heal you , and on the third day you will come to the house of the Lord
&quot; I will increase your life by fifteen years , and I will deliver you and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria ; and I will keep it for myself and for my servant David
Then Isaiah said , &quot; When you have taken a piece of unleavened bread , and people have taken it , and put it on the wound , the king is healed
Then said Hezekiah to Isaiah , &quot; The Lord will heal me . What signs will I have when I come to the house of the Lord on the third day
Then Isaiah said , &quot; The Lord will fulfill what He has spoken . This is the sign He has given you . Do you want the shadow to go forward ten degrees or backwards ten degrees ?
Hezekiah answered , &quot; It is easy for the shadow to go forward ten degrees . I want the shadow to go back ten degrees .
And the prophet Isaiah cried unto the LORD , saying , The LORD hath made the dial of Ahaz a shadow that went forward and turned back ten degrees
And when Baladan the son of king Babylon heard that Hezekiah was sick and was healed , he sent letters and presents to him
And when the house of Hezekiah heard the word of the messenger , he showed them all the gold , and the silver , and the spices , and the precious oil , and all the armor of his treasure , and all his treasures ; and there was none in his house , nor in all his land , that the house of Hezekiah would not show them
Then the prophet Isaiah came to the king of Hezekiah , and said to him , &quot; What do these men say ? They came to see you from there , &quot; and Hezekiah said , &quot; They came from Babylon far off
Then said Isaiah , What have they seen in your house ? And the house of Hezekiah said , They have seen all that is in my house , and there is none in my treasure that I should not show them .
Then Isaiah said to the house of Hezekiah , &quot; Listen to the word of the Lord
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and all that is in your house , and all that your fathers have stored up to this day , will be taken captive to Babylon , and not left behind .
&quot; And of the children of yourselves who are born , there will be some who will be taken captive and imprisoned in the palace of Babylon .
And Hezekiah said unto Isaiah , What is good in the word of the LORD that thou hast spoken ? is it not good that in my days there should be a very peaceful and firm state ?
The rest of the acts of Hezekiah , and his might , and how he dug the wells , and dug the ditches , and drew water into the city , were written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah
Hezekiah slept with his fathers ; and Manasseh his son reigned in his stead .
Manasseh was twelve years old when he ascended to the throne ; and he reigned fifty-five years in Jerusalem . His mother &apos;s name was Cosiba
And Manasseh did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD , according to the abominations of the strangers whom the LORD had driven out before the children of Israel
rebuild the altar which Hezekiah his father destroyed , and build the altar for Baal , as an image of Asher , according to all the works of Ahasuerus king of Israel , and worship all the images of heaven ;
&quot; In the house of the Lord , wherein the Lord has spoken concerning this house , &quot; I will raise up my name in Jerusalem
He built an altar for all the images of heaven in the two courts of the house of the Lord .
And he made his son to pass through the fire , and to watch , and to do witchcraft , and to deal with demons , and to do witchcraft , and to do that which was evil in the eyes of the Lord , and to provoke him to anger
And in the temple there was a statue of Asher , whom the Lord said to David and to Solomon his son , &quot; This is Jerusalem , which I have chosen among the tribes of Israel , and this is the house , which will bear my name forever and ever
&quot; If the children of Israel will keep all that I have commanded them , and all that my servant Moses has commanded them , I will not cause them to move away from the land which I have given to their fathers
And they obeyed not ; and Manasseh led them to evil more than the nations which the LORD destroyed before the children of Israel
&quot; The Lord has spoken through His servants and through all the prophets ,
For Manasseh king of Judah did these abominable evil deeds , more than the Amorites had done before , and the idols of Judah worshipped him fell into sin
Thus saith the Lord , the God of Israel ; Behold , I will bring evil upon Jerusalem and upon Judah , and I will make the ears of all that hear not
&quot; I will take the cords of Samaria , and the cords of the house of Ahab , and I will lay them on Jerusalem , and I will cleanse it , as a man cleanses a dish and pulls it down .
&quot; I will forsake the remnant of my children , and I will give them into the hand of the enemy , and I will make them the captivity of all the enemy .
For they have done evil in my sight , and provoked me to anger , from the days of their fathers , even unto this day :
And Manasseh did that which was evil in the sight of the Lord , and put the Jews in sin ; and the blood of many innocent men was poured out , and Jerusalem was filled from one side to the other
The rest of the acts of Manasseh , and all that he did , and all his sins , were written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah
And Manasseh slept with his fathers , and he was buried in the garden of Uzzah in his own house : and his son Aram reigned in his stead .
Adam was twenty-two years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned two years in Jerusalem . His mother &apos;s name was Meshullim , the daughter of Harus the Jothibanite
And Adam did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD , as Manasseh his father did
Do all that his father has done , and worship the idols that his father worships .
Forsaking the Lord , the God of his fathers , and not obeying the way of the Lord
&quot; The servants of king Adam betrayed him and killed him in the palace
But the people killed those who betrayed the king of Aram , and made Josiah his son king in his stead
And all that Adam did was written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah
And Adam was buried in his own tomb in the garden of Uzzah ; and Josiah his son reigned in his stead .
Jehoshaphat was eight years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned thirty and one years in Jerusalem . His mother &apos;s name was Jedidah , the daughter of Ahaziah the Persian .
&quot; Joseph did righteousness in the sight of the Lord , and did not deviate from all that David his father had done
And it came to pass in the eighteenth year of king Josiah , that the king sent Shaphan the scribe , the son of Asahel the son of Mizreel the son of Mizreel , to the house of the LORD , and commanded him , saying ,
&quot; Go to the house of the high priest , to the house of the Philistines , and count the silver that they will bring into the house of the Lord , the silver that they have gathered from the people who guard the gates ;
to those who work in the house of the Lord , and to those who work in the house of the Lord , to repair the ruins thereof ;
That is , to transfer woodworkers and workers , and masons , and to buy wood and stones , and to repair the palace
Pay the money in the hands of those who do the work , and do not account with them ; for they do it honestly .
Then the chief priest said to the scribe , &quot; I have received the law in the house of the Lord , &quot; and the chief priest delivered it to Shaphan , and Shaphan saw it .
Then Shaphan the scribe came to the king and said to him , &quot; Your servants have counted the silver of the house , and have given it to the men who do the work in the house of the Lord
And Shaphan the scribe said unto the king , The house of the priest Hilk hath given me a book ; and Shaphan read it before the king
When the king heard the words of the law , he tore his clothes
And he commanded the house of the priests , and Ahigan the son of Shaphan , and Egbon the son of Micaiah , the scribe of Shaphan , and Asa the servant of the king , saying ,
&quot; Go , ask the Lord for me , for the people , for all Judah , according to the words of this book ; for the Lord is very angry with us , because our fathers did not listen to the words of this book , nor did they do what they had commanded us to do .
Then the priests , the house of Shelah , and the sons of Ahigan , and the sons of Agim , and the sons of Zaban , and the sons of Asaiah , went to the prophetess Hurrah , the wife of Shalon the ruler , the son of Terah , the son of Harhaz , who lived in the second district of Jerusalem , and they asked him
And he said unto them , Thus saith the Lord , the God of Israel , that ye may return unto the man whom ye sent unto me , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord ; I will bring evil upon this land and upon all the inhabitants thereof according to all that the king of Judah hath read in that book
For they have forsaken me , and burned incense to other gods , and provoked me to anger with what they have done with their hands ; therefore will my wrath be on this place , and will not cease .
&quot; But send yourselves to ask the king of Judah of the Lord , saying , &apos; Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel , concerning all that you have heard
&quot; Hear what I say concerning this land and the inhabitants thereof , that I will make it a wilderness , and curse the people ; and you have obeyed me in your heart , and have humbled yourself before me , and have torn your clothes , and have wept at me ; therefore I have obeyed you , &quot; says my Lord .
&quot; And I will bring you to your graves , and to your fathers , in peace ; and I will bring down all the evil that is in the land , and you will not see it with your own eyes ; and they will return to the king .
&quot; The king sent and gathered together the elders of Judah and Jerusalem
Then the king and all Judah , and the inhabitants of Jerusalem , and the priests , and the prophets , and all the people , of every sort , came together to the house of the Lord , and the king recited unto them the book of the covenant that was in the house of the Lord
And the king stood by the pillars , and made a covenant before the Lord , to obey the Lord with all his heart , and to keep his commandments , and his statutes , and his laws , and to do the words of the covenant written in this book ; and all the people obeyed the covenant
And the king commanded the house of the high priests , and the high priests , and the porters of the gates , to bring out from the house of the LORD all the vessels that were made for Baal and for Asher , and for all the animals of the sky , and to burn them in the midst of the field by the stream , which was outside Jerusalem , and to bring the ashes to Bethlehem
The priests who used to worship idols burned in the high places of the cities of Judah and around Jerusalem . Now the kings are gone , and they are gone to Baal , and to the sun , and to the moon , and to the planets , and to the twelve palaces , and to all the elephants in the heavens , who burn .
&quot; And he brought Asherrah out of the house of the Lord to Jerusalem , and burned him on the banks of the river , and broke him into ashes , and cast them into the graves of the people
&quot; The house of the children of Ammon was destroyed in the house of the Lord , the house of the women who weave the tents for Asher .
And he brought up all the priests from the cities of Judah , the high places where the unclean priests burned incense , from Capernaum even unto Beer-sheba , and destroyed the high places by the gate , which were before the gate of Uzziah Joshua to the left of the gate
But the priests of the high altar do not go up to the altar of the Lord in Jerusalem , but eat unleavened bread among their brethren
and in the valley of Hinnom , which was defiled , it was forbidden to burn the sons and the daughters therein , and to offer them to Moses
And the king of Judah went to the house by the gate of the house of the LORD , which is by the porch of Nathanael the governor , and burned the horses which he had offered to the sun , and burned the chariots of the sun
And the altar that the king of Judah had built on the top of the house of Ahaz , and the altar that Manasseh had built in the two houses of the house of the Lord , the king demolished and broke them , and cast the ashes into the streams of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the waters of the
And the high places which Solomon king of Israel had built before Jerusalem , on the right side of the mountains , were defiled for Asheroth , the god of the Sidonians , the god of the Moabites , the god of the Ammonites , and for Melchizedek ,
And he broke down the pillars , and cut down the dolls , and filled the bones of men therein .
&quot; He destroyed the altar of Bethlehem , which Jeroboam the son of Neriah , the son of Israel , had built for the sins of Israel , and burned it , and broke it into ashes , and burned Asherrah
Then Joshua turned and looked at the tomb in the mountains , and sent a messenger to take out the bones of the tomb , and burn them on the altar , and defile the altar , as the prophets of the Lord had said
Then said Josiah , What is this stone that I have seen ? And the men of the city answered and said unto him , This is the stone of his tomb , which the Gods of Judah had spoken before , saying , This is what the king hath done unto the altar of Bethlehem
Then said Josiah , Let him alone , and let not his bones be moved : for they will not move his bones , nor the bones of the prophet that came from Samaria .
The kings of Israel , who had built the high places in the cities of Samaria , provoked the wrath of the LORD , have been destroyed in Josiah , just as he did in Bethlehem
