and killed the remnant of the Amalekites who escaped , and dwelled there until this day .
&quot; The eldest son of Israel was a filthy man ; for he defiled his father &apos;s bed ; and the name of his eldest son was given to Joseph , but he was not the eldest according to the genealogy
Judah overcame all his brethren ; and the king came out of him ; and the name of the eldest son was to Joseph .
And the sons of Reuben , the eldest of Israel , were Hanoah , and Pharaoh , and Hezron , and Gami .
And the son of Joel was Shemaiah ; and the son of Shemaiah was Gog ; and the son of Gog was Shimei
And the sons of Shemei were Micah ; and the sons of Micah were Elias ; and the sons of Elias were Bali
The son of Balak was Belah , who was the leader of the tribe of Reuben , who was taken captive by the king of Assyria , Tegur-Labinish
And his brothers were Jeliah , and Zacariah , and Beera , according to their families , according to their genealogy
And Beer-sheba was the son of Asa , and Asa was the son of Shema , and Shema was the son of Jour ; and the place where Jour dwelled was from Aroer even unto Nebo and Baal-imah
And they went eastward into the wilderness by the river Beer-sheba , because their cattle were multiplied in Gilead
And they fought with the Shechemites in the years of Saul ; and the Shechemites fell under their hand , and dwelt in their tents in all the land east of Gilead .
And the sons of Gad dwelt in Bashan in the river , and passed over to Zakah .
And among them was Joel the chief , and Shaphan the second chief , and Aaron , and Shaphah of Bashan .
And their brothers were Micah , and Mizrah , and Sheba , and Jorah , and Jachin , and Sheba , and Heb , seven .
These are the sons of Abijah , the son of Huri , the son of Jeroah , the son of Keilah , the son of Micah , the son of Jesse , the son of Jehad , the son of Bus
And the sons of Goni , and Ahi the son of Abbeaz , chief of the tribe .
And they dwelt in Gilead , and in Bashan , and in the country of Bashan , and in the suburbs of Sharon , even to the border round about .
&quot; These men were entered into the genealogy in the years of Jotham king of Judah , and in the years of Jeroboam king of Israel
Of the tribe of the Reubenites , of the Gadites , and of the half tribe of Manasseh , forty-four thousand and seven hundred and sixty mighty men with shields , and with swords , and with bow , and with arrows , to fight in the battle of good .
And they fought against the Shathites , and against the Ithonites , and against the Nephites , and against the Nothites .
They received the help of God , and the Shechemites and those with them were given into their hands , because they cried to God in the battle , and they trusted in God , and God answered them .
And they took away the livestock of the Shechemites , five thousand camels , twenty-five thousand sheep , and two thousand donkeys , and a thousand men
And many of the enemies were slain , because the battle was against God ; and they dwelt in the land of the enemy until the time of their captivity
And the half tribe of Manasseh dwelled there , from Bashan even unto the Balakhites , and to Shinner , and to mount Hermon .
And the chief of their fathers were Ephraim , and Ishmael , and Elel , and Assyria , and Jeremiah , and Jehodaiah , and Japhaz ; all of them were mighty men of war , and were well-known , and were chief of their fathers .
They have sinned against the God of their fathers , and have committed wickedness with the people of the land , whom God has destroyed before them .
Therefore the God of Israel stirred up the hearts of Pharaoh king of Assyria , and of Tigris king of Assyria , and they took away the children of Reuben , and the children of Gad , and the children of the half tribe of Manasseh , and carried them away to Harah , and Habah , and Harah , and to the banks of the river Goshen , even to this day .
And the sons of Levi were Gershon , and Goshen , and Mirali .
And the sons of Kohath were Amran , and Esha , and Hebron , and Uzzah .
And the sons of Amran were Aaron , and Moses , and the daughters of Millam ; and the sons of Aaron were Nethan , and Abihu , and Eleazar , and Ishmael
