And Obed , the son of Shemaiah , the son of Harah , the father-in-law of Judah ; and Bile , the son of Asa , the son of Elihanan , who lived in the villages of the Nethites .
And the keepers of the gate were Shalon , and the valley , and Dan , and Ahimen , and their brethren ; and Shalon was chief .
&quot; They guarded the king &apos;s gate to the east , and now they guard the gates in the camp of Levi .
Pharaoh &apos;s father-in-law , Sharon the son of Kareah , the son of Abiathar , and the children of Kareah , his brothers , were over the work of the service , and over the doors of the tabernacle of the congregation ; and their ancestors were over the camp of the Lord , and over the doors of the camp
&quot; Behold , Phinehas the son of Eleazar had been over them , and the Lord was with him
And Zechariah the son of Mizlimiah was over the doors of the tabernacle of the congregation .
The number of those who were appointed to guard the gate was 212 , according to the number of their families in their villages , according to the appointments given to them by David and Samuel the prophet at this time .
&quot; They and their sons shall watch the doors of the house of the Lord in order , and they shall be the doors of the Tent of Meeting
There are gates to the east , west , south , north , and on all sides .
And their brethren dwell in the villages , and alternate with them every seven days
These four gatekeepers were Levites , each of them having a prominent office , guarding the storehouse of the temple .
They dwelled around the temple , because they had entrusted them to keep it , to open it every morning .
Of the Levites , those who handle the vessels , take them out by number , and take them in .
And there were men over the instruments , and over the vessels of the sanctuary , and over fine flour , and over wine , and over oil , and over milk , and over spices
Some of the priests used spices to make oil
The Levite , Mahathiah , was the eldest son of Sharon of the Chalaeans , and his chief duty was to steward the baked bread
And of the sons of Kohath , the brothers of their fathers , there was one who handled the bread , and prepared it on the Sabbath day
The chief of the tribe of the uncircumcised that singeth shall dwell in the houses of his household , and shall serve day and night , and shall do no other work .
These are the chiefs of the Levites , the prominent men of Israel , who dwell in Jerusalem
