And Moses begat Phineah , and Phineah begat Lephaiah , and Eleazar the son of Lephaiah , and Azer the son of Eleazar ,
And he had six sons , whose names were Ashlig , and Pochri , and Ishmael , and Sheariah , and Obediah , and Hanan : these were the sons of him .
The Philistines fought with the Israelites ; and the Israelites fled before the Philistines ; and there were slain servants on Mount Gilead .
And the Philistines pursued after Saul and his sons , and slew Jonah the son of Saul , and Abiathar , and Machishuah ,
The force was great , Saul was pursued by the archers , and he was severely wounded
And he said unto those who took his armor , Draw forth the sword , and smite me , lest the uncircumcised should offend me : but those who took his armor were very afraid , and would not smite him .
And Saul fell upon his own sword ; and the men that took the weapons saw that Saul was dead , and they fell upon his sword
So Saul and his three sons , and all his household , died together
And when all Israel that dwelt in the plain saw that the men of Israel fled , Saul and his sons died , and fled from the city , and the Philistines came to dwell there
The next day , when the Philistines came to take off the clothes of the slain , they saw Saul and his servants lying on mount Gilead .
And they stripped him of his armor , and cut off his chiefs , and sent messengers to the four corners of the land of Philistine to convey the message to their idols and to the people .
And he put Saul &apos;s armor in the temple of his gods , and nailed his firstborn in the temple of Dagon
And the men of Gilead heard all that the Philistines did unto Saul
And all the mighty men among them arose , and went forth , and brought the bodies of Saul and his sons unto Jabbar , and buried their bodies under the oak tree of Jabbar , and fasted seven days
So Saul died because he had sinned against the LORD , and had not kept the commandment of the LORD , and because he had asked the woman of the devil
&quot; Because he did not ask the Lord , the Lord killed him , and gave the kingdom to David the son of Jesse
Then all Israel gathered themselves together to Hebron to David , and said , &quot; We were your bones
&quot; It was you who led the children of Israel from the days of Saul king , and the Lord your God said to you , &apos; You shall feed my people Israel , and you shall be kings over Israel
So all the elders of Israel came to Hebron to see David king , and David made a covenant with them before the Lord of Hebron , and anointed David king of Israel , as the Lord had said by the voice of Samuel
When David and all Israel came to Jerusalem , which was Jebus , the Jebusites lived there
And the Jebusites said unto David , Thou shalt not enter into this place : but David took the shield of Zion , which is the city of David
And David said , Whosoever shall first attack the Jebusites shall be captain of the host : and Joab the son of Zeruiah went up first , and made him captain of the host
David dwells in a safe haven ; therefore it is called the city of David .
And David built the walls from Miro all around ; and the rest was repaired by Joab
For the Lord of hosts is with David on that day
&quot; The following is the record of the captains of the mighty men who went with David to help him in the land , and to make him king with the children of Israel , as the Lord commanded the children of Israel
Behold , the number of the mighty men of David is as follows : Jacob the son of Haghmon , captain of the captains of the host , shot three hundred men with a fire
And Eleazar the son of Dodo , the son of Ahidian , was one of the three mighty men
And the Philistines were gathered together to fight with David in Bashan : and there was a field full of wheat , and the people fled before the Philistines
And the mighty man stood in the field , and struck the Philistines , and saved the field ; and the LORD overcame the people of Israel
And three of the thirty men of the mighty men went down to the rock , and entered into the cave of Adullam to meet David . And the army of the Philistines encamped in the valley of Lyman .
At that time David was in the camp , and the camp of the Philistines in Bethlehem
And David was thirsty , and said , &quot; Would that a man had poured water into the well by the gate of Bethlehem for me to drink
And the three mighty men went through the camp of the Philistines , and poured water out of the well by the gate of Bethlehem , and brought it for David , but he refused to drink , and laid it before the Lord
They said , &quot; My God , these three men have taken their lives to drink water , like their blood , and I refuse to drink it ; and David refused to drink it ; and this is what the three mighty men did . &quot;
And Abishai the brother of Joab was the captain of the three mighty men ; and he slew three hundred men with the edge of his spear ; and he became known among the three mighty men .
He is the most noble of the three warriors ; therefore he is their leader ; but he is shorter than the first three warriors
And Benaiah the son of Jehiedad , a mighty warrior of the Kohathites , did a mighty thing , and slew the two sons of Eliel the Moabitess , and went down into the pit , and slew a lion in the snow
And he slew an Egyptian , and he was five cubits in height , and he had a sword in his hand , and a staff of the sword as thick as a cloth : and Benaiah took the sword out of the hand of the Egyptians , and struck him with the sword .
&quot; This is what Jehoiada the son of Neriah did ; and he received a name among the three mighty men .
He was no more precious than the thirty warriors , but less than the first three . David appointed him captain of the guard
Among the mighty men of the army was Asahel the brother of Joab , and Elhanan the son of Dodo the Bethlehemite .
Shama the Harite , and Hiles the Beerothite
And Elah the son of Michiel the Tikoite , and Abiezer the Anathonite ,
