When David was afraid of Saul the son of Kish , when he hid himself in Zechariah , there came to him warriors to help him in the battle
They were able to draw bows , and to shoot arrows with both their left and right hands . These were the brothers of Saul the Benjaminite
And the first was Ahiezer , and the second Joash , the sons of Shema the Gibeonite , and Jesheh , the son of Azmaveh , and Bly , and Belacah , and Jehu the son of Anathoth ,
Among the thirty men who ruled over them was Ishmael the Gibeonite , who was a mighty man , and Jeremiah , and Jahaz , and Johanan , and Joseph the Gideonite
Eli Uzziah , Jeremiah , Abiaiah , Shemaiah , Zephathiah the Harfite ,
the children of Korah , Elicanah , Jeziah , Azaleh , Joash , and Jashoban
and Jerah the son of Jeroboam the Gideonite , and Shebadeah the son of Zechariah ,
And of the tribe of Gad there came men into the wilderness to fight against David , mighty men with shields and swords ; and their faces were like lions , and they ran like deer in the mountains
the first , Ezer , the second , Obediah , the third , Eliab
the fourth of Mizmanah , the fifth of Jelim
The Sixth Adam , the Seventh Eli
Eighth Johar Khan , Ninth Elizaba
The tenth Jeremiah , the eleventh and the last Barnabas
These are the captains of the children of Gad : the small can be one hundred , and the great one a thousand .
In the new moon , when the waters of the Jordan were overflowing on both banks , they passed over the river , and all the inhabitants of the plain fled eastward and westward .
And Benjamin and Judah came to the camp of David
Then David went out to meet them , and said to them , &quot; If you help me in peace , my heart will be with you , and if you sell my innocent man into the hands of the enemy , let the God of our fathers see the punishment
Then the Spirit of God touched Amaziah , the leader of the thirty mighty men , and he said , &quot; O David , we belong to you , O son of Jesse , and we help you ; peace be to you , and peace be to those who help you ; for your God helps you ; and David took them and made them captains
And David went with the Philistines before to fight with Saul ; and there came men of Manasseh to pursue David , but they had no help for the Philistines : for the princes of the Philistines had made an agreement to send them back , saying , I am afraid that David will take our princes and give them over to Saul his master
And it came to pass , when David was come to Shezreel , that Abner , and Joseph , and Jephthah , and Micah , and Joseph , and Elihu , and Zeruiah , the captains of the thousands of the men of Manasseh , came to pursue him
&quot; These men helped David to attack the thieves . They were mighty warriors and captains
Then every day came men to help David , and made him a great army , as the army of God .
&quot; The soldiers who were ready to fight came to Hebron to meet David , and according to the word of the Lord gave David the kingdom of Saul , and the number of them was as follows :
Of the children of Judah six thousand and eight hundred men prepared for war with shields and with swords .
Of the tribe of Simeon there were seven thousand and one hundred men , mighty men of valour .
The Levites had 4,600 .
Jehoiada was the head of the house of Aaron , and three thousand seven hundred men were with him
And there was a young man , a mighty warrior , named Zechariah : and with him were twenty-two chiefs of the people .
And of the tribe of Benjamin , the brethren of Saul , three thousand ; most of them were of the house of Saul .
Of the tribe of Ephraim , mighty men of valour , there were twenty and eight hundred men of honour among our people .
And the half tribe of Manasseh , and the names of them that were in the book , were eleven thousand and eight thousand : and they came to make David king
And of the tribe of Issachar were two hundred elders , who were appointed over the affairs of the land , and knew what the children of Israel were doing ; and their brethren obeyed their commandments .
There were fifty thousand men of the tribe of Zebulun able to stand up , to fight with all kinds of weapons , to join forces , and not to be scattered
And of the tribe of Naphtali , a thousand captains , and threescore and seven thousand men with their shields and their spears .
But there were twenty-eight thousand and six hundred that could stand .
Of the tribe of Asheah , 40,000 were able to fight .
Of the tribe of the River Ben , of the tribe of Gad , of the tribe of Manasseh , and of the half tribe of the east Jordan , twelve thousand fought with all kinds of armor
&quot; These are the soldiers who are able to defend themselves . They have come to Hebron with all their heart to make David king over Israel , and all the rest of Israel with all their heart to make David king over Israel
They ate and drank there with David for three days , because their brethren had prepared for them
And the men that were near to them , and the children of Issachar , and the children of Zebulun , and the children of Naphtali , brought bread offerings , and cakes without fruit , and dried grapes , and wine , and oil , with donkeys , and camels , and oxen , and cattle , and brought many cattle and sheep ; for the children of Israel rejoiced exceedingly
David consulted with the chief captains of thousands and hundreds , and with all the princes
And David said unto all the congregation of Israel , If ye will be beautiful , and see that it is from the LORD our God , then we will send men throughout the land of Israel to see our future brethren , and to see the Levites , the priests who dwell in the suburbs , and to gather them together
&quot; We will bring the ark of God to us ; for in the days of Saul we did not ask God before the ark .
And all the congregation said , This is so ; and it was well in the eyes of all the people
And David gathered the children of Israel together from the Jordan of Egypt even unto the mouth of Hamath , to bring the ark of God from Gilead
And David went up with all Israel unto Barah , which is Gilead of Judah , to bring forth the ark of the covenant , which is the name of the Lord God , sitting on the two reins .
And they brought forth the ark of God out of the house of Abi-Nadab , and laid it in a new cart : and Uzzah and Ahijah drove away .
David and all Israel danced and sang before God with harps , psalteries , harps , trumpets , and with mighty dances
And it came to pass , when he was come to the field of wheat in Gideon , that he lifted up his hand against the ark , because he had lost his forefoot for the cattle ;
And the LORD was angry with him , because he stretched out his hand against the ark and struck him , and he died before God
And David was troubled because of the LORD &apos;s smite of Uzzah , and called the place Blessed Uzzah to this day
David feared God that day , and said , &quot; How can the ark of God be brought to me
And David brought not the ark into the city of David , but into the house of Obedeem the Gadites
The ark of God was in the house of Edom three months : and the LORD blessed the house of Edom and all that were with him
Then Hilan king of Tyre brought the acacia trees to David , and sent messengers and stonemasons and carpenters to build him the house
And David knew that the LORD had established him king over Israel , and for his people Israel , that his kingdom might prosper
and David became his wife in Jerusalem , and bore children
The sons of Jerusalem : Shemaiah , Sheothaim , Nathan , Solomon
Ephraim , Elisha , Ephraim
Noah , Nephiah , Japhiah
Elishama , Beeri Jadah , Eliphael ,
And when the Philistines heard that David was anointed king over all Israel , they went up to seek David , and when David heard it , he went out to fight against the enemy
And the Philistines came , and spread themselves out in the valley of Lymeon
Then David asked God , saying , &quot; Can I go up and fight against the Philistines , and you will deliver them into my hand ? &quot; The Lord said , &quot; You can go up , and I will deliver them into your hand
Then the Philistines came to the heart of Babylon , and David slew them there : and David said , God has struck the enemy with my hand , as the waters struck the enemy ; therefore the name of the place is called the heart of Babylon
The Philistines left the image of God in it . David commanded the people to burn it with fire
The Philistines spread out again in the valley of Lymeon
Then David asked God again , and God said , &quot; Do not go up straight , but turn to their backs , and attack them from the side of Sanin
And when thou hearest the voice of the footsteps on the top of the palm tree , then shalt thou fight : for God hath come before thee to smite the army of the Philistines
And David did as God had commanded him , and struck the army of the Philistines from Gibeon even unto Gibeon
Then the name of David was proclaimed among the nations , and the Lord made the nations afraid of him
And David built for himself the house in the city of David , and prepared a place for the ark of God , and a tent for the tent
Then David said , &quot; No one can lift up the ark of God except the Levites , for the Lord has chosen them to lift up the ark of God , and to serve him for ever and ever
David gathered all Israel together to Jerusalem , to bring up the ark of the Lord to the place which he had prepared
And David gathered together the sons of Aaron and the Levites
And of the sons of Kohath were Uzel the chief , and his brethren an hundred and twenty .
Among the sons of Merari were the chief of the tribe , Ahaziah , and his brothers two hundred twenty .
And of the sons of Gershon , Joel the chief , and his brethren an hundred and thirty
Of the sons of Eleazar , Shemaiah the chief , and two hundred of his brethren ,
And of the sons of Hebron were Eliel the chief , and eighty of his brethren .
Among the sons of Uzziah were Amminadab the chief of the tribe , and eleven and twelve of his brethren .
David called Zadok the priest , and Abiathar , and Uriel the Levite , and Azariah , and Joel , and Shemaiah , and Eli , and Amminadab
And he said unto them , Ye are the chief of the Levites , and ye and your brethren shall be clean , that ye may bring up the ark of the LORD God of Israel unto the place which I have prepared
&quot; Because you have not lifted up the ark before , and have asked the Lord our God by statute , he has punished us
Then the priests of the Levites cleansed themselves , and brought up the ark of the LORD God of Israel
And the sons of Levi lifted up the ark of God with bars on their shoulders , as the Lord commanded by Moses
And David commanded the elders of the Levites to send their singing brothers , and to sing with harps and psalteries , and to sing with joy
And the Levites sent Haman the son of Joel , and Asa the son of the Philistines among his brethren , and Ephthon the son of Rechaziah the son of Mirali the son of their brethren ,
And after them were their brothers Zechariah , Ben , and Jasheel , and Shemiramoth , and Jesheh , and Uni , and Eliab , and Benaiah , and Maaseiah , and Mattathiah , and Eliphihu , and Micahiah , and Ebed-edom , and Jeli , the gatekeepers
Thus did Heman , Asa , and Edom , who were singing , sound with a loud voice ,
and Zechariah , and Jasheel , and Shemiramoth , and Jesheh , and Uni , and Eliab , and Maaseiah , and Benaiah , and Kosor , and the sons of the daughters of Israel ,
And of the sons of Mattathiah , and of the sons of Eliphihu , and of the sons of Jakneiah , and of the sons of Obed-edom , and of the sons of Jeli , and of the sons of Azariah , captains of the harps ,
And the chief of the Levites , Kenaiah , was the chief of the singers , and taught the singers , because he was wise in the matter
And the house of Believed , Elihanan , was the porter of the door of the ark of the covenant
And the priests of Sheban , and of Jehoshaphat , and of Nathaniel , and of Amaziah , and of Zechariah , and of Benaiah , and of Eliezer , blew before the ark of God ; and Edom and Jehijah were porters before the ark
So David and the elders of Israel , and the captains of thousands , went up from the house of Edom , and brought up the ark of the LORD with joy
&quot; Then the Levites , who were given by God and carried up the ark of the Lord , offered seven bulls and seven rams
David and the Levites who carried the ark of the covenant , and the captain of the singers , Kenaiah , and the singers , were clothed in fine linen , and Ephrod in fine linen .
Then all Israel lifted up the ark of the Lord with a loud voice , and with a trumpet , and with a psaltery , and with a psaltery , and with a loud voice ,
When the ark of the LORD came into the city of David , Micah the daughter of Saul looked out of the window and saw the king dancing and dancing , and looked down on him in her heart
And they brought in the ark of God , and laid it in the tent which David had set up , and offered burnt offerings before God , peace offerings
And when David had finished the burnt offering and the sacrifice of peace , he blessed the people in the name of the Lord
And he gave unto the children of Israel , both men and women , a cake , and a meat cake , and a grape cake
David sent a number of the Levites before the ark of the LORD to praise , to give thanks , and to praise the God of the LORD , Israel
The first was Asa , and the second Zechariah , and Jasheel , and Shemiramoth , and Jesheh , and Mahathiah , and Eliab , and Benaiah , and Edom , and Jeli , and Bethel , playing the harp ; but Asa sounded with a loud trumpet ,
The priests Benaiah and Jahaziel used to blow before the ark of God
On that day David , through Asa and his brothers for the first time , praised the Lord in songs , saying ,
&quot; You shall give thanks to the Lord , and call on His name , and proclaim His works among the people
to sing to him , to praise him , to talk about all his wonderful works
Let them exalt themselves in His holy name , and let them rejoice in the hearts of those who seek the Lord
to seek the Lord and His power , and to seek often His face
&quot; Remember , O sons of Israel , his servant , and the sons of Jacob whom he has chosen , his wonderful works , and his wonders , and his words in his mouth ,
See Up
He is the Lord our God , and His judgment is in all the earth .
Remember His covenant for ever , and His commandments for millennia .
&quot; This is the covenant which Abraham made with Isaac , and the oath which he swore to Isaac
And he made this covenant a law unto Jacob , and an everlasting covenant unto Israel
&quot; I will give you the land of Canaan as your inheritance ,
At that time your people were limited , few in number , and settled there
They travel from this country to that country , and from that country to that country
&quot; The Lord will not allow anyone to deceive them , and will punish the king for their sakes
He said , &quot; No one who is anointed for me will be harmed , nor one who is evil toward my prophet .
Sing unto the LORD in all the land , and proclaim his salvation daily
He shall declare His glory among the nations , and His wonders among the people .
For the LORD is great , when he is praised exceedingly , and when he is feared above all gods
All the gods of the nations are void : only the Lord created the heavens .
There is glory and majesty before Him , and power and joy in His sanctuary
&quot; You , all the tribes of the people , will give to the Lord the power of glory ;
&quot; You shall give him the glory of the name of the Lord , and bring offerings before him , and worship the Lord in holy garments .
The whole earth will shake before Him , and the world will not shake .
May the heavens rejoice , and may the earth rejoice , and may the people of the nations say , The Lord is king
May the sea and all that is therein flourish , and may the field and all that is therein rejoice .
Then the trees of the forest shall rejoice before the LORD ; for he is come to judge the whole earth
Blessed be the Lord , for He is good , and His mercy endures for ever .
&quot; Save us , O God of our salvation , and gather us together , that we may go out of the land of the nations ; that we may glorify Your holy name , that we may exalt Your praise
Blessed is the Lord , the God of Israel , from everlasting to everlasting : and all the people said , Amen , and praise the Lord
And David sent Asa and his brethren , and served the Lord continually before the ark of the covenant , one day to the end of the day
And he sent Obed-edom , and his brethren , sixty-eight men , with Obed-edom the son of Jeduthun , and Hoshea the porter
And they shall send the priest Zadok and all the priests of his brethren to offer burnt offerings to the LORD in the high altar of Gibeon , before the ark of the LORD , on the altar of burnt offering , day and night , as the LORD commanded the children of Israel in the book of the law
See Up
&quot; And those who were sent with them , Heman , and Jeduthun , and the rest of the chosen ones , who were recorded in the book , thank the Lord , for His mercy endures for ever and ever .
And Heman and Jethrodon with them blew with the trumpets , and with the trumpets , and with a loud voice , and with other instruments to sing praises unto God ; and the sons of Jethrodon were porters
Then the people returned to their families , and David returned to bless their families
David lived in his own house , and said to Nathan the prophet , &quot; Behold , I live in the house of acacia trees , and the ark of the Lord is against the veil
Then Nathan said to David , &quot; You can do according to your heart , for God is with you
And it came to pass in the night , that the word of God came to Nathan , saying ,
&quot; Go and tell my servant David , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; You shall not build a house for me to dwell in
&quot; I have not lived in the house from the time I brought the children of Israel out of Egypt to this day , but from the tent to the tent , from the tent to the tent
&quot; Wherever I went with the children of Israel , I said to an Israelite warrior , to the shepherd of my people , &apos; Why don &apos;t you build me a palace of acacia trees ?
&quot; Now tell my servant David , &apos; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; I have called you out of the flock , that you may no longer be with the flock , and that you may be king over my people Israel
Wherever you go , I will always be with you ; I will cut off all your enemies , and I will make you a great name , as a great man in the world .
And I will choose a place for my people Israel , and I will cultivate them , and I will make them dwell in their own place , and they shall not move ; and the sons of the wicked shall not disturb them as before .
&quot; Behold , I will rule over all your enemies , and I will set up houses for you , as my Lord has promised you
&quot; When your days are fulfilled with your ancestors , I will make your descendants succeed you , and I will establish his kingdom .
He will build houses for me , and I will establish his throne for ever and ever .
I will be his father , and he will be my son ; and my loving kindness will not leave him , as Saul did before you .
&quot; But I will establish him forever in my house and in my land , and his throne will be firm forever .
&quot; Take the book and follow all these words , and tell David according to the commandment
Then king David went in and sat before the Lord , and said , &quot; Who am I , O Lord God , and what is my house , that you have brought me to this place
&quot; This is small in your eyes , O God , and you promise the house of your servants for a long time . You look at me , O Lord God , as at a noble man .
&quot; But I have more to say to you than the glory of your servants , for you know your servants .
&quot; You have done this great thing , O Lord , and made it manifest , for the sake of your servants , and according to your heart .
&quot; O Lord , as we have heard in our ears , there is no one like You , and there is no God except You
&quot; There is no nation in the world like your people Israel . Your God redeemed them from Egypt as his own children , and did great and terrible things before the people whom you redeemed , and expelled the nations , and made known your great name .
&quot; You have made Israel your people for ever and ever , and you , Yahweh , are their God
&quot; Be steadfast , O Lord , in the words that You have promised to your servants and to their families forever , and do as You have said .
&quot; Let your name stand forever , and be glorified , saying , &apos; The Lord of hosts is the God of Israel , the God who governs Israel ; and the house of your servant David will stand before you
&quot; For you , my God , have inspired your servants , saying , &apos; I will build a house for you , &apos; so they boldly pray before you
&quot; But you , O Lord , are God , and you shall give this blessing to your servants
Blessed are you , O Lord , and blessed are you forever in the house of your servants , in which you rejoice .
Then David struck the Philistines , and subdued them , and took Gath and the villages thereof out of their hand
Then they attacked Moab , and the Moabites surrendered to David , and gave him a ransom
And Hadadezer king of Zobah went up to the River Beersheba to establish his kingdom ; and David struck him , and went straight to Hama
He took his chariots , 1 , 000 horsemen , 7,000 infantrymen , and 20,000 foot soldiers , and cut off the horses of the chariots , but left behind the horses of the hundred chariots
And the children of Aram of Damascus came to help Hadadezer king of Zobah ; and David slew the children of Aram twenty and two thousand
Then David set up a camp in the land of Aram in Damascus ; and the children of Aram surrendered to him , and gave him a ransom ; and David went not into it ; and the Lord overcame him
And he took the gold shield which the servant of Hadadezer had taken , and brought it to Jerusalem
And David took much of the copper from Tibah of Hadadezer , and from the two cities , and Solomon made therewith the sea of copper , and the pillars of copper , and all the vessels of copper
And the king of Hama heard that David had smitten all the army of Hadadezer king of Zobah
Then he sent Hadoran his son to king David , and asked him for an安 , and blessed him , because he had defeated Hadadezer , for he had often fought with Hadadezer . Hadoran brought with him all the vessels of silver and brass
And the vessels which king David took , and the silver and the gold which he took out of the kingdoms , were holy to the LORD , according to all that they had taken out of Edom , Moab , Ammon , Philistine , and Amalek
And Abishai the son of Zeruiah slew eighteen thousand men eastward in the valley of salt
And David set up a camp in the land of Edom , and all the Edomites came to him : and David went there without saying , and the LORD overcame him
David was king over all Israel , and he did righteousness to all the people
And Joab the son of Zeruiah was captain , and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahithophel historian .
And Zadok the son of Ahithophel , and Ahimiel the son of Abijah , were over the priests ; and Shavestah was the scribe .
And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada ruled over the tribe of Gilead and the tribe of the Philistines ; and all the sons of David were captains of the king &apos;s side and of the king &apos;s side
And after this Nathan the king of the children of Ammon died , and his sons reigned in his stead
Then David sent messengers to comfort him for his father &apos;s death , and his servants came to him in the land of the children of Ammon to comfort him
But the princes of the children of Ammon said to Hanun , &quot; Have David sent a man to comfort you ? Do you think that he respects your father , and that his servants come to see you to spy on the land and to overthrow it ?
And Hanun shaved the beard of the servants of David in half , and cut off their garments in half , and exposed them , and sent them back
Then there was a man who told David what had happened to his servants ; and he sent messengers to meet them , because they were ashamed ; and he told them , &quot; You can stay in Jericho until your beard grows and you come back . &quot;
And when the children of Ammon knew that David hated them , Hanun and the children of Ammon sent messengers , and took a thousand pieces of silver from Mesopotamia , and from Armagh , and from Zobah , and hired chariots and horsemen
So they hired thirty-two thousand chariots and king Magah and his army ; and they encamped before Medeba ; and the children of Ammon came out of their cities , and gathered themselves together to battle .
And when David heard it , he sent Joab out with all his mighty army
And the sons of Ammon came out , and pitched before the gates of the city ; and the kings that came pitched in the fields .
And when Joab saw that the enemy stood before him and behind him , he chose men of valour out of the army of Israel , and set them before the children of Aram
And the rest of the army joined themselves with his brother Abijah , and pitched against the children of Ammon .
And Joab said to Abishai , &quot; If the children of Aram oppress me , you will help me ; and if the children of Ammon oppress you , I will help you
&quot; We are strong , and great husbands to the people of our land , and to the cities of God . May the Lord do according to his will
So Joab and his men attacked the children of Aram , and the children of Aram fled before Joab .
And when the children of Ammon saw that the children of Aram fled , they fled into the city before Abishai the brother of Joab ; and Joab returned to Jerusalem
And when the children of Aram saw that they were defeated by the children of Israel , they sent an apostle , and brought the children of Aram by the river ; and Shaopha the general of Hadaliah led them .
And there came a man to David , and he gathered all Israel together , and passed over the Jordan , and came unto the children of Aram , and pitched against them ; and David pitched against the children of Aram , and the children of Aram fought against him
And the children of Aram fled before the children of Israel ; and David slew the men of 7,000 chariots and 40,000 foot soldiers of Aram , and Shaopha the general of Aram
And when the kings of Hadadezer saw that they were defeated by the children of Israel , they surrendered unto David with goodness : and the children of Aram would not help the children of Ammon any more
And it came to pass after a year , when the kings were at war , that Joab took the army and besieged Rabbah , destroying the land of the children of Ammon ; and David lived in Jerusalem ; and Joab struck and overthrew the city of Rabbah .
And David took the crown of gold that the king of the children of Ammon had worn , and the gold that was on it was multiplied by weight , and it was engraved with stones ; and they put it on David &apos;s head ; and David took much of the treasures of the city
Thus did David to the inhabitants of the cities of Ammon , when he brought forth the men of the city , and put them under saws , or under bars , or under axes of iron ; and David and all the host returned to Jerusalem .
Then the children of Israel fought against the Philistines at Gibeah , and the Hussites killed a son of a mighty man , and the Philistines were put under siege .
And he fought against the Philistines ; and Eleazar the son of Jair slew Raham the brother of Galilee the Gathite , whose rods were as the axes of a weaving cloth .
And in the battle of Gath there was a man of great stature , whose feet were six fingers , and his head twenty-four ; and he was the son of a mighty man .
Then Jonathan the son of Shemiah , David &apos;s brother , slew him , and cursed the children of Israel .
And these three were the sons of Gad ; and they died under the hand of David and his servants
Then Satan came and attacked the children of Israel , and David was moved to number them
Then David commanded Joab and the chiefs of the people , saying , &quot; Go and count the children of Israel from Baal-zerah to Dan , and come back and tell me , for I know the number of them .
And Joab said , May the LORD multiply his people a hundred times more than they are now : are they not all thy servants , O my lord , my king , and what is my lord commanded to do , and why is Israel put in sin ?
But the king &apos;s commandment overcame Joab , and he went out , and passed through the land of Israel , and returned to Jerusalem
And he told David the number of the people : of the children of Israel were an hundred and eleven thousand , and of the children of Judah forty-seven thousand .
Only the Levites and the Benjaminites were not numbered among them , because they hated the king &apos;s commandment for Joab .
&quot; But God was not pleased with the number of the people , so He delivered the plague upon the children of Israel
And David prayed unto God , saying , I have sinned greatly in that which I have done ; and now I pray thee to remove the iniquity of the servant , for I have done much foolishness
And the LORD spake unto Gad the firstborn of David , saying ,
&quot; Go and testify against David , saying , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I have three plagues , and I have chosen one with you , and I am well with you
So Gad came to David and said to him , &quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; You can choose yourselves
Or three years of famine , or three months of defeat before your enemies , or the sword of your enemies , or the sword of the Lord in your land , or the plague of three days , which the angels of the Lord destroyed in all the four quarters of Israel . Now think , and I will return to those who sent me .
David said to Gad , &quot; I am in great distress . I want to fall into the hand of the Lord , for he has abundant mercy , and I do not want to fall into the hand of men
Then the LORD struck the plague with the children of Israel ; and the children of Israel died seventy thousand
God sent messengers to destroy Jerusalem ; and when the Lord saw that it was about to be destroyed , he repented , and did not bring it down ; and the angels that destroyed the city said , &quot; Get down , and hold your hand . &quot; Then the angels of the Lord stood at the field of the herbs of Arnan the Jebusite
And David lifted up his eyes , and saw the angel of the Lord standing in heaven and earth , with a sword drawn out of his hand , stretched out over Jerusalem ; and David and the elders were clothed in linen , and laid faces upon the ground
David prayed to God , saying , &quot; Is it not I who commands the people to number ? I have sinned and done evil ; but what have these sheep done ? May the hand of the Lord my God attack me and my father &apos;s house , and do not attack your people , and send a plague with them
And the angel of the Lord commanded Gad to go and testify against David , and to bring him up , and to build an altar for the Lord in the field of Arnon the Jebusite
And David went according to the words which Gad spoke in the name of the LORD
At that time he was wrestling wheat , and when he looked back at the angel , he hid himself with his four sons
And when David came to Arnon , and he saw David , he went out of the field , and bowed himself to the ground , and worshipped him
Then David said to Arnan , &quot; You have sold me this field and the land that is with it , and I will give you the price of it , that I may build an altar for the Lord on it , and that the plague of the people may cease
Then Arnan said to David , &quot; My lord , my king , let this field be yours , that you may go according to your pleasure ; and I will give you cattle for burnt offerings , and the instruments for feeding for firewood , and the barley for a sustenance offering , and all these will I send to you
Then the king said to Arnan , &quot; No , I need to buy it for you at a reasonable price ; I will not offer your things to the Lord , nor will I offer anything of white for a burnt offering
And David poured out for the land six hundred shekels of gold for Arnun
And David built therein an altar unto the LORD , to offer burnt offerings and sacrifices of peace ; and he cried unto the LORD ; and the LORD answered him , and made fire come down from heaven upon the altar of burnt offerings
&quot; The Lord commanded the messenger , and he took the sword into the sheath
And when David saw that the LORD had obeyed him in the field of Arnon the Jebusite , he sacrificed there
And the tabernacle of the LORD , which Moses made in the wilderness , and the altar of burnt offering , were in the high places of Gibeon
&quot; But David did not dare to ask God , for he feared the sword of the messenger of the Lord .
And David said , This is the house of the Lord God , the altar of burnt offerings for the children of Israel
And David commanded the foreigners that dwelled in the land of Israel to gather together stoneworkers out of them to build the house of God
David promised more iron as a nail and a hook for the door , and more copper than could be measured .
And he prepared a multitude of acacia trees for David , because he delivered them for the children of Sidon and for the children of Tyre .
And David said , Solomon my son , when he was yet young and tender , that the house which he would build for the LORD would be great and glorious , and that the glory of his name might be spread throughout all the nations ; therefore will I prepare for it ; and David prepared much before he died
And David called Solomon his son , and commanded him to build a house for the LORD God of Israel
He said to Solomon , &quot; My son , I have in my heart a desire to build a house in the name of the Lord my God
&quot; It is only the word of the Lord that came to me , saying , &apos; You have poured out the blood of many people , and have fought many battles ; and you shall not build houses for my name , for you have poured out the blood of many people on the earth before my eyes
And thou shalt give birth unto a son , and he shall be a man of peace : and I will make him quiet , and he shall not be disturbed by the enemies that are round about him : and his name shall be Solomon ; and in the days of his reign will I make the children of Israel to be in peace in Canaan .
He will build houses in my name ; He will be my son , and I will be his father ; He will be king over Israel , and I will establish his throne forever .
&quot; Now , my son , I pray that the Lord will be with you to make you prosper , and to build the house of the Lord your God according to what He has spoken concerning you
&quot; May the Lord give you wisdom , that you may reign in the land of Israel , and keep the law of the Lord your God
&quot; If you will keep the law of the LORD , which Moses commanded Israel , you will prosper ; and when you are strong and courageous , do not be afraid , nor be afraid
&quot; I have prepared for the house of the Lord a hundred thousand pieces of gold , and a hundred thousand pieces of silver , brass and iron , in the midst of hardship ; and I have prepared wood and stone , and you can add to it
Thou hast many craftsmen , stoneworkers , woodworkers , and all skillful craftsmen
And there is a multitude of gold , and a multitude of silver , and a multitude of copper , and a multitude of iron : when thou standest up and doest , let the LORD be with thee .
And David commanded all the princes of Israel to help Solomon his son , saying ,
Is not the LORD your God with you , that you may have peace all around you ? For he has delivered the inhabitants of this land into my hand , and the land has fallen before the LORD and his people .
&quot; Now therefore , be determined to seek the Lord your God , and to build the sanctuary of the God of the Lord , and to bring the ark of the Lord and the vessels of God into the house that is built in the name of the Lord .
David was old and full of days , and made Solomon his son king over Israel
David gathered together all the princes of Israel , and the Levites , the priests
All the Levites were numbered from thirty years old and upward , and the number of their males was three and eight thousand .
And of them twenty and four thousand were over the affairs of the house of the LORD , and six thousand were captains and scribes .
Four thousand guarded the gates , and four thousand praised the LORD with the instruments of David .
And David divided the children of the Levites into two tribes : the sons of Gershon , and the sons of Goshen , and the sons of Mirali ,
And the sons of Gershon ; Ladan and Shechem .
And the sons of Ladan ; Jesheh , and Shetan , and Joel , three ;
And the sons of Shemei ; Shelomim , and Haserah , and Haran , the chief of the children of Ladan ;
And the sons of Shemei : Jaha , and Shena , and Jeush , and Beeriah , four .
And Jaha was the firstborn , and Shesha the second ; but there were not many of the sons of Jeush and of Beer-sheba ; so they were one tribe
The sons of Kohath : Amran , Ishah , Hebron , Uzziel , four .
&quot; The sons of Amran were Aaron and Moses . Aaron and his sons were separated to the holy things , and they burned incense before the Lord , and served him , and blessed in his name , for ever and ever
As for Moses , the man of God , and his sons , their names are written in the book of the tribe of Levi
And the sons of Moses were Gershon , and Eliezer .
The eldest son of Guang Shun was a seamstress .
The son of Eliezer was Rehabiah ; and Eliezer had no sons , but Rehabiah had many sons .
The eldest son of Esha was Shilomi
The firstborn of Hebron was Elijah ; the second , Amariah ; the third , Jahaziel ; and the fourth , Jegamah .
The firstborn of Uzziah was Micah ; and the second was Jesse .
And the sons of Merari were Maphiah , and Shemaiah , and the sons of Maphiah were Eleazar , and Kiz .
And Eleazar died , and had no sons , but daughters : and the sons of their own tribe Kiz took their wives
And the sons of Maaseiah were Teruel , and Edad , and Jeremiah , three .
And the sons of Levi shall be princes in the house of the LORD , according to the number of the males , from twenty years old and upward ,
David said , &quot; The Lord , the God of Israel , has made his people safe , and he will live forever in Jerusalem .
And the Levites shall no more lift up the tabernacle , and all the vessels that are in it
The Levites were numbered , from twenty years old and upward , according to the commandment of David at the end of the world
&quot; Their duty is to minister to the sons of Aaron in the house of the Lord , and in the courts , and in the houses , and to cleanse all the holy things , and to do the work of the house of God .
and the arrangement of the cakes , the fine breads of the supper , or of the unleavened breads , or of the breads baked on a plate , or of the oil mixtures , and the measures of the raising of all kinds
Every morning and evening stand and give thanks to the Lord
&quot; On the sabbath day , and on the month , and on the sabbath day , and on the feast day , they shall offer burnt offerings often to the Lord , according to the number
and watch over the tabernacle of the congregation and the sanctuary , and watch over the work of the house of the Lord , as the Lord commanded the sons of Aaron their brother
The sons of Aaron : Nadab , and Abihu , and Eleazar , and Ehamma ,
And it came to pass , when Abihu died before his father , that he had no sons left : and Eleazar and Ishmael were appointed priests
The sons of Eleazar , the sons of Zadok , and the sons of Ishmael , the sons of Ishmael , divided themselves among their brethren with David ,
Of the sons of Eleazar , sixteen were chiefs ; of the sons of Ithamar , eight were chiefs .
And the sons of Eleazar , and the sons of Ishmael , were princes before the sanctuary and before God ,
And Shemaiah the son of Nethaniah the Levite , who was the scribe , recorded their names before the king and the princes , and before the governor of the priests , and Ahimiel the son of Abijah , and before the chief priests of the Levites ; and they took a tribe of the sons of Eleazar , and a tribe of the sons of Ishmael ,
At the time of the signing , the first that came out was Jehiel , and the second was Jedaiah
The third was Harlin , and the fourth was Thorin
And the fifth was Machiah , and the sixth the Midianites
The seventh was Hagath , and the eighth Abijah
The ninth was Jeshua , and the tenth Shechaniah
The eleventh was Elijah , and the twelfth Jachin
The thirteenth was Hubbar , and the fourteenth Jeroboam
The fifteenth is Picah , and the sixteenth is the wheat
The seventeenth is Hezekiah , and the eighteenth is Habakkuk
The nineteenth is Beth-Hiah , and the twenty-first is Hezekiah
&quot; The twenty-first is Jachin , and the twenty-second is Gath
&quot; The twenty-third is Delaiah , and the twenty-fourth is Maaseiah
&quot; This is their division to enter into the house of the Lord , and to do the work according to the commandment of the Lord , the God of Israel , by the hand of Aaron their father .
The rest of the sons of Levi were as follows : of the sons of Amran was Shebaiah , and of the sons of Shebaiah was Jehideah ,
And of the sons of Rehabiah was Isiah the eldest .
And of the sons of Issachar was Shelom , and of the sons of Shelom was Jaha .
And of the sons of Hebron were Elijah the firstborn , and Amariah the second , and Jahaziel the third , and Jega the fourth .
And of the sons of Uzziah was Micah ; and of the sons of Micah was Shami .
And the brothers of Micah were Ishmael : and of the sons of Ishmael was Zechariah .
And the sons of Merari were Maphiah , and Shemaiah , and Jaziah ; and the sons of Jaziah were Beer-noah .
And of the sons of Merari were Beno , and Shumon , and Zechariah , and Ibil , the sons of Jaziah .
And Eleazar the son of Machir had no son .
And of the sons of Kish was Jerah .
And the sons of Shemaiah were Teruel , and Edom , and Jeremiah : and these are the sons of Levi according to their families
As the sons of Aaron , their brothers , so did they cast lots before king David , and before Zadok , and before Ahimeleh , and before the elders of the Levites , the priests ; and the elders of the tribes were not separated from their brothers
And David and the chiefs of the host divided the sons of Asa , and the sons of Haman , and the sons of Jeduthun , to play the harp , and the psaltery , and the psaltery , and to sing , and the number of their service was written as follows
And the sons of Asa , Zechariah , and Joseph , and Nethaniah , and Azariah , came to Asa to teach , and to sing , according to the will of the king
And the sons of Jeduthun , Gilead , and Shili , and Jesheiah , and Hashabiah , and Mattaiah , and Shechem , six , were to their father Jeduthun , teaching , playing the harp , singing , and giving thanks , and praising the Lord
And the sons of Heman ; Bukiah , and Mattaniah , and Uzziel , and Shebuiah , and Jerimo , and Hananiah , and Hananiah , and Eliathah , and Gidalith , and Lomanti , and Isheh , and Joshbekah , and Maroth , and Hothi , and Mahahide
And these are the sons of Haman , who are praised by the trumpet : and Haman was a prophet by the commandment of God ; and God gave him fourteen sons and three daughters
They all taught to their fathers , singing in the house of the Lord , and whistling , and playing the harp , and drumming , and performing the service of the house of God ; and the king commanded Asa , and Jeduthun , and Heman .
They and their brethren learned to praise the Lord , and the singers were two hundred eighteen and eighteen .
&quot; They were divided into groups , men of all sizes , teachers and disciples .
And it came to pass at the time of the signing , that the first to come out was Joseph the son of Asa , and the second to Gedaliah , he and his brethren and his sons , twelve :
And the third was Zechariah , twelve with his sons and his brethren
And the fourth was Jezebel , twelve with his sons and his brethren
And the fifth was Nethaniah , twelve with his sons and his brethren
And the sixth was Bukiah , twelve with his sons and his brethren :
And the seventh was Jezreel : twelve were with him , and his sons and his brethren .
And the eighth was Jeshua , twelve with his sons and his brethren :
And the ninth was Mattaniah , twelve with his sons and his brethren
And the tenth was Shechem , twelve men with his sons and his brethren
And the eleventh was Azariah , twelve with his sons and his brethren
The twelfth was Hashabiah , twelve with his sons and his brethren .
The thirteenth to Shuba , he , his sons , and his brethren , were twelve
The fourteenth was Mattaiah , twelve with his sons and his brethren .
The fifteenth was Jeremiah , twelve with his sons and his brethren
The sixteenth was Hananiah , twelve with his sons and his brethren
The seventeenth was Jozbekah , twelve with his sons and his brethren
The eighteenth was Hanani , twelve with his sons and his brothers
The nineteenth was Maroti , twelve with his sons and his brothers
And Elia , he , and his sons , and his brethren , were twelve :
The twenty-first was Geth ; and he and his sons and his brethren were twelve
The twelfth to Gedalith , he , his sons , and his brethren , were twelve :
And the thirty-third was Mahashide , twelve with his sons and his brethren :
And the twenty-fourth to Rehoboam , Ishmael ; twelve with his sons and with his brethren :
And of the sons of Asa , of the tribe of Kohath , Mizlimiah the son of Kohath ,
The firstborn of Mizlimiah was Zacariah , the second Japhaz , the third Sibadiah , and the fourth Jetinim
the five sons of Edom , the six sons of Jehohanan , the seven sons of Elijah ,
The firstborn was Shemaiah , the second was Jehoshaphat , the third Joah , the fourth Shath , and the fifth Nathaniel
the sixth to Amiel , the seventh to Issachar , and the eighth to Uliath ; for God had blessed the land of Edom
His son Shemaiah had several sons , all of them mighty men , who ruled over his father &apos;s house .
And the sons of Shemaiah were Odin , and Rephaim , and Obed , and Elishaba ; and the brothers of Elishaba were mighty men ; and Elihu and Shimaiah
These are the sons of Obed-Edom : they and their sons and their brethren were mighty men of valour : and the sons of Obed-Edom were sixty-two .
And the sons of Mizlimiah , and his brethren , were mighty men , eighteen .
The sons of Mirali , Joses , had several sons ; and the firstborn was Sheni ; and he was not the firstborn , but his father made him the firstborn
The second to Shelah , and the third to Debaliah , and the fourth to Zacchael ; and the sons of Joses and his brethren were thirteen .
These are the captains of the gates , and they serve in the house of the Lord in their divisions with their brethren
They were sealed by the tribes , and guarded the gates , great and small
And he that guarded the east gate was Shelemiah ; and his son Zechariah was a wise counselor , and he that guarded the north gate
And he guarded the south gate eastward , and his son guarded the treasure house .
and they were guarded at Shemmon with Hosah , in the streets that lead up to Sheribim , facing one another .
There are six Levites daily at the East Gate , four at the North Gate , four at the South Gate , two at the Warehouse and two in turn
There are four on the west side of the street and two on the corridor
These are the divisions of the gatekeepers , the sons of Kola and the sons of Mirali .
Among the sons of Levi was Ahijah , who was over the treasures of the temple , and over the treasures of the holy things .
of the sons of Ladan , of the tribe of Gershon , Jehiel the son of Ladan of the tribe of Gershon ,
and Sitan the son of Jehiel , and Joel his brother , were over the treasures of the house of the Lord
The Ammonites , the Issathites , the Hebrews , and the Uchites also had offices .
and Shebaiah the son of Gershon , the son of Moses , was over the treasure house .
And his brother Eliezer ; and the son of Eliezer was Rehabiah , and the son of Rehabiah was Jesse , and the son of Jesse was Joram , and the son of Joram was Hezekiah , and the son of Hezekiah was Shelomith .
These are the holy things which Solomon and his brethren kept in the treasures of the house of David , the holy things of king David , and of the princes of the nations , and of the thousands , and of the hundreds , and of the captains of the armies ,
&quot; They shall sanctify the treasures they took in battle , to build the house of the Lord .
And behold , Samuel , Saul the son of Jesse , and Abner the son of Ner , and Joab the son of Zeruiah , were over all the holy things , which were given to Shelomith and to his brethren
And of the children of Issachar were Kenaniah and all his sons captains and officers over the foreign affairs of Israel
And of the children of Hebron , Hashabiah and his brethren , one thousand seven hundred , were mighty men , doing the work of the Lord and the king in the land of Israel , on the west side of Jordan
Among the Hebrews was Elijah the chief , and in the fourteenth year of David &apos;s reign he found mighty warriors among them in Jasheth of Gilead
And the brothers of Jeremiah were two thousand and seven hundred , men of valour , and chiefs of the house : and king David sent them to do the work of God and the king in the tribe of Reuben , and in the tribe of Gad , and in the tribe of Manasseh , and in the half tribe
The chief of the tribes , the chief of the thousands , the chief of the hundreds , and the chief of the officers of the children of Israel shall be appointed in divisions , twenty-four thousand in each division , alternating in the year according to the month , in exchange for the king of the service
And the captain of the first class in the first month was Jashoban the son of Zabadiel , and in his class were twenty and four thousand .
And he was the son of Pharaoh , and the captain of all the host of the month .
The captain of the month of February was Dodeus the Ahazite , and the deputy , Michiro ; and in his division were twenty and four thousand .
The captain of the third class in March was Benaiah the son of Jehoiada the priest ; and in his class were twenty and four thousand
And Benaiah was a mighty man among the thirty , and he ruled over the thirty ; and in his company was his son Ahimsaph .
And in the fourth month Asahel the brother of Joab was captain of the host ; and Zabadiah his son was in his stead : and in his host were twenty and four thousand .
The captain of the fifth class in May was Shen Ai , an Israelite , and he had twenty-four thousand men
The captain of the sixth class in June was Ela , the son of the Gideonites , of whom were twenty and four thousand .
The captain of the seventh class in July was Hiles of Beer-sheba of the children of Ephraim ; and in his class were twenty and four thousand .
The captain of the eighth battalion in August was Siberia , a Shusha of the Shelahs , of whom were twenty-four thousand
The captain of the ninth battalion in September was Abiezer of the Anakims of Benjamin , and in his battalion were twenty-four thousand
The captain of the tenth class in October was Mahalay , a Nethite of the Shelahs , and he had twenty-four thousand men in his class
And the captain of the eleventh band in November was Phinehas of Ephraim , and Phinehas of Ladon , and Phinehas of Naiah : and in his band were twenty and four thousand .
The leader of the twelfth class in December was the Nethite of the Odonites , Hachi , who had 24,000 men in his class
Behold , the princes over all the tribes of Israel were : over the Benites was Eliezer the son of Shekkiel ; over the Simeonites was Shephathiah the son of Maacah .
And over the Levites was Hashabiah the son of Gemoriel ; and over the sons of Aaron was Zadok .
And over Judah was Elihu the brother of David ; and over the children of Issachar was Amri the son of Micah .
of the children of Zebulun , Ismaiah the son of Obediah ; of the children of Naphtali , Jelim the son of Assyria ;
And of the children of Ephraim was Hoshea the son of Azariah ; and of the half tribe of Manasseh was Joel the son of Daiah .
And of the half tribe of Manasseh in Gilead , Edo the son of Zachariah ; and of the children of Benjamin , Jaziah the son of Abner ;
And over Dan was Asahel the son of Jeroboam ; and these are the chiefs of the tribes of Israel
The twenty-year-old of Israel , whose number David did not remember , because the Lord had promised , saying , &quot; I will increase Israel as the stars of heaven
Then Joab the son of Reuiah began to count , and the wrath of the LORD came upon the children of Israel , and the number was not fulfilled , neither was it written in the book of David
And Absmawi the son of Aphaz was in charge of the king &apos;s house ; and Jonathan the son of Uzziah was in charge of the storehouses of the field , and of the cities and villages .
And the man that was over the fields was Ezra , the son of Gideon
The man who was in charge of the vineyard was Shimei the Ramathite , and the man who was in charge of the wine cellar was Sabath the Shemmite
And over olive trees and fir trees in the plain was Balahanan the Gideonite ; and over the well was Joash .
The man who was in charge of Sharon &apos;s cattle was Shetihan the Sharonite ; and the man who was in charge of the cattle of the valley was Shaphah the son of Adian .
And over the camels was Abel the Ishmaelite , and over the donkeys Jehideah the Meronite , and over the sheep Jazeel the Shathite .
These are all for the king David to take over the industry
And Jonathan David &apos;s uncle was a man of counsel , a wise man , and a clerk ; and Jesheh the son of Hammonite was the master of the king &apos;s sons
And Ahithophel was king &apos;s counselor ; and Hushai the Ahithophel was king &apos;s companion .
And after him were Jehideah the son of Benaiah , and Abijah his son , to be captains over him ; and Joab was captain over the king .
And David gathered together the chiefs of the tribes of Israel , and the captains of the hosts of the king , and the captains of thousands , and captains of hundreds , and the captains of the king &apos;s household , and the princes &apos; household , and the overseers , and the mighty men of war , to Jerusalem
Then King David stood up and said , &quot; Listen to me , my brothers and my people , for I have in mind to build a house and to set up the ark of the Lord as a bench for my God , and I have prepared the materials for it
&quot; But God said to me , &apos; You cannot build a house in my name , for you are a warrior , and have poured out the blood of men .
&quot; But the Lord , the God of Israel , has chosen me to be king of Israel in all the houses of my father for ever , because He has chosen Judah to be his head , He has chosen my father &apos;s house in the tribes of Judah , He has pleased me in all the children of my father , He has made me king over all Israel
&quot; The Lord has given me many sons , and He has chosen Solomon from among my sons to sit in the throne of the Lord and to rule over Israel
And the LORD said unto me , Solomon thy son shall build my house and my house : for I have chosen him for my son , and I will be his father
&quot; If he keeps my commandments forever , as I do today , I will establish his throne forever
&quot; Now our God has heard before the eyes of all Israel what he has said in the assembly of the Lord , saying , &apos; You shall seek and keep all the commandments of the Lord your God , so that you may possess this beautiful land , and give it to your children for a possession forever .
&quot; O my son Solomon , when you know the Lord , the God of your father , you serve him with all your heart and with all your joy ; for he knows the hearts of all men , and knows all the thoughts of all hearts ; and if you seek him , he will find you ; and if you forsake him , he will forsake you forever .
&quot; Be cautious , for the Lord has chosen you to build the house as a sanctuary , and be steadfast in your ways .
And David commanded Solomon his son the pattern of the courts , and of the side rooms , and of the storehouses , and of the houses , and of the inner house , and of the sanctuary
And he shall be inspired by the pattern of the house of the house of the Lord , and of the houses around it , and of the treasures of the house , and of all the treasures of the holy things ,
And he commanded the divisions of the priests and the Levites , and all the work of the house of the LORD , and all the vessels of the house of the LORD
and that the samples should be divided by gold instruments and the samples by silver instruments
The gold lamp stand and the silver lamp stand , the silver lamp stand and the silver lamp stand , each lightweight
Two pieces for the gold table and two pieces for the silver table
the forks of meat of pure gold , and the plates , and the spoons of the count , and the bowls of gold , and the bowls of silver ,
And he divided the altar of pure gold , and made it with gold as a carriageway , to open its wings , and to cover the ark of the Lord
David said , &quot; The pattern of all these works was drawn out by the Lord by his hand , that I might understand
Then David said to Solomon his son , &quot; Be courageous , and do not be afraid , neither be afraid ; for the God of the Lord is my God , and he is with you , and he will not forsake you , nor forsake you , until the work of the house of the Lord is finished .
There are the priests and the Levites to do all the work of the house of God ; and there are wise men to help you in all things ; and there are the chiefs and the people who are obedient to your commandments .
And king David said unto the assembly , Solomon my son is a chosen man of God , and he is young and tender , and this is a great work : for this house is not for men , but for the LORD God
I have prepared the house of my God with all my might , gold for gold , silver for silver , copper for copper , iron for iron , wood for wood , and stones of red marble , and stone of color , and all stones , and lots of gold .
&quot; Because I love the house of my God in my heart , I will build the house of my God out of the materials that I have prepared for the house of my God , and out of the gold and silver that I have stored up ,
And three thousand of the gold of Ophir , and seven thousand of the silver of refined gold , to put it on the walls of the house ;
&quot; The gold is a gold vessel , and the silver is a silver vessel ; and by the hands of craftsmen they make all things.Who is willing to offer himself to the Lord today ?
Then the princes of the tribes , and the chiefs of the tribes of Israel , and the thousands , and the hundreds , and the captains of the guard , and the officers of the king &apos;s servants , were glad to offer
&quot; For the service of the temple they offered five thousand pieces of gold , ten thousand talents , ten thousand pieces of silver , eight thousand pieces of copper , and ten thousand pieces of iron
And all the stones that were in the treasures of the LORD &apos;s house were given to Jesheh the son of Gershon
And the people rejoiced , and the king rejoiced greatly , because they had dedicated their hearts to the Lord
So David praised the Lord in the presence of the congregation , saying , &quot; The Lord , our Father , the God of Israel , is to be praised , even to the ends of eternity
Yours is the glory , the power , the glory , the might , and the majesty , O Lord ; and to you belongs all that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth ; and to you belongs the kingdom ; and you are the Most High , the Head of all things
From thee come riches and honour , and thou hast dominion over all things ; and in thy hand is great power and might , and in thee come all the mighty .
&quot; Now , O God of ours , we give thanks to You , and praise Your glory
&quot; What am I and what are my people willing to give ? For all things have come from you , and we have given you what we have from you
&quot; We are travellers and dwellers before you , as our fathers were , and in the days of the world we will not live , as shadows .
&quot; Lord , our God , we have prepared many things to build houses for your holy name . They have come from you , and they belong to you
I know , O my God , that thou hast tested the hearts , and that thou hast rejoiced in righteousness ; and I have bestowed all these things with the joy of a righteous heart ; and now I rejoice in thy people , and here I am glad to offer them unto thee .
&quot; Lord , God of our fathers , Abraham , Isaac , and Israel , make your people to keep such thoughts in mind , and make their hearts firm to you .
&quot; And grant Solomon my son a faithful heart , to keep your commandments , and your statutes , and your laws , and to do all these things , and to build the house which I have prepared
And David said unto all the congregation , Praise the LORD your God ; and the congregation praised the LORD God of their fathers , and bowed down to the LORD and to the king
On the next day they shall offer the peace offering and the burnt offering to the Lord , a thousand bulls , a thousand rams , a thousand lambs , and a drink offering with them , and many sacrifices for all Israel ; and on that day they shall eat and drink before the Lord in great joy
They obeyed the commandment of the Lord , and anointed Solomon the son of David king , and Zadok priest
And Solomon sat in the throne which the LORD had given him , and succeeded David his father to be king over all things ; and all Israel listened to him
The princes and the mighty men , and all the sons of king David , obeyed the king of Solomon
The LORD hath made Solomon great in the sight of all Israel , and great in his majesty , above all the kings of Israel before him
David the son of Jesse king over all Israel
He reigned forty years in Hebron seven years , and in Jerusalem thirty and three years .
When his days were fulfilled , and he was filled with riches and honour , he died , and his son Solomon succeeded him as king
&quot; All that king David had done was written in the book of Samuel , and in the book of Nathan the prophet , and in the book of Gad
His kingdom , and his might , and all that he and all the nations of Israel have done , are written in this book
Solomon the son of David , the kingdom was established , and the Lord his God was with him , that he might be glorified
And Solomon commanded all Israel , even the captains of thousands , and the captains of hundreds , and the judges , and the princes , and the princes of the tribes , to come
And Solomon and the congregation went to the high place of Gibeon , because there was in it the tabernacle of God , which Moses the servant of the Lord had made in the wilderness
&quot; But the ark of God , which David had brought from Gilead to the place which he had prepared , because he had set up the tabernacle of the ark in Jerusalem
And the bronze altar which Beer-sheba the son of Uri , the son of Hur , made was before the tabernacle of the congregation of the LORD at Gibeon ; and Solomon and the congregation were near before the altar
And Solomon came up to the LORD in the copper altar of the tabernacle of the congregation , and offered a thousand burnt offerings
And it came to pass at night , when God appeared to Solomon , that He said unto him , What wilt thou that I give thee ?
Solomon said to God , &quot; You have shown mercy to my father David , and made me to succeed him as king
&quot; Now , O Lord God , I seek thee to do that which thou hast promised my father David : for they are as the dust of the earth , because thou hast made me king over them .
&quot; Give me wisdom and wisdom , that I may go in and out before these people ; or who will judge the multitude of these people ?
And God said unto Solomon , I have made thee king over my people , and thou hast not desired riches , nor glory , nor destruction of the life of those who hate thee , nor a great number of years , but wisdom , and understanding , and judgement for my people
I will give thee wisdom and wisdom , and I will give thee honour and riches , which were not before thee , nor after thee .
Then Solomon returned from the high place of Gibeon , before the Tent of Meeting , to Jerusalem , to rule over the children of Israel
And Solomon gathered together chariots and horsemen : and there were a thousand and four hundred chariots and twelve thousand horsemen ; and they were set up in the cities of Tune , and in Jerusalem , where the king was
The king made silver and gold as stones in Jerusalem , and cedars as fir trees in the high places
The horses of Solomon were brought from Egypt , and they were purchased by the king &apos;s merchants at a fixed price
The cars which they bought from Egypt were seven hundred shekels for each silver , and one hundred fifty shekels for each horse ; and the horses which the kings of Hesh and of Aram bought were also by their hand
Solomon planned to build houses in the name of the Lord , and palaces for his own country
Solomon chose 70,000 men who carried them , and 80,000 men who dug stones in the mountains , and thirty and six hundred officers .
Then Solomon sent to Hilan king of Tyre , and said to him , &quot; Be kind to me also , for you have planted palm trees and built the house with my father David
&quot; I will build houses for the name of the Lord my God , dedicated to him , and I will burn incense before him , and I will set up tables for cakes , and I will offer burnt offerings every morning and evening , on the Sabbath day and on the moon , and on the feasts that the Lord our God has ordained for us ; and this is the statute of Israel for ever .
For the house which I will build is great ; for our God is greater than all the gods .
&quot; The heavens and the heavens above are not enough for him to dwell in . Who can build a house for him ? Who am I ? Who can build a house for him ? It is not to burn incense before him .
&quot; Now I ask you to send a craftsman , a craftsman of gold , of silver , of copper , of iron , and of purple , red , and blue thread , who is skillful in carving , to work with the craftsmen that my father David prepared in Judah and Jerusalem
&quot; And bring me from Lebanon some cedars , pine trees , and sandalwoods ; for I know that your servants are good at cutting down the trees of Lebanon ; and my servants shall work with your servants .
&quot; Therefore much wood will be prepared for me ; for the house which I will build is marvelous .
&quot; Your servants will cut down trees , and I will give them twenty thousand pieces of wheat , twenty thousand pieces of barley , twenty thousand pieces of wine , twenty thousand pieces of oil ,
And Hilan king of Tyre wrote and answered Solomon , saying , The LORD make thee king over them , because thou lovest his people
&quot; Blessed is the Lord , the God of Israel , the Creator of the heavens and the earth , who has given a wise son to King David , so that he may have wisdom , and build houses for the Lord , and houses for his own country ,
Now I have sent to you a man of skill and wisdom , whom my father Hilan used
&quot; This is the son of a woman of Dan , whose father was a Tyrolean , who made good of gold , silver , copper , iron , stone , wood , and purple , blue , and purple , and scarlet , and fine linen , all things , and was skillful in carving , and devised all kinds of craftsmen ; and send him to work with your craftsman , and with the craftsman of your father David my lord ,
&quot; The wheat , and the barley , and the wine , and the oil , which my Lord has spoken , shall be delivered to my servants
&quot; We will cut down trees from Lebanon , and we will put them in rafts , and we will bring them to Joppa by sea , and you will be brought to Jerusalem from there .
Solomon imitated David his father and numbered all the foreigners who dwelt in the land of Israel , a total of fifty-three thousand and six hundred
70,000 men carried loads , 80,000 dug stones in the mountains , and thirty-six hundred supervised the work
Then Solomon prepared himself in Jerusalem , on Mount Moriah , which the Lord appeared to David his father , on the field of the herbs of Arnon the Jebusite , in the place which David had appointed , and began to build the house of the Lord
Construction began in the fourth year of Solomon &apos;s reign , on the first day of February
This is the foundation of the house of Solomon , sixty cubits long and twenty cubits wide , according to the measure of the ancient times
And the porch in front of the house was twenty cubits , as the breadth of the house , and as the height of the house , an hundred and twenty cubits ; and gold was engraved therein .
And the walls of the house were covered with pine boards , and gold was engraved on them , and palm trees and chains were carved on them .
And they adorned the walls of the house with stones , and made the house beautiful ; and all the gold that was used was of the gold of Baasha .
And the buildings of the house and the thresholds thereof , and the walls thereof , and the doors thereof , were plastered with gold ; and the walls were carved with gold .
And he built the sanctuary twenty cubits long , as the breadth of the house , and the breadth twenty cubits ; and he put gold on it , and he joined it with six hundred pieces of gold .
The gold nail weighs fifty shekels . All buildings are gold-plated
Two reins were made in the image of the sanctuary , and they were wrapped in gold .
And the two wings of Reuben were twenty cubits ; and one wings of Reuben was five cubits by the wall of the house , and the other five cubits by the wall of the house .
And one of the wings of Reuben was five cubits , and beside the wall of the house was another five cubits , and beside the wings of Reuben was another five cubits .
And the two wings were opened , twenty cubits in length , and stood toward the inner court .
And with blue , purple , and scarlet , and a mantle of fine linen , and embroidered it with embroidery .
And two pillars were built before the house , thirty-five cubits high , and five cubits high for each of the pillars .
And a chain was made according to the pattern of the refinery in the sanctuary on the top of the pillar , and a hundred pomegranates were made on the chain
And he set up two pillars in front of the house , one on the right hand , and one on the left ; and the name of the one on the right hand was Jachin , and the name of the other on the left was Boaz .
And he made an altar of brass twenty cubits long , twenty cubits wide , and ten cubits high .
And a bronze sea was cast round , five cubits high , ten cubits in diameter , and thirty cubits round .
There was a pattern of wild cucumbers around the sea , ten cucumbers per elbow in two rows , cast at the time of the casting of the sea .
There were twelve copper cows carrying the sea , three to the north , three to the west , three to the south , three to the east . The sea was on the cow , and on the tail
A palm of the sea is as thick as a cup , and as a hundred petals , and it can contain thirty thousand .
And he made ten bowls , five on the right side , and five on the left side ; and in them washed all that they offered for a burnt offering ; and the sea washed for the priest .
And he made ten golden lampstands according to the pattern which he had ordained , five on the right side and five on the left side of the house .
And ten tables were made in the house , five on the right hand , and five on the left ; and a hundred golden bowls were made
And the priest &apos;s house , and the great house , and the gates of the house , were built , and the doors were enclosed with brass
And Haan shall be on the right side of the gate , that is , on the south side ;
And Huran made pots , and shovels , and bowls ; and he finished the work of the house of God for king Solomon
And two pillars were made , and on the pillars two like the tops of the balls , and two nets over the pillars .
And four hundred pomegranates on two nets , two rows for each net , covered with two pillars , like the top of a ball .
The basin and the basin above it
Twelve Cows in the Sea and beneath the Sea
The pots , the shovels , and the fillets of flesh , and all the vessels of the house of the Lord , were made by the skillful craftsman Huran of bright copper for king Solomon .
It was cast out of clay in the plains of Jordan , in the trenches , and in the midst of Zaredan .
Solomon made a great deal of it . The weight of the copper was light and untraceable
And Solomon made in the temple an altar of gold , and a table for cakes
And a lampstand of gold , and lamps , to be set before the inner court ;
And the flowers on the lampstand , and the lamps , and the candlesticks , were gold , and pure gold .
And of pure gold were made the staves , and the plates , and the spoons , and the staves ; and the doors of the temple , and the doors of the sanctuary , and the doors of the temple , were all made of gold .
And when Solomon had finished all the work of the house of the LORD , he brought with him the silver and the gold of his father David , and the vessels , and put them in the treasury of the house of God
Then Solomon gathered together the elders of Israel , and the chiefs of the tribes , and the chiefs of the tribes of Israel , to Jerusalem , to bring up the ark of the LORD from the city of David to Zion
And all Israel gathered themselves together unto the king before the feast of July
And the elders of Israel came , and the Levites lifted up the ark of the covenant
&quot; The Levites brought up the ark of the covenant , and brought up the tabernacle and all the instruments of the congregation
And king Solomon , and all the congregation of Israel that was gathered unto him , sacrificed bulls and lambs before the ark , as many as could not be numbered
And the priest brought up the ark of the Lord into the inner house , which is the sanctuary , and laid it under two winged wings
And he stretched out his wings over the ark , and covered the ark , and the bars of the ark .
The bars are long , and the bars can be seen in front of the inner temple , but they cannot be seen outside the temple ; and they are still there to this day
There were only two tablets of stone in the ark , which Moses laid in Mount Horeb , after the children of Israel had come out of Egypt , in the time of the covenant of the Lord with them , and nothing else
And all the priests therein were cleansed , and were not divided in ranks
And it came to pass , when they were come out of the sanctuary , that Asa the Levite , and Heman , and Jeduthun , and all their sons and brethren , who were singing , were clothed in linen , and stood on the east side of the altar , and whistling , and drumming , and playing the harp , and with them were a hundred and twenty priests blowing
The trumpeters and the singers were all together , singing praises to the Lord ; and the trumpets and the trumpets and the instruments were singing praises to the Lord , saying , &quot; The Lord is good , and His mercy endures forever ; and the house of the Lord will be filled with clouds
Even the priests cannot stand up to serve , for the glory of the Lord fills the house of God
Then Solomon said , &quot; The Lord said , &apos; He will live in the darkness
&quot; But I have built the house for you as your dwelling place , and as your dwelling place forever .
The king turned his face to bless the congregation of Israel , and all the congregation of Israel stood up
Solomon said , &quot; The Lord , the God of Israel , is to be praised , because what he promised to my father David with his mouth has also been fulfilled with his hands
He said , &apos; Since I brought my people out of the land of Egypt , I have not chosen a city , nor built a house , nor dwelled in my name among the tribes of Israel , nor have I chosen a king over my people Israel
&quot; But he chose Jerusalem as his dwelling place in My name , and David as his ruler over my people Israel
Solomon said , &quot; My father David made a plan to build a house for the name of the Lord , the God of Israel
&quot; But the Lord said to David my father , &quot; It is good that you intend to build a house for my name
Only thou shalt not build a house ; but thy son that is born of thee shall build a house in my name .
&quot; Now the word of the Lord has been fulfilled , that I may sit in the throne of Israel after David my father , according to the word of the Lord , and build a house in the name of the Lord , the God of Israel
&quot; In it I will set up the ark of the covenant , in which is the covenant of the Lord , which he made with the children of Israel
And Solomon stood before the altar of the Lord in the presence of the congregation of Israel , and lifted up his hand
And Solomon made a table of brass , five cubits long , five cubits wide , and three cubits high , in the house ; and he stood on the table , and knelt down before the congregation of Israel , and lifted up his hand to heaven
He said , &quot; Lord , God of Israel , there is no God above and below you , and you have made a covenant of mercy with the servants who are before you .
&quot; The word which you swore to your servant David my father , has now been fulfilled ; and as it is today , your word has been fulfilled , and your hand has been fulfilled
&quot; Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel , which you have promised to your servant David my father , saying , &apos; If your sons will be prudent in their conduct , and will keep my law , as you did before me , they will not forsake the seat of the kingdom of Israel ; and now please prove it . &apos; 
&quot; Lord , God of Israel , fulfill what you have promised your servant David ,
&quot; Doth God dwell with the people of the earth ? Behold , the heavens and the heavens above are not enough for you to dwell in ; and what about this house which I have built ?
&quot; But pray to the Lord , my God , to hear the prayers of his servants , and to hear the prayers of his servants before you
&quot; Look at this house , which you have promised to set up for your name , day and night ; and listen to the prayers of your servants to this place .
&quot; When your servants and your people Israel pray here , hear from heaven your abode , and hear , and forgive ;
&quot; If a man sins against his neighbor , he is called to swear , and comes to this house , and swears before your altar
Hear thou from heaven , and judge thy servant , and make the wicked to be guilty , and recompense him according to what he hath done , and make him righteous , and give him according to his righteousness
&quot; If your people Israel sin against you and lose in the sight of their enemies , and turn their hearts to confess your name , and pray to you in this house
Listen from heaven , and forgive the sins of your people Israel , that they may return to the land which you gave them and their fathers
Your people have sinned against you , and you have punished them , and the heavens have not been shut up to rain ; and if they pray to this place , and confess your name , then leave their sins .
&quot; Listen in heaven , and forgive the sins of your servants and of your people Israel , that they may do righteousness , and teach them , and rain rain on your land , which you have given to your people for a possession
If there be famine , plague , drought , mold , locusts , grasshoppers in the land , or if there be enemies in the land , and cities are besieged , whatever plague or disease befall them
&quot; Your people , Israel , or all of you , or one person , will lift up their hands to this house , knowing that the plague is very grievous , whatever you pray , whatever you pray
Forgive , O Lord , from the heavens , wherein thou art ; for thou knowest the hearts , and doest to them as men do ; but thou knowest the hearts of the world .
that they may fear thee for a lifetime , and walk in thy ways , in the land which thou hast given to our fathers
&quot; The foreigners , who are not of your people Israel , come from afar and pray to this house for your great name and for your mighty hand , and for your outstretched arm ,
&quot; Listen to your dwelling place from heaven , and do as the Gentiles have prayed ; that all the people of the earth may know your name , and fear you , as your people Israel did , and that they may know that the house which I have built is called under your name
If your people are sent to fight against your enemies , wherever they may go , pray to the city of your choice , and to the house that I have built for your name .
Listen to their prayers and supplications from heaven , that they may be victorious
And if thy people sin against thee , thou shalt be angry with them , and shalt deliver them into captivity unto the enemy , far or near
&quot; If they remember sin in the land of captivity , and turn their hearts , and ask You , saying , &apos; We have sinned , we have rebelled , we have done evil ,
&quot; If they turn to You in all their hearts in the land of captivity , and return to their own land , which You have given to their fathers , and to the city which You have chosen , and to the house which I have built in Your name ,
&quot; Listen to the prayers of your people in your dwelling-place from heaven , and forgive them their sins ,
&quot; Now , O my God , open your eyes and listen to the prayers that are offered here ,
Arise , O Lord God , with the ark of your power , and enter into the place of rest ; let your priests be clothed with salvation , and let your saints rejoice .
O Lord God , do not despise your anointed , but remember the kindness of your servant David ,
And when Solomon &apos;s prayer was finished , fire came down from heaven , and consumed the burnt offerings and other sacrifices ; and the glory of the Lord filled the house
&quot; For the glory of the Lord has filled the house of the Lord , so that the priests cannot enter it
When the glory of the Lord was in the temple , when the fire came down , all Israel saw it , and bowed down and worshipped on the rock , and thanked the Lord , saying , &quot; The Lord is good , and His mercy endures forever . &quot;
The king and all the people offered sacrifices before the Lord
And the king of Solomon sacrificed with twenty and two thousand bulls and twelve thousand sheep : and the king and all the people did the service of the house of God
The priests stood and ministered , and the Levites took the instruments of the Lord , which King David had made , and praised the Lord through the Levites ; and the priest shouted before the people , and all Israel stood
And Solomon sanctified the first house of the house of the Lord in the midst of it for the copper altar which he had made , wherein he offered burnt offerings and the fat of peace offerings
And it came to pass at that time , that Solomon and all Israel , all the children of Israel , from the mouth of Hamath even unto the little river of Egypt , were gathered together , and were gathered together in assembly , to keep the Sabbath seven days
A solemn meeting shall be established on the eighth day , on the seventh day of the service of the altar , and on the seventh day of the feast .
And it came to pass on the thirty-threeth day of July , that the king sent away all the people , and they rejoiced in their hearts , and went every man to his house , because they saw the favour which the LORD had bestowed upon David and upon Solomon and upon Israel his people .
Solomon created the house of the Lord and the kingdom , and in the house of the Lord and the kingdom he did all that was in his heart according to the law
Then the Lord appeared to Solomon at night , and said to him , &quot; I have heard your prayer , and I have chosen this place for my sanctuary
&quot; If I make the heavens not to rain , or the locusts to eat the fruit of the land , or the plague to spread among my people ,
These are the sons of my name : if they humble themselves , and pray , and seek My face , and turn away from their evil deeds , I will hear from heaven , and forgive their sins , and heal their land .
&quot; I will open my eyes and listen to the prayers that I offer here
&quot; Now I have chosen this house , holy and holy , that my name may be in it forever ; and my eyes and my heart shall be there forever .
&quot; If you do what your father David did before me , and do all that I have commanded you , and keep my statutes ,
&quot; I will strengthen your kingdom , as I said in the covenant I made with your father David , saying , &apos; Your sons will be kings over Israel forever and ever .
&quot; If you turn away from the commandments of your law which I have commanded you , and go to worship other gods
&quot; And I will bring forth the roots of Israel out of the land which I have given them , and the sanctuary which I have sanctified for My name , and I will forsake it , and make it a mockery and a derision among the people
&quot; Those who pass by in the future will be astonished at how the Lord has done to this place and to this house , even though it is very high .
And they shall say , It is because they have forsaken the LORD , the God of their fathers , the God that brought them out of the land of Egypt , to come near unto other gods , and to worship and serve him ; therefore hath the LORD brought upon them all this evil
&quot; For twenty years Solomon built the house of the Lord and the king &apos;s palace
Then Solomon rebuilt the cities which He sent to him , and the children of Israel lived therein .
And Solomon went to Hamathoba , and took the place
Solomon built Damoah in the wilderness , and built all the cities of the storehouses of Hama .
And they built the upper chambers of Bethlehem and the lower chambers of Bethlehem as a shelter , with walls , with gates , and with bars
and to build Barah , and all the cities of the storehouses , and the cities of the army of horsemen , which they may build with Jerusalem and Lebanon , and with all the kingdoms which they may rule ;
And concerning the remnant of the land , which were not of the children of Israel , the Hittites , the Amorites , the Beer-shebaites , the Hivites , the Jebusites ,
&quot; For Solomon , who was not destroyed by the children of Israel , chose their descendants to be slaves to suffering , even to this day
&quot; But the sons of Israel did not make Solomon their servants , but his soldiers , captains of armies , captains of chariots , and captains of horses
The king of Solomon had two hundred and fifty governors and overseers
Then Solomon took the daughters of Pharaoh out of the city of David , and went up to the house which Solomon had built for him ; for Solomon said , &quot; The place where the ark of the Lord is is is a holy place ; therefore my wife shall not dwell in the house of David king of Israel
Solomon offered a burnt offering to the Lord on the altar of the Lord , which he had built before the porch
And on the sabbath day , and on the month Sabbath , and on the third day of the year , the feast of the unleavened , and on the seventy-seventh day , and on the tent of tents , according to the commandment of Moses , to offer every day the sacrifice which is due
Solomon appointed divisions of the priests according to the commandment of David his father , that they should serve each other , and that the Levites should do their duties , and praise the Lord , as they did every day before the priests , and that the guards should guard the gates according to the divisions , as David the man of God had commanded
Neither did the priests nor the Levites disobey what the king commanded them to do , whether in the treasury or in anything else
Solomon built the house of the Lord from the foundation to the day of his success , and all the work was done , and the house of the Lord was completed
Then Solomon went to Ezun-cabe and Elah by the sea in Edom .
And he sent his servants , and brought the ships , and the servants that were acquainted with the sea , to Solomon : and they came to Ophir with Solomon &apos;s servants , and they received forty and five hundred , and he received gold , and brought it to king Solomon
And when Sheba heard the fame of Solomon , she came to Jerusalem to inquire of him in difficult words : and there were many with him , and camels carrying incense , and precious stones , and much gold ; and when he saw Solomon , he spoke to him all that was in his heart .
Solomon answered all that he had asked , and there was not a word that he could not understand or answer
Queen Sheba saw Solomon &apos;s wisdom , and the palace that he had built
And it came to pass , when they saw the delicacies of the seats , and that the people sat in rows , and the servants stood by them , and their garments , and the wine-making and the wine-making garments , and they saw him on the steps of the house of the Lord , that they were astonished that God would not forsake him
He said to the king , &quot; What I have heard in my country concerning your affairs and your wisdom is true .
&quot; I did not believe those words until I saw them with my own eyes , and I knew not half of the wisdom of Yours , nor half of what men have told me . Your signs are greater than the fame that I have heard .
Blessed are thy servants , and thy servants , who stand before thee continually , and hear thy wisdom .
Blessed is the Lord your God , who has pleased you , and has made you sit in His throne , and has made you king for the Lord your God ; for your God loves Israel , and will uphold them forever ; therefore make you their king , that you may do righteousness
Then the queen of Sheba delivered unto the king of Solomon one hundred and twenty gold and jewelry , and a great multitude of spices , which he had given to the king ; and there was no more such thing after him .
And the servants of Hilan , and the servants of Solomon , brought gold out of Ophir , and brought fir trees and stones ,
The king made a table for the house of the Lord and the king &apos;s palace out of acacia trees , and a harp for the singers , which the land of Judah had never seen .
Then the king of Solomon gave him his present , and all that the queen of Sheba had brought him , and all that he had desired ; and the queen and her servants returned to their land
And of the gold that Solomon received every year were six hundred sixty and sixty and six .
And there was gold brought in by merchants ; and the kings of Arabia and the governors of their provinces brought gold and silver to Solomon
And the king of Solomon made two hundred faces of gold out of the hammer , and six hundred shekels of gold for each face .
And three hundred faces of shields were made of gold hammered , and three hundred shekels of gold for each face ; and they were set in the house of the forest of Lebanon .
The king made a great throne out of ivory , and wrapped it in gold .
There were six steps to the Throne , and a bench of gold ; and it was joined to the Throne ; and there was a mantle on either side of the Throne , and near to the mantle stood two lions .
There stood twelve lions on the six steps , two on each floor , one on the left and one on the right . This was not done in all the nations .
All the drinking vessels of the king of Solomon were of gold ; and all the vessels of the house of Lebanon were of pure gold ; and in the days of Solomon silver was no measure
For the king &apos;s ships were sent to him with the servants of the Philistines , and he brought back gold , silver , ivory , monkeys , and foxes every three years .
The riches and wisdom of king Solomon are greater than the kings of the earth .
All the kings of the earth seek Solomon , to hear the words of God , which have given him wisdom
And they brought gifts of gold , and silver , and clothing , and weapons , and spices , and horses ; and there was an ordinance every year .
Solomon had four thousand tents of horses with chariots , and twelve thousand horsemen ; and they were set up in the cities of Tune and Jerusalem , the king &apos;s place
Solomon ruled over the kings , from the great river to the land of Philistine , and straight to the border of Egypt
And the king made silver as a stone in Jerusalem , and cedar as a palm tree in the high places
Some people came from Egypt and other countries to chase horses for Solomon
Have not the rest of Solomon &apos;s affairs been written from the beginning to the end in the book of Nathan the prophet , and in the prophecy of Ahijah the Hebrew , and in the counsel of Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar concerning Edom ?
Solomon reigned forty years in Jerusalem as king over all Israel
And Solomon slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David his father : and his son Rehoboam reigned in his stead
And he went to Shechem , because all the children of Israel came to Shechem to make him king
And Jeroboam the son of Nebuchadnezzar fled before the king of Solomon to Egypt , and lived there : and when he heard this , he came back from Egypt
And the men of Israel sent messengers to him , and he came to him with all the people of Israel , and spoke to him
&quot; Your father has burdened us with a heavy yoke . Now , please , lighten the burden of our burden , and we will serve you
And he said unto them , Come again unto me on the third day : and the people went away .
And in the days of Solomon the father of Rehoboam , king Rehoboam and the elders who were before him consulted with them , saying , What counsel have you given me , that I may return to this people ?
The elders said to him , &quot; If the king is kind to these people , and pleases them , and answers them with good words , they will always be servants of the king
But the king did not use the counsel of the elders , but consulted with the young men who grew up with him , and stood before him .
&quot; The people said to me , &apos; Your father has put us on a heavy yoke , and please make it easier for us . What idea have you given me , and I will respond to them
Then he said to the young men who grew up with him , &quot; The people said to the king , &apos; Your father has put us on a heavy yoke , and please make us lighter . &apos; Thus will the king say to them , &apos; My thumb is thicker than my father &apos;s waist
&quot; My father has yoked you with a heavy yoke , and I will yoke you with a more heavy yoke . My father will scourge you with a whip , and I will scourge you with a scorpion .
And Jeroboam and all the people did according to that which the king of Jeroboam said , &quot; You shall come again to me on the third day , and they will come on the third day
The king answered them with severe words , and not with the counsel of the elders
And he said unto them according to the counsel of the young men , My father hath yoked you with a heavy yoke , and I will yoke you with a greater yoke ; and my father hath wounded you with a whip , and I will whip you with a scorpion
The king refused to obey the people , because it was from God , to test the words of Yahweh , which Ahijah the Shelonite spoke to Jeroboam the son of Ner ,
And when the people of Israel saw that the king did not obey them , they said unto the king , What portion have we with David , that we have no concern with the sons of Jesse ? O Israel , go every man to his own house , O house of David ; and all Israel returned to their own houses .
Only the children of Israel , who dwell in the cities of Judah , did Rehoboam reign over them
And king Rehoboam sent Hadoran , the ruler of the people , to the children of Israel , and they struck him with stones ; and he hurried in his car , and fled to Jerusalem .
Thus have Israel rebelled against the house of David , even to this day
And when Rehoboam came to Jerusalem , he gathered together all the people of Judah , and the house of Benjamin , an hundred and eighty thousand men , chosen men to fight against the children of Israel , that they might take away the land and return to themselves
But the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah the man of God , saying ,
Go and tell Rehoboam the son of Solomon king of Judah , and all Israel that dwell in Judah in Benjamin , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord ; Ye shall not go up and fight with your brethren ; but go every man to his own house , for it is mine ; and they shall hear the word of the Lord , and shall not return and fight with Jeroboam .
And he lived in Jerusalem , and built cities in the land of Judah
Construction of Bethlehem , Ethan and Tikoa for security
Bermuda , Sogo , Aduran
Gath , Marisa , Siph
Adolescence , Lagos , Ashikaga
Zorah , and Jaalun , and Hebron : these are the strong cities of Judah and Benjamin .
And Roban strengthened the security of every place , and put in it captains , and prepared food , oil , and wine
He prepared shields and guns in the cities , and made them strong ; and Judah and Benjamin were his inheritance .
The priests and the Levites from all the land of Israel came to Rehoboam from all sides
The Levites left their suburbs and their possessions , and came to Judah and Jerusalem , because Jeroboam and his sons rejected them , and did not allow them to serve the Lord as priests
And Jeroboam made a priest for the high place , and for the devil , and for the calf that he had cast ,
&quot; All the tribes of Israel who sought the Lord , the God of Israel , came with the Levites to Jerusalem to worship the Lord , the God of their fathers
Thus he strengthened the great nation of Judah , and strengthened for three years the sons of Solomon , because they kept the way of David and Solomon .
And he took to wife Mahara the daughter of Jelim the son of David , and Abiah the daughter of Eliab the son of Jesse ,
And of him were born Jeush , and Shemaiah , and Zahan ,
And afterward he took Magah , the daughter of Absalom , the daughter of Uriel , and from him he brought forth Abijah , and Asiaph , and Shessah , and Shelomith
And he took eighteen wives , and set up sixty concubines , and begat twenty-eight sons , and sixty daughters : but he loved the daughter of Absalom , Magah , more than any other concubine .
And Abijah the son of Rimachah became prince over his brethren , because they desired to make him king again .
And he was wise in his ways , and spread out his sons throughout all the strong cities of Judah and Benjamin , and gave them much food , and sought for them more wives
And the land of Rehoboam was strong , and when he was strong , he forsook the law of the LORD , and all Israel followed him
In the fifth year of king Rehoboam , Zechariah king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem , because the king and the people had sinned against the Lord
He brought with him a thousand two hundred chariots , and 60,000 horsemen , and with him the Levites , and the Sukkites , and the Gothites , who came out of Egypt ;
And he took the strong city of Judah , and came to Jerusalem
Then the chiefs of Judah were gathered together in Jerusalem because of Shezar ; and the prophet Shemaiah went to Rehoboam and to all the chiefs , and said to them , Thus saith the Lord ; Because you have forsaken me , therefore have I put you in the hand of Shezar
Then said the king and all the princes of Israel , &quot; The Lord is righteous
And the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah , when the LORD saw their selfishness , saying , &quot; Behold , they are selfish , and I will not destroy them ; I will save them a little ; I will not put my wrath in Jerusalem by the hand of Sheba .
&quot; But they will be servants to Sheba , that they may know what is the difference between serving Me and those who serve the Gentiles
Then the king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem , and took away all the treasures of the house of the Lord and of the king &apos;s house , and the gold shields of Solomon
And the king of Rehoboam made a bronze shield for the gold shield , and gave it to the captain of the guard , who guarded the gates of the king &apos;s house
&quot; Whenever the king enters the house of the Lord , the guard takes the shield , and brings it back to the house of the guard .
And the wrath of the LORD was turned away in the days of the king &apos;s selfishness , and he would not destroy him ; and there was good in Judah
And the king of Rehoboam reigned in Jerusalem forty-one years at the time of his ascension , seventeen years in the city which the LORD had chosen of the tribes of Israel to name him : and his mother &apos;s name was Naamah , a son of Ammon
For he hath sinned , because he hath not set his heart to seek the LORD
Have not the acts of the prophet written in the book of Shemaiah the prophet and in the book of Edo the prophet , from the beginning to the end , wherein he fought with Jeroboam continually ?
And he slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David ; and Abijah his son reigned in his stead
the eighteenth year of king Jeroboam ; and Abijah ascended to the throne of Judah
And he reigned three years in Jerusalem : and his mother &apos;s name was Micaiah , the daughter of Uri the Gibeonite , who often fought with Jeroboam
There was a time when the chosen army of Abijah was forty thousand men , all men of valor , and Jeroboam chose eighty thousand men of might , all men of might , to fight against Abijah .
And Abijah stood on mount Shebamah in the plains of Ephraim , and said , Hear me , Jeroboam and all Israel
&quot; For the Lord , the God of Israel , has made a covenant of salt , to give the kingdom of Israel forever to David and to his sons ; do you not know ?
But the servant of Solomon the son of David , Jeroboam the son of Nethan , rebelled against his master
Then gathered together against him a band of ungodly robbers , and assaulted Roban the son of Solomon , when he was yet weak , and could not stand against them
&quot; Now you intend to oppose the kingdom of the Lord , which the sons of David ruled ; and there are many among you , and in it is a golden calf which Jeroboam made for you as God .
&quot; You are not the descendants of Aaron , and the Levites , the priests of the Lord who expelled him , and you are not the priests for yourselves according to the wickedness of the Gentiles ; and whoever takes one bull and seven rams , and separates them , then you are the priests of the gods of vanity .
&quot; As for us , the Lord is our God , and we have not forsaken Him ; and we are the sons of Aaron , and the Levites do all their duties as priests to the Lord
&quot; You shall offer burnt offerings to the Lord morning and evening , and burn sweet incense , and place your cakes on a table of gold ; and there shall be lamps and lamps of gold ; and they shall be lit up every night , because we have obeyed the commandment of the Lord our God ; but you have forsaken him .
&quot; For God is our leader , and there are priests of God among us ; and the trumpet speaks to you with a loud voice : O Israel , fight not against the God of the Lord , the God of your fathers ; for you will not prosper .
And Jeroboam pitched behind Judah ; and the children of Israel pitched before Judah , and pitched behind Judah .
Then the Jews looked back , and behold , there were enemies before and after them ; and they cried unto the LORD , and the priest cried out :
And when they cried , God defeated Jeroboam and all Israel before Abijah and the Jews
The children of Israel fled before the Jews , and God delivered them into the hand of the Jews
And Abijah and his army slew the children of Israel greatly ; and there were fifty thousand men of valour that fell to the sword .
At that time the children of Israel were subdued , and the children of Judah were victorious , because they trusted in the Lord God of their fathers
And Abijah pursued after Jeroboam , and took his cities , even Bethlehem , and the cities of Bethlehem , and Jeshanah , and the cities of Jeshanah , and the cities of Ephraim , and the cities of Ephraim .
And in the days of Abijah Jeroboam was no more strong ; and the LORD struck him , and he died .
And Abijah waxed strong , and took fourteen wives and concubines , and begat twenty-two sons and sixteen daughters
The rest of the acts of Abijah and his sayings were written in the book of the prophet Edo .
And Abijah slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David ; and Asa his son reigned in his stead ten years in the land .
And Asa did that which was good in the sight of the LORD his God
Take away the altar of the gods of the nations , and the high altar , and break down the pillars , and cut down the figurines ;
commanded the Jews to seek the Lord , the God of their fathers , and to obey His laws and commandments
And the high places and the images of the sun were removed from the cities of Judah ; and the land was at peace .
And in Judah were built fortified cities ; and there was no war in the land for many years , because the Lord had given him peace
And he said unto the Jews , We will build these cities round about , walls , and towers , and gates , and bars ; and the land belongeth unto us , because we seek the LORD our God , and we seek him , and he hath given us peace in all our quarters : and they shall be built , and all things shall be accomplished .
And the army of Asa was thirty thousand men of Judah with shields and swords ; and the army of Benjamin with shields and bows was twenty-eight thousand ; and they were mighty men of valour .
And Shelah king of Goshen went out against the Jews , with a hundred thousand men of war , and three hundred chariots , and came to the city of Malisha
So Asa went out , and fought with him , and pitched against each other in the valley of Shephelah in the land of Malisha .
And Asa cried unto the LORD his God , and said , O LORD , only thou canst help the weak above the strong ; O LORD our God , help us , for we rely on thee in thy name to attack this great army ; O LORD , thou art our God , and thou wilt not let any man prevail over thee .
Then the LORD defeated the Philistines before Asa and Judah , and they fled .
And Asa and his army pursued them straight to Gilead ; and many of them were slain , and they could not be strengthened : for they had taken away much wealth for their defeat before the LORD and his army .
And he broke the cities that were round about Gilead , and the LORD made all the people of Gilead afraid ; and the Jews took all the cities into captivity , because of the multitude of their riches .
Then he destroyed the herds , and took away many sheep and camels , and returned to Jerusalem
The Spirit of God touched Azariah the son of Odysseus
He came out to meet Asa and said to him , &quot; Listen to me , Asa and Judah and Benjamin , saying , &apos; If you obey the Lord , the Lord will be with you ; if you seek Him , you will find Him ; if you turn away from Him , He will turn away from you
For a long time have the children of Israel not believed in the true God , nor in the priests who were not instructed , nor in the law
But when they returned to the Lord , the God of Israel , in the hour of distress , they sought him , and he was found by them
Then there will be no peace for those who go in and out , nor for the inhabitants of the nations .
The nations shall attack the nations , and the cities shall attack the cities , and they shall destroy one another ; for God has spoiled them with all kinds of calamity
&quot; Be strong now , and not weak ; for you shall be rewarded for what you do .
And when Asa heard these words , and the prophecy of Azariah the prophet , the son of Odysseus , he arose with great courage , and took away the abominations in all Judah , and in all Benjamin , and in all the cities which he had taken in the land of Ephraim , and built the altar of the LORD again in the porch of the house of the LORD
And they gathered together all Judah and Benjamin , and the Ephraimites , and the Manassehs , and the Simeonites that dwelled among them ; and many of the children of Israel returned to Asa , because they saw the Lord his God with him .
And it came to pass in March 15 , that they were all gathered together at Jerusalem
On that day they offered to the Lord seven hundred oxen and seven thousand sheep out of the captivity which they had taken
They made a covenant to seek the Lord , the God of their fathers , with all their heart and with all their soul
&quot; Everyone who does not seek the Lord , the God of Israel , male or female , of any size , shall be put to death
Then they cried with a loud voice , and blew their trumpets , and swore unto the LORD
The people of Judah rejoiced in the oaths they had made , because they had sworn with all their heart to seek the Lord , and the Lord was found among them , and he gave them peace in all the land .
And the king Asa denied the throne of his mother Magdalene , because he had made Asher the detestable idol . And Asa cut down his idols , and broke them , and burned them on the banks of the stream .
But the high places have not yet been removed from Israel ; but the heart of Asa was faithful all his life
And Asa presented all that his father had sanctified , and all that he had sanctified , silver and gold , and vessels , to the house of God
From this time even to the thirty-fifth year of Asa there was no battle
In thirty-six years Asa king of Israel came up against Judah , and built Ramah , that no man should come out of Asanah king of Judah
Then Asa took silver and gold out of the treasury of the house of the Lord and of the king &apos;s house , and sent it to Benhadad king of Aram , who lived in Damascus .
&quot; Your father made a covenant with my father , and I will also make a covenant with you ; and now I will give you gold and silver ; so that you may break your covenant with the king of Israel , and let him go from me
Then Benhadad listened to the words of king Asa , and sent the captains of the army to attack the cities of Israel , and they struck Eun , Dan , and Abram , and all the storehouses of Naphtali
And when Bashar heard it , he ceased to work , and did not build Ramah
Then king Asa led all Judah , and sent all the stones and timber that he had used to build the house of Ramah out of Bashan , to build the houses of Gabah and Mizpah
Then Hanani came to Asa king of Judah and said to him , &quot; Because you have not relied on the Lord your God , because you have relied on King Aram , the army of King Aram has departed from your hand
&quot; Isn &apos;t the way of the ancients greater than the army of men , and the army of chariots and horses greater than the army of men ? Only because you rely on the Lord , He will deliver them into your hand
&quot; The eyes of the Lord are upon all the earth , to show great power to those who are faithful in His heart . You are foolish in doing this , and afterwards you will have battle .
So Asa was angry at the first sight , and imprisoned him ; and he also mistreated some people
All that Asa did from the beginning to the end is written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel
And it came to pass in thirty-nine years , that Asa king of Judah had a sickness on his feet , and it was very grievous ; and in the time of sickness there was no cry to the Lord , but to the physician .
And he died forty and one years as king , and slept with his fathers
And he was buried in the tomb that he had dug in David &apos;s city , and laid on his bed , and his bed was filled with all kinds of sweet incense , sweet incense according to the manner of incense ; and many things were burned for him .
And Jehoshaphat the son of Asa reigned in his stead , and was mighty and strong , and guarded the children of Israel
&quot; They shall set up their armies in all the strong cities of Judah , and their guards in the land of Judah , and in the cities of Ephraim , which Asa his father possessed
&quot; The Lord is with Jehoshaphat , because he did not seek Balak in the way of his father David ,
&quot; He seeks only the God of his father , and obeys his commandments , and does not obey the ways of the children of Israel .
Therefore the LORD strengthened his kingdom , and all the people of Judah gave to him a ransom ; and Jehoshaphat was great in glory and in riches
He was exalted in the way of the Lord , and he removed from Judah all the high places and the statues
In the third year of his reign he sent his servants to teach the people in all the cities of Judah , to Benaiah , and to Obed , and to Zechariah , and to Nathaniel , and to Micaiah .
And the sons of Shemaiah , and Nethaniah , and Sibadiah , and Asahel , and Shemiramoth , and Jonathan , and Adonijah , and Dobiah , and Hambadonijah , and Elishama the priest , and Joram ,
They went through all the cities of Judah , teaching the people with the law of the Lord
For the LORD hath made all the nations round about Judah afraid , and have not dared to fight against Jehoshaphat
Some of the Philistines gave gifts to Jehoshaphat , Nagorn silver , and the Arabs gave him seven thousand and seven hundred sheep and seven thousand and seven hundred goats
Joseph grew stronger and stronger , and built camps and cities of goods in Judah .
He had many works in the cities of Judah ; and there were warriors in Jerusalem , mighty warriors .
The number of them according to their families is as follows : The captain of the thousands of the children of Judah , and the captain of the mighty warriors , were thirty thousand .
The second was Jehoiachin the captain of the thousands , a mighty man of twenty-eight thousand .
The second was Amaziah the son of Shechemiel , who sacrificed himself for the LORD , and led two and twenty thousand mighty men of war .
The children of Benjamin , Elijah the mighty warrior , commanded twenty thousand men with arrows and shields .
The second was Joseph , who commanded 18,000 men to prepare for war .
&quot; They are all servants of the king , and those who are not in the king &apos;s strong city in all Judah
And Jehoshaphat was greatly honored and rich ; and he became a kinsman with Ahab
A few years later he went down to Samaria to meet Ahasuerus ; and Ahasuerus slaughtered many sheep and goats for him and for those who followed him , and persuaded him to go with him to Ramoth of Gilead .
And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat king of Judah , Willest thou go with me to take Latham of Gilead ? And he answered and said , Thou shalt not be divided from me , neither shall my people be divided from thy people ; but they shall fight with thee
And Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel , Ask the Lord first
Then the king of Israel gathered together four hundred prophets , and said to them , &quot; Can we go up and take Latham of Gilead , or can we not ? &quot; They said , &quot; We can go up , for God will deliver the city into the king &apos;s hand
And Jehoshaphat said , Is there not here a prophet of the Lord , that we may ask him
Then the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat , &quot; There is another man , Micaiah the son of Nunrah , whom we can call upon the Lord ; but I hate him , because he speaks no good words , nor speaks evil words , concerning the prophecy which I have spoken . &quot; And Jehoshaphat said , &quot; The king has no need to say this
Then the king of Israel called a captain of the guard , and said to him , &quot; Go quickly and call Micaiah the son of Nunrah
And the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah sat upon a seat in array in the open field before the gate of Samaria ; and all the prophets prophesied before them
And the house of Zedekiah the son of Kenanah made two horns of iron , saying , Thus saith the Lord ; Thou shalt strike the children of Aram with this horn , even to the point of their destruction
Thus prophesied all the prophets , saying , &quot; If you go up to Ramoth of Gilead , you will surely win ; for the Lord will deliver it into the hand of the king .
Then the messengers of Micaiah who came to him said to Micaiah , &quot; The prophets have spoken to the king in the same voice , and it is better for you to speak a similar word to them and speak a good word
And Micaiah said , &quot; I swear by the Lord of everlasting life , and what my God says , I will say
And Micaiah came to the king , and the king said unto him , Micaiah , whether we go up and take Latham of Gilead , or not , he said , Go up , and ye shall surely prevail ; and the enemy shall be delivered into your hand .
&quot; The king said to him , &quot; I have commanded you several times , but you have not spoken to me the truth in the name of the Lord
Then Micaiah said , &quot; I have seen the people of Israel scattered in the mountains like sheep without shepherds , &quot; and the Lord said , &quot; These people have no master , and they will go home in peace to their families .
Then the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat , &quot; Have I not told you that this man speaks no good words , nor speaks any evil words , concerning the prophecy I have spoken ?
And Micaiah said , &quot; Listen to the word of the Lord ; for I have seen the Lord sitting on the throne , and all the hosts of heaven standing around him .
Thus saith the LORD ; Thus saith the one that seeketh to persuade Ahab king of Israel to flee to Latham of Gilead ; and thus saith the one that seeketh to persuade Ahab king of Israel to flee
Then a spirit came out , and stood before the Lord , and said , &quot; I am going to seduce him ; &quot; and the Lord asked him , &quot; What law do you use ? &quot;
He said , &quot; I am going to be a spirit of lies in the mouths of his prophets , &quot; and the Lord said , &quot; You will be able to seduce him , and you will do so .
&quot; Now the Spirit of lying has entered into the mouths of your prophets in the Lord , and the Lord has ordained evil for you
Then Zedekiah the son of Kenanah came before the house of Zedekiah , and struck Micaiah &apos;s face , and said , &quot; Is the Spirit of the Lord gone from there to speak to you ?
And Micaiah said , &quot; In the day when you enter the houses of refuge , you will see
Then the king of Israel said , &quot; Take Micaiah back , and give it to Uzziah and Joash the son of the king , saying ,
&quot; Then the king said , &quot; Put this man in prison , and make him suffer , and eat and drink not enough , and wait for me to return in peace and security
Then Micaiah said , &quot; If you return in peace , it is because the Lord has not spoken this word through me , &quot; and said , &quot; Listen , all you people
And Jehoshaphat king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah went up to Ramoth of Gilead
And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat , I will put on my new raiment , and thou shalt still put on the king &apos;s garment : and the king of Israel put on his new raiment , and they went up to the battle
And the king of Aram commanded the captains of the chariots , saying , &quot; You shall not fight with their captains , whether they be great or small , but with the king of Israel
And when the captain of the chariot saw Jehoshaphat , he said , This is the king of Israel ; and he turned and fought against him ; and when Jehoshaphat cried out , the LORD helped him , and God moved them to depart from him .
And when they saw that he was not the king of Israel , they turned and did not pursue him
Then there came a man with a bow , and shot at the king of Israel in the armor , and the king said to him who drove , &quot; I am severely wounded ; turn your car , and take me out of the way
The battle was fierce that day , and the king of Israel stood in his car against the children of Aram until the evening , and he died at the sunset .
Then Jehoshaphat king of Judah returned to Jerusalem in peace , and went into the palace
Then Jehu the son of Hanani came out to meet king Jehoshaphat , and said to him , &quot; Will you help the wicked , and love the one who hates the Lord ? Therefore the wrath of the Lord is upon you
Yet you also have good deeds , for you have removed the dolls from the land , and have set your heart on seeking God
And Joshua lived in Jerusalem , and afterward he went out among the people from Beersheba even unto the land of Ephraim , and guided the people unto the LORD God of their fathers
and set up judges in the strong cities of the land of Judah ,
And he said unto them , Be careful in what ye do : for ye judge not for man , but for the LORD ; and he shall be with you at the time of judgment .
Now therefore fear the Lord , and be careful : for the Lord our God is not wicked , neither is he presumptuous , neither is he bribed .
Then Jehoshaphat sent men from among the Levites , and from among the priests , and from among the elders of Israel , to judge for the Lord in Jerusalem , and to hear the arguments of the people , and returned to Jerusalem
And Jehoshaphat commanded them , saying , &quot; Have fear of the Lord , and be faithful , and do righteousness
&quot; If your brethren who dwell in the cities come to you for a dispute , or for bloodshed , or for breaking the law , the commandments , the statutes , the ordinances , you shall warn them , lest they sin against the Lord , so that His wrath may come upon you and upon your brethren , and so you will not be guilty .
&quot; The great priest Amaziah oversees you in all the affairs of the Lord ; and the prince of the tribe of Judah oversees you in all the affairs of the king ; and Zebadiah the son of Ismael oversees you ; and the Levites are overseers before you ; and you should be brave in your deeds ; that the Lord may be with the righteous .
And after this Moab and the children of Ammon and the Miunites came together against Jehoshaphat
And there came a man to report to Jehoshaphat , saying , There is a great army against thee from beyond the land of Aram , even to the east ; and now they are in Hazarib and Hamath , and they are in the land of Egypt .
Then Jehoshaphat was afraid , and sought the Lord , and proclaimed a fast throughout all Judah
Then the Jews gathered themselves together to seek the help of the Lord ; and in all the cities of Judah there came forth men to seek the help of the Lord
And Jehoshaphat stood in the midst of the congregation of Judah and Jerusalem before the new court of the house of the Lord
Saying , O LORD God of our fathers , art thou not the God of heaven , and the ruler of all the nations , and in thy hand is great power , and there is none that can withstand thee ?
&quot; Have you not , O God of ours , destroyed the inhabitants of this land before your people Israel , and given it to the seed of your friend Abraham for ever ?
&quot; They will dwell in this place , and they will build sanctuaries in your name , &quot;
&quot; If a calamity comes upon us , or a calamity of the sword , or a calamity of famine , and we stand before this house in the hour of distress , and cry to You , You will hear and save ; for Your name is in this house
&quot; When the children of Israel came out of the land of Egypt , you did not allow them to invade the children of Ammon , the children of Moab , and the children of Mount Siir , and they left them , and did not destroy them .
&quot; Behold , how they will retaliate against us to drive us out of your land , which you have given us for a possession
&quot; Do you not punish them , O God of ours , for we have no power to resist this who attacks our army , and we do not know how to do it , and our eyes are only on You ?
And all the people of Judah stood before the LORD , and their little ones , and their wives , and their children
Then came the Spirit of the Lord in the congregation to Jahaz , the son of Zacariah , the son of Benaiah , the grandson of Jeli , the firstborn of Mattaniah , the son of Asa the Levite ,
He said , &quot; Listen , all Judah , and the inhabitants of Jerusalem , and the king of Jehoshaphat ; Thus says the Lord to you : Fear not this great army , nor be afraid , for victory is not yours , but God &apos;s
Tomorrow you shall go down to meet the enemy , and they shall come up from the valley of Shezbol ; and you shall meet them in the valley before the wilderness of Jerubim
O Judah and Jerusalem , do not fight this time , but stand up , and see the salvation of the LORD for you : fear not , neither be afraid : for the LORD is with you tomorrow , when ye shall go out against the enemy .
Then Jehoshaphat fell on his face , and all Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem fell on their faces before the Lord , and worshipped the Lord
And all the Levites of the tribe of Kohath and of the tribe of Kohath rose up , and praised the LORD God of Israel with a loud voice
And it came to pass early the next day , that they arose and went out into the wilderness of Tikoa . And it came to pass at the time of their departure , that Jehoshaphat stood and said , &quot; Listen to me , O inhabitants of Judah and Jerusalem , that you may believe in the Lord your God , and that you may prosper ; and that you may believe in his prophets .
And after he had talked with the people , he set up singers to praise the Lord , and put them in holy garments , and walked before the army to praise the Lord , saying , &quot; Praise the Lord , for His mercy endures forever .
And it came to pass at the time when all the people sang praises , that the LORD sent foot soldiers to smite the children of Ammon , and the children of Moab , and the children of Tyre , which came to attack Judah ; and they were defeated .
For they rose up for the children of Ammon and for the children of Moab , and slew the men of mount Seir , and destroyed them ; and after they had destroyed the men of mount Seir , they slew one another .
And the Jews came to the tower of the wilderness , and looked at the great army , and saw bodies lying all over the earth , and none escaped .
And Joseph and his people came to collect the enemy &apos;s treasures ; and they saw many treasures and treasures in the bodies ; and they could not carry much of what they had taken away ; for they were many , and they collected them three days straight .
And it came to pass on the fourth day , that all the people were gathered together in the valley of Beer-sheba , wherein they praised the LORD : and the name of the place was called Beer-sheba to this day .
And the children of Judah and the people of Jerusalem returned to Jerusalem with joy and gladness ; and Jehoshaphat led them ; for the Lord had made them rejoice in the victory of their enemies
They played the harp and the psaltery and the trumpet , and came to Jerusalem , and entered the house of the Lord
The nations were terrified when they heard that the Lord had defeated the enemy of Israel
Thus shall the land of Jehoshaphat be at ease : for God hath given him peace in all its quarters
Jehoshaphat was thirty-five years old when he ascended to the throne of Judah , and he reigned twenty-five years in Jerusalem . His mother &apos;s name was Azubah , the daughter of Sherish
&quot; Joshaphat did as his father Asa did , and did righteousness in the sight of the Lord
Only the high places have not been destroyed , nor have the people set their hearts on the God of their fathers
The rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat , from beginning to end , were written in the book of Jehu the son of Hanani , which is in the book of the kings of Israel
Then Jehoshaphat king of Judah made peace with Ahaziah king of Israel ; and Ahaziah did great evil
And the second king &apos;s company built a ship for him ; and he built a ship in Ewang-cabe
Then Eliezer the son of Dodevah , the man of Malisha , prophesied to Jehoshaphat , saying , &quot; Because of your dealings with Ahaziah , the Lord will destroy what you have built , and the ship will certainly destroy , and it will not be able to go to him . &quot;
And Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David , in the sepulchre of his fathers : and Jehoram his son reigned in his stead
And Joram had brothers , Azariah the son of Jehoshaphat , and Jesse , and Zacariah , and Azariah , and Michael , and Shephatiah , the sons of Jehoshaphat king of Israel .
&quot; Their father will give them more gold and silver , and riches , and a strong city in the land of Judah ; but the kingdom will be given to Joram , because he is a great son
Then Jehoram rose up from his father &apos;s seat , and fought for himself , and slew with the sword all his brothers , and several of the princes of Israel
Jehoram was thirty-two years old when he ascended , and reigned eight years in Jerusalem .
He walked in the way of the kings of Israel , as the house of Ahab did ; for he took the daughter of Ahab as his wife , and did that which was evil in the eyes of the Lord .
&quot; But the Lord will not destroy David &apos;s house because of the covenant He made with David , but He will give him and his sons light forever , as He has promised them
And in the days of Joram the Edomites rebelled against Judah , and went out of his power , and reigned themselves .
And Joram rose up at night , and the captain of the host , and all the chariots , and attacked the Edomites that were besieged against him , and the captain of the chariots
Thus the children of Edom rebelled against Judah , and departed from his authority , even to this day ; and the children of Reuben rebelled at that time , because they had forsaken the Lord , the God of their fathers
And he built high places in the mountains of Judah , and made the inhabitants of Jerusalem to commit adultery , and to tempt the Jews
Eliada the prophet believed and said to Joram , &quot; Thus says the Lord , the God of your father David , because you are not able to do the way of your father Joseph and of Asa king of Judah
&quot; It is the way of the kings of Israel , that they committed adultery , as did the house of Ahab , and that they killed your fathers and your brothers who were better than you .
&quot; Therefore the Lord will bring a great calamity upon your people , and upon your wives , and upon your children , and upon all your possessions
&quot; Your intestines will be sick , and the day will be heavy , and your intestines will fall down .
Then the LORD stirred up the Philistines , and the Aramites near Goshen , to attack Joram
And they came up against Judah , and entered into the land , and took away all the treasures of the king &apos;s house , and his wives and his children ; and they left not a son , save Jehoash his little son .
And it came to pass after these things , that the Lord made Joram &apos;s intestines sick with an incurable disease
He suffered from the disease for a long time , and after two years his intestines fell down , and he died of the disease , and his people burned no good for him , as they had burned for their fathers .
&quot; Joram was thirty-two years old when he ascended to the throne , and he reigned eight years in Jerusalem . He died without a name ; and they buried him in the city of David , but not in the tombs of the kings
And Ahaziah the son of Tyre , the inhabitant of Jerusalem , reigned in his stead ; for the men of war that came with the Aramites to the camp had slain all the elders of Ahaziah ; and Ahaziah the son of Tyre , king of Judah , reigned in his stead
And Ahaziah was forty-two years old when he ascended to the throne ; and he reigned one year in Jerusalem : and his mother &apos;s name was Ahaziah , the daughter of Amri .
And Ahaziah did the way of the house of Ahaziah , because his mother had given him counsel , and made him do evil .
He did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD , as did the house of Ahab : for after the death of his father there was a man of the house of Ahab who had given him counsel , that he might perish .
He listened to the counsel of the house of Ahab , and went to Ramoth of Gilead to fight with Hazer king of Aram , the son of Ahab king of Israel ; and the children of Aram wounded Joram
And Joram returned to Jerusalem , and healed the wounds that he had suffered in the battle of Latham with Ahaziah king of Aram , and went down to see Joram the son of Ahaziah king of Judah , because he was sick .
And when Ahaziah went to meet Joram , he was slain ; for it was of God &apos;s own accord ; for when he came , he went out with Joram to smite Jehu the son of Nineveh , whom the Lord anointed to cut off from the house of Ahaziah
And it came to pass , when Jehu had condemned the house of Ahasuerus , that he met the princes of Judah , and the sons of Ahasuerus , who served Ahasuerus , and slew them all
And Ahaziah hid himself in Samaria , and Jehu sought him ; and they took him , and brought him unto Jehu , and slew him , and buried him , because they said , He is the son of Jehoshaphat , the seer of the Lord ; and so the house of Ahaziah was powerless to keep the kingdom
And when Ahaziah &apos;s mother Ahaziah saw that his son was dead , she arose and destroyed the kingdom of Judah
But Jehoshaphat the daughter of the king took Joash the son of Ahaziah out of the prince who had been slain , and hid him and his mother in the bedroom , the daughter of the king of Jordan , the sister of Ahaziah , and the wife of Jehied the priest , and kept Joash , and sheltered herself from Ahaziah , lest he should be slain
Joash hid himself in the temple six years with them ; and Artaiah took the throne .
In the seventh year Jehoiada strengthened himself , and called Azariah the son of Jehoiada , the son of Ishmael , the son of Jehoiachin , the son of Obadiah , the son of Azariah , the son of Azariah , and Elishaph the son of Shikkiel , and made a covenant with them
And they went through Judah , and gathered together the Levites and the elders of Israel from all the cities of Judah to Jerusalem
Then Jehoiada said to them , &quot; Behold , the sons of the king will be kings , as the Lord promised the sons of David
And he said to them , &quot; You shall do this ; and the priests and the Levites shall keep the doors of the sabbath one third of the time .
A third part shall be in the king &apos;s house , and a third part in the gate of the foundation , and all the people shall be in the house of the Lord
&quot; No one shall enter the house of the Lord except the priests and the Levites who minister , but they shall enter , because they are holy , and all the people shall keep what the Lord has commanded them .
&quot; The Levites shall take every man his armor in their hands , and guard the king four times ; and whoever enters the house shall die ; and when the king comes in , you shall follow him .
And all the Levites and all the people of Judah did according to all that Jehoiada the priest had commanded them : and they came every man by his own class , and every man by his own class , to observe the Sabbath day : for Jehoiada the priest had forbidden them to go to work
Then Jehoiada the priest gave to the captains of hundreds the guns , and the shields , and the shields , which David had hidden in the house of God
And he distributed among the people , every man with his weapon in his hand , from the altar and from the house to the house , from right to left , standing round about the prince
Then he brought out the prince , and put on his crown , and gave him the book of the law , and made him king ; and Jehoiada and all the children anointed him , saying , &quot; May the king live forever
And when Athaliah heard the people running , and the voice of the king praising him , he came to the people , and entered into the house of the Lord
And it came to pass , when the king stood by the pillars of the gate , that the captains of hundreds and the trumpeters stood beside the king , and all the people shouted with joy ; and there were also singers , and instruments of all kinds , and the captains singing praises ; and Ahiaria rent her clothes , and cried out , saying , Again , Again
Then Jehoiada the priest came out with hundreds of the captains of the army , and commanded them , saying , &quot; Throw him out of the camp , and all who follow him shall be put to death with the sword ; for he said to the priest , &apos; You cannot kill him in the house of the Lord
Then the whole army fled , and let him go ; and he went to the gate of the king &apos;s house , and slew him there
Yahweh and his people and the king will make a covenant with them , and they will be the people of the Lord .
Then all the people came to the temple of Balak , and demolished the temple , and broke the altar and the images , and killed the priest of Balak , Mattan , before the altar
And the officers of the house of the Lord were under the hand of the priests of the Levites , which David divided in the house of the Lord , to offer burnt offerings unto the Lord , as it was written in the law of Moses , and to sing with joy , according to the commandment of David
&quot; No unclean person shall enter the gates of the house of the Lord , which are guarded by the keepers of the gates , for whatever purpose .
&quot; They shall bring the king down from the house of the Lord , and enter into the king &apos;s house through the upper gate , and shall sit on the throne of the king ,
All the people rejoiced , and the city was quiet ; and all the people struck him with the sword
Jehoash was seven years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned forty years in Jerusalem : and his mother &apos;s name was Sibiah , not Baalim
In the days of Jehoiada the priest , Joah did righteousness in the sight of the Lord
And Jehoiada took two wives for him , and gave birth to sons and daughters
After this , Joash intended to rebuild the house of the Lord
Then he gathered together the priests and the Levites , and said to them , &quot; Go to all the cities of Judah , and give money to all Israel , that they may repair the house of your God every year , and do it quickly ; but the Levites do not quickly .
Then the king called the high priest Jehoiada , and said to him , &quot; Why don &apos;t you bring the Levites from Judah and Jerusalem for the cost of the house , as Moses , the servant of the Lord , did before , for the ark of the law , and for the contributions made to the congregation of Israel ?
For the house of God was destroyed by the children of the wicked woman Ahaziah , and they divided the holy things of the house of the Lord for Baal .
And the king commanded , and all the people made an ark , and put it outside the door of the house of the Lord
And he commanded the people of Judah and Jerusalem to bring unto the LORD the gift which Moses the servant of God commanded the children of Israel in the wilderness
Then the princes and the people brought the money with joy , and put it into the ark , and it came to an end .
And when the Levites saw that there was much money , they brought the ark before the king &apos;s ministers , and before the king &apos;s scribes , and before the chief priest &apos;s officers , and the ark was empty , and it remained where it was day by day ; and there was much money stored up .
Then the king and Jehoiada gave the silver to those who did the work in the house of the Lord ; and they employed stonemasons and woodworkers to repair the house of the Lord , and ironworkers and brassworkers to repair the house of the Lord
&quot; The workers work , and they build , and they build the temple , as before , and they are strong .
And when the work was finished , they took the rest of the silver , and brought it before the king and Jehoiada , to make the vessels of the house of the LORD , and the bowls , and the vessels of gold and silver ; and in the days of Jehoiada , all the people offered burnt offerings in the house of the LORD
&quot; Yahweh is old and old , and the days are fulfilled , and he dies ; and the year of his death is one hundred and thirty years .
He shall be buried in the tomb of the kings of David , because he did good among the children of Israel , and served God , and repaired the house of God .
After Jehoiada died , all the princes of Judah came to worship the king , and the king listened to them .
For they have forsaken the house of the Lord , the God of their fathers , to serve Asheroth and idols ; and wrath has come upon Judah and Jerusalem for their sins
But God sent the prophets to them , and guided them to the Lord ; and the prophet warned them , but they did not listen
Then the Spirit of God stirred up Zechariah the son of Jehoiada the priest ; and he stood up and said to the people , Thus saith God ; Why do ye not obey the commandment of the Lord , that ye may not prosper ? Because ye have forsaken the Lord , he has also forsaken you
And the people plotted against him with one heart , and slew him with stones in the house of the Lord , as the king had commanded them
And king Jehoash remembered not the favor which Jehoiada the father of Zechariah had bestowed on him , when he killed his son : and when Zechariah was come to die , he said , Let the LORD judge righteousness
A year passed when the army of Aram came to attack Joash , and came to Judah and Jerusalem , and slew the chiefs of the people , and delivered the spoils of the people to the king of Damascus .
And when the army of the children of Aram came , even a small army , the Lord gave them a great army in their hands , because the Jews had forsaken the Lord , the God of their fathers : therefore the children of Aram punished Joash by means of the children of Aram
&quot; When the children of Aram left Joash , he was sick , and his servants betrayed him , to avenge the bloodshed of Jehoiada the priest , and to kill him in the bed , and to bury him in the city of David , but not in the tomb of the kings
And they that betrayed him were Zabbabel the son of Shemeiab the Ammonite , and Joseph the son of Shemei the Moabitess .
His son Amaziah reigned in his stead , and the warnings that he received , and the restoration of the house of God , were written in the book of the kings .
Amaziah was twenty-five years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem ; and his mother &apos;s name was Jehoiada , a man of Jerusalem
Amaziah did righteousness in the sight of the Lord , but his heart was not perfect
And when the kingdom was firm , he slew the servants of his father king .
&quot; But there is no one to put their sons to death , as the Lord commanded in the book of Moses , saying , &apos; You shall not kill your father for a son , nor your son for a father , but each man shall die for his own sin .
And Amaziah gathered together the men of Judah according to the tribes of Judah and Benjamin , and set up thousand captains , and hundred captains , and numbered them , from twenty years old and upward , mighty men with swords and shields , to go out to war , thirty thousand men .
And with one hundred talents of silver he gathered from Israel a thousand mighty men
And a man of God came to Amaziah , and said unto him , O king , let not the army of Israel go with thee ; for the LORD is not with the seed of Ephraim the son of Israel
If you must go , fight hard ; but God will defeat you in the face of the enemy ; for God helps and defeats
Then said Amaziah unto the man of God , How shall he receive the silver of the hundred that I have given unto the army of Israel ? And the man of God answered , The LORD will give thee more
Then Amaziah brought forth the soldiers of Ephraim separately , and sent them home ; and they went home in anger and wrath against Judah
Then Amaziah rose up , and led his people to the valley of salt , and slew ten thousand of the children of Seir .
And the Jews took ten thousand again , and brought them up to the cliff , and threw them down from there , and they were all crushed
Then Amaziah sent back those who were not allowed to go out with him , and struck the cities of Judah from Samaria even to Beer-sheba , and slew 3,000 men , and plundered many things .
Then Amaziah killed the Edomites , and came back , and brought back the image of the God of Seir , and stood before him as his God , and worshipped and burned incense
Then the wrath of the Lord came upon Amaziah , and he sent a prophet to him , saying , &quot; Why do you seek him , when these gods cannot deliver his people out of your hand ? &quot;
When the prophet spoke to the king , the king said to him , &quot; Who made you king as a counselor , and why do you keep your mouth shut ? Then the prophet stopped , and said , &apos; You do this thing not in accordance with my counsel , for I know that God intends to destroy you
Then Amaziah king of Judah , having consulted with the people , sent messengers to Joash the son of Jehoash , the son of Jehu , king of Israel , saying , Come , see us at the battle
Then Jehoash king of Israel sent messengers to Amaziah king of Judah , saying , &quot; The resin of Lebanon , send messengers to the acacia tree of Lebanon , saying , &apos; Take your daughter for my son &apos;s wife . &apos; Then a beast passed over Lebanon , and trampled the resin
&quot; You said , &apos; Behold , I have defeated the Edomites , and you are proud to be proud , and you dwell in your own houses . Why do you bring evil upon yourself and the land of Judah ?
&quot; But Amaziah refused to obey , and it was ungodly to put them in the hands of the enemy , because they sought the God of Edom
So Jehoash king of Israel came up , and saw Bethshemesh king of Judah and Amaziah king of Judah at the battle
And the Jews were defeated before the children of Israel , and they fled to their own houses
And Jehoash king of Israel took Amaziah the son of Jehoash , the son of Ahaziah , king of Judah , who was at Beersheba , and brought him to Jerusalem , and destroyed the walls of Jerusalem , from the gate of Ephraim even unto the gate of the corner , forty cubits
And he took all the gold and silver , and all the vessels , and all the treasures of the king &apos;s house , which he had kept in the house of God , which he had kept in the east , and brought them to Samaria as prisoners ;
And after the death of Joash the son of Jehoash king of Israel lived Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah fifteen years
Have not the rest of the acts of Amaziah , from the beginning to the end , been written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel
And when there was a traitor in Jerusalem after he had forsaken the Lord from Amaziah , he fled to Ragi , and the traitors sent messengers to Ragi , and killed him
And they carried his body with horses , and buried him in the city of Judah , in the sepulchre of his fathers
The children of Judah , Uzziah the son of Remaliah , also called Azariah , reigned in his father &apos;s stead at the age of sixteen .
And when Amaziah slept with his fathers , Uzziah took Elah , and returned to Judah , and repaired it again .
And Uzziah was sixteen years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned in Jerusalem fifty-two years ; and his mother &apos;s name was Jecoliah , a Jew of Jerusalem
And Uzziah did that which was right in the sight of the LORD , according to all that Amaziah his father did
&quot; When he knew that God was silent in the days of Zechariah , he sought God , and God made him king , Lord .
And he went out against the Philistines , and destroyed the cities of Gad , and the cities of Jabin , and the cities of Ashdod ; and among the Philistines he built cities in Ashdod .
God helped him against the Philistines , and against the Arabs who lived at Auer-Baal , and against the Miunites
And the sons of Ammon went in to buy Uzziah ; and his fame came to Egypt , because he was mighty .
And Uzziah built the gates of Jerusalem , and the gates of the valleys , and the corners of the walls , and the buildings of the city , and they were strong .
And in the wilderness , and in the high places , and in the plains , he built towers , and dug wells , because of the multitude of his cattle ; and in the mountains , and in the land of beauty , there were farmers , and men repairing vineyards , because he rejoiced in the work of the field .
And Uzziah also had soldiers , numbered according to the number of the scribes , and according to the number of the officers , under Hananiah the king &apos;s captain .
The chief mighty warrior had a total of 26 hundred men
Their army , a total of thirty-seven thousand and fifty , was mighty , able to fight , and to help the king against his enemies
Uzziah prepared for the whole army shields , guns , helmets , armor , bow , and stone throwers
And in Jerusalem he made craftsmen to make machinery , and in the buildings and in the pillars he made stone with arrows ; and the fame of Uzziah was spread abroad , because he had received great help , and was mighty .
&quot; He is strong , and he is arrogant in his heart , so that he does evil , and commits evil against the Lord his God , and enters into the house of the Lord , and burns incense on the altar
And the priest Azariah led the eighty of the valiant priests of the Lord , and went in with him
And they prevented the king of Uzziah , and said unto him , O Uzziah , it is not for thee to burn incense unto the LORD , but for the sons of Aaron to be priests of the holy office : go forth out of the sanctuary , because thou hast sinned , and that which thou hast done will not make the LORD thy God glorious
Then Uzziah was wroth , and took the fireplace with his hand to burn incense ; and when he was wroth with the priests in the house of the LORD before the priests by the altar , a great sigh of madness came out of his forehead
Then the high priest , and all the priests , looked , and , behold , a great thunderbolt came on his forehead , and they chased him out of the house , and he himself hurried forth , for the Lord had struck him
&quot; When Uzziah grew up and became mad , he lived in other palaces and was separated from the house of the Lord until the day of his death ; and his son Jonathan was over the household and over the people .
All the rest of Uzziah , from the beginning to the end , were written by Isaiah the prophet , the son of Amos
And Uzziah slept with his fathers , and was buried in the fields of the king &apos;s palace , in the sepulchre of his fathers : for it was said , He is grown up mad ; and his son Jonathan succeeded him as king
And Jotham was twenty-five years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem : and his mother &apos;s name was Jerusalem , the daughter of Zadok .
And Jotham did righteousness in the sight of the LORD , according to all that Uzziah his father had done ; but he did not enter into the house of the LORD ; and the people did evil deeds .
And Jotham built the upper gate of the house of the LORD ; and much was built in the city of Ophir
And cities were built in the mountains of Judah , and camps were built in the trees , and high places
And the king of the children of Ammon was victorious over them in the battle ; and in that year they offered him a hundred talents of silver , ten thousand pieces of wheat , ten thousand pieces of barley , in the second year , and in the third year
&quot; Jotham walked in the right way before the Lord his God , so that he became stronger and stronger
The rest of the acts of Jotham , and all the battles , and all his deeds , are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel and of Judah
He was twenty-five years old when he ascended , and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem .
And Jotham slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of David ; and Ahasuer his son reigned in his stead
Ahaz was twenty years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem ; and he did not do that which was right in the eyes of the Lord , as David his father did
But he walked in the way of the kings of Israel , and cast down the image of Baal .
And he burned incense in the valley of Hinnom , and burned his sons and his daughters with fire , according to the abominations of the strangers whom the LORD had driven out before the children of Israel
And burnt incense on the high altar , and on the mountains , and under every green tree .
Therefore the LORD his God delivered him into the hand of the king of Aram , and the king of Aram defeated him , and took away many of his people , and brought them to Damascus ; and God delivered him into the hand of the king of Israel , and the king of Israel slew him with a great slaughter
Begat the son of Remaliah killed in one day twelve thousand Jews , all of them mighty men , because they had forsaken the Lord God of their fathers
And one of the mighty men of Ephraim , whose name was Shekkiel , slew Maaseiah the son of the king , and Absalom the ruler of the king &apos;s house , and smote Elihanan
And the children of Israel took away their brethren , and twenty thousand women and their children , and plundered many things , and brought them to Samaria
But there came out a prophet of the Lord , called Od , to meet the soldiers who were going to Samaria , and said to them , &quot; Because the Lord , the God of your fathers , is angry with the Jews , and has given them into your hands , and you are angry with the heavens , and you commit great slaughter
&quot; Now you intend to make the Jews and the Jerusalemites your slaves . Have you not sinned against the Lord your God ?
&quot; Now listen to me , and release the captive brothers , because the Lord is very angry with you
And the chiefs of the children of Ephraim were the men that stood up to hinder the return of the army , the sons of Azariah , the son of Jehohanan , the son of Bile , the son of Meshullim , the son of Jesse , the son of Sharon , and the son of Amaziah , the son of Hadadeh .
And he said to them , &quot; You shall not bring this captive into the land ; for you want to make us sin against the Lord , and to add to our sins ; for our sins are great , and they have come upon the children of Israel in a fierce wrath
And the people that were taken captive , and the goods that were taken captive , were left before the chiefs of the people and before the congregation , the men that were armed
And those who were named above stood up , and brought before the captives , and the naked among them , and took their clothes and shoes out of the spoil , and put them on them , and gave them food and drink , and anointed them , and the weak among them , and brought them on a donkey , and brought them to their brethren in the city of the palm trees , to Jericho ; and they returned to Samaria .
Then king Ahasuerus sent messengers to the kings of Assyria to seek their help
For the children of Edom have come again against Judah , and have taken away their children .
And the Philistines came and took the cities of the plain , and the cities of the south of Judah , and took Beersheba , and Aijalon , and Keilah , and Sogo , and the villages of Sogo ; and they dwelt therein , in the villages of Tiennah , and in the villages of Tiennah , and in the villages of Jinlock ,
&quot; Because Ahasuerus king of Israel was scattered in Judah , and did greatly evil to the Lord , therefore the Lord humbled Judah
