And Ahaz slept with his fathers , and was buried in the city of Jerusalem , and was not brought into the tomb of the kings of Israel ; and his son Hezekiah succeeded him as king .
Hezekiah was twenty-five years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem . His mother &apos;s name was Abijah , the daughter of Zechariah .
Hezekiah did righteousness in the sight of the Lord , according to all that David his father did
In the first month of the year the doors of the house of the Lord were opened and repaired .
And he called the priests and the Levites , and gathered them together in the broad place on the east side
He said to them , &quot; Listen to me , you Levites , and now purify yourselves , and purify the house of the Lord your God your fathers , and remove the filth from the sanctuary
For our fathers have sinned , and have done evil in the sight of the Lord our God , and have forsaken him , and have turned their faces to his dwelling place
&quot; They shall shut the doors of the gates , and they shall not burn incense to the God of Israel in the holy place , nor offer burnt offerings
&quot; Therefore the wrath of the Lord came upon Judah and Jerusalem , and threw away those who were among them , as you have seen with your own eyes , as an astonishment and a mockery
&quot; Therefore our fathers fell under the sword , and our wives and our children were taken captive .
&quot; Now I have made a covenant with the Lord God of Israel in my heart , that his wrath may be turned away from us
