Be strong and courageous , and be not more afraid of the king of Assyria , and of the great army that is with him , than of those who are with us .
&quot; He who is with them is the arm of the flesh ; and he who is with us is the Lord , the God of ours ; He will help us and fight for us ; and the people will be secure by the words of Hezekiah king of Judah .
Then Nebuchadnezzar king of Assyria and all his army attacked Lachish , and sent servants to Jerusalem to meet Hezekiah king of Judah and all the Jews who were in Jerusalem , saying ,
Thus said Nebuchadnezzar king of Assyria , &quot; What do you rely on in Jerusalem ?
&quot; The house of Hezekiah said to you , &apos; The Lord our God will deliver us from the hand of the king of Assyria . Is this not a temptation for you to die of thirst ?
&quot; Isn &apos;t this the house of Hezekiah , who has destroyed the high places and the altars of the Lord , and has commanded Judah and the people of Jerusalem , saying , &apos; You shall worship before an altar , and burn incense on it ? &apos;
&quot; Do you not know what I have done to the nations with my fathers ? How can the God of the nations deliver their nations from my hand ?
&quot; Who among the gods can deliver his people out of my hand , the land that my fathers destroyed ? Can your God deliver you out of my hand ?
Therefore do not tempt the house of Hezekiah to tempt you , nor do you believe him ; for there is no God in a nation and in a nation that can deliver his people from my hand and the hand of my fathers ; nor can your God save you from my hand
&quot; And the servants of Sinai and the house of Hezekiah , the servants of the LORD , also spoke other words against the God of the LORD and against his servants
