They speak of the God of Jerusalem as they speak of the God of the hands of men
Then Isaiah the prophet , the king of Hezekiah and the son of Amos , prayed and cried unto heaven
Then the LORD sent an angel into the camp of the king of Assyria , and destroyed all the mighty men of war , and the captains of the guard , and the captains of the guard ; and the king of Assyria returned to his own country in shamefulness , and entered into the temple of his God , where his own son slew him with the sword .
Thus will the Lord deliver the house of Hezekiah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem from the hand of Zedekiah king of Assyria , and from the hand of all their enemies , and will give them peace in all their quarters
Many came to Jerusalem to offer sacrifices to the Lord , and to give treasures to Hezekiah king of Judah ; and Hezekiah was great in the eyes of the Gentiles
Then when Hezekiah was sick and dying , he prayed to the Lord , and the Lord answered him , and gave him a sign
&quot; But the house of Hezekiah did not respond to the Lord according to the grace which he had received , because of his pride , so that wrath came upon him and upon Judah and Jerusalem
But the house of Hezekiah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem were so proud in their hearts that the wrath of the Lord did not come upon them in the days of Hezekiah
The house of Hezekiah had great honour and riches , and built houses , and stored silver and gold , and jewelry , and spices , and shields , and all kinds of jewels
And storehouses were built , and storehouses for fifths , and new wine , and oil , and for cattle of all kinds , and tents were built .
And cities were built , and sheep and cattle were multiplied , because God had given him a great wealth
