And Hezekiah slept with his fathers , and was buried in the high tomb of the sons of David ; and when he died , all Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem respected him ; and Manasseh his son reigned in his stead .
Now Manasseh was twelve years old when he ascended to the throne , and reigned fifty-five years in Jerusalem .
He did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD , and did that which was abominable in the sight of the foreigner whom the LORD had driven out before the children of Israel
He rebuilt the altar that his father Hezekiah had destroyed , and built the altar for Baal , and made it a statue , and worshipped all the images of heaven .
&quot; In the house of the Lord , wherein the Lord said concerning this house , &apos; My name shall be in Jerusalem for ever .
He built an altar for all the images of heaven in the two courts of the house of the Lord .
And in the valley of Hinnom , He burned his sons and his daughters with fire ; and he who witnessed , and did witchcraft and evil deeds , and dealt with demons , and did witchcraft , did much evil in the sight of the Lord , and provoked him to anger .
God said to David and to Solomon his son , &quot; The Jerusalem and this house which I have chosen among the tribes of Israel will bear my name forever and ever .
&quot; If the children of Israel will keep all the laws , and the statutes , and the ordinances , which Moses commanded them , I will no longer cause them to move away from the land which I gave to their fathers
Then Manasseh drew the inhabitants of Judah and Jerusalem away , so that their evil deeds were greater than the nations which the Lord destroyed before the children of Israel
&quot; The Lord warned Manasseh and his people , but they did not listen
So the LORD sent the captain of the king of Assyria to attack them , and struck Manasseh with a hammer and a chain of brass , and brought him to Babylon
When he was in trouble , he pleaded with the Lord , his God , and was humbled before the God of his fathers
Then he prayed to the Lord , and the Lord answered his prayers , and listened to his prayers , and brought him back to Jerusalem , and sat in the throne ; and it came to pass that Manasseh knew that only the Lord was God
Then Manasseh built a wall out of the city of David , from the valley to the west of Gibeah , even to the gate of the fish , round about Ophir , and it was built high ; and in the strong cities of Judah he set up captains of mighty men .
And he removed the idols of the Gentiles , and the idols of the house of the Lord , and destroyed them on the mountains of the house of the Lord , and the altars which he had built in Jerusalem , and cast them out of the city
Restore the altar of the Lord , and offer on it the sacrifice of peace , and the sacrifice of thanksgiving , and command all the people of Judah to serve the Lord God of Israel
&quot; But the people sacrificed on the high altar only to the Lord their God
The rest of the acts of Manasseh , and his prayers to his God , and his words of warning in the name of the Lord God of Israel , were written in the book of the kings of Israel
