Behold , it is written , in the years of king Ahasuerus , with those who came to me from Babylon , and with their fathers , and with their genealogy ,
The sons of Phinehas were Gershon , the sons of Ithamar were Daniel , the sons of David were Hatun ,
And of the sons of Baroth , the sons of Shechaniah , Zachariah ; and with him one hundred fifty males according to the number of their families .
And of the sons of Barhammoab , Elioni the son of Shelahiah , and with him two hundred males ;
And of the sons of Shechaniah were the sons of Jahaziel , and with him three hundred males .
And of the sons of Adin , Ebed the son of Jonathan ; and with him fifty males .
And of the sons of Edom , Jeshua the son of Athariah ; and with him seventy males .
And the sons of Shephatiah ; Sibadiah the son of Micah ; and with him eighty males .
And of the sons of Joab was Obediah the son of Jesse , and with him two hundred and eighteen males .
And the sons of Shelomim ; the sons of Joseph ; and with him one hundred sixty males .
And of the sons of Bebai , Zachariah the son of Bebai ; and with him twenty and eight males .
And of the sons of Absalom , Jehohanan the son of Hagatan ; and with him an hundred and ten males .
The sons of Adonijah , the last of them , whose names were Eliphael , Eli , and Shemaiah ; and with them sixty males .
And of the sons of Begevah , Utah and Zab ; and with them seventy males .
And I gathered them together by the river that floweth into the land of Ahab ; and we tarried there three days ; and I looked at the people and the priests , and behold , there were no unrighteous men there .
And they called Elisha , and Elisha , and Shemaiah , and Elisha , and Elisha , and Elisha , and Elisha , and Elisha , and Elisha , and Elisha , and Elisha , and Zechariah , and Mizpah , and taught Joel , and Elisha ,
&quot; I sent them to the land of Capernaum to see Eldo , the chief ruler thereof , and to tell them what they should say to Eldo and to his brother Nethinim , that they should come with them to the house of our God .
and with the hand of the grace of our God they helped us , and they brought one of the sons of the fathers of Israel , the sons of Levi , and the sons of Machir , and Shephib , and all his sons , and his brothers , forty-eight .
And Hashabiah , and Jeshua the son of Merari with him , and all his sons , and his brethren , twenty
Now there are two hundred and twenty men from Nineveh , whom David the former and the chief of the chiefs sent to serve the Levites , by their names :
Then I proclaimed a fast by the river Ahab , that I might suffer in the sight of our God , and that he might make a straight path for us and for the children of women , and for all things .
For I am ashamed that I have asked the king to send foot soldiers and horsemen to help us against our enemies in the way , because I said to the king , &quot; The hand of our God will help all who seek him , &quot; but his power and his wrath will attack all who turn away from him .
So we fasted and prayed to our God , and He answered us .
And I appointed twelve of the chief priests , Sherib , and Hashabiah , and ten of their brethren :
And the king , and the captains of the guard , and the captains of the armies , and all Israel that were therein , weighed the silver and the gold , and the vessels , which they had offered for the house of our God , and gave them
And I have weighed the silver which was given in their hands , six hundred and fifty , and the weight of the silver , an hundred ; and the gold , an hundred ;
Twenty golden bowls weighing a thousand drams , and two tablewares of fine brass , precious as gold
&quot; I said to them , &apos; You are holy to the Lord , and the vessels are holy , and the silver and the gold are sweet offerings to the Lord , the God of your fathers .
&quot; Be watchful and watchful , and pass the scale before the chief priests and the chief of the Levites and the chiefs of the tribes of Israel in the treasury of the house of the Lord in Jerusalem
Then the priests , the Levites , took the silver and the gold and the vessels according to the measure , and brought them into the house of our God in Jerusalem
&quot; On the twentieth day of the month we will go up from the banks of the river Ahab to Jerusalem . The hands of our God will protect us , and deliver us from our enemies , and from the hands of those who are buried in the way .
&quot; When we came to Jerusalem , we stayed there three days
And it came to pass on the fourth day , in the house of our God , that the silver and the vessels were weighed , and they were given into the hand of Mimelech the son of Urijah the priest ; and with him Eleazar the son of Phinehas , and Joseph the son of Jeshua the Levite , and Noah the son of Binnai ,
At that time the number was pointed and written on the book by weight
&quot; The one who returns from the captivity to the land shall offer a burnt offering to the God of Israel : twelve bulls , ninety-six rams , seventy-seven lambs for the people of Israel , and twelve goats for a sin offering , all burnt offerings to the Lord .
And they delivered the word of the king unto the governor whom the king had sent , and unto the governor of the West River ; and they helped the people , and provided for the service of the house of God
And it came to pass at the end of this , that the princes came to me , and said , &quot; The people of Israel and the priests and the Levites have not left the Canaanites , the Hebrews , the Philistines , the Jebusites , the Ammonites , the Moabites , the Egyptians , the Amorites , to do abominations to the people of these lands .
For they have taken the foreign women as wives for themselves and for their sons , so that the holy ones and the people of the nations are mixed , and the chiefs and the governors are guilty in this matter .
&quot; When I heard this , I tore my clothes and my robe , and pulled my hair and my beard , and sat in awe and sorrow
&quot; Everyone who fears the word of the God of Israel has gathered to Me for the sins of the captives , and I sit in fear and sorrow until the time of the evening sacrifice .
&quot; In the time of the offering of the Passover I arose in sorrow , in a torn robe , and kneeled on my knees , and lifted up my hand to the Lord my God
&quot; I am ashamed and ashamed , O my God , and do not dare to look up to my God , for our iniquity is consumed , and our iniquity is poured out .
From our ancestors even to this day , our iniquity is great , because of our iniquity we and the kings and the priests have been delivered into the hands of the kings of the nations , killing , plundering , taking , and shaming our faces , as it is in the sight of this day .
Blessed be our God in the Lord for a while , that he may give us escapers , that we may be secure as nails in His sanctuary , and that our God may shine in our eyes , and that we may be revived a little in his dominion .
&quot; We have been slaves , but our God has not abandoned us in his dominion . He has given us mercy in the sight of the King of Persia , to revive us , to rebuild the house of our God , to repair its ruins , and to build walls in Judah and Jerusalem .
&quot; O God of ours , what have we to say ? For we have forsaken Your commandments .
&quot; This is what you have commanded by the prophets of your servants , saying , &apos; You shall go to an unclean land for your business , because of the uncleanness of the people of the nations , and of the abominations ; and the whole land shall be full of uncleanness from one side to another .
&quot; You shall not therefore marry your daughters to their sons , nor marry their daughters to your sons , nor seek their peace and their good , that you may prosper , and eat the good things of the land , and leave it to your sons for ever .
&quot; O God , we have suffered all these things because of our evil deeds and our great sins ; and you have punished us less than we deserved for our sins , and have left these among us .
&quot; Will we again break your commandments and be associated with the people who do this abomination ? If so , will you not be angry with us and destroy us , so that there is not one left to escape ?
&quot; O Lord , God of Israel , for you are righteous , and let the remnant of us escape , as it is in the sight of this day . Behold , we have sinned before you , and no man can stand before you .
When Ezra prayed , confessed , and wept , and fell down before the house of God , the children of Israel , men and women , were gathered together in Ezra , and were assembly , and the people wept bitterly .
Then Zechariah the son of Jesse , of the sons of Edom , said to Ezra , &quot; We have married foreign women in this land , and have sinned against our God , but the children of Israel have hope
&quot; Now , when we have made a covenant with our God , and have taken away the wives of all these from among them , we shall do according to the law , as my Lord and those who tremble at the commandment of God have spoken .
&quot; Arise ! This is what you do ; We will help you , and you will work hard .
And Esau rose up , and sware unto the chief priests , and unto the Levites , and unto all Israel , saying , Thus shall it be done ; and they sware
And Esau went up from before the temple , and entered into the house of Johanan the son of Eleazar , and did not eat therein , nor drink therein , because he was grieved for the sins of the captives .
And they told Judah and Jerusalem , the captives that were returned , that they should gather themselves together in Jerusalem
&quot; Whoever does not come within the three days that are appointed by the Head and the elders , shall be cut off from his house , and shall leave the congregation of the captives .
And all Judah and Benjamin gathered themselves together in Jerusalem in three days ; and it was the twentyth day of September , and they sat in the broad place before the temple ; and they were afraid because of this , and because of the great rain .
And Ezra the priest stood up , and said unto them , Ye have sinned , because ye have taken foreign women for wives , and have added to the iniquity of Israel
&quot; Now therefore , when you have confessed to the Lord , the God of your fathers , and have obeyed his will , you shall forsake the people of these lands and the daughters of the nations
And all the congregation answered with a loud voice , and said , We shall do according to thy word
&quot; But when there is a great multitude of people and a great rain , we cannot stand outside , nor is it done for a day or two , because we have sinned greatly in this matter .
&quot; Behold , those who marry foreign women in our cities come with the elders and the scribes of our city on the appointed day , and do it , and the wrath of God is turned away from us .
Only Jonah the son of Asahel , and Jahaz the son of Tawa , prevented it ; and Mizrah and Shabbi the Levite helped them exceedingly .
And it came to pass on the first day of October , that the priest Ezra and some of the elders of the tribes , according to their families , were appointed to the congregation , to do the work together
&quot; On the first day of January , the number of those who marry foreign women shall be determined .
And he found among the priests a stranger , the son of Jehoshaphat , the son of the sons of Jesse , and his brethren Maaseiah , Eliezer , Jael , and Gideel ,
And they swore to rest their wives ; and for their sins they offered a sheep of the flock for a ransom
And of the sons of Zanmah were Hanani , and Sibadiah .
