And they took foreign women as wives , and they gave birth to children among them
&quot; Twenty years and twenty years of king Ahasuerus I was in the palace of Shushan
Then came one of my brothers , Hanani , with a few men from Judah , and I asked them about the sight of the Jews who had escaped , and the sight of Jerusalem , who had been taken captive .
They said to me , &quot; The remnant of those who were taken captive have suffered great tribulation and abuse in the province of Judah , and the walls of Jerusalem have been destroyed , and the gates of the city have been burned with fire .
When I heard this , I sat down and wept and mourned for a few days , and I fasted and prayed before the God of heaven .
&quot; Lord , God of heaven , the great and terrible God , who loves you , who keeps your commandments , who keeps the covenant of mercy ,
May you open your eyes and listen to the prayers of your servants , the children of Israel , day and night , before you , and acknowledge the sins that our Israel have committed against you ; for I and my father &apos;s house have sinned .
&quot; What we have done to you is evil , and we have not kept the commandments , the statutes , and the ordinances , which you commanded by your servant Moses .
&quot; Remember what Moses your servant commanded you , saying , &apos; If you commit any sin , I will spread you out among the people
&quot; But if you return to Me , and keep My commandments , I will gather them from where you have been driven away , even to the ends of the earth , and bring them to My chosen abode in My name .
These are thy servants , and thy people , whom thou hast redeemed with a mighty and mighty hand .
&quot; Listen , O Lord , to the prayers of your servants , and to the prayers of those who love to fear your servants , that your servant may now be glorified in the sight of the king ; for I am the king of wine .
&quot; In the twentyth year of king Ahasuerus , in the month of Nisan , I put wine before the king , and I took it and offered it to the king ; and I was not sorrowful before the king
Then the king said to me , &quot; Why do you have sorrow in your face , when you are not sick ? It is nothing else , but sorrow in your heart ; and I was very afraid
&quot; I said to the king , &apos; Lord , may the king live forever . Will I not be sad in the desolation of the city where my ancestors were buried , and in the burning of the gates of the city ?
And the king said unto me , What askest thou ? And I prayed unto the God of heaven
And I said unto the king , If my servant have mercy in the sight of the king , and if the king be pleased , send me unto Judah , unto the city where the sepulchre of my fathers is , that I may rebuild it .
Then the queen sat by the king , and he asked me , saying , &quot; How many days will you go and when will you return ? I have set a date , and the king likes to send me
Then I said to the king , &quot; If the king likes , give me a letter from the king , inform the governor of the West River , and let me pass right through to Judah
&quot; And he gave an ordinance to Asa , who was in charge of the king &apos;s garden , that he should give me timber for the side posts of the gates of the palace , and for the walls of the city , and for my own house ; and the king gave me permission , because of the hand of my God , to help me
Then the king sent the captains of the army and the horsemen to protect me ; and I came to the governors of the West River , and the king &apos;s letter was delivered to them
And when they heard that there was a man to seek favor for the children of Israel , they were exceedingly angry , when they heard that there was a man to seek favor for the children of Israel , even to Shebarah , and to Dobiah , the son of Ammon who was a slave
&quot; When I came to Jerusalem , I lived there three days
&quot; I arose in the night , and a number of men arose with me ; but what God had commanded me to do for Jerusalem , I had not told any man ; and there was no other cattle besides the cattle that I had ridden ,
And in the night I went out of the gate of the valley unto the well of the wild dog , and unto the gate of the dungeon , and looked at the wall of Jerusalem , and behold , it was destroyed , and the gates were burned with fire .
&quot; I went back to the spring gate and to the king &apos;s pond , but there was no place for the cattle that I had ridden .
Then he went up by the brook at night , and looked at the walls of the city ; then he turned and entered the gate of the valley , and came back
&quot; I have not yet told the people of Judah , the priests , the nobles , the governors , and the rest of the workers what I have done , neither has the governor known what I have done
Then I said to them , &quot; You have seen how desolate Jerusalem has been for us , how the gates of the city have been burned with fire . Come , let us rebuild the walls of Jerusalem , so that we will not be humiliated again .
Then I told them how my God &apos;s hand had helped me , and what the king had said to me ; and they said , Let us build ; and they did this good work
But when they heard it , they ridiculed us , and despised us , and said , &quot; What are you doing ? Are you going to betray the king ? &quot;
&quot; I said to them , &apos; The God of heaven will deliver us ; and we who are His servants will rise up and build ; but you have no share , no power , and no remembrance in Jerusalem .
Then Elijah the high priest , and all the priests of his brothers , arose , and built the sheep gates , which were holy , and the windows of the gates , and the walls of the city , which were holy , to the house of Hamiah , even to the house of Hanun .
The second was built by the Jerichoites , and the third by Zechariah the son of Nun .
And the sons of Hasinah built the gates of the fish , and the posts , and the windows , and the bars
The second was Mizreel the son of Urijah , the son of Haqos , the second Mizreel the son of Bilhah , the son of Mizreesab , the second Zadok , the son of Bana ,
The second was the work of the Tigris , but their nobles did not shoulder the work of their lord .
And Jehoiada the son of Brazil , and Mizreel the son of Bezor , repaired the ancient gates , and the posts , and the shutters , and the bars ;
The second was repaired by the Gibeonites , Melatites , and Jathonites of Meren , and by the Gibeonites , and by the Mizpahites , which were under the governor of Hezekiah .
Then Uzziah the son of Hagiah the silversmith , and Hananiah the perfumer ; and they fortified Jerusalem until the broad wall
And the second half of Jerusalem was built by Rephaiah the son of Hur
Then Jedaiah the son of Harummah built his house , and Hatoun the son of Hasani built his house ,
And Machiah the son of Harin , and Hashub the son of Bar-hamoab , built a part , and a furnace ;
And the second half of Jerusalem was under the hand of Sharon the son of Haroah , and his daughters .
And the inhabitants of Hanun and Zanoah shall build the gates of the valley ; and they shall set up the gates , and the shutters , and the bars ; and they shall build the walls of the city a thousand cubits , even unto the gates of the dung mill .
And he oversaw Machiah the son of Berhachilon the Rechit , and repaired the gates of the dungeon , and set up the doors , and opened the doors , and locked the gates .
And he was over Mizpah , and over Sharon the son of Joses , to build the gates of the fountain , and to set up the gates , and to cover the top of the gates , and to open the doors , and to buckle the gates , and to build the wall of the pool of Zoar , which is near the king &apos;s house , even unto the steps that come down from the city of David
And the second was over half of Beersheba , and over Nehemiah the son of Ab , over against David &apos;s sepulchre , and over the well that was dug , and over the house of the mighty .
Then the Levites repaired the house of Lehihon the son of Bani ; and the half of Gilead was under his hand ; and the land of Hashabiah was under his hand .
And the second of the brethren of the Levites was Bawai the son of Hinadah , who was over the half of Gilead .
And the second was over Mizpah , the son of Jeshua , to build a portion at the top of the hill , at the turning of the wall of the city , over against the arch of the city .
Then Baruch the son of Zabbai did a great work in repairing a portion from the wall straight to the door of the house of Elijah the high priest .
And the second was Miles the son of Haqos , the son of Urijah , who built a portion from the gate of the house of Elijah straight to the end of the house of Elijah .
Secondly , the priests of the plains
Then Benjamin and Hashish built their houses , and Azariah the son of Maaseiah , the son of Achan , built their houses near to them
Then Benaiah the son of Hinadah built a portion from the house of Azariah , straight toward the wall , and toward the corner of the city ,
And Balak the son of Uzziah built the turn of the wall , and the tower that came out of the king &apos;s house , near the portion of the tabernacle of the guard , and Bhadaiah the son of Baroth .
( Nitinin lived in Ophelile , opposite the east entrance to the waters , and the outlying city buildings .
The second was that the Tekoaites repaired another part of the tower , which had been raised up , toward the wall of Ophir
From the top of the Mount , the priests built their houses
The second was Zadok the son of Nun , who built his house ; and the second was Shemaiah the son of Shecaniah , who was over the east gate
Then Hananiah the son of Shelimiah , and Hanan the sixth son of Zarah , repaired another part ; and Mizrah the son of Bilhah , repaired his house
Then the silversmith Machiah built the houses of the merchants and the houses of the men of Nineveh , which were toward the gate of Hamiph , toward the corner of the city .
The silversmiths and merchants built between the corners of the city and the sheep gates
And when Shebalah heard that we had built the walls , he was angry , and greatly displeased , and mocked the Jews
He said to his brothers and to the soldiers of Samaria , &quot; What do these weak Jews do , to protect themselves , to offer sacrifices , to succeed in a day , to take out stones of fire from the dust , and to build walls ?
And the sons of Ammon stood by Dobiah , and said , The stone walls which they have built , even the fox , shall fall upon them .
&quot; Listen , O God of ours , for we have been denied ; and put their slander on their heads , and plunder them in the land of captivity .
Do not conceal their iniquity , nor blot out their iniquity from before thee ; for they provoke thee to anger in the sight of the builders .
Thus did we build the walls , and the walls were joined together , up to half the height , because the people were diligent in their work .
And when they heard that the wall of Jerusalem was built , and that they were beginning to work , and that they had shut up the place that was broken , they were very angry
&quot; They plotted to attack Jerusalem , and to disturb the city
&quot; But we prayed to our God , and for their sakes sent guards , guarding day and night .
Then said the Jews , &quot; The ashes are too much , and the power of the men who carry them is decayed , so that we cannot build a wall
&quot; And our enemies said , &apos; Let us enter into their midst , and kill them , and put an end to the work , while they do not know or see .
&quot; The Jews who lived near the enemy came to us from every place ten times , saying , &apos; You must return to us
So I caused the people , by their families , to stand in the low place behind the wall , with swords , with guns , and with bows ,
And when I saw it , I came up and said unto the nobles , and to the princes , and unto the rest , Fear them not : for the Lord is great and terrible in remembrance : and ye shall fight for your brethren , and for your children , and for your wives , and for your children .
&quot; The enemies will not come when they hear that we know their hearts , and when God destroys their schemes ; and we will all return to the walls , every man doing his work
From that day onward , half of my servants worked , half with guns , and half with shields , and half with bows , and half with armor ; and the captains of the guard stood behind the people of Judah
who build the walls , who carry the materials , who work with one hand , and who take the weapons with another
&quot; Beside me are the repairers , all with swords in their waist , the blowers of blows .
I said to the nobles , to the governors , and to the rest , &quot; This is a great work , and we are far from the walls of the city
&quot; When you hear the sound of the trumpet there , gather yourselves to us ; and our God will fight for us .
So we worked , half of us with weapons , from the dawn to the appearance of the stars
Then I said to the people , &quot; Let every man and his servant stay in Jerusalem , to keep us at night , and to work day and night
&quot; So I and my brethren and my servants , and my guards , did not take off their clothes , and went out to water and to carry out their weapons
And the people and their wives cried with a loud voice , and mourned their brethren , the Jews
Some say , &quot; We and our children are many , and we must go to get food for our lives
&quot; Some say , &quot; We have given us fields , vineyards , and houses , so that we may be filled with food
&quot; Some say , &quot; We have borrowed money by means of fields and vineyards , and we have paid taxes to the king
Our bodies are like the bodies of our brothers , and our daughters are like their daughters . Now we will make our daughters servants of men , and our daughters have been servants , and we will not be able to save them ; for our fields and our vineyards have passed over to others .
I was very angry when I heard their calls and said these things
Then I took counsel in my heart , and rebuked the nobles and the rulers , and said , &quot; You all profit your brothers , &quot; and I gathered the assembly against them .
And I said unto them , We have redeemed our brethren , the Jews that were sold with the Gentiles : will ye also redeem our brethren , that we may be redeemed ? And they were silent , and answered nothing .
&quot; And I said , &apos; What you do is evil . Do you not fear our God ? Otherwise our enemies , the foreigners , will surely blaspheme us .
&quot; I and my brethren and my servants will lend to the people money and food , and all of us will be exempt from interest
&quot; Now therefore I urge you to return to them their fields , their vineyards , their olive groves , their houses , and all the silver money , and all the food , and all the new wine , and all the oil , which you have taken from them , with one percent interest .
&quot; They said , &quot; We will return , and we will not ask them again , but we will do as you have said ; and I have called the priests to make a vow to all the people , and to do what I have promised them .
And I trembled with my chest , and said , Whosoever shall not do that which is promised , let God tremble upon him as he trembleth from his house and from his labour , until he trembleth empty ; and all the congregation said , Amen , and praise the Lord ; and the people shall walk according to their promise .
Neither I nor my brethren have received the wages of the governor from me , from twenty years to thirty-two years , from king Ahasuerus to king Zedekiah .
&quot; The governors who were before me increased the burden of the people , asking for food and wine and forty shekels of silver a day ; and their servants ruled over the people ; but I did not do so because of my fear of God .
&quot; I have built the walls of the city , and there is no field to buy ; and my servants have gathered themselves together to work therein .
A hundred and fifty men ate in my seat , besides the Jews who came from the foreign lands round about
&quot; I will prepare a bull every day , six fat sheep , and poultry every ten days , and wine of all kinds . Nevertheless , I will not save my wages , for the people are heavy in service .
&quot; Remember , O my God , all that I have done for this people , and give me mercy .
And it came to pass , when Samaria , and Dobiah , and Gideon the Aramaic , and the rest of our enemies , heard that I had finished the walls , and there was no part of them that broke ;
Then sent Shebalah and Gideon to me , saying , &quot; Come , I pray you , and we will meet in a village in the plains of Noah ; but they want to harm me
Then I sent messengers to see them , saying , &quot; I am doing a great work , and I cannot go down ; why can I stop my work , and go down to see you ? &quot;
&quot; They sent to me four times , and I answered them
And it came to pass on the fifth time , when he sent his servant to me , and he had an unwritten letter in his hand
And it was written in it , saying , There is a voice among the Gentiles , and Hazmuth also saith , Thou and the Jews seekest to rebuild the walls , and thou shalt be their king
&quot; You also sent prophets to Jerusalem , saying , &apos; There is a king in Judah , and this will be preached to the king . Therefore , come and discuss with us
&quot; I sent a messenger to see him and said , &quot; What you have said is nothing but a fabrication in your heart .
&quot; They will make us afraid , saying , &apos; Their hands will be weak , so that the work will not be accomplished .
&quot; When I came to the house of Shemaiah the son of Pedahiah , the son of Michiadabe , and he did not shut the doors , he said , &apos; It is better for us to meet in the house of God and to shut the doors of the house , because they are going to kill you at night
&quot; I said , &quot; Will a man like me flee , and a man like me enter the temple to save his life , and I will not enter ? &quot;
&quot; I know that God did not send him ; but he attacked me with his own words ; and Dobiah and Shebalah bribed him .
&quot; For they have bought him to make me afraid , and to obey him in his sins ; and they have spread evil and deceived me .
&quot; My God , Dobiah , and Shebalah , and Noah &apos;s daughter , and the other prophets , make me afraid , and remember what they have done .
On February 25 , the walls of the city were finished and repaired for 52 days
&quot; When all our enemies , and all the foreigners around us , heard it , they were afraid , and did not rise up , because it was beyond our God to see this work accomplished
In those days the nobles of Judah wrote many times to Dobiah , and Dobiah also wrote to them .
And there were many in Judah who had a covenant with Dophiah , because he was the son of Arah , the son of Shechan , and because Jehoash his son had not taken the daughter of Mizrah the son of Bilhah to wife
And they spoke before me of the good deeds of Tobiah ; and my words were passed on unto him ; and Tobiah sent letters to make me afraid
&quot; The walls of the city are finished , and I have set up the doors , and those who guard the gates , and those who sing , and the Levites are appointed .
I sent my brother Hananiah , and Hananiah the governor of the camp , to oversee Jerusalem ; for Hananiah was faithful and fearful of God above all men .
And I commanded them , saying , &quot; You shall open the gates of the city of Jerusalem until the sun rises , and when the people have guarded it , then you shall shut the gates , and mount up the bars , and send the inhabitants of the city of Jerusalem , in ranks , to guard the opposite side of their houses
The city is vast , the population is small , and the houses have not yet been built
&quot; My God touched my heart , and gathered the nobles , the rulers , and the people together to reckon according to the genealogy : and I looked for the genealogy of the first coming , and there was written on it :
&quot; Now the sons of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , who had been taken captive in the province of Judah , are returning from the land of their captivity to Jerusalem , and all Judah to their cities
And they came again with Zerubbabel , and Jeshua , and Nehemiah , and Azariah , and Rami , and Naaman , and Thamud , and Bethshan , and Mizbite , and Begumiah , and Nimron , and Barnabas .
