Of the priests , the sons of Habakkuk , the sons of Haqos , and the sons of Brezhly : for their fathers took the daughters of Brezhly of the Philistines as wives , and called them Brezhly
The three families searched for their genealogy in the genealogy , and found it not : therefore they were defiled , and were not allowed to serve as priests .
And the governor said unto them , Ye shall not eat of the holy things until the priests of Urling and Thumming , who are in doubt , are raised up .
The total number of members of the Assembly was 42,360
And their servants , seven thousand three hundred and thirty-seven , and two hundred forty-five singing men and women
They had seven hundred and thirty-six horses , and two hundred and forty-five oxen .
Forty-three hundred and thirty-five camels and six thousand seven hundred and twenty donkeys
Some chieftains contributed to the project . The governor contributed 1 , 000 dollars of gold , fifty bowls , and fifty-three priests &apos; garments to the treasure
The chiefs also contributed 20,000 dinars of gold and 2,200 dinars of silver to the project fund
Of the money which the rest of the people gave , twenty thousand drams , and two thousand minas of silver , sixty-seven garments for the priests .
Then the priests , and the Levites , and the porters , and the singers , and the men of the people , and the Nethinim , and all Israel , dwelt in their own cities
And it came to pass in July , when the children of Israel were in their own city , that they gathered themselves together as one in the broad place before the gate of the waters , and asked Ezra the scribe to bring the law which the LORD had revealed unto the children of Israel through Moses
And it came to pass on the first day of July , that the priest Ezra brought the book of the law unto the assembly of men and women that understood it
Read this law in the open place before the gate , from morning until noon , in the presence of men and women , who have heard it all , and who have understood it ; and the people listen .
And Ezra the scribe stood on the wooden table for this purpose ; and Mattathiah , and Shema , and Anyaiah , and Uliah , and the house of Helah , and Maaseiah , stood on his right hand ; and Bidaiah , and Mizhaliah , and Machiah , and Hasun , and Habakkuk , and Zechariah , and Mizrah , stood on his left hand .
And Ezra stood above the people , and opened the book before the people ; and when he had opened it , all the people stood up
And all the people lifted up their hands , and said , Amen , amen , and bowed down their heads , and worshipped the Lord
&quot; Jeshua , and Bani , and Shephib , and Benjamin , and the valley of Ahaz , and Shabita , and Hodiah , and Maaseiah , and Kiriath , and Azariah , and Joseph , and Haran , and Blyjah , and the Levites , to make known to the people the law ; and the people stood in their places
They remember the law of God with a clear knowledge , and they speak the meaning , and make known to the people what they are thinking .
Then Nehemiah the governor , and Ezra the scribe , the priest , and the Levites , who taught and taught the people , said to the people , &quot; This day is the holy day of the Lord your God , and do not weep , because you have wept for the people , because you have heard the words of the law .
And he said unto them , Go ye and eat the fat and the sweet and the unprepared , and give it unto him ; for this day is the holy day of our Lord : grieve not , for the joy of the Lord is your strength .
Then the Levites quieted the people , saying , &quot; This day is a holy day ; do not cry out , nor grieve
&quot; The people went out to eat and drink , and gave to others , and rejoiced greatly , because they understood what they had been taught
The next day the elders of the people , the priests , and the Levites gathered themselves together to Ezra the scribe , to keep the word of the law
When they saw that it was written in the law , &quot; The Lord by Moses commanded the children of Israel to dwell in tents on the Sabbath
And they shall proclaim in the cities and in Jerusalem , saying , &quot; When you are on the mountains , take the branches of olive trees , wild olive trees , pomegranates , palm trees , and all kinds of bush trees , according to the writing of the tent
And the people went out , and took branches , and pitched on their roofs , or in the courts , or in the courts of the house of God , or in the broad gates of the waters , or in the broad gates of Ephraim ;
And all the congregation that was returned from the captivity pitched in tents , and dwelt in tents , which the children of Israel did not do from the days of Joshua the son of Nun unto this day : and the people rejoiced
From the first day even to the last day , Ezra recited the law to God every day ; and there was a solemn gathering of the people on the seventh and the eighth days .
On the twenty-fourth day of this month , the children of Israel were gathered together to fast , clothed in linen , and their heads covered with dust
And the children of Israel departed from all the heathen , and stood and confessed their iniquity , and the iniquity of their fathers
One quarter of them stood in their own place that day , and read the law of the Lord their God , and one quarter confessed , and worshiped the Lord their God
And Joshua , and Bani , and Korah , and Sheban , and Bani , and Bin , and Sherib , and Bani , and Kenani , stood on the throne of the Levites , and cried out unto the LORD their God
And the Levites , Jeshua , and Kohath , and Bani , and Hasani , and Sherib , and Hordeiah , and Sheban , and Beth-hijah , said , &quot; You shall stand up to praise the Lord your God for ever and ever ; and the name of your glory , O Lord , is to be praised above all praise and praise .
You alone are the Lord , who created the heavens and the heavens above them , and all the images of the heavens , and all the earth and the earth , and all that is in the sea and in the sea ; all these things have you preserved , and the armies of heaven have worshipped you
&quot; You , the Lord God , have chosen Abraham , and brought him out of the land of Ar , and called his name Abraham
&quot; When you see that he is truthful in your hearts , then make a covenant with him , and promise to give to his seed the land of Canaan , and of Hesh , and of Amoly , and of Belize , and of Jebus , and of Goshen , and to prove your words , for you are righteous .
Have you seen the affliction of our fathers in Egypt , and heard their cry on the Red Sea ?
And he did miracles in Pharaoh and in all his servants , and in all the people of his land ; and thou wast glorified , as it is today , because thou knewest that they were proud of our fathers .
&quot; You have divided the sea before our fathers , and made them walk in the sea on dry land ; and you have cast their people into the deep sea as stones into the great waters .
And they guided them in the day by pillars of clouds ; and in the night by pillars of fire they illuminated their way .
And thou art come down to mount Sinai , and speakest unto them from heaven , and hast given them the law of righteousness , and the law of truth , and the law of goodness , and the commandment
&quot; And let them know your Sabbaths , and the commandments , and the statutes , and the law , which Moses your servant gave them
Give them food from heaven to feed their hunger , and water from a rock to quench their thirst , and command them to enter into the land which you swore to give them
&quot; But our ancestors were arrogant , and they did not obey your commandments with their necks stiff .
And they will not obey , nor remember the miracles which thou hast done among them , when thou hast stubbornly put thy neck to the neck , and hast turned thy heart against the leaders of thy own righteousness , and hast returned unto their land as a slave : but thou art a God of forgiveness , a God of grace , a God of compassion , a God that is not easily angry , a God of abundance of mercy , and a God that does not forsake them .
And when they cast a calf , they said to one another , &quot; This is the God who brought you out of Egypt , and thus has greatly provoked your anger
Thou hast not abandoned them in the wilderness , neither have the clouds left them in the day , nor guided them in the way ; neither have the pillars left them in the night , nor have they lighted their way .
&quot; You have also given them your good spirit to teach them . Have you not tasted it and given them food and water to quench their thirst
&quot; You have raised them in the wilderness forty years , and they have no shortage , neither are their clothes torn , nor their feet swollen .
And as thou hast given them the land of the nations , so they shall have the land of Sihon , the land of Heshbon king , and the land of the night of Bashan king
And Thou hast made their seed as the stars of heaven , and hast brought them into the land wherein thou hast promised their fathers to dwell .
Thus they entered and possessed the land ; and you conquered before them the inhabitants of the land , the Canaanites , and delivered them into their hands , and their kings , and the inhabitants of the land , and left them to their own devices .
And they shall have strong cities , and fertile land , and houses full of all kinds of beauty , and wells of wells , and vineyards , and olive groves , and many fruit trees ; and they shall eat and be filled , and be fat , and rejoice in thy great grace .
&quot; But they disobeyed you , and betrayed you , and cast your law behind their backs , and killed the prophets whom they had persuaded to return to you , and greatly provoked your anger .
Therefore deliver them into the hands of the enemy , and afflict them ; and when they are in distress , pray to thee ; and hearken from heaven , and give them a savior according to thy great mercy , and deliver them out of the hand of the enemy .
But when they are in peace , they do evil in your sight ; so you cast them into the hands of the enemy , and made the enemy rule over them ; yet they turn to You , and pray to You , and You hear them from heaven , and save them with Your mercy many times .
And warn them , that they may be obedient to thy law ; but they are arrogant , they do not obey thy commandments , they do not obey thy statutes , and they turn their shoulders , and their necks are stiff , and they do not obey
&quot; But you have been forgiving them for many years , and you have warned them by your Spirit and by the prophets , but they have not listened ; therefore you have delivered them into the hands of the people of the nations .
Nevertheless , you have great mercy , and have not destroyed them at all , neither have you abandoned them : for you are a God of grace and mercy .
O God of ours , Thou art the great , the mighty , the fearless , the God of mercy ; and I will not ask thee , O our kings , chiefs , priests , prophets , fathers , and thy people , from the days of the kings of Assyria even to this day , for the affliction which they have suffered .
&quot; You are righteous in all things that come to us ; for what you do is true , and what we do is evil .
&quot; Our kings , our princes , our priests , our fathers have not obeyed your law , neither have they obeyed your commandments , nor have you kept their word
&quot; They will not serve you , nor turn away from their evil deeds , when they have received your favor in their own land , in the vast and beautiful land which you have given them .
&quot; Behold , we have been made slaves in this land , that you may enjoy the inheritance and the beauty of the land which you gave to our fathers .
&quot; Many of the fruits of the land have been given to kings ; for you have judged us for our sins ; and they have judged our bodies and our livestock at will ; and we are in great distress .
For all these things we have made a true covenant written in the book , and our leaders , the Levites , and the priests have signed the names
