The rest of the people , the priests , the Levites , the keepers of the gates , the singers , the Nethinims , and all the inhabitants of the land that is beyond the border , who are obedient to the law of God , and their wives , and their children , all who have knowledge and understand .
&quot; They swear by their noble brethren , that they will keep the law which God has revealed through Moses his servant , and keep the strict commandments , the statutes , and the law of the Lord our Lord
Neither shall we marry our daughters to the inhabitants of the land , nor our sons to their daughters
&quot; If the inhabitants of the land bring to us goods or food on Sabbaths or other holy days , we shall not buy them ; neither shall we sow in the seventh year , nor shall any of those who owe us repay them .
And we have ordained for ourselves a third of a shekel of silver each year for the service of our temple .
that is , for the bread of the tabernacle , for the continual sacrifice , and for the burnt offering , and for the sabbaths , and for the month , and for the festivals , and for the holy things , and for the sin offerings of the children of Israel , and for all the expenses of our temple
And our priests , the Levites , and the people , shall put a seal upon the timber of the offering , according to their families , every year , in the house of our God , and burn it in the altar of the Lord our God , as it is written in the law
And it shall be established every year that the first fruits of the earth , and the first fruits of every tree , shall be brought into the house of the Lord
&quot; And the sons of our firstborn , and the firstborn sheep and goats , as it is written in the law , shall be delivered into the house of our God , and to the priests who minister in the house of our God
And he shall take the firstfruits of the firstfruits of the barley , and the firstfruits of the firstfruits of the trees , and new wine , and oil , and offer them to the priests in the treasure house of our house of God ; and he shall give to the Levites one tenth of the fruit of our land , because the Levites have taken one tenth of the inheritance of all our cities .
When the Levites took one tenth of the children of Aaron , and there was a priest with the Levites , and the Levites took one tenth of the tenth of the children of Aaron , and delivered them into the house of our sanctuary , into the treasury
&quot; Then the children of Israel and the children of Levi shall offer fifty grains , and new wine , and oil , for a sacrifice , to the house of the vessels of the sanctuary , the house of the ministering priests , the house of the guards , and the house of the singers ; and we shall not depart from the house of our God .
And the princes of the people dwelt in Jerusalem ; and the rest of the people cast lots , and of the ten let one dwell in the holy city of Jerusalem , and the nine in other cities .
Blessed be the people who are willing to live in Jerusalem
&quot; The sons of Israel , and the priests , and the Levites , and the Nethinims , and the sons of the servants of Solomon , dwelled in the cities of Judah , and the princes of their provinces dwelled in Jerusalem , each in his own land , as follows :
