Then Esther said , &quot; If the king is beautiful , please , you Jews of Shushan , to do tomorrow as you have done today , and to hang the dead bodies of the ten sons of Haman on a wooden shelf
And the king commanded to do so , and the commandment came to Shushan : and the men hanged up the dead bodies of the ten sons of Haman
And it came to pass on the fourteenth day of Adad , that the Jews of Shushan gathered themselves together again in Shushan , and slew three hundred men , and there was none to take away their possessions
Then the rest of the Jews gathered themselves together in the provinces of the kingdom , and slew seventy-five thousand men that hated them ; and there was no hand to take away their property ; so they were delivered from their enemies , and they were in peace .
And it was done on the thirteenth day of the month Adah ; and on the fourteenth day there was a sabbath , and it was a day of feasting and gladness .
&quot; But the Jews of Shushan gathered together on the thirteenth and fourteenth days to kill their enemies ; and on the fifteenth day they rested , and prepared the feast of joy on that day
Therefore all the Jews that dwell in the country without walls present themselves to each other on the fourteenth day of Adah , a day of feast and joy .
And he made a new record of it , and wrote to all the Jews that were near in the provinces of king Ahasuerus
And he commanded them to keep the month of Adah forty-five and two days a year
&quot; The two days of this month shall be a day of peace for the Jews to be delivered from their enemies , and a day of joy for sorrow , and a day of joy for sorrow ; and on those two days they shall have a feast of joy , and they shall give gifts to one another , and they shall feed the poor .
Then the Jews , according to the letter that was written with them in the end of the book , shall bear the first commandment for ever .
because Haman the son of Hamediah the Ahithophel , the enemy of the Jews , sought to kill the Jews , and sought to kill them , and sought to destroy them ;
Then the king commanded that Haman should put the evil deeds of the Jews on his head , and that he and all his sons should be hanged on a tree-top
And the Jews called these two days the days of Pur , after the name of Pur , because of the words of this letter , and because of what they saw and what they encountered
&quot; Then they shall inherit themselves and their offspring , and those who belong to them ; and they shall observe these two days every year in due season , and they shall not be abolished .
Every province , every city , every household , every generation shall remember these two days , so that they may not be abolished among the Jews , nor shall they be forgotten among their descendants .
And Esther the daughter of Abimelech , the queen of Judah , and Mordecai the Jew , wrote with all authority a second letter , enjoining Judah to keep the day of Tyre
in peace and truth , writing to all the Jews in all the provinces of the kingdom of Ahasuerus ,
to keep this day , and to fast , and to pray according to the commandment of the Jews , according to the commandment of Thamud , and according to the commandment of Esther the queen , and according to the commandment of the Jews for themselves and for their seed
And Esther commanded to keep the day of Pur : and it was written in the book .
King Ahasuerus offered sacrifices to the people of the dry land and the islands
Is not that which he did in power , and lifted up the bottom , and raised him up , written in the history of the kings of Mede and Persia ?
And he became the governor of king Ahasuerus , and was great among the Jews , and rejoiced in all his brethren , and pleaded for the good of his people , and spoke peace to them
There was a man named Job , who was completely upright , and feared God , and was far from evil
He had seven sons and three daughters
And he had seven thousand sheep , and three thousand camels , and five hundred sheep , and five hundred donkeys , and many servants ; and he was great among the people of the east
And his sons made a feast in their own houses according to the days , and sent messengers , and invited their three sisters to eat and drink with them
And it came to pass , when the days of the feast were over , that Job sent men to cleanse themselves ; and he arose early in the morning , and offered burnt offerings according to the number of them all , because he said , I am afraid that my son has sinned , and that he has forsaken God in his heart ; and Job did so often
One day the children of God will stand before the Lord , and Satan will be among them
Then the Lord said to Satan , &quot; Where did you come from ? &quot; And he answered , &quot; I have come and gone from land to land , and I have come and gone back and forth
Then the Lord said to Satan , &quot; Have you considered my servant Job ? There is no man on earth like him , who is perfect in integrity , fearful of God , and far from evil
Then Satan answered the Lord , &quot; Is it right for Job to fear God
&quot; Are you not a fence round about him and his house , and all that he has ? Blessed are you for all that his hands have done , and his inheritance is multiplied in the earth .
And thou shalt stretch out thine hand , and destroy all that he hath , and he shall turn away from thee face to face
And the LORD said unto Satan , All that he hath is in thine hand ; but thou shalt not touch him . And he turned away from before the LORD
One day the daughters of Job were eating and drinking in the house of their elders
Then came a messenger to Job , saying , &quot; The cattle are grazing , and the donkeys are grazing by the side
Then suddenly the Shebaites came , and took away the livestock , and slew the servants with the sword ; but I was one of them that escaped and delivered the letter to you
And when he was yet speaking , another man said , &quot; God has sent down fire from heaven , and has burned the flock and the servants ; but I am the one who escapes to deliver the message to you .
&quot; When he was speaking , another man said to him , &quot; The Chaldeans were divided into three groups , and suddenly they broke in and took away the camels , and struck the servants with the sword . Only one of me escaped to deliver the message to you
While he was yet speaking , another man said to him , &quot; Your children are eating and drinking in the house of their elders
And suddenly a wind came from the wilderness , and struck the corners of the houses , and the houses fell upon the young men , and they were all dead ; but I was one that escaped and delivered the message to you .
And Job arose , and rent his robe , and shaved his head , and fell down on the ground , and worshipped
&quot; I am bare from the womb , and I will be bare again . The reward is the Lord , and the recompense is the Lord ; and the name of the Lord is to be praised .
In all these things Job did not commit any sin , nor was he foolish of God
On another day the children of God will stand before the Lord , and Satan will be among them
Then the Lord said to Satan , &quot; Where did you come from ? &quot; And he answered , &quot; I have come and gone from land to land , and I have come and gone back and forth
And the LORD said unto Satan , Didst thou not diligently observe that there was no Job my servant , and that there was no man in the earth like him , who was perfect in integrity , fearing God , and away from evil ? And though thou mightest excite me to attack him , and destroy him without cause , yet he kept his integrity
And Satan answered the Lord , and said , A man is willing to give away all things , and to save the life of all
And thou shalt stretch out thine hand and hurt his bones and his flesh , and he shall turn away from thee in the sight of thee .
And the LORD said unto Satan , He is in thine hand , save his life
Then Satan departed from the presence of the Lord and struck Job , and he had a long plague from his feet to his head
And Job sat in the ashes of the furnace , and shaved himself with a piece of cloth .
Then his wife said to him , &quot; Have you kept your integrity , and have you forsaken God and died ?
And Job said unto him , Thou speakest as a foolish woman : are we not blessed in the hand of God , neither are we afflicted ? And in all these things Job did not sin by mouth
And it came to pass , when the three friends of Joab , Eliphah of the Timnites , and Biledah of the Kohathites , and Zophah of the Naamathites , heard that all these evil things were come upon him , that they came together from this place of the covenant , to grieve him , and to comfort him
And they lifted up their eyes from afar , and did not recognize him ; and they cried with a loud voice : and they rent their robes , and lifted up the dust to heaven , and fell upon their heads .
And they sat on the earth with him seven days and seven nights , and none spoke to him , because he was in great pain .
