I have declared my case , and know my righteousness
&quot; If anyone argues with me , I will remain silent and die in despair .
&quot; There are only two things that will not be done to me , and I will not hide myself from Your face .
Turn away thy hand from me , and let not thy terror frighten me .
&quot; So when you call , I will answer ; or when you let me speak , you will answer me
How many are my iniquities and my sins ? Let me know my sins and my sins .
Why do you hide your face , and take me as your enemy ?
Will you shake the leaves blown by the wind , and chase away the rotten straw ?
&quot; You have punished me according to my sins , and caused me to bear the iniquity of my youth .
He has put dogs on my feet ; He has seen all my paths ; He has set the limits for my feet .
I have passed through the garments of decay , and the garments of worms .
A man is born for a woman , and his days are short , and he suffers more .
They come forth as flowers , and are cut down ; they fly away as shadows , and cannot be preserved .
Will you open your eyes to him , and call me to judgment ?
Who can make the clean out of the filth , and who can not ?
&quot; Because the days of a man are limited , and his months are with you , and you have set limits for him , so that he cannot go beyond them .
Turn your eyes from him , that he may rest , and that he may finish his days as a worker .
If a tree is cut down , it is hoped to sprout , and its young branches will not grow
Though its roots are old in the earth , they die dry in the earth
And when water is given , it will sprout , and its branches will grow , as a newly planted tree
But man dies and perishes , and where is he in despair ?
Water in the sea is exhausted , rivers dissipate and dry
And so is man , lying down , and not rising up , until the day is gone , and he shall not be awakened , nor be awakened from his sleep
&quot; Let me be hidden in the shadows , and in secret places , until your wrath has passed , and set a date for me , and remember me .
If a man dies , can he live again ? I will only come in the days of all my struggles , until the time of my release .
&quot; When you call , I will answer ; and you will envy what your hands have done .
&quot; But now , when you count my steps , do you not spy on my sins ?
&quot; My transgression is enclosed in your handbags , and my iniquity is sealed up .
The collapse of the mountains became nothing . The rocks moved away from their place
As waters grind stones , so they wash away the dust of the earth , and as thou hast destroyed the hopes of men .
Thou hast often won against him , and killed him ; thou hast changed his appearance , and caused him not to return
He does not know that his son is worthy of honor , nor does he feel that he is inferior
But know pain in the body , and sorrow in the heart
Eliphah the man of Timan answered ,
Can a wise man answer with an empty knowledge , and fill his belly with the wind of the east ?
Shall he use vain words and vain rhetoric ?
Thou hast rejected the fear , and hindered the heart of piety in the sight of God
&quot; Your iniquity is your mouth to teach ; You have chosen the tongue of the wicked .
&quot; It is not my fault that you are guilty , but your own mouth witnesses that it is not your fault
&quot; Are you the first to be born ? Are you made before the mountains ?
Have you heard the secrets of God , and have you been full of wisdom ?
What do you know that we do not know ? What do you understand that we do not understand
&quot; We are white-haired and older than your father
God comforts you with gentle words . Are you too small
Why is your heart forcing you away ? Why are your eyes opening up Mars
&quot; Your spirit turns against God , and your mouth speaks this word .
What is man that is clean , and what is a woman that is born righteous ?
God does not believe in His saints , nor is He clean before His eyes
What about the world that is filthy and abominable , and drinks iniquity as water ?
&quot; I have instructed you , that you should listen , and I will tell you what I have seen .
A wise man , who receives from his fathers a legend , and does not hide it .
The land was given only to them , and no stranger passed through among them .
Likewise the days of the wicked , the years of labour , and the years of the violent .
Fearful voices are often in his ears . The robber will come to him in peace .
He did not believe that he could turn from the darkness . He was awaited by the sword
And he wandered out seeking food , and said , Where is food ? And he knew that the days of darkness were prepared by his hand .
He was afraid of hardships and troubles , and they overcame him , as the king prepares for battle .
He stretched out his hand against God , and with pride attacked the Almighty
Standing on their necks , with thick shields , and facing straight to the Almighty .
It is because his face is covered with fat , and his waist becomes fat .
He has lived in desolate cities , and no one will dwell in them , and they will become houses of confusion .
Neither shall he be rich , nor shall his riches endure , nor shall his inheritance increase on the earth
He will not come out of darkness , but the fire will consume his branches , and he will perish because of the breath of God &apos;s mouth .
He shall not deceive himself by falsehood , for falsehood shall be his recompense .
&quot; This will be accomplished before His Day , and His branches will not be green .
&quot; He will be like the grape of a vine , which is not ripe and falls , and like the flower of an olive tree , which blooms and gives thanks .
&quot; The generations of those who have not been pious will not bear fruit . The tents of those who are bribed will be burned with fire .
What they have is poison ; what they have been born is iniquity ; what their hearts have prepared is deceit .
Job answered ,
&quot; I have heard many such words . You comfort people , but you make them sad
Are empty words exhausted ? What words do you have to answer
I can say the same thing to you . If you are in my situation , I will also make contact with words to attack you , and shake my head at you
&quot; But I will strengthen you with my mouth , and I will remove your sorrows with my mouth .
Though I speak , my sorrow shall not be dissolved ; and though I cease , and say nothing , shall my sorrow leave me ?
But now in God I am weary , and my friends are far from me
And seize me , and testify against me ; and it is not my flesh that beareth witness against me .
The LORD hath torn me in anger , He hath pressed me , He hath cut off my teeth ; My enemy hath seen me in anger .
They have opened their mouths to me , they have slandered me with their faces , they have attacked me at the gathering
God has delivered me into the hands of the ungodly , and cast me into the hands of the wicked .
&quot; Behold , I have come to rest ; He has broken me , He has pinched my neck , He has broken me , He has set me as his arrow .
His bow and his arrows are round about me ; He has broken my heart , and has not spared me ; He has cast down my courage on the earth .
He will break me again and again , as a mighty man breaks straight at me .
&quot; I sew cloth on my skin , and put my corners in the dust .
My face is purple in crying , and there is shadow of death on my eyelids .
&quot; In My hands is no violence ; My prayers are pure .
O earth , do not cover my blood , do not hold back my supplications
&quot; There is now a witness of Me in heaven , and a guardian of Me in heaven .
My friend scoffed at me , but I wept at God .
Let a man contend with God , as a man contends with his friends
For in a few years &apos; time , I will walk the way that I have not returned
&quot; My soul shall be consumed , My days shall be consumed , And the grave shall be prepared for me .
&quot; There is indeed a joke about me in my place ; I see them stirring me with my eyes .
&quot; May the Lord give me proof , and protect Himself for me ; and who will shake hands with me besides You ?
For thou hast made their hearts unreasonable ; therefore thou shalt not lift them up .
He accuses his friends of robbery , and his children &apos;s eyes are blind .
God made me laugh among the people , and they spit on my face
My eyes are dim in sorrow ; my bodies are like shadows .
The upright shall be astonished , and the innocent shall rise up against the ungodly .
But the righteous shall keep his way , and the clean shall strengthen his hands .
As for all of you , let us debate again ; I have not found among you a wise man .
&quot; My days have passed , My calculations have failed , My desires have failed .
They took the night for the day , and said , &quot; The light is near to darkness .
If I look to the shadow for my house , and if I lie in darkness ,
&quot; If you say to the wicked , &apos; You are my father , &apos; and to the worm , &apos; You are my mother and sister , &apos;
&quot; There is my hope ; and who can see what I hope for ?
&quot; When he rests in the dust , the hope will descend into the lattice of the shadow .
Billada , a Shuite , answered
How long will it take for you to search for words ? You can think , and then we will speak
&quot; Why do we consider ourselves to be animals , and to be defiled in your eyes ?
&quot; Has the earth been abandoned for you , and the rocks moved away from their place , because your anger has torn you apart ?
The light of the wicked shall be consumed , and his flame shall not shine .
The light of his tent shall be turned to darkness , and the lamps above him shall be extinguished .
His steadfast foot shall see the narrowness , and his own devising shall stumble him .
For he is caught in the net by his own feet , and walks in the nets of men .
The encirclement will seize his feet , and the organs will seize him .
To keep him in the earth , and to keep him in the way
Fear on all sides shall make him afraid , and chase after his feet
His strength shall fade because of hunger , and evil shall await him .
His own bodies shall be swallowed up ; and the eldest of the dead shall swallow up his bodies .
&quot; And he shall be brought out of the tent upon which he leaned , to the king of terror .
&quot; He who is not of his will dwell in his tent , and sulfur will be poured out in his dwelling place .
Behold , his roots are dry at the bottom , and his branches are cut off at the top .
His remembrance shall perish in the earth ; His name shall not be left in the streets .
He shall be driven out of the light into the darkness ; he shall be driven out of the world .
&quot; There will be no sons nor sons among the people , and no one will remain in the land of their dwelling .
Then the days of his coming shall be as if they had gone before , and they shall be as if they had gone before .
&quot; This is the dwelling place of the wicked ; this is the way of those who do not know God .
Job answered ,
&quot; When will you disturb my heart , and crush me with words ?
You have humiliated me ten times , and you have suffered me for no shame .
Truly , I have a fault , and it is in me
&quot; Indeed , you exalt me , and accuse me of my shame .
Know that God overthrew me , and surrounded me with nets .
&quot; For I have called by deceit , but I have not heard it ; I have called , but I have not heard it .
God has blocked my way with a fence ; He has prevented me from passing ; He has made my way dark .
He has taken away my glory , He has taken away my crown from my head
He attacks me all around , and I am to death ; He brings forth my hope like a tree .
His wrath is kindled against me , and he has made me an enemy
And his armies shall come together , and build a way against me , and camp in the four corners of my tent
&quot; He has separated my brothers from me , so that all that I know is alienated from me .
My relatives , who are cut off from me , and my close friends , have forgotten me .
&quot; Those who dwell in my house and my apostles regard me as strangers , and in their eyes I am a stranger .
&quot; I called my servant , and he did not answer , even though I asked him in his mouth
The smell of my mouth hates my wife , My supplications hates my compatriots .
Even the little ones despise me ; and if I arise , they will laugh at me
My close friends hate me , and the people I love turn their faces to me
My flesh clings to my bones , and all I have left is the skin of my teeth .
My friend , pity me , pity me , for the hand of God is upon me
Why do you think that God has oppressed me , and that you are not able to eat my flesh ?
&quot; But my words are written , and they are recorded in the book .
Inscribed with iron pen , poured on rocks with lead , forever .
&quot; I know that my redeemer is alive , and that at last he will stand on the earth
&quot; When my flesh is consumed , I shall see God outside of my flesh
&quot; I will see him myself , I will see him with my own eyes , and I will not be like strangers . My heart is consumed in me .
&quot; If you say , &apos; What is the burden of our oppression on him ? &apos; the root of the oppression is in him
&quot; Be afraid of the sword , for the punishment of the sword is in your wrath , that you may know that there is a recompense .
Zophah the Naaman answered ,
My heart is stubborn , so my thoughts call me to answer
I have heard the reproach of my reproach , and my understanding calls me to answer .
Do you not know from the ancient days , from the earth of life
Is the exaggeration of the wicked temporary , and the joy of the disobedient is but the turning of an eye
His glory is in heaven , and his head is in the clouds .
&quot; He will perish as his own dung , and his people will come and say , &apos; Where is he ? &apos;
He will fly away like a dream , and he will not find it ; and he will be driven away like a night vision .
&quot; He who has seen Him with his own eyes will never see Him again ; and his place will never be seen again without Him .
His children seek the mercy of the poor , and his hands repay unrighteousness .
His bones , though young , lie with him in the dust
He hid himself under his tongue , though sweet in his mouth for evil
Love is unforgiving , contained in the mouth .
His food is in his belly , but it turns into acid , and in him becomes the poison of the snake .
He swallowed up his treasures and spit them out , and God will take them out of his belly .
He will drink the poison of the snake , and the tongue of the viper will kill him .
A river of milk and honey , and he shall never see again .
He will not repay what he has earned , nor enjoy what he has gained , nor rejoice in what he has gained .
He oppresses the poor and leaves them , forcing houses which he has not built .
For he hath no lust , neither can he keep that which is pleasurable
There is none of the rest that He will not swallow up , so that His bliss will not last long .
He will go to a narrow place when he is satisfied , and all the afflicted will lay hands on him .
&quot; When he is full of belly , God will bring upon him a fierce wrath , and when he is eating , He will bring upon him a rain of wrath .
He will hide himself from the iron , and the arrows of the bronze bow will pierce him
And he drew out his arrow , and it came out of him ; and the arrow of light came out of his fury ; and there was terror in him .
His treasure is in darkness , and the fire that no man blows shall burn him , and the remnant of his tents shall be burned .
Heaven will reveal his iniquity , and the earth will rise up against him .
His inheritance shall surely pass , and his goods shall be destroyed in the days of the wrath of God .
&quot; This is the inheritance of the wicked from God , the inheritance which God has given him .
Job answered ,
You will listen carefully to my words , even if you comfort me
Forgive me , and I will speak again ; and after that , let your ridicule be yours .
&quot; Why am I not anxious to plead with men ?
You will look at me and be amazed , and shake your hands and your mouth
Whenever I think , my heart trembles , and my body trembles
Why does the wicked live long and have great power ?
&quot; They see their children , and stand firm with them .
Peace in their houses , and no fear ; and the staff of God is not upon them .
Their bulls breed and die , and their mothers lay their calves without giving birth .
They sent out little children like sheep , and their children danced and danced
They sang with the harps , and rejoiced at the sound of the flute
And they do all things day by day , turning their eyes into darkness .
&quot; They said to God , &quot; Get away from us , for we do not want to know your way .
Who is the Almighty , and what will we serve Him ? And what is the use of pleading to Him ?
Behold , they do not care for themselves ; and the evil man &apos;s plan is far from me .
How shall the lamp of the wicked be quenched , and how shall affliction come upon them , and how shall God be angry , and spread evil upon them ?
How shall they taste as straw before the wind , and as a branch that is shattered by the wind ?
&quot; But you said , &apos; God has accumulated iniquity for the children of the wicked . &apos; I said , &apos; It is better for me to be recompensed , so that he may know for himself .
Let him see his own destruction with his own eyes , and drink the wrath of the Almighty himself
His years have come to an end . Will he take care of his home
&quot; Who can teach knowledge to him who is in high places , as God judges ?
Some are strong to death , and rest in peace .
His barrel is full , and his bones are moistened
There are those who have suffered to death in their hearts , and have not tasted the joy of life
Like them they lie in the dust , covered by worms .
&quot; I know what you mean , and I know what you plot against me .
&quot; You say , &apos; Here is the house of the mighty , and there is the tent of the wicked .
Have you not inquired of the way , and have you not known the evidence which they have drawn ?
That the wicked may dwell in the days of evil , and escape in the days of wrath
Who will show him in front of him what he has done , and who will answer him for what he has done ?
&quot; But he will be brought up to the ground , and there will be a watchman over the grave
And he shall make the earth sweet in the valley , and innumerable of them that went before him , and more that went after him .
What comfort do you give me when you answer falsely ?
Eliphah the man of Timan answered ,
Can a man profit God , but a wise man profits himself
Are you righteous to man , that the Almighty may rejoice ? Are you perfect in your deeds , that he may profit ?
&quot; Is it because you fear Him that He reproaches you and judges you ?
Is not your iniquity great , and your iniquity is not endless ?
&quot; For you have taken your brother &apos;s head without cause , and have stripped the clothing of the poor
The poor man , thou hast not given him water to drink ; and the hungry man , thou hast not given him food
A land shall be given to the competent , and in it shall dwell the noble .
Thou hast sent the widow away empty-handed ; thou hast broken the arm of the orphan
&quot; There is therefore a snare around you , and fear is about to terrorize you .
Or darkness covers you , and floods overwhelm you
Is not God in the high heavens ? How high are the stars when you see them !
&quot; You say , &quot; What does God know ? Can He judge in darkness ? &quot;
A cloud covereth him , and he seeeth not ; and he passeth through the heavens .
Will you obey the ancient way , which the wicked do ?
When they are not ready to die , they are suddenly extinguished , and their roots are destroyed , as if they had been swept away by the river .
They said to God , &quot; Leave us , &quot; and said , &quot; How will the Almighty deal with us ? &quot;
Knowing that God fills their houses with good things , yet the evil man &apos;s plan is far from me .
The righteous rejoice when they see their end ; and the innocent laugh at them .
He said , &quot; The one who attacked us from the beginning has been cut off , and the rest is burned with fire .
&quot; If you will know God , you will have peace , and blessings will come to you
When thou hast received the lesson of his mouth , thou hast put his words in thy heart
&quot; If you turn to the Almighty and remove iniquity from your tents , you will be set up
&quot; You shall cast your treasures into the dust ; and you shall cast the gold of Ophir among the stones of the stream .
&quot; The Almighty will be your treasure , and your silver .
Then you will rejoice in the Almighty , and will rise up to God
If you pray to Him , He will hear you , and you will return your wish
Whatever you intend to do will surely be accomplished for you , and the light will illuminate your way .
&quot; He has made you humble , and you can say , &apos; You will be exalted . God will save the humble .
&quot; He is innocent , and God will save him ; and he will be saved by the cleansing of your hands .
Job answered ,
And now is my mourning against me ; and my rebuke is greater than my mourning .
&quot; If only I knew that I could find God there , and that I could come to His throne .
I have made my case clear before him , and I have spoken it out
&quot; I will know what he says to me , and what he says to me
&quot; Will he argue with me with great power ? He will not do so ; he will take me into account .
&quot; In him a righteous man shall contend with him ; and I will be cut off from the judgment of my own for ever .
&quot; But I went forward , and he was not there ; and I turned back , and I could not see him .
He acts on the left , and I see him not ; and hides on the right , and I see him not .
&quot; But he knows the way that I am walking ; and after he has tried me , I will be like gold .
I follow His footsteps , and I follow His ways , and I do not deviate .
I have not rejected the commandment of his lips , and I have regarded the words of his mouth more than the food I need .
&quot; But it is his will that is determined ; who can make him change his mind ? And what is in his heart will come forth
He will create what He has ordained for me , and He has many such things .
&quot; Therefore I was afraid before him , and when I remembered it , I was afraid of him
God has deceived me , and the Almighty has terrified me
My fear covers my face , not because of darkness , nor because of darkness
Why does the Almighty not make those who know him see that day , when he rebukes them on a regular basis ?
Some people have moved land , robbed livestock and raised them
They took away the donkey of the orphan , and took the ox of the widow as their head
They have driven away the poor from the right path , and the poor in the world are hidden .
&quot; The poor go out in the wilderness like wild donkeys seeking food , and feed their children and their daughters in the wilderness
He harvests the weeds of the fields of others , and takes away the grapes of the wicked .
The night was without clothes , and the weather was cold without cover
He was wet in the mountains , and came near to the rocks , for he had no refuge
And they took the orphan out of his mother &apos;s womb , and took the clothes of the poor for their heads
He made the people unclothed , and spread abroad , and carried the grains of the fields because of hunger .
They make oil and wine in their walls , and they are thirsty .
And in the cities of the multitude there is a mourning , and a wounded crying ; but God does not understand the folly of the wicked .
And some turn away from the light , and do not know the way of the light , and do not dwell on the way of the light
The dawn of the murderer rises , and he kills the poor and the needy , and at night he is a thief .
The adulterer waits for the twilight and says , &quot; He who has no eyes will see me , so cover his face .
Thieves dig holes in the darkness , hide in the daylight , and do not know the light
They see the morning as darkness ; for they know the horror of darkness .
These wicked men float like birds , and their share is cursed in the world , and they shall no longer walk in the paths of the vineyards
Drought and heat have wiped out the snow and the shadows have wiped out the generations of criminals
His mother will forget him , and the worms will eat him , and he will be sweet ; and he will no longer be remembered ; and the wicked will be cut down like a tree .
He hath done evil unto a woman that hath not conceived and hath not given birth , and hath done no good unto a widow .
Yet God uses His power to preserve those who have power , and those who are unable to preserve their lives are still rising up
God has made them secure , and they are trustworthy ; and God &apos;s eyes are on their way .
They were exalted but for a moment , and they were lost ; and they were humbled , and destroyed , as all the people , and as the ears of the field were cut down .
&quot; If not , who can prove that I am a liar and refute my words as empty ?
Billada , a Shuite , answered
God has the power to rule , and He is awesome in might , and He makes peace in high places .
Can his armies count ? Who can not see his light with a shining glance ?
How then can a man be justified in the sight of God , and the womb of a woman purified
In the sight of God , the moon is not bright , and the stars are not clean .
And what of man as a worm , and of man as a maggot ?
Job answered ,
What help do you give to the helpless , and what salvation do you give to the helpless with your arms ?
How much more wisdom have you given to the wise man who has no wisdom !
Whom have you spoken to , and whose spirit has come from you ?
In the great waters and below the waters , the ghost trembled
The darkness shall be revealed before God , and death shall not be concealed .
God lays the north pole in the air , and the earth hangs in the void .
Put the water in the clouds , and the clouds will not break
He will cover His Throne , and He will spread clouds over it .
Boundaries are drawn around the surface of the water , straight to the intersection of light and darkness .
The pillars of heaven were shaken at his reproach
He stirred the sea with his power , He wounded Lahab with knowledge
He has made the heavens adorned with His Spirit , and His hands have struck the serpents .
&quot; Behold , this is nothing but a little of God &apos;s work . What little voice do we hear of Him ! Who can hear His mighty thunder ?
Then said Job
God has taken away my reason , the Almighty has grieved my heart , and I swear by the God of everlasting life .
My life is still in me , and the breath of God is still in my nostrils
&quot; My mouth shall not speak unrighteous words , neither shall my tongue speak deceitful words
I refuse to take it for your sakes . I will not take it for my own sakes until I die
&quot; My righteousness will not be loosened , neither will my heart reproach me in the days of the world .
Let my enemy be like the wicked , and let him come upon me like the wicked .
What hope do the ungodly have when God takes away their lives , even though they have gained ?
Woe be to him ! Can God hear his cry ?
Will he be pleased with the Almighty , and call on God at all times ?
&quot; I will teach you the works of God , and I will not conceal what the Almighty does .
You have seen it yourself . Why have you become nothing but a delusion
&quot; This is the reward of God for the wicked , and the reward of the mighty from the mighty .
&quot; If his children increase , he will be slain with the sword , and his sons will not be able to eat .
And he that is left of him shall die and be buried , and his widow shall not weep
He stores up silver like dust , and prepares his garments like clay
He only prepares , and the righteous wears ; and his silver is divided among the innocent .
He builds houses as nests for worms , and as shelters for watchers .
Though he lay and lay with his feet , he could not take it ; and he was absent from the turning of his eyes .
Fear like a wave chases him , and the wind blows him away at night .
And the east wind blew him away , and shattered him from his place .
God will shoot at him , and he will not spare ; and he will not despise the hand of God .
&quot; They shall shake hands at him , and scold him , and leave him from this place
Silver has minerals and refineries .
Iron is excavated from the ground , copper is enriched from stone .
Man sets the limits of darkness , and searches for the stone of darkness , and reaches to the extreme .
They dig holes in places where no one dwells , and those who pass by do not know them , and they are far away from men , and they are hanging in the air , rocking and rocking .
As for the earth , there is food for it , and it is as if it were turned up by fire
In the rocks of the earth are blue stones , and gold sand
The road birds in the mine do not know , neither do the eagle &apos;s eyes see
The fierce beast has not passed , nor the fierce lion has passed
A man stretches out his hand and digs out a rock , and casts down the mountains
He dug a well out of a rock , and saw with his own eyes all kinds of treasures
He closed the water so that it would not drip , and made the hidden visible .
But there is a place of wisdom , and there is a place of wisdom .
The value of wisdom is not known , nor is it found in the land of the living
&quot; The deep says , &apos; Not in me . &apos; The tide says , &apos; Not in me . &apos; 
Wisdom is not of gold , neither is it worthy of silver
Feather , and precious scarlet pearls , and blue stones , are insufficient and plentiful .
gold , and glass , inadequate for comparison , vessels of pure gold , inadequate for exchange
Corals and crystals are in vain ; wisdom is worth more than pearls .
The red pearls of ancient times are inadequate for comparison , and the gold is inadequate for comparison .
Where does wisdom come from , and where is wisdom ?
It is a covering for the eyes of all living , and a covering for the birds of the air .
Saying , We have heard its name by the wind
God knows the way of wisdom , and knows where it is .
For he searched the earth , and looked under the heavens .
Take light weight for the wind , and measure all the water
He gave orders for rainfall and for lightning and electricity .
Then he saw wisdom , and spoke , and was firm , and searched .
He said to men , &quot; It is wise to fear the Lord , and it is wise to stay away from evil
Then said Job again
May my days be as the months of old , as the days of God who keeps me
Then His light shined on my head , and I went through darkness through His light .
I wish that when I was grown up , when I was in the tent , God had a close friendship with me
&quot; The Almighty is with me , and my children are around me .
Milk will wash my feet , and rocks will make a river of oil for me .
I went out to the city gate , and set up my seats in the street
The young men turned away when they saw me , and the old men stood up .
All the princes stopped talking and put their hands in their mouths
The chief was silent , his tongue pressed against his chest
Blessed are the ears that hear me ; and the eyes that see me praise me .
For I have saved the needy and the orphan without help
Blessed be the one who shall perish for me , and I will rejoice in the heart of the widow
I have clothed myself with righteousness , and I have clothed myself with fairness , and I have crowned myself with crowns
