He hath not despised the mighty , He is king over the proud of the waters
And Job answered the LORD , saying ,
I know that you can do all things , and that your will is not hindered .
Who conceals Your will in a word of ignorance ? I do not understand what I say , and these things are strange , and I do not know .
&quot; Listen to me , I will speak ; Ask me , and direct me
&quot; I heard you before , and now I see you with my own eyes .
Therefore I despise myself , and repent in the dust and in the ashes
Then the Lord spoke to Joab after he had spoken , and said to Elisha the man of Timan , &quot; My anger is kindled against you and against your two friends , because you have spoken to me less than my servant Joab has said :
&quot; Now therefore take seven bulls and seven rams , and go in to my servant Job , and offer a burnt offering for yourselves ; and my servant Job will pray for you ; and I will not do to you according to your foolishness , because I am pleased with him ; and you will talk about me less than my servant Job said :
Then Eliphah of the Timnites , and Biledah of the Shunites , and Zophah of the Naamathites , did as the Lord commanded them ; and the Lord pleased Job
And when Job prayed for his friend , the Lord brought Job back from his affliction , and doubled that which the Lord had bestowed upon him ,
And the brothers and sisters of Job and those whom he knew before came to him and ate with him in his house , and all the evil that the Lord had brought upon him comforted him in sorrow , and they each sent him a silver ring and a gold ring
So the Lord came and blessed Job more than before : he had fourteen thousand sheep , six thousand camels , a thousand oxen , and a thousand donkeys
He also had seven sons and three daughters
And he named the eldest daughter Jeremiah , and the second daughter Kirjath-sheba , and the third daughter Kirjath-harpon .
They found no beauty in all the women of the land like the daughter of Job ; and their father made them inheritance among their brethren .
And afterward Job lived another hundred and forty years , to see his sons , even to the fourth generation .
Thus , when Job was old and old , his days were fulfilled and he died
Do not stand in the way of the wicked , and do not sit in the seats of the blasphemers .
Blessed is he who loves the law of the Lord , and his thoughts day and night
&quot; He will be planted like a tree by the stream , bearing fruit in due season , and its leaves will not dry up ; and all that he does will be well
&quot; The wicked is not like a branch blown away by the wind .
Therefore the wicked will not stand in the judgment , neither will the sinner in the meeting of the righteous .
For the Lord knows the way of the righteous , and the way of the wicked shall perish .
Why do the nations quarrel , and why do the peoples plot foolishness ?
&quot; The kings of the world are gathered together , and the princes are consulted , to oppose the Lord and His anointed
&quot; We will take away their cords and their ropes ,
He who sits in heaven will laugh , and the Lord will scoff at them .
Then he will reproach them in anger , and terrorize them in fierce anger .
&quot; I have raised up my lord in the holy mountain of Zion ,
And the anointed said , I will preach the word ; and the Lord said unto me , Thou art my son , and I have born thee this day
&quot; If you ask Me , I will give you all the nations as a base for your livelihood , and I will give you all the land as a crop
And thou shalt break them with a rod of iron ; and thou shalt break them as the stones of a carpenter .
Now your kings shall be saved ; and your judges in the world shall be instructed
Blessed be the Lord when you fear , and rejoice when you fear
&quot; Behold , I am afraid that he will be angry , and you will perish in the way ; for his anger is about to come ; and whoever leans on him is blessed .
O LORD , how is my enemy multiplied , and many men come up against me ?
There were many who argued with me , saying , &quot; He needs no help from God . &quot;
&quot; But you , Yahweh , are my shield around me , and my glory , and your call to my head .
I cried out to the Lord in my voice , and He answered me from His holy mountain .
I lie down to sleep ; I awake ; and the Lord blesses me .
&quot; I am not afraid , though thousands of people come around me to attack me
Arise , O LORD , and save me , O God of mine ; for thou hast smitten the breasts of all my enemies , and smitten the teeth of the wicked .
Salvation belongs to the Lord , and may Thou bless thy people .
Show me , O God of righteousness , when I cry , that thou mayest hear me : for thou hast made me wide in my affliction : now therefore have mercy on me , and hear my prayers .
How long , O ye upright men , will ye turn my glory into shame ? How long will ye love falsehood , and seek falsehood ?
&quot; You shall know that the Lord has given to Himself the righteous by way of separation ; and I call on the Lord , and he will hear me .
Be afraid , and do not commit iniquity ; and when you are in bed , think in your heart , and be quiet .
When you offer the sacrifice of righteousness , and when you rely on the Lord
Many say , &quot; Who can show us what is good ? Lift up your face , O Lord , and shine upon us
Thou hast made my heart rejoice above him that harvesteth the new wine of the fifth valley
&quot; I will lie down and sleep in peace ; for your Lord alone has made me to dwell in peace
&quot; Listen to my words , O Lord , and consider my heart
O my king , O God of mine , hear the voice of my cry ; for I pray unto thee
&quot; In the morning , O Lord , you will hear My voice , and in the morning I will reveal to you My thoughts , and you will be watchful
For thou art not the God of evil , and the wicked shall not dwell with thee .
A proud man cannot stand before thee ; and whosoever doeth iniquity , he hateth thee evil .
&quot; You will destroy those who lie , and those who deceive with their own blood will be hated by the Lord .
&quot; As for me , I will enter your dwelling-place with Your abundant mercy , and I will worship Your holy temple with Your fear .
&quot; Lord , lead me by your righteousness , and by my enemies , and make your way straight before me .
For there is no truth in their mouths ; their hearts are full of evil ; their throats are an open tomb ; and they flatter with their tongues .
Determine their sins , O God ; let them fall by their own devices ; and cast them out of the multitude of their transgressions , for they have betrayed thee .
Let them rejoice when they rely on You , for You have sheltered them ; and let those who love Your name rejoice in You .
&quot; For you will bless the righteous , and you will protect him with your mercy , O Lord , like a shield on all sides .
O Lord , do not reproach me in anger , nor punish me in fierce anger
O LORD , pity me , because I am weak ; O LORD , heal me , because my bones and my hair are at war ;
How long wilt thou save me , O LORD , O my heart , when thou art come to me ?
Turn , O Lord , and deliver me ; for thy mercy has delivered me .
For no man remembereth thee in the land of death ; and in the shadows there is one that giveth thanks unto thee .
I am weary of my weeping , I tear every night , I lift up my bed , I make it wet
My eyes are dry because of sorrow , and my enemies all are dim .
&quot; For the Lord has heard my cry , all you who do iniquity , and have left me .
The Lord has listened to my prayers ; and the Lord will receive my prayers
And all my enemies shall be ashamed , and greatly astonished ; and they shall turn back , and be ashamed
&quot; Lord , my God , I have put my trust in You ; save me from all those who persecute me , and lift me up ,
&quot; I am afraid that they will tear me apart like a lion , and they will tear me apart , and no one will be saved .
&quot; If I do this , O Lord , my God , sin is in my hand
&quot; If I recompense the one who is good to me , even the one who is unjustly an enemy to me , I will save him
&quot; He will pursue me by the enemy until he catches me . He will trample my life underground , and my glory will be in the dust . &quot;
&quot; Arise , O Lord , in anger , stand up against the wrath of my enemies , and rise up for me , for you have ordained judgment .
Let the people be round about you , and let you be exalted above them .
&quot; The Lord judges the people ; Judge me , O Lord , according to my righteousness and to the purity of my heart .
May the evil of the wicked be cut off , and may you uphold the righteous : for the God of righteousness examineth the heart and the lungs of men .
God is my shield . He saves the righteous in his heart
God is the judge of righteousness , and the God that wraths on the wicked every day
&quot; If a man does not turn back , his sword will be sharpened , and his bow will be raised , and he will be ready .
He also prepared weapons for killing . He fired rockets
Let the wicked be tempted by evil deeds . What is in store is poison , and what is born is false .
He dug a hole , and dug deeper , and fell into the well that he had dug
And his poison shall come upon his own head , and his violence upon his own head .
I will give thanks to the Lord in his righteousness , and I will sing praises to the name of the Most High
How beautiful is thy name , O LORD our Lord , in all the earth ; and thy glory hast thou exalted in heaven
For the sake of the enemy , You have established power in the mouths of infants and of those who eat milk , and you have made the enemy and the vengeful to shut up their mouths .
&quot; I see the heavens that you have created with your fingers , and the moon and the stars that you have set up
Then he said , &quot; What is man , that you care for him , and what is the world , that you care for him ?
Thou hast made him a little less than an angel , and hast given him the crown of glory and honour
&quot; You have sent him to rule over all that your hands have created , and He has subjected under His feet all things , the cattle and the sheep , the beasts of the field , the birds of the air , and the fish of the sea , and all those who go by the sea
