&quot; How beautiful is thy name , O Lord our Lord , in all the earth !
I will give thanks to the Lord with all my heart , and I will preach all your wonderful works
I will rejoice in You , and I will sing Your name , O High One .
&quot; When my enemies turn their backs , when they see thee , they fall into ruin .
For thou hast justified me , and hast justified me ; and thou hast sat upon the throne , and hast judged according to righteousness .
Thou hast reproached the nations , Thou hast destroyed the wicked , Thou hast blotted out their names for ever and ever .
The enemy has come to an end , and they have been destroyed for ever . You have destroyed their cities , and their names have been lost .
&quot; But the Lord sits as King for ever , and He has set up His throne for judgment .
He will judge the world in righteousness , and judge the people in integrity
&quot; The Lord will also raise up the oppressed , and raise up them in the time of trouble .
&quot; Those who know thy name , O Lord , will rely on thee ; for thou hast not forsaken those who seek thee .
Sing praises to the Lord who is in Zion , and let his works be preached among the people
For he that seeketh the sin of the blood of men remembereth the oppressed , and remembereth not the cry of the afflicted .
O LORD , thou hast lifted me up from the door of death ; have mercy on me ; see the affliction of those who hate me .
Let me declare all your virtues , and I will rejoice in your salvation at the gates of Zion .
The foreigners are trapped in the pits which they have dug , and their feet are entangled in the nets which they have set up .
The LORD hath made himself manifest , and hath executed judgment : and the wicked is entangled in that which he hath done with his own hand ; or that he hath made the wicked tired of that which he hath done with his own hand .
&quot; The wicked , the foreigner who forgets God , will all return to hell
The poor shall not be forgotten for ever ; and the hope of the needy shall not be forgotten for ever .
&quot; Arise , O Lord , and let no man prevail ; and let the Gentiles be judged before you .
O LORD , make the heathen afraid , and let them know that they are not men .
&quot; Why do you stand afar off , O Lord ? Why do you hide yourself in the hour of trouble ?
Let the wicked pursue the needy in pride , and let them fall into their own schemes .
For the wicked will boast , and the wicked will turn away from the LORD , and will weaken Him .
The wicked are proud in their faces , and say , &quot; The Lord will not seek after him ; all that he has in mind is for the absence of God
And all that he does is firm ; and thy judgment is beyond his sight ; and all his enemies blaspheme against them .
He said in his heart , &quot; I will not be shaken , neither will the generations of the world suffer disaster .
He is full of curses , deceit , and oppression , and his tongue is poison and wickedness
He waits in the villages ; he kills the innocent in secret ; his eyes spy on the helpless .
He is buried in the darkness , as a lion in a cave ; He is buried , to take away the needy ; He draws the net , and takes away the needy .
And he who bow down , and is unreliable and unsupported , falls under his claws , or as a violent man .
He said in his heart , &quot; God has forgotten , and he has covered his face , and he will never look
Arise , O LORD ; raise up thy hand , O God ; and forget not the troubled .
&quot; Why does the wicked despise God , saying in his heart , &apos; You will not be pursued
&quot; Indeed , you have seen , and you have seen , for the corruption of the wickedness , and for the recompense of the hands of those who do not trust in you ; and you have been a helper to the orphans
Let the arm of the wicked be broken ; and let the wicked pursue his evil to the end .
The Lord is a king forever and ever ; and the Gentiles have perished out of His land
&quot; You know , O Lord , the desire of the humble , and you will prepare their hearts , and listen to their prayers .
to redress the orphans and the oppressed , and to make the wicked no more to intimidate them
&quot; I have put my trust in the Lord . How do you say to me , &apos; You will go to your mountains like a bird
Behold , the wicked bend his bow , and set his arrow upon the strings , to shoot in the darkness the righteous in his heart .
If the foundations are destroyed , what can the righteous do
The Lord is in His sanctuary . The throne of the Lord is in heaven . His eyes see the world .
&quot; The Lord tests the righteous , but the wicked and those who love violence hate evil in their hearts
He will give Mib-nero to the wicked , and there will be fire , sulfur , and a hot wind , as a portion in their cups .
For the Lord is righteous , and he loves righteousness ; and the upright shall see his face .
Help , O Lord , for the devout is cut off , and there is no faithful among the people of the world
People lie to their neighbours . They speak with their lips smooth , and their hearts are divided .
&quot; The Lord will cut off the lips that are smooth , and the tongues that are exaggerated .
They said , &quot; We will prevail by our tongues ; our lips are our own ; and who will be our Lord ? &quot;
&quot; For the iniquity of the afflicted , and for the sigh of the poor , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; I am rising , and will place him in the place that He desires , in a secure place .
The word of the Lord is pure , as silver was refined seven times in a furnace of clay .
&quot; You will protect them , O Lord , and you will keep them from this generation forever .
As the lower ones rise up among the people , so do the wicked march .
How long wilt thou forget , O LORD , how long shall it be , and how long shall it be for ever , and how long wilt thou hide thy face from me ?
&quot; When will my heart be full of sorrow and sorrow all the days ? When will my enemies rise up and oppress me ?
&quot; Look at me , O Lord my God , and hear me , and light my eyes , lest I fall asleep to death .
&quot; Do not let my enemy say , &apos; I have overcome him . &apos; Do not let my enemy rejoice when I shake
But I rely on thy mercy , and my heart rejoiceth in thy salvation .
&quot; I will sing to the Lord , because He has been kind to me
Saying in the foolish heart , There is no God ; they are all wicked , they do abominations ; and none doeth good .
&quot; The Lord watches the world from heaven , to see whether there is one who understands or does not , and whether there is one who seeks God
They have all strayed from the right path , and have become unclean together ; and there is none that does good , not a single one .
&quot; Have the wicked no knowledge ? They eat my people as they eat , and do not ask the Lord
And there was great fear in them , because of God among the righteous .
&quot; You call the calculation of the needy a disgrace ; but the Lord is his refuge .
&quot; Let the salvation of Israel come out of Zion , and let the Lord bring back His captive children , and let Jacob rejoice , and let Israel rejoice
&quot; Lord , who can dwell in your tents , and who can dwell in your holy mountains
A man who does righteousness , works righteousness , and is truthful in his heart
&quot; He does not slander with his tongue , He does not harm his friends , He does not scoff at his neighbours
He hath despised the bandits in his sight , but hath respected him that feareth the LORD ; and he hath sworn , though he be weak , that he shall not be changed
He does not lend for profit , nor is he bribed to harm the innocent . Those who do these things will never be shaken .
Bless me , O God , for I have put my trust in You
O my heart , thou hast said unto the LORD , Thou art my Lord , and my goodness is not beyond thee
I am most pleased about the saints of the world , beautiful and good
&quot; Their sorrows will increase for those who substitute the Lord for other gods ; I will not offer their blood , nor will my lips bear the name of other gods .
The LORD is my inheritance , and a portion in my cup ; and thou shalt keep my gain for me .
Give me the land by rope , and sit in a beautiful place ; and my inheritance is in beauty .
&quot; I will praise the Lord who taught me , and my heart will watch over me at night .
&quot; I will put the Lord before me , and I will not shake , because he is on my right hand .
Therefore my heart shall rejoice , and my spirit shall rejoice , and my flesh shall dwell safely .
For thou shalt not leave my soul in the shadow , neither shalt thou make thy saints desolate .
You will guide me to the path of life . Pleasure is before You , and in Your right hand is eternal happiness .
O Lord , hear the righteousness , hear my call , and be attentive to me ; for it is not a prayer of deceitful lips .
May My judgment be delivered from before you , and may your eyes see justice .
Thou hast tested my heart ; thou hast tested me at night ; thou hast tried me and found none ; and I have made a vow that there be no error in my mouth .
&quot; By the words of your lips I speak concerning man &apos;s deeds , and I guard myself against the way of violent men .
My foot has set your path , and my feet have not slipped .
&quot; I have pleaded with you , O God , that you may hear me , and that you may listen to my voice .
Show your wonderful mercy , for you are the one who delivers with his right hand , who leans on you , and who departs from them and attacks them .
Protect me , as the eye that keeps his eyes , and hide me under the shadow of thy wings .
&quot; The evil one who oppresses me will encircle me , and he will destroy my life .
Their hearts are wrapped in grease , and they speak arrogantly in their mouths
They have encircled our footsteps , and they are staring at us , and they will bring us down to the ground
He is as a lion , seeking to devour , and as a young lion in the darkness
&quot; Arise , O Lord , and go before the enemy , and smite him ; and with thy sword save my life from the wicked .
Save me , O LORD , by the hand , from the world , and from the world that is blessed in this life ; and fill their bellies with thy treasures ; and they will be satisfied with their children , and leave the rest to their little ones .
&quot; As for me , I will see Your face in righteousness ; and when I wake up , I will be satisfied to see Your image .
&quot; The words of David , the servant of the Lord , who remembered them in the days when the Lord would deliver him out of the hand of all the enemies and of Saul , saying , &quot; Lord , my strength , I love you
The LORD is my rock , my dwelling place , my Savior , my God , my rock , upon which I have leaned ; He is my shield , my corner of salvation , my high place
I pray to the Lord , who is praised , that I may be delivered from the hand of the enemy
There was a dead rope around me , and I was terrified by the rush of bandits .
The rope of the shadow encircles me , and the net of death approaches me .
I cried to the Lord in distress ; I cried to my God ; He heard my voice from the temple ; My cry before Him entered into His ears .
Then the earth trembled because of his wrath , and the foundations of the mountains trembled .
From his nostrils smoke was poured out , and fire burned from his mouth , and coal was burned .
And He brought down the heavens , and came down in person ; and under His feet were black clouds .
He sat down to fly , and he flew fast with the wings of the wind .
He hid himself in darkness , in the darkness of water , in the thick clouds of the sky , and in the palaces around him .
For the light before Him , and His thick clouds , and hail and charcoal .
And the Lord casts a thunderbolt upon the heavens ; and the Most High makes a voice , and there is hail and charcoal
He casts out his arrows , and the enemies are scattered , and he sends out lightning , and disturbs them .
&quot; Your reproach , Yahweh , will come out of your nostrils , and the bottom of the sea will appear , and the roots of the earth will be revealed .
He stretched out his hand from heaven and seized me , and pulled me up from the great water .
He has delivered me from my enemies , and from those who hate me ; for they are stronger than I.
&quot; In the days of my calamity they will come against me ; but the Lord is my trust .
He has also brought me to a wide place ; He has lifted me up , because He is pleased with me .
&quot; The Lord answers me according to my righteousness ; He rewards me according to the cleanness of my hand
For I have obeyed the way of the Lord , and have not departed from my God with evil
All his statutes are before me , and I have not forsaken his statutes .
I have been perfect before him , and I have kept myself from my iniquity
Therefore the Lord will repay me according to my righteousness , according to the cleanness which I have in His sight .
Thou art the merciful , and Thou art the perfect , and Thou art the perfect
A clean man , Thou hast treated him with cleanness ; and a perverse man , Thou hast treated him with bend .
Thou wilt save the people who are afflicted ; Thou wilt make the proud eyes humble .
Thou shalt light my lamp , and the LORD my God shall light my darkness .
I have jumped into the enemy with you , I have jumped through the walls with my God
As for God , his way is perfect ; the word of the Lord is pure ; and whoever puts his trust in Him , He will be their shield .
&quot; Who is God except the Lord ? Who is the rock except our God ?
&quot; But He is God , Who bound me with strength , and perfected my ways .
He made my feet as the feet of a deer , and I was secure in high places .
He taught my hands to fight , and even my arms to open bronze bows
You have given me your salvation as a shield . Your right hand supports me . Your gentleness makes me great .
Thou hast made the foot of my feet wide , and my feet have not slipped .
&quot; I will pursue my enemies , and I will pursue them ; I will not destroy them , and I will never return .
I will strike them , and they will not be able to rise up ; and they will fall under my feet .
For thou hast bound my loins with strength , that I might fight ; and thou hast subjected under me all that have come up against me .
Thou hast also turned my enemies away before me , that I might cut off those who hate me .
They cry , and no one saves them ; they cry to the Lord , and He answers them not
I will break them as the dust before the wind , and I will cast them down as the mud of the streets .
Thou hast delivered me from the strife of the people ; Thou hast made me the head of the nations ; and the people that I know not shall serve me .
&quot; As soon as they hear My name , they will obey Me ; and the foreigners will surrender to Me .
The foreigners shall be weakened , and shall go out of their camps in fear of war .
The LORD is the living God ; let my rock be praised ; let the God of my salvation be glorified
&quot; This is the God who justified me , and who made all the people to serve under me .
Thou hast delivered me from the enemy , and lifted me up above them that arose against me , and delivered me from the wicked .
Therefore , O LORD , I will give thanks unto thee in the land of the nations , and I will sing praises unto thy name
&quot; The Lord has given great salvation to the king whom He has appointed , and to the anointed whom He has given mercy , to David and to his seed forever and ever
The heavens proclaim the glory of God , and the heavens proclaim His means
From that day to that day shall speak , and from that night to that night shall proclaim knowledge .
No words , no words , and no sound to hear
And his multitude was spread throughout the whole earth , and his words were spread unto the ends of the earth ; and God set a tent between them for the sun and the moon .
As the bridegroom goes out of his chamber , and as a mighty man walks on his way ,
He came out from the side of heaven , and went round to the side of heaven ; and there is none hidden from the heat of it .
The law of the Lord is ready to awaken the heart , and the law of the Lord is firm , and the fool is wise .
The word of the LORD is upright , and quickeneth the heart ; and the commandment of the LORD is clean , and the eyes of men are bright .
The Word of the Lord is pure and eternal ; and the Book of the Lord is true and perfect .
They are more envyable than gold , and more envyable than the abundance of pure gold , and sweeter than honey , and sweeter than the droplets of honey beneath the beehive .
And your servants will be warned , and they will have a great reward for them .
Who can know his own faults ? May Thou forgive my transgressions which are hidden and not manifested .
&quot; Hold up your servant , and do not commit indecency , and do not let this sin rule over me ; I will be completely free from the great sin .
&quot; Lord , my rock , my Redeemer , please the words of my mouth and the thoughts of my heart before you .
May the Lord hear you in the days of your tribulation , and may you be exalted in the name of the God of Jacob
May he deliver you from the sanctuary , and strengthen you from Zion
&quot; Remember all your offerings and your burnt offerings .
Give to you what you wish , and accomplish all your calculations
&quot; We will exalt ourselves for your salvation , and we will raise up our banners in the name of our God . May the Lord do all that you ask .
&quot; Now I know that the anointed , whom the Lord has saved , will obey him from His holy heaven , and will save him with the power of his right hand
Some ride in cars and some in horses , but we will mention the name of the Lord our God
&quot; They all fell down , but we rose up , and stood up with integrity .
&quot; Let the Lord deliver us , and let the king hear us in the time that we cry .
O Lord , the king shall rejoice in thy power ; how great shall be his joy in thy salvation !
&quot; You have given him what he desires in his heart , and you have not denied what his lips desire .
Blessed be thou that hast received him , and hast put upon his head the crown of gold
&quot; He asks of you for life , and you give him long days , straight to eternity .
He is glorified for thy salvation ; and thou hast added to him honour and glory .
Thou hast blessed him for ever , and made him rejoice before thee .
&quot; The king will rely on the Lord , for the loving kindness of the Most High will not shake .
Your hand shall search out all your enemies , and your right hand shall search out those who hate you .
&quot; When you are angry , make them as in a hot furnace ; the Lord will swallow them up in His wrath , and the fire will consume them .
&quot; You will destroy their offspring from the earth , and their descendants from among men .
For they intend to harm you . They have devised schemes , but they are not able to make them
And thou shalt cause them to turn their backs , and to flee ; and thou shalt set arrows upon their faces
&quot; Lord , may you be exalted in your power , and we will sing to you , and praise your great power .
My God , my God , why do you turn away from me , why do you not save me , why do you not listen to my whisper ?
&quot; My God , I cry in the daytime ; You do not answer ; I cry in the night , and you do not keep your voice .
But you are holy , and you are the throne of the praise of Israel .
Our ancestors rely on You , and they rely on You , and You will deliver them .
They will be saved when they cry to You ; and they will not be ashamed when they rely on You
&quot; But I am a worm and not a man , and I am ashamed and despised by the people
&quot; Everyone who sees me laughs at me , and shakes his head , and says ,
&quot; He puts his trust in the Lord , and the Lord will save him ; and the Lord will be pleased with him , and will rescue him
&quot; But You have brought me out of my mother &apos;s womb ; You have placed me in my mother &apos;s womb , and You have given me a heart of trust .
&quot; I was born from my mother , and I was given into your hand . You are my God , who gave birth to me from my mother .
&quot; Do not depart from me , for I am near to trouble , and no one has helped me
A great multitude of bulls surrounded me ; and Bashan &apos;s mighty bulls were round about me .
They opened their mouths to me , as if they had caught a lion that cried
I am cast out like water , and my bones are cut off , and my heart is waxed in me .
My energy is dry , like a tile ; my tongue is on my toothbed ; You will place me in the dust of the dead .
&quot; The dogs have surrounded me ; the wicked have surrounded me ; they have bound my hands and my feet .
My bones , I can count them all , and they stare at me staring at me
&quot; And they divided my garments , and cast lots for my inner garments
Do not depart from me , O Lord ; come quickly , O my Savior , and help me .
Save my soul from the sword , and save my life from the dogs .
&quot; Save me from the mouth of the lion ; You have listened to me ; You have delivered me from the corner of the beast .
I will pass on your name to my brethren , and I will praise you in the congregation .
You shall fear the LORD , and praise him ; and the seed of Jacob shall glorify him ; and the seed of Israel shall fear him .
For he hath not despised the oppressed , nor hid his face from him ; and when the oppressed cried , he listened .
I praise thee in the assembly , and it is from thee ; and I will give my will before the people who fear the LORD .
The humble shall be filled , and those who seek the Lord shall praise Him . May your hearts live long .
&quot; All the corners of the earth will remember the Lord and obey Him ; and all the nations will worship before You
For the LORD hath dominion over all the nations , and over all the kingdoms .
All the rich men of the earth shall eat and drink and worship ; and all those who go down into the dust and cannot live their lives shall worship before Him .
&quot; He shall have descendants to serve him , and the works of the Lord shall be passed on to the next generation .
&quot; They will come to convey His righteousness to the people who are to be born , and will tell them that this is what He has done .
The Lord is my shepherd , and I will not be lacking
&quot; He laid me down on the grass , and brought me by the waters of Ko-Anshi
He has awakened my soul , and guided me in his name to righteousness
Though I walk through the shadow of death , I am not afraid to be struck : for thou art with me , and thy rod and thy rod comfort me .
&quot; You have prepared a feast for me before my enemies ; You have anointed my head with oil , and filled my cup with blessings .
&quot; There will be grace and mercy with me all my life , and I will dwell in the house of the Lord forever and ever .
The earth and all that is in it , the world and all that dwells therein , belong to the Lord
He built the earth upon the sea , and set it firmly upon the waters
Who can ascend the mountain of the Lord , and who can stand in His sanctuary ?
A man whose hands are clean , who does not deceive , and who does not swear to treachery
Blessed be he by the Lord , and justified be he by the God of his salvation
&quot; This is the tribe that seeks the Lord ; this is Jacob that seeks your face .
Lift up your heads , O gates of the city ; the doors of everlasting shall be lifted up , and the glorious king shall come in .
Who is the King of glory , the mighty and mighty Lord , the mighty Lord in battle ?
Lift up your heads , O gates of the city ; lift up your heads , O everlasting gate ; and the glorious king shall come in .
&quot; Who is the King of glory , the Lord of hosts , the King of glory ?
My heart is lifted up to thee , O LORD
O my God , I have put my trust in You ; do not make me ashamed ; do not make my enemies boast against me
Whosoever waiteth for thee shall not be ashamed ; but he that committh wickedness without cause shall be ashamed .
Show me thy ways , O Lord , and teach me thy ways
Guide me and teach me by thy truth ; for thou art the God of my salvation ; and I await thee all the days .
Remember , O LORD , thy mercy and thy loving kindness , for this is everlasting .
&quot; Remember not my sins of my youth , and my transgressions ; O Lord , remember me by Your grace , and by Your mercy .
&quot; The Lord is good and righteous ; therefore He will guide sinners to the right path
He will guide the humble according to justice , and teach them His doctrine .
&quot; He who keeps his covenant and his statutes is merciful and faithful to him
&quot; Lord , forgive me my sins in Your name , for My sins are great .
Whoever fears the Lord , the Lord will guide him to the path he chooses
He shall dwell safely , and his seed shall bear the land .
The Lord is intimate with those who fear Him ; He will direct them by His covenant .
&quot; My eyes are always on the Lord , for He will take my feet out of the net .
Turn to me , and have mercy on me , for I am a lonely and afflicted
My heart is full of sorrow ; save me from my affliction .
See my affliction , and my hardship , and forgive me all my sins
Look at my enemies , for they are many , and they hate me with bitterness .
Protect my life , and save me , that I may not be ashamed , for I have put my trust in You
Keep me pure and upright , for I await thee
Redeem Israel , O God , from all his sorrows
O Lord , forgive me , for I have done righteousness , and I have put my trust in the Lord , and I am not shaken
&quot; Look at me , O Lord , and test me , and quench my bowels and my intestines
For your loving kindness is always before me , and I do according to your truth .
I do not sit with the liars , nor with those who hide the truth .
&quot; I hate the meeting of the wicked , and I will not sit with the wicked .
&quot; I will wash my hands , O Lord , to show my innocence , and I will surround Your altar
I have a good voice of thanksgiving . I also want to mention all your wonderful deeds
&quot; I love the house in which you dwell , O Lord , and your glorious dwelling place
Don &apos;t take away my soul with the sinners , and don &apos;t take away my life with the bloodthirsty
In their hands is wickedness , and in their right hand is bribery .
&quot; But as for me , be pure ; forgive me , and have mercy on me .
My feet stand in a plain place : I will praise the LORD in the congregation
The LORD is my light , and my salvation ; and who am I afraid of , and who am I afraid of , and who am I afraid of , and who am I afraid of , and who am I afraid of , and who am I afraid of ?
&quot; The evildoer , my enemy , falls upon his feet when he comes to eat my flesh .
My heart shall not be afraid , neither shall the camps of the army attack me ; and I shall be secure even as the swords rise up against me .
&quot; There is one thing which I have asked of the Lord , and which I will seek : to dwell in the house of the Lord for a lifetime , and to look on His glory , and to ask in His house .
&quot; He will keep me secretly , because I am in trouble ; He will hide me in his tent , He will hide me in the secret place of his tent ; He will raise me up on a rock .
Behold , I am able to rise above the enemy on all sides ; I will sacrifice in his tent with joy ; I will sing and sing praises to the Lord .
&quot; Hear , O Lord , when I call with a loud voice , and have mercy on me , and obey me ;
Then said I unto thee , O LORD , I seek thy face , when thou saidst , Seek my face
&quot; Do not hide your face from me , and do not drive away your servants in anger . You have always helped me . God who has saved me , do not forsake me , and do not forsake me .
&quot; My parents have forsaken me , and the Lord will receive me
Teach me , O Lord , by thy ways , and guide me in a straight path for the sake of my enemies
&quot; Do not give me to the enemy according to his will ; but come up against me for those who bear false witness and speak evil words .
&quot; If I had not believed in the land of the living to see the grace of the Lord , I would have been ashamed early
&quot; Wait for the Lord , and be courageous , and strengthen your heart , and I say , &quot; Wait for the Lord
I beg thee , O LORD , that thou shut not thy mouth unto me , O rock of mine ; and if thou shut thy mouth unto me , I will be as the dead .
&quot; When I call to you to raise my hand to the Holy One , hear the voice of my supplication .
&quot; Do not separate me from the wicked and the wicked , who speak peacefully to their neighbours , but are wicked in their hearts .
Blessed be thou according to their works , and according to their evil deeds , and according to their hands , and add unto them their recompense .
&quot; If they do not keep in mind what the Lord has done and what His hands have done , He will destroy them and not build them up .
Blessed is the Lord , for he has heard my plea
The LORD is my strength and my shield ; I will rely on him in my heart , and he will help me ; therefore I will rejoice in my heart , and I will sing praises to him in songs .
The Lord is the strength of His people , and the salvation of His anointed
&quot; Save your people , bless your inheritance , feed them , support them forever
O children of God , give glory to the Lord , and give power to the Lord
to give him the glory of the name of the Lord , and to worship the Lord in holy garments
The voice of the LORD is on the waters : the God of glory thundereth , and the LORD thundereth upon the great waters .
The voice of the Lord is powerful , and the voice of the Lord is mighty
The voice of the LORD trembleth against the acacia tree : the LORD trembleth against the acacia tree of Lebanon .
And he made him to leap like a calf , and Lebanon and the West like a wild calf
The voice of the LORD divided the flame
The voice of the LORD stirred up the wilderness , and the LORD stirred up the wilderness of lowliness .
The voice of the LORD stirred the deer , and the trees were taken away from their brightness ; and all that were in His temple glorified Him
&quot; The Lord sits as king when the flood is overflowing , and the Lord sits as king forever and ever
The Lord will give strength to His people , and the Lord will give peace and blessing to His people
I will praise thee , O LORD , because thou hast lifted me up , and the enemy shall not boast against me
&quot; Lord , my God , I have prayed to You , and You have healed me
&quot; Lord , You have delivered my soul from the shadow , and have kept me alive , and have not come down to the pit
O holy people of the LORD , sing praises unto him , and praise him that is holy to be remembered
For his anger is but a turning of an eye , and his mercy a lifetime ; and he will weep in the morning , though he weep in the night .
&quot; As for me , I keep all things straight , and say , &apos; I will never shake
&quot; Lord , You have blessed my mountains to stand firm ; You have covered my face , and I am terrified
&quot; I have asked thee , O Lord , and I have pleaded with the Lord , saying ,
&quot; What good is it for me , that I am slain with blood , that I go down to the pit ? Can the dust praise You , and tell Your truth ?
O LORD , hear me , and have mercy on me ; O LORD , help me
You have turned my weeping into dancing ; You have taken off my linen , You have clothed me with joy .
&quot; Let my spirit sing praises to You , and not cease ; O Lord , my God , I will thank You forever and ever .
&quot; I have leaned on You , O Lord , that I should never be ashamed , and that You might save me by Your righteousness
&quot; Hear with your ears , and save me , and make me a strong rock , and a shield for me .
&quot; For you are my rock and my shelter ; therefore guide me , and point me in your name .
Save me from the snares of men , which they have set up for me ; for thou art my shield .
&quot; I have delivered my soul into your hand . You have redeemed me , O Lord God of truth .
&quot; I hate him who believes in the God of nothing , but I rely on the Lord
I will rejoice and rejoice in thy mercy , for thou hast seen my affliction , and knowest the hardships of my heart .
Thou hast not delivered me into the hand of the enemy ; thou hast set my feet in the broad place .
&quot; Lord , have mercy on me , for I am in distress , and my eyes are dried up by sorrow , and my soul and my flesh are not comforted .
My life is consumed by sorrow ; my years are wasted by sighing ; my strength is weakened by my iniquity ; and my bones are dried up .
For I am ashamed of all my enemies , even more so in my neighbourhood . Those who know me are afraid of me , and those who see me from the outside hide themselves from me .
I am forgotten as a dead man , and no one remembers me ; I am like a broken vessel .
I have heard the slander of many , and all the surroundings were terrified ; and when they had agreed to attack me , they plotted to destroy my life .
&quot; I am still counting on You , Lord , and I say , &apos; You are my God .
&quot; My life is in your hand ; save me from the hand of my enemies and from those who oppress me .
Make thy face to shine upon thy servants , and save me by thy mercy
O LORD , make me not to be ashamed , for I have called on thee ; make the wicked ashamed , and make them shut up in the shadow .
Let his mouth be dumb , and let his lips be silent .
How great is the favour which thou hast stored up for them , which thou hast bestowed upon them in the sight of the world !
And thou shalt hide them in secret before thee , lest there be any plot against them ; and thou shalt keep them secretly in the tents , lest there be wrangling of tongues .
Blessed is the LORD , for he hath shown me a strange mercy in a strong city
&quot; As for me , I hastened to say , &apos; I am cut off from Your sight . &apos; Yet when I call on You , You hear my plea .
O holy people of the LORD , love him ; for the LORD keepeth the faithful , and giveth full recompense to the proud .
Be courageous , and strengthen your hearts , all you who rely on the Lord
Blessed is he who forgives and covers his sins
&quot; There is no deceit in every heart ; and the Lord is not guilty ; and he is blessed
&quot; When I shut my mouth and do not confess , My bones are dried up because of the Last Day
Thy hands are heavy upon me in the night and in the day , and my semen is consumed as dryness in the summer .
&quot; I declare my sins to you , and I do not conceal my evil deeds ; I say , &apos; I will confess my sins to the Lord , and you will forgive my evil deeds . &apos; &quot;
Therefore all the pious will pray to You when You will find them , and they will not be able to come to Him in the day when the waters are overflowing .
Thou art my hiding place , and thou wilt deliver me from my affliction : and a song of salvation is round about me .
&quot; I will teach you , and direct you to the way that you should walk , and I will keep my eyes fixed on you , and I will warn you
Thou shalt not be like the unwise horse , and thou shalt gnaw his head with the rings ; otherwise thou shalt not be able to tame him .
The wicked will suffer more , and the one who trusts in the Lord will be surrounded by mercy
Let your righteous men rejoice in the Lord ; let those who are upright in their hearts rejoice
O you who are righteous , rejoice in the Lord ; for the praise of the upright is righteous .
&quot; You shall sing praises to the Lord by playing the harp , and by singing hymns with ten strings
Sing a new song to him , and play it cleverly , and sound it loud
For the word of the Lord is upright , and all that He does is truthful .
He loves righteousness and justice , and the loving kindness of the Lord is in all the earth
The heavens are made by the life of the Lord , and all things are made by the breath of his mouth
He gathered the sea as a basin , and gathered the deep sea in a treasure house
Let all the earth fear the Lord , and let all the inhabitants of the earth fear Him .
For he said yes , and there was ; and he commanded , and there was .
&quot; The Lord has made the calculation of the nations void , and the thoughts of the people have no effect
The plan of the Lord is for ever , and the thoughts of his heart are for ever .
Blessed is the land which the Lord hath chosen for his inheritance , and blessed is the people which he hath chosen for his inheritance
And the Lord looked from heaven , and he saw all the people of the world
From his dwelling place , He looks outwards at all the inhabitants of the earth .
He that made their hearts whole , and observed all that they did .
A king can &apos;t win with more troops ; a warrior can &apos;t save with more power .
It is in vain to be saved by a horse , and a horse cannot save a man by force
The eyes of the Lord look upon those who fear Him , and upon those who look upon His mercy
to save their lives from death , and to keep them alive in famine
Our hearts wait for the Lord ; He is our help , our shield .
Our hearts shall rejoice in him , for we have relied on his holy name
&quot; O Lord , grant us mercy according to what we have been counting on You .
&quot; And David went mad in the sight of Abimelech , and was driven out of his presence ; and I will praise the LORD when I will , and the words of his praise shall be in my mouth all the time
&quot; My heart will be exalted by the Lord ; and the humble hears , and rejoices .
&quot; You and I shall glorify the name of the Lord with greatness
&quot; I have sought the Lord , and He has answered me ; He has delivered me from all fear
All who look on Him will be glorified , and their faces will not be ashamed .
&quot; The Lord listens to my cry , and delivers me out of all trouble .
&quot; The angels of the Lord will surround those who fear Him and will rescue them
You will taste the grace of the Lord , and you will know that He is good . Blessed are those who put their trust in Him .
O ye saints of the LORD , fear him ; for there is none lacking in fear of him
The young lion lacks food and is hungry ; but the one who seeks the Lord has no shortage of goodness .
&quot; Listen to me , all you disciples , and I will teach you to fear the way of the Lord
Who loves to live , loves to live long , and enjoys happiness
Let your tongue not speak evil words , and your lips not speak deceitful words
To do good from evil , to seek peace , and to pursue with one heart
The eyes of the Lord look upon the righteous , and his ears hear their cry
&quot; The Lord will turn his face to the wicked , and will blot out their name from the earth
The righteous cry , and the Lord hears , and delivers them out of all trouble
The LORD is near to the wounded , and saveth the soul of repentance .
The righteous suffers much ; but the Lord delivers him out of all this
And He preserved his bones , and not one of them was broken .
Evil will kill the wicked , and he who hates the righteous will be condemned .
&quot; The Lord redeems the soul of His servant ; and whoever leans on Him will not be condemned .
Lord , fight against me , fight against them ; fight against me , fight against them
Come up and help me , with your shields of all sizes
Take out your guns , and stop those who chase after me ; and say to my soul , I am your Savior .
Let him who seeks my life be ashamed , and let him who murders me be ashamed afterwards .
&quot; Let them be like a branch before the wind , and let the angels of the Lord drive them away
Let their paths be dark and slippery , and let the angels of the Lord pursue them .
For they have appointed snares for me without cause ; they have dug pits without cause , and they will destroy my life .
May the calamity come upon him suddenly , and may the nets of darkness bind him , and may he fall into the calamity thereof .
My heart shall rejoice in the Lord , and in His salvation shall my heart rejoice
&quot; All my bones will say , &apos; Lord , who can save the needy like you , from the one who is stronger than you , from the needy , from the one who has taken him ?
&quot; The wicked witness will rise up and question what I do not know .
For they recompense me with evil , and make my soul to suffer .
As for me , when they were sick , I clothed myself in linen , and fasted , and suffered my soul ; and all that I desired was returned to me .
I do so as if he were my friend and my brother ; and I give myself up to mourning , as a man mourns for his mother
And they rejoiced in my affliction ; and they gathered themselves together ; and those whom I knew not gathered themselves against me ; and they could not break me apart .
&quot; They bite my teeth like fools who laugh at their seats
&quot; How long will it be , O Lord , that thou seest in vain , and savest my soul from their oppression , and my life , and from the little lion ?
I will give thanks to you in the assembly , and I will praise you in the people
&quot; Do not allow those who hate me without cause to boast against me ; Do not allow those who hate me without cause to close their eyes to me
For they speak not peaceful words , but deceitful words , and harm the peaceful of the earth .
And they opened their mouths greatly against me , saying , Aha , Aha , our eyes have been seen
&quot; You have seen , O Lord ; do not shut your mouth , and do not depart from me , O Lord .
&quot; My God , my Lord , awaken me , and judge my affairs , and prove my iniquities .
&quot; Lord , my God , judge me according to your righteousness , and let them not boast against me .
Let them not say in their hearts , &quot; Ah , our will has come to pass ; let them not say , &quot; We have swallowed him up
Let him who loves my affliction be ashamed , and let him who denies me be ashamed , and let him be ashamed
Let those who rejoice in My righteousness rejoice , and let them say , &quot; Rejoice in the Lord , and let the Lord rejoice in the peace of His servants .
&quot; My tongue will speak of Your righteousness all the day long , and praise You often .
For the sin of the wicked man said in his heart , I fear not God in my eyes
He exalts himself , and his iniquity is not revealed , nor hated
The words of his mouth are full of iniquity and deceit , and he is cut off from doing good with wisdom .
He seeks iniquity in his bed , and is determined to do evil deeds , and does not hate evil .
O Lord , Your loving kindness , above and above the heavens ; Your faithfulness reaches to the heavens .
Your righteousness is like the high mountains ; Your judgments like the depths ; O LORD , save the livestock of the people .
How precious is Your loving kindness , O God ! The world dwells in the shade of Your wings
And they shall be filled with the sweetness of thy house , and thou shalt cause them to drink of the water of thy river ;
For there is a spring of life in you ; and in your light we shall see the light .
May You always show mercy to those who know You , and to those who are honest in their hearts ,
Let not the foot of the proud tread upon me ; let not the hand of the wicked pursue me .
The wicked in it have been subdued ; they have been overthrown , and will not rise again .
Let not the heart be troubled for the wicked , nor let jealousy arise from the unrighteous
For they are as the grass that is cut down , and as the herbs that are dried up .
&quot; Believe in the Lord and do good , and dwell on the earth with His faith as a sustenance
And rejoice in the Lord , and He will give you that which is in your heart
&quot; When you give your affairs to the Lord and rely on Him , He will accomplish them
He will make your righteousness as light , and your equity as noon .
Rely silently on the Lord , and wait patiently for Him ; and let not the hearts of those who have been guided by the way and the works of wickedness be troubled .
Stop your anger , and turn away from it ; and do not be filled with distress to do evil .
For the wicked shall be cut off ; but the waiter of the Lord shall bear the earth .
There is also a time when the wicked shall be desolate ; and thou art the watcher over his dwelling place , and he shall be desolate .
But the humble shall bear the earth , and rejoice in the abundance of peace .
The wicked seeks the righteous , and bites his teeth
laugh at him , for the days of his punishment are coming .
The wicked has mounted up his bow , he has cut off his sword , he has overthrown the needy and the afflicted , he has killed the upright .
&quot; Their sword will pierce their hearts , and their bow will be broken .
A righteous man &apos;s wealth , though small , exceeds that of many evil men .
For the arm of the wicked will be broken ; but the Lord is the supporter of the righteous .
The LORD knoweth the days of the perfect man , and their inheritance is for ever .
They shall not be ashamed in the time of trouble , nor shall they be satisfied in the days of famine .
But the wicked shall perish ; and the enemy of the Lord shall be as the fat of a lamb ; and they shall be destroyed , as smoke .
The wicked borrows and does not repay , but the righteous are kind and give
&quot; He who is blessed by the Lord will bear the earth , and he who is cursed will be cut off
The footsteps of the righteous are determined by the Lord ; and the Lord loves his ways .
And he shall not fall down , though he lose his feet : for the Lord is with him by his hand .
I have not seen the righteous abandoned , nor have I seen his seed beggar , when I was young and old ,
He has been merciful to man all the days , and lent to him ; and blessed are his seed .
When thou doest righteousness from evil , thou shalt dwell far away
For the Lord loves righteousness , and does not forsake His saints : they shall be blessed for ever : but the seed of the wicked shall be cut off .
The righteous shall bear the earth , and shall dwell therein forever .
The mouth of the righteous speaks wisdom ; and his tongue speaks justice .
The law of God is in his heart , and his feet never slip .
The wicked sees the wise man , and seeks to kill him .
&quot; The Lord will not leave him in the hands of the wicked , neither will he judge his sins at the time of judgment
&quot; When you wait for the Lord , and obey His ways , He will raise you up , and make you bear the earth ; and you will see when the wicked are cut off .
I have seen the wicked have power , as a green tree grows in the land
A man passed through it , and he did not expect it ; and I sought him , but he did not find it .
Behold the perfect man , and behold the upright : for the peaceful have a good end .
As for those who do evil , they will be destroyed , and the wicked will be cut off .
&quot; But the righteous are saved because of the Lord , who is their shelter in times of distress
&quot; The Lord has helped them , He has delivered them from the wicked , He has delivered them out of the hand of the wicked , For they have put their trust in Him
O Lord , do not reproach me in anger , and do not punish me in fierce anger
For your arrows have struck me , and your hands have pressed me .
My flesh is full of your wrath , and my bones are not restless because of my sins .
My iniquity is high above my head , as a burden that I cannot bear .
Because of my foolishness , my wounds smelled like puss .
My pain , the great wrestling , the end of the day grief
My waist is full of fire . My flesh is full of nothing
I am afflicted and weary , and in my distress , I groan
My heart is before thee , O LORD ; my sighs are not hidden from thee .
My heart trembled , my strength weakened , and there was not even light in my eyes
My good friends have stood by me because of my affliction , and my relatives have stood far away from me .
&quot; He who seeks my life sets up nets , and he who seeks to harm me speaks evil words , and devises devises all the days .
But I hear not as a deaf , nor open my mouth as a dumb tongue
As for me , who heareth not , there is no answer in my mouth
&quot; I look on you , Lord , and you will hear me , O Lord , my God .
&quot; I said , &apos; I am afraid they exalt themselves against me , and they exalt themselves against me when I am lost .
I almost fell . My pain is always before me
I will confess my iniquity , and I will mourn for my sin .
But my enemies are vigorous and mighty , and they have multiplied against me without cause .
&quot; The evil-doers are against me , because I seek the good .
Do not forsake me , O LORD ; do not depart from me , O God of my soul .
&quot; Help me , O Lord of my salvation , quickly .
&quot; I said , &apos; I will guard my words and my deeds , lest my tongue sin ; and when the wicked are before me , I will squeeze my mouth with rings . &apos; &quot;
I was silent , and I could not speak good words ; and my sorrow was set in motion .
My heart is hot in me , and when I meditate , the fire burns , and I speak with my tongue
&quot; Lord , let me know the end of my life , and the number of my days , and let me know that my days are not long .
Thou hast made my days as narrow as the palms of my hands ; and the years of my life are as nothing before thee ; and the time of every man &apos;s security is nothing but vanity .
They are busy and in vain . They accumulate treasures and do not know who will collect them in the future .
&quot; What am I waiting for now , O Lord ? My hope is in You
Save me from all transgression , and let me not be ashamed of the foolish .
&quot; Because what I have encountered is from You , I will not speak silently
Take away from me thy reproach , and I will perish because of the rebuke of thy hand .
Thou hast punished man for his iniquity , and when thou hast punished him , thou hast destroyed his smile , as the garment is bitten by the beast ; and the world is a delusion .
&quot; Listen to my prayers , O Lord , and listen to my calls ; I weep , O Lord , and do not be silent ; for I am before you as a traveller and as a dweller , as my fathers were
Forgive me , that I may return before I go , and be healed with strength .
I waited patiently for the Lord , and He listened to my cry
He brought me up out of the pit , out of the dust , He set my feet on a rock , He made my steps steady
&quot; He has made me sing a new song , which is the praise of our God . Many will see and fear , and will rely on the Lord
Blessed is he who puts his trust in the Lord , and does not take heed of the proud and false generations ;
&quot; Lord , my God , the wonders that you do , and the thoughts that you have for us , cannot be made clear to you ; and if they should be made clear , they cannot be numbered .
&quot; You do not rejoice in offerings and gifts ; You have opened my ears to burnt offerings and sacrifices for sins , which you do not want .
Then said I , &quot; Look , I am come ; my affairs are recorded in the book of the record .
&quot; My God , I am glad to do your will , and your law is in my heart .
&quot; I will proclaim the sound of righteousness in the great assembly , and I will not stop my lips ; as you know , Lord ,
I have not concealed Your righteousness in my heart ; I have declared Your faithfulness and Your salvation ; I have not concealed Your mercy and Your truth in the assembly
O Lord , do not restrain thy mercy from me ; and let thy loving kindness and thy truth always bless me .
My iniquity has overtaken me , and I am not able to stand up ; it is more than my hair , and I am afraid in my heart .
&quot; Help me , O Lord , with grace ; and help me , O Lord , with speed .
Let those who seek me and destroy my life be ashamed together , and let those who rejoice in my affliction be ashamed afterwards .
May those who say to me , &quot; Ah , Ah , Ah , &quot; perish in shame
Let all that seek thee rejoice in thee ; let those that love thy salvation say , The Lord is great
&quot; But I am afflicted and needy , and the Lord cares for me . You are my help and my salvation . Don &apos;t delay , O God .
Blessed be the poor , and the LORD shall deliver him in the days of trouble
&quot; The Lord will save him , and he will live , and he will rejoice in the earth . Do not give him to the enemy , as he pleases
&quot; When he is sick , the Lord will support him ; and when he is sick , You will give him a bed
&quot; I said , &quot; Lord , have mercy on me , and heal me , because I have sinned against You
&quot; My enemy speaks against me with evil words , saying , &apos; How long will he die before his name is destroyed ?
&quot; When he comes to see me , he speaks lies ; and when he comes out of his heart , he speaks evil .
&quot; All who hate me speak of me in unison , and they intend to harm me .
They said , &quot; There is a sickness on him , and he has laid down and will not be able to rise again .
Even my friends , on whom I rely , who have eaten my food , kick me with their feet
