&quot; They will be stumbled by their tongues , and everyone who sees them will shake his head .
All men should fear , preach God &apos;s work , and understand His works
The righteous will rejoice in the Lord , and will put their trust in Him ; and the upright in all their hearts will boast .
O God , the people of Zion await the praise of thee , and the promises which thou hast promised shall be repaid unto thee
&quot; He who has blood will come to you , O Lord who hears and prays ,
My iniquity hath overcome me ; and forgive us our transgressions .
Blessed is he whom thou hast chosen , and whom thou hast brought near unto thee , and whom thou hast kept in thy house ; and we shall be filled with the goodness of thy dwelling place , and of thy sanctuary .
&quot; Save us , O God of our salvation ! You will obey us with majesty and righteousness , and you will be the trustee of all the ends of the earth and of the sea .
He stretched out his loins with great strength , and set the mountains in order with strength
He calmed the sound of the seas , and the sound of the waves therein , and the noise of the people .
Fear for thy signs , O man that dwelleth in the ends of the earth : thou hast made the land of sunrise and sunset rejoice .
Thou hast taken care of the land , and rainedst it with rain , and madest it fat ; and the rivers of God were full of water ; and thus hast thou watered the land , and prepared for man five valleys .
You have watered the wells of the field , You have watered the ridges of the field , You have brought down the rain , You have made the earth soft , And blessed are those who grow in it .
Thou hast crowned thee with grace for years , and thy paths are poured down with oil .
Drops on the grass fields of the wilderness , and the hills bend with joy .
The grass field was clothed with sheep , and there were five valleys in the valley , and they all shouted and sang
All the earth cries out to God
Praise the glory of His name , and invent His glory with words of praise .
When you say to God , &quot; What a dreadful thing your deeds are ! Your great enemy will surrender to you
All the earth shall worship You , and praise You , and praise Your name .
&quot; Come to see what God does , and what He does to the world is awesome .
He turned the sea into dry land , and the people walked over the river , and we rejoiced therein
He governs all people in His power for ever and ever . His eyes see the nations , and the rebellious cannot boast .
O people , praise our God , and let the voice of his praise be heard .
&quot; He kept our lives alive , and did not shake our feet .
&quot; You have tested us , O God , and have made us like silver .
&quot; You have brought us into the net , and placed the burden on our bodies .
Thou hast caused men to ride upon our heads , and we passed through water and fire ; and thou hast brought us to a land of abundance .
&quot; I will bring a burnt offering into your house , and I will return my vows to you
&quot; It is what I have spoken in my lips , and what I have promised in my mouth in times of distress .
&quot; I will burn the fat cattle , and I will offer you the burnt offering of the goats , and I will offer the goats and the lambs .
&quot; Listen , all you who fear God , and I will tell you what He has done for me .
&quot; I have prayed to him with my mouth , and my tongue has called him high .
&quot; If I put my heart on iniquity , the Lord will not listen
But God heard , and he listened to my prayer .
Blessed is God , who has not turned away my prayers , nor left me His mercy
May God have mercy on us , and bless us , and shine upon us with his face .
Let the world know thy way , and let the nations know thy salvation
Blessed be the land of Israel , O God , and blessed be all the people
May all the nations rejoice , for thou wilt judge all the people with justice , and guide all the nations of the world .
Blessed be the land of Israel , O God , and blessed be all the people
The earth has passed through her inheritance ; and God is our God , and will bless us .
Blessed be God with us , and all the ends of the earth shall fear Him .
May God rise , and spread out his enemies , and let those who hate him flee from before him
They are driven away as smoke is blown away by the wind ; and the wicked are destroyed in the sight of God , as wax is burned with fire .
Only the righteous shall rejoice , and shall be exalted before God
Sing unto God , and praise his name : repair the way of him that rideth through the wilderness : his name is the LORD : rejoice before him .
God is the father of the orphans in His holy place , and the avenger of the widows
God gives home to the lonely , and brings forth the captive to prosperity ; but the rebellious dwell in a dry land .
&quot; You have come out before your people , O God , walking in the wilderness .
Then the earth trembled when she saw the face of God , and the heavens rained , and the mountain of Sinai trembled when she saw the face of the God of Israel .
O God , You have rained a great rain ; You have strengthened your inheritance Israel in the time of weakness .
Thy congregation dwelleth therein ; and thy mercy , O God , is prepared for the afflicted .
The women who gave the main orders and transmitted the information became a large group
The king of the host fled , fled . The women who waited at home were divided .
As the wings of a dove are of silver , and the feathers of a dove are of gold .
When the Almighty chases away kings in the land , it is as snow in Samaria
The mountain of Bashan is the mountain of God . The mountain of Bashan is the mountain of many mountains .
&quot; Why do you , mountains of mountains , incline to the mountains where God wills to dwell , where the Lord will dwell forever and ever ?
God &apos;s chariots are multiplied , and the Lord is in them as in Mount Sinai
&quot; You have been sacrificed in the high heavens , and have taken away your enemies , and have been offered among men , and among the rebellious , that the Lord God may dwell with them
Blessed is the Lord , who bears the burden of our burdens daily , the God of our salvation .
&quot; God is the God of all salvation for us , and man can be delivered from death , and he is in the Lord Yahweh
But God will break the head of his enemy , the head of the wicked .
&quot; I will bring the people back from Bashan , and I will bring them back from the depths , &quot; said the Lord
To break the enemy , To kick your feet in the blood , To scorn your dog &apos;s tongue out of it
Thou art my God , O God , my King ; and they have seen thee walking , and entered into the sanctuary
The singing line before and the singing line after , in the midst of the drumming girl .
Blessed is the Lord God , who came from the beginning of Israel , when he praised him in the congregations
And there were over them Benjamin , and the princes of Judah , and their multitude , and the princes of Zebulun , and the princes of Naphtali ,
The power of Israel is God &apos;s ; O God , strengthen that which thou hast done for us
&quot; For your house in Jerusalem , the kings will bring you their offerings
Rebuke the beasts of the reed , and the herds of bulls , and the calves of the tribes , and smite the pieces of silver under their feet ; God has driven away the tribes that are at war .
The princes of Egypt shall come forth to God , and the ancients shall lift up their hands to pray .
Sing unto God , O ye nations of the earth , and praise the LORD .
Praise the Lord , who rides from the ancient days above the heavens ; He makes a voice , a great voice .
You shall give your power to God . His glory is above Israel , and His power is in the heavens .
Blessed is the God of Israel , who has given power to his people , O God , from the Holy One .
Save me , O God , for the waters of the people shall overflow me
I am embedded in a deep muddy place , where I have no foothold ; I am in the depths of water , and great waters are overflowing me
My throat is dry because of my cry , and my eyes are blind because I wait for God .
He that hateth me without cause hateth me more than my hair ; and he that hateth me without cause is mighty , and he that cut me off is mighty ; and he that hath not taken , let him repay me .
My foolishness , O God , Thou knewest it ; and my sins cannot be hidden .
O Lord , Lord of hosts , let not those who wait for you be ashamed of me ; O God of Israel , let not those who seek you be ashamed of me
For I have been reproached for your sake , and I am full of shame
My brethren see me as a foreigner , and my brethren as a foreigner
For I am anxious for your house as a fire , and the reproach of your people is upon me .
&quot; I cried and fasted to torment my heart . It was a shame for me
And I took cloth as a garment , and made them laugh .
Speak of me at the gates of the city , and the drunkards sing of me
&quot; But I pray to the Lord your God , when I am well pleased : O God , hear me in the abundance of your mercy , and in the truth that you have saved me .
Save me from the dust , and do not let me fall into it ; deliver me from those who hate me , and from the depths of the waters .
Don &apos;t let the great waters pass over me , Don &apos;t let the depths swallow me up , Don &apos;t let the pits meet above me
&quot; Listen to me , O Lord , for your loving kindness is good ; and turn to me with your abundant mercy .
Do not hide thy servant from me ; for I am in distress , and hasten to hearken to me .
&quot; Come near to me , and redeem me ; and redeem me for my enemies
You know the reproach , the deceit , and the shame which I have suffered ; and my enemies are before you .
The insults have broken my heart , and I am filled with sorrow . I hoped for comfort , but there was none . I hoped for comfort , but there was none
They give me bitterness as food ; I am thirsty ; they give me vinegar to drink
Let their feast be a snail before them , and in their times of peace a crow .
May their eyes be darkened , and they see not ; and may Thou make their waist tremble often .
Turn away your anger from them , and pursue them with your wrath .
Let their dwelling place be turned into a wilderness , and let their tents be inhabited by no one .
For they that thou hast struck are oppressors ; and they that thou hast wounded are making fun of his sorrow .
Let them sin on their sins , and let them not be justified before thee
May they be blotted out of the book of life , and not be recorded among the righteous
&quot; But I am in distress and sorrow . May Your salvation place me in high places , O God .
I will praise the name of God in poetry , and I will praise him in thanksgiving
&quot; Then the Lord will rejoice , as if he had offered a cow , or a bull with horns and feet
Let the humble see , and rejoice ; and let your hearts be refreshed , those who seek God .
For the Lord hears the poor , and does not despise the prisoner
May the heavens and the earth , and the sea , and all the beasts thereof , praise Him
For he will save Zion for God , and he will build cities for Judah , and his people will dwell therein , and they will be employed .
The descendants of his servants shall be his inheritance , and those who love his name shall dwell therein .
O God , quicken me , and help me , O Lord , quicken me ,
Woe to those who seek my life ! Woe to those who rejoice in my slaughter ! Woe to those who turn back !
Let those who say to me , &quot; Ah , Ah , Ah , &quot; turn back in shame
Let all those who seek you rejoice in your joy , and let those who love your salvation say , &quot; God is great .
&quot; But I am afflicted and needy . Come to me quickly , O God . You are my helper and my rescuer . Don &apos;t delay , O Lord .
&quot; Lord , I have put my trust in You , and You will never make me ashamed
&quot; Save me by Your righteousness , and lift me up , and listen to me , and save me
Thou art my rock , and my shelter ; and thou hast been appointed to save me .
Save me , O my God , from the hand of the wicked , and from the hand of the wicked , and of the wicked .
&quot; You are my hope , O Lord Yahweh , on whom I have relied from my youth .
I have been supported by thee from the womb , and thou hast brought me out of the womb ; and I will often praise thee .
Many people blame me , but You are my strong refuge .
Your praise and your glory will fill my mouth all the days .
Do not forsake me in my old age ; Do not forsake me in my weakness .
My enemies speak of me , and those who spy for my life speak to one another .
&quot; God has forsaken him , and we are chasing him , and seizing him , for there is no rescuer .
O God , do not depart from me ; O God of my soul , help me quickly .
Woe to him who is an enemy of my life ! Woe to him who murders me !
&quot; But I will long for you , and praise you more and more
My mouth shall speak of thy righteousness and thy salvation all the day long ; for I have not counted it .
I will speak of the great power of the Lord Yahweh , and of your righteousness .
&quot; You taught me , O God , when I was young , and now I preach Your wonderful works .
&quot; Lord , do not forsake me when I grow old , until I show your power to the next generation , and your greatness to the generations to come .
O God , Your righteousness is great ; O God of great works , who can be like You ?
Thou hast caused us to suffer great tribulations , and hast raised us up from the depths of the earth .
May Thou increase me and comfort me
I will sing praises to You , O God of my soul , and praise Your righteousness ; and I will sing praises to You , O Holy One of Israel , by playing the harp
&quot; When I sing praises to You , My lips and the soul You redeemed will rejoice .
&quot; And my tongue will speak your righteousness to the ends of the day , because it has been ashamed of those who murdered me .
O God , give the king judgment , and give righteousness to the king &apos;s son
He will judge your people according to righteousness , and he will judge your oppressors according to justice .
Mountains and hills shall be filled with peace for righteousness .
He will avenge the needy among his people , and save the poor , and crush the oppressor .
&quot; The sun is still , and the moon is still , and people will fear You for ever .
He will come as rain upon the grass that has been cut down , as the fields that have been watered .
The righteous shall prosper in his days , and there shall be great peace , as the moon endures .
He will take power from this sea to that sea , from the great river to the pole
&quot; He who dwells in the wilderness will worship before Him , and his enemies will need the earth .
&quot; He will offer gifts to the kings of the Isles , and to the kings of Sheba and Siba .
All the kings shall worship Him , and all the nations shall serve Him
For he will deliver the needy in the hour of his cry , and he will deliver the needy who has no helper .
He will have mercy on the poor and needy , and save the life of the poor and needy .
He will redeem them from oppression and violence , and their blood will be precious in His sight .
And the gold of Sheba shall be given unto him , and they shall pray unto him continually , and praise him all the days .
On the top of the mountains of the earth will be five valleys , and the fruit of the valley that is formed will be as the forest of Lebanon , and the people of the city will flourish as the grass of the earth .
His name shall endure for ever , and be preached as a day , and blessed shall be mankind for him , and blessed shall all the nations be .
Blessed is the Lord , the God of Israel , the One who performs miracles
Blessed be the name of His glory for ever and ever , and filled be His glory in all the earth .
The prayer of David the son of Jesse was finished
Truly God is gracious to the righteous in Israel
As for me , my feet are a little faint , and my feet are a little slippery
&quot; When I see the wicked and the proud in peace , I am troubled
When they die , there is no pain ; and their strength is strong .
They suffer not like other people , nor like other people
Therefore pride is as a chain on their chains , and violence as a garment covers their bodies .
Their eyes were swollen with fatness , and what they had gained was too much for their hearts .
They make fun of men , and with malice deceive men ; and they speak arrogantly
Their tongues blaspheme the heavens , and their tongues blaspheme the earth .
So the people of God returned to this place , and drank the full cup of bitter water
They said , &quot; How can God know ? Does not the Most High have knowledge ? &quot;
Behold , these are the wicked : they are at ease , and their riches increase .
&quot; I have cleansed my heart , and I have washed my hands to show my innocence
For I am tormented all the day , and punished every morning
&quot; If I say , &apos; This is what I am saying , &apos; it is to treachery against your people
I wondered how I could understand it , and it was difficult to see the truth
When I enter the sanctuary of God , I think of their end
Thou hast indeed made them to lie down on the slippery slope , and cast them into the abyss .
As they turned their eyes , what a desolation ! They were consumed by terror .
As a man awakes , so will he see his dreams ; and as thou awakest , O Lord , so will thou lightly see their images .
So my heart is acidified , and my lungs are stabbed
&quot; Behold , I am as a beast before thee , as a foolish and ignorant
Nevertheless , I am always with you , and you are holding my right hand .
&quot; You will guide me by Your commandments , and afterwards You will take me to glory
&quot; Who am I in heaven besides you , and on earth have I no love besides you
My flesh and my intestines are weakened ; but God is the strength of my heart , and the blessing of my soul , and he is righteous for ever .
Those who are far from you shall die ; and those who are far from you who commit wickedness shall be destroyed .
&quot; But my nearness to God is good to me , and I have taken refuge in the Lord Yahweh , that I may declare all your works
O God , why hast thou forsaken us for ever , and why hast thou made the sheep of thy pasture angry like smoke ?
Remember the congregation of your ancient days , which you redeemed as a branch of your inheritance ; and remember Mount Zion , where you lived
Take a step , and see all the evil deeds of the enemy in the holy place , in the desolate land of that day
Your enemies shout at your meetings , and they raise up their own flags as marks
They are like men who lift up axes , and cut down trees in the forest
All the carvings of the sanctuary are now broken with axes and hammers
&quot; They burnt your sanctuary with fire , and defiled your houses in your name , and destroyed it .
&quot; They said in their hearts , &apos; We will do all we can to destroy ; &apos; and they burned all the congregations of God in all the land
We do not see our flag . There is no prophet any more . No one among us knows how long this calamity will last .
&quot; How long will the enemy blaspheme you , O God ? How long will the enemy blaspheme your name forever ?
Why turn thou away from thy right hand , and stretch out thy hand from thy chest , and destroy them ?
&quot; For God has been my king from the beginning , and He has delivered me on the earth
You have divided the sea with your power , and you have broken the head of the great fish in the water
Thou hast broken the head of the crocodile , and fed him to the beasts of the wilderness
You have divided rocks , and waters have become streams , and you have made rivers flowing forth .
The day and the night belong to You , and the light and the sun are Your provisions .
All the borders of the earth are yours , and the summer and the winter are yours .
&quot; Remember this , O Lord , when your enemies blaspheme and the foolish people blaspheme your name
Don &apos;t give the life of your turtle to the beasts . Don &apos;t forget the life of your miserable people forever
&quot; Remember the covenant that is made , for the darkness of the earth is full of violent dwellings .
Let not the oppressed be ashamed , and let the needy praise thy name .
&quot; Arise , O God , and plead for yourself , and remember how the foolish reproaches you all the days .
Don &apos;t forget the voice of your enemies ; the noise of those who are your enemies always rises
&quot; We thank You , O God , we thank You , for Your name is near , and all men speak of Your wonderful works .
&quot; I have come to the appointed time , and I will execute judgment in truth .
The earth and all that dwells thereon have digested ; and I have set up the pillars of the earth .
&quot; I say to the arrogant , &apos; Do not be arrogant , &apos; and to the wicked , &apos; Do not raise your heads . &apos; 
Don &apos;t raise your horns high ; don &apos;t speak with your necks upright
For to exalt is not from the east , not from the west , not from the south .
Only God judges , and He humbles him , and He exalts him
&quot; In the hand of the Lord is a cup , and the wine is poured out , and the cup is full of mixed wine , and He drops it ; and all the wicked on the earth will drink of the residue of it , and they will be consumed .
&quot; But I will proclaim it forever , and I will sing praises to the God of Jacob
I will cut off all the horns of the wicked ; but the horns of the righteous shall be exalted .
The God of Judah is known , and in Israel his name is Great .
And his tabernacle was in Samaria , and his dwelling place in Zion
There he broke the rockets on the bow , and the shields , and the swords , and the weapons of war .
From the mountains of the wilderness have you come , glory and majesty .
The brave of hearts were taken away , and they slept a long time ; and there was not a hero who could shake his hand .
&quot; Your rebuke , O God of Jacob , has made all those who rode and rode to sleep .
Only thou art a dreadful thing ; who can stand before thee in thy wrath ?
Thou hearest judgment from heaven , and God judgeth , and saveth all the humble men of the earth ; and in that day they shall fear and be quiet .
See Up
The wrath of men shall be your glory , and the wrath of men shall be forbidden .
&quot; You shall make a vow to the Lord your God , and all those who are around him shall offer their offerings to the Lord of hosts .
He will frustrate the prince &apos;s pride , and he will be fearful of the kings of the earth .
I will call to God , and I will cry to God , and he will listen to me
I seek the Lord in the day of affliction ; I raise my hands in prayer in the night when I am absent ; my heart is not comforted .
When I think of God , I am troubled , and when I meditate on my sorrow , my heart faints .
You have made me unable to close my eyes . I am troubled and unable to speak
I remember the days of old , the years of old
I remember my songs at night , and ask myself , and I keep my heart in mind .
Don &apos;t you forsake me forever , don &apos;t you forgive me ?
Will His mercy be exhausted for ever , and His promises forsaken ?
Did God forget His grace , and His mercy ceased because of His wrath ?
I said , &quot; This is my weakness ; but I will remember the days of the right hand of the high . &quot;
I will mention the works of the Lord , and I will remember your wonders of old .
I also want to think about your business and your actions
&quot; O God , Your works are pure . What God is greater than God ?
Thou art the God of wonders : thou hast manifested thy power in the kingdoms
Thou hast redeemed by thy arm thy people , the sons of Jacob and Joseph .
The waters , O God , when they see thee , tremble , and the depths tremble .
Drop water out of the clouds , and the sky will sound , and your arrows will fly all around .
Your thunder is in the whirlwind . Electric light illuminates the world . The earth shakes and shakes .
Your way is in the sea , Your way in the great waters , Your footsteps are not known .
Thou hast guided thy people by the hand of Moses and Aaron like a flock of sheep .
My people , listen to my teachings , and listen to the words of my mouth .
I &apos;m going to speak metaphors . I &apos;m going to tell old riddles
&quot; This is what we have heard , and what we have known , and what our fathers told us .
&quot; We will not conceal these things from their children , but we will speak the goodness of the Lord and His power and His wondrous works to the generations to come .
&quot; For he established the law in Jacob , and set the law in Israel , which he commanded our fathers to pass on to their children .
And they shall come up and tell their children , that they may know the generations to come .
That they may look on God , and not forget His deeds , but keep His commandments .
Do not be like their ancestors , the generations of obstinate rebellion and disobedience , the generations of disobedience to God .
And the sons of Ephraim turned their backs on the day of the battle ,
They do not keep the covenant of God , nor do they obey His law .
And forget what He has done , and His wondrous deeds which He revealed to them .
He did wonders in the land of Egypt , in Zoan , in the sight of their fathers .
He divided the sea , and caused them to pass over , and raised up waters as a barrier .
He guides them by clouds in the daytime , and by fire at night .
He divided the rocks in the wilderness , and gave them plenty of water to drink , as from the depths
He poured out waters from the rocks , and waters came down like rivers .
Yet they are still guilty of Him , rebelling against the Most High in the dry land .
In their hearts they seek God , seeking food according to their own desires
And they denied God , saying , &quot; Can God prepare a feast in the wilderness ? &quot;
He has struck rocks , and waters have poured forth , and they have become rivers . Can He feed or prepare meat for His people ?
So the Lord heard , and he was angry ; and there was a fire that burned against Jacob , and there was wrath upon Israel
For they have not believed in God , nor put their trust in His salvation
He commanded the heavens , and opened the gates of the heavens
&quot; Is it good for them to eat like rain , and to give them the food of the heavens ?
Every man eats the food of the mighty , and He gives them food , and fills them .
He brought forth the east wind in the sky , and drew forth the south wind with power
He brings down the flesh like rain in their midst , like dust , and the birds like sea sand .
And it fell upon their camps , and on all sides of their dwellings
They ate and were filled , and so they followed what they desired .
They are greedy and stubborn , and food is in their mouths
And the wrath of God descended upon them , and slew the mighty among them , and slew the young men of Israel .
Nevertheless , they still commit crimes , and do not believe in his wondrous works
Therefore he called their days to nothing , and their years to terror .
When He killed them , they asked Him , turning their hearts to Him , seeking God sincerely .
They also remember God , their rock , the Most High , their Redeemer .
But they flattered him with their mouths , and lied to him with their tongues
For their hearts are unrighteous toward him , and they are not faithful to his covenant
But He has mercy , and forgives their iniquity , and does not destroy them , and does not extinguish his wrath , and does not extinguish his wrath
He thought that they were nothing but blood , a wind that would not return
&quot; Why do they rebel against him in the wilderness , and fear him in the wilderness ?
They have tried again to seek God , to provoke the saints of Israel
They do not remember the days of His power , and of His hands , and of His redemption from the enemy
How did he show signs in Egypt , and wonders in Zoan ?
They have turned their rivers and their waters into blood , so that they cannot drink
And he gathered the flies together , and fell among them , and smote them ; and the frogs destroyed them .
Give their inheritance to grasshoppers , and their hard work to locusts
A hail fell upon their vines , and a frost upon their fir trees .
And gave their cattle to hail , and their herds to lightning .
And he brought upon them a great wrath , and wrath , and anger , and distress , and made them an apostle of calamity
He has repaired the way for his wrath , and has given them to the plague , and has caused them to die
And all the elders of Egypt shall be slain , and the firstborn of them shall be slain in the tents which they contain , when they were strong .
He brings forth his people as sheep , and draws them as sheep in the wilderness
He has taken them safely and securely , so that they are not afraid ; and the sea has drowned their enemies .
And he brought them unto the border of his holy place , unto the mountains which he had taken with his right hand
&quot; He will drive out the foreigners before them , and he will give them the land of the foreigners for a possession by rope , and the children of Israel will dwell in their tents
Yet they have sought the God of the highest , and have not kept his law .
As their ancestors , they have turned back and dealt treacherously ; and they have changed like a bow turned back .
For their high places provoked him to anger , and their idols provoked him to indignation .
And when God heard it , He was wroth , and hated Israel exceedingly
And he turned away from the tent of Sheol , which he had set up among men
He has delivered his covenant into captivity , and his glory into the hand of the enemy .
And He will give his people to swords , and will be angry with his inheritance .
The young man was burnt down by fire , and the virgin was without songs .
The priest fell under the sword , and the widow did not weep .
Then the Lord awoke as the world awoke , and cried as a mighty man drinking wine
Then he turned back his enemies , that they might be ashamed for ever .
And he forsook the tent of Joseph , and chose not the tribe of Ephraim
&quot; But he chose the tribe of Judah , the mountain of Zion , which he loved
He built His sanctuary as a mountain , and as a place to dwell forever .
And he chose David his servant , and called him out of the flock
Let him no longer go with the lambs that bear milk , to feed his people Jacob , and his inheritance Israel ,
Then he raised them up in the purity of his heart , and guided them with the skill of his hand
O God , the foreigners have entered into your inheritance , and have defiled your temples , and have made Jerusalem a desolation
&quot; Bring the dead bodies of your servants to the birds of the sky for food , and the flesh of your saints to the beasts of the earth .
They were surrounded in Jerusalem by blood like water , and no one was buried .
We are a reproach to our neighbours , and a derision to those around us
&quot; When will this be , O Lord ? Will your anger be for ever ? Will your indignation burn like a fire ?
Let your wrath be poured out on the countries that do not know your name , and on the countries that do not seek your name .
For they swallowed up Jacob , and turned his dwelling place into a wilderness
Remember not the iniquity of our forefathers , and seek not for us ; and let thy mercy be upon us , for we are come down to a humble step .
Save us , O God of our salvation ; help us for the glory of thy name ; save us for thy name &apos;s sake ; forgive our sins .
&quot; Why do the foreigners say , &apos; Their God is in it ? &apos; May you let the foreigners know that you are before us , and that you have stretched out the blood of your servants
May the sigh of the prisoner come to you , and may you save those who are to die by your great power .
&quot; Lord , may you return to them seven times the shame which our neighbours have done to you .
Thus shall thy people , and thy flock in the field , give thanks unto thee for ever , and praise thy words for ever and ever .
Hear thou , O shepherd of Israel , that shepherd the flock of sheep ; O thou that sitest on the two reins , that shineth light ;
&quot; Exert your great power before Ephraim , Benjamin , and Manasseh , to save us
&quot; Return us , O God , and make your face shine , and we shall be saved .
&quot; When will you be angry at the prayers of your people , O Lord , God of hosts ?
When you feed them with tears , you pour out more tears for them
You have divided the neighbours for our sakes , and our enemies have laughed at each other .
Turn us , O God of hosts , and make thy face shine , and we shall be saved
&quot; You removed a vine from Egypt , and drove out the foreigners , and planted it
Thou hast prepared a place before the roots of this tree , and it is deeply rooted and filled
His shadow covered the mountains , and its branches were like beautiful cedar trees
He spreads out branches to the sea , He spreads out vines to the river
Why have you demolished the fence of the tree , and taken it away from all those who pass by ?
The wild pig that comes out of the forest , and tramples him ; the beast of the field , and takes him for food .
Turn , O God of hosts , and look up from heaven , and see the vine ;
Protect that which your right hand has planted , and that which you have firmly established for yourself .
The tree has been burned by fire and cut down by the sword ; and they have perished because of the wrath of your face .
May your hand be with him who is on your right hand , the son of a man you have established for yourself .
&quot; Therefore we will not turn away from you , and we will ask you to save us , and we will ask for your name .
Turn us , O Lord , God of hosts , and make thy face shine , and we shall be saved
Sing to God with a loud voice of our strength , and with a loud voice of joy to the God of Jacob
Singing poems , playing drums , playing the violin and singing hymns
When the moon is full , and the moon watches the day of our feast ,
For this is the law of Israel , and the law of the God of Jacob .
This is the witness in Joseph , when he went to attack the land of Egypt , and I heard in it words which I did not understand .
&quot; I will take off your shoulders , &quot; God said , &quot; and your hands will lay down your baskets
&quot; I will rescue you when you cry out in distress ; I will answer you in the shadow of a thunderstorm ; I will test you in the waters of Meribah .
&quot; Listen , O my people , and I will warn you ; O Israel , if only you would listen to me
&quot; There is no other God among you ; neither can you worship the God of the nations .
&quot; I am the Lord , your God , who brought you up out of the land of Egypt ; and I will fill you with a great mouth
But my people have not listened to my voice , and Israel has not listened to me .
And I gave them the strength of their hearts , and they did according to their own schemes
&quot; I wish my people would listen to me , and Israel would walk in my way
And I will deliver their enemies quickly , and I will strike their enemies with the back of my hand .
&quot; The one who hates the Lord will surrender , but his people will live forever .
And he shall bring forth good wheat for them to eat , and honey out of a rock , that they may be filled .
God stands in the gathering of the mighty , judging among the gods
&quot; When will you judge the unrighteousness and the wickedness of men ? &quot;
As for the poor and the orphan , so do ye justice ; and as for the afflicted and the needy , so do ye justice .
Protect the poor and the needy , and deliver them from the hand of the wicked .
You do not know , nor do you understand , walking in the darkness , and the foundations of the earth are shaken .
&quot; I said , &apos; You are God , and you are the sons of the Most High .
&quot; But you will die like the world , and you will fall like a prince .
Arise , O God , and judge the world : for thou wilt have the kingdoms for a possession .
O God , do not be silent , O God , do not shut your mouth , and do not make no voice
For your enemies have screamed , and hated you lifted up their heads .
They have plotted against your people with treachery , and they have negotiated against each other against those whom you have hidden .
&quot; Come , &quot; they said , &quot; and we will cut them off , and they will no longer be a nation , and the name of Israel will no longer be remembered
&quot; They have agreed with one another , they have made alliances with one another , and they will stand against you .
And the children of Edom , and the children of Ishmael , and the children of Moab , and the children of Shechem , who dwelled in the tents ;
and the inhabitants of Jabbar , and of Ammon , and of Amalek , and of Philistine , and of Tyre ,
And Assyria joined with them , and they were helpers unto the sons of Lot .
&quot; Remain with them as with Midian , and as with Sisaria and Jebin in the river Kishon
And they perished in the land of Egypt , and became dust on the earth
Call their princes , as Olyth and Sib , and their princes , as Sheba and Samunah
They said , &quot; We will have God &apos;s dwelling place as our inheritance
&quot; My God , make them like the dust of the wind , like the straw before the wind .
How the fire burneth the forests , and how the flame burneth the mountains
Likewise seek thou to pursue them with the wind , and to frighten them with the rain
Let them be ashamed , that they may seek the name of the LORD your God
May they always be ashamed and terrified . May they be ashamed and perish .
&quot; That they may know that only You , in the name of the Lord , are the Most High over all the earth
How lovely is thy dwelling place , O Lord of hosts !
I envy the house of the Lord , and my heart and my flesh cry to the God of everlasting life .
&quot; Yahweh of Armies , my king , my God , in your altar the sparrow seeks a home for himself , and the swallow a nest for itself .
Blessed be he that dwelleth in thy house , and they shall praise thee .
Blessed is he who seeks the way of Zion with thy strength in his heart
They passed through the valley of tears , and turned it into a spring ; and the blessing of the autumn rain covered the whole valley .
And they went forth , and strengthened themselves , and came every man unto Zion unto God
O Lord , God of hosts , hear my prayers , O God of Jacob , listen .
O God , thou art our shield ; look upon the face of thy anointed ,
It is better to live a day in your house than a thousand days elsewhere , and to look at the doors of My temple , and not to dwell in the tents of the wicked .
For the Lord God is the head of the sun , the shield , to give grace and glory ; and he has not left any benefit to the upright .
Blessed are those who rely on You , O Lord of hosts .
O LORD , by the grace of thy land hast thou delivered Jacob the captive
Thou hast forgiven the iniquity of thy people , and covered all their transgressions .
&quot; You have turned away your wrath and your fierce anger .
&quot; Save us , O God of our salvation , and turn our backs , and let your anger cease against us .
Will you be angry with us forever ? Will you keep your anger forever ?
Will you no longer save us , and make your people rejoice in you ?
&quot; Lord , make us see Your mercy and give us Your salvation .
&quot; I will listen to the words of the Lord God ; for he will promise to give peace to his people , his holy people , and they will not turn away from their deeds .
His salvation is indeed near to those who fear Him , that glory may dwell in our land .
Mercy and truth meet each other , and righteousness and peace are close to each other .
Trueness is born from the earth , and righteousness from heaven .
&quot; The Lord will give us good things , and our land will produce more fruit .
The righteous shall walk before him , and his footsteps shall be a way to walk .
&quot; Listen to me , O Lord , for I am in distress and in need .
Save my life , O my God , for I am a devout man ; save this servant that trusteth in thee
&quot; My Lord , have mercy on me , for I have prayed to You all the days
Rejoice in the heart of thy servant , O Lord ; for my heart is lifted up to thee
&quot; Lord , You are good , forgiving , and full of mercy , and have given to all those who ask You
&quot; Listen to my prayer , O Lord , and listen to the voice of my supplication .
&quot; I ask of you in the day of trouble , because you will obey me .
Lord , there is none like you among the gods , neither are your works like .
All the people that you have created will come to worship you , O Lord , and they will glorify your name .
&quot; For you are great and do wonderful things , and you alone are God .
Teach me thy ways , O LORD , that I may walk in thy truth , and that I may fear thy name with all my heart
O Lord my God , I will praise thee with all my heart , and I will glorify thy name for ever
For great is thy mercy upon me , and thou hast delivered my soul from the depths of darkness .
&quot; O God , the proud have come up against me , and a band of arrogant seek my life , and they have not put You in their sight .
O Lord , you are a God of mercy and grace , not easily angry , and full of mercy and truth
Turn your face to me , and have mercy on me , and give your strength to your servants , and save the son of your maidservant
Show me the proof of your grace toward me , that those who hate me may see and be ashamed , because your Lord has helped me and comforted me
The foundation of the Lord is on the holy mountain
He loved the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob
Glory be to you , O city of God .
&quot; Behold , the Philistines , and Tyre , and the Philistines of old , and the Babylonians , who are known to me , were born there
And he shall say concerning Zion , Every one shall be born therein ; and the Most High shall establish the city himself
&quot; When the Lord records the time of all the people , He will bring forth the living there .
&quot; Whoever sings and dances will say , &apos; My fountain is in you
&quot; The song of the sons of Korah , the song of the instruction of Heman of the children of Israel , and the voice of the elders , and the voice of the sons of Azariah , and the voice of the sons of Ammon : &quot; Lord , God of my salvation , I cry before you day and night .
May my prayer come to you , and hear my call .
For my soul is full of trouble , and my life is near to the pit
I am like those who fall into the pit , as those who are helpless .
I have been cast among the dead , as though I had been slain , lying in the tomb ; they are those whom you will no longer remember , and they are separated from you .
You have put me in the depths of the pit , in the darkness , in the depths
Your wrath has overwhelmed me , and you have straitened me with all the waves .
Thou hast separated me from that which I know , and hated me for their sakes ; and I have not come out in captivity .
&quot; My eyes are dried up in distress ; I pray to You daily , O Lord , and raise up my hand to You
Will you do miracles to the dead ? Will the soul rise up to praise you ?
Can you declare your loving kindness in the tomb , and your faithfulness in death ?
Will thy wonders be known in darkness , and thy righteousness in oblivion ?
&quot; Lord , I pray to You , and my morning prayer will come before You
Why have you forsaken me , O LORD , and hid your face from me ?
I suffered from my childhood and almost died . I was terrified and even panicked by you
Your fierce anger has covered me ; Your terror has cut me off .
They encircle me all the days as waters , and they encircle me all at once .
Thou hast separated my good friends from the farthest places , and hast cast into darkness those whom I know .
&quot; I will sing the loving kindness of the Lord forever and ever , and I will proclaim your word in my mouth to all generations
For I said , &quot; Your mercy will be established for ever , and your faith will be established in heaven .
&quot; I have made a covenant with my chosen , and I have sworn to my servant David
I will establish your descendants to eternity , and I will establish your throne to eternity .
Praise be to the heavens , O LORD , for thy wonders ; praise be to thy faith in the congregation of the saints .
Who is like the Lord in the heavens ? Who is like the Lord among the children of God ?
He is a mighty God in the congregation of the saints , more fearful than all that are around him
&quot; Lord , God of hosts , a mighty one like your Lord . Your faith is all around you .
Your arrogance governs the sea ; and when the waves overflow , You calm it .
You have broken Lahab , who seems to have been killed ; You have scattered your enemies with your mighty arm
Heaven belongs to you , and the earth belongs to you , and the world and all that is therein is built for you .
The south and the north are created for thee ; he rejoiceth in thy name , and the gates of darkness .
You have a mighty arm ; Your hands are strong , and your right hand lifts up .
Justice and righteousness are the foundations of your throne . Mercy and truth are before you .
Blessed are the people who know that they rejoice in thee , and walk in the light of thy face , O LORD .
They rejoice in thy name all the days , and are exalted in thy righteousness .
Thou art the glory of their strength : for thou hast pleased us , and our horns shall be exalted .
Our shield is the Lord , and our king is the Holy One of Israel .
Then thou spakest in the vision unto thy saints , saying , I have added the power of salvation unto the mighty , and I have exalted the chosen of the people .
&quot; I have found my servant David , and I have anointed him with my anointing
My hand shall strengthen him , and my arm shall strengthen him .
The enemy will not forsake him , neither will the son of the wicked harm him .
I will break his enemies before him , and I will slay those who hate him .
Only my faith and my loving kindness will be with him , and his horns will be lifted up in my name .
&quot; I will stretch out his left hand to the sea , and his right hand to the river
&quot; He will call me , saying , &apos; You are my Father , my God , and my rock of salvation .
&quot; And I will raise him up as a son , and as the highest king in the world .
I will keep my mercy for him for ever , and my covenant with him will be firm .
And I will make his seed to abide for ever , and his throne as the days of heaven .
&quot; If his sons depart from My law , they shall not do according to My statutes
&quot; Forsake My statutes , and do not obey My commandments
&quot; I will punish them with a rod for their transgressions , and with a rod for their iniquities
&quot; But I will not take away my loving kindness at all , nor will I make my faith abolished .
&quot; I will not forsake my covenant , nor alter what I say in my mouth .
I have sworn my holiness once . I will never lie to David
And his seed shall be for ever , and his throne shall be before me as the continuation of the day .
And as the moon endureth for ever , and as a true testimony in the heavens .
&quot; But when you are angry with your anointed , you forsake him .
You have despised the covenant of your servant , and have trampled on his crown .
Thou hast destroyed all his fences , and made his shield a barren land .
All those who pass by seize him , and he becomes a reproach to his neighbours .
Thou hast exalted the right hand of his enemy , and hast made all his enemies rejoice
Thou hast called his sword a sword , that he should not stand in battle .
Thou hast made his light cease , and his throne has fallen to the ground .
Thou hast reduced his youth , and made him ashamed .
&quot; How long will it be , O Lord ? How long will you hide yourselves forever ? How long will your wrath burn like fire ?
&quot; Remember what a short time it is for you to remember me . What a voidness have you created the worlds for them ?
Who can live for ever , and save his soul from the power of the shadow ?
Wherein , O Lord , hast thou sworn by thy faith unto David the mercy to be done ?
Remember , O Lord , the shame of the servants , and how I put the shame of all the mighty in my arms .
&quot; Your enemy , Yahweh , has humiliated your servants with this , and has humiliated the footsteps of your anointed .
Blessed is the Lord for ever and ever .
&quot; Lord , make your generations our dwelling place
Thou hast not created the mountains , nor the earth , nor the world ; Thou art God from the beginning to the end .
&quot; You have brought people back to the dust , saying , &apos; Your people will return
Thou seest the thousand years as yesterday , and as the night
You send them away like water , and they sleep like a bed ; and in the morning they grow like grass .
Grows in the morning , dries in the evening .
&quot; We shall be destroyed by your wrath , and we shall be terrified by your wrath .
Thou hast put our iniquity before thee , and our wickedness in thy sight .
The days that we have passed are under your wrath , and the years that we have spent are as a sigh .
The year of our life is seventy years ; and if we were strong , we would reach eighty years ; but the boasting thereof is no more than labour and sorrow ; and when we turn our eyes to the sky , we will go away like flies .
Who knows the power of your wrath , and who knows your wrath according to your fear ?
Teach us how to count our days , that we may have a wise heart
&quot; How long shall we wait , O Lord ? Return , and repent for your servants .
May Thou fill us with Thy mercy early and early , that we may rejoice and rejoice for ever
Rejoice in the days of our affliction , and in the years of our tribulation , according to thee ;
May your service be manifest to your servants , and may your glory be manifest to their children .
May the glory of our God be upon us , O LORD , and may the work of our hands be established , and the work of our hands be established
He who dwells in the secret of the Most High will dwell in the shadow of the Almighty .
&quot; I will speak to the Lord , saying , &apos; He is my refuge , my dwelling place , my God , my trust
&quot; He will deliver you from the snares of the birds , and from the plague of poison .
He will cover you with his feathers , and you will lean under his wings . His integrity is a great shield .
Thou shalt not be afraid of the terror of the night , nor of the arrows of the day .
Neither fear the plague of the night , nor the poison of the midday .
Thou shalt not come near to thee , though thousands fall by thy side , and thousands fall by thy right hand
&quot; You only look with your own eyes and see the evildoers recompensed
&quot; The Lord is my refuge ; You have made the Most High your dwelling place .
No evil shall come upon thee , neither shall disaster come near thy tent .
&quot; For he will protect you by His angels , whom He has commanded for you , in all your ways .
And they shall trust in thee with their hands , lest thy feet touch a stone .
Thou shalt kick upon the lion and the snake , and trample upon the little lion and the great snake .
God said , &quot; Because he loves me wholeheartedly , I will rescue him ; and because he knows my name , I will place him in high places .
&quot; If he asks of me , I will answer him ; and if he is in distress , I will be with him ; and I will rescue him , and make him honorable .
&quot; I will make him live long enough , and I will show him My salvation
Blessed be the Lord , and praise the name of the Most High
&quot; This is the beauty of the ten-stringed instrument and the harp , and of the sound of the harp , to proclaim your loving kindness in the morning , and your faithfulness at night .
