I will rejoice because your Lord has borrowed from you , and I will rejoice because of the work of your hand
How great is thy work , O LORD , and how great is thy heart !
The beast does not know , neither does the fool understand .
&quot; When the wicked grows like grass , and all the wicked grow , it is that they shall perish forever .
&quot; But You , Lord , are the Most High , forever and ever .
&quot; Your enemies shall perish , O Lord , and all iniquity shall be cut off .
&quot; But you have lifted up my horns like the horns of a cattle : I am anointed with new oil .
&quot; My eyes see the recompense of the enemy , and my ears hear the punishment of the wicked who rise up against me .
A righteous man shall prosper as a palm tree , and grow as a cypress in Lebanon
&quot; They are planted in the house of the Lord , and they prosper in the house of our God .
When they are old , they still want results . They want to be full of juice and often bleed
&quot; Behold , the Lord is righteous ; He is My rock , and in Him there is no iniquity
The Lord is King , He clothes himself with glory , He clothes himself with power , He binds himself with strength , The world is firm , and it cannot be shaken .
&quot; Your throne has been established from the beginning , and you have been there for ever .
&quot; Yahweh , the great waters are rising , the great waters are rising , the waves are rising .
The LORD is mighty in high places above the sound of all waters , and above the waves of the sea
O LORD , thy law is perfect , and thy house shall be called holy , and it shall be well-pleased .
O LORD , thou art the God of righteousness ; O God of righteousness , send forth light .
Stand up , O Lord , who judges the world , that the proud may receive his reward .
&quot; Lord , how long will the wicked boast ? How long will they boast ?
They are puffed up with boasting , and all the wicked exaggerate themselves .
&quot; Lord , they have oppressed your people , and they have afflicted your inheritance .
They kill widows and those who dwell , and they kill orphans .
They said , &quot; The Lord will not see , and the God of Jacob will not remember .
How long shall your people , the beasts of your people , think ? How long shall you be wise , you fools !
He that hath ears hath not heard ; and he that hath eyes hath not seen .
Is he who preacheth the nations , and teacheth knowledge , not he who punisheth men ?
The Lord knows that men &apos;s thoughts are vain
Blessed is he who teaches , O Lord , and teaches by the law .
Thou hast given him peace in the days of distress ; but the wicked are in the pits dug .
For the Lord will not forsake His people , nor His inheritance
Judgment shall be turned to righteousness , and the upright in heart shall follow .
Who will stand up for me against evil , and who will stand up for me against iniquity ?
&quot; If the Lord had not helped me , I would have lived in silence
&quot; When I say , &apos; I have lost my feet , Lord , &apos; Your mercy will help me
&quot; My heart is troubled and doubted ; You have comforted me , and made me rejoice
&quot; Can a man who abuses and commits wickedness in his office by means of the law be associated with you ?
And they gathered themselves together to attack the righteous , and to make the innocent to die .
But the LORD hath made me a high place ; and my God hath made me a rock upon which I shall lean .
He has brought their iniquity upon them ; they are in wickedness ; He will cut them off , and the Lord our God will cut them off .
&quot; Come , we will sing to the Lord , and we will sing to the rock that saved us
We will come to thank him , and to cheer him with songs
For the Lord is the Great God , the Great King , above all gods
The depths of the earth are in His hands ; and the mountains are His .
The sea belongs to Him ; He created it ; and the dry land belongs to His hands
&quot; Come , O Lord , and we will bow down in homage to the Lord who created us
For he is our God , and we are the sheep of his pasture , and his people under his hand : hear ye therefore his word this day .
&quot; You shall not be hardened , as in the day of Milla , in the wilderness of Massah .
Then your ancestors tried me , and looked at my deeds
For forty years I have bored the generation , saying , &quot; This is a people who are confused in their hearts , and do not know what I am doing .
Therefore I swear in anger , saying , &quot; They will not enter into my rest
&quot; You shall sing a new song to the Lord ; and all the earth shall sing to the Lord .
Sing to the Lord , praise His name , and proclaim His salvation daily
He shall declare His glory among the nations , and His wonders among the people .
For the LORD is great , when he is praised exceedingly , and when he is feared above all gods
All the gods of the nations are void : only the Lord created the heavens .
There is glory and majesty before Him , and power and beauty in His sanctuary
&quot; You , all the tribes of the people , will give to the Lord the power of glory ;
&quot; You shall return to him the glory of the name of the Lord , and bring offerings into his house .
And worship the Lord in holy garments , and shake before Him in all places .
&quot; They shall say among the nations , &apos; The Lord is the King , and the world will stand firm , and it will not be shaken ; and he will judge the people with justice .
May the heavens rejoice , and may the sea and all that is therein thrive .
Let the field rejoice , and all that are in it ; and the trees of the forest shall rejoice before the Lord
For he is come to judge the whole earth , to judge the world according to righteousness , and to judge the people according to his faithfulness
Blessed be the LORD king , and blessed be the islands of the sea .
The clouds and the darkness are round about him . Justice and justice are the foundations of his throne .
A fire went before him , and burned all his enemies around him .
His lightning illuminated the world . The earth trembled as it saw .
&quot; When the mountains see the face of the Lord , the Lord of all the earth , they digest it like wax
The heavens show His righteousness , and the people see His glory
Let all things be ashamed of the idols that are carved , and of the God of nothing : O God , worship Him
&quot; Rejoice , O Lord , when Zion hears your judgment , and the cities of Judah rejoice ,
For you , Lord , are exalted above all the earth , and are exalted above all the gods .
&quot; You who love the Lord will hate evil and evil ; He protects the lives of the saints , and delivers them out of the hand of the wicked .
To spread light is for the righteous , and to prepare joy is for the upright .
Rejoice in the Lord , ye righteous , and give thanks unto His holy name , which is remembered
Sing a new song unto the LORD , for he hath done wonders , and his right hand and his holy arm do mercy
The LORD hath revealed His salvation , and righteousness hath appeared before the heathen
Remember his lovingkindness toward the house of Israel , and his faithfulness . The four corners of the earth saw the salvation of our God .
Let all the earth rejoice in the LORD , and let them lift up their voices , and let them sing and praise him .
Sing praises to the Lord with the harp , and with the voice of the harp and the voice of the song .
Sing with the trumpets and with the horns in the presence of the Lord , the King of hosts
May the sea , and all that is therein , and the world , and all that dwell therein , be heard .
Let the great waters shake hands and let the mountains rejoice before the Lord
For he came to judge all the earth , and to judge the world in righteousness , and to judge the people in justice .
&quot; The Lord is King , and the people are shaken , and He sits on two reins , and the earth is shaken
The LORD is great in Zion ; He is above all the people
They praised His great and dreadful name . He was holy .
The king is able to love justice , to uphold justice , and to do justice and righteousness in Jacob
&quot; Honor the Lord our God , and worship at His feet ; He is holy .
Among his priests were Moses and Aaron ; and among those who asked for his name was Samuel ; and they asked for the Lord , and He answered them .
He spoke to them in the clouds , and they observed His statutes and His laws which He had given them .
O Lord , God of ours , answer them ; forgive them , and recompense them according to what they do .
&quot; You shall worship the Lord our God in His holy mountain , for the Lord our God is holy .
Praise be to the Lord in all the earth
&quot; You shall serve the Lord with joy , and sing to Him when you come
Know ye that the LORD is God , and that we are His created , and are His , and that we are His people , and that we are the sheep of His pasture
Let thanks enter into His gates , Let praise enter into His houses , Let thanks enter into His houses , Let praise His name
For the Lord is good , and His mercy endures for ever , and His faithfulness endures for ever .
I will sing mercy and righteousness , and I will sing praises to You , O Lord
&quot; I will walk in a perfect way with wisdom . When will you come to me ? I will keep my whole heart in my house .
&quot; I have not seen the evil in my sight ; I hate the evil done by the rebellious , and I do not allow it to touch me .
I will turn away from the wicked , and I do not know all the wicked .
&quot; I will destroy him who slanders his neighbours in the darkness ; I will not allow him who is proud in his eyes and proud in his heart .
I will see the righteous in the land , that they may dwell with me ; and he will be perfect in his deeds ; and he will serve me
&quot; Those who deceive shall not dwell in My house ; and those who lie shall not stand before Me .
&quot; I will destroy every wicked man in the land every morning ; and I will cut off all the wicked from the city of the Lord
O Lord , hear my prayer , and let my cry come to you
Turn your ears to me in the days of distress , and do not hide your face from me ; and hear me in the days of my cry .
For my years are consumed like smoke , and my bones are burned like fire .
My heart is injured , as the grass is dried up , and even I forget to eat
For the voice of my weeping , my flesh is fastened to the bones
I &apos;m like a pelican in the wilderness . I &apos;m like an owl in the wilderness
I wake up and do not sleep . I am like a lonely sparrow on the roof
My enemies scourge me all the day long , and they curse me against those who are mad at me .
I have eaten the ashes of the furnace as if I had eaten ; and my drink is mixed with tears in my eyes
&quot; This is because of your anger and your wrath ; You have lifted me up , and have cast me down .
My years are as the shadows of the sun , and I am as the grass that is dry .
&quot; But you , Yahweh , will live forever , and your name will be remembered for ever and ever .
Thou shalt come up and have mercy on Zion ; for the time is come to have mercy on him ; and the day is come .
&quot; Your servant is a stone that pleases him , and a dust that pits him .
The nations shall fear the name of the LORD ; and the kings of the earth shall fear thy glory
For the LORD hath built Zion , and hath appeared in His glory
He listens to the prayers of the poor , and does not despise their prayers
&quot; This shall be recorded for the generations to come , and the generations to come shall praise the Lord .
For he looked from the highest holy place , and the Lord looked from heaven to the earth
Listen to the sighs of the prisoners , and release those who will die .
&quot; They proclaimed the name of the Lord in Zion , and the words of praise in Jerusalem
