Remove from me the reproach and the contempt which I have suffered , because I have observed thy statutes .
&quot; While the chiefs sit and deceive Me , Your servants think Your statutes .
&quot; Your law is my pleasure , and it is my counsel .
&quot; My life is almost in the dust ; save me according to Your word ,
&quot; I tell you what I have done , and you have given me your word ; and teach me your law .
Make me understand Your words , and I will think of Your wonders .
My heart digesteth with sorrow ; and I pray that thou mayest strengthen me according to thy word .
Turn me away from the way of treachery , and give me your law with grace .
&quot; I have chosen the way of faith , and have set before me Your statutes .
&quot; I keep your statutes , and do not make me ashamed , O Lord .
When thou hast opened my heart , I will run straight on the way that thou hast commanded me
Teach me , O Lord , Your statutes , and I will keep them to the end
Give me understanding , and I will keep thy law , and keep it with all my heart .
Ask me to obey your commandments , for this is my joy .
Make my heart incline unto thy law , and not unrighteous riches .
Let me not turn my eyes to falsehood , and let me live in your way
Be firm in thy servants , as thou hast promised them that fear thee ;
Turn away from me the shame which I fear : for thy statutes are beautiful .
I envy Your teachings . Please let me live in Your righteousness
&quot; Lord , according to your word , let your mercy , your salvation , come upon me
I will answer the reproach of my shame , because I have trusted in your word .
Never leave not my mouth , that thou mayest call it truth : for I look upon thy statutes .
&quot; I will keep your law forever and ever and ever .
I will walk freely , or I will walk in a broad place , because I have diligently studied Your commandments .
&quot; I will also speak before the king concerning your law , and I will not be ashamed
I want to rejoice in your commandments , which I love
And I will keep thy commandments , which I love , and I will think of thy statutes .
&quot; Remember what you have promised your servant , that I may have hope
&quot; It has saved me , and comforted me in my affliction .
A proud man has insulted me , and I have not strayed from your law .
&quot; I am comforted , O Lord , when I remember Your statutes from ancient times
&quot; When I saw the wicked depart from your law , I was filled with anger , like a fire
I have dwelled in the world , and have been singing with Your statutes
&quot; I remember Your name at night , O Lord , and keep Your law .
&quot; I am so because I keep your commandments
&quot; The Lord is my blessing ; I said , &apos; I will keep your word
May you have mercy on me according to your words .
And I will return to thee according to the way that I have walked .
I abide by your orders without delay
The rope of the wicked encompasses me , but I have not forgotten thy law .
&quot; I will come up at midnight to thank you for your law of righteousness
&quot; I am with him who fears You and keeps Your commandments
O LORD , thy mercy is upon all the earth ; teach me thy statutes
&quot; Lord , you have always been kind to your servants according to your word .
Give me wisdom and knowledge , because I have believed in your commandments .
I went astray before I suffered , and now I obey Your word
&quot; You are good , and what you do is good . Teach me your law
A proud man fabricates lies against me ; but I will keep Your commandments with all my heart .
&quot; Their hearts are full of fat , but I love Your law .
My suffering is good to me , that I may learn thy statutes
&quot; The words of your mouth are more profitable to me than a thousand gold and silver .
Thy hand hath made me , and established me ; give me understanding , that I may learn thy commandments .
Those who fear You will rejoice when they see Me , because I have looked to Your word .
&quot; I know , O Lord , that Your judgment is righteous ; You have afflicted me , and have been faithful to me .
comfort me with mercy , according to the word of the servant ;
May thy mercy come upon me , that I may live : for thy law is my beloved .
Let the proud be ashamed , for they overwhelm me unjustly ; but I will think of Your commandments .
Let those who fear You return to Me , and they will know Your law .
Let my heart be perfect in thy statutes , that I may not be ashamed
I long for Your salvation , and I look to Your promises
&quot; I am blind in my hope for your promise , saying , &apos; When will you comfort me ?
I am like a bag of tobacco fragrance , but I do not forget your law
How long shall thy servant &apos;s years be , and when wilt thou judge those who oppress me ?
&quot; He who is proud of your law has dug a pit for me ,
Your commands are truthful , and they oppress me unjustly . Help me
They have almost destroyed me from the world , but I have no commandment to turn away from You
Save me according to thy mercy , and I will keep the law of thy mouth .
&quot; Your words , O Lord , will be established in heaven forever .
Thy righteousness endureth for ever , and when thou standest firm , it endureth for ever .
And the heavens and the earth are according to thy arrangement to this day ; and all things are thy servants .
&quot; If I had not loved your law , I would have been extinct in agony
I will never forget your words , for you have saved me by them
&quot; I belong to You . Please save me , for I have sought Your words .
The wicked await me , and they will destroy me ; but I will ponder Your law .
I see that all things are finite , but Your commands are extensive .
How long shall I love thy law , and not dwell in everlasting thought ?
&quot; Your commandments are always in my heart , and I am wiser than the enemy .
I am more wise than my master , because I think of your law .
&quot; I understand more than the elderly , for I have kept your commandments .
&quot; I have forbidden my feet from all evil ways , to keep Your word .
I have not strayed from thy statutes , because thou hast taught me .
How sweet are thy words in my mouth , and sweeter than honey in my mouth !
I have been made to understand by Your commandments ; therefore I hate all falsehoods .
Your word is the light of my feet , and the light of my ways .
I have sworn to obey your law of righteousness , and I will do according to my oath .
&quot; I am in great distress . Please , Lord , save me according to your word
&quot; O Lord , please accept the praise that is in my mouth as a sacrifice , and teach me Your statutes ,
&quot; My life is in danger , but I do not forget Your law
The wicked have set up nets for me , but I have no commandment to depart from You .
I will be an everlasting inheritance by thy law : for it is the love of my heart .
&quot; My heart is devoted to Your statutes , and I will keep them forever and ever .
For I hate those who have two minds ; but for I love Your law .
Thou art my hiding place , and my shield ; and I rejoice in thy words .
&quot; Depart from me , you wicked people , and I will keep my God &apos;s commandments .
Help me according to your word , and keep me alive ; and do not make me shy in disappointment .
&quot; Help me , and I will be saved , and I will always respect your statutes .
&quot; Those who deviate from your statutes , you will despise them ; for their deceit will be vanity .
Thou hast removed the wicked from all the earth , as the dust from me : therefore I love thy law .
&quot; For I feared you , and my flesh trembled ; and I feared your judgment .
I have done justice and righteousness : leave me not to those who oppress me
Protect me as a servant , and profit me ; and let not the proud oppress me .
&quot; I am blind because of your salvation and your righteous words ,
Teach me thy statutes by thy mercy toward thy servants
&quot; I am thy servant ; give me understanding , and let me know thy statutes .
&quot; This is the time of the Lord &apos;s punishment : for men have abolished your law .
Therefore I love your commandments more than gold , more than pure gold
&quot; I am upright in all things in all your teachings , but I hate all falsehoods .
Your law is wonderful . So I keep it with all my heart .
As soon as your words are cleared , light shines , and makes the fools understand .
I open my mouth and breathe , because I cherish your commandments .
Turn to me , and have mercy on me , as on those who love your name
&quot; Please make my steps steady with your words , and do not let sin rule over me
Save me from the oppression of men , and I will keep thy commandments .
Show me thy servant with thy face , and teach me thy statutes .
&quot; My tears are poured down into the river , because they do not keep your law .
&quot; You are righteous , O Lord , and your judgments are upright .
The law which You have ordained is by righteousness and truth .
My heart is troubled as a fire , because my enemies have forgotten your words .
&quot; Your words are perfect , and your servants love them .
I am small and despised , but I do not forget Your commandments .
Thy righteousness endureth for ever , and thy law is true .
I have suffered and suffered , and thy commandment is my beloved .
&quot; Your law is righteous for ever . Give me wisdom , and I will live .
&quot; I call on thee , O LORD , to hearken unto me ; and I will keep thy statutes .
I call on thee , and I seek thy salvation ; and I will keep thy law
I cried before the sun ; I looked up to thy words .
I will open my eyes while the night is still unchanged , to reflect on Your words
&quot; Hear my voice , O Lord , according to your loving kindness , and save me according to your statutes , O Lord .
The men who seek wickedness are near , and they are far from thy law .
&quot; You are near to me , O Lord , and all your commandments are true .
I have known for a long time that thou art established for ever , because I have learned thy law .
Take heed to my affliction , and deliver me ; for I remember not thy law .
Repent for me , and redeem me , and save me according to thy word
Save the wicked , for they seek not thy statutes .
&quot; Your mercy is great , O Lord ; save me according to your statutes .
There are many who oppress me , and many who resist me , but I have no right to depart from You .
&quot; I hate those who commit wickedness , because they do not keep your word .
See how I love thee , O LORD , and save me by thy mercy
Your word is true , and all your law of righteousness endures forever .
The prince has compelled me without cause , but my heart is afraid of your words .
&quot; I love your words as if a man had taken many captives .
Lies are hateful to me , and hateful to me ; but Your law is my beloved .
I praise thee seven times a day for thy law of righteousness .
Blessed are those who love thy law , for nothing can make them stumble .
&quot; I have looked to Your salvation , O Lord , and have obeyed Your commandments
I have kept your law in my heart , which I love very much .
I have obeyed thy commandments and thy statutes ; for all that I have done is before thee
&quot; Let my cry come to you , O Lord , and give me understanding according to your word .
&quot; Let my supplication come to you , and save me according to your word .
Let my mouth speak praise : for thou hast taught me the law .
Let my tongue sing thy words ; for all thy commandments are righteous .
May you help me with your hand , for I have chosen your words
I love thy salvation , O LORD ; and thy law is my delight .
May my life live , and may praise thee ; and may thy statutes help me .
I am lost like a lost sheep : seek thy servant ; for I remember not thy commandment .
And I cried unto the LORD in affliction , and he answered me
&quot; Lord , save me from the lips of lies and the tongues of deceit .
What shall I give you , O tongue of deceit , and what shall I add to you ?
And the arrows of the mighty , and the fire of the rodents .
&quot; Woe to me that I dwell in Mizpeh , and that I dwell in the tents of Kida
&quot; I will dwell with him who hates evil and is in peace for a long time .
I wish for harmony , but when I speak , they will fight
I will lift up my eyes to the mountain . Where is my help
My help came from the Lord of heaven and earth .
He will not shake your feet , and he will not take a nap to protect you .
Protect Israel , neither do they take a nap nor sleep
&quot; The LORD is your Protector , and the LORD is your Right Hand .
The sun shall not hurt thee , neither shall the moon hurt thee at night .
&quot; The Lord will protect you from all calamity ; He will protect your life
&quot; From now on , and from now on , and forever , the Lord will protect you
And they said unto me , We shall go unto the house of the LORD , and I will rejoice
Our feet , O Jerusalem , stand in thy gates
And Jerusalem was built , as a city that is joined together
The tribes , the tribes of the Lord , shall go up therein , and praise the name of the Lord according to the ordinance of Israel ;
For in it is the throne of judgment : it is the throne of the house of David .
Peace be to Jerusalem , O Jerusalem ; surely those who love thee shall thrive
Peace be in thy city , and prosperity in thy palace .
&quot; For the sake of my brothers and companions I say , Peace be with you
Blessed be thee , O Lord , for the sake of the house of our God
I lift up my eyes unto thee , O Lord that sitteth in heaven
&quot; Behold , how the eyes of a servant look at the hand of his master , and how the eyes of a woman look at the hand of her mother ; and how our eyes look at the Lord our God until he has mercy on us
Have mercy on us , O Lord ; have mercy on us ; for we have been despised to the utmost
&quot; We have come to the end of the reproach of the peaceful , and of the proud .
And the children of Israel shall say , If it were not for the Lord to help us ,
&quot; Unless the Lord helps us , when men come to attack us
When He was angry with us , He swallowed up our life .
Then the waves shall pass over us , and the waters shall overwhelm us
The proud waters shall overwhelm us .
Blessed is the LORD , who hath not given us for a prey unto them to eat
We fled like birds from the snares of the hunters . The snares broke , and we escaped .
&quot; We are to be helped by the name of the Lord , who has made the heavens and the earth
&quot; The man who relies on the Lord is as Mount Zion , and will not be shaken .
As the mountains surround Jerusalem , so the Lord surrounds His people from now on forever
The rod of the wicked does not often fall on the righteous , lest the righteous reach out to do evil .
O Lord , be kind to those who do good and are upright in their hearts
&quot; As for the one who strays from the way , the Lord will punish him and the wicked together . Peace be to Israel .
&quot; When the Lord brought back the captives to Zion , we were like dreamers
&quot; When our mouths were full of laughter and our tongues were full of joy , and there was a man in the foreign lands saying , &apos; The Lord has done great things for them
Surely the Lord has done great things for us , and we rejoice
&quot; Return , O Lord , our captives , as the waters of the South .
He that sows with tears shall rejoice in the harvest .
The one who brings out tears , the one who brings back the bundle of wheat , the one who must rejoice
Unless the Lord builds houses , he that builds is a waste of labour ; Unless the Lord guards the pond , he that guards is a waste of vigilance
Woe to you that you wake up early in the morning , and rest in the night , and eat the bread of your labour ! Only the beloved of the Lord will make him sleep at ease .
Sons and daughters are the inheritance of the Lord , and the wombs that are conceived are his reward .
As the arrows of a mighty man , so are the children of his youth .
Blessed are the people who are full of arrows , and they shall not be ashamed when they speak at the gates of the city with their enemies
Blessed is he that feareth the LORD , and keepeth his commandments
You will eat your bread , and you will be happy , and things will be well
Your wife is in your house like a vine with many branches , and your children are around your table like olive trees .
&quot; Behold , blessed are those who fear the Lord
Blessed be the LORD from Zion , and see the goodness of Jerusalem for a lifetime
May you see the children of your daughters , and peace be upon Israel
And Israel said , My enemies have afflicted me many times since I was a child
My enemies have afflicted me many times since I was a child , but they have not overcome me
Like those who plow , and plow on My back ; and the pits of plow are long .
The Lord is righteous ; He has cut off the rope of the wicked
And those who hate Zion shall be ashamed
May they be as the grass on the roof of the house , not grown , but desolate
The harvester is not a bundle , neither is the bundle full of wheat .
Neither do those who pass by say , &quot; May the blessings of the Lord be with you , and we bless you in the name of the Lord . &quot;
I pray to You from the depths , O Lord
&quot; Listen to my voice , Lord , and listen to my supplications .
&quot; If you , Lord Yahweh , search for iniquity , who will stand ?
&quot; But in Your forgiveness , let men fear You
&quot; I await the Lord , my heart awaits , and I look on His word .
&quot; My heart waits for the Lord , more than the night watchers wait for the light , more than the night watchers wait for the light
O Israel , look on the Lord , for He has mercy and abundant salvation
He will redeem Israel from all iniquity
O Lord , my heart is not arrogant , my eyes are not great , and I dare not do that which is great and cannot be measured .
My heart is quiet and steady , as a child who has given up milk in the arms of his mother . My heart is in me as a child who has given up milk
O Israel , when you look on the Lord , from now on to everlasting life
Remember , O Lord , all the affliction which David suffered
How did he swear to the Lord , and to the mighty man of Jacob
&quot; I will not enter my tent , nor my bed , &quot; he said .
I will not let my eyes sleep , neither will my eyes go to sleep
&quot; As soon as I have found a place for the Lord , and a place for the mighty One of Jacob ,
We heard that the ark was in Ephesus ; and we found it in Gilead .
&quot; We will go into his house , and worship before his bench
Rise up , O Lord , and enter into the place of rest with the ark of your power
Let your priests be clothed with righteousness , and let your saints rejoice .
&quot; Do not despise your anointed for the sake of your servant David
&quot; The Lord has sworn to David in truth , and he will not repeat it , saying , &apos; I will place your living creatures on your throne
&quot; If your children keep My covenant and the law which I have taught them , their children will sit on Your throne for ever and ever .
For the LORD hath chosen Zion to be his dwelling place
and said , &quot; This is the place where I will rest for ever ; and I will dwell here , because it is what I will .
And I will make the food thereof full , and the poor thereof full
I will make the priests clothe themselves with salvation , and the saints will cry out with a loud voice
&quot; I will call the corner of David , and it will happen therein ; I will prepare the lamps for My anointed .
I will cover his enemies with shame ; but his crown will shine on his head .
Behold , what good and what beauty is brotherhood and harmony ?
Like the precious oil that was poured on Aaron &apos;s head , and flowed into his beard , and into his collar ,
And it is like the valley of Ganroth of the gates of darkness , which descendeth into mount Zion : for therein is the blessing of the LORD , which is everlasting life .
Servants of the Lord , stand in the house of the Lord at night , and praise the Lord
Lift up your hands to the holy place , and praise the Lord
Blessed be the Lord of the heavens and the earth from Zion
Praise the Lord , praise the name of the Lord , praise the servant of the Lord , who stands in the house of the Lord , in the house of our God ,
See Up
Praise the Lord , for the Lord is good ; and praise His name , for it is good .
The LORD hath chosen Jacob for himself , and hath chosen Israel for his own people
&quot; I have known the Lord from the beginning , and that our Lord is above all gods
&quot; The Lord acts according to His will in heaven , and in the earth , and in the sea , and in all the depths
He poured out clouds from the poles of the earth ; He made electricity flashing with rain ; He brought out winds from the wells
And he slew all the firstborn of Egypt , men and cattle ,
&quot; He has done miracles among you , Pharaoh , and all his servants ,
He has slain many people , and he has slain the mighty king .
that is Sihon king of Amorah , and the night of Bashan king of Bashan , and the king of all Canaan
He gave their land , and gave it to His people Israel for a possession .
&quot; Your name , O Lord , will last forever ; Your name , O Lord , will be remembered for ever and ever .
&quot; The Lord will avenge His people , and repent for His servants
The idols of the nations are of gold and silver , and of man &apos;s hands .
A mouth cannot speak , and an eye cannot see
He who has ears cannot hear , and he who has no breath in his mouth
&quot; He who creates Him is like Him , and so is he who relies on Him .
O house of Israel , praise the Lord ; O house of Aaron , praise the Lord
&quot; Bless the Lord , O house of Levi , and those who fear the Lord ,
Blessed be the LORD that dwelleth in Jerusalem from Zion : praise ye the LORD
&quot; Praise the Lord , for He is good , and His mercy endures for ever .
Praise the God of all the gods , for His mercy endures for ever and ever .
Praise ye the Lord of hosts , for his mercy endureth for ever and ever .
Blessed is he that alone doeth great wonders : for his mercy endureth for ever and ever .
Blessed is He who created the heavens with wisdom , for His mercy endures forever
Praise be to Him Who laid the foundation above the waters , for His mercy endures for ever and ever
Praise be to him who made a great light , for his mercy endures forever
He hath made the day to be day , and his mercy endureth for ever .
He hath made the moon and the stars to keep the darkness ; for His mercy endureth for ever and ever .
Praise be to him who struck the eldest son of the Egyptians , for his mercy endures forever and ever .
He brought the children of Israel out of among them , for His mercy endures for ever and ever
For His hand is great , and His arm is stretched out , and His mercy endures for ever and ever .
Blessed is He that divideth the Red Sea : for his mercy endureth for ever and ever .
He will lead Israel through it , for His mercy endures for ever
But he overthrew Pharaoh and his army in the Red Sea ; for his mercy endures for ever and ever .
Blessed is he that guideth his people in the wilderness : for his mercy endureth for ever and ever .
Praise be to him who struck the great king , for his mercy endures for ever .
For he slew the famous king ; for his mercy endureth for ever .
&quot; He killed Sihon king of Amoly , for his mercy endures forever .
And slew the night of Bashan ; for his mercy endureth for ever and ever .
He has given his land for a possession to His people , for His mercy endures forever .
&quot; He has given His servant Israel for a possession , for His mercy endures forever and ever
He remembers our humble steps , for His mercy endures forever .
&quot; He has delivered us from the enemy , for His mercy endures forever .
He gives food to those who have blood , for His mercy endures for ever .
Praise the God of heaven , for His mercy endures forever .
We sat by the river of Babylon , and we cried for Zion .
We hang the harp on the willow trees in it
For those who seize us in it will sing for us , and those who seize us will sing for us , and they will make music for us , saying , Sing to us a song of Zion .
How can we sing the song of the LORD in a foreign land ?
&quot; If I forget you , O Jerusalem , I wish my right hand would forget the skill
&quot; If I do not remember You , if I do not see Jerusalem as my delight , let my tongue be on my chest
&quot; In the days of Jerusalem &apos;s trouble , the Edomites said , &apos; Destroy ! Destroy ! Destroy ! Destroy ! Destroy ! &apos;
Blessed is the man , O city of Babylon , which shall be destroyed , who will recompense thee , as thou didst to us ;
&quot; Blessed is he who takes your child and falls on a rock .
I will give thanks to you with all my heart , and I will sing praises to you before all the gods
I will worship in your sanctuary , and I will praise your name for your loving kindness and for your truthfulness , because you have made your words great beyond what you have promised them .
&quot; You will hear me in the days I cry for , and encourage me , and give me strength in my heart
&quot; All the kings of the earth will thank you , Lord , for they have heard the words of your mouth .
They shall praise the work of the Lord , because the Lord is great in glory .
The Lord is high , and he sees the humble ; but he sees the proud from afar
&quot; While I am in tribulation , You will save me ; My enemies will be angry ; You will stretch out your hand against them ; Your right hand will save me .
&quot; The Lord will do all that concerns me . Your mercy endures forever , O Lord . Do not forsake what your hands have created .
&quot; You have judged me , O Lord , You have known me
&quot; I sit down , and I arise , and you know ; and you know my thoughts from afar
&quot; Behold , I walk , I lie down , and you see , and you know all that I do .
&quot; There is not a word that you do not know , O Lord , from my tongue .
You surround me before me and behind me , and hold your hand on me
Such knowledge is marvelous , which I cannot measure , and supreme , which I cannot reach
I will go there to hide my soul from you , and I will go there to hide my face from you
&quot; If I ascend to heaven , you are there ; and if I lie in the shadow , you are there .
If I open my wings in the morning , I will fly to the Arctic to dwell
&quot; In it your hand will guide me , and your right hand will support me .
&quot; If I say , &apos; The darkness will cover me , and the light around me will become a night
And the darkness cannot hide me from you ; and the night is as the day ; and darkness and light are one thing in your sight .
&quot; You have created my lungs ; You have covered me in my mother &apos;s womb .
&quot; I will thank you for the wonder of my creation , and for your wonderful works , which I know from my heart .
&quot; I was created in darkness , and I was bound in the depths of the earth ; and my form was not hidden from you .
&quot; I have not been formed , and your eyes have seen me before ; and I have not lived one day of the days that you have appointed for me , and you have written them in your book .
How precious to me are Your thoughts , O God ! How many are they ?
If I number more than the sand , I will be with you when I wake up
&quot; O God , you must kill the wicked ; so leave me , you bloodthirsty people !
For they have struck you with evil words , and your enemies have denied your name .
&quot; Lord , will I not hate those who hate You , and those who attack You , and will I not hate them ?
&quot; I hate them very much , and take them for enemies .
&quot; Examine me , O God , know my heart , test me , know my thoughts
See what evil works are in me , and guide me to the way of everlasting life .
Save me , O Lord , from the wicked , and from the violent ,
They plot evil in their hearts , and often gather themselves together to fight
They make their tongues as sharp as snakes , and their mouths have the poison of snakes .
&quot; Save me , O Lord , from the hand of the wicked , and protect me , from the wicked , who seek to bring me down .
The proud lay nets and ropes for me ; they laid nets and girdles by the wayside .
&quot; I said to the Lord , &apos; You are my God ; O Lord , listen to my pleas
&quot; You have covered my head in the days of battle , O Lord , my salvation .
&quot; Lord , do not fulfil the will of the wicked , and do not fulfil their plans , lest they become proud .
Let the wickedness of their lips seize them that encircle me with their high heads .
Let the charcoal fall upon them , and let them be cast into the fire , and cast into the pits , and they shall not rise again .
The wicked will not stand firm on the earth , and the evil will hunt down the violent and overthrow him .
&quot; I know that the Lord will avenge the needy , and will give up the poor
The righteous shall praise thy name ; and the upright shall dwell before thee
&quot; I have prayed to You , O Lord , that You may come to me , and that You may listen to my voice in the time when I pray to You
Let my prayers be as candles before you , and let my hands be as evening sacrifices
&quot; Forbid my mouth , O Lord , and keep my mouth
&quot; Do not make my heart incline to evil , so that I may accompany the wicked with evil , and do not make me eat their food .
Let the righteous strike me , for it is mercy ; let him reproach me , for it is oil on my head ; my head shall not hide , and I will pray in the time of their wickedness .
&quot; Their judges have been thrown under rocks ; and they will listen to My word , for it is sweet .
&quot; Our bones are scattered by the tomb , like the soil of a man who plows the field ,
&quot; My eyes are on you , O Lord Yahweh ; I have put my trust in you ; do not leave me alone ,
Protect me from the snares of the wicked , and from the snares of the wicked .
Let the wicked fall into his own net , and I will be able to escape .
I cry unto the LORD , I pray unto the LORD
I have revealed my suffering in front of him . Chen said of my affliction
&quot; You know my way when my spirit fades in me , and the enemy has set up nets for me in the way I walk .
Look to my right hand , for no man knows me ; I have no refuge , and no one is near to me .
&quot; I have cried to You , O Lord , and said , &apos; You are my refuge ; You are my blessing in the land of the living .
Listen to my cry , for I have fallen into the most humble place ; save me from those who oppress me , for they are stronger than I.
Bring me out of the land of captivity , that I may praise thy name ; and the righteous shall encircle me , because they have been kind to me for thy sake
O Lord , hear my prayers , and keep my supplications , and answer me in truth and righteousness .
&quot; Do not question your servants , for none of the living is righteous before you .
For the enemy that came upon me oppressed me , and struck me to the ground , and made me dwell in darkness as a long-suffering man .
So my spirit fades in me , and my heart is in me grievous .
I remember the days of old , think of all that you have done , and remember the work of your hands .
I lift up my hand unto thee , and my heart longeth for thee as for rain in a dry land .
&quot; O Lord , hear me quickly , for my heart and my God are consumed ; and do not hide your face from me , lest I be like those who fall into the pit .
May I hear your loving words in the morning , because I have trusted in you ; and may I know the way to go , because my heart is on you .
&quot; Lord , save me from my enemies , and I will hide myself in Your presence .
Teach me to do thy will , for thou art my God , and thy spirit is good ; and lead me to a plain land
&quot; Please , O Lord , save me in Your name , and bring me out of trouble by Your righteousness .
And by thy mercy shew me away my enemies , and destroy all the affliction of my people : for I am thy servant .
Blessed is the LORD my rock , who taught my hands to fight , and taught my fingers to fight
&quot; He is the Lord of my mercy , my dwelling place , my high place , my Savior , my shield , in whom I have put my trust ; and He has made my people subservient to me .
&quot; What is man , O Lord , that you know him ? What is the world , that you care for him ?
A man is like a mouth . His days pass away like shadows
&quot; Lord , make the heavens come down , and touch the mountains , and the mountains will smoke
Give them lightning , that they may be dispersed ; cast out your arrows , that they may be troubled .
Lift me up from above , and deliver me out of the great waters , and deliver me out of the hand of the Gentiles
Their mouths speak lies , and their right hand swears .
I will sing a new song to you , O God ; I will sing to you with ten strings of hymns
Thou hast saved the king , and delivered David thy servant from the sword of death .
Save me , and deliver me out of the hand of the Gentiles , whose mouths speak lies , and whose right hand swears .
&quot; Our sons have grown up as seeds in their youth , and our daughters as the cornerstones of the house ; they have been carved according to the pattern of the palace .
&quot; Our barns are full , and we can produce all kinds of food ; and our sheep grow in the fields tens of thousands .
&quot; Our cattle are full , and no man has entered into them to plunder them , and no man has gone out to fight , and there is no cry in our streets ,
Blessed are the people who meet this vision , and blessed is the Lord their God , and blessed are the people
My God , my king , I will glorify You , and I will praise Your name forever and ever
I will praise you every day , and I will praise your name forever and ever
Blessed be the Lord , for His greatness cannot be measured .
&quot; This generation will praise you for your deeds , and proclaim your greatness
I will remember your majesty and your wonderful works
People will tell you the power of what you fear , and I will preach your greatness .
&quot; They will remember your great grace , and spread it out , and sing your righteousness .
The Lord is gracious , merciful , not easily angry , and greatly merciful
The Lord is good to all people , and His mercy covers all that He has created
All that thou hast done , O LORD , shall be praised of thee ; and thy saints shall praise thee .
Legends of the glory of your country , and of your great power .
Let the world know your mighty works , and the glory of your majesty
Thy kingdom shall be for ever , and thy dominion for ever and ever .
The Lord will support those who fall , and He will support those who are oppressed .
All the people lift up their eyes to thee , and thou hast given them food at all times
You stretch out your hand , and fill all those who are angry .
&quot; There is no unrighteousness in all that the Lord does , and there is mercy in all that He does
&quot; Whoever asks the Lord with sincerity , the Lord will be near to them
Those who fear Him , He will fulfill their desires , He will hear their cry , He will save them .
&quot; The Lord protects all those who love Him , but He will destroy all the wicked
&quot; My mouth will sing praises to the Lord ; but let all those with blood praise His holy name forever and ever .
Praise ye the LORD , O my heart , praise ye the LORD
I will praise the LORD all my days ; and in the days of my life I will praise my God
&quot; You shall not rely on a king , nor on the world , for he will not help you
And when his breath hath ceased , he shall return unto the dust , and that which he intended shall be destroyed that day .
Blessed is he who has been helped by the God of Jacob , who has looked on the Lord his God
&quot; The Lord created the heavens , the earth , the sea , and all that is in them , and He is faithful forever and ever
For he hath justified the oppressed , and hath given them food and hunger ; and the LORD hath delivered the captive
The LORD hath opened the eyes of the blind ; the LORD hath lifted up the oppressed ; the LORD hath loved the righteous .
&quot; The Lord protects those who dwell , He supports the orphans and widows , but He bends the way of the wicked .
The Lord will reign forever and ever ; and your God , O Zion , will reign for ever and ever ; and you shall praise the Lord
&quot; You shall praise the Lord , because you have praised the good and the beautiful God of ours ; and the words of praise are fitting .
&quot; The Lord has built Jerusalem , and gathered together the people of Israel who were driven away
He heals the wounded , and wraps up their wounds
And he numbered the hosts of the stars , and called them by their names .
Our Lord is the greatest and the most able . His wisdom cannot be measured .
The Lord supports the humble , He overthrows the wicked in the land
Sing unto the LORD in thanksgiving , and sing unto our God with the harp
He covered the sky with clouds , and rained on the earth , and made the grass grow on the mountains
He gave food to the beasts , and to the crow that cried
He is not pleased with the strength of the horse , nor with the speed of the legs of the lover
The Lord loves those who fear Him and hope in His mercy
O Jerusalem , praise the Lord ; O Zion , praise your God
&quot; For he has strengthened your gates , and blessed the children among you
&quot; He has made peace in your land , and satisfied you with good wheat .
He commands on the ground . His words are the quickest to be pronounced
It snows like wool , and frosts like ashes
He casts down hail as scraps ; He sends out cold ; Who can stand up when he is ready ?
He sends a commandment , and they are digested ; He sends the wind to blow , and water flows
He showed his ways to Jacob , and his statutes to Israel
&quot; He has not done so in any other land ; nor have they known his statutes . Praise be to the Lord !
Praise the Lord , praise the Lord from heaven , praise Him in high places
All his apostles will praise him , and all his armies will praise him .
Praise Him , the moon at the beginning of the day , and the stars that shine , all of you .
Praise him , the heavens of heaven , and the waters of heaven ;
Let all these praise the name of the LORD ; for he hath commanded them to do all things
He sets them straight for ever and ever , and He sets his life , and cannot be abolished .
All that is on the earth , the great fish , and all the deep sea
Fire and hail , snow and mist , the wind of his life accomplished
mountains and hills , and the resulting trees , and all acacia trees
Animals and all livestock , insects and birds
The kings of the world , and the people , and the princes , and all the judges of the world
The young men and the virgins , the elderly and the children , all praise the Lord
Let all these praise the name of the LORD : for his name alone is glorified , and his glory is above the heavens .
And he lifted up the horns of his people , and all the saints of Israel , which were near to him , praised him ; and ye shall praise the LORD .
&quot; You shall praise the Lord , sing a new song to the Lord , and praise Him in the congregation of the saints
Let Israel rejoice in the LORD that hath made him , and let the people of Zion rejoice in their king
May they dance , praise His name , and sing His praises
For the LORD loveth his people ; and he will make mercy a covering for humble men .
Let the saints rejoice in the glory that they have received , and let them rejoice on their beds
Let them praise God in their mouths , for he has a sword with two edges in his hand .
To retaliate against the nations , to punish the whole people
to bind their kings with chains , and their ministers with chains of iron ;
And the judgment that is recorded shall be done on them : and the glory of his saints shall be ; and ye shall praise the LORD .
Praise the Lord , praise him in the holy place of God , praise him in the heavens of his power
Praise him for his great power , and praise him according to the greatness of his majesty
To praise him with the horn , and to praise him with the harp
Praise Him with drums and dances , with stringed instruments , and with the sound of flutes
Praise him with a loud voice , Praise him with a loud voice
Praise the Lord , all who breathe ; praise the Lord , all of you
Proverbs of Solomon the son of David king of Israel
To make man know wisdom and instruction . To discern the words that are communicable .
To enable man to act ; to receive the instruction of wisdom , righteousness , justice , and uprightness
To enlighten the foolish , and to enlighten the young man with knowledge and cunning
To make the wise hear , to increase in knowledge , and to give the wise counsel .
To make men understand proverbs and parables , and to understand words and riddles of the wise .
The fear of the Lord is the beginning of knowledge ; and the foolish despise wisdom and doctrine
&quot; My son , listen to the teachings of your father ; you shall not forsake the law of your mother .
For this shall be the crown of your head , and the chain of gold on your head .
&quot; My son , if the wicked seduce you , you will not follow
&quot; If they say , &apos; You will go with us , &apos; we will bury the blood of the fleeing , and we will bury the innocent .
We have swallowed them up as the shadows ; they have been swallowed up as the people of the pit .
&quot; We shall have all kinds of treasures , and fill the houses that we have taken away .
You share with us all . We share a bag
&quot; My son , I will not go with them , and you shall not walk in their ways with your feet
For their feet run in wickedness , and their blood is poured out rapidly .
Like a flying bird , the net is still in front of you
They have laid down their bodies for their own blood , and they have squatted for their own souls .
Thus is the way of every one who lusts for riches ; and the heart of lust takes away the life of the rich .
Wisdom shouteth in the streets , and speaketh in the broad places .
He cried in the bustling streets , at the gates of the city , and in the midst of the city
Saying , &quot; When will your fools love foolishness , and those who blaspheme rejoice in blasphemy , and those who are stubborn hate evil knowledge ?
&quot; Return to Me for My reproach : I will pour out My Spirit upon you , and direct my words to you .
&quot; I call , but you do not obey ; I stretch out my hand , and no one listens .
For they have rejected all My admonition , and will not receive My reproach .
&quot; When you are in trouble , I will laugh , and when I fear you , I will laugh .
Fear cometh upon you like a wind , and calamity cometh like a stormy wind , and pain cometh upon you like a hurricane .
Then ye shall call upon Me , and I will not answer ; and ye shall seek Me in earnestness , but ye shall not find .
For you hate evil knowledge , and do not love to fear the Lord
&quot; Do not listen to my counsel , and despise all my reproach .
Therefore they shall eat fruit of their own accord , full of their own devising .
A fool turns away , and kills himself ; and a fool rests , and kills his own soul .
&quot; But he who listens to Me will dwell in peace , in quietness , without fear of evil .
&quot; My son , if you receive My words , remember My commandments .
Listen to wisdom in your ears , focus on seeking wisdom .
Call for wisdom , cry for wisdom
Look for him as for silver , and for him as for hidden treasures
&quot; You will understand the fear of the Lord , and you will know God
&quot; For the Lord gives wisdom , and wisdom and wisdom come out of His mouth .
He gives true wisdom to the upright , and shields those who do righteousness .
To preserve the path of the righteous , and to protect the path of the pious
You will also understand righteousness , justice , and righteousness , and all kindness .
Wisdom shall enter into your heart , and your spirit shall be beautiful in knowledge .
Thought shall protect thee ; wisdom shall keep thee .
to deliver you from the wicked way , from those who speak wickedly .
Those who forsake the way of righteousness and walk in the way of darkness
Happy is he that doeth evil , and loveth the wicked one that is far off
twisted in their ways , and straitened in their paths ;
Wisdom will deliver you from the woman of prostitution , the foreigner with a smooth tongue .
He has forsaken his childhood spouse , and forgot the covenant of God
His house is in the land of death , and his way is toward darkness .
Whoever goes to Him shall not return , nor shall he have a way of life .
Wisdom will make you walk in the way of the righteous , and keep the way of the righteous .
A righteous man shall dwell in the world , and a perfect man shall dwell on the earth .
Only the wicked will be cut off , and the treacherous will be brought forth .
&quot; My son , do not forget My law , and keep My commandments in your heart .
&quot; For He will give you long days and years of life and peace .
&quot; There is no way that mercy and truth will depart from you . It will be bound to your neck and engraved on your heart .
Thus you will be favoured in the sight of God and the world , and you will be wise .
&quot; If you rely exclusively on the Lord , you cannot rely on your own wisdom
Recognize Him in all that you do , and He will guide you on your way .
Do not think that you are wise , but fear the Lord , and stay away from evil
It will heal your belly and nourish your bones .
&quot; You shall honor the Lord with all your possessions and with all your first fruits .
Thus will your storehouse be filled with abundance , and your wine-press will be filled with new wine .
&quot; My son , you shall not despise the Lord &apos;s doctrine , nor be ashamed of His reproach .
For he that the Lord loveth shall reproach , as the father reproacheth the son that he loveth .
Blessed is he who is wise , and he who is wise ,
For wisdom is better than silver , and its benefits are as fine gold .
More precious than pearls , and all that you love is not worthy of comparison .
His right hand is long-lived and his left hand is rich .
His way is peace , and His path is all peace .
He is a tree of life with those who keep Him , and blessed are those who keep Him .
The LORD standeth in wisdom , and establisheth the heavens in wisdom .
With knowledge he breaks the depths , and the sky drops down sweetness .
&quot; My son , keep true wisdom and cunning ; he cannot be taken away from your eyes .
&quot; In this way He will make your life an ornament for your neck .
And you shall walk straight , and not touch your feet .
You lie down , and you will not be afraid ; You lie down , and you sleep sweetly .
Fear not the sudden terror ; fear not the destruction of the wicked ;
For the LORD is thy trust , and he will keep thy feet from falling into the net .
&quot; If your hand has the strength to do good , and it cannot be denied , it shall do it to whom it is due .
&quot; You shall not say to your neighbours , &apos; Go , and I will come to you tomorrow , &apos; if there is anything present in you
&quot; You shall not harm your neighbour , who dwells near you .
&quot; No man has done any harm to you , nor has he argued with you for any reason .
A man who is jealous of violence cannot choose the way in which he goes
For the wicked hates the LORD , and the upright is intimate with him
Cursed is the house of the wicked , blessed is the abode of the righteous
He reproaches the good reproacher , and gives grace to the humble
A wise man shall be honored , and a fool shall be a reproach .
O children , listen to the lesson of your father , and be mindful of wisdom .
For what I have taught you is a good lesson , and you shall not forsake My law .
I am a loving child in the eyes of my father , and a loving child in the eyes of my mother
&quot; My father taught me , &apos; You must keep my words in mind , and obey my commandments , that you may live
Be wise , be wise , that thou mayest not forget , nor depart from the words of my mouth
Thou shalt not forsake wisdom , for wisdom will guard thee ; and if thou love him , he will keep thee
Wisdom is first ; therefore be wise , and be wise in all that thou hast gained .
He will exalt you with wisdom , and He will honor you with wisdom
&quot; He will put the crown of glory on your head , and give you the crown of glory .
&quot; My son , if you will listen to My word , you will live long and long .
&quot; I have taught you the way of wisdom , and guided you to the path of righteousness
As you walk , your steps will not be narrow ; as you run , you will not fall .
Be heedful of the instruction , for it is not easy for you to relax ; and be steadfast , for he is your life
Do not walk in the way of the wicked ; do not walk in the way of the wicked
Avoid , do not pass ; turn and go .
&quot; If they can &apos;t do evil , they can &apos;t sleep ; if they can &apos;t make a man fall , they can &apos;t sleep .
For they eat bread with wickedness , and drink wine with violence
But the way of the righteous is as the light of the dawn , the brighter the light , until the even .
The path of the wicked is like darkness , and they do not know why they fall .
&quot; My son , listen carefully to My words , and listen to My words .
Do not leave anything from your eyes , and keep it in your heart .
For he that hath received him hath life , and he hath gotten the good medicine of the whole body .
For the fruit of a lifetime is from the heart , that thou mayest keep thy heart above all things .
Take away the mouth of the wicked , and cast away the mouth of the wicked .
&quot; Your eyes shall look forward . Your eyes shall look straight ahead .
Repair the way under your feet , and firm all your ways .
Do not be left or right , and let your feet be removed from evil .
&quot; My son , keep my words of wisdom , and listen to my words of wisdom .
To keep your lips from evil , and to preserve your knowledge
For he drops honey into the mouth of the prostitute , and his mouth is smoother than oil .
In the end , it will be as a sword with two edges .
His feet will descend into the land of death , and his foot will walk in the shadows .
so that he seeks a way that is not straight in life ; and his way is uncertain , and he knows not .
&quot; You children , who are now listening to me , cannot depart from my mouth .
&quot; You shall walk far from him , and you shall not come near to his door .
I fear that I will give your glory to others , and your years to the cruel .
&quot; For I am afraid that strangers will be filled with your strength , and those who have come for your labour will return to the houses of strangers
As long as your flesh and your bodies are destroyed , you will weep
&quot; How hated I the evil teachings , and how despised I the reproach in my heart
&quot; You will not listen to my master , nor listen to those who teach me
I am almost fallen into all evil in the holy church
You shall drink the water of your pond , and the living water of your well
Will your fountain be poured out , and your rivers flow in the streets ?
&quot; It is only for you to be one , and you cannot be of any use to others .
Blessed be thy fountain , and thou shalt rejoice in the wife of thy youth .
He is like a lovely deer , a happy mother deer . May His breasts make you know from time to time . May His love make you always fall in love
My son , why do you love a prostitute , and why do you hold the breasts of strangers
For the ways of men are before the LORD , and he repairs all the ways of men .
The wicked shall be caught by his own iniquity , and he shall be bound by his own iniquity as a rope
He will die because he has not been instructed , and he will go astray because of his foolishness .
&quot; My son , if you are a friend , shake hands for strangers
You are caught by the words of your mouth , and by the words of your mouth .
&quot; My son , if you fall into the hands of your friends , you will save yourself in this way ; and you will humble yourself and make supplication to your friends .
Don &apos;t let your eyes sleep , and don &apos;t let your eyelids take a nap
Save yourself , as a deer from the hand of a hunter , and as a bird from the hand of a catcher
&quot; O lazy man , if you look at the movements of the ants , you will have wisdom .
Ants have no commanders , no governors , no kings
And prepare food in the summer , and gather it in harvest
How long wilt thou sleep , O lazy man , and when wilt thou awake ?
Then take a nap , take a nap , hold your hand and lie down
&quot; Your poverty will come as a thief , and your lack as a man with weapons .
A foolish wicked man , he speaks with a disobedient tongue
To convey God with the eyes , with the feet , with the fingers
Dishonest in heart , always plotting evil , spreading strife
So a calamity shall come upon him suddenly , and he shall perish suddenly , and he shall not be healed
Six are the things that the Lord hates , and seven are the things that his heart hates
A proud eye , a tongue of lies , a hand that pours out innocent blood
A heart that deviseth evil , and a foot that runeth evil .
the false witnesses of lies , and the scatterers among brethren ,
&quot; My son , keep the commandments of your father , and do not forsake the law of your mother .
Always hang on your heart , and hang on your chains
Walk , and He will guide you ; lie down , and He will keep you ; and when you fall asleep , He will talk to you
For the commandment is a light , and the law is light , and the reproach of the commandment is the way of life
He will keep you from the evil woman , and from the tongue of a woman who flatters you .
Don &apos;t love his beauty in your heart , nor be drawn by his eyes
For the prostitute leaves only one piece of bread , and the prostitute seeks the precious life of man
If a man have fire in his belly , will his clothes not be burned ?
If a man walks on charcoal , will his feet not be scorched ?
And so is the wife of the near neighbour ; and whosoever is near to him shall be punished .
The thief steals for his hunger , and no man despises him
If he is found , he will repay sevenfold , and he will repay all that is in his house .
&quot; He who commits adultery with a woman is ignorant , and he who does it will perish .
He shall be injured and humiliated , and his shame shall not be blotted out .
For hatred for man is turned into wrath , and the time of vengeance is not turned away .
He will not take care of anything for redemption , and he will not rest , even though you give many gifts
&quot; My son , keep my words , and keep my commandments in mind .
He will live by My commandments , and keep My law as the eye of the keeper .
On your fingers , and on your heart .
Say to wisdom , &quot; You are my sister ; call wisdom your kinsman .
He will keep you from the prostitute , and from the foreigner who speaks flattery .
&quot; In the windows of my house , I looked out from among my windows ,
See , among the foolish , among the youth , a youth who is ignorant .
And passed through the street , and passed by the lane of the prostitute , and went straight to his house .
In the twilight , or at night , or at midnight , or in the darkness
&quot; Behold , a woman comes to him , dressed as a prostitute with a deceitful heart .
The woman shouted without restraints , without stopping her feet at home
Sometimes on the streets , sometimes in broad spaces , or squatting in the alleys
And He took the young man , and kissed him , and spoke to him without shame
The sacrifice of peace is here with me ; and today is the fulfillment of my promise
&quot; Therefore I came out to meet you , and to seek your face in earnestness , and I found you by chance .
I have laid my bed with embroidered carpets , and with linen of Egyptian yarn .
And I laid my bed with no medicine , and with a sweet scent , and with cinnamon
Come , and we shall be filled with love until the morning , and we shall love one another and rejoice
Because my husband is not at home , and goes far off
He has a silver bag in his hand ; he will not return until the moon .
The prostitute tempted him with many cunning words , and compelled him with flattering mouths
And immediately the young man followed him as a cattle to slaughter , and as a fool with chains to be punished
He waits for the arrow to pierce his liver , like a bird in the net , but he does not know that he has lost his life .
&quot; Now , O children , listen to me , and keep your ears attentive to what I say .
Thy heart shall not turn aside from the way of the prostitute , and thou shalt not go astray from him .
For there are many servants who have been hurt by Him , slain by Him , and many more
His house is the way of darkness , and the palace of death .
Wisdom does not cry , Wisdom does not speak
And he stood on the top of the high place by the way , at the crossroad
&quot; Beside the gates , at the gates , at the gates ,
&quot; O you people , I call on you , and I speak to the world
Saying , &quot; You fools , you will be enlightened , and you fools , you will understand in your hearts .
&quot; Listen , for I will speak beautiful words , and I will speak uprightly .
My mouth shall speak truth , and my mouth shall hate evil and evil .
&quot; All the words of my mouth are righteous , and they are not devious .
A wise man to be manifest , and a knowledgeable man to be honest
Take instruction from Me , and receive not silver ; but know knowledge is better than gold .
For wisdom is more beautiful than pearls ; and all that is pleasing is not worthy of comparison .
My wisdom dwells in wisdom , and I seek knowledge and counsel
Fear the Lord , and hate evil and evil : for I hate the pride , and the madness , and the wickedness , and the foolish tongue
I have cunning and true knowledge . I am wise . I have power .
The emperor sits on the throne through me , and the king establishes justice through me
&quot; In My hand are the princes and the princes and the judges of all the world .
He that loveth me , I love him ; and he that seeketh me , he shall find it .
Glory is abundant in me , and everlasting riches and righteousness are in me
My fruit is stronger than gold , and stronger than gold ; and my fruits are exceedingly precious .
I walk in the way of righteousness , and in the way of justice
Let those who love me bear their goods , and fill their treasures
&quot; I am in the beginning of the creation of the Lord , and in the beginning of all creation ,
From the ancient times , from the very beginning , before there was no world , I have been raised
No depth , no fountain of great water , I have been born
The great mountains have not been laid down , and the small mountains have not been before , and I am born
&quot; I was born before the Lord had created the earth , and the field , and the earth of the world
&quot; He stands high in the sky , and I am in it , and He draws circles around the edge of the abyss .
He made the heavens firm above , and the fountains firm beneath .
He sets the limits for the sea , and the waters go beyond His commandments , and sets the foundations of the earth .
&quot; In those days I was in him as a craftsman , and I danced before him day by day , as I loved him
dancing in the land which He has prepared for man , and dwelling in the midst of the world
&quot; O children , listen to me now , for blessed are those who keep my word .
To hear a lesson is wisdom , and it cannot be forsaken .
&quot; Blessed is he who listens to Me , who looks at My door day and night , and waits by My doorway .
For he that seeketh me seeketh life , and the grace of the Lord shall be upon him .
He who has sinned against me has harmed his own life ; and he who hates me loves death .
Wisdom builds houses , and carves seven pillars .
slaughtering livestock , mixing wine , and arranging feasts
And he sent forth the woman , and called her in the midst of the city unto the high places
He said , &quot; Whoever is a fool can turn to this place , &quot; and said to the ignorant .
&quot; Come , eat my cakes , and drink my sweet wine .
You are foolish , and if you turn away from foolishness , you will live , and you will walk in the way of light .
He who reproaches the blasphemers shall be reproached ; and he who reproaches the wicked shall be defiled .
&quot; Do not reproach the humble , lest he hate you ; but reproach the wise , and he will love you
He that teacheth the wise increaseth in wisdom ; and he that guideth the righteous increaseth in knowledge .
Fearing the Lord is the beginning of wisdom ; knowing the Holy One is wisdom .
Thou hast borrowed from me , and the days shall increase , and the years shall add .
&quot; If you are wise , you are good to yourself ; and if you blaspheme , you are alone .
A foolish woman cries out , and he is a fool , and has no knowledge .
He sat at the door of his own house , in the high seat of the city
He who calls through the way is he who walks straight in his way .
He said , &quot; Whoever is a fool can turn to this place , &quot; and said to the ignorant .
The water that is stolen is sweet , and the cake that is eaten in the dark is good
But man knows not that there is a soul in him , and his guests are in the depths of the shadow .
Proverbs of Solomon ; A son of wisdom rejoiceth his father ; A son of foolishness troubleth his mother .
The wealth of iniquity is of no use ; but righteousness saves from death .
The Lord does not hunger the righteous ; He will drive away what the wicked desire .
Those who are lazy in their hands shall be afflicted , and those who are diligent in their hands shall be rich .
He that gathereth in the summer is the son of wisdom ; He that sleepeth in the harvest is the son of shame .
Welfare is upon the head of the righteous , and violence covers the mouth of the wicked .
The remembrance of the righteous is praised . The name of the wicked shall perish .
The wise in their hearts will be commanded , and the foolish in their mouths will be overthrown .
He who walks in a straight path will walk in safety , and he who walks in a strait path will be exposed .
&quot; He who sends his eyes to God causes grief , and he who is foolish in his mouth will fall .
The mouth of the righteous is the fountain of life , and the mouth of the wicked is the covering of violence .
Hatred can stir up controversy . Love can hide all wrongdoing .
A wise man has wisdom in his mouth ; and a fool is hanged on his back .
A wise man stores up knowledge . The speed of a foolish man is defeated .
The wealth of the rich is his strong city , and the poverty of the poor is his ruin .
The work of the righteous brings life , and the work of the wicked brings death .
