For as the beasts have suffered for the world , so are the beasts ; and as the one dies , so the other dies ; and as the breath is one ; and man is not stronger than the beast ; and they are all empty
They are all in one place . They are all out of the dust , and they are all in the dust
Who knows that the spirit of man ascends upward , and that the soul of beasts descends downward ?
&quot; Therefore I see no man rejoicing in what he does ; for this is his portion ; and who can bring him back to see what is behind him ?
And I remembered all the oppression that was done under the sun ; and behold , the tears of the oppressed , and no one comforted them ; and their power was oppressed , and no one comforted them .
Therefore I praise the dead that died early , more than the living that is still alive
And I thought that those who were not born , that had not seen evil in the light of the sun , were stronger than those of the second class
I have also seen men jealous of their neighbours for all their labour and all their skillful work , which is also vanity and the catching of the wind .
A fool holds his hand and eats his own flesh
Be filled with one squad , and be quiet ; be filled with two squads , and be busy catching the wind
Then I remembered again , and saw that there was an empty thing under the sun
&quot; There is a man who is lonely , without sons , without brothers , who does not work , and whose eyes are not sufficient with money and riches . He says , &quot; Who am I for , that I work , and suffer myself , and do not rejoice ? This is also emptyness , and it is a great hardship
Two are better than one , for good works are done for two
&quot; If he falls , he can rescue his companion ; but if he falls alone , and no one comes to rescue him , he is in trouble .
And when two sleep together , they are at peace ; and when one sleeps alone , how can they be at peace ?
A man shall prevail over a lonely one , and two men shall be able to defend him . A rope made of three parts is not easy to break .
A poor and wise young man is better than an old foolish king who refuses to obey
&quot; This man came out of prison to reign , and was born poor in his land .
And I saw in the light of the sun that all the living were acting , and they followed the second , the young man that came up to replace the old king .
And all the people whom He ruled , his people , were innumerable , and they did not please Him in the generations to come after Him . That is vanity , and it is the catching of the wind .
&quot; Go to the house of God with caution ; for they have not known that what they have done is evil , because they have listened and sacrificed more than the foolish .
Thou shalt not open thy mouth in the sight of God , nor speak hastily : for thou art under heaven for God &apos;s sake , and thine words shall be few .
Many things make a man dream , and many words show folly .
You cannot delay the repayment of your vows to God , for He does not please the foolish , and therefore your vows must be repaid .
You promise not to return , rather than not
&quot; You shall not let your mouth cause the flesh to sin , nor say in the presence of the priests that you have sinned . Why is God angry with your voice , and destroys what your hands have done ?
Many dreams and many words , and many of them are illusions ; but fear God .
&quot; Do not be surprised when you see the poor in one province being oppressed and deprived of justice , for there is a high judge who lives above them , and there is a higher judge above them .
And the good of the land belongeth to all , and the king shall be provided with the land .
Those who love money do not know enough for money , and those who love riches do not know enough for profit , and that is also vanity .
Added is the goods , and added is the man who eats ; and what is the profit of the owners of things , except by glance ?
A labourer sleeps sweetly without having to eat more or less ; but the abundance of the rich does not allow him to sleep .
&quot; Behold , under the sun there is a great calamity : the owners of wealth accumulate their wealth against themselves .
&quot; In the midst of adversity , the wealth will be destroyed ; and if a man bears a son , he will have nothing in his hand .
As he comes from the womb naked , so shall he go naked ; and he that bringeth forth his labour shall not be carried away in his hand .
How is he come and how is he gone ? This is also a great affliction . What good is he for his labour
And he ate and drank in the darkness , with much trouble and sickness and vomiting
For what I see as good and what I see as beautiful is the good that man shall eat and drink in the days of his life , which God hath given him , and which he shall work in the sunlight ; for that is his portion .
God has given man abundance , so that he may eat , and take his portion , and rejoice in his labour : that is the grace of God .
He does not think much of the years of his life , for God pleases him in his heart
I have seen a calamity under the sun , and a heavy burden on man
&quot; It is a man who has been blessed by God with riches , riches , and honours , so that he does not lack anything in his heart ; but God has made him useless against the use of strangers ; and that is vanity and evil .
&quot; If a man bears a hundred sons and lives many years , and has many years of life , he will not be happy in his heart nor be buried ; and I say that the womb that has not come to term is better than he .
For the name is obscured by darkness , for it comes and goes in vain .
And he has not seen the day nor the night , nor is he aware of it ; and the womb shall rest more than he .
&quot; While he has lived a thousand years and a thousand years , and has not been blessed , will not all of them return to one place ?
A man &apos;s labour is for his mouth , but his heart is inadequate
Then how is the wise man better than the foolish man , and how is the poor man better than he that knoweth how to do in the sight of all men
What the eye sees is better than what the mind deceives . It is also empty , and it catches the wind
All who were before him had a name , and knew what he was , and he could not contend with that which was greater than himself .
What good is it to man that more and more things are vanished ?
A man &apos;s days of vanity pass like shadows . Who knows what is good for him , and who can tell him what is behind him under the sunlight ?
The days of death are better than the days of life .
Go to the house of the slain , as to the house of the banquet ; for death is the end of all , and the living will keep it in mind .
Sorrow is strong as laughter , for the sorrow of the face will make the heart rejoice
The heart of a wise man shall be in the house of the slain , and the heart of a fool in a happy house .
Hear the reproach of the wise ; Hear the singing of the foolish .
&quot; The laughter of the foolish is like the burning of thorns under a pot , and it is empty
Lesson makes the wise foolish ; bribery defeats the wise
The end of things is as strong as the beginning of things . The patient is better than the proud .
Do not be hasty in your heart , for anger is in the breasts of fools
&quot; Do not say , &apos; What is the reason why the days of old are stronger than the days of this day ? &apos; It is not wisdom to ask this question .
Wisdom and inheritance are good , and it is more profitable for a man who sees the day of heaven .
For the shepherd of wisdom is like the shepherd of silver ; and wisdom saves the life of the wise ; that is the profit of knowledge .
Look at God &apos;s deeds . Who can be straight for God &apos;s sake ?
Rejoice in the days of Hunting , and think in the days of affliction ; for God has joined these two things together , so that one cannot see what is behind him .
And the righteous do righteousness , and they perish ; and the wicked do evil , and they live long . These things have I seen in the days of vanity .
Do not exceed in righteousness , nor exceed in self-control , nor in wisdom ; for what is the cause of self-defeat ?
Do not commit excess wickedness , nor be foolish of men . Why should you die without the due time ?
And keep this beautiful , and let not that loose his hand ; for he that feareth God shall come forth out of these two
Wisdom makes the wise more able than ten officers in the city
There is no righteous man in the world who does good and does not sin
&quot; Do not put all the words of men on your heart , lest your servants curse you .
For you know in your heart that you have cursed others many times
&quot; I tested all these things with wisdom ; and I said , &apos; You must have wisdom , but wisdom is far from me .
How far away from Me is the law of all things , and how deep is it ! Who can discern it ?
&quot; I turn my mind to know , to examine , to seek wisdom , and to know the cause of all things , and to know that evil is foolishness , and foolishness is madness
I know that there is a woman like him who suffers more than death , whose heart is a net , and her hands a chain ; and whoever is pleasing to God will be able to escape him , and whoever is guilty will be entangled in him .
And the prophet said , &quot; Behold , I have found a righteous man among a thousand men , but I have not found one among the women . I have compared this thing one by one , seeking its justification , and I have sought it , and have not found it .
See Up
What I have found is only one thing , that God created men honest , but they have devised many schemes
Who is as a wise man , and who knows the interpretation of things ? A man &apos;s wisdom makes his face shine , and changes his anger .
I urge you to obey the commandment of the king , as God has sworn
Do not be hasty to leave the king , and do not be stubborn in evil ; for he does all things according to his own heart .
&quot; The word of the king has power . Who can ask him , &quot; What are you doing
Whosoever keepeth his commandment shall not suffer affliction ; and the heart of a wise man knoweth the time and the law .
For all things are accomplished in due time and in due cause : for the torment of man is heavy upon him .
He does not know the future , for who can tell him what the future will be
No one has the power to control life , to keep it alive , and no one has the power to control the time of death . No one can escape this battle , nor can evil save the righteous who do evil .
I have seen all these things , and have been attentive to all that is done in the light of the sun ; and it is he who , at times , ruleth over him , and afflicteth him .
&quot; I have seen the wicked buried , and returned to the grave ; and I have seen the upright left the holy place , and forgotten in the city ; and this is also vanity .
&quot; The world is filled with evil because it does not punish immediately for a crime .
Though the sinner has done a hundred evil deeds , he will live for many years ; but I know that he who fears God , and he who fears before him , will be blessed for ever .
But the wicked shall not rejoice , neither shall the years be prolonged , which are like shadows , because he hath not feared God
&quot; There is an empty thing in the world , which the righteous encounters in the way of the wicked , and another which the wicked encounters in the way of the righteous ; and I said , &quot; This is also an empty thing
I praise the joy , for a man is not able to eat and drink in the light of the sun ; for God has given him years of his life in the light of the sun , that he may rejoice in the fruits of his labour ,
I seek wisdom , to see what is done in the world . There are those who do not sleep day and night ,
I see all the works of God . I know that no man can find out what he does under the sun . No man can find out how much effort he puts into it . A wise man can find out even if he wants to .
And I have set all these things in my heart , and have studied them , and know that the righteous and the wise are in the hand of God , and that love and hatred are before them , and no man knows .
All things that come to all are the same . The righteous and the wicked are in the same situation . The good and the clean and the unclean are in the same situation . The one who sacrifices and the one who does not sacrifice is in the same situation . The good and the sinner are in the same situation . The one who swears and the one who fears to swear is in the same situation .
There is a calamity in all that is done under the sun , and it is the same with all that is done ; and the hearts of the world are filled with evil , and in the days of life they are deluded , and they return to the dead .
And he that is joined to all the living has hope ; for the living dog is stronger than the dead lion .
The living know that they shall die ; and the dead know not , neither shall they be rewarded , neither shall their names be remembered .
Their love , their hatred , their jealousy , have vanished before , and they shall have no part in all that they do under the sun .
You shall eat your food with joy , and drink your wine with joy in your heart ; for God has accepted your deeds
Your clothes were always clean at that time . There was no lack of oil on your head
The days of your life , which are empty , are the days which God has given you in the light of the sun , that you may live in peace with your beloved wife ; for that is the portion of your labour before you were born in the light of the sun .
Do all that your hands do ; for there is no work , no calculation , no knowledge , and no wisdom in the shadow to which you shall go .
And I remembered again , when I saw under the sun , that those who run fast do not win , those who fight hard do not win , those who are wise do not get food , those who are wise do not get riches , those who are wise do not get joy , and that what came to all was for the opportunity of the time
&quot; And the people of old did not know their own time , neither were the fish caught in the net of evil , nor the birds caught in the net of evil , nor were the people of the world caught in the time of evil .
&quot; I have seen wisdom under the sun , and in my eyes it is vast .
&quot; There is a small city , few in number , and a great king who attacks , builds forts , and besieges the city .
There was a poor wise man in the city , who saved the city with wisdom , but no man remembered the poor man
Then said I , Wisdom is better than strength ; but the wisdom of the poor man is despised , and his words are not heard .
Rather listen in silence to the words of the wise , and not to the cry of the foolish .
Wisdom is better than the weapon of war ; but a sinner can defeat many good deeds .
The dead flies make the odor of the ointment of fragrance ; and thus a foolishness defeats wisdom and honour .
The heart of the wise is to the right , and the heart of the foolish to the left .
And the fool goes astray in ignorance , and says to the people , &quot; He is a fool .
&quot; If the heart of the ruler is angry with you , let it not leave your throne , for it is too great for meekness .
I saw under the sun a calamity , seeming to be the fault of the ruler
A fool stands high , and a rich man sits low
I saw a servant riding on horseback , and the prince walked like a servant on the ground
He who digs a pit will fall in it , and he who breaks a wall will be bitten by a snake .
Whoever carries out stones shall be injured , and whoever breaks down wood shall be in danger .
The iron is dull , and if it is not sharpened , it will take more energy ; but wisdom teaches , and it is profitable .
If a snake bites a man , then it is useless to practice witchcraft .
The mouth of a wise man speaketh good words ; and the mouth of a fool destroyeth himself .
The beginning of his speech is foolishness , and the end of his speech is folly of evil .
The fool has many words , but he knows not what is to come . Who can tell him what is behind him ?
For every fool &apos;s labour makes him weak , and he knows not the way to the city .
&quot; Woe to you , O king of the land , if your king is a child , and your subjects have a feast in the morning
Blessed are you , O king of the land , if your king is the son of nobles , and your subjects eat and drink according to the time , to refresh themselves , and not to be drunken .
For laziness , the roof is fallen ; For laziness of hands , the houses are leaky .
A feast is for laughter ; wine makes a man rejoice , and money makes all things glad .
Thou shalt not curse the king , neither shalt thou remember it ; neither shalt thou curse the rich man in thy bedroom : for the birds of the air shall proclaim it , and the wings shall speak it .
&quot; When you lay down your food on the surface of the water , it will be for a long time .
&quot; You shall divide it among seven , or among eight ; for you do not know what evil shall come upon the earth in the future .
If the clouds are full of rain , they will fall upon the earth . If the trees fall to the south , or to the north , wherever the trees fall , wherever they exist
He who sees the wind will not sow ; and he who sees the clouds will not harvest .
&quot; You will not know how the bones grow in the womb of a pregnant woman , nor how the winds come forth , nor how the bones grow in the womb of a pregnant woman ; neither will you know the works of the God of all things .
&quot; You shall plant your seed in the morning , and you shall not rest your hands in the evening ; for you do not know whether it is good to plant it early or late or both .
The light is beautiful , and the sight of the sun is pleasant
For as long as a man lives , so long as he is happy ; but when he thinks of the days of darkness , for these days will be many , and all that is to come is nothing .
O young man , rejoice in your youth , and in the days of your youth make your heart rejoice , do what your heart desires , see what your eyes love to see , and know that God will question you for all these things .
Therefore remove your sorrow from your heart , and turn away from the flesh from evil ; for the beginning of life and the beginning of childhood are void
&quot; Behold , the days of youth and decay have not come , when you said , &apos; I will not rejoice in those days which have not come near , &apos; when you remember your Lord .
Don &apos;t wait until the sun , the light , the moon , the stars , turn into darkness , and the clouds return after the rain
The shaking of the watchmen of the houses , the strong submission , the rare grinding ceased , and the view from the window was dim .
The gates were shut , and the noise of grinding was low , and the birds cried , and the people arose , and the women who sang weakened .
A man is afraid of high places , and fear is in the way , and the almonds blossom , and the grasshoppers are a burden ; and all that man desires is vanished ; for he is returned to his eternal home , and the hanged up come in the streets .
Silver chains broken , gold cans broken , bottles damaged by the spring , water wheels broken at the well mouth
The earth belongs to the earth , and the Spirit to the God who gave it
The prophet said , &quot; A void void of voidness ; all things are void
Again , the prophet teaches wisdom by reason of wisdom , and ponders , and examines , and prophesies many proverbs
The prophet seeks a pleasurable word , a truth written with integrity
The words of a wise man are like a stick , and the words of a teacher in the congregation are like a firm nail , which is given by a minister .
My son , there is another layer , when thou art persuaded . When thou readest much , thou shalt not be exhausted . When thou readest much , thou shalt be weary
&quot; All these things have been heard . It is the duty of men to fear God and to keep His commandments .
For God will question all that is done for man , and all that is hidden , whether it be good or evil
The song of Solomon is the beauty of the song .
May he kiss me with his mouth , for your love is better than wine
Your ointment smells sweet . Your name is like the ointment that falls down . Therefore all the little girls love you .
If thou seekest me , we shall run with thee ; and the king shall bring me into the inner chamber ; and we shall rejoice in thee ; and we shall praise thy love as a wine ; and it is of course that they love thee
&quot; Women of Jerusalem , though I am black , I am beautiful , as the tent of Kida , as the curtain of Solomon
&quot; Don &apos;t look at me lightly because the sun has turned me dark . My mother &apos;s brothers are angry with me , and they keep watch over my vineyard , my own vineyard , and they have no watch over it .
&quot; Tell me , O my beloved , where do you shepherd the sheep , and where do you make the sheep rest at noon , and where will I be by your flock like a man with faces ?
&quot; If you do not know , you , the most beautiful of the women , follow the footsteps of the flock , and shepherd your lambs by the shepherd &apos;s tent
My darling , I will put you on a horse like an old French car
Your breasts are beautiful for their braided hair ; Your neck is beautiful for the strings of pearls .
&quot; We will make you gold braids and silver nails
&quot; When Wang was sitting , my ointment smelled
I take my good man as a bag of medicine , and he is always in my arms
&quot; I will take my good man as a fig tree in the vineyards of the bottomless pit
My darling , how beautiful are you ! How beautiful are you ! Your eyes are like the eyes of a dove
O my good man , how beautiful and lovely are you ! We have laid our beds on grass
and the beams of the houses of acacia trees , and the pine trees of bark ;
&quot; I am the rose of Sharon , and the sapphire of the valley .
My beauty is among the women , as a flower in thorns .
My good man is in men as an apple tree in the forest ; and I sit in his shade , and taste his fruit sweetly .
&quot; He brought me to the banquet , and loved me above me as a flag
Give me grapes to increase my strength , and give me apples to refresh my heart ; for I have become sick in my love
His left hand is under my head , and his right hand holds me
&quot; And I command you , O daughters of Jerusalem , by the antelope , or by the deer of the field , not to tremble , neither to wake up my beloved , until he pleases himself ; neither to wake up the cloud , nor to stir up love until he pleases himself .
&quot; Hear , O , the voice of my righteousness ; behold , he comes up from the mountains and over the hills
&quot; My good man is like an antelope , or like a deer . He stands behind our walls , looking from the window to the inside , and peering from the window to the inside
&quot; My good man said to me , &apos; Arise , my beauty , my beauty , and come with me
For the winter is gone . The rain has stopped
&quot; Behold , the time has come when the flowers of the earth are opened , and the time of the birds to shout has passed , and the voice of the doves has been heard in our midst .
The fruit of the fruitless tree is ripened , and the vines are blooming , and they are fragrant ; and my maiden , my beauty , arise , and go with me .
O my dove , thou art in the cave of rocks , in the secret place of steep rocks ; let me see thy face , and hear thy voice ; for thy voice is soft , and thy face is beautiful .
Take away the fox , the little fox that destroys the vineyard ; for our grapes are blooming .
The good man belongs to me , and I belong to him ; and he shepherds his flock among the lilies .
&quot; My beloved , wait until the day is cool and the shadows fly away , and turn like an antelope , or like a deer on Mount Beth
I lie down in bed at night , seeking my beloved ; I seek him , and find him not .
I said , &quot; I will rise up in the city , and in the streets , and in the broad places , to seek my beloved , and I will seek him , but I will not find him .
&quot; When the guards of the city met me , I asked them , &quot; Do you see what I love ? &quot;
&quot; When I left them , I met the one whom my heart loved ; I held him , I did not let him go , I brought him into my mother &apos;s house , into the inner chamber of those who loved me .
&quot; And I command you , O daughters of Jerusalem , by the antelope , or by the deer of the field , not to tremble , neither to wake up my beloved , until he pleases himself ; neither to wake up the cloud , nor to stir up love until he pleases himself .
&quot; Who is it that comes up from the wilderness , like a pillar of smoke , with no medicine and no perfume , and with all kinds of incense poured on the merchants ?
Behold , the chariot of Solomon was surrounded by sixty mighty men , all of Israel .
They have swords in their hands , and are good at fighting . They wear swords in their waist , and guard themselves at night .
And king Solomon made for himself a carriage in China out of the timber of Lebanon
&quot; The pillars of the chariot were of silver , and the bottom of the chariot of gold , and the cushions of purple , and the love of the daughters of Jerusalem was laid therein .
&quot; Go out , O daughters of Zion , and see the crown of king Solomon , which his mother gave him in the days of his wedding , in the joy of his heart ,
Thou art very beautiful , my darling , thou art very beautiful : thy eyes are as dove &apos;s eyes , and thy hair as a flock of sheep , lying by mount Gilead
&quot; Your teeth are like a newly trimmed flock of sheep . They are cleansed , and they are twins , and they have not lost a single child .
Your lips are like a red line , and your mouth is beautiful ; your two teeth are like a pomegranate in a basket .
&quot; Your neck is like David &apos;s high mount , which he built to store up his weapons , and on which are hanging a thousand shields , all of which are the wings of the mighty .
&quot; Your two breasts are like a pair of deer eating grass in a flower : they are twins of a mother deer .
I will go to the mountains of medicine and to the fountains of milk , until the day comes when the wind is cool and the shadows fly away .
My darling , you are absolutely beautiful , without defects
My new wife , go with me out of Lebanon , go with me out of Lebanon , and look down from the top of Armanah , from the top of Shenior , and from the top of the Black Gate , from the cave of the lion , and from the mountain of the leopard ,
&quot; My sister , my new wife , you have taken my heart ; You have taken my heart with your eyes , with a chain of gold on your head
My sister , my new wife , how beautiful is your love ! Your love is more beautiful than wine ! The fragrance of your oil is better than all fragrances !
&quot; My new wife , Your lips dribble like honey in a beehive ; There is honey and milk under your tongue ; The smell of your clothing is like Lebanon .
My sister , my new wife , is an enclosed garden , an enclosed well , an enclosed spring
The pomegranate that thou hast planted in thy garden , with its beautiful fruit , and the fig tree ,
And there were sweet and red flowers , and irises , and almond trees , and all kinds of milkweed , and intoxicants , and fragrances , and all kinds of high fruit
Thou art the fountain of the garden , the well of living water , the stream that floweth down from Lebanon
Arise , O north wind , and arise , O south wind , and blow in My garden , and let the fragrance thereof come forth : let my good men enter into their own garden , and eat of His good fruits .
My sister , my new wife , I have entered into my garden , and have taken my poison and my fragrances , and have eaten my honey and my honey , and have drunk my wine and my milk , and have eaten , my friends , and have drunk much of what I love .
&quot; I lie down , and my heart awakes ; and this is the voice of my goodness ; and he knocks on the door , saying , &apos; My sister , my doll , my dove , my perfect man , open the door to me , for my head is full of water , and my hair is wet at night .
&quot; I said , &quot; How can I take off my clothes , and put them on again ? How can I wash my feet , and defile them again ?
&quot; My good man stretched out his hand from the door , and I moved my heart because of him
&quot; I arise , and open the door to my righteous man ; and my hands have dropped the poison , and my fingers have dropped the poison on the bar .
I have opened the door to my good man , and he has turned away . My God was not forbearing when he spoke , and I sought him , and found him not ; and I called him , and he answered not .
And the watchmen of the city met me , and struck me , and injured me ; and the watchmen of the wall took away my shoulder
&quot; Women of Jerusalem , I command you , if you meet my good man , that you report to him , for I am sick in love
&quot; Your good man , the most beautiful of the women , how is he stronger than the good man of others ? How is he stronger than the good man of others ? Thus do you command us
My good man , white and red , is above all men .
His head is as pure gold , and his hair is as thick as a raven , and black as a crow
His eyes are like the eyes of a dove by the stream ; he washes them with milk , and is well rested .
His cheeks are like lawns of herbs , and his lips like lilies , and there is no medicine in them .
His hands are like pipes of gold , and his bodies like carved ivory , and his surroundings like blue stones .
His legs are as white pillars , and he sits on the throne of gold ; and his form is as Lebanon , and his beauty is as a cedar tree .
&quot; And his mouth is sweet , and he is lovely : O daughters of Jerusalem , this is my good man , and this is my friend
Where is your good man , the most beautiful of you , and where is your good man turned , that we may go with you to seek him
&quot; My good men have entered into their own gardens , and they have gone down to the flower beds , and they have kept sheep in the gardens , and they have taken hundreds of flowers .
&quot; I belong to my good man , and my good man also belongs to me ; and he shepherds his flock among the lilies .
My darling , you are as beautiful as Dess , as beautiful as Jerusalem , and as mighty as an army spreading a banner .
Turn away from me , and do not look at me ; for your eyes have troubled me : your hair is as a flock of sheep , and you lie by mount Gilead .
Thy teeth are cleansed like a flock of sheep , and every one of them hath twins , and none hath lost a son .
As a pomegranate are your two teeth in the palm tree
There are sixty queens and eighty concubines , and countless daughters
Only this is my dove , my perfect man , the only one born by his mother , the beloved of those who gave birth to him ; and when all the women saw him , they blessed him ; and when the concubines saw him , they praised him .
Who is it that looks outward like the morning light , beautiful as the moon , bright as the sun , mighty as the army of the banner ?
I went down to the Nutcracker to see the green plants in the valley , and to see the grapes without buds , and the pomegranates without flowers
Unconsciously , my heart has placed me in the car of my dignity
Come back , come back , O Shulammite , come back , come back , that we may see thee : why do ye see thee , O Shulammite , as the dance of Mahan ?
How beautiful are your feet , O Queen , in your shoes ! Your thighs are round , as a jewel ; They are created by the hand of a skillful craftsman .
Your belly is like a cup full of wine , and your waist is like a pile of wheat , and around it are lilies .
Your two breasts are like a pair of deer , the twins of mother deer .
Your neck is like a toothbrush ; your eyes like a pond by the gates of Shesh-ben-barthrah ; your nose like the tower of Lebanon to the great horse .
Your head is on you like Mount Carmel , and your hair on your head is purple and black ; and the king &apos;s heart is fastened by this hanging hair .
How beautiful and pleasurable are You , whom I love , that make people rejoice
Your body is like a palm tree , and your breasts are like the fruit of the tree above it .
&quot; I said , &apos; I will go up to the palm tree and take hold of its branches . May your breasts be as grapes , and the scent of your nose as apples .
&quot; Your mouth is full of good wine , &quot; she said , &quot; flowing into the mouth of the sleeping man for my good man .
I belong to my good man . He also loves me .
Come , my good man , and I will go to the fields , and I will lodge in the villages
We arise in the morning in the vineyard to see whether the grapes have bloomed or whether the pomegranates have buds . In it I will give you my love
The cigars are fragrant , and in our gates are all kinds of new and beautiful fruits ; and all these have I stored up for you , My good man .
Behold , thou art as my brother , and as a brother that eateth my mother &apos;s milk ; and when I meet thee from the outside , I will kiss thee ; and no man shall look me lightly .
&quot; I will guide you , and bring you into my mother &apos;s house , and I will teach you , and I will make you drink of the fragrance of pomegranates
His left hand will be under my head , and his right hand will hold me
I command you , O daughters of Jerusalem , not to be alarmed , nor to awaken my beloved , until he has sought it ; neither to awaken the cloud , nor to stir up love until he has sought it ;
&quot; Who is he who came from the wilderness , and leaned on the righteous ? I woke you under the apple tree , and your mother labored for you there , and those who raised you there labored for you
For love is strong as death , and jealousy as the wickedness of the shadow ; and the light that shineth is the light of the flame , the flame of the LORD .
Love cannot be swallowed up by the waters , nor by the floods ; and if a man take all the treasures of his house in exchange for love , he will be despised
&quot; We have a little sister whose breasts are not yet full , and how shall we deal with her in the day when she shall be brought forth as a kinsman
If he were a wall , We would build upon it a tower of silver ; and if he were a door , We would surround him with cedar boards .
I am a wall , and my breasts are like the buildings above it ; and I was in his eyes as a man of peace
