&quot; My own vineyard is before me ; Thou , Solomon , art one thousand shekels to thee , and two hundred shekels to the keepers of the fruit
&quot; Your companions who dwell in the garden will listen to your voice , and you will make me hear .
&quot; Come quickly , my good man , like an antelope or a deer on a mountain of herbs
In the days of Uzziah , and of Jotham , and of Ahaz , and of Hezekiah king of Judah , Isaiah the son of Amos murmured concerning Judah and Jerusalem
&quot; Listen , O earth , and listen to your ears , for the Lord says , &apos; I raise up children and raise them up , and they are rebellious against me
The cattle know their masters , and the donkeys know their masters ; but Israel does not know , and my people do not take heed .
The people of iniquity , the people of iniquity , the children of wickedness , the children of corruption ; they have forsaken the Lord , they have despised the Holy One of Israel , they have strayed from Him , they have gone backward .
For what have you been rebellious many times , and are you to be punished ?
From the palm of the foot to the head , there is none that is complete : all wounds , and swollenness , and new wounds ; neither hath there been any opening , nor wrapping , nor oiling .
Your land is desolate ; your cities are burned with fire ; and your fields are desolate , as they have been swallowed up before you by strangers , and as they have been overthrown by strangers .
Only Zion remains , as the vineyards of grapes , and the barns of fields , and the cities of the besieged .
&quot; If it were not for the Lord of hosts who had left us a little seed , we would have been as Sodom and Moor before
&quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , O governor of Sodom , and listen to the counsel of our God , O people of Moor .
&quot; What good is it to me , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; for the many sacrifices you have offered , the burnt offering of sheep , and the fat of fat animals , for I have passed through , and the blood of cattle , and the blood of lambs , and the blood of goats , and I am not pleased
&quot; When you come to me , who will ask you for this and trample on My house ?
Do not offer any more vain offerings ; for I hate the fragrances ; and I hate the moon and the sabbath and the assembly that calls , and I am not able to tolerate sin and solemnity .
&quot; I hate your months and your festivals in my heart , and I am troubled , and I am not patient in my duty .
When you raise your hands to pray , I will not be able to see ; but when you pray a lot , I will not be able to hear ; and your hands are full of the blood of murderers .
You shall wash yourselves and be clean , and remove your evil deeds from before me , and cease from doing evil .
To seek justice , to rescue the oppressed , to redress the orphans , and to bow down to the widow
&quot; Come , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; and we will debate with one another , and your sins will be turned into snow and white , and red as tan , and white as wool .
&quot; If you are willing to obey , you will eat the good things of the earth
&quot; If you do not obey , you will be destroyed by the sword , &quot; says the Lord
A city of faithfulness is turned into a prostitute , where justice and righteousness dwelled , and where murderers dwell now .
&quot; Your silver will become dust ; Your wine will be mixed with water .
Your officers are rebellious , accompanied by thieves . They all love bribery and seek their own private life . They do not avenge the orphans and widows , nor do they bring their case before them .
Therefore thus said the Lord , the Lord of hosts , the Almighty of Israel , Behold , I will make snow upon my face , and I will bring vengeance upon my enemies
&quot; I will turn my back on you , and I will purify your debris , and I will cleanse your filth .
And I will restore your judges as at the beginning , and your counselors as at the beginning , and you will call them cities of righteousness and cities of faithfulness .
Zion shall be redeemed for righteousness ; the righteous among them shall be redeemed for righteousness
But the transgressors and the sinners shall perish together , and those who forsake the Lord shall be destroyed .
&quot; They will be ashamed of the oak that you love , and you will be ashamed of the garden that you choose
For you shall be as a barren oak with leaves , as a garden without water .
