Then he will say with a loud voice , &quot; I am not a physician for you , because I have no food or clothing in my house , and you shall not make me a ruler over the people .
Jerusalem is fallen , and Judah is fallen : for their tongues and their deeds are against the LORD , and their eyes of glory are drawn to him .
Their faces bear witness of their iniquity , and they confess their sins without concealment , as in the case of Todomah : woe unto them , because they have committed evil .
&quot; You shall say to the righteous , &apos; He will be happy , because he will eat the fruit of his deeds . &apos; 
