The children of Aram to the east , and the Philistines to the west ; and they opened their mouths to eat Israel : yet the wrath of the Lord is not turned away , and his hand is not stretched out .
The people have not returned to fight against their Lord , nor have they sought the Lord of hosts .
Therefore the Lord will cut off the head and the tail , the palm tree and the reed from Israel in one day .
The elders and the nobles are the heads ; and the prophet who teaches lies is the tail .
For He has led this people astray , and those who are guided shall perish .
Therefore the Lord will not rejoice in their young men , nor will he have mercy on their orphans and widows ; for they are blasphemers and wicked , and their mouths speak foolishly ; yet the wrath of the Lord is not turned away , and his hands are not stretched out .
Evil is like the burning of fire , and the burning of thorns and resin ; and when it rises up in the dense forest , it becomes a pillar of smoke , and it rotates .
For the fierce anger of the Lord of hosts has consumed the earth , and the people have become firewood , and no man has pity on his brethren .
And on the right hand there is a man who plundereth , and yet is hungry ; and on the left hand there is a man who devoureth , and yet is not full ; and every man eateth the flesh of his own arm .
And Manasseh swallowed up Ephraim , and Ephraim swallowed up Manasseh , and they attacked Judah together : yet the wrath of the LORD was not turned away , neither was his hand stretched out .
Woe to those who set up the law of iniquity , and record the judgments of treachery !
For the cause of the needy , and the cause of the needy among my people , to take away the widow as a captive , and the orphan as a prey
&quot; In the day of vengeance , when evil shall come from afar , how will you do ? To whom will you flee to seek salvation ? Where will your glory remain ?
But they shall submit themselves under the captive , and under the slain : yet the wrath of the LORD is not turned away , neither is his hand stretched out .
&quot; Assyria is the stick of my anger , and the rod of my wrath in my hand
&quot; I will send him to attack the people who are blasphemed , and I will command him to attack the people who are angry with me , and to plunder their wealth , and to plunder their goods , and to trample them like the mud of the streets
