&quot; This is what the Lord of hosts has commanded , that he may defile the glory of every noble person , and that he may despise all the nobles of the earth .
&quot; O people whom He has given , the land of yours will be as the Nile , and there will be no waistband upon you .
The Lord has stretched out His hand toward the sea , and shaken the nations ; and as for Canaan , He has commanded to destroy its security .
Then he said , &quot; You inhabitants of Sidon , who are oppressed , you shall no longer rejoice . Arise , and go to Keddi , where you shall not rest .
Behold , the land of the Chaldeans was without them ; and the land was established by the Assyrians for the inhabitants of the wilderness ; and now they have built forts , and have destroyed the palaces of Tyre , and have made it desolate
And all the ships that He hath given shall mourn ; for your protection is turned into a wilderness .
In that day shall Tyre be forgotten for seventy years in the days of a king ; and after seventy years shall the sight of Tyre be like a song sung by a prostitute .
You , the forgotten prostitute , who plays the harp in the city , and sings many songs , and makes people forget you .
After seventy years , the Lord will look at Tyre as soon as possible , and he will still receive interest in the bargain with all the nations of the earth .
His goods and his interest shall be holy to the Lord , and shall not be stored up ; for his goods shall be for those who dwell in the presence of the Lord , that they may eat and be clothed with enduring clothing .
&quot; Behold , the Lord has made the land void and desolate , and turned it around , and dispersed its inhabitants .
Then how was the people , and the priest , and the servant , and the master , and the maid , and the mother , and the buyer , and the seller , and the lender , and the borrower , and the profiter , and the profiter ?
&quot; The land will be emptied and desolate , &quot; says the Lord
Woe to the earth ! Woe to the world ! Woe to the high places !
The land is defiled by the inhabitants thereof , because they have transgressed the law , and have abolished the law , and have transgressed the covenant of the everlasting .
Therefore the earth is cursed , and those who dwell therein are guilty ; and the inhabitants of the earth are burned with fire , and few are left .
The new wine grieves , the vines are decayed , the hearts rejoice , all sigh
The music of drumming ceased , the music of the banquet ceased , and the music of the violin ceased .
A man shall not drink wine and sing ; and he that drinketh of it shall suffer .
The desolate city is demolished , and the houses are shut , and no man can enter
There are voices of mourning in the streets for wine ; all joy is turned to darkness ; the joy of the earth is turned to nothing .
There is nothing in the city but desolation , and the gates of the city are destroyed
&quot; There will be no remnant of all the people of the earth like an olive tree that has been beaten , or like a grape that has been harvested .
And they shall give a loud cry , and they shall lift up their voice from the sea for the glory of the Lord
Therefore you shall glorify the Lord in the east , and the name of the Lord God of Israel in all the islands of the sea
We have heard from the earth singing , saying , &quot; The glory belongs to the righteous , &quot; but I said , &quot; I am extinct , I am extinct , and I am in trouble , for the deceitful deceit , the great deceitful deceit . &quot;
O inhabitants of the earth , fear , pits and snares are near to you .
He that escapeth the voice of terror shall fall into the pit ; and he that cometh out of the pit shall be entangled with nets : for the windows of heaven are opened , and the foundations of the earth shaken .
The earth was completely destroyed , all collapsed , and tremors were great
The earth will turn eastward and westward like a drunken man , and shake and shake like a bed ; and the sin is heavy upon it , and it will surely fall , and it will not be restored .
&quot; In that day the Lord will punish the armies of the high places , and the kings of the earth on the earth
&quot; They shall be gathered together as prisoners gathered together in prison , and they shall be imprisoned in prison , and after a number of days shall they be condemned .
In that day the moon shall be ashamed , and the sun ashamed : for the Lord of hosts shall reign in mount Zion , and in Jerusalem ; and glory shall be in the sight of his elders who fear him
O LORD , thou art my God , and I will honour thee , and I will praise thy name : for thou hast done wonderful things in faithfulness , and hast fulfilled that which thou hadst promised in the old days .
Thou hast made the city a desolation , and the strong city a desolation , and the palaces of the Gentiles a city no more , and no more built .
Therefore the mighty shall glorify thee , and the cities of the mighty shall fear thee .
For in the time when the mighty oppress them , as a storm blows against the walls , you will be a refuge for the poor , a refuge for the needy in distress , a place of refuge from the storm , and a cooling from the heat .
Thou shalt suppress the noise of strangers , as if the hot air of a dry place descended , and the cry of a mighty man were forbidden , as if the hot air were swallowed up by a cloud
&quot; The Lord of hosts will set up a feast on this mountain for the people with sweetness , with wine , and with sweetness full of marrow , and with clear wine ,
&quot; He will also destroy on this mountain all that covers all people , and all that covers the faces of all nations .
