&quot; In that day they will say , &apos; Behold , this is our God ; we have been waiting for him , and he will save us ; this is the Lord ; we have been waiting for him , and we will rejoice in his salvation .
&quot; The hand of the Lord will be upon this mountain , and the land of Moab will be trampled upon as the grass of a dung pot .
He will stretch out his hand in it , as the stretching out of the hand of a water , but the Lord will bring down his pride and the deceit of his hands .
&quot; The LORD has cast down the high places of your city , and has made them dust .
&quot; In that day the people of Judah will sing this song , saying , &apos; We have a strong city , &apos; and the Lord will make salvation a wall and a fortress
Open the gates of the city , so that the faithful may enter
&quot; He who relies on You with all his heart , You will keep him safe , for he relies on You
Rely on the Lord for ever and ever : for the Lord is a rock for ever and ever .
He has destroyed the high places , He has destroyed the high cities , He has torn them down , He has torn them straight to dust
To be trampled is the feet of the needy , and the feet of the poor .
The way of the righteous is upright : for thou , Lord of uprightness , hast made the way of the just .
&quot; Lord , we wait for you in the way of your judgment ; and what we envy in our hearts is your name , the name of your memory .
At night I envy thee in my heart , and my spirit seeketh thee : for the inhabitants of the earth shall learn righteousness when thou judgest in the world .
He does not learn righteousness by grace to the wicked , and he will act unjustly in the land of righteousness , and he will not be attentive to the majesty of the Lord
&quot; Your hands are lifted up , O Lord ; yet they do not see ; but they see your enthusiasm for the people , and they are ashamed of you ; and the fire burns your enemies .
&quot; You will send us into peace , O Lord ; for all that we have done You have accomplished for us .
&quot; O Lord , God of ours , there have been other appointed over us besides You , but we will rely exclusively on You , and call Your name .
When they die , they will not be able to live ; when they die , they will not be able to rise again ; for you have punished them , and destroyed them , and their name will be utterly destroyed .
Thou hast multiplied thy people , O LORD , Thou hast multiplied thy people : thou hast obtained glory , and hast multiplied thy borders .
&quot; Lord , they seek You in distress ; Your punishment comes upon them , and they pray to You with all their heart and with all their courage .
&quot; As a woman conceives , and in pain she bears , and in pain she cries , &apos; Lord , we are before you
We have been pregnant with pain , and what we have delivered is like the wind , and we have not done any salvation on the earth , nor have the inhabitants of the world fallen .
The dead shall be raised up , and the dead shall rise up , and the dead shall sing , O sleeper in the dust : for thy sweetness is as the sweetness of herbs and herbs ; and the earth shall deliver the dead .
&quot; O my people , come into the inner chamber , and shut the doors , and hide yourselves for a while , until the wrath has passed .
For the LORD is come out of his dwelling place to punish the iniquity of the inhabitants of the earth ; and the land shall reveal its blood , and shall no more cover the slain .
&quot; In that day , the Lord will punish the crocodile , the snake that walks , and the crocodile , the snake that walks , with His mighty sword , and the great fish of the sea ,
&quot; In that day there will be a vineyard with wine , and you will sing to it , saying ,
