&quot; In it the Lord will be glorified with us as a vast river , and there will not come to it a ship with an oar and a roar , nor a ship with a mighty arm .
&quot; For the Lord is our Judge , and the Lord has made law for us ; and the Lord is our King , and he will save us .
&quot; Your ropes are loose , and you can &apos;t plant a strong mast , and you can &apos;t raise up a tent . Many of the captives were divided , and the lame took away the captives .
&quot; The inhabitants of the city will not say , &apos; I am sick , &apos; and the people who dwell therein will be forgiven for their sins .
O nations , listen closely ; O people , listen attentively ; the earth and all that is full thereof , and the world and all that comes out of it ,
For the LORD is wroth with all the nations , and with all their hosts , and hath destroyed them , and delivered them into slaughter
The slain shall surely be abandoned , and the bodies of the dead shall melt , and the mountains shall be melted with their blood .
All the images of the heavens shall perish , and the heavens shall be rolled up as a book , and all the images thereof shall be desolate , as the leaves of a vine , and as the leaves of a fruitless tree .
&quot; For my sword is drunk in heaven , and it shall come to Edom and to the people whom I have cursed , to execute judgment .
And the sword of the LORD was full of blood , and filled with fat , and with the blood of lambs and goats , and with the fat of the waist of sheep : for the LORD did a great slaughter in the land of Edom , when he offered a sacrifice in Bozrah .
&quot; The cattle , and the calves , and the bulls shall come down together ; their land shall be drunk with blood , and their dust shall be defiled with fat .
For the LORD hath a day of vengeance , and a year of recompense for the argument of Zion .
The waters of the east shall be turned into oil , the dust into sulfur , and the soil into burning oil
Day and night shall not be extinguished , and smoke shall be poured out for ever ; and generations shall be desolate , and no man shall pass by them for ever .
&quot; But the pelicans and the swine of the arrows shall be their livelihoods , and the eagle and the crow shall dwell among them ; and the LORD will draw upon them an empty cord , and a chaotic cord ,
And the Edomites will call nobles to rule over the land , but none of them will rule over it ; neither will the chiefs rule over it .
And the palace of the east shall be of thorns , and of saplings and of thorns ; and it shall be a dwelling place for the wild dogs , and a dwelling place for the ostrich .
The beasts of the wilderness shall meet the wolves ; the sheep of the field shall call with them ; and the monsters of the night shall dwell therein , seeking rest .
And the arrows and snakes shall lodge therein , and they shall lay down their eggs , and they shall lay down their eggs , and their offspring , and their offspring shall be gathered under its shadow , and the eagle and the dove shall be gathered therein together .
&quot; You shall examine and read the book of the Lord , which is not lacking , neither has it any companion ; for my mouth has commanded , and his Spirit has gathered them together .
&quot; And He will give them lots for their gain , and He will give them their land by hand and by rope ; and they shall live therein for ever , generation after generation .
The wilderness and the dry land shall rejoice , and the desert shall rejoice , and the flower of the roses shall bloom
And they shall blossom , and rejoice , and rejoice ; and they shall give him the glory of Lebanon , and the glory of Carmel and Sharon ; and they shall see the glory of the LORD , the glory of our God .
You shall make the weak hand strong , and the weak knee firm .
Say to those who are afraid , &quot; Be strong , and do not be afraid ; for your God will come to recompense you , to do a great recompense , and he will save you .
Then the eyes of the blind shall be opened , and the ears of the deaf shall be opened .
In that day the lame will leap like a deer , and the dumb tongue will sing ; waters will be poured out in the wilderness , and rivers will flow in the desert .
The sand that shines shall become a pond , a dry land , and a spring ; and there shall be grass , reeds , and pomegranates in the place where the dogs lie down
In it will be a road called the Holy Way , which the unclean shall not pass through ; it will be for the redemption of the people ; and the man who walks will not be lost , though he be foolish .
There shall be no lion therein , and no beast shall ascend therein , nor shall they be seen therein ; only the redeemer shall walk therein .
And the people that the LORD redeems shall return , and sing to Zion ; and everlasting joy shall be upon their heads ; and they shall flee with joy and gladness , and with sighs of sorrow .
In the fourteenth year of king Hezekiah , Nebuchadnezzar king of Assyria came and struck all the strong cities of Judah , and took them
And the king of Assyria sent Rabshakeh the captain of the host from Lachish to Jerusalem unto the king of Hezekiah ; and he stood by the fountain of the upper pond in the great way of the dust
Then the house of the sons of Hilkiah took Elijah , and Shebna the scribe , and Joah the son of Asa the scribe , and went out to Rabshakeh
Then Rabshakeh said to them , Go and tell the house of Hezekiah , Thus saith the king of Assyria , What is it that ye trust in ?
You say , &quot; You have the means and the power to fight . I do not see it as a lie . Whom do you rely on to betray me ? &quot;
&quot; Behold , the land of Egypt on which you rely is a reed rod that is crushed ; and if any man leans on it , it will pierce his hand ; and so Pharaoh the king of Egypt did to all who leaned on him
&quot; If you say to me , &apos; We rely on the Lord our God , &apos; aren &apos;t the house of Hezekiah the one who has destroyed the high places of God and the altar , and said to the people of Judah and Jerusalem , &apos; Will you worship before this altar ? &apos;
&quot; Behold , I have given thee two thousand horses , when thou hast given them to my lord , King Assyria ; and behold , there is a man riding on this side of thee
&quot; If not , how can you defeat the least of my lord &apos;s servants ? Why do you rely on the horsemen of Egypt ?
&quot; Isn &apos;t it the Lord &apos;s will that you come up against me to destroy the land ? The Lord said to me , &quot; Go up and destroy the land
Then Elijah , and Shebna , and Joah , said to Rabshakeh , &quot; Speak in the language of Aram , and in the language of the servants ; for we know that we shall not speak in the language of Judah , and that we shall not speak in the ears of the hundreds of the people of the city
Then Rabshakeh said , &quot; Has my Lord sent me to speak these words to you and to your Lord alone , or to those who sit in the city and eat their own dung and drink their own urine with you ?
Then Rabshakeh stood up and cried with a loud voice in the language of Judah , saying , &quot; Listen to the words of King Assyria
Thus said the king , &quot; You shall not be deceived by the house of Hezekiah , for he cannot save you .
&quot; Don &apos;t listen to the house of Hezekiah , who says to you , &apos; The Lord must save us , and this city will not be given to the king of Assyria
&quot; Do not listen to the words of the house of Hezekiah , for this is what the king of Assyria said : &apos; You shall come out with me and surrender to me , and each of you shall eat his own grape tree , and the fruit of his own trees , and drink his own water in the wells
&quot; Behold , I will bring you to a place like your own land , a land of five valleys and new wines , a land of food and vineyards
&quot; Beware , lest the house of Hezekiah persuade you , saying , &apos; The Lord will save us ; has the God of the nations a savior out of the hand of the king of Assyria ?
Behold , the God of Hama and Arbor , and the God of Zephaniah , have they delivered Samaria out of my hand ?
&quot; The God of these nations , who has saved his own country from my hand ? Can the Lord save Jerusalem from my hand ?
&quot; The people did not speak silently nor answer a word , because the king had commanded them not to answer him
Now the house of the sons of Hezekiah , the slayer of Elijah , and Shebna the scribe , and Joah the son of Asa the scribe , torn their clothes , and came to the house of Hezekiah , and told him the words of Rabshakeh .
And when the king of Hezekiah heard it , he rent his clothes and put on linen , and entered into the house of the Lord
And Elijah the governor of the house , and Shebanah the scribe , and the elders of the priests , were clothed in linen , to see Isaiah the prophet , the son of Amos
And he said unto him , Thus saith the house of Hezekiah ; Today is a day of trouble , and of punishment , and of humiliation , as a woman shall bear a child , but shall not be able to bear .
Or , &quot; When the Lord your God hears the words of Rabshakeh , the king of Assyria , his master , which he sent to reproach the God of everlasting life , the Lord your God hears and reproaches him ; therefore pray with a loud voice for the remnant of the people ,
And the servants of the king of Hezekiah went to see Isaiah
Then Isaiah said to them , &quot; Tell your master , Thus says the Lord : &apos; When you have heard the servants of king Assyria blaspheme me , do not be afraid
&quot; I will shake his heart , and he will return to his place when he hears the wind , and I will put him under the sword in it
Then Rabshakeh returned , and found king Assyria fighting against Rena : for he had heard earlier that king Assyria had withdrawn from Ragi
And when the king of Assyria heard that Zechariah the king of Antioch said , He is come out to fight with thee , he sent messengers to the house of Hezekiah , and commanded them , saying ,
&quot; You have said to Hezekiah king of Judah , &apos; Do not listen to the God in whom you rely to deceive you , saying , &apos; Jerusalem will not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria
&quot; You have heard all the times that the kings of Assyria have done to the nations : they have destroyed them . Can you save them ?
&quot; The people of Gathshan , Haran , and Lichr , and the children of Eden of Tyre , whom my fathers destroyed . What God saved them ?
Wherein were the kings of Hama , the kings of Arbor , the kings of the city of Siphah-wan , and the kings of Shenah and Ewa ?
And when Hezekiah had received the letter from the messenger , and had finished it , he went up into the house of the Lord , and opened it before the Lord
The house of Hezekiah prayed to the Lord
&quot; Seat on the throne of the Lord , the God of Israel , the Almighty . You alone are the God of all the kingdoms of the earth . You created the heavens and the earth
&quot; Listen , O Lord , and open your eyes , O Lord , and listen to all the words of Sinai , who sent an apostle to blaspheme the Everlasting God
Indeed , O Lord , the kings of Assyria have made the nations and the land of the nations desolate
&quot; Throw all the images of the gods of the nations into the fire ; for he is not God , but a man made of wood and stone ; therefore destroy him
&quot; Lord , our God , behold , I ask you to deliver us from the hand of the king of Assyria , that all the nations of the earth may know that you are the Lord .
Then Isaiah the son of Amos sent messengers to Hezekiah , saying , Thus saith the Lord God of Israel , Since you have asked me to smite Sinai king of Assyria
Therefore thus says the Lord concerning him , &quot; The virgins of Zion have despised you , they have mocked you , and the women of Jerusalem have shaken their heads at you
Who do you blaspheme , who do you blaspheme , who do you raise your voice , who do you lift up your eyes to attack , the Holy One of Israel ?
&quot; You have insulted the Lord through your servants , saying , &apos; I have commanded many chariots to the tops of the mountains to the depths of Lebanon , and I will cut down the tall cedar trees and the beautiful pine trees thereof ; I will go up to the very high places and enter the forests of the fields .
I have dug wells to drink water , and I will sow all the rivers of Egypt with my feet .
&quot; Have you not heard what I have done in the ancient days ? With you I have made the strong city desolate , and turned it into a pile of dust
Therefore the inhabitants thereof are weak and ashamed , and they are as the grass of the field , and as the herbs of the field , and as the grass of the roof of the house , and as the weeds of the field that have not grown
&quot; You sit down , You go out , You come in , You are angry with me , I know it
&quot; Because of your wrath on me , and because of your arrogance in my ears , I will hook your nose with hooks , and put a chewing ring in your mouth , that you may return from the way of old .
&quot; O Israel , I have given you proof that you will eat of your own flesh this year , and that you will eat of your own fruit next year ; and in the years to come you will sow and reap and plant vineyards and eat of their fruit
The remnant of Judah , who escaped , will still be rooted downwards , and will come upwards .
And the remnant of the people shall come forth from Jerusalem , and the escaped from mount Zion ; and the wrath of the Lord of hosts shall accomplish it .
Therefore thus says the Lord concerning the king of Assyria , &quot; He shall not come to this city , nor shoot at it , nor take a shield before it , nor build a stronghold against it
&quot; He will come from that way , and he will return from that way , and he will not come to this city , &quot; says the Lord
For my own sake , and for the sake of my servant David , I will save this city
And the angel of the LORD went out , and slew in the camp of Assyria eighteen thousand and five thousand ; and when a man came up early in the morning , he saw that they were all dead bodies
Then Nebuchadnezzar king of Assyria took up his camp , and lived in Nineveh
And it came to pass on that day , when he worshipped in the temple of his God , which was in Nisloh , that his sons Admiel and Saleh slew him with the sword , and fled into the land of Ararat , and Isaac his son reigned in his stead .
And it came to pass at that time , when the house of Hezekiah was sick to death , that Isaiah the prophet , the son of Amos , came to meet him , and said to him , Thus saith the Lord ; Leave thy life with thy house , for thou shalt die and not live
Then the house of Hezekiah turned their faces to the wall , and prayed to the Lord , saying ,
Remember , O LORD , how I have kept my whole heart before thee , and have walked in truth , and have done that which is good in thy sight : and the house of Hezekiah wept bitterly .
And the word of the LORD came to Isaiah , saying ,
&quot; Go and tell the house of Hezekiah , &apos; Thus says the Lord , the God of your father David , &apos; I have heard your prayers , I have seen your tears , and I will increase your life by fifteen years
&quot; I will save you and this city from the hand of the king of Assyria , and I will protect it .
&quot; Behold , I , the Lord , will accomplish what I have said ; I have given you a sign beforehand
And the shadow that went forward turned back ten degrees , and the shadow that went forward turned back ten degrees on the dial .
And when Hezekiah king of Judah was healed from his sickness , he began to recite a poem
&quot; I said , &apos; In the day of my middle age I will enter the gates of the shadow , and I will not enjoy the rest of my years .
I said , &quot; I will not see the Lord , nor the Lord in the land of the living , nor will I see the inhabitants of the world any more .
&quot; My dwelling place has been moved away from me like the tent of the shepherd ; I will roll up my life like the roll of a cloth ; the Lord will cut me off from the head of the machine , from morning to evening , and he will finish me .
I have made myself at ease to the dawn ; He has broken all my bones like a lion ; He will finish me from morning until evening .
&quot; I am as a swallow who murmurs , and as a white crane who cries , and as a dove who mourns ; I am weary of my eyes , and of my gaze ; O Lord , I am oppressed , and seek Your protection for me
&quot; What shall I say ? He has fulfilled what He has promised me , and I will walk quietly through the years of my life , because of the pain of my heart .
For this is the purpose of man &apos;s life , O Lord ; and my spirit is here , and all things are here ; therefore make me to heal , and remain alive .
Behold , I have suffered greatly , and you have given me peace ; and you have delivered me from the pit of desolation by your love for my soul ; for you have thrown all my sins behind your backs .
&quot; The shadows will not thank you , death will not praise you , and the people of the pit will not hope for your truth .
Only the living will give thanks to You , just as I give thanks to You today ; and the Father will make known Your truth to His children .
&quot; The Lord will save me , and we will live forever in the house of the Lord with stringed instruments , singing my songs
Then Isaiah said , &quot; When you take a piece of unleavened bread and put it on the wound , the king will be healed
Then said the house of Hezekiah , What signs do I have that I may go up into the house of the Lord ?
And it came to pass at that time , when Mirada Baradan the son of Baradan king of Babylon heard that Hezekiah was sick and was healed , that he sent letters and presents to him
And the house of Hezekiah rejoiced at the messenger , and showed them the gold , and the silver , and the spices , and the precious oil of his treasure , and all the weapons of his army , and all the treasures of his riches ; and there was not a thing that the house of Hezekiah did not show them , neither in his house , nor in the land .
Then the prophet Isaiah came to the king of Hezekiah , and said to him , &quot; What are these men saying ? They came to see you from there ; and Hezekiah said , &quot; They came to see me from Babylon far away
And Isaiah said , What have they seen in your house ? And the house of Hezekiah said , They have seen all that is in my house , and there is none of my treasure that I do not show them .
Then Isaiah said to the house of Hezekiah , &quot; Listen to the word of the Lord of hosts .
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and all that is in your house , and all that your fathers have stored up to this day , will be taken captive to Babylon without a trace , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; And of the children of yourselves who are born , there will be some who will be taken captive and imprisoned in the palace of Babylon .
And Hezekiah said unto Isaiah , Good is the word which thou hast spoken unto the LORD : for in my days there shall be a very peaceful and steady state
&quot; You shall comfort my people , &quot; says your God .
&quot; And I will speak comforting words to Jerusalem , and proclaim to her , &apos; The days of her battle are fulfilled , and her iniquity is forgiven , and all her sins are doubled in the Lord &apos;s hand .
&quot; There is a voice crying out , &apos; Prepare the way of the Lord in the wilderness , &apos; or &apos; Prepare the way of the Lord in the wilderness , &apos; to repair the way of our God in the desert .
All the lowlands shall be filled , and the mountains of great and small shall be cut down , and the high and low shall be made flat , and the rough shall be made plain .
&quot; The glory of the Lord will surely be revealed , and everyone with blood will see it together ; for this is the word of the Lord spoken by mouth .
And one said , What am I crying for ? And one said , Whosoever hath blood is as the grass , and his beauty as the flowers of the field
The grass will dry up , and the flowers will fade away ; for the Spirit of the Lord is blowing on it ; and the people are indeed grasses .
The grass will dry up , and the flowers will fade away ; but the word of our God will be established for ever .
&quot; Give good tidings to Zion , that you may go up to the mountains ; and give good tidings to Jerusalem , that you may speak with a loud voice , and fear not ; and say to the cities of Judah , &apos; Look , your God !
&quot; The Lord Yahweh will come like a mighty man , and his arm will be in his hand ; his reward is with him , and his recompense before him .
&quot; He will be like a shepherd who feeds his flock , and gathers the lambs with his arms in his arms , and guides the lambs slowly .
Who has measured the waters with his hand , and the heavens with his mouth , and the dust with his great spear , and the mountains with his scales , and the hills with his mountains ?
Who has measured the heart of the Lord , or who has instructed the Spirit of the Lord , or who has instructed His counselors ?
Who will negotiate with him , who will teach him , who will guide him to the way of justice , and who will teach him knowledge , and who will teach him the way of guidance ?
Behold , the people are like a drop of water , and like dust on the horizon : He raises up the islands of the sea as a small thing .
&quot; The forests of Lebanon shall not be burned as wood , nor the beasts thereof as burnt offerings .
For all the people are as nothing before him , and he is seen not as nothing , but as nothing
Who do you compare with God in any form ?
The idol is made by the craftsman , and the silversmith wraps it with gold , and casts chains of silver for him .
&quot; The poor who cannot afford such a provision chooses trees that will not decay , and seeks craftsmen for himself , and sets up idols that will not shake .
Have you not known ? Have you not heard ? Have you not been told from the beginning ? Have you not understood from the foundation of the earth ?
God sits on the earth as a locust ; He spreads out the heavens as a mantle , and spreads out the heavens as a tent for dwelling .
He made the king void , and made the judges of the earth void
They have been planted , and they have been planted , and the roots have been planted in the ground ; and as soon as he blows on them , they are dried up , and the wind blows them away like straw .
&quot; The Holy One said , &quot; Who do you consider equal to me , that he may be equal to me ?
Lift up your eyes , and see who created all these angels , and brought them forth by number , and called them by their names ; and not one is lacking in His power , nor in His mighty power .
Why sayest thou , O Jacob , that my way is hidden from the LORD , and why sayest thou , O Israel , that my God is unjust and unquestionable ?
Knowest thou not , or hearest thou not , that the Lord God , the everlasting God , the Lord of the heavens and the earth , is neither weary nor weary , and his wisdom cannot be measured ?
He gives strength to the weak , and strength to the weak .
&quot; The youth will be weary and weary , and the strong will fall completely .
&quot; But those who wait for the Lord will be strengthened from the beginning , and they will rise up like an eagle , and they will run without fatigue , and they will walk without fatigue .
O islands of the sea , when they are silent before me , and when the people are newly strengthened , that they may speak , and we may debate among ourselves ;
Who hath risen up from the east , and called him by righteousness to his feet ; and the LORD hath given him the kingdoms , and he hath given him kings over them ; and he hath given them as a sword unto him , and as a bow unto him as a straw blown by the wind
He pursues them , and walks in the way He has not walked , and walks openly .
&quot; I am the Lord , who created this thing , and has called it from the beginning for generations ; I am the first , and I am with the last
The islands were afraid when they saw it , and the earth trembled , and came near
Each of them helped his neighbor , and each of them said to his brothers , &quot; Be courageous
The woodworker exhorts the silverworker , and the hammer that lights exhorts the cutting-edge , and the welder says , &quot; It is well welded , and firmly nailed with a nail , lest an idol shake . &quot;
&quot; But you , Israel , my servant , my chosen Jacob , my friend Abraham &apos;s seed ,
&quot; You are the one whom I have taken from the poles of the earth , and called from the corners of the earth , and said to you , &apos; You are my servant ; I have chosen you , and I have not forsaken you .
Fear not , for I am with thee ; fear not , for I am thy God ; I will strengthen thee , I will help thee , I will strengthen thee with my right hand of righteousness .
&quot; Whoever is angry with you will be ashamed ; and whoever fights with you will be like nothing , and will perish .
Whoever fights with you , you will not find them ; and whoever fights with you , he will be like nothing , and become nothing .
&quot; For I , the Lord , your God , will help your right hand and say to you , &apos; Don &apos;t be afraid ; I will help you
&quot; Don &apos;t be afraid , you worm Jacob , and you Israel , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; I will help you , and your Redeemer , the Holy One of Israel ,
&quot; Behold , I have made you a new vessel for feeding with quick teeth ; you shall break down the mountains , and make the hills like a branch .
You will blow him away with a gust of wind , and the wind will blow him away , and you will rejoice in the Lord , and exalt the Holy One of Israel .
&quot; The poor and needy seek water , but it is not available ; they are thirsty and their tongues are dry . My Lord will answer them , and my God of Israel will not forsake them .
I will make rivers in the high places of pure light , and springs in the valleys ; I will make the desert a pool of water , and the dry land a spring .
I will plant in the wilderness cedar trees , saplings , pomegranates , and wild olives ; and in the desert I will plant pine trees , cedar trees , and pine trees
&quot; This is the work of the hands of the Lord , and the work of the Holy One of Israel , that they may see and know and think and understand
&quot; The Lord said to the false gods , &apos; You will present your case , &apos; said the king of Jacob , &apos; and you will declare your true reasons .
to declare , to indicate to us what is to be done in the future , what the former is , to make us ponder , to know the end of things , or to communicate to us the future
&quot; That we may know that you are God , and that we may be astonished when we look at you , whether for good or for evil ,
Behold , you belong to nothingness , and your deeds to nothingness ; and your choice is abominable .
&quot; I have raised up from the north a man who asks for my name from the land of the sun , and he will come to the throne as if he were ashes , as if he were a carpenter throwing mud .
Who has revealed this from the beginning , that we may know it ? Who has revealed it before , that we may say that he is right ? Who has not revealed it , who has not explained it ? Who has not heard your words ?
And I said unto Zion first , Behold , I will give unto Jerusalem a message of good news
When I looked , there was no man , and when I asked , there was no chief among them , to answer
Behold , they and their works are empty and void ; and the idols which they have cast are all winds and are all void .
&quot; Behold , my servant , whom I have supported , whom I have chosen , and whom I have pleased in my heart , I have given him my Spirit , and he will preach righteousness to the nations
He does not shout , nor make noise , nor make his voice heard in the streets
He breaketh not the reeds that are afflicted , He breaketh not the flames that are left , He extinguisheth not the fires that are left , He exalteth righteousness by truth .
He is not despairing , nor despairing , but he is directed to establish righteousness on earth ; and the islands await His instruction .
&quot; Thus says the Lord God , who created the heavens , who spread out the heavens , who joined the earth with the earth , and breathed into all the people of the earth , and gave the Spirit to those who are on it ,
I the LORD will call thee by righteousness , and I will strengthen thy hand , and keep thee , and make thee a watchman of the people , and a light of the Gentiles
He who opens the eyes of the blind , He who leads the captive out of prison , He who leads the seated in darkness out of prison .
&quot; I am the Lord , and this is my name ; I will not give my glory to false gods , nor my praise to idols that are engraved
Behold , the former things have been accomplished ; now I will make known to you the new things , which were not made before , but I will tell you
All those who sail , and all the islands of the sea , and all the inhabitants thereof , sing to the Lord a new song , and praise Him from the earth
The wilderness and the cities thereof , and the villages of the Kidianites , were lifted up , and the inhabitants of Shelah shouted on the top of the mountains .
&quot; When they give glory to the Lord , they proclaim His praise on the islands of the sea
&quot; The Lord will go forth like a warrior , and like a warrior with an enthusiasm ; He will cry out , He will shout out , He will strike the enemy with a mighty sword
&quot; For a long time I have shut my mouth , I have not spoken , I have not spoken ; now I will cry like a woman in labor , I will weep in anguish .
I will make the mountains and the valleys a desolation , and the plants on them dry up ; I will make the rivers an island , and the ponds dry up .
I will lead the blind to the way they do not know , and guide them to the way they do not know ; and I will make darkness to light before them , and bend to straightness ; and I will do all these things , and will not forsake them .
He leans on the idols that are carved , and says to the idols that are cast , &quot; You are our God ; these people will turn back , and will be utterly ashamed .
Listen , you deaf , and see , you blind , that you may see .
Who is blinder than my servant , and who is deaf than the messenger whom I sent , and who is blinder than the good that is with me , and who is blinder than the servant of the Lord ?
You see many things , but do not perceive them ; and your ears are open , but do not hear
For the sake of his righteousness the Lord loves to magnify the law and to exalt it
&quot; But these people have been taken , they have been taken , they have been confined in pits , they have been hidden in prisons , they have been plundered , and no one has saved them , they have been plundered , and no one has returned them .
&quot; Who among you will listen to this ? Who will listen to this ? Who will guard against the future ?
&quot; Who has delivered Jacob into captivity , and delivered Israel into captivity ? Is it not the Lord , the one whom we have sinned against ? They do not obey His ways , nor do they obey His commandments
So he poured out upon Israel the fierce anger and the might of the battle , and the fire was kindled round about him , and he did not know , and burned him , and he did not care .
&quot; Now , Jacob , the Lord who created you , O Israel , who made you , says , &apos; Do not be afraid , for I have redeemed you ; I have called you by your name , and you are mine .
&quot; When you pass through water , I will be with you ; When you pass through rivers , water will not pass through you ; When you pass through fire , you will not be burned , nor will the flame be upon you .
For I am the Lord your God , the Holy One of Israel , your Savior ; and I have made Egypt your ransom , and made Goshen and Sheba your substitute
&quot; Because I have regarded you as a treasure , and because I love you , I have made men to replace you , and the Gentiles to replace your life
&quot; Do not be afraid , for I am with you . I will bring your descendants from the east and gather you from the west
&quot; I will say to the north , &apos; Bring me out ; &apos; and to the south , &apos; Don &apos;t detain me ; &apos; and I will bring my sons from far away , and my daughters from the land .
&quot; He who is called in My name is the glory that I have created , and I have created , and I have made .
&quot; You shall bring forth the blind with eyes , and the deaf with ears
Let all the nations assemble themselves , let all the peoples assemble themselves , and who among them will make this proclamation , and tell us the things that were before ? They may bring a witness , and prove it , or they may hear and say , This is true .
&quot; You are my witnesses , my chosen servants , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and so they will know , and will believe in me , and will know that I am the Lord . There was no true God before me , neither will there be any after me .
&quot; But I am the Lord , and there is no Savior except Me
&quot; I have instructed , I have saved , I have declared , and there is no other God among you , &quot; says the Lord . &quot; You are my witness , and I am God
&quot; I am God for a long time . No one can deliver a man from my hand . I will act . Who can stop me ?
Thus saith the Lord your Redeemer , the Holy One of Israel ; For your sakes I have sent to Babylon , and I will cause the Chaldeans , as fugitives , to sit down in their pleasant ships
&quot; I am the Lord your Holy One , the Creator of Israel , and your King .
The LORD hath opened the way in the midst of the sea , and hath opened the way in the midst of the great waters
And they brought forth the carriages , and the horses , and the soldiers , and the mighty men , and lay down together , and did not rise again ; and they did not consume the lamp as it were consumed
Thus says the Lord : &quot; You shall not remember the things of the past , nor think of the things of the ancient days
&quot; Behold , I am about to do a new thing , and I am about to discover it . Do you not know that I will make my way in the wilderness , and I will make my rivers in the desert
&quot; The beasts of the field will respect me , and the dogs of the field and the ostrich will respect me ; for I have given the wilderness water , and the desert rivers , and have given drink to my people , and to my chosen ones .
&quot; These are the people that I have created for myself ; they speak well of my goodness .
&quot; You have not asked me , O Jacob ; and you have bored me , O Israel .
Thou hast not brought thy sheep for a burnt offering unto me , neither hast thou respected me with a sacrifice ; neither have I made thee to serve by offering , nor have I bored thee by incense
&quot; You have not purchased irises for me with silver , nor have you filled me with fat from the sacrifices ; You have made me to serve for your sins , and have made me tired for your sins .
&quot; But I blot out your transgressions for my own sake , and I do not remember your sins .
Wake me up , and you and I shall debate together ; and you shall declare your cause , and make your righteousness manifest .
&quot; Your fathers have sinned , and your masters have rebelled against me .
Therefore I will insult the chief of the unholy places , and make Jacob a curse , and make Israel a curse
&quot; Now , O Jacob my servant , O Israel whom I have chosen , listen
&quot; Thus says the Lord who made you and gave you birth , and who will help you : &apos; My servant Jacob , O Jerusalem whom I have chosen , be not afraid
For I will pour water on the thirsty , I will pour water on the dry land , I will pour my spirit on your seed , I will pour my blessing on your sons .
And they shall be born in the grass , like a fig tree by the stream
&quot; This one shall say , &apos; I belong to the Lord , &apos; and the other in the name of Jacob , and the other in the hand of the Lord , and he shall call himself Israel .
Thus says the Lord , the King of Israel , the Redeemer of Israel , the Lord of hosts : &quot; I am the first , and I am the last , and there is no true God except me
Who , since I created the ancient people , can proclaim , and indicate , and declare for himself , as I did , and let him declare the things of the future , and the things that will be done ?
&quot; Do not be afraid , neither be afraid . Am I not a prophet to you from the ancient times , and you are My witnesses ? Is there a true God besides Me ? There is no rock , and I do not know one .
The idolaters are empty , and their joy is of no use ; and their testimony is not seen , nor known , and they are ashamed .
Who made idols of God , and cast idols of no profit ?
Behold , all his companions shall be ashamed ; neither shall the craftsman be a man ; let them gather together , let them stand , and they shall fear , and be ashamed .
He burned the iron in charcoal , and hammered it with a hammer , and hammered it with his mighty arm ; and he was hungry and powerless , and weary without water .
draw a line , draw a figure with a pen , make a figure out of a bow , draw a figure out of a circle , make a figure like a man , and live in a house
He cut down the acacia trees , and took the fir trees and the oak trees , and chose one from the forest , and planted pine trees for rain .
&quot; This tree shall be used for a fire , and he shall take some of the fire himself , and burn baked cakes ; and he shall worship God as a kneeling , and worship him as a carved idol .
He burned a fraction in the fire , and a fraction of the roast was eaten ; and he roasted himself , and said , &quot; Ah , I am warm , I see the fire
He made a god out of the remnant , an idol , which he had carved ; and he bowed down to it , and worshipped it , and prayed to it , saying , Save me , for you are my God
&quot; They do not know , nor think ; for the Lord shuts their eyes , and they cannot see , and their hearts are closed , and they cannot understand .
Who is not awakened in his heart , nor has he knowledge , nor has he wisdom , to say , &apos; I have burned a portion in fire , and baked cakes in charcoal fire , and I have baked meat , and what remains of it will I make abomination , and will I worship the trees ? &apos;
He feeds himself with ashes , and is deluded in his heart , and leads him astray . He cannot save himself , nor can he say , Is there not a lie in my right hand ?
Remember these things , O Jacob , O Israel , you are my servant ; O Israel , you are my servant ; I have made you , and you will not forget
I have blotted out your transgressions like a thick cloud ; I have blotted out your sins like a thin cloud ; and you shall return to me because I have redeemed you .
Sing , O heavens , for the LORD hath created it ; and let the depths of the earth rejoice , and let the mountains sing , and let the trees and all the trees thereof be as it were ; for the LORD hath redeemed Jacob , and hath glorified himself for Israel
&quot; Thus says the Lord , your Redeemer , who created you from the womb , &apos; I am the Lord of all creation , who alone laid the heavens and the earth .
that the signs of falsehood are vanished , that the wizards are deceived , that the wise man is turned back , that his knowledge is made foolish
that the words of my servant may be established , and that the counsels of my messenger may be fulfilled ; that Jerusalem may be inhabited , and that the cities of Judah may be built , and that the wilderness thereof may be raised up ,
And he said to the deep , &quot; You have done it ; and I will also drown your rivers .
&quot; He is my minister , &quot; says Goliath , &quot; and he will accomplish my pleasure , and he will command to build Jerusalem , and he will command to lay the foundations of the sanctuary
&quot; I , the LORD , have anointed Goliath , and I have given him my right hand , and I will make all the nations subdue before him , and I will loose the king &apos;s belt , and the gates of the city will be opened before him , and they will not be shut , &quot; I said to him .
I will walk before you , and I will repair the rough land ; I will break the brass gates , and I will cut off the bars .
&quot; I will give you the treasures of the unseen and the treasures of the hidden , that you may know that the name that is called upon you is my Lord , the God of Israel
&quot; For the sake of my servant Jacob , and for the sake of Israel whom I have chosen , I have called you by your name ; and although you do not know me , I have added to your name
&quot; I am the LORD , and there is no god but I ; and there is no god but I ; and if you do not know me , I will bow down to you
&quot; From the place where the sun rises to the place where the sun sets , that they may know that there is no god but I , and that there is no god but I , the Lord ,
&quot; I have made light and darkness ; I have given peace and evil ; and it is my Lord who made all these things
&quot; O heavens , drop from above , and the heavens will bring down righteousness , and the earth will break apart , and deliver salvation , and righteousness will come together ; these are the works of my Lord .
&quot; Woe to him who disputes with the Lord who created him ! He is no more than a piece of a tile in the earth ! Will the earth say to him , &apos; What are you doing ? &apos; Or , &apos; What have you done ? &apos; Or , &apos; You have no hand ? &apos;
&quot; Woe to him who says to his father , &apos; What are you born of ? &apos; or to his mother , &apos; What are you born of ? &apos;
&quot; Thus says the Lord , the Holy One of Israel , the Maker of Israel , &apos; You may ask me about the things to come , and about my children , and about the work of my hands , and you may ask me to judge them .
&quot; I have made the earth , and I have made man on the earth , and I have spread out the heavens with my hands ; and all the images of the heavens I have commanded .
I will raise up the ancients in righteousness , and I will restore all their ways , and he will build my city , and release my captives , neither for a wage nor for a reward , &quot; says the Lord of hosts .
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; The goods of Egypt , and the goods of the ancients , will be yours ; and the great Ziba will surrender to you , and they will be yours ; and they will come with chains to follow you ; and they will pray to you , saying , &apos; God is indeed among you , and there is no other God , and there is no other God&apos;
O God of Israel , the Savior , you are a God in secret
All who make idols shall be ashamed , and all shall be ashamed together .
Only Israel shall be saved by the Lord , and shall have eternal salvation ; and ye shall not be ashamed nor be ashamed , until the endless days .
&quot; The Lord who created the heavens , the God who created the whole earth , He created a firm earth , not to desolate it , but to inhabit it , saying , &apos; I am the Lord , and there is no other God
&quot; I have not spoken in darkness , neither have I spoken to Jacob &apos;s seed , saying , &apos; You seek me for nothing ; what I have spoken is righteousness , and what I have spoken is righteousness .
Gather yourselves together , those who have escaped from the nations , and those who carry statues and pray to the God who cannot save , and have no knowledge .
&quot; You shall proclaim your reason , and they shall discuss it among themselves . Who said in the ancient times , &apos; Is it not my Lord ? There is no God except me . I am the God of righteousness and the Savior , and there is no God except me&apos;
&quot; When all the people of the earth look on me , they will be saved ; for I am God , and there is no other God .
&quot; I swear by myself , and by my mouth I speak in righteousness , and not in reverse ; and every knee shall kneel before me , and every mouth shall swear by me
&quot; They say to me , &apos; Only the Lord is worthy of righteousness and of power . All men will return to Him , and whoever is angry with Him will be ashamed
&quot; The seed of Israel will be called righteous by the Lord , and they will be exalted
Pilate bowed down , and Nebo bent down ; and the idols of Babylon were carried on beasts and cattle ; and what they carried is now heavy , and the cattle are weary .
For they are all bent together , and are not able to bear their burdens , and are taken away captive .
&quot; Listen to me , the house of Jacob , and all the remnant of the house of Israel ; You have taken me in your arms from birth , and you have given me in your breasts from the womb
As for your old age , so am I ; as for your whiteness , so am I ; and as for what I have created , so will I hold ; and as for what I will hold , so will I save .
Who do you compare with me , who are equal to me , who can be compared with me , and who are we ?
Those who take gold out of their pockets , and make idols out of silver from heaven , and hire silversmiths , they fall down and worship
They lift up the image of God , they carry it on their shoulders , they place it in a place , and he stands , and he does not depart from his throne ; and people call on him , and he cannot promise , nor save a man from trouble .
&quot; Remember this , and be great husbands to yourselves ; and think in your hearts , O rebellious people .
&quot; Remember the things of old , for I am God , and there is no other God . I am God , and there is no one like me .
&quot; I have spoken from the beginning of the end , and from ancient times of things that have not been done , saying , &apos; My calculation will be determined , and all that I please will be accomplished .
&quot; I will call the birds from the east , and the man who will accomplish what I have planned from afar ; I have spoken , and it will be accomplished ; I have devised , and it will be created .
&quot; Listen to what I say , O you stubborn ones who are far from righteousness .
I will bring near my righteousness , and it will not be far from me ; and my salvation will not delay ; and I will bring forth my glory to Israel , and deliver it in Zion .
&quot; Sit down in the dust , O virgin of Babylon , and sit on the earth , O daughter of Galilee , without a throne ; for you are no longer called soft and tender .
to polish the face , to uncover the pajamas , to take off the long-sleeved shirts , and to expose the legs to the river .
Your lower parts shall be exposed , and your uglyness shall be seen ; and I will retaliate , and no one will tolerate me .
The name of our Redeemer is the Lord of hosts , the Holy One of Israel .
&quot; Sit quietly , daughter of Galilee , and enter into the darkness ; for you will no longer be called the mother of the nations .
&quot; I have provoked my people to anger , I have defiled my inheritance , I have given them into your hand , and you have not pity on them , and you have added a heavy yoke to the elderly .
&quot; You yourself said , &apos; I will always be a mother , &apos; so do not put this matter in your heart , nor think of the end of it .
&quot; Now , when you hear this , in your heart , you who are a pleasant feast and a safe dwelling place , say , &apos; I am the only one , and there is none else but me , and I will not be widowed nor be slain .
&quot; The two things of the widow and the deceased will come to you in a day of turning your eyes , when you do many evil deeds and exert many spells , and the two things will come to you at all .
&quot; You have come to rely on your own evil deeds , saying , &apos; No one sees me . Your wisdom , your wisdom , makes you wicked , and in your heart you say , &apos; There is none but me , and there is none but me
Therefore evil shall come upon thee , and thou knowest not when it shall come upon thee ; and evil shall come upon thee , and thou shalt not be able to remove it ; and destruction which thou knewest not shall come upon thee suddenly .
&quot; Stand up , and use the spells of your youth , and your many evil deeds , that you may profit or prevail .
&quot; You have planned so much that you are weary . Let those who see the heavens and the stars and those who prophesy in the moon rise and save you from what is to come to you .
They will be burned like straw , and they will not be able to save themselves from the power of the flame ; neither will they be able to sit in the fire before it , nor will they be able to roast the charcoal .
&quot; This is no good to you for what you have done to God ; and those who have traded with you from childhood have gone about in the land , and no one will save you .
&quot; Listen to me , the house of Jacob , who are called by the name of Israel , who come from the waters of Judah ; and you swear by the name of the Lord , &quot; The God of Israel , &quot; but not in truth , nor in righteousness
( They call themselves the people of the Holy City , and they rely on the God of Israel , the Lord of hosts . )
&quot; The things which I said from ancient times have passed through my mouth , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and also what I commanded , and all of a sudden I did , and it was accomplished .
For I know that thou art stiff-necked : thy neck is of iron , and thy forehead of brass .
&quot; Therefore I have declared these things to you from ancient times , and not beforehand , lest you should say , &apos; These are the things which my idols have done , the things which I have carved , and the things which I have cast down . &apos; 
&quot; You have heard all these things , and now you will see them . Do you not tell me that from now on I will tell you the new things , secret things that you do not know ?
&quot; This is the creation of the world , and it has not been in the past ; and you have not heard it before this day , lest you say , &apos; I knew it before . &apos; 
Thou hast not heard , nor known ; thy ears have never been opened ; and I knew that thou didst great deceit ; and thou hast been called rebellious from the beginning of thy life .
&quot; For my name &apos;s sake I will endure anger for a while ; I will praise my name ; I will tolerate you , and I will not cut you off .
&quot; I will grind you , but not like silver ; I have chosen you in the furnace of distress .
&quot; I will do it for my own sake ; I will not defile my name , nor will I give my glory to false gods .
&quot; Listen to me , Jacob , O Israel whom I have chosen ; I am the Lord , the first and the last
&quot; I have laid the foundations of the earth with my right hand ; I have spread the heavens with my right hand ; and I have raised them up with a greeting .
&quot; When you gather yourselves together , listen to those who have spoken these things among them ; and the beloved of the Lord will do to Babylon what he pleases , and his arms will be added to the Chaldeans .
&quot; But I have said , &apos; I have chosen him and brought him , and his path will be straight . &apos; 
&quot; Come near to me to hear this ; for I have not spoken in secret from the beginning , and I have been there ever since this happened ; and now the Lord Yahweh has sent me and his spirit .
Thus says the Lord your Redeemer , the Holy One of Israel : &quot; I am the Lord your God , who teaches you to benefit you , and guides you in the way you walk
&quot; If only you would listen to my commandments . Your peace is like the waters of the river , Your righteousness like the waves of the sea .
Thy seed shall be as the sand of the sea , and whatsoever is born in thy belly shall be as the grain of sand ; and His name shall not be cut off before Me , nor shall it be destroyed .
&quot; You shall come out of Babylon , and escape from the Chaldeans , and proclaim with a voice of joy , saying , &apos; The Lord has redeemed Jacob his servant , &apos; and you shall proclaim it to the ends of the earth
&quot; The Lord has guided them through the desert , and they are not thirsty ; He has poured out water for them from the rocks , and the waters of the rocks have been split , and they are poured out
&quot; The wicked will not have peace , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; Listen to me , O islands of the sea , and listen to me , O people of the farthest places . When you give birth , the Lord will appoint me , and when you give birth from the womb , He will name me .
He has made my mouth like a sharp sword ; He has hid me under His shadow ; He has made me arrows of polishing ; He has hid me in His bag of arrows .
&quot; You are my servant Israel , and I will be glorified for you
&quot; But I said , &apos; My labour is nothing , and my effort is nothing ; but in the Lord is my righteousness , and my reward is with my God
&quot; The Lord has made me his servant from my womb , that Jacob may return to him , and that Israel may assemble in him ; for the Lord has considered me worthy , and my God has become my strength .
&quot; Now he says , &apos; You are my servant , that you may revive the tribes of Jacob , and that you may bring back the salvation of Israel , which is but a small thing ; and I will make you the light of the Gentiles , that you may do my salvation to the ends of the earth .
Thus says the Lord , the Holy One of the Redeemer of Israel , concerning him who is despised , hated in his own land , and abused by the governors : &quot; The king stands when he sees , and the princes when they worship ; for the Lord is the True One who has chosen you , the Holy One of Israel
Thus saith the LORD ; I have given thee my consent in the day of thy approval , and I have helped thee in the day of thy salvation : I will protect thee , and make thee a watchman over the people , and I will renew the whole earth , and give to men the land of the desolate for a possession
Say to the bound , &quot; Come out , &quot; and to the dark , &quot; Disclose yourselves ; they will have food on the way , and they will have food in the high places of all clear light .
No hunger nor thirst , neither shall the heat nor the hot day harm them ; for with mercy He will lead them , and bring them to the waters .
&quot; I will make all my mountains a highway , and my highway will be raised up .
Behold , these are from far , these are from north , these are from west , these are from the land of Qin
Sing , O heavens ; and rejoice , O earth ; and sing , O mountains ; for the LORD hath comforted his people , and hath mercy on his troubled people .
Then Zion said , &quot; The Lord has forsaken me , and the Lord has forgotten me
&quot; If a woman forgets the child that she has nursed , and does not have mercy on the son that she has born , or if she forgets , I will not forget you
&quot; Behold , I will inscribe You in My hand ; Your walls are always before Me
&quot; Your children will return quickly , and those who destroy you , and those who make you desolate , will all go away from you .
&quot; Look around and see , and they are all gathered together to you , &quot; says the Lord ; &quot; and I swear by my eternal life that you will put on their adornment , and you will gird your loins as a new woman
As for the place where thou wast desolate , and the land where thou wast destroyed , it shall be too narrow for the people to dwell , and they that swallowed thee up shall be far from thee .
And thou shalt hear the children that are born after the death say , My place is too narrow ; give me a place to dwell in
&quot; In that day you will say in your heart , &apos; I have lost my son , and I have been taken captive , and I have drifted abroad . Who gave me these things , and who raised them up ? In the days when I was left alone , these things are there .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; I will raise up my hand to the nations , and I will raise up a great flag to the people , and they will carry your sons in their arms , and your daughters on their shoulders ,
&quot; The kings will be your fathers , and the queens your mothers ; and they will be humbled and worship you , and they will wipe the dust from your feet , and you will know that I am the Lord , and that those who wait for me will not be ashamed
Will the brave take back what he has taken , and will the captive be saved ?
&quot; But thus says the Lord : &apos; He who is taken away by the mighty will be taken back , and he who is taken away by the violent will be saved . I will fight against him who is fighting against you , and I will save your children
&quot; And I will make those who oppress you to eat their own flesh , and to drink their own blood as a drink of sweet wine ; and whoever has the blood will know that My Lord is your Savior , your Redeemer , and the mighty One of Jacob .
Thus saith the LORD ; I have shut up your mother , and I have shut up the book in it ; and which of my creditors will I sell you unto me ? for your iniquity you have been sold , and for your transgressions your mother has been shut up ,
Why is no one waiting for the time of my coming , and why is no one agreeing to the time of my calling ? Are not My arms shortened , and cannot be redeemed , and I have no power to save ? Behold , when I rebuke , the sea dries up , and I make the river a wilderness , and the fish thereof die without water , and without smell , and without thirst .
I have clothed the heavens with darkness , and clothed them with cloth
&quot; The Lord Yahweh has given me the tongue of the disciple , that I may know how to help the weak with words ; He awakens my ears every morning , that I may hear , as a disciple
&quot; The Lord Yahweh has opened my ears , and I have neither rebelled nor turned back
&quot; He strikes me on the back , and I let him strike ; He pulls out the beard of my cheek , and I pull it from him ; He insults me and spits on me , and I do not hide my face .
&quot; The Lord Yahweh will help me , and I will not be ashamed ; I will be hard as a rock in my face , and I know that I will not be ashamed
Those who call me righteous are near to me ; those who argue with me stand with me ; those who are righteous with me come near to me .
&quot; The Lord Yahweh will help me ; and who will judge me for my sins ? They are as the garments of old age , which the worms bite
Who among you fears the Lord , and listens to the words of His servant , who walks in darkness , and has no light , and trusts in the name of the Lord , and in his God
&quot; Whosoever of you sets fire around himself with a staff of fire , shall walk in your flames and in the staff of fire that you set , as I have ordained ; and you shall lie in misery .
&quot; Listen to me , you who seek the Lord in your pursuit of righteousness , and seek the rock that is cut out , and the hole that is dug out .
Remember Abraham your father , and Sarah your mother ; for when Abraham was alone , I chose him , and blessed him , and multiplied the number of others .
&quot; The Lord has comforted Zion , and all the wilderness of Zion , He has made the wilderness like Eden , He has made the desert like the garden of the Lord . There will be joy , joy , thanksgiving , and a voice of singing
O my people , listen to me ; O my people , listen to me ; for I will give you the instruction , and I will establish my righteousness for the light of the people .
&quot; My righteousness is near ; My salvation is coming ; My arm will judge all people ; The islands of the sea will await Me ; They will rely on My arm .
Lift up your eyes to heaven , and look on the earth : for the heaven will be as a cloud , and the earth as a garment , and the inhabitants thereof will die as a worm ; but My salvation endures forever , and My righteousness will not be abolished .
Know the righteousness , and teach My word in the hearts of the people , and hear My words , and be not afraid of the reproach of men , nor be afraid of the slander of men .
For the worms shall bite them as the cloth ; and the worms as the wool ; but My righteousness endureth for ever , and My salvation for ever .
Rise , Rise , O arms of the Lord , as the days of old , as the generations of old ; Isn &apos;t it You who cut down Lahab , and pierced the great fish ?
&quot; Have you not dried up the sea and the waters of the depths , and made the depths of the sea the way of redemption ?
And the people of the LORD , who are redeemed , shall return , and sing to Zion ; and everlasting joy shall be upon their heads ; and they shall flee with joy and gladness , and with grief and sigh .
&quot; But I am the consolation for you . Who are you , that you are afraid of those who will die , and of those who will become like grass ?
But forget to lay the heavens , and lay the foundations , and to create the Lord of yours ; and fear the wrath of the oppressors , which they seek to destroy , all day long ; wherein is the wrath of the oppressors ?
The captive shall be released , and shall not die but fall into a pit ; and his food shall not be lacking .
I am the LORD your God , Who stirred up the sea , Who caused the waves of the sea to wave ; The LORD of hosts is my name .
&quot; I have spoken My word to you , and I have covered you with My shadow , that I might plant the heavens and lay the foundations ; and I said to Zion , &apos; You are my people
Arise , arise , arise , arise ! You have drunk out of the hand of the Lord the cup of His wrath , the count that turned men eastward and westward , until it was consumed
None of his offspring guided him , and none of his offspring supported him .
Desolation , destruction , famine , and swords come upon you . Who mourns for you ? How can I comfort you ?
&quot; Your children are fallen asleep , lying in the mouths of the cities , as the lambs in the net ; they are filled with the wrath of the Lord , with the reproach of your God .
&quot; So listen to me , for your trouble is not drunken by wine .
&quot; Thus says your Lord , the God of submission to His people , &apos; Behold , I have taken out of your hand the cup that turned men eastward and westward , the count of my wrath , and you will not drink it again .
&quot; I will deliver this cup into the hands of those who suffer you . They said to you , &apos; Get down , and walk past us ; and you will pass by on your backs like a street .
Rise up , Rise up , clothe yourself with your strength , O Jerusalem , the holy city , and put on the robes of your glory ; for those who are not circumcised and unclean will not enter you from now on .
Shake the dust , O Jerusalem , and rise up , and sit on your seats ; O captive inhabitant of Zion , take away the chains of your neck ,
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; You are sold for nothing , and you will be redeemed for nothing
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; Before my people came down to Egypt and settled there , the Assyrians oppressed them without cause
&quot; What am I doing here , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; because my people have been taken for nothing , and my name is blasphemed all the day long
&quot; Therefore my people shall know my name ; and on that day they shall know that it is I who said it ; behold , it is I.
&quot; The one who preached the good news , the peace , the good news , and the salvation , said to Zion , &apos; Your God has become king . How beautiful is the foot of this man on the mountain
&quot; Listen to the voice of those whom you have watched , and let them sing together ; for they will see with their own eyes when the Lord returns to Zion .
Sing with a loud voice , O the wilderness of Jerusalem ; for the Lord has comforted his people , and redeemed Jerusalem .
The Lord is revealed in the sight of all the nations , and the salvation of our God is seen by all the peoples of the earth .
&quot; Go forth , go forth , and come forth out of Babylon , and do not touch unclean things , but come forth out of it ; and cleanse yourselves , you who carry the vessels of the Lord
Neither will you go out hastily nor run away ; for the Lord will go before you , and the God of Israel will be your shield .
&quot; My servant will be wise in all that he does ; and he will be exalted , and will be exalted to the highest .
Many are astonished at him , for his face is weaker than others , and his descriptions are weaker than the world .
Thus he will purify many nations , and the kings will shut their mouths to him , and they will see what has not been preached to them , and they will understand what they have not heard .
Who believes what we have preached , and to whom the arms of the Lord are revealed ?
&quot; He grows in the sight of the Lord as a young bud , as a root in the dry land . He has no beauty , and when we saw him , we envied him .
He is despised , despised , suffered more and more , and suffered more and more ; he is despised , as though he were not seen , and we have not respected him .
He is indeed the bearer of our sorrows , and the bearer of our pains ; but we are punished for him , and suffered by God .
Knowing that he hath afflicted us for our transgressions , and afflicted us for our iniquities , that we shall have peace in the punishment that he hath afflicted us , and that we shall be healed in the whips that he hath afflicted us .
&quot; We are lost like sheep , and each one follows his own way ; and the Lord has laid all the iniquity of all our people upon him .
He is oppressed , and does not speak in the time of suffering ; He is like a lamb that is taken to the slaughter , and like a sheep that is silent under a shearer &apos;s hand , so he does not speak .
He was taken away by oppression and judgment ; and who among his fellow men would expect him to be beaten and cut off from the land of the living for the sins of my people ?
He did not commit violence , nor did he deceive in his mouth ; but he was buried with the wicked ; and who knows when he dies he will be buried with the rich ?
&quot; But the Lord is determined to afflict him and to afflict him ; and the Lord will offer him up for a sin offering , and he will see his seed , and will prolong the years ; and in his hand will be the joy of the Lord .
And he shall see the fruit of his labour , and be content : and many shall be called righteous because they know My righteous servant , and he shall bear their iniquity .
Therefore I will make him a sharer with the great , and a sharer with the mighty ; for he will bring down his life to death , and he will be among the sinners , and he will bear the sins of many , and he will ask for the sinners .
Sing , thou that hast not conceived , nor begotten ; and thou that hast not laboured , sing with a loud voice , and sing with a loud voice ; for there are more children than there are sons without a husband , saith the LORD .
Expand the land of thy tabernacle , and broaden the mantle of thy dwelling place , and be not restrained ; stretch out thy cords , and strengthen thy rods .
&quot; For you will go from left to right , and your descendants will be in possession of many lands , and inhabit the desolate cities .
Fear not , for thou shalt not be ashamed ; neither be ashamed , for thou shalt not be ashamed : for thou shalt forget the shame of thy youth , and the shame of thy absence .
For he that made you is your husband ; and the Lord of hosts is his name ; and he that redeems you is the Holy One of Israel ; and he shall be called the God of the whole earth .
&quot; The Lord calls you , as the wife who is bereaved in her heart , as the wife who is abandoned in her youth , &quot; says your God
&quot; I forsake you for a little while , but I will bring you back with grace .
&quot; My anger is overflowing , and I will hide myself from you in a moment , but I will have mercy on you for ever , &quot; says the Lord your Redeemer
Like the flood of Noah , I swear that I will not cause the flood of Noah to pass through the land , neither will I be angry with you , nor will I reproach you .
A great mountain can be moved , and a small mountain can be moved ; but my mercy will not leave you , neither will my covenant of peace , &quot; says the Lord who has mercy on you
&quot; O you who are in distress and are not comforted by the wind , I will place your stones in colours , and I will lay your foundations in blue stones
And the walls of thy daughters shall be of red stone , and the gates of thy city of red jasper , and the borders of thy borders of stone .
Your children shall be taught by the Lord , and your children shall have great peace .
Thou shalt stand firm in righteousness ; thou shalt not be afraid of oppression ; thou shalt not be afraid of terror , and terror shall not come near thee .
&quot; Whoever gathers to fight against you will fall because of you , or because of your surrender .
&quot; I am the builder of coal , the builder of instruments , and I am the destroyer of the destroyers .
&quot; You shall not use the instruments which you have created to attack you ; and whoever comes up to attack you with his tongue in the judgment , you shall surely be guilty of him . This is the inheritance of the servants of the Lord , and the righteousness which they have received from Me , &quot; says the Lord .
All of you who are thirsty come near the water ; and those who have no silver money come ; and you all come to buy and eat , and to buy wine and milk without silver money , and without value
&quot; Why do you spend your money on what is not enough to eat , and on what is not enough to be satisfied with your labour ? If you listen to my words , you will eat the good things , and you will be filled with sweetness and joy in your hearts .
&quot; When you come near to me , and listen to me , you will live ; and I will make an everlasting covenant with you , which is the promise of David &apos;s faithful grace .
I have set him as a witness to the people , a king and commander for the people .
And the nations that thou hast not known shall be called unto thee , and the nations that thou hast not known shall run forth unto thee , because the LORD thy God , the Holy One of Israel , hath glorified thee
&quot; When the Lord seeks , seek him ; and when he is near , seek him .
Let the wicked depart from his way ; and let the wicked depart from his thoughts ; and let him return to the Lord , and the Lord will have mercy on him ; and let him return to our God , for God will forgive in abundance .
&quot; My thoughts are not with your thoughts , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; My ways are not with your ways
As the heavens are exalted above the earth , so are My ways exalted above your ways , My thoughts exalted above your thoughts
And rain and snow come down from the sky , and return not ; but they nourish the earth , and cause the earth to sprout , and cause the seed to grow , and cause the food to be eaten .
And so shall be the word which I speak ; and it shall not return , but it shall accomplish that which I am pleased with ; and it shall be accomplished in that which I have sent him to accomplish .
And ye shall come forth joyfully and joyfully , guided in peace ; and the mountains and the hills shall sing before you , and the trees of the field shall shake their hands .
The pine tree is for the thorns , and the pomegranate for the resin . This is for the name of the Lord , as a proof for ever , and it cannot be cut off .
Thus saith the Lord ; Be just , and do righteousness : for my righteousness shall be manifest when my salvation cometh .
He keeps the Sabbath without sin , and forbids his hands without evil ; and he who does this , and keeps it , is blessed .
&quot; The foreigners who are united with the Lord shall not say , &apos; The Lord will surely separate me from his people ; neither shall the captives say , &apos; I am a dead tree . &apos; 
&quot; For thus says the Lord : &apos; Those who keep my Sabbaths , and choose that which pleases me , and keep my covenant ,
And I will make them in My house and in My walls a memorial and a name better than children , and I will give them a name for ever , and they will not be cut off .
&quot; And the foreigners who are united with the Lord , and serve Him , and love the name of the Lord , and are His servants , those who keep the Sabbaths without sin , and keep His covenant ,
I will bring them to My holy mountain , and make them rejoice in My house of prayer ; their burnt offerings and their peace offerings will be acceptable in My altar ; for My house will be called the house of prayer for all the people .
&quot; This is the Lord Yahweh , who has gathered the Israelites who have been driven away , saying , &apos; Beside those who have been gathered here , I will gather others to return to them .
&quot; The beasts of the field shall eat ; and so shall the beasts of the forest .
He who watches him is blind , and has no knowledge ; and he is a dumb dog , and cannot call ; but he dreams , and sleeps , and is thirsty .
These dogs are greedy and unfulfilled , and these shepherds do not understand , and they follow their own ways , and they seek their own interests from every side
&quot; Come , &quot; they said , &quot; I am going to drink , and we are full of wine . Tomorrow will be like today , a day of great feasting .
A righteous man dies , and no man puts him in his heart ; and a devout man is taken away , and no man thinks ; and this righteous man is taken away , and he is saved from the evil of the future .
Peace , and righteousness , and rest in the tomb .
&quot; The seed of the sons of the witch , and the seed of the adulterer , and of the prostitute , shall come to you .
Whom do you laugh at , and to whom do you pronounce your tongue ? Are you not rebellious children and liars ?
You want to devour your hearts in the middle of oak trees , under the green trees , and kill your children in the valleys , and under the rocks
And in the valley are thy portions in smooth stones : these are the portions which thou hast earned : and thou hast poured down unto him drink offerings , and offered sacrifices : will I be tolerated for this ?
&quot; You will lay down your bed on high mountains , and there you will offer your offerings .
Behold , thou standest behind the gate , and behind the frame of the gate , and standest in remembrance of thee , and behold , thou art exposed unto strangers , and goest up and spreadest out thy bed , and makest a covenant with them ; and there thou seest their beds , and lovest them exceedingly .
&quot; You bring oil to the king , and add more spices to it , and send messengers far away , and humble yourself and go straight to hell .
&quot; You are weary of your way , and do not say , &apos; This is futile . &apos; You think that there is a resurrection , so do not feel weary
Whom do you fear , and for whom do you fear , and lie , and do not remember me , and do not put this thing in your heart ? Am I not a long-suffering mouth , and do you not fear me ?
I will show you your righteousness , and all that you do will be of no benefit to you .
Let those whom you have gathered save you in the time of your supplication ; the wind shall blow them away , and a breath shall blow them away ; but the land which you shall rely on Me shall receive , and the holy mountains of Me shall be your possessions .
&quot; You build , you build , and you prepare the way , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and you will remove the stumbling block from the way of my people
For thus saith the Most High , who is holy for ever and ever , I dwell in the Most High , and am with the humble in heart , that the spirit of the humble may be revived , and that the heart of the humble may be revived .
&quot; I will not contend for ever , nor be angry for a long time ; for I am afraid that the man whom I have created and the spirit will perish .
For his greedy iniquity , I have struck him in anger , and I have hid my anger from him , and he is still turning away .
I have seen the way that he walks , and I will heal him , and guide him , and comfort him with the one who is grieved .
&quot; I have made the fruit of the lips : Peace be to him that is far off , and to him that is near ; and I will heal him , &quot; says the Lord .
Only the wicked will not be at ease , as a sea that is turned upside down , and the waters thereof will flow with filth and mud .
&quot; My God said , &quot; The wicked will not have peace
&quot; You will shout with a loud voice , You will not cease , You will raise up your voice like a trumpet , You will show My people their transgressions , You will show the house of Jacob their sins
They seek me every day , and are glad to understand my way , as a righteous nation , who do not forsake the scriptures of their God , and seek me the judgment of righteousness , and are glad to be near to God .
They said , &quot; Why do you not see that we are fasting , and why do you not understand that we are working hard on our own hearts ? Behold , the days of your fasting are still seeking profits , and forcing people to work hard for you .
You have fasted , but you have fought against one another , and you have struck with a fierce sword ; and you have not fasted today , so that your voice may not be heard .
Is this the day of fasting that I have chosen , that I may make men suffer their own hearts ? Is this the day that I shall cause them to bow down like reeds , and lay their heads under him in cloth and in ashes ? Is this the day that you shall call fasting acceptable to the Lord ?
Is not the fast that I have chosen to loose the rope of evil , to break the yoke of the yoke , to free the oppressed , to break the yoke of all ?
Is it not that I will give your bread to those who are hungry , and I will take the poor who floats to your house , and I will clothe him who is naked , and I will cover him with clothing , and I will not hide myself from my bones ?
Thus shall thy light be found as the morning light ; and the healing which thou hast received shall be quickened ; and thy righteousness shall go before thee ; and the glory of the Lord shall be thy shield .
&quot; When you call , the Lord will answer you ; and when you cry , He will say , &apos; I am here ; &apos; if you remove the yoke from among you , and point the fingers of men , and speak evil words
If thy heart have mercy on the hungry , and satisfy the afflicted , thy light shall be found in darkness , and thy darkness shall be as noon .
&quot; And the Lord will guide you from time to time , and will make your heart content in the land of drought , and your bones strengthen ; and you will be like a garden watered , and like an everlasting fountain
&quot; Those who come from you will repair the desolate places , and you will build the foundations of the generations to come , and you will call them repairers and repairers of paths and dwellers with people .
&quot; If you turn away from your steps on the Sabbath day , and do not rejoice in My Sabbath day , and call it joyful , and honor the Sabbath day of the Lord , and respect it , and do not do your own private business , and do not follow your own private counsel , and do not speak your own private words ,
&quot; You will rejoice in the Lord , and He will make you ride in the high places , and raise you up in the inheritance of your father Jacob , &quot; says the Lord .
The arm of the Lord is not shortened to save , neither are the ears dispersed to hear .
But your iniquity separates you from God , and your iniquity covers him from hearing you .
For your hands are bound with blood , and your fingers are bound with iniquity , and your lips speak lies , and your tongues speak evil words .
There is none who confesseth by righteousness , and none who discerneth by truth ; and they rely upon falsehood and lies ; and whatsoever is in them is poison , and whatsoever is born is iniquity .
&quot; They gnaw on the eggs of vipers , and gnaw on the webs of spiders ; and the man that eats them shall die ; and the egg that is trampled shall come forth from the viper .
The nets of which they are bound are not clothed , neither can they cover themselves : their deeds are iniquity , and their hands are violent .
Their feet run in wickedness , and the blood of innocents flows rapidly ; their thoughts are in sin ; and the paths that are passed are desolate and desolate .
The way of peace , they do not know ; there is no justice in what they do ; they have set their own course , and whoever follows it does not know peace .
Therefore justice is far from us , and righteousness is far from us ; and we seek light , and it is dark ; and we seek light , and it is dark .
We seek the walls as blind men ; we seek as blind men ; we stumble at midday as at twilight ; we are in the midst of the mighty as dead men .
We roar like bears , and we mourn like doves ; We hope for justice , but it is not ; We hope for salvation , but it is far from us .
Our transgressions are multiplied before thee , and our iniquities bear witness to us ; and our transgressions are with us , and we know our iniquities .
&quot; It is rebellion that does not know the Lord , and turns away from our God , and speaks deceitful and rebellious words , and lies in his heart , and speaks them .
And justice turns back , and righteousness stands afar off ; and honesty falls in the street , and integrity enters not .
The wicked turn against the prey , and the Lord sees that there is no justice , nor much joy .
He was astonished when he saw that no one was saved , and no one asked for him ; and he saved himself with his own arm , and supported himself in righteousness
He is the armor of righteousness , the helmet of salvation , the garment of vengeance , and the robe of enthusiasm
He will recompense according to the deeds of men , and will provoke his enemies to anger , and will recompense his enemies , and will execute his recompense on all the islands .
Thus shall men fear the name of the Lord from the sunset , and the glory of him from the place from which the sun rises ; for the enemy is driven away by the Spirit of the Lord , as a torrent of waters .
&quot; There will come a redeemer from among the children of Jacob to the prisoners of Zion , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; This is the word of the covenant I made with them , &quot; says the Lord ; &quot; I have added to you the Spirit , and the word that I have spoken to you will not be cut off from your mouth , nor from the mouth of your seed , nor from the mouth of your seed , nor from the mouth of your seed , from now on , and forever , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; Behold , the glory of the Lord shines on you , for your light has passed through .
&quot; Behold , darkness covers the earth , darkness covers all the people ; but the Lord will appear before you , and His glory will be on you now
All nations will come for your light , and kings for the light you have found .
Lift up your eyes , and behold , all the people are gathered unto thee ; and thy sons come from afar , and thy daughters are begotten .
Then you will see the glory , and your heart will be moved , and your heart will be filled with joy : for the goods of the sea will return to you , and the treasures of the nations will return to you .
&quot; And the camels of Midian and Ephraim will cover you , and all the people of Sheba will come , and they will offer golden milk , and they will proclaim the praise of the Lord .
And the flock of Kida shall be gathered unto thee , and the goats of Nineveh shall be for thy service : and they shall be delighted in my altar , and I will glorify the house of my glory .
&quot; Who are those who come as clouds , and as doves fly back to windows ?
&quot; All the islands of the sea will wait for me , first the ships which He has sent to bring your children , and their silver and their gold , from afar , in the name of the Lord your God , and the Holy One of Israel , because He has glorified you
&quot; The foreigners will build your walls , and their kings will obey you ; and I have struck you in anger , but now I have shown you mercy .
&quot; Your gates will be open day and night , and they will not be shut , and they will bring the wealth of the nations to you , and their kings will be seized by them .
&quot; A nation that does not serve you will perish , and a nation that does not serve you will be completely desolate
The glory of Lebanon , the pine trees , the cedar trees , and the pine trees , will be with thee to beautify my sanctuary , and I will make the place of my feet to be glorified .
&quot; He who has suffered for you will bow down to you , and his sons who have despised you will kneel under your feet , and they will call you the City of the Lord , and Zion , the Holy One of Israel .
Though thou hast been abandoned , hated , and not passed by , yet have I made thee a glory for ever , and a joy for generations to come
You will eat the milk of all the nations , and the milk of the kings ; and you will know that my Lord is your Savior , your Redeemer , the mighty One of Jacob .
I will take gold for copper , and silver for iron , and copper for wood , and iron for stone ; and I will be your governor in peace , and your overseer in righteousness .
Thou shalt hear no more violence in the land , nor destruction in the land : thou shalt call thy walls of salvation , and thy gates of praise .
The sun will no longer be your daylight , neither will the moon be your light ; but the Lord will be your light forever , and your God your glory .
Your sun shall not fall , neither shall your moon recede ; for the LORD shall be your light for ever , and your days of mourning shall be ended .
&quot; Your inhabitants are righteous people ; they are for ever an occupation ; they are the seed of My seed , the work of My hands , that I may be glorified .
And the tribe of the little ones shall be multiplied a thousandfold ; and the weak nation shall be made strong ; and I the Lord will do it in due season .
For the Spirit of the Lord Yahweh is in me , because the Lord has anointed me , that I may preach good news to the humble , to the poor , to the sick , to the sick , that the captive may be released , and that the captive may go out of prison .
Speak of the year of grace of the LORD , and of the day of vengeance of our God , and comfort all the mourners .
to give the crown of the Lord to those who mourn in Zion , to replace the dust , to replace the oil of gladness , to replace the mourning , to replace the garments of praise , to replace the spirit of sorrow , that they may be called the trees of righteousness , which the Lord has planted , that He may be glorified
&quot; They will build an old desolate land , and build a desolate place , and rebuild an old desolate city .
&quot; Then the foreigners will come and shepherd your flock , and the foreigners will make your fields , and repair your vineyards .
&quot; You shall be called the priests of the Lord , and they shall call you servants of our God ; and you shall eat of the riches of the nations for their glory .
&quot; You shall have multiplied benefits in place of shame , and the joy of division in place of humiliation , and multiplied inheritance in the land , and everlasting joy shall be with you . &quot;
For I the LORD love righteousness , and hate robbery and iniquity ; and I will execute judgment in truth , and I will make an everlasting covenant with my people
Their seed shall be known among the nations , and their sons among the nations ; and he that seeth them shall know that they are the seed of the blessing of the LORD .
I rejoice greatly in the LORD , and my heart rejoiceth in God ; for he hath clothed me with salvation , and hath clothed me with righteousness , as the bridegroom hath put on his crown , and as the bride hath put on her ornaments .
Thus will the Lord Yahweh send out righteousness and praise among all the people , as the field bears fruit , and as the garden bears fruit .
For Zion I will not be silent ; for Jerusalem I will not be silent ; His righteousness is as a light , His salvation as a lamp .
The nations shall see your righteousness , and the kings your glory ; and you shall be called by a new name , which is from the mouth of the Lord .
&quot; You shall be a crown in the hand of the Lord , and a crown in the hand of your God .
&quot; You will no longer be called a deserted land , and your land will no longer be called a desolate land ; but you will be called what I please , and your land will be called a wife of a husband ; for the Lord is pleased with you , and your land will belong to Him
As a young man marries a virgin , so will all your people marry you ; and as a newlywed rejoices in her , so will your God rejoice in you .
&quot; I have set watch over your city , O Jerusalem ; they will not be silent day and night ; you will not be silent when you call on the Lord .
And let him not rest , until he establisheth Jerusalem , that it may be glorified on the earth
&quot; And the Lord swore by His right hand and by His mighty arm , saying , &apos; I will no more feed Your five valleys to Your enemies , nor will the heathen drink the new wine of Your labour
&quot; But he who harvests shall eat and praise the Lord ; and he who gathers shall drink in My sanctuary .
Pass through the gates , prepare the way for the people , build up the highways , pick up the stones , and raise up a great flag for the people .
&quot; Behold , the Lord has spoken to the inhabitants of Zion at the end of the earth , saying , &apos; Your savior has come , and his reward is with him , and his reward before him .
&quot; They shall call themselves saints , redeemers of the Lord ; and you shall be called a city that is not left behind .
&quot; Who is this that comes from the east , from Persia , clothed in red , clothed in beauty , with great power , walking with great steps ? It is I who speak in righteousness , and am able to deliver with great power .
Why is your dress red , and why is your clothing like a hammer ?
&quot; I have poured out wine alone , and none of the people is with me ; I have poured them down in anger , and I have trampled them in fierce anger ; their blood has splashed upon my garments , and has polluted all my garments .
For the year of redemption of my people has come , when the day of vengeance is in my heart
I look up and see no helper ; I wonder that no one supports me ; so my own arm delivers me , and my wrath supports me .
For I am angry , and I have smitten the people , and I am fiercely angry , and I have made them drunken , and I have laid their blood upon the earth
&quot; I will call on all that the Lord has given me for His mercy and for His goodness , and for the great grace which He has bestowed on the house of Israel , for His mercy and for His abundant mercy
He said , &quot; Indeed , they are my people , and they are not children of falsehood , &quot; and he became their Savior .
He suffers with them in all their affliction ; and the angels before Him have delivered them , and He has redeemed them with mercy and compassion ; He has always loved them in the ancient days , and has loved them .
And they rebelled , and the Holy Ghost of the Lord was troubled ; and he turned himself into their enemy , and attacked them in person .
At that time they remembered the days of Moses and his people , saying , &quot; Where is he who brought up the people from the sea , and all his people , and brought down his Holy Spirit among them ? &quot;
Let his glorious arm go on the right hand of Moses , and let water come forth before them , that he may establish his name for ever .
&quot; And lead them through the depths like horses through the wilderness , so that they do not stumble therein .
&quot; The Spirit of the Lord has given them rest as if the cattle had descended into the valley . Thus you have guided your people to establish your glory .
Look on from heaven , and see from the house of your holy glory , wherein is your enthusiasm and your mighty acts , and wherein rests your heart of love and mercy .
&quot; Even though Abraham did not recognize us , neither did Israel recognize us . You are our Father , Lord , You are our Father , and Your name has been our Redeemer for ever
Why hast thou caused us to go astray from the way of thee , O LORD , and hast made our hearts hard to despise thee ? return , O LORD , for thy servants and for thy branch of the inheritance .
Thy saints have not obtained this inheritance for a while : our enemies have trampled upon thy sanctuary
We are as those whom thou hast not governed , and as those whom thou hast not called by thy name
Let the heavens fall , and let the mountains tremble before you
Like a fire that burneth dry wood , and like a fire that burneth water : that thy enemies may know thy name , and that the nations may tremble before thee .
And when thou camest , and the mountains trembled before thee , and we could not wait for the terrible things which thou didst .
&quot; Which god , other than you , has waited for those who have not heard , heard , or seen , from the ancients ?
You have welcomed those who remember the joy of righteousness , and remembered what you said . You were angry , and we are still sinners . This is a long time ago . Can we be saved ?
We are like unclean men ; all righteousness is like filthy clothing ; we are like leaves that are drying up ; and our iniquity is like the wind that blows us away .
And no man asks for thy name , nor seeks to seize thee ; for thou didst hide thy face from us , and didst digest us for our iniquity
&quot; Now , O Lord , you are still our father in You ; we are mud , you are a carpenter , and we are all the work of your hands .
&quot; Lord , don &apos;t be angry , and don &apos;t remember your iniquity forever . Turn to us , for we are your people .
&quot; Your holy cities shall be a wilderness , and Zion a wilderness , and Jerusalem a wilderness
The house of our holiness , where our fathers praised you , is burned with fire ; and the beautiful land which we envy is desolate .
&quot; Will you endure these things , O Lord ? Will you keep quiet , and cause us to suffer greatly ?
&quot; Now ask me those who have not visited me , and those who have not sought me , and I have called them to meet , and those who have not called themselves by my name , and I have said to them , &apos; Here I am , here I am
I stretched out my hand to greet the rebellious people all day long , and they did evil according to their own thoughts
&quot; The people have provoked me to anger , and have offered sacrifices in the garden , and have burned incense on the altar
They sit in the tombs , and dwell in secret places , and eat pork , and there is in their vessels soup of abominations .
And he said unto them , Stand still , and come not near me ; for I am holier than thou : for they are the smoke of my nose , and the fire of the whole day .
&quot; Behold , it is written before me , &apos; I will not be silent , but I will execute vengeance , and I will recompense your iniquity , and the iniquity of your fathers , and I will burn incense on the mountains , and I will profane my iniquity on the hills , and I will recompense them in the arms of their successors , and I will first give them the measure of what they have done , &apos; says the Lord .
See Up
Thus says the Lord : &quot; When you seek new wine in the vineyard , you say , &apos; I will not destroy it , for it is blessed , and I will do so for the sake of my servants , and I will not destroy them at all .
&quot; I will bring forth descendants from Jacob , and from Judah mountains to be inherited ; My chosen people will be inherited , and My servants will dwell therein .
&quot; The plains of Sharon will be a circle for sheep , and the valley of Asher a place for cattle to lie down , for the people who seek Me .
&quot; But you , who have forsaken the Lord , and forgot My holy mountain , have set up tables in time , and have filled the life of heaven with wine and savour .
&quot; I will command you to be put under the sword and to be slain ; for I have not given you a promise , neither have I spoken , neither have you obeyed ; but do that which is evil in My sight , and choose that which I do not like .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; My servants shall eat , and ye shall be hungry ; My servants shall drink , and ye shall be thirsty ; My servants shall rejoice , and ye shall be ashamed
My servants rejoice in their hearts , but you weep in your hearts , and cry in your hearts .
&quot; You shall keep your name , and curse my chosen people ; and the Lord will kill you , and call his servants by another name .
Thus shall he that seeketh for himself on the earth seek for the true God ; and he that sweareth on the earth shall swear by the true God ; for the troubles of old have been forgotten , and are hid from My sight .
Behold , I have created a new heaven and a new earth , and the former things shall not be remembered , nor shall they be remembered .
Rejoice for ever in that which I have made , and rejoice in that which I have made in Jerusalem , and in the inhabitants thereof .
I will rejoice in Jerusalem , and I will rejoice in my people ; and they shall hear no more the voice of weeping and mourning
There shall be no child that dies a few days , and no old man that is not full of years ; for he that dies a hundred years is still a child ; and the sinner that dies a hundred years is cursed .
And they shall build houses , and dwell in them ; and they shall plant vineyards , and eat of their fruit .
For the days of my people shall be as the days of trees , and those of my chosen shall enjoy them for ever , for no man shall dwell in them , nor shall any man eat that they have built .
&quot; They shall not labour in vain , neither shall they be destroyed because of what they have produced ; for they are the seed of the blessed of the Lord , and so are their children .
When they have not asked , I will answer ; and when they speak , I will listen .
&quot; The wolf will eat like the lamb , and the lion like the grass and the ox ; and the dust will be the food of the snake ; and all these things will not hurt nor harm any man in all my holy mountains , &quot; says the Lord
Thus saith the LORD ; The heavens are my seats , and the earth my benches : what house shall ye build for me , wherein shall I rest ?
&quot; All these things have been made by my hand , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; so they are ; but I have looked on those who are afraid of my words , and are grieved for them .
The hypocritical slaughter of cattle is like the slaughter of a man , and the lamb is like the cutting off of a dog &apos;s head , and the offering is like the offering of pigs &apos; blood , and the burning of milk is like the praise of idols ; and they have chosen their way , and are glad in their hearts to do abominations .
And I will choose that which troubleth them , and that which they fear cometh unto them ; for I call , and no man answereth ; and I speak , and they hearken not ; and they do that which is evil in My sight , and choose that which I do not like .
&quot; You , who are afraid of the word of the Lord , when you hear it , your brethren , who hate you , who have driven you out in my name , have said , &apos; May the Lord be glorified , that we may see your joy . &apos; But it is they who are ashamed
A voice of noise came out of the city , and a voice came out of the temple , as the Lord recompenseth the enemy .
For Zion hath not laboured , but hath produced ; and hath not felt pain , but hath born a son .
A nation shall be born in a day , and a people in a time ; for Zion shall bear sons and daughters as she labours : and who has heard and seen such things ?
&quot; I have given birth to him , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I have not given birth to him ; and your God says , &quot; I have given birth to him , and can he not conceive ? &quot;
You who love Jerusalem will rejoice with him , and you who mourn for him will rejoice with him .
And that ye may be filled with milk in His comforting breasts , and that they may be filled with His glorious glory , as with milk , full of joy .
&quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I will spread peace to him as a river , and the glory of the nations as a river that flows , and you will enjoy it , and you will be wrapped around your ribs and shaken on your knees .
&quot; As the mother comforts her sons , so will I comfort you ; and you will be comforted in Jerusalem
&quot; When you see it , you rejoice in your hearts ; your bones will be as tender grass , and the hand of the Lord will be known to His servants , and he will be angry with his enemies .
Behold , the Lord will come down in fire , and his chariot will be like a wind , to recompense with fierce anger , and to punish with fire .
For the Lord will execute judgment on every bloodthirsty person with fire and sword , and more will be slain by the Lord .
&quot; Those who are holy and clean will enter the gardens , and will eat pigs and cattle and abominations , after one of them , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and they will be destroyed together .
&quot; I know their deeds and their thoughts . The time will come , and I will gather all nations together , and they will see My glory .
&quot; I will make a sign among them , and I will send the escaped to the nations , to Hesh , and to Plah , and to Lud , and to Toba , and to Japheth ; and they have not heard My name , nor seen My glory in the vast islands of the sea ; and they will spread My glory among the nations .
&quot; They will bring back your brothers from all the nations , and they will bring them on horseback or in chariots , or in chariots , or in horseshoes , or in camels , to my holy mountain , Jerusalem , as a sacrifice to the Lord , as the children of Israel do in the house of the Lord with a clean vessel , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; I will also take from among them a priest for the Levites , &quot; said the Lord
&quot; As the new heaven and the new land which I will create will stand before me , so will your descendants and your names stand before me , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; At the beginning of the month and on the sabbath day every bloodthirsty man shall come and worship before me , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; They will go out and see the dead bodies of those who have rebelled against my people ; for their worms are not dead , and their fire is not extinguished ; and all the bloodthirsty will hate them .
Behold , the words of Jeremiah the son of Hilkiah , which were written in the priests of Natan in Benjamin--
The word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , when Josiah the son of Aram king of Judah was thirteen years old
From the time of Jehoia the son of Josiah king of Judah to the end of the year of Zedekiah the son of Josiah king of Judah , in the month of May the eleventh , when the people of Jerusalem were taken captive , the word of the Lord came to Jeremiah
Then Jeremiah said , &quot; The word of the Lord has come to me , saying ,
&quot; I have not created you in the womb ; I have known you ; you have not given birth ; I have sanctified you separately ; and I have sent you as a prophet to the nations .
&quot; I said , &quot; Lord , I don &apos;t know how to say this , for I am young
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; You shall not say that I am young , for to whom I have sent you , you shall go ; and I have commanded you what you shall say
&quot; Do not be afraid of them , for I am with you to save you , &quot; says the Lord
Then the LORD stretched out his hand upon my mouth , and said unto me , I have spoken unto thee what I said
Behold , I have set you today on the thrones of the nations , to expel , to destroy , to destroy , to overthrow , and to plant ;
Then came the word of the Lord again to me , saying , &quot; What have you seen , Jeremiah ? &quot; I said , &quot; I have seen a branch of an almond
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; You are right , for I have kept my word , and I have accomplished it
The word of the Lord came to me the second time , saying , &quot; What do you see ? &quot; And I said , &quot; I see a boiling pot , which is boiling from the north
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; A calamity will come from the north , and it will come upon all the inhabitants of the land
&quot; Behold , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; I will summon the people of the north , and they will come and attack the walls around the gates of Jerusalem , and all the cities of Judah ,
&quot; As for all the evil of these people , that they turn away from me , and burn incense to other gods , and kneel down to what their hands have created , I will issue My judgment against them .
&quot; Therefore rise and tell them all that I have commanded you , and do not be afraid of them , lest I cause you to be afraid before them .
Behold , I have made you this day a strong city , an iron pillar , a copper wall , against all the land , and against the kings , and the princes , and the priests , and against all the people of the land
&quot; They will attack you , but they will not prevail against you ; for I am with you to save you , &quot; says the Lord .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord , I remember the love of thy youth , and the love of thy marriage , how thou followedst me in the wilderness , and in the land which was not sown :
Then shall Israel be holy unto the LORD , as the first fruits of the earth : and whosoever shall eat of him shall be guilty , and a calamity shall come upon them , saith the LORD .
&quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , O house of Jacob and house of Israel ,
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; When your fathers saw what was wrong with me , they turned away from me , and followed the God of nothing , and became vain .
Neither did they say , &quot; Where is the Lord who brought us out of the land of Egypt , who guided us through the wilderness , through the land of pits and dry shadows , through which no man passed , and in which no man dwelled ? &quot;
I have brought you into a fertile land , where you will eat its fruit and its beauty ; but when you enter , you will defile My land , and make My inheritance abominable .
Neither did the priests say , &quot; The Lord is there , &quot; nor did those who preached the law know me , nor did the chief officers defy me , nor did the prophet prophesy by Baal , nor did he follow a god that was of no benefit .
&quot; I will therefore contend with you , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; and I will contend with your children
&quot; And you shall go to the island of Kitti , and see ; and send men to Kida , and be careful , and see whether there has been such a thing .
&quot; Has a nation replaced its God ? The truth is that it is not God ; but My people have replaced their glory with the God of no profit .
&quot; Woe to you , O heavens , for you are astonished and terrified and desolate , &quot; says the Lord
For they have done two evil deeds for my people : they have forsaken the spring of my living water , and they have dug a pond for themselves , a pond that cannot contain water .
Is Israel a servant , or a servant of the house ? Why is he a prey ?
And the young lion cried unto him , and cried with a loud voice , and made his land desolate ; and the cities were burned with fire , and no man dwelt therein .
And Noah and Reuben broke your heads , as they broke your heads .
&quot; Has this not come upon you from your own accord , and have you forsaken the Lord your God , when he guided you in your ways ?
Why do you drink the waters of the Nile in the way of Egypt , and the waters of the great river in the way of Assyria ?
&quot; Your own wickedness will punish you , and your transgressions will punish you , and you will know that you have forsaken the Lord , your God , and have not feared my heart , &quot; says the Lord , the Lord of hosts .
&quot; I have broken your yoke from ancient times , and I have cut off your cords , and you said , &apos; I will not serve the Lord , for you have committed adultery in the high mountains and under the green trees . &apos; Or , &apos; I have broken your yoke from ancient times , and I have cut off your cords , and you have said , &apos; I will not serve any god , who knows that you have committed adultery in the high mountains and under the green trees . &apos; 
&quot; But I have planted you as a grape tree of high standing , and as a true seed at all . How can you turn to me as a bad branch of a foreign grape tree ?
Even though you wash with alkali and soap , yet the traces of your iniquity are revealed before me , says the Lord Yahweh
How canst thou say , &quot; I am not defiled , neither have I followed the people of Baal ; and when thou seest the way of thy valley , thou knowest that which thou hast done ; and thou art a camel on the way , and a chariot on the way .
&quot; You are a wild donkey used to the wilderness , and it takes the wind when it wants to stir up its heart . Who can turn it when it is conceived ? He who seeks it will not be weak , and in his months he will find it .
&quot; I said , &apos; Do not make your feet without shoes and your throats thirsty , but say , &apos; This is vain ; I love other gods , and I will follow them . &apos; &quot;
How shall the house of Israel be ashamed when the thief is taken , and the kings , the princes , the priests , the prophets ,
And they said to the tree , Thou art my Father ; and to the stone , Thou art my birth ; and they turned their backs to me , and not their faces to me ; and they said in the time of trouble , Save us .
&quot; The number of your God is equal to the number of your cities , O Judah , when you are in trouble .
&quot; Why do you argue with me , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; and you have rebelled against me
&quot; I have reproached your sons and your daughters in vain , and they are not punished . Your own sword has swallowed up your prophets like a lion .
&quot; O you of this generation , see the word of the Lord : shall I make Israel a wilderness , or a dark place , and my people say , &apos; We will not return to you from our bondage&apos;
Will the virgin forget his adornment , or will the newlywed forget his beautiful garments ? My people have forgotten my countless days
How hast thou fashioned thy way , and demanded love ; and thou hast called the evil women to walk in thy way
And on thy collar is the blood of the innocent poor : thou shalt slay them , and shalt not find their pits , but for all these things .
And thou hast said , I am innocent ; and the wrath of the Lord shall be turned away from me ; behold , I will question thee , because thou hast said of thyself , I have no sin .
Why do you run east and west to change your way ? You will be ashamed of Egypt as you were ashamed of Assyria before
&quot; And you shall come out of Egypt with your heads held together ; for the Lord has forsaken those whom you have trusted in , and you shall not prosper because of them
&quot; It is said , &apos; If a man takes away his wife and leaves her , and becomes another &apos;s wife , will the former husband bring her back again ? If he brings her back , will not the land be greatly defiled ? But you and many of your loved ones will return to me for your wickedness , &quot; says the Lord .
And thou liftest up thine eyes unto the high places of the pure light , and where is there no prostitution ? and thou sitest by the wayside , and waitest , as the children of Aram were buried in the wilderness : and thy evil prostitution has spoiled the whole land
So the rain stopped , and the spring rained not ; and you still had the face of a prostitute without shame
&quot; Are you not going to cry to me from now on , saying , &apos; My Father , You are the Lord of my childhood
Behold , you speak evil again , and do evil again , and do it with your own selfishness ; and if you say this , it is evil to indulge your heart
&quot; And the Lord said to me in the days of king Josiah , &apos; You see nothing that the backward Israel has done ; they have gone up on high mountains , and they have prostituted themselves under green trees .
After he had done these things , I said , &quot; He will return to me , but he will not return to me ; and his treacherous sister Judah has also seen
For this cause I have given him rest , and I have seen Judah , his sister , who was not afraid , and went into prostitution
And the land was defiled because Israel neglected his lusts , and because of the stone and timber of prostitution
Even though all these things have happened , yet Judah , his treacherous sister , has not returned to me with all her heart , neither has she returned to me with falsehood , says the Lord
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; The Israel of the wicked is more manifest than the treacherous Judah
&quot; Go to the north and proclaim , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; Return , you Israel of the wicked , and I will not be angry at you , for I am merciful , and I will not be angry forever , &apos; &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; As long as you confess your iniquity , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; you have rebelled against the Lord your God , running east and west under the green trees , and have not listened to my voice , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; The Lord said , &apos; Come back , daughters of the wicked , for I am your husband , and I will bring you from one city to another , and from one tribe to another , to Zion .
And I will give you the ministers of My heart , and they will feed you with knowledge and wisdom .
&quot; In those days , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; there will be no more people in the land to say , &apos; The ark of the Lord ; &apos; nor to think , nor to remember , nor to feel lacking , nor to make it .
Then shall men call Jerusalem the throne of the Lord , and the nations shall assemble themselves in Jerusalem in the name of the Lord , and they shall no more follow their own stubborn wickedness .
&quot; In those days , you shall go with the house of Israel from the land of the north to the land which I have given to your fathers for a possession .
&quot; I said , &apos; How can I place you among the children and give you a beautiful land , the riches of all the nations ? &apos; And I said , &apos; You will call me your father , and you will no longer turn away from me .
&quot; You have dealt treacherously with me , O house of Israel , as a wife deals treacherously with her husband , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; Hear the voice of the people in the high places of clear light , the voice of the crying of the children of Israel , because of their rebellion , and because they forgot the Lord their God
&quot; Return , you children of your wickedness , and I will heal your wickedness : behold , we are come to you ; for you are the Lord our God
&quot; It is vain to look up from the small mountains or from the noise of the great mountains for help ; and Israel shall be saved , and in the Lord our God they will be faithful .
&quot; The shameful idol has eaten the sheep , the oxen , and the children of our fathers , which they have worked for ever since we were children .
Let us lie down in shame , and let shame cover us ; for we and our forefathers have often sinned against the Lord our God , and have not obeyed the word of the Lord our God , since they were children of God .
&quot; The Lord said , &quot; If you return to me , O Israel , and remove your abominations from before me , you will not be moved
Thou shalt swear by the Lord of everlasting life in truth , equity , and righteousness ; and the nations shall exalt themselves because of the Lord , and because of him they shall be blessed
Thus saith the LORD unto Judah and unto Jerusalem , Restore your land , and plant not it in thorns
O Jews and inhabitants of Jerusalem , circumcise yourselves , and turn to the Lord , and remove the filth of your hearts ; for I am afraid that my wrath will be kindled like a fire because of your evil deeds , and no one will be able to put it to an end .
&quot; You shall proclaim in Judah , and proclaim in Jerusalem , saying , &apos; You shall make a noise in the land , and cry out with a loud voice , &apos; Come together , that we may enter a strong city&apos;
A great flag shall be raised over Zion , and they shall flee , and not delay : for I will come from the north with evil and great destruction .
A lion has come up out of the wilderness , destroying the nations ; and he has moved himself out of his place , to make your land desolate , and your cities desolate , and there is no inhabitant .
Therefore you are clothed in sackcloth , and weep with a loud voice ; for the wrath of the Lord is not turned away from us .
&quot; In that day , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; the hearts of kings and princes will be destroyed , and the priests will be amazed , and the prophets will be amazed .
&quot; I said , &apos; Woe to you , Lord Yahweh , for you have deceived this people and Jerusalem with a great deal , saying , &apos; You shall have peace , and their sword will kill you and your life .
Then it will be said to this people and to Jerusalem , &quot; A fierce wind will come down from the heights of the clear light of the wilderness against my people , neither to shake them , nor to purify them .
And a greater wind shall come forth for me from these places ; and now I will make judgment against them again .
Behold , the enemy shall come up as a cloud , and his chariot as a wind , and his horses faster than an eagle : woe unto us , and we are defeated .
&quot; When will you wash away the evil in your heart , O Jerusalem , that you may be saved ? How long will evil be in your heart ?
There was a voice from Dan , and a voice from Mount Ephraim ,
&quot; Speak to the nations concerning the attack on Jerusalem , and say , &apos; A man who seeks out has come from a far place , and cries out to the cities of Judah with a loud voice .
&quot; He attacked Jerusalem around them as if he were guarding the fields , because he had betrayed me , &quot; says the Lord .
Your deeds and your deeds have provoked it . This is the result of your sins . It is indeed painful and harmful to your hearts .
O my lungs , O my lungs , my heart is sore , my heart is troubled within me , and I cannot remain silent , for I have heard the voice of the trumpet and the cry of war
There is no end to the message of destruction : for it is desolate for the whole earth : My tent is suddenly desolate , and my curtain breaks suddenly .
&quot; When will I see the great flag , and hear the sound of the horns ?
&quot; My people are foolish , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and they do not know me ; they are children of foolishness and ignorance ; they are wise to do evil , and they do not know good .
&quot; When I look at the earth , &quot; the prophet said , &quot; I do not expect it to be empty and chaotic ; and when I look at the heavens , the heavens are lightless
&quot; When I looked at the great mountains , I did not expect them to tremble ; and the small mountains were shaken and shaken
And I looked , and , behold , there was no man ; and the birds of the air fled .
&quot; I have seen , and I have not expected , that the fields would be turned into a wilderness , and that all the cities would be destroyed before the Lord because of His wrath
Thus saith the Lord ; Surely the whole land shall be desolate , and I will not destroy it
Therefore the earth will mourn , and the heavens above will be dark ; for I have spoken , and I have purposed , and I will not repent , nor turn away from doing it .
And the men of the cities fled , because of the noise of horsemen and archers , and went into the wilderness , and climbed up on rocks ; and the cities were left behind , and there was no man in them .
How shall it be done in thy desolate times , when thou art clothed in purple and red , and hast adorned thy eyes with gold and painted them , that thou mayest be glorified ? love thyself , and despise thee , and seek thy life
And I heard a voice , as the voice of a woman in labor , as the voice of the womb in pain , the voice of the woman of Zion ; and he breathed , and put forth his hand , and said , Woe unto me ; and before the slayer my heart was consumed .
&quot; While you are in the streets of Jerusalem , run and run , seeking in the open , and see if there is a righteous man , and if there is no truth , then I will forgive this city
&quot; Those of them who swear by the Lord of everlasting life are false .
&quot; Isn &apos;t your eyes , O Lord , righteous ? You have struck them , and they are not grieved . You have destroyed them , and they are not punished . They have made their faces hard as rocks , and they will not turn back .
&quot; I said , &apos; These are poor and foolish people , because they do not know the works of the Lord and the law of their God .
&quot; I will go to the nobles and speak to them , for they know the works of the Lord and the law of their God , and they will break the yoke and break the ropes in their hearts .
Therefore the lion of the forest will kill them , and the wolf of the night will destroy them , and the leopard will spy on them outside the city ; and whoever goes out of the city will be torn , for their sins are exceeding great , and the transgressions have increased .
How can I forgive you , when your children have forsaken me , and have taken away the oath that is not of God ? I have filled them , and they have committed adultery , and they have gathered themselves together in a house of prostitutes .
And they ran about like a full horse , and cried out to their neighbors &apos; wives
Then said the Lord , Shall I not plead guilty for these things , and shall I not recompense the people of this kind ?
&quot; You will destroy the walls of his vineyards , but you will not destroy them completely ; you will only remove his branches , for they are not of the Lord
&quot; The house of Israel and all Judah have come against me with great deceit , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; They disbelieve in the Lord and say , &apos; This is not Him , and the calamity will not come upon us , and the sword and the famine we do not see .
&quot; The word of the prophet will become a wind , and the way will not be in them ; and the plague will come upon them .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord , the God of hosts : &apos; Because I have spoken this word to the people , I will make my word a fire in your mouth , and I will make them wood , and the fire will consume them
&quot; I will send a people from afar to attack you , O house of Israel , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; a nation that is strong and old , and you do not know their words , nor do you understand their words .
Their bag of arrows is an open tomb ; they are all warriors .
&quot; They will eat all your crops and your food that your children should eat ; they will eat all your cattle and your sheep ; they will eat all your grapes and your fruitless fields ; and they will destroy with the sword the strong city on which you have relied .
&quot; I will not destroy you , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; until then
&quot; If the people say , &apos; Lord , our God , why do you do all these things to us ? &apos; Then you will say to them , &apos; How can you turn away from the Lord in your land , serving the gods of the nations , and serve the aliens in the land that is not yours ?
&quot; When he preached in the house of Jacob , and reported in Judah ,
&quot; O foolish and ignorant people , you have eyes that do not see , and ears that do not hear ,
&quot; How can you not be afraid of me , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; because I have set the limits of the sand for the sea for ever , and the waters cannot go beyond them ; therefore do you not be afraid before me , because the waves do not go beyond them , and they do not pass through them .
But the people are rebellious ; they are rebellious against Me , and go away .
Neither do they say in their hearts , &quot; Let us fear the Lord our God , who gives us rain in due season , autumn rain and spring rain , and a statute for our harvest forever and ever .
&quot; Your iniquity has turned these things away from you , and your iniquity has made you unfruitful .
For there are wicked men among my people , who hide themselves and spy like birds , and set traps for their enemies .
As the cage is full of birds , and as their rooms are full of deceit , so shall they be great and rich .
&quot; They are fat and rich , and do much evil , and do not redress for man , nor redress for the orphan , nor make him prosper , nor give up for the poor
Then said the Lord , Shall I not plead guilty for these things , and shall I not recompense the people of this kind ?
There are terrible and abominable things in the land
&quot; For the prophets prophesy falsely , and the priests have dominion over them , and my people love them ; and how will you do in the end ?
&quot; O Benjamin , you will flee from Jerusalem , and you will raise up your flags at Tikoa and at Berachileen ; for there is evil and great destruction , and you will look from the north
&quot; I will cut off the beautiful and tender woman of Zion .
And the shepherd shall bring his flock unto him , and set tents around him , every one in his own possession , and he shall feed the sheep .
Get up , and we will be able to go up in the middle of the day . Woe to you , for the day is declining , and the shadow of the night is delayed .
&quot; Arise , and we will go up at night , and destroy His palace .
&quot; For thus saith the Lord of hosts , &apos; You shall cut down trees and build strongholds against Jerusalem ; and this is the city to be punished , and it is full of oppression .
As the well springs out of water , so the city also springs out of evil ; and in it is heard violence and destruction , and the sick and the injured are before me .
&quot; O Jerusalem , when you have been taught , do not let my heart depart from you , and do not let me desolate you , and make you a dwelling place for no one
Thus said the Lord of hosts : &quot; The enemy will take away the remnant of Israel like a clear grape , and you will pick it again and again , and put it back in the basket
Behold , I am able to testify to those who speak , and to make them hear , whose ears have not been circumcised , neither can they hear : behold , the word of the Lord they deem to be a reproach , and not a joy
Therefore I am filled with the wrath of the Lord , and cannot bear it ; and I will pour it on the children of the streets , and on the youths of the congregation ; and every man with his wife , and every old man that is satisfied with his days , shall be taken captive .
&quot; Their houses , their fields , and their wives will be returned to others ; and I will stretch out my hand against the inhabitants of the land , &quot; says the Lord .
For they are greedy from the least to the greatest , and from the prophets to the priests they lie .
And they healed the wounds of my people gently , and said , Peace , peace ; but there is no peace .
Do they know that they are ashamed of their abominations ? Or are they not ashamed , nor do they know that they are ashamed ? Therefore they will fall among those who fall , and they will fall when I make atonement for them , says the Lord .
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; When you stand in the way and look , and visit the ancient way , which is a good way , you will walk in it ; and you will have rest in your hearts ; &apos; but they say , &apos; We will not walk in it
&quot; I have set up watchers over you , saying , &apos; Listen to the voice . &apos; But they say , &apos; We do not listen . &apos; 
Therefore listen , O nations , and know , O congregation , what they shall suffer .
&quot; O earth , when you hear me , I will bring evil upon this people , the fruit of their hearts , because they have not listened to My word , and they have rejected My teachings .
&quot; What is the use to me of the scent of Sheba , or of the iris from the far , or of sugarcane ? Your burnt offerings will not be acceptable to me , nor will I be pleased with your peace offerings .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord : &apos; I will lay a stumbling block before this people , and the father and the son will fall upon it together , and the neighbor and the friend will perish ,
Thus saith the Lord ; Behold , a people cometh from the north , and a great nation is stirred up from the earth
Their voices are like waves of the sea . They ride on horses , and they set out their armies , as those who are on the battlefield would attack you , O city of Zion .
And when we heard their wind , our hands were softened , And the pain seized us , And the pain was as a woman in labor .
&quot; You shall not go into the fields , nor walk on the roads ; for the sword of the enemy is round about you , and for fear .
O my people , you shall be clothed in linen , rolling in ashes ; and you shall be grieved , as the cry of a single child ; for the destruction shall come upon us suddenly .
I have made thee high among my people , to be a shelter , and to test them , that thou mayest know their works .
&quot; All of them are rebellious , and slanderers , and copper and iron , and do evil deeds .
The windmill burned , and the lead was burned ; and they refined and refined , and it was vanity ; and the evil-doers were not removed .
&quot; They shall call themselves a waste of silver , because the Lord has forsaken them
The word of the Lord came to Jeremiah , saying ,
&quot; When you stand at the door of the house of the Lord , and proclaim the word therein , and say , &apos; Enter this gate , all you Jews who worship the Lord , and listen to the word of the Lord
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Correct your deeds , and I will cause you to dwell in this place
&quot; Do not rely on falsehood , saying , &apos; This is the house of the Lord , the house of the Lord , the house of the Lord
If you correct your deeds and do justice between you and your neighbours honestly ,
&quot; He who does not oppress the dwellers and the orphans and widows , and does not pour out the blood of innocents in this place , and does not fall into the hands of other gods
&quot; I will make you dwell in this place , which I gave to your ancestors in the ancient days , forever and ever .
&quot; Behold , you rely on false and useless words
Ye steal , kill , commit adultery , swear , burn incense unto Baal , and follow other gods whom ye know not
&quot; And come to the house which is called My name , and worship before Me , and say , &apos; We are free ; are you doing such abominations ?
&quot; Will this house , which I have called it , be regarded in your eyes as a house of thieves ? I have seen it all , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; Go to Sheol , the place where I used to dwell in my name , and see what I have done to it for the sins of this people Israel .
&quot; Now , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; because of all these things which you have done , I have been warning you from the beginning , but you have not listened , nor called , nor promised
&quot; Therefore I will call it by my name , the house on which you rely , and the land which I have given to you and to your fathers , as I did to Sheol before .
&quot; I will drive you out of my sight , as I drive out all your brothers , even all the seed of Ephraim .
Therefore do not pray for this people , nor call for them , nor pray to Me for them , for I have not listened to you
Have you not seen what they did in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem ?
&quot; The child picks up wood , the father burns fire , and the woman bakes bread , and gives it to the afterlife , and pours out a drink offering to another god , and provokes me to anger
&quot; Have they provoked me to anger , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; or have they provoked themselves to shame ?
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will pour out my wrath and my wrath upon the people and the livestock of this place , and upon the trees of the field , and upon the fruit of the earth ; it shall be as a fire , and it shall not be quenched .
Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; &quot; You shall add the burnt offering to the sacrifice of peace , and eat the flesh
&quot; For on the day that I brought forth your fathers out of the land of Egypt , the burnt offering and the sacrifice of peace , I had no question , nor had I commanded them
&quot; I command them only this , saying , &apos; Listen to me , and I will be your God , and you will be my children , and you will be blessed by all the ways that I have commanded you .
But they have not listened , they have not listened , they have followed their own schemes , and their stubborn evil hearts , and they have not gone forward .
&quot; From the day your fathers came out of the land of Egypt to this day , I sent my servants the prophets to you , and sent them from the beginning every day
&quot; But you have not listened , nor listened , and have done evil with your necks , even more than your fathers
&quot; You shall tell them all these things , but they will not obey ; you shall call them , but they will not give you a promise .
&quot; You shall say to them , &apos; This is a nation that has not listened to the word of the Lord their God , and has not been taught , and the truth has been destroyed from their mouths .
&quot; Shear , O Jerusalem , and mourn in the high places of the clear light , for the Lord has forsaken the generations that provoked him to anger .
&quot; The Jews will do evil in my sight , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and they will set up abominations in the house that is called by My name , and will pollute it
&quot; They have built the high places of Dophith in the valley of Hinnom , so that they may burn their children in the fire ; neither have I commanded them , nor have I purposed them .
&quot; The day will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that this place will no longer be called the valley of Dophith and the valley of Hinnom , but the valley of slaughter ; for there will be no place to bury the dead in Dophith , nor will there be any place to bury the dead
&quot; Their bodies will feed the birds of the air and the beasts of the earth , and no one will drive them away .
&quot; In that day I will cause the voice of joy and gladness to cease in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem , the voice of the bridegroom and the bride ; for the land will be a desolation .
&quot; At that time , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; they will take out of the tomb the bones of the king of Judah , and the bones of his princes , the bones of the priests , the bones of the prophets , and the bones of the inhabitants of Jerusalem
And they shall be cast down under the sun , and under the moon , and under the stars of heaven , which they loved , which they served , which they followed , which they asked , which they worshipped ; and they shall no more be taken away , nor buried ; and they shall be as dung upon the earth .
&quot; The remnant of the wicked will choose death rather than life wherever I drive them , &quot; says the Lord of hosts .
Say unto them , Thus saith the Lord ; Will man fall , and not rise again ? and will man turn , and not turn again ?
Why do the people of Jerusalem stubbornly deny the truth , and keep their deeds of deceit , and turn not back ?
I have listened to their unrighteous words , and no man repents of his evil deeds , and says , &quot; What have I done ? Every one of them goes his own way , like a horse on the battlefield .
The birds of the air know the time of their coming and going , and the swallows and the white cranes wait for the time of their coming ; but my people do not know the law of the Lord .
&quot; Why do you say , &apos; We have wisdom ; the law of the Lord is here with us . &apos; Behold , the pen of the scribes is false .
The wise are ashamed and terrified , and are seized : how much more wise are they in their hearts when they forsake the word of the Lord ?
&quot; Therefore I will give their wives to others , and I will give their land to others for a possession ; for they are greedy , from the least to the greatest , and from the prophet to the priest , and they are liars .
And they healed the wounds of my people gently , and said , Peace , peace ; but there is no peace .
Do they know that they are ashamed of their abominations ? Or are they not ashamed of their shame , nor do they know that they are ashamed ? Therefore they will fall among those who fall , and they will fall when I make atonement for them , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; I will destroy them completely , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and there will be no grape on the vine , and no fruit on the flower tree , and the leaves will be dried up , and I will leave what I have given them , and I will go away from them
&quot; Why do we not sit still ? When we gather , we enter the strong city , and do not speak there silently ; for the Lord , our God , has made us silent , and has given us bitter water to drink , because we have sinned against the Lord .
We hoped for peace , but it was not good ; and when we hoped for healing , we feared and were afraid .
Hearing the sound of the enemy &apos;s horses in Dan , and his mighty horses whispering , the whole land trembled : for they came to destroy the land and all that was on it , and to destroy the city and its inhabitants .
&quot; Behold , I will bring a poisonous serpent among you , and he who does not obey the law will bite you , &quot; says the Lord .
I have sorrow , I wish to be comforted ; my heart is in me .
&quot; Behold , the cry of my people comes from far away , saying , &apos; Isn &apos;t the Lord in Zion , and isn &apos;t the King of Zion among them ? &apos; &apos; Why do they provoke me to anger with idols , and with the wicked God of the nations ? &apos;
The autumn is over , the summer is over , and we have not yet been saved
&quot; Because of the wounds of my people , &quot; said the prophet , &quot; I am also wounded , and I mourn , and fear seizes me .
Is there no perfume in Gilead ? Is there no doctor there ? Why should not my people be healed ?
May my head be water , and my eyes a fountain of tears , and I cry day and night for my people , the slain among them .
&quot; If only I had a lodging in the wilderness for the travellers , that I might go out from among my people , for they are all adulterers and a party of treacherous men .
&quot; They bend their tongues like a bow to speak lies , and they increase in power in the land , not for righteousness , but for evil , and they do not know Me , &quot; says the Lord .
Beware of your neighbours , and do not trust in your brothers ; for they deceive every man , and their neighbours deceive every man .
They deceive their neighbours , and do not speak the truth . They teach lies with their tongues , and they work hard in their iniquity .
&quot; You dwell among the wicked , and they do not know me for their wickedness , &quot; says the Lord .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Behold , I will melt them and make them bitter ; or how shall I do for the sins of my people ?
Their tongues are arrows of poison , and they speak deceitfully ; and they speak peacefully with their neighbours , but their hearts plot against them .
Then said the Lord , Shall I not avenge them for these things , and recompense them ?
I will weep for the mountains , I will weep for the fields of the wilderness ; for they are consumed , and no man passes by ; and no man hears the voice of the beasts ; and the birds of the air and the beasts of the earth have fled .
I will make Jerusalem a desolation , and a place for wild dogs ; and I will make the cities of Judah a desolation , and no man shall dwell therein .
&quot; Who is the wise man who can understand this ? Who is it that the word of the Lord has spoken to him , so that he can tell the story ? Why is the land as wilderness , and no man passes through it ?
&quot; For this people has rejected the law which I have set before them , and has not kept it , nor listened to my word , &quot; says the Lord
Act according to their own indomitable hearts , according to the teachings of their fathers , and according to the voice of the Philistines ;
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel : &apos; Behold , I will feed this people with raisins , and I will drink theirs with bitter water
And I will scatter them among nations , nations which they know not , nor their fathers ; and I will slay them with the sword , and consume them .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Think , and call the women that sing good songs , and send forth the women that weep ,
Let them mourn for us , and let their tears be poured out , and let the skin of our eyes be poured out .
For there is a cry in Zion to hear , saying , How we are defeated ! We are greatly ashamed ; we have left the earth and the earth , and men have destroyed our houses .
&quot; Women , listen to the word of the Lord , receive the word of his mouth , and teach your children to weep , and teach your neighbors to sing .
For he has come up for death , he has entered into our windows , he has entered into our palaces ; he will cut off the children from the outside , he will cut off the young men from the streets .
&quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; A man &apos;s body will be cast down in the field as dung , and as the grain of the harvester &apos;s field , and no one will pick it up .
Thus saith the Lord ; The wise man shall not exalt himself for his wisdom ; the mighty man shall not exalt himself for his might ; and the rich man for his riches .
&quot; For he is wise , and knows that I am the Lord , and that I am pleased to do righteousness and justice in the world , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; Behold , the days come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will punish all those who are circumcised , but whose hearts are not circumcised
For there was no circumcision for the nations , neither was there any circumcision in the hearts of Israel , neither was there any circumcision for Egypt , nor for Judah , nor for Edom , nor for the Ammonites , nor for Moab , nor for all that dwell in the wilderness
&quot; Listen to what the Lord has spoken to you , O house of Israel
&quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; You shall not do the works of the nations , nor be afraid of the heavens , for the nations are afraid of it .
The custom of the people is empty . They cut down a tree in the forest with axes , and the craftsmen made idols by hand
And they adorned him with gold and silver , and fixed him with nails and hammers , that he should not shake
&quot; He is like a palm tree , which is cut down , and cannot speak , nor walk ; and a man shall bear him ; and you shall not fear him ; he cannot bring forth evil , nor is he able to bring forth good .
&quot; There is no one like you , O Lord . You are a great and mighty name .
Who hath not feared thee , O king of the kingdoms of the nations ? It is right to fear thee : for the glory of the kingdom is not like thee among the wise of the nations .
All of them are beasts and fools . What is the doctrine of idols ? They are no more than wood .
And silver , which he brought , and gold , which he brought out of Ur , were the hands of craftsmen and silversmiths ; and clothing of blue and purple , the work of cunning craftsmen .
&quot; But the Lord is the true God , the living God , and the king forever ; and in anger and in tremendous earthquake , and in wrath , the nations will not be able to bear the burden
&quot; You shall say to them , &apos; No God who created the heavens and the earth will be cut off from the earth and from the heavens .
The LORD hath created the earth with his power , He hath established the world with his wisdom , He hath opened the heavens with his wisdom
With a voice , he stirred the air with water , and made the clouds rise from the earth &apos;s poles ; and he made electricity shining with the rain , and brought out winds from his storehouse .
Every man is a beast without knowledge . Every silversmith is ashamed of the idols he carries out . The idols he carries out are false and devoid of breath .
They are nothing , and they are a mischief , and they shall be extinguished in the time of reckoning .
Jacob &apos;s divisions are not like these : for he is the Lord of all things , and Israel is a branch of his inheritance ; and the Lord of all hosts is his name .
&quot; O you who are besieged , take your possessions out of the land when you have gathered them .
&quot; For thus says the Lord : &apos; In this hour I will cast out the inhabitants of the land like a slingshot , and I will harm them , and make them perceive
The people said , &quot; Woe to me ! I am injured , and my wounds are great . But I said , &quot; This is indeed my suffering , and I must endure it . &quot;
&quot; My tent is broken , My rope is broken ; My children are gone from me ; There is no man to support my tent , nor to hang up my curtain .
&quot; For the shepherds have become cattle , and have not asked the Lord ; so it is not well , and their flocks are scattered
Behold , there is a wind , and behold , the enemy is come , and great trouble is coming out of the north , to make the cities of Judah desolate , and to make them dwellings for the dogs of the field .
&quot; I know , O Lord , that the way of a man is not his own ; and he who walks is not able to set his own foot .
&quot; Repent not on me , O Lord , and do not punish me in your wrath ; for I am afraid that you will make me destitute
Let your wrath be poured out on the nations that do not know your name , and on the nations that do not call your name : for they have swallowed up Jacob , and not only swallowed him up , but have destroyed him , and have made his dwelling-place a wilderness .
The word of the Lord came to Jeremiah , saying ,
&quot; Hear the word of the covenant and tell the Jews and the inhabitants of Jerusalem
And he said unto them , Thus saith the Lord God of Israel ; Cursed is he that heareth not the word of this covenant
&quot; This is the covenant which I commanded your fathers on the day I brought them out of the land of Egypt from the furnace of iron , saying , &apos; Listen to me , and do all that I have commanded you ; and you will be my children , and I will be your God .
&quot; As I have sworn to your fathers , to give them a land of milk and honey , just as I have sworn to you today , &quot; I said , &quot; Lord ,
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; You shall proclaim all these words in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem , saying , &apos; You shall obey the word of this covenant
&quot; For from the day that I brought forth your fathers out of the land of Egypt , even to this day , I warned them , saying , &apos; Listen to me ,
&quot; But they did not listen , they did not listen , they did not follow their own stubborn wickedness ; therefore I brought upon them all the curses of the covenant , which I commanded them to do , but they did not do it
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; There is a conspiracy among the Jews and among the inhabitants of Jerusalem
&quot; They have turned away from following their fathers , and have sinned , and have not listened to My word , and have served Him with other gods ; and the house of Israel and the house of Judah have forsaken My covenant with their fathers .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord : &apos; I will bring evil upon them , and they will not escape ; and they will cry to me , but I will not hear them .
Then the inhabitants of the cities of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem went to pray to the gods whom they had burned incense for , but they did not save them in the time of trouble .
The number of your God , O Judah , is as the number of your cities , and as the number of the streets of Jerusalem , wherein you have built the altar of incense for the shameful Baal .
Therefore do not pray for this people , nor cry for them ; for when they cry to Me in distress , I will not hearken
&quot; What have you done in my house ? My beloved has departed from you with many lusts , and with the holy flesh ; and you will rejoice in your evil deeds .
&quot; Now the Lord has called you olive trees , beautiful and fruitful , and He has set fire on them with a loud voice , and the branches have been broken .
&quot; For it is written of the Lord , who brought forth all your armies , that he will bring evil upon you because of the evil of the house of Israel and of all the children of Judah , and because he has burned incense to Baal , and provoked me to anger , and because he has made himself ashamed
&quot; The Lord has directed me , and I know ; and you have shown me what they do .
&quot; But I am like a gentle lamb brought to the land of slaughter , and I do not know that they have plotted against me , saying , &apos; Let us destroy the trees and the fruit , and cut him off from the land of the living , that his name may not be remembered .
&quot; But I will see Your vengeance on them , O Lord of hosts , who judge according to righteousness , and examine the whole body and the whole soul , because I have revealed to You my case .
Therefore thus said the Lord concerning the Anakim , who sought your life , saying , &quot; You shall not prophesy in the name of the Lord , lest you die in our hand
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Behold , I will punish them , and their little ones , and they shall be put to death by the sword ; and their children shall perish by famine
And there was no remnant left for them : for in the year of recompense I will bring evil upon the Anakim .
&quot; When I contend with you , O Lord , you were righteous ; but I also had a theory with you : Why is the way of the wicked to prosper , and why is the way of the wicked to rest ?
Thou hast cultivated them , and they are rooted , and grown , and are fruitful ; and their mouth is near to thee , and their heart is far from thee .
Know me , O Lord , and see me , and test my heart toward thee ; and bring them forth as sheep that are slain , that they may wait for the day of their slaughter .
How long shall the land mourn , and the grass of the land be dried up ? for the wickedness of its inhabitants , and the cattle , and the birds , have perished ; and they said , He seeth not the end of us .
Then said the Lord , &quot; How can you run with a man who walks , when you are tired , and you run with a horse , when you are in the land of peace , and are secure , and in the forests by the river Jordan ?
For your brothers and your father &apos;s house have been treacherous against you , and they have cried with a loud voice behind you , and you will not believe them , even though they speak good words to you .
&quot; I have left my house , I have left my inheritance , I have given to his enemies what I love in my heart
My inheritance is to me like a lion in the forest ; he cries out against me ; therefore I hate him .
&quot; Will my inheritance be like a spotted bird against me , and will the bird attack him all around ? Go gather the beasts of the field , and bring them forth to eat .
Many shepherds have destroyed my vineyards , trampled upon my portion , and turned my good portion into a wilderness of desolation .
They have made the land desolate . The land is desolate , and they mourn at me . The whole land is desolate because no one cares
The sword of the LORD shall smite from one side of the earth even to the other side of the earth ; and the bloodthirsty shall not have peace .
&quot; They sow wheat , and they harvest thorns ; and labor and hardship are of no avail ; and you shall be ashamed of your inheritance because of the wrath of the Lord .
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; All the evil neighbours , who have taken possession of me and made the inheritance of the people of Israel , I will bring them out of the land , and I will bring all the children of Judah out of their midst
&quot; After I have taken them out , I will turn to them with mercy , and bring them back , every one to his own business , and every one to his own land
&quot; If they diligently learn the way of my people , and swear by my name , and say , &apos; I swear by the Lord who lives forever , &apos; as they taught my people by Baal , they will be established among my people
&quot; If they do not listen , then I will bring out the land , and bring it out , and destroy it , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; Thus says the Lord to me , &apos; Go and buy a belt of linen for your waist , and you shall not put it in the water
&quot; I bought a belt and a girdle , according to the word of the Lord .
&quot; The word of the Lord came to me the second time
&quot; Take your belt that you have bought , the belt that is on your waist , and go up to the River Berah , and hide your belt in the stone hole therein ;
&quot; So I went and hid my belt by the river Beer-sheba , as the Lord commanded me .
&quot; After many days the Lord said to me , &apos; Arise , go to the River Berah , and take out the belt that I commanded you to hide in it
Then I went to the River Berah , and cut out the waistband from the place where I hid it , and behold , it was defiled and useless
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord ; Thus will I destroy the pride of Judah and the great pride of Jerusalem
&quot; The wicked will be like this waistband , and they will become useless , because they will not listen to me , and will walk in their own stubborn hearts , and will worship other gods .
&quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; As the waistband straitens the waist , so I straitened all the house of Israel and all the house of Judah , that they may belong to me as children , and that I may be known , praised , and glorified ; but they did not listen
Therefore say to them , Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel , &apos; They will be filled with wine ; &apos; and they will say to you , &apos; Do we not know that they will be filled with wine ?
&quot; You shall say to them , &apos; Thus says the Lord : &apos; I will make all the inhabitants of this land drunken , the kings and the priests and the prophets who sit on the throne of David , and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem
&quot; I will make them meet one another , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; as fathers and sons meet one another ; and I will not be pitiful , neither will I be pitiful , neither will I be merciful , that I may destroy them
&quot; Listen , and listen to your ears , and be not proud ; for the Lord has spoken
&quot; The Lord your God has not brought darkness , neither have your feet stumbled on dark mountains before He gave you glory ; He has made light shadow and darkness , lest you look for light .
&quot; If you do not listen to this , I will weep in darkness for your pride ; and my eyes will weep and weep because the people of the Lord have been taken captive
&quot; You shall say to the kings and to the queens , &apos; Sit down , humble yourself ; for your scarf , your crown , has been removed .
The cities of the south shall be shut up , and no man shall be opened ; and Judah shall be taken captive , and it shall be taken away clean .
Take a look at the people from the north ; wherein is the multitude which was given to you , the multitude of your beauty ?
&quot; What will you say at that time , when the Lord has put your friends before you and has judged you ? Will not pain seize you like a woman in labor ?
&quot; If you say in your heart , &apos; Why have all these things come to me ? &apos; Your collar is uncovered , and your thighs are hurt , because of your great iniquity
&quot; Can the ancient man change his skin , or can the leopard change his spots ? If so , you who practice evil will do good .
Therefore I will blow them out with the wind of the wilderness , as the straw that is blown .
&quot; This is what you deserve , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and this is the portion which I will give you , because you have forgotten me and have relied on falsehood .
&quot; Therefore I will uncover your collar , and cover your face , and show your ugliness .
&quot; I have seen all your abominations , your adultery on the mountains of the fields , and your blasphemy , and your abominations . Woe to you , Jerusalem ! How long will it be before you will not be clean ?
The word of the LORD concerning the plague of the drought came to Jeremiah
And Judah mourned , and the gates of the city were desolate , and they sat upon the earth in darkness : and the cry of Jerusalem was heard .
And when they came to the pond , and saw that there was no water , they took the empty vessels , and turned back in shame , and bowed their heads
Woe to the people of the land ; for it is dried up because there is no rain on it .
And the deer of the field , when it hath begotten a young deer , forsaketh it , because there is no grass
The donkey stands in the high places of clear light , breathing like a wild dog ; for there is no grass , and the eyes are blind
&quot; Our iniquity , O Lord , though it was testified to us , and we asked You to do it for Your name &apos;s sake , We have denied You many times and have sinned .
Why dwellest thou in this land as a dweller , and as a wayfarer , and dwellest there only for one night , O Israel , who hopes to be his Savior in affliction ?
Why are you like a man who is astonished , and as a mighty man who cannot save a man ? You are still among us , O Lord , and we call you by your name ; do not leave us .
Thus saith the LORD unto this people ; They love to deceive , and they do not forbid their feet : therefore the LORD hath not pleased them ; remember their iniquity , and seek after their iniquity
&quot; The Lord said to me again , &quot; Do not pray for the benefit of this people
When they fasted , I did not hear their cry ; neither did I accept their offering of burnt offerings and sacrifices ; but I will destroy them with the sword , with famine , with pestilence ,
And I said , Alas , Lord Yahweh , the prophets used to say unto them , Ye shall see no sword , neither shall there be famine ; and the Lord will give you in this place everlasting peace .
&quot; Thus says the Lord to me , &apos; The prophets who trust in my name prophesy falsely . I have not sent them , nor commanded them , nor spoken to them . What they prophesy to you is false visions , and divination , and deceitful things , and deceit of the heart .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord concerning the prophets who prophesy in My name ; I have not sent them , nor do they say that there will be no sword or famine in the land ; but they will be destroyed by the sword or famine .
&quot; The people who listen to their prophecies will be thrown into the streets of Jerusalem by the sword of famine , and no one will be buried ; so will their wives and their children ; and I will bring their evil on them , or I will bring their evil on them .
Say thou unto them , Let my tears melt , and I will not rest day and night : for my people are sore wounded by the cleavage .
&quot; If I go out into the fields , I see a slain man ; if I enter into the city , I see a sick man because of the famine ; and the prophet who brought the priests into the land has no knowledge .
&quot; Have you abandoned Judah at all ? Have you despised Zion ? Why have you struck us so that we cannot be healed ? We have hoped for peace , but it has not been good . We have hoped for healing , but we have been frightened ,
&quot; We confess our sins , O Lord , and the iniquities of our fathers , because we have sinned against You .
&quot; For the sake of your name , do not despise us , do not despise the throne without your glory , and remember , and do not forsake the covenant which you made with us .
Is it not thee , O LORD , our God , that raineth in the God of the Gentiles , and the heaven raineth in its own abundance , and it is not thee , that we wait for thee , because all these things are thy creation ?
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; My heart is not troubled by this people , even though Moses and Samuel stood before me in prayer ; but you will drive them out of my sight , and let them go
&quot; They ask you , &apos; Where are we going ? &apos; And you tell them , &apos; Thus says the Lord : &apos; Whoever is dead will die ; and whoever is slain will be slain with the sword ; and whoever is hungry will be hungry ; and whoever is taken away will be taken away .
&quot; Then the Lord said , &apos; I have commanded four things to do to them : to kill with the sword , to tear the dogs apart , to devour the birds of the air and the beasts of the earth
And I will cast them away among all the nations of the earth , because of all that Manasseh the son of Hezekiah king of Judah did in Jerusalem
&quot; Who will pity you , O Jerusalem ? Who will grieve for you ? Who will turn to ask you for peace ?
&quot; You have turned away from me , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I have stretched out my hand against you , and have destroyed you , and I will not be able to bear my repentance .
&quot; I have shaken my people in the gates of the land , and they have lost their children , and I have destroyed them , and they have not turned away from the way that they used to walk .
And their widows are before me more than the sand , and I have brought the midday of death upon the mother of the young man , and pain and terror have come upon him suddenly .
&quot; The woman who has given birth to seven children is weak and weary , and is still in the daytime , and the sun is down , and she is ashamed ; and I will bring the rest of the people before their enemies with swords , &quot; says the Lord .
Woe to me , my mother , for you have raised me as a competitor in the land ; I have not borrowed from any man , neither have any men borrowed from me , and every man curses me
&quot; I need to strengthen you , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; to do good to you , and to make your enemies plead with you in the time of trouble and tribulation
&quot; Can a man break copper and iron , the iron of the north ?
&quot; For all your sins which you have committed in the four corners of the earth , I will take away your goods and your treasures , and I will give them to your enemies white and white .
And I will cause the enemy to bring the prey unto a place which thou knowest not : for the fire of my wrath shall burn you .
Remember me , O LORD , and be close to me , and avenge me against those who oppress me , and take not my life from them in anger , and know that I am oppressed for your sakes ,
&quot; I have eaten your word , O Lord , God of hosts ; and your word is the joy of my heart , for I am called by your name .
I am neither sitting in the banquet nor in joy ; I sit alone because of thy touch , because thou hast filled me with indignation
Why is my pain prolonged , and my wounds are not healed , and are not healed ? Have you deceived me like a dry river ?
Thus saith the Lord ; If thou returnest , I will bring thee again , that thou mayest stand before me ; and if thou separatest the good from the bad , then thou shalt be my mouth ; and they shall return unto thee , and thou shalt not return unto them .
&quot; I will make you a strong copper wall to this people , and they will attack you , but they will not prevail against you ; for I am with you to save you , to deliver you , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; I will deliver you from the hand of the wicked , and redeem you from the hand of the violent .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
&quot; You shall not marry a wife in this place , nor give birth to a daughter
&quot; For this is the word of the Lord concerning the children that are born in this place , and concerning their parents that are brought up in this land ,
And they shall die in bitterness , and no man shall weep , nor be buried ; they shall be as dung upon the earth , and shall be consumed by sword and famine ; and their bodies shall feed the birds of the air , and the beasts of the earth .
&quot; Do not enter into the houses of the slain , neither do you go to mourn , neither do you grieve for them , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; for I have taken away my peace , my mercy , and my compassion from this people , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; In this land shall all men die , small and great , and they shall not be buried ; no man shall weep for him , nor cut himself with a sword , nor make his head bald .
For they have lost , and no man breaketh bread for them ; for the dead comforteth them ; they have lost their father and their mother , and no man giveth them a cup of wine to comfort them .
&quot; You shall not enter the houses of the banquets , nor sit and drink with them
For thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts , the God of Israel ; Behold , the days of your life are before you , and I will make an end of the voice of joy and gladness , the voice of the bride and the bride , from this place
&quot; You have spoken all these words to this people , and they ask you , &apos; Why does the Lord say that he will bring this great evil upon us ? What is our iniquity ? What sin have we committed against the Lord our God ?
And thou saidst unto them , Thus saith the Lord ; Because your fathers have forsaken me , and have followed other gods , and have worshipped , and have not kept my law
And ye have done evil more than your fathers : for ye have done evil to every man according to your own stubborn heart , and have not listened to me .
&quot; Therefore I will drive you out of this land , and drive you straight to a land which you and your fathers did not know ; and you will serve other gods there day and night , for I will not give you mercy .
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; when no man shall again swear by the Lord , the Everlasting One , who brought the children of Israel up out of the land of Egypt
&quot; But I will bring them again into the land which I gave them to their fathers from the north , and I will bring them into the land which I gave them from the north , and I will bring them into the land which I gave them from the north ,
&quot; Then I will call upon those who hunt more fish , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will call upon the men of Israel who hunt more fish , and I will call upon those who hunt more fish , and I will hunt them out of the mountains , and out of the pits , and out of the pits ,
For my eyes see all their deeds , and they cannot hide their iniquity from me , nor conceal their iniquity from me .
I will double their iniquity and their iniquity , because they have defiled My earth with abominations , and filled My inheritance with abominations .
Thou art my strength , O LORD , and my shelter , and my refuge in the days of distress ; and the nations shall come to thee from the ends of the earth , saying , What our fathers endured is nothing but falseness , and nothing but vanity .
Can a man make God for himself ? It is not God , in fact
&quot; I will tell them , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; this is the time that they will know my hands and my power , and they will know that my name is the Lord .
The sins of Judah were recorded with iron pens and with diamonds ; they were engraved on their hearts and on the corners of the altar .
Remember their children , and the altar by the green trees in their high mountains , and the dolls ,
&quot; O mountains of my fields , I will give your goods , your treasures , and your high places to your enemies for your sins in the four corners of the earth .
&quot; And you will lose the inheritance which I have given you for your sins ; and I will make you serve your enemies in the land which you do not know , because you have set my anger on fire , and burned it for ever .
&quot; Woe to him who turns away from the Lord in his heart , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; who leans on the arm of the flesh and blood of men
&quot; For he will be like Dushanbe in the desert ; he will not see the joy , but will dwell in the dry land of the wilderness , in the base of which no man dwells .
Blessed is he who puts his trust in the Lord , and trusts in the Lord
He will be like a tree planted by water , rooted by rivers , when the heat comes , without fear , and its leaves will be green , and in the dry years there will be no fear , and there will be more than that .
The heart is more deceitful than all things , and is worse than all things . Who knows ?
&quot; I am the Lord of the hearts , the testator of the souls , to report to him according to all that every man does and according to all that he does .
He who does not have the righteous means is as if he had not laid down an egg for himself ; and when he reaches the middle age , all his wealth will be gone from him , and he will be a fool for ever .
&quot; Our sanctuary is the throne of glory , which was placed in high places from the beginning .
&quot; The hope of the Lord , O Israel , whoever turns away from you will be ashamed , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; for whoever turns away from me , their names will be written in the earth , for they have turned away from me the fountain of living water
&quot; Heal me , O Lord , and I will be healed ; save me , and I will be saved ; for you are my praise .
&quot; They said to me , &apos; What is the word of the Lord in it ? Let it be proved .
&quot; You know that I , who am a minister to you , have not turned away hastily , nor thought of the days of affliction ; and all the words that I speak are before you
&quot; Don &apos;t make me afraid because of you . You are my refuge in the days of distress .
Let those who oppress me be ashamed , but let them not be ashamed ; let them not be ashamed , but let me not be ashamed ; let the days of calamity come upon them , and they be destroyed twice as much .
&quot; Thus says the Lord to me , &apos; Go and stand at the gate of the people , which is the entrance of the king of Judah , and at the gates of Jerusalem
He said to them , &quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , you king of Judah , and all the people of Judah , and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem , whoever enters through these gates
&quot; Be careful , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that you do not carry a burden on the Sabbath , and enter the gates of Jerusalem
&quot; You shall not carry a burden out of your house on the Sabbath day ; no work shall be done on the Sabbath day except as a holy day , as I commanded your fathers .
&quot; But they have not listened , they have not listened with their ears , they have not listened with their necks , they have not been taught
&quot; If you will listen to me , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; you will not carry any burden into the gates of this city on the Sabbath day , but on the Sabbath day , and you will not do any work on that day .
Then the kings and the princes sitting in the throne of David , and they and the Jews , and the inhabitants of Jerusalem , shall enter into the gates of this city by carriage or by horse , and it shall be for ever .
And there shall come from the cities of Judah , and from all the places round about Jerusalem , from Benjamin , and from the high places , and from the mountains , and from the south , bringing burnt offerings , and peace offerings , and frankincense , and thanksgiving , to the house of the Lord
&quot; If you do not obey me , and do not take the Sabbath as a holy day , and bear the burden of the Sabbath , and enter into the gates of Jerusalem , I will set a fire in the gates , and it will burn the palace of Jerusalem , and it will not be quenched .
And the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , saying ,
&quot; Arise , and go down to the house of the carpenter , where I will make you hear my words
Then I went down to the carpenter &apos;s house , and met him turning wheels to make vessels .
When the craftsman &apos;s vessel of clay was broken in his hand , he made another vessel out of it , and how well he looked , how well he made it
And the word of the LORD came unto me , saying ,
And the LORD said , O house of Israel , will I not be able to make mud for you , O house of Israel , as the mud is in the hand of the carpenter , and as you are in my hand ?
When do I speak of a nation , or a nation , saying , &quot; I will take it out , and I will destroy it , and I will destroy it
&quot; If the nation I have spoken of turns away from their evil deeds , I will repent , and will not bring back the evil that I desire to do to them .
When do I speak of a nation , or a nation , that is to be established and planted
If they do that which is evil in My sight , and do not obey My word , I will repent , and will not give them the blessing which I have spoken .
&quot; Thus says the Lord to the Jews and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem , &apos; I will bring upon you a plague , and I will punish you , and you will turn your backs from the evil that you have done , and you will rectify your deeds .
But they said , &quot; It is in vain . We will do according to our own plans , and each one will do according to his own stubborn malice .
&quot; So thus says the Lord : &apos; Whoever has heard this , you and all the nations , has done an abomination to the children of Israel
Shall the snow of Lebanon be cut off from the rocks of the field , and the cold waters of the farthest places dry ?
My people have forgotten me , they have burned incense to false gods , they have stumbled on the ancient paths , and they have walked on slopes not built .
&quot; Their land is astonishment and ridicule ; and whoever passes through it will shake his head .
I will disperse them in the presence of the enemy like the wind of the east ; I will turn to them in the days of distress , and not toward them
Then they said , &quot; Come , we can plot against Jeremiah , for we have priests who preach the law , and wise men who plot , and prophets who prophesy , and they can &apos;t deny ; come , we can strike him with our tongues , and we won &apos;t listen to all his words . &quot;
&quot; Listen to me , O Lord , and hear the words of those who strive against me .
Remember how I stood before you , and I asked for them , that your wrath might be turned away from them .
Therefore give their children to famine and sword , and let their wives be barren and widows , and let their men be put to death , and let their young men be slain in battle .
&quot; When the enemy suddenly comes to them , let them hear the voice of mourning from their houses ; for they dug pits to catch me , and hid nets to stumble on my feet .
&quot; You know , O Lord , their plot to kill me ; do not forgive their iniquity , nor blot out their iniquity from before You ; let them fall before You , and punish them in the time of Your wrath .
&quot; Go , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; to buy the pottery of the carpenter , and bring the elders of the people , and the elders of the priests
&quot; Go out to the entrance of the valley of Hinnom , which is called Harsi , and proclaim the words which I have commanded you .
&quot; Now , O king of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem , listen to the word of the Lord , the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , saying , &apos; I will bring evil upon this place , and all who hear will hear
For they , and their fathers , and the kings of Judah , have forsaken me , and have regarded this place as ordinary , and have burned incense there unto other gods , whom they knew not , and have filled it with the blood of innocent men .
And he shall build the high place of Baal , that he may burn in the fire his son as a burnt offering unto Baal : it is not my commandment , nor my counsel , nor my heart &apos;s will .
&quot; Therefore the days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that this place will no longer be called the valley of Dophith and the valley of Hinnom , but the valley of slaughter
&quot; In this place I will destroy the plots of Judah and Jerusalem , and I will put them under the sword before the enemy , and under the hand of those who seek their life ; and I will feed their bodies to the birds of the air and to the beasts of the earth .
I will make this city to be a mockery , and all those who pass by will be a mockery of the evil that is done to it .
I will make them to be encircled in embarrassment , when their enemies and those who seek their lives will be embarrassed , eating the flesh of their children and the flesh of their friends .
And thou shalt break the bottle in the sight of him that is with thee ;
And he said unto them , Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Likewise will I break this people and this city , as a man breaketh the stones of a carpenter , so that there shall be no more carpenter ; and they shall bury their heads in Tophet , and there shall be no place to bury them .
&quot; I will do this to this place and to all its inhabitants , and I will make this city like Tophith , &quot; said the Lord
&quot; The houses of Jerusalem and the palaces of the kings of Judah have been defiled ; the houses of the heavenly images on which they have burned incense , and poured out their sacrifices to other gods , will be like the houses of Dophite .
Then Jeremiah returned from Dophith , the place where the Lord had sent him to prophesy , and stood in the house of the Lord , and spoke to the people
Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; &quot; I will bring on this city and on all the cities that belong to it all the evil that I have spoken , because they are stiff-necked and do not listen to my words .
Then Baruch the son of Nun the priest , who was over the house of the Lord , heard Jeremiah prophesy concerning these things
Then he struck Jeremiah the prophet , and put his fetters in the high gate of Benjamin in the house of the Lord
Then the next day Baashaur delivered Jeremiah out of his fetters , and Jeremiah said to him , &quot; The Lord does not call your name Baashaur , but Magor Mizpah ,
&quot; For thus says the Lord : &apos; I will cause you to tremble , and you will cause all your friends to tremble , and they will fall under the sword of the enemy , and you will see with your own eyes , and I will deliver all the Jews into the hand of the king of Babylon , and he will take them captive to Babylon , and he will kill them with the sword
And I will deliver into the hand of their enemies all the goods of this city , and all the labour thereof , and all the treasures thereof , and all the treasures of the kings of Judah ; and they shall bring them into Babylon as robbers .
&quot; You , Baashaur , and all those who dwell in your house will be taken captive . You and all your friends will go to Babylon , where they will die and be buried , as you falsely prophesied to them .
&quot; You have guided me , O Lord , and I have listened to your counsel ; You are stronger than I , and have overcome me ; I am always a laughter , and every man plays with me .
&quot; Whenever I speak , I crie out with a cry , and say , &apos; There is violence and destruction ; for the word of the Lord is my reproach and my derision all the days long .
&quot; If I say , &apos; I will no longer call on the Lord , nor speak in His name , &apos; I will feel in my heart as if there was a burning fire , which is confined to my bones , and I will not be able to resist it , nor will I be able to restrain myself .
I have heard the slander of many , and all around me is terror ; for my friends , whom I know , have also spyed on me , lest I fall down and say , &quot; Tell him , and we will tell him ; or if he is tempted , we will prevail over him , and we will avenge him . &quot;
&quot; But the Lord is with me as a mighty warrior ; so they who oppress me will stumble , and will not prevail ; and they will be greatly ashamed , and will never be forgotten , because they do not have wisdom .
&quot; Lord of hosts , who test the righteous , who watches the heart and the soul , let me see that you repay them , for I have revealed to you my case .
Sing unto the LORD , and praise the LORD : for he hath delivered the life of the poor out of the hand of the wicked .
Cursed be the day that I was born , and cursed be the day that my mother bore me
&quot; And he wrote to my father , saying , &apos; You have a son , which rejoices my father ; let him be cursed
Let him hear the voice of mourning in the morning , and let him hear the cry at noon , as the Lord has overturned cities without repentance .
&quot; For he did not kill me when I was not born , and made my mother my grave ; and the womb is often great .
&quot; Why have I been born in labour and sorrow , and my years have been destroyed by shame ?
Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , and the king of Zedekiah sent Baashaur the son of Machiah , and Zephaniah the priest the son of Maaseiah , to Jeremiah , saying ,
Ask the Lord for us , that he may come against us for the king of Babylon , Nebuchadnezzar , or that the Lord may send forth the king of Babylon from among us , according to all his wondrous works
And Jeremiah said unto them , Thus shall ye say unto the house of Zedekiah
Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel ; &quot; I will turn back the weapons of your hand , the weapons of the battle that you fought against the king of Babylon outside the city , and against the Chaldeans who besieged you , and I will gather them all together in this city
And I will attack you in anger , and in wrath , and in great anger , with my hand stretched out , and with a mighty arm ,
And the inhabitants of the city shall be struck with a great plague , both men and cattle .
Then I will deliver the house of Zedekiah king of Judah and his servants , and the remnant of the city from the plague , and from the sword , and from the famine , into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , and into the hand of their enemies , and into the hand of those who seek their life ; and the king of Babylon will slay them with the sword , and he will not spare them , neither will he have mercy , nor will he have pity , says the Lord
&quot; Thus says the Lord to this people , &apos; Behold , I have set before you the way of life and the way of death
&quot; Those who dwell in this city shall die by the sword , and by famine , and by pestilence ; but those who go out and besiege you , the Chaldeans , shall live , and take their own lives as a prey .
&quot; I will turn my face to this city , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and it will be handed over to the king of Babylon , and he will burn it with fire
&quot; As for the house of the king of Judah , listen to the word of the Lord
Thus saith the Lord , O house of David ; You shall do righteousness every morning , and deliver the captive out of the hand of the oppressor ; for fear of my wrath , because your evil deeds are like fire , and no man can extinguish them .
&quot; Behold , I am an enemy to you , O inhabitants of the valley , O inhabitants of the rock of peace , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; who can come down and attack us , and who can enter into our dwellings ?
&quot; I will punish you according to your deeds , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will send a fire into the forest of Jerusalem , and I will burn all that is around him with fire
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; Go down to the king of Judah &apos;s house , and speak in it these words
&quot; Hear the word of the Lord , O king of Judah , who sits at the throne of David , you and your servants , and all the people who enter the gates of the city
Thus saith the LORD ; You shall do justice and righteousness , and deliver the captive from the hand of the oppressor ; you shall not defraud the dwellers and the orphans and the widows ; you shall not oppress them ; and you shall not shed the blood of the innocent in this place .
&quot; If you believe that you do this , there will be a king sitting on the throne of David and his servants and the people , both in carriages and in horses , entering through the gates of this city
&quot; If you do not listen to these words , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; I swear by myself that this city will become a desolation
&quot; Thus says the Lord concerning the house of the king of Judah , &apos; I see you as Gilead , and as the top of Lebanon ; but I will make you a wilderness , and a city of no man
&quot; I will prepare those who destroy you , and they will attack you with instruments , and they will cut down your beautiful cedar trees , and throw them into the fire .
&quot; Many nations will pass through this city , saying to their neighbors , &quot; Why does the Lord do this to this great city ?
&quot; They will answer , &apos; It is because they have forsaken the covenant of the Lord their God and worshipped other gods .
Do not weep for the dead , nor grieve for him ; but weep for the people who have left their homes , for they shall not return , nor see their homeland again .
For the Lord said , &quot; Saron the son of Josiah king of Judah , who came out of this place , is the successor of Josiah his father to be king , and he shall not come again to this place .
&quot; But if you die in the land of captivity , you shall not see it again .
Woe to those who do not build houses , who do not build public buildings , and who do not pay the wages of the hands of men ,
He said , &quot; I will build for myself a large house , an open house , and open windows for myself . The walls of this house are of acacia wood , and the buildings are of fine paint .
&quot; Have you been king in order to build a palace of cedars ? Did not your father eat and drink , and do justice and righteousness ? Then he was blessed
&quot; When he has justified the poor and the needy , then he has rejoiced ; Knowest thou that I have no concern for this , saith the Lord ?
Only your eyes , and your heart , will be attentive to greed , to the blood of innocents , to oppression and violence .
Therefore thus says the Lord concerning Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah : &quot; No man shall mourn for him , saying , &apos; My brother , &apos; or &apos; My sister , &apos; nor shall he mourn for him , saying , &apos; My Lord , &apos; or &apos; The glory of my Lord , &apos;
&quot; He is buried like a donkey , to be brought out and thrown outside the gates of Jerusalem
&quot; You shall raise up your voice in Lebanon , in the voice of Bashan , and in the voice of Abilene ; for you have destroyed all that you loved .
&quot; When you were prosperous , I spoke to you , but you said , &apos; I do not listen . This is how you have been since you were a child , and you do not listen to me .
Your shepherds will be swallowed up by the wind , and those whom you love will be taken captive ; and you will be ashamed of all your evil deeds
&quot; When pain comes to you , as pain to a woman in labor , when you dwell in Lebanon in a bush of acacia trees , how shall you be pitied ?
And the Lord said , &quot; Gonijah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah , even though it is the ring that I have sealed on my right hand , I swear by my eternal life , I will take it away from you
And I will deliver you into the hand of those who seek your life , and into the hand of those whom you feared , Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , and into the hand of the Chaldeans
&quot; I will also drive you and your mother who gave birth to you to another country , and not to the place where you were born , and you will die there
But he will not return to the land that he desired to return to
Is this man a vessel that is neglected , a vessel that is destroyed , a vessel that is not loved ? Why is he and his seed driven to a place that is not known ?
O land , O land , O land , when you hear the word of the Lord
&quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; Tell me that this man is barren , and that he shall not be able to live a lifetime ; for none of his seed shall be able to be able to sit on David &apos;s throne and rule over Judah .
&quot; Woe to the shepherds , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; who have scattered the sheep of my pasture
&quot; The Lord , the God of Israel , has reproached the shepherds of his people , saying , &apos; You have scattered my flock , and have not looked after them ; I will requite you for your evil deeds , &apos; says the Lord
&quot; I will gather the remnant of my flock out of all the countries where I have driven them , and I will bring them back to my fold , and they will be multiplied .
&quot; I will set up a shepherd over them , and I will feed them ; and they will no longer be afraid , nor be afraid , nor lack one , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will raise up to David a righteous seed , who will reign , and act wisely , and do justice and righteousness in the land
In his days Judah shall be saved , and Israel shall dwell safely ; and his name shall be called the righteousness of the Lord our God
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; when no more man shall swear by the Lord , who has ruled over Israel from the land of Egypt for ever and ever
&quot; But they shall swear by the LORD , who is the Lord of everlasting life , concerning the seed of the house of Israel , which came from the north , and from all the nations to which they were driven ; and they shall dwell in the land .
Concerning the prophets , my heart is grieved in me , and my bones tremble : for by the word of the Lord and His holiness , I am as a drunken man , as a man overcome by wine
The land is full of prostitutes , and the land mourns because of their deeds , and the fields of the wilderness are dried up ; their ways are evil , and their might is wicked .
Even the prophets and the priests were defiled ; and I saw their evil in my house , says the Lord .
Therefore their way will be like a slippery path in darkness , and they will be pursued , and they will fall in it ; for in the year of persecution I will bring evil upon them , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; I have seen foolishness in the prophets of Samaria , who prophesied by Baal , and led my people Israel astray .
I have seen abominations in the prophets of Jerusalem ; they commit adultery and deceit ; and they are firm in the hands of the wicked ; and no one turns away from his evil deeds ; they are before me like Sodom , and the inhabitants of Jerusalem like Moor .
Therefore thus says the Lord of hosts concerning the prophet , &quot; I will feed them with raisins , and I will drink them with bitter water ; for the blasphemy that came out of the prophet of Jerusalem was spread throughout all the land
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; These prophets prophesied unto you , saying , Ye shall not hear them ; but they have taught you in vanity , and the visions which they have spoken are from their own hearts , and not from the mouth of the Lord .
&quot; They say to those who despise me , &apos; The Lord says , &apos; You will have peace ; &apos; and to all those who walk in their own stubborn hearts , &apos; No evil shall come upon you . &apos; 
Who stands in the congregation of the Lord , and hears and understands His words , and who listens to His words ?
Behold , the wrath of the LORD is come forth like a stormy wind : it is a fierce cyclone , and it shall turn on the heads of the wicked .
&quot; The wrath of the Lord will not be turned away , but it will come straight to the fulfillment which He has appointed in His heart , and you will understand it in the days to come .
&quot; I did not send the prophets ; they ran away ; I did not speak to them ; they prophesy
&quot; If they stand in My assembly , they will make My people hear My words and turn away from the evil way and the evil that they have done .
&quot; I am not the God of the near , nor the God of the far , &quot; said the Lord .
&quot; Will a man hide himself in secret so that I do not see him , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and will I not fill the heavens and the earth
&quot; I have heard the prophets say , &apos; I have dreamed , I have dreamed , &apos; a false prophecy which they have spoken in my name .
How long will they wait for the prophets who prophesy falsely , the prophets who prophesy deceitfully with their own hearts ?
&quot; All of them will tell their dreams to their neighbors , saying , &apos; I want to make my people forget my name , just as their ancestors forgot my name in Babylon .
&quot; A prophet who dreams can tell that dream ; and a man who receives My words can speak My words in truth ; and how can a branch be compared to a wheat , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; Isn &apos;t my word like fire , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; or like a hammer that breaks a rock ? &quot;
&quot; The prophets have stolen My words from their neighbours , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; so I will be against them
&quot; The prophets spoke with their tongues , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; and I will be against them
&quot; I will be against them , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; those who prophesy with illusions and describe them with lies and pride , and lead my people astray , and I have not sent them nor commanded them , and they are of no use to this people , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; When the people , the prophets and the priests , asked you , &apos; What is the Lord &apos;s word ? &apos; you said to them , &apos; What is the Lord &apos;s word ? &apos; &apos; I will leave you , &apos; said the Lord
&quot; Whether it be the prophet , or the priest , or the people , who speak by the word of the Lord , &quot; I will punish that man and his family
&quot; Every one of you shall say to his neighbor , and every one to his brother , &apos; What is the answer of the Lord ? What has the Lord said ?
&quot; You shall no longer question the word of the Lord , for it will be a burden to you , because you have invented the word of the Lord our God , the God of Armies , the Everlasting God .
&quot; You shall say to the prophet , &apos; What is the answer of the Lord to you ? What has the Lord said ?
&quot; If you speak the word of the Lord , the Lord will say , &apos; Because you have spoken the word of the Lord , I have sent men to you to tell you not to speak the word of the Lord
Therefore I will forget you at all , and I will forsake the city which you and I have given to you and to your fathers
And I will bring upon you everlasting humiliation and everlasting shame , which cannot be forgotten .
Then Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon took Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah , and the princes of Judah , and the craftsmen and the ironsmiths , from Jerusalem , and brought them to Babylon ; and after this the Lord said to me , &quot; Behold , two baskets without fruit are laid before the house of the Lord
A basket is good without fruit , as if it were first ripe ; and a basket is bad without fruit , so bad that it cannot be eaten
Then the Lord asked me , saying , &quot; What do you see , Jeremiah ? &quot; I said , &quot; I see no fruit , good and good , and bad and bad , and bad and bad , and they cannot be eaten
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord , the God of Israel ; The captive Jews , whom I have sent out of this land unto the land of the Chaldeans , I will look upon them as they are without fruit , that I may profit them
&quot; I will take care of them , and benefit them , and bring them back to this land ; and I will build them , and I will not destroy them , nor plant them , nor cut them out .
&quot; I will give them my heart to know that I am the Lord , and they will be my children , and I will be their God , because they will return to me with a single heart .
Thus saith the LORD ; I will send forth the house of Zedekiah king of Judah , and his princes , and the remnant of Jerusalem that remaineth in the land , and the Jews that dwell in the land of Egypt , as a very evil fruit that cannot be eaten
&quot; I will send them forth , and throw them away in all the nations of the world , and I will cause them to suffer calamity , and I will drive them away from every place where I have driven them , to be a reproach , a laugh , a derision , and a curse .
&quot; And I will bring upon them swords , and famine , and pestilence , and I will destroy them from the land which I have given them and their fathers .
The word of the LORD concerning the people of Judah came to Jeremiah in the fourth year of Joiah the son of Josiah king of Judah , in the first year of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon
Then the prophet Jeremiah spoke these words to all Judah and to all the inhabitants of Jerusalem
&quot; From the thirteenth year of Josiah the son of Aram king of Judah to this day , and throughout the twenty-three years , the word of the Lord has come to me , and I have told you from the beginning , but you have not listened .
&quot; The Lord has risen from the beginning and sent His servants the prophets to you , but you have not listened , neither have you listened with your ears
&quot; When you return from the evil way and the evil that you have done , you will live in the land which the Lord gave you and your fathers in the ancient days for ever and ever .
&quot; Do not follow other gods and worship them , and do not provoke me to anger because of what you do with your hands ; otherwise I will not harm you .
&quot; But you have not listened to me , and have provoked me to anger , and have taken yourselves captive by what you have done with your hands , &quot; says the Lord .
Therefore thus saith the Lord of hosts ; For ye have not listened to my word
&quot; I will call the people of the north , and Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , my servant , to attack the land , and the inhabitants thereof , and all the people that are around it ; and I will destroy them in all their deeds , and they will be astonishment , and a mockery , and a perpetual desolation , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; And I will stop the voice of joy and gladness , the voice of the bridegroom and the bride , the voice of the grinding , and the light of the lamp from among them .
The whole land will surely be desolate and terrible . These people will serve the king of Babylon for seventy years
&quot; At the end of seventy years , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; I will punish the king of Babylon and his people , and the land of the Chaldeans , because of their iniquity , and they will make it desolate forever .
&quot; And I will bring to the land all that I have spoken to it , which is written in this book , and which Jeremiah spoke to these nations
For I will make the Chaldeans slaves for many nations and great kings , and I will recompense them according to their deeds and according to their hands .
Thus saith the LORD God of Israel unto me ; Take this cup of the wine of wrath out of my hand , and drink it for the people of the nations to which I have sent thee
&quot; When they have drunk , they will turn eastward and westward , and they will be mad ; for I have brought the sword among them
&quot; I took this cup from the hand of the Lord , and drank it for the people of the nations to which the Lord sent me
Jerusalem and the cities of Judah , and the kings of Jerusalem , and their princes , have desolated them , as it is today , with astonishment , and with derision , and with curse
Pharaoh king of Egypt , and his servants , and his princes , and his people
and the people of the tribe , and the kings of Uzziah , and the kings of the Philistines , and Assyria , and Gaza , and Ephraim , and the remnant of Assyria
Edom , Moab , and the children of Ammon
the kings of Tyre , the kings of Sidon , the kings of the islands of the sea
Dan , and Timah , and Bush , and all that shave their heads round about ,
the kings of Aram , the kings of the people of the wilderness ,
the kings of the heart , the kings of Ephraim , the kings of Medezia
The kings of the north , and the kings of the far north , and all the nations of the earth , shall drink ; and the king of Shechem after him shall drink .
Say to them , &quot; Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , &apos; You shall drink , and you shall be drunk , and you shall vomit , and you shall fall , and you shall not rise again , because I have brought the sword upon you
&quot; If they will not take this cup from you , then say to them , &apos; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; You must drink
&quot; Shall you be exempt from punishment from the beginning of the evil that I have done in the city which I have called My name ? You will not be exempt , for I have commanded the sword to come upon all the inhabitants of the earth , &quot; said the Lord of hosts .
Therefore prophesy to them all these words against them , saying , &quot; The Lord will roar from heaven , and from the Holy One , and from his flock , and he will cry to all the inhabitants of the earth like a roar of grapes .
&quot; There will be a noise to the depths of the earth , because the Lord fights with the nations , and He will question those who have blood , and He will give the sword to the wicked , &quot; says the Lord .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Behold , a calamity shall come from the land to the land , and a great wind shall blow from the earth
&quot; In that day , from one side of the earth to the other shall be the slain of the Lord ; no one shall weep , nor be taken away , nor be buried , nor be turned into dust in the earth .
O shepherds , weep and cry ; O heads of the multitude , roll in the ashes ; for the days of your slaughter are come , and they shall be scattered , and you shall be broken as a beauty .
The shepherds have no way to escape , nor can the heads of the masses escape
&quot; Hear , O LORD , the voice of the shepherds , and the voice of the heads of the people ; for the LORD has made their pasture a desolation
For the LORD &apos;s wrath is kindled , and the flock of peace is silent
He went away in secret like a lion , and their land became terrible because of the oppression of the sword , and because of his fierce anger .
&quot; When Jehoia the son of Josiah king of Judah came to worship him , the word of the Lord came to Jeremiah
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; You shall not be cut off in one word from the people of the cities of Judah , who come to worship in the house of the Lord , when you stand in the court of the house of the Lord ,
Or if they obey , and turn their heads away from the wicked way , so that after me they will not repent of the evil that they have done , and of the evil that they desire to do , and will be healed with them
Say unto them , Thus saith the Lord ; If ye will not obey me , neither will ye keep the law which I have set before you
&quot; You have not listened to the words of my servants the prophets , whom I sent to you from the beginning ;
&quot; I will make this house like Sheol , and make this city the curse of all the nations of the earth
The prophet the priest and all the people heard these words which Jeremiah spoke in the house of the Lord
When Jeremiah had finished all that the Lord had commanded him to say to all the people , the priests , the prophets , and all the people came and seized him , saying , &quot; You must die
&quot; Why do you prophesy in the name of the Lord , saying , &apos; This house will be like Sheol , and this city will become a wilderness without inhabitants ? &apos; Then all the people gathered themselves together in the house of the Lord to Jeremiah
When the princes of Judah heard this , they went up from the king &apos;s house to the house of the Lord , and sat at the new door of the house of the Lord
&quot; The priest , the prophet , said to the leader and to the people , &apos; This man is to die , for he has spoken of a warning against this city , as you have heard in your ears
Then Jeremiah said to the chiefs and to the people , &quot; The Lord has sent me to prophesy against this house and against this city , saying all these words which you have heard
&quot; Behold , the Lord your God will repent , and will not bring back the evil that he has spoken to you , when he will correct your deeds and listen to the word of the Lord your God .
&quot; As for me , I am in your hands , and your eyes see what is good and what is right ; so be with me
&quot; But you will know that if you execute me , you will return the blood of the innocent to you , and to this city , and to its inhabitants ; for the Lord has sent me to you , and has spoken all these words to your ears .
Then the chief captain and the people said to the priest and to the prophet , &quot; This man is not worthy of death , for he speaks to us in the name of the Lord our God
And the elders of the land arose , and spoke to the people of the congregation , saying ,
In the days of Hezekiah king of Judah , Micah of the Moors prophesied to all Judah , saying , Thus saith the Lord of hosts , Zion shall be sown as a field , Jerusalem shall be desolate , and the mountains of this house as the heights of the jungle
Is it not Hezekiah king of Judah and all Judah who executed him ? Is it not Hezekiah who feared the Lord and pleaded for His mercy ? Then the Lord repented and did not bring to them the evil that He had spoken to them ; and if Hezekiah were executed , we would have done great evil and have taken our own lives .
And another prophesied in the name of the Lord , Uriah the son of Shemaiah of the Philistines , which prophesied according to all that Jeremiah had said , to attack this city and this land
And when king Jehoiakim and all his mighty men and his princes heard the words of Uriah , the king desired to put him to death ; and when Uriah heard them , he was afraid , and fled to Egypt
Then king Jehoiakim sent Eleazar the son of Ahab , and led a few men to Egypt
And they took Uriah out of Egypt , and brought him to king Jehoiakim ; and the king struck him with the sword , and cast his body into the graves of the people .
But Ahigan the son of Shaphan , who was to protect Jeremiah , did not deliver him into the hand of the people to put him to death .
And it came to pass , when Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah , the son of the tribe of Zedekiah , was ascended , that the word of the Lord came to Jeremiah
&quot; Thus says the Lord to me , &apos; You shall make a rope and a yoke on your neck ,
By the hand of the servants of the house of Zedekiah king of Judah who came to Jerusalem , they brought the ropes and the yoke to the king of Edom , to the king of Moab , to the king of Ammon , to the king of Tyre , to the king of Sidon
And he charged his servants to tell their masters , saying , Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel
&quot; I have created the earth and the people of the earth , beasts , with great power and outstretched arm , and have given it to whomever I will
&quot; Now I have given this land to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , my servant , and I have given to him the beasts of the field .
And all the nations shall serve him and his seed , until the day that is announced in his own land , when the kingdoms and the great kingdoms shall make him their servant .
&quot; I will punish that nation with the sword , with the famine , with the pestilence , and with the punishment , and destroy it by the hand of the king of Babylon , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; whether it will not obey Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , nor put his neck under his yoke ,
And they said unto you , Ye shall not obey your prophets , nor those who do divination , nor those who dream , nor those who make signs , nor those who do evil , saying , Ye shall not serve the king of Babylon
&quot; They prophesy falsely to you that they will cause you to move away from the land , so that I will drive you out and destroy you
&quot; But if a nation will put its neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon , and serve him , I will make it dwell in the land , and cultivate it , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; So I said to the house of Zedekiah king of Judah , &apos; Put your necks under the yoke of the king of Babylon , and serve him and his people , that you may live
&quot; Why do you and your people die of the sword , and of famine , and of pestilence , as the Lord said to the land of Babylon , which did not obey him ?
&quot; Do not listen to what the prophets said to you , saying , &apos; You will not serve the king of Babylon . &apos; Indeed , they prophesy falsely to you
&quot; I have not sent them , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; but they prophesy falsely in my name , that I may drive you out and those who prophesy to you and destroy them together
&quot; And I said to the priests and to the people , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; You shall not hear the prophet &apos;s prophecy against you , saying , &apos; The vessels of the house of the Lord will be brought back from Babylon ; &apos; for they speak falsely to you
&quot; Do not obey them ; only serve the king of Babylon , and he will live . Why is this city turned into a wilderness ?
&quot; If the word of the Lord comes to them , if they are prophets , let them pray to the Lord of hosts that the vessels left in the house of the Lord and in the house of the king of Judah , and the vessels left in Jerusalem , may not be brought to Babylon .
For the LORD of hosts hath spoken of the pillars , and of the copper sea , and of the basin , and of the vessels that are left in this city
The vessels which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had not plundered in the days of Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah , and in the days of all the nobles of Jerusalem in Judah
Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , concerning the vessels that remain in the house of the Lord , and in the king &apos;s house of Judah , and in Jerusalem
&quot; They will be brought to Babylon , where they are , in the days when I will be with the children of Israel , and I will bring back the vessel and give it back to the land , &quot; says the Lord .
In that year , in the fourth year of the reign of Zedekiah king of Judah , in the presence of the priests and the people in the house of the Lord , Hananiah the son of Absalom the prophet of the Gibeonites spoke to me
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; I have broken the yoke of the king of Babylon
&quot; In two years I will plunder Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon from the land , and bring back the vessels of Babylon , and all the vessels of the house of the Lord ,
&quot; I will also bring back here Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah , and all the Jews who were taken captive to Babylon , because I will break the yoke of the king of Babylon , &quot; says the Lord .
Then the prophet Jeremiah spoke to the prophet Hananiah , when he was with the priests , and with all the people that stood in the house of the Lord
&quot; May the Lord do so , and fulfill the word which you have spoken , and bring back from Babylon the vessels of the house of the Lord , and all the captives ,
&quot; But listen to what I say to you and to the people ,
&quot; For from ancient times , the prophets before you and before me prophesy to many nations and great countries concerning wars , plagues , and plagues
&quot; When the peace of the prophet &apos;s prophecy is fulfilled , man will know that he is indeed the Lord &apos;s messenger
Then Hananiah the prophet took down the yoke that was on Jeremiah &apos;s neck , and broke it
Then Hananiah said to the people , Thus saith the Lord ; In two years &apos; time I will break the yoke of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon from the necks of all the nations . So Jeremiah the prophet departed .
Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , when Hananiah the prophet had broken the yoke that was on Jeremiah &apos;s neck
&quot; Go to Hananiah and tell him , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; You broke the yoke of wood , and replaced it with the yoke of iron
&quot; For thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel : &apos; I have put a yoke of iron on the necks of these nations , that they may serve Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , and they shall serve him , and I have given him the beasts of the field .
Then the prophet Jeremiah said to the prophet Hananiah , &quot; Hear , Hananiah , for the Lord has not sent you , but you have made this people rely on lies
Therefore thus saith the Lord ; Behold , I will cause thee to die , and thou shalt die this year , because thou hast spoken rebellious words to the Lord
Thus the prophet Hananiah died in July of that year .
The prophet Jeremiah sent letters from Jerusalem to the priests who were taken captive , and to the prophet , and to the people , and to the elders who survived ; and it was Nebuchadnezzar who went from Jerusalem captive to Babylon
( The king of Jeconiah , and the queen , and the governor , and Judah , and the princes of Jerusalem , and the craftsmen , and the ironsmiths , left Jerusalem after him . )
And he sent by the hand of Eleazar the son of Zaban , and of Kimarel the son of the house of Helah , two of them , the sons of Zedekiah king of Judah , to Babylon to meet king Nebuchadnezzar .
&quot; Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , to all the captives , whom I have taken from Jerusalem to Babylon ,
&quot; You shall build houses and dwell therein , and plant fields and eat of the fruit thereof .
Take wives to give birth to children , and take wives for your sons , and make your daughters to marry , and give birth to sons and daughters , and have many children therein , and not fewer .
&quot; Peace be to the city which I have taken you into captivity , and pray to the Lord for it ; for it will have peace , and you will have peace with it .
Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; &quot; Do not be tempted by your prophets and your divinations , nor listen to your dreams ,
&quot; For they prophesy falsely against you in my name , and I have not sent them , &quot; says the Lord .
Thus saith the LORD ; After the seventy years which I have appointed for Babylon have come to pass , I will come near unto you , and I will accomplish my word unto you , that ye may return unto this place
&quot; I know , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; that my thoughts toward you are thoughts of peace , and not of evil , that you may have hope after the end .
&quot; When you call on me and pray to me , I will answer you
&quot; If you seek Me , If you seek Me with all your heart , You will find
&quot; I will be found by you , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will bring back your captives , and gather you from all the nations , and from all the places to which I have driven you ; and I will bring you back to the place from which I have driven you away , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; You said , &apos; The Lord is a prophet for us in Babylon .
Therefore the Lord says , &quot; The king who sits at the throne of David and all the people who live in this city are brothers who were not taken away with you
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Behold , I will bring upon them swords , and famine , and pestilence , and make them as the flowerless of the evil , so that they cannot be eaten
And I will chase them with swords , and with famine , and with pestilence , and I will cast them out of all the nations of the earth , and curse , and terror , and derision , and shame , among the nations to which I have driven them .
&quot; This is because they have not listened to me , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; because I sent my servants and the prophets from the beginning to speak , but they have not listened , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; Therefore all of you who were taken captive , whom I sent from Jerusalem to Babylon , listened to the word of the Lord
&quot; Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , concerning Ahab the son of Kareah , and Zedekiah the son of Maaseiah , saying , &apos; They prophesy falsely to you in my name , and I will deliver them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , and he will kill them before your eyes .
&quot; All the captive Jews who dwell in Babylon will swear by these two men , saying , &apos; May the Lord make you like Zedekiah and Ahab , the king of Babylon , who were burned in the fire
&quot; These two men have done abominations in Israel , and have committed adultery with their neighbors &apos; wives , and have taken my name to speak against them , saying , &apos; I have not commanded them ; I am the one who knows , and I am the one who bears witness , &apos; says the Lord
And concerning Shemaiah the Nethilonite , say thou :
Thus said the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; &quot; You have sent letters in your name to the people of Jerusalem , and to Sibaniah the son of Maaseiah the priest , and to all the priests ,
&quot; The Lord has appointed Sibaniah your priest , to replace Jehoiada the priest , and to appoint officers in the house of the Lord , so that all the foolish ones who call themselves prophets will be chained and chained
&quot; Behold , Jeremiah of Anakim calls himself a prophet to you ; why do you not blame him ?
For he wrote to us in Babylon , saying , &quot; The days of captivity will be long , and you shall build houses and dwell therein , and plant fields and eat of the fruit thereof .
Then Zephaniah the priest gave this conviction to Jeremiah the prophet
Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah , saying ,
&quot; When you send letters to all the captives , say , &apos; The Lord has spoken to Shemaiah the Hebrew , saying , &apos; Because Shemaiah has prophesied to you , I have not sent him , and he has made you rely on lies
Therefore thus saith the LORD ; I will punish Shemaiah the son of Ner , and his seed , and none of them shall remain among them , nor shall he see the blessing which I will give unto my people , because he hath spoken rebellion unto the LORD , saith the LORD .
And the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord , the God of Israel ; All that I have spoken unto thee thou hast written in the book
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that I will bring back my people Israel and the captives of Judah , and I will bring them back to the land which I gave to their fathers , and they will possess it , &quot; says the Lord .
Below is what the Lord said concerning Israel and Judah
Thus saith the Lord ; We have heard a voice , a voice of trembling and fear , and not of peace
And you shall visit , and see , is there a man in labor ? How can I see that men are strangling his waist , like a woman in labor , and their faces are turned blue ?
&quot; Woe to you ! The day is great and unparalleled ! This is the time of Jacob &apos;s trouble , but he will be saved
&quot; In that day , &quot; said the Lord of hosts , &quot; I will break the yoke of the enemy from your neck , and turn his cords , and the foreigners will no longer make you their servants
&quot; But you will serve the Lord your God , and the King David , whom I will raise up for you
Therefore thus saith the Lord ; Fear not , O Jacob my servant ; fear not , O Israel ; for I will save thee from afar , and I will save thy seed from the land of captivity ; and Jacob shall return in peace and security , and no man shall make him afraid .
&quot; Because I am with you to save you , and to destroy the nations to which I have driven you out , but I will not destroy you , but I will punish you with ease , and I will not punish you , neither will I make you innocent , &quot; says the Lord .
Thus says the Lord : &quot; Your wounds cannot be healed ; Your scars are great .
&quot; No one will testify against you , and your wounds will be wrapped up , and you will not have any good remedy .
For all those whom thou lovest have forgotten thee , and have not come to inquire of thee ; for thy iniquity is great , and the wicked are many , and I have afflicted thee with the hurt of the enemy , and I have afflicted thee with the punishment of the wicked , and I have afflicted thee with the punishment of the oppressor .
&quot; Why do you mourn for the hurt ? Your pain is not healed . I have added to you many sins and great injustices because of your iniquity .
&quot; Therefore whoever eats you will be eaten , and all your enemies will be taken away , and whoever takes you will be taken away , and whoever takes you will be taken away .
&quot; I will heal you , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will heal your wounds , because they have called you a fugitive , saying , &apos; This is Zion , and no one has come to inquire&apos;
Thus saith the LORD ; I will bring back the tents of Jacob that were taken away , and I will neglect his dwelling place ; and the city shall be built in the former hills , and the palace as there were inhabited
There will be a voice of thanksgiving and joy from which I will increase them , and not diminish them , and make them honourable , and not humble .
&quot; Their sons and their daughters will stand firm before me , as they have been , and I will punish him who oppresses them .
&quot; Their kingdom will be theirs , and the princes will come out of their midst ; I will bring him near to me , and he will come near to me ; or who has the courage to come near to me , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; You will be my children , and I will be your God .
&quot; Behold , the wrath of the Lord will turn on the head of the wicked , as if a storm had passed away , a storm of destruction .
The wrath of the Lord will not cease , but will return to the fulfillment which He has set in His heart , and in the latter days you will understand .
Then shall I be the God of the houses of Israel , and they shall be my children , saith the LORD
&quot; Thus says the Lord : &apos; The man who is cut off from the sword is the son of Israel , who was blessed in the wilderness when I gave him rest
In ancient times the Lord appeared to Israel from afar , saying , &quot; I love you with everlasting love , therefore I am attracted to you with mercy
&quot; O people of Israel , I will build you again , and you will be built , and you will go forth dancing with those who rejoice at the sound of the trumpet .
And on the mountains of Samaria will be a vineyard , and the sower will eat of the fruit thereof .
&quot; The days will come when those who watch over mount Ephraim will cry out , &apos; Arise , we can go up to Zion to the Lord our God
Thus saith the Lord ; Sing ye for Jacob , for the glory of the kingdoms , and proclaim , and say , O Lord , save thy people , and save the remnant of Israel
And I will bring them from the north , and gather them from the farthest parts of the earth , and they who come with them , blind , lame , pregnant , and barren , they shall be a great host , and they shall return to this place .
&quot; They will come crying , and I will guide them according to their pleas , that they may walk uprightly by the waters , and not stumble upon them ; for I am the Father of Israel , and Ephraim is my eldest son .
&quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , O you nations , and proclaim it in the distant islands of the sea , saying , &apos; Those who scatter Israel will gather them together and watch over them as the shepherd watches over the flock
For the LORD redeemed Jacob , and redeemed him from the hand of a mightier than he
They will come to sing in the high places of Zion , and they will return to the land of the Lord &apos;s grace , which is the land of five valleys , new wine and oil , and lambs and calves ; their hearts will be like a well watered garden , and they will no longer be sorrowful .
In that day the women will dance with joy , and the young and the old will rejoice together ; for I will make their sorrow a joy , and comfort them , and make their sorrow a joy .
&quot; I will fill the hearts of the priests with fat oil , and my people will be filled with my grace , &quot; says the Lord .
Thus saith the LORD ; The voice of the trumpet that crieth in Ramah is the cry of Ramah ; for his children are not comforted , because they are not there
Thus saith the LORD ; Forbid not the voice to weep , nor the eyes to weep ; for your work shall be rewarded , and they shall return from the enemy , saith the LORD .
&quot; There will be hope in the end of your days , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and your children will return to their own land
&quot; I heard Ephraim mourning for himself , saying , &apos; If you punish me , I will be punished , like a calf that does not bear the yoke ; and if you turn me , I will turn ; for you are the Lord , my God
When I return , I repent , and when I have been taught , I weep with my legs , and I am ashamed of my childhood &apos;s abuse .
&quot; Is Ephraim my beloved son , or my joyful child , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; when I reproach him , I take great care of him ; therefore my heart loves him , and I need to have mercy on him
&quot; O Israel , when you set up signposts for yourselves and raise up pillars for your way , keep your minds on the high way , which is the way to which you have gone ; and when you turn , turn to your cities ,
&quot; How long will you return , O people of the wicked ? The Lord has created a new thing in the earth , a woman to guard men .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Blessed be the LORD , O holy mountain , O dwelling place of righteousness , when I shall bring back the captives in the land of Judah and in the cities thereof
Judah and all the people of the cities of Judah , the farmers and the shepherds , shall dwell there together
&quot; I have filled the weary , and filled the anxious , and I have given him sufficient knowledge
&quot; I am awake , &quot; said the prophet , &quot; and I am asleep sweet
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will sow the seed of men and the seed of cattle in the house of Israel and in all Judah
Thus saith the LORD , As I have watched them before , and removed them , and destroyed them , and overturned them , and suffered them , so will I have watched them build and plant them ;
In those days , it was no longer said , &quot; The father has eaten grapes , and the son &apos;s teeth are turned to acid . &quot;
But every man shall die for his own sin ; and whosoever eats the grapes , his teeth shall be turned to acidity .
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with all Judah
&quot; It is not like the covenant I made with their fathers when I took them out of the land of Egypt , and I was their husband ; but they have rejected my covenant , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; This is the covenant which I made with the house of Israel in those days , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that I will put my law in their hearts , and write it in their hearts , and that I will be their God , and they will be my children .
&quot; Every one of them will no longer teach his neighbors and his brothers , saying , &apos; You must know the Lord ; for they will know Me from the least to the greatest ; and I will forgive their iniquity , and will not remember their iniquity any more , &apos; says the Lord .
&quot; He has made the sun to shine , and the moon to shine , and the night to shine , and he has stirred up the sea , and he has caused the sea to wave , and the Lord of hosts is his name , &quot; he said .
&quot; If these statutes are to be abolished before me , then the seed of Israel will be abolished before me , and they will no longer be a nation , &quot; says the Lord
Thus saith the LORD ; If I could measure the heavens , and find the foundations of the earth , I would forsake them for all that the children of Israel have done , saith the LORD .
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and this city will be built for the Lord from the house of Canaan up to the gate of the corner
And the cords shall be drawn out , and they shall go straight up to Mt . Galilee , and they shall turn to Goa .
The whole valley of the slain , and the place where the ashes are cast down , and all the land , shall be holy to the LORD , even to the brook that is drawn down , and to the corner of the east gate of Manasseh ; no more shall it be cut out , no more shall it be overturned , and no more shall it be for ever .
In the tenth year of Zedekiah king of Judah , in the eighteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar , the word of the Lord came to Jeremiah
Then the army of the king of Babylon besieged Jerusalem ; and Jeremiah the prophet was imprisoned in the house of the guard , in the king &apos;s house
&quot; Because the house of Zedekiah , king of Judah , had imprisoned him , and said , &apos; Why do you prophesy , saying , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I will deliver this city into the hand of the king of Babylon , and he will take it
&quot; The house of Zedekiah king of Judah will not escape from the hands of the Chaldeans ; but they will be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon , and they will speak to one another , and they will see one another .
&quot; The king of Babylon will bring the house of Zedekiah to Babylon , and the house of Zedekiah will dwell there until the time when I will be near to him , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; even though you fought against the Chaldeans , yet you did not prosper .
Then Jeremiah said , The word of the Lord came to me , saying ,
&quot; The son of Pharaoh , your uncle , Hananah , will come to you and say , &apos; I ask you to buy the land of Anathoth , for it is worthy of redemption for you to buy it .
&quot; Indeed , according to the word of the Lord , Hanan , the son of my uncle , came into the court of the guard , and said to me , &apos; I am in the land of Benjamin , in the land of Anathoth , and I ask you to buy it ; for it is lawful for you to buy it , and for your own redemption ; and I , Jeremiah , know that this is the word of the Lord
Then I bought the land of Anathoth to Hananah the son of my uncle , and gave him seventeen shekels of silver
&quot; I sealed the covenant , and I made the covenant sealed , and I invited witnesses to come , and I poured out the silver upon him with the heavenly plates
I will set forth the ordinance of the purchase , that is , that which is sealed , and that which is open ,
and delivered it to Baruch the son of Neriah , the son of Maaseiah , in the presence of Hananiah my uncle &apos;s son , and of all the Jews that sat in the court of the guard ,
&quot; I commanded Baruch , when he was in the sight of all his people ,
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Put the two sealed and the two open covenants in a vault , that they may be kept for many days
For thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts , the God of Israel ; In the future there shall be a purchaser of houses , of fields , and of vineyards in this land
Then I gave the purchase to Baruch the son of Neriah , and prayed to the Lord , saying ,
O Lord GOD , thou hast created the heavens with great power and with a stretched out arm , and thou hast done no difficult thing
&quot; You have shown mercy to tens of thousands , and repaid the iniquity of your father in the arms of his seed after him . Your name is the God of all might , the Lord of hosts .
He is a man of great wisdom , and of great power , and watches all the actions of the world , and reports to Him according to what they do , and according to what they do .
And the signs and wonders were done in the land of Egypt , even unto this day among Israel and among others , that they might be glorified , even as they are today .
&quot; Your people Israel have come out of Egypt with miracles , with mighty hands , and with arms stretched out , and with great wonders .
&quot; And you will give them this land , which you swore to their fathers to give them for milk and honey
&quot; They have entered into the land for their possession , but they have not obeyed Your word , nor have they obeyed Your law . They have done all that You have commanded them , and they have done nothing . Therefore You have brought all this evil upon them
&quot; Behold , the enemy has come and has set up a fort to take this city , and it has been delivered into the hands of the Chaldeans who have taken it , because of the sword , and because of the famine , and because of the plague ; and what you said has been fulfilled , and you have seen it .
&quot; You , Lord Yahweh , have said to me , &apos; Buy the land for yourselves with silver , and call witnesses , for the city has indeed been given into the hands of the Chaldeans .
And the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , saying ,
&quot; I am the Lord , the God of all the bloodthirsty . Is there anything that I cannot do ?
Thus saith the LORD ; I will deliver this city into the hand of the Chaldeans , and into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , and he shall take it
&quot; The Chaldeans who have taken the city will come and burn it with fire , and the houses thereof , wherein men have burned incense to Baal , and poured water on other gods , and provoked me to anger .
&quot; They have provoked me to anger with all that they have done in their hands , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; for they have done evil in my sight , Israel and Judah , from their youth .
&quot; From the day that it was built to this day it has provoked me to anger and wrath , and I have taken it away from before me .
For all the wickedness of the children of Israel and of the children of Judah , which they and their kings , and their princes , and their priests , and their prophets , and all Judah , and the inhabitants of Jerusalem did , provoked me to anger .
They turned to Me , and not to Me ; and though I had taught them from the beginning , they did not obey , nor were they taught
&quot; He has made abominations in the house that is called in My name , and has defiled it .
&quot; In the valley of Hinnom they have built the high places of Baal , that their children may be brought back to Jerusalem by fire ; and they have done this abomination , and have caused Judah to sin ; it is not my commandment , nor my heart &apos;s will .
&quot; Now concerning this city , thus says the Lord , the God of Israel , which you said was delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon by the sword , by the famine , by the plague ,
&quot; In anger , and in wrath , and in great anger , I will drive out the children of Israel into all the nations , and I will gather them out of them in the days to come , and bring them back to this land , and I will make them dwell therein safely .
&quot; They will be my children , and I will be their God
I will cause them to be with one another in heart and mind , that they may fear me for ever , and that they and their seed in the afterlife may rejoice .
And I will make an everlasting covenant with them , and I will bless them , and I will not leave them , and I will not leave their hearts to fear Me
&quot; I will rejoice in my grace with them , and I will plant them in this place with all my heart and all my soul , with all my sincerity
&quot; For thus says the Lord : &apos; As I have brought all this great evil upon this people , so will I bring upon them all the blessings which I have promised them .
&quot; You say , &apos; This land is desolate , without people and without livestock , the land which the hands of the Chaldeans have delivered ; and in the days to come there will be a man to buy the land in it .
&quot; In the land of Benjamin , and in all the cities around Jerusalem , in the cities of Judah , in the cities of the mountains , in the cities of the high places , and in the cities of the south , they shall buy the land with silver , and they shall write it down , and seal it , and bring forth witnesses ; for I will bring back the captives , &quot; says the Lord .
Then came the word of the LORD to Jeremiah the second time , when he was in the house of the guard
&quot; The LORD is that which is accomplished , and the LORD is that which is built , and the LORD is his name , &quot; he said .
&quot; When you ask me , I will answer you and direct you to great and difficult things that you do not know .
Thus says the Lord God of Israel , &quot; The houses of this city and the palaces of the king of Judah have been destroyed , and the forts and the swords of the enemy have been destroyed .
&quot; They will fight against the Chaldeans , and they will fill the house with dead bodies ; they are the ones whom I have killed in anger and wrath ; for all their evil I have hid my face from the city .
&quot; Behold , I will make this city healed and prosperous , and the people of the city healed , and I will make abundant peace and truth manifest to them .
&quot; I will also bring back the captives of Judah and the captives of Israel , and I will establish them and the first kind
&quot; I will cleanse them of all their sins , which they have committed against me ; and I will forgive them of all their sins , which they have committed against me and transgressed against me .
&quot; This city shall be praised and glorified in the sight of all the nations of the earth , and shall be called the City of Joy and Pleasure ; and all the nations will fear and tremble because they have heard the blessings and the mercy which I have bestowed on it .
&quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; You say that this place is a desolate land without people and without livestock , but in this desolate city of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem without people and without livestock
Then you will hear the voice of joy and gladness , the voice of the bride and the groom , and the voice of those who say , &quot; Praise the Lord of hosts , for the Lord is good , and his mercy endures forever , &quot; and the voice of those who offer sacrifices in the house of the Lord ; for I will bring back the captives of the land , as at the beginning , &quot; says the Lord .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; In this wasteland , where there is no people nor livestock , and in all the cities thereof , there shall be shepherds to dwell , and they shall lay the flock therein
In the cities of the mountains , and in the cities of the high places , and in the cities of the south , and in the land of Benjamin , and in all the borders of Jerusalem , and in the cities of Judah , there shall pass again a flock of sheep by the hand of men of number , saith the LORD .
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will make sure that the good words of the house of Israel and of all Judah will be fulfilled
&quot; In that day , in that time , I will raise up the seed of David the righteous , and he will do justice and righteousness in the land .
In that day Judah shall be saved , and Jerusalem shall dwell safely ; and his name shall be called the righteousness of the Lord our God
For thus saith the Lord ; David shall sit continually upon the throne of the house of Israel
Neither did the Levites , the priests , with me forsake the offering of burnt offerings and burnt offerings , nor did they perform the ordinance of the offering
And the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord ; If ye can depart from the covenant of my day and night , that the day and night may not turn in due season ,
Then I will break my covenant with David my servant , that he may have no son to reign in his throne ; and I will break my covenant with the Levites , the priests who minister to me
For the heavens cannot be counted , neither the dust of the sea can be counted : thus will I multiply the seed of my servant David , and the Levites that serve me .
And the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , saying ,
Have you not pondered the words of these people , who say , &quot; The two tribes which the Lord has chosen have passed away , and they have despised My people so that they will not be a nation again
Thus saith the Lord ; If I have not kept the covenant of day and night , neither have I set the pattern of the heavens and the earth ,
And I will forsake the seed of Jacob , and the seed of David my servant , and will not cause the seed of David to rule over the seed of Abraham and Isaac ; for I will bring back their captives , and will have mercy on them .
Then came the word of the LORD to Jeremiah , saying , Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , with all his army , and with all the kingdoms of the earth that belonged to him , struck Jerusalem and all the cities that belonged to Jerusalem
&quot; Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel , &apos; Go and speak to the house of Zedekiah king of Judah , saying , &apos; I will deliver this city into the hand of the king of Babylon , and he will burn it with fire
Thou shalt not escape from his hand , but shalt be taken and delivered into his hand ; and thy eyes shall see the eyes of the king of Babylon , and he shall speak with thee , and thou shalt go to Babylon .
&quot; Hear also the word of the Lord , O house of Zedekiah king of Judah , saying , &apos; You will not be struck by the sword , &apos; says the Lord
&quot; You will die in peace , and people will burn for you like your ancestors , like the first kings before you ; and people will mourn for you , saying , &apos; Woe to you , Lord , &apos; says the Lord , &apos; This is what I said
Then Jeremiah the prophet brought all these words to the house of Zedekiah king of Judah in Jerusalem
At that time the army of the king of Babylon was attacking Jerusalem , and the cities that remained of Judah , which were Ragi and Assyria , two of the strong cities of Judah .
And the king of Zedekiah made a covenant with all the people of Jerusalem , that he should proclaim liberty to them , and that they should set forth every man his servant and his maid of Hebrews , and that no man should make his brother a slave .
See Up
Then all the princes of the covenant , and all the people , set free his servants and his maids , and no man called them any more to be servants ; and they were all obedient , and set them free .
Then he repented again , and brought back the slaves whom he had appointed to be free , and made them slaves .
Therefore the word of the Lord came to Jeremiah , saying ,
Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel ; &quot; I made a covenant with your fathers , when I brought them out of the land of Egypt as slaves ,
&quot; If a brother of yours , a Hebrew , is sold to you to serve you six years , and in the seventh year you shall let him go forth free ; but your ancestors have not listened to me , nor listened to me
&quot; Now therefore turn again , and do what is right in My sight , and proclaim liberty to your neighbours , and make a covenant before Me in the house that is called in My name .
&quot; But you have repented again , and defiled My name ; and you have called back the slaves whom you have appointed freely , and you have made them slaves .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord : &apos; You have not listened to me , and have declared liberty to your brothers and neighbors . Behold , I declare liberty to you because of the sword , and because of the famine and the plague , and because of the sword , and because of the plague , and because of the sword , and because of the plague , and because of the sword , and because of the sword , and because of the sword , and because of the sword , and because of the sword , and because of the sword , and because of the sword , and because of the sword , and because of the sword , &apos; says the Lord .
&quot; The heads of Judah , the heads of Jerusalem , the overseers , the priests , and all the people of the land have divided the calf into two parts , and have made a covenant before me , and have gone astray from my covenant , and have not kept the words of this covenant
See Up
And I will deliver them into the hand of the enemy , and into the hand of those who seek their life ; and their bodies shall feed the birds of the air , and the beasts of the earth .
And I will deliver the house of Zedekiah king of Judah and his princes into the hand of their enemies , and into the hand of the king &apos;s army of Babylon , and into the hand of those who seek their life ,
&quot; I will command them to return to this city , and to attack it , and to take it , and to burn it with fire ; and I will make the cities of Judah a desolation , and no man shall dwell therein , &quot; said the Lord .
The word of the Lord came to Jeremiah in the days of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah
&quot; Go to the men of the tribe of Rechab , and speak to them , and bring them into the house of the Lord , and give them drink
and I will take Jason the son of Jalemiah , the son of Habakkuk , the son of Neriah , and his brothers , and his sons , and all the children of Rephaim ,
And he brought them into the house of the LORD , into the house of the sons of Hakah , the son of Iquidael the God , which was by the house of the chief , above the house of Machiah the son of Shalon , which had the door
And I set before the children of Rec a table and a cup full of wine , and said unto them , Drink ye
&quot; But they said , &apos; We will not drink ; for Jonah the son of Rechab our father commanded us , saying , &apos; You and your sons shall never drink
Neither shall you build houses nor plant vineyards ; but you shall live in tents for the years of your life , that your days may be prolonged in the land of your dwelling .
&quot; We have obeyed all that Jonah the son of Rechab our father commanded us , and we and our wives and our children have not drunk from the first year of life
Neither were there houses to dwell in , nor vineyards , nor fields , nor seed
&quot; But stay in the tents , and obey the words of Jonah our father , and do as he has commanded us .
&quot; When Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to this place , and we feared the army of the Chaldeans and the army of the children of Aram , he said , &apos; Come , we will go to Jerusalem , &apos; and we lived in Jerusalem
And the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Go and say unto the Jews and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem , The Lord saith , Did ye not receive instruction , and hearken not unto my word ?
&quot; They have kept the commandment of Jonah the son of Rechab , which he commanded his sons not to drink , and to this day they do not drink , because they obeyed the commandment of their fathers ; and I warned you from the beginning , but you did not obey me .
&quot; I arose early and sent My servants and the prophets , saying , &apos; When you turn away from the wicked way and repent and do not follow other gods , you will live in the land which I have given to you and to your fathers ; but you have not listened to me , nor listened to my voice .
&quot; The sons of Jonathan the son of Rechab , who kept the commandments of their fathers , but they did not listen to me
Thus says the Lord , the God of hosts , the God of Israel : &quot; I will bring upon the Jews and upon all the inhabitants of Jerusalem all the evil that I have spoken to them ; for they have not listened , and I have called upon them , and they have not given me a promise .
And Jeremiah said unto the men of Lyme , Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Because ye have obeyed the commandment of Jonah your father , and kept all his commandments , and walked in all that he commanded you
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Jonathan the son of Rechab shall stand before me without any man
In the fourth year of Jehoia the son of Josiah king of Judah came the word of the Lord to Jeremiah , saying ,
Take a book , and write on it all the words that I have spoken to you against Israel and against Judah and against all the nations from the day that I spoke to you , from the days of Josiah even to this day ,
&quot; Or if all the Jews hear that I seek to deliver them from all their evil , they will turn away from the evil way , and I will forgive their iniquity and their sins
Then Jeremiah called for Baruch the son of Neriah ; and Baruch wrote from the mouth of Jeremiah all the words which the Lord had spoken to Jeremiah in the book
Then Jeremiah said to Baruch , &quot; I am not able to enter the house of the Lord
&quot; Therefore go and recite the word of the Lord to the people and to all who come out of the cities of Judah in the house of the Lord in the days of fasting , as you have written in my mouth in the book .
Or they make supplications before the Lord , and turn away from the wicked way ; for the wrath and the wrath of the Lord is great against this people
And Baruch the son of Neriah did according to all that Jeremiah the prophet had commanded , to walk in the house of the Lord , and to read the word of the Lord in the book
In the fifth month , in September , Jehoia the son of Josiah king of Judah proclaimed a fast before the Lord to the people of Jerusalem and to the people who came to Jerusalem from the cities of Judah
Then Baruch read the words of Jeremiah to the people in the upper court of the house of the LORD , in the new gate of the house of the LORD , in the house of Benjamin the son of Shaphan ,
and Micaiah the son of Kimariah , the son of Shaphan , heard all the words of the LORD in the book
And he went down into the king &apos;s house , and entered into the house of the scribes : and there sat in it Elishama the scribe , and Delaiah the son of Shemaiah , and Elinathan the son of Ahab , and Kimariah the son of Shaphan , and Zedekiah the son of Hananiah , and the rest of the princes .
Then Micaiah spoke to them all the words which he had heard , when Baruch remembered the book to the people .
Then the princes sent Judah the son of Nethaniah , the son of Shelemiah the son of Zedekiah the prophet , to Baruch , and said to him , &quot; Take the book which you have read to the people in your hand , and come to us ; &quot; and Baruch the son of Neriah took the book in his hand , and came to them
And they said unto him , Sit down , and recite unto us ; and Baruch recited unto them
And when they heard all these words , they were afraid , and looked one at another , and said unto Baruch , We must bring all these words to the king
They asked Baruch , &quot; Tell us , please , how do you write all these words in his mouth
Then Baruch answered and said , He spoke all these words to me in his mouth , and I wrote them in writing
And the chiefs said unto Baruch , Go hide , thou and Jeremiah , and let no man know where ye are
Then the princes entered into the king &apos;s house , and put the book in the house of Elishama the scribe , and he told the king all these words
Then the king sent Judah to take the book , and took it out of the house of Elishama the scribe , and read it to the king , and to all the princes who were with him .
It was September , and the king sat in the house of winter , and there was a flame of fire in the pot of fire before him .
And when Judah had remembered the three or four verses , the king broke the scroll with the sword of the scribe , and cast it into the pot of fire , and it was consumed in the fire
&quot; The king and his servants who heard all these words were not afraid , neither did they tear their clothes
And Eleazar , and Delaiah , and Gimariah , besought the king not to burn the scroll , but he did not hear
And the king commanded Jerah the son of Hamel , and Silas the son of Assyria , and Shelemiah the son of Abib , to take Baruch the Nethinim , and Jeremiah the prophet ; and the Lord hid them
And the king burned the book , and upon it was written the words of Baruch , which were written in Jeremiah &apos;s mouth : And the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah after him , saying ,
Take another book , and write on it all the words which Jehoiakim king of Judah burned in the first book .
&quot; Thus says Yahweh , &apos; You burned the book , and said , &apos; Why did you write on it , &apos; The king of Babylon must destroy the land , and the livestock of the people must be cut off from it ? &apos;
Therefore the Lord spoke to Jehoia king of Judah , saying , &quot; There shall not be a man among his seed sitting on David &apos;s throne ; his bodies shall be cast out , and the day shall be hot , and the night cold
And I will punish them for his iniquity , and for his seed , and for the iniquity of his servants ; and all the evil that I have spoken will come upon them , and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem , and upon the Jews ; but they will not listen .
Then Jeremiah took another book , and gave it to Baruch the scribe , the son of Neriah ; and he wrote out of Jeremiah &apos;s mouth all the words of Jehoiakim king of Judah concerning the burnt offering , and added to it a number of similar words
And Zedekiah the son of Josiah reigned in the place of Goniah the son of Jehoiakim king of Babylon , and Nebuchadnezzar king of Judah reigned in Judah
But the house of Zedekiah and his servants and the people of the land did not listen to the word of the Lord through Jeremiah the prophet
And the king of Zedekiah sent Jephthah the son of Shelemiah , and Sibaniah the son of Maaseiah the priest , to meet Jeremiah the prophet , saying , Pray to the Lord our God for us
Then came Jeremiah out of the people , because they had not yet put him in prison .
And when Pharaoh &apos;s army had come out of Egypt , the Chaldeans who had besieged Jerusalem heard their voice , and drew out their camps from Jerusalem
The word of the Lord came to Jeremiah the prophet , saying ,
Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel ; &quot; The king of Judah sent you to ask me , saying , &apos; Thus will you say to him : &apos; The army of Pharaoh , which is coming to help you , will return to the land of Egypt
&quot; The Chaldeans will come again and attack this city , and they will take it and burn it with fire .
Thus saith the Lord ; Do not deceive yourselves , saying , The Chaldeans shall surely depart from us ; for they shall not depart
&quot; Even if you destroy all the army of Chaldeans , who fought with you , but the remnant of the wounded will rise up from the tents and burn the city with fire
When the army of Chaldeans , fearing the army of Pharaoh , drew out their camps from Jerusalem ,
Then Jeremiah departed from Jerusalem among the people , and went to the land of Benjamin , where he made his own possession
And he came to the gate of Benjamin , and there was a watchman , whose name was Elijah , the son of Shelimiah , the son of Hananiah ; and he took Jeremiah the prophet , and said unto him , Are ye surrender to the Chaldeans ?
Then Jeremiah said , &quot; You are a liar , and I am not a surrender to the Chaldeans ; but if Elijah does not listen to his words , he will take him and deliver him into the hand of the leader .
Then the chief captain was angry with Jeremiah , and struck him , and put him in the house of Jonathan the scribe , because they regarded it as a prison
And Jeremiah came into the prison , and entered the prison , and spent many days in it
Then the king of Zedekiah sent messengers to bring him , and asked him privately in his own house , saying , &quot; What has come to you from the Lord ? &quot; Jeremiah said , &quot; Yes , &quot; and said , &quot; You will be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon .
Then Jeremiah said to the king of the house of Zedekiah , &quot; What have I sinned against you , or against your servants , or against this people , that you have imprisoned me
&quot; I have prophesied to you that the king of Babylon will not come to attack you and the prophets of this land , and he is now in it .
&quot; Now , O Lord , my King , listen to me , and grant me my supplication before you ; and do not cause me to return to the house of Jonathan the scribe , lest I die there
And the king of Zedekiah commanded , and they delivered Jeremiah into the house of the guard , and every day they took a cake from the baker &apos;s street to him , and the cake that went straight into the city was consumed ; and Jeremiah was still in the house of the guard
Zephaniah the son of Mattan , Kidaliah the son of Bah Shur , and Jemah the son of Shelimiah , Bah Shur the son of Machiah , when Jeremiah heard what he had said to all the people ,
For thus saith the Lord ; He that dwelleth in this city shall die by the sword , by famine , and by pestilence ; but he that goeth forth to deliver up the Chaldeans shall live , and he that plundereth his own life shall live
Thus saith the LORD ; This city shall be delivered into the hand of the army of the king of Babylon , and he shall take it
Then the prince said to the king , &quot; Please put this man to death , because he has spoken these words to the remnant of the men of war and to the people of the city , that their hands may be weakened ; for he is not asking for peace for the people , but for evil for them
And the king of the house of Zedekiah said , He is in your hand ; and the king shall not oppose you in any thing
And they took Jeremiah , and brought him down into the prison of Machiah , the son of Hamel , the king &apos;s son , which was in the house of the guard , and they laid down Jeremiah with ropes ; and there was no water , but mud ; and Jeremiah fell into the mud .
And it came to pass , when Ebermelech the ancient man , the prince of the king &apos;s house , heard that they had put Jeremiah into prison , that the king sat at the gate of Benjamin
Then came Ebermelech out of the king &apos;s house , and spoke to the king
&quot; They have done evil to Jeremiah the prophet , O king of my Lord , and have put him into prison , where he will die of hunger , and there will be no more food for the city .
Then the king commanded Ebermelech the ancient , saying , &quot; Take thirty men from here , and bring him out of the prison before the prophet Jeremiah dies
And Ebermelech went with them into the king &apos;s house , and went under the treasury , and took of it pieces of cloth , and of the garments that were broken , and cast them down by ropes into the prison , and came to Jeremiah
Then Ebermelech the ancient man said to Jeremiah , &quot; Put these pieces of cloth and the filthy garments on the ropes , and cover your armpits , &quot; and Jeremiah did so .
So they brought Jeremiah up from the prison with ropes ; and Jeremiah was still in the court of the guard .
Then the king of Zedekiah sent and brought Jeremiah the prophet into the third door of the house of the Lord to meet the king ; and the king said to Jeremiah , &quot; I have a question for you , and you cannot hide it from me .
Then Jeremiah said to the house of Zedekiah , &quot; If I tell you , will you not kill me ? If I warn you , you will not listen to me
Then the king of Zedekiah said to Jeremiah privately , &quot; I swear by the Lord , the Everlasting One , who created our life , that I will not kill you , nor hand you over to those who seek your life
And Jeremiah said unto the house of Zedekiah , Thus saith the LORD God of hosts , the God of Israel ; If thou goest forth unto the head of the king of Babylon , thy life shall be saved , and this city shall not be burned , neither thou , nor all thy household ;
&quot; If you do not go out and return to the princes of Babylon , this city will be given to the Chaldeans , and they will burn it with fire , and you will not be able to escape from their hands
And the king of Zedekiah said unto Jeremiah , I am afraid of the Jews that have surrendered to the Chaldeans ; I am afraid that the Chaldeans will deliver me into their hands , and that they will play with me
And Jeremiah said , The Chaldeans will not deliver thee : hear thou the word of the LORD which I have spoken unto thee , that thou mayest have good , and that thy life may live .
&quot; If you will not go out , this is what the Lord has commanded me
And the remnant of the women that were left in the house of the king of Judah shall be brought unto the princes of Babylon , and they shall say , Thy friends , whom thou knowest , have exalted thee over thee : behold , thy feet are in the mire , and thou hast turned back
And they shall bring thy wife and thy children unto the Chaldeans ; and thou shalt not escape from their hand , nor be caught by the hand of the king of Babylon ; and thou shalt burn this city with fire .
And the house of Zedekiah said unto Jeremiah , Thou shalt not die , if thou make no man know these things
&quot; If the prince hears me speaking to you , he will come to you and ask you , &apos; What do you say to the king ? Do not hide it from us , or we will not kill you ; and tell us what the king has said to you
Then saidst thou unto them , I have pleaded before the king that I should not return unto the house of Jonathan to die there
Then the princes came to Jeremiah and asked him , and he answered them according to all that the king had commanded them ; and they spoke no more to him , for there was no leakage of the matter .
Then Jeremiah remained in the court of the guard , until the day that Jerusalem was taken .
In October 9th , Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came and besieged Jerusalem with all his army
On the ninth day of the first month of April , the city of Zedekiah was besieged
And it came to pass , when Jerusalem was taken , that the princes of the king of Babylon , and Nicoshazzar , and Timneph , and Zacchin , and Lazarus , and Nicoshazzar , and Ram , and all the princes of the rest of the king of Babylon , sat in the middle gate
And when Zedekiah king of Judah and all the men of war saw them , they fled out of the city at night , from the gates of the two cities which were near the king &apos;s house , and fled to Rabbah
And the army of the Chaldeans pursued after them , and pursued the house of Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho , and took him , and brought him to Riblah of Hamath , to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon ; and Nebuchadnezzar judged him .
And king Babylon slew his sons and all the nobles of Judah before the house of Zedekiah in Liblah
And they took away the eyes of the house of Zedekiah , and locked him with chains of brass , and brought him to Babylon .
&quot; The Chaldeans burned the king &apos;s palace and the houses of the people with fire , and destroyed the walls of Jerusalem
Then Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard took away the remnant of the people that remained in the city , and his fugitives , and the rest of the people , to Babylon
And Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard left the poor among the people in the land of Judah , and gave them vineyards and fields
And Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to Jeremiah , and commanded Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard , saying ,
&quot; If you take him away and treat him well , you will not harm him . Whatever he says to you , you will do to him .
And the captains of the guard were Nebuchadnezzar , and Nebuchadnezzar , and Lazarus , and Nethaneshazzar , and Ram , and all the princes of king Babylon
And he sent and brought Jeremiah out of the house of the guard , and brought him home to Gilead the son of Ahikam , the son of Shaphan the son of Zaban ; and Jeremiah dwelt among the people
And the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah , when he was in the barracks , saying ,
&quot; Go to Ebermelech , the ancient man , and tell him , &apos; Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , &apos; The word that I have spoken concerning evil and not evil will come to this city , and it will be fulfilled before you
&quot; In that day , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; I will save you , and you will not be delivered into the hand of those whom you fear
&quot; I will rescue you , and you will not fall under the sword , but you will take your own life for a prey , because you have trusted in me , &quot; says the Lord .
The word of the Lord came to Jeremiah , when Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard had delivered him out of Ramah , when Jeremiah was locked up among the people who were taken captive in Jerusalem and Judah to Babylon
Then the captain of the guard called Jeremiah and said to him , &quot; The Lord , your God , has said to bring this evil upon this land
&quot; The Lord has brought this evil upon you , according to all that He has spoken ; for you have sinned against the Lord , and have not obeyed His word ; therefore it has come upon you
&quot; Behold , I have cut off the chains from your hand . If you see that it is good for you to go with me to Babylon , you can go ; I will have mercy on you . If you see that it is bad for you to go with me to Babylon , you will not go . Behold , it is all before you , and you think that it is good in it , and it is right in it ; so go there alone .
And it came to pass , when Jeremiah had not returned , that the captain of the guard said , &quot; You may go back to Gilead the son of Ahigan , the son of Shaphan , king of Babylon , to be governor of the cities of Judah ; and you may dwell therein among the people ; or you may go up therein , if you see fit . &quot; And the captain of the guard sent him food and presents , and let him go .
Then Jeremiah came to Mizpah , and saw Gilead the son of Ahikam , among the remnant of the people that dwelt in him
And all the captains of the field , and all that belonged to them , heard that Babylon had set up a governor in the land of Gedaliah the son of Ahikam , and that there would be no man , nor woman , nor child , nor any poor man in the land , that were taken captive in Babylon .
So Ishmael the son of Nethaniah the captain of the army , and Johanan the son of Gallia , and Jonathan , and Silas the son of Nun , and all the sons of Ephesus the Nethite , and Jeshaniah the son of Maacah , and all the men that were with them , came to Mizpah to Kedaliah
Then Gideel the son of Ahigan , the son of Shaphan , swore to them and to his men , saying , &quot; Do not be afraid to serve the Chaldeans , but live in this land , and serve the king of Babylon , and you will be blessed
&quot; As for me , I will dwell in Mizpah to serve the Chaldeans who come to us ; but you shall store up wine , oil , and summer fruits in vessels , and dwell in the cities which you possess .
And all the Jews in the land of Moab , and in the land of the children of Ammon , and in the land of Edom , and in all the kingdoms , heard that the king of Babylon had left some Jews , and that Gilead the son of Ahikam , the son of Shaphan , was over them
And all the Jews returned from all the places where they had been driven , to Mizpahgilead in the land of Judah , and stored up much wine and summer fruit
And Jehohanan the son of Kareah , and all the captains of the army that were in the field , came to Mizpah unto Gilead
And he said unto him , Knowest thou that Balak king of the children of Ammon sent Ishmael the son of Nethaniah to seek thy life ? But Gilead the son of Ahikam believed not their words
Then Jehohanan the son of Galilee privately said to Gedaliah in Mizpah , &quot; Please let me kill Ishmael the son of Nethaniah , and no man will know why he asks for your life , and why the Jews who came to you are scattered , and the remnant of Judah is destroyed .
Then said Gilead the son of Ahikam unto Johan the son of Galilee , Thou shalt not do this thing : but what thou sayest concerning Immael is false .
And it came to pass in July , that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah , the son of Elishama the son of the king &apos;s household , came to Mizpah with ten men , to see Gedaliah the son of Ahikam , and they ate with him at Mizpah .
And Ishmael the son of Nethaniah rose up , and the ten men that were with him , and slew with the sword Gedaliah the son of Ahigan , the son of Shaphan , king of Babylon , governor over all the land .
And Ishmael slew all the Jews that were at Mizpahgilead , and the Chaldeans whom he met
He killed Gideon , and no one knew
And it came to pass on the second day , that eighty men came out of Shechem , and of Shero , and of Samaria , and shaved their beards , and rent their clothes , and broke their bodies , and took in their hands alms and frankincense , to minister unto the house of the LORD
And Ishmael the son of Nethaniah went out of Mizpah to meet them , and wept with them ; and when he had met them , he said unto them , Come to see Kidaliah the son of Ahikam
And when they were come into the city , Immael the son of Nethaniah and his men slew them , and cast them into the pit
But ten men among them said to Immael , &quot; Don &apos;t kill us , for we have many wheat , and little wheat , and oil , and honey hidden in the fields ; &quot; and he held his hand , and did not kill them among his brethren
And Immael the son of Nethaniah filled the pits of the slain , when he threw the bodies of the slain by the side of Requidael the pit , which king Asa had dug out for fear of Bashan king of Israel .
And the remnant of Mizpah , all the princesses , and all the people that remained in Mizpah , whom Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard had given to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam , were taken captive ; and Ishmael the son of Nethaniah took them captive , to go into the land of the children of Ammon .
And Jehohanan the son of Kareah , and all the captains of the host with him , heard all the evil that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah had done .
And he led all the people to meet him by the great waters of Gibeon , to fight against Ishmael the son of Nethaniah .
And when all the people of Ishmael saw Jehohanan the son of Galilee , and all the captains of the host with him , they rejoiced
And all the people that Ishmael had taken away from Mizpah turned and fled to the refuge of Johan the son of Galilee
And Ishmael the son of Nethaniah fled to the children of Ammon , and eight men with him , out of the hand of Joash .
And Ishmael the son of Nethaniah slew Kidaliah the son of Ahikam ; and after that he had taken away from Mizpah all the remnant of the people , the soldiers , and the women , and the children , and the captives , to Gibeon , Jehohanan the son of Galilee , and all the captains of the host with him ,
And he brought them unto the house of Canaan , which is near Bethlehem , to dwell therein , and went into Egypt .
For Jehoahaz was not afraid of the Chaldeans , because Ishmael the son of Nethaniah had killed Gilead the son of Ahikam , king of Babylon , governor .
And the captains of the host , and Johanan the son of Galilee , and Jezaniah the son of Josiah , and all the people , from the least even to the greatest , came in
Then he said to Jeremiah the prophet , &quot; Please let us pray before you , and pray to the Lord your God for the remnant of us ; for we were many , and now we are few , and that is what you saw with your own eyes .
May the Lord , your God , show us the way that we should walk , and what we should do
Then Jeremiah the prophet said to them , &quot; I have heard you , and I will pray to the Lord your God according to your words , and whatever the Lord answers , I will tell you without concealing
And they said unto Jeremiah , If we do not do all that the LORD thy God hath sent forth unto thee , let the LORD be a witness among us of true faith
&quot; Now , when we call you to the Lord our God , we will hear what he says , good and evil ; and we will be blessed if we listen to the word of the Lord our God
Ten days passed , and the word of the Lord came to Jeremiah
Then he called Johan the son of Galilee , and all the captains of the host with him , and all the people , from the least to the greatest ,
And he said unto them , Thus saith the Lord , the God of Israel , the Lord whom ye have asked of me before Him for your sakes :
&quot; If you remain in this land , I will build you , and you will not be destroyed , nor plant you , nor excavated ; for I have repented for my goodness and for the evil of yours .
&quot; Do not be afraid of the king of Babylon , whom you fear , &quot; says the Lord ; &quot; do not be afraid of him , for I am with you to deliver you out of his hand .
&quot; I will also make him have mercy , and have mercy on you , that you may return to your own land
&quot; If you say , &apos; We do not live in this land , so that we do not obey the word of the Lord your God
&quot; We will not dwell in this land , but will enter the land of Egypt , where there will be no fighting , no voice , and no hunger ; and we will dwell there .
&quot; Now , O you remnant of Judah , listen to the word of the Lord , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , &quot; if you intend to enter Egypt and dwell there ,
The sword that you fear shall pursue you in the land of Egypt , and the famine that you fear shall follow you in Egypt , and you shall die there
&quot; Whoever intends to enter Egypt , and dwells therein , shall die by the sword , by famine , by pestilence ; and none shall remain , except he escape from the calamity which I have brought upon him and from their calamity .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Thus will I pour out my wrath and my wrath upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem when ye enter into Egypt , and I will pour out my wrath upon you , that ye may reproach , and be ashamed , and curse , and be ashamed , and ye shall see this place no more
&quot; But the Lord said to the remnant of Judah , &apos; You shall not enter Egypt ; but you shall know that I have warned you today .
&quot; For you have called me to the Lord your God , saying , &apos; Pray for us to the Lord our God , and tell us what the Lord our God has spoken , and we will do it . &apos; 
&quot; Today I will tell you this ; but you have not listened to what the Lord your God sent me to do for you
&quot; Now you shall know for certain that you shall die by the sword , by the famine , by the pestilence , in the land to which you shall dwell .
Then Jeremiah spoke to the people all the words of the Lord their God , which the Lord their God sent to him
Then Azariah the son of Josiah , and Johanan the son of Galilee , and all the proud men , said to Jeremiah , &quot; You are lying . The Lord our God has not sent you to enter Egypt , to dwell there
&quot; Behold , Baruch the son of Neriah exhorted you to kill us , and to deliver us into the hands of the Chaldeans , that we might be slain , and be taken captive to Babylon
Then Jehohanan the son of Kareah lived in the land of Judah , and all the captains of the host , and all the people , and did not obey the word of the LORD
Then Jehohanan the son of Galilee and all the captains of the host brought back the remnant of the Jews , the men , the women , the children , and the princes , who had dwelt in the land of Judah , from the captivity to the nations , and guarded all those who were with Gilead the son of Ahikam , the son of Nebuchadnezzar , the son of Zaban , who had stayed with the prophet Jeremiah , and Baruch the son of Neriah ,
See Up
And they brought them into the land of Egypt , and came to Rebekah , because they had not obeyed the word of the Lord
And the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah , saying ,
And thou shalt take great stones by the hand before the Jews , and hide them in the dust of the bricks , in the gate of the house of Rebekah , before Pharaoh .
And he said unto them , Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Behold , I will call my servant Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , and I will place his throne upon the stones which he hid , and he will lay the tabernacle of the glory upon it
&quot; He will come to the land of Egypt , and he who is slain will die , and he who is taken captive will be taken captive , and he who is slain will be struck with the sword .
&quot; I will set a fire in the temple of the God of Egypt , and the king of Babylon will burn the temples , and God will be taken captive ; and he will be clothed in the land of Egypt , as a shepherd clothed in sackcloth ; and he will go in peace from there .
And he shall break the pillar of Shemaiah the Egyptian , and burn the temple of the God of Egypt with fire .
Then came the word to Jeremiah concerning all the Jews that dwelled in the land of Egypt , the Jews that dwelled in Michael , and in Tabin , and in Noph , and in Bethel , saying ,
Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; &quot; You have seen all the evil that I have done to Jerusalem and to all the cities of Judah ; and they are desolate to this day , and no man dwells therein .
&quot; This is the wickedness of the inhabitants , which provokes me to anger , to burn incense to another God , whom they and you and your fathers did not know .
&quot; I sent my servants from the beginning , the prophets , saying , &apos; Will you not do this abomination which I hate ?
&quot; But they do not listen , they do not listen , they do not turn away from evil , and they burn incense to another God
Therefore my wrath and my wrath have come down like a fire in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem , and they have been desolate and desolate as it is today .
Thus says Yahweh , the God of Armies , the God of Israel : &quot; Why do you commit this great evil to your own souls , and cut off your men , and your women , and your babies , and your milkmen from Judah , and leave not one man ?
&quot; It is because of what your hands have done , that they have provoked me to anger by burning incense to other gods in the land of Egypt to which you have gone , that you have been cut off , and that they have cursed and humiliated in all the kingdoms of the earth .
Have you forgotten the evil deeds of your fathers , the evil deeds of the kings of Judah and their wives , the evil deeds of yourselves and your wives , which they did in the land of Judah in the streets of Jerusalem ?
&quot; There is no repentance , nor fear , nor obedience to the law which I have set before you and your fathers
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; Behold , I will turn my face against you , and bring evil upon you , that I may cut off all Judah
&quot; I will destroy all the remnant of the Jews who were determined to enter the land of Egypt and settle there , and they will fall into the land of Egypt , and they will be destroyed by the sword of famine ; and from the smallest to the greatest they will die by the sword of famine , and they will be made to be ashamed , ashamed , ashamed ,
&quot; As I punish Jerusalem with the sword , with famine , with pestilence , so will I punish the Jews who dwell in the land of Egypt
Even those who dwell in the land of Egypt , the remnant of the Jews , shall not escape , nor remain , nor return to the land of Judah , wherein they long to dwell ; and none shall return except those who have escaped .
Then answered Jeremiah those who lived in the land of Egypt , and knew that their wives had burned incense to another god , and all the women that stood by them gathered themselves together .
&quot; We will not obey what you have spoken to us in the name of the Lord
&quot; We will accomplish all that is spoken in our mouths , and burn incense to the heavens , and pour out sacrifices according to the customs of our fathers and our fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers &apos; fathers
We have lacked everything since we ceased to burn incense to the heavens and to pour out sacrifices ; and the famine is consumed by the sword
And the women said , &quot; Are we to burn incense to the afterlife , and to pour out sacrifices , and to offer to him afterlife-like cakes , and to pour out sacrifices to him , beside our husband ?
Then Jeremiah answered all the men and women that were with him , saying ,
Will not the Lord remember , and think , the incense burned in the cities of Judah , and in the streets of Jerusalem , by you and by your fathers , and by your kings , and by your princes , and by the people of the land ?
&quot; The Lord will no longer tolerate your evil deeds and your abominations ; so your land will be desolate and terrible and cursed , and there will be no inhabitants , as it is today .
You have burned incense , and have sinned against the Lord , and have not listened to His word , and have not obeyed His statutes , ordinances , and ordinances ; so you have suffered this plague as it is today
Then Jeremiah said to the people and to the women , &quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , all you Jews in the land of Egypt
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel ; &apos; You and your wives shall say in their mouths , &apos; Do with your hands , and say , &apos; We will repay our vows , and we will burn incense to the heavens , and we will pour out drink offerings ; &apos; and now you shall repay only what you have promised .
Therefore all the Jews who dwell in the land of Egypt hearken to the word of the Lord , saying , &quot; I swear by my great name , that in all the land of Egypt my name will no longer be called by the mouth of a Jew , saying , &apos; I swear by the Lord , the Everlasting Lord ,
&quot; Behold , I have warned them that evil does not bring good , and that all the Jews in the land of Egypt will be consumed by the sword and by the famine .
Few return from the land of Egypt to the land of Judah from the sword ; and whoever enters into the land of Egypt and dwells therein , the remnant of the Jews , shall know whose word endures , and my word , and their word .
&quot; I will punish you in this place , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and there will be a sign for you , that you may know that I have spoken evil to you , and that you will stand firm .
Thus saith the LORD ; As I have delivered the house of Zedekiah king of Judah into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , who sought his enemy and his life , so will I deliver Pharaoh king of Egypt into the hand of Aphraim , his enemy and his life .
In the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah , Baruch the son of Neriah wrote in the book the words which Jeremiah the prophet had spoken , saying ,
Then said Baruch , The Lord God of Israel ,
For Baruch said , &quot; Woe to me ! The Lord will add sorrow to my affliction , and I will not rest because of my weeping .
&quot; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I will destroy what I have built , and I will pull out what I have planted , and I will do so throughout all the earth .
Do you seek great things for yourselves ? Do not seek them ; for I will bring evil upon every bloodthirsty man ; but wherever you go , I will make you a prey for your own life , says the Lord
The word of the LORD concerning the nations came to Jeremiah the prophet
Concerning the army of Pharaoh , king of Egypt , which encamped at Gachemish by the river Berah , which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon defeated in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah
&quot; You shall prepare shields of great and small sizes , and stand before them .
&quot; Take your carriages , ride your horses , stand on top of your helmets , and sharpen your weapons
&quot; Why do I see them turning back in terror ? Their mighty men have been defeated , they have fled in a hurry , and they have not turned back . The terror is all around them , &quot; says the Lord .
Do not let the fleeing flee , nor let the warrior flee . They stumbled on the banks of the River Bela in the north
Who is like the running of the Nile , and like the flooding of the rivers ?
As the Nile rises up , and as the waters of the river rise up , so shall Egypt rise up , and I will cover the whole earth , and I will destroy the cities and the inhabitants thereof
Get up the horses , and the chariots , and go out , the mighty men of old , the Philistines with their shields , and the Luddites with their bow ;
&quot; The day will be the day of vengeance from the Lord , the Lord of hosts , and of vengeance from the enemy ; and the sword will devour , and the blood will drink , because of the sacrifice of the Lord , the Lord of hosts , on the banks of the River Bela in the north
&quot; O Egyptians , go up to Gilead and take incense , and you will not be healed , though you take many good medicines .
The nations heard thy shame , and the earth was filled with thy mourning : and the mighty touched one another , and the mighty fell together .
&quot; This is what the Lord said to Jeremiah the prophet concerning Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon coming to attack the land of Egypt
&quot; You shall proclaim in Egypt , and proclaim in secret , and report in Noah , and answer in Babylon , saying , &apos; Stand up , and prepare yourselves , for the sword that will devour you around you .
&quot; Why have your mighty men been driven away ? They have not stood up , because the Lord has driven them out
And many stumbled , and they also stumbled at one another , saying , Arise , and let us go again to the land of our people , to escape the sword of oppression .
And they cried therein , saying , Pharaoh king of Egypt is no more than a voice ; he has missed the time appointed .
&quot; The King , the Lord of hosts , said , &apos; I have sworn by my eternal life , that the people of Nebuchadnezzar will be as he was in the mountains , as the people of Gami by the sea .
&quot; O you who dwell in the land of Egypt , the things which you shall prepare for your captivity ; for Noah will be a wilderness , and it will be burnt down , and there will be no inhabitants .
Egypt is a fat calf , but the destruction of the north has come , and it has come
Their labor is like a calf in a circle . When they have turned their backs , they flee together , and do not stand ; for the days of their trouble and the time of their persecution have come .
The voices of them are like serpents , and the enemy will come in multitudes , as the hands of a tree-cutter strike him with axes .
&quot; The forests of Egypt , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; will be cut down , even though they cannot find them ; for they are more than locusts , and cannot be numbered .
Surely the people of Egypt shall be ashamed , and they shall be delivered into the hands of the north .
&quot; Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel , &apos; I will punish the sons of Ammon , the God of Egypt , and Pharaoh , and Egypt , and the God of Egypt , and the kings , and Pharaoh , and those who rely on him ,
&quot; I will deliver them into the hand of those who seek their life , and into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , and into the hand of his servants ; and there will be inhabited Egypt as there was before , &quot; says the Lord .
Fear not , O Jacob my servant ; fear not , O Israel : for I will save thee from afar , and thy seed from the land of captivity ; and Jacob shall return in peace , and no man shall make him afraid .
&quot; Don &apos;t be afraid , O Jacob my servant , for I am with you , and I will destroy the nations to which I have driven you , and I will not destroy you , but I will punish you with ease , and I will not punish you , neither will I make you innocent , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; Before Pharaoh attacked Gaza , the word of the Lord came to Jeremiah the prophet concerning the Philistines
Thus saith the LORD ; Water shall spring up from the north , and it shall become a river , and it shall flow over the whole land , and all that are therein , and the cities , and all that dwell therein ; and they shall cry , and all that dwell therein shall weep .
Hearing the sound of the horses of the enemy , and the roaring of the chariots , and the roaring of the wheels of the chariots , he softened his hands for his father , and looked not back at his children .
For the day is coming to destroy all the Philistines , and to cut off the remnant of the people who helped to drive out the city of Rosydon ; for the Lord will destroy the Philistines , the remnant of the island of Capernaum .
