And it came to pass in the ninth year , in the first tenth month of October , that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon led all his army against Jerusalem , and encamped against it , and besieged it with four walls .
So the city was besieged , and it came to the king of Zedekiah in the eleventh year .
On the ninth day of April , there was a great famine in the city , and even the people had no food
And the city was defeated , and all the men of war fled from the gates of the two cities which were near the king &apos;s house at night ; and the Chaldeans were besieging the city , and they fled to Rabbah
And the army of Caleb pursued the king of the house of Zedekiah , and pursued him in the plains of Jericho ; and all his army was scattered from him .
And the Chaldeans took the king , and brought him unto the king of Abiram in Hamath ; and the king of Abiram judged him .
And king Babylon slew his sons in the sight of the house of Zedekiah , and all the princes of Judah in Libnah .
And he took the eyes of the house of Zedekiah , and locked him with chains of brass , and brought him to Babylon , and put him in prison until the day of his death .
On the first tenth of May , in the nineteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard who stood before the king of Babylon entered Jerusalem
He will burn the houses of the Lord and the kingdom with fire , and the houses of Jerusalem with fire , the houses of the houses of the fathers .
and with all the army of the captain of the guard of the Chaldeans , they demolished the walls of Jerusalem that were round about it
Then Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard took away the poorest of the people , and the remnant of the people that remained in the city , and the people that had surrendered to the king of Babylon , and the remnant of the great multitude .
But Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard left the poorest of the people to repair their vineyards and their fields
&quot; The Chaldeans broke down the copper pillars of the house of the Lord , and the basin of the house , and the sea of copper , and brought it to Babylon
And the pot , and the shovel , and the scissors , and the dishes , and the spoons , and all the vessels of brass , which they used ,
And the captain of the guard took away the cup , and the spear , and the bowl , and the basin , and the lampstand , and the spoon , and the count , and all the silver of gold
How much more was the copper that Solomon made for the house of the Lord , two copper pillars , and a copper sea , and twelve copper bulls that sat under it ,
And the pillars were eighteen cubits high , and four fingers thick , and empty , and twelve cubits round about .
And the pillars were of brass , five cubits high ; and around the pillars were nets and pomegranates of brass ; and the same was the pillar of pomegranates .
There were 96 pomegranates on all sides of the pillars . A hundred pomegranates were all around the net .
And the captain of the guard took Zedekiah the high priest , and Zephaniah the deputy priest , and the three porters
And he took out of the city an officer in charge of the army , and seven of the king &apos;s servants whom he met in the city , and the secretary of the captain of the army , and sixty men of the people whom he met in the city .
The captain of the guard , Nebuchadnezzar , brought the men to king Rababel of Libye
And the king of Babylon slew them at Liblah in Hamath ; and the Jews were taken captive , and departed from the land
The number of the captives of Nebuchadnezzar is as follows : In the seventh year of Nebuchadnezzar they carried away three thousand twenty and three Jews .
In the eighteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar eight hundred and thirty-two people were taken captive from Jerusalem
And it came to pass in the thirty-three years of Nebuchadnezzar , that Nebuchadnezzar the captain of the guard took away from Judah seven hundred forty-five and four thousand six hundred men .
Joiachin king of Judah was taken captive thirty-seven years , and on the twenty-fifth day of December , in the year of Edomimoda king of Babylon , he lifted up Joiachin king of Judah , and brought him out of prison
And they blessed him , and exalted him in the throne of the kings of Babylon with him
And they took him out of his prison , and he did eat all his days before the king of Babylon .
And the king of Babylon gave him the food that he needed , and gave him one penny day by day , for ever and ever until the day that he died .
The cities which were full of people , and where they sat alone , and where they were great among the nations , and where they were widows , and where they were queens among the provinces , and where they were enriched ,
He cries in the night , and tears are on his cheeks ; and there is not a comforter for him among all those whom he loves ; and his friends deceive him , and become his enemies .
And Judah went abroad because of his affliction , and because of his many labours : and he dwelled in the nations without rest ; and they that pursued him pursued him in the narrow land .
The way of Zion is grieved because there is no one to keep the feast ; the gates of his city are desolate ; his priests weep ; his virgins are troubled , and he himself grieves .
His enemies are at the head , and his enemies are at the head : for the Lord hath afflicted him with many sins , and his children are taken away by the enemy .
The glory of the city of Zion has been lost , and its leaders have no power to walk before the pursuers , like the deer who find no pasture .
&quot; When Jerusalem was in distress and distress , it remembered all the good things of the ancient days ; and its people fell into the hands of the enemy , and no one helped them ; and when the enemy saw it , they mocked at its desolation .
And Jerusalem was greatly wicked , and was therefore unclean ; and those who had respected him were ashamed of him , when they saw him exposed , and he himself wept .
His filth is on his collar , and he thinketh not of his own end ; therefore he is very desolate , and no one comforteth him : and he said , O LORD , see my affliction , for the enemy is exaggerating
And the enemy stretched out his hand , and took away his beauty ; and he saw a stranger entering into his sanctuary ; and concerning this stranger thou commandedst him not to enter into thy congregation
And all his people wept and sought food , and exchanged it for good things , that they might save their lives : and they said , O Lord , look , for I am very low
&quot; Do you not care , all you who have gone astray , that you may see that there is no affliction like this which has come upon me , the affliction which the Lord has afflicted me in the days of His wrath ?
He hath entered into my bones from the fire of the high angels ; He hath restrained me ; He hath laid down nets ; He hath stumbled my feet ; He hath turned me back ; He hath made me desolate all the days .
The yoke of my sin is bound by his hand , like a rope tied to my neck : he has weakened my strength , and he has delivered me into the hand of men whom I cannot resist .
&quot; The Lord has abandoned all the mighty men among me , and gathered many to fight against me , and to crush my young men ; and he has struck down the inhabitants of Judah as in a winepress
For these things I weep , and my tears are poured out ; for they that comfort me and save my life are far from me ; my children are in need , and the enemy is victorious .
And Zion lifted up his hand , and there was no consolation ; and the Lord spoke concerning Jacob , saying , The enemies of the people round about him have been commanded ; and Jerusalem was among them as an unclean thing
&quot; The Lord is righteous , and he has done this to me because I have rebelled against his commandments . Listen to my words , O people , and see my affliction ; my virgins and my young men are taken captive
I greeted those whom I loved , and they fooled me ; and my priests and my elders were exhausted in the city when they sought food to save their lives .
&quot; Look , O Lord , for I am in distress , and my heart is troubled , and my heart is troubled within me ; for I am very rebellious , and the swords of the outside destroy children , and death is in my house .
He that heareth my sighs heareth none that comforteth me ; and all my enemies hearken unto my affliction ; and they rejoice because of that which thou hast done ; and thou shalt bring forth the days of thy report , and they shall be like me .
Let their evil deeds be revealed to thee ; and as thou didst deal with me for all my sins , so do thou deal with them ; for I weep and faint in my heart .
Why is it that the Lord is angry , and the dark clouds cover Zion , and he cast down the glory of Israel from heaven on the earth , and in the days of his anger he does not remember his stool
And the LORD swallowed up all Jacob &apos;s dwellings , and did not spare ; and he overthrew the shield of Judah with wrath , and the shield fell to the ground ; and he defiled the land , and the princes thereof
In his fierce anger he has cut off the horns of Israel completely , and he has taken his right hand from the enemy , and he has consumed them like a flame , and he has burned Jacob
He stretches out his bow like an enemy , He stands and lifts up his right hand like an enemy , He kills all that pleases the eyes of men ; His wrath is cast down on the tents of the people of Zion like fire .
For the LORD hath swallowed up Israel and all the houses of Zion , and hath destroyed the shield of the people , and increased the cry of the children of Judah .
He has taken up his tents as shelters in the garden , and has destroyed the place where he gathered , and the feasts and the sabbaths of the Lord have been forgotten in Zion , and the kings and the priests have been despised in anger and wrath .
&quot; The Lord has abandoned his altar , hated his sanctuary , and delivered the walls of the house to his enemies ; and they cried out in the house of the Lord as on the Sabbath day
The LORD hath purposed to destroy the walls of Zion ; He hath drawn cords , He hath not taken back his hand , He hath purposed to destroy ; He hath caused the outskirts and the walls to mourn and to perish together
&quot; The gates of Zion have fallen into the ground . The Lord has broken and broken his gates . His kings and his princes are among the nations without law . His prophets shall not see the vision of the Lord .
The elders of Zion sat in silence on the earth , and they lifted up the dust , and fell on their heads , and clothed themselves with linen , and the virgins of Jerusalem were hanging their heads to the ground .
My tears are in my eyes , and I am blind : my heart is troubled , and my liver is sore : for my people have been destroyed , and my children and those who eat milk have fallen asleep in the streets of the city .
Then they fainted in the streets of the city , as if they had been wounded , and were to die in the womb of their mother ; and they said to their mother , &quot; Where is the wine ? &quot;
O people of Jerusalem , what shall I prove to you ? What shall I compare to you ? O people of Zion , what shall I compare to you to comfort you ? For your fractures are like the sea . Who can heal you ?
&quot; Your prophet has seen false and foolish visions for you , and has not revealed your iniquity to bring you back to your captivity ; but he has seen false revelations for you , and has driven you out of your land .
Everyone who passes by applauds you , and laughs at Jerusalem and shakes his head , saying , &quot; Is this the city which men call beautiful , and the joy of the whole earth ?
&quot; Your enemies will open their mouths to you , and they will laugh and tear their teeth , saying , &apos; We have swallowed him up . This is the day that we have hoped for , and we have seen it with our own eyes .
The LORD hath fulfilled that which he hath commanded , and hath fulfilled that which he commanded in the ancient days : He hath turned back , and hath not neglected , and hath exalted thy enemies against thee , and hath lifted up the horns of thy enemies
The heart of Zion crieth unto the LORD ; O wall of Zion , let thee weep like a river , day and night ; let the eyes of thy eyes be full of tears .
Wake up in the night , and cry before the LORD every more time , and be as water before the LORD ; and lift up your hands to the LORD for their lives , as your children fainted in the mouths of the cities .
&quot; Look , O Lord , and see to whom you do this . Will a woman eat the child that is shaken in her hand , and the priests and the prophets be slain in the holy place of the Lord ?
The young men and the old lay down in the streets ; my virgins and my strong men fell under the sword ; and in the days of your wrath slew them ; and you killed them without care
Thou hast gathered all those that feared me round about , as in the days of the congregation : in the days of the wrath of the LORD there is no escape , no escape : I have shaken the little ones that I have brought up , and the enemies have been cleansed .
&quot; I am in distress because of the rod of the wrath of the Lord
He guides me , and makes me walk in darkness , and not in light
He really attacked me three times over the whole day
He hath dried up my flesh , and he hath broken my bones
He has set up a barrier against me , and has encircled me with bitterness , and with hardship .
He has made me to dwell in the darkness , as a long-suffering man
He has surrounded me with a fence , so that I cannot go out ; He has made my copper heavy
&quot; I cried out for salvation ; He made my prayers not come to pass
He hath hindered my way with stones , and he hath made my way crooked .
He lay down before me as a bear , and as a lion in secret
He has turned me away from the right way , He has torn me apart , He has made me desolate
He used my bow as an arrow target
&quot; He has thrown the arrows in the bag into my lungs
I am the laughter of the people . They sing for me all day long
He fills me with affliction , and fills me with incense
He cut off my teeth with sandstone , and covered me with dust .
You have kept me away from peace . I forgot the benefits .
&quot; I said , &quot; My strength is weakened , and I have no hope in the Lord .
&quot; Remember , O Lord , my affliction and my distress , as the rain and the pestilence .
When I think of these things , I am troubled within
When I remembered it , I had hope in my heart
We will not perish , because of the mercy of the Lord , because of His mercy , and because of His loving kindness ,
It &apos;s new every morning . Your honesty is great .
&quot; I said in my heart , &apos; The Lord is my portion ; therefore I will look on Him
&quot; He who waits for the Lord and seeks Him in his heart will receive His grace
&quot; It is good for a man to look on the Lord , and to wait silently for His salvation
It was good for a man to be yoked in his youth .
&quot; He sat alone and did not speak ; for this is what the Lord has added to him .
He sticks dust in his mouth , or has hope
When he is beaten on the cheek , he is full of humiliation .
For the Lord will never forsake a man
Though the Lord grieves , yet with all his mercy he has mercy
For he is not willing to make men suffer , to make men grieve
A man who is imprisoned in the world is slaughtered under his feet
or in the presence of the Most High
Or in the affairs of men , is it not reversed ? It is not in the sight of the Lord .
&quot; Who can say that it will be accomplished unless the Lord commands ?
Hail and blessings come not from the mouth of the Most High ?
Why does a living man complain about his own sins ?
Let us examine our deeds deeply , and return to the Lord
We pray with sincerity to the God of heaven
For we have transgressed , and thou hast not forgiven .
Thou hast pursued us in anger , and hast slaughtered , and hast not spared .
Thou coverest thyself with a black cloud , that prayer may not pass through .
Thou hast made us defiled and waste among the people
All our enemies have opened their mouths to us
Fear and calamity , destruction and destruction are all near us
For the destruction of my people , I will pour down tears like a river
My eyes are full of tears , and I never stop
&quot; Wait for the Lord to look at you from heaven
For my eyes have grieved my heart , because of the people of my city .
He that pursueth me without cause for his enmity with me is like a bird of prey .
&quot; They have cut off my life in the prison , and have cast a stone upon me
The waters flowed over my head , and I said , &quot; I am cut off .
&quot; Lord , I pray for Your name from the deepest prison .
You have heard my voice ; I seek your salvation ; do not hide your ears and do not listen .
&quot; In the days when I pray for you , you come near to me , saying , &apos; Do not be afraid
&quot; Lord , You have justified my iniquity ; You have redeemed my life .
O Lord , thou hast seen my affliction ; forgive me , O Lord .
&quot; You have seen that they hated me and murdered me .
&quot; Hear , O Lord , what they say against me , and know what they plan against me
and those who rose up to attack me , and what they said in their mouths , and what they devised against me at the end of the day
Behold , they sit down and rise up , and sing with me
Act according to their hands , O Lord , and recompense them
&quot; You will harden their hearts , and your curse will come upon them .
&quot; You will pursue them in anger , and you will destroy them from the land of the Lord
How is the gold lost , how is the pure gold changed in colour , how is the stone of the sanctuary fallen at the gates of the cities
The precious sons of Zion are like gold : where is the work of the carpenter ?
&quot; The wild dogs have given birth to their young , and the women of my people have become cruel like the ostrich in the wilderness .
The tongue of the breastfeeding child is sealed up for thirst ; the child seeks bread , and no one breaks it for him .
Those who used to eat good food are now isolated in the streets ; those who used to lie on red beds are now lying on dust piles .
For the iniquity of my people is greater than the iniquity of Sodom ; and Sodom was overthrown in the midst of the turning of his eyes , though no man put his hand on him .
The nobles of Zion are whiter than snow , and whiter than milk ; and their bodies are red than a jewel of gold , like a bright blue stone .
Now their faces are darker than coal , so that no one knows them in the streets ; their skins are as stiff as bones , and they are as dry as stubble .
Better is he that dieth of hunger than he that is slain with the sword ; for this is the inheritance of the field ; and he weakeneth , and perisheth .
&quot; Woman of mercy , when my people are destroyed , she boils her children with her hands as food .
And the LORD hath fulfilled his purpose in anger , and hath cast out his wrath : and he hath set fire in Zion , and he hath burned the foundations thereof .
The kings of the earth and the inhabitants of the world do not believe that enemies and enemies can enter into the gates of Jerusalem
For the iniquity of his prophets , and the iniquity of the priests , who poured out the blood of the righteous in the city
They walk in the streets like blind men , and are defiled with blood , so that no man can touch their garments .
And they cried unto them , saying , Unclean : hide , hide , and come not near me . And when they fled in the midst of the winds , some of the nations said , They cannot remain here .
And the LORD is angry , and hath scattered them , and hath no more pity on them ; and no man regardeth the priests , nor is he kind to the elders
It is not in vain that we look to men to help us , so that our eyes are blind ; but what we have hoped for is a nation that cannot save .
The enemy chases after us like a hunter , so that we dare not walk in our own streets . Our end is near , Our days are fulfilled , Our end is come .
Those who pursue us are faster than the eagle in the air ; they pursue us in the mountains , they lie in the wilderness , they wait for us .
&quot; The anointed of the Lord are caught in their pits like the breath in our nostrils ; and we have spoken to him , saying , &apos; We will live under his shadow in the nations . &apos; 
&quot; In the land of Uzziah , O Edom , rejoice and rejoice , and bitterness will come to you , and you will be drunk and exposed .
&quot; The punishment of your iniquity is sufficient , O people of Zion ; the Lord will not take you away again ; O people of the east , He will seek your iniquity , He will reveal your iniquity .
&quot; Remember , O Lord , what we have suffered , and see the reproach we have suffered .
&quot; Our inheritance belongs to strangers , and our houses to those who go astray .
We are fatherless orphans . Our mother is like a widow .
We only get water from money . Our wood is sold to us
He chases after us , and reaches to our necks , and we cannot rest in fatigue .
&quot; We surrendered the Egyptians and the Assyrians , to be fed
Our fathers have sinned , and now they are gone ; and we are responsible for their iniquity .
&quot; The servants rule over us , and no man saves us from his hand .
For the sword of the wilderness We risked to get food
Our skin is as dark as a furnace because of hunger and heat
The enemy has defiled women in Zion , and virgins in the cities of Judah
They lifted up their heads , and did not respect the face of the old man
The young man carried a millstone , and the child a wooden staff , and they all stumbled .
The young men were cut off at the gates of the city , and the young men were no longer entertained
The joy of our hearts ceased , dancing became sadness
&quot; The crown has fallen from our heads . We have sinned , and we are in trouble .
These things fade into our hearts . Our eyes fade away .
The wild dogs &#91; or foxes &#93; walked on Mount Zion in the wilderness
&quot; Lord , you will live forever , and your throne for ever and ever .
Why do you forget us forever , why do you forsake us for so long
&quot; Lord , make us return to You , and we shall return ; and renew our days as in the old days .
&quot; Why do you turn away from us completely , and are very angry with us
And it came to pass on the first and fifth day of April thirty years , that the heavens were opened , and the vision of God was seen in the captivity that was by the river Jabbar
This is the first and fifth day of April of the fifth year , when king Jehoiakim was taken captive
And the word of the LORD came unto Jesse the priest , the son of Bath-sheba , in the land of the Chaldeans by the river Jabbar , when the Spirit of the LORD came upon him
And I looked , and behold , the wind came from the north , and with it was a great cloud , and there was light round about it , and out of the fire thereof came as a shining gold .
And out of it came four figures of living creatures , whose appearance was like this : a figure of a man .
Each has four faces and four wings .
Their legs are straight , and their feet are as the feet of a calf , and they are as bright brass .
&quot; Below the wings of the four faces is a man &apos;s hand ; so are the faces and the wings of the four living creatures .
And the wings are joined together , and they walk , and turn not , and each one goes straight ahead .
As for the figures of the faces , there were faces of men before them , and faces of lions on the right side , and faces of cows on the left side , and faces of eagles behind them .
The two wings on the upper sides shall be joined together , and the two wings on the lower sides shall be shielded .
All of them go straight to it , and the Spirit goes into it , and they go into it , and walk , and turn not .
And the likeness of the four living creatures is as the likeness of the burning of charcoal , and as the likeness of the chain of fire ; and the fire ascends and descends among the four living creatures , and it shines , and shines from the fire .
The living creature runs like a flash of light
&quot; When I look at the living creatures , I see that there is one wheel on the earth beside the faces of the living creatures
The shape and the colour of the wheels are like blue and blue . The four wheels are one pattern , the shape and the manner , like a pair of wheels in a wheel
When you walk in a circle , you can walk straight on all sides and not turn .
As for the wheels , they are tall and dreadful , and the four wheels are full of eyes
Life walks and the wheels walk by , and life ascends from the earth , and the wheels also ascend
And the Spirit went into it , and the living went into it ; and the living rose up , and the wheel rose up beside the living ; for the Spirit of the living was in the wheel
Those who walk , and those who walk , and those who stand , and those who stand , and those who rise from the ground , and the wheels rise by ; for the Spirit of the living is in the wheels
Above the head of the living creature , there is a figure of the sky , looking like a dreadful crystal , spread over the head of the living creature .
Below the dome , the wings of the living creatures are straight and relative . Each living creature has two wing coverings
When the living creature walks , I hear the sound of the wings , like the sound of the great water , like the voice of the Almighty , and like the voice of the army ; and when the living creature stands , the wings fall down
And there was a voice above the heaven above their heads ; and when they stood up , their wings fell down .
Above the heaven above their heads is a statue of the throne , like a blue stone . Above the statue of the throne is a statue of a man .
From above his waist I saw gold as if it were shining , and the shape of fire around it , and from below his waist I saw gold as if it were fire , and the shape of fire around it ,
How is the shape of the rainy day , how is the shape of the rainbow in the cloud , how is the shape of the glory around it ? This is the image of the glory of the Lord : I fell down upon the earth , and heard a voice speaking
He said to me , &quot; Son of man , stand up , and I will speak to you
When he spoke to me , the Spirit entered into me , and raised me up , and I heard the voice that spoke to me .
He said to me , &quot; Son of man , I have sent you to the rebellious people of Israel , who have rebelled against me , and they and their fathers have rebelled against me to this day .
&quot; Behold , I have sent you to them , and you shall say to them , &apos; Thus says the Lord Yahweh ,
Whether they hear it or do not , they will know that there is a prophet among them
Son of man , though there be thorns and rustles in you , yet you dwell among the scorpions , and do not fear them , nor fear their words ; and though they are a rebellious house , do not fear their words , nor be afraid of their faces
Whether they listen or do not listen , you only tell them what I say . They are rebellious .
Son of man , listen to what I say to you , and do not be rebellious like the rebellious house , and open your mouth to eat of what I have given you .
And I looked , and I saw a hand stretched out to me , and in his hand was a scroll
And he opened the book before me , and wrote words both within and outside , and wrote on it a cry , and a sigh , and a lamentation .
And he said unto me , Son of man , eat of that which thou hast received , and eat of this book , and speak unto the house of Israel
Then I opened my mouth , and he made me eat the scroll
Then he said to me , &quot; Son of man , eat the book which I have given you , and fill your belly with it ; and I have eaten it , and it tastes sweet in my mouth .
And he said unto me , Son of man , go thou into the house of Israel , and speak unto them my words
&quot; You are not sent to the house of Israel , but to the people who speak depths and cannot understand words .
&quot; Do not go to the depths of the tongues of the nations , whose words you do not understand . If I send you to them , they will listen to you .
&quot; But the house of Israel will not listen to you , because they will not listen to me ; for the whole house of Israel is a stiff-necked man .
&quot; Behold , I have made your face harder than theirs , and your forehead harder than theirs
&quot; I have made your foreheads as diamonds of gold and steel , harder than stones of fire . Do not fear them , nor be afraid of their faces , though they are houses of rebellion .
And he said unto me , Son of man , hear in your heart all that I have said unto thee
&quot; Go to the captives of your land , and speak to them , and tell them , whether they will listen or not , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
Then the Spirit lifted me up , and I heard a trembling sound behind me , saying , &quot; Blessed is the glory that is revealed from the Lord
And I heard the sound of the wings of the living creature touching , and the wheels of the living creature turning round
Then the Spirit lifted me up , and took me away ; and there was great sorrow and wrath in my heart ; and the Spirit of the Lord was mighty in me
And I came to Tyre , and to the captives that dwelt by the river of Capernaum , to the place where they dwelled , and sat among them sorrowfully seven days
And after seven days the word of the Lord came to me , saying ,
Son of man , I have set you as a watchman over the house of Israel ; therefore hear what I say , and warn them for my sake
&quot; When do I say to the wicked , &apos; He must die ; if you do not warn him , nor persuade him , to turn him away from his wickedness , to save his life , he will die in his iniquity ; but I will requite you for the sin of his death . &apos; &quot;
&quot; If you warn the wicked , he will not turn away from sin , nor from evil deeds ; but he will die in iniquity ; and you will save yourself from sin
And when a righteous man sins from his righteousness , I will lay a stumbling block before him , and he will die ; for you have not warned him , and he will die in sin , and the righteousness of his doings will not be remembered ; but I will requite you for the sin of his death .
&quot; If you warn a righteous man that he does not commit sin , he will not commit sin ; and he will live because of your warning ; and you will save yourself from sin
Then the Spirit of the Lord descended on me in it , and said to me , &quot; Go up to the plain , and I will speak to you there
Then I arose and went to the plain , and I did not expect the glory of the Lord , as I saw on the banks of the river Jabbar , to be in it ; and I fell down on the ground
Then the Spirit entered into me , and raised me up ; and the Lord said to me , &quot; Go into the house , and shut the door
Son of man , men will bind you with ropes , and you will not be able to go out among them
&quot; I will put your tongue on your chest , so that you will not be able to blame the people who were a rebellious house
&quot; But when I speak to you , I will make you speak , and you will say to them , &apos; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; He who hears can hear , and he who does not hear will not listen ; for they are a rebellious house .
Son of man , take a brick , and place it before you , and draw on it a city of Jerusalem
&quot; And besieged the city , and built its fortifications , and encamped against it , and set hammer against it round about
&quot; You shall take an iron rod and place it between you and the city as a wall of iron , and you shall attack it in front of you , and you shall make it desolate , as a sign to the house of Israel .
&quot; You shall lie down to the left , and bear the iniquity of the house of Israel ; and you shall bear their iniquity according to the number of days you lie down to the left .
&quot; Because I have set the number of years of their iniquity for you to lie on your left side , three hundred and ninety days , that you may bear the iniquity of the house of Israel .
&quot; And when you have fulfilled these days , I will lay down on your right side forty days , one day for a year , to bear the iniquity of all Judah .
&quot; You shall open your arms to Jerusalem , which is in distress , and prophesy against it ,
&quot; I have bound you with ropes , so that you will not be able to turn around , until you are full of the days of the city .
&quot; You shall take wheat , and barley , and beans , and red beans , and millet , and barley , and put them in a dish for a cake for yourselves ; and you shall eat it on your side for three hundred and ninety days .
&quot; You shall eat two portions of what you have eaten , twenty shekels a day , according to the time .
And drink water according to the measure , and drink one sixth of a hin every day according to the time .
&quot; You shall eat this cake like a cake of wheat , and burn it in the sight of the people with man &apos;s dung
&quot; This is how the children of Israel will eat unclean food in the countries to which I have driven them , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; I said , &quot; Oh , Lord Yahweh , I have not been defiled from my youth to this day , neither have I eaten of the flesh of my own life , nor have I eaten of the flesh torn by beasts , nor have the abominations of the flesh entered into my mouth .
Then he said to me , &quot; Behold , I have given you cow dung instead of man &apos;s dung , and on it you shall bake your bread
Then he said to me , &quot; Son of man , I will break their staff in Jerusalem , and cut off their food ; they will eat their bread in two , and they will eat in fear , and they will drink their water in order , and they will drink in fear
And they were deprived of food , and of water , and were afraid of one another ; and their iniquity was destroyed
Son of man , take a sharp knife to shave your head , and shave your hair with it , and your beard with it , and make your beard smooth .
&quot; The days of the siege of the city are fulfilled , and you shall burn a third of it with fire , and cut off a third of it with the sword , and a third of it with the wind , and I will chase it with the sword .
&quot; Take a few of them and wrap them in your collar
Then take some of them and burn them in the fire ; and there shall come out fire from within , and burn it in the house of Israel .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; This is Jerusalem ; and I have set it among the nations , and the nations are round about it
For he has done evil , and has transgressed my statutes , and has exceeded the nations , and has transgressed my statutes , and has exceeded the nations around him ; for he has forsaken my statutes , and has not kept my statutes
Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; Because you have fought in the nations around you , and have not kept My statutes , nor kept My ordinances , nor have you been content with the evil deeds of the nations around you
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I am against thee , and I will judge in the sight of the nations , and in the midst of thee
&quot; For all your abominations , I will do in your midst what I have not done before , so that I will not do it again .
&quot; The father shall eat the son among you , and the son shall eat the father ; and I will judge you , and I will disperse all that remains of you .
&quot; I swear by my eternal life , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; because you have defiled my sanctuary with all abominations and abominations ; therefore I will reduce your number , and my eyes will not spare you nor pity you
A third of your people shall die by the plague , and a third among you shall be destroyed by famine ; and a third shall fall under the sword around you ; and I will disperse a third on all sides , and I will draw out the sword to pursue them .
&quot; This is how I will accomplish what I have commanded in my anger ; and when I have ceased my wrath from them , I will be comforted ; and when I have accomplished what I have commanded in their anger , then they will know that what I have said , the Lord , is from the heart of my soul .
&quot; And I will make you a desolation and a shame among the nations around you , in the sight of all those who pass by .
Thus will I judge you in anger and wrath , and in rebuke with fierce anger ; and you will be a reproach , and a reproach , and a warning , and a terror among the nations that are around you , says my Lord
&quot; In that day I will cast out the evil arrows of destruction and famine on you , the arrows of destruction , and I will increase your famine , and cut off the food on which you rely .
&quot; And I will cause famine and evil beasts to come to you , and the slaughter of your children , and the plague , and the bloodshed , will be on you ; and I will bring the sword to you , &quot; said my Lord .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , prophesy to the mountains of Israel
&quot; Listen to the word of the Lord Yahweh , O mountains of Israel , to the mountains , to the valleys , to the valleys , to the fountains , to the fountains , to the valleys , saying , &apos; I will bring the sword upon you , and I will destroy your high places .
&quot; Your altar will be desolate , and your image will be destroyed ; and I will cause those who were slain to fall before your idols .
&quot; I will also lay the dead bodies of Israel before their idols , and I will cast your bones around your altar .
&quot; In all your dwellings , cities will be desolate ; the high places will be desolate ; your altars will be desolate ; your idols will be cut down ; your days will be cut down ; your works will be destroyed .
The slain shall fall among you , and you shall know that I am the Lord .
&quot; When you are scattered among the nations , I will be among the nations , and there will be among you those who are left from the sword .
Those who are cut off from the sword will remember me in the countries where they have been taken captive , how they have been hurt in their hearts , because they have become obedient , and have gone away from me , and have committed adultery with their eyes to idols , and they will be ashamed of themselves for all their abominations .
&quot; They will know that I am the Lord . It is not an empty word that I say to bring this evil upon them
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; When you shake your hands and your feet , say , &apos; Woe to the house of Israel for all their abominations ! They will fall under the sword , and under the famine , and under the plague .
The far off shall die of the plague ; and the near shall fall under the sword ; and the remnant of them that are besieged shall die of famine ; and thus will I accomplish in them that which I have commanded in my wrath .
And they that were slain fell among the idols that surrounded their altar , under the hills , and under the tops of the mountains , and under the green trees , and under the oak trees , which they offered sweetly to all the idols ; and they knew that I was the LORD .
And I will stretch out my hand against them , and make their land desolate , from the wilderness even unto Deborah , and all their dwellings ; and they shall know that I am the LORD .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord GOD unto the land of Israel , Son of man ; The end is come , the end is come to the four corners of the land
&quot; Now that your end has come , I will return my anger to you , and judge you according to your deeds , and punish you according to all your abominations .
&quot; My eyes will not spare you nor pity you ; but I will recompense you according to what you have done , and I will punish you according to the abominations among you ; and you will know that I am the Lord .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , a plague , a single plague , is near
The end has come , and the end has come , and it has risen up to you ; behold , it has come
&quot; O inhabitants of the land , the time has come for the calamity which has been determined to come upon you , and the day is near ; it is a day of mockery , and not of mockery on the mountains .
I am about to pour out my wrath upon thee , to do to thee what I have commanded in my wrath , to judge thee according to thy ways , and to punish thee according to all that thou hatest .
&quot; My eyes will not spare you , nor will they pity you ; I will recompense you according to what you have done , and I will punish you according to the abominations of your hearts ; and you will know that my Lord is the one who has struck you .
Behold , the days are near , and the appointed calamity is come forth , and the staff has bloomed , and pride has sprouted .
And there shall not be left of the children of Israel , or of their people , or of their treasures , nor shall there be among them any worthy of honour
The time has come , and the days are near , and the buyer cannot rejoice , and the seller cannot grieve ; for the wrath has come upon all their people
&quot; The seller , though he lives , cannot return what he has sold ; for the parable concerns all of them ; neither can any return , nor can any stand firm in his iniquity .
They have been blown , they have been prepared , but none has fought because of the wrath of My wrath upon all their people .
Outside there is a sword , and within there is a plague , and a famine ; and in the field he shall die by the sword ; and in the city there shall be a famine , and a plague , and they shall devour him .
And whosoever escapeth therefrom shall escape ; and every man shall cry on the mountains for his iniquity , as the dove in the valley crieth .
The hands were soft and knees weak as water
And they shall be clothed in linen , and covered with fear ; and they shall be ashamed in their faces , and bald in their heads .
&quot; They will throw silver into the streets , and it will be defiled ; and in the days of the Lord &apos;s wrath , their silver will not save them , nor fill their hearts , nor fill their belly ; for it is the stumbling block of their iniquity .
&quot; I have made the house of the Lord as a filthy thing for them , because the Lord has beautified the house of His glory , and He has built it with great majesty , and they have made therein abominations and idols
&quot; I will deliver this house to the foreigners as a spoil , and to the wicked on the earth as a spoil ; and they will also profane it
&quot; I will turn my face away from the people of Israel , and they will blaspheme My secrets ; and the robbers will go in and blaspheme
For the land is full of bloody sins , and the cities are full of violence .
Therefore I will make the worst of the nations to occupy their houses ; I will make the pride of the violent to cease ; their sanctuaries will be defiled .
Destruction is near , and they ask for peace , but there is no peace
&quot; There will be disaster after disaster , and wind after wind , and they will seek visions from the prophet , but the law of the priests and the counsel of the elders will be cut off .
&quot; You shall mourn , and the king shall be clothed with ashes , and the hands of the people shall tremble , and I will judge them according to their deeds , and according to what they shall have ; and they shall know that I am the Lord .
On the first and fifth day of June the sixth year I sat in my house , and the elders of Judah sat before me , and the Spirit of the Lord Yahweh descended upon me
And I looked , and I saw a figure like the shape of a fire , and from beneath his waist there was a fire , and from above his waist there was a shape of glory , and like shining gold .
He stretched out his hand as if it were a hand , and seized my hair , and the Spirit lifted me up in the midst of heaven and earth , in the image of God , and brought me to the entrance of the inner house toward the north of Jerusalem , where there was a seat that touched the idols of the Lord &apos;s wrath , that provoked evil .
Who knows that the glory of the God of Israel is in it , as I saw it on the plains ?
And God said unto me , Son of man , lift up thine eyes toward the north ; and I lifted up my eyes toward the north , and behold , on the north side of the door of the altar , there is an idol of evil at the door
And he said unto me , Son of man , what the house of Israel hath done is this great abomination , that it hath driven me away from my sanctuary : seeest thou , and yet another great abomination ?
And he brought me to the door of the house , and I looked , and behold a hole in the wall
And he said unto me , Son of man , thou shalt dig a wall ; and I have dug a wall , and behold a door
And he said unto them , Go in , and see the abominations which they do here
&quot; When I went in and looked , &quot; Who knows , on the walls of the four sides were all kinds of reptiles and abominable beasts , and all the idols of the house of Israel
And there stood before them as before seventy elders of the house of Israel ; and there stood also Jason the son of Shaphan : and all the people took a fire , and poured out the smoke of the clouds .
He said to me , &quot; Son of man , have you seen what the elders of the house of Israel have done in the darkness in their houses ? They say , &apos; The Lord does not see us ; the Lord has forsaken the land .
Then he said , &quot; You will also see another abomination of theirs
And he brought me to the door of the court of the house of the Lord , which is toward the north ; and , behold , there sat a woman weeping for Baal-Maaz
He said to me , &quot; Son of man , have you seen anything more abominable than this ?
And he brought me into the inner court of the house of the Lord , and , who knows , at the door of the house of the Lord , between the porches and the altar , about twenty-five men turned toward the house of the Lord , toward the east , and worshipped the sun
And he said unto me , Hast thou seen , O man , that all Judah are small in this abomination which they do in this land ? and they have multiplied their violence in this land , and have provoked me to anger again , and have stretched out branches before their nostrils
Therefore I will act in wrath , and my eyes will not spare nor pity them , even though they cried out in my ears , but I did not listen .
&quot; He cried out in my ears , saying , &quot; Let the men who are in charge of this city come before me with weapons of death in their hands
Suddenly six men came from the northern gate , each with his weapons , and one of them was clothed in fine linen with a box of ink between his loins , and they entered and stood by the altar of brass
And the glory of the God of Israel is lifted up from there to the threshold of the house , and God has called him who is clothed in fine linen , and has a box of ink in his waist .
Then the Lord said to him , &quot; Go and walk through all Jerusalem , and signs on the foreheads of those who weep and mourn for the abominations they have done in the city .
&quot; In my ears I heard him say to the rest , &apos; Go with him through the whole city to kill , and your eyes will not spare nor pity them .
&quot; They shall kill the elderly , and the young , and the female , and the infant , and the woman , from the sanctuary ; but those who have the mark shall not come near him ; and they shall kill the elders of the temple from before them .
And he said unto them , Defile this house , and fill it with the slain : go ye out , and they shall go out , and slay in the city .
&quot; When they struck me , I was left behind , and I fell down on my face , and said , &apos; Lord Yahweh , will you pour out your wrath on Jerusalem , and destroy all the remnant of Israel ?
And he said unto me , The iniquity of the house of Israel and of all Judah is great , and there is blood upon the whole earth , and there is iniquity in all the cities , because they say , The LORD hath forsaken the land , and he seeth us not
Therefore my eyes will not spare them , nor pity them ; but I will recompense them according to their deeds
Then the man who was clothed in fine linen , and had a box of ink in his waist , answered , &quot; I have done as you have commanded me .
And I looked , and , behold , a blue stone appeared in the clouds above my head , as if it were a throne .
And the Lord said unto the man clothed in fine linen , Go in , under the wheels that rotate , and take charcoal out of the midst of the wheels , and cast it upon the city , and I saw him go in
When he entered , he stood on the right side of the temple , and the inner court was filled with clouds .
The glory of the Lord ascends from the threshold , and stands above the threshold ; and the house is full of clouds , and the houses are filled with the glory of the Lord .
The sound of the winged wings came to the court , as the voice of the Almighty
And he commanded the man clothed in fine linen , saying , Take fire out of the wheels that rotate , and draw fire between the wheels ; and he went in and stood by a wheel
&quot; There will come to pass a man who reaches from the fire into the midst of the fire , and takes some of it in the hands of the man who is clothed in fine linen , and the man will go out .
Under the wings of the ruler , the pattern of mankind is manifested
And I looked again , and behold , there were four wheels beside the reed , and there was one wheel beside the reed , and there was one wheel beside the reed , and every reed was like that ; and the colour of the wheels was like the colour of a pearl of water
As for the shape of the four wheels , they are one pattern , as if they were a set of wheels
When they walk in a circle , they walk straight on all sides , and do not turn back . Wherever their heads are , and wherever they follow , they do not turn back when they walk .
All their bodies were full of eyes , with their hands and wings on their backs , and with their wings around them ; and so were the four wheels of the reins .
&quot; As for these wheels , I heard in my ears that they were rotating
Each of them has four faces : the first is the face of a man , the third is the face of a lion , the fourth is the face of an eagle
And the reins were lifted up ; and this is the living creature that I saw by the river of Capar
And the wheels walk by them ; And the wheels spread their wings ; And they rose up from the earth ; And the wheels did not turn away from them .
Those who stand , those who stand , those who rise , those who rise together , for the Spirit of the living is in the wheel
The glory of the LORD went forth from the threshold of the house , and stood above the threshold
When the reins were lifted up , they spread out their wings , and rose up from the earth before me ; and the wheels stood by them at the east gate of the house of the Lord ; and above them was the glory of the God of Israel .
&quot; Behold , these are the creatures which I saw on the banks of the river Jabbar , beneath the glory of the God of Israel ; and I knew that they were a mighty people
Each has four faces , four wings , and below the wings there is a pattern of human hands .
As for their faces and their bodies , I saw them before on the banks of the river Jabbar , and they went straight forward .
Then the Spirit lifted me up , and brought me to the east gate of the house of the Lord , which is toward the east ; and , behold , there were twenty-five men at the gate ; and I saw among them the chief of the people , Jason the son of Absalom , and Bhali the son of Benaiah .
&quot; The Lord said to me , &quot; Son of man , this is he who plots evil in this city
They said , &quot; The time of building the house is not yet near ; this city is a pot , and we are flesh .
Therefore , Son of man , when you prophesy , prophesy against them
&quot; The Spirit of the Lord descended on me and said to me , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I know what you have said in your mouths , O house of Israel , and what you have thought in your hearts ,
Thou hast multiplied the slaughter in this city , and filled the streets of the slain .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; Those you kill in the city are flesh , and this city is a pot , and you shall be taken out of it .
&quot; You are afraid of the sword , and I will bring it upon you , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; I will take you out of this city , and deliver you into the hands of strangers , and I will execute judgment among you
&quot; You will fall under the sword , and I will judge you in the land of Israel ; and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; This city shall not be your pot , nor your flesh therein ; and I will judge you in the borders of Israel .
&quot; You will know that I am the Lord , because you have not kept My statutes , nor My ordinances , but have followed the evil deeds of the nations around you
And it came to pass at the time of my prophecy , when Bhaliath the son of Benaiah was dead , that I fell on my face , and cried with a loud voice , saying , O Lord GOD , wilt thou destroy the remnant of Israel ?
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , the inhabitants of Jerusalem have said to your brethren , to your families , to your relatives , and to all the house of Israel , &quot; Stay away from the Lord , for this is the land which has been given to us for a possession
Therefore thus says the Lord , &quot; While I have moved all Israel far away into the nations , and have scattered them among the nations , I will also make them a sanctuary in the nations to which they have come ,
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; I will gather you from among all the people , and gather you from the scattered nations , and I will give you the land of Israel
And they shall come there , and they shall remove from it all that is abominable .
&quot; I will have a united heart among them , and I will put a new spirit in them , and I will remove the stone heart from their flesh , and give it to their flesh .
&quot; Let them obey My statutes , and keep My ordinances , and they shall be My children , and I will be their God .
&quot; As for those who follow in their hearts abominations , I will recompense them on their heads according to what they have done , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
Then the reins spread out their wings , and the wheels were by them ; and above them was the glory of the God of Israel .
The glory of the Lord ascends from the city , and stands on the mountain east of the city
And the Spirit lifted me up , and borrowed the Spirit of God in the visions , and brought me into the land of Galilee , into the captivity ; and the visions which I saw ascended from me .
&quot; I will tell the captives all the things that the Lord has commanded me
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , you dwell in the houses of the rebellious , who have eyes to see and ears to hear , for they are the houses of the rebellious
Therefore , O son of man , prepare for your captivity the things which you shall use , and move away from the place where you dwell in the daytime when they are in their sight , though they may be houses of rebellion , or think
You shall bring forth your goods in the daytime before them , as if they were ready to be taken captive for use ; and at night you shall go forth in their sight , as if they were taken captive .
&quot; You shall dig through the walls before them , and take your possessions out of them
&quot; When it is dark , you shall take them out on their shoulders , and cover your faces in the unseen ; for I have set you as a sign to the house of Israel .
And I went as I had been commanded , and brought forth my goods in the daytime , as if I had prepared them for captivity ; and at night I dug through the walls with my hands ; and when it was dark , I brought them out on their shoulders before their eyes .
&quot; The next morning the word of the Lord came to me
Son of man , the house of Israel is the house of iniquity . Have you not asked yourself , &quot; What are you doing ?
&quot; You shall say to them , &apos; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; This is the foretelling of the king of Jerusalem and of all the house of Israel around him
&quot; You shall say , &apos; As I am a sign to you , and as I shall do , and as they shall be confronted , they shall be taken captive .
And the king among them shall bring forth on his shoulders in the day of darkness , and they shall dig through the wall and bring forth out of it ; and he shall cover his face , and he shall be invisible .
&quot; I will spread my net over him , and he will be wrapped in my net , and I will bring him to Babylon , the land of the Chaldeans , where he died , and saw not the land .
I will surround him with all his helpers , and with all his armies , and I will disperse them all around , and I will chase them with the sword .
&quot; When I have scattered them among the nations , and have scattered them among the nations , they shall know that I am the Lord .
&quot; But I will leave a few of them free from the sword , and from the famine , and from the pestilence , that they may speak all their abominations in all the countries to which they come ; and they shall know that I am the Lord .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , you will be afraid to eat , and you will be afraid to drink water
Say to the people of the land , &quot; The Lord Yahweh speaks of Jerusalem and the inhabitants of the land of Israel , and they will be troubled to eat and to drink , and they will be troubled to drink , and the land will be desolate for all the abominations of those who dwell therein .
And the cities that dwell therein shall be desolate , and the land shall be desolate ; and ye shall know that I am the LORD .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , in your land of Israel , how is it said , &quot; The days are delayed , and all the wonders have fallen into the sky ? &quot;
&quot; Tell them , &apos; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; I will put an end to this saying , and it will no longer be spoken in Israel ; but you will say to them , &apos; The days are near , and all visions will be fulfilled
From now on there shall be no more false visions and oaths in the house of Israel .
&quot; My word , which I the Lord have spoken , will surely be fulfilled , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; and it will be fulfilled in the days of your rebellious house , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , the house of Israel said , &quot; The vision he has seen concerns many days to come , and the prophecy he has spoken concerns a long time
Therefore say unto them , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; There shall be no more delay in my word , neither shall there be any more delay in my words ; but that which I say shall be fulfilled , saith the Lord GOD
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , prophesy against the prophets who prophesy against Israel , and say to those who prophesy with their own hearts , &quot; Listen to the word of the Lord
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Woe to the foolish prophets , who follow their own hearts , and see nothing
Your prophet , O Israel , is like a fox in the wilderness
Neither did he go up and break the gates , nor did he rebuild the walls for the house of Israel , that they might stand in the battle in the days of the Lord
What they saw was a false and a false divination , and they said , &quot; It is the Lord who said , &apos; In fact , the Lord has not sent them , &apos; and they made people expect that it would be settled .
Have you not seen false visions ? Have you not spoken false divination ? Have you not said , &quot; This is what the Lord has said , &quot;
Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; Because what you say is false , and what you see is false , I am against you , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; My hand will attack the prophets who have seen false visions and deceived them , and they will not be in the congregation of my people , nor in the book of the house of Israel , nor enter the land of Israel ; and you will know that I am the Lord Yahweh .
For they have tempted My people , saying , &quot; Peace , but there is no peace , &quot; like a man who sets up a wall and wipes it with ashes that do not melt .
Therefore say to those who do not spread ashes , &quot; The wall will fall , and rain will pass over it ; and you will fall , O great hail , and the winds will break the wall .
&quot; When the wall has fallen , will no man ask you , &apos; Did you put ashes that did not melt in it ? &apos;
Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will be angry , and blow the wall with a gale , and in my anger I will cause a storm to pass over it , and I will send down a great hail , and destroy the wall
Thus will I destroy your walls , which have not been washed with ashes , and will break them down to the ground , so that the roots will be exposed , and the walls will fall , and you will perish in it ; and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; I will accomplish in my anger what I have commanded against the walls and against those who do not bury the walls with ashes , and I will say to you , &apos; There is no wall , and there is no one to bury the walls .
&quot; These are the prophets of Israel , who spoke the word of Jerusalem , saying , &apos; Behold , there is no peace in this city , &apos; says the Lord Yahweh .
Son of man , prophesy against the nations , against the women who prophesy from their hearts , and attack them
&quot; Woe to these women , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; for they have tied their arms to pillows for the people , and have made scarves for the lowly , and have sought the life of men ; have you sought the life of my people , and have saved them for your own sakes ?
&quot; You have defiled me among my people for two wheats , and for a few cakes ; you have lied to those who listen to lies ; you have killed those who should not die , and you have saved those who should not live .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; Behold , I am against your pillows , which you use to hunt for men , and which make the life of men fly like birds ; and I will take them out of your arms , and release them that you hunt like birds .
&quot; I will also tear off your scarves , and deliver my people from your hand , and they will no longer be hunted and fall into your hands ; and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; I do not grieve the righteous , but you grieve him with lies . You strengthen the hands of the wicked , so that he does not turn away from the evil way and is saved .
&quot; You will no longer see false visions , nor do divination ; I will save my people from your hand , and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; Some of the elders of Israel came to me and sat before me
And the word of the LORD came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , have they taken their false God into their hearts , and set before them the stumbling blocks of sin ? Shall I be asked of them at all ?
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; Whoever of the house of Israel takes his false god in his heart , and puts the stumbling block of sin before him , and the prophet has come , I the Lord will answer him according to his many false gods in all that he asks , or according to his many false gods I will repay him according to his many false gods
Take hold of them in the hearts of the house of Israel , for they have borrowed false gods to live with me
Therefore tell the house of Israel , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Turn away from your idols , and turn not your faces from all your abominations
&quot; For every one who is separated from me , the house of Israel , or any stranger who dwells in Israel , has taken his false God into his heart , and has placed stumbling blocks in his face , and has asked me for his own sake , and I , the Lord , will answer him in person .
&quot; I will turn my face to him , and make him a warner , a laughter , and a terror , and I will cut him off from among my people , and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; If a prophet is troubled , and he prophesies , &apos; I , the Lord , am troubled by the prophet , and I will stretch out my hand against him and destroy him from among my people Israel
&quot; They will bear their own iniquity , the iniquity of the prophets , and the iniquity of the inquirer .
&quot; So that the house of Israel will no longer depart from me , nor defile themselves in all their sins ; but that they may be my children , and I will be their God , &quot; says the Lord GOD .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , if a nation commits a crime against me , I will stretch out my hand against it to break its staff , to cut off its food , to bring famine to the land , and to cut off man and cattle from it .
&quot; Three of them , Noah , Daniel , and Job , saved their lives only by their righteousness , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
&quot; If I cause the evil beasts to pass through and trample the land , and make the land desolate , that no man may pass through because of them
&quot; While these three are among them , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; I have sworn by my eternal life , that they will not be saved , neither will they be saved , neither will they be saved , neither will they be saved , but they will be saved themselves ; and the land will be desolate
&quot; Or I will bring the sword to the land , and say , &apos; The sword will pass through the land , &apos; so that I will cut off men and cattle from it
&quot; Three of them are among them , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; and I swear by my eternal life that they will not be saved , neither will they be saved , neither will they be saved , neither will they be saved
Or I will cause the plague to spread over the land , and I will pour out on it the wrath of my death , that I may cut off men and cattle from it
&quot; Though Noah , Daniel , and Job were among them , &quot; said the Lord Yahweh , &quot; I swear by my eternal life , that they will not save their own lives , neither will they save their sons nor their daughters , except by their righteousness .
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; Shall it not be that I will bring down these four great plagues , the sword , and the famine , and the beasts of evil , and the plague , into Jerusalem , and will cut off men and cattle from there ?
&quot; But the remnant of them will come to you with their sons and their daughters , and you will see what they have done , and you will be comforted because of all the evil that I have sent down to Jerusalem .
&quot; You are comforted when you see what they have done , and know that what I have done in Jerusalem is not without cause , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , what is the strength of the vine above all other trees , and what is the goodness of the vine above all trees ?
For what work shall wood be taken on it , or for what vessel to hang a nail on it ?
Behold , it has been thrown into the fire as a firewood ; and the fire has burned two heads , and has been burned in the middle ; is it profitable for the work ?
What good is the perfect time , and what good is it to be burned ?
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; As I have made the grape tree within the trees to be a wood in the fire , so will I do to the inhabitants of Jerusalem
&quot; When I turn my face to them , you will know that I am the Lord , even though they come out of the fire , and the fire will burn them down .
&quot; I will make the earth desolate because of their deeds , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , make Jerusalem know his abominations
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh to Jerusalem , &apos; You were born in the land of Canaan , and your father was of the Amorites , and your mother of the Hebrews
&quot; For there was no circumcision for you in the days of your birth , nor wash you with water to purify you , nor wash you with salt , nor wash you with cloth
&quot; No eye can have pity on you , nor can it have pity on you for such a thing as this ; but your first days were thrown into the fields because you were despised .
&quot; When I passed by you , and saw you rolling in blood , I said to you , &apos; While you are in blood , you are alive , &apos;
&quot; I have made you grow as a field , and you have grown great in beauty , and you have become two breasts , and you have grown hair , and you are still naked .
&quot; I have passed by you , and I have seen your love in the days of love , and I have put my collar on you , and I have covered your redness , and I have sworn to you , and I have made my covenant with you , and you will be mine , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
Then I will wash you with water , and I will cleanse your blood , and I will anoint you with oil
And I will make you clothed in embroidered garments , and your feet in sandals of the skin of a mermaid ; and I will make you girded in linen , and I will clothe you with silk
&quot; He will dress you with ornaments ; He will put bracelets on your hands ; He will put gold on your bracelets .
&quot; I will put a ring on your nose , an ear ring on your ears , and a crown on your head .
Then you will have gold and silver , and you will wear fine linen and silk and embroidered flower garments , and you will eat fine flour and honey and oil , and you will be exalted in beauty and honour to the queen .
&quot; You are beautiful in all the nations because of the glory which I have added to you , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; But you have committed adultery because of your beauty , and because of your fame , and you have indulged in adultery , and have done what you will by the wayside .
&quot; You have adorned yourselves in high places with garments , and have done evil in them . There will be no such thing in the future , nor will there be any more .
And thou hast made for thyself idols of gold and silver , and of jewellery , which I have given thee of the beauty , and hast committed adultery with him
And clothe him with thy embroidered garments , and set before him my oil and my spices
&quot; And the food which I have given you , which I have given you , is fine flour , oil , and honey , a sweet offering before him , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
And thou shalt burn unto him the children that I have born
&quot; Isn &apos;t your prostitution a small thing , and you have killed my children , so that they may return to Him through fire ?
Thou hast done all these abominations and all these abominations , and hast not remembered the days of thy youth , when thou wast bare and rolled in the blood
&quot; Woe to you , &quot; said the Lord Yahweh , &quot; because you have done all these evil things
And they built for themselves towers , and high places in the streets .
Thou hast built high places at the gates of every city , and hast made thy beauty abominable ; and thou hast done many abominations with all that pass by .
And thou hast multiplied thy prostitution , and hast provoked me to anger with the Egyptians , which have given lust to thy neighbours .
&quot; Therefore I will stretch out my hand against you , and I will cut off your food , and I will give you to the daughters of the Philistines who hate you , that they may serve you freely , and that they may be ashamed of your wickedness .
&quot; You are not satisfied with the Assyrians because of your greed and your reluctance , and after your sexual intercourse with them
And you have done much wickedness , until you were not satisfied in the land of the ease , Caledonia .
&quot; You have done all these things without the knowledge of the shameful prostitute , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; and you have seen how weak your heart is
&quot; For you have built the tops of all the gates of the city , and raised up high places in the streets ; but you have despised the reward , and have not been like a prostitute
&quot; Woe to you , your obscene wife , who would rather receive a stranger than a husband
&quot; For every prostitute is given by men , and you give back to those whom you love , and bribe them to prostitute with you from all around .
&quot; You are contrary to other women , because you have given to others , and they have not given to you , and no one has given to you ; therefore you are contrary to other women
&quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , you prostitute .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : Because your filth is poured out , and your prostitution with your beloved is exposed , and because you have worshipped all the abominations , you have given to him the blood of your daughters and of your sons
I will gather together all those who love you , and all those who hate you , and I will attack you from all sides , and I will reveal your lower parts , and they will be exhausted .
And I will judge you as the ruler judges a prostitute and a woman who bleeds , and I will bring the sin of blood upon you in my wrath and in my hatred .
&quot; And I will deliver you into their hands , and they will break down your towers , and your high places , and strip away your clothes , and take away your treasures , and leave you bare .
&quot; They will bring many to attack you , and they will kill you with stones , and they will pierce you with swords .
&quot; I will burn your houses with fire , and judge you in the sight of many women ; and I will make you cease from prostitution and from giving to others .
&quot; I will cease my wrath against you , and my hatred will leave you , and I will be quiet and not angry .
&quot; Because you have not remembered the days of your youth , and because you have provoked me to anger in all these things , I will recompense you on your head according to what you have done , and you will no longer indulge in the abomination of prostitution , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; Everyone who speaks the tongue will strike you with the tongue , saying , &apos; How is the mother , and how is the daughter ?
You are the daughter of your mother , and you are the sister of your sisters , and you are the father of the Amorites , and you are the mother of the Hittites , and you are the sister of your sisters , and you are the father of the Amorites
Thy sister is Samaria , and she dwelleth with her brethren on thy left , and thy sister is Shedomah , and she dwelleth with her brethren on thy right
Thou hast not exercised thy power over their deeds , nor done that which is hateful unto them ; thou hast taken it for a small thing , and all that thou hast done is worse than they .
&quot; I swear by my eternal life , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; that your sister Sodom and her daughters have not yet done what you and your daughters have done
Behold , thus is the iniquity of thy sister Toomah ; and she and all her daughters are proud , and are full of food , and are well-off , and have no hand to help the needy and the poor .
&quot; They are arrogant and do abominations in front of me , and I see that they are removed .
&quot; Your sisters are justified because of all the abominations you have done , for Samaria has not sinned half as much as you , and you have done more abominations than he did .
If thou judgest thy sisters righteous , thou shalt bear the shame of thyself ; for the sins that thou hast committed are more abominable than they , and they are more righteous than thou ; and if thou makest thy sisters righteous , thou shalt be ashamed of the shame of thyself
&quot; I will bring back those who were taken captive ; I will bring back Sodom and her daughters , and Samaria and her daughters , and those who were taken captive among you .
so that you may bear the shame of yourselves , and comfort them for all that you have done , and you will be ashamed
Thy sister Sodom and her daughters shall be restored , and Samaria and her daughters , and thou and thy daughters , shall be restored
&quot; In the days of your pride , your evil deeds were not revealed , and your mouth did not speak of your sister Sodom ; and the daughters of Aram , who were oppressed , and the daughters of the Philistines around Aram , hated you , and despised you .
