&quot; The Lord said , &quot; You have fulfilled your lusts and your abominations
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; As for this oath which thou hast taken lightly , and hast rejected the covenant , I will be with thee according to that which thou hast done
&quot; But I will remember the covenant I made with you in your youth , and I will make an everlasting covenant with you
&quot; When you receive your sister and your sister , you will be ashamed of what you have done , and I will give them to you as daughters , but not according to the former covenant .
&quot; I will establish my covenant with you , and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; This is what the Lord Yahweh has said , that when I forgive you for all that you have done , you will remember and be ashamed of yourself , and will not speak again because of your shame
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , thou shalt make a riddle and a parable for the house of Israel
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; A great eagle , with great wings , and long feathers , and full of feathers , and full of colors , came to Lebanon , and twisted the tops of the acacia trees
&quot; It is to cut down the young branches of the palm tree , and to bring them into the land of trade , and to put them in the city of trade .
And the branches of the land of Israel shall be planted in the fertile fields , and they shall be planted by the great waters , as a leaf-tree .
And it grew , and became a little vine spreading out , and its branches turned toward the eagle , and its roots were under the eagle , and it became a vine , and it gave forth branches , and it gave forth little branches
And there was a great eagle , with many wings and many feathers ; and the vine came over its roots from the bed where it had been planted , and made branches for its watering .
The tree is planted next to a fertile field full of water , and bears good branches and fruit , and becomes a beautiful grape tree
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; Will this vine prosper ? Will the eagle not bring forth its roots , remove its fruit , and dry it up , and dry up its young leaves ? Will it not bring forth its roots without power and multitude ?
Will the grape tree , though it has been planted , prosper ? Will it not be dried up by the east wind , and will it be dried up in the bed where it grows ?
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Say to the house of the rebellious , &quot; Do you not know what these things mean ? Tell them , &apos; The king of Babylon came to Jerusalem and brought the kings and the chiefs thereof into Babylon himself
&quot; Take from among the house of Israel a man who has made a covenant with him , and make him swear , and take away those who have power in the land
The nations can &apos;t stand on their own because they keep their covenants
&quot; But he betrayed the king of Babylon , and sent messengers to Egypt , asking them to give him horses and multitudes ; will he be able to prosper , and will those who do this escape , and will he be able to break the covenant ?
&quot; I swear by my eternal life , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; that he will die in Kyoto , where he will be king over Babylon .
&quot; When the enemy built forts and pitches , and fought with him , to cut off many people , Pharaoh could not help him , though he had a great army and a great multitude
He will not be able to escape from his oaths , from his covenant , from his surrender , and from all these things .
Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; I swear by my eternal life , and I must put this sin on his head , because he has neglected my oath and has rejected my covenant
&quot; I will spread my net upon him , and he will be bound in my net ; I will bring him to Babylon , and I will punish him there for my sins .
And all his army , and all that flee , shall fall under the sword , and all that remaineth shall be scattered around ; and ye shall know that it is the LORD that saith this
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; I will cut down the tops of the acacia trees and plant them , and I will cut down a branch from the tip of the top , and plant it on a high mountain .
He will plant it in the high mountains of Israel , and it will bear branches and fruit , and it will become a beautiful acacia tree ; and all the birds of the sky will dwell under it , under the shade of its branches .
All the trees of the field shall know that my Lord has made the tall trees small , and the low trees tall , and the green trees dry , and the dry trees have grown ; thus saith the Lord , and thus hath he done
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
&quot; How do you say in the land of Israel , &apos; The father has eaten grapes , and the son &apos;s teeth are turned into acid ? &apos;
&quot; I swear by my eternal life , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; that there will be no more excuse for you in Israel to use this proverb
Behold , all the world belongs to me ; as the father belongs to me , so the son belongs to me ; and he who commits a sin shall die .
If a man is righteous , and does righteous and reasonable things ,
He has not eaten of the idols of the mountain , nor looked upon the idols of the house of Israel , nor defiled his neighbor &apos;s wife , nor approached him in the days of his wife .
He will not lose a man , but give back to him the head of the debtor ; He will not take away his property , but will feed the hungry , and clothe the naked .
&quot; The brothers who have not borrowed money shall not profit , and the brothers who have not borrowed food shall not be exceedingly needy . They shall not shrink their hands in iniquity , and they shall judge between them according to the law .
&quot; He that keeps my statutes , and keeps my ordinances , and walks in truth , he that is righteous , he shall live , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
&quot; If he brings forth a son as a robber , and is a bloodthirsty man , he can do no more than that which is good in that which he says , and that which is evil in that which he does : he has eaten of the idols of the mountains , and has defiled his neighbor &apos;s wife
