&quot; He who has lost the poor and the needy , and who has taken away the things of men , has not given the head to men , and has looked to idols , and has done abominations .
&quot; The brother who borrows money will gain , and the brother who borrows food will need more . Will this man live , and he will not live , and he will do all these abominations , and he will die , and his sins will return to him
&quot; When he bears a son , and sees all the sins of his father , he is afraid that he will not do it .
They have not eaten idols in the mountains , they have not looked upon the idols of the house of Israel , they have not defiled their neighbors &apos; wives
He has not defrauded a man , He has not taken a man &apos;s head , He has not robbed a man &apos;s property , He has given food to the hungry , He has given clothing to the naked
He shall not cut off his hand from the poor , nor profit from his brother who has not borrowed money , nor give much to his brother who has not borrowed food ; and he shall not die for his father &apos;s iniquity , but he shall live by My statutes , and by My laws .
As for his father , he shall die for his own iniquity , because he deceived and robbed his brothers , and did evil in the people of his land .
&quot; You also say , &apos; Why does a son not bear the iniquity of his father ? If he does righteousness and righteousness , and keeps all my statutes , he will surely live .
&quot; But he who commits a sin shall die , and the son shall not bear the iniquity of his father , neither shall the father bear the iniquity of his son ; and the good of the righteous shall be his own , and the evil of the wicked his own .
&quot; If the wicked turns away from all his sins , and keeps all my statutes , and does righteousness and righteousness , he shall live , and not die .
He will not be remembered for all his sins ; but for the righteousness of his works he will live .
&quot; Is it good for me , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; that the wicked should die , or that he should return from his way of life ? &quot;
Will a righteous man live if he turns away from righteousness and commits iniquity , and follows all the abominations of the wicked , and all his righteousness is not remembered , and he shall die for the evil of his sins ?
&quot; You also say , &apos; The way of the Lord is not fair . &apos; Listen , O house of Israel , &apos; Is not my way fair ? Is not yours fair ?
&quot; If a righteous man turns away from righteousness and dies for his iniquity , he is dead for his iniquity .
And if the wicked man turns away from his evil deeds , and does righteousness and righteousness , he will save his life .
For when he thinks , and turns away from all his sins , he shall surely live until he die .
And the house of Israel said , &quot; Is not the way of the Lord fair ? Is not my way fair , O house of Israel ? Is not your way fair ?
Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; O house of Israel , I will judge you according to all your deeds , and you shall turn your backs from all your sins , and iniquity shall not defeat you .
&quot; You shall forsake all your sins and all your deeds , and make a new heart and a new spirit for yourselves . Why will you die , O house of Israel ?
&quot; I do not like the death of the dead , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; so return and live
When you mourn for the king of Israel ,
Saying , &quot; What is your mother ? She is a mother of lions . She sits in the middle of the lions , and raises little ones among the young ones .
He raised one of his little lions , and became a young lion , and learned to eat and eat men
And when the nations heard it , they took him in their pits , and drew him with hooks to the land of Egypt
When the lion saw that he was waiting , and lost hope , he took another from his little lion , and brought it up as a young lion
He walked among the lions , and became a little lion , and learned to eat and to eat men
Knowing the palaces of the nations , He made their cities a desolation ; for the voice of His roaring the whole earth was desolate , and all of them .
Then came the men of all the provinces of the land round about him , and cast nets upon him , and caught him in their pits
And they hooked him with hooks , and put him in a cage , and brought him to the king of Babylon , and put him in a strong place , and his voice was no more heard in the mountains of Israel .
&quot; Your mother was like a grape tree , and it grew exceedingly abundant ; and she planted it by the waters ; for when there was more water , it yielded more fruit and was full of branches .
A strong branch is formed , a staff for the ruler . It is raised up in a dense branch , and it grows tall and has many branches , and it is seen far away .
But the grape tree was brought forth out of wrath , and fell upon the earth ; and the east wind dried up the fruit thereof ; and the strong branches were broken and dried up , and were burned with fire .
Now planted in the wilderness , dry and without water
And the fire burneth the fruit out of his branches , so that there is no strong branch to be a staff for the ruler : this is a lamentation , and it shall be a lamentation .
On the tenth day of the first month of the seventh year , some of the elders of Israel sat before me , asking the Lord
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , tell the elders of Israel , &quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; Have you come to ask me ? &apos; &apos; I swear by my eternal life that I will not be asked of you
Son of man , will you question them , and tell them the abominations of their ancestors ?
And he said unto them , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; In that day have I chosen Israel , and have sworn unto the seed of the house of Jacob , and have revealed myself unto them in the land of Egypt , saying , I am the Lord your God
&quot; In that day I will swear to them that I will bring them out of the land of Egypt into the land of milk and honey which I have seen for them , a land of glory among all the nations .
&quot; I said to them , &apos; You shall all forsake the abominations which your eyes love , and you shall not defile yourselves with the idols of Egypt ; I am the Lord your God .
&quot; But they have rebelled against Me , they have not listened to Me , they have not forsaken the abominations of their eyes , and they have not forsaken the idols of Egypt ; and I said , &apos; I will pour out my wrath upon them , and I will accomplish in the land of Egypt what I have commanded them in my wrath .
&quot; But I have not done this for my name &apos;s sake , lest my name be defiled in the sight of the nations in which they dwell ; and I will bring them out of the land of Egypt , and I will appear to them in the sight of them .
&quot; So I brought them out of the land of Egypt , and brought them into the wilderness
Give them My law , and direct them My statutes ; and if they obey , they shall live .
&quot; And He gave them My Sabbath as a proof between Me and them , that they might know that My Lord has sanctified them
&quot; But the house of Israel have rebelled against me in the wilderness , they have not obeyed my statutes , they have rejected my ordinances , and they have greatly corrupted my Sabbath , and I said , &apos; Put my wrath on them in the wilderness , and destroy them
&quot; But I have not done this for my name &apos;s sake , lest my name be profaned in the sight of the nations that I brought them out of Egypt .
&quot; And I swore to them in the wilderness , &apos; I will not bring them into the land of milk and honey which I have given them ; it will be glorious in all the nations .
For they have rejected My statutes , they have not obeyed My statutes , they have broken My Sabbaths , and their hearts have followed their idols .
Nevertheless , my eyes spare them , and I will not destroy them , and I will not destroy them in the wilderness
&quot; I said to their children in the wilderness , &apos; Do not obey the law of your fathers , do not keep their evil deeds , and do not defile yourselves with their idols
&quot; I am the Lord , your God ; you shall obey my statutes , and keep my ordinances .
&quot; And I have sanctified my Sabbath , which is a sign between me and you , that you may know that I am the Lord your God .
&quot; But their children have rebelled against Me , they have not obeyed My statutes , and they have not kept My statutes , and they have committed a sin on My Sabbath , and if they have done so , they will live ; and I will pour out My wrath upon them , and in the wilderness I will accomplish what I have commanded them in my wrath .
&quot; However , for my name &apos;s sake I have not done so , lest my name be defiled in the sight of the nations that I brought them out of Egypt .
&quot; And I swore to them in the wilderness , that I would spread them out among the nations , and disperse them among the kingdoms
For they have not obeyed My statutes ; they have despised My statutes ; they have defiled My Sabbaths ; they have looked with their eyes upon the idols of their fathers .
And I have appointed them to obey the law that is not good , and to keep the evil that cannot make man live
&quot; Because they have burned all the firstborn , I have appointed them to defile themselves in their offerings , that they may be desolate , and that they may know that I am the Lord .
Son of man , tell the house of Israel , Thus says the Lord Yahweh : Your fathers have defiled me in my sins
&quot; Because I brought them to the land which I swore to give them , and they saw the high mountains and the bush trees , and sacrificed therein , and offered sacrifices that provoked me to anger , and burned incense therein , and poured out drink offerings
And I said unto them , What is the name of the high place which ye have taken up ? And the name of that high place is called Baasha unto this day .
Therefore say unto the house of Israel , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Have ye defiled yourselves as your fathers have defiled themselves , and committed adultery as they have committed abomination ?
&quot; Will I be questioned by you , O house of Israel , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; when you have offered sacrifices to burn your children in the fire , and have defiled all your idols to this day ?
&quot; You say , &apos; We will go to work with wood and stone , as the foreigners and as the nations of the nations , and this will not be accomplished . &apos; 
&quot; I swear by my eternal life , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; that I will be king over you with a mighty hand , and with an outstretched arm , and with an outcast wrath .
&quot; I will bring you out of the peoples , and gather you from the scattered nations , with a mighty hand , and with an outstretched arm , and with the outpouring of wrath .
&quot; I will bring you into the wilderness of the Gentiles , and I will punish you there face to face
&quot; As I have punished your fathers in the wilderness of Egypt , so will I punish you , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; I will make you pass under the rod , and you will be bound by the covenant .
&quot; I will take out of your midst those who are rebellious and sinful against me , and I will bring them out of their dwelling places , and they shall not enter into the land of Israel ; and you shall know that I am the Lord .
&quot; You , O house of Israel , thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; From now on , if you will not listen to me , you will appoint yourselves to minister to idols , but you will no longer profane my holy name by your offerings and by your idols .
&quot; In my holy mountain , which is the high mountain of Israel , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; all the house of Israel will serve me , and I will please you there , and I will give you provisions , and first fruits , and all the holy things
&quot; I will bring you out of all the people , and gather you from the scattered lands , and I will make you acceptable as a sweet offering , and sanctify you in the sight of the Gentiles .
&quot; I will bring you into the land of Israel , which I swore to give to your fathers , and you will know that I am the Lord
In it you shall remember your defiled deeds , and you shall despise yourselves for all evil deeds which you have done .
&quot; You will know that I am the Lord , &quot; said the Lord Yahweh , &quot; because of my name , O house of Israel , I will not deal with you according to your evil deeds and your evil deeds .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , turn toward the south , and pour down the prophecy toward the south , and smite the forests of the south
&quot; Speak to the forests of the south , &apos; Listen to the word of the Lord , &apos; says the Lord Yahweh ; &apos; I will cause a fire to rise in your midst , and I will burn all the green trees and the dead trees in your midst ; and the fierce flame will not be quenched ; and from the south to the north the faces of men will be burned .
&quot; Everyone who has blood will know that I , the Lord , have set fire , and it will not be quenched .
Then I said , &quot; Oh , Lord Yahweh , all have pointed to me , saying , Is he not a parable ?
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , prophesy against Jerusalem and the sanctuary , and attack the land of Israel
&quot; Thus says the Lord to Israel , &apos; I am an enemy with you , and I will take the sword out of the sheath , and cut off the righteous and the wicked from among you
&quot; I will cut off the righteous and the wicked from among you ; so I will cast out my sword from the sheath , and I will attack every bloodthirsty one from the south to the north .
And every bloodthirsty man shall know that my Lord hath taken the sword out of the sheath , and shall not enter therein any more .
Son of man , shout , and bend your back before them , and shout bitterly .
&quot; When they ask you , &apos; Why are you sighing ? &apos; you will say , &apos; Because there is a wind , and a calamity is coming , and the hearts will digest , and the hands will weaken , and the spirit will fail , and the knees will weaken like water . Behold , the calamity is near , and it will be accomplished , &apos; says the Lord Yahweh .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , thus saith the Lord unto me , Prophesy : There is a sword , and there is a sword , which is polished and polished
Blessed are we that grind for slaughter , that polish for lightning , that we despise the trees with the rod of punishment of my son ?
The sword has been given to a man to be polished , to be used by his hands ; and the sword has been polished , to be given to a man who kills .
Son of man , cry out and mourn ; for the sword has come upon my people and upon all the princes of Israel , and they and my people are delivered under the sword ; therefore weep with our feet .
&quot; But what if the rod of despise becomes desolate , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
Thou shalt prophesy , O man , with a clapping hand , that I , the Lord , will cause this sword , the sword of death , to come into their houses , and to smite them twice and three times , and that the adult that is injured may die with it
&quot; I have set up this sword of terror against all their gates , and I have made their hearts to digest , and I have increased their fall : for it is made like lightning , sharpened and sharpened to kill .
&quot; O sword , turn to the right hand , and place it to the left , and turn to that side , and slay it .
&quot; I will also shake my hands and put an end to my wrath , &quot; says my Lord
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , you shall make two ways , that the sword of the king of Babylon may come ; and they shall be separated from one place ; and you shall draw a hand at the intersection of the city .
&quot; You shall make a way for the sword to come to Rabbah of the Ammonites , and a way for the sword to come to Jerusalem , the strong city of Judah .
For the king of Babylon stood at the crossroads at the two intersections , and he waved his hand , and asked for the image of God , and looked at the liver of the slain .
He has in his right hand a sign for Jerusalem , that he may set up a hammer against the city , and open his mouth to shout , and shout , and build a fort , and a platform , to strike the hammer against the city , and to smite the gates thereof
It seemed to the Jews who had sworn it to be a false divination , but the king of Babylon was going to remind them of their iniquity , and to seize them
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Because your transgressions are manifested , and your iniquities are remembered , and your iniquities are manifested in your deeds , and because they are remembered , they are seized
&quot; The end of your iniquity has come , O king of Israel , who has suffered death and wound and evil , and the days of your recompense have come
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; When the crown is removed and the crown is removed , the situation will be no more as it was before ; raise up the low one , and lower down the high one
&quot; I will overwhelm this country , and overwhelm it , and overwhelm it again , and it will no longer be , until the righteous man comes , and I will give it to him
&quot; Son of man , prophesy , and say , &apos; Thus says the Lord Yahweh concerning the children of Ammon and their oppression : &apos; There is a sword , and there is a sword that has come out , that has been polished for slaughter , that it may be swallowed up like lightning ,
They have seen for you false visions and false divinations , and they have put you on the neck of the wicked who are injured ; their iniquity has come to an end , and the days of recompense have come .
&quot; I will punish you in the place where you were made and where you grew .
I will pour out my anger on you , and I will pour out my fury on you , and I will deliver you into the hands of the beasts that are able to destroy .
Thou shalt be burned as a wood , and thy blood shall flow in the land , and thou shalt not be remembered again : for this is what the LORD hath spoken
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , will you question this bloodthirsty city , and let it know all that it hates ?
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; Behold , there is a bloody thing in this city , and the day has come for it to be recompensed , and it has defiled itself , and it has defiled itself .
For you have sinned because of the blood of men , and you have made idols , and you have defiled yourselves ; and the day of your recompense is near , and the year of your recompense is come ; therefore I call you to the reproach of the nations , and to the reproach of the nations .
&quot; Those who are near to you and far from you will mock you , O you filthy and troubled city .
&quot; Behold , the heads of Israel have done all that they could , and have poured out blood among you
Among you are those whose parents are weak , those whose dwellings are oppressed , and those whose widows are weak .
Thou hast despised my holy things , and hast broken my sabbaths
There is among you a slanderer who pours out blood , and a man who eats idols on the mountains , and a man who commits adultery .
Among you is he who dishonors his father by exposing himself to his mother , and a woman who is unclean in her menstruation .
He commits abominations with his neighbour &apos;s wife ; he defiles his daughters with lust ; and he defiles his father &apos;s sisters .
&quot; Behold , among you there are those who are bribed for bloodshed ; and there are those who lend to their brothers for profit , and those who lend to their brothers for food for much ; and they have forgotten me because of their greed , and because of their oppression , and because of their possessions , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; Behold , I will weep with my hands because of the unrighteousness of your riches and the blood that flows between you
&quot; When the days come when I will punish you , will your heart endure , and your hand be strong , and I the Lord will do as I have said
&quot; I will scatter you among the nations , and I will scatter you among the nations , and I will remove your filth from among you .
Thou shalt be defiled in the sight of the heathen for that which thou hast done : and thou shalt know that I am the LORD .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , the house of Israel is a waste to me ; they are all copper , tin , iron , and lead in the furnace ; they are all silver waste
Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will gather you together in Jerusalem , because ye are become dust
&quot; As a man gathers silver , copper , iron , lead , and tin into a furnace , and burns them with fire , so will I also be angry and wrathful , and gather you into the city , and burn you with fire .
And I will gather you together , and I will pour out My wrath upon you , and in it you will be destroyed .
&quot; As silver rots in the furnace , so will you rot in the city ; and you will know that My Lord has cast His wrath upon you
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , you shall say to him , &quot; You are a land that has not been cleansed , and there is no rain above you in the days of anger .
And the prophets of them dealt treacherously , as the roaring lion devoured the spoil ; and they swallowed up the people , and took away the treasures , and multiplied the widows in the land .
And the priests of them have enforced My law , and have profaned My holy things , and have not distinguished between the holy and the profane , neither have they made a distinction between the clean and the unclean , nor have they shut their eyes to My Sabbath , and I have been profaned among them
&quot; Their leaders are like wolves , who take away loot , and kill and bleed , and injure people , and earn injustice .
And the prophet of them that washed the walls of the people with ashes that had not been poured out , said , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; and the Lord GOD said not
The oppression of the peoples of the country , the practice of robbery , the loss of their livelihoods , the poverty of the afflicted , and the deceitful settlements
I have sought among them a man to repair the walls , to stand before me for the land , to break the gates , that I may not destroy it ; but I have found none
Therefore I will lay my wrath upon them , and I will destroy them with the fire of my wrath , and I will recompense them on their heads according to all that they have done , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , there are two women , one of whom is a mother .
They have committed adultery in Egypt ; they have committed adultery in childhood ; and when they were in it as maidens , they were embraced in their arms , and touched in their breasts .
Their name is Hera , and their sister &apos;s name is Aholibah ; and they are all to Me , and they have given birth to children ; and concerning their name , Hera is Samaria , and Aholibah is Jerusalem
And after that Aholah returned to me , he committed adultery , and lusted for his beloved , the Assyrians , his neighbours .
They were all in blue robes , ministers and vice-ministers , and riding on horses . They were lovely young men
And Aholah indulged in prostitution with the most beautiful of the Assyrians ; and he defiled himself with all the idols of the man whom he had loved .
He has not departed from prostitution since he was in Egypt ; for the Egyptians have been with him , touching his breasts , and sexual desires with him , when he was a virgin in his youth .
Therefore I will deliver him into the hand of his beloved , the Assyrian , whom he loved .
And they revealed his body , and took away his children , and slew him with the sword , and made him a detestable name among women , because they judged him .
His sister Aholiba , though she saw it , was more ugly than his sister , and more lustful than his sister , and more obscene than his sister
He loved the Assyrians of his neighbourhood , the princes of horses , and the vice-ministers , who were lovely young men , clothed in fine clothes .
I saw him defiled , and his two sisters followed him all the way
Moreover Aholibah increased in prostitution , because he saw the image of men painted on the walls , the image of the Chaldeans painted in blue .
And they had bands between their waist and their heads , and their caps hanging down from their heads ; and they were like the image of the Pharisees , like the image of the Babylonians ; and their place was in Galilee .
And when Aholibah saw them , he envied them , and sent messengers to see them in Galilee
Then came the Babylonians to the bed of his love , and they defiled him with his prostitution ; and he was defiled , and then he was separated from them in his heart
Thus he revealed his prostitution , and he revealed his lower body ; and my heart was with him as I was with his sister before .
He adds to his prostitution , and remembers the days of his youth in the land of Egypt .
Greedy lovers , strong and well-fit , as donkeys and horses
Then thou shalt remember the prostitution of thy youth , when the Egyptians embraced thy arms , and touched thy breasts .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; I will stir up those whom you loved first and who were born younger to you , and I will make them come and attack you around you
And all the Babylonians , and all the Chaldeans , and the Sepharites , and the Shu &apos;aites , and the Goats , and all the Assyrians with them , were governors , and vice- governors , and captains of armies , and were well-known , and they rode in horses , and were lovely young men
And they shall come against thee with weapons , and with chariots , and with chariots , and they shall lead the people : and they shall stand against thee with shields of great size , and they shall surround thee : and I will give them judgment , and they shall judge thee according to their own ordinances .
I will strike you with hatred , and they will execute you with wrath , and they will cut off your nose and your ears ; and those whom you have left will fall under the sword , and they will take away your children , and what you have left will be burned with fire .
&quot; They will strip away your clothes , and take away your precious treasures .
Thus will I put an end to your prostitution , and to the prostitution which you have inherited from the land of Egypt ; so that you will no longer look to Assyria , nor to Egypt .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will deliver thee into the hand of him that hateth thee , and into the hand of him that hateth thy heart .
&quot; They will do you evil , and take away all your labour , and leave you naked , and your nakedness , and your prostitution , and your prostitution with it , will be revealed .
&quot; They will do these things to you , because you have committed adultery with the Gentiles , and have been defiled by their idols .
&quot; You have walked the way of your sister ; therefore I will give her cup into your hand
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; You shall drink the cup of your sister , which is deep and wide , and full of abundance , that you may be reproached and ridiculed
&quot; You will be drunk , full of sorrow , and drink the cup of your sister Samaria , which is a dreadful cup
&quot; You shall drink this cup until it is consumed , and it will break and tear your breasts , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; because I have spoken it
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Because thou hast forgotten me , and hast cast me behind thy backs , then thou shalt be responsible for thy prostitution and for thine adultery
And the LORD said unto me , Son of man , wilt thou question Aholah and Ahholibah , and show them the abominations which they have done ?
&quot; They have committed adultery , and have the blood of murderers in their hands , and they have committed adultery with idols , and they have burned their children for my sake into idols by fire .
And what they have done to me is that they have defiled my sanctuary on the same day , the Sabbath day of my transgressions .
&quot; They killed their sons and offered them to idols , and entered in My sanctuary that day , and defiled My sanctuary ; this is what they did in My house .
And your two wives sent messengers to the far off , and the messengers came to them ; and you bathed yourselves for them , and adorned your eyes , and adorned yourselves
&quot; Set down on the bed of Huamei , and set a table in front of it , and put on it my ointment oil
There was a voice of peace and joy among the people ; and there came from the wilderness the wicked and the drunken , and they put bracelets on the hands of the two women , and put crowns on their heads .
And I said concerning this woman who was an old woman who had committed adultery , &quot; Now she will also be with him , and he will also be with him
And the man was with Ahara , and with the prostitute of Aholibah , as with a prostitute
There will be a righteous man who will judge them according to the example of the prostitutes and the women who shed blood , because they are prostitutes and have the blood of murderers in their hands .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; I will send many to attack them , and I will throw them away , and they will be taken away
&quot; They shall slay them with stones , they shall kill them with swords , they shall kill their children , and they shall burn their houses with fire .
Thus will I put an end to the prostitution in the land , that all women may be warned against your prostitution .
&quot; They will recompense you for your wickedness , and for your idolatry ; and you will know that I am the Lord Yahweh
The word of the Lord came to me again on the first tenth day of October the ninth year
Son of man , this day is the day of the king of Babylon near Jerusalem , and you shall record it .
&quot; You shall make a parable to the house of the wicked , saying , &apos; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; Put the pot on fire , and when it is done , pour water into it
And all the fat meat , the legs and the shoulders , shall be gathered therein ; and fill the pot with a good bone .
&quot; Take the best of the flock , and put the wood under the pot , and roll the pot , and boil the bones therein .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; Woe to this city of blood ! It is a pot of rust , and the rust of it has not been removed ; and the meat shall be taken out of one of them , and there shall not be a lot for it
&quot; The blood that flows in the city shall not fall on a rock of pure light , nor on the earth , but shall be covered with soil .
&quot; The blood that flows in this city falls on a rock of pure light . It cannot be hidden . It is from Me , that I may bring vengeance and recompense .
Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; Woe to this bloody city ! I will also pile up a great pile of firewood
Add wood , let the fire be boiled , let the meat boil , let the soup boil , and let the bones be roasted
&quot; Set the pot on the fire , and heal the pot , and make the copper red , and purify the filth thereof , and purify the rust thereof .
The boiler is weary , and the great rust that it has grown has not been removed ; it cannot be removed with fire .
There is prostitution in your filth ; I have cleansed you , but you are not clean ; and your filth will not be clean again , until I have stopped my wrath against you .
&quot; This is what the Lord Yahweh has spoken ; He will do according to his word , He will not return , He will not despair , He will not repent ; He will judge you according to your actions , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , I will suddenly take away what your eyes love , and you will not weep nor weep .
&quot; Only sighs shall be heard , and no voice shall be heard , and no mourning shall be done ; and they shall be clothed with scarves on their heads , and they shall be clothed with shoes on their feet , and they shall not be covered with lips , and they shall not eat the food of the hanging . &quot;
Then I told it to the people in the morning ; and my wife died in the evening ; and the next morning I did as I was commanded .
&quot; The people asked me , &quot; What do you have to do with us , and do you not tell us
&quot; I answered them , and the word of the Lord came to me
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh to the house of Israel , &apos; I will desecrate my sanctuary , which is the glory of your power , the love of your eyes , the love of your heart , and the children that you have left , and they will fall under the sword
&quot; At that time you will do what my servant has done , and you will not have your lips covered , and you will not eat the food of the hanging .
And you shall wrap your heads in a veil , and you shall put shoes on your feet ; and you shall not weep , but you shall weep for your iniquity , and it shall come to pass that you shall perish
&quot; This is how He will prophesy for you , and you will do as He did ; and when it comes , you will know that I am the Lord Yahweh .
Son of man , I have removed from them the glory in which they rely , the joy in which they rejoice , and the children whom they love in their eyes , and in their hearts ,
&quot; Did not the man who fled that day come to you to make your ears hear this ?
Thou shalt speak unto them that flee , and shalt not be dumb any more : thus shalt thou prophesy unto them , and they shall know that I am the LORD .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , prophesy against the children of Ammon , and attack them
&quot; Listen to the words of the Lord Yahweh ; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; My sanctuary has been defiled , and the land of Israel has become desolate , and the people of Judah has been taken captive . &apos; 
&quot; Therefore I will give your land to the people of the east , and they will dwell in your land , eating your fruit , and drinking your milk .
&quot; I will make Rabbah a camel &apos;s field , and the land of the children of Ammon a bed for sheep ; and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; For thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; You have rejoiced in the land of Israel because of your clapping hands and feet , and because of your heart &apos;s anger
&quot; Therefore I will stretch out my hand against you , and I will deliver you into captivity among the nations , and I will cut you off from among the people , and I will destroy you from among the nations , and you will know that I am the Lord .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Because the men of Moab and the children of Seir said , Behold , Judah is like all the nations
&quot; Therefore I will cut off the cities on the border of Moab , which are Beer-sheba , Baal-sheba , and Gilead , which the Moabites consider to be the glory of their country .
And I will give the land of the children of Ammon to them for a possession , and they shall not be remembered in the nations .
&quot; I will judge Moab , and they will know that I am the Lord .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : For it is a great sin that Edom hates to retaliate against all Judah , and to retaliate against them
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; I will stretch out my hand against Edom , and cut off men and cattle , and I will cause Edom to come up from the top of the mantle , and men shall fall under the sword , and the land shall be desolate , and straight to the bottom of Dan .
And I will recompense Edom by the hand of my people Israel , and they shall recompense it with my wrath , and with my wrath ; and they shall know that I recompense it , saith the Lord GOD .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Because the Philistines have avenged the Jews , they have avenged them with bitterness , with bitterness , with everlasting hatred , to destroy them
Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD ; I will stretch out my hand against the Philistines , and cut off the Chaldeans , and destroy the remnant of the coastal inhabitants
&quot; When I retaliate against them , they will know that I am the Lord
The word of the Lord came to me on the first day of November the eleventh year
Son of man , because Tyre said to Jerusalem , &quot; Aha , the gate of the people , has been destroyed , opens to me , and he has become a wilderness , and I will be rich
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; I will be an enemy unto thee , O Tyre ; and I will cause many nations to come upon thee , as the sea brings forth a wave
&quot; They will destroy the walls of Tyre , and the buildings of his city ; and I will cleanse the dust , and make him a rock of pure light .
&quot; He will be a net in the sea , and a captivity for the nations , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
And the inhabitants of the cities of Tyre shall be slain with the sword ; and they shall know that I am the LORD .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will send Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , king of all the kings , and I will drive forth against thee from the north horsemen , and horsemen , and many people ,
And he shall slay the inhabitants of thy cities with the sword ; and he shall set up bases and shields against thee .
He will strike your walls with a hammer , and break down your buildings with iron .
For his horses are many , and the dust is lifted up to cover you , and he enters into your gates as if he had entered a city that is broken , and your walls will shake with the sound of horses and chariots and heavy vehicles .
His hoofs shall trample upon all thy streets , and he shall slay thy inhabitants with the sword ; and thy strong pillars shall fall upon the earth .
&quot; They will take away your treasures , they will take away your goods , they will destroy your walls , they will destroy your beautiful houses , they will throw your stones , your wood , and your dust into the waters .
And I will make the voice of thy singing cease ; and the voice of thy harp shall no more be heard .
&quot; I will make you a rock of pure light , a place of sunshine , and you shall not be built again , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh to Tyre , &apos; Will not the islands be shaken by the noise of your fall , when you kill among you , and the wounded mourn ?
Then shall all the kings that are by the sea come down , except to be clothed , and to take off their garments , and to be clothed in terror , and to sit on the ground , trembling at the same time , and trembling for you .
&quot; They will mourn for you , saying , &apos; What is the destruction of this famous city , which is the strongest in the sea , wherein you and your inhabitants dwell , and wherein all those who dwell are terrified ?
Now , in the days of thy overwhelming , the islands of the sea shall tremble ; and the islands of the sea shall tremble when they see that thou art desolate .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; I have made you a desolate city , like a city without inhabitants , and I have made deep waters pass over you , and great waters have drowned you .
Then I will cause you to go down into the abyss , and to dwell with the ancients in the depths of the land , in the desolate land , that you may have no inhabitants ; and I will be glorified in the land of the living .
&quot; I will make thee a terror to man , and he shall not dwell in the world ; and they will seek thee , but they will not find thee , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , weep for Tyre
&quot; You dwell at the mouth of the sea , and you are a merchant for the people , and your merchandise reaches to many islands , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh . &quot; You said , &apos; I am absolutely beautiful ,
Your boundaries are in the sea , and He has made you beautiful .
And they made all the boards of thee of the pine trees of Shenner , and of the acacia trees of Lebanon masts .
Use the oak tree of Bashan for your oars , and make boards of the fig tree of the island of Tihi with ivory .
&quot; Your sails shall be of fine embroidered linen from Egypt ; they shall be your flags ; and your shelters of blue and purple from the island of Elisha .
&quot; The inhabitants of Sidon and Apheum will be your oars , and the wise among you will be your stewards .
And the elders of the Chaldeans and the wise men were among you to make a seam ; and all the ships of the sea and the sailors were among you to do business .
The Persians , the Luddites , and the Philistines were soldiers in your camps , and they hanged shields and helmets among you , to show your glory
&quot; Behold , the children of Ammon and your army are on the walls that surround you , and on your towers there are brave men who hang shields , and they are all your beauty .
And he made him a merchant for you , because of all your riches : he took silver , iron , tin , lead , and exchanged your goods .
And the children of Jacon , and the children of Tyre , and the children of Mizpah , have traded with thee , and have exchanged thy goods with people and with vessels of brass
&quot; Your goods are exchanged by the tribe of陀gamah with horses and battle horses and oxen
The people of Dan trade with you , and many islands are your ports , and they exchange elephants and wood with you .
&quot; They are your merchants because of your work , and they exchange your goods with green stones , purple embroidery , fine linen , corals , and red stones .
The people of Judah and the land of Israel trade with you , and they exchange your goods with wheat , cakes , honey , oil , and frankincense
And the great horsemen , because of thy work , and because of thy abundance of riches , took wine and white wool to trade with thee .
And the people of Dan and the people of Japheth shall exchange thy merchandise for threads , and for iron , and for pearls , and for irises .
&quot; O men of the earth , trade with you in expensive carpets , saddles , drawers ,
&quot; The children of Aram and all the princes of Kida are your merchants ; they trade with you with lambs , rams , and goats
The merchants of Sheba and Ramah trade with you , and they exchange your goods with all kinds of good spices , and with all kinds of jewels , and with gold
and the Haranites , and the Canaanites , and the children of Eden , and the merchants of Sheba , and the Assyrians , and the Gibeonites , to trade with you
&quot; These merchants have traded with you with goods of goods , wrapped in embroidered blue garments , and with beautiful clothes , bound with ropes in boxes of acacia wood .
And the ships which He hath appointed shall be joined together to carry the goods for thee , and thou shalt be exalted in the sea .
The rowing oars have brought you to the great waters , and the east winds have broken you in the sea .
Your treasures , your goods , your merchandise , your sailors , your stewards , your repairers , your traders , and your soldiers , and your people , will be drowned in the sea in the days of your destruction .
As soon as the voice of your steering wheel blows , the countryside will shake
Every rover , and every sailor , and every captain of the sea , shall go down and come to shore .
&quot; They will weep for you with a loud voice , and they will roll the dust on their heads in ashes .
and make your head bald , and your loins clothed with linen , and your wings cried and mourned ,
When they cry , they will make a lamentation for you , saying , &apos; What city is there like Tyre , and what city is there like him alone in the sea ? &apos;
Thou hast provided many nations with goods by sea ; and thou hast enriched the kings of the earth with many riches and goods .
When you were broken by the waves in the depths , all your goods and all the people among you fell down .
The inhabitants of the islands are astonished at you , and their kings are terrified and sorrowful
All the merchants of the nations have cried unto thee , and thou hast terrorized the people , so that they shall not be left in the world for ever .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , you said to the king of Tyre , &quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; Because of your pride you say , &apos; I am God , and I sit in the seat of God in the sea , and you are neither man nor God , even though you are God in your heart
Behold , thou art wiser than Daniel , and nothing secret can hide from thee .
You are rich and rich in your own wisdom , in your treasures , in your treasures of income
You add to your wealth by your great wisdom and trade , and you are proud of your wealth .
Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD ; Because thou hast set thy heart above God ,
And I will bring unto thee the heathen , the mighty men of the nations ; and they shall cut down the beauty of thy wisdom , and blaspheme thy glory .
And they shall cause thee to sink , and thou shalt die in the sea , as the slain .
&quot; And you will say in the presence of those who kill you , &apos; Am I God ? Indeed , you are neither man nor God in the hand of those who kill you
&quot; You shall die in the hands of strangers , as those who are not circumcised , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , make a lamentation for the king of Tyre , saying , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Thou art full of all things , full of wisdom , and full of beauty
In the garden of the God of Eden you wore all kinds of jewels : red stone , red pearls , gold and steel , blue stone , blue stone , green stone , red stone , and gold ; and there were beautiful drums with you ; they were prepared in the day of your creation .
Thou art the veil of the anointed , the covering of the ark of the covenant : I will place thee on the holy mountain of God : thou art among the stones of fire .
You have done all things from the day you were created , and you have discovered injustice in your midst .
&quot; Because you have traded a great deal , you are filled with violence and crime ; therefore I have driven you out of the mountains of God for your blasphemy of the holy land ; and I have destroyed you from the treasures of fire-like brightness , O covering the ark of the covenant .
I have cast thee down to the ground , because thou art exalted in thy beauty , and hast destroyed wisdom by glory ; and I have laid thee down before the kings , that they may see .
You have profaned the sanctuary thereof because of the multitude of your iniquities and your unrighteousness in trade ; therefore have I sent out fire from among you , and have burned you , and have made you ashes on the earth before all those who look at you .
Everyone among the nations who knows you will be astonished at you . You have made people astonished , and you will not remain in the world for ever .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , prophesy against Sidon , and smite him
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; O Sidon , I am an enemy unto thee , and I will be glorified among thee , and I will judge among thee in the holy hour , and they shall know that I am the Lord
I will send a plague into Sidon , and blood will flow in his streets ; and he who is slain will fall in it , and swords will come upon him all around , and they will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; Those who encircle the house of Israel , and hate them , will no more be a thorn in their midst , nor a rustle in their midst ; and they will know that I am the Lord Yahweh .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will gather the house of Israel , which are scattered among all the people , and I will sanctify them in the sight of the heathen , and they shall dwell in the land which I have given to my servant Jacob ;
&quot; They shall dwell in peace in this land ; and they shall build houses and vineyards , and dwell in peace , after that I have judged them all around , and I have hated them ; and they shall know that I am the Lord their God
&quot; The word of the Lord came to me on the twentieth day of October ,
Son of man , prophesy against Pharaoh king of Egypt and against him and against all the land of Egypt
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; I am an enemy to you , O Pharaoh king of Egypt , the great fish that lies in your river ; for you said , &apos; This river is mine , and I have made it for myself
&quot; I , Yahweh , will hook your cheeks with hooks , and I will cause the fish of the river to stick to your scales , and I will bring you up out of the river , and all the fish that stick to your scales
&quot; You shall be thrown into the wilderness , and the fish in the rivers ; you shall be laid down in the fields , and not taken away , nor buried ; I have given you food for the beasts of the field , and for the birds of the air .
&quot; All the inhabitants of Egypt will know that I am the Lord , because I have made a rod for the house of Israel
&quot; When they hold on to You with their hands , You break them , You hurt their shoulders , They lean on You , You break them , You light their waist
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; I will bring the sword upon you , and cut off men and cattle from among you
And the land of Egypt shall be desolate and desolate , and they shall know that I am the LORD : for they said unto Pharaoh , This river is mine , and I have made it
Therefore I will be an enemy to thee , and to thy rivers ; and I will make the land of Egypt desolate and desolate , from the land of Chernith even unto the land of the ancients .
The feet of men and the feet of beasts have not passed , and no man has dwelt forty years .
I will make the land of Egypt desolate in the land of desolation , and the city of Egypt desolate in the land of desolation forty years ; and I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations , and among the kingdoms .
&quot; Forty years have passed , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; and I will gather the Egyptians from among the nations
And I will bring back the captives of Egypt , and I will bring them back to the land of Bath-theroah , wherein they shall be a lowly nation .
I will be the least of the nations , and I will no longer be above the nations . I will reduce them , and I will no longer rule over the nations .
And Egypt shall no more be the house of Israel upon which they rely ; and when they look upon the Egyptians , they shall remember their iniquity ; and they shall know that I am the Lord GOD .
&quot; The word of the Lord came to me on the first day of the first month of January ,
Son of man , Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon made his army strive against Tyre with great might , so that their heads were bald and their shoulders weakened ; yet he and his army strive against Tyre , and there was no reward therefrom
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will give the land of Egypt unto Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon , and he shall plunder the people of Egypt , and plunder their riches , and plunder their goods ; and this shall be the recompense of his army .
&quot; I will give him the land of Egypt for his labour , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; because the king and the army have worked for me
&quot; In that day , I will make the corners of the house of Israel open , and you will be able to speak in the midst of them , and they will know that I am the Lord .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , prophesy , saying , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Woe unto you this day , ye shall cry out
For the day of the Lord is near , the day of the clouds , the time of punishment for the nations .
And the sword shall come upon Egypt , and the ancients shall suffer , and the people shall be taken captive , and the foundations shall be destroyed , when the slain shall fall .
The ancients , the Philistines , the people of Lybia , the Luddites , the Gentiles , the Cubans , and the land of the Allies shall fall under the sword with the Egyptians
Thus saith the LORD ; The helpers of Egypt shall fall , and the pride of Egypt shall be low , and the people thereof shall fall under the sword , from Sheolphnetha , saith the Lord GOD ;
The land of Egypt shall be desolate in the land of desolation ; and the city of Egypt shall be desolate in the city of desolation .
&quot; When I set out a fire in Egypt , and all those who helped Egypt were destroyed , and they knew that I was the Lord
And it shall come to pass in that day , that there shall be an apostle in a ship , and he shall come forth from before me , and he shall terrorise the ancients who were restless , and pain shall come upon them as in the days of Egypt : behold , it is nigh !
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; By the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon will I destroy all Egypt
&quot; He and those who are with him , the mighty men of the nations , will come in and destroy the land , and they will strike Egypt with swords , and there will be slain in all the land .
&quot; I will drown the rivers and sell the land in the hands of the wicked , and I will make the land and all that is therein desolate by the hand of the heathen , &quot; says my Lord .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will destroy the idols , and the images of God from Noah ; and there shall be no more kings from the land of Egypt ; and I will make the people of the land afraid
&quot; I will desolate Bath-theroah , I will set fire in Zoan , I will judge Noah .
&quot; I will lay down my wrath on the shelter of Egypt , that is , on the instruction , and I will cut off all the people who disperse .
&quot; I will set out a fire in Egypt , and the punishment will be great , and Noah will be destroyed , and Noah will see his enemy in the day of darkness , or at the end of the day
And the young men of Aven and Beer-sheba shall fall under the sword ; and the men of these cities shall be taken captive .
And I will answer the yoke of Egypt , and I will make him proud of his power , and I will rest therein ; then shall the sun be turned away , and there shall be clouds covering the city , and the women therein shall be taken captive
&quot; I will thus judge Egypt , and they will know that I am the Lord
The word of the Lord came to me on the seventh day of the first month of the eleventh year
Son of man , I have broken Pharaoh the king of Egypt &apos;s arm , and there is no medicine or cloth to bind him , so that he may hold the sword strongly
Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I am an enemy unto Pharaoh king of Egypt , and I will cut off all his mighty arm , and his broken arm , and the sword shall fall from his hand
&quot; I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations , and I will scatter them among the kingdoms
I will strengthen the arm of the king of Babylon , and I will put my sword in his hand , and I will break Pharaoh &apos;s arm , and he will mourn before the king of Babylon like a man who is injured to death .
&quot; I will support the arm of the king of Babylon , and the arm of Pharaoh will fall , and I will give my sword into the hand of the king of Babylon , and he will strike the land of Egypt with his sword , and they will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations , and I will scatter them among the nations , and they will know that I am the Lord .
The word of the Lord came to me on the first day of March the eleventh
Son of man , you shall say to Pharaoh king of Egypt and to all his people , &quot; Who can be compared to you in power ?
The king of Assyria was like a cypress tree in Lebanon , its branches were beautiful , its shadows like a forest , and its height was exceeding high , and its branches were placed in the clouds
The waters of the earth grow him up , and the deep waters grow him up ; and the land that he planted was surrounded by rivers and streams , and watercourses that stretched out to all the trees of the field
Therefore he is greater than all the trees of the field , and branches are multiplied in the days of prosperity , and branches are long because of the power of great water .
And the birds of the air lodged in branches ; and the beasts of the field gave birth under branches ; and under His shadow dwelled all the peoples of great power .
The tree grows tall , and becomes glorious , because it is by the waters of the people
The acacia trees of the Garden of God will not cover him ; the pine trees will not have His branches , and the maple trees will not have His branches ; and the trees of the Garden of God will not have His glory .
I have multiplied his branches , and I have made them glorious , so that the trees of the Garden of Eden of God are jealous of him .
Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; Because he is great , and the tops of the trees are in the clouds , and he is proud
And I will deliver him unto the mighty of the nations , and he shall do him ; and I have driven him away for his iniquity .
And the heathen , the mighty among the heathen , have cut him down , and his branches have fallen in the mountains and in all the valleys ; and his branches have been broken , and he has fallen by all the rivers of the earth ; and the people of the earth have passed by , and have departed from his shadow .
The birds of the air shall dwell in the fallen tree ; and the beasts of the field shall lie under its branches .
That the trees by the waters may not be proud of their height , and that they may not put their branches in the clouds ; and that those who are filled with water may not be strong , and that they may not be proud of themselves : for they are brought to hell , both in the world and in the pits .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; In the day when he falls into the shadows , I will make men mourn ; I will cover the depths for him ; I will make the rivers melt and the waters melt ; I will make Lebanon mourn for him ; I will make all the trees of the field faint for him .
And I cast him into the shadow , and went down with the men of the pit : and when all the nations heard the sound of his fall , they trembled , and all the trees of Eden , the best and most beautiful trees of Lebanon , were comforted in the shadow .
And they shall be with him in the shadow of the slain : they shall be his arm , and they shall dwell in his shadow in the nations .
&quot; Who can be compared to you in this glory among the trees of the Garden of Eden ? But you shall go down to the dungeon with the trees of Eden , and lie down with the slain among the uncircumcised , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
The word of the Lord came to me on the first day of December twelve :
Son of man , you shall mourn Pharaoh king of Egypt , saying , &quot; You used to be like a small lion among the nations , and now you are like a great fish in the sea . You have poured out the rivers , and with your claws have stirred up the waters , and have made the rivers turbid
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; With the multitude of the nations I will spread my net upon thee , and bring thee up
&quot; I will cast you down on the earth , and throw you into the fields , and the birds of the air will fall on you , and the beasts of the earth will eat you .
&quot; I will cast your flesh into the mountains , and fill the valleys with your great bodies .
And I will pour out thy blood upon the land wherein thou didst swim , and I will pass over the mountains , and the rivers shall be full
When I destroy you , I will cover the heavens , and the stars will be darkened , and the sun will be covered with clouds , and the moon will not shine .
&quot; I will make the light of the heavens dim above you , and I will make darkness in your land , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
I will send a wind of your defeat to countries you do not know , and I will cause the hearts of many people to grieve for you .
&quot; When I shake my sword at you in the presence of many nations and kings , the nations will be astonished at you , and the kings will be terrified at you ; and in the days of your fall they will tremble for their own lives .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; The sword of the king of Babylon shall come upon thee
&quot; I will bring down your people with the sword of the mighty , the mighty of the nations , and they will make the pride of Egypt desolate , and the people of Egypt shall be destroyed .
And I will cut off all the beasts of the field from the waters of Egypt ; and the feet of men and beasts shall no more stir up the water .
&quot; In that day I will make the river of Egypt clear , and the river will be as oil , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
I have made the land of Egypt desolate and desolate , a land that had not been filled , and I have struck all its inhabitants , and they shall know that I am the Lord
And the daughters of the nations shall mourn with this lamentation for Egypt and for his people , saith the Lord GOD
The word of the Lord came to me on the fifteenth day of December twelve :
Son of man , you shall cry out for the people of Egypt , and throw Egypt and the women of the land of fame into the dungeon together with the men of the pit .
&quot; Who is more beautiful than you in Egypt ? Go down and lie down with the uncircumcised
And they shall be servants to the slain , and he shall be given to the sword , and he and his people shall be driven away .
The mighty warriors shall speak to the king of Egypt and help him in the darkness : they are slain without circumcision , they have passed through , they lie still .
Assyria and all his people were in it ; and his people &apos;s graves were around him ; and they were all slain under the sword .
Their grave is in the depths of the pit , and all their people are slain with the sword round about their grave ; they have terrorized in the land of the living .
And Edom was there , and his people round about his tomb ; they were slain with the sword , and cast down uncircumcised : they had terrorized in the land of the living , and they were ashamed with the men of the pit .
He and his people set up beds among the slain , and the graves of his people were round about him . They were all uncircumcised and slain by the sword , and they terrified in the land of the living , and they were ashamed with those who fell into the pit , to prevent them from being placed among the slain .
Mizpah , and Toba , and all their multitude were in it ; and the tombs of their people were round about them ; they were all slain with the sword , uncircumcised ; and they were astonished in the land of the living .
They shall not lie down with the warriors who have not been circumcised ; they carry their own iniquity under their weapons , and their swords upon their heads , and their bones upon their heads ; they have terrorized the warriors in the land of the living .
&quot; You will perish among the uncircumcised , O Pharaoh , and lie down with the slain .
And Edom is in it ; and his king and all his princes shall lie down with the uncircumcised , and with the people of the pit , despite their might , among the slain .
And all the princes of the north , and all the Sidonians , went down with the slain : and they were astonished and ashamed , though they might warn : and they were not circumcised ; and they lay down with the slain ; and they were ashamed with the people of the pit .
And when Pharaoh saw them , he was comforted for the army that was slain against him , saith the Lord GOD
&quot; I have appointed Pharaoh as a terror in the land of the living , and Pharaoh and his people will be put among the uncircumcised and among the slain , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , tell the children of your land , &quot; I have brought the sword to that country , and the people of that country have chosen one of them to be their guardian .
And when he saw the sword coming upon the land , if he blow a trumpet , he would warn the people
&quot; Whoever hears the sound of the horn and is not warned , and the sword destroys him , his sin shall be upon his head .
He heareth the voice of the trumpet , and is not warned : his sin shall be upon himself ; and if he be warned , he shall save his own life .
&quot; If the watchman sees the sword coming , and does not blow a blow , so that the people are not warned , and the sword kills a man among them , and he dies in iniquity , yet I will requite the watchman for the sin of his death .
Son of man , I have set you as a watchman over the house of Israel ; therefore hear what I say , and warn them for me .
And I said unto the wicked , O wicked man , thou shalt surely die ; and if thou wilt not open thy mouth unto the wicked , and cause him to depart from the way that he hath done , he shall surely die in iniquity ; but I will requite thee for the sin of his death .
&quot; If you warn the wicked that they will turn away from what they have done , and they will not turn away , they will die in their iniquity , but you will save yourselves from sin
Son of man , say to the house of Israel , &quot; You often say , &apos; Our sins are on us , and we will perish ; how can we survive ? &apos;
Say thou unto them , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; I swear by my everlasting life that I will not cause the wicked to die , but that the wicked will turn away from the way that they have walked : turn again , O house of Israel , turn again , turn away from the wicked way ; and why shall they die ?
Son of man , say to the people of your land , &quot; The righteous man &apos;s righteousness will not save him in the day of sin , nor will the evil of the wicked man turn him away in the day of evil deeds , nor will the righteous man survive in the day of sin because of his righteousness . &quot;
&quot; I said to the righteous , &apos; You will surely live ; if he sins on his righteousness , his righteousness will not be remembered , and he will die for his iniquity .
Again , I said to the wicked , &quot; You shall surely die ; if he turns away from his sins and does righteousness and righteousness ,
He who returns his head and what he snatches will not sin , but will keep the law of life , and he will live and not die .
He will not be remembered for all the sins he has committed ; and he will surely live when he does righteousness and justice .
And the children of thy land say , The way of the Lord is not fair ; but their way is not fair .
A righteous man turns away from his righteousness and commits iniquity , and will die thereby .
As for the wicked , when he turns away from his wickedness and does righteousness and righteousness , he shall live .
&quot; You also say , &apos; The way of the Lord is not fair . &apos; &apos; I will judge you , O house of Israel , according to all your deeds
&quot; In the first five days of October of the twelfth year after our captivity , a man fled from Jerusalem and came to me , saying , &apos; The city has been destroyed .
Until the night of the first day , when the Spirit of the Lord came upon me , and opened my mouth , and the second morning he came to me , and my mouth was opened , and I remained silent .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
&quot; Son of man , &quot; said the man who lived in the desolate land of Israel , &quot; there is only one man who can possess this land ; and we are many , and this land is more for us to possess .
Therefore say to them , &quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; Will you eat bloody things , worship idols , and kill bloody people , and gain this land for yourselves ?
&quot; Do you trust in your own swords , and do abominations , and defile your neighbor &apos;s wives ? Can you also serve in this land ?
Thus shalt thou say unto them , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; I have sworn by my everlasting life , that he that is in the wilderness shall fall under the sword , and he that is in the fields shall be eaten by the beasts , and he that is in the shadows and in the holes shall die by the plague .
And I will make the land desolate and terrible ; and his pride shall cease , because of his power ; and the mountains of Israel shall be desolate , and no man shall pass by them .
I have made the earth desolate and terrible for all their abominations ; and they knew that I was the Lord
Son of man , the children of your land speak to you at the door of the house by the wall , and they say to each other , &quot; Come and hear what is from the Lord
They come unto thee as a people , and sit before thee as if they were my people ; and they hear not thy word , but go not forth : for their mouth is full of love , and their heart followeth riches .
They see thee as the singer of a noble voice , and they hear not thy words
Behold , what they say shall be fulfilled ; and when it is fulfilled , they shall know that there is a prophet among them .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , prophesy against the shepherds of Israel , and say to them , &quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; Woe to the shepherds of Israel ! They know how to shepherd themselves ! Will they not shepherd their flock ?
&quot; You eat fat , you wear wool , you slaughter fat , but you do not feed sheep .
Weak , you have no strength , you have no sickness , you have no healing , you have no wounds , you have no encirclement , you have no persecution , you have no return , you have no loss , you have no search .
For the sheep that have no shepherd are dispersed ; and when they are dispersed , they feed all the beasts
My sheep have been scattered in the mountains , and in the high places , and in all the earth ; no one seeks them , no one seeks them .
&quot; Therefore listen to the word of the Lord , you priests
&quot; I swear by my eternal life , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; for my sheep have become a prey to no shepherd , and have made food for all the beasts ; and my shepherds have not sought my sheep ; and they know not to shepherd themselves , nor to shepherd my sheep
&quot; Therefore listen to the word of the Lord , you priests
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will be an enemy unto the shepherds , and I will pursue my sheep by their hand , that they may no more shepherd the flock , neither shall the shepherd feed himself ; and I will save my sheep from their mouths , and I will no more be their food .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will seek the sheep of mine own accord , and I will find them
&quot; As the shepherd seeks his sheep in the days when they are scattered among the flock , so will I seek my sheep ; and in the days of darkness and darkness , when they are scattered , I will deliver them from there
&quot; And I will bring them out of all the people , and gather them from every land , and guide them back to their land ; and I will feed them on the mountains of Israel , and on every stream , and in every place of the land ,
And I will feed them in a good pasture ; and their fold shall be on the high mountains of Israel ; and they shall lie down in the fold of beauty ; and they shall graze in the fertile pasture of the mountains of Israel .
&quot; I will be my own shepherd of my sheep , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; that they may lie down
I will search for the lost , I will bring back the persecuted , I will wrap up the wounded , I will wrap up the sick , I will heal them ; I will exterminate the fat and the strong , and I will feed them with justice .
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh concerning you , O my flock : &apos; I will judge between sheep and sheep , between sheep and goats .
Do you , these fat sheep , eat grass in the beautiful fields for a small thing , and you trample the remaining grass with your feet ? Do you drink water , and do you trample the remaining water with your feet ?
&quot; As for my sheep , they shall eat only that which you trample , and drink that which you stir up
Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD ; I will judge between the fat and the lean
For you have scattered all the weak with your shoulders , and with your horns you have scattered them .
So I will save my flock from being a prey , and I will judge between the sheep and the sheep .
&quot; I will set up a shepherd for them , David my servant , to shepherd them , and he will be their shepherd
&quot; My Lord will be their God , and my servant David will reign among them , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; I will make a covenant of peace with them , and the beasts of the wicked will be cut off from the land ; and they will dwell in the wilderness , lying in the woods .
I will make their surroundings and My mountains a source of blessing , and I will cause the rain to fall when it rains , and blessings will come down like the rain of the spring .
And the tree of the field shall come forth , and the land shall yield fruit , and they shall dwell in peace in the land : and I will break their yoke , and deliver them from the hand of the man whom they have made a slave , and they shall know that I am the LORD .
They shall no longer be a prey to the Gentiles , and beasts of the earth ; nor shall they devour them ; but they shall dwell safely , and no one shall be afraid .
And I will give them a well-known plant , and they shall no more be destroyed in the land for famine , nor shall they be ashamed of strangers .
&quot; You shall know that I , the Lord , their God , am with them , and that their house Israel is my people , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
&quot; You are my sheep , the sheep of my pasture , the children of Israel , and I am your God , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
&quot; Son of man , turn to mount Siir and prophesy against him ,
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; Behold , I am an enemy to you , mount Siir , and I will stretch out my hand against you to strike you , and I will make you desolate and terrible .
&quot; I will make your cities desolate and desolate , and you will know that I am the Lord .
For thou hast always hated Israel , and struck them with the sword at the end of their affliction and of their iniquity .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; I swear by my eternal life that I will bring you to the vengeance of bloodshed , and that sin will chase you away , because you do not hate the bloodshed of evildoers .
&quot; I will make Mount Siir desolate and terrible ; I will cut off those who pass by .
&quot; I will make Mount Siir full of slain men , and they who are slain by the sword will fall into your mountains , and into your valleys , and into all the streams .
And I will make thee desolate for ever , and thy cities shall not be inhabited : and thy people shall know that I am the LORD .
&quot; Because you said , &apos; The two nations and the two kingdoms will be mine , and I will have them for my possession .
Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; I swear by my eternal life that I will be with you according to your wrath , and according to the jealousy of your hatred toward them ; and when I judge you , I will make myself manifest among them
&quot; You will also know that my Lord has heard all your blasphemies , which you have spoken against the mountains of Israel , saying , &apos; These mountains are desolate and are ours to destroy .
&quot; I have heard you exaggerate against me in your mouths , and add to my opposition .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; I will make thee desolate in the joy of all the earth
&quot; As you rejoice in the desolation of the land of the house of Israel , I will be with you according to what you have done ; and you and all the land of Edom will be desolate , O Mount Siir , and you will know that I am the Lord .
Son of man , prophesy to the mountain of Israel , saying , &quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , O mountain of Israel
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Because of the enemy he saith , Aha , the everlasting mountains are all mine inheritance
Therefore prophesy , saying , &quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh , &apos; Because your enemies have made you desolate and swallowed you up all around , so that you may be a possession to the rest of the heathen , and that many tongues and tongues may call you , and the people may say that you have a bad name .
Therefore the mountains of Israel shall hear the word of the Lord Yahweh , the great mountains and the valleys of the ditches , the desolate land , the abandoned city , the reproach that the rest of the strangers round about have taken .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh to you , &quot; I am as fiery as a fire , and I am angry with the rest of the foreigners and with all the people of the East , who rejoice and hate evil , and who take My land for a possession , and see it as a forsaken prey .
Therefore prophesy concerning the land of Israel , and say to the mountains , and to the valleys , and to the valleys of the fountains , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Because you have been ashamed of the Gentiles , I am wroth and wrathful
Therefore I have sworn , Thus saith the Lord GOD , Every foreigner round about you shall bear his own shame
O mountain of Israel , thou shalt give branches , and bear fruit for my people Israel ; for they are about to come
Behold , I am your helper , and I will turn to you , that you may sow
&quot; I will increase the number of all Israel above you , and the cities will be inhabited , and the wilderness will be built again .
&quot; I will add men and cattle to you , and they will multiply in number ; and I will make you dwell as before , and I will bless you more than before ; and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; I will cause men , my people Israel , to walk above you , and they will gain your wealth , and you will no longer cause them to lose their children
&quot; This is what the Lord Yahweh says , because people have said to you , &apos; You have swallowed up men , and you have slaughtered the people
Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD ; Thou shalt no more devour men , nor shalt thou cause the people to perish
&quot; I will make you no more to hear the reproach of the nations , nor to be reproached by the people , nor to stumble the people , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
Son of man , the house of Israel have defiled the land in their deeds , when they lived in the land ; and their deeds are defiled before me as the defilement of a woman in her period .
Therefore I have poured out my wrath upon them because of the blood that they poured on the land , and because they defiled it with idols .
I have scattered them among the nations , and I have scattered them among the kingdoms , and I have punished them according to their deeds .
&quot; When they have come to the nations where they have gone , they have profaned My holy name , because they say of them , &apos; This is the people of the Lord , and they have come out of the land of the Lord . &apos; 
&quot; But I forsake my holy name , which the house of Israel has profaned among the nations to which they have come .
Therefore say unto the house of Israel , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; O house of Israel , I do this thing not for your sakes , but for my holy name , which I have profaned in the nations wherein ye come
&quot; I will sanctify my great name , which has been profaned among the nations , and which you have profaned among them ; and when I will be sanctified in their sight and in your bodies , they will know that I am the Lord , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; I will take you from the nations , and gather you from the tribes , and guide you back to your land
&quot; I will sprinkle water on you , and you will be clean . I will cleanse you , and you will be cleansed from all filth , and you will be cleansed from all idols .
&quot; I will also give you a new heart , and I will put a new spirit in you , and I will remove the heart of stone from your flesh , and give it to your flesh .
&quot; I will put my Spirit in you , that you may obey My statutes , and keep My ordinances .
&quot; You shall dwell in the land which I gave to your fathers , and you shall be my children , and I will be your God
&quot; I will deliver you from all corruption , and I will cause the five valleys to flourish , and you will not go into famine .
&quot; I will cause the trees to bear fruit and the fields to yield more fruit , so that you will no longer be reproached by the heathen for your famine
Then you will remember your evil deeds and your wicked deeds , and you will despise yourselves for your iniquity and for your abominations .
&quot; You shall know , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; that I do this not for you , O house of Israel , when you are ashamed of your own deeds
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; I will cleanse you , and I will bring you out of all iniquity , and I will make cities to dwell , and the wilderness to be built again .
The people who pass by see it as a desolate land , but it is still a desolate land to cultivate .
&quot; They will say , &apos; The land that was once desolate is now like the garden of Eden ; and the cities that were desolate and desolate are now inhabited by a people strong .
Then the rest of the nations around you will know that my Lord has built the desolate place , and planted the desolate land , and that what I the Lord said will be accomplished .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; I will increase the number of the house of Israel as a flock of sheep , and they will ask me for it , and I will accomplish it for them .
As the flock of sheep which Jerusalem sacrifices for the feast , so shall the cities of the wilderness be filled with multitudes , and they shall know that I am the Lord .
&quot; The Spirit of the Lord descends on me , and the Lord takes me out through His Spirit , and puts me in the plain , which is full of bones
And he made me pass through the wrecks ; and who knows how many wrecks are in the plains , and how they are dried up
And he said unto me , Son of man , will these bones be raised again ? And I said , Thou knowest , O Lord GOD .
Then he said to me , &quot; You have prophesied to these bones , saying , &apos; Listen to the word of the Lord , you dead bones
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh to these bones : &apos; I will breathe into you , and you will live .
&quot; I will add to you muscles , and I will give you flesh , and I will cover you with skins , and I will breathe into you ; and you will live , and you will know that I am the Lord .
Then I obeyed to prophesy , and in the hour of prophecy there was a sound and an earthquake , and the bones were joined together
And I looked , and behold , there were muscles on the bones , and flesh that was long , and skin covering them : but there was no breath yet .
And the Lord said to me , Son of man , prophesy , and prophesy to the wind , saying , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; A breath , come from all sides , and blow upon the dead , and make them live ;
&quot; So I obeyed my prophecy , and the breath entered into the bone , and the bone lived , and rose up , and became a mighty army
And the Lord said unto me , Son of man , these are the bones of the whole house of Israel ; and they said , Our bones are dried up , our hopes are lost , we are consumed
Therefore prophesy , and say to them , Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; O my people , I will open your graves , and you will come out of them , and I will bring you into the land of Israel
&quot; O my people , I have opened your graves , and I have brought you out of them , and you will know that I am the Lord .
&quot; I will put my spirit in you , and you will live ; and I will place you in the land , and you will know that my Lord has spoken , and that he has done it , &quot; says the Lord .
And the word of the LORD came again unto me , saying ,
&quot; Son of man , take a stick , and write on it , &apos; For Judah and his companions Israel ; &apos; and take a stick , and write on it , &apos; For Joseph , &apos; &apos; For Ephraim , &apos; &apos; For his companions Israel , &apos;
&quot; You shall make the two sticks joined together into one stick in your hand .
&quot; The children of your land asked you , &quot; What is this ? Did you not tell us ?
And thou shalt say unto them , Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I will make the staff of Joseph and his companions , the staff of the tribe of Israel , which is in the hand of Ephraim , one with the staff of Judah , and one in my hand
&quot; You shall take the two rods which you have written in their hand before their eyes .
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; I will gather the children of Israel from all the countries where they have come , and gather them from all the borders , and guide them back to their land
I will make them a nation in that land , in the mountains of Israel , and a king shall be king over all their people ; and they shall no longer be two nations , nor shall they be divided again .
And they shall no more defile themselves with idols and abominations and all sins ; but I will deliver them out of all their dwellings , the place of their sins ; and I will purify them ; and they shall be my children , and I will be their God .
&quot; My servant David will be their king , and the people will be ministers , and they will obey My statutes , and keep My law .
&quot; They shall dwell in the land which I gave to my servant Jacob , the land of your fathers ; and they and their sons and their sons &apos; sons shall dwell therein for ever and ever ; and David my servant shall be their king for ever and ever .
&quot; And I will make a covenant of peace with them , an everlasting covenant ; and I will place them in the land , and multiply their number , and establish among them My sanctuary for ever and ever .
My dwelling place shall be in their midst , and I shall be their God , and they shall be my children .
&quot; My holy is in the midst of Israel forever and ever ; and the Gentiles will know that I am the Lord of Israel .
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
Son of man , you shall prophesy against Gog of the land of Magog , the king of Tyre , Rosh and Mizheth , to smite him
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Behold , I am an enemy unto thee , O Gog , king of Rosh , and Mizpeh , and of Toba
&quot; I will hook your cheeks with hooks , and I will turn you around , and I will bring you and your army , horses , and horsemen , out of the midst of you , and I will cover them all , and I will make you a great army , with shields and with swords ,
The Persians , the Ancients , and the Philistines , each with a shield , and with helmets on their heads ,
and the people of Gath , and his army , and the people of the northern end , and the people of the northern end , and his army , and the people of many lands , are with you
And all the armies that are gathered unto thee shall be ready , and thou shalt be ready as their captain .
After many days you will be sent , and in the latter year you will come to the land which you have taken away from the nations from the sword , to the wild mountains of Israel ; and those who are gathered from the nations will dwell therein in safety .
&quot; You and your army , and the people of many countries with you , will come up like a stormy wind , like a cloud covering the ground .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; In that day your hearts will think and plot evil
&quot; I will go up to a country without walls , and I will go to the quiet people , who have no walls , no gates , no bars , and are safe to dwell .
&quot; Behold , I am going to plunder , and to plunder , and to take back the land that was desolate before and inhabited , and the people that dwell in the midst of the world , who have gathered themselves from nations , and have obtained livestock and goods
And the children of Sheba and the children of Dedan , and the merchants whom he made , and the young lion among them , shall say unto thee , Art thou come to take the spoil , and to gather the army , and to take the spoil , and to take the silver , and to take the spoil of the livestock , and to take the spoil of much treasure ?
Son of man , thus prophesy to Gog , saying , Thus says the Lord GOD : Do you not know the day when my people Israel shall be in peace ?
&quot; You shall come from the land , and from the ends of the north , and lead the people of many lands on horseback , a great army of mighty men .
&quot; You will come up against my people Israel as a cloud covering the ground , and in the latter days I will bring you up against my land , to the time when I will be holy in your sight before the Gentiles , that they may know me .
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; Is it you that I have spoken in ancient times through my servants , the prophets of Israel , when they foretold many years that I would bring you to attack the children of Israel
&quot; My wrath will come out of my nostrils , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; when I come up to Gog to attack the land of Israel .
And I said with indignation and with a fury like fire , There shall be a great trembling in the land of Israel that day
Even the fish of the sea , and the birds of the sky , and the beasts of the field , and all the beasts of the earth , and all that are upon them , shall shake when they see Me ; the mountains shall fall , the steep rocks shall fall , and the walls shall fall .
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; I will send my mountains with swords to attack Gog , and they will all kill their brothers with swords
And I will punish him with pestilence and bloodshed , and I will send down rain and hail and fire and sulfur upon him and upon his army and upon the people that he leads .
&quot; I will be great and holy , and will appear before the nations , and they will know that I am the Lord .
Son of man , prophesy against Gog , saying , &quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; I am an enemy to you , O Gog , king of Rosh , and Mizpeh , and of Toba
&quot; I will turn you , and I will lead you to the mountains of Israel , and I will bring you up from the northern end of the earth
&quot; I will strike your bow from your left hand , and your arrow from your right hand .
&quot; You and your army and all your people will fall on the mountains of Israel , and I will feed you to all kinds of birds of prey and all kinds of beasts of the field .
&quot; You will fall in the fields , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; for I have said it
&quot; I will set fire on the inhabitants of Makkah and the island of the sea , and they will know that I am the Lord .
I will manifest my holy name among my people Israel , and I will not allow my holy name to be profaned again ; and the nations will know that I am the Holy One of the Lord in Israel .
&quot; This day is near , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; and it will be fulfilled , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; the day that I have spoken
&quot; The inhabitants of the cities of Israel will go out and pick up instruments , shields and arrows , and rods and spears , and burn them with fire as wood , seven years straight
And they shall not gather wood out of the field , nor cut down trees out of the forest ; for they shall burn with fire with instruments ; and they shall take away those who have taken them , and take away those who have taken them , saith the Lord GOD .
And it shall come to pass in that day , that I will give the valley of the land of Israel , the valley which the people of the east passed through , unto Cain for a tomb , and I will cause the people of the east to cease from passing by ; and they shall bury Cain and his people therein , and they shall call it the valley of Ham .
&quot; The house of Israel shall bury them for seven months , to cleanse the whole land
And all the inhabitants of the earth shall bury them , and this shall make them known in the day of my glory , saith the Lord GOD .
And they shall scatter the earth , and bury the remains of the dead with those who pass by , in a clean place ; and after seven months they shall scatter the earth .
And he that passeth through the land shall pass through the whole land ; and when he seeth the carcass of a man , he shall set up a sign beside him , and he that is buried shall bury it in the valley of Haman .
&quot; This is how they shall cleanse the land ; and there is a city called Hamona
Son of man , thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; Speak to all the birds of the air and to the beasts of the field , &apos; Come , gather yourselves together , and gather from all sides to the land where I will offer a great sacrifice to you , a land of sacrifice on the mountains of Israel , that you may eat flesh and drink blood ,
&quot; You shall eat the flesh of the mighty , and drink the blood of the head of the land , as the sheep , and the lamb , and the goat , and the ox , are fat beasts of Bashan .
&quot; You will eat the sacrifice I have offered for you , and you will be filled with fat and drunken with blood .
&quot; You shall eat of the horses and of the riders and of the warriors and of all the fighters in my seat , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
I will show My glory among the nations , and the people will see the judgment that I have done , and the hand that I have put on them .
From that day onward the house of Israel shall know that I am the Lord their God
And the nations shall know that the house of Israel was taken captive because of their iniquity ; and they have sinned against me , and I have hid my face from them , and have delivered them into the hand of the enemy , and they have fallen under the sword .
I have treated them with their filth and their sins , and I have covered my face against them
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; I will bring back the captive Jacob , and will have mercy on all the house of Israel , and will have a great heart for my holy name
&quot; They dwell in peace in the land , and there is no fear . I have brought them back from among all the people , from the land of the enemy ; and they will bear their shame and all their sins before the people of many lands , when I will be holy on them .
See Up
&quot; For when I have taken them captive among the heathen , and gathered them together , and brought them back to their own land , they shall know that I am the Lord their God , and I will not leave any more of them in the heathen
&quot; I will no longer hide my face from them , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; for I have poured out my spirit on the house of Israel
&quot; In the twenty-fifth year of our captivity , and in the fourteenth year of the siege of Jerusalem , on the first day of the month , and on the tenth day of the month , the Spirit of the Lord descended on me , and brought me into the land of Israel
He brought me into the land of Israel in the vision of God , and placed me on a high mountain ; and on the south side of the mountain was a city built as if it were a city .
And he brought me there , and behold , a man standing at the door , of colors like brass , with a cord of linen in his hand , and a rod of measure ;
And he said unto me , Son of man , whatsoever I have commanded thee , thou shalt see with the eyes , and hear with the ears , and put it on thy heart ; and I have brought thee here to command thee ; and whatsoever thou seest , thou shalt tell the house of Israel .
And I saw a wall round about the house ; and he had a rod of measure in his hand , six cubits long , one cubit by one cubit ; and he measured the wall with a rod , a rod thick , and a rod high .
And when he came to the gate toward the east , he took up the steps of the gate , and measured it with a broad rod , and measured it with a broad rod
And there was a guardhouse , one rod long and one rod wide , five cubits apart ; and the threshold was the threshold of the way toward the house , one rod wide .
And he measured the porch toward the entrance of the temple , a rod wide
And the porch shall be eight cubits wide , and the pillars two cubits thick ; and the porch shall be toward the house
And there was a guardhouse in the gate toward the east ; and the three beside them and the three beside them were the same measure ; and the pillars on this side and the pillars on that side were the same measure
He measured the gate ten cubits wide and thirteen cubits long
The border of the exhibition before the tabernacle shall be an elbow on this side , and an elbow on that side ; six elbows on this side , and six elbows on that side
And the gate shall be measured from the rear eaves of the house of the guard to the rear eaves of the house of the guard twenty-five cubits wide .
And the length of the porch was sixty cubits , and beyond the pillars were courts , with porches on the sides of the gates .
50 cubits from the main gate to the entrance to the inner hall
And between the pillars of the guardhouse and of the gate , and between the porches , were firm windows , and on the inside were windows , and on the pillars were palm trees carved .
And he brought me to the outer court , and behold , there were thirty houses on the outer court round about .
The stone ground is a low stone ground on either side of the gates , according to the length and breadth of the gates .
&quot; From the bottom of the gate to the outside of the inner court he was one hundred cubits wide , east and north .
He measured the doors of the court to the north , a few in length and breadth
And the guard rooms of the gate , three by three , and three by three ; and the pillars and the porches of the gate , as the first gate : fifty cubits long , and twenty-five cubits wide .
And the windows thereof , and the porches thereof , and the palm trees that were carved thereof , were the same size as the doors to the east : and they went up seven steps unto the door , and there was a porch before them .
&quot; There were gates in the inner court , opposite to this gate , from the north to the east ; and he measured from this gate to that gate an hundred cubits .
And he brought me southward , and behold , there were gates toward the south ; and the pillars and the porches of the gates were measured according to the former measures .
And on both sides of the gate were windows , like the windows of the prophet , round about the porch , fifty cubits long and twenty-five cubits wide .
And it came to pass on the seventh floor , that they went up to this gate , and there was a porch before it , and on the pillars were palm trees carved , one on this side and one on that side
There were gates to the south of the inner court , from this gate to the gate to the south , an hundred cubits .
And he brought me from the south gate into the inner court , and measured the south gate according to the former measure
And the tabernacle , and the pillars , and the porch , were according to their former measures ; and on both sides of the gate and around the porch were windows ; and the length of the gate was fifty cubits , and the breadth twenty-five cubits .
A porch was round about , twenty-five cubits long and five cubits wide .
And the porch was toward the courtyard , and on the pillars were palm trees carved ; and they went up eight steps , and came to this gate
And he brought me to the east side of the inner court , and measured the east gate according to the former measure
And the tabernacle , and the pillars , and the porch , were according to the measure of the first : and on both sides of the gate and around the porch were windows , fifty cubits long and twenty-five cubits wide .
And the porch was toward the courtyard , and the pillars by the two sides of the gate were of palm trees carved ; and they went up eight steps unto the gate
And he brought me to the north gate , and measured it according to the former measure
And the storehouse , and the pillars , and the porches ; and round about the gate were windows ; and the length of the gate was fifty cubits , and the breadth twenty-five cubits .
And the pillars were toward the outer court , and on the sides of the gate were palm trees carved ; and they went up eight steps to the gate
And by the posts of the gate were houses and gates , in which the priests were to wash the burnt offerings .
&quot; There shall be two tables in the porch on this side , and two tables on that side , wherein shall be slaughtered the burnt offerings , and the sin offerings , and the trespass offerings
And it came to pass at the gate toward the north , that there were two tables on this side , and two tables on the other side of the porch
There were four tables on the one side of the gate , and four tables on the other side , eight in all , on which the priests slaughtered and sacrificed .
And for the burnt offering there shall be four tables of stone cut , one and a half cubits long , one and a half cubits wide , and one and a half cubits high : and the priest shall put upon them the slaughter of the burnt offering and the vessels of peace offerings
And there were hooks , and a broad palm , and they were hanged round the porch : and there was slain flesh on the table .
And beside the north gate there was a house in the inner court for the singers , which went southward ; and beside the south gate there was another to the north .
&quot; He said to me , &apos; The house to the south is for the priests who guard the temple .
The chamber to the north was for the priests who guarded the altar : these were the sons of Zadok among the Levites , who came near to minister to the Lord
And he measured the inner court , an hundred cubits long and an hundred cubits wide ; and the altar was before the temple .
Then he brought me to the porch in front of the temple , and measured the pillars of the porch , five cubits thick , and five cubits thick ; three cubits on either side of the door , and three cubits on the other side
And the length of the porch was twenty cubits and the breadth eleven cubits ; and there were steps in the upper porch near the pillars of the wall , and pillars on one side and on the other side
And he brought me into the temple , and measured the pillars , six cubits thick , and the other six cubits thick , and the breadth was as the curtain of the congregation .
He measured the length of the house forty cubits , and the breadth twenty cubits , on the two sides of the gate , five cubits on one side , and five cubits on the other side .
And he came into the inner house , and measured the pillars , two cubits thick , six cubits wide at the door , and seven cubits wide at the sides of the door .
He measured the inner house twenty cubits long and twenty cubits wide , and said to me , &quot; This is the sanctuary
And he measured the walls of the house , six cubits thick ; and around the house were side rooms four cubits wide
The side chamber is three stories tall , thirty in each row . The beams of the side chamber are laid on the canopy of the wall , lest they enter the wall .
The higher the side chambers of the enclosure , the broader they shall be ; for the side chambers of the enclosure are overlaid ; so the higher they shall be , and the broader they shall be , from the lower one , from the middle one , to the upper one
And I saw a high mount round about the house ; and the foundation of the house beside it was a rod with six elbows .
The outer wall of the side chamber was five cubits thick . Outside the side chamber , there was room
There shall be space between the side chamber and the house opposite , twenty cubits wide .
The doors of the side chambers were toward the remnant , one toward the north and one toward the south ; and the remnant around them was five cubits wide .
On the west side there was a house , seventy cubits wide and ninety cubits long , and five cubits thick round about .
Thus he measured the house an hundred cubits , and the empty space and the house and the wall an hundred cubits .
And the space before the house , and the space on both sides , was an hundred cubits wide .
And he measured the house that was behind , and the porches that were on both sides , an hundred cubits in length .
and the inner courtyard , and the porch , and the threshold , and the fenced windows , and the three-storey porch with the threshold , from the ground to the fenced windows ,
And the walls of the inner court and the walls of the outer court and the walls of the four walls of the inner court shall be covered with boards of wood , according to their measure , until they are over the gates .
On the walls were carved a palm tree and a palm tree . In the middle of each palm tree were two faces .
On this side is a man faced to a palm tree , and on that side a lion faced to a palm tree ; and so it is all around the house .
From the earth to the gates , there are reins and palm trees ; so is the wall of the temple .
The pillars of the palace are square , like the shape of the palace before the sanctuary
&quot; The altar was made of wood , three cubits high and two cubits long , and the corner of the altar , and the face of the altar , and all the sides of the altar , were of wood . He said to me , &quot; This is the table before the Lord
&quot; There are two doors to the house and to the sanctuary
Each door is divided into two , and the two doors are folded , and the two doors on this side are divided , and the two doors on that side are divided
The doors of the palace are carved with cornices and palm trees , as is the case with the walls . There is a cornice in front of the porch .
And on the other side of the porch were firm windows and palm trees , and the side rooms of the house and the thresholds .
He brought me out to the north , to the courtyard , and brought me into the sanctuary , which was row by row along the empty ground , and row by row with the stone houses on the north side .
And the length of the tabernacle was an hundred cubits , and the breadth fifty cubits ; and the doors were toward the north
And on the twenty cubits of the space of the inner court , and on the pavement of the outer court , on the third floor , was a porch toward the porch .
There was a way in front of the sanctuary , ten cubits wide and an hundred cubits long , and the doors were toward the north
The sacred chamber is narrow on the upper floor than on the lower two , because it occupies some space for the corridor
There are three floors of the house , but there are no pillars , and there are no pillars in the houses of the courtyard . Therefore the upper floor is narrower than the lower two
The outer chamber of the sanctuary , with walls on the east side , was fifty cubits long by the courtyard .
And the sanctuary by the outer court was fifty cubits , and the sanctuary on the north side of the house an hundred cubits .
Below the sanctuary there shall be an entrance to the east , and it shall be the entrance from the outer court .
To the south there was a house of the sanctuary in the walls of the inner court , one row on the stone ground , one row on the empty ground .
And the way before the sanctuary shall be as the way of the north side of the sanctuary ; and the way of the entrance shall be as the way of the north gate .
At the east end of the way , in front of the wall , there is a gate to enter , as it is to the south of the house of the saints
And he said unto me , The houses of the south and the houses of the north are holy in the midst of the void ; and the priests of the Lord &apos;s proximity shall eat therein the holy things , and the holy things shall be laid therein , the firstfruits , and the sin offering , and the trespass offering ; and they shall be holy
&quot; When the priest enters and goes out of the sanctuary , he shall not go straight into the outer court ; but he shall lay down his garments of service in the sanctuary , for they are sacred garments ; and he shall not enter into the outer court of the people unless he puts on other garments .
And when he had finished the inner court , he took me out of the east gate , and round about the court .
He measured with the rod of measure four quarters and five hundred cubits eastward .
500 elbows on the north side with a rod
Five hundred cubits to the south with a rod
And turned to the west with a rod of five hundred cubits .
And he measured the walls round about , five hundred cubits in length and five hundred cubits in breadth , to separate the holy place from the profane .
Then he brought me to a gate toward the east ,
The glory of the God of Israel came from the east : his voice is as the voice of waters : for his glory shineth upon the earth .
It is like the vision that I saw when he destroyed the city before , and I fell down on the ground like the vision that I saw by the river Jabbar .
The glory of the Lord came into the house from the east gate
And the Spirit lifted me up , and brought me into the inner house ; and behold , the glory of the Lord filled the house
And I heard a man speak unto me out of the temple , and a man stood by me
And he said unto me , Son of man , this is the place of my throne , and the place where I have trodden with my feet , and I will dwell there among the children of Israel for ever ; and the house of Israel and their kings shall no more defile my holy name , which is to commit adultery , and bury the dead bodies of their kings in the high places of Zion .
And I have made their thresholds to be near to My thresholds , and their gates to be near to My gates , and they are only a wall between Me , and they have defiled My holy name by doing abominable things , and I am angry to destroy them .
&quot; Now they shall be removed from before me from all wickedness , and from the dead bodies of their kings ; and I will dwell among them for ever and ever .
Son of man , direct this house to the house of Israel , that they may be ashamed of their iniquity , and that they may measure the size of the house .
&quot; If they are ashamed of all that they have done , then you shall write to them in their sight the size of the temple , its pattern , its entrance , and all its forms , and its statutes , and its ordinances , and its laws , and they shall do according to the scale of the temple .
Thus is the law of the house ; and the whole world around it on the top of the mountain shall be called holy ; and this is the law of the house .
&quot; The altar shall be measured by an elbow , an elbow of ten cubits : the base shall be an elbow high , and the sides shall be an elbow wide , and the sides shall be an elbow high round about : this is the seat of the altar .
From the base to the lower throne , two cubits high , one cubit wide , from the small throne to the great throne , four cubits high , one cubit wide
The altar was four cubits high , and on the four corners of the altar were corners .
For a table , twelve cubits long , twelve cubits wide , on four sides
The length of the tabernacle was fourteen cubits , and the breadth fourteen cubits , and it was seen from all sides ; and it was round about four cubits high and half-high ; and the sides of the seat was round about four cubits wide . The steps were toward the east .
&quot; And he said to me , &apos; Son of man , Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; Build an altar , and pour out your blood on it for a burnt offering . &apos; 
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &apos; You shall offer a calf for a sin offering to the seed of Zadok the priest of the Levites , who is near to me and serves me .
Take some of the blood of the bulls , and sprinkle it on the four corners of the altar , and on the four corners of the altar , and on the sides that are around it ; and you shall cleanse the altar , and it will be clean .
&quot; You shall also burn the calf for a sin offering outside the temple , outside the holy place , as you have prepared .
&quot; The next day you shall offer the unimpaired goats for a sin offering , and you shall cleanse the altar like the cleansing of a bull .
&quot; When you have cleansed the altar , you shall take one unimpaired calf and one unimpaired sheep out of the flock .
&quot; The priest shall pour salt on it and offer it as a burnt offering with the Lord
&quot; In seven days you shall prepare a goat for a sin offering every day , and a calf for a sin offering , and a ram of the flock without blemish .
&quot; On the seventh day the priest shall cleanse the altar , and the altar shall be cleansed ; and he shall sanctify the altar according to the manner
&quot; When the seven days are fulfilled , and after eight days the priest shall offer your burnt offerings on the altar , a peace offering , and I will please you , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
He brought me again to the outer gate of the Holy Land eastward , which was closed
&quot; The door must be shut , &quot; the Lord said to me , &quot; and it cannot be opened , neither can anyone enter it ; for the Lord God of Israel has entered through it , so it must be shut
&quot; As for the king , he shall sit in the king &apos;s place , and eat bread before the Lord ; and he shall enter through the porch of this gate , and he shall come out through it .
And he brought me from the north gate unto the house : and I looked , and behold the glory of the LORD filled the house of the LORD ; and I fell down on the ground
&quot; The Lord said to me , &apos; Son of man , I have spoken to you all the laws and ordinances of the Lord &apos;s house , that you should put them on your heart , and look with your eyes , and hear with your ears , and keep your mind on the entrances of the house and the sanctuary
&quot; Thus says the Lord Yahweh to the rebellious house of Israel , &apos; O house of Israel , do all the abominations when they are done
&quot; When you offered My food , fat and blood , you brought uncircumcised foreigners into My holy land , and defiled My temple , and you turned away from My covenant , and added this layer to all your abominations .
&quot; You have no holy things to guard against Me , but you send others to guard for you in the holy place , as I have commanded you
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Neither shall the foreigner of Israel , who is not circumcised in body and mind , enter into my holy place
&quot; When the children of Israel go astray , it is better for them not to go astray from me , but to go astray from my idols , and they will bear their own iniquity .
&quot; But they shall be servants in My holy place , and they shall keep the doors of the house , and serve in the house ; and they shall kill burnt offerings for the people , and sacrifice peace offerings ; and they shall stand before the people and serve them .
&quot; Because the Levites who served them before the idols have become a stumbling block for the iniquity of the house of Israel , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; I have sworn to them that they will bear their own iniquity .
They shall not come near to me , nor give me the office of priest , nor the holy thing , the most holy thing , which is near to me ; but they shall bear their shame and the recompense of their abominations .
&quot; But I will make them watch over the temple , and do all that is in it , and do all the work that is in it
&quot; The sons of Zadok , the priest of the Levites , will keep watch over my sanctuary when the children of Israel go away from me ; and they will come near to me , and serve me , and stand before me , and offer me fat and blood , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
&quot; They will enter into My sanctuary , and serve Me near My table , and keep My commandments .
They shall enter the gates of the house in fine linen , and they shall not be clothed in wool when they minister in the gates of the house and in the temple .
They shall wear scarves of fine linen on their heads and fine linen trousers on their waist . They shall not wear clothes that cause sweat
&quot; When they come out to the people in the outer court , they shall take off their garments of service , put them in the holy chamber , and put on other garments , lest the holy garments make the people holy .
&quot; You shall not shave your head , nor let your hair grow long , but cut it off .
&quot; When the priest enters the inner court , he shall not drink
&quot; You shall not marry a widow or a divorced woman , except a virgin of the children of Israel , or a widow left by the priest .
&quot; They will make known to my people the distinction between the holy and the unholy , and will distinguish between the clean and the unclean .
&quot; When there is a dispute , they shall stand and judge according to My statutes . They shall keep My statutes and ordinances in all My seasons , and My Sabbaths shall be holy days .
They shall not touch themselves with the dead bodies ; they shall only touch themselves with the father , the mother , the son , the daughter , the brother , and the unmarried sister
&quot; After the priest has cleansed himself , seven days shall be reckoned
&quot; When he enters into the inner house , into the sanctuary , and in the days of his ministry in the sanctuary , he shall offer a sin offering for himself , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
The priests shall have an inheritance ; I am their inheritance ; I shall not give them an inheritance in Israel ; I am their inheritance
&quot; They shall eat the firstfruits , the sin offerings , and the ransom offerings ; and all that is ever offered in Israel shall be theirs
&quot; First , the firstfruits and all the offerings that you have offered shall be given to the priest , and you shall grind the firstfruits of the wheat for the priest , and the blessing shall come to your house .
&quot; No bird or beast shall be eaten by any priest who dies or is torn
&quot; You shall give a lot of the land for a possession , and you shall give the second lot to the Lord for a holy offering , twenty-five thousand cubits long and ten thousand cubits wide , and within it shall be holy all around .
And the place of the sanctuary thereof shall be five hundred cubits long and five hundred cubits wide , and it shall be on all sides ; and fifty cubits shall be round about it for a suburb .
&quot; The measure of the land shall be twenty-five thousand cubits in length and ten thousand cubits in breadth , and in it shall be a sanctuary holy .
&quot; This is a holy part of the whole land , to be returned to the priests who minister to the holy office , who serve the Lord closely , as their dwelling place , and the holy place of the sanctuary .
And a portion of twenty and five thousand cubits long and ten thousand cubits wide shall be given to the Levites who served in the house for the service of twenty houses .
And the land of the city shall be divided , five thousand cubits wide and twenty-five thousand cubits long , by the holy altar ; and it shall be to the house of Israel .
And the king &apos;s land shall be on the side of the sanctuary and the land of the province , that is , on the side of the sanctuary and the land of the province , from west to west , from east to east ; and the length thereof shall be as the length of every tribe .
&quot; This land shall be a king &apos;s inheritance in Israel ; and my king shall no longer oppress my people ; but he shall divide it among the house of Israel according to their tribes .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; Know ye , O king of Israel , to put an end to the violence and to the plunder , and to do justice and righteousness , and to cease to oppress my people , saith the Lord GOD
&quot; You shall walk in the straight way , in the straight way , in the straight way , in the straight way ,
And Ephah was the same as Zakat , and Zakat celebrated one tenth of Meor , and Ephah celebrated one tenth of Meor , according to the size of Gomer .
The Shekel is the twenty-third Shekel , the twenty-fifth Shekel , the twenty-fifth Shekel , the fifteenth Shekel , the mina for you
&quot; This is the offering that you shall offer : A sixth of an ephah of the wheat of Gomorrah ; A sixth of an ephah of the barley of Gomorrah
&quot; You shall offer one tenth of the oil , according to the number of the oil you have divided , one cake of oil ; and the tenth cake shall be a greeting cake .
&quot; You shall offer one lamb out of every two hundred lambs from the pasture that is fertile in Israel for a freewill offering , a burnt offering , and a sacrifice of peace , for the redemption of the people , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; All the people of the land shall offer this offering to the king of Israel
&quot; The king &apos;s property is to offer burnt offerings , and sacrifices , and drink offerings , on the feast day , and on the moon , and on the sabbath day , which is the feast day of all the house of Israel , to prepare a sin offering , and a sin offering , and a burnt offering , and a peace offering , to redeem the house of Israel
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; On the first day of the month you shall take a calf without blemish from the holy place ,
&quot; The priest shall take some of the blood of the sin offering , and sprinkle it on the pillars of the temple , and on the four corners of the altar , and on the frames of the inner court
And so shall it be on the first day of this month , the first day of the seventy-seventh month , for the transgressors , and for the foolish , for the redemption of the house .
&quot; On the fourteenth day of January you shall observe the Passover , seven days , and eat unleavened bread .
&quot; On that day the king shall prepare a bull for a sin offering for himself and for the people of his land
He shall prepare seven bulls without blemish for a burnt offering , and seven rams for a sin offering , for the Lord on the seven days of this week , and one ram for a sin offering .
And he shall prepare a meat offering , a meal for a bull , and a meal for a ram , and a hin for each meal .
&quot; This shall he do on the fifteenth day of July , on the seventh day of the feast , according to the ordinance of the sin offerings , the burnt offerings , the meal offerings , and the oil of the Passover
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; The doors of the inner house to the east shall be shut during the six days of the service , except on the sabbath day and on the moon .
&quot; The king shall enter and enter by the porch of the gate , and the priest shall prepare for him a burnt offering and a peace offering , and he shall worship at the threshold ; and he shall go out ; and the gate shall not be shut until the evening .
&quot; The inhabitants of the land shall worship before the Lord in the Sabbath day and in the month .
&quot; The burnt offering that the king shall offer to the Lord on Sabbath shall be six lambs without blemish , and one ram without blemish
And he shall offer an ephah for the sheep , and an ephah for the lamb , according to his power , and a hin for the fuel
And in the month of Sabbath he shall offer a calf without blemish , six lambs , and a ram without blemish ;
&quot; And he shall prepare a meal offering , an ephah for the bull , an ephah for the ram , and an ephah for the lamb , according to his power , and a hin for the ephah
&quot; When the king enters , he will enter through the porch of this gate , and he will come out through it
&quot; When the inhabitants of the land come to the Lord in the seasons , they shall go in and out of the north gate to worship , and from the south gate they shall go in and out , and from the north gate they shall go in and out . They shall not go in and out of the gates into which they enter , but they shall go straight ahead and out of the opposite gate .
The people shall enter , and the king shall enter among the people ; and the people shall go out , and the king shall go out together
And for the meat offering , on the sabbaths and in the feasts , he shall offer an ephah for a bullock , and an ephah for a ram , and for the lamb according to his power , and an ephah for a drink .
&quot; The burnt offering , or the peace offering , which the king has prepared willingly , shall be offered willingly to the Lord , when someone opens the door to him to the east , and he prepares the burnt offering , and the peace offering , as he did on the Sabbath day ; and when he has offered it , he goes out ; and after he has gone out , when someone closes the door ,
&quot; You shall prepare daily a lamb without blemish , one year old , for a burnt offering with the Lord , and prepare it every morning
And every morning a meal offering with it shall be prepared : one sixth of an ephah of fine flour , and one third of a hin of oil , mixed with fine flour ; and it shall be a continual offering unto the Lord for a statute for ever .
&quot; You shall prepare a lamb , a meal offering , and oil for a continual burnt offering every morning
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; If the king gives a possession to his son , it will become the inheritance of his son , and they will bear it as a possession
&quot; If the king gives a portion of his inheritance to his servants , it becomes the inheritance of his servants ; and they shall return to the king in the year of freedom ; and the inheritance of the king shall be to his sons
&quot; The king will not take the inheritance of the people to drive them away from what they have received , but he will give the inheritance of his own land to his sons , lest my people be dispersed , and they all leave what they have received .
And he that brought me into the place where I entered by the door , into the holy house prepared for the priest , which is toward the north , and behold , there is a piece of land on the west side
&quot; He said to me , &apos; This is the land of the priests for the offering of the offering of the heifer , for the offering of the sin , and for the burnt offering , lest he bring them into the courts to sanctify the people .
And he brought me to the outer court , and made me pass through the four corners of the court , and behold , there was a court at every corner
&quot; The four corners of the houses shall have walls around them ; each house shall be forty cubits in length and thirty cubits in breadth ; and the measure of the four corners of the houses shall be one .
There was a row of houses around it , and there was a place for boiling meat in the house
&quot; He said to me , &apos; These are the houses for boiling meat , the servants of the house , to boil the offerings of the people here .
Then he brought me back to the door of the temple , and behold , under the threshold of the temple , water was pouring out eastward from under the threshold , from the right side of the temple , and from the south side of the altar .
And he brought me out of the north gate , and turned me from the outer gate toward the east , and behold , water came out from the right side
And he measured a thousand cubits , when he drew out his hand with the rope eastward , and made me pass through the waters , and the waters to the ankle bones
Then he measured another thousand cubits , and overtook me , and the water was to my knees ; and another thousand cubits , and overtook me , and the water was to my waist
And he measured a thousand cubits , and the water became a river , that I could not pass ; for it rose up for the waters , and became a river of waters , a river of waters not to be watered .
And he said unto me , Son of man , what hast thou seen ? And he brought me to the river
When I returned to the bank of the river , I saw that there were trees on the other side of the river , and on the bank thereof .
And he said unto me , The water that floweth to the east shall come down unto Rabbah , and straight unto the sea ; and the water that hath come forth shall flow into the salt sea , and make it sweet .
All the living creatures shall live wherever this river comes , and there shall be abundant fish in it , and the waters shall be sweet , and wherever this river comes shall be hundreds of creatures .
There will be a fisherman standing by the river , from the bottom of the valley to the top of the valley of Ephraim , as a net of sunshine ; and there will be many fish of their kinds , as the fish of the sea .
It is only a muddy land , and a place of desolation . It will not be healed , but it will be a salt land .
On the other side of the river , and on the banks thereof , trees of every kind shall grow , and their fruit shall be food , and their leaves shall not decay , and their fruit shall not be cut off ; and new fruit shall come forth every month , for this water is from the Holy One ; and the fruit of the trees shall be food , and the leaves for healing .
Thus says the Lord Yahweh : &quot; You shall divide the land according to its borders , according to the twelve tribes of Israel , and Joseph shall have two shares .
&quot; You shall inherit this land , and divide it among yourselves ; for I have sworn to give it to your fathers , and it shall be yours to inherit .
Thus is the four borders of the earth : the north border from the sea to Shethren , and straight to the mouth of Siddah .
And to Hama , and Beeroth , and Zebulun , which is between Damascus and Hama , to Haza &apos;at-tiken , which is on the border of Haran
And the border shall be from the sea to the border of the land of Damascus , which is the border of the land of Gaza , and the border of the land of Hamath , which is the border of the north
And the border of the east is the Jordan in the midst of Haran , and in the midst of Damascus , and in the midst of Gilead , and in the midst of the land of Israel ; and you shall measure it from the north to the east sea ; and this is the border of the east
The southern boundary is the waters from Tema to Miribaghab , to the small river of Egypt , to the sea
The west boundary is the sea , from the south boundary straight to the mouth of Hama . This is the west boundary
&quot; You shall divide the land according to the tribes of Israel ,
&quot; You shall divide the land in lots , and give it to the foreigners who dwell among you , the foreigners who have children among you ; and you shall see them as they were born among the children of Israel ; and they shall possess the land with you among the tribes of Israel .
&quot; In that tribe , where strangers dwell , you shall divide your possessions among them , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
Below is the land of the tribes according to their names : from the north , from Hethren , to the mouth of Hamath , to Hazar , on the border of Damascus ; and on the north side is Hamath , which is the border of all the tribes , a part of Dan .
And by the border of Dan , from east to west , was the portion of Assyria .
And the border of Assyria from east to west was a portion of Naphtali .
and the border of Naphtali from east to west was a portion of Manasseh .
And the border of Manasseh from east to west was a portion of Ephraim .
And by the border of Ephraim , from east to west , was a portion of the river .
A part of Judah is the border of the rivers , from east to west .
And by the border of Judah from east to west shall be the offering which you shall offer , twenty and five thousand cubits in breadth ; and from east to west shall be the same length as the borders of the provinces ; and in it shall be the holy place .
&quot; You shall offer your offering to the Lord twenty-five thousand cubits long and ten thousand cubits wide .
&quot; The Holy Place of the Lord shall be returned to the priests , twenty-five thousand cubits north , ten thousand cubits west , ten thousand cubits east , twenty-five thousand cubits south ,
&quot; This land shall be given to the sons of Zadok as holy priests , as I have commanded them ; and when the children of Israel went astray , they did not go astray like the Levites
And it shall be a sanctuary in all the earth , and it shall be a land of sustenance to them , which shall be near to the land of the Levites .
The land that the Levites shall possess shall be twenty-five thousand cubits long and ten thousand cubits wide , even as the border of the priest &apos;s land was twenty-five thousand cubits long and ten thousand cubits wide
&quot; The land shall not be sold , nor exchanged ; neither shall the firstfruits be given to any man , for they are holy to the Lord
The twenty-five thousand cubits of the land that remained before , which was five thousand cubits wide , shall be for the common use , for the suburbs of the houses of the city ; and the city shall be in the midst thereof .
That is the size of the city , four thousand and fifty cubits northward , four thousand and fifty cubits southward , four thousand and fifty cubits eastward , and four thousand and fifty cubits westward
&quot; And the suburbs of the city shall be two hundred fifty cubits north , two hundred fifty cubits south , two hundred fifty cubits east , two hundred fifty cubits west
And the residue of the sanctuary , which is ten thousand cubits in the east , and ten thousand cubits in the west , shall be equal to the sanctuary ; and the inheritance thereof shall be for the food of the workers of the city .
All the tribes of Israel that work in the city shall sow the land
&quot; The sanctuary which you offered , and the land which you returned to the city , was on all sides , twenty-five thousand cubits long and twenty-five thousand cubits wide .
The rest of the land on both sides shall belong to the king , even to the land of the city ; the land eastward , north-south twenty-five thousand cubits , east-east , north-south twenty-five thousand cubits , west-west , the same as the parts of the land ; they shall all belong to the king . The holy land of the sanctuary and the holy land of the temple shall be in it
And the land of the Levites , which is between the king &apos;s land and the land of the city , which is extended eastward , shall be returned to the king between the borders of Judah and Benjamin .
Concerning the rest of the tribes , from east to west , a portion of Benjamin .
and the border of Benjamin , from east to west , was a part of the land of Simeon .
and by the border of Simeon , from east to west , is the portion of Issachar .
and by the border of Issachar , from east to west , a part of the West Bank .
that is by the border of the west of Hebron , from east to west , a part of Gad .
And the southern border of Gad was from the waters of Herma unto the waters of Miribaghath unto the little river of Egypt unto the sea .
&quot; This is the land which you shall give to the tribes of Israel for a possession , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
The north side of the city was forty-five cubits , and the outward part of the city was as follows :
The gates of the city shall be named after the tribes of Israel : three gates shall be on the north side , one for Reuben , one for Judah , and one for Levi
and on the east side four thousand and five hundred cubits were three gates , one for Joseph , one for Benjamin , and one for Dan .
and on the south side four thousand and five hundred cubits , three gates : one for Simeon , one for Issachar , one for Zebulun ,
And on the west side four thousand and five hundred cubits were three gates , one for the gate of Gad , one for the gate of Assyria , and one for the gate of Naphtali
&quot; There will be eight thousand cubits around the city , and from that time onwards the name of the city will be called the place of the Lord .
In the third year of Jehoiakim king of Judah Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to Jerusalem and besieged the city
Then the Lord delivered to Jehoia king of Judah the portion of the vessel in the temple , and he brought it into the land of Shenath , and entered into the temple of his God , and put it in the treasure of his God
And the king commanded the overseer , Assyria , to bring a few men out of the house of Israel , and of the nobles ,
They were young , without any infirmity , beautiful in appearance , able to learn all things , wise in knowledge , and able to serve in the king &apos;s palace , to teach them the words of Galilee
And the king commanded to give them a penny a day for their sustenance and for their drink , and to raise them up for three years , when the three years were fulfilled , that they might stand before the king
Among them were the children of Judah , Daniel , Hananiah , Mizhaliah , and Azariah
And the overseer gave them names , saying , Daniel be Betheshaz , and Hananiah Shadra , and Mizhali be Mesha , and Azariah Abeniah :
&quot; But he made a vow not to defile himself with the food of the king and with the wine of the king ; so he asked the High Priest to allow him not to defile himself
God blessed and pitied Daniel in the sight of the overseer
And the high overseer said unto Daniel , I fear my lord my king ; for he hath ordained your food ; and if he should see your face as thinner than that of a young man of your age , how good would it be , then ye would make my head hard to keep in the king &apos;s presence
And Daniel said unto the governors of Daniel , and of Hananiah , and of Mizhali , and of Azariah , who were appointed by the overseers :
&quot; Try , my servants , for ten days , to eat our meat and drink our water
Then look at the face of us , and the face of the young man of the king &apos;s household ; and be servants as you see .
And the governor gave them permission to do this , and to test them for ten days
After ten days , I saw their faces , and they were more beautiful and fat than all the young men of the king &apos;s household .
And they removed their food , and their drink , and gave them their meat
God gave these four young men wisdom in all the Scriptures , and they understood all the visions and dreams .
When the time had come for the king of Nebuchadnezzar to bring the young men , the overseer brought them before the king
&quot; When the king spoke to them , and saw that there was none among the young men but Daniel , Hananiah , Mizhali , and Azariah , they stood before the king
And when the king had examined all their affairs , he saw that their wisdom was greater than the wisdom of all the wise men of the land , and more than the wise men of the law
By the year of the king of old , Elijah was still alive
In the second year of his reign , Nebuchadnezzar dreamed , and was troubled , and could not sleep
And the king commanded that men should summon the wizards , and the scribes , and the evildoers , and the Chaldeans , that they should tell the king the dreams of the king ; and they came and stood before the king
And the king said unto them , I dreamed a dream , and I was troubled in my heart , to know what it was
Then the Chaldeans spoke to the king in the words of Aram , saying , &quot; Lord , in the days of your life , tell the dream to your servant , and he will be able to explain it
And the king answered and said unto the Chaldeans , I have forgotten my dreams ; and if ye shall not tell me the interpretation of dreams and dreams , then ye shall be delayed , and your houses shall be a wasteland
&quot; If you tell me the interpretation of dreams and dreams , you will receive from me a gift and a reward and a great honour . Now tell me the interpretation of dreams and dreams
And the second time they said unto the king , Ask the king to declare the dream unto his servant , that he may interpret it
Then the king answered , &quot; I know that you are delayed , because you know that I have forgotten that dream
If you do not tell me your dreams , there is only one way for you , for you have prepared lies and rumours to tell me , and wait for the change of the times ; and now tell me your dreams , for I know that you can tell me the interpretation of your dreams .
And the Chaldeans answered in the presence of the king , saying , There is no man in the world that can speak that which the king hath asked : for there is no king , nor minister , nor ruler , nor scribe , nor scribe of the law , nor of the Chaldeans ,
&quot; The king &apos;s question is very difficult . No one can speak before the king except God , who is not with the world .
Therefore the king &apos;s wrath was kindled , and he commanded that all the wise men of Babylon should be destroyed
Then it was commanded , saying , &quot; The wise men will see the slaughter , and they will seek Daniel and his companions , and kill them . &quot;
And the king &apos;s captain of guard , Elijah , came out to kill the wise men of Babylon , and Elijah answered him , saying ,
Then Elijah , the captain of the king &apos;s guard , said to Daniel , &quot; Why is the king &apos;s command so urgent ?
&quot; But when he entered into the king &apos;s house and asked for forgiveness , he could tell the king the interpretation of his dream .
But Eli returned to his house , and brought it to his companions Hananiah , and Mizhaliah , and Azariah
May they pray for mercy from God in heaven , and declare this mystery , lest Daniel and his companions , and the rest of the wise men of Babylon , perish together
The mystery was revealed to Daniel in the night visions , and he praised the God of heaven .
But Elijah said , &quot; The name of God is to be praised from the beginning to the end , for all wisdom belongs to Him
He changed the time , the date , the kingdom , and the kingdom , and gave wisdom to the wise , and knowledge to the wise
He reveals the deepest secrets , and knows all that is hidden , and the light is with him .
&quot; I thank You , O God of my seed , and praise You , for You have given me wisdom , and have granted us what we ask , and have made clear to us the king &apos;s affairs .
Then Daniel went in to meet Elijah , the king &apos;s messenger who had sent to destroy the wise men of Babylon , and said to him , &quot; Do not destroy the wise men of Babylon , but bring me before the king , that I may declare to the king the interpretation of the dream
So he hurried to bring Daniel before the king , and said to the king , &quot; I have met a man among the captives of Judah who can tell the king the interpretation of the dream
Then the king said to Daniel , who was called Betheshaz , &quot; Can you tell me my dreams and the interpretation of my dreams ?
But Elijah answered the king , saying , &quot; None of the wise men , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes , nor of the scribes
&quot; There is only one God in heaven who reveals the secrets which He will reveal to the king of Nebuchadnezzar . Thus are your dreams and the visions in your heads in bed .
&quot; Remember , O king , in your bed the things to come , and the Lord of manifest mysteries will show you the things to come .
&quot; For the mystery is revealed to me not because of my wisdom above all living things , but because of the interpretation of dreams and the thoughts of my heart
&quot; You dream , O king , of a great statue , which is high and luminous , and stands before you , and its shape is terrible
&quot; The head of the likeness is of gold , and the breasts and arms of silver , and the belly and waist of brass .
The legs are iron , and the feet are half iron and half clay .
&quot; When you look , you see a stone that was not cut out by man , and he strikes it on its feet like iron and like clay , and breaks it down .
Then the gold , the silver , the copper , the iron , and the clay were all crushed together , and they became like a branch on a field of wheat in the summer ; it was blown away by the wind , and there was no place to find it ; and the likeness of the stone was crushed , and it became a great mountain , and filled the whole earth .
&quot; This is the dream , and we shall explain it before the king
O king , you are the king of all kings , and the God of heaven has given you the kingdom , the power , the power , and the glory
&quot; He has delivered into your hand all the beasts of the earth , and the birds of the sky , wherein all the people dwell , and He has given you power over all these things , and you are the gold .
&quot; There will be another kingdom after you , which will not be yours ; and there will be a third kingdom , which will be of copper , and will rule over all the earth .
A fourth nation shall be as strong as iron ; and iron shall crush all that is besieged , and it shall crush all that is oppressed ; and it shall crush all that is oppressed .
Thou hast seen the like feet and the fingers of the feet ; half of them are clay of a carpenter , and half of them are iron ; and the land shall be divided in the future ; and thou hast seen the iron mixed with the clay , and the land shall have the strength of iron .
The foot shall be half iron and half clay , and the land shall be half strong and half weak .
&quot; You have seen the iron mixed with the mud , and the people will mix with all kinds of people , but they will not be able to match one another , just as the iron cannot match the mud
&quot; In the days of the kings , the God of heaven will raise up a new nation , which will never be defeated , nor belong to any other nation ; but he will break down and destroy the good nation , and it will live forever .
&quot; Behold , you saw a stone cut out of the mountains by no man &apos;s hand , and it shattered gold , silver , copper , iron , and mud . That is how the Most Great God revealed to the king what will come after him . That dream is true , and that interpretation is true .
And king Nebuchadnezzar fell down on the ground , and worshipped Daniel , and commanded the people to offer him offerings and spices
The king said to Daniel , &quot; You are the God of all the gods , the Lord of all the kings , and the one who reveals the mystery .
Then the king lifted up Daniel , and bestowed upon him a great gift , and sent him over all the provinces of Babylon , and made him the prince , and over all the wise men of Babylon
&quot; But when Daniel asked the king , the king sent Shadra , Meshach , and Abneziah to oversee the affairs of the province of Babylon ; but he was always a minister to the people
And king Nebuchadnezzar made a golden image , sixty cubits high and six cubits wide , standing in the plains of Dura in the province of Babylon
Then the messenger of the king of Nebuchadnezzar called the governors , the sheriffs , the governors-generals , the governors-generals , the governors-generals , the governors-generals , the judges , and the officials of the provinces , and made a light offering for the image of the king of Nebuchadnezzar .
Then the governor , the sheriff , the governor , the governor-general , the governor-general , the governor-general of the land , the governor-general , the judge , and the officials of the provinces assembled together , and stood before the image of king Nebuchadnezzar , to perform the light service .
And he that sent the word at that time cried with a loud voice , saying , &quot; Who among the peoples , and among the nations , and among the peoples , has sent the word with you ? &quot;
And when ye heard the sound of the horns , and the flutes , and the fiddles , and the harps , and the psalteries , and the instruments of all kinds , ye fell down to worship the golden image of king Nebuchadnezzar
&quot; He who does not bow down and worship will be thrown into the midst of the flames when he stands up .
So all the parties , and all the nations , and all the peoples of the nations , when they heard the sound of the horns , and the flutes , and the harps , and the harps , and the harps , and all the instruments of music , fell down to worship the golden image of king Nebuchadnezzar .
At that time several of the Chaldeans came forward and accused the Jews
And they said unto the king of Nebuchadnezzar , Long live the king .
&quot; You have commanded , O king , that everyone who hears the sound of the horn , the flute , the bow , the harp , the harp , the harp , the harp , and all the instruments of music , shall bow down and worship the golden image
&quot; He who does not bow down and worship will be thrown into the midst of the flames .
Now there are certain Jews , Shadra , Meshach , Abenika , king of Babylon , whom the king sent to do the affairs of the province , who do not obey you , do not serve your God , and do not worship your golden image
Then Nebuchadnezzar was very angry , and commanded that they should bring Shadra , Meshach , and Abner , and they brought them before the king
Then Nebuchadnezzar said to them , &quot; Sadra , Meshach , Abner , do you not serve my God , and do you not worship the golden image which I have set up ?
&quot; When you hear the sound of the horns , the flutes , the harps , the harps , the harps , the harps , the harps , and all the instruments of music , if you bow down to the image that I have made , and if you do not bow down to it , you will be thrown into the midst of the flames . What God will save you from my hand ?
And Shadra , and Meshach , and Abnekah , said to the king , We will not answer thee concerning this matter , Nebuchadnezzar
Even so , the God whom we serve will deliver us out of the midst of the flames of the fire , and he will deliver us out of your hand , O king .
&quot; You know , O king , that we will never serve your God , nor worship the golden image that you have set up
Then Nebuchadnezzar filled his chest with anger , and turned his face to Shadra , Meshach , and Abimelech , and commanded them to burn the heifer seven times as often
And he commanded some of the mighty men of his army to bound Shadra , Meshach , and Abner , and to cast them into the midst of the flames
And the three were bound in their trousers , and in their robes , and in their outward garments , and in other garments , and cast into the midst of the fire
For the king &apos;s life was urgent , and the earth was hot , and the men who carried the sand were burned in the flames , even the men of Delah , and the men of Meshach , and the men of Abihuth
And Shadra , and Meshach , and Abnekah , were bound in the midst of the flames
Then the king of Nebuchadnezzar was astonished , and hurried , and said to the spies , Am I not bound and cast into the fire three men ? And they answered the king , O king ,
&quot; The king said , &quot; Behold , I have seen four men who were not bound , who walked in the fire , and were not injured . The fourth man looked like the Son of God
Then Nebuchadnezzar came near the door of the fire , and said , &quot; The servant of the Most High God , Shadra , Meshach , and Abennego , come up , and come out of the fire .
And the governors , and the scribes , and the governors , and the king &apos;s officers gathered themselves together , and looked upon the three men , and saw that the fire had no power to harm their bodies , neither had their hair burned , neither had their garments changed color , nor had their smell burned
Then Nebuchadnezzar said , &quot; Blessed is the God of Shadra , Mizhach , and Abner , who sent messengers to save and to rely on his servants , and they have not obeyed the king &apos;s commandment , and have forsaken themselves , and have not worshipped any god other than their God
&quot; It is written in my decree that he who slanders Shadra , Meshah , and the God of Aban , from every nation and country , will be defeated , and his house will be a dunghill ; for there is no other God who can deliver in this way .
And it came to pass at that time , that the king lifted up Shadra , and Meshach , and Abner , in the province of Babylon
&quot; The king of Nebuchadnezzar spoke to all the people of the land , and to all the nations , saying , Peace be to you
I am glad that the Most High God will proclaim to me the miracles and wonders of my works
How great are His signs , and how great are His wonders ! His kingdom is eternal , and His dominion endures for ever and ever .
&quot; I Nebuchadnezzar dwell in the palace , and in the temple in peace .
&quot; I had a dream that made me afraid . My thoughts in bed , and the visions in my mind , made me afraid .
&quot; Therefore I have commanded all the wise men of Babylon to come before me , and to tell me the interpretation of their dreams .
Then came in all the magicians , the scribes , and the Chaldeans , the watchers , and I told them the dream , but they could not tell me the interpretation of the dream
Then came to me Daniel , who was called Bethesda , in the name of my God , and had the Spirit of the Holy God in his head , and I told him in a dream
For I know that the Spirit of the Holy God is in you , and that no secret thing can trouble you . But now , Bethesda , the leader of the wizards , he is bringing to me the visions and the interpretations of my dreams .
That is the vision in my mind in bed . I saw a tree in the ground , and it was very tall .
The tree grows and becomes strong , and is as high as the sky , and it can be seen from the poles of the earth
&quot; The leaves are beautiful , and the fruit is abundant , and it is the food of all living creatures ; the beasts of the field , and the birds of the sky , and the birds of the sky , that dwell in branches ; and every bloodthirsty man shall eat of it
I saw in my bed the vision in my head , and a holy man who was guarded came down from heaven .
&quot; There will be a great cry , saying , &quot; Cut this tree , cut down its branches , shake down its leaves , and throw away its fruit , and let the beasts of the field leave the tree , and the birds of the sky hide from the branches
&quot; But the tree shall remain in the land , and shall be girded with iron and brass , and shall drip in the grass of the field , and the sun shall be dew , and he shall eat grass with the beasts of the earth .
and changed his heart rather than his heart , and gave him an animal heart , and made him pass through seven periods
&quot; This is the commandment of the watcher , and the commandment of the Holy One , that the world may know that the Most High has dominion over the kingdom of man , and whoever will give him the kingdom , he will give it to whomsoever , or the humble man will have dominion over the kingdom .
&quot; This is the dream of my king Nebuchadnezzar , Bethesda , that you should explain it to me ; for all the wise men in my country cannot explain it to me , except you , because the Spirit of God is in your head .
Then the king said to Daniel , who was called Bethesda , &quot; Do not be afraid , O Bethesda , because of the interpretation of dreams and dreams . &quot; But Bethesda answered , &quot; Lord , let the interpretation of these dreams be with those who hate you , and with your enemies .
And the tree which thou hast seen groweth , and is strong , and is as high as the heavens , and thou shalt see it from the ends of the earth
The leaves are beautiful , and the fruit is abundant , and it is the food of all living creatures ; the beasts of the field dwell under it ; the birds of the sky dwell in branches
&quot; You are the tree that grows and is strong , O king . Your power grows and the heavens are established . Your power reaches to the ends of the earth .
And the king saw a holy watcher come down from heaven , and said , &quot; Destroy this tree , and it shall remain in the earth , and be enclosed in a ring of iron like a bronze ring , in the grass of the fields , and the heavens shall be dew , and he shall eat grass with the beasts of the earth , until the seventh time . &quot;
&quot; This is the interpretation , O king , that comes to my Lord and to my king , from the life of the Most High .
&quot; You will be driven out of the world , and you will live with the beasts of the field , and you will eat grass like cattle , and you will be drenched in the sun , and you will pass through seven periods , until you know who the Most High has dominion over the land of men , and who you will give it to .
&quot; The watchman has commanded you to keep the tree until you know that the heavens are in power , and then your land will be yours .
&quot; O king , please accept my words , that you may do righteousness and forgive sins , and have mercy on the poor and remove iniquity , or that your peace may be prolonged
All these things came to king Nebuchadnezzar .
After twelve months he walked in the palace of Babylon
He said , &quot; Isn &apos;t this great Babylon that I built with great power for Kyoto , to show my great glory ?
And it came to pass , when the word was not yet finished in the mouth of the king , that a voice came down from heaven , saying , King Nebuchadnezzar , there is a saying unto thee , Thy kingdom is departed from thee
&quot; You will be driven out of the world , and you will live with the beasts of the field , and you will eat grass like cattle , and you will pass through seven periods . When you know who the Most High is in the kingdom of men , who you will give the kingdom to , you will give it to
&quot; Then it shall be tested in the case of Nebuchadnezzar , who was driven out of the world , eating grass like a cow , and drenched in the sun , and his hair as the hair of an eagle , and his nails as the nails of a bird
&quot; The days are fulfilled , and I , Nebuchadnezzar , lift up my eyes to heaven , and my wisdom is returned to me , and I praise the Most High , and I praise the God who lives forever , and his dominion endures forever , and his kingdom endures for ever .
All the inhabitants of the world are desolate , and all the armies in heaven and the inhabitants of the world act according to their own will . No one can stop his hand or ask him , &quot; What are you doing ? &quot;
Then will my wisdom return to me , and the glory and majesty and the light of my nation will return to me ; and my counselors and my ministers will come to me ; and I will be established in the throne , and great power will be added to me .
Behold , Nebuchadnezzar , who is in me , praises the king of heaven , because all that he has done is true , and all that he has done is just ; and he is proud of his deeds , and he is able to be humbled .
And the king of Beer-sheba set up a feast for a thousand of his ministers , and he drank wine in front of the thousand
And it came to pass , while Beer-sheba was drinking , that he commanded that he should take the silver and gold vessels which Nebuchadnezzar his father had plundered out of the house of Jerusalem , and that the king and the queen of the king &apos;s household should drink of them
Then they took the gold vessels which they had plundered in the treasury of the temple of Jerusalem ; and the king and the queen of the king &apos;s household drank of them
They drink wine , and praise the God made of silver and brass and iron and timber
At that time a man &apos;s finger appeared and wrote on the powder walls of the king &apos;s palace and the lampstand . The king saw the fingers of the writing
Then his face turned , and his heart trembled , and his thighs were as if they had been cut off , and his knees touched one another
And a great voice commanded him to bring in the scribes , and the Chaldeans , and the prophets , and to say to the wise men of Babylon , &quot; Whoever can read this scripture , and tell me its interpretation , he shall be in purple robes and chains of gold , and shall be numbered third in my land .
Then all the wise men of the king came in , but could not read the letter , nor make a plea to the king
Then behold , the king of Bashar was astonished , and his face was changed , and all his ministers were astonished
Then the queen entered into the banquet hall , because of the words of the king and of his ministers , saying , &quot; May the king live forever , and do not be afraid , nor change your face . &quot;
There is a man in your land , in whose head is the Spirit of the Holy God , and in whose heart is the light of your father in the days of the world , and wisdom as the wisdom of God ; and your father king Nebuchadnezzar , the father of the king , made him a scribe , and a scribe of the scribes , and a leader of the Chaldeans , and a prophet .
&quot; In him is a good spirit , and knowledge , and wisdom , and a dreamer , and a scribe , and a questioner ; and his name is Daniel , whom the king of Nebuchadnezzar called Betheshaz ; and he will now call him , and he will explain what he means .
Then Daniel was brought before the king ; and the king said to him , &quot; Are you Daniel of the captive Jews , my father the king , who came out of the captivity of Judah ?
I have heard that in you is the Spirit of God , and light in your heart , and wisdom and good wisdom .
&quot; The philosophers and the scribes have come to me to read the Scripture and to explain it to me , but they cannot explain it .
&quot; I have heard that you are good at explaining and at resolving doubts . Now , if you can read the Scripture and explain it to me , you will be in purple robes and chains and will be numbered third in my country .
Then answered Elijah before the king , &quot; Your gift may be to yourself , and your reward to others ; but I will read this word for the king , and make it known to the king
&quot; O king , the Most High God has given your father Nebuchadnezzar the throne , the power , the glory , the might ,
For the great power which God has bestowed upon him , the people of all nations and tribes are afraid before him , and he can kill at will , and he can ascend at will .
&quot; But he was arrogant , and the spirit was stiff , and he was even arrogant , and he was removed from the throne , and he was taken away from the glory
He was driven out of the world , and his heart became like a beast &apos;s heart , and he lived with a wild donkey , and he ate grass like a cow , and his body was drenched in the rain of the heavens , until he knew that the Most High God had dominion over man &apos;s land , and that He had made man rule by His will .
Behold , thou art his son , and thy heart is not humbled , though thou knowest all these things
&quot; Behold , the Lord of heaven is exalted , and he has brought before you the vessels of his house , and you and the queens of the king and queen drink from them ; and you praise the God who can neither see nor hear nor know , who is made of gold and silver and copper and iron and timber , and who has not the breath of your glory in his hand , and who controls all your deeds .
&quot; Therefore it is revealed from God that he writes this word
And the writings of the LORD were Mian , and Mian , and Tigris , and Uphar ,
&quot; This is how it is explained : &quot; Myne , God has counted the days of your country , until the end of the year .
&quot; It is you , Tychler , who is called to bear witness in the heavens of your sins
Blessed is the new covenant of Uphraim , the division of your land , to the Medes and to the Persians
And he commanded , and the people put on the purple robe for Daniel , and put on his neck a chain of gold , and commanded that he should be numbered third in the land
On the night of Belshazzar king of Galilee was killed .
and Reu of the children of Gad , being sixty-two years old , took the land of Caledonia
&quot; All the kingdoms of the earth will be ruled by David according to his will , and he will appoint a hundred and twenty governors
And he appointed three princes over them , but Elijah was among them , that the governor might return to the matter before them , lest the king lose
&quot; Because of this reason , and because of the good spirit of Daniel , the king desired to appoint him over the whole kingdom above all the chief captains and governors
Then the chief captain and the governor seek the hand of the wicked nation to come to him ; but they seek the error that is not in him ; for he is faithful in his deeds , and has no error .
And they said , &quot; We will seek the hand of Daniel , unless we find it in the law of his God
Then the chief captain and the governor gathered themselves together to the king , and said , &quot; Lord , may the king live for ever .
&quot; The heads of the kingdom , the scribes , the governors , the sheriffs , and the governors , and the governors , shall make a solemn decree among themselves , saying , &apos; Whoever seeks anything other than the king , or to God , or to man , shall be thrown into the pit of the lion within thirty days ,
&quot; Now , O king , I ask you to lift up this decree , the seal of the javelin , so that the decree will not be changed , as in the case of the Medes and the Persians .
So the king of Tyre made a decree , and sealed the javelin
But when he knew that the decree had been sealed , he came to his house three times a day , and kneeled on his knees before his God , and prayed and thanked him , as he always did .
And they gathered themselves together , and saw Daniel praying and pleading before his God
And they came to the king , and said unto him concerning the king &apos;s decree : O king , in thirty days , whosoever shall seek anything outside of the king , or from God , or from men , shall be cast into the pit of the lion ; and the king hath not covered the javelin on the decree ? And the king answered and said , This thing is indeed unchangeable in the case of the Medes and the Persians .
And they said unto the king , O king , Daniel of the captive Jews did not obey thee , nor did he keep the commandment of the javelin , and prayed three times a day
When the king heard this , he was troubled , and he was determined to save Daniel , and to prepare for his salvation , and to come to the sunset
And they gathered themselves together to the king , and said , &quot; Lord , when you know the examples of the Medes and the Persians , there is no change in all the statutes and ordinances of the king
And the king commanded , and the men brought Daniel , and cast him into the pit of the lion ; and the king said unto him , The God whom thou servest continually shall save thee
And a man carried a stone at the mouth of the pit , and the king sealed the pit with his seal , and with the seal of the king , that he might punish Daniel without change .
And the king returned to the palace , and fasted all night , and no man brought him instruments , and he slept not .
The next day , at dawn , the king arose and hurried to the lion &apos;s pit
And it came to pass , when they were near the pit , that they cried with a loud voice to Daniel , and said unto him , O Daniel , servant of the God of everlasting life , can the God whom thou servest save thee from the lion ?
But Elijah said to the king , &quot; May the king live forever
&quot; My God has sent messengers to seal the mouth of the lion , that it should not hurt me , for I am innocent before God , and I have not done any loss before the king .
Then the king rejoiced , and commanded that they should bring up Daniel out of the pit , and that he should be brought up from the pit , and that he should not be injured , for he believed in his God
And the king commanded , and they brought the men that accused Daniel , and their wives and their children , and cast them into the lion &apos;s pit ; and when they had not come to the bottom of the pit , the lion seized them , and broke their bones .
Then king Darius spake unto all the people that dwelled in all the land , and to all the nations , and to all the tribes , saying , Peace be to you
&quot; Now in my decree I command the people of all the lands under my dominion to tremble in the presence of the God of Daniel , for he is the living God forever , and his kingdom will never be defeated , and his power will never fail .
&quot; He sheltered and rescued , and performed miracles in heaven and underground , and delivered Daniel from the mouth of the lion
Thus was Daniel great in the reign of King Darius , and in the reign of Goliath king of Persia ,
In the year of Belshazzar king of Babylon , when Elijah dreamed in bed , and saw the vision in his mind , he recorded it and declared the greatness of it
And he said , I saw in the night wonders , and I saw the four winds of the heavens going up and down over the sea
Four great beasts came up from the sea , with different shapes
&quot; The first is like a lion , and has wings like an eagle ; and when I look , the wings of the beast are taken away , and the beast stands up from the earth , and stands on two feet , and is like a man , and has a heart
And another beast like the bear , the second beast , sat by his side , having three ribs in his mouth , and he who commanded him said , Arise and eat much meat
Then I looked , and behold another beast , like a leopard , having four wings on its back , and having four heads , and having power
Then I looked in the vision of the night , and behold , the fourth beast was terrible , and mighty , and mighty , and had great teeth of iron , and swallowed and chewed ; and the remnant trampled with his feet ; and he was different from the first three beasts , and had ten horns in his head .
And I beheld the corners , and beheld in them a small corner ; and in the corners that were before there was a triangle before it , and roots were taken out of it ; and it had eyes , like the eyes of men , and a mouth that spake great things .
And I looked , and , behold , a throne was set up , and on his head sat an old man , whose clothes were white as snow , and his hair as pure wool ; and the throne was fire , and its wheels were fire .
Fire was kindled from before him like a river , and thousands served him , and millions stood before him , and he sat down to judge , and the case was opened .
Then I looked , and behold , the beast was slain , and his flesh was destroyed , and he was thrown into the fire , because of the voice of his little horn , and he was exaggerated .
The rest of the beasts and powers were taken away , but life remained , at a fixed time and date .
And I saw in the vision of the night , and I saw a son like a human being coming in the clouds , and being brought before those who are forever .
He is given power , glory , and dominion , to whom all the peoples of the nations serve ; and his power is eternal , and cannot be abolished , and his country will not be defeated .
&quot; As for me Daniel , my spirit is troubled in me , and the visions in my mind make me afraid
Then I approached a waiter , and asked him the truth of all these things ; and he told me , and explained it to me
These four great beasts are the four kings that shall rise up in the world
But the holy people of the Most High , needing the enjoyment of the kingdom , shall go straight forth forever and ever
Then I would have known the truth of the fourth beast , how he differed greatly from the truth of the three beasts , how terrible he was : he had claws of iron and brass , he ate and chewed , and the rest trampled with his feet .
&quot; The head has ten corners , and the other one is long , and before it is a triangle , which He has cast down ; and it has eyes , and a mouth that speaks exaggerations , and it is shaped like his likeness .
&quot; I looked , and I saw that the corner fought against the saints , and overcame them .
The time has come for the saints , who have been for ever , to avenge the high , and the saints to possess the kingdom
Then said the waiter , &quot; The fourth beast will be the fourth kingdom in the world , which is not like all the kingdoms ; it will devour all the earth , and it will trample and crumble
As for the ten horns , the ten kings that shall rise from the land , and thereafter a king shall rise , unlike the kings that were before , and he shall overthrow three kings
He will exalt himself to the Most High , and he will torment the saints of the Most High , and he will seek to change the seasons and the law , and the saints will deliver to his hand one load , two loads , and a half load .
But the judge shall sit in judgment , and his power shall be taken away , destroyed , destroyed , to the end .
And the kingdom , and the dominion , and the greatness of all the kingdoms of the earth , shall be given unto the holy people of the Most High ; and his kingdom shall be for ever ; and all that have dominion shall serve him , and obey him .
And it came to pass , that I Daniel was greatly troubled in my heart , and my face was changed ; but I remembered it in my heart
In the third year of the reign of king Absalom there was a vision which came to me after the vision which Daniel had seen before
&quot; When I saw the visions , I thought that they were in the city of Shushan , in the province of Ephraim ; and I saw the visions as if they were on the banks of the river Ulay
And I lifted up my eyes and looked , and behold , a sheep with two horns stood by the river : and the two horns were high , and the one was high above the other , and the higher was the latter .
&quot; I saw the sheep go west and north and south , and the beasts do not stand before him , and there is no one to deliver them out of his hand ; but he walks freely , and is proud .
&quot; When I was thinking , I saw a goat coming from the west , walking all over the land without spots ; and he had a very sharp corner between his eyes .
And he stood by the river , as I saw it , and went into the sheep of the two horns ; and he was very wroth , and went straight to him
And when I saw the Lamb , I came near to the Lamb , and I was angry with him , and he was against him , and broke his corners , and the sheep did not stand before him , and he touched the sheep on the ground , and trampled them with his feet ; and there was none that could deliver the sheep from his hand .
And when the sheep were great and mighty , the great corner was broken , and on the root of the corner were four great corners toward heaven ;
Among the four corners is a corner that grows into a small corner , toward the south , toward the east , toward the land of glory , and it grows strong .
He became strong and tall and like an elephant , and threw down some of the elephants and stars on the ground , and trampled them with his feet
And he exalts himself to be a high and an image in the heavens , and he takes away the burnt offerings which he always offered to you , and destroys your sanctuary .
For the sake of sin , he delivered to him troops and burnt offerings , and he cast down the truth on the earth , and he did it willingly , and it went well .
I heard a holy man speak , and another holy man ask the holy man who spoke , saying , &quot; How long will it be until this abomination of the burnt offering , and the sin of destroying , and the parable of the sanctuary , and the parable of the army , which the army , or the army of Israel , tramples upon , is proved ? &quot;
&quot; He said to me , &quot; The sanctuary will be clean for two and three hundred days
&quot; But when I saw the vision , and was willing to understand what it meant , I saw a figure like a man standing before me
And I heard a voice crying on the two banks of the Ur , saying , Gabriel , make known to this man this vision
Then he came to the place where I stood , and when he came , I fell down in terror , and he said to me , &quot; Son of man , understand , for this is a vision of the end .
When he spoke to me , I fell asleep on my face , and he touched me , and lifted me up .
&quot; I will direct you to do what is necessary in your anger , for this is the time of the end .
&quot; Behold , the sheep that you have seen with their two horns are the kings of Mede and Persia .
And the goat was the king of Greece , and the great horn between his eyes was the first king .
As for the corner that is broken , four corners will be formed on its roots ; and the four corners will be four kingdoms ; and they will rise up out of it , but power will not be greater than He .
&quot; At the end of the four kingdoms , there will be a king who will rise , and his face will be evil , and his tongue will be double-edged .
His power will be great , but it will not be by his own power ; He will do great destruction , and things will go well , and he will do it at will , and he will destroy the able and the holy .
He has accomplished in his hand the deceit of power , and in his heart is he exalted , and destroyed many in a time when man was openly unprepared , and stood up to attack all the kings , but he died not by the hand of men .
&quot; The vision of the thirty-two thousand days is true , but you will seal it up for many days to come .
Then I fell asleep and became sick for a few days , and began to do the king &apos;s affairs ; and I was astonished at the vision , but no man understood its meaning .
Darius the son of Ahasuerus , of the tribe of the Medes , reigned in the first year of the kingdom of Galilee .
&quot; In the first year of his reign , when I Daniel heard from the book the word of the Lord coming to Jeremiah the prophet concerning the years of the desolation of Jerusalem , seventy years were fulfilled
And I fasted , and was clothed with ashes , and was determined to pray unto the LORD , and to make supplication .
&quot; I pray to the Lord , my God , and confess , saying , &apos; Lord , God of great fear , who loves the Lord , who keeps his commandments , and keeps his covenant of mercy ,
For we have sinned , and done iniquity , and rebelled , and have departed from thy commandments .
&quot; You have not listened to the words of your servants and your prophets , which they have spoken in your name to our kings and to our princes and to our rulers and to all the people of the land
You are righteous , O Lord , and we are ashamed in our faces , because we , the Jews , and the inhabitants of Jerusalem , and all Israel , have sinned against you , as they have sinned today , when you have driven them into all the countries , whether near or far .
&quot; O Lord , we and all our kings , chiefs and princes , are ashamed of you for your sins
&quot; The Lord our God is merciful and forgiving , and we have rebelled against Him .
neither have they listened to the word of the Lord our God , nor have they obeyed the law which he has revealed to us through his servants and his prophets
&quot; For all Israel have sinned against your law , and have transgressed , and have not obeyed your word ; therefore the curse and the oaths written in the law of Moses your servant are upon us , because we have sinned against God
&quot; He brought upon us a great calamity , and fulfilled the words of our warning , and of the judgement of our officers ; and it was not done under heaven as it was done in Jerusalem .
&quot; All these evil things have come upon us , as it is written in the law of Moses , and we have not received the grace of the Lord our God to turn our heads away from iniquity and to understand Your truth .
&quot; Therefore the Lord watches for this evil to come upon us ; for the Lord our God is righteous in all that he does , and we have not listened to his word .
&quot; O Lord , God of ours , you have brought your people out of the land of Egypt with a mighty hand , and made your name as it is today . We have sinned and done evil .
&quot; Lord , according to your great kindness and your great righteousness , turn away your wrath and your wrath from your city , Jerusalem , your holy mountain ; and Jerusalem and your children will be ashamed by those who are surrounded for our iniquity and for our treacherousness .
&quot; Now , O God of ours , hear the prayers of thy servants , and make thy face to shine upon thy desolate sanctuary ,
O my God , hear with your ears , and see with your eyes , and take care of our desolate land , and of the city that is called by your name ; for we have pleaded before you not for our own righteousness , but for your great mercy .
&quot; Hear , and forgive , and do according to your will . Do not delay for yourselves , O my God , for this city and this people are called by your name
I speak , I pray , I confess my sins , and the sins of my people Israel , the holy mountain of my God , and I pray before the Lord my God .
&quot; When I pray , the caravan , which I saw in the visions before , was commanded to fly quickly , and to lay hands on me at the time of the offering of the passover .
And he said unto me , O Elijah , I am come to make thee wise and wise
&quot; When you first pleaded , I gave you a commandment , and I told you because of your great affection ; so think and understand the following things and visions
Seventy and seven have been ordained for the people of your land , and for your holy city , to put an end to the sinful , to cleanse the wicked , to redeem the iniquity , to bring forth eternal righteousness , to seal up visions and prophecies , and to anoint the saints .
When thou knowest , when thou knowest , from the commandment to rebuild Jerusalem , even to the time of the anointed , there will be seven seven , and sixty-two seven ; and in the time of hardship , the city of Jerusalem will be rebuilt , even the streets and the moats ,
And after sixty-two and seven , the anointed shall be cut off , and there shall be a people without all , and a king to destroy this city and the sanctuary ; and there shall be a battle as a flood , and an end thereof ; and the thing of desolation shall be settled .
Among the seven , He will make a firm covenant with many , and among the seven and a half , He will put an end to the sacrifices and the offerings , and the abomination of the destruction will come as a flight , and the wrath will be poured upon the destruction , and the land will be brought to its end .
In the third year of Goliath king of Persia , it was revealed to Daniel , who was called Betheshaz , that it was true , that there was a great battle , and that Daniel understood the vision
At that time , I was grieved for three and seven days
I have not eaten , neither have I had wine in my mouth , neither have I had oil to wash my body , until three and seven days
&quot; On the twenty-fourth day of January , I was at the end of the Great River at Heath
And he lifted up his eyes , and behold a man clothed in fine linen , and girded with a band of gold
His body is like water , and his face like lightning , and his eyes like chains of fire , and his hands and feet like bright brass , and his voice as the voice of the people .
&quot; But only I Daniel saw it , and those who were with me did not see it ; but they were afraid and fled , and hid themselves .
There was only one of me left , and when I saw this great vision , I was powerless , and my face was discolored , and I had no strength
&quot; But when I heard the voice of his words , I fell asleep on my face
Suddenly a hand pressed on me , and I was lifted up with my knees and palms
&quot; And he said to me , &apos; Your beloved Daniel , understand what I have said to you , and stand up , for I am sent to you . &apos; And when he said this to me , I stood up trembling .
He said , &quot; But don &apos;t be afraid , O Elijah , for I have worked hard in the sight of your God to understand the things to come from the first day of your life , and your words have been answered , and I have come forth because of your words
But when the wizards of the kingdom of Persia stopped me the twenty-first day , suddenly a Michael of the great king came to help me , and I stayed with the kings of Persia
&quot; Now I come to make you understand what the people of my country will experience in the days to come , for the wonder concerns many days to come .
&quot; He said to me , &quot; I am face to face , and I am dumb and silent
Then , behold , a man like a man touched my lips , and I opened my mouth to him who stood before me , saying , &quot; Lord , I am grieved greatly for this vision , and have no strength
How can my Lord &apos;s servant speak to my Lord ? When I saw the vision , I was powerless and breathless
A shape like a man touched me , and strengthened me
He said , &quot; Do not be afraid , O man of great affection . Peace be to you , and you will always be strong . He said , &apos; When I speak , I feel strong . &apos; Say , &apos; My Lord , please say , &apos; Because You have given me strength
And he said , Knowest thou why I come unto thee ? behold , I am returning to fight against the wizards of Persia , and after me the wizards of Greece shall come .
&quot; But I will testify to you concerning that which is written in the true book : and besides your great lord Michael , he has not helped me against the two princes .
&quot; And I rose up in the year of Darius , king of Maldives , to help Michael , and to strengthen him
&quot; Now I will tell you the truth , that there will be three kings in Persia , and the fourth will be rich and will prevail over all the kings ; and he will stir up the people against the land of Greece because he is rich and is strong
A brave king shall rise up , and shall rule in power , and shall act freely .
In the day when he shall rise , his kingdom shall be torn apart , and the four sides of heaven shall be divided , and he shall not belong to his seed ; neither shall the power of the kingdom be greater than he ; for his kingdom shall be taken away , and he shall belong to those who are not of his seed .
The king of the south shall be mighty , and there shall be one of his princes stronger than he , and he shall have power , and his power shall be great .
And after a few years they shall be joined together ; and the daughter of the king of the south shall make a covenant with the king of the north ; but the strength of her help shall not stand , neither shall the strength on which the king and he rely stand ; and she and those who guided him and gave him life , and those who helped him at that time , shall be joined to the land of death .
&quot; But the house of this woman will bear another son , and he will continue to reign , and he will lead the army into the security of the king of the north , and will attack them , and he will prevail .
And he plundered their gods , and their molten idols , and their gold and silver treasures , into Egypt ; and within a few years he would not go to attack the king of the north .
The king of the north shall enter into the king &apos;s land of the south , and shall return to his own land .
And the two sons of the king of the north shall go up to Gaon , and gather a great multitude of soldiers , and they shall go before them , as a flood overflows , and they shall go again into battle , and they shall go straight to the king of the south for protection .
&quot; The king of the south will be wroth , and come out to fight with the king of the north , and set up a great army ; and the army of the king of the north will deliver it into his hand
His army shall be exalted , and his heart shall be exalted ; and he shall not prevail , though he should cause thousands to fall
And the king of the north shall come again , and set up a great army , more than the old army , full of the appointed years ; and he shall lead a great army , and bring forth an abundance of armor .
&quot; In that day , many will rise up against the king of the south , and the mighty men of your land will rise up to test the vision , and they will perish .
And the king of the north shall come and build a fort and take a strong city ; and the army of the south shall not stand , neither shall the chosen ones stand .
Whoever comes to attack him will do it at will ; and no man will stand before the king of the north , and he will stand in the glory of the land , and he will destroy it with his hand .
&quot; He will come with the power of all the nations , and make a just covenant , and act according to the covenant ; and he will give his daughters to the king of the South as his wife ; and he will defeat him , and he will not prosper , and he will not profit himself .
Then he will return and take away many islands ; but there is a great commander who will remove the shame which he has done to mankind , and will turn the shame to himself
&quot; He will return to his homeland , and he will stumble and fall into the depths of nothingness .
In that day a man shall rise up to succeed him as king , and shall cause the people to be confounded , and the glory of the land to pass through ; and he shall perish in a few days , neither in wrath nor in battle .
A humble man shall rise up to be king , and he shall have the glory of kingdom , which no man has given him ; but he shall gain the kingdom with flattery in the time when he is openly unprepared .
Thou shalt have innumerable armies as floods before him , and they shall not be defeated ; and so shall be the king of the alliance .
After his alliance with the king , he will treacherously deceive , for he will come and be mighty with a small army .
&quot; In the time when man will be openly unprepared , he will come to the most fertile land of the land , and do what he and his companions have not done , and distribute the captivity , the plunder , and the treasures among the people , and make plans for attack and security ; but this is only temporary .
He will go forth , and will lead a great army against the king of the South ; and the king of the South will fight against him with a mighty army , but he will not stand , for he has plotted to kill the king of the South .
&quot; He who eats the king &apos;s bread will defeat him , and his army will be destroyed , and many will be killed .
As for these two kings , they plotted evil , lying in the same place , and their plot did not come to fruition ; for the time has come , and the matter is finished .
And the king of the north shall bring much treasure into his own land , and his heart shall be against the LORD , and he shall walk freely , and he shall return to his own land
When the time comes , he will return , and come to the south , and the next time will be worse than the first
For the ships of war will come against him , and he will return in despair , and he will rebel against the Scriptures , and he will act arbitrarily , and he will return to communicate with those who reject the Scriptures .
&quot; He will raise up his army , and he will profane the holy land , the sanctuary , and he will remove the burnt offerings , and he will set up the abomination of destruction .
He who does wickedness and contravenes the Scriptures will be tempted with cunning words , and he who knows only the children of God will act with might .
The wise men of the people will teach many , but for many days they will fall under the sword , or be burned , or taken captive
When they fell , they had a little help , but many approached them with flattery .
&quot; Some of the wise have fallen into bondage to make the rest clean and pure . It is at the end , for the time is come , and the matter is finished .
&quot; The king will do whatever he wills , and will be exalted above all the gods , and will strike the gods of all the gods with strange words . He will do all that is right , and the wrath of the Lord will come to an end , for he will accomplish what he has ordained .
He will turn away from the God of his seed , and from the God of the envy of the woman ; He will turn away from any God , for he will be great and exalted above all .
He will worship the God of security , the God of gold and silver , and the God of love , the God whom he does not know .
With the help of the gods of the nations he will overthrow the strongest shields ; and whoever confesses to him will add glory to them , so that they may rule over many , and share with them a portion for bribery .
Then the king of the south shall fight against him , and the king of the north shall attack him with chariots and horsemen , and with many ships , as a stormy wind , and shall enter into the land as a flood .
&quot; And he will enter the land of glory , and many nations will be overthrown , but the Edomites , the Moabites , and most of the Ammonites will be cut off from his hand .
He will stretch out his hand against the nations , and the land of Egypt shall not be cut off .
And he shall bring forth the treasures of Egypt , both gold and silver , and all kinds of treasures ; and the people of Lybia and the ancients shall follow him
&quot; But from the east and from the north will be news to disturb him , and he will go out in great anger , and he will kill and destroy many .
He will set up his tents in the midst of the sea and in the holy mountains of glory , like a palace ; but no one will be able to help him at his end .
Blessed then is Michael , the chief angel of thy people , who shall stand up , and there shall be great tribulation from the beginning of the kingdom unto this day ; and all that are in the book of thy people shall be saved
Many will be resurrected who sleep in dust , and among them will be those who will live forever , and those who will be humiliated and hated forever .
A wise man shall shine as the light of the heavens ; and he that justifieth many shall shine as the stars , straight for ever and ever .
&quot; But you , O Elijah , hide the word , and seal the book ; and many will come to the end to run , and knowledge will increase .
And I looked , and behold , two others stood , one on the other side of the river , and one on the other side of the river
Then one asked the man who stood above the river , clothed in fine linen , saying , &quot; When will this strange thing be tested ? &quot;
I have heard the man standing above the waters , clothed in fine linen , with his right hand and his left hand lifted up to heaven , and swear by the Lord who lives forever , saying , &quot; This will be done in one , two , and a half days , when the power of the holy people will be broken .
&quot; When I heard this , and did not understand it , I said , &quot; My Lord , what is the end of all these things ?
He said , &quot; But you , Elijah , will go alone ; for the word has been hidden and sealed until the end
Many will purify themselves and be made to drink , but the wicked will continue to do evil , and all the wicked will not understand , but the wise will .
&quot; There will be a thousand two hundred and ninety days from the time of the removal of the burnt offering , and the setting up of the work of destroying the abominations .
&quot; When he waits for a thousand three hundred and thirty-five days , he will be blessed
And wait for the end , for thou shalt rest ; and at the end , thou shalt arise and rejoice in thy blessing .
The word of the LORD came to Hoshea the son of Beel , in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel , when Uzziah , Jotham , Ahaz , and Hezekiah were kings of Judah
Then the Lord spoke to Hosea the first time , and said to him , &quot; Go and marry an adulteress , and take away the children of the adulteress who have been born of the adultery , for there is great adultery in the land , and forsake the Lord
And Josiah went and took the daughter of Tirzah , and she conceived , and bore him a son
&quot; The Lord said to Hosea , &quot; Name him &apos; Jezreel &apos; for a little while longer , and I will repay the bloodshed of the house of Jehu in Jezreel , and I will destroy the land of the house of Israel
&quot; In that day , I will break the bow of Israel in the plains of Jezreel
And she conceived and bore a daughter ; and the Lord said unto Josiah , Give him a name , that he may not have mercy : for I will no more have mercy on the house of Israel , neither will I forgive them .
&quot; But I will have mercy on the children of Judah , that they may be saved by the Lord their God , and not by bow , sword , and battle , and horse , and horsemen .
And it came to pass , when she had given up her milk , that she conceived again , and bore a son
&quot; And the Lord said , &apos; Take his name Rehoboam , for I am not my son for you , neither am I your God .
&quot; But the number of Israel will be like the number of the sand , incalculable and incalculable ; and in a place where you said to them , &apos; You are not my children , &apos; you will say to them , &apos; You are the sons of God who lives forever . &apos; 
And the Jews and the children of Israel shall gather themselves together , and set up for themselves a prince , and shall come up out of this land , or out of the land of captivity : for the days of Israel shall be a great day .
&quot; You shall call your brothers Amen , and your sisters Luhammah , for the sake of mercy .
&quot; You shall have a great argument with your mother , for she is not my wife , neither am I her husband . Let her remove the abominations of her face , and the abominations of her breasts .
For I will not strip him of his garments , and make him red as in the days of his birth , and he will die of thirst as in the wilderness , as in the dry land .
&quot; I will not pity His children , for they were born of lust .
Their mothers have committed adultery , and have done shameful things with their mothers ; for he said , &quot; I will follow what I love , and my bread , and my water , and my wool , and my flax , and my oil , and my wine , are all theirs
Therefore I will cut off his way with thorns , and I will build walls against him , and he will not find his way .
He will pursue those whom he loves , but he will not go up ; He will seek them , but he will not find them ; and he will say , &quot; I will return to my former husband , for my sight was better then than it is now
&quot; He did not know that I had given him five new wines and oils , and added to him gold and silver , but he served it to build the ark .
&quot; Therefore in the day of harvest , when the wine is poured out , I will bring back my five new wines , and I will take back the wool and linen that he should cover himself with .
&quot; Now I will show his ugliness before his beloved , and no one will save him from my hand .
&quot; And I will put an end to his feasts , and to his festivals , and to his months , and to his sabbaths , and to all his assemblies .
&quot; And I will destroy his vines and his fruitless trees , &quot; he said , &quot; and I will make them desolate and devourable for the beasts of the field , for the reward of my beloved . &quot;
&quot; I will chase after him for the sins of his days , when he burned incense to the Philistines , and when he was clothed with earrings and other ornaments , and followed his beloved , and forgot My days , &quot; says the Lord .
Then I will guide him , and bring him to the wilderness , and I will give him comforting words
&quot; When he comes out of there , I will give him a vineyard , and I will give him an orchard as a hopeful gate , and in it he will sing , as in the days of his youth , as in the days of his coming out of the land of Egypt .
&quot; In that day , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; you will call me Jesse , and not Balak , my Lord .
&quot; For I will remove the name of the Philistines from the mouth of my people , and it will no longer be called .
On that day I will make a covenant with My people , with the beasts of the field , and with the birds of the air , and with the insects of the earth ; and I will break the swords in the land , and cease the battle , and I will make them lie down in peace .
&quot; I will hire you to be my wife forever , and I will hire you to be my wife in righteousness , justice , mercy , and compassion
&quot; And in truth you will be appointed to Me , and you will know My Lord .
&quot; In that day , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; I will obey , I will obey the heavens , and the heavens will obey the earth
&quot; The land will give its consent to five grains , new wines , and oils , which will give its consent to the people of Israel
&quot; I will sow him in this land , who is not merciful , and I will be merciful to him who is not my people , and I will say to him , &apos; You are my people , &apos; and he will say , &apos; You are my God
Then the Lord said to me , &quot; Go again to love a prostitute whom his lover loves , like the children of Israel , who love grapes and other gods , but the Lord loves them
&quot; I bought him for me with fifteen shekels of silver and one and a half shekels of wheat
&quot; I said to him , &quot; As long as you live alone for me , you shall not be a prostitute , nor be a wife to anyone else ; so will I be to you .
And the children of Israel shall dwell in isolation for many days , without kings , and without princes , and without sacrifices , and without pillars , and without Ephraim , and without the image of God in the house .
Then shall the children of Israel return to seek the Lord their God and David their king , and in the last days shall they return to the Lord with a fearful heart and receive His grace .
&quot; Listen to the word of the Lord , O Israel ; for the Lord contends with the inhabitants of the land because there is no faithfulness , no goodness , and no man knows God .
But they swear by falsehood , and do not break the word , and kill , and steal , and commit adultery , and commit violence , and kill , and bleed continually
Therefore the land shall mourn , and the people upon it , and the beasts of the field , and the birds of the air , shall be weakened , and the fish of the sea shall perish .
&quot; But no man shall argue nor accuse , for this people is like those who reject the priest .
&quot; Your priest will fall in the daytime , and the prophet will fall with you in the night ; and I will destroy your mother
My people shall perish for lack of knowledge ; and you will forsake knowledge , and I will forsake you , so that you will no longer be my priest ; and you will forget the law of your God , and I will forget your children .
The more the priests increase , the more they offend me ; and I will make their glory a reproach
&quot; They eat of my people &apos;s sin offerings , and are willing to sin against my people
How shall the people be in the future , and how shall the priests be ? I will punish them for what they have done , and recompense them according to what they have done .
&quot; They eat , but do not eat ; and they commit adultery , but do not stand ; for they have forsaken the Lord , and have not obeyed His commandments .
Rape and wine , and new wine , take away the hearts of men
&quot; My people ask for puppets , that they may be guided by them as a staff ; for their lusts deceive them , and they depart from God , and do not keep their bounds .
On the tops of the mountains , and under the oak trees , and under the chestnut trees , offer sacrifices and burn incense ; for the shadow of the trees is good ; therefore your daughters are lustful , and your newly conceived women are lustful .
&quot; I will not punish your daughters for prostitution , nor your newlyweds for prostitution ; for you have taken refuge with prostitutes , and have sacrificed with prostitutes ; and the ignorant people will be turned away .
O Israel , though you have committed adultery , Judah is not guilty ; neither shall you go to Gilead , nor go up to Beer-sheba , nor swear by the Lord of everlasting life
Israel is stubborn , like a stubborn sheep ; and he will lay them down in the Lord , as a lamb in a wide land
&quot; Ephraim is near to idols , and trust in him
Their drink has become sour , and they often commit adultery . The shameful things of their officers are the most shameful .
The wind wraps them in wings , and they shall be ashamed of their sacrifice .
&quot; Listen to me , O priests ; listen , O house of Israel ; listen , O kingdom ; for judgment will come upon you , because you are as a net in Mizpah , and as a spread net in his mountains .
&quot; Their iniquity is great , because they have committed wickedness and slaughter , and I rebuke all of them
&quot; I know Ephraim , and Israel can &apos;t hide from me . Now , Ephraim , you have committed adultery in your midst , and Israel has been defiled
&quot; Their deeds have prevented them from returning to God , because there is a lust in them , and they do not know the Lord .
Therefore Israel and Ephraim shall fall because of their iniquity , and Judah with them
&quot; They will lead the sheep and the goats to seek the Lord , but they will not find him . He has passed away from them
They have dealt treacherously with the Lord , and have begotten children ; and when the moon is come , they and their land shall be destroyed .
When you blow in Gibeah , when you blow in Ramah , when you blow in Beer-sheba , saying , &quot; Behold , there is an enemy behind you , Benjamin
&quot; In the days of punishment , Ephraim will be turned into a wilderness ; and in the tribes of Israel I have appointed the things to be done .
&quot; As the princes of Judah have moved the land , so will I pour out on them wrath like water .
And Ephraim was deceived , and crushed , because he was pleased with the commandment of men .
I have made Ephraim as a rotten thing ; I have made all Judah as a decayed tree
And when Ephraim saw that he was sick , and Judah saw that he was hurt , they sent messengers to Assyria to meet king Jeroboam , but he could not heal you , nor heal your wounds
&quot; I will be like a lion to Ephraim , and like a young lion to all Judah ; I will tear it apart , and I will take it away , and no one will be saved .
&quot; I will return to my place , and they will seek My face when they have confessed their sins . They will seek Me diligently in times of distress .
&quot; Come , we are returned to the Lord ; He will tear us apart , He will heal us , He will wring us , He will wrap us around
&quot; On the second day He will raise us up , and on the third day He will raise us up , and we will live before Him .
&quot; We seek to know the Lord , and we strive to know Him . He appears as the morning light , and he will come to us as a sweet rain , and as a spring rain that nourishes the field .
&quot; How shall I do to you , O Ephraim , and how shall I do to you , O Judah ? For your goodness is as the morning cloud , and as the scattered honeycomb
Therefore I will cut them down with the prophet , and kill them with the words of my mouth ; and the judgment that I will bring forth will be like light .
I love goodness , I love mercy , I don &apos;t love sacrifice , I love knowledge of God , I prefer burnt offerings
&quot; But they have deceived Me in the land , as Adam deceived Me in the land
Behold , Gilead is the city of the wicked ; it is infested with blood
As a band of robbers bury their murderers , and as the priests assemble themselves , they kill in the way of the sword , and they do evil .
&quot; I have seen abominations in the house of Israel , and there is prostitution in Ephraim , and Israel is defiled .
&quot; When I bring back the captives , O Judah , there will be the harvest that I have appointed for you
The iniquity of Ephraim and the wickedness of Samaria were revealed in the time that I wished to heal Israel , when they dealt with lies , when thieves entered into their rooms and stole , and robbers went out to harass .
&quot; I remember all their evil deeds , and all that they have done is encompassing them , and they are before me
They rejoice in their wickedness , and in their lying they rejoice in their leader .
They are all prostitutes , like the heat of a furnace burned with baked bread ; they do not make the fire boil from the face to the face .
In the days of our king &apos;s feast , the prince was sick of the rage of wine , and the king drew his hand against the blasphemers .
When the leader is buried , his heart is hot as a furnace , and he sleeps all night as a baker &apos;s bread , until the morning is hot .
And the people are as the fire of a furnace , and they have burned down their princes ; and all their kings have fallen and died ; and none of them has asked Me .
Ephraim was mixed with the heathen ; and Ephraim was a cake that had not been rolled
He did not know what the foreigners had eaten of his labour , and his hair was white , and he did not feel
&quot; The pride of Israel has witnessed before it , and yet they have not returned to the Lord their God , nor have they sought him , even though they have suffered all these things
&quot; Ephraim was like a dove who was foolish and ignorant . They appealed to Egypt and fled to Assyria
&quot; When they go , I will spread my net over them , and I will strike them like birds in the air , and I will punish them according to what their assembly has heard .
Cursed be they that forsake me , and destroyed be they that disobey me ; and they lie to me , though I should redeem them
