&quot; Hear this , and warn the house of Jacob , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , the God of hosts .
&quot; In the days of my vengeance on Israel , I will also vengeance on the altar of Bethlehem ; and the horns of the altar will be cut down , and fall to the ground .
&quot; I will destroy the houses of the winter and of the summer , and the houses of the ivory will be destroyed , and the houses of the high places will be desolate , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; You dwell in the mountains of Samaria like a cow in Bashan . When you hear my words , you deceive the poor , and crush the needy , and say to your master , &apos; Bring us wine , that we may drink
&quot; The day is near , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh in his holiness , &quot; and he will take away your hooks , and take away your remaining hooks with fish hooks
&quot; You shall go straight from the mouth of your enemies to Haman , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; O Israel , let your sins go to Bethlehem , and add to your sins to Gibeah ; and offer your offerings every morning , and one tenth of your offerings every three days .
&quot; You shall offer the thanksgiving offerings of yeast , and proclaim the sweet offerings to the people , because they are your beloved , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh .
&quot; I have cleansed your teeth in all the cities , and there is no food in all your places ; yet you will not return to me , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; In the first three months of harvest I have stopped the rain from falling on you ; I have rained on this city , and on that city ; and the land has rained , and the land has no rain ; and the land that has no rain has dried up
&quot; So the people of two or three cities gathered together in one city to seek water , but they did not have enough ; yet you will not return to Me , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; I will strike you with the wind and with the dust , and many herbs and fruits and vines and fruitless trees and olive trees will be eaten in your gardens , and you will not return to me , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; I will send a plague among you , as in Egypt , and I will kill your young men with the sword , and your horses with the sword , and the smell of the corpses in the camp will rise up , and you will not return to me , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; I will overthrow the cities among you , as I overthrew Sodom Moor , and you will be like a wood from the fire , and you will not return to me , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; I will do this to you , O Israel , and I will do this to you , O Israel , when you are ready to meet your God
He who creates mountains , He who creates winds , He who guides the mind , He who makes the morning dark , He who walks on the high places of the earth , His name is the Lord , the God of hosts .
O house of Israel , hear my cry for you ,
And the children of Israel fell down , and shall not rise again ; and they lay on the earth , and no man helped them .
Thus saith the Lord GOD ; For the city of the house of Israel hath sent forth a thousand men , and there is one hundred left ; For the city of Israel hath sent forth one hundred , and there is ten left
Thus saith the LORD unto the house of Israel ; If ye seek me , ye shall live
&quot; Do not seek for Bethlehem , nor enter into Gilead , nor go to Beer-sheba ; for Gilead will be taken away , and Bethlehem will be desolate .
&quot; If you seek the Lord , you will live , lest He burn like a fire in the house of Joseph , and no man be destroyed in Bethlehem
&quot; You have turned fairness into a fig tree , and have cast away righteousness from the earth .
&quot; Seek him who made the stars of Pleiades and Saturn , who turned the shadow of death into the morning light , and turned the sun into the night , and caused the waters to be poured out on the earth ,
He caused the mighty to perish , so that they might be destroyed .
&quot; You hate him who reproaches at the gates of the city , and you hate him who speaks the truth .
Thou trampledst upon the poor , and robbedst them of their wheat ; and thou builtest houses with stones cut down , but thou shalt not dwell therein ; and thou plantedst good vineyards , but thou shalt not drink of the wine thereof .
I know how much your sins are , and how great your sins are ; and you suffer for the righteous , and receive bribes , and reject the poor at the gates of the city .
Therefore he who reaches out will not speak silently when he sees such a time ; for it is evil for time .
&quot; If you ask for good , and do not ask for evil , you will live ; and the Lord God of hosts will be with you , as you have said
Or the Lord God of hosts will give mercy to the remnant of Joseph
Thus saith the Lord GOD , the God of hosts ; There shall be a voice of mourning in all the plains ; and in the streets and in the cities there shall be a voice of mourning , and a voice of mourning , and a voice of mourning for the farmers , and a voice of mourning for the good .
&quot; There will be a cry in the vineyards ; for I will pass through you , &quot; says the Lord .
Woe unto you that ye seek the day of the LORD , when it cometh ; for why seek ye the day of the LORD , when there is no light in the darkness ?
It is as if a man fled from a lion and met a bear , or entered a house with his hand against the wall , and was bitten by a snake .
Is not the day of the Lord darkness without light , darkness without light ?
I hate your feasts , and I am not pleased with your solemn feasts
&quot; However you offer me burnt offerings and sacrifices , I do not approve of them , nor of the peace offerings you offer with fat animals .
Let the sound of your singing be far from me ; for I do not hear the sound of your harp
Let fairness be as the flow of waters , and righteousness as the flow of rivers
&quot; Have you offered sacrifices and offerings to me in the wilderness forty years , O house of Israel ?
&quot; You shall lift up the tabernacle of Moses , which you have made for yourselves , and the horns of idols , and the stars of your gods ,
&quot; Therefore I will take you captive beyond Damascus , &quot; says the Lord , the God of hosts .
Woe to him who is the head of the nations , the most prominent man , and to the house of Israel , who is restless in Zion and mount Samaria !
And you shall pass over to the land of Canaan , and from there to the great city of Hama , and down to Gath of the Philistines , and see whether there are nations stronger than your own , and borders broader than your own .
&quot; You think that the days of evil are far off , and sit on your seats and do violence , until the judgment is near .
&quot; You lie on an ivory bed , and rest on your beds , and eat the lambs of the flock , and the calves of the flock
The harpsichords sing leisurely songs , and make instruments for themselves , as David did .
drink a large bowl of wine , and wash yourselves with fine oil , but fear not Joseph &apos;s affliction
Therefore they shall be first taken captive among the captives ; and the joy of the refreshed shall be consumed .
&quot; As the Lord Yahweh , the God of hosts , has sworn by himself , &apos; I hate the glory of Jacob , and I hate his palaces ; therefore I will deliver the city and all of it into the hand of the enemy .
If there were ten people left in one house , they would all die .
&quot; The uncle of the deceased , who has burned his body , will take it out of the house , and ask the people in the house , &apos; Is there anyone in you ? &apos; He will say , &apos; No . &apos; And he will say , &apos; Do not speak , for we cannot call on the name of the Lord . &apos; 
&quot; Behold , the Lord has commanded , &apos; The large house will be destroyed , and the small house will be torn .
Can a horse run on a cliff , and a man sow cattle therein ? But you have made fairness bitterness , and the fruit of righteousness rhinestone .
Have we not taken a corner by our own power , when ye boast , and love vanity ?
&quot; The Lord , the God of hosts , said , &apos; I will raise up a nation against you , O house of Israel , and they will oppress you from the mouth of Hama to the river of Ahab .
&quot; The Lord Yahweh has directed me to do one thing : After the king &apos;s harvest , there will be another harvest , and the Lord will make locusts in the days of his birth .
&quot; The locusts have eaten up all the green things of the land , and I said , &apos; Lord , forgive me , for how could Jacob stand and live when he was weak ?
Then the Lord repented and said , &quot; This plague can be averted
&quot; The Lord Yahweh has also instructed me : He has commanded fire to punish Israel , and it will swallow up the depths , and it will devour the land .
Then I said , &quot; Repent , Lord Yahweh , for how can Jacob stand , because he is weak ? &quot;
Then the Lord repented and said , &quot; This plague is also forgiven
And he commanded me another thing : There was a wall built by cords , and the master stood on it with cords .
And the LORD said unto me , What seeest thou , O Amos ? And I said , I see the cord ; and the LORD said , I will raise up the cord among my people Israel , and I will not forgive them any more
Surely the high places of Esau shall be desolate , and the sanctuaries of Israel shall be desolate ; and I will rise up and smite the house of Jeroboam with the sword
Then Amaziah the priest of Bethlehem sent to Jeroboam the king of Israel , saying , &quot; Amos is in the house of Israel plotting to betray you , and all that he has said is not in the hands of this nation .
For thus saith Amos , Jeroboam shall be struck with the sword , and the children of Israel shall be taken captive , and they shall be driven out of their land
Then Amaziah said to Amos , &quot; Behold , you are to flee to the land of Judah , where you will live and prophesy
&quot; But I will not prophesy again in Bethlehem : for there is a king &apos;s sanctuary and a king &apos;s palace for it .
And he said unto Amaziah , I am not a prophet , neither a prophet &apos;s disciple ; but I am a minister , and repairer of the savannah
&quot; The Lord has chosen me that I should not follow the sheep , and He has said to me , &apos; Go prophesy to my people Israel
&quot; Now , Amaziah , listen to the word of the Lord in your midst , saying , &apos; You shall not prophesy to Israel , nor do you prophesy to the house of Esau
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord : &apos; Your wives will be prostitutes in the city , and your children will fall under the sword , and the rope will be used to divide your land ; and you will die in the land of defilement , and the children of Israel will be taken captive and driven out of the land .
&quot; The Lord Yahweh has also instructed me : I have seen a basket of summer fruit
And he said , What seeest thou , O Amos ? And I said , I see a basket of summer fruit ; and the LORD said , The end of my people Israel is come , and I will not forgive them any more
&quot; In that day , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; the songs of the house will become a lamentation , and many bodies will be abandoned everywhere , and no one will speak .
&quot; You shall eat the poor , and the needy shall be weakened . Listen to me
&quot; When the moon passes , &quot; you say , &quot; we will sell the grain ; when the Sabbath passes , we will spread out the wheat ; we will sell it with small pitchers ; we will collect the money with large spears ; and we will deceive people with a deceitful sky .
It is good to buy the poor with silver , to replace the poor with a pair of shoes , and to sell the bad wheat to a man
&quot; The Lord swore by the glory of Jacob , saying , &quot; I will never forget all their deeds
Will not the earth be shaken by this , and the inhabitants thereof mourn ? The earth will rise up like the Nile , and the river of Egypt will rise up and fall down
&quot; In that day , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; I will make the sun fall at noon , and the earth dark at daybreak .
I will make your feasts mourning , songs mourning ; and they will be clothed in linen , and bald on their heads ; and I will make this mourning like the loss of a single child , and like a painful day to come .
&quot; The days will come , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh , &quot; and I will cause famine to descend on the earth ; and people will not be hungry because they have no bread , nor because they are thirsty , nor because they have no water , but because they have not listened to the word of the Lord
They will flow from this sea to that sea , from north to east , running for the word of the Lord , but they will not find it .
On that day , the beautiful virgin and the young man shall faint from thirst .
&quot; But we swear by the living God who is with you , and we swear by the Word of God that is not in Baal ; and they will all fall , and never come up again .
I saw the Lord standing by the altar , and he said , &quot; You shall strike the top of the pillar , and shake the threshold , and break the top of the pillar on the heads of all the people ; and I will slay the remnant with the sword , and none will escape , and none will escape .
Though they dig through the shadows , My hand will take them out ; Though they climb up to heaven , I will take them away .
&quot; While I am hiding on the top of Mount Carmel , I will seek to catch them ; and while I am hiding from My sight at the bottom of the sea , I will bite the snake to bite them .
Though they are taken captive by their enemies , I will slay them with the sword , and I will set my eyes on them ; and evil is not good
The Lord of hosts touches the earth , and the earth digests it ; and all that dwell on the earth will mourn ; and the earth will rise up like the Nile , and the Egyptian River will fall down .
&quot; The name of the Lord is he who builds palaces in the heavens , and sets up stables in the earth , and causes water to be poured out on the earth .
&quot; Have I not regarded you , O Israel , as an ancient people , and have I not brought Israel out of the land of Egypt , and the Philistines out of Capernaum , and the children of Aram out of Geer ?
&quot; Behold , the eyes of the Lord Yahweh look on this sinful land , and he will destroy it from the earth , but not the house of Jacob , &quot; says the Lord Yahweh
&quot; I will send a commandment to disperse the house of Israel among the nations , as a screen for a screen for a valley , and not a grain will fall on the earth .
&quot; All the sinners among my people say , &apos; The evil will not pursue us , nor meet us ; they will die under the sword .
&quot; In that day I will build David &apos;s collapsed tent , and I will shut the doors thereof , and I will raise up the ruined building , and I will repair it , as in the old days .
Thus saith the Lord that doeth this , that Israel may possess the remnant of the east , and all the nations that are called by my name :
&quot; The day will come , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that he who sows will reap again , and he who sows grapes will reap again , and the mountains will pour out sweet wine , and the small mountains will be milked .
&quot; I will bring back my people Israel , the captives ; they will inhabit the desolate cities , and plant vineyards , and drink the wine thereof , and make vineyards , and eat the fruit thereof .
&quot; I will plant them in the land , and they will no longer come forth out of the land which I have given them , &quot; says the Lord your God .
And Obadiah received the word of the Lord concerning Edom , saying , I have heard the word of the Lord , and there are messengers sent to the nations , saying , Arise , and fight with Edom together
I have made you the least of the nations in the east , and greatly despised
O thou that dwellest in the pits and in the high places , thou hast deceived thyself in pride , saying , Who will bring me down ?
&quot; I will bring you down from there , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; even though you are as the eagle that flies high , and lodges in the starry places .
&quot; If a thief comes to you , or a robber comes to you at night , will he not steal straight to the well , and if a grape harvester comes to you , will there be no grapes left ?
How was the secrets of Esau searched , and how were his hidden treasures discovered ?
Those who have made alliances with you will lead you on the way until the border . They will deceive you and overcome you with the good . The nets that eat with you will engulf you , and there is no intelligence in your heart .
&quot; In that day , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; will I not destroy the wise from Edom , and the wise from Mount Esau ? &quot;
&quot; Your mighty men will be terrified , O Timan , so that the men of the mountains will be slain and cut off
Shame will cover you , and you will be cut off forever , because you have done violence to your brother Jacob
&quot; When strangers plundered Jacob &apos;s possessions , and foreigners entered his gates , and you stood by him as if you were with them in the days of a lot for Jerusalem
When your brothers are in trouble , do not stare with your eyes , When the Jews are destroyed , Do not rejoice , When they are in trouble , Do not speak arrogantly
&quot; In the days of my people , do not enter their gates ; In the days of their affliction , do not stare at their suffering ; In the days of their affliction , do not reach for their treasures
Thou shalt not stand at the crossroads , and cut off those who escape among them ; and thou shalt not deliver the remnant of them unto the enemy in the days of their affliction .
&quot; The day of the Lord &apos;s retribution is near for all the nations ; He will do to you as you do , and your recompense will be on your head .
As ye have drunk the bitter cup in my holy mountain , so shall all the nations drink , and drink and swallow ; and they shall be without .
And there shall be escapers in mount Zion , and the mount shall be sanctified , and the house of Jacob shall have the inheritance which it had .
And the house of Jacob shall be a great fire , and the house of Joseph a flame ; and the house of Esau shall be as stubble , and the fire shall devour him with fire ; and the house of Esau shall be left no more , saith the LORD .
And the south shall be able to sweep the mountains ; and the high places shall have the land of Philistine , and the land of Ephraim , and the land of Samaria ; and the children of Benjamin shall have Gilead .
All Israel , who were taken captive among the Canaanites , shall be brought straight to Saleh ; and Jerusalem , who were taken captive among the Philistines , shall be brought to the cities of the south .
And there shall come up a savior unto mount Zion , and he shall judge mount Esau : and the kingdom shall be unto the LORD
The word of the LORD came to Jonah the son of Amity , saying ,
&quot; Arise , go to the great city of Nineveh , and cry to the inhabitants thereof ; for their evil has come to me .
And Jonah arose , and fled unto him , to hide himself from the LORD ; and he came down to Joppa , and behold a ship to be delivered unto him ; and he gave him the price of the ship , and went up into the ship , to hide himself from the LORD with the men of the ship .
But the Lord caused a great wind to rise in the sea , and the sea was overwhelmed with wind , and the ships were almost destroyed
And the sailors were afraid , and they cried unto their God : and they cast the goods of the ship into the sea , that they might lighten the ship : and Jonah went down to the end of the chamber , and lay down , and fell asleep .
And the captain came to him , and said unto him , Why is this , O thou sleeper ? arise , and pray unto thy God , that he may take care of us , lest we perish
And the men of the ship said unto one another , Come , let us cast lots , and see for whose cause this calamity came upon us . And they cast lots , and cast out the book of Jonah
And they said unto him , Tell us , for whose sake is this calamity come unto us , and what work hast thou done , and whereest thou come from , and what nation art thou , and of that people ?
He said , &quot; I am a Hebrew , and I fear the Lord , the God of the heavens , who created the sea and the dry land
And they feared greatly , and said unto him , What is it that thou hast done ? for they knew that he fled from the LORD , because he had told them
And they said unto him , How shall we do unto thee , that the waves may be quiet , because the waves are rising and rising ?
And he said unto them , When ye have lifted me up , and cast me into the sea , the sea is at rest ; and I know that for my sake ye are afflicted by the wind
But those who rowed and tried to bring the ship to the shore were unable , for the waves turned against them more and more
And they cried unto the LORD , saying , Lord , we beseech thee not that we should die because of this man &apos;s life , and that the sin of innocent blood should come unto us ; for thy Lord doeth according to his own will .
And they lifted up Jonah , and cast him into the sea ; and the waves of the sea ceased .
And they feared the LORD greatly , and offered sacrifices unto the LORD , and made vows
&quot; The Lord arranged for Jonah to be swallowed up by a great fish , and he was in the belly of the fish three days and three nights
Jonah prayed in the belly of the fish to the Lord his God
&quot; When I am in trouble , call on the Lord ; You will hear me ; Call from the depths of the shadows ; You will listen to my voice .
Thou castest me down into the depths of the sea ; great waters encircle me , and thy waves overflow me .
&quot; I said , &quot; While I have been driven out of your sight , I will still look at your temple
The waters encircle me ; they almost overwhelm me ; the depths encircle me ; the grass encircles my head .
&quot; I have come down to the mountains , and the gates of the earth will shut me up for ever ; but you , Lord , my God , have delivered my life out of the pit .
When my heart fades in me , I remember the Lord ; and my prayers come into thy temple , and reach before thee
For he that believeth in the God of vanity hath forsaken the Lord of his mercy
&quot; But I will sacrifice with a voice of thanksgiving to you , and I will repay my vows . Salvation is from the Lord
&quot; The Lord commanded the fish , and the fish threw Jonah into the dry land
And the word of the Lord came to Jonah twice , saying ,
&quot; Arise , and go to the great city of Nineveh , and proclaim to its inhabitants what I have commanded you
And Jonah arose , and went to Nineveh , according to the word of the LORD ; and it was a great city , a journey of three days .
Then Jonah went into the city one day , and said , &quot; Wait forty days , and Nineveh will be overthrown .
The Ninevites , believing in God , declared a fast , and wore sackcloth from the greatest to the smallest .
And it came to pass in the ears of the king of Nineveh , that he went down from his throne , and was clothed in linen , and sat in ashes .
Then he sent to the city of Nineveh , saying , &quot; The king and the minister have a decree that no man shall taste anything , beasts , sheep , or grass , nor drink water
When men and cattle are clothed in linen , they pray diligently to God ; and they turn away from the wickedness of their deeds , and from the violence of their hands .
Or God repents , and does not become angry , so that we do not perish ?
Then God saw their deeds , and when he saw that they departed from the wicked way , he repented , and did not bring back the evil that he had said unto them
The covenant was greatly displeased and exceedingly angry
And they prayed unto the LORD , saying , Thus saith the LORD , when I am in my own land : I know that Thou art a God of grace and mercy , not easily angry , not abundant in mercy , and not repentant of the evil that Thou hast spoken : therefore hast I fled quickly unto him
&quot; Now , O Lord , seek my life ; for I am better dead than alive .
&quot; The Lord said , &quot; Is it reasonable for you to be so angry
Then Jonah went out of the city , and sat on the east side of the city , and set up a tent for himself therein , and sat under the shade of the tent , to see how the city was
And the LORD God hath set up a castor , and it hath risen above Jonah , and shadow hath covered his head , and delivered him out of his affliction ; and Jonah rejoiced greatly because of the castor
Then the next day , at dawn , God arranged for a worm to bite the castor , so that it would decay
And it came to pass , when the sun was set , that God prepared a hot east wind ; and the sun was set on Jonah &apos;s head , and he fell asleep ; and he cried for his own death , saying , &quot; I am dead better than alive .
And God said unto Jonah , Is it lawful for thee to be angry with this cashew ? And he said , It is lawful for me to be angry even to death
&quot; This castor has not been planted by you , neither has it been cultivated by you , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and it will happen one night , and you will die one night , and you will be happy and loving
&quot; And in the great city of Nineveh , where there are more than twelve thousand men who cannot tell the right hand from the left , and many beasts , will I not love them ?
Speaking of Samaria and Jerusalem , in the days of Jotham , and of Ahaz , and of Hezekiah king of Judah ,
&quot; Listen , all you people , and listen to the earth , and to all that is on it ; and it is not for you that the Lord Yahweh witnesses from His temple .
&quot; Behold , the Lord comes out of His dwelling place , and comes to the height of the foothills
The mountains will digest beneath him , and the valleys will break down , as wax in the fire , as waters pour down the slopes .
For the sins of Jacob , and for the sins of the house of Israel : where is Jacob &apos;s sin , not in Samaria , and not in the high places of Judah , and not in Jerusalem ?
Therefore I will make Samaria a desolation in the fields , and a place of grapes ; and I will lay down his stones in the valleys , and I will reveal his roots .
All the idols of his carvings shall be cut down , and all the riches of his riches shall be burned with fire ; and I will destroy all the idols ; for they are gathered together from the wages of the prostitute , and they shall be returned to the wages of the prostitute .
&quot; Therefore I will cry with a loud voice , I will walk barefoot , I will cry like a wild dog , I will weep like a camel , &quot; said the prophet .
For the wounds of Samaria cannot be healed , and the gates of Judah and Jerusalem cannot be opened
&quot; Don &apos;t report this in Gath , and don &apos;t weep . I am rolling in the dust in Beersheba
Woe to you , O inhabitants of Shapheh , for you have gone astray in your nakedness ; and the inhabitants of Zannah have not dared to come out ; and the weeping of the Philistines has left you no place to stand .
&quot; The inhabitants of Maldives were in great distress and hoped for good , because the evil was coming from the Lord to the gates of Jerusalem
&quot; O inhabitants of Lach , ride in a chariot . The sins of the women of Zion are yours , and the sins of the children of Israel are manifest in you .
&quot; You , O Judah , will give gifts to Moses and Zechariah , and you will deceive the kings of Israel by the people of Assyria
&quot; O inhabitants of the land of Malisha , I will bring to you those who have taken you , and the nobleman of Israel will come to Adullam .
&quot; Your beloved daughters , O Judah , cut off your hair , and make your head bald , and make it bald like a bald eagle ; for they are all taken away from you .
Woe to those who commit iniquity in bed , and commit wickedness ; and the heavens are opened , and they come forth , because of the power of their hands .
They have taken possession of the fields , they have taken possession of houses , they have oppressed people , they have taken possession of houses and industries
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord : &apos; I have prepared a plague for this people , which cannot be removed from your necks , neither can you lift up your heads , for it is evil at this time .
&quot; In that day there will be a grievous mourning for you , and a derision , saying , &apos; We are all defeated ; the Lord has turned our portion to another ; why has he taken it away from us ? He has divided our land for the rebellious .
&quot; There will be no man among you in the congregation of the Lord to draw cords
They said , &quot; You shall not prophesy , nor prophesy to these people , nor do you inhabit the land to shame us .
&quot; Will you say , O house of Jacob , &apos; The heart of the Lord is not patient ? &apos; &apos; Is it that He does these things ? &apos; &apos; Isn &apos;t my word , the word of the Lord , beneficial to the upright ? &apos;
But my people have risen up as enemies , and have stripped themselves of their garments from those who are safely passed by who are unwilling to fight .
&quot; You have driven out the women of my people from the houses of peace , and have taken away my glory from their children .
&quot; Arise and go , for this is not your resting place ; for the filth destroys men and greatly destroys them .
&quot; If any man has a false heart , and speaks a lie , and says , &apos; I will prophesy to you of pure and strong wine , &apos; he will be a prophet to this people .
And I will gather you together , O house of Jacob , and gather the remnant of Israel together , as the sheep of Bozrah , and as the flock of the field : for there will be great noise because of the multitude .
Those who set the way went up before them , and they broke through the gates of the city , and went out of the gates ; and their king went before them , and the Lord guided them .
I said , &quot; Listen , you princes of Jacob and the princes of the house of Israel ; do you not know justice ?
&quot; You are evil , good , and evil ; you have stripped the skins of men , and cut off the flesh from their bones .
And eat of the flesh of my people , and strip their skins , and break their bones , and break them into pieces like the flesh of a pot , and like the flesh of a pot .
&quot; In the time of calamity , they will cry to the Lord , but He will not listen to them ; and then He will cover them with the evil of their deeds .
&quot; The prophets who sent my people , when their teeth were chewed , cried out , saying , &apos; Peace ! &apos; Whoever does not give them food , they prepare to attack him , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; You will be confronted with darkness , so that you will not see miracles , and with darkness , so that you will not be able to prophesy . The sun will fall on you , and the day will become darkness .
They will be ashamed of their sight , and the prophets will be ashamed , and they will be filled with their lips , because God has not listened to them
&quot; And I , through the Spirit of the Lord , with power and righteousness , can declare to Jacob his transgressions , and to Israel his sins
&quot; Listen to me , O prince of the house of Jacob , O prince of the house of Israel , for you despise justice , and forsake integrity in all things .
He built Zion with the blood of men , and Jerusalem with iniquity .
&quot; The chief judges judge for bribes , and the priests teach for wages , and the prophet for silver and fortunes ; but they rely on the Lord , saying , &apos; Isn &apos;t the Lord among us , and the evil will not come upon us ?
Therefore for your sake Zion shall be sown as a field , and Jerusalem as a pile , and the mountains of this house as the heights of the forests
