&quot; But I will leave among you the poor and the needy , and they will put their trust in the name of my Lord .
&quot; The remnant of Israel will not sin , nor speak lies , nor have a tongue of deceit in their mouths ; and they will eat and drink and lie down , and no one will be afraid .
Sing , O people of Zion ; and rejoice , O Israel ; and rejoice , O people of Jerusalem ;
&quot; The Lord has removed your punishment from you , and has driven out your enemies ; and the Lord , the King of Israel , is among you , and you will no longer be afraid of evil
In that day , it will be said to Jerusalem , &quot; Don &apos;t be afraid , and don &apos;t be weak , O Zion .
&quot; The Lord , your God , the Lord of salvation , the Almighty , will rejoice in you , loving you in silence , and rejoicing in you
&quot; I will gather those who belong to you who are troubled for the sake of no assembly , and for your shamefulness .
Then I will punish all those who suffered you , and I will save those who lacked legs , and gather those who were driven out of you ; and I will make the reproached all over the earth to be praised and glorified .
&quot; In that day I will bring you in , and gather you together ; and when I bring back your captives , I will make you a name and a praise among the people of the earth , &quot; says the Lord .
And it came to pass in the second year , on the first day of June , in the second year of king Darius , that the word of the LORD came to Jehoshaphat the son of Zeruiah , governor of Judah , and to Joshua the son of Jehoshaphat , high priest , by the hand of the prophet Haggai
Thus says the Lord of hosts , &quot; The time has not come for the building of the house of the Lord , &quot; says this people
Then came the word of the LORD to the prophet Haggai , saying ,
&quot; Is this palace still desolate , and you yourselves dwell in lofty houses ?
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Beware of your deeds ,
Thou shalt not eat , nor be satisfied , nor drink , nor be satisfied , nor be clothed , nor be warmed ; and whosoever hath earned a wage , he shall put it in a leaky bag .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Beware of your deeds ,
&quot; For this cause I rejoice and am glorified , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that you will go up into the mountains , and take up wood , and build this house
&quot; Behold , you have hoped much , and received little ; and when you received the house , I blew it away ; for my house is desolate , and all of you look to your houses ; &quot; says the Lord of hosts .
Therefore for your sake the heavens shall not rain , neither shall the earth yield fruit .
&quot; And I have commanded that drought should come upon the earth , and upon the mountains , and upon the hills , and upon the earth , and upon the fruit of the earth , and upon the people , and upon the cattle , and upon all the labour of the hands of men
And it came to pass at that time , that Zerubbabel the son of Zareth , and Joshua the son of Jehoshaphat , the high priest , and the rest of the people , listened to the word of the LORD their God , and to the word of the prophet Haggai , which the LORD their God had sent , and the people feared the LORD .
Then Hachi the messenger of the Lord sent to the people , saying , &quot; The Lord said , &apos; I am with you
And the LORD stirred up the hearts of Zerubbabel the son of Zeruiah the governor of Judah , and of Joshua the son of Jehoshaphat the high priest , and of the remnant of the people ; and they came to work for the LORD of hosts in the house of their God .
It was in the second year of king Darius , on the 24th of June
The word of the Lord came to the prophet Haggai on the twenty-first day of July
Speak unto Zerubbabel the son of Zeruiah the governor of Judah , and unto Joshua the son of Josua the high priest , and unto the rest of the people , saying ,
&quot; Who among you has seen the glory of this house before ? How do you see it now ? Is it not as if it were nothing in your eyes ?
And the LORD said , Thou , Zerubbabel , be strong , and Joshua the son of Jehoshaphat , chief priest , be strong ; and all the people of the land be strong , and work hard ; for I am with you , saith the LORD of hosts
&quot; This is the covenant I made with you when you came out of Egypt ; and my Spirit dwelled among you at that time , and you should not be afraid .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; I will shake the heavens and the sea and the dry land one more time
&quot; I will shake all the nations , and the treasures of all the nations will come , and I will make this house full of glory , &quot; said the Lord of hosts .
&quot; The Lord of hosts said , &quot; The silver is mine , and the gold is mine
&quot; The glory that will come after this house will be greater than the glory that was before it ; and I will give peace in this place , &quot; said the Lord of hosts .
The word of the LORD came to the prophet Haggai in the second year , on the twenty-fourth day of September ,
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Ask the priests the law
&quot; If a man wears a garment of holy flesh , and is it holy to eat bread , or soup , or wine , or oil , or any other kind of food , &quot; the priest said , &quot; It is not .
And he said , &quot; If a man touches a dead body with an unclean stain , and then touches one of these things , is it unclean ? &quot; And the priest said , &quot; It is unclean .
And he said , Thus saith the LORD ; Thus is this people , and thus is the land before me , and so is all that they do , and so is all that they offer on the altar .
&quot; Now remember that before this day there was not a stone tower in the house of the Lord on stone
On that day , a man will come to the mountains , and he will get twenty oxen , and he will get ten oxen ; and a man will come to the pool , and he will get fifty oxen , and he will get twenty oxen
&quot; I will strike you with the wind and with the dust and with the hail in all your work , and you will not return to me , &quot; says the Lord .
&quot; Remember the days before this day , from the twenty-fourth day of September , until the foundation of the house of the Lord .
&quot; Do the trees of grapes and the trees of pomegranates and pomegranates and olives bear no fruit ? From this day on , I will bless you
&quot; On the twenty-fourth day of this month the word of the Lord came to Hachijah two times , saying ,
And thou shalt say unto Zerubbabel the governor of Judah , I will shake the heavens and the earth
I will overthrow the throne of the nations , and I will destroy the power of the nations , and I will overthrow the chariots and those who sit on them , and the horses will fall , and the horsemen will fall , and everyone will be killed by the sword of his brothers .
&quot; In that day , &quot; said the Lord of hosts , &quot; I will sign you , O Zerubbabel the son of Sarath my servant , because I have chosen you , &quot; said the Lord of hosts .
In the second year , in August , the word of the LORD came to Zechariah the prophet , the son of Bile the son of Iddo , saying ,
&quot; The Lord was very angry with your fathers
Therefore say unto the children of Israel , Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; Turn unto me , and I will turn unto you ; thus saith the Lord of hosts
&quot; Do not obey your fathers , &quot; the prophets of old called them , &quot; saying , &apos; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; You shall turn away from your evil deeds , and they will not listen to me , nor obey me , &apos; &quot; says the Lord
In it are your ancestors . Will the prophets live forever ?
Will not my word and my statutes come to your ancestors , which were commanded by the prophets of my servants ? Then they turned and said , &quot; As the Lord of hosts intends to do to us according to our deeds , so He has done to us .
The word of the LORD came to Zechariah the prophet , the son of Bile the son of Edo , in the second year of Darius , in the month of Zechariah , on the twenty-fourth day of the month , saying ,
&quot; I watched at night , and saw a man riding a red horse standing in the middle of the pomegranate trees of the lowland , and behind him were a red horse , a yellow horse , and a white horse .
And I said unto the angel that spake unto me , Lord , what is this ? And he said , I will shew thee what is this
And the man that stood in the middle of the pomegranate tree said , These are the things which the Lord sent throughout all the earth
Then the riders said to the angel of the Lord , who stood in the middle of the pomegranate tree , &quot; We have come and gone in all the land , and all the land is resting
Then the angels of the Lord said , &quot; How long , O Lord of hosts , will you not have mercy on Jerusalem and the cities of Judah for seventy years ?
Then the Lord answered the angel who spoke to me with good and good words
&quot; The angel who spoke to me said to me , &apos; Tell me , &apos; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; I am for Jerusalem and for Zion in my heart a fierce fire
I am very angry with the countries of peace , for they have exaggerated my people a little , because I was angry with them before .
&quot; Therefore thus says the Lord : &apos; Now I am returning to Jerusalem , and I will have mercy , and my house will be in it again , and cords will be laid on it , &apos; says the Lord of hosts .
&quot; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; My cities will grow again , and the Lord will comfort Zion , and choose Jerusalem .
&quot; I lifted up my eyes and looked , and I saw four corners
Then I asked the angel who spoke to me , saying , What is this ? And he answered , It is the corner of Judah , and of Israel , and of Jerusalem
&quot; The Lord also showed me four craftsmen
And I said , What have they come to do ? And he said , This is the horn of the destruction of Judah , that men should not lift up their heads ; but these craftsmen that come to terrorize the nations , and to strike their horns , are the horns that lift up the destruction of the land of Judah .
Then I lifted up my eyes again , and saw a man with a rope in his hand
&quot; I said , &apos; Go there . &apos; He said to me , &apos; Go and measure Jerusalem , how wide it is and how long it is .
And it came to pass , when the angel that talked with me was gone , that another angel came to him
Then he said to him , &quot; Go and tell the boy , saying , &apos; Jerusalem will be inhabited as a country without walls , for many people and livestock
&quot; The Lord said , &quot; I will make Jerusalem a city of fire around it , and a glory in it
&quot; I have scattered you throughout the heavens , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and now you shall flee from the land of the north , &quot; says the Lord .
Flee , O Zion , which dwelleth with the Babylonians .
Then said the Lord of hosts , &quot; Behold , I am sent to punish those who plundered your nations after their glory , and those who touch you are the eyes of His eyes .
&quot; Behold , I will shake my hand against them , and they will serve as captives to their people ; and you will know that the Lord of hosts has sent me .
Sing with joy , O city of Zion ; for I am come to dwell among you , saith the Lord
&quot; In that day there will be many nations to belong to the Lord as His children , and He will dwell among you , and you will know that the Lord of hosts has sent me to you .
&quot; The Lord will restore Judah as a portion of His holy land , and He will choose Jerusalem again
&quot; Everyone who has blood will be silent in the presence of the Lord , for he is risen from the holy place
Then the angel pointed to me , and said , &quot; Joshua the high priest is standing before the angel of the Lord , and Satan is standing on his right hand , and he is in opposition to him
And the LORD said unto Satan , O Satan , the LORD hath rebuked thee of thee , the LORD that hath chosen Jerusalem : is it not a wood that is taken out of the fire
Joshua stood before the messenger in an unclean garment
And the angel commanded those who stood before him , saying , Take away his filthy garments ; and he said unto Joshua , I have delivered thee out of iniquity , and I will clothe thee with a beautiful garment
&quot; I said , &apos; Put a clean crown on his head , and they will put a clean crown on his head , and put on his beautiful garments . The angel of the Lord will stand by him .
And the angel of the Lord spake unto Joshua , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; If thou wilt walk in my ways , and keep my commandments , then thou shalt be able to keep my house , and to guard my house ; and I will send thee among them that stand .
&quot; Listen , Joshua the high priest , you and those who are sitting before you ; for they are prophets ; and I will send forth the seed of my servant David
&quot; Behold , I have seven eyes on a stone that I have set before Joshua , &quot; said the Lord of hosts , &quot; and I will carve it myself , and in one day I will blot out the iniquity of the land
&quot; In that day , &quot; said the Lord of hosts , &quot; you shall ask your neighbors to sit under vines and fruitless trees .
&quot; The angel who spoke to me awakened me again , as a man who sleeps is awakened .
Then he said to me , &quot; What have you seen ? &quot; I said , &quot; I have seen a lamp of pure gold , and there are seven lamps on it , and seven tubes for each lamp .
Next to it were two olive trees , one on the right side of the lamp , and one on the left side of the lamp
&quot; I asked the angel who spoke to me , &quot; Lord , what is this
The angel who spoke to me answered me , &quot; You do not know what this means . I said , &apos; Lord , I do not know
He said to me , &quot; This is the Lord &apos;s commandment to Rehoboam , &quot; and the Lord of hosts said , &quot; It is not by power , nor by power , but by my Spirit that you can do things .
&quot; What are you , O mountain ? You will be a plain before Zerubbabel , and he will bring forth a stone , and he will be on the top of the house , and people will cry out with a loud voice , saying , &apos; Blessed be you , and return to this house . &apos; 
Then the word of the Lord came again to me , saying ,
&quot; The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of the house , and his hands will complete the work ; and you will know that the Lord of hosts has sent me to you .
&quot; Who despises the smallness of this day ? These seven eyes are the eyes of the Lord , and they are all over the earth ; and he rejoices when he sees the hand of Zerubbabel taking the cord of tin .
Then I asked the angel , &quot; What is the meaning of the two olive trees on the left and on the right of the lampstand
&quot; I asked him twice , &quot; What do these two olive branches mean next to the two golden mouths that pour out gold oil
He said to me , &quot; Do you not know what this means ? &quot; I said , &quot; Lord , I do not know
And he said , These are the two anointed standing by the Lord of the whole world
And I lifted up my eyes again , and beheld a scroll in flight
Then he said to me , &quot; What do you see ? &quot; And I answered , &quot; I see a scroll that flies , twenty cubits long and ten cubits wide
He said to me , &quot; This is the curse of traveling all over the earth . He who steals will be destroyed by the word of the scroll , and he who swears will be destroyed by the word of the scroll .
&quot; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; I will roll this book out into the house of the thief , and into the house of the slanderer , and into the house of the slanderer who has sworn by my name , and he will be in his house forever , and he will destroy every house with its stones .
&quot; The angel who spoke to me came out and said to me , &quot; Look with your eyes and see what has come out
And I said , What is this ? And he said , It is a measure ; and he said , It is the shape of the wicked in all the earth .
( I saw a piece of round lead lifted up . ) There was a woman sitting in the counter
And the angel said , This is evil ; and he cast the woman into the ark , and cast the piece of lead into the mouth of the ark
And I lifted up my eyes , and saw two women come forth , and there was a wind in their wings , and they flew very fast , as the wings of a bird of prey : and they lifted up the scale , and set it in the midst of heaven .
&quot; I asked the angels who spoke to me , saying , &quot; Where are they going to carry the scale ?
He said to me , &quot; Go to Shenath to build a house for him ; and when the house is ready , place him in his own place .
And I lifted up my eyes again , and behold , four chariots came out of the midst of the two mountains : and the mountain was Mount Copper
The first car was fitted with a red horse . The second car was fitted with a black horse
The third carriage was clothed with white horses . The fourth carriage was clothed with spotted horses
Then I asked the angel who spoke to me , saying , &quot; Lord , what is this
And the angel answered and said unto me , These are the four winds of heaven , which came out of the Lord of all the earth
Carriages of black horses went north , followed by white horses . Horses with spots went south .
&quot; The horses came out , and they went about and around and around . &quot; The angel said , &quot; You are in charge of walking around and around , and they do the same
And he called me again , saying , Behold , he that went to the north comforted my heart in the north
And the word of the Lord came unto me , saying ,
And thou shalt take of the captives the silver and the gold of the sons of Shebai , and of the sons of Dobiah , and of the sons of Jedaiah , which came from Babylon unto the house of Josiah the son of Shebaniah , and shalt enter into his house that day
And he took the crown of gold and silver , and put it upon the head of Joshua the son of Jehoshaphat the high priest
&quot; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; Behold , the name of the seed of David will rise up in this place , and he will build the house of the Lord
&quot; He shall build the house of the Lord , and shall bear the glory , and shall sit on his throne , and shall reign ; and he shall be a priest on his throne , and make peace between the two offices .
And the crown shall be to Herod , and to Dobiah , and to Jedaiah , and to Zephaniah the son of Zephaniah , to be placed in the house of the Lord for a memorial .
And the people of the far shall come to build the house of the LORD ; and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you , and that it shall come to pass , if ye keep the word of the LORD your God
The word of the LORD came to Zechariah in the fourth year of king Darius , in the first day of the month Kiz , in the fourth month .
At that time the men of Bethlehem , having sent to Saleh , and to Rechin-melech , and with their men , pleaded for the grace of the Lord
And he asked the priests and the prophets in the house of the Lord of hosts , saying , &quot; Shall I fast in the month of May , crying and fasting for many years ?
And the word of the Lord of hosts came unto me , saying ,
&quot; You shall proclaim to the people of your land and to the priests , saying , &apos; Have you been fasting to me for seventy years in the month of May and in the month of July ?
Do you eat and drink for yourselves , or do you drink for yourselves
&quot; Do you not obey the word of the Lord , which he proclaimed by the prophets of old , when there were inhabitants in Jerusalem and in the cities around it , and when there were inhabitants in the hills of the south ?
And the word of the LORD came again to Zechariah , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord of hosts unto your fathers , Judge according to the wisdom , and each one with mercy and compassion unto his brethren
&quot; Do not oppress widows , orphans , orphans , orphans , or the poor , and do not commit murder in the heart of your brothers .
And they turn their shoulders , and they hearken not .
Therefore the Lord of hosts is wroth with a great wrath , because he has hardened his heart as a stone of gold , and has not obeyed the law , and has spoken by the Spirit of the Lord of hosts through the prophets of old .
&quot; The Lord of hosts said , &quot; I have called on them , but they have not listened ; and in the future they will call on me , but I will not listen
And I will send a wind upon all the nations which they know not , and their land shall be desolate , and no man shall pass through it ; for they have desolated the good places .
The word of the Lord of hosts came to me , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; I am hot for Zion in peace ; I am hot for him , and I am wroth with his enemies
Thus saith the Lord ; Behold , I am returning to Zion to dwell in Jerusalem , which shall be called a city of truth , and the mountain of the Lord of hosts shall be called a holy mountain
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; In the future there shall be old men and old women sitting in the streets of Jerusalem ; for they shall take the rods of their hands for an old man
The streets of the city must be filled with boys and girls playing
Thus saith the LORD of hosts ; In that day shall this be seen as a wonder in the eyes of the remnant of the people , and in my eyes as a wonder , saith the LORD of hosts
Thus saith the Lord of hosts , I will deliver my people from the east and from the west
&quot; I will bring them and make them dwell in Jerusalem , and they will be my children , and I will be their God in truth and righteousness
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; The words of the prophet , who built the house of the Lord of hosts , and laid the foundation of the Day of Resurrection , behold , they are heard in your hands , and they shall be strengthened .
&quot; In that day they shall not be paid the price of the ancients , neither shall the cattle ; neither shall the inhabitants of the land be secure because of the enemy ; for I have made all men to attack one another .
&quot; But now I will not be as before with the remnant of the people , &quot; said the Lord of hosts .
For they shall sow in peace , and the vines shall bear fruit , and the earth shall bear fruit , and the heavens shall bear sweetness ; and I will make the remnant of the people to enjoy all these blessings .
Thus will I save you , O ye Jews and house of Israel , as ye have been cursed in the nations , that they may call you blessed : fear not , but strengthen your hands .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; How will I not repent when your fathers have provoked me to anger
&quot; Behold , I have made a covenant with Jerusalem and with all Judah , so that you will not be afraid
Thus do ye : every man speaketh with his neighbour in truth , and judgeth at the gates of the city according to righteousness , and maketh peace .
&quot; No man can murder his neighbor in his heart , nor can he love to swear , for all these things I have hated , &quot; says the Lord .
The word of the Lord of hosts came to me , saying ,
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; The days of fasting in April and May , and the days of fasting in July and October , shall be a joyful day and a feast of joy for all Judah ; therefore love righteousness and peace .
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; In the future there shall come nations and inhabitants of many cities
&quot; The inhabitants of the city will come to the city and say , &apos; We are going to seek the favor of the Lord , to seek the Lord of hosts , and I am going to go
And the people of the nations and the people of the strong shall come to Jerusalem , seeking the Lord of hosts , and pleading for the grace of the Lord
Thus saith the Lord of hosts ; In those days there shall come forth ten men out of the tribes of the nations , and they shall take up the collar of a Jew , saying , We will go with you , because we have heard that God is with you
The word of the Lord shall be tested in the land of Hadrah , where the eyes of all the people and of all the tribes of Israel shall be on the Lord
and Hama nearby , and Tyre , and Sidon ; for the men of these two cities were exceeding wise .
And he built for himself a shelter , and stored up silver as dust , and set up gold as the dirt of the streets
The Lord will drive him out , He will defeat his power in the sea ; He will be burned with fire .
The sight of Assyria shall be feared , and the sight of Gaza shall be grievous ; and Ephraim shall be ashamed because of his hope , and Gaza shall have no king , and Assyria shall have no inhabitants .
&quot; The sons of men shall dwell in Ashdod , and I will destroy the pride of the Philistines .
&quot; I will remove the flesh of blood from his mouth , and the abominations in his teeth , and he will be a remnant to our God , and he will be like the elders of Judah , and the children of Ephraim like the children of Jebus
I will make camps around my house , so that the enemy will not come at will ; and the wicked will not pass by ; for I have looked at my house with my own eyes .
Rejoice greatly , O people of Zion ; and rejoice greatly , O people of Jerusalem ; behold , thy king cometh unto thee : he is righteous , and delivereth , and humble , and humble ; and he that rideth upon a donkey is the son of a donkey .
And I will cut off the chariots of Ephraim , and the horses of Jerusalem , and the bow of the battle ; and he will speak peace to all the nations ; and his hand shall be from the sea to the sea , and from the great river to the poles .
&quot; O Zion , for the blood of your covenant I have delivered out of the pits of water those who were taken captive among you
Those of you who have been imprisoned and have hope will return to safety . Today I have declared that I will multiply your blessings .
I have taken Judah for a bow , and I have taken Ephraim for a bow ; and I will stir up your children , O Zion , against the children of Sherah , that you may be like the sword of the mighty .
The Lord will appear above them , and his arrows will be like lightning , and the Lord Yahweh will blow with the south wind .
The Lord of hosts will protect them , they will swallow up their enemies , they will trample upon stones , they will shout like wine , they will be like a bowl full of blood , and like the four corners of the altar full of blood
In that day the Lord , their God , will see his people as sheep , and will save them ; for they will be as a crown of jewels , and will be exalted above his land , and will shine in his land .
How great is his mercy , how exalted is his glory ! Five valleys are full of young men , and new wine grows virgins .
&quot; When it rains in the spring , ask rain from the Lord who shines with lightning , and He will send down sweeteners for all people , and bring forth fruit and vegetables in the fields .
For that which is spoken for the house of God is vanity , and that which the prophets see is false , and that which the dreamers say is false ; and they are white and white comforters ; therefore all flee as sheep , and suffer because there is no shepherd
&quot; My anger is kindled against the shepherd , and I will punish the goats , because the Lord of all my hosts will take care of his flock , which is all Judah , and will make them stand before him like horses
The cornerstones of the house , and the nails , and the bow of war , and all that have dominion , are from Him .
They will walk like warriors in battle , trampling their enemies in the dirt of the streets ; they will fight because the Lord is with them , and the riders will be ashamed .
I will strengthen Judah , I will save the house of Joseph , I will bring them back , I will have mercy on them , and they will be like uncircumcised , because I am the Lord their God , and I will answer their prayers
The people of Ephraim shall be as a mighty man , and their hearts shall be as wine , and their children shall see and rejoice , and their hearts shall rejoice in the LORD .
&quot; I will raise up my neighbours , and gather them together ; for I have redeemed them ; and their number will increase as it did before .
&quot; While I will spread them out among the nations , they will remember Me from afar , and they and their children will live , and they will be returned .
And I will bring them again out of the land of Egypt , and gather them together out of Assyria , and will bring them to Gilead and Lebanon , where they shall not dwell
The LORD shall pass through the sea of affliction , and shall strike against the waves , and the depths of the Nile shall be dried up ; and the pride of Assyria shall be humble ; and the power of Egypt shall perish .
&quot; I will make them to rely on Me , and I will make them strong , and they will walk in My name , &quot; says the Lord .
Open thy gates , O Lebanon , and let fire devour thy cedar trees
O pine tree , mourn ; for the cedar trees have fallen ; the beautiful trees have been destroyed ; O oak tree of Bashan , mourn ; for the forests of the forests have passed away .
Behold , there is a cry of the shepherds , because their glorious fields are desolate ; and there is a roar of the lion , because the forests by the river Jordan are desolate .
Thus saith the LORD my God ; Thou shalt feed this flock of sheep , which thou shalt slay
He bought them , and slaughtered them for his own sake , and sold them , and said , &quot; The Lord is to be praised , for I am rich ; but he does not feed them , and does not have mercy on them
&quot; I will no longer have mercy on the inhabitants of the land , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; and I will deliver them into the hands of their neighbours and their kings , and they will destroy the land , and I will not save them out of their hands .
And I have shepherded the flock that shall be slaughtered , which is the most afflicted of the flock ; and I have taken two rods , one of which I have called glory , and one of which I have called union ; and I have shepherded the flock
In January , I destroyed three priests , because my heart hated them , and their heart hated me .
&quot; I said , &apos; I do not feed you . Those who die will die by him . Those who die will die by him . The rest will feed one another .
&quot; I have broken the rod of glory , to show that I have rejected my covenant with the people .
&quot; They will know that the word of the Lord has been spoken to those who look on the sheep of my affliction .
And I said unto them , If ye will be good to me , give me the price ; or else it shall be no more : and they gave me thirty dollars as my price
And the LORD commanded me , saying , &quot; Send to the sons of Hinnom the good estimation of all men ; and I will cast the thirty dollars into the house of the LORD to the sons of Hinnom .
&quot; And I have broken the rod that is called the tongs of UNOS , to show that I have forsaken the friendship between Judah and the brethren of Israel
Then the Lord said to me , &quot; Take again the instruments of the foolish
For I will raise up in this land a shepherd , who will not look upon the dead , nor seek the dispersed , nor heal the wounded , nor feed the strong , but will eat the flesh of the fat sheep , and will tear his feet
Woe to the shepherd who is useless , who abandons his flock ! The sword will come upon his arms and his right eye , and his arms will be dried up , and his right eye will be dim and blind .
&quot; This is the word of the Lord concerning Israel , &quot; says the Lord who lays up the heavens , and builds the foundations , and creates the spirit of man .
&quot; When Jerusalem is besieged , I will make the people of the four besieged nations a cup to be drunken , and this is also concerning Judah .
&quot; In that day , I will make Jerusalem a heavy stone against all the people who gather against it , and whoever lifts it up will be severely wounded .
&quot; In that day , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; I will shake all the horses , and I will make the riders mad , and I will look upon all Judah , and I will make all the horses of the nations blind .
&quot; The elders of Judah will say in their hearts , &apos; The inhabitants of Jerusalem will be able to rely on the Lord of hosts , their God ,
&quot; In that day , I will make the chiefs of Judah as a pot of fire in a wood , and as a fire in a bundle of wheat , and they will burn the people of the four countries round about them , and the people of Jerusalem will dwell in their place , which is Jerusalem .
The Lord will first save the tents of Judah from the glory of the house of David , and from the glory of the inhabitants of Jerusalem , above Judah
In that day the Lord will protect the inhabitants of Jerusalem , and the weak among them will be like David , and the house of David will be like God , as the messenger of the Lord before them .
&quot; In that day I will surely destroy the people of the nations of Jerusalem ,
And I will pour out the Spirit of grace upon the house of David and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem , and they will look upon me , as they were bound , and they will mourn for me as for the dead , and they will mourn for me as for the old .
In that day there shall be great sorrow in Jerusalem , as at the gate of Hadad in the plain of Midian .
Every house in the land will mourn ; the house of David , the one man , the one woman ; the one house , the one man , the one woman ;
The house of Levi , the one for men , the one for women . Show each house , the one for men , the one for women
The rest of the households , men alone , women alone
&quot; In that day He will open a spring for the house of David and for the inhabitants of Jerusalem , to wash away sin and filth .
&quot; In that day , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; I will remove the names of idols from the earth , and they will no longer be remembered , and I will no longer have false prophets and filthy spirits in the land .
&quot; If another man prophesies , his parents will say to him , &apos; You will not live , for you prophesy falsely in the name of the Lord . His parents will pierce him when he prophesies .
&quot; In that day the prophet who prophesies will be ashamed of the vision that he speaks , and will no longer be clothed in caps to deceive .
&quot; He will say , &apos; I am not a prophet ; I am a farmer ; I have been a slave from my youth
And one shall say unto him , What wound is in the middle of thy arms ? And he shall answer , This is the wound which I have suffered in my kinsmen &apos;s house
&quot; The Lord of hosts says , &apos; Arise , O sword , and strike my shepherd and my companions , and strike the shepherd , and the sheep will be scattered ; and I will put my back on the little ones .
&quot; Two-thirds of the people of the whole land will be cut off and die , and a third will remain , &quot; says the Lord
&quot; I will burn the third of them with fire , like silver , like gold ; and they will ask for my name , and I will answer them ; and I will say , &apos; This is my people ; &apos; and they will say , &apos; The Lord is my God
&quot; The days of the Lord are near , and your wealth will be plundered and scattered among you .
For I will gather all the nations together to fight against Jerusalem , and the city shall be taken , and the houses taken , and the women defiled , and half the people of the city taken away , and the remnant of the people in the city shall not be cut off .
Then the Lord will go out and fight with the nations as he had fought before
On that day his foot shall stand on the Mount of Olives , which is toward the east of Jerusalem ; and it shall cleave from the midst of it from east to west , and become a great valley , and half of it shall be moved northward , and half southward .
&quot; You will flee from the valley of my mountains , for the valley will reach to Asa , and you will flee like the people of Uzziah king of Judah from the great earthquake ; and the Lord , my God , will come , and all the saints will be with him .
On that day there will be no light , and three lights will recede .
&quot; In that day the Lord will know that there will be neither day nor night , and there will be no light until the evening .
&quot; In that day , there will come out of Jerusalem living waters , half to the east and half to the west , and so will be in winter and summer .
The Lord will be king over all the earth , and in that day the Lord will be unique , and His name will be unique .
And all the land from Capernaum even to the gate of the south of Jerusalem , which shall be turned into Aram , and Jerusalem shall remain high , from the gate of Benjamin even to the first gate , and to the corner gate , and from the house of Canaan even to the king &apos;s winepress ;
And in it shall dwell mankind , and there shall be no curse ; and the inhabitants of Jerusalem shall dwell safely .
Thus shall the Lord do to the nations that fight against Jerusalem with a plague : when they stand on their feet , the flesh shall be consumed , and the eyes shall be dry in their orbits , and the mouth shall be swallowed up .
&quot; In that day the Lord will cause great distress to them , and they will hold each other and shake their hands .
And Judah shall fight in Jerusalem ; and the riches of the nations that were round about , many silver and gold garments , shall be gathered together
&quot; The punishment that shall come upon horses , oxen , camels , donkeys , and all the cattle of the camp is like that punishment
&quot; All the remnant of the people who came to attack the land of Jerusalem shall year by year worship the Lord of the great king and all his armies , and keep the Tent of Meeting
&quot; Whoever does not go up to Jerusalem to worship the Lord of the kings and armies of the earth will not have rain on their land
&quot; If the Egyptians do not come up , neither will the rain fall on their land ; and the Lord will strike them with this plague against all the nations that do not come up to keep the Tent of Meeting .
That is the punishment of Egypt , and the punishment of the nations that do not keep the sabbath .
&quot; On that day the bells of the horses will bear the words of holiness to the Lord ; and the bowl in the house of the Lord will be like the bowl before the altar .
And all the pots of Jerusalem and Judah shall be holy unto the Lord of hosts ; and all that offer sacrifices shall come and take the pot , and boil the flesh therein ; and there shall be no Canaanite in the house of the Lord of hosts that day .
The word of the LORD that was spoken unto Israel through Malachi
The Lord said , &quot; I loved you , but you said , &apos; Why do you love us ? &apos; &quot; The Lord said , &quot; Isn &apos;t Esau Jacob &apos;s brother , but I love Jacob
Evil has desolated his mountains , and has given his land to the wild dogs of the wilderness .
&quot; The people of Edom said , &apos; We are now in the place of destruction , but we will rebuild the place of destruction . Thus says the Lord of hosts : &apos; Let them build , and I will destroy ; and they will call their land a place of sin , and their people a people of anger , and the Lord will be angry for ever .
&quot; You will see with your own eyes and say , &apos; May the Lord be glorified beyond the borders of Israel
&quot; The Lord of hosts , O priests who despise my name , says to you , &apos; Sons , respect your father , servants , respect your master ; wherein I am my father , and wherein I am my master , and wherein you say , &apos; Why do we despise your name ? &apos;
&quot; You will offer unclean food on my altar , and say , &apos; What have we done to defile you ? &apos; For you say , &apos; The table of the Lord is despisable .
Is it not evil that you offer the blind as an offering , and that you offer the lame and sick as an offering ? Is it not evil that you offer to your governor , that he may be pleased with you , and that he may see your face , &quot; says the Lord of hosts
&quot; Now I urge you to pray to God for mercy with us , that he may see your faces , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; because you have done this thing in your own hands . &quot;
&quot; I wish there were one among you who would shut the doors of the house , lest you burn in my altar , &quot; said the Lord of hosts , &quot; I am not pleased with you , nor will I receive any offering from your hand
&quot; From the land of the sunrise to the land of the sunset , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; My name will be glorified in the land of the nations , and in every place people will burn incense in My name , and offer clean offerings ; for My name will be glorified in the land of the nations .
&quot; But you have profaned my name , saying , &apos; The table of the Lord is filthy , and the food on it is despisable .
&quot; And you say , &apos; What are these things ? &apos; And you scoff at them with your nose , &quot; says the Lord of hosts ; &quot; and you bring the robber , and the lame , and the sick , and offer them for a sacrifice ; will I receive them out of your hand , &quot; says the Lord
Cursed is he who promises to the Lord with a handicapped sheep , for I am a great king , and my name is a dreadful name in the land of the nations , says the Lord of hosts .
&quot; This commandment is given to you , O priests ,
&quot; If you do not obey , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; and do not put your hearts on My name , I will curse you , and turn your blessings into curses ; for I have cursed you because you do not put your commandments on your hearts .
And I will rebuke your seeds , and I will blot out the dung that you have sacrificed on your faces , and you shall be taken away with the dung .
&quot; You will know that I have sent this commandment to you , that my covenant with the Levites may be established forever , &quot; says the Lord of hosts .
I have made with him a covenant of life and peace , and I will give them to him , that he may have a fearful heart , and that he may fear Me , and fear My name .
The law of truth is in his mouth , and there is no unrighteousness in his mouth ; and he walks with me in peace and righteousness , and many turn away from their iniquity .
For knowledge is in the mouth of the priest , and men seek the law in his mouth ; for he is the Lord of hosts .
&quot; But you have strayed from the right way , and many have fallen by the law ; and you have forsaken My covenant with Levi , &quot; says the Lord of hosts .
&quot; Therefore I have made you despised and despised by all , because you have not kept My ways , and have turned away from the law
Have we not all been fathers , or have we not all been created by God ? How have we all deceived our brethren , and turned away from the covenant of God with our fathers ?
Judah dealt treacherously , and did abominations in Israel and in Jerusalem , for desecrating the holy things which the Lord delighted in , and marrying a woman of the gods of the Gentiles .
And whosoever shall do this thing , and whosoever it is that is promised , it shall be the Lord of hosts , and the Lord shall cut him off from the tent of Jacob .
&quot; You have done another thing , so that your former wife weeps with tears , and covers the altar of the Lord , so that the Lord will no longer look at the offering , nor will he take it out of your hand .
&quot; And you say , &apos; Why ? Because the Lord is a witness between you and the wife whom you married when you were little ; and though he is your spouse and the wife of your covenant , yet you deceive him
Is not God , though He has the power of the Spirit to create many , the One Who creates only one , the One Who desires to be a pious offspring ? Therefore , beware of your hearts , and let no man deceive a wife whom he has married as a child .
&quot; This is what the Lord , the God of Israel , says , &apos; I hate the evil of the wife , and the evil of the violent wife ; so keep your hearts from treachery , &apos; says the Lord of hosts .
&quot; You are annoying the Lord in your speech , and you say , &apos; What are we annoying him about ? &apos; For you say , &apos; The Lord sees the evildoers as good , and pleases them ; &apos; or , &apos; In them is the God of righteousness . &apos; 
&quot; I will send my messengers , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; to prepare the way before me ; and the Lord whom you seek will suddenly enter into His house ; and the messenger of the covenant , whom you worship , will come .
Who will stand in the day of his coming , and in the time of his manifestation ? For he is like the fire of the refiner , and like the alkali of the bleacher .
&quot; He will sit down like silver , and he will cleanse the Levites , and he will anoint them like gold and silver , and they will offer their offerings to the Lord in righteousness
Then the offerings of Judah and Jerusalem will be acceptable to the Lord , as in the days of old , as in the years of old .
&quot; I will come to you , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; and I will judge you , and I will testify to you quickly , and I will warn those who practice evil deeds , and those who commit adultery , and those who swear , and those who defraud others of their wages , and those who oppress widows and orphans , and those who deny their dwelling places , and those who do not fear Me
&quot; Because my Lord is unchanging , therefore your son Jacob shall not perish
&quot; Now , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; from the days of your fathers , you have often turned away from My statutes , and have not kept them ; and now , when you turn to Me , I turn to you ; and you say , &quot; How have we turned ? &quot;
&quot; Why do men take away the things of God , and you take away my offerings , and you say , &apos; Why do we take away your offerings ?
Curses will come upon you because all your people who go abroad have taken away My offerings
&quot; Thus says the Lord of hosts , &apos; You shall bring one tenth of the tenth of the hosts into the warehouses , to give me food for my house , and to test me whether I will open the windows of heaven for you , and bless you , and there will be no room for you .
&quot; I will rebuke the locust for you , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; because he will not allow it to destroy your inheritance ; neither will your vines of the field lose their fruit before they are ripe .
&quot; The Lord of hosts says , &apos; All the nations will call you blessed , for your land will be a joyful place
&quot; You struck me with words , &quot; said the Lord , &quot; and you said , &quot; What words have we struck you with ? &quot;
&quot; You say , &apos; God &apos;s service is eternal . What good is it to keep what God has commanded , to fast and suffer in the presence of the Lord of hosts ?
&quot; Now we call the proud to be blessed , and the wicked to be established ; and they shall seek God , but be delivered from the calamity .
Then the fearful of the Lord spoke to one another , and the Lord listened , and there was a memorial before Him , a record of those who feared the Lord and remembered His name .
&quot; In the days that I have appointed , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; they will belong to me , they will belong to me , and I will have mercy on them , as a man has mercy on his own son .
Then you shall return , and separate the good from the evil , and those who serve God and those who do not serve God .
&quot; The day is near , &quot; says the Lord of hosts , &quot; like a burning furnace ; and whoever is arrogant and wicked will be like a straw , and will be consumed on that day , and no branch will be left .
But to him who fears my name from among you , the day of righteousness will come , whose light has healing power ; and you will come out jumping like a calf in a circle .
&quot; You will trample the wicked , and they will be under your feet like dust in My appointed days , &quot; says the Lord of hosts .
Remember the law of my servant Moses , which I commanded him in Mount Horeb for all Israel
&quot; Behold , before the great and dreadful day of the Lord , I will send the prophet Elijah to you
&quot; He will turn the heart of the father to the daughters , and the heart of the daughters to the father , lest I come to curse all the earth
The genealogy of the seed of Abraham , the seed of David , and the genealogy of Jesus Christ
Abraham was born Isaac . Isaac was born Jacob . Jacob was born Judah and his brothers
And Judah begat Pharaoh and Shelah Pharaoh of his tribe , and Shelah of his tribe , and Aaron of his tribe ,
Aram , Aminada , Aminada , Nahshon , Nahshon , and Sammon
Simon was born of Laodicea , and Boaz was born of Ruth , and Hezekiah was born of Ruth .
And Jesse was born king David ; and Solomon was born of the wife of Uriah .
And Solomon begat Rehoboam , and Rehoboam begat Abijah , and Abijah begat Asa .
Yasath was born Joseph . Joseph was born Jordan . Jordan was born Uzziah .
Usia was born to Jotan . Jotan was born to Ahasuerus . Ahasuerus was born to Hesse .
The house of Hezekiah begat Manasseh , and Manasseh begat Adam , and Adam begat Josiah .
And it came to pass , when the people were brought to Babylon , that Josiah the son of Jeconiah and his brethren
After they had moved to Babylon , Zeconiah was born Sarath ; and Sarath was born Zerubbabel .
Abigail the son of Zerubbabel , Abigail the son of Elijah , Elijah the son of Ahaz ,
The son of Asaph , the son of Zadok , the son of Akin , the son of Eli
Elijah the son of Elijah , the son of Mattan , the son of Jacob ,
Jacob was the son of Joseph , the husband of Mary ; and Jesus , called Christ , was born of Mary
So there were fourteen generations from Abraham to David , and fourteen generations from David to the time of the migration to Babylon , and fourteen generations from the time of the migration to Babylon to Christ
Behold , the resurrection of Jesus Christ is recorded , when Mary , his mother , was promised to be Joseph &apos;s wife , but she was not yet married , and Mary conceived from the Holy Spirit
Joseph , his husband , was a righteous man , and he would not shame him in plain sight , but he would put him to rest in darkness .
And it came to pass in that day , when the angel of the Lord appeared to him in his dream , saying , &quot; Joseph the son of David , fear not , but take Mary your wife , for the womb which he has conceived is from the Holy Spirit
He will give birth to a son , and you shall call his name Jesus : for he will deliver his people from sin .
All these things were accomplished to test the word of the Lord through the prophet
And he said , There shall be a daughter , and she shall conceive and bear a son , and they shall call his name Emmanuel .
Then Joseph awoke , and arose , and took his wife , as the Lord &apos;s angel had commanded him ,
But he did not dwell with him until he had given birth to a son , and called him Jesus
When Jesus was born in Bethlehem , Judea , in the days of King Herod , certain doctors came to Jerusalem from the east , saying ,
&quot; There is he who was born king of the Jews ; and we have seen his stars in the east , and have come to him .
And when the king heard it , he was troubled , and all the people of Jerusalem were troubled
Then he called together the chief priests and the scribes of the people , and asked them , &quot; Where was Christ born ? &quot;
And they answered and said , In Bethlehem of Judah : for there is written a prophet
O Bethlehem of Judah , thou art not the least of all the cities of Judah ; for there shall come out of thee a king for the future , to shepherd my people Israel .
Now Herod summoned the Doctor in secret , and asked him when the star appeared
Then he sent them to Bethlehem , and said to them , &quot; Go and search for the child , and when you have found him , send a letter , and I will also come to him
And when they had heard the word of the king , they departed , and the star which they had seen in the east , when it came before them to the place of the children , stood still above them .
And when they saw the star , they rejoiced greatly
And when he entered into the house , and saw the child and his mother Mary , he bowed down to the child , and opened the treasure box , and offered him the golden frankincense , without any medicine .
For he was instructed by the Lord in his dreams not to return to Herod , but to return from another way to his place .
After they had gone , the angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in his dream , saying , &quot; Arise , take the child with his mother , and flee to Egypt , and dwell there , as I command you ; for Herod will seek the child to destroy him . &quot;
Joseph arose and went into Egypt at night with the little child and his mother
And he lived there until he died , that he might prove the word of the Lord by the prophet , saying , I have called my son out of Egypt .
And when Herod saw that he was fooled by the doctor , he was very angry , and sent messengers , and killed all the boys of Bethlehem , and all the boys of all the land , as he had examined the doctor &apos;s son : and all the two-year-olds were slain .
This is the word of Jeremiah the prophet , saying ,
The voice of the great crying of the trumpet was heard in Ramah , when he cried to his daughters , and they could not be comforted , for they were all gone .
And it came to pass after the death of Herod , that the angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in the dream of Egypt , saying ,
Arise , take the child and his mother , and go into the land of Israel ; for those who kill the child are dead .
And Joseph arose , and brought the child and his mother into the land of Israel
And it came to pass , when he had heard that Agrippa and Herod his father had made him king of Judah , that he feared to go there , and was instructed by the Lord in a dream , and went into Galilee
And he came to a city called Nazareth , and dwelled therein ; and this was to test the words of the prophet , saying , He will call it the Nazarene
Then came out the baptized John , and preached in the wilderness of Judah , saying ,
The kingdom of heaven is near , and you should repent
&quot; This is what the prophet Isaiah said , saying , &apos; There is a voice in the wilderness , saying , &apos; Prepare the way of the Lord , and straighten his way .
John was clothed in camels &apos; hair , and had a girdle and a belt ; and he ate locust bees .
Then went out Jerusalem , and all Judah , and all the people that were by the Jordan , to John
Recognize their sins , and be baptized in the river Jordan ;
When John saw many Pharisees and Sadducees coming to be baptized , he said to them , &quot; What sort of vicious snake is he who will tell you to avoid the wrath of the future ? &quot;
&quot; You shall bring forth fruit that is worthy of repentance .
&quot; Do not say in your hearts , &apos; There is Abraham for us ; &apos; but I tell you , &apos; God will raise up sons from these stones for Abraham
Now the axe has been laid on the root of the tree ; and every tree that does not bear fruit shall be cut down , and cast into the fire .
&quot; I am the water for you to wash , and for you to repent ; but it is not worthy of me to wear shoes for him , for he is greater in power than I am in the days to come , and he will wash you with the Holy Spirit and with fire .
In his hand is a bucket to cleanse his field , and he has gathered the wheat into the barn , and he has burned the branch with an inextinguishable fire .
Now Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan , and saw John to be baptized
John wanted to stop him , saying , &quot; Will you come back to me when I am washed by you ? &quot;
Jesus answered and said to him , &quot; You will promise me for a while , because we are righteous in all things . &quot; John promised him
When Jesus was baptized , he came up out of the water , and the heavens opened for him , and he saw the Spirit of God as if a dove had descended and fallen on him
&quot; There is a voice from heaven saying , &apos; This is my beloved Son , whom I rejoice in
At that time , Jesus was taken by the Holy Spirit into the wilderness , being tested by the devil
He fasted forty days and forty nights , and afterwards became hungry
Then came the examiner and said to him , &quot; If you are the son of God , you can command these stones to be food
Jesus answered , &quot; It is written , &apos; Man is alive , not by food alone , but by all that is spoken in the mouth of God .
Then the devil brought him into the holy city , and commanded him to stand on the top of the temple ,
And he said unto him , If thou art the son of God , thou shalt go down : for it is written in the scripture , The messengers whom He hath sent unto thee shall trust in thee with their hands , lest thy feet touch a stone .
And Jesus said unto him , And it is written again , Thou shalt not test the Lord thy God .
Then the devil took him up to the highest mountain , and showed him all the kingdoms of the world and the glory of all the kingdoms
And he said unto him , If thou wilt submit unto me , I will give thee all this
Jesus said , &quot; Satan , go away , &quot; for it is written in the Scriptures , &quot; Be obedient to the Lord your God .
Then the devil departed from Jesus , and an angel came to seek him
When Jesus heard that John had been put in prison , he returned to Galilee
And he departed from Nazareth , and went to Capernaum , and dwelled there on the side of the sea , on the border of Zebulun and Naphtali .
This is the word of Isaiah the prophet to testify
And he said , The land of Zabron , the land of Naphtali , the way of the coast , the land of Galilee of the Gentiles , beyond the Jordan ;
The people who sat in the darkness saw the great light , and the people who sat in the shadow of death , and the light was found to shine upon them .
From that time onward Jesus preached , saying , &quot; The kingdom of heaven is near , and you should repent
And as he passed by the sea of Galilee , he saw two brethren , Simon , whom he called Peter , and Andrew his brother , casting nets in the sea ; and they were fishermen .
Jesus said to them , &quot; Follow me , and I will make you receive men as you receive fish
They immediately gave up the net and followed him
Going from there , he saw two brothers , Jacob the son of Zebedee , and John his brother , and Zebedee their father , who were on the ship to make nets . Jesus greeted them
Immediately they abandoned the ship , left their father , and followed Jesus
Jesus went through Galilee , teaching in the synagogues , preaching the gospel of the kingdom of heaven , and healing the sicknesses of the people
And his fame spread throughout Syria , and there they brought all the diseases , all the diseases , all the pains , and those who were possessed by demons , and those who had epilepsy , and those who were paralyzed , and Jesus healed them
Now there are many following him from Galilee , and from low Galilee , and from Jerusalem , and from Judah , and from beyond the Jordan
And when Jesus saw the multitude , he went up into the mountain and sat down , and the disciples came with him
He opened his mouth and taught them what to say
Blessed are the wicked : for the kingdom of heaven is theirs
Blessed are the mourners , for they shall be comforted
Blessed are the gentle : for they shall bear the earth .
Blessed are those who are hungry for righteousness , for they shall be filled
Blessed are the merciful , for they shall have mercy
Blessed are the righteous , for they shall see God
Blessed are the peaceable : for they shall be called the sons of God .
Blessed are the oppressed for righteousness : for the kingdom of heaven is theirs
Blessed are you if a man reproaches you because of me , and compels you , and fabricates evil words against you ,
Rejoice , for your reward in heaven is great , and so the prophets before you have oppressed them .
You are salt in the world . If salt loses its taste , how can you make it salty again ? Then it will be useless , and it will not be cast out , and it will be trampled upon .
&quot; You are the light of the world . A city is built on the mountains and cannot be hidden .
A man lights a house , not under a fountain , but on a lampstand .
And your light shall shine before men , that they may see your good deeds , and shall give glory to your Father in heaven .
Don &apos;t think that I am coming to abolish the law and the prophets ; I am not coming to abolish them , but to accomplish them
Verily I say unto you , that all things are vanished in the heavens and in the earth ; neither can a picture of the law be vanished , nor can it be perfected .
Whoever therefore abolishes the least of these commandments and teaches them to do so shall be called the least in the kingdom of heaven ; but whoever obeys them and teaches them to do so shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven .
&quot; I have told you that your righteousness will not enter the kingdom of heaven unless it is greater than that of the scribes and Pharisees .
You have heard the words of the ancients , saying , &quot; You cannot kill , &quot; and saying , &quot; Whoever kills shall surely be tried . &quot;
&quot; But I tell you , that whoever is angry with his brothers will surely be judged ; that whoever scolds his brothers will surely be judged by the council ; that whoever scolds his brothers will surely be judged by the LORD , and that whoever scolds his brothers will surely be judged by the fire of hell .
&quot; So when you offer your offerings on the altar , remember your brothers &apos; resentment against you .
&quot; Then leave the gift in front of the altar , and go with your brothers and goodness , and present it
&quot; Behold , you are on your way , and you are with your enemy ; so shout out to him ; for he will send you to the judge , and the judge to the governor ; and you will be put in prison .
Verily I say unto thee , If there be any money that is not repaid , thou shalt not be able to come out of it
You have heard that it is said , &apos; You must not commit adultery .
&quot; But I tell you that he who sees a woman has committed adultery with her in his heart , and he who sees a woman has committed adultery with her
&quot; If your right eye causes you to fall , pluck it out and throw it away ; rather than lose one of the hundred bodies , let not your whole body be thrown into hell .
If your right hand should cause you to fall , cut it down and cast it away ; and it is better to lose one of the hundred bodies than to go into hell with all your bodies .
&quot; And it is said , &apos; If a man leaves his wife , let him leave his book
&quot; But I tell you , whoever leaves his wife , if it is not for the sake of prostitution , he is made a prostitute ; and whoever marries the woman who has been left , he commits adultery .
You also heard the words of the ancients , saying , &quot; You shall not swear , but you shall keep your oath to the Lord .
&quot; But I tell you that no oath can be taken , nor can it be taken by the heavens , for the heavens are the seats of God
No one can swear by the land , for it is his bench ; nor can he swear by Jerusalem , for it is the capital of the great ruler
&quot; You shall not swear by your head , for you cannot turn a hair from black to white
&quot; If you say yes , you say yes ; if you say no , you say no ; and if you say more , it is from the wicked .
You have heard it said , &apos; Eye for eye , and teeth for teeth .
&quot; But I tell you that you shall not be opposed to the wicked . Someone strikes your right face , and turns your left face to him .
&quot; There is a man who wants to tell you that he will take your inner garments , and his outer garments
Someone forces you to walk a mile , and you walk two miles with him
And whosoever asketh of thee , give him ; and whosoever borroweth from thee , he cannot be denied .
You have heard it said , &apos; Love your neighbor and hate your enemy .
&quot; But I tell you to love your enemies , and to pray for the oppressors
&quot; So you will be the sons of your Father in heaven ; for he has called the sun to look after the good and the evil , and has rained on the righteous and on the unrighteous .
If you love only the one who loves you , what reward is there ? Is it not the taxpayer who does it ?
&quot; What advantage do you have over men , if you ask your brethren to be comforted ? Is it not so among the Gentiles ?
So you shall be perfect , just as your heavenly Father is .
Be careful , lest you do good in the sight of men , and make them see ; lest you receive the reward of your Father in heaven .
&quot; Therefore , when you give , do not make a proclamation before you , as the hypocrite did in the synagogues and in the streets , seeking to gain the glory of men ; for I tell you , they have received their reward .
&quot; When you give , do not let the left hand know what the right hand does .
&quot; Your father will surely answer you in the dark , when he sees what you give in the dark .
&quot; When you pray , do not be like the hypocrite who loves to stand in the synagogue and pray at the crossroads of the Ten Commandments in order to be seen . I tell you , they have received their reward .
&quot; When you pray , enter your inner chamber , and shut the door , and pray to your father in the darkness , and your father will answer you in the darkness .
&quot; You do not pray , and do not repeat your words as a foreigner , for they think that more will be heard .
&quot; You shall not do them any favour , for your father knew that you had no prayer beforehand .
&quot; Therefore pray , and say , &apos; Let your name be holy , O our Father in heaven ,
May your kingdom come , and your will be done on the earth , as it is done in heaven
Give to us today our daily food ,
Forgive us our debts , as we have forgiven the debts of men .
&quot; Do not let us be tempted , save us from evil , for the kingdom , the dominion , and the glory are all yours for ever and ever , Amen . &quot;
Forgive your sins , and your heavenly Father will forgive your sins .
&quot; You will not forgive your sins ; neither will your Father forgive your sins .
When you fast , do not be like the hypocrites who pretend to be righteous with sorrow on their faces ; for they make their faces difficult to see , and deliberately make people see that they are fasting . I tell you , they have received their reward .
When you fast , wash your face with a comb
&quot; Do not let anyone see your fasting , but let your father in secret see it . Your father sees it in secret , and he will answer you .
&quot; Do not store your treasures in the earth ; there are worms in the earth that bite you , and rust you ; and there are thieves that dig holes to steal .
As long as there is treasure in heaven , there is no worm to bite , no rust to break , no thief to dig a hole to steal
For there is your treasure , and there is your heart .
The eyes are the light of the body . If your eyes shine , the whole body shines .
If your eyes fade , your whole body is dark ; and if the light in your head be dark , how great is that darkness ?
A man cannot serve two lords , neither evil nor love , nor heavy nor light ; neither can you serve God nor marmon .
&quot; Therefore I say to you , &apos; Do not worry about life , what to eat , what to drink , and what to wear ; is life better than food , or is the body better than clothing ?
&quot; You see the bird of that day , which neither grows nor harvests nor stores in the barn ; your heavenly Father lives and feeds him ; how much more are you than the bird of that day !
&quot; How can one of you increase his life by a moment , or by an elbow ?
&quot; Why should you worry about your garments ? How long will the lilies grow in the wilderness ? They will not labour , nor spin yarns .
&quot; However , I tell you , in the days of Solomon &apos;s great glory , what is less than this flower that he wears ?
&quot; O men of your little letter , the grass of the field is still today , and tomorrow it will be cast into the furnace ; and God has given him such adornment . What about you ?
&quot; Therefore do not worry , saying , &apos; What do you eat , what do you drink , what do you wear ?
&quot; This is what the foreigners ask of you ; and your Father knows all that you need .
&quot; You shall first seek His kingdom and His righteousness and add them to you .
Don &apos;t worry about tomorrow , for tomorrow has its own worries . One day &apos;s hardship is one day &apos;s hardship .
&quot; Do not judge men , lest you be judged
For as ye judge men , so shall ye be judged ; and as ye measure men , so shall ye measure you .
&quot; Why do you see in your brothers a beam , but do not think in your own eyes a beam of wood ?
&quot; How can you say to your brothers , &apos; Let me remove the bark from your eyes
&quot; You hypocrite , you good man , take away the beams in your eyes , and then you will be able to see clearly , and take away the beams in your brothers &apos; eyes .
&quot; Do not give your holy things to your dogs , nor cast your pearls before the pigs ; for he will trample them and turn to bite you .
&quot; When you pray , He will give you ; when you seek , He will find you ; when you knock , He will open the door for you .
For he that prayeth shall receive it ; and he that seeketh shall find it ; and he that knocketh shall open the door unto him .
&quot; Who among you has a son who seeks bread and gives him stones ?
Ask for the fish , and give him the snake
&quot; You are not good , but you know that you give good things to your children . Why do you not give good things to the Father in heaven who asks of you ?
&quot; Therefore whatever you will do , you will do as you will , for this is the law and the wisdom of the prophet .
&quot; You shall enter into narrow gates ; for the gates are wide , and the paths great , and there are many to enter for the cause of destruction .
The gate is narrow , and the way is small , and few are those who seek it .
&quot; Beware of false prophets . They come to you in sheep &apos;s clothing , and in them are violent wolves .
They will be recognized by their fruit . Can a thorn pick up grapes , or a resin without flowers ?
Thus every good tree bears good fruit , but the bad tree bears bad fruit .
A good tree cannot bear a bad fruit , and a bad tree cannot bear a good fruit
&quot; Every tree that does not bear fruit will be cut down and thrown into the fire .
Therefore by their fruit they shall be recognized .
&quot; Whoever calls on my Lord , the Lord , will not enter the kingdom of heaven ; but he who obeys the will of my Father in heaven will enter it .
Many will say to me on that day , &quot; Lord , Lord , have we not preached in Your name , deceived in Your name , done many works in Your name ?
Then I told them plainly , saying , &quot; I never know you , you wicked people ; leave me
&quot; Therefore whoever hears me shall go forth , and cover the house with a rock like a wise man
When the rain and the water and the wind blow against the house , the house never collapses , for the foundation is on a rock
&quot; He who hears me will not go astray , but he who is ignorant will cover his house with sand .
It rained , the water poured , the wind blew , and hit the house , and the house collapsed , and it collapsed greatly
And when Jesus had finished these words , all were astonished at his lesson
For he taught them as a man of authority , and not as a scribe among them .
Jesus went down the mountain , and many followed him
A great madman came to him and said , &quot; If the Lord wills , He will purify me
Then Jesus stretched out his hand and touched him , and said , &quot; I will ; you are clean , &quot; and immediately his great madness was cleansed .
And Jesus said unto him , Thou shalt not tell any man , but go and examine the body to the priest , and offer the gift which Moses commanded , and testify unto all the people
Then Jesus entered into the land of Capernaum , and a hundred men came in and asked him
&quot; My servant is paralyzed , and lies at home in great pain .
Jesus said , &quot; I am going to heal him
Then answered the centurion , &quot; Lord , I am not willing to let you go to me ; but if you speak a word , my servant will be well
&quot; Because I am under the authority of men , and there are soldiers under me . Say to him , Go , and he will go . Say to him , Come , and he will come . My servant said , &apos; You do this , and he will do it
And when Jesus heard it , he wondered , and said unto those who followed him , Verily I say unto you , I have not met such a great faith in Israel
&quot; I also tell you that from the east and from the west many will come and sit in the kingdom of heaven with Abraham , Isaac , Jacob ,
Only the children of their land are driven out into the darkness , where they must mourn and tear .
Then Jesus said to the centurion , &quot; Go back , and in your faith you will be perfected . &quot; Then his servant was well
When Jesus came to Peter &apos;s house , he saw Peter &apos;s mother-in-law lying sick of the fever
And Jesus touched his hand , and the heat departed , and he arose , and ministered unto Jesus
And it came to pass in the evening , that a multitude of demons came before Jesus , and he cast out all the demons in one word , and healed all the sick .
This is to test the words of Isaiah the prophet , saying , &quot; He will replace our weaknesses , and he will take care of our sicknesses .
When Jesus saw that many people were around him , he commanded them to pass over to the other side
And a scribe came and said unto him , Husband , wheresoever thou goest , I will follow thee
Jesus said , &quot; The fox has a hole , and the bird of the sky has a nest , but the son of man has no place for a pillow
Then another disciple said to Jesus , &quot; Lord , allow me first to go back and bury my father
Jesus said , &quot; Let the dead bury their dead , and follow me
And Jesus went up into the ship , and the disciples followed him
Suddenly there was a storm in the sea , and even the ship was covered by the waves , and Jesus was asleep
Then the disciples woke him up , and said , &quot; Lord , save us , and we shall perish
Jesus said , &quot; Why are you , little believers , so timid ? &quot; Then he arose and rebuked the wind and the sea , and the wind and the sea were greatly calm .
And all the people said , What man is he ? and the wind and the sea heard him
And when Jesus had passed over there , and had come to the place of the Canaanites , two men of the devils came out of the tomb to meet him , exceedingly violent , and no man could pass through the way .
And they cried out , saying , Son of God , what have we to do with thee ? and when the time is not come , come thou here to suffer us ?
Far from them , there was a large group of pigs eating
Then the devil begged Jesus , saying , &quot; If you want to drive us out , send us into the flock of pigs
Jesus said , &quot; Go , &quot; and the devil came out and entered into the pigs ; and all of them hurried down the cliff and drowned in the sea .
Then the pig-bearer fled into the city , and told all these things , and all that was encountered by those who were possessed by the devil .
And all the people of the city came out to meet him , and when they had seen him , they besought him that he should leave their borders
Then Jesus took the ship , and passed over the sea , and came into his own city
Then a man took a paraplegic with a bed , and came to Jesus . When Jesus saw their confidence , he said to him , &quot; Peace be upon you , little child , your sins have been forgiven you .
Some of the scribes said in their hearts , &quot; This man has spoken a blasphemy
Jesus , knowing their hearts , said , &quot; Why do you have evil thoughts in your hearts ?
Or say , &quot; Your sins have been forgiven ; &quot; or , &quot; Arise and walk ; &quot; and that is easy .
&quot; But when you know that the Son of man has power to forgive sins on the earth , say to the paralyzed , &apos; Arise , take your bed home ,
Then the man arose and went home
And when they saw it , they were astonished , and glorified God , because he had given such power to man
And when Jesus went from there , he saw a man named Matt sitting at the gate , and said unto him , Follow me ; and he arose , and followed Jesus
When Jesus sat in the house , many tax collectors and sinners sat with him and his disciples
When the Pharisees saw it , they said to the disciples of Jesus , &quot; Why do your masters eat with the tax collectors and sinners ?
When Jesus heard it , he said , &quot; A healthy man does not need a doctor , but a sick man .
For it is written , &quot; I love mercy , but I do not love sacrifice , &quot; which means , &quot; Take heed , and I am not a caller , but a sinner
Then the disciples of John came to Jesus and said , &quot; Why do we and the Pharisees fast often , and your disciples do not ?
Jesus said to them , &quot; How can the bridegroom and his companions mourn when they are with them ? But the days will come when the bridegroom will leave them , and they will fast
No man puts a new cloth on an old cloth ; for the cloth that is put on is greater than the cloth that is broken .
No man puts a new wine in an old sack ; then the sack breaks , the wine leaks out , and the sack is broken ; but put a new wine in a new sack , and both are preserved .
When Jesus had spoken these words , a ruler of the synagogue came and said to him , &quot; My daughter has just died . Please put your hand on her , and she will live
Then Jesus arose and followed him , and the disciples followed him
And a woman came behind Jesus , having had a bleeding wound for twelve years , and touched his garments .
For he said in his heart , &quot; I will heal myself only by touching his garments
Then Jesus turned and looked at him , and said , &quot; Daughter , rest assured , Your faith has saved you , and from that time on the woman has been healed
And when Jesus came to the house of the synagogue , he saw that there was a lot of shouting and many people shouting
Then said they , &quot; Go away ; for the girl is not dead , but asleep ; and they laugh at him
And when they had been driven out , Jesus entered in , and took her hand , and she rose up
Then the wind spread through the place
Then Jesus went forward from there , and two blind men followed him , and cried out , saying , &quot; O children of David , be merciful to us
Jesus entered the house , and the blind man came to him . He said , &quot; Do you believe that I can do this ? &quot; They said , &quot; Lord , we believe
Then Jesus touched their eyes and said , &quot; Let your letter be fulfilled for you
And their eyes were opened , and Jesus commanded them , saying , Be careful , lest any man know
And they went out , and spread his fame throughout the land
When they went out , a dumb man with a demon was brought before Jesus .
Then the devil was driven out , and the dumb man spoke , and all the people cried out , saying , &quot; This has never happened in Israel
But the Pharisees said , &quot; He is the king of the devil who chases the devil
Jesus went through cities and towns , teaching in the synagogues , preaching the gospel of the kingdom of heaven , and healing all sorts of diseases
And when he saw many , he pitied them : for they were cast out as sheep without shepherds .
Then he said to his disciples , &quot; More is to be harvested and fewer are to be employed
Therefore be ye the Lord of the crops , and send out the workers , and receive his crops .
Jesus called the twelve disciples and gave them power to cast out the devils and to heal all sorts of diseases
And the names of the twelve were , Simon the first , Peter , and Andrew his brother , Jacob the son of Zebedee , and John the brother of Jacob ,
Philip , and Bardorah , and Dormah , and Matt the tax collector , and Jacob the son of Alphaeus , and Datah ,
Simon of Zechariah , and Judas of Galilee , who sold Jesus
Then Jesus sent the twelve , and said to them , &quot; You shall not go in the way of the Gentiles , nor enter the city of the Samaritans
Rather go to the lost sheep of the house of Israel
&quot; The kingdom of heaven is near , &quot; he said .
Heals the sick , revives the dead , cleanses the mad , drives out the demons ; and you , white and white , must come , and you , white and white , must go .
Don &apos;t carry silver and gold and copper money in your waistbag .
&quot; Do not take your pockets on the way , nor two coats , nor shoes , nor crutches ; for it is right for the workers to eat
&quot; Whenever you enter a city or a village , and ask who is good therein , you shall live in his house , and live straight until you leave .
Go into his house , and ask for his peace .
&quot; If the house is worthy of peace , the peace you seek will come to it ; and if it is not worthy , the peace you seek will remain with you .
&quot; Whoever does not receive you , or listen to what you say , stamps the dust on your feet when you leave the house or the city
Verily I say unto you , Is it easier for Sodom and Moor to suffer in the days of judgment than for that city ?
&quot; I have sent you as sheep into wolves , so that you may be as serpents , and as doves as doves .
&quot; Beware of men , for they will deliver you into the synagogue , and will whip you in the synagogue .
&quot; And you shall be brought before the kings for my sake , to testify against them and against the Gentiles
When you are given , do not think about what you will say or what you will say . Then you will be given what you will say .
For it is not your own word , but the Spirit of your Father that speaketh in your heads
&quot; Brothers shall send their brothers , and fathers their sons to the land of death ; and children shall be enemies of their parents , and slay them .
&quot; And you will be hated for My name , but those who endure to the end will surely be saved
&quot; Some people who oppressed you in this city fled to that city , and I tell you , the cities of Israel have not yet been visited , and the children of men have come .
The student cannot be above the master , and the servant cannot be above the master
As a student and a teacher , and as a servant and a master , so shall it be ; and they shall call the master of the house Beseb , and his family.Beseb is the name of the king of demons
Therefore fear them not , for there is nothing that is concealed that is not revealed , and nothing that is hidden that is not known .
&quot; What I have told you in the dark , you shall speak out in the clear ; and what you have heard in your ears , you shall proclaim in the house .
He who kills the body cannot kill the soul , nor fears them ; but he who destroys both the body and the soul in hell will be destroyed .
&quot; Are not two sparrows sold for a penny of silver ? If your father refuses , neither will one fall on the earth .
It is your hair , too , that has been counted
So do not be afraid . You are more valuable than many sparrows
&quot; Whoever confesses me before men , I will confess him before my Father in heaven .
&quot; Whoever does not recognize me in the sight of men , I will not recognize him in the sight of my Father in heaven
&quot; Do not think that I am coming to call the earth peaceful ; I am coming not to call the earth peaceful , but to cause the sword to move on the earth
&quot; For I am come to make men separate from their fathers , and to make women separate from their mothers , and to make their wives separate from their mothers .
The enemy of man is the man of his own house .
Love parents more than love me , not to be my disciples ; Love children more than love me , not to be my disciples
&quot; He who does not follow me on his cross is not worthy to be my disciple .
Whosoever shall have life shall lose it ; and whosoever shall have life for me shall have it .
&quot; The man who receives you receives me , and the man who sent me receives me
For he that receiveth the prophet in the name of the prophet shall receive the reward of the prophet ; for he that receiveth the righteous in the name of the righteous shall receive the reward of the righteous
&quot; Truly I tell you , whoever , in the name of his disciples , gives a cup of cold water to one of the children , he will not be able to recompense
And when Jesus had finished the twelve , he departed from there , and went into the cities to preach and to teach
When John heard what Christ had done in prison , he sent two disciples
He said to him , &quot; Is it you who will come , or are we waiting for someone else
Jesus answered , &quot; Go and tell John what you have heard and seen .
&quot; The blind see , the lame walk , the clean grow up , the deaf hear , the dead are raised up , and the poor have the gospel preached to them
Blessed is he who does not fall because of me
And when they were gone , Jesus spoke to the people concerning John , saying , &quot; What have you come out of the wilderness to see , a reed blown by the wind ?
&quot; What is it that you go out to see , a man clothed in fine linen ? The man clothed in fine linen is in the palace
&quot; Go out , and see the prophet . I tell you , he is greater than the prophet .
And it is written , &quot; I will send my messenger before thee , and I will prepare the way . &quot; That is the man
Verily I say unto you , Of all the women that are born there is none that hath risen above the baptism of John ; but the least in the kingdom is greater than he .
From the time of John &apos;s baptism to this day , the kingdom of heaven is for those who strive to enter , and for those who strive .
For he prophesied for the prophets and for the law until John
&quot; If you will receive it , this is Elijah who should come
If any have ears to hear , let them hear .
&quot; What can I do better than this generation ? It is as if a child sat on the street and greeted his companions and said ,
We whistle to you , you don &apos;t dance ; We mourn to you , you don &apos;t beat your breasts
When John came , he neither ate nor drank , and they said that he was possessed by demons
And the Son of man came , and he ate , and he drank , and they said , He is the friend of the drunkards , and of the tax collectors , and of the sinners ; but the Son of Wisdom is always Wise .
Jesus did many miracles in the cities , and at that time he reproached them , saying , &quot; The people of those cities have not repented
Woe to you , O flood of Gorah ! Woe to you , O Bethsaida ! For if the evil that was done among you were done in Tyre , they would have repented beforehand in ashes .
&quot; But I tell you , that in the days of judgment , it will be easier for Tyre to suffer than for you .
&quot; You have ascended to heaven , O Canaan , and you will fall into darkness in the future ; for the power which you have done in your midst , if it be in Sodom , will remain to this day .
&quot; But I tell you , that in the days of judgment , it is easier for Sodom to suffer than for you .
Then Jesus said , &quot; Father , Lord of the heavens and the earth , I thank you because you have revealed these things to the wise and to the wise , and hid them and made them manifest to the infant
Yes , Father , for so is your beauty
&quot; All things are delivered to me by my Father . No man knows the Son except the Father . No man knows the Father except the Son and the Son , whom He wills to instruct .
&quot; I will give rest to all of you who are burdened with hardship , so that they may come to me
&quot; Be gentle in my heart and humble , and bear my yoke , and learn my ways ; and in that way you will have rest in your hearts .
For my yoke is easy for me , and my burden light .
Then Jesus passed through the wheat field on the Sabbath day , and when his disciples were hungry , he snatched up the ears of the wheat to eat
And when the Pharisees saw it , they said unto Jesus , Behold , thy disciples have done that which is impossible on the Sabbath
Jesus said to them , &quot; Have you not remembered what David and his companions did when they were hungry in the Book ?
&quot; When he entered the house of God , he ate a table of cakes , which he and those who followed him could not eat , except the priests
&quot; Have you not remembered , as it is written in the law , that the priests did not sin on the Sabbath day , when they were in the temple ?
&quot; But I tell you , there is a man here greater than the temple
If you understand the meaning of this saying , you will not be guilty of sin , but of sin
For he is the Lord of the Sabbath for the Son of man .
Jesus left the place and entered into a synagogue
And there was a man whose hand was dried up ; and they asked him , saying , Can I cure him on the Sabbath day , or can I not ? That was to accuse him
Jesus said , &quot; Who among you has a sheep that falls into a pit on the Sabbath day and does not grasp it and bring it up
How much more is a man than a sheep ! Therefore it is possible to do good on the Sabbath day
Then He said to the man , &quot; Stretch out your hand , &quot; and he stretched out his hand , and he restored it , just as he had done to the one hand .
&quot; The Pharisees went out and talked about how they might destroy Jesus
And when Jesus knew it , he departed from there ; and many followed him , and he healed all the sick among them .
and commanded them not to give him a name
&quot; This is to test the words of Isaiah the prophet , saying ,
&quot; Behold , my servant , whom I have chosen , whom I have loved , whom I have pleased in my heart , I will give him my Spirit , and he will preach the law to the nations
He did not fight , nor shout , neither did any man hear his voice in the streets
He will not break a reed that has been crushed , He will not destroy the remnant of the lightning , He will not extinguish it until he has done justice , and justice will prevail .
All the foreigners will bow to his name .
Now a man , blind and dumb , who was possessed by the devil , was brought to Jesus , and he healed him , and even the dumb man could speak and see .
And all the people were astonished , saying , Is not this the son of David ?
But when the Pharisees heard it , they said , &quot; This man is chasing the devil , because of the king of the devil , Bezekiah .
Knowing their thoughts , Jesus said to them , &quot; A nation that is divided against itself will become a wilderness , and a city that is divided against itself will not stand .
&quot; If Satan drives out Satan , he will be divided among himself . How can his country stand ?
&quot; If I rely on Belize to cast out demons , and on your sons to cast out demons , then they will judge your evil deeds .
&quot; If I cast out demons by the Spirit of God , the kingdom of God will come to you .
How can a man enter into the house of a mighty man , and take away his furniture , unless he binds the mighty man first , and takes away his property ?
&quot; He who is not with me is an enemy to me , and he who is not with me is gathered together , and he who is divided .
&quot; Therefore I tell you that all sins and blasphemies of men are forgiven , but blasphemies of the Holy Spirit are not forgiven .
Whoever speaks and sins the Son of man shall be forgiven ; and whoever speaks and sins the Holy Spirit shall not be forgiven in this world .
You are either good for the tree , or good for the fruit ; and the tree is bad , and the fruit is bad ; for by seeing the fruit you know the tree .
&quot; How can you speak good words , for you are wicked , like serpents , and speak in your mouths , because your hearts are full of them ?
A good man brings forth good out of the good that is in his heart , and a evil man brings forth evil out of the evil that is in his heart
&quot; I also tell you , that the words of every man will be spoken in the days of judgment .
&quot; For by your words you will be justified , and by your words you will be guilty .
Then some of the scribes and Pharisees said to Jesus , &quot; Father , we would like you to show us a sign
Jesus answered them , &quot; A generation of wicked and lustful men seeks signs , and there is no sign to show them , except the sign of Jonah the prophet
And Jonah was in the belly of the fish three days and three nights ; and the son of man was in the land three days and three nights
And it came to pass at the time of judgment , that the Ninevites rose up to judge the sins of this generation ; for they repented , because they had heard that which Jonah had spoken : behold , there is a greater man than Jonah in this place .
&quot; When it is judged , the queen of the south shall rise up to judge the sins of this generation ; for he has come from the ends of the earth to hear Solomon &apos;s wisdom . Behold , there is a greater man than Solomon in this place .
&quot; When the devil has departed from man , he comes and goes in a land without water , seeking rest , and finds it not .
Then he said , &quot; I will go back to the house from which I came , and when I come , I will see that it is empty , cleansed and repaired .
Then he took seven other devils , worse than himself , and went in to dwell therein ; and the end of that man was worse than the beginning , and so was the generation of the wicked .
And it came to pass , when Jesus was speaking to all the people , that , behold , his mother and his brethren were standing on the outside , to speak to him
&quot; So someone told him , &quot; Look , your mother and your brother are standing outside to speak to you
And he answered and said unto him , Who is my mother and who is my brother ?
Then he stretched out his hand to the disciples , and said , &quot; Look , my mother , my brother
&quot; All who do the will of my Father in heaven are my brothers and sisters and mothers .
On that day Jesus came out of the house and sat by the sea
And many gathered themselves together unto him , and he had to go up and sit down ; and they all stood on the shore
He spoke to them many things in parables , saying , &quot; There is a sower who goes out to sow
&quot; In the day of judgment , the birds of the field , which were by the wayside , were consumed .
There are those who fall on shallow rocky ground , which is neither deep nor quick to sprout .
As soon as the sun comes out , it dries up because it has no roots
And he that is fallen into thorns , and the thorns grow and crush him ;
And he that is laid down in a good land , he will be fruitful , one hundred times , sixty times , thirty times .
If any have ears to hear , let them hear .
Then the disciples came and asked Jesus , &quot; Why do you speak to the people by parable ? &quot;
Jesus answered them , &quot; For the mystery of the kingdom of heaven is for you to know , not for them .
He that hath shall be added unto him , that he may have more ; and he that hath not shall be taken away , even all that he hath .
Therefore I speak to them with parables , because they see and see and see not , and hear and hear not , and understand not
And it was in them that Isaiah &apos;s prophecy was fulfilled , saying , &quot; You hear to hear , but you do not understand ; and you see to see , but you do not know .
&quot; Because I have anointed the hearts of these people with oil , and the ears have become dull , and the eyes have closed ; for I fear that the eyes will see , and the ears will hear , and the heart will understand ; and I will turn back and heal them .
But blessed are your eyes , because they have seen ; blessed are your ears , because they have heard ;
&quot; Truly , I tell you , there were many prophets and righteous men before , who saw what you saw but did not see , and heard what you heard but did not hear .
So listen to this parable of seedlings .
&quot; The evildoer comes , and takes away that which is in his heart , and that which is by the wayside , whoever hears not the law of the kingdom of heaven .
&quot; He who is cast down on the stone is the one who hears and rejoices ,
Only because there is no root in the heart , neither is it temporary , and when the way is troubled or oppressed , it falls down at once
It is in the thorns that man hears the way , and then the thought of the world , and the confusion of money and wealth , encompasses the way , and it is not able to bear fruit .
&quot; And he that is planted in a good land , he hears and understands , and afterwards becomes faithful , one hundred times , sixty times , thirty times .
Then Jesus made another parable to them , saying , &quot; The kingdom of heaven is like a man planting his seed in a field
And it came to pass , when they were asleep , that the enemy came , and cast the young bullock into the wheat , and went away .
By the time that the seed hath sprouted its ears , the plums shall also appear .
The servant of the lord of the field came and told him , saying , &quot; Lord , aren &apos;t you the well-grown ox of the field from which you came
And the master said , This is the enemy &apos;s work ; and the servant said , Will you let us go out
&quot; No , &quot; said the master , &quot; because I am afraid that even the wheat will not be taken out
&quot; When the harvest is done , I will say to the harvester , &apos; First take the barley out , and bound it in bundles , and burn it ; but the wheat will be harvested in the barn
And he used another parable to them , saying , &quot; The kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed , which is taken and planted in the field
It was the smallest of the hundred ; and when it was grown up , it was greater than all kinds of food ; and it became trees , and birds of the sky lodged in its branches .
Then he spoke to them a parable , saying , &quot; The kingdom of heaven is like yeast ; a woman has brought it , and hid it in three bowls , and immediately the whole congregation has risen up .
These are the words which Jesus spoke to the people in parables ; and if there were no parables , he would not speak to them
This is to test the prophet , saying , &quot; I will open my mouth with a parable , and I will invent the hidden things that have been hidden since the beginning of the world .
Now Jesus left the people and entered the house , and his disciples said to him , &quot; Tell us the parable of the ox in the field ,
He answered , &quot; The one who plants the good seed is a son of man .
&quot; The field is the world ; the good seed is the son of the kingdom of heaven ; and the ox is the son of the wicked .
The enemy of Satan is the devil . The time of the harvest is the end of the world , and the harvester is the angel .
&quot; And the rods shall be cut out and burned with fire , and so shall the end of the world be .
&quot; The Son of man shall send an apostle , and bring forth out of his land all those who cause people to fall and all those who do evil .
Lost in the furnace . In it is necessary to weep and tear teeth
Then the righteous shall shine in the land of their fathers as the sun : and those who have ears to hear shall hear .
&quot; The kingdom of heaven is like a treasure hidden in the earth ; and when a man meets it , he hid it ; and he rejoices , and sells everything , and buys the land .
And the kingdom of heaven is like a merchant seeking good pearls
And when he found a precious pearl , he went and bought it , and sold all that he had .
&quot; The kingdom of heaven is like a net spread out in the sea , gathering together all kinds of people .
And when the net is full , they will bring them up to the shore and sit down ; and the good will be taken away in the vessels , and the bad will be thrown away .
&quot; This is the end of the world ; and the angels will come out of the righteous and separate the wicked .
Lost in the furnace . In it is necessary to weep and tear teeth
Jesus said , &quot; Do you understand all these things ? &quot; They said , &quot; We do .
He said , &quot; Every scribe who is taught to be a disciple of the kingdom of heaven comes out of his barn like a householder , bringing out old and new things
And when Jesus had finished these parables , he departed from there
Then he came to his hometown , and taught in the synagogue , and they all wondered , saying , &quot; Wherein does this man have such wisdom and power ? &quot;
Is he not the son of a carpenter , and his mother is not Mary , and his brethren are not Jacob , Joseph , and Simon , and Judah ?
His sisters are not all here with us . Where does this man have all this
And they abhorred him ; and Jesus said unto them , There is no prophet that is not respected , save in his own house
Jesus was not able to do much in it because they did not believe
At that time Herod the king of the sepulchre heard the fame of Jesus
And he said unto his servants , This is John the Baptizer , who is risen from the dead ; therefore these things come forth out of him
For the first time Herod put John in prison for Herod the wife of his brother Philip
For John said to him , &quot; It is unreasonable for you to marry this woman
And Herod desired to kill him , but feared the people , because they called John a prophet
And it came to pass , on the birthday of Herod , that the daughter of Herod danced in the presence of all the people , and Herod rejoiced
Then Herod swore to give him that which he had asked of him
Then the daughter , being delivered by her mother , said , &quot; Bring me John &apos;s head , and put it in a dish ,
Then the king grieved , but because of his oath , and because of the people who were with him , he commanded him
Then sent messengers , and slew John in prison .
And he laid his head in the dish , and brought it to the woman , and the woman brought it to his mother
Then came the disciples of John , and took the body , and buried it , and went to tell Jesus
When Jesus heard this , he boarded a ship and departed alone into the wilderness ; and when they heard this , they followed him on foot from every city .
Jesus came out , and saw many , and had mercy on them , and healed their sick .
&quot; When the day is late , and the disciples come in , and say , &apos; This is the wilderness , and the time has passed ; let them go away , and go to the villages , and buy their own food . &apos; 
Jesus said , &quot; Do not go with them , but eat with them
&quot; The disciples said , &quot; We have only five cakes and two fish
Jesus said , &quot; Bring it to me
And he commanded all the people to sit on the grass , and to take the five loaves and the two fish , and to look at the heaven , and to bless , and to break the loaves , and to give them to the disciples , and the disciples to all the people
And they all ate , and were filled ; and they took up the rest of the garbage , and filled the twelve baskets
About five thousand people ate , except women and children .
Then Jesus took the disciples to the ship , and passed over to the other side , until he had sent them away
And when he had scattered all the people , he went up to the mountain alone to pray ; and it came to pass at night , that there was only one of him
At that time the ship was shaken by the waves in the sea , because of the wind
Four more days in the night Jesus went up to the disciples by the sea
When the disciples saw him walking on the sea , they were astonished , and said , &quot; It is a demon ; &quot; and they cried out in fear .
Immediately Jesus said to them , &quot; Relieve yourselves ; it is I who am not afraid
Peter said , &quot; Lord , if it is you , please let me go to you from the water
Jesus said to him , &quot; Come , &quot; and Peter went down from the ship on the waters to go to Jesus .
He was afraid when he saw the great wind , and when he was about to sink , he cried out , &quot; Lord , save me ! &quot;
Then Jesus stretched out his hand to him , and said , &quot; Who is it that doubts , O man of this little letter ?
They got on the boat , and the wind stopped
And all that were on the ship worshipped him , saying , Thou art indeed the Son of God
And when they had passed over the sea , they came to the place of the children of Gilead
And when the men there recognized that he was Jesus , they sent to the place around them , and brought to him all the sick
&quot; Only ask Jesus to let them touch his garments and the people who touch them , and it will be well
Then came the Pharisees and the scribes from Jerusalem to Jesus , saying :
Why do your disciples sin on the inheritance of the ancients , because they do not wash their hands at mealtime
Jesus answered them , &quot; Why do you sin against the commandments of God because of your inheritance ?
&quot; God said , &quot; When you respect your parents , and curse your parents , you will be put to death .
&quot; But you say , &apos; Whoever says to his parents , &apos; What I have offered to you has already been offered
And he shall not respect his parents : it is by your inheritance that ye have abolished the commandment of God .
&quot; You hypocrites , &quot; he said , &quot; the prophecy to which Isaiah referred concerning you is not wrong .
The people respected me with their lips , but their hearts were far from me
&quot; It is not right that they should call on Me , but that they should follow the commandments of men , and teach them the truth .
Then Jesus called the people and said to them , &quot; Listen and understand
Whoever enters cannot be defiled , and whoever leaves can be defiled .
Then the disciples came forward and said to him , &quot; Do you know that the Pharisees , when they heard this , did not obey ?
Jesus answered , &quot; Everything that is planted , if it is not planted by my Father , must be brought forth
Let them alone ; for they are blind guides ; and if the blind guide the blind , both of them shall fall into the pit .
Peter said to Jesus , &quot; Listen to this parable , please
Jesus said to them , &quot; Do you not understand now ?
Do you not know that every entrance is carried into the belly , and is laid down in the toilet ?
&quot; The only thing that comes out is that which comes out of the heart , and that is the filthy man .
For evil thoughts , murders , adultery , covetousness , stealing , false witnesses , slanders ,
&quot; This is an unclean man , and he who does not wash his hands and eat is not an unclean man .
Jesus departed from there , and returned to the land of Tyre
Then a woman of Canaan came out of the place , and cried , saying , &quot; Lord , son of David , forgive me , for my daughter has suffered greatly from the devil .
Then the disciples came and asked him , saying , &quot; This woman is crying after us , and send her away
Jesus said , &quot; I am sent to go into the lost sheep of the house of Israel
&quot; The woman came to him and said , &quot; Lord , help me
And he answered and said , It is not good to take the cakes of the children and to give them to the dogs to eat
The woman said , &quot; Lord , it is not wrong ; but the dog also eats the scraps that fell on his master &apos;s table
Jesus said to her , &quot; Woman , your faith is great ; give you what you want , and from then on his daughter will be well
And Jesus departed from that place , and came near the sea of Galilee , and sat down on the mountain
Many came to him with lame , blind , dumb , handicapped , and many others , and laid them at his feet , and he healed them .
And all the people were astonished : for the healer of the dumb and the speechless saw , and the lame walked , and the blind saw , and glorified the God of Israel .
Jesus said to his disciples , &quot; I have pity on these people , for they have not eaten three days with me here , and I will not send them back hungry , for I am afraid they will be weak on the way
&quot; The disciples said , &quot; Why do we have so many cakes in the wilderness that so many people can eat
Jesus said , &quot; How many cakes do you have ? &quot; They said , &quot; Seven and a few small fishes
And he commanded all the people to sit on the ground
And he took the seven loaves and a few fishes , and blessed them , and broke them and gave them to the disciples , and the disciples gave them to all the people
And all the people ate , and were filled ; and they filled the seven baskets with the remnant of their garbage
A total of four thousand people ate , besides women and children .
Then Jesus sent them away , and they boarded a ship , and came to the border of Magadan
&quot; The Pharisees and the Sadducees came to seek Jesus and asked him to show them a sign from heaven
Jesus answered , &quot; The night is red , and you say , &apos; It must be clear
When the sky turns red and dark in the morning , you say , &quot; Today it will rain , &quot; and you know not the colour of the sky , nor the signs of this hour .
A generation of evil-doers asked for signs , and there was no sign for them , except the sign of Jonah ; and Jesus departed from them .
The disciples passed over and forgot to bring the cake
Jesus said to them , &quot; Be careful to guard against the yeast of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees
And the disciples reasoned among themselves , saying , This is because we have no bread
When Jesus saw it , he said , &quot; Why do you , little believers , argue with one another without bread ?
Do you not understand ? Do you not remember the five loaves distributed to 5,000 people , and how many baskets have you scattered ?
Do you not remember how many baskets you have scattered , and how many of the seven cakes you have distributed to 4,000 people ?
&quot; I said to you , &apos; Beware of the yeast of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees . &apos; This is not a word of cakes ; why do you not understand ?
Then the disciples knew that what he said was not to preserve the yeast of the bread , but to preserve the lesson of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees
And when he was come into the land of Philip of Caesarea , he asked the disciples , saying , &quot; Who is my son ? &quot;
They said , &quot; John the Baptizer , and Elijah , and Jeremiah , or one of the prophets
Jesus said , &quot; Who do you say I am
Then Simon Peter answered and said unto him , Thou art the Christ , and the Son of the everlasting God
And Jesus said unto him , Blessed art thou , Simon , for this is not the commandment of the flesh , but of my Father in heaven
&quot; And I tell you , you are Peter , and I will build my church on this rock ; and the power of the shadow will not prevail over him .
&quot; I will give you the key of the kingdom of heaven ; and whoever you bind on the earth will be bound on the heavens ; and whoever you release on the earth will be released on the heavens .
Now Jesus commanded his disciples not to say to any man that he was Christ
From that time onward Jesus instructed his disciples that he should go up to Jerusalem , and suffer much from the elders of the priests and scribes , and be killed , and be raised again on the third day
Then Peter drew him and counseled him , saying , &quot; Lord , this will not happen to you
Then Jesus turned and said to Peter , &quot; Get behind me , Satan ; for you have stumbled on my feet , because you do not obey God , but obey men .
Then Jesus said to his disciples , &quot; If any man follows me , let him turn his back on his cross and follow me
For whosoever shall save his life shall lose it ; and whosoever shall lose it for me shall have it .
What is the profit of man if he earns the whole world and loses his life , and what can he take in exchange for his life
The Son shall come in the glory of his Father , with the apostles ; and he shall recompense every man according to his deeds .
Verily I say unto you , Whosoever standeth here shall see the Son of man come into his land before he tasteth no death .
Six days later Jesus went up into the mountains in darkness with Peter , Jacob , and John the brother of Jacob .
And the appearance was changed before them , and their faces were as bright as the sun , and their garments as white as light .
And suddenly Moses and Elijah appeared to them , and spoke to Jesus
Peter said to Jesus , &quot; Lord , it is good that we are here . If you will , I will set up three tents here , one for you , one for Moses , and one for Elijah
And it came to pass , when they were speaking , that a bright cloud covered them , and a voice came out of the clouds , saying , &quot; This is my beloved Son , whom I rejoice in , and whom you shall hear .
When the disciples heard it , they bowed themselves to the ground in fear .
Jesus came and touched them and said , &quot; Arise , do not be afraid
They saw no man , but Jesus there
And when he was come down from the mountain , Jesus said unto them , The Son of man hath not yet risen from the dead , and ye shall not tell man what ye have seen .
The disciples asked Jesus , &quot; Why do the scribes say that Elijah must come first
Jesus answered , &quot; Elijah certainly comes first and will restore all things
&quot; But I tell you that Elijah has passed away , and people do not know him , and they treat him arbitrarily , and so will the sons of men suffer their hurt .
Then the disciples understood that Jesus spoke of John the Baptizer
When Jesus and his disciples came to the people , a man came to him and knelt down , saying :
&quot; Lord , have mercy on my son , for he suffered greatly from the disease of epilepsy , falling many times into the fire , and many times into the water
&quot; I brought him to your disciples , but they could not heal him
Jesus said , &quot; How long will I be here with you , O generation that is disbelieving and perverse ? How long will I be patient with you ? Bring him to me
Then Jesus rebuked the devil , and the devil came out , and the child was healed .
The disciples came to Jesus in darkness and said , &quot; Why can &apos;t we drive out the devil ?
Jesus said , &quot; It is because your faith is small . I tell you , if you have faith like a mustard seed , you say to this mountain , &apos; You move from one side to another , and he will move ; and there is nothing you cannot do .
As for this kind of devil , if he does not pray for a fast , he will not come out .
And when they were yet in Galilee , Jesus said unto his disciples , The Son of man shall be given into the hand of men
They will kill him , and on the third day he will be raised again ; and the disciples were greatly troubled
And it came to pass , when he was come to Capernaum , that the tax collectors came to Peter , and said unto him , Will not your lord pay the tax ?
And Peter said , Nay . And when he was come into the house , Jesus said unto him , Simon , what meanest thou , king of the world , to whom shall the customs be levied , to his own son , and to strangers ?
Peter said , &quot; It is to a stranger . &quot; Jesus said , &quot; Because of this , the son will be tax-free
&quot; But I fear that if you trespass against them , and go to the sea to fish , and pick up the first fish that you caught , and open his mouth , you will receive a buck , and you will bring it to them as a tax money for you and for me .
Then came the disciples and asked Jesus , &quot; Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven
Then Jesus called a little child , and made him stand among them
&quot; Truly I tell you , if you do not turn back and become like children , you will not enter the kingdom of heaven .
Therefore he who humbles himself as this little child is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven
&quot; Whoever receives a child like this in my name receives me .
&quot; It is not better for a little child of mine to fall into this faith than for a great millstone to be bound to his neck and to sink in the deep sea
Woe to the world , for it stumbles a man ; and it is inevitable that a man stumbles , but woe to him that stumbles !
&quot; If your hand or foot causes you to fall , cut it down and throw it away . If you lack one hand or foot , you will enter eternal life , as if you had two hands and two feet , and you will be thrown into eternal fire .
&quot; If one eye of yours causes you to fall , cast it out and cast it away . Only one eye of yours enters into eternal life , as if two eyes were cast into the fire of hell .
Be careful that you do not look down on one of the little ones ; for I tell you that their messengers are in heaven , and they see the face of my Father .
The Son of man came to save the lost
&quot; What do you mean , if a man has a hundred sheep and one of them goes astray ? Will he not leave the ninety-nine and go to the mountains to find the lost sheep ?
&quot; If he had found it , I tell you , he would have rejoiced more for the sheep than for the ninety-nine lambs who had no way .
&quot; You fathers in heaven would not like to lose one in this child
&quot; If your brother sins against you , you will go and point out his fault while he is alone with you ; and if he listens to you , you will gain your brothers .
&quot; If he does not listen , then you shall take one or two others with you , and testify by the mouth of two or three witnesses , and every word shall be confirmed .
&quot; If you do not listen to them , you will tell the church . If you do not listen to the church , you will see him as a foreigner and a tax collector
Verily I say unto you , Whosoever ye bind upon the earth shall be bound upon the heavens , and whosoever ye release upon the earth shall be released upon the heavens
&quot; I also tell you , &apos; If there are two of you on the earth who ask for something with one accord , I , the Father in heaven , will accomplish it for them .
&quot; Because there were two or three people gathered in My name , and I was among them .
Then Peter came in and said to Jesus , &quot; Lord , how many times will my brother sin against me , and I forgive him ?
Jesus said , &quot; I say to you , not seven times , but seventy and seven times
&quot; The kingdom of heaven is like a king , and he is accountable to his servants
And at the time of reckoning , a man brought with him a thousand thousand talents of silver
&quot; For he had nothing to repay , the master commanded to sell him and his wife and his children , and to repay them all
Then the servant bowed down and said to him , &quot; Lord , forgive me , and in the future I will be cleansed
Then the master of the servant moved with mercy , and set him free , and redeemed his debts
Then the servant came out , and found a companion of his , who lent him ten and two pieces of silver , and took him , and struck his throat , saying , &quot; You have returned me what you owe me
Then his companion fell down and begged him , saying , &quot; Forgive me , and I will be clean in the future
&quot; But he refused , and went to put him in prison , until he had repaid his debts .
And when all the companions saw that which he had done , they were grieved , and went and told the master all these things
Then the master called him , and said to him , &quot; You wicked slave , you have pleaded with me , and I will forgive you all your debts
Should you not have mercy on your companions , as I have on you ?
Then the master was very angry , and handed him over to execution , until he had paid off his debts
&quot; This is what my Father will do to you , all of you , if he does not forgive your brothers from his heart .
When Jesus had finished these words , he departed from Galilee , and came to the border of Judah , beyond the Jordan
Many followed him , and there he healed his sick
Then came the Pharisees to test Jesus , saying , &quot; Can a man rest without reason
Jesus answered , &quot; He who first created man is a man and a woman .
Have you not remembered that it is so that one leaves his parents and joins with his wife and becomes one body
Now therefore , the couple are no longer two , but one body ; therefore God is with them , and they cannot be separated
Then said the Pharisees , &quot; What is it that Moses commanded his wife to leave her book , and that she may leave him ?
Jesus said , &quot; Moses , because of your hard hearts , gave you permission to divorce your wives , but it was not so at first
&quot; I tell you , whoever takes another wife , if it is not for the sake of adultery , is adulterous ; and whoever takes the woman who has been taken , is also adulterous .
&quot; The disciples said to Jesus , &quot; It is better not to marry , neither to have a wife
Jesus said , &quot; It is not a word that can be received by all , but it is given to whomsoever it can be received .
For he who is born is circumcised , and he who is circumcised is circumcised , and he who is circumcised is circumcised for the sake of the kingdom of heaven .
Then came a man to Jesus with little children , and asked him to pray with their hands , and the disciples rebuked them .
Jesus said , &quot; Let the little ones come to me , and do not forbid them ; for this is the one who is in the kingdom of heaven
And when Jesus had given them his hand , he departed from the place
A man came to Jesus and said , &quot; Friend , what good deeds should I do that I may live forever
Jesus said to him , &quot; Why do you ask me for good things ? Only one is good . If you want to enter into eternal life , keep the commandment
He said , &quot; What commandment ? &quot; Jesus said , &quot; You shall not kill , nor commit adultery , nor steal , nor bear false witness
Be respectful to your parents and love them as yourself
Then said the young man , &quot; All these things have I observed ; what is missing ?
Jesus said , &quot; If you want to become a perfect man and sell all your possessions and give them to the poor , then there will be treasures in heaven and you will follow me
When the young man heard this , he went away sorrowfully , for he had many possessions .
Jesus said to his disciples , &quot; I tell you , it is hard for the rich to enter the kingdom of heaven
&quot; And I tell you , it is easier for a camel to enter the land of God than for a rich man to enter the land of a needle through the eyes of an acupuncture .
When the disciples heard this , they were astonished , saying , &quot; Who then can be saved
Jesus looked at them and said , &quot; It is impossible in man , and everything is possible in God
Then Peter said to him , &quot; Behold , what shall we do in the future , since we have forsaken all that follows you ?
&quot; I tell you , &quot; Jesus said , &quot; that in the time of the resurrection , when you will be with my people , the Son of man will sit on the throne of his glory , and you will also sit on the twelve thrones to judge the twelve tribes of Israel
&quot; Everyone who leaves his house for My name , or his brothers , or his sisters , or his father , or his mother , or his children , or his daughters , or his daughters , or his land for My name &apos;s sake , shall have a hundredfold need , and shall bear eternal life .
However , there are many things that are ahead that will be behind , and things that are behind that will be ahead
For he is like a master to the kingdom of heaven , and goes early to hire a man , and to work in his vineyard
And he said unto the workers , One day he shall send them into the vineyard for a penny and a silver
And he went out for the first time , and saw that there was still a man standing in the city
And he said unto them , Go ye also into the vineyard , and I will give you that which is given ; and they went in
And it came to pass at noon , and at the beginning of Shen , that he went out again , and so it was
And it came to pass at the beginning of the month , when he saw that there were still people standing there , that he asked them , &quot; Why do you stand here all day long ?
They said , &quot; Because there is no man to hire us . &quot; He said , &quot; You also go into the vineyard
And it came to pass in the evening , that the lord said unto the governor , Let all the workers come , and give them their wages from the latter to the former
And the first hired men came about the same time , and each man received a penny and a silver
And when the first hired came , they thought that it was necessary to get more ; and who knows that they each got one .
And when they had received it , they complained to their lord
We worked all day long and suffered the heat , and then only for a little while . Why do you call them like us ?
Then answered one of them , &quot; My friend , I am not in debt to you ; is not what you have promised me a penny ?
Take yours , and I will give you a copy of that which is later , and of that which I will .
Will not my east and west be used according to my will ? For I am a good man , and you have turned your eyes red ?
Thus the latter will be before , and the former will be after . &#91; There is ancient scripture in it that there is fewer chosen because of the many who are called
And when Jesus was come to Jerusalem , he took the twelve disciples by the way , and said unto them :
&quot; Behold , we go up to Jerusalem , and the Son of man shall be delivered to the chief priests and scribes , and they shall condemn him to death .
And he gave it to a stranger , and made him play , and whipped him , and crucified him ; and on the third day he shall be raised again .
At that time the mother of the son of Zebedee came up with his two sons , and prayed to Jesus , saying ,
Jesus said , &quot; What do you want ? &quot; He said , &quot; Let me and my two sons sit on your right hand and on your left in your land
Jesus answered them , &quot; You do not know what you are asking . Can you drink the cup I am going to drink ? &quot; They said , &quot; We can .
Jesus said , &quot; You must drink the cup that I have drunk , but sit on my right hand , and it is not for me to give it ; it is for whom my Father has prepared it , and he will give it to whomever it is
When the ten heard it , they were angry with their two brothers
Jesus called them and said to them , &quot; You know that foreigners have kings over them , and ministers over them
&quot; But it shall not be so among you ; and whoever among you desires to be great will be your servant .
&quot; Whoever wishes to be first will be your servant
&quot; As the Son of man comes , he is not to be obeyed , but to be obeyed ; and he is to give his life for a ransom for many .
When they came out of Jericho , many followed him .
And two blind men sat by the wayside , and when they heard that Jesus had passed by , they cried out , saying , Lord , be merciful to us , the sons of David
And they reproached them , and forbade them from speaking ; but they cried more and more , saying , Lord , forgive us , O children of David
Then Jesus stood and called them and said to them , &quot; What shall I do for you
They said , &quot; Lord , let our eyes see
Then Jesus moved with mercy , and touched their eyes , and they immediately saw , and followed Jesus
Jesus and his disciples came near Jerusalem to Bethphage at Mount Olives
Then Jesus sent two disciples and said to him at his door , &quot; Go to the other side of the village and see a donkey tied in it , and a donkey in the same place ; and untie yourselves and come to me
&quot; If any man speaks to you , you will say , &apos; Use him first , &apos; and he will bring you back when he stands up
&quot; This is accomplished for the testimony of the prophet ,
&quot; Speak to the inhabitants of Zion , saying , &apos; Behold , your king comes to you gently , riding a donkey , and a son of a donkey .
And the disciples did as Jesus commanded them
He took the donkey and the donkeys , and put his clothes on them , and Jesus rode on them
More than half the people laid their clothes on the road , and some cut down branches to lay them on the road
And all those who went before and after shouted , saying , &quot; Blessed is he who has come in the name of the Lord and has delivered the sons of David , &quot; which is the word of praise for salvation .
And when Jesus had come into Jerusalem , all the people were astonished , saying , Who is this
And they said , This is Jesus , the prophet of Galilee and Nazareth
Jesus entered into the temple of God , and drove out all those who traded in the temple , and overturned the tables of those who exchanged silver , and the benches of those who sold doves
He said to them , &quot; It is written , &apos; My house will be called the house of prayer ; and you have made him a thief &apos;s nest .
There were blind and lame in the temple , and they came to Jesus , and he healed them .
And when the chief priests and the scribes saw the miracles that Jesus did , and saw the little children crying in the temple , saying , &quot; Bring away the sons of David , &quot; they were very angry .
And he said unto him , Didst thou hear what these men said ? And Jesus said , Yea ; it is written , Thou hast perfected the words of praise from the mouth of the child , and from the mouth of the breast ; have ye not remembered ?
So he departed from them , and went out of the city to Bethany , and lodged there
When he returned to the city in the morning , he was hungry
And when he saw a tree without fruit by the way , he went to it , and found nothing in the tree except leaves : and he said unto the tree , From now on thou shalt not bear fruit ; and the tree without fruit was dried up immediately
When the disciples saw it , Hezekiah said to them , &quot; How is it that the tree that has no fruit has dried up immediately
Jesus answered , &quot; I tell you , if you have faith and have no doubt , not only will you do what you do without fruit trees , but you will also say to this mountain , &apos; Move this land and cast it into the sea , and it will be accomplished
&quot; Whatever you ask , and whatever you believe , you will receive .
And it came to pass , when Jesus was entering into the temple , that the chief priests and the elders of the people came to him , and asked him , &quot; By what authority do you do these things ? Who is it that gives you this authority ?
Jesus answered , &quot; I will also ask you one thing : If you tell me , I will tell you what authority I have to do these things
The baptism of John came from there , and from heaven , and from among men ; and they reasoned among themselves , saying , If we say from heaven , he will say to us , Thus , why do you not believe him ?
&quot; We fear the people also from among men , because they have taken John as their prophet
Then answered Jesus , We do not know ; but Jesus said , Neither have I told you by what authority I do these things
Then came a man , having two sons , and said to the eldest son , &quot; My son , you are going to work in the vineyard today
Then he answered , &quot; I will not go , and I will go after my repentance
Then he answered , &quot; Father , I am going , but he is not going
They said , &quot; Son , &quot; Jesus said , &quot; I have told you , tax collectors and prostitutes , that there is no kingdom more advanced than your God . &quot;
&quot; For John came to you in the way of righteousness , but you did not believe him ; and the tax collectors and the prostitutes did not believe him ; and you saw him , and went to him without repentance .
&quot; You have heard another parable : A man has planted a vineyard , and has made a fence around it , and has dug a winepress in it , and has covered a building , and has rented it to the gardeners , and has gone abroad .
And it came to pass , when the time for the harvest was near , that he sent his servant to the gardener to harvest the fruit
And the gardener took his servant , and struck one , and slew one , and struck one with a stone
And the lord sent other servants , more than before ; and the gardeners treated them likewise .
Then he sent his son to them , saying , &quot; They will respect my son .
Then when the gardeners saw his son , they said to one another , &quot; This is his inheritance ; come , let us kill him , and take his inheritance . &quot;
And they took him , and threw him out of the vineyard , and slew him .
&quot; When the lord of the garden comes , how shall he deal with these gardeners ?
They said , &quot; Let the wicked be put to death by the wicked , and let the vineyards be rented to the gardener who waits for the fruit in due time .
Jesus said , &quot; It is written in the Scriptures , &apos; The stone which the craftsmen have rejected has become the headstone of the corner of the house . This is the Lord &apos;s work which is wonderful in our eyes .
Therefore I say unto you , The kingdom of God shall be taken away from you , and given unto the people of the fruitful .
&quot; Whoever falls on this stone must be crushed ; and whoever falls on the head of this stone must be crushed .
When the chief priests and the Pharisees heard his parable , they saw that he was speaking to them
&quot; They desired to seize him , but feared the people , because they called him a prophet for the people
Then Jesus spoke to them again in a parable
&quot; The kingdom of heaven is like a king who sets up a banquet for his son ,
Then he sent his servants , and invited those who had been called , but they would not come .
Then the king sent other servants , saying , &quot; Tell the man who was called , &apos; My feast has been prepared , and the cattle and the fat have been slaughtered , and everything is ready . Come and sit down
The men left without reason . One went to his own field . One went to buy and sell .
And the rest took their servants , and insulted them , and killed them .
Then the king was very angry , and sent out his army to destroy the murderers , and to burn up their cities
Then he said to his servant , &quot; The feast is ready , but the people who are called are not worthy
&quot; Therefore go up to the crossroads , and call every one whom you meet .
And the servants went out to the highway , and all that they met were gathered together , not for good or for evil ; and the feast was filled with guests
And the king came in to see the guests , and behold , there was a man without clothes
And he said unto him , Friend , how comeest thou to this place without clothing ? And the man said nothing .
Then the king said to the caller , &quot; Bring his hands and his feet , and cast him into the darkness that is outside , where you must mourn and tear your teeth
Because there are more called and fewer chosen
At that time the Pharisees went out to negotiate , and how could they deceive him by the words of Jesus
Then they sent their disciples and the Hebrews to Jesus , and said , &quot; Father , we know that you are an honest man , and that you are faithful in the word of God , and that you do not show mercy to anyone , because you do not see the appearance of men
Tell us , please , what is your opinion . Is it possible or not to pay taxes to Caesar
When Jesus saw their wickedness , he said to them , &quot; Why do you seek me , you hypocrites of goodness ?
They took a silver coin and gave it to him
Jesus said , &quot; Whose is this image and this ? &quot;
And they said , It is Caesar ; and Jesus said , Thus shall the things of Caesar be to Caesar , and the things of God to God
And when they heard it , they began to laugh , and departed from him
And they came that day and asked Jesus , saying , There is no resurrection .
&quot; Son of man , &quot; Moses said , &quot; If a man dies and has no children , then his brother shall take his wife and give birth to his brother
There were seven brothers before us : the first took a wife , died , had no children , and left her to his brothers
The second , the third , the seventh , and so on
At the end , the woman also died
And in the resurrection he will be the wife of one of the seven , because they have married him .
Jesus answered them , &quot; You are wrong , for you do not understand the Scriptures , nor know the great power of God
&quot; In the resurrection no man will marry nor marry . He is like an angel in heaven .
Have you not remembered what God said to you in the Book concerning the resurrection of the dead ?
He said , &apos; I am the God of Abraham , the God of Isaac , and the God of Jacob . &apos; God is not the God of the dead , but the God of the living
When they heard it , they marveled at his teaching
When the Pharisees heard that Jesus had shut up the mouth of Satan , they gathered together
And one of them , being a scribe , asked him to test him
Son , what is the greatest commandment of the law ?
Jesus said to him , &quot; Love the Lord your God with all your heart , with all your soul , with all your heart
This is the first and the greatest of the commandments
Secondly , to follow the example , to love others as oneself
These are the two commandments , the law and the prophet &apos;s counsel of all things .
When the Pharisees were gathered together , Jesus asked them ,
And they answered and said unto him , Whose son is Christ ? And he said unto them , The son of David
Then Jesus said , &quot; How is it that David was moved by the Holy Spirit to be called Lord ? &quot;
&quot; The Lord said to my Lord , &apos; Sit on my right hand , and I will put your enemy under your feet .
How then did David call himself Lord , and be his son ?
They had no one to answer , and from that day on no one would dare ask him anything again .
At that time Jesus spoke to the people and to the disciples
And the scribes and the Pharisees sat upon Moses &apos; seat ,
&quot; Be obedient to all that they command you , and do it ; but do not obey their deeds , for they say they cannot do it .
They bound the burden of burden upon the shoulders of men , but they could not move one finger .
And all that they did was to be seen : therefore the scripture that they wore was broadened , and the collar of their garments was lengthened .
Love the first seat at the feast , the high places in the synagogue ,
And the beloved asked him in the streets , and called him Rabbi .
But you shall not be called Rabbi , for only one is your husband , and you are brothers .
Neither shall he that is on the earth be called a father ; for only one is your father , and he is a father in heaven .
Neither shall you be called a teacher ; for only one is your teacher , and that is Christ
&quot; Whoever is greater among you will be your servant
He that is high shall be low , and he that is low shall be high .
Woe to your hypocritical scribes and Pharisees , for you have shut the gates of the kingdom of heaven before the righteous , and you do not allow those who are about to enter in , neither do you allow them to enter .
&quot; Woe to your hypocrisy as scribes and Pharisees who are good , for you have forged the widow &apos;s house for long prayers , so that you will be punished more severely
Woe to your hypocrisy , the scribes and Pharisees who are good , for you have gone through the land of the sea and the sea to seduce a man , and have made him a son of hell twice as much as you .
&quot; Woe to you , you blind guides , who say , &apos; Whoever swears by the temple is nothing , but whoever swears by the gold in the temple , he shall keep it
&quot; What is the great thing , you ignorant and blind ? Is it gold , or what do you call the temple of gold holy ?
&quot; But you say , &apos; Nothing is the matter with him who swears by the altar ; but with him who swears by the gift on the altar , he shall keep it
&quot; What is the great gift , you blind men , or the altar that sanctifies the gift ?
Therefore men swear by the altar , that is , by the altar and by all that is on the altar
A man swears by the temple , that is , by the temple and by him that dwells therein
&quot; He swears by the heavens , by the throne of God , and by the one who sits on it .
Woe to your hypocritical scribes and Pharisees , for you have offered one tenth of the flour , and of the anise , and of the spices ; and the greater thing in the law is righteousness , mercy , and faithfulness , and you do not do it ; and the greater is that which you do , and that which you do not .
&quot; You blind guides , you worms , you filter out , you camels , you swallow down
Woe to you , you hypocrites , scribes and Pharisees of goodness , for the outside of the cup , where you wash , is full of provocation and rebellion .
&quot; You blind Pharisee , first wash the inside of the cup , that the outside may be clean
Woe to your hypocritical scribes and Pharisees , for you are like a marbled tomb , beautiful on the outside , and filled with the bones of the dead , and with all filth
And so are you ; for righteousness is manifested outside before men , and in it is full of false good and wickedness .
&quot; Woe to the scribes and Pharisees who pretend to be good , for you have built the tombs of the prophets , and have adorned the tombs of the righteous ,
&quot; If we had been in the days of our fathers , we would not have flown with the blood of their prophets
&quot; This is the testimony of yourselves , that you killed the sons of the prophets .
Go fill yourself with the wickedness of your father
&quot; How can you escape the punishment of hell , you serpents , you poisonous snakes ?
&quot; Therefore I have sent to you prophets and wise men and scribes ; some of you will kill and crucify , and some of you will whip in the synagogue and drive out of this city into that city .
&quot; That the blood of the righteous in the world may return to you , from the blood of the righteous Abel , even to the blood of Zechariah the son of Barabbas , whom you killed in the midst of the temple and the altar .
Verily I say unto you , All these sins shall return unto this generation
O Jerusalem , O Jerusalem , thou shalt often slay the prophet and slay with stones those who are sent to thee , and many times have I desired to gather thy daughters as a hen gathers her little ones under her wings , but thou wilt not
&quot; Behold , your houses have become a wilderness , and they are left to you .
&quot; I tell you that from now on you will not see me again until you say , &apos; Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord&apos;
When Jesus came out of the temple , and was about to go , the disciples came in and showed him the temple
Jesus said to them , &quot; Do you not see the temple ? I tell you , there is not a stone left on a stone that will not be demolished in the future
He sat down on the Mount of Olives , and said to the disciples , &quot; Tell us when these things will happen , and what are the signs of your coming and the end of the world ? &quot;
Jesus answered them , &quot; Be careful , lest someone mislead you
For for the sake of the future there come good men in my name , saying , I am Christ , and I will trouble many
Do not be afraid to hear the winds of war and of war , for these things are necessary , but the end has not yet come .
The people will attack the people , and the country will attack the country . There will be famine and earthquakes in many places .
These were the beginnings of the disaster . &#91; The original disaster was a productive difficulty
Then they will put you in trouble , and they will kill you , and you will be hated by all the people for My name .
In that day many people will fall , and they will fall upon one another , and they will hate one another .
And there are many falsehoods which are foretold , and which trouble many
It is only because of the increase in wrongdoing that the love of many people has cooled down
Only those who endure to the end will be saved .
&quot; The gospel of the kingdom of heaven shall be preached throughout all the earth , and it shall be testified to all the people , and the end shall come
&quot; You have seen that which the prophet Daniel said , which destroyed the abominations , stands in the Holy Place .
At that time the Jews should flee to the mountains
What is in the house , do not come down to take things from home
&quot; He who is in the field will not go back to take his clothes
When the days of pregnancy and of breastfeeding are upon them
&quot; You shall pray that when you flee , you shall not find winter or sabbath
For there will be a great calamity from the beginning of the world to this day , and there will be no such calamity afterwards
If that day is not reduced , there will be none to be saved from the bloody , but for the chosen , that day will be reduced .
Then if any man say to you , &quot; Christ is here , &quot; or , &quot; Christ is there , &quot; you will not believe .
For the false Christ , the false prophet , will rise , and show great signs and wonders ; and if it were to do , even the people would be troubled .
&quot; Behold , I have already told you
&quot; If any man says to you , &apos; Look , Christ is in the wilderness , &apos; do not go out , or &apos; Look , Christ is in the inner house , &apos; you will not believe .
And lightning shall come from the east , and it shall shine straight toward the west ; and so shall the Son of man come .
The dead bodies will be there , and the eagle will be gathered there .
When the disaster of those days had passed , the sun had turned black , and the moon had no light , and the stars had fallen from heaven , and the heavens were shaken
Then the signs of the Son of man shall be manifested in heaven , and all the nations of the earth shall weep , and they shall see the Son of man come down with power and great glory , riding in the clouds of heaven .
He will send messengers , and with a loud trumpet he will gather his people from all sides , from the side of heaven to the side of heaven .
You can learn an equation from a fruitless tree . When the branches grow tall , you know that summer is near
&quot; Then when you see all these things , you should know that the Son of man is near , and is at the door
Truly I tell you , this generation has not yet passed away , and all these things are to be accomplished
&quot; The heavens and the earth will be wasted , and My words will not be wasted .
&quot; But no man knows that day and that hour , neither do the angels in heaven know , nor do the children ; only the Father knows .
How shall the days of Noah be , and how shall the Son of man come ?
&quot; In the days before the flood , people were eating and drinking and marrying as usual , on the day that Noah entered the ark
And the flood came unconsciously , and drove them all away ; and so shall the children come .
At that time two men were in the field , taking one and leaving another
Two women grind . Take one and leave another
&quot; Be watchful therefore , for you do not know that your Lord will come on that day .
&quot; If the lord of the house knows that a thief will come in a few more days , he will be watchful and will not allow anyone to dig through the house , as you know .
&quot; Therefore prepare yourselves , for the Son of man will come in a time which you cannot imagine .
&quot; Who is a faithful and wise servant , sent by the Lord , who takes care of his household , and distributes food to them in due season ?
Blessed is the servant when the master comes and sees him do this
&quot; Verily , I tell you , the Lord will send him over all things
&quot; If the wicked servant said in his heart , &apos; My master will be late
and struck his companion , and ate and drank with the drunken .
The master of the servant will come in days unforeseen and unknown .
heavily punished him , or cut him off from his loins , and made him guilty with those who pretended to be righteous . In that there is a need for mourning and teeth .
&quot; In those days the kingdom of heaven was better than ten little girls , carrying lamps and going out to greet the bridegroom
Five of them are foolish , and five are wise
The foolish holds a lamp , but does not prepare oil
The wise hold the lamp , and prepare oil in a vessel
When the groom was late , they all fell asleep
&quot; In the middle of the night someone shouted , &quot; The bridegroom is here , and you come out to greet him
All the little girls rose up to pick up the lamps
Speak the foolish to the wise : Give us oil , for our lamps are to be turned off .
The wise man answered , &quot; I &apos;m afraid you &apos;re not the one I &apos;m going to use , but go and buy yourselves some oil
And it came to pass at the time when they were to buy , that the bridegroom came , and sat down with him , and the door was shut .
Then came the rest of the daughters , saying , &quot; Lord , Lord , open the door for us
&quot; But he answered , &quot; I tell you , I do not know you
&quot; Be watchful , therefore , for you do not know the day and the hour .
&quot; The kingdom of heaven is better than a man who goes abroad , and calls his servants and gives them his household
And according to the wisdom of every man , He gave them silver : one gave them five thousand , one gave them two thousand , one gave them a thousand ; and they went abroad
Then the man who received the thousand took them and sold them ; and he made another thousand
&quot; The one who received 2,000 earned another 2,000 in the same way .
&quot; But the one who took the thousand went and dug the ground , and hid his master &apos;s silver .
After a long time , the masters of the servants came and counted with them
Then the man who took the 5,000 , and brought the other 5,000 , said , &quot; Lord , you have given me 5,000 ; look , I have earned another 5,000
&quot; Well , &quot; said the master , &quot; you are a good and faithful servant . You are faithful in a few things , and I will send you over many things , so that you may come in and enjoy the joy of your master .
And the man who had the two thousand said , &quot; Lord , you have given me two thousand pieces of silver ; look , I have earned another two thousand
&quot; Well , &quot; said the master , &quot; you are a good and faithful servant . You are faithful in a few things , and I will send you over many things , so that you may come in and enjoy the joy of your master .
&quot; I know that you , Lord , are a man of patience . You will harvest in places where there is no seed , and gather in places where there is no dispersion .
&quot; Behold , I am afraid , and I will bury your thousand silver in the ground . Behold , your original silver is here .
Then said the lord , &quot; You , evil and lazy servant , know that I will harvest in places where I have not sown , and gather in places where I have not gathered
&quot; When I come , I will give my money to the one who exchanges it for money , and he will receive it with interest .
Take him the thousand , and give him the ten thousand
For He will add to all that is , that he may have more ; and He will take away all that is not , and all that is .
Put this useless servant out in the darkness , where we must mourn and tear our teeth .
&quot; When the Son of man is in His glory , and comes with the angels , he shall sit on the throne of His glory .
And all the people shall gather themselves together before Him , and He shall bring them forth separately , as the sheep separated from the goats , as the sheep separated from the goats .
Place the sheep on the right , and the goats on the left
Then the king said to the one on the right , &quot; You who have been blessed by my Father will bear the kingdom which you have prepared for the creation
&quot; Because I am hungry , you give me to eat ; and when I am thirsty , you give me to drink ; and I travel as a guest , and you keep me
&quot; Behold , I am naked , and you clothe me ; I am sick , and you look after me ; I am in prison , and you come to see me .
Then the righteous answered , &quot; Lord , when shall we wait for you , when you are hungry to eat and thirsty to drink
When will they wait for you to stay on a pilgrimage , or will they dress you in your nakedness
&quot; When will they wait for you when they are sick , or when they are in prison to see you
Then said the king , Verily I say unto you , These things have ye done on the least of my brethren , and on me
Then the king said to the one on the left , &quot; Depart from me , you cursed people , and go into the eternal fire prepared for the devil and his messengers .
&quot; Because I am hungry , you do not give me food ; and when I am thirsty , you do not give me drink
&quot; I am a traveller , and you do not keep me ; I am naked , and you do not give me clothing ; I am sick , and I am in prison , and you do not come to see me
And they shall answer , saying , Lord , when shall we wait for thee , when we are hungry , or thirsty , or traveling , or naked , or sick , or in prison , and will not serve thee ?
And the king answered and said , Verily I say unto you , Ye shall do these things neither on the least of my brethren , nor on me
These shall go to eternal punishment , and those who are righteous to everlasting life .
When Jesus had finished all these words , he spoke to the disciples
&quot; You know that two days are the Passover , and that the Son of man will be delivered to man , and crucified .
At that time the chief priests and the elders of the people were gathered together in the house of the great priest , which is called Caiaphas
&quot; They agreed to take Jesus and kill him by deceit
&quot; But he said , &apos; It is not possible for the feast days , for fear of the rebellion of the people
Jesus was in the house of Simon the madman of Bethany
And a woman came , and took a bottle of precious ointment , and poured it on his head while Jesus sat down
When the disciples saw it , they were displeased and said , &quot; What is this waste of money
This ointment can be sold for a lot of money , helping the poor
Jesus perceived their counsel , and said , &quot; Why is it hard for this woman ? What he has done to me is a good thing
Because the poor are always with you . But you don &apos;t always have me
&quot; He poured it on me , and buried it for me .
&quot; Truly I tell you , under heaven , wherever the gospel is preached , I will tell you of the things that this woman did in remembrance .
Now there was one of the twelve , called Judas of Galilee , who went to the chief priest , and said ,
I handed him over to you , and they gave him thirty dollars of what you wished to give me
From that time onwards he sought the opportunity to give Jesus to them
Then the disciples came to Jesus on the first day after the feast of yeast and said to him , &quot; You will eat the Passover feast and we will prepare it for you
Then Jesus said to him , &quot; Go into the city , and go to a man . He said to him , &apos; My time is near , and I will spend the Passover with my disciples in your house .
And the disciples went and prepared the Passover feast according to the commandment of Jesus
And it came to pass at night , that Jesus sat down with the twelve disciples
As they were eating , Jesus said , &quot; I tell you , there is a man among you who wants to sell me
Then they were grieved , and one by one asked him , &quot; Is it me , Lord ? &quot;
Jesus answered , &quot; He who dipped his hand in the dish with me is the one who will sell me
&quot; The Son of man must die , as it is written in the Scriptures ; but woe to the man who sells the Son of man , who is not born in the world and does not prosper
Judas , who had betrayed Jesus , said to him , &quot; Is it me , Rabbi ? &quot; Jesus said , &quot; It is
When they had eaten , Jesus took the cake and blessed it , and broke it , and gave it to the disciples , saying , &quot; Take it and eat ; this is my body .
Then he took another cup , and gave thanks , and gave it to them , saying , &quot; This is for you all to drink
For this is the blood of my covenant , which is poured out for many , that sin may be forgiven
&quot; But I tell you that from now on I will no longer drink this grape juice , until the new day when I drink it with you in my father &apos;s land .
And when they had sung a poem , they went out to Mount Olives
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; Tonight you will fall for my sake ; for it is written , &apos; I will smite the shepherd , and the sheep will be scattered .
&quot; But when I am resurrected , I will go before you to Galilee
Peter said , &quot; Even though people fall for your sake , I will never fall
&quot; I tell you , &quot; Jesus said , &quot; that tonight the chicken calls E first , and you will not recognize me three times
Peter said to them , &quot; I must die with you , and I cannot deny you , &quot; as all the disciples said
Then Jesus came with the disciples to a place called Caesarea , and said to them , &quot; Sit here , until I come over there to pray
Then he took Peter with him , and the two sons of Zebedee with him , and wept , and was exceedingly sorrowful
Then he said to them , &quot; In my heart is great sorrow , and I am about to die . You are waiting here , and watch with me
Then he went a little further , and bowed himself to the ground , and prayed , saying , &quot; Father , if it is possible , let the cup go from me , but do not do as I will , but as you will
Then he came to the disciples and saw them asleep , and said to Peter , &quot; How is it that you cannot watch with me while I am awake ?
Be watchful , and pray , lest you enter into trouble ; for your hearts are willing , but your bodies are weak .
Then he went again to pray , and said , &quot; Father , if this cup can &apos;t leave me and I need to drink it , let your will be fulfilled
Come again to see them asleep , because their eyes are weary
And Jesus departed from them again , and the third prayer and the words were as before
Then he came to the disciples , and said to them , &quot; Stay still in your sleep ; for the time has come , that the Son of man may be sold into the hands of sinners . &quot;
Arise , let us go ; behold , the man who sells me is near
And it came to pass , while they were speaking , that Judah of the twelve disciples came with him from the chief priests and the elders of the people , with many men with knives .
&quot; The one who sold Jesus gave them a code saying , &apos; Whoever I kiss is he , and you can take him .
Then Judas came to Jesus and said to him , &quot; Please Laban , &quot; and kissed him
And Jesus said unto him , My friend , do that which thou art come to do : and the men went up and took him by the hand
Then a man who was with him drew out his sword , and cut off a sword from the servant of the high priest , and cut off an ear from him
Jesus said to him , &quot; Take the sword into the sheath . Whoever moves the sword will die under it .
Do you think that I cannot seek my Father , and that there are more angels than twelve camps sent for me ?
&quot; If that is the case , how shall it be proved that it is the case , as it is written ?
Then Jesus said to the people , &quot; Do you take me out with your swords like robbers ? I sit every day in the temple teaching and you do not have me
But all these things were done for the testimony of the book of the prophet , and the disciples fled from him .
Then the men of Jesus took him and brought him to Caiaphas , the high priest , where the scribes and the elders had been gathered together
And Peter followed Jesus far away , and went straight into the house of the high priest , and entered into it , and sat down with the officers , to see what was the end of this thing
And the chief priests and the whole congregation sought false witness , and accused Jesus , that they might put him to death .
Although there are many people who come as false witnesses , they must not bear the evidence .
&quot; This man said , &apos; In three days I will destroy the house of God and build it again
Then the high priest stood up and said to Jesus , &quot; What do you not answer ? What do these men testify to you ?
And the high priest said unto him , I speak of a God that liveth , that thou shalt swear unto us , Thou art not the Christ , the son of God
Jesus said to him , &quot; You said yes , but I told you that afterwards you will see the Son sitting on the right hand of the Almighty , riding the clouds of heaven .
Then the high priest tore his clothes , and said , &quot; He has spoken a blasphemy , which you have heard , saying , &apos; Why shall we bear witness any more ?
And they answered and said , He is dead
And they spit on his face , and struck him with their fists , and with their hands they struck him , saying ,
&quot; O Christ , you are the prophet , and tell us who it is that has struck you
Peter sat outside in the court , and a woman said to him , &quot; You were with Jesus the Galilean .
But Peter did not confess before the people , saying , &quot; I do not know what you say
And as he went out , and came to the door , a woman saw him , and said unto those who were there , This man was also with Jesus of Nazareth .
Then Peter refused to confess , and swore , &quot; I do not recognize the man
And it came to pass after a little while , that the man who stood beside him came and said unto Peter , Thou art one of them , and thy voice hath revealed thee
Then Peter , who had taken a vow , said , &quot; I do not recognize the man ; &quot; and the cock cried when he stood up .
When Peter remembered what Jesus had said , the chicken cried first , &quot; You will not recognize me three times , &quot; and he went out weeping
And it came to pass in the morning , that the chief priests and the elders of the people were all consulted concerning the execution of Jesus
and bound him , and delivered him to Pilate the governor
And it came to pass at that time , when Judas , who had betrayed Jesus , saw that Jesus had confessed his sin , he repented , and brought back the thirty dollars to the chief priests and elders ,
&quot; I have sold the blood of innocent people for sin , &quot; they said , &quot; and what does that have to do with us ?
And Judah cast the silver into the temple , and went out , and hanged it to death .
&quot; The priest picked up the silver and said , &quot; This is the price of blood ; it shall not be put in the treasure
And they agreed , and with the silver they bought a field for the house of the tribe to bury the foreigners .
Therefore the field is called the field of blood to this day .
&quot; This is according to the words of Jeremiah the prophet , saying , &apos; They have used the thirty dollars , the price of the estimated , the estimated of the children of Israel .
I have bought a field for the tribe of the sons of Ammon , as the LORD commanded me .
Jesus stood before him , and he asked him , &quot; Are you the King of the Jews ? &quot; He said , &quot; Yes , you are .
When he was accused by the priests and elders , he answered nothing
Then said Pilate unto him , Didst thou not hear that they testify unto thee of all these things ?
And Jesus answered not , neither said he a word , so that the multitude was astonished
There is an ordinary custom of the guards , that , at this season , they release a prisoner to them , as the people desire .
At that time , there was a famous prisoner named Barabba
And it came to pass , when they were gathered together , that Pilate said unto them , Ye ask me to release unto you the one that is Barabbas , Jesus whom ye call Christ .
And they knew that they had redeemed him out of jealousy .
&quot; When he was sitting in the synagogue , his wife sent to him , saying , &apos; You have no control over this righteous man , for I have suffered much for him in my dreams today .
The chief priests and elders exhorted all the people to release Barabbas and to destroy Jesus
And the governor said unto the people , These two men , wilt thou that I release the one unto thee ? And they said , Barabbas
Then said Pilate , &quot; How shall I deal with Jesus , who is called Christ ? &quot; They all said , &quot; Kill him on the cross . &quot;
And they cried with a loud voice , and said , crucify him .
And when Pilate saw that it was not good for him to do so , he took water to wash his hands before the people , and said , &quot; Bring the blood of this righteous man , for the sin is not in me , but in you .
And all the people answered and said , His blood is returned to us and to our children .
Then Pilate released Barabbas to them , and whipped Jesus , and gave him to be crucified
Then the soldiers of the guard brought Jesus into the gate , and commanded the whole camp to gather themselves together in him .
They took off his clothes and put on a red robe
And he made a crown of thorns upon his head , and put a reed in his right hand , and kneeled before him , and made him play , saying , &quot; Congratulations , O king of the Jews !
And spit on his face , and strike his head with a reed ;
And when the play was finished , he took off his robe , and put on his own clothes , and took him out to crucify him .
When they came out , they met a Galilean named Simon , and urged him to go with them , to be on the cross of Jesus
&quot; And they came to a place called each other , which is a place of bones
Then the soldier took the bitter wine and gave it to Jesus ; and when he had tasted it , he would not drink it
And they crucified him , and divided his garments in lots
And he sat there and watched over him
And above his head was a sign writing his sins , saying , This is Jesus , the King of the Jews
At that time two robbers were crucified with him , one on the right hand and one on the left
Then the people who passed by laughed at him and shook their heads
&quot; If you destroy the temple and build it again in three days , save yourself ; and if you are the Son of God , come up from the cross .
&quot; The chief priests , the scribes , and the elders played him likewise , &quot; he said .
He has saved others , and cannot save himself ; He is the King of Israel , and we believe in Him , that He can come down from the cross
He trusts in God , and if God pleases him , He is able to save him ; for he said , &quot; I am the son of God .
&quot; The robber who was with him , and the robber who nailed him , also reproached him
From noon till the beginning of the day , it was dark all over the earth .
And it came to pass at the beginning of Zephaniah , that Jesus cried with a loud voice , saying , Elijah , Elijah , and Ramsabaroth , saying , My God , my God , why hast thou forsaken me
And when the men who stood there heard it , they said , This man calls Elijah .
And one of them ran away , and took a cloth full of vinegar , and tied it to a reed , and gave it to him to drink
The rest said , &quot; Wait and see if Elijah will come to save him . &quot;
Then Jesus cried again with a loud voice , and the spirit ceased
Suddenly the mantle of the temple was cut in half from top to bottom , and the earth trembled , and the rocks were broken .
And the tomb was opened , and the bodies of the saints that had fallen asleep were multiplied .
When Jesus was resurrected , they came out of the tomb , and entered the Holy City , and appeared to many
And when they saw the earthquake and the things that were done with him , they were exceeding afraid , saying , This is indeed the Son of God .
And there were many women watching afar off from Galilee , who followed Jesus and ministered unto him
Among them was Mary Magdalene , the mother of Jacob and Josiah , and Mary the mother of the two sons of Zebedee ,
And it came to pass at night , that there came a rich man named Joseph , of the tribe of the tribe of Elimathah , who was also a disciple of Jesus
And he went to see him , and asked for the body of Jesus , and he commanded him :
Joseph took his body and wrapped it in a clean cloth
And he laid him in his new tomb , which he had dug in a rock ; and he rolled the head of the great stone to the door of the tomb , and went .
And there was Mary Magdalene , and the same Mary , sitting at the tomb .
&quot; The next day , the second day of the Preparation Day , the priests and the Pharisees gathered together to see Pilate , and said ,
&quot; Lord , we remember the tempter , when he was still alive , saying , &apos; In three days I will be raised again . &apos; 
So he commanded them to keep the tomb in order until the third day , when his disciples would come and steal him away , and they would say to the people , &quot; He has been raised from the dead . &quot; Thus the confusion that followed would be more beneficial than the one before .
Then said Pilate , &quot; You have a guard , and go , do as you can , and keep your guard .
And they went with the guards , and sealed up the stones , and made the tomb a proper place for them .
&quot; The Sabbath will come to an end , the first day of the seven days , at the dawn of the day , to see Mary Magdalene and that Mary to the tomb .
And there was a great trembling , because the angel of the Lord came down from heaven , and rolled up the stone , and sat upon it
His appearance is like lightning , and his clothes are white as snow
For the watchman is as a dead man , and as a terror to him .
And the angel said unto the woman , Fear not : for I know that ye seek Jesus who is crucified
&quot; He is not here , but has been raised up according to what he has said . Come to the place of the Lord &apos;s rest
Go and tell his disciples , saying , &quot; He has been raised from the dead , and you will go to Galilee first , where you will see him . Behold , I have told you
Then the women hurried away from the tomb , fearing , and with great joy , and ran to offer their offerings to his disciples
Then Jesus came to them and said , &quot; Peace be to you ; &quot; and they rose up and worshipped him , holding on to his feet .
Jesus said to them , &quot; Don &apos;t be afraid . Go tell my brothers to go to Galilee , where you will see me
When they went , several of the guards entered into the city , and reported to the priests all that they had experienced .
Then the chief priest and the elders gathered themselves together , and spake to the soldiers , saying ,
&quot; You shall say , &apos; When we sleep at night , His disciples come and steal him
&quot; If this word is heard , and we persuade him , you shall be safe .
When the soldiers received the silver money , they did as they were commanded to do , according to the legend among the Jews , even to this day .
And the eleven went to Galilee , and came to the mountain which Jesus had set in appointment
When they saw Jesus , they worshipped him ; but there were doubts
Then Jesus came and said to them , &quot; All the powers of the heavens and the earth have been given to me
&quot; Therefore go and baptize the people in the name of the Holy Spirit of the Father , that they may be my disciples , or baptize them in the name of the Holy Spirit of the Father
&quot; Everything that I command you , and teach them to obey me , will always be with you to the end of the world .
The beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ , the Son of God
As it is written in the book of Isaiah the prophet , &quot; Behold , I will send My messenger before you , and I will prepare the way
In the wilderness there is a voice crying , &quot; Prepare the way of the Lord , and straighten his way . &quot;
According to this John came , baptizing in the wilderness , preaching the baptism of repentance , and forgiving sin
And all Judah and the people of Jerusalem went out to John , and confessed their sins , and were baptized in the Jordan .
John was clothed in camels &apos; hair , with a waistband , and ate locust bees
Then he proclaimed , &quot; There is a man who is greater than me in power than I am , and I bend my knees to remove his shoes , and he is unfit .
&quot; I am the water for you to wash , but he will wash for you with the Holy Spirit
At that time Jesus came from Nazareth of Galilee , and was baptized by John in the Jordan
And when he came up out of the water , he saw the heavens split , and the Holy Spirit descended upon him as a dove
And there was a voice from heaven saying , &quot; You are my beloved Son , and I rejoice in you
Then the Holy Spirit drove Jesus into the wilderness
And he was tested by Satan forty days in the wilderness , and he was with the beasts in one place : and there were angels waiting for him
After John &apos;s imprisonment , Jesus came to Galilee to preach the gospel of God
&quot; The days are fulfilled , and the kingdom of God is near ; so repent and believe in the gospel .
And he went down by the sea of Galilee , and saw Simon and Andrew his brother casting nets in the sea ; and they were fishermen
Jesus said to them , &quot; Follow me , and I will make you receive men as you receive fish
They immediately gave up the net and followed him
And Jesus went a little further , and saw Jacob the son of Zebedee , and John the brother of Jacob , repairing the nets in the ship .
Then Jesus greeted them , and they left their father Zebedee and the servants on the ship , and followed Jesus
And when he was come to Gagan , Jesus entered into the synagogue on the Sabbath day to teach
They marveled at his teaching , for he taught them as a man of authority , and not as a scribe .
There was a man in the synagogue who was bound by the devil , and he cried out
&quot; Jesus of Nazareth , what have we to do with you ? Have you come to destroy us ? I know who you are , the Holy One of God
Then Jesus reproached him , saying , &quot; Do not speak , but come out of this man
Then the devil cried out with a loud cry , and the man went out
And all the people were astonished , and asked one another , saying , What is this , a new doctrine ? And he commanded the devil by authority , and even the devil obeyed him
The fame of Jesus spread throughout Galilee
And when they were come out of the synagogue , they entered into the house of Simon and Andrew , with Jacob John .
And the mother of Simon lay sick of the fever , and a man cried unto Jesus
Jesus took his hand before him , and lifted him up , and the heat departed , and he served them
And it came to pass in the evening , when the sun was set , that a man came before Jesus with all the evildoers , and with the demons .
And all the people of the city gathered themselves together before the gate
Jesus healed many who were afflicted by various diseases , and He sent out many devils , and He did not allow them to speak , for the devils knew Him
In the morning of the next day , when the sun was not risen , Jesus arose and went into the wilderness , and prayed there
Simon and his companions pursued him
And when he had met them , he said unto them , All are seeking thee
Jesus said to them , &quot; We can go to another place , to the neighboring country , and I will preach there , for I came for this purpose
And he went into the synagogue throughout Galilee , and preached the devils
Then a great madman came to Jesus and knelt down and said to him , &quot; If you will , you will make me clean
Then Jesus moved with mercy , and touched him , saying , &quot; I will , and you shall be clean
As soon as the great madman left him , he was cleansed
And when Jesus had commanded him strictly , He sent him away
Then he said to him , &quot; Be careful , and do not tell anyone anything ; but go and examine the body to the priest , and present the gift which Moses commanded , as a proof to all the people , because he is clean for you
Then the man went out , and spoke many words , and preached it , saying that Jesus should no longer enter the city manifestly , but in the wilderness , and that he should be sent from every place
A few days later , Jesus entered again into the country of Capernaum , and the people heard him in the house
And many people gathered together , and there was not even space in front of the door , and Jesus spoke to them
&quot; A man came to Jesus with a paralyzed child , brought by four men
For it was not possible for many to come near , he demolished the house where Jesus was , and the roof of the house was demolished , and it was opened , and the paralyzed and the beds that were lying down were cut down
And when Jesus saw their confidence , he said unto the paralyzed , Son , thy sin is forgiven
Then some of the scribes sat there and reasoned in their hearts
Why does this man say this ? He speaks a blasphemy . Who can forgive sins besides God ?
Knowing this in their hearts , Jesus said , &quot; Why do you speak this in your hearts ?
Or say to the paralyzed , &quot; Your sin is forgiven you ; &quot; or , &quot; Arise , take your bed and walk ; &quot; that is easy .
&quot; But tell the paralyzed that you know that the Son of man has power to forgive sins on earth
&quot; I have commanded you to rise up and take your bed and go home
And he arose , and immediately took the bed , and went out before all the people ; and all the people were astonished and glorified , and said to God , We have never seen such a thing
Then Jesus went out again to the sea , and all the people followed him , and he taught them
And it came to pass , as Jesus passed by , that he saw Levi the son of Alphaeus sitting at the customs gate , and said unto him , Follow me : and he arose and followed Jesus .
When Jesus sat in the house of Levi , many taxpayers and sinners sat with him and his disciples , for many of them followed him
When the scribes among the Pharisees saw Jesus eating with the sinners and the tax collectors , they said to his disciples , &quot; Will he eat and drink with the tax collectors and the sinners ? &quot;
And when Jesus heard it , he said unto them , A healthy man hath no doctor , but a sick man : for I am not a caller of righteousness , but a caller of sinners
Now the disciples of John and the Pharisees were fasting , and they came to Jesus and said , &quot; Why are the disciples of John and the Pharisees fasting ? Why are your disciples not fasting ? &quot;
Jesus said to them , &quot; Can the bridegroom and his companions fast while they are with him , and the bridegroom while they are with him , and they cannot fast
&quot; But the days will come when the bridegroom will leave them , and on that day they will fast
No man sews a new cloth on an old cloth . I am afraid that the new cloth that is added will be bigger than the old cloth that is broken .
And no man put the new wine in the old sack . I fear that the wine will break the sack and that the wine and the sack will be broken . But put the new wine in the new sack
Jesus passed through the wheat field on the Sabbath day , and when his disciples were on their way , He took hold of the ears of the wheat
The Pharisees said to Jesus , &quot; Why do they do things that are impossible on the Sabbath ?
Jesus said to them , &quot; Have you not remembered what David and those who followed him did when they were hungry ?
&quot; When he entered the house of God in Abijah , when he was a great priest , he ate the table of cakes and gave them to his followers , which no man could eat except the priest
And he said unto them , The Sabbath is for man , and man is not for the Sabbath
Therefore the Son of man is the Lord of the Sabbath
Then Jesus entered the synagogue , and there was a man who had dried up a hand
And they peered at Jesus , and healed him on the Sabbath day , and not healed him ; that is , they should accuse him
Jesus said to the man with the dead hand , &quot; Arise and stand in the midst
And they said unto the people , Is it possible to do good and to do evil on the Sabbath day , and to save life and to destroy life ? And they did not speak .
Then Jesus looked at them with anger , and grieved their hearts , and said to him , &quot; Stretch out your hand , &quot; and he stretched out his hand , and his hand was restored .
&quot; The Pharisees went out and negotiated with the people of the tribe of Herod how they might destroy Jesus
Jesus and his disciples returned to the sea , and many followed him from Galilee
And when many heard of the great things which he had done , they came unto him from Judah , and from Jerusalem , and from Edom , and from beyond the Jordan , and from all sides of Rhodes .
And he commanded his disciples , because of the multitude , that a small ship should serve him , lest all the people should crowd him
&quot; He has healed many , so that all who are afflicted are crowded in to touch him .
Whenever the devil saw him , he fell down before him , and cried out , &quot; You are the Son of God
And again Jesus commanded them not to reveal Him
And when Jesus ascended the mountain , he called by his own will , and they came to him
And he made twelve men , that they should be with him continually , and that he should send them to preach .
and give them power to chase the devil
And the twelve had Simon , whom Jesus called Peter
And Jacob the son of Zebedee , and John the brother of Jacob ; and he called them half-Nichiah , which is the name of the lightning :
And Andrew , and Philip , and Bartholomew , and Matthew , and Thomas , and Jacob the son of Alphaeus , and Datah , and Simon the mighty ,
And Judas , a Galilean who sold Jesus
And when Jesus entered into a house , the people gathered together again , and he could not even eat
When Jesus &apos; relatives heard this , they came out to seize him , because they said that he was mad
And the scribes that came down from Jerusalem said , He is bound by Beth-zebu , and by the king of the devils , to chase the devils
Jesus called them and said to them in a parable , &quot; How can Satan drive out Satan
If a nation divides itself , it will not stand .
If a house is divided against itself , it will not stand .
&quot; If Satan fights with one another , he will not stand and die .
&quot; No man can enter the house of the mighty man and take away his furniture . He must first bind the mighty man and take away his house .
Verily I say unto you , All the sins of the world and all blasphemy shall be forgiven
Whoever blasphemes the Holy Spirit shall never be forgiven , but shall bear eternal sin
&quot; This is because they said , &apos; He is bound by the devil .
Now the mother of Jesus and his brethren stood by the side , and sent to call him
Many people sat around him and told him , &quot; Look , your mother and your brothers are looking for you outside
Jesus answered , &quot; Who is my mother , and who is my brother
Then he looked around at the people who sat around him , and said , &quot; Behold , my mother and my brothers
&quot; All who do the will of God are my brothers and sisters and my mothers
And Jesus taught by the sea : and many gathered themselves together unto him , and he was only to take a ship and sit down : and the ship was in the sea , and all the people stood on the shore by the sea
Jesus taught them many things in parables , and while he taught them , he said to them :
Listen , there &apos;s one planting . Go out and plant .
&quot; In the day of judgment , the birds of the field , which were by the wayside , were consumed .
There is one who falls on a shallow stone , and the soil is not deep , and grows fastest .
As soon as the sun comes out , it dries up because it has no roots
&quot; When a man falls into a thorn , and the thorn grows , and he is crushed , he will not be able to bear fruit .
And he that is laid down in good soil grows , and bears fruit thirty times , and sixty times , and one hundred times .
And said , &quot; He who has ears to hear , let him hear .
When there was no man , the men who followed Jesus and the twelve disciples asked him what this parable meant .
Jesus said to them , &quot; The secrets of the kingdom of God are only for you to know . If you speak to strangers , everything is a parable
&quot; When they see and see , they do not know ; when they hear and hear , they do not understand ; for I fear that they will turn back and be forgiven
Then said He unto them , Do ye not understand this parable ? how then can ye understand all parables ?
And that which the sower sows , it is the way .
And it came to pass , when the man who sat by the way heard the word , that Satan immediately came and took away the word which sat in his heart
And he that is laid on the stone shall be glad at once , when he heareth the word
But he had no root in his heart , neither was it temporary , and when he suffered or was compelled to do so , he fell down immediately
And that which is scattered in thorns , it is the man who hears .
Then the worldly worries , the confusion of money and riches , and other selfish desires came in and crowded the way , and they could not be established .
&quot; Whosoever is planted in a good land , thirty times , sixty times , and one hundred times will hear , and receive , and be made whole .
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; Do people bring lights and put them under the battlement , under the bed , and not on the lampstand ?
For that which is concealed is not manifest , and that which is concealed is not revealed .
If any have ears to hear , let them hear .
And say , &quot; Be careful of what you hear ; what measure do you give to men , and what measure will you give to you , and what measure will you give more to you ?
For he that is for him shall be given ; and he that is not shall be taken away , even all that he is .
And said , &quot; The kingdom of God is like the seeds of men that are planted on the earth .
When the night sleeps and the day rises , it grows and grows , and the man does not know how
The earthly fifth valley is natural . First seedlings , then long ears , then full grains on the ears
When the valley is ripe , it is cut down with a sickle ; for the time of harvest is come .
&quot; And what comparison can we make with the kingdom of God , and what metaphor can we use to show it ? &quot;
It is like a grain of mustard seed when it is planted in the earth , though it is fewer than a hundred seeds on the earth .
But when he hath planted it , he groweth , and is greater than every kind of meat , and hath grown great branches ; and even the birds of the heavens dwell in His shade .
Jesus spoke to them with many such parables , as they could hear
He speaks not unto them without a parable ; and in the days of no man he speaketh unto his disciples all the ways .
On that night Jesus said to his disciples , &quot; Let &apos;s go over there
When the disciples had left the crowd , Jesus was still in the ship , and they took him with them , and other ships were with him .
Suddenly there was a storm , and the waves entered the ship , and even the ship was full of water
And when Jesus was upon the stern of the ship , and was asleep on his pillow , the disciples called him and said unto him , Son of man , are we to die for you ?
Then Jesus awoke , and rebuked the wind , and said to the sea , &quot; Stay , and be quiet ; and the wind will cease , and be greatly calm . &quot;
Jesus said to them , &quot; Why are you afraid ? Have you not yet had faith
And they feared greatly , and said to one another , Who is this , even the wind and the sea have listened to him
They came to the sea , to the place of the Galatians
And when Jesus had come down from the ship , a man with a demon attached to him came out of the tomb and greeted him
&quot; He lives in the grave , and no man can bind him with chains , nor with iron chains .
For he was chained many times with fetters and chains , and the chains were broken by him , and the fetters were broken by him , and none could subdue him .
He cries day and night in the tombs and in the mountains , and cuts himself with stones
And when he saw Jesus afar off , he ran over to worship him
And they cried out with a loud voice , saying , &quot; What have I to do with you , Jesus , son of the Most High , that God has pleaded with you not to make me suffer ?
For Jesus commanded him , saying , &quot; Come out of this man , you devil
Jesus said to him , &quot; What is your name ? &quot; He answered , &quot; My name is the multitude , because we have many
And again they asked Jesus , saying , Let them not go out of the place
On the hillside there was a great herd of pigs eating
Then the devil cried to Jesus , saying , &quot; Please send us into the flock of pigs , attached to them
Then Jesus gave them permission , and the devil came out and entered into the pigs ; and the pigs went down the cliff , and were cast into the sea , and drowned ; and there were about two thousand of them
And the slayer fled , and preached to the people of the city and the country , and they came to see what was done .
When they came to Jesus , and saw the man who was bound by the devil , sitting , clothed in his garments , and being bound by a multitude of devils before , they perceived it in their hearts , and were afraid .
And when he saw it , he told all the people what he had seen with the companions of the devil , and what he had seen with the pigs .
And all the people begged Jesus to leave their borders
When Jesus was on the ship , the man who had been possessed by the devil was with him in prayer .
Jesus refused and said to him , &quot; Go home and tell your relatives what great things the Lord has done for you , and how he has mercy on you .
And he went down to Galilee , and preached the great things which Jesus had done for him ; and all the people were astonished
And when Jesus was in the ship , he passed over to the other side ; and many people gathered themselves together to him , and he was on the seashore
And there came a man of the synagogue , whose name was Jairus , to see Jesus , and fell down before his feet
Then he said to him , &quot; My little daughter is about to die , and I ask you to lay your hand on her , that she may be healed and live again
Then Jesus went with him , and many followed him , and crowded him
There was a woman who had a leak of blood for twelve years
He suffered a great deal in the hands of many doctors , and spent all that he had , and at one point he did not see well , and his condition became worse .
When he heard what Jesus had said , he came from behind and touched the garment of Jesus among the people .
&quot; I will heal myself only by touching his garments
So immediately the source of his blood leaked out , and he did so ; and he perceived that the plague had healed him .
Immediately Jesus , being able to go out of his own body , turned around among the people and said , &quot; Who touched my garment
&quot; The disciples said to him , &quot; You see the crowds crowding you , and who touches me ? &quot;
He looked around and saw the woman who was doing this
And when the woman knew what was done to her , she bowed down before Jesus with fear and trembling , and told him all the truth
Jesus said to him , &quot; Daughter , your faith has saved you . Go back in peace , and your affliction is healed .
&quot; When I was speaking , a man from the house of the synagogue said to me , &quot; Why should your daughters die , sir ?
When Jesus heard what he said , he said to the synagogue , &quot; Do not be afraid , but believe
And he took Peter , and Jacob , and John the brother of Jacob , and said , No man shall go with him
And when they came to the house of the synagogue , Jesus saw there a great cry and a great mourning
And when he entered , he said to them , &quot; Why do you weep ? The child is not dead , but asleep .
