And those who are wrought by the devils , and are healed ;
And all the people desired to touch him , because he had the power to come out of him and to heal them
Jesus lifted up his eyes and said to his disciples , &quot; Blessed are your poor people , for the kingdom of God is yours
Blessed are those who are hungry , for they shall be filled ; and blessed are those who weep , for they shall laugh .
Blessed are you when men hate you for their own sakes , reject you , scoff at you , and forsake your name for evil
And on that day ye shall jump in joy : for your reward in heaven is great : and so were their fathers prophets .
Blessed are the rich among you , because you have received your comfort
Woe to those who are full of you , for they will starve ; woe to those who laugh , for they will mourn and weep
&quot; They say , &apos; Woe to you , when it is good for you , &apos; because their ancestors were false prophets .
&quot; But I tell you , those who listen to me , that your enemies will love him , and those who hate you will be kind to him
Curse yourselves , and bless Him ; and insult yourselves , and pray for Him .
A man shall strike your face on this side , and his face on that side ; and a man shall take away your coat , and his coat shall be taken away .
&quot; He who asks of you will give it to him ; and someone will take away what you have , and there will be no need to return .
What do you want men to do to you , and what do you want men to do to you
If you love only those who love you , what is your reward ? For sinners also love those who love them .
If you do good to those who do good to you , what is your reward ? Even so do sinners .
If you lend to a man , and expect to receive it back from him , what is your reward ? The sinner also lends to the sinner , and receives it back as a number .
&quot; You shall love your enemies , and be kind to them , and lend them without expectation of repayment . Your reward will be great , and you will be the sons of the Most High , for He has mercy on the unthankful and the wicked .
Be merciful , as your Father is merciful .
If you do not condemn , you will not be condemned ; if you do not condemn , you will not be condemned ; if you forgive , you will be forgiven .
And whatsoever ye shall give unto man shall be given unto you , and shall fall upon your wrists with a full lifting , and with a shovel , from the top to the bottom ; for whatsoever measure ye shall give unto man , whatsoever measure ye shall give unto you .
Then Jesus said to them in a parable , &quot; Can a blind man take a blind man , and both of them fall into the pit ?
