Then said the Lord , &quot; What shall I use more than these generations , and what shall they be like ?
&quot; It is as if children were sitting on the streets , calling to one another , saying , &apos; We are whistling to you , you are not dancing , we are weeping to you , you are not weeping
&quot; John , the baptized , came not to eat bread , nor to drink wine ; and you say that he was possessed by demons
&quot; The Son of man comes and eats and drinks , and you say that he is a drunkard and a friend of the tax collectors and sinners .
But the sons of wisdom are all in wisdom
There was a Pharisee who asked Jesus to eat with him , and Jesus went to the Pharisees and sat down
And there was a woman in the city , a sinner ; and when she knew that Jesus was sitting in the house of Pharisees , she took a jar full of ointment
And they stood behind him , weeping at his feet , and tears wet his feet , and wiped their hair , and kissed his feet with their mouths , and anointed them with oil
Then the Pharisees of Jesus asked him to see it , and said in their hearts , &quot; If this man were a prophet , he would know who touched him , and what kind of woman he was , and he was a sinner
Jesus said to him , &quot; Simon , I have something to say to you . &quot; Simon said , &quot; Father , say
Jesus said , &quot; There is a debtor , and two men owe him , one fifty-two and one fifty-two
Because they were unable to repay , the creditor pardoned the debts of their two ; and the other loved him more
Then Simon answered , &quot; I think he is the one who is most forgiving . &quot; Jesus said , &quot; It is good that you have said no
Then he turned to the woman , and said to Simon , &quot; Do you see this woman ? I came into your house , and you did not water my feet , but she wet my feet with tears and dried my hair
&quot; You did not kiss me , but when this woman came in from me , she did not live and kissed my feet with her mouth .
&quot; You have not anointed my head with oil , but this woman anointed my feet with oil
Therefore I tell you that he has forgiven many sins , because he loves more ; but when he forgives less , his love is less .
Then he said to the woman , &quot; Your sin is forgiven
In the hearts of those who were with him they said , &quot; Who is this who forgives sins ?
Jesus said to the woman , &quot; Your faith has saved you . Go back in peace .
After a few days Jesus went around the cities and villages preaching the gospel of the kingdom of God , and with him were twelve disciples
And among the women who were afflicted by the devil , and afflicted by sickness , and were healed , was Mary , called Magdalene ; and seven devils were driven out of him .
And Joanna the wife of the house of Herod , and Susanna , and many other women , who had been slaughtered by the hand of the fathers of the children of Israel , served Jesus and his disciples with their possessions
When many people gathered together , and some came out of the cities to see Jesus , Jesus spoke in a parable
And a sower went forth to sow ; and in the time of sowing , there fell a man by the wayside , and he was trampled ; and the birds of the heaven were consumed .
As for those who fall on rocks , they are dry from thence for lack of nourishment .
&quot; There is one that falls in thorns , and the thorns grow together , and crowd them .
Then there was a tree that was laid down in good soil , and grew up , and became a hundredfold fruitful ; and when Jesus had said this , He spoke with a loud voice , He that has ears to hear should hear
The disciples asked Jesus , &quot; What does this parable mean
He said , &quot; The secrets of the kingdom of God are only for you to know , and for others they use metaphors to make them see and see and see and hear and hear not .
That is the parable ; and the seed is the way of God .
Those who were by the way were men who heard the word , and then the devil came from their hearts and took away the word , lest they believed in salvation .
Those who are on rocks hear and rejoice , but have no root in their hearts , and have no temporary faith ; and they turn away when they are tested .
&quot; The one who falls in the thorns is the one who hears the word , and walks away , and is surrounded by the thought of the present , and by the joy of riches and wealth , so that no ripe seeds come forth .
&quot; It is in the good land that a man hears the word , and keeps it in the heart of a good and true heart , and endures the truth .
&quot; No man lights a lamp on a vessel or under a bed , but on a lampstand , and lets those who come in see the light .
For what is concealed is not manifest , and what is concealed is not made known .
Therefore be careful how ye hear : for to him that hath it shall be added , and to him that hath not it shall be taken away , even as he thinketh it to be .
The mother of Jesus and his brethren came because of the multitude who could not follow him
&quot; So someone told him , &quot; Your mother and your brothers are standing outside to see you
Jesus answered , &quot; My mother and my brothers are the ones who have listened to God &apos;s word and followed it .
One day Jesus and his disciples boarded a ship , and said to them , &quot; We can go over to the side of the lake , &quot; and they sailed
While he was walking , Jesus fell asleep . Suddenly there was a storm on the lake , and the ship was filled with water , and it was very dangerous
Then the disciples awoke him , and said , &quot; O husband , husband , we have lost our lives ; &quot; and Jesus awoke , and rebuked the great wind , and the wind ceased , and was quiet .
Jesus said to them , &quot; Your faith is in it ; &quot; and they feared and wondered , saying to each other , &quot; Who is this ? He commanded the wind and the water , and the wind and the water also obeyed Him
And they came unto the place of the Gerasen , which was before Galilee .
And when Jesus was come to the shore , a man of the city , who was possessed by the devil , appeared to him , and he was not clothed , nor dwelled in a house , but lived in a tomb for a long time .
And when he saw him , he bowed down before him , and cried with a loud voice , saying , &quot; What have I to do with you , Jesus , Son of the Most High , that you do not make me suffer
For Jesus commanded the devil to come out of him ; and the devil seized him many times , and he was kept by men , and was chained with chains and fetters ; and he broke the chain , and was driven into the wilderness by the devil
And he said unto him , What is thy name ? And he said , My name is the multitude , because of the multitude of the devils that are with him
Then the devil begged Jesus not to command them to go into the pit without foundation
And there was a great multitude of pigs eating on the mountain : and the devil besought Jesus that they should enter into the pigs , and Jesus gave them permission
Then the devil came out of him and entered into the pig , and the pigs went down the cliff , and drowned in the lake .
And when the shepherd saw it , he fled , and told the people of the city and the country
When they came to Jesus , and saw the man who had left the demon sitting at his feet , clothed in clothing , and understood in his heart , they were afraid
&quot; When he sees this , he will tell them how to save those who are bound by the devil .
And all the people that were round about Galilee , being very afraid , asked Jesus to go away from them , and he went back on the ship .
The man who had left the devil was with Jesus , and he begged , and Jesus sent him back
&quot; Go home and tell God what great things He has done for you , &quot; he said . Then he went about the city preaching what great things He had done for Him
When Jesus came back , all the people welcomed him , for they were waiting for him
And there came a certain man of the synagogue , named Jairus , and fell down before Jesus &apos; feet , and asked him to come to his house
For he had a single daughter , about twelve years old , and was about to die ; and when Jesus was gone , the people crowded him
&quot; There was a woman whose blood had leaked for twelve years , and all that the doctor had given her to nourish her had been spent on her ; and there was none to cure her
And when he came behind him , he touched his garment , and immediately the blood leaped and stopped .
Jesus said , &quot; Who touched me ? &quot; They all refused . Peter and those who were with him said , &quot; Father , the crowds are gathered together against you .
Jesus said , &quot; Man touches me , because I feel the power to go out of me
Knowing that she could not hide herself , the woman bowed down in fear before Jesus &apos; feet , and touched him for his sake , and how it was done , when she had spoken to all the people
Jesus said to him , &quot; Daughter , your letter has saved you . Go in peace
&quot; When I was speaking , someone from the household of the synagogue said , &quot; Your daughter is dead , and you do not want a laborer
When Jesus heard it , he said to him , &quot; Don &apos;t be afraid ; if you believe , your daughter will be saved
&quot; When Jesus came to his house , no one was allowed to enter with him except Peter , John , Jacob , and the parents of his daughters
And all the people wept for her ; and Jesus said , Do not weep ; for he is not dead , but asleep .
And when they knew that the daughter was dead , they mocked Jesus
Then Jesus took his hand and called and said , &quot; Daughter , arise
Then his soul returned , and immediately he arose , and Jesus commanded him to eat
His parents were astonished , and Jesus commanded them not to bring to light what they had done .
Jesus summoned the twelve disciples , giving them power and power to overcome all devils , and to heal all diseases
And sent them to preach the way of the kingdom of God , and to heal the sick
They said to them , &quot; When you are on the way , you shall not bring a staff , nor a pocket , nor food , nor silver , nor two coats .
&quot; Whether you enter the house , you will live there , and you will walk from there .
&quot; Whoever does not receive you , when you leave the city , stamp down the dust on your feet , to testify that they are not
Then the disciples went out , and spread the gospel in every country , and healed everywhere
And when Herod the king of the sepulchre heard all that Jesus had done , he was troubled , because some said , John is risen from the dead
Then another said , &quot; Elijah has appeared , &quot; and another said , &quot; A prophet of old is alive
And Herod said , John , who is this that I have been crucified , and that I would see him , when I have heard of such things
Then the apostles returned , and told Jesus what they had done ; and he took them away in secret from there to a city called Bethsaida
And when they knew it , they followed him , and Jesus received them , and spoke to them of the way of the kingdom of God , and healed those who needed healing .
The twelve disciples came to him at the beginning of the day , saying , &quot; Please let everyone go away , that they may go to the villages to lodge and eat ; for we are in the wilderness
Jesus said to them , &quot; Eat for them . &quot; The disciples said , &quot; We have only five loaves and two fishes , and we will not buy food for so many to go to
And Jesus said unto his disciples , Sit down row after row , about fifty men in row after row .
And the disciples did so , and all the people sat down
And Jesus took the five loaves , and the two fishes , and broke them , and blessed the heavens , and presented them to the disciples before the people
And they ate , and were filled ; and they took up the rest , and filled the twelve baskets
When Jesus himself was praying , the disciples were there with him , and Jesus asked them , &quot; Who am I ? &quot;
They said , &quot; John the Baptizer , &quot; and &quot; Elijah , &quot; and &quot; A prophet from the ancients is alive . &quot;
Jesus said , &quot; Your door says , &apos; Who am I ? &apos; Peter answered , &apos; The Christ of God
Jesus strongly commanded them not to bring this matter to the people
&quot; The Son of man must suffer many things , and be rejected by the elders , the chief priests , and the scribes , and be killed , and be raised up on the third day
And Jesus said unto the people , If any man follow me , let him give himself , and come every day on his cross , and follow me
For whosoever shall save his own life shall lose it ; and whosoever shall lose it for me shall save it .
If a man earneth all the world , but loseth himself , and repayeth himself , what profit is there ?
&quot; Whoever makes me ashamed and my way ashamed shall be ashamed when the Son of man comes in his own glory , and in the glory of the Father and the Holy Angel .
Verily I say unto you , Whosoever standeth here shall see the kingdom of God before the taste of death .
And it came to pass about eight days after he had spoken these words , that Jesus went up with Peter , John , and Jacob , and prayed
When he was praying , his face was changed , and his clothes were clean and shining
And suddenly two men of Moses spoke to Jesus , saying ,
And they appeared in glory , and spoke of the death of Jesus , that which he should do in Jerusalem
And Peter and his companions fell asleep , and when they were awakened , they saw the glory of Jesus , and the two that stood with him
When they were about to be separated from Jesus , Peter said to him , &quot; Father , it is good that we are here , and we can set up three tents , one for you , one for Moses , and one for Elijah , &quot; but he did not know what he was saying .
When they spoke these words , a cloud covered them , and they were afraid as they entered into it .
A voice came out of the clouds , saying , &quot; This is my son , whom I have chosen ; this is my beloved Son from ancient times , whom you will listen to . &quot;
The voice stopped , and there was only one Jesus ; and in those days the disciples did not report what they had seen , neither did they report it to the people .
And it came to pass on the second day , when they were come down from the mountain , that many came to meet Jesus
And one of them cried out , and said , Son , look upon my son , for he is my only son
And when he was seized by the devil , he cried out , and the devil made him mad , and poured out his mouth , and heavily hurt him , and it was hard for him to leave him
&quot; I have asked your disciples to drive out the devil , but his door is not open .
Jesus said , &quot; What time will I be here with you , O generation that is disbelieving and perverse , and enduring you ? Bring your son here
And it came to pass in the time of coming , that the devil threw him down , and made him mad again and again : and Jesus rebuked the devil , and healed the child , and gave it to his father .
And all the people marveled at the great power of God : and it came to pass , when all the people wondered about all that Jesus had done , that Jesus said unto his disciples :
You shall keep these words in your ears , for the Son of man shall be delivered into the hand of man .
&quot; They do not understand the word , and the meaning is hidden , so that they cannot understand it , and they dare not ask the meaning of it .
And there was a discussion among the disciples concerning who would be the greatest
And when Jesus saw the argument in their hearts , he took a little child and made him stand by himself
He said to them , &quot; Whoever receives this child in my name receives me ; and whoever receives me receives him who sent me ; and the least of you will be the greatest
John said , &quot; Father , when we saw a man chasing away demons in your name , we forbade him , because he did not follow you with us
Jesus said , &quot; Do not forbid him , for he who does not oppose you is helping you
The day came when Jesus was raised up , and he decided to go to Jerusalem
And he sent messengers before him , and they came to a village in Samaria to prepare for him
The people of that city did not receive him , because he went to Jerusalem
When his disciples Jacob and John saw it , they said , &quot; Lord , do you want us to command fire to come down from heaven to destroy them , as Elijah did ? &quot;
Jesus turned and reproached the two disciples , saying , &quot; What is your heart , and you do not know
&quot; The Son of man came not to destroy man , but to save him , &quot; he said , &quot; and went to other villages . &quot; &#91; There are only fifty-fifth and fifty-sixth verses of the Old Testament &#93;
When they were walking , a man said to Jesus , &quot; Wherever you go , I will follow you
Jesus said , &quot; The fox has a hole , and the bird of the sky has a nest , but the son of man has no pillow
Then he said to a man , &quot; Come with me . &quot; He said , &quot; Lord , let me go back and bury my father
Jesus said , &quot; Let the dead bury their dead , and you will preach the word of God only
Then another said , &quot; Lord , I will follow you , but let me first leave my family . &quot;
Jesus said , &quot; Those who look back with their hands on the plow are not worthy of the kingdom of God .
And after this the Lord set up seventy men , two of them and two of them , to go before him to the cities where he would go .
Then said He to them , &quot; There is more to be harvested and fewer to work ; so you , as the Lord of the harvest , send out workers to harvest His harvest .
&quot; Go , and I will send you out like a lamb into the flock of wolves
Don &apos;t carry pockets , don &apos;t carry pockets , don &apos;t carry shoes , and don &apos;t ask for peace on the way
&quot; Whenever you enter that house , say first , &quot; Peace be to this house
&quot; If there is in it a man of peace , the peace you seek will come to that house , or it will return to you .
Ye shall dwell therein , and eat and drink of that which they have provided ; for it is right for the workers to be paid their wages ; and ye shall not move from this house unto that house
&quot; Whether you enter that city , if any man receives you , what shall he offer you , and what shall you eat
to heal the sick in the city , and to say to them , &quot; The kingdom of God is near to you
&quot; Whether you go into that city , if no man receives you , you will go into the streets
&quot; The dust of your cities is on our feet , and we wipe it off with you ; yet you should know that the kingdom of God is near .
&quot; I tell you , that in the days of judgment , what was suffered in Sodom is easier to suffer than that city .
Woe unto thee , O flood of Gorah , woe unto thee , O Bethsaida ! for if the power which was done among you were done in Tyre , they would have repented , sitting on the earth in ashes .
Is it easier to suffer than you in the days of judgment ?
&quot; You have ascended to heaven , O Canaan , and in the future you will be brought down into the darkness .
Then he said to the disciples , &quot; Listen to you , and listen to me , and forsake you , and forsake me , and forsake me , and forsake those who sent me
Then the seventy returned rejoicing , saying , &quot; Lord , in your name the devil has subdued us .
Jesus said to them , &quot; I have seen Satan fall from heaven like a lightning
&quot; I have given you power to trample serpents and scorpions , and I have overcome all enemies , and nothing can harm you .
But you shall rejoice not because of the devil , but because of the record of your name in heaven .
And it came to pass at that time , when Jesus was moved by the Holy Spirit , that he rejoiced , and said , &quot; Father , Lord of the heavens and the earth , I thank you , for you have hid these things to the wise and to the wise , and for you have made them manifest to the little ones ; and indeed , Father , for so is your goodness .
&quot; All things are delivered to me by my Father . No one knows who the Son is except the Father . No one knows who the Father is except what the Son and the Son will command him .
Then Jesus turned and said to his disciples , &quot; Blessed is the eye that sees what you see
&quot; I tell you , there were many prophets and kings before , who saw what you saw but did not see , and listened what you heard but did not hear .
Then a scribe stood up to examine Jesus , and said , &quot; O my husband , what shall I do that I may live forever
Jesus said to him , &quot; What is written in the law , and what do you think ?
He answered , &apos; You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart , with all your soul , with all your strength , with all your heart , and you shall love your neighbor as yourself .
Jesus said , &quot; You answered , &apos; If you do this , you will have eternal life
Then he said to Jesus , &quot; Who is my neighbor ? &quot;
Then Jesus answered and said , &quot; A certain man went down from Jerusalem to Jericho , and fell into the hands of the robbers , and they stripped him of his garments , and beat him to death , and threw him away .
And it came to pass , that a priest came down from this way , and passed over there , when he saw him
Then another Levite came to the place , and saw him , and passed over from there likewise .
And there came to him a Samaritan by foot , and when he saw him , he was moved with mercy .
He poured oil and wine on his wounds , and wrapped him , and helped him to ride on his own cattle , and brought him into the store to take care of him .
Then on the second day he took out two pieces of silver and gave them to the owner of the store , saying , &quot; You shall do according to him , and I will return to you for all the expenses you have incurred .
&quot; What do you think of these three men , and of the neighbor that fell into the hands of the robbers ?
Jesus said to him , &quot; Go and do likewise
As they walked , Jesus entered into a village . A woman named Martha took him to her own house
And he had a sister named Mary , who sat at the feet of Jesus , and heard his word
And when he was filled with many things to serve , he went in and said , &quot; Lord , do you not care that my sister leaves me alone to serve ? Command him to help me
Jesus answered , &quot; Ma &apos;am , Ma &apos;am , you are troubled by many things
But there is not less than one , and Mary , having chosen the good reward , cannot be taken away .
And when the prayer was finished , a disciple said unto him , Ask the Lord to guide us in our prayers , as the disciples of John taught him
Jesus said , &quot; When you pray , say , &apos; Father in heaven , let all men honor your name ; let your kingdom come , and let your will be done on the earth as it is done in heaven . &apos; &quot;
Give to us daily our daily food ,
Forgive us our sins , for we also forgive all those who owe us ; and let us not be tempted ; save us from evil .
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; Who among you has a friend ? &quot; They came to him at midnight and said , &quot; Friend , lend me three loaves
&quot; Because I have a friend who comes to me on foot , and I have nothing for him
Then the man answered , &quot; Do not disturb me ; the door is shut , and the children are in bed with me , and I cannot come up to you
&quot; I tell you , not because he is a friend , but because of his words , and because of his urgency , he will be given what he needs .
&quot; And I tell you again , &apos; Your prayers will be given to you , and your search will be found , and your doors will be opened by knocking .
For he that prayeth receiveth , and he that seeketh findth ; and he that knocketh openeth unto him the door .
&quot; Who among you who is a father has a son who seeks bread instead of stone , and seeks fish instead of snakes ?
Ask for eggs , and give him scorpions
&quot; You are not good , but know that you give good things to your children ; and the Father of heaven gives the Holy Spirit to those who seek Him
Jesus chased out a devil who called man dumb ; and when the devil went out , the dumb spoke , and all the people were astonished
&quot; But some among them said , &apos; He is the king of the devil , and he has driven away the devils .
And another man sought Jesus , and asked him for signs from heaven
Knowing their thoughts , he said to them , &quot; A nation divided against itself will become a wilderness , and a family divided against itself will be defeated .
&quot; If Satan had divided himself , how could his kingdom stand ? For you say , &apos; I have been driven away by the devils of Bethel . &apos; 
&quot; If I rely on Belize to cast out demons , and on your sons to cast out demons , then they will judge your evil deeds .
&quot; If I defeat the devil by the power of God , then the kingdom of God will come to you
And the mighty man was clothed , and guarded his house , and all of him was safe
But there came a mightier than he , and he overcame him , and took away his armor and his weapons , and divided his spoil .
He who is not with me is an enemy to me ; and he who is gathered together is dispersed .
Then the devil departed from him , and came and passed in the land without water , seeking rest ; and he found it not , and said , &quot; I will return to the house from which I came .
When you get there , you &apos;ll see that the inside is cleaned and repaired
Then he took seven other devils , worse than himself , and went in to dwell therein ; and the end of that man was worse than the beginning .
As he spoke these words , a woman among the multitudes said , &quot; Blessed are those who bear and nurture you
Jesus said , &quot; Yes , but it is less good for a man who obeys the way of God
And it came to pass , when they were gathered together , that Jesus began to speak , saying , &quot; This generation is a generation of evil , and they seek to see signs , and there is no sign for them , except the sign of Jonah .
How was Jonah a sign to the Ninevites , and how was the Son of man a sign to this generation ?
&quot; When it is judged , the Queen of the South shall rise up to judge this generation &apos;s sins ; for he has come from the ends of the earth to hear Solomon &apos;s wisdom . Behold , there is a greater man than Solomon in this place .
And it shall come to pass at the time of judgment , that the children of Nineveh shall rise up and make atonement for this generation ; and they shall repent , because they have heard that which Jonah hath spoken unto the children of Nineveh : behold , there is a greater man than Jonah in this place .
No man puts a lamp in the ground , or under the fountain , and always puts it on a lampstand , so that those who come in may see the light
Your eyes are lights on your body ; if your eyes are bright , they are all bright ; if your eyes are dim , they are all dark .
Therefore beware , lest the light or darkness be in your head
&quot; If your whole body is light , and there is no darkness , it will be full of light , as the brightness of a lamp illuminates you .
As he spoke , a Pharisee asked Jesus to eat with him , and Jesus entered and sat down
When the Pharisees saw that Jesus was not washing his hands before the meal , they were astonished
And the Lord said unto him , Now ye Pharisees wash yourselves outside the table , and your faces are full of lust and evil
&quot; Are you , O man of ignorance , making an outer face , or an inner face ?
&quot; As long as you give to people what is in you , everything is clean to you
Woe to you , Pharisees ! For you did not perform the righteous act of loving God by offering one tenth of the flour and of the spices and of all kinds of herbs , which you did , and which you did not do , nor could you do .
Woe to you , Pharisees , for you are the first in the synagogue , and the first to ask your peace in the streets .
&quot; Woe to you ! For you are like an unrevealed tomb , and you walk on it without knowing .
Then one of the scribes answered Jesus , &quot; Father , you have also spoiled us by saying this
&quot; Woe to your lawyers , &quot; Jesus said , &quot; because you laid the burden of the burden on people and did not move one finger of your head
&quot; Woe to you , for you have built the tomb of the prophet , whom your fathers killed .
Behold , what your fathers did , you proved it and liked it ; for they killed the prophets , and you repaired their graves .
Therefore God said in wisdom , &quot; I will send the prophets and the apostles to them , and some of them will kill and some of them will oppress
The sins of the prophet &apos;s blood , which have been poured out since the foundation of the world , shall be asked of this generation
From the blood of Abel even to the blood of Zechariah , who was slain in the midst of the altar and the temple ; and I tell you , these things shall be asked of this generation .
Blessed are your lawyers , for you have taken away the keys of knowledge , and you have prevented those who are about to go in from entering ;
Then Jesus came out from there , and the scribes and the Pharisees pressed him with great force , and urged him to speak more
To spy in secret , to take hold of his word
At that time , tens of thousands of people gathered together and trampled one another , and Jesus began to speak and said to his disciples , &quot; You must guard against the yeast of the Pharisees , which is false for good
There is nothing hidden that is not revealed . There is nothing hidden that is not known .
Therefore what you say in the darkness shall be heard in the clear place ; and what you say in the inner room shall be proclaimed in the room .
&quot; My friends , I say to you , &apos; There is nothing that can be done after the slaughter of the body , and do not fear them .
&quot; I will tell you who you are afraid of , and who is to be cast into hell after he has killed you . I tell you that you are afraid of him .
&quot; Are not five sparrows sold for two pieces of silver , and not one of them is forgotten in the sight of God ?
&quot; Your hair is counted , and you are no more precious than many sparrows . Don &apos;t be afraid .
&quot; I also tell you that whoever recognizes Me before men , the Son of man will recognize Him before the angel of God .
&quot; He who does not recognize Me in the sight of men will not recognize Him in the sight of the messenger of God
Whoever speaks and acts as a criminal shall be forgiven ; and whoever defiles the Holy Spirit shall not be forgiven .
&quot; You shall not be brought into the synagogue , nor into the courts , nor into the hands of those who have authority .
For at that time the Holy Spirit will teach you what to say
One of the people said to Jesus , &quot; Father , tell my brother and me to separate our households
Jesus said , &quot; Who , you man , has made me an officer in your affairs to divide your households ?
Then He said to them , &quot; Be careful of yourselves , and avoid all greed , for the life of man is not enriched by the household .
And he said to them in a parable , &quot; There is a rich man whose fields are full
What shall I do if I have no place to collect my produce
And I will do so ; I will break down my barn , and cover it with a larger one , wherein I will gather all my food and all my possessions .
Then say unto my soul , O soul , thou hast many treasures to store up for many years , and thou shalt eat and drink and be merry .
But God said to him , &quot; Tonight , O foolish man , you need your soul ; to whom will you return what you have prepared ? &quot;
Thus is it with those who accumulate wealth for themselves , but are not rich in the sight of God
Then Jesus said to his disciples , &quot; So I tell you , do not worry about what you eat for your life , or what you wear for your body
For life is better than food , and the body than clothing
How much more valuable are you than the birds that fly , that you will neither plant nor harvest , neither have a barn nor a storehouse , and God is holy and sustains him
&quot; How can one of you increase his life by a moment , or by an elbow ?
Why do you worry about the least thing , which you are not able to do ?
