They said , &quot; Lord , he has passed through ten ingots
&quot; I tell you , &quot; said the master , &quot; that all that is there will be added to him ; and that which is not will be taken , even all that he has ,
&quot; If my enemies do not want me to be their king , take them and kill them before me
When Jesus had finished speaking these words , he went ahead and went up to Jerusalem
And he came near to Bethphah and to Berdan in a mountain called Mount Olives , and sent two disciples , saying ,
&quot; Go to the opposite village , and when you enter , you will see a donkey tied therein , which no man has ever ridden , and it can be pulled apart .
&quot; If anyone asks what it is for , you will say , &apos; Use it primarily . &apos; 
&quot; The man who sent went and met him , as Jesus said
When they had loosed the donkeys , the master asked them , &quot; What did you do to loose the donkeys
&quot; They said , &quot; It &apos;s mainly for him
They took him to Jesus , and put their clothes on him , and helped him to ride
When they were going , all laid their clothes on the road
And it came to pass , when Jerusalem was near , and the mount of Olives was coming down , that all the disciples rejoiced because of all the wonders which they had seen , and praised God with a loud voice
&quot; A king who comes in the name of the Lord is to be praised . Peace is in heaven , and glory in the highest places .
Some of the Pharisees among the people said to Jesus , &quot; Son , reproach your disciples
Jesus said , &quot; I tell you , if they do not shut their mouths and say , &apos; These stones must be called
Immediately Jesus came to Jerusalem to see the city and wept for him
&quot; You will not know in this day what is in your peace , but it is hidden , so that your eyes will not see it .
&quot; For the days will come , and your enemies will set up barriers around you , and they will surround you , and they will engulf you on all sides .
&quot; He will destroy you and your children , and not one stone will remain on the stone ; for you do not know when you will be visited .
Jesus entered the temple and drove out the merchants
And he said to them , &quot; It is written , &apos; My house will be a house of prayer . &apos; And you have made him a thief &apos;s nest
Jesus taught in the temple daily , and the chief priests and the scribes and the princes of the people wanted to kill him
But he did not find a law , because all the people listened to him .
One day , when Jesus was teaching the people in the temple and preaching the gospel , the chief priests and the scribes and the elders came
Then said he , &quot; Tell us , by what authority do you do these things , and who gave you this authority ?
Jesus answered and said , &quot; I will also ask you a question , and you will report to me .
The baptism of John came from heaven , and from among men .
And they reasoned among themselves , saying , &quot; If we say from heaven , he will say , &apos; Why do you not believe him ?
&quot; If it were from among men , the people would slay us with stones , because they believed that John was a prophet .
Then he answered , &quot; I do not know where it came from
Jesus said , &quot; I do not tell you what authority I have to do these things
Jesus , by parable , said to the people , &quot; Someone planted a vineyard and rented it to a gardener , and went abroad to live for a long time
And it came to pass at that time , that he sent a servant to the gardener , that they should give him the fruit of the garden ; and the gardener struck him , and sent him away empty-handed .
Then they sent a servant , and they struck him , and insulted him , and caused him to return empty-handed
And sent forth a third servant , and they wounded him , and threw him out
Then said the gardener , &quot; What shall I do ? I shall send my beloved son away , or they will respect him
And when the gardeners saw him , they reasoned among themselves , saying , This is the inheritance ; let us kill him , and let the inheritance be ours .
Then they cast him out of the vineyard , and killed him ; and how shall the lord of the vineyard deal with them ?
&quot; He will come to destroy these gardeners , and will give the vineyards to others . &quot; The people who heard said , &quot; This is impossible
Jesus looked at them and said , &quot; It is written , &apos; The stone which the craftsman left has become the headstone of the corner of the house . &apos; &quot;
Whoever falls on that stone must be crushed ; and whoever the stone falls on , it will crush him to the ground .
When the scribes and the chief priests saw that the parable was about what they were saying , they wanted to smite him and take him , but feared the people
Then they spyed on him , and made him to be a good man , and to have power over his words , and to put him under the rulership of the visitation
Then the adulteress said to Jesus , &quot; O husband , we know that what you have spoken is true , and that you do not take the appearance of a man , but that it is the way of the truthfulness of God .
We pay taxes to Caesar , yes or no
When Jesus saw their deceit , He spoke to them
&quot; Take me a penny and show me who it is , like this , and like this . &quot; They said , &quot; It is Caesar .
Jesus said , &quot; The things of Caesar belong to Caesar , and the things of God belong to God
They were a people , and had no power over it ; and they wondered at his answer , and shut their mouths .
And Satan often said that there was no resurrection : and several came to Jesus and said :
&quot; O husband , &quot; Moses wrote for us , &quot; A man who has a wife and has no children dies , and his brothers take his wife and raise up children for his brothers
There were seven brothers . The first took a wife and died without children .
The second , the third , also married him
And the seven married him , and died without children .
The next woman died too
So he will be the wife in the resurrection , because all seven of them have married him .
Jesus said , &quot; The men of this world marry each other .
Only the world will be worthy of those who are raised from the dead , neither to marry nor to marry .
For they shall not die again , as the angels : for they are the sons of God , both of the resurrected .
As for the resurrection of the dead , Moses made clear in the book of thorns that the Lord was the God of Abraham , the God of Isaac , and the God of Jacob
God is not the God of the dead , but the God of the living ; for all men are alive therein
Some of the scribes said , &quot; Friend , you speak well
Then they dare not ask him anything again
Jesus said to them , &quot; How can people say that Christ is the son of David ?
David himself said in the poem , &quot; Thus says the Lord to my Lord , &apos; You are sitting on my right hand
Wait till I make your enemy your bench .
How then did David call himself Lord , and be his son ?
When the people heard it , Jesus said to his disciples :
&quot; Beware of the scribes , who walk in long robes , and ask their peace in the streets , and rejoice in the high places of the synagogue , and in the first places of the feast .
They invaded the widows &apos; houses , pretending to pray for a long time , and these men are to be punished with greater punishment
And Jesus lifted up his head , and looked , and behold , the lord of the treasury cast the money into the barn
Again he saw a poor widow , and she gave him two small pieces of money
&quot; I tell you , &quot; he said , &quot; that this poor widow has invested more than all the people
For he had enough of himself for the people , and he brought it forth and put it into the alms ; but the widow was not enough of herself , and put it into all that she fed him .
&quot; Some speak of the temple , which is adorned with fine stones and offerings .
Jesus said , &quot; The days of the future come , concerning all these things which you have seen , and there is not a stone left here on a stone , nor has it been destroyed
And they said unto him , O husband , when shall this happen ? and what is the sign of the time that it shall come ?
Jesus said to them , &quot; Be careful and do not be troubled , for in the future there will be some good men who will name me , saying , &apos; I am Christ , &apos; and saying , &apos; The time is near , and do not follow them .
&quot; Do not be alarmed when you hear wars and disturbances , for these things must come first ; but the end is near , when you cannot stand .
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; The people will attack the people , and the country will attack the country
The earth will shake greatly , and there will be famines and plagues in many places , and terrible visions and great signs will appear from heaven
&quot; But before all these things , they will take you with their hands , and oppress you , and deliver you into the synagogue , and put you in prison , and bring you before the kings in my name .
But these things shall be witnesses to you at the end .
&quot; Therefore set your hearts firm , and do not prejudge your thoughts .
&quot; For I will give you wisdom in your mouths , wherein all your enemies will not dwell , neither will they turn back .
Even your parents , your brothers , your relatives , your friends , will betray you , and you will be slain by them .
&quot; For my name &apos;s sake , you will be hated by all
&quot; But you will not damage a single hair .
&quot; If you endure , you will keep your souls alive .
&quot; When you see Jerusalem besieged , you will know him . The days of the wilderness are near .
&quot; Then those who are in Judah shall flee to the mountains ; those who are in the city shall come out ; and those who are in the country shall not enter the city .
For this is the day of reckoning , that all that is written in the Scriptures may be proved .
Woe to those who are pregnant and to those who breastfeed in those days ! And anger shall come upon the people because of the great calamity which shall come upon the land
They will fall under the sword , and they will be taken into captivity , and Jerusalem will be trampled upon by strangers , and the days of returning to strangers will be fulfilled .
The sun and the moon and the stars will show signs , and the kingdoms of the earth will be troubled , and they will be troubled by the sound of the waves in the sea .
And the heavens shall shake , and the souls shall be astonished when they remember that which shall come upon the world
Then they shall see the Son of man , having power , and great glory , coming down in the clouds .
When these things come to pass , you shall stand upright , for the days of your redemption are near .
Jesus also spoke to them in a parable , saying , &quot; You see trees without fruit , and all kinds of trees ; and when he hath sprouted , you see that the summer is near .
See Up
&quot; Behold , these things are accomplished , and you shall know that the kingdom of God is near .
Truly I tell you , this generation has not yet passed away , and all these things are to be accomplished
&quot; The heavens and the earth will be wasted , and My words will not be wasted .
Be careful , lest your hearts be weighed down by your lusts and your drunkenness , and by your thoughts of this life ; and the day cometh unto you like a snare .
For this shall come to all the inhabitants of the earth for that day
&quot; Be watchful from time to time , and pray often , that you may escape all these things , and stand before the Son of man
Jesus taught in the temple daily , and he went out of the city every night to lodge in a mountain called Mount Olives
And all the people went up early into the temple , and came to Jesus to hear what he said
Behold , the feast of yeast , and the Passover , are near
How did the chief priests and the scribes think to kill Jesus , because they were afraid of the people
Then Satan entered into the heart of the Jews of Galilee , who were among the twelve disciples
&quot; He went to the chief priests and ministered to the rulers , and asked them how he could deliver Jesus to them
And they rejoiced , and agreed to give him silver
And when he had answered , he sought the opportunity to deliver Jesus to them while all the people were not present .
&quot; The day has come for the slaughter of the lambs beyond the feast of yeast ,
Jesus sent Peter and John , saying , &quot; Go and prepare for us the Passover feast that we may eat
And they asked him , saying , &quot; Prepare for us in it
Jesus said , &quot; When you enter the city , a man will come to you with a bottle of water , and you will follow him to the house where he enters .
And he said to the master of the house , &quot; The room is there , where I and my disciples may eat the Passover feast
&quot; He will say , &apos; A large building will be set up for you , and you will be prepared therein .
&quot; They went and met , as Jesus said , and prepared the Passover feast
When the time came , Jesus sat down , and the apostles sat with him
Jesus said to them , &quot; I am willing to eat this Passover feast with you before I am slain
&quot; I tell you , I will not eat this feast again until it is accomplished in the land of God
And Jesus took the cup , and blessed it , and said , &quot; Take this , and drink it together
&quot; I have told you that from now on I will no longer drink of this grape juice , until I come to the land of God .
Then he took the cake and blessed it , and broke it and gave it to them , saying , &quot; This is my body , which I have given you ; so you should do , for you remember me .
And after the meal he took up a cup , and said , &quot; This cup is the new covenant made with my blood , and it has come forth for you
&quot; Behold , the hand of the man who sold me is with me on the table
The Son of man will surely die according to the appointed time ; but woe to those who sell the Son of man !
Then they asked one another , &quot; Who is the one who will do this ? &quot;
And the disciples disputed , and the one among them was great
Jesus said to them , &quot; There is a king over the Gentiles , who is called the Lord of Mercy .
&quot; But you shall not do that ; but you shall be great in your heads , as a child , and as a leader , and as a servant .
Who is greater than he who sits down and is a servant ? Is he not greater than he who sits down ? Yet I am among you as a servant
&quot; You are always with me , as I am in the procession .
&quot; I will give you the kingdom , just as my Father gave me it
&quot; Sit in my country , eat and drink in my seats , and sit on the throne , and judge the twelve tribes of Israel .
Then said the Lord , &quot; Simon , Simon , Satan wants to have you , and to sew you like the seed of wheat
&quot; But I have prayed for you that you do not lose your faith , and that you turn back and strengthen your brothers .
Peter said , &quot; Lord , I am a prisoner with you , and a death with you , and a mercy
Jesus said , &quot; Peter , I tell you , the chicken has not cried today , and you will say three times that you do not recognize me
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; When I sent you out , there were no pockets , no pockets , no shoes , and what was missing from you ? &quot; They said , &quot; No
Jesus said , &quot; But now whoever has pockets can carry them , and whoever has pockets can carry them ; and whoever does not have knives will sell clothes and buy knives .
&quot; I tell you that it is written in the Scripture , &apos; He is among the sinners , &apos; and this shall be proved in me , for that which concerns me shall be accomplished .
They said , &quot; Lord , look , here are two knives . &quot; Jesus said , &quot; It &apos;s a knife .
Jesus went out to Mount Olives as usual , and the disciples followed him .
Then he came to the place , and said to them , &quot; Pray , lest you enter into confusion .
Then he departed from them , and threw away a stone , and kneeled down and prayed
He said , &quot; Father , if you will , take away the cup , but do not do my will , but do yours .
An angel appeared from heaven , and strengthened him
Jesus healed his wounds and prayed more earnestly . His sweat dropped like a great drop of blood on the ground
And when the prayer was finished , he arose , and came to the disciples , and saw that they were asleep in sorrow
Then He said to them , &quot; Why do you sleep ? Arise and pray , lest you enter into confusion .
And as they were speaking , a great multitude of them , of the twelve , named Judas , came forward , and approached Jesus , to kiss him
And Jesus said unto him , Judas , have thou sold the sons of men by the secret of thy mouth
And the men on the left and on the right , when they saw that the sight was not good , said , &quot; Lord , let us cut off the sword , or not , or not ,
And one of them cut off a sword from the servant of the high priest , and cut off his right ear
Jesus said , &quot; Come to this place , it is for them ; and touch the man &apos;s ear , and heal him . &quot;
Jesus said to those who came to him , the chief priests , and the rulers , and the elders , &quot; Do you bring out me with your swords , like a robber ? &quot;
&quot; I am in the temple with you every day , and you do not take me by hand ; but now it is your time , and darkness is at hand .
And they took Jesus , and brought him into the house of the high priest ; and Peter followed him far away .
And they sat together in the garden , and the fire was kindled ; and Peter sat among them
And when a woman saw Peter sitting in the light of the fire , she looked on him , and said , This man is of the same people .
But Peter did not confess , saying , &quot; Woman , I do not recognize him
And it came to pass after a little while , that another saw him , and said , Thou art also of their party ; and Peter said , I am not this man
And it came to pass after a little while , that another man spoke with great power , saying , He is indeed with him , for he is also a Galilean
Peter said , &quot; I have no idea what you are talking about , you man . As you spoke , the chicken cried out
Then the Lord turned and looked at Peter , and Peter remembered what the Lord had said to him , saying , &quot; Today the chicken calls E first , and three times you will not recognize me
He went out crying
The watchmen of Jesus played him , and beat him
Then he looked at him , and said to him , &quot; Tell us , you are a prophet , and who has struck you ? &quot;
They also insulted him with many other words
And it came to pass on the morning , that all the elders of the people gathered together , the chief priests and the scribes , and brought Jesus into their synagogue
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; If I tell you , you will not believe
If I ask you , you will not answer
From now on , the Son of man shall sit on the right hand of the power of God
They all said , &quot; Are you the Son of God ? &quot; Jesus said , &quot; What you say is true .
They said , &quot; What else will we testify to ? We have all heard what he said in person .
And all the people rose up , and delivered Jesus before Pilate
Then he said to him , &quot; We have seen this man seduce the people , and forbid them to pay taxes to Caesar , and say that he is Christ , and the king
Then Pilate asked Jesus , &quot; Are you the King of the Jews ? &quot; Jesus answered , &quot; You are the King of the Jews
Then said Pilate unto the chief priest and to all the people , What sin hath this man committed ?
But the more they spoke , the more he stirred up the people , and preached throughout all Judea , from Galilee even to this place .
And when Pilate heard it , he asked , Is this man a Galilean ?
Knowing that Jesus was under the hand of Herod , he sent him to Herod ; and Herod was in Jerusalem at that time
And when Herod saw him , he rejoiced , for he had long desired to see him , because he heard what he had seen , and hoped to see him do a sign
Then he asked him many things , and Jesus answered not one word .
The chief priests and the scribes stood and spoke to him with great power
Then Herod and his men despised him , and played him , and put on his fine clothes , and brought him back to Pilate
Herod and Pilate had fought one against another ; and on that day they became friends
Then Pilate delivered the chief priests , and the governors , and the people
Then he said to them , &quot; You have brought this man here to me , saying that he has seduced the people . Behold , I also told him what you said , and tested him before you , and found no fault in him .
And so was Herod ; therefore he was brought back : and behold , he did nothing worthy of death .
Therefore I will punish him , and release him .
Each time this season &apos;s patrol must release a prisoner to them
And all the people shouted together , saying , Remove this man , and release Barabbas for us
&quot; This Barabbah was put in prison for his rebellion in the city
And when Pilate was willing to release Jesus , he persuaded them again
&quot; But they cried out , &quot; Nail him ! Nail him ! &quot;
And Pilate said unto them a third time , Why , what evil has this man done ? for I have not found out what he is guilty of , and I will punish him , and release him .
And they cried out unto him , and urged him that he should crucify Jesus : and their voice was won .
This was the case they sought , Pedro
&quot; He released those who were imprisoned as murderers , whom they had asked , and gave Jesus to them , according to their will .
And it came to pass , when they had taken him away , that a certain Simon of the Galileans came down from the country , and they seized him , and laid the cross upon him , and commanded him to follow him on his back .
There were many people who followed Jesus , and among them were many women who cried out for him
Then Jesus turned and said to them , &quot; Women of Jerusalem , do not weep for me , but weep for yourself and your children
&quot; For the days will come , and they will say , &apos; Blessed are those who have not been born , and those who have not conceived , and those who have not given birth to babies .
&quot; Then they will say to the great mountain , &apos; Be upon us , &apos; and to the small mountain , &apos; Shut us down . &apos; 
&quot; How will it be in the future , when these things will be done on the tree that has water , and on the tree that is dry ?
And there were two prisoners who brought him to death with Jesus
And he came to a place called the Rock , and there he nailed Jesus on the cross , and he nailed two prisoners , one on the left , and one on the right
Then said Jesus , &quot; Father , forgive them ; for they do not know what they have done . &quot; And the soldiers divided his garments in lots .
And the people stood there , and watched ; and the princes laughed at him , saying , He saved others ; and if he were Christ , the chosen of God , he could save himself
And the soldier made fun of him , and gave him vinegar before him to drink
&quot; If you are the King of the Jews , you can save yourself
There was a sign above Jesus , written , &quot; This is the king of the Jews
Then one of the two prisoners who were with him mocked him and said , &quot; Are you not the Christ ? Save yourself and us
Then he shall reproach him , and say , &quot; Have you no fear of God , though you are a prisoner
We are righteous because what we have received is equal to what we have done . But this man has not done a bad thing
Then he said , &quot; Jesus , remember me when you are to come into the kingdom .
Jesus said to him , &quot; Truly I tell you , today you will be with me in Paradise
And it was about noon , and the darkness was all over the earth , even unto the beginning
And the sun was darkened , and the mantle of the house was cut in two from the midst of Dan .
Jesus cried out with a loud voice , saying , &quot; Father , I have given my soul into your hand , &quot; and when he had said this , his spirit ceased
When the centurion saw what was done , he glorified himself and said to God , &quot; This is a righteous man
And all that were gathered together to see it , when they saw that which was done , they bowed their chests to it
And all those who knew Jesus , and the women that followed him from Galilee , stood afar off to see these things
&quot; There is a man named Joseph , a priest , a man of good and righteousness
For he had no associate in all that they had devised , and he was a man who longed for the kingdom of God in the city of Arimathah Judah
The man went to see Pilate , and asked for the body of Jesus
Then he took it and wrapped it in fine linen , and laid it in a tomb made of stone , where no one had ever been buried .
&quot; That day is the Preparation Day , and the Sabbath Day is near .
And the women that came with him from Galilee followed , and saw the tomb and the rest of his body
Then they returned , and prepared the anointing oil , and on the Sabbath day they rested according to the commandment
On the first day of the seven days , at the dawn , the women came to the tomb with the preparations prepared
The stone was seen rolling away from the tomb
They entered in , but saw not the body of the Lord Jesus
In the midst of suspicion , suddenly two men stood by . The clothes lighted up
And the women were afraid , and bowed their faces : and the two said unto them , Why seek ye life in the dead ?
&quot; He is not here , but has been raised again . How do you know when he was still in Galilee ?
&quot; The Son of man must be delivered into the hands of sinners , crucified , and raised up on the third day .
And they remembered the words of Jesus
Then he returned from the tomb , and told the eleven apostles and the rest of the people all these things .
And those who told the apostles were Mary Magdalene , and Joanna , and Mary the mother of Jacob , and women who were with them
&quot; The apostles did not believe these words , because they were lies .
And Peter arose , and ran to the tomb , and looked down , and behold , there was a piece of cloth alone ; and he returned , and remembered what Hezekiah had done .
On that day two of the disciples went to a village named Emmaus , about twenty-five miles from Jerusalem
They talked to each other about all the things they had encountered
When they were talking , Jesus himself came near to them and accompanied them
Only their eyes were confused , and they did not know him
Jesus said to them , &quot; What is it that you walk and talk to each other ? &quot; And they stood still , their faces grieved .
Then one of the two men , whose name was Gereuba , answered , &quot; Do you not know what has happened in Jerusalem these days ?
Jesus said , &quot; What is this ? &quot; They said , &quot; It is the case of Jesus of Nazareth , a prophet who has great power to speak and to do in the sight of God and the people .
&quot; But the chief priest and our scribes have set him free and crucified him for a crime of death
But he is the one whom we have longed for to redeem the children of Israel ; not only so , but it has been done three days
And there were among us a number of women who marveled us , and they came to the tomb early in the morning
&quot; But when he saw not his body , he came back and told us , saying , &apos; I have seen an angel appearing , and he is alive .
And a few of us went to the tomb , and found him , as the women said , but did not see him .
Jesus said to them , &quot; You ignorant people , your hearts are too slow to believe in all the words of the prophet .
Isn &apos;t it right that Christ should be thus afflicted and enter into his glory ?
Then Moses and the prophets made clear to them all the words which he had spoken in the Scriptures
As he came near the village where they were going , Jesus seemed to be going forward
And they pressed him , and said , It is late , and the day is come to pass ; so dwell with us ; and Jesus went in , and dwelled with them .
And it came to pass , when he had sat down , that he took up the bread , and blessed it , and broke it , and gave it to them
When their eyes were brightened , they recognized him , and suddenly Jesus was gone .
&quot; And they said to one another , &apos; Isn &apos;t our heart hot when he speaks with us on the way , and teaches us the Scriptures ?
And when they stood up , they returned to Jerusalem , and saw eleven apostles and their companions gathered together in one place
He said , &quot; The Lord is indeed resurrected and has appeared to Simon
And the two men spoke all the things which they had encountered on the way , and how they were known when they broke bread .
And when he had spoken these words , he stood in their midst , saying , Peace be to you
And they were astonished , and feared ; and what they saw was a soul .
Jesus said , &quot; Why are you troubled ? Why do you have doubts in your hearts
&quot; When you see my hands and my feet , you know that I am indeed there ; touch me , and see ; soul without bone without flesh ; and you see that I am there .
And when he had said this , he showed them his hands and his feet
They were so glad that they did not dare to believe , and they wondered . Jesus said , &quot; What have you eaten here ?
And they gave him a burnt fish , and there was an ancient scroll and a honeycomb
He came and ate before them
Jesus said to them , &quot; This is what I told you when I was with you , saying , &apos; Everything that is written in the law of Moses , in the book of the prophets , and in the poems , will be tested
Then Jesus opened their hearts , that they might understand the Scriptures
And he said unto them , As it is written , Christ shall be put to death , and shall be raised from the dead on the third day .
And the way of repentance and forgiveness , which shall be preached in his name , shall be preached straight from Jerusalem unto all the nations
You are witnesses of these things .
I will bring upon you the blessings which my Father has promised you , and you shall wait in the city , and come straight to the power which you have received from above .
Jesus took them to the other side of the Jordan , and raised his hand to bless them
And when he was blessed , he departed from them , and was carried up into heaven .
And they worshipped Him , and went back to Jerusalem with great joy
Always praise God in the temple
Earlier , the way was with God , and the way was with God
This way is too early to be with God
All things are made by Him , and none of what is made is made by Him .
Life is in him , and this life is the light of man .
Light shines in darkness , but darkness does not accept light
There was a man sent from God , named John ,
&quot; This man came to testify for light , that the people might believe in him
He is not the light , but a witness for the light .
&quot; That light is true , and it shines on all the living in the world .
He is in the world , and the world has been created by Him , and the world does not know Him .
When he comes to his own place , his own people do not receive him
Whoever receives Him is one who believes in His name , and He gives them power as children of God .
They are not born of blood , nor of desire , nor of the will of man , but of God
He has become a flesh , and dwells among us , full of grace and truth ; and we have seen his glory , the glory of the only begotten Son of the Father .
John , bearing witness for him , cried out , &quot; This is what I said , and it has been done against me and against me , because he was before me
&quot; And we have received from His abundant grace , and have been blessed
The Law , which was preached by Moses , the grace and the truth , came from Jesus Christ
No man ever sees God ; only the only begotten child in the Father &apos;s womb manifests Him
Then the Jews sent the priests and the Levites from Jerusalem to John , and asked him , &quot; Who are you ? &quot;
He said , &quot; I am not the Christ , &quot; and he did not hide it
Then they asked him , &quot; Who then are you , Elijah ? &quot; He said , &quot; I am not . Is it the prophet ? &quot; He answered , &quot; No
Then they said , &quot; Who are you in the end ? Let us reply to those who sent us , and you say , &quot; Who are you ? &quot;
He said , &quot; I am the one who cried out in the wilderness , &apos; Restore the way of the Lord , &apos; as the prophet Isaiah said .
Those who are sent are of the Pharisees .
Then they asked him , saying , &quot; Why are you baptized , if you are not Christ , or Elijah , or the prophet ?
John answered , &quot; I was baptized with water , but there is one standing among you whom you do not know
&quot; And that which is in me , and that which is afterwards , I have given him , and it is not worthy
This is the testimony of John , which was baptized at Bethany , which is beyond the Jordan .
The next day John saw Jesus coming to him and said , &quot; Look , the Lamb of God , who will remove the iniquity of the world
&quot; This is what I said : &apos; There is a man who has been before me , and who has been after me , and who has been before me , because he was before me
&quot; I did not know him before , but now I come to wash with water , that I may make him manifest to the children of Israel
John testified again , saying , &quot; I have seen the Spirit as a dove descending from heaven and dwelling on him
&quot; But he who sent me to baptize with water said to me , &apos; You see the Holy Spirit coming down , who lives on whom , and who is baptized with the Holy Spirit ?
When I saw it , I proved that he was the Son of God
Again the day came , and John stood there with the two disciples
When he saw Jesus walking , he said , &quot; Behold , this is the Lamb of God
When the two disciples heard his words , they followed Jesus
Then Jesus turned and saw them following him , and asked them , &quot; What do you want ? &quot; They said , &quot; Rabbi , dwell in it . &quot;
Jesus said to them , &quot; Come and see , &quot; and they went and saw him dwelling therein ; and he lived with him that day ; and it was confirmed at that time
Hearing the words of John , Andrew , the brother of Simon Peter , was one of those who followed Jesus .
Then he went to his brother Simon , and said to him , &quot; We have met Messiah , who has risen from the dead , which is Christ
Then he led him to Jesus , and Jesus looked at him , and said , &quot; You are Simon the son of John , and you shall be called Kiphah ; and Kiphah is Peter . &quot;
The next day , when Jesus wanted to go to Galilee , he met Philip and said to him , &quot; Follow me
Philip , the lord of Beersheba , and Andrew , Peter , and the city
Philip , looking for Nathaniel , said to him , &quot; We met Jesus , the son of Joseph , of Nazareth , whom Moses wrote in the law and the prophets wrote
And Nathanael said unto him , What good thing shall Nathanael do ? And Philip said unto him , See
When Jesus saw Nathaniel coming , he pointed to him and said , &quot; Behold , this is a true Israelite , and he has no deceit in his heart
Then Nathaniel said to Jesus , &quot; Do you know me from there ? &quot; Jesus answered , &quot; Before Philip said hello to you , you were under a tree without fruit , and I saw you
Then Nathaniel said , &quot; Rabbi , you are the son of God , and you are the king of Israel
Jesus said to him , &quot; Because I said , &apos; See you under a tree without fruit , &apos; do you believe ? You will see something greater than this
&quot; And I tell you , as I am , that you will see the heavens opened , and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of man
On the third day there was a wedding feast at Canaan in Galilee , where the mother of Jesus was
Jesus and his disciples were also invited
When the wine was consumed , Jesus &apos; mother said to him , &quot; They have no more wine
Jesus said , &quot; Mother , what have I to do with you ? My time has not yet come
His mother said to the servant , &quot; What did he tell you , and what did you do
&quot; There were six stone cylinders placed therein , according to the cleansing of the Jews , and two or three buckets of water for each one .
Jesus said to the servants , &quot; Put the pot full of water , &quot; and they filled it , and went straight to the mouth of the pot
Then Jesus said , &quot; They are now ready to be picked up and given to the people at the feast , and they sent them away
And he that was over the feast tasted the wine that was turned into water , and knew not what was in it ; but the man that took the water knew it ; and he that was over the feast called the bridegroom .
He said to him , &quot; Everyone puts up a good wine first , and then puts it up the second time , until the guests have finished drinking , and you keep the good wine until this day .
This was the first sign of Jesus , which came in the way of Canaan in Galilee , to show His glory , and his disciples believed in him .
Then Jesus went down to Capernaum , and his mother , and his brothers , and his disciples , and lived there a few days .
When the Passover of the Jews was near , Jesus went up to Jerusalem
And he saw in the temple a man who sold sheep and goats , and a man who exchanged silver , sitting in it
Then Jesus took the rope and made whips , and drove the sheep and the goats out of the temple , and threw down the money of the moneychangers , and overturned their tables .
&quot; And to those who sell doves , &apos; Take these things away , and do not take my father &apos;s house for a place of sale .
Then his disciples remembered that it was written , &quot; I am as anxious in my heart for your house as a fire .
Then the Jews asked him , saying , &quot; What signs do you show us , that you have done these things
Jesus answered them , &quot; You have destroyed the temple , and I will be raised up again in three days
And the Jews said , &quot; Have you been building this house for forty-six years , and it will be built again in three days ? &quot;
But the word of Jesus is the temple of his body
So when the disciples remembered that he had spoken these words after he had been raised from the dead , they believed the Scriptures and what Jesus had said
When Jesus was in Jerusalem at the Passover , many saw the signs of his works , and believed in his name
But Jesus gave Himself not to them , because He knew all the people
For he knows what is in the heart .
And there was a certain Pharisee , whose mother was called Nicodeus , a Jewish officer
And he came to Jesus in the night , and said , Rabbi , we know that thou art a master in God ; for without God no man can do the signs that thou hast done .
Jesus answered , &quot; I tell you , as I am , that if a man does not be resurrected , he will not see the kingdom of God
Then said the mother of Nicodemus , &quot; How can a man , when he has grown old , be born again , and come into his mother &apos;s womb again ?
Jesus said , &quot; I tell you , as I am , that a man cannot enter into the land of God unless he is born of water and of the Holy Spirit
From the flesh is the flesh , and from the Spirit is the Spirit
I said , &quot; You must be resurrected , and you shall not be called Hezekiah
&quot; The wind blows with a purpose , and you hear the sound of the wind , but you do not know where it comes from or where it goes ; and so does everyone who is born of the Holy Spirit
Then Nicodemus &apos; mother asked him , &quot; How can this happen ?
Jesus answered , &quot; You are the Lord of Israel . Do you not understand this
&quot; Truly I am telling you that what we say is what we know , and what we witness , and what we see , but you do not receive our witness .
&quot; When I speak to you concerning the earth , and yet you do not believe , how can you believe concerning heaven ?
&quot; No one has ascended to heaven except the sons of men who were in heaven from heaven .
As Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness , so shall the Son of man be lifted up
that all who believe in him may live forever .
God loves the world , and even gave them His only begotten Son , so that all who believe in Him will not perish , but will live forever
For God sent his Son to be raised up , not to judge the sins of the world , but to save the world for his sake .
He who believes in him is not condemned ; and he who does not believe is condemned because he does not believe in the name of God , the only Son .
Light is come into the world , and the world is evil for its own deeds ; it does not love light , but loves darkness ; and its sins are here .
For he that doeth evil hateth light , and cometh not forth for light , lest he be reproached for his deeds
But he that walketh in truth shall come in light , to show that he walketh in the name of God .
After this came Jesus and his disciples to the land of Judah , where they dwelt and were baptized .
John was baptized in Reuben , which was near to Salem , because there was much water ; and all the people went to be baptized
John had not yet been put in prison
John &apos;s disciples and a Jew debated the cleanness of the service
Then they came to John and said , &quot; Rabbi , the one whom you witnessed before with you outside the Jordan is baptized , and all the people have gone to him
John said , &quot; If it is not given from heaven , nothing can be given to man
&quot; I said , &apos; I am not the Christ ; I am sent before him . You can testify to me
The bridegroom is the bridegroom , and the bridegroom &apos;s friend stands and hears the bridegroom &apos;s voice , and I am filled with joy .
He shall prosper , and I shall weaken .
He who comes from heaven is above all things . He who comes from the earth belongs to the earth , and what He says belongs to the earth . He who comes from heaven is above all things
He brings forth the testimony of what he has seen and heard ; but no one receives his testimony
And whoever receives His witness , He will seal it , and prove that God is true .
He that is sent speaketh the word of God : for God hath given him the Spirit without limit .
For the Father loves the Son , and all things are given into His hand
The believer has eternal life , and the unbeliever has no eternal life . God &apos;s wrath is on him all the time .
The Lord knew that the Pharisees heard more of his disciples than John
( It was not Jesus himself who was baptized , but His disciples
Then he departed from Judah , and went again to Galilee
It must pass through Samara
And they came to a city in Samaria , which is called Shephah , near the land which Jacob gave to Joseph his son
And there was a well in it ; and Jesus sat by it because of his weakness in walking ; and it was about noon
And a woman of Samaria came to water him , and Jesus said unto him , Give me water to drink
Then the disciples went into the city to buy food
And the woman of Samaria said unto him , How canst thou , being a Jew , give me water from a woman of Samaria ? for the Jews and the Samaritans came not unto me
Jesus answered , &quot; If you know the grace of God and tell you who gave me water , you will ask Him early , and He will give you the living water early
&quot; The woman said , &quot; Sir , if there is no watering device , and the well is deep , where can you get fresh water ? &quot;
&quot; Are you greater than Jacob , our father-in-law , who left this well for us ; and he himself and his sons and his cattle drink the water in it ?
Jesus answered and said , &quot; Whoever drinks this water will thirst again
If a man drinks of the water which I have given , he will never be thirsty ; and the water which I have given shall be a spring in his head , and it shall flow for ever and ever .
And the woman said , Sir , give me this water , that I may not thirst , nor come so far as to water
Jesus said to him , &quot; Go and let your husband also come here
The woman said , &quot; I have no husband . &quot; Jesus said , &quot; Is it not right that you say you have no husband
You have five husbands . You have one now , and not your husband . That is true of you
And the woman said , Sir , I see that thou art a prophet
&quot; Our ancestors worshipped on this mountain ; but you said , &apos; The place where you should worship is in Jerusalem . &apos; 
Jesus said to her , &quot; Woman , if you believe me , the time will come when you will not worship the Father on this mountain nor in Jerusalem
What you worship , you do not know ; what we worship , we know ; for salvation came out of the Jews
The time will come , and it is now , that those who truly worship the Father should worship him with the heart and with integrity ; for the Father wants such to worship him
God is a Spirit , so those who worship Him must worship Him with the heart and sincerity
The woman said , &quot; I know that Messiah , who is called Christ , is coming , and he will tell us all things .
Jesus said , &quot; It is he who spoke to you
Now when the disciples returned , they heard Jesus speak to a woman , but no man said , &quot; What do you want ? &quot; or , &quot; Why do you speak to him ? &quot;
Then the woman left a can of water and went into the city , and said to the people ,
&quot; Behold , there is a man who has spoken to me all that I have done , saying , Is this not Christ ?
And all the people went out of the city unto Jesus
Then the disciples said to Jesus , &quot; Rabbi , please eat
Jesus said , &quot; I have food to eat , which you do not know
Then the disciples asked one another , saying , &quot; Is there no man who can give him anything to eat
Jesus said , &quot; My food is to do the will of the One who sent me and to create His work
&quot; Will you not say , &apos; There are four months left until the harvest ? &apos; I tell you , &apos; Look with your eyes to the field , and see , the harvest is ripe , and it can be harvested&apos;
He who harvests shall receive his wages , and store up five valleys for ever . Happy shall be he who sows and he who harvests .
&quot; That man sows , and that man harvests , &quot; says the proverb , &quot; and it is evidently true
&quot; I send you to receive what you have not suffered . Others suffer , and you enjoy what they suffer
There were many Samaritans in the city who believed in Jesus , because the woman testified , &quot; He has spoken to me all that I have done
Then the Samaritans came to Jesus and asked him to dwell with them ; and he lived there two days .
More and more people believed because of the word of Jesus
Then he said to the woman , &quot; We believe in you , not because of your word , but because we have heard it ourselves , knowing that it is the Lord of the world .
After two days Jesus departed from the place to Galilee
For he testified for himself , saying , The prophet was not respected in the land
And when they were come to Galilee , the Galileans received him , seeing all that he had done for the Passover in Jerusalem ; for they were also going up for the Passover
And Jesus came again to Cana of Galilee , where he had made water wine : and there was a minister , and his son was sick in Capernaum .
When he heard that Jesus had come from Judah to Galilee , he came to him and asked him to go down and heal his son , for his son was about to die
Jesus said to him , &quot; If you do not see the miracles of God , you will never believe
The minister said , &quot; Sir , please go down while my child is not dead
Then Jesus said to him , &quot; Go back ; your son is alive ; and he who believed the words of Jesus went back . &quot;
When he was coming down , his servants greeted him , saying , &quot; His son is alive .
They said , &quot; It was too hot to leave yesterday
He knew that it was at the time when Jesus said to him , &quot; Your son is alive , &quot; and he and his whole family believed .
This is the second sign of the way of Jesus in Galilee , when he went back from Judah to Edom
After this came a feast for the Jews , and Jesus went up to Jerusalem
And there was a pond near the sheep gate in Jerusalem , which the Hebrews called Pisces : and beside it were five porches
There lay in it many blind , lame , bloodthirsty , and sick.There was an ancient scroll waiting for water
Whoever went down first , after the angel had stirred up the pond in due season , was healed of any disease
There was a man there who was sick for thirty-eight years
When Jesus saw him lying down , knowing that he had been sick for a long time , he asked him , &quot; Will you be healed ?
The patient answered , &quot; Sir , no man put me in the pond when the water was moving , and when I was going down , there was someone who went down before me .
Jesus said to him , &quot; Arise , take your bed and go
And the man recovered immediately , and took up his bed and went away
&quot; The day was a Sabbath , &quot; so the Jews said to the healer , &quot; It is a Sabbath , and it is impossible for you to take a bed
And he answered and said unto him that healed me , Take away thy bed
&quot; They asked him , &quot; Who told you to take the bed
The healed man did not know who he was , but Jesus had escaped because of the multitude thereof .
Then Jesus met him in the temple , and said to him , &quot; You have been healed . Do not sin again , for I fear that what you have experienced will be more beneficial to you .
Then he went to the Jews and told them that Jesus was the one who healed him
So the Jews oppressed Jesus because he did this on the Sabbath
Jesus said to them , &quot; My Father has done right now , and I have also done
Therefore the Jews sought to kill him more and more , because he not only committed the Sabbath , but also called God his Father , and treated himself equal to God
Jesus said to them , &quot; As I am , I tell you that the Son can do nothing by himself , but by seeing what the Father has done , and that the Son does what the Father has done .
&quot; Father , my son , I will show him all that I have done , and I will show him things greater than this , that you may be amazed .
How did the Father raise up the dead , and keep them alive , and the Son kept them alive according to his own will ?
&quot; The Father does not judge any man , but he gives all judgment to his son .
Let every man respect his son as he respects his father ; and whoever does not respect his son , that is , he does not respect the father who sent him
&quot; Truly I tell you , whoever listens to My words and sends My messengers will have eternal life , and will not be condemned , but will be raised from the dead to the living .
&quot; Truly I have told you that the time will come , and that it is at hand . The dead will hear the voice of the Son of God , and those who hear will live .
For as the Father had life in himself , so he gave his son life in himself
And because he is a son of man , He gave him authority to judge
&quot; Do not regard this as a miracle ; for the hour is coming , and all who are in the tomb will hear his voice , and will come out .
The resurrection of the good is alive , and the resurrection of the evil is condemned
I can do nothing on my own . How can I hear and judge ? My judgement is just , for I do not seek my own counsel , but that of the one who sent me .
&quot; If I testify for myself , my testimony will not be true
There is another who bears witness to me , and I know also that the witness he bears to me is true
&quot; You sent men to John , and he testified to the truth .
&quot; In fact , the testimony I have received is not from men ; but I speak these things to save you .
John is the light that shines , and you wish to rejoice in his light for a while
But I have a greater witness than John : for that which he hath given me for my Father , that I might accomplish , is that which I have done ; and this is the testimony that I am sent by the Father
And the Father that sent me beareth witness unto me : ye have never heard his voice , nor seen his image
And ye have no way in your hearts : for ye believe not in that which He hath sent down .
You examine the Scriptures , or should examine the Scriptures , because you think there is eternal life in them ; and this is the Scriptures which bear witness to me
However , you do not want to come to me here to get life
I do not receive the glory from men
But I know that in your hearts there is no love of God .
&quot; I have come in the name of my Father , and you will not receive me ; and if any man comes in his own name , you will receive him .
How can you believe me , when you are glorified among yourselves , and do not seek the glory of one God ?
&quot; Do not think that I will tell you in the presence of my Father . There is one who tells you , Moses , on whom you rely .
&quot; If you believe Moses , you will believe me , for in his book is written what I have written .
&quot; If you do not believe in his books , how can you believe in my words ?
After this , Jesus passed over the sea of Galilee , the sea of Tiberias
And many followed him , because they saw the signs which he did on the sick .
And Jesus went up into the mountain , and sat there with the disciples
At that time the Passover of the Jews was near
When Jesus saw the multitude , he lifted up his eyes , and said to Philip , &quot; Shall we buy bread from there for these people to eat ? &quot;
&quot; He said these things to test Philip , and he himself knew how to do it .
And Philip answered and said , It is a cake of twenty and two silvers , that each of them may eat one thing , and not another
And one of the disciples , Andrew the brother of Simon Peter , said unto Jesus ,
&quot; There is a child here with five loaves of wheat and two fish . What is it that you give to so many people ?
Jesus said to them , &quot; Sit down , all of you ; for the grass of the place was plentiful , and all sat down , and the number was about five thousand
And Jesus took the cake , and blessed it , and divided it among the seated , and the fish according to their desire .
When they had eaten , Jesus said to his disciples , &quot; Take away the remnant and put it in order , lest it be spoiled
And they took the five pieces of the bread , which they had eaten , and put them in twelve baskets .
When they saw the signs of Jesus , they said , &quot; This is indeed the prophet who will come to the world
Knowing that they were coming to make him king , Jesus returned to the mountain on his own
And it came to pass at night , that his disciples went down to the sea
And they boarded a ship to pass over the sea to Capernaum ; and it was dark , and Jesus had not yet come to them
Suddenly there was a great wind , and the sea was overflowing
And when the disciples went about ten miles , and saw Jesus walking on the sea , and coming nearer and nearer to the ship , they were afraid
Jesus said to them , &quot; It is me . Don &apos;t be afraid
The disciples liked to receive him on board the ship , and when they were on board , they came to the place where they were to go
And it came to pass on the second day , that all the people who stood by the sea knew that there was no other ship , but a small one , and that Jesus had not taken a ship with his disciples , but that they were going by themselves .
But a few small ships came from Tiberias , near the place where the Lord gave thanks and gave bread to the people
When they saw that Jesus and the disciples were not there , they boarded a ship to the farmers of Capernaum to seek Jesus
And when they had found it by the sea , they said unto him , Rabbi , when have ye come here ?
Jesus answered and said to them , &quot; I am indeed here to tell you that you seek me , not because you have seen the signs , but because you have eaten the bread
&quot; Do not labour for the evil food , but for the everlasting food , which the Son of man will give to you ; for the Son of man is the seal of the Father God .
And they asked him , saying , What shall we do , that we may be God &apos;s work ?
Jesus answered , &quot; This is the work of God , that you believe in what God has sent
And they said , &quot; What signs do you do that we believe in you when we see it ? What are you doing ? &quot;
Have our fathers eaten in the wilderness , as it is written in the Scriptures : He hath given them food from heaven to eat .
Jesus said , &quot; As I stand , I tell you that the food that comes from heaven was not given to you by Moses , but the true food that my Father gave to you from heaven
For the food of God is that which came down from heaven and gave life to the world
&quot; They said , &quot; Lord , often give us this food
Jesus said , &quot; I am the food of life ; whoever comes to me will not be hungry , and whoever believes in me will never be thirsty
&quot; But I said to you , &apos; Have you seen me or have you not believed ?
&quot; Whoever the Father has given me will come to me ; and whoever comes to me , I will not forsake him
For I came down from heaven not according to my own will , but according to the will of the one who sent me .
&quot; This is the meaning of the One who has sent me ; He has given me that I should not be lost , but that he should be raised to life in the Last Day .
For my Father &apos;s purpose is that he who believes in the sight of all the children may live forever , and I will raise him up at the last day .
The Jews privately discussed him because they said to him , &quot; I am the food that came down from heaven
&quot; Isn &apos;t this Jesus , the son of Joseph , whose parents we do not recognize ? How does he now say , &apos; I am descended from heaven &apos; ?
Jesus answered them , &quot; You do not want to discuss
&quot; If the Father who sent me had not attracted him , he would not have been able to come to me . I will call him to life at the end of the day
It is written in the book of the prophets , &quot; All of them will receive the lesson of God . &quot; Whoever hears the lesson of the Father and learns it , come to me
&quot; This is not to say that someone has seen the Father , but that he who comes from God has seen the Father
&quot; I tell you , in truth , that those who believe have eternal life .
I am the food of life
Have your fathers eaten in the wilderness , or have they died ?
&quot; This is the food that came down from heaven , and no man shall die if he eats it
&quot; I am the food of life , which came down from heaven ; and if any man eats of it , he shall live for ever and ever ; and the food which I will give is my flesh , which I have given to the life of the world .
So the Jews argued among themselves , saying , &quot; How can this man eat his flesh for us ? &quot;
Jesus said , &quot; I am telling you , that if you do not eat the flesh of the Son of man and drink the blood of the Son of man , there will be no life in you
He who eats my flesh and drinks my blood shall have eternal life ; and I will raise him up at the end of the day .
My flesh is indeed edible , and my blood is indeed drinkable
&quot; He who eats my flesh and drinks my blood is always in me , and I am always in him
&quot; As the Father of everlasting sent me , so will those who eat my flesh live for my Father &apos;s sake
&quot; This is the food that came down from heaven , and he who eats it will live for ever and ever . Did not your fathers eat it or die ?
These were the words which Jesus taught in the synagogue of Capernaum
When some of his disciples heard it , they said , &quot; How hard is this ! Who can hear it ? &quot;
Knowing in his heart that the disciples were arguing about this , Jesus said to them , &quot; Is this saying that you despise it ?
&quot; What if you see the Son of man ascending to where he came from ?
&quot; It is the Spirit that makes man alive , and the flesh is useless ; and what I say to you is the Spirit , and it is life
Jesus knew from the beginning who did not believe him and who would sell him
Then said Jesus , &quot; Therefore I said to you , &apos; Without the grace of my Father , no man will come to me
From that time onward many of his disciples turned away , and did not go with him .
Then Jesus said to the twelve , &quot; Will you also go ?
Then Simon Peter answered , &quot; Lord , to whom do we return , for you have the way of everlasting life
&quot; We have believed and know that you are the Holy One of God
Jesus said , &quot; Have I not chosen your twelve disciples , but one of you is a devil
Jesus spoke of Judas , the son of Simon the Galilean , one of the twelve disciples , who was about to sell Jesus
After this , Jesus went forth in Galilee , but he would not go forth to the Jews , for the Jews wanted to kill him
The Jewish Tent Festival was near at the time
Then the brother of Jesus said to him , &quot; Depart from here , and go up to Judah , that your disciples may see what you do
A man is to be glorified , and he does not act in secret ; and if you do these things , then you shall make yourselves known to the world .
For the sake of his brothers , and because they believed not in him ;
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; My time has not yet come . It is often convenient for you
&quot; The world cannot hate you , but hates me ; for I testify that what they do is evil .
You go up for the feast . I will not go up for the feast now , for my time is not yet full
Jesus said this , and he lived still in Galilee
But his brothers went up after him , and he went up to fast , and it was not light , but it seemed dark .
The Jews were looking for Jesus at the feast , and said , &quot; Here he is
And all the people debated about him ; and some said , He is a good man ; and some said , Otherwise , He is a mischief to all the people .
&quot; But no man speaks of him openly for fear of the Jews .
And it came to pass at the feast , that Jesus went up into the temple to teach the people
Then the Jews said to him , &quot; How can a man who has not learned understand the book ?
Jesus said , &quot; My lesson is not mine , but that of the one who sent me .
&quot; If a man sets his heart to do his will , he will know whether it is from God or I speak by myself
A man asks for the glory of himself by his own word ; but he asks for the glory of the one who sent him ; and he is true , and there is no iniquity in his heart .
&quot; Isn &apos;t Moses preaching the law to you , and none of you keeps it ? Why do you want to kill me ?
And they said , Thou art bound by the devil ; and who will kill thee
Jesus said , &quot; I have done one thing , and you are all wondering
Moses preached the circumcision to you , not from Moses , but from your ancestors ; therefore you also circumcise on the Sabbath day
&quot; If a man is circumcised on the Sabbath day , so that he does not violate the law of Moses , and I make a man whole on the Sabbath day , will you give me mercy ?
Do not judge evil by appearance , judge evil by fairness
Some of the men of Jerusalem said , &quot; Is this not the man whom they want to kill ?
And you see that he speaks plainly , and they say nothing to him : doth not the officer know that this is Christ ?
&quot; But we know where this man came from ; but when Christ came , no man knew where he came from
Then Jesus , teaching in the temple , said with a loud voice , &quot; You also know me , and you know where I came from . I did not come for myself , but it is true that he sent me , and you do not know him .
&quot; But I know him , for I have come from him , and he has also made me worse
And they desired to seize Jesus , but no man laid hands on him , for the time had not yet come for him .
But there were many among them who believed in him , saying , &quot; Can the signs of Christ in the time of his coming be greater than the signs of this man ? &quot;
And when the Pharisees heard that all the people were talking about him , the chief priests and the Pharisees sent messengers to seize him
Then Jesus said , &quot; I have little time to be with you . Then I went back to him who sent me
You want me , but you can &apos;t . You can &apos;t go to the place where I am
Then the Jews asked one another , saying , &quot; Will this man go there , that we may not find him ? Will he go to the Jews who dwell in the midst of the Philistines and teach them ? &quot;
He said , &quot; What does it mean that you seek me but do not find me where I am ?
And it came to pass on the last day of the Sabbath , the greatest day of the Sabbath , that Jesus stood up and said with a loud voice , &quot; If any man is thirsty , let him come to me to drink
Believers in Me , as it is said in the Scriptures , a river of living water will flow out of their bellies
Jesus said this to those who believed in him , that they should receive the Holy Spirit ; but the Holy Spirit had not yet come , because Jesus had not yet been glorified
&quot; When they heard it , some said , &quot; This is indeed the prophet
Some say , &quot; This is Christ ; &quot; but others say , &quot; Isn &apos;t Christ from Galilee ? &quot;
&quot; Isn &apos;t it said in the Scriptures that Christ is the descendant of David , who came out of Bethlehem , David &apos;s hometown ?
So they divided themselves against Jesus
Some of them will seize him , but no one will touch him .
Then they returned to the priests and the Pharisees , and said to them , &quot; Why have you not brought him ?
And the officer answered and said , There is never such a thing as he speaketh
Then said the Pharisees , &quot; Have you also been misled ?
&quot; Do any of the rulers or the Pharisees believe in him ?
But those who do not understand the law are cursed .
And the mother of Nicodemus , who had seen Jesus before , said to them ,
&quot; Doth not he hear his own testimony , and know not what he hath done ? Is it not our law that judges his sins ?
They said , &quot; Are you also from Galilee ? If you go and search , you will know that Galilee did not have a prophet . &quot;
So they all went home , and Jesus went to Mount Olives
And he returned to the temple early in the morning ; and all the people came to him , and he sat down to teach them
And the scribes and the Pharisees came , and took a woman who had been taken in prostitution , and commanded her to stand in the midst
Then said Jesus , Son of man , this woman was taken while she was in prostitution
&quot; But as Moses commanded us in the law , &quot; Slay such a woman with a stone , and how shall you deal with him ? &quot;
&quot; They said these words to test Jesus , and to be told of the handle of his hand ; but Jesus bent on his back and drew on the ground with his fingers .
And when they had not yet dwelt , Jesus straightened himself and said to them , &quot; Who among you is innocent , and who can first strike him with a stone ? &quot;
Then he bent his back again , and drew on the ground with his fingers
When they heard this , they went out from old to young , and there remained only one Jesus , and the woman still standing in the midst .
Then Jesus straightened himself and said to him , &quot; Woman , what are those who are in it ? Has no man judged you for your sin ?
He said , &quot; Lord , no . &quot; Jesus said , &quot; I have not determined your sin . Go , and no more sin from now on .
And Jesus said unto them , I am the light of the world ; and he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness , but shall have the light of life .
And the Pharisees said unto him , Thou art a witness unto thyself , and thy testimony is not true
Jesus said , &quot; I testify for myself , but my testimony is true , because I know where I came from and where I go , and you do not know where I came from and where I go
You judge by appearance , and I do not judge by flesh
&quot; I judge , and my judgment is true ; for I am not alone here , and my Father who sent me is with me .
And it is written in your law , saying , The testimony of two men is true
&quot; I am a witness for myself , and the Father who sent me is also a witness for me
They said to him , &quot; Your Father is in it . &quot; Jesus answered , &quot; You do not know me , nor my Father . If you know me , you will know my Father
These are the words which Jesus spoke in the treasure house of the temple , when he taught , and no man took him , because his time had not yet come
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; I am going , and you will seek me , and you will die in sin , and you will not be able to come to the place where I have gone
&quot; The Jews said , &quot; Is it because he says that you cannot come to the place where I have gone , and he wants to end himself
Jesus said to them , &quot; You are from the bottom , and I am from the top , and you are of this world , and I am not of this world
Therefore I said unto you , If ye believe not that I am Christ , ye shall surely die in sin
They asked him , &quot; Who are you ? &quot; Jesus said to them , &quot; It is the one whom I told you from the beginning
I speak many things concerning you , and judge you ; but it is true that I am sent ; and what I have heard in him , I have passed on to the world .
They did not understand that Jesus was referring to the Father
Then Jesus said , &quot; When you raise up the Son , you will know that I am Christ , and that I have not done anything by myself ; but I speak these things as my Father taught me .
&quot; He who sent me is with me ; and he has not left me alone here , because I do often what is pleasing to him
When Jesus spoke these words , many believed in him
Jesus said to the Jews who believed in him , &quot; If you keep my ways , you are my disciples
You shall know the truth , and the truth shall make you free
They answered , &quot; We are Abraham &apos;s descendants ; we have never been servants to anyone . What do you say , &apos; You will be free&apos;
Jesus answered them , &quot; I tell you in truth , that all sinners are slaves to sin .
Slaves can &apos;t live in the house forever , sons will live in the house forever
&quot; If therefore the Son of God calls you free , you are truly free
&quot; I know that you are the sons of Abraham , but you want to kill me , because you do not tolerate my way
&quot; What I say is seen in my Father , and what you do is heard in your Father .
They said , &quot; Our father was Abraham . &quot; Jesus said , &quot; If you are Abraham &apos;s sons , you will do what Abraham did
I will tell you the truth that I have heard in God , and now you want to kill me , and it is not Abraham &apos;s doing
&quot; You do what your father did , &quot; they said , &quot; but we were not born of lust , and only one father is God .
Jesus said , &quot; If God were your Father , you would love me ; for I came from God , and from God , and not from myself , but He sent me
Why do you not understand My words , except because you cannot hear My word ?
&quot; You are the devil of your father , the lust of your father , and your desire to do things . He was a murderer from the beginning , and did not keep the truth . Because he had no truth in his heart , he lied to himself , because he was a liar , and he was the father of the liars .
I tell you the truth , and you do not believe me
Who among you can testify that I am guilty ? Why do you not believe me , when I have told you the truth ?
&quot; He that is of God hears the word of God ; but you do not listen , for you are not of God .
The Jews answered , &quot; Is it not true that we say that you are a Samaritan , and that you are possessed by demons ?
Jesus said , &quot; I am not attached to demons ; I respect my Father , and you are slow to me .
I do not seek the glory of myself . There is one who seeks glory for me
&quot; I tell you in truth , that if a man obeys my way , he will never die .
And the Jews said unto him , We know now that thou art a devil : and Abraham is dead , and the prophets are dead ; and thou hast said , If a man keep my way , he shall never taste death .
Are you greater than our father Abraham ? He is dead , and the prophets are dead . What do you think of yourself
Jesus answered , &quot; If I glorify myself , my glory is nothing ; but my Father is my glory , and what you say is your God
You did not know him , but I know him . If I say I do not know him , I am lying , just as you are , but I know him , and I obey his ways
&quot; Your father Abraham rejoiced in the days when he looked at me , and he was glad to see .
&quot; The Jews said , &quot; Have you not seen Abraham before you were fifty years old
Jesus said , &quot; Truly , I have told you that Abraham was not there , but I was there
So they took a stone and struck him , but Jesus hid himself and went out of the temple .
When Jesus passed away , he was blind to the coming of a life
The disciples said to Jesus , &quot; Rabbi , this life has come to the blind , who has sinned , this man , and his parents
Jesus answered , &quot; This man has not sinned , neither have his parents sinned , but God &apos;s acts have been revealed to him
We must do the work of those who sent me in the daylight ; and when the night comes , no one will be able to do the work .
When I am in the world , it is the light of the world .
When Jesus had said this , he spit on the ground , and sprinkled the eyes of the blind with saliva and mud
And he said unto him , Go to the pond of Zeruiah , and wash ; and Zeruiah turned up , and was sent ; and he went and washed , and behold , he turned back .
And his neighbours and those who used to see him bargaining said , Is not this the man who sat bargaining before ?
Some said it was him , and others said no , it was like him ; and he himself said it was I
And they said unto him , What are thy eyes ?
Then he answered and said unto me , A man whose name is Jesus , and he washed my eyes with mud , and said unto me , Go and wash in the pond of Tyre , and I went and washed , and behold
And they said , The man is there ; and he said , I know not .
And they brought the blind to the Pharisees
The days when Jesus and the mud opened his eyes were Sabbaths
Then the Pharisees asked him how he could see ; and the blind man said to them , &quot; He has poured mud on my eyes , and I went to wash , and I have seen .
Some of the Pharisees said , &quot; This man is not from God , because he does not observe the Sabbath , &quot; and others said , &quot; How can a sinner do such signs ? &quot; Then they disputed .
And they said unto the blind man , What sayest thou of him , when he hath opened thy eyes ? And he said , He is a prophet .
The Jews did not believe that he was blind before , and that he could see afterwards , until he had called his parents
They said , &quot; Is this your son ? Why do you say that he was born blind ? How can he see now ? &quot;
And his parents answered and said , He is our son , and we know that he was blind when he was born
How can he see now ? We do not know . Who opened his eyes , we do not know . He has become a man ; ask him , and he himself will say .
His parents said this because they were afraid of the Jews , because it was agreed for the Jews that if any man should confess that Jesus was Christ , he should be driven out of the synagogue .
So his parents said , &quot; You ask him , for he has become a man
Then the Pharisees called the blind man the second time , and said to him , &quot; Give glory to God , for we know that he is a sinner
He said , &quot; He is a sinner . No , I do not know . One thing I know . I was blind before , and now I can see .
And they said unto him , What hath he done unto thee , and how hath he opened thy eyes ?
Then he answered , &quot; We have only told you that you did not listen . Why do you listen ? Will you not also be His disciples ? &quot;
And they cried unto him , saying , Thou art his disciple , and we are the disciples of Moses
&quot; We know that God spoke to Moses , but we do not know where he came from .
Then he answered , &quot; He has opened my eyes , and it is strange that you do not know where he comes from
&quot; We know that God does not listen to sinners , but he listens to those who fear God and do His will .
&quot; There has not been a man who opened the eyes of the blind from birth since the beginning of the world
&quot; If this man is not from God , he can do nothing
And they answered and said unto him , Art thou born in iniquity at all , and teachest us ? And they cast him away .
When Jesus heard that they had driven him out , when he had met him , he said , &quot; Do you believe in the Son of God ? &quot;
He answered , &quot; Lord , who is the Son of God that I should believe in ?
Jesus said , &quot; You have seen him , and it is he who is speaking to you
He said , &quot; Lord , I believe , and worship Jesus .
Jesus said , &quot; I am coming to judge the world so that those who cannot see can see , and those who can see will be blinded .
And when the Pharisees who were with him heard this , they said , Are we also blind ?
Jesus said to them , &quot; If you were blind , there would be no sin ; but now you say , &apos; We can see , &apos; so your sins are still
&quot; Truly I tell you , when a man enters the sheepfold , and does not go in from the door , but climbs in from elsewhere , he is a thief and a robber
&quot; He who enters from the door is the shepherd of the sheep .
He who sees the door opens it for him ; and the sheep hear his voice ; and he brings forth the sheep , whom he calls his own sheep .
&quot; When he has laid down his sheep , he walks ahead , and the sheep follow him , because they know his voice .
The sheep do not follow the living man , for they do not recognize his voice ; they must flee .
Jesus told them the parable , but he did not understand what it meant
Then Jesus said to them again , &quot; I tell you , while I am , that I am the Lamb
&quot; Everyone who came before me was a thief and a robber , and the sheep did not listen to them .
&quot; I am the gate ; and whoever comes in from Me must be saved and must eat grass
&quot; The thief comes to steal , to kill , and to destroy . I came to give life to the sheep , and to give them more abundance .
&quot; I am a good shepherd , a good shepherd for the sheep
&quot; If a servant is not a shepherd , and the sheep are not his own , and he sees the evil , he leaves the sheep and flees ; and the wolf seizes the sheep , and destroys the flock .
The hired man flees , for he is a hired man , and does not care for the sheep
I am a good shepherd , and I know my sheep , and my sheep know me
&quot; As the Father knows me , so do I know the Father , and I give my life for the sheep
And I have sheep , which are not in the circle ; and I must bring them , that they may hear my voice , and that they may form a flock , and become a shepherd .
&quot; My Father loves me , because I will spare my life and bring it back .
&quot; No man has taken my life , but I have given it to myself ; and I have the right to give it , and I have the right to take it back ; and this is the commandment which I have received from my father .
And the Jews disputed again for these things .
Some of them said , &quot; He is possessed by demons and mad . Why do you listen to him ? &quot;
Then another said , &quot; This is not what the devil &apos;s associates have said . Can a devil open the eyes of the blind ?
There is a feast in Jerusalem . It is the time of winter
Jesus walked in the hall of Solomon in the temple
The Jews surrounded him and said , &quot; When will you cause us to doubt ? If you are the Christ , tell us plainly
Jesus answered them , &quot; I have told you that you do not believe . What I have done in the name of my Father can be testified to me
&quot; But you do not believe , for you are not my sheep .
&quot; My sheep hear My voice , and I know them , and they follow Me
&quot; And I gave them life , and they shall never perish ; and no man shall take them out of My hand .
&quot; My father has given me sheep , and he is greater than all things ; and no man can take them away from my father &apos;s hand
I was the same as my father
And the Jews took again a stone to strike him
Jesus said to them , &quot; I have shown you many good things from the Father , and you have beaten me for that stone
The Jews answered , &quot; We did not stone you for good deeds , but for your sakes , and for your sakes , as individuals , and as gods .
Jesus said , &quot; Is it not written in your law , &apos; I said you were God&apos;
The word of the Scriptures cannot be abolished : but those who bear the doctrine of God are called God .
&quot; You also say to him , &apos; Do you speak blasphemous words , &apos; when the father , who is sanctified and has been sent into the world , claims to be the son of God
&quot; If I do not do what my father did , you will not believe me .
&quot; If I do so , even though you do not believe me , believe these things , that you may know and understand : The Father is in me , and I am in the Father
They will take him again , and he will flee out of their hands and go away
Then Jesus went out to the Jordan , and lived in the place where John was first baptized
Many came to him and said , &quot; John has not done a miracle , but all that he says is true .
And there were many more who believed in Jesus
There was a sick man named Lazarus , who lived in the village of Bethany , in the village of Mary and her sister Magdalene .
Mary was the one who anointed the Lord with oil , and wiped his feet with hair ; and Lazarus , who was sick , was his brother .
Then sent his sisters to Jesus , saying , &quot; Lord , the man whom you love is sick
When Jesus heard it , he said , &quot; This disease is not to die , but to God &apos;s glory , that the Son of God may be glorified
Jesus came to love Martha , and his sister , and Lazarus
When he heard that Lazarus was sick , he lived two days in the land where he lived .
Then he said to his disciples , &quot; Let us go again to Judah
&quot; The disciples said , &quot; Rabbi , the Jews are about to throw stones at you . Are you still going there
Jesus answered them , &quot; Isn &apos;t it twelve o &apos;clock in the day ? When a man walks in the day , he falls not , because he sees the light of the world
&quot; If he walks in the darkness , he will fall , for he has no light
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; Our friend Lazarus is asleep , and I am going to wake him up
The disciples said , &quot; Lord , if he sleeps , he will be well
Jesus said that he was dead ; but they thought that he slept as usual
And Jesus told them plainly , saying , Lazarus is dead
I have not rejoiced there , but it is for your sakes that you may believe ; and now we may go to Him .
Then said Domar , also called Lower Tyre , to the fellow disciple , &quot; Let us go and die with him .
When Jesus came , he knew that it had been four days since Lazarus was in the tomb
And Bethany was not far from Jerusalem ; it was about six miles
A number of Jews came to see Martha and Mary to comfort them for their brothers
When he heard that Jesus had come , he went out to meet him , and Mary sat still at home .
And he said unto him , Lord , if thou werest here early , my brother would not die
&quot; Now I know that whatever you ask of God , He will give it to you
Jesus said , &quot; Your brother must be resurrected
And he said , I know that in the resurrection of the last day he shall be resurrected
Jesus said to him , &quot; Resurrection is in me , and life is in me . Those who believe in me will be resurrected even though they are dead
Whoever lives and believes in Me will never die . Do you believe this ?
He said , &quot; Yes , Lord , I believe that you are Christ , the Son of God , who is coming to the world
And when he had said this , he went back into the darkness , and called his son Mary , and said , Son , come , and call on thee
When Mary heard it , she hurried to Jesus
At that time Jesus had not yet entered into the village , but was still in the place where he was received at Madal
And when the Jews who comforted him at his house saw him hurrying up and going out , they followed him , thinking that he would go to the grave to weep
When Mary came to Jesus , and saw him , she fell down at his feet , and said , &quot; Lord , if you were here before , my brother would not die
And when Jesus saw him weeping , and the Jews who were with him weeping , he wept with great sorrow .
Then they said , &quot; You have put him in it . &quot; They answered , &quot; Please let the Lord come . &quot;
Jesus cried
Then said the Jew , &quot; Look how much he is earnest in love with this man
And one of them said , &quot; Have he opened the eyes of the blind , and can he not cause him not to die ?
Then Jesus wept again , and came to the tomb ; and the tomb was a hole , and a stone was against it
Jesus said to him , &quot; Move the stone away . &quot; The sister of the dead man , Magda , said to him , &quot; Lord , it will be a smell in his presence ; for four days have passed since he died
Jesus said , &quot; I did not say to you , &apos; If you believe , you will see the glory of God
And they removed the stone , and Jesus lifted up his eyes to heaven , and said , Father , I thank thee , because thou hast heard me
&quot; I also know that you listen to me , but I say this to all those who stand around , that they may believe that you sent me
And when he had said this , he cried out with a loud voice , saying , Come out of Lazarus
Then the dead man came out , and was clothed with cloth on his feet and with a scarf on his face ; and Jesus said to them , &quot; Get him out , and let him go
The Jews who came to Mary and saw what Jesus did believed more in him
But among them were those who went to the Pharisees to testify against them concerning what Jesus had done
Then the chief priests and the Pharisees gathered themselves together in the synagogue , and said , &quot; What shall we do with this man , who has done some good signs
&quot; If it is so by Him , all men will believe in Him ; and the Romans will come to seize our land and our people
And there was a man among them , whose name was Caiaphas , who was high priest this year , and said unto them , Know ye not ?
&quot; It is in your interest that a man should die for the people , lest he perish in the land .
&quot; This is not because of himself , but because he was a great priest this year , and he prophesied that Jesus would die for this country
&quot; Not only will he die for this country , but he will gather together all the children of God who are scattered
And from that day onward they made a covenant to kill Jesus
So when Jesus was no longer evident among the Jews , he departed from there to a place near the wilderness , and came to a city called Ephraim , and dwelt there with the disciples
The Passover of the Jews was near , and many went up from the country to Jerusalem to cleanse themselves before the Passover
And they sought Jesus , and stood in the temple , and said unto one another , What do ye mean , that he is not come at the feast ?
Then the chief priests and the Pharisees commanded early , saying , &quot; If any man knows that Jesus is there , let him declare it , and go and take him
On the sixth day before Passover Jesus came to Bethany , the place where he raised Lazarus from the dead
And there was in it a man that prepared a feast for Jesus : and he served , and Lazarus was also among the men that sat with Jesus .
And Mary took a pound of precious ointment , and anointed Jesus &apos; feet , and wiped them with her own hair ; and the house was full of ointment
There was a disciple , Judas the Galilean , who would betray Jesus
&quot; Why does this ointment not sell thirty-two silvers for the poor ?
&quot; He said this not in remembrance of the poor , but because he was a thief , and carried a bag of money , and often took what was in it .
Jesus said , &quot; It is by him that I will be buried
Because the poor are always with you . But you don &apos;t always have me
Many of the Jews knew that Jesus was there , and came , not for the sake of Jesus , but to see the way of Lazarus , where he was raised from the dead
But the chief priest agreed to kill even Lazarus
For the cause of Lazarus many of the Jews returned to believe in Jesus
And it came to pass on the second day , that a great number of the Passover-makers heard that Jesus was coming to Jerusalem
Then they took the palm trees and went out to meet him , and cried out , saying , &quot; Blessed is the King of Israel , who has come in the name of the Lord and has spread them out
Jesus took a donkey and rode on it , as it is written
Don &apos;t be afraid , O people of Zion ; Your king has come on a donkey &apos;s hoof .
The disciples did not understand these things at first , but when Jesus was glorified , they remembered that it was written to him , and so they did to him
When Jesus called Lazarus to be raised from the dead from the tomb , he testified with all those who were with him
And when they heard that Jesus had done these signs , they went to meet him
Then the Pharisees said to one another , &quot; Behold , you are a vain work , and the whole world has followed him
And at that time some of the Galileans came up from among the people who worshipped .
And they came to Philip of Galilee , the great , and asked him , saying , Sir , we would advise Jesus
Philip went to tell Andrew , and Andrew and Philip went to tell Jesus
Jesus said , &quot; The time has come for the Son of man to be glorified
&quot; Truly I am telling you , a grain that has not fallen to the ground is still a grain ; and if it die , many grains will be formed .
He who loves his own life loses it ; and he who hates his own life in this world keeps it for ever .
&quot; If any man obeys me , follow me ; and those who obey me will be there ; and if any man obeys me , my Father will respect him .
&quot; Now I am grieving in my heart , and what shall I say ? Save me , Father , from this hour ; but I was waiting for it
Father , glorify thy name : and there was a voice from heaven saying , I have glorified my name , and I will glorify it again .
And when all the people that stood by heard it , they said , There is a thunderbolt ; and another said , There is an angel speaking to him
Jesus said , &quot; This voice is not for me , but for you
The king of this world shall be driven out , and he shall be judged in this world .
&quot; If I am lifted up from the earth , I will draw a people to me
The word of Jesus was originally about how he would die
And they answered and said , We have heard that it is written in the law that Christ is everlasting : how sayest thou that the Son of man must be raised up ? and who is this Son of man ?
Jesus said to them , &quot; There is not much time left for the light among you . Walk in the light , lest darkness come upon you . Those who walk in the darkness do not know where to go .
&quot; When you have light , believe in it , and become children of light .
And when Jesus had said this , he departed from them , and hid himself ; and though he had done many signs before them , yet they did not believe him
This is to test the words of Isaiah the prophet , saying , &quot; Lord , who believes in what we have preached , and to whom is the arm of the Lord revealed ? &quot;
Therefore they could not believe , because Isaiah said ,
&quot; The Lord has made them blind and hard of heart , lest their eyes see , and their hearts understand , and turn back , and I will heal them .
And Isaiah , seeing the glory of him , referred to him when he spoke these words
Nevertheless , some of the officers believed in him , and for the sake of the Pharisees they did not confess , and were afraid of being driven out of the synagogue .
For this is the glory of them that love men , and the glory of them that love God more than God
Jesus cried out , &quot; Believe in me , not in me , but in him who sent me
&quot; When a man sees me , he sees him who sent me .
&quot; I have come to the world as light , so that those who believe in me will not be in darkness .
&quot; If any man hears My words and does not obey them , I will not judge him ; I came not to judge the world , but to save the world .
Whoever turns away from Me and does not receive My word , He will be judged . That is the way I speak , and He will be judged in the Last Day .
For I have not spoken by myself ; but the Father who sent me has commanded me what I should say and what I should say
I know also that His commandment is eternal life ; therefore my words are according to the Father &apos;s words to me
Before the Passover , Jesus knew that the time had come for him to return to his Father , and he loved them to the end , since he loved those who belonged to him in the world
And it came to pass at the time of the supper , that the devil had put in the heart of Judah the Galilean , the son of Simon , the word of the sale of Jesus
Jesus knew that the Father had given all things into his hand , and that he had come out of God , and that he would return to God
And he arose from his seat , and took off his clothes , and put on a scarf
Then he poured the water into the basin , and washed the feet of the disciples , and washed them with the scarf that he had wrapped himself in .
Then Peter came to Simon Peter , and said to him , &quot; Lord , do you wash my feet
Jesus answered , &quot; You do not know what I have done now , but you will later know .
Peter said , &quot; You will never wash my feet . &quot; Jesus said , &quot; If I do not wash you , you will be nothing to me
Simon Peter said , &quot; Lord , not only my feet , but also my hands and my head , will I wash
Jesus said , &quot; Everyone who has taken a bath is cleansed of his whole body by a single wash of his feet ; you are clean , but not all of you
&quot; When Jesus knew who was to sell him , he said , &quot; You are not clean
After he had washed their feet , he put on his clothes , and sat down , and said to them , &quot; Do you understand what I have done to you
&quot; You call my husband and my Lord , and you are right in saying that I was
&quot; I am your Lord and your husband , and I wash your feet , and you wash your feet with one another .
&quot; I have set you an example , that you may do according to what I have done to you .
&quot; Truly , I tell you , a servant cannot be greater than his master , neither can a messenger be greater than his servant
Blessed are you if you go forth , knowing this
&quot; My word is not for all of you . I know who I have chosen . Now let us test the Scriptures , saying , &apos; Those who eat with me kick me with their feet .
Now that things have not yet been accomplished , I will first tell you that when things are accomplished , you may believe that I am Christ
&quot; Truly I tell you , that whoever receives what I send receives me , and whoever receives me receives what I send
And when Jesus had said these things , in his sorrow , he said plainly , &quot; In truth I have told you that there is a man among you who is about to sell me
The disciples looked at each other and could not guess who it was that they had spoken
There was a disciple whom Jesus loved , and he bowed himself near to him in his arms
Then Simon Peter nodded and said to him , &quot; Tell us who the Lord has spoken
Then the disciple leaned on his chest , and asked him , &quot; Lord , who is this ? &quot;
Jesus answered , &quot; Who am I to dip a piece of bread for ? &quot; Then Jesus dipped a piece of bread , and gave it to Judas the son of Simon the Galilean
And when he had eaten , Satan entered into his heart , and Jesus said unto him , Do quickly what thou hast done .
None of the people in the room knew why he had said this to him
And there was a man who , because of Judah , carried a purse for Jesus , said to him , &quot; Go and buy for us the things we use for the Passover , or for the poor
And when Judah had received the bread , he went out at once ; and it was night
When he had gone out , Jesus said , &quot; Now the Son of man is glorified , and God is glorified in him
God will glorify the Son of man for his own sake , and will glorify him quickly
Little children , I have been with you for a short time , and afterwards you will seek me , but you will not be able to come to the place where I have gone ; as I said to the Jews , so I say to you now .
&quot; I have given you a new commandment , that you love one another . How I love you , how you will love me
&quot; If you have a love for one another , then all will know that you are My disciples .
Then Simon Peter said to Jesus , &quot; Lord , go into it . &quot; Jesus answered , &quot; You cannot go with me to the place where I went , but you will follow me .
Peter said , &quot; Lord , why am I not able to go with you now , and I will give my life for you
Jesus said , &quot; Would you give up your life for me ? I have told you , while I am here , that the chicken calls E first , and you will not recognize me three times
&quot; Do not grieve in your hearts . Believe in God , and believe in Me
There are many dwellings in my father &apos;s house ; and if there were none , I would have told you ; and I went to a place prepared for you .
&quot; If I go and prepare a place for you , I will bring you again to me , and I will be there , and you will be there
I will go there , and you will know it , and you will know the way.There is an ancient scroll in which I will go there , and you will know the way
Then said Domar to him , &quot; Lord , we do not know where you are going ; how do we know the way
Jesus said , &quot; I am the way , the truth , and the life ; and without me no man could go to the Father
&quot; If you know me , you will know my Father . From now on you will know him and have seen him
Philip said to him , &quot; Lord , show us the Father , and we will know .
Jesus said to him , &quot; Philippe , have you not known me , since I have been with you so long ? The people have seen me , but the Father . What do you say , &apos; Show the Father to us ? &apos;
&quot; I am in the Father , and the Father is in me . Do you not believe that what I said to you was not by myself , but by the Father who lives in me
Believe in me , I am in the Father , and the Father is in me , whether you believe it or not , and believe in me for what I have done
&quot; I am truthful in telling you that those who believe in me will do what I have done , and will do greater things than this , because I have gone to the Father
&quot; Whatever you ask in My name , I will accomplish , that the Father may be glorified for his sons .
&quot; Whatever you ask in My name , I will accomplish .
&quot; If you love me , you will obey my commandments
&quot; I ask the Father to give you another guardian , or a comforter , to be with you forever .
He is the Holy Spirit of truth , which the world cannot accept , because they do not see him , nor know him ; but you know him , because he is always with you , and will be with you
&quot; I will not leave you as orphans ; I will come to you
And in a few days the world shall see me no more ; but ye shall see me ; for I am alive , and ye shall also be alive .
&quot; In that day you will know that I am in the Father , and you are in me , and I am in you
&quot; He who loves me and obeys my commandments will make my Father love him , and I will also love him , and I will appear to him
Judas ( not Galilee ) said to Jesus , &quot; Lord , why do you show yourself to us , and not to the world ? &quot;
Jesus answered , &quot; If a man loves me , he will follow my way , and my father will love him , and we will go to him and live with him
Those who do not love Me do not obey My way , and the way you have heard is not mine , but the way of the Father who sent me .
&quot; I told you these things when I lived with you
&quot; But the Holy Spirit , which the Father has sent in my name , will teach you all things , and will remind you of all that I have spoken to you .
I have left you peace , and I have given you my peace ; and what I have given you is not like what the world has given you ; neither shall you be troubled nor be afraid in your hearts .
&quot; When you hear that I have said to you , &apos; I will go and I will come to you , &apos; you will rejoice , if you love me , because I have come to my Father , for he is greater than I am
&quot; Now that things have not yet been accomplished , I foretold to you that when things are accomplished , you may believe
&quot; I will not speak to you any more after this , for the king of the world is coming , and he is nothing in me .
&quot; But let the world know how I love the Father , and how he commands me , and how I will do it ; Arise , let us go .
I am the true vine , and my father is the cultivator
&quot; He will cut off the branches which I do not bear , and he will cleanse the branches which he bears , and increase the fruit of the branches .
Now ye are cleansed because of the way which I have spoken unto you
&quot; You shall be in me , and I will be in you ; and if the branches are not in the vine , they will not bear fruit ; and if you are not in me , so will it be
&quot; I am a vine , and you are branches ; and he who is always in me , and I am always in him , bears more fruit ; and you will do nothing because he has left me .
&quot; If a man is not in me , he is as a branch that is dried up outside , and a man picks it up and throws it into the fire .
&quot; If you are always in Me , My words are always in you , and all your desires will be fulfilled in prayer .
&quot; For your fruit is multiplied , and my Father is glorified ; and you are my disciples .
&quot; I love you , just as the Father loves me ; and you will always be in my love .
If you obey my commandments , you will be in my love , just as I obeyed my father &apos;s commandments , and you will be in his love .
&quot; I have spoken these things to you , that they may please me , and be in your hearts , and that your joy may be fulfilled .
&quot; It is my commandment that you love one another , just as I love you .
There is no greater love than the sacrifice of a man for a friend
&quot; If you do what I command you , you will be my friends .
Then will I no more call you servants , because the servants do not know what the master has done ; but I will call you friends , because all that I have heard from my father has been told you .
&quot; You have not chosen me , but I have chosen you , and I have sent you to bear fruit , that your fruit may remain , and that you may serve in my name , and that whatever you ask of the Father , he may give it to you
&quot; This is what I have commanded you , that you should love one another
&quot; If the world hates you , you know that it hates you , and that it hates me beforehand .
If you belong to the world , the world will love itself ; but because you are not of the world , and because I have chosen you from the world , the world will hate you .
&quot; Remember what I said to you before : No servant is greater than his master ; if they oppress me , they will oppress you ; if they obey me , they will obey you .
&quot; But they will do all these things to you in my name , because they do not know who sent me .
If I had not had something to teach them , they would not have sinned ; but now their sins are in vain .
Who hates me , and hates my father
If I had not done among them that which no man had done , they would not have sinned ; but now even I and my Father see and hate .
This is to testify to what is written in their law , saying , &quot; They have no reason to hate me .
&quot; But I will send a minister from the Father , the Holy Spirit of truth from the Father ; and when he comes , he will bear witness for me
&quot; You also shall bear witness , because you were with me from the beginning .
&quot; I have told you these things , so that you will not fall
&quot; They will drive you out of the synagogue , and the time will come that whoever kills you will serve God
For they have not known the Father , neither have they known me
I tell you this because it is time for you to remember what I said to you ; I did not tell you this at first , because I was with you
&quot; Now I go to the Father who sent me , and there is no one among you who asks me , &apos; Where will you live ? &apos;
&quot; For I have told you this , and you are filled with sorrow
But I will tell you the truth , that it is good for me to go , and that if I do not go , the Beneficent One will not come to you ; and if I go , I will send him
He has come , and will call the world to sin , to righteousness , to judgment , and to reproach himself
For sin , because they do not believe in me
&quot; For righteousness is because I went to the Father , and you will not see me again .
For judgment , for the king of the world is judged
I have other good things to tell you , but you are no longer in charge .
Only when the Holy Spirit of truth comes will he guide you to understand all the truth ; for he speaks not by himself , but by what he hears ; and he will inform you of the things to come .
&quot; He will glorify me , because he will tell you what he will receive from me .
&quot; All that the Father has is mine ; therefore I said , &apos; Tell you that he will receive it from me .
If you wait no longer , you will not see me . If you wait no longer , you will see me again
Then some of the disciples said to one another , &quot; He said to us , &apos; If you wait no longer , you will not see me , and if you wait no longer , you will see me . &apos; And he said , &apos; What does this mean , that I go to the Father ?
The disciples said to one another , &quot; What does he mean when he says , &apos; We do not understand what he says
When Jesus saw that they were asking him , he said , &quot; I said , &apos; You will not see me until a little while , and until a little while , you will also see me .
Truly I am telling you that you will weep and weep , and the world will rejoice , and you will grieve , and your grief will be turned into joy .
When a woman bears a child , she grieves ; for his time is come ; and when she bears a child , she remembers no more the pain ; for she has given birth to a man for joy in the world .
You are sad , but when I see you again , your heart will rejoice , and no one will take it away .
&quot; In that day you will not ask me anything , and I will tell you in truth , &quot; Whatever you ask of the Father , he will give it to you in my name
&quot; You did not ask for anything before in My name ; but now you will receive it , that your joy may be satisfied .
&quot; I have spoken these things to you in parables . The time will come when I will no longer speak to you in parables , but I will tell you the Father plainly .
&quot; In that day you will pray in My name ; I will not say to you , &apos; I will ask for your father&apos;
The Father himself loves you , because you have loved me and believed that I came from the Father
I have come out of the Father into the world , and I have departed from the world , and have gone to the Father
&quot; The disciples said , &quot; Now you speak plainly , and do not use any metaphor
Now we know that thou knowest all things , and that no man asketh thee : therefore we believe that thou art of God
Jesus said , &quot; Do you believe now
Behold , the time is coming , and it is past ; and you shall be divided , and go to your own place , and leave me alone ; for I am not alone , for my Father is with me
&quot; I tell you these things , that you may have peace in me , and that you may have tribulations in the world ; but you may rest assured that I have overcome the world .
When Jesus had said this , he lifted up his eyes to heaven and said , &quot; Father , the time has come that you may glorify your son , and that your son may also glorify you
&quot; Just as you gave him power to rule over all who have blood , that he might give everlasting life to those whom you have given him
Know thy only true God , and Jesus Christ , whom thou hast sent , that is eternal life
&quot; I have been glorified by You in the earth ; I have fulfilled all that You have promised me .
Father , I ask you to make me glory with you , that I may be glory with all of you before the world .
&quot; Those whom thou hast given me from the world , I have made thy name manifest unto them ; they are thys , and thou hast given them unto me , and they have kept thy way .
&quot; Now they know that all that you have given me has come from you
&quot; For I have given them the way which You have given me , and they have received it ; and they know that I have come out of You , and that You have sent me in faith .
&quot; I pray for them , not for the world , but for those whom You have given me , for they are Yours .
&quot; Everything that is mine is yours , and yours is mine , and I am glorified for them
&quot; From now on I am not in the world , but they are in the world , and I will go to You . O Holy Father , keep them in the name that You have given me , that they may become one like us
&quot; I have kept them while they were with them , because of the name which You have given me , and I have kept them , and none of them perished except the Son of perdition , that the word of the Scripture may be fulfilled .
&quot; Behold , I go to you , and I say this in the world to fill their hearts with my joy .
I have given them thy way , and the world hates them , because they are not of the world , as I am not of the world .
&quot; I do not ask you to let them go out of the world , but to keep them from the wicked .
They are not of the world , as I am not of the world
May Thou sanctify them with the truth : Thy way is the truth .
&quot; As you have sent me to the world , so have I sent them to the world
I sanctify myself for their sakes , that they may also be sanctified by the truth
I pray not only for these men , but also for those who believe in me because of their words
As your Father is in me , so am I in you ; and as they are in us , that the world may believe that you have sent me .
&quot; I have given them the glory which you have given me , that they may be united as we are united
&quot; Behold , I am in them , and you are in me , that they may be united in oneness , that the world may know that you have sent me , and that you love them as you love me .
Father , I am in it , and let those whom You have given me be in it with me , that they may see the glory which You have given me , for You have loved me before the creation of the world .
O Father of righteousness , the world did not know you , but I know you ; and they also know that you sent me
&quot; I have instructed them by your name , and I have instructed them , that your love for me may be in them , and I in them
And when Jesus had said this , he went out with the disciples , and passed over the stream of water , and there was a garden in it , and he entered in with the disciples
Judas , who sold Jesus , also knew the place , because Jesus and his disciples were gathered there many times
And Judah took a company of men , and the chief priests , and the officers of the Pharisees , and came into the garden with lanterns , and spears , and weapons
When Jesus knew that all things were about to come to him , he came out and said to them , &quot; Who are you looking for
And they answered and said unto him , Seek Jesus of Nazareth ; and Jesus said unto them , I am he ; and Judas , which sold him , stood there with them .
When Jesus said , &quot; I am , &quot; they turned back and fell on the ground
Then he asked them , &quot; Who are you looking for ? &quot; They said , &quot; Jesus of Nazareth
Jesus said , &quot; I have told you that I am . If you seek me , let these men go
&quot; This testifies what Jesus said before , saying , &apos; I have not lost one of those whom you have given me
And Simon Peter took a sword , and drew it out , and cut off the servant of the high priest with a sword , and cut off his right ear ; and the servant &apos;s name was Mark
Then Jesus said to Peter , &quot; Take the sword into the sheath ; will I not drink the cup my father has given me
Then the captain of the army and the centurion and the officer of the Jews took Jesus and bound him
And he brought it before Anah , for he was the father of Caiaphas the high priest this year
&quot; This was Asaph , who had spoken before to the Jews , saying , &apos; A man who died for the people was beneficial .
Simon Peter followed Jesus , and a disciple followed him , whom the high priest knew , and went in with him into the house of the high priest
But Peter stood outside the door ; and the disciple whom the high priest knew came out , and the woman who looked at the door said aloud , and led Peter in .
And the woman that looked at the door said unto Peter , Art thou not also a disciple of this man ? And he said , I am not
And the servants and the servants stood there and made a fire because of the cold ; and Peter stood there and made a fire with them .
Then the high priest questioned him with the disciples of Jesus and with his teachings
Jesus answered , &quot; I have always spoken plainly to the world . I am often in the synagogues and in the temples , where the Jews are gathered together to teach , and I am in the darkness and have nothing to say
Why do you ask me ? You can ask those who have heard what I have said to them . They know what I have said
And when Jesus had spoken these words , a messenger stood by , and touched him with his hand , saying , Thus answerest thou the high priest ?
Jesus said , &quot; If I say no , you can prove it . If I say yes , why do you beat me ? &quot;
Then he delivered Jesus to Caiaphas the high priest , who was still bound .
Simon Peter was standing on the fire , and someone said to him , &quot; Are you not also his disciple ? &quot; Peter refused to confess , saying , &quot; I am not .
And there was a servant of the high priest , Peter &apos;s kinsman , who had cut off his ear , and said , Have I not seen you in the garden with him ?
Peter refused to admit it again . The chicken cried out in the morning
And they removed Jesus from the gate of Kohath into the courtyard ; and it was early in the day , and they themselves entered not into the courtyard , lest they might eat the feast of the Passover , because they were defiled .
Then he went out to them , and said to them , &quot; Why do you tell this man ?
And they answered and said unto him , If this man had not done evil , we would not have given him unto thee
Then said Pilate , Take him with you , and judge him according to your law : and the Jews said , We have no power to kill
&quot; This is to test what Jesus said , &quot; How will he die ? &quot;
And he went into the court again , and called Jesus , and said unto him , Art thou the king of the Jews
Jesus answered , &quot; Is this what you said , or what others have said to you about me ? &quot;
Then said Pilate , &quot; Am I a Jew ? What have you done , that your people and the priests have given you to me ?
Jesus answered , &quot; My country does not belong to this world . If my country belongs to this world , my servants must fight so that I will not be given to the Jews , but my country does not belong to this world
Then said Pilate unto him , Art thou king ? And Jesus answered him , Thou sayest that I am king : for this cause I was born , and for this cause I came into the world to testify unto the truth : and all that are of the truth hearken unto me
Then said Pilate , What is the truth ? And when he had said this , he came out to the Jews , and said unto them , I find no fault in him .
&quot; But you have a statute : &apos; Do you want me to release a man to you on the Passover ? Do you want me to release the king of the Jews to you ?
Then they cried again , saying , &quot; Do not ask for this man , but for Barabbas , who is a robber
Now Pilate whips Jesus
&quot; The soldier will wear a crown of thorns on his head , and put on his purple robe
And they came near unto him , and said , Congratulations , O king of the Jews ; and they struck him with their hands .
Then he came out again and said to the people , &quot; I will bring him out to you , that you may know what sin I have committed against him .
Then Jesus came out , and was clothed with a crown of thorns , and clothed in purple robes . Then Pilate said to them , &quot; Look at this man ,
And when the chief priests and the officers saw him , they cried out , &quot; Crucify him , crucify him ! &quot; And Pilate said , &quot; You yourself crucify him ; for I cannot find out what sin he has committed .
And the Jews answered and said , We have a law according to which he is to die , because he is the son of God for himself
When Pilate heard this , he was more and more afraid .
Then he entered into the office and said to Jesus , &quot; You are there ; &quot; but Jesus did not answer .
Then said Pilate , &quot; Do you not speak to me ? Do you not know that I have the right to release you , and that I have the right to crucify you
Jesus answered , &quot; If it is not given to you from above , you have no authority over me ; therefore the man who has given me to you is more guilty .
But the Jews cried out , saying , &quot; If you release this man , he will not be a servant of Caesar ; for he who has made himself king has betrayed Caesar . &quot;
When Pilate heard this , he took Jesus out , and went to a place called the stone of Pevvah , which is called Ebadiah in Hebrew , and sat there
Then said Pilate unto the Jews , Behold , this is your king ; for it is the day of the feast of the Passover , about noon
And they cried out , and said , Cast him off , cast him off , and crucify him . And Pilate said , May I crucify your king ? And the chief priest answered , We have no king but Caesar
Then Pilate gave Jesus to them to crucify
And they took him away , and he came out on his own cross , and came to a place called a place of bones , and called each one of them in Hebrew :
And there they nailed him on the cross , and two others and he were nailed together , one on one side , and Jesus was in the middle
And he wrote a name on the cross with a sign , Jesus , King of the Jews of Nazareth .
For the place where Jesus was crucified was near to the city , and it was written in Hebrews , Romans , and Hebrews ,
And the chief priest of the Jews said unto Pilate , Write not unto the king of the Jews , but write unto him , saying , I am the king of the Jews
Then said Pilate , &quot; I have written what I have written
And the soldier , having crucified Jesus , took his garment four times , one for each soldier , and his girdle , which had no seams , and was woven up and down
And they said unto one another , We will not tear it apart , but we will give it for a lot , and see who shall receive it , according to the words of the Scriptures : They have divided my garments , and for my inner garments for a lot . And the soldier did so
And there stood by the cross of Jesus his mother , and the sisters of his mother , and Mary the wife of Gershon , and Mary Magdalene
When Jesus saw his mother and the disciple whom he loved standing by , he said to his mother , &quot; Mother , look at your son
Then he said to the disciple , &quot; Look at your mother , &quot; and from then on the disciple took him to his own house .
Then Jesus , knowing that all things had come to pass , said , &quot; I am thirsty , &quot; that he might prove the words of the Scriptures
And there was a vessel full of vinegar , and they laid it in it ; and they dipped it in the seaweed , and bound it on the knees of cattle , and brought it to his mouth .
When Jesus had tasted the vinegar , he said , &quot; It is done ; &quot; and he lowered his head , and delivered his soul to God .
And the Jews , because it was a day of preparation , and because the Sabbath was a great day , asked Pilate to cut off their legs , and to take them away , lest the dead be left on the cross on the Sabbath day
Then came the soldier , and cut off the first man &apos;s leg , and nailed the second man &apos;s leg with Jesus
&quot; But when they came to Jesus and saw that he was dead , they did not break his legs
And there came forth blood and water , when one of the soldiers put his gun by his ribs
And he that seeth it beareth witness , and his witness is true , and he knoweth that what he saith is true , that ye may believe .
These things have been done in order to test the words of the Scriptures , &quot; No bone of his is broken . &quot;
There is another verse in the Scriptures which says , &apos; They shall rely on those whom they have set up .
After these things , Joseph of the Amalekites , a disciple of Jesus , who was afraid of the Jews , came to Pilate to take away the body of Jesus , and when Pilate had consented , he took away the body of Jesus .
And the mother of Nicodemus , who had come to Jesus in the night before , came with about a hundred cattle , without medicine and with incense ,
And they took the body of Jesus , and wrapped it with fine linen and spices , according to the custom of the Jews :
There is a garden in the place where Jesus crucified , and in the garden is a new tomb , which has never been buried
For the Jews had prepared the day , and because the tomb was near , they laid Jesus in it
And it came to pass on the first day of the seventh day , early in the morning , when it was dark , that Mary Magdalene came to the tomb , and saw the stone moved away from the tomb .
Then they ran to see Simon Peter , and the disciple whom Jesus loved , and said to them , &quot; Someone has moved the Lord out of the tomb , and we do not know where he is
Peter and the disciple went out to the tomb
The two men ran together , and the disciple ran faster than Peter , and came to the tomb
And he looked down , and behold , the linen was still in it , but it had not entered .
And Simon Peter came after him , and went into the tomb , and saw the fine linen that was laid therein
And he saw the scarf of Jesus , which was not wrapped with linen on one side , but wrapped on the other side
Then the disciple who had come to the tomb entered in , and believed when he saw it .
For they had not yet understood the meaning of the Scriptures , that Jesus must be raised from the dead
Then the two disciples returned to their place of residence
But Mary stood outside the tomb and wept ; and when she wept , she looked down into the tomb
And he saw two angels sitting in white robes in the place where he had laid the body of Jesus , one on his head and one on his feet
Then the angel said to him , &quot; Woman , why do you weep ? &quot; He said , &quot; Because someone has taken away my Lord , and I do not know whether he has put him in it
And when he had said this , he turned around and saw Jesus standing there , but he knew not that it was Jesus .
Jesus said to him , &quot; Woman , why are you crying ? Who are you looking for ? &quot; Mary , who was looking for the garden , said to him , &quot; Lord , if you take him away , tell me that if you put him in it , I will take him away
And Jesus said , Mary . And Mary turned and spoke unto him in Hebrew , saying , Rabbani ; for Rabbani is the word of the husband .
Jesus said , &quot; Do not touch me , for I have not yet ascended to my Father . Go to my brothers and tell them , &apos; I will ascend to my Father and your Father . See my God and your God .
Then Mary of Magdalene went to testify to the disciples , saying , &quot; I have seen the Lord , &quot; and he told them again what the Lord had said to him
And it came to pass in the evening , on the first of the seven days , that the doors were shut where the disciples were , for fear of the Jews : and Jesus stood in the midst of them , and said unto them , Peace be unto you
And when he had said this , he stretched out his hand and his ribs , and pointed them , and the disciples rejoiced when they saw the Lord
Then Jesus said to them , &quot; Peace be to you , and as the Father sent me , so will I send you
And when he had said this , He breathed into them , and said , &quot; You have the Holy Spirit
Whose sins you forgive , and whose sins you forgive ; and whose sins you leave , and whose sins you leave behind
Among the twelve disciples was a man named Dorma the lowly , who was not with them when Jesus came
And the disciples said unto him , We have seen the Lord ; and he said unto them , I have not seen the mark of his hand , neither have I looked into it with my fingers , neither have I looked into his ribs with my hands , but I have never believed
And after eight days the disciples were in the house , and the horse was with them , and the doors were shut ; and Jesus stood in the midst , saying , Peace be to you
Then said thou unto Thomas , stretch out thy finger over thy head , and touch my hand ; stretch out thy hand , and search by my ribs ; be not doubtful , but believe .
Then said Domar , &quot; My Lord , my God
Jesus said to him , &quot; You believe in me because you see me . Blessed is he who does not see but believes
Jesus did many other miracles before his disciples , which are not recorded in this book
