But when they disagreed with one another , they dispersed ; and they did not disperse . Paul said , &quot; It is not wrong that the Holy Spirit spoke to your fathers through the prophet Isaiah
He said , &quot; Go and testify to the people , saying , &apos; You hear , but you do not understand ; you see , but you do not know&apos;
For oil has covered the hearts of these people , and the ears have become dull , and the eyes have closed ; and I fear that the eyes will see , and the ears will hear , and the hearts will understand ; and I will turn and heal them .
Therefore know that God &apos;s salvation is now sent to the Gentiles , and they will hear it .
And when Paul had spoken these words , the Jews went away , when they had debated .
Paul lived in the house which he had rented for two years , and all those who came to see him received him
Be brave in preaching the word of the kingdom of God , and in teaching the things of the Lord Jesus Christ , and no man forbids them
Paul , the servant of Jesus Christ , the apostle and messenger of the gospel
This is the gospel which God promised through the prophets in the Scriptures
And concerning his son , my Lord Jesus Christ , born of the seed of David according to the flesh ,
According to the Spirit of goodness , because he is raised from the dead , he is manifested in great power as the Son of God
&quot; We have received grace from him , and the office of an apostle , that we may cause people to believe in the truth in his name among all the nations
Among them are those of you who are called to Jesus Christ
I write unto you in Rome , beloved of God , and called to be saints : Grace and peace be to you from our Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ .
First , I thank my God for all of you through Jesus Christ , for your faith has spread throughout the whole world
&quot; In the gospel of his son , I , the God of the Spirit , can witness to you how I have not dwelt .
In prayer and supplication , or according to the will of God , there is a straight path to you
For I desire to see you , and to give you some of the gifts of the Spirit , that you may be strong .
Then I will be comforted among you , because of your faith in one another with me .
&quot; Brothers , I do not want you to know that I have been determined many times to go to you and to bring fruit among you , as among the rest of the foreigners ; but there is still a barrier to this day .
&quot; I owe them their debts , whether they be the Philistines , the aliens , the wise , or the foolish .
&quot; Therefore I will do my utmost to preach the gospel to you in Rome
I am not ashamed of the gospel , which is the great power of God to save all the believers , first of the Jews , and then of the Philistines
For the righteousness of God is manifested in this gospel , which is based on faith , that it may be believed . As it is written , &quot; The righteous shall live by faith . &quot;
The wrath of God was revealed from heaven to all the ungodly , who are the ones who resist the truth by doing wickedness
For the things of God were manifest in the hearts of men as they knew them , because they were revealed to them by God .
&quot; For the eternal power and the divine nature of God is manifest from the creation of the heavens and the earth , and the eyes cannot see , but by what He has created , He knows , and no one can be deceived .
For though they knew God , they glorified Him not as God , nor thanked Him ; and their thoughts became vain , and their hearts of ignorance were dim .
Call yourselves clever , and turn them into fools
And the glory of the God that cannot perish shall become an idol , as a man that perisheth , and as the likeness of birds and beasts and insects .
Therefore God entrusted them to defile themselves with the desires of their hearts , so that they defiled one another &apos;s bodies
They have turned the truth of God into a lie , and have worshipped the things that were created , and have not worshipped the Lord of the things that were created . The Lord is praiseworthy for ever .
Therefore God entrusted their shameful desires , and their women , to the use of righteousness , and to the use of evil .
Thus do men , who forsake the woman &apos;s utility , who seek to devour her heart , who lust for one another , who do shameful things between men , and who receive in themselves the reproach of their own self-worth .
And because they knew not God deliberately , God caused them to do unreasonable things in their wicked hearts .
Filled with all kinds of iniquity , evil , greed , and poison , filled with jealousy , murder , strife , deceit , and wicked hatred
and those who are destroyed , those who say things behind their backs , those who hate God , those who insult others , those who are arrogant , those who boast , those who fabricate evil deeds , those who are against their parents .
the ignorant , the disobedient , the unfaithful , the unmerciful
Though they know that God judges those who do such things when they are dead , yet they go not only for themselves , but also for others
&quot; Whoever you are , you have no authority to judge . In whatever matters you judge , you judge your own sins . For in whatever matters you judge , what you do is like that of others
We know that God will judge him according to the truth
&quot; What , O you man , do you judge a man who does such things and does what he does in the same way as others ? Do you try him to escape from God ?
Or do you despise His abundant mercy , His forgiveness , His patience , and do not know that His mercy leads you to repentance ?
You have appointed your hard-hearted , unrepentant heart to accumulate wrath for yourselves , that the days of God &apos;s wrath may come , when He will judge with justice
He shall recompense each man according to his deeds .
Whoever works righteousness , and seeks glory and honour , and the blessing of immortality , shall be rewarded with everlasting life
&quot; But those who are assembled and do not obey the truth , and do not obey the wicked , will recompense them with wrath and anger .
He will add tribulation and distress to all the wicked , first the Jews , and then the Philistines
He will give glory , honor , and peace to all those who do good , first to the Jews , and then to the Philistines
For God does not despise men
Whoever sins without the law shall not perish according to the law ; and whoever sins under the law shall be tried according to the law .
For in the sight of God it is not righteousness to hear the law , but righteousness to do the law
The foreigners who have no law , even though they have no law , if they obey the law of their own sexuality , they are their own law .
&quot; This is the work of the law which is written in their hearts , and their unrighteous hearts bear witness to it , and their thoughts are compared with one another , whether for a cause or for a purpose .
In the days of the mystery of God , in the judgment of men through Jesus Christ , according to my gospel
&quot; You call yourself a Jew , and you rely on the law , and you exalt God
He who has been instructed by the law knows the will of God , and can distinguish between righteousness and evil , and do and love the good things
and believed that he was a guide to the blind , and a light in the darkness
A teacher of foolishness , a teacher of children , a model of knowledge and truth in the law
Are you teaching others and not teaching yourself ? Are you saying that no man can steal , and you are also stealing
Do you say that no man can commit adultery , and that he commits adultery himself ? Do you despise idols , and that he steals from the temple ?
&quot; Have you exaggerated the law , and have you transgressed the law , and defiled God ?
The name of God is in the Gentiles , because you have been defiled , as it is written in the Scriptures .
If you do the law , it is good for you to be circumcised ; and if you do the law , it is not good for you to be circumcised
So if the uncircumcised be obedient to the ordinances of the law , is he not circumcised , though he is uncircumcised ?
And he that is not circumcised , if he keepeth the law , shall he not judge thee , who hath the manner and circumcision , and doeth the law ?
For they that are Jews outside are not true Jews ; neither is the circumcision of the flesh outside true circumcision
&quot; But the true Jew is what is done in him , and the true circumcision is in his heart , and he cares not for the spirit , nor for the instruments ; and his praise is not from men , but from God
&quot; What good is it for the Jews , and what good is it for the circumcision
All things are greatly beneficial . The first is that the Word of God is given to them
Even if there are disbelievers , what is there to prevent them ? Does their disbelief destroy the faith of God ?
Rather than say , &quot; God is true , and all men are liars . &quot; As it is written , &quot; When thou reproachest men , it is righteousness ; and when they dispute , thou shalt prevail . &quot;
How can I say , according to the sayings of men , If our iniquity should be manifested by the righteousness of God ? Is not God angry ?
If so , how can God judge the world
If the truth of God is made manifest through my falsehood , and the glory of God is made manifest through my falsehood , why am I still judged as a sinner ?
&quot; Why do we not say , &apos; We can do evil for good &apos; ? These are the ones who deny us , saying , &apos; We have this ; &apos; and it is right for them to be condemned
How is it that we are stronger than them ? It is certainly not ; for we are proved to be under sin , both Jews and Hebrews
As it is written in the Scriptures , &quot; There is not a righteous man , neither is there a single
without understanding , without seeking God
They are all astray from the right path , and become useless together ; and none does good , neither does one .
Their throat is a tomb open ; they deceive with their tongues ; and in their lips is the poison of snakes .
The mouth is full of curses and poisons
The killer bleeds His feet flew away
The paths that have been taken have done abominations and atrocities
The way of peace , they did not know .
They have no fear of God in their eyes .
&quot; We know that the words of the law are spoken to those who are not under the law , to seal the mouths of every man , that all the world may be put under the judgment of God .
Therefore none of the bloodthirsty can be justified before God by the law , for the law is for the knowledge of sin
But now the righteousness of God is manifested beyond the law , and the law and the prophet are witnesses
It is the righteousness of God , which , by faith in Jesus Christ , has been given to all believers without distinction
For they have sinned for the world , and have lacked the glory of God
But now with the grace of God , and with the redemption of Christ Jesus , the glory is white and white
God created Jesus as a redemption offering , by the blood of Jesus , by the faith of men , to show God &apos;s righteousness , because He has forgiven the sins of men in the past with a heart of endurance
&quot; That he may show his righteousness in this day and age , that they may know that he is righteous , and that those who believe in him are righteous
If so , then where is the exaggeration ? There is no exaggeration . What law is there that is not , that is , the law of merit ? No , it is the law of the faithful
&quot; Therefore we have determined that men are justified by faith , and are not heedless of the law
Is God the God of the Jews alone , and not the God of the Gentiles ? Yes , and the God of the Gentiles
For God is one , and justifies by faith those who are baptized , and justifies by faith those who are not baptized
&quot; Have we thus abolished the law by faith ? In fact , the law is stronger .
Thus saith the LORD ; What hath Abraham , our father , gained by flesh ?
If Abraham had been righteous in his deeds , he would have been exalted ; but he is not exalted before God
What does the Scripture say ? It says , &quot; If Abraham believed in God , it would be righteousness for him . &quot;
The price of a work is not a mercy , but it is to be gained .
&quot; But he who does not work believes only in the God who calls sinners righteous , and even his faith is righteous .
Blessed is the man who is justified by God , as David said , except in deeds
He said , &quot; Forgive him , and cover his sins ; for he is blessed
Blessed is he who is not counted guilty by the Lord .
&quot; Is this blessing given to the circumcised alone , and not to the uncircumcised , because we said , &quot; The faith of Abraham is righteousness for him ? &quot;
When he was baptized , when he was not baptized , not when he was baptized , but when he was not baptized
And he received the seal of circumcision as a sign of righteousness in his uncircumcision , that he might be the father of all the uncircumcised , and of the believers , that they might also be justified .
and the father of the circumcised , those who have not only been circumcised , but have followed the faith of Abraham our father , who was not circumcised .
For God has promised Abraham and his seed to bear the world , not by law , but by faith
&quot; If a man belongs to the law , he shall be a heir ; but faith shall be in vain , and promises shall be abolished .
For the law is wrathful , and there is no law , and there is no transgression .
Therefore it is in faith to have a son , and it is in grace that the promise is given to all the seed , not only to the lawful , but also to the faith of Abraham according to the lawful .
Abraham believed that he was the God who raised the dead from the dead and made them unchanged , and that he was the father of our people in the sight of the Lord , as it is written , &quot; I have approved you as the father of many nations . &quot;
In the time of hopelessness , he was able to be the father of many nations because of hope , just as he said before , &quot; This is what your descendants will do . &quot;
When he was about a hundred years old , his faith was not weak , though he thought that his body was dead , that Sarah &apos;s birth had been cut off .
And there shall be no doubt in the heart for the promise of God , and in faith shall the heart be firm , and glory be given to God .
And with full faith , God will create what He has promised .
So it &apos;s just right for him
The words that are worthy of him are not written for him alone
It is written for those who shall be counted righteous in the future , for those who believe in God , who have raised up our Lord Jesus from the dead
Jesus was delivered to man for our transgressions , and for our redemption , and for our righteousness
For we are justified in our faith , that we may be reconciled with God through our Lord Jesus Christ
We also borrowed from him , because we believed that we might enter into the grace which is in our presence , and rejoice in the glory of God
And not only so , but also in affliction , and rejoicing : for they know that they endure affliction .
. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
Hope is not ashamed , for the Holy Spirit which is given to us pours out the love of God into our hearts
Because we were weak , Christ died for sinners on the appointed day
Death for the righteous is few , death for the merciful , or for those who dare
&quot; But Christ died for us when we were still sinners , and the love of God was revealed to us here
&quot; Now we rely more on his blood for our righteousness , and on him for our deliverance from the wrath of God
For it is better for us to be with God in the time of our enemies , and to be saved by the death of the Son of God , for it is better for us to be with God , and for it is better for us to be saved by his life .
Not only that , but that we may be with God and good through Jesus Christ my Lord , and that we may borrow from him for God &apos;s sake
&quot; This is as sin enters into the world from one person , and death comes from sin ; and death comes to all because they have sinned for all
Without the law , sin has passed through the world ; but without the law , sin does not count .
And he made him king from the death of Adam unto the death of Moses , even those who had not sinned as he did ; and Adam was the foretold of those who shall come after him .
But the transgression is less than the grace . If a man &apos;s transgression causes all to die , is not the grace of God more than the reward of the one grace of Jesus Christ ?
It is not as if a man is condemned for a crime as it is for a gift : for the judgment is condemned by one , and the gift is justified by many transgressors
If death is for the transgression of a man , then he is made king for it ; but those who are blessed and have the righteousness that is given , will they not become kings in life because of Jesus Christ ?
Thus it is said , &quot; For one transgression the sinners are condemned , and for one righteousness all are called to life .
For by one man &apos;s rebellion they are all sinners ; and by one man &apos;s obedience they are all righteous
The law is an addition to the sins ; but in it sins are multiplied , and mercy is multiplied .
Just as sin reigns to death , so grace reigns by righteousness to life for our Lord Jesus Christ
How much more can we be in sin , that mercy may be manifested ?
Will those of us who die in sin live in sin ?
Do they not know that we who are baptized into Christ Jesus are baptized into his death ?
Therefore we are brought to death by the baptism , and buried with him , that we might walk in a new way , as Christ was raised from the dead by the glory of the Father .
If we are united with him in the form of his death , we shall be united with him in the form of his resurrection
For we know our old men , who crucified them with him , that they might put an end to their sins , and that we should no longer be sinners .
For he who is dead is delivered from sin .
If we die with Christ , we will live with him in faith
For it is known that Christ will not die , neither will death be his lord , since he was raised from the dead
He died for sin , but only once . He lives for God
So you see yourselves dead to sin , and you see yourselves alive to God in Christ Jesus
&quot; Therefore do not be a king of sins on those of you who are to die , that your gates may be obedient to your own selfish desires
&quot; Do not offer your bodies to sin as an instrument of iniquity ; but offer yourselves to God as a resurrected man from the dead , and give your bodies to God as an instrument of righteousness .
Sin shall not be your Lord : for you are not under the law , but under grace .
How is it that we can commit sins under grace , and not under the law ?
Do you not know who you have dedicated yourselves to as servants , and who you obey , and who you serve ? Or who you serve , and who you sin , and who you die ? Or who you serve , and who you obey , and who you become ?
Thank God , for you , even though you were once sinners , have now , in your hearts , obeyed the example of the doctrine which was preached to you
&quot; You have been freed from your sins , and you have become righteous servants .
And I said unto you , Because of the weakness of your flesh , according to the sayings of men , How was it that ye were not able to minister uncleanly to the flesh , that ye were not able to do so ; and now shall ye also minister uncleanly to righteousness , that ye might be holy ?
For you are not bound by the covenant in the time of your sinful bondage .
What fruit will there be in that day of the shameful things which you now regard as shameful , and the end of which is death ?
&quot; But now that you have been freed from your sins , and have been servants of God , you will have the fruit of holiness , and the end will be eternal life .
For the price of sin is death ; but the grace of God is eternal life in our Lord Jesus Christ
&quot; Brothers , I am speaking to those who understand the law . Do you not know that the ruler of the law is alive ?
As a woman has a husband , and the husband is alive , she is bound by the law ; and if the husband dies , she is cut off from the law of the husband
So when a husband is alive , if he belongs to another , he calls himself a prostitute ; and when a husband dies , he departs from the law of his husband , and is not a prostitute , though he belongs to another
&quot; My brethren , you are dead by the body of Christ according to the law ; and if you belong to another , it is to him who is raised from the dead ; and if we bear fruit to God ,
For in the days of our flesh , the lusts of the law were stirred up in our bodies , and they became fruit of death .
But since we have died by the law of our bondage , we have departed from the law , that we may serve the Lord in the new way of the heart , and not in the old way of the instrument .
Then what shall we say ? Is the law a sin ? It is certainly not ; but if it were not for the law , I would not know what was the sin ; and if it were not for the law , I would not know what was the sin ; and if it were not for the law , I would not know what was the sin
But sin takes advantage of the opportunity , and commands all kinds of greed to be stirred up in me : for sin is dead without the law .
I had no law before that I was alive , but when the commandment came , sin was alive again , and I died
&quot; It is the commandment that brought man to life , and I am to die .
&quot; For he seduced me by the commandment , and killed me , when he had the opportunity for sin
In this way the law is holy , and the commandments holy , and righteous , and good
&quot; If it is the good that causes me to die , is it not ? It is sin that causes me to die ; but if sin causes me to die by the good that causes me to die , then it is sin indeed ; and if sin by the commandment is more evil ,
&quot; We knew that the law belonged to the Spirit , but I belonged to the flesh , and have been sold for sin
For I do not understand what I do ; I do not do what I will ; I do what I hate .
&quot; If what I do is what I do not want , then I ought to accept that the law is good
If so , it is not my doing ; it is the sin that dwells in me
And I know that there is no good in me , nor in my flesh ; for the good is mine , but it is not mine to do .
Therefore I will not do the good that I will , and I will not do the evil that I will not .
&quot; If I go to do what I do not want to do , it is not what I do ; it is the sin that dwells in me
I think there is a law , that when I am willing to do good , evil is with me
For according to the word that is in me , I am the law of God
But I perceived that there was another law in the flesh , which was in conflict with the law in my heart , which had taken me captive , that I should be subjected to the law of sin in the flesh .
&quot; I am indeed in distress . Who can save me from the body that takes death ?
For thanks to God I am able to be delivered by the Lord Jesus Christ ; and it seems that I have obeyed the law of God in my heart , and my flesh has obeyed the law of sin
Now those who are in Christ Jesus are not condemned
For he has delivered me from the law of the Holy Spirit , which gave me life , in Christ Jesus , and from the law of sin and death
For the law was weak in the flesh , and incapable of doing anything , and God sent His Son as a form of sin , and made a sin offering , and made a sin in the flesh .
and that the righteousness of the law may be accomplished in those who are not of the flesh , but of the Holy Spirit
For he who follows the flesh follows the flesh . He who follows the Holy Spirit follows the Holy Spirit .
To care for the flesh is death ; and to care for the Holy Spirit is the peace of life
For he that hateth the flesh hath fought God : for he hath not obeyed the law of God , neither is he able to obey it .
And those who belong to the flesh cannot receive the favor of God
If the Spirit of God dwells in your hearts , you are not of the flesh , but of the Holy Spirit ; and if a man has not the Spirit of Christ , he is not of Christ
If Christ is in your hearts , the body dies for sin , and the heart lives for righteousness
&quot; But if the Spirit of the resurrection of Jesus from the dead dwells in your hearts , then Christ Jesus will also be resurrected from the dead , and by the Holy Spirit that dwells in your hearts will your dead bodies be brought back to life .
Brothers , it seems that we are not indebted to the flesh to live according to the flesh
If you live according to the flesh , you must die ; and if you cure the evil deeds of the dead by the Holy Spirit , you must live
For he that is led by the Spirit of God is the Son of God .
&quot; What you have received is not the heart of a slave , but the fear of a son ; therefore we call on your father , Father .
The Holy Spirit bears witness with our hearts that we are the children of God
If we suffer with him , we shall be glorified with him , if we be children , if we be children , if we be children , if we be children of God , and if we be children of Christ
I do not care for the suffering that is present , if it should be manifested to us in glory than in the future
The creatures who wait for the coming of the children of God
For it was not his own will that he should be obedient to the things that were made in the void , but because of that which he called it
But the creatures still await the glory of the liberty of God &apos;s sons and daughters from the wicked dominion .
We know all things that were created , and we weep and weep , and we come to this day .
Not only that we have the first fruits of the Holy Spirit , but we also weep in our hearts , waiting for the name of the Son , and our bodies are to be redeemed
We are saved by hope ; but the hope that is seen is not hope ; and who hopes for what he sees ?
But if we look forward to what we do not see , we will wait patiently
And our weaknesses have the help of the Holy Spirit ; and we know not how to pray ; but the Holy Spirit speaks a sigh for us , and prays for us .
For he that discerneth the heart , and knoweth the grace of the Holy Spirit , praying for the saints according to the will of God
For we know that all things work together , and that it is profitable for those who love God , those who are called by His will
For he , who had known before , had prescribed the way of his son , that he might raise up his son among many brethren
They are called again by those whom He has appointed , and they are called righteous , and they are called righteous , and they are glorified .
That is it , and what is it that is said : If God help us , who will be our enemy against us ?
Did God not spare His Son for us all , and give us all things white and white with Him ?
Who can accuse those whom God has chosen of righteousness ?
Who can determine their sins ? Is there Christ Jesus , who has passed away and is risen from the dead , and is now on the right hand of God , who prays for us ?
Who can separate us from the love of Christ ? Is it affliction , or tribulation , or oppression , or hunger , or nakedness , or danger , or sword ?
As it is written , &quot; For your sakes we are slain all the days , and people see us as sheep that are slaughtered .
Yet in all these things there is more to be gained by the Lord , who loves us .
For I am convinced that whatever is dead , whatever is alive , whatever is angelic , whatever is in power , whatever is able , whatever is present , whatever is in the future
Neither the high nor the low nor any other creature can separate us from the love of God , which is in our Lord Jesus Christ
I speak the truth in Christ , and am not a liar ; and my conscience is moved by the Holy Spirit to bear witness to me
I am very sad , and my heart often hurts
For my brother , the kinsman of my flesh , who is cursed , and is separated from Christ , I also will
They are the children of Israel ; and the name , and the glory , and the covenants , and the statutes , and the ordinances , and the promises , are theirs
The fathers are their fathers , and Christ , according to the flesh , came out of them , and he is a God in all things , praiseworthy forever .
&quot; This is not an empty word of God ; neither are they all Israelites born of Israel
And they were not of Abraham &apos;s seed ; but they were his daughters ; and they were called your seed from the sons of Jesse .
&quot; This is to say , &apos; The children of the flesh are not the children of God ; only the children promised are the descendants . &apos; 
For this is the word that was promised : &quot; When I come next year , Sarah will bear a son .
Not only that , but also Libeka , conceived from one man , and from our ancestors , Isaac
The twins have not yet been born , neither has good nor evil been done , but for the purpose of manifesting the will of God who has chosen him , not for the deeds of men , but for the Lord who calls .
And God said unto Rebekah , The great shall serve the little .
As it is written in the Scriptures , &quot; Jacob is my beloved , and Esau my evil .
Then what shall we say ? Is there not injustice in God ?
For he said to Moses , &quot; Whoever I will have mercy on , I will have mercy on ; and whoever I will have mercy on , I will have mercy on . &quot;
&quot; Therefore , it is not a matter of the will , nor of the running , but of the God of mercy .
For there was a saying in the Scriptures to Pharaoh , &quot; I will raise you up , I will show my power in you , and I will spread my name throughout the whole earth . &quot;
Thus it seems , Whomsoever God will have mercy , He will have mercy ; Whomsoever He will make hard , He will make hard
Then you will say to me , &quot; Why does he blame people ? Who will resist his will ? &quot;
&quot; Who are you , this man , that you dare to speak to God ? Can the creature that was created say to those who made him , &apos; Why did you make me this way ? &apos;
Haven &apos;t the carpenters power to take a precious vessel out of a pile of clay , and a humble vessel out of it ?
&quot; If God wants to show His wrath and His power , He will tolerate the vessel of wrath prepared for destruction
And the glory of his abundance shall be made manifest in the holy vessel of mercy , which he prepared beforehand .
&quot; What is this vessel , which we are called by God , not of the Jews , but of the Gentiles ?
As God says in the book of Hosea , &quot; This is not my son , but I will call him my son ; and this is not my beloved , but I will call him my beloved
Wherefore it was said unto them , Ye are not my children : therein shall they be called the sons of the everlasting God .
Isaiah cried out , referring to the Israelites , saying , &quot; The remnant of Israel , though they are more than the sand , are saved
For the purpose of His Word , which is chiefly to be done in the world , that His Word may be fulfilled , and that it may come to an end quickly .
And as Isaiah had said before , &apos; If the Lord of hosts had not given us a remnant , we would have been as Sodom and Moor before .
Then what shall we say ? The foreigner who has not pursued righteousness has received righteousness , the righteousness of faith .
But the children of Israel pursued the righteousness of the law , but they were not righteous in the law
Why is this ? Because they do not seek by faith , but by works : for they are falling upon the stumbling stone
As it is written , &apos; In Zion I laid down a stumbling stone , a stumbling stone for men ; and those who believe in Him shall not be ashamed .
My brethren , what I desire in my heart , and what I ask of God , is that the children of Israel may be saved
I can prove their enthusiasm for God , but not according to true knowledge
For if they do not know the righteousness of God , and seek to establish their own righteousness , they do not obey the righteousness of God
The sum of the law is Christ , that all who believe in him may be justified
Moses wrote , &quot; If a man does that which is right in the law , he shall live accordingly .
Only the righteousness of faith says , &quot; You shall not say in your heart , &apos; Who will ascend to heaven ? &apos; but to bring down Christ
Who will go down to the shadow , to bring Christ up from the dead ?
And he said , This way is not far from thee , it is in thy mouth , it is in thy heart : that is the way of the Lord which we have sent unto thee
&quot; If you confess in your mouth Jesus as Lord , and believe in God in your heart that He may raise you from the dead , you will be saved
For if you believe in the heart , you will be justified ; and if you confess with your mouth , you will be saved .
The Scripture says , &quot; Whoever believes in Him will not be ashamed .
And there was no distinction between the Jews and the Philistines : for he had a Lord unto all the people , and he was kind unto all that pleaded unto him
For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved .
But if a man has not believed in Him , how can he seek Him ? If a man has not heard Him , how can he believe in Him ? And if a man has not preached , how can he hear ?
How can we preach without sending ? How beautiful are the tracks of those who preach the gospel and rejoice , as it is written in the Scriptures .
For Isaiah said , &quot; Lord , who believes in what we have preached ? &quot;
Behold , faith is from hearing , and hearing is from the word of Christ
But I said , &quot; Have they not heard ? Truly , they have heard . &apos; Their voices have spread throughout the world , and their words to the ends of the earth .
Then said Moses , &quot; I will provoke you to anger with those who are not children , and I will provoke you to anger with those who are ignorant .
Then Isaiah dared to say , &apos; I have called them to meet those who have not sought me ; and those who have not visited me , I have appeared to them .
As for the Israelites , he said , &apos; I stretch out my hand all day to greet the people who are rebellious .
&quot; And I said , &apos; Has God forsaken His people ? No indeed ; for I am of the tribe of Benjamin , of the children of Israel , the descendants of Abraham .
Do you not know what the Scriptures say concerning Elijah , and how he accuses the children of Israel before God ,
&quot; Lord , they have killed your prophets , they have broken your altar , and I am one of them , and they seek my life .
What is God &apos;s reply ? He said , &quot; I have left for myself seven thousand people who have not kneaded themselves to Balak .
And so it is now , and there remaineth a remnant according to the grace of the chosen
If it is from grace , it is not for action ; otherwise , grace is not grace .
How is it that the Israelites did not have what they asked of them ? Only the chosen did have what they asked of them , and the rest became stubborn .
As it is written , &apos; God has given them a confused heart , whose eyes cannot see , and whose ears cannot hear , even to this day .
And David said , &quot; Let their feast be a net , and a spoil , and a stumbling block , for their recompense
May their eyes be darkened , and they see not ; and may Thou bend their backs continually .
&quot; And I said , &apos; Do they lose their feet , that they may fall ? No indeed ; but because of their transgression , salvation comes to the Gentiles to provoke them to anger .
What if their transgression is for the riches of the world , and their lack for the riches of the Gentiles , and what if their abundance is full ?
&quot; I say this to your Gentiles , because I am an apostle of the Gentiles ; so respect my office ,
Or to stir up my bones of anger to save some of them
&quot; If they are abandoned , the world will be good with God . If they are received , will they not be raised from the dead ?
If the new offering is holy , the whole congregation is holy ; and if the roots are holy , the branches are holy
&quot; If a few branches are broken , then you shall take the wild olive and the fat of the root of the olive in it .
&quot; You will not exaggerate against the old branch ; if you exaggerate , you will know that it is not you who lays the foundation , it is you who lays the foundation
&quot; If you say , &apos; The branch has been broken down , &apos; it is for me to take it
Yes , they are broken down because they do not believe ; and you stand because you believe ; and you cannot boast , nor be afraid .
God will not despise the original branch , nor will he despise you
See God &apos;s mercy and severity . He is severe toward those who fall , and He is merciful to you , as long as you remain in His mercy ; otherwise , you will also be cut down .
And if they had not been faithless for a long time , they would still be received : for God will raise them up from the dead .
&quot; You have been cut down from the wild olive that was born , and you are reverent to the good olive ; and the branches of this tree will be on this tree .
&quot; Brothers , I do not want you to know this secret , for I fear that you think that you are wise , that the hearts of Israel are hard , until the number of the foreigners is full
Then all the house of Israel will be saved , as it is written , &quot; There will be a Savior coming out of Zion to remove all the sins of the house of Jacob . &quot;
&quot; This is the covenant I made with them when I removed their sins .
He said in the gospel , &quot; They are enemies for your sakes , &quot; and in the election , &quot; They are beloved for the sake of their fathers
For there is no repentance for the grace and the calling of God
&quot; You used to disobey God ; now you have mercy for their disobedience .
Thus they also disobeyed , that they might be moved by the mercy which they have shown to you , and that they may also be moved by it .
For God has encircled all men in disobedience , and has been special in compassion on them
Blessed is God , the Wise and the Wise : how hard is His judgment , and how hard is His trace !
Who knows the heart of the Lord , and who has been his counselor ?
Who gave him first , and repaid him later ?
For to Him belongs all things , and to Him belongs all trust , and glory belongs to Him forever and ever .
Therefore , brethren , I counsel you with the mercy of God to offer your bodies for a living sacrifice , that it may be holy and acceptable to God , and that it may be lawful for you to do so .
Do not obey this world ; but let your mind be renewed and changed , that you may know what is God &apos;s good and purely pleasing will .
&quot; In the fruit of my grace , I said to all of you , &apos; Do not look on yourselves beyond what you have seen , but according to the measure of the faith which God has given to you , that it may be acceptable to you .
Just as we have better bodies on our bodies , bodies are not the same
And so are many of us who are one in Christ , joined together as limbs
&quot; There are different blessings according to the grace which We have given them , and when they prophesy , they prophesy according to the measure of faith .
or as a tutor , as a tutor ; or as a tutor , as a tutor
Whoever is persuaded , he is persuaded ; whoever gives , he is honest ; whoever governs , he is kind ; and whoever is merciful , he is kind .
Love is not false , evil is hateful , good is near
Love one another , brothers , and sisters , and respect one another , and give one another rest
Enthusiasm is not laziness , but passion in the heart , and often obeys the Lord .
Rejoice in hope ; endure in affliction ; pray for ever .
The saints lack help . The guests need a taste of hospitality
Blessed be those who oppress you , and blessed be those who do not curse .
Those who rejoice shall rejoice , and those who weep shall weep .
Have compassion on one another , and do not be arrogant , and do not bow down to the humble , and do not think of yourself as wise
Don &apos;t retaliate with evil , but keep your heart on what is good for all
&quot; If you can do it , you must do your utmost to be in harmony with all men
Beloved , let yourselves not be wronged , but let yourselves go , and listen to the wrath of the Lord ; for it is written in the Scriptures , &apos; Thus says the Lord , Repent with me , and I will repay . &apos; 
&quot; If your enemy is hungry , feed him ; if he is thirsty , give him drink ; for you have set a fire on his head .
Thou shalt not prevail against evil , but shalt prevail against evil by good .
And every man obeyeth him that hath power ; for it is not from God that he hath no power ; but it is from God that he hath power .
Therefore whoever resists authority , he resists the life of God ; and whoever resists , he will receive his own punishment .
The fear of the ruler is not the fear of doing good , but the fear of doing evil . Will you not fear the ruler ? If you do good , you will be praised by him
For he is God &apos;s servant , and he is good to you ; and if you do evil , fear him ; for he is not an empty sword ; he is God &apos;s servant , and he is righteous , and the punishment is evil .
Therefore you must obey , not only for the punishment , but also for the conscience
For this cause also do you feed , for they are God &apos;s servants , and they do it frequently .
Whoever is worthy shall be given , and whoever is worthy of food shall be given , and whoever is worthy of tax shall be taxed , and whoever fears shall fear him , and whoever is respectful shall respect him .
For all things are not to be indebted to man , but to be indebted to one another in love : for the law is perfect for those who love one another
&quot; The words of non-violence , of non-killing , of non- stealing , of non-greed , and of other commandments are enclosed in the love of one &apos;s own self
Love is not harmful to man , therefore love perfects the law
&quot; And now you know that it is time to wake up early , for our salvation is nearer than the time of the first letter .
The darkness is deep , and the day is near , and we are taken away from darkness , and we are armed with light weapons .
To do righteous deeds for men is as to do in the daytime . Don &apos;t be drunk at a feast , don &apos;t be colorless , don &apos;t be jealous
Always put on the Lord Jesus Christ , and do not make arrangements for the flesh , and do not indulge in selfish desires
Believers who are weak , accept , but do not debate doubts
A man believes that he can eat a hundred things , but the weak eats only vegetables .
He who eats cannot be taken lightly , he who eats not , and he who eats not , he who eats cannot be denied , for God has accepted him for himself .
Who art thou that judgest the servant of another , who standeth or falls , and hath his master in himself ; and he must stand , because the Lord hath made him stand
There are those who see this day as stronger than that day , and there are those who see day and day as one , but in every heart is a firm mind .
He who keeps the day is the Lord &apos;s , and he who eats is the Lord &apos;s , for he thanks God ; and he who does not eat is the Lord &apos;s , and he who does not eat is the Lord &apos;s .
We have none to live for ourselves , and none to die for ourselves
If we live , we live in the Lord ; and if we die , we die in the Lord ; therefore we are always the Lord , whether we live or die
Therefore Christ died and lived again , to be the Lord of the dead and of the living
Why do you , O man , dispute with your brethren , and take them lightly ? For we are all to stand before the table of God
&quot; It is written , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I swear by my eternal life that every knee will kneel before me , and every mouth will confess to me .
It seems to me that each one of us must declare his deeds before God
&quot; Therefore we shall not dispute with one another any more ; but rather we shall determine that no man shall give to his brethren the things that fall upon him .
&quot; In the Lord Jesus I am surely convinced that there was no uncleanness in all things , and that only he who was unclean was unclean in Him
&quot; If you mourn your brothers for your food , it is not according to the law of the beloved ; for Christ died for him ; and you cannot make him perish for your food
Don &apos;t let your goodness be denied
For the kingdom of God careth not for food and drink , but for righteousness , peace , and joy in the Holy Spirit
&quot; Those who obey Christ in these things rejoice in God and in the promises of men
Therefore we must seek harmony and establish good deeds with one another
&quot; The works of God cannot be destroyed because of food . While everything is clean , it is the sin of one who causes a person to fall because of food .
&quot; Eat meat , drink , or anything else , and let your brethren fall , and do nothing .
Blessed is the man who is not blameless in what he does for himself , when he has confidence , and when he stands before God .
He who eats in doubt is guilty ; for he eats not out of faith ; and he who eats not out of faith is guilty .
We who are strong should bear the weaknesses of those who are not strong , and not seek the joy of ourselves
&quot; We each work to please our neighbor , to benefit him , and to establish good works .
For he did not seek his own pleasure for Christ , as it is written , &quot; The reproach of your people is upon me .
The Scriptures that were written before were written to teach us , that we might have hope in the patience and comfort of the Scriptures
May the God of endurance comfort you , that you may be with one another , and obey Christ Jesus
Glory to God , the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ , with one heart and one mouth
Therefore receive one another , as Christ also received you , that glory may return to God
&quot; I said , &apos; Christ is the minister of the circumcised for the truth of God , to confirm the promise of the fathers .
And I will praise thee in the land of the nations , and I will sing thee &apos;s name , as it is written .
&quot; You foreigners , rejoice with the Lord &apos;s people , &quot; he said .
And he said , Praise the LORD , O ye nations , and praise him , all ye people .
Then Isaiah said , &quot; In the future there will be a root of Jesse , who will rise up to rule over the Gentiles , and the Gentiles will look on him .
May the God of hope fill your hearts with all joy and peace through faith , that you may have great hope through the power of the Holy Spirit .
Brothers , I myself am convinced that you are full of goodness , full of all kinds of knowledge , and able to counsel one another
&quot; But I am a little daring to write to you , to awaken your memories , because of the grace which God has given me .
that I may be a servant of Christ Jesus to the Gentiles , and a priest of the gospel of God , that the Gentiles whom I have offered may be sanctified and acceptable by the Holy Spirit
Therefore I am exalted in Christ Jesus concerning the things of God
I have no doubt of anything other than that which Christ has done through me , but that through my words He has done , through the power of miracles and miracles and the power of the Holy Spirit , to subject the Gentiles
Even I went straight from Jerusalem to Elimelech , where I preached the gospel of Christ
I have set my sight on preaching the gospel in a place not called in the name of Christ , lest I should be built on the foundations of others
As it is written , &apos; He who has not heard his word shall see , and he who has not heard shall understand .
I have been hindered many times , and I will not be able to go in with you
But now there is no place to be known here , and for many years I have been looking forward to the time when you will be able to go to Shebanah .
Hope to pass through from you , to see you , first to communicate with you , to be a little content in your hearts , and then to send you forth
&quot; But now I go to Jerusalem to supply the saints
For the Macedonians and the Achaeans were glad to raise up their contributions to the poor among the saints of Jerusalem
That is indeed what they are pleased with , and that is indeed the debt they owe . For the aliens , having a share in the goodness of their own Spirit , give them what they can bear
&quot; When I have finished this thing , and have delivered the good fruit to them , I will pass over to you and go to Shebanya
&quot; I also know that in the time when I go , I will go with the grace of Christ , which is abundant
&quot; Brothers , in the love of our Lord Jesus Christ and of the Holy Spirit , I exhort you to do your utmost with me , and to pray to God for me
Let me be delivered from the disobedient in Judah , and let my contribution to Jerusalem be acceptable to the saints .
&quot; And let me come to you joyfully , according to the will of God , and rest with you .
Blessed be the God of peace , who is always with you all .
&quot; I present to you our sister Phinehas , who is a woman priest in the church of Keilah
&quot; Receive him , O Lord , in the integrity of the saints , and help him in all that he asks of you ; for he has helped many , and has helped me
Ask Berkhel and Aijaan , who work with me in Christ Jesus
And for my life he has removed his neck , and I thank him not only , but also the churches of the Gentiles
And to the church in their houses , and to my beloved Abimelech , the fruit of the first fruits of Christ in Asia
And asked Maryam : &quot; How much more will he rejoice for you
Then I asked of my relatives , Andrew and John , who were in prison with me ; and they were well-known among the apostles , and were in Christ before me
Ask me also of Amphibiah , whom I have loved in the Lord
and to the servants of Elban , who work with us in Christ , and to the high priest Gaius , whom I love
Ask Abilene , who was tested in Christ ; Ask the men of the house of Alydobe ,
&quot; And to my relative Herod , and to those who are with him in the Lord ,
Ask the sons of Phinehas , and the sons of Siphonas , who laboured for the Lord ; Ask the sons of Pisces , who laboured for the Lord most
&quot; And to Rufus , and to his mother , whom the Lord has chosen . His mother is my mother
Then he asked the sons of Assyria , and the sons of Pharaoh , and the sons of Hamim , and the sons of Harobah , and the sons of Hama , and the brethren that were with them
Then they asked Phirron , and Judah , and Nileah , and his sisters , and Arima , and the saints that were with them in one place
Greet one another with your mouths , and be holy to one another ; and all the churches of Christ greet you
&quot; Brothers , I counsel you to be careful to avoid them , those who depart from you and fall away from the way you have been taught .
For they do not obey our Lord Christ , but obey their own belly , and tempt the hearts of the upright with cunning words .
&quot; I rejoice for you because your obedience has been preached to all , but I want you to be wise in good and foolish in evil .
The God of peace will soon trample Satan under your feet , and the grace of my Lord Jesus Christ will always be with you .
&quot; Peace be to Timothy , who works with me , and to Reuben my relative , the son of Jesse , the son of Zedekiah ,
&quot; Blessed are you in the Lord , Dede , the scribe of my generation ,
&quot; Then he who received me , and the Jews of the whole church , greeted you .
Ephraim , who was in charge of the treasury in the city , and the brothers , salute you .
Only God will strengthen your hearts according to the gospel which I have preached , and according to Jesus Christ , whom I have spoken , and according to the secrets which have been hidden for ever .
Now this mystery is revealed , and according to the life of God , and according to the book of the prophets , it is revealed to the people of all the nations , that they may believe in the truth .
May glory be in Jesus Christ , the God of all wisdom , for ever and ever . Amen
Paul , who was called an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God , and his brother Zedekiah
The church of God , which is sanctified in Christ Jesus , and called to be saints , and all that call upon the name of my Lord Jesus Christ in all places ; and Christ is their Lord and our Lord
Grace and peace be to you from God , our Father and Lord Jesus Christ .
I always thank my God for you , for the grace which God has given you in Christ Jesus
&quot; For in him you are rich in all things , and your mouths are full of knowledge .
As I bear witness to Christ , I am firm in your hearts
So that you are no less in grace than men , and wait for the appearance of our Lord Jesus Christ
&quot; He will also strengthen you to the end , that in the days of our Lord Jesus Christ you will have no reproach .
&quot; For God is faithful , and you were called to score with His Son , our Lord Jesus Christ .
&quot; Brothers , in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ I exhort you all to speak the same words , and you shall not be divided among yourselves , but be one mind and one mind .
&quot; For the men of the house of Gilead called on me brothers , saying , &apos; There is a dispute between you
&quot; I mean , every one of you said , &apos; I belong to Paul , I belong to Apollos , I belong to Caiaphas , and I belong to Christ
Is Christ divided ? Is Paul crucified for you ? Are you baptized in the name of Paul ?
&quot; I thank God that I have not baptized one of you , except for Gilead and Judah
&quot; Do not let anyone say , &apos; You have been baptized in my name .
&quot; I also baptized the house of Zedekiah , and I have not baptized anyone else , but I do not remember .
Christ sent me not to be baptized , but to preach the gospel , and not in words of wisdom , lest the cross of Christ fall into the void
For the righteousness of the cross is foolishness in those who perish ; but the mighty power of God is in those whom we are to save .
As it is written , &quot; I will destroy the wisdom of the wise , and the wisdom of the wise . &quot;
Where is the wise man , and where is the scribe , and where is the defence of the world ? Did not God make the wisdom of the world foolish ?
In his wisdom the world does not know God , but God is pleased to save those who believe by the foolishness of men , and that is the wisdom of God .
The Jews seek signs , and the Philistines seek wisdom
&quot; But we are Christ , who has been crucified , a stumbling block to the Jews , and a foolishness to the Gentiles
But in him who is called , whether he be Jew or Greek , Christ is the power of God , the wisdom of God
For God &apos;s foolishness is greater than man &apos;s wisdom ; and God &apos;s weakness is greater than man &apos;s strength .
Brothers , behold , you are called by the flesh , few in wisdom , few in power , and few in honour .
But God has chosen the foolish in the world to be ashamed of wisdom , and the weak in the world to be ashamed of strength .
God has also chosen the humble in the world , the despised , and those who have nothing , to destroy those who have nothing
&quot; No man can boast in the sight of God , who has made all things bloody
But in Christ Jesus , who is God &apos;s , God made him our wise , righteous , holy , and redeeming
As it is written in the Scriptures , &quot; The exaggeration refers to the exaggeration of the Lord .
&quot; Brothers , I have come to you before , and I have not spoken the secrets of God to you with great wisdom .
For I have determined my will , and I know nothing but Jesus Christ , and he has crucified him among you
&quot; Behold , I am weak , and fearful , and trembling with you
The words I speak are not words of wisdom , but signs of the Holy Spirit and of great power
Let your faith be not in the wisdom of men , but in the might of God
But among the perfect , we speak wisdom ; but it is not the wisdom of this world , nor the wisdom of the one who has the right to perish in this world .
&quot; What we say is the hidden wisdom of God , the wisdom of God , which He has prepared before the worlds to glorify us .
No one in the world has the right to know this wisdom ; and if they had , they would not have crucified the Lord of glory .
As it is written , &quot; God has prepared for those who love Him eyes that have not seen , ears that have not heard , and hearts that have not thought . &quot;
Only God made it clear to us through the Holy Spirit ; for the Holy Spirit has seen all things , and also the deep things of God .
&quot; There is no one who knows the things of man except the Spirit of man , and no one knows the things of God except the Spirit of God .
&quot; It is not the spirit of the world that we receive , but the spirit that comes from God , that we may know what God has given us .
And we speak these things , not in the words of wisdom , but in the words of the Holy Spirit , speaking the word of the Spirit , and interpreting the things of the Spirit .
But those of blood do not receive the things of the Holy Spirit , but are foolish , and do not know them ; for only the Spirit can see them .
A man of the Spirit can see all things , but none can see Him
Who knew the Lord &apos;s heart to teach him ? But we have the heart of Christ .
&quot; Brothers , I have spoken to you before , and I cannot regard you as spirits , but as flesh , and as infants in Christ .
I fed you with milk , and not with food . You could not eat then , nor can you eat now
&quot; You are still of the flesh ; for there is jealousy among you . Is it not of the flesh , as the world does ?
&quot; I belong to Paul , and I belong to Apollos . Is this not the same as you and the world ?
&quot; What is Apollos , and what is Paul ? He is the ruler , guiding you in the faith , as the Lord has given to every one of them
&quot; I have planted , and Apollos has watered ; but God has caused him to grow
Behold , what is planted is worthless , and what is watered is worthless , and only in the God whom He called to grow .
Both those who sow and those who water are one and the same ; but in the future every man shall do according to his own way and receive his own reward
For we work with God , and you are the fields and houses which God has planted and built .
As a wise workman , I have laid the foundations according to the grace of God , and others have built on it ; but each man must be careful how he builds on it .
For the foundation of goodness is Jesus Christ ; and there is no one that can lay another foundation .
&quot; If a man builds on this foundation of gold , silver , stone , grass , and timber ,
The works of every man shall surely be manifested , for in that day he shall be manifested , and a fire shall be discovered , and it shall test the works of every man .
A man shall be rewarded for the work that he has built on that foundation , if it remains alive .
If a man &apos;s work is burned , he will lose , but he himself will be saved , though saving is like walking through the fire .
Do you not know that you are the house of God , and that the Spirit of God dwells in your heads ?
&quot; If any man destroys the house of God , God must destroy him ; for the house of God is holy , and it is you
No man can deceive himself . If there be any among you who thinks he is wise in this world , it is better for him to become foolish than for him to become wise
For the wisdom of the world is foolish in the sight of God . As it is written in the Scriptures , &quot; The Lord has deceived himself among the wise .
He said , &quot; The Lord knows that the thoughts of the wise are vain .
Therefore let no man exaggerate , for all things are yours .
or Paul , or Apollos , or Caiaphas , or the world , or life , or death , or the present , or the future , are all yours
And you belong to Christ , and Christ belongs to God .
We shall be the ministers of Christ , and the stewards of the mystery of God
What is desired of the ruler is that he be faithful
I am judged by you or by others , and I am judged by a small thing , and I am not judged by myself .
Though I didn &apos;t feel guilty , I couldn &apos;t be justified ; but the Lord judges me
Therefore the time is not yet come , let nothing be disputed , but wait for the Lord to come , who will reveal the secret thoughts of the hearts , and in that time everyone will be praised by God .
For your sakes , my brethren , I take these things from myself and from Apollos , that we may do as is written in the Scriptures , lest you be exalted , exalted , and despised .
Who is it that makes you different from men ? What have you that is not received ? If it is received , why boast as if it were not received ?
&quot; You are full , and you are rich , and you are king without us ; and I would that you were truly king , and that we should also be kings with you
&quot; I think that God has clearly placed our apostles in the latter part of the world as prisoners of death , for we have made a spectacle for the world and for angels to watch .
We are foolish for the sake of Christ ; you are wise in Christ ; we are weak ; you are strong ; you are glorious ; we are despised
Now we are hungry and thirsty and barefoot and beaten and have no place to live
And labor , and work with hands ; and when they are cursed , we bless ; and when they are oppressed , we endure .
We are well advised by men who are slandered , and to this day they regard us as the filth of the world , the dust of all things .
&quot; I write these words not to be ashamed of you , but to warn you , as my beloved children .
For ye have learned Christ , and there are ten thousand masters , but few for the Father : for I have raised you in Christ Jesus by the gospel
So I ask you to act on me
Therefore I have sent to you Timothy , the faithful son of my beloved in the Lord , who will awaken you to remember how I have dealt in Christ , and how I have taught in all the churches .
&quot; Some are proud that I will not go in with you
&quot; But if the Lord wills me , I will come to you quickly ; and what I want to know is not the words of the proud , but their power .
For the kingdom of God careth not for words , but for power
What do you want ? Do you want me to come to you with a rod , or do you want me to have a gentle heart ?
There is an evil thing in your midst , and there is no such evil thing among the Gentiles : for there is a man who takes his mother-in-law .
&quot; You are also proud , and do not grieve , and drive out from among you those who do these things .
&quot; My body is not with you , but my heart is with you , as if I myself were with you , and had judged a man to do it .
&quot; In the time of your gathering , my heart is with you , in the name of our Lord Jesus , and in the power of our Lord Jesus
to give such a man to Satan , to destroy his flesh , that his soul may be saved in the days of the Lord Jesus
It is not good for you to boast . Can a piece of yeast cause the whole congregation to rise up
&quot; You who are unleavened should purify the old yeast , that you may become a new congregation ; for our Passover Lamb , Christ , has been sacrificed through the slaughter
Therefore we shall not keep this Sabbath with old yeast , nor with the poisonous yeast of wickedness , but with an unleavened bread of truth and truth .
&quot; I wrote to you before , saying , &apos; You shall not associate yourself with a man who is lustful .
&quot; This is not to say that there is no one in the world who is obscene , or greedy , or fornicating , or idolatrous ; if so , you shall not leave the world unless you
But now I write unto you , saying , Whosoever is called a brethren , who is obscene , or greedy , or idolatrous , or blasphemed , or drunken , or fornicated , shall not be able to associate with him , neither shall he eat with him .
For what is it with me that those who are outside the Church judge ? Are not those who are within the Church judged by you ?
As for the strangers , God judges them ; and you shall drive out the wicked from among you .
How can one contend with another among you before the wicked , and not before the saints ?
Do not the saints judge the world ? If the world judges you , are you not worthy of judging the least thing ?
&quot; Do you not know that we will judge the angels , and the things of this life ?
&quot; If that is the case , are you judges of the things that are in the flesh , of those whom the church regards lightly ?
&quot; I say this to shame you . Is there not a wise man among you who can judge the brothers ?
&quot; Behold , you are brothers and brothers , proclaiming before the unbelievers
You accuse one another , and it is a great error in you ; why do you not want to be deceived , and why do you not want to lose ?
&quot; You are oppressors and losers , and the losers of oppression are brothers .
Do you not know that the wicked cannot bear the kingdom of God ? Do not deceive yourselves , whether they be adulterers , idolaters , adulterers , or child prostitutes , or beloved men
The stolen , the greedy , the drunken , the reproached , the extorted , they are all countries that cannot bear God .
&quot; Some of you were before , but now you have been sanctified in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ , and by the Spirit of our God have you been cleansed .
Whatever I may do , it will not be of any benefit to me . Whatever I may do , it will not be of any benefit to me in any case
The food is for the belly , and the belly is for the food ; but God will make them both to decay ; and the body is not for prostitution , but for the Lord , and for the body
And God has raised us up through the Lord , and will raise us up by His own power
Don &apos;t you know that your bodies are the bodies of Christ ? Can I make the bodies of Christ prostitutes ?
Did he not know that he who joined himself to the prostitute was one with him ? For the Lord said , &quot; Two are to be one .
But he that is united with the Lord is one Spirit with the Lord .
Avoid prostitution ; for all sins that a man commits are not in his own body ; but he who commits prostitution commits it in his own body .
&quot; Do you not know that your body is the house of the Holy Spirit , which came from God and dwells in your heads , and that you are not your own people ?
Blessed be God in your bodies , for you have been bought at great prices .
Concerning what you have written in your letter , I say that men are better than women
But to be free from adultery , men shall have their own wives , and women their own husbands .
The husband treats his wife with the appropriate division , and the wife treats her husband with the same division
A wife has no authority to claim her own body , but in her husband . A husband has no authority to claim his own body , but in his wife
Neither man nor wife shall be indebted to one another unless they are willing to divide their houses for a while , to pray with one another , and then to remain together , lest Satan tempt you while you are in restlessness .
&quot; When I said this , it was for your sakes , not for your sakes .
I desire all men to be like me , but to receive the grace of God , one like me , and one like me
&quot; I said to the unmarried and widows , &apos; If they are like me
If he forbids himself from dwelling , he may marry ; but it is better to marry than to be in love with him .
&quot; As for those who have been married , I have commanded them , not as I have commanded them , but as the Lord commanded them , saying , &apos; A wife shall not leave her husband
&quot; If you leave , you shall not marry again , or remain in good company with your husband , and the husband shall not leave his wife .
&quot; I said to the rest , &quot; It is not the Lord who says , &apos; If a brother has an unbelieving wife , and the wife wishes to live with him , he shall not forsake her .
A wife has an unbelieving husband , and if the husband wishes to live with him , he will not forsake the husband .
For the husband of unbelievers is sanctified by his wife ; and the wife of unbelievers is sanctified by her husband ; otherwise , your children will not be sanctified ; but now they are sanctified .
&quot; If the unbeliever is to leave , leave him alone . Brothers and sisters should not be bound by such things . God called us to peace
How do you know that your husband cannot save your wife ? How do you know that your husband cannot save your wife ?
&quot; This is what I command all the churches to do , as the Lord has given them , and as God has called them .
If a man has been baptized , he will not be baptized . If a man has not been baptized , he will not be baptized .
No circumcision shall be counted , and no circumcision shall be counted , unless the commandment of God is fulfilled
What is the identity of the time when each man is called , and to keep it
Do you serve as slaves ? Don &apos;t worry about it . If you can be free , seek freedom better
For whoever is called to the Lord as a slave is freed by the Lord ; and whoever is called as a free man is a slave of Christ .
You have been bought at a high price . You are not servants of men
&quot; Brothers , what is the time of your calling , and what is your standing before God ?
&quot; As for the child , I have no commandment from the Lord , but I tell you my own thoughts , for I am a man of the Lord &apos;s mercy and faithful heart .
In my opinion , it is better to keep oneself safe in the present times of hardship
If you have a wife , you will not ask her to leave you . If you have no wife , you will not ask her to leave you
&quot; If you marry a wife , it is not a crime ; and if you marry a virgin , it is a crime ; but the flesh of such men will suffer , and I will spare you from that suffering .
&quot; Brothers , I say to you , &apos; The time is shortened , and from now on he who has a wife will be as if he had no wife .
Let him that weep be like him that weepeth not , and let him that rejoice be like him that rejoiceth , and let him that buyeth be like him that hath no gain
To use the world is like not to use the world , for the world will pass away .
&quot; I wish you would have nothing to worry about , but to worry about the matter of the Lord , and how to please the Lord , who is not married
&quot; He who has married a wife is anxious for the things of the world . How can he please his wife ?
There is also a distinction between a woman and a virgin : that which is not married is the first thing , and that which is holy to the body and to the soul ; that which is married is the first thing , and that which is holy to the world , and that which is to please the husband .
&quot; I say this for your benefit , not to trap you , but to make you do what is right , to serve the Lord with diligence , and without disobedience .
&quot; If a man treats his daughter unjustly for his own sake , and the daughter is old , and things are done according to his will , he will do them according to his will , without guilt , and they will become kin .
&quot; If a man is certain that nothing can be done and that he has to be lord of himself , and he decides not to marry his daughter , so it will be
It seems that it is good to marry one &apos;s daughter , and it is better not to marry him
When the husband is alive , the wife is constrained ; and when the husband dies , she is free and free to marry again ; only to the man in the Lord
Nevertheless , in my opinion , it is better to keep fast regularly . I also think that I am inspired by God .
Concerning the things of the idols , we know that we all have knowledge ; but knowledge makes one great , and only love can make one great
If a man knoweth what he knoweth for himself , as he knew it , he knoweth it not .
If a man loves God , God knows him
Concerning the offering of idols , we know that idols are nothing in the world , and that there is only one God and no other God
&quot; Whether he is called God , or in heaven , or in the earth , he is like the Lord of many Gods .
&quot; But we have only one God , the Father , to whom all things belong , and to whom we belong ; and one Lord , Jesus Christ , to whom all things belong , and to whom we belong
But no man has such knowledge ; but there are some who , because they have become accustomed to idols , eat idols for a sacrifice ; and their conscience is weakened , and they are defiled .
In fact , food can &apos;t make God see us , for we don &apos;t eat , neither do we harm , neither do we benefit
&quot; But be careful , lest your freedom become a stumbling block to the weak .
&quot; If a man sees you in the temple of idols , and sees that which you know , will his conscience , if it is weak , not be bold to eat the things of the idols ?
&quot; Therefore Christ , the weak brother who died for him , has fallen because of your knowledge
You have thus sinned , brethren , and have hurt their weak conscience , and have sinned against Christ .
&quot; So if food causes my brother to fall , I will never eat meat , lest it cause my brother to fall
Have I not been free ? Have I not been an apostle ? Have I not seen our Lord Jesus ? Have you not done my work in the Lord ?
If I am not an apostle in others , I am always an apostle in you ; for you are the seal of me in the Lord
&quot; This is how I judge the man who questioned me
Don &apos;t we have the power to eat and drink from the gospel
&quot; Have we not the power to take the sisters of the believers as wives , and to go with them as the rest of the apostles , and as the brothers of the Lord , and as Jacob ?
Only I and Barnabas have no power to work .
Who is a soldier , and prepares his own wages ? Who plants vineyards , and eats not the fruit thereof ? Who feeds sheep and goats , and eats not the milk of sheep and goats
&quot; Is it according to the opinion of men that I say this , and according to the law ?
As it is written in the law of Moses , &quot; When the cow is in the field , you shall not cover his mouth . &quot; Is it the cow that God misses ?
Isn &apos;t that what it says to us ? It &apos;s clearly what it says to us . For those who cultivate have hope to cultivate , and those who fight have hope to fight when they have food .
&quot; If we sow the seeds of the Spirit among you , will we be able to harvest the flesh out of you and feed it ?
If any have this authority over you , how about us ? Yet we have not exercised it , and endure all things , lest the gospel of Christ be hindered
Do you not know that those who work for the holy things eat of the things in the temple , and those who serve the altar divide the things on the altar ?
&quot; This is also how the Lord commanded that those who preach the gospel should live by the gospel
&quot; But this power is of no use to me . I write these words , and I do not want you to treat me like this ; for I would rather die than let anyone take away my boasting .
I preached the gospel without exaggeration , for I was unworthy ; and if I did not preach the gospel , I would be in trouble .
&quot; If I am willing to do it , I will be rewarded ; and if I am not willing , I will be entrusted with responsibility .
And what is my reward , when I preach the gospel , that no man should spend money for the gospel , and that no man should use his power to preach it ?
Though I am free , and have no authority , yet I am willing to be a servant to all , that I may gain more
To the Jews , I am a Jew , that I may be a Jew ; to the Gentiles , that I may be a Gentile ; to the Gentiles , that I may be a Gentile , that I may be a Gentile
For I am a man without law , that I may be a man without law ; for I am before God , not without law , but before Christ , and under the law
To a weak man I am a weak man , and to a weak man I am a weak man . To whomsoever I am a weak man , and to whomsoever I am a weak man , I will save some .
All that I have done is for the sake of the gospel , that I may have the goodness of the gospel with men
&quot; Do you not know that all those who run in the field run , but only one who receives the reward , and you run so that you may receive the reward
And those who are stronger in battle are disciplined in all things ; they only have the crown of evil , and we have the crown of no evil .
So I run , not as a man without direction ; I fight , not as an airman .
&quot; I have attacked myself , and I have called on myself to obey ; for I am afraid that I will be rejected when I preach the gospel to others .
&quot; Brothers , I do not want you to know that our ancestors passed through the sea under clouds
All were washed in the clouds and in the sea , and returned to Moses
And they all ate a kind of spiritual food
And they all drank a kind of spirit water , which came out of the rock of their spirit , which is Christ .
But most of them are people whom God does not like , so they die in the wilderness .
These are our warnings , that we should not be niggardly in evil , as they are .
And they shall not worship idols , as they have worshipped others . As it is written , &apos; The people sit down to eat and drink , and rise up to play .
Neither shall we commit adultery , as some of them have done ; and thirty-two thousand men shall be put to death in one day .
Neither shall they test the Lord , as they test men , but shall be destroyed by the serpent .
&quot; Do not complain , neither do you ; for as they complain , so shall they be destroyed , as the dead are destroyed .
When they encounter these things , they are to be warned , and it is written in the Book that warns the people of our last days .
So that he may stand firm , and be careful , and not fall
God is faithful , and he will not let you be tempted beyond what you can bear . In the time of temptation , He will always give you a way out , so that you can endure .
My beloved brethren , avoid idolatry
&quot; It seems to me that I have spoken to a man who understands . You are going to testify against me
Is not the cup that we bless the blood of Christ , and the bread that we break the body of Christ ?
We are a bread , a body , even though we are many ; for we are all divided by this bread .
&quot; You are a fleshly Israelite . Is not he who eats of the sacrifice a share in the altar ?
What shall I say , or what shall the things of idols be , or what shall the idols be
&quot; I say , &apos; The sacrifices of strangers are devils and not gods , and I do not want you to associate with devils .
&quot; You will not drink the cup of the Lord nor the cup of the devil , nor will you eat the feast of the Lord nor the feast of the devil .
Are we capable of provoking the Lord &apos;s wrath ? Are we more capable than He
All things are possible , but not of any benefit . All things are possible , but not of any benefit to man
Whoever asks not for his own benefit , but for the benefit of others
&quot; You shall eat of all that is sold in the marketplace , and you shall not ask anything for your conscience .
For to the Lord belongs the earth , and all that is filled therein .
&quot; If a man who does not believe asks you to come , and you are willing to do so , what will he do to those who are before you ? He will eat and will not ask for his conscience
&quot; If any man says to you , &apos; This is a sacrifice , &apos; he will not eat it for the sake of those who have told you it , and for the sake of conscience .
The conscience that I speak is not yours , but his . My freedom , why is it disputed by the conscience of others ?
&quot; If I give thanks and eat , why is that which I give thanks denied ?
&quot; Therefore eat ye or drink ye , and do ye whatsoever ye may for glory to God
Neither you , the Jew , nor the Philistine , nor the church of God , will bring him down
It is as if I have made all things to be pleasing to all , not seeking my own benefit , but the benefit of all men , that they may be saved
&quot; You should obey me , just as I obey Christ
I praise you for remembering me in all things , and for upholding what I have preached to you .
I wish you would know that Christ is the head of every man , that men are the head of women , and that God is the head of Christ .
&quot; When a man prays or speaks , and bears his head , he humbles his head
If a woman prays or speaks without her head on , she is ashamed of her head , for it is like shaving her hair
If a woman is not covered with her head , she should shave her hair ; and if a woman is ashamed of shaving her hair , she should be covered with her head
A man should not wear his head , for he is the image and glory of God ; but a woman is the glory of a man
At first , men did not come from women . Women came from men
And men are not made for women ; but women are made for men
Therefore , for the sake of the angels , a woman should have a sign of authority on her head
But according to the Lord &apos;s arrangement , neither are women without men , nor are men without women .
For the woman is of men , and the man is of women ; but all things are of God
Is it lawful for you to test yourselves , and for women to pray to God without a head ?
Does not your nature show you that a man with long hair is a shame to him ?
But a woman with long hair is his glory ; for it is for him to cover his head .
If any man wishes to argue , we do not have such a statute , neither do the churches of God
&quot; Now I command you not to praise you , for your gatherings are not profitable , but harmful .
First , I heard that when you gathered , you divided your doors among yourselves , and I believed it a little
There is a division among you , so that those who have experience may be made manifest .
When you are gathered together , it is impossible to eat the Lord &apos;s supper
For at the time of eating , each man eats first his own food , and even this hunger , and this drunkenness
&quot; What shall I say to you , that there is no house for you to eat and drink , or that there is no shame for the church of God ? What shall I say to you , that there is no shame for you ? I do not praise you .
&quot; I took up the bread that I preached to you that day , which was from the Lord , that night when the Lord Jesus was sold
Then he broke it , and said , &quot; This is my body , which I have given to you ; so you should do , because you remember me . &quot;
&quot; And after the meal they took a cup and said , &apos; This is the new covenant made with my blood . Do this every time you drink , remembering Me .
&quot; Whenever you eat this cake and drink this cup , it is a sign of the Lord &apos;s death , until he comes .
Therefore whoever does not eat the bread of the Lord and drink the cup of the Lord in righteousness is the blood of the master of the Lord who has sinned .
&quot; Then a man shall take care of himself , and eat the cake , and drink the cup
For if a man eats and drinks , he eats and drinks his own sin , if he does not discern it from the body of the Lord
&quot; There are therefore many among you who are weak and sick , and many who die .
We would not have been tried if we had first identified ourselves .
&quot; When we are tried , the Lord will punish us , and we will not be condemned together with the world .
Therefore , my brethren , wait for one another at the time of your gathering
And if any man is hungry , let him eat first at home , lest ye gather together and sin on yourselves ; and the rest shall be arranged when I come .
&quot; Brothers , I do not want you to understand the grace of the Spirit
As you know , when you are foreigners , you are led astray in all things , and serve the dumb idols .
&quot; Therefore I say unto you , He who is moved by the Spirit of God is not cursable , and he who is not moved by the Holy Spirit is not Lord
Grace was separated , but the Holy Spirit was one
The offices are separate , but the Lord is one
There is also a distinction between works , but God is One Who performs all things in the presence of all
The Holy Spirit is manifest in every man , that he may profit
He received the word of wisdom from the Holy Spirit , and he received the word of knowledge from the Holy Spirit
And another gave him faith in the Holy Spirit , and another gave him healing in the Holy Spirit
A man who can do other things , and a man who can be a prophet , and a man who can distinguish spirits , and a man who can speak tongues , and a man who can translate tongues
All these things are the work of the Holy Spirit , which is given to every man according to his own will .
Just as the body is one , but has many limbs , and even though there are many , it is one , and so is Christ
Neither were we Jews , nor were we Hebrews , nor were we slaves , nor were we free : but we were baptized from the Holy Spirit , and became a body , and drunk from the Holy Spirit .
The body is not a body , but many bodies
He said , &quot; Because I am not a hand , I do not belong to the body , and because he cannot be , he does not belong to the body
He said , &quot; I am not an eye , therefore I am not of the body ; neither can he , therefore he is not of the body .
If the whole body were eyes , where would it hear ? If the whole body were ears , where would it smell ?
But now God , by His own will , has arranged all the members of his body
If it were one body , what body would be in it ?
But now there are many limbs , and the body is one
The eyes cannot say to the opponent , &quot; I am not worthy of you ; nor can the head say to the feet , &quot; I am not worthy of you &quot;
Not only that , but the body and the limbs of men are innumerablely weak
&quot; The more the body and the more the faces are added to him , for we see him as unfit ; and the more he is unfit , the better he becomes .
Our beautiful bodies are not naturally adorned , but God has assembled them , and multiplied them for the missing bodies .
Avoid compartmentalizing your body . Always take care of one another &apos;s bodies .
If a body suffers , all the bodies suffer together ; and if a body is glorified , all the bodies rejoice together
&quot; You are the body of Christ , and each one of you is his own body
The first is the apostle , the second is the prophet , the third is the teacher , the second is the divine , the third is the healer , the helper , the ruler , the spoken word .
Are they all apostles , prophets , teachers , and prodigals ?
Are they all blessed with healing ? Are they all spoken ? Are they all translated ?
I now direct you by the most wondrous way to seek the greater grace .
&quot; If I could speak the tongues of men , and the words of angels , and have no love , I would be like a sounding gong and a sounding harp .
&quot; If I have the power of the prophet to speak , and understand all the secrets , and all the knowledge , and if I have the letter that I may go over mountains , and have no love , I will have nothing .
&quot; If I burn all the poor , and give myself up , and have no love , it will be of no benefit to me .
Love is endurance , and mercy . Love is not jealousy . Love is not boasting . Love is not madness .
Don &apos;t be shy . Don &apos;t seek your own advantage . Don &apos;t be easily angry . Don &apos;t count the evil of men .
I don &apos;t like injustice . I just like truth .
To include everything . To believe everything . To hope everything . To endure everything .
Love never ceases . The power of the prophet to speak will be lost . The power of the tongue will cease , and knowledge will be lost .
We are now limited in what we know , and limited in what the prophets have spoken
When the perfect comes , the finite shall return to nothingness
When I am a child , words are like children , hearts like children , thoughts like children ; and when I am a man , I forsake the things of children
&quot; Now we look in the mirror and are confused . Then we shall be face to face , and the knowledge that I have now is limited , and I shall know it all , as the Lord knows me .
There is faith , hope , and love , and the greatest of these is love
&quot; You shall seek love , and seek the blessings of the Spirit , and most desirable of them is the prophetic word .
And he that speaketh the tongue speaketh not unto man , but unto God : for no man heareth it ; but in his heart he speaketh secrets of all kinds .
&quot; But he speaks as a prophet , speaking to men , to establish , to comfort , and to comfort .
He that speaketh in tongues is he that fashioneth himself ; and he that prophesieth is he that fashioneth the church
I would rather you all speak the tongue , and I would rather you preach the word ; for whoever speaks the tongue will be stronger than he who does not turn and establish the church , and whoever preaches will be stronger than he .
&quot; Brothers , if I come to you and explain to you in tongues and not with revelations or knowledge or prophecies or teachings , what will be my gain with you ?
How can a thing that has no voice , or a violin , or a harp , be separated from the sound that comes out ? How can one know what one blows and what one plays ?
Who can prepare war if he blows an uncertain noise
And so are you ; how can you know what is said if your tongue does not speak a thing that is easy to understand ? That is the speech to the air .
The voices of the world , or much of them , are nothing but meaningless
&quot; If I do not understand the meaning of that voice , then he who speaks will be alienated from me , and I will be alienated from him
And so are you , both of the grace of the spirit , and of the church , when you seek more
So the one who speaks the tongue turns out when he seeks
If I pray in tongues , it is my spirit ; but my enlightenment has no effect .
What about this ? I will pray with the Spirit , and I will pray with the Wisdom . I will sing with the Spirit , and I will sing with the Wisdom
&quot; If not , how can the one who is not able to speak the tongue , who does not understand what you say , say , &apos; Amen , &apos; when you give thanks ?
It is good that you are grateful , but you are not able to make others
&quot; I thank God , and I speak more tongues than all of you
But in the synagogue , it is better to teach a man five words with understanding , as strong as a thousand words in tongues .
Brothers , do not be children in your hearts , but be children in evil deeds , and always be adults in your hearts .
&quot; It is written in the law , &apos; Thus says the Lord , &apos; I will speak to this people with the tongues of the foreigners and with the lips of the foreigners ; yet they have not listened to me .
Thus it seems that speaking tongues is not proof of a believer , but of a disbeliever ; speaking prophets is not proof of a disbeliever , but of a believer
So when the whole congregation is gathered together in one place , and they all speak the tongue , and there come in by chance a man who cannot speak the tongue , or a man who does not believe , saying , Are you mad ?
&quot; If a prophet speaks , and by chance a disbeliever or a speaker of no tongue comes in , he is awakened and judged by all
&quot; And when the secrets of his heart are revealed , he will humble himself and worship God , saying , &apos; God is indeed among you . &apos; 
But how is it , brethren , that at the time of your gathering every one of you has a poem , or a lesson , or a revelation , or a tongue , or a word that has been translated out ?
&quot; If any man speaks a tongue , two or three persons shall speak it in turn , and one person shall speak it in turn .
&quot; If no man turns his back , he will shut his mouth in the congregation , and say to himself and to God ,
As for the prophets , it is for two or three men to preach , and for the rest to discern with care .
&quot; If anyone who sits beside him receives a revelation , he who speaks first will not speak
For every one of you is a prophet to preach , and to teach reason to all , and to be admonished .
The Spirit of the prophet was originally obedient to the prophet
For God does not call men to confusion , but to quietness
Women shall keep their mouths shut in the synagogues , as in the churches of the saints , because they are not permitted to speak ; and they shall obey , as the law says
Whatever they want to learn , they can ask their husbands at home , for it was shameful to speak for women in meetings
&quot; Is God &apos;s Word coming from you , or has it come to you ?
&quot; If any man is a prophet or a spirit for himself , he shall know that what I have written to you is the commandment of the Lord
If there is one who does not know , let him not know
Therefore , my brethren , you shall love to speak as a prophet , and you shall not forbid speaking tongues .
Everything has to be regulated in order .
Now , brethren , I have told you the gospel that was preached to you , which you also received , and upon which you stand ,
&quot; If you do not believe , and hold fast to what I have taught you , you will be saved by this gospel .
The first which I received and preached to you that day was that Christ died for our sins , as it is written in the Scriptures
And he was buried , and , as it is written in the Scriptures , he was raised again on the third day
And he showed it to Caiaphas , and to the twelve apostles
And it came to pass at a certain time , that he showed it to more than five hundred brethren , and most of them were still to this day , and some had fallen asleep .
Then he showed it to Jacob , and to the apostles .
And it came to pass at the end , that I was as a man born unto the end of his life .
I was the least of the apostles , and I was not worthy to be called an apostle , because I used to oppress the church of God
&quot; However , I am made today by the grace of God , and the grace which He has bestowed on me is not vain . I have worked harder than all the apostles , and it was not I ; but the grace of God is with me .
&quot; Behold , I am the apostle ; so have we preached , and so have you believed .
How is it that some among you say that there is no resurrection of the dead , even though Christ is raised from the dead ?
Without the resurrection of the dead , Christ will not be resurrected
If Christ has not been resurrected , what we have preached is vain , and what you believe is also vain
And it is evident that we bear false witness to God , because we bear witness that God has raised Christ ; and if the dead are not raised , God has not raised Christ
For if the dead are not raised again , Christ is not raised again
Without the resurrection of Christ , your faith is void , and you are in sin .
For those who slept in Christ also perished
If we have hope in Christ in the present life , we will be poorer than all
But Christ was raised from the dead , and became the firstfruit of the sleeping man
Death is for one man , and the resurrection of the dead is for one man
All men died in Adam ; and all men are to be raised up in Christ
But each one is raised in his own order . The first ripe fruit is Christ , and those who belong to him in the time of his coming
Then came the end , when Christ destroyed all that were in power , and all that were in power , and all that were able , and gave the kingdom to the Father
For it is necessary for Christ to reign , until God puts all his enemies under his feet
And death is the end of the enemy that is destroyed .
For in the Scriptures it is said , &apos; God has called all things under His feet . &apos; Even though all things have been called to Him , it is evident that all things are not within Him
&quot; When all things have submitted themselves to Him , then the Son will submit himself to him who calls all things to Him , that God may be above all things , Lord of all things
What will happen to those who are baptized for the dead ? If the dead never come back , why are they baptized for them ?
What time are we taking the risk again
&quot; Brothers , I am in Christ Jesus my Lord , and I speak with great power of your exhortations , saying , &apos; I die every day
&quot; What good will it be to me if I fight with the beasts in Ephesus on that day , as a stranger ? If the dead do not come to life , we shall eat and drink and drink , for tomorrow they shall die .
Do not deceive yourselves . Misuse is defeating good deeds .
&quot; You shall awaken for good , and do not sin ; for some do not know God ; and I say this to make you ashamed .
Or someone asks , &quot; How does the dead come back to life ? What body does he bring with him ? &quot;
&quot; O foolish man , what you have planted will not be born unless you die .
And whatsoever thou plantest , it is not of the form of the future , nor of the grains , or of the wheat , or of any other grain ;
But God , according to His own will , gave Him a form , and called every grain its own form .
Every body is different : man is one , beast is one , bird is one , fish is one
There are bodies in heaven , and there are bodies on earth ; but the glory of the bodies in heaven is one , and the glory of the bodies on earth is one
The glory of the day is the glory of the day , the glory of the moon is the glory of the moon , and the glory of the star is the glory of the star . There is also a distinction between the glory of that star and the glory of that star
Thus is the resurrection of the dead ; and that which is planted shall perish , and that which is raised up shall not perish .
He that is planted is ashamed , and he that is raised to life is glory ; He that is planted is weak , and he that is raised to life is strong .
For he that is planted is a body of blood , and the resurrection is a body of spirit ; and if there be a body of blood , there must also be a body of spirit .
And it is written in the Scriptures , &quot; The first Adam became a living man with a spirit , and the last Adam became a spirit to make man alive
But the Spirit is not first , and the Spirit of blood is first , and afterwards there is the Spirit .
The first man is from the earth , and he belongs to it ; and the second man is from heaven
As for that land , so shall all the land be ; and as for heaven , so shall all the heaven be
We have the form of the earth , and in the future we shall have the form of heaven
&quot; Brothers , I have told you that the flesh and blood cannot bear the kingdom of God , and that it will perish , and that it will not perish forever .
I tell you a mysterious thing today . We are not going to sleep , but we are going to change
In a moment , in the blink of an eye , the last trumpet will sound . For the trumpet will sound , and the dead will be raised to life , and we will also change
This shall be desolate , and it shall be incorruptible ; this shall be dead , and it shall be incorruptible
And it shall be desolate , and it shall become incorruptible ; and it shall be dead , and it shall become incorruptible ; and at that time shall be fulfilled that which is written : Death shall be swallowed up .
Death , therein is the power of your victory . Death , therein is the hook of your poison .
The hook of death is sin . The power of sin is the law .
Thank God , that we may be victorious through our Lord Jesus Christ
Therefore , my beloved brethren , be steadfast and steadfast , and be steadfast in your stewardship ; for I know that your labour is not vain in the Lord .
&quot; How have I commanded the churches of Galatia to give money to the saints , and how have you done
Every seventh day , on the first day , each man shall draw forth his own account , lest the time of my coming should come upon him .
And when I am come , I will send to whom you write letters of encouragement , and I will send your contributions to Jerusalem
If I should go , they could go with me
I will pass through Macedonia ; and after I have passed , I will go to you
or to stay with you for a few days , or to spend the winter ; wherever I go , you may send me
&quot; I am not willing to go over to see you now . If the Lord wills me , I will hope to live with you for a while
&quot; But I will still live in Ephesus until the feast of Pentecost .
For there is a wide and effective door opened for me , and many opponents ; and as I am the workman of the Lord , so do I.
&quot; If Timothy comes , be careful that he has no fear in your midst ; for I expect him to come with my brethren because of his labor
&quot; Therefore no one shall despise him , but let him come to me before I send him to peace , and he will not be willing to go , and he will go when he has the opportunity
&quot; As for the brother Apollos , I again urged him to go with the brethren to you , but at this time
Be watchful , stand firm in the way of truth , be great husbands , and be strong .
&quot; Whatever you do , do it with love
&quot; Brothers , you know that the house of Zedekiah is the fruit of the first fruits of Achaia , and that they serve only the saints
I urge you to obey such men , and all those who work with one another ; and they will fill me with what I cannot do .
&quot; Behold , I love you , when you come to me from Antioch , and from Phoenicia , and from Assyria ,
They make me and your hearts rejoice , and you should be honoured among them ; for the Lord has asked you many things .
And the churches of Asia beseech you , saying , Peace be unto you , and unto the churches of Ahijah and Berkhel , and unto their houses :
All the brethren shall ask you for peace , and you shall ask for peace with your mouths , and keep one another holy
I Paul ask you in writing
Cursed be he that loveth not the LORD , for the LORD must come
May the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ always be with you all
My love in Christ Jesus is with you all . Amen
By the will of God , Paul the apostle of Christ Jesus , and Timothy the brother , wrote to the church of God at Corinth , and to the saints throughout Achaia
Grace and peace be to you from God , our Father and Lord Jesus Christ .
Blessed be the God the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ , the Father of mercy , the God of comfort in all things
&quot; In all our troubles He comforts us , that we may use the comfort of God to comfort those who are afflicted by all kinds of affliction .
For we are comforted more by Christ than by the sufferings of Christ
Our suffering is to be comforted and saved , and our comfort is to be comforted and to be comforted by you , so that you may bear the pain we have suffered .
Our hope for you is certain , knowing that you are both suffering and comforted .
&quot; Brothers , we have suffered in Asia before , and we have been overwhelmed , we have not been able to prevail , and our hope of life has been cut off .
&quot; And I have determined in my heart that I will die , that we should not rely on ourselves , but on God , who brings the dead to life .
He saved us from the great death , and he is still saving us , and we hope that he will save us in the future
&quot; You pray to help us , so that many may give thanks for us , as you have done for many .
What we boast of is our own conscience , and what we witness by the holiness and truth of God , in the world for men , not by the wisdom of men , but by the grace of God , even more so to you .
&quot; As we write to you , I do not differ from what you think and know , and I hope that you will know it at last .
as you have known us for a few days , and exalt with us , as we exalt with you in the days of our Lord Jesus
&quot; Because I am so convinced , I thought to go to you early , that you might gain more .
And they shall pass through from you to Macedonia , and from Macedonia shall return to you , and you shall send me to Judah
&quot; Is it that I intend to do it repeatedly ? Is it that I intend to do it out of desire ?
&quot; By the faithful God , I say , &apos; We have not spoken to you the way that we have spoken to you , whether it be yes or no
For there is neither a Yes nor a No in Jesus Christ , the Son of God , whom I and Silas and Timothy have preached among you , and in him is only one Yes
The promise of God is true in Christ , no matter how many ; therefore by him is it also true , that God may be glorified for us
&quot; It is God who strengthens us and you in Christ , and anoints us
He also sealed us with a seal , and gave the Spirit as a proof in our hearts .
&quot; I call on God to testify to my heart . I have not gone to Corinth to forgive you
&quot; We do not rule over your faith , but help your joy ; for by faith you stand .
I have made my own plan , and I will come to you again , and you must not be grieved
&quot; Who will make me happy , if I call you to sorrow , except the one whom I call sorrowful ?
&quot; I have written this to you , for I am afraid that those who make me happy will make me sad when I come , and I am sure that all of you will take my joy for yourselves .
I have written to you in my former heart of sorrow and tears , not to grieve you , but to know that I love you exceedingly .
&quot; If anyone grieves , not only does he grieve me , but he also grieves all of you , and I say , I am afraid I say too much
&quot; Then he who is like this shall be punished by all men , and shall be put to death .
Better to forgive him , to comfort him , to prevent his sorrow from becoming too great , and even to sink
&quot; Therefore I urge you to show to Him a firm love
&quot; For this reason I wrote to you before , to test you , and to see whether you obeyed or not .
&quot; Whoever you forgive , I forgive ; and whoever I forgive , I forgive for you in the presence of Christ .
For we know not his deceit , lest Satan should prevail over us at any opportunity .
&quot; I came to Troy from the gospel of Christ , and the Lord opened the door to me
Then , being troubled that I had not found Titus my brother , I departed from the people there to Macedonia
&quot; Thanks to God , the centurion has guided us to triumph in Christ , and has lent us the fragrance of the knowledge of Christ everywhere
For in the presence of God we have the aroma of Christ , whether in the body of the rescued or in the body of the destroyed
And in them they made a smell of death to make him die ; and in them they made a smell of life to make him live ; and who will be able to do this ?
We are not like the multitude of men who speak in order to confuse God , but in truth , and in God , and in Christ before God .
&quot; Are we to recommend ourselves , or are we to give you a letter of recommendation like others , or a letter of recommendation like yours ?
&quot; You are our admonition , written in our hearts , and recited by all that know it .
You are evidently the letter of Christ , which we have made by ourselves , not written in ink , but by the Spirit of the Everlasting God , not on a stone , but on a heart
We have such faith in God because of Christ
And it is not by ourselves that we bear the burden ; but it is from God that we bear it
He commanded us to bear the charge of the new covenant , not by word , but by spirit ; for the word is to die , and the spirit is to live .
The office of death , which is engraved on a stone , is glorious , and the glory of Moses is not seen by the eyes of the children of Israel , for it has passed away .
How much more glorious is the ministry of the Spirit ?
If the office of condemnation be glorified , the glory of the office of righteousness shall be increased
For that which was glorified before was not glorified , because of the great glory
If that which is wasted is glorious , and that which endures is more glorious
We have such hope , and we speak with great boldness
Like Moses , when he covered the face of Pharaoh , so that the children of Israel could not see the end of the destroyer .
But their hearts were hardened , and until this day , when they read the Old Testament , the cup had not been opened , but in Christ it had been broken
But to this day , when they read the book of Moses , Paschal was still in their hearts
But their hearts returned to the Lord , and they were removed from him .
&quot; The Lord is the Spirit , and the Spirit of the Lord is there , and in it is freedom .
&quot; Now that we have opened our faces , and have seen the glory of the Lord , as if it were reflected back from the mirror , we have become the shape of the Lord , glorified in glory , as if we were made from the Spirit of the Lord
&quot; Because we are compassionate , and have received this office , we shall not be discouraged
For he has forsaken the dark and shameful things , and has not done deceit , nor spoken the truth of God , but revealed the truth , that he might present himself before God to the conscience of men .
If our gospel is shielded , it is shielded against the dead
These unbelievers have been blinded by the God of this world , that the glory of the gospel of Christ should not shine upon them ; for Christ is the likeness of God
We did not preach ourselves , but preach Christ Jesus as Lord , and made ourselves your servants because of Jesus
&quot; The God who commanded the light to shine out of darkness has been revealed in our hearts , that we may know the glory of God in the face of Jesus Christ
We have this treasure in the vault to show this great power , which is from God and not from us
We are enemies on all sides , but we are not trapped ; We are troubled in our hearts , but we are not disappointed
Forced , but not abandoned ; overthrown , but not to death
And the death of Jesus was always in them , and the life of Jesus was manifest in us .
For our living are often given to the land of death for Jesus , that the life of Jesus may be manifested in our mortals .
It seems that death is on us , and life on you
But we have faith , as it is written , &quot; Because I believe , so I speak , &quot; and we believe , so we speak
Knowing that he who calls the Lord Jesus will also call us to life with Jesus , and we will stand before him with you
For all things are for you , that the grace may be multiplied by the multitude , and that thanks may be multiplied exceedingly , that you may be glorified in God
So we are not discouraged . Although the outside is destroyed , inside is a new day like a day
&quot; For this we shall suffer for a little while , but for our accomplishment there shall be no greater glory than ever .
For we are not the things that are seen , but the things that are not seen ; for what is seen is temporary , and what is not seen is eternal .
&quot; We knew that if our tents on the earth were to be destroyed , they would be a house of eternal life in heaven , built by God , and not by men .
We wept in the tent , and thought deeply of the house that came up from heaven , as if we were clothed
If you put on it , you will not be naked when you are met
&quot; In this tent we are weeping and weeping , and we are not willing to take it off , but to put on it , that the dead may be swallowed up by life .
And it is God who hath sown us , and hath given us the Spirit as a proof .
&quot; Therefore , when we are open and fearless , and know that we dwell within ourselves , we depart from the Lord
For we act for men by faith , and not by sight
We are openly fearless , more willing to leave the body and live with the Lord
&quot; Therefore whether we dwell in ourselves or go out of ourselves , we have set our sight on the joy of the Lord
For it is necessary for all of us to be revealed in the presence of Christ , that everyone may be recompensed according to what he has done , for good or for evil .
&quot; We know that the Lord is awesome , so we exhort , but we are manifest in the sight of God , and hope is manifest in your consciences
&quot; We do not recommend ourselves to you again , but that you may answer those who boast about us because of our boasting , and not because of their appearance .
&quot; If we are mad , it is for God ; if we are obedient , it is for you .
The love of Christ which was originally inspired us , because we thought that one died for all , and all died
And he died for all , that those who are alive might no longer live for themselves , but for the Lord who raised up for them from the dead .
Therefore we have not recognized Christ by appearance from this day onward , though we recognized him by appearance , but now we do not recognize him that way
If any man is in Christ , he is a new creation ; and the old things have passed away , and they are become new
&quot; All things are from God , who , through Christ , has made us good with Him , and has given us the ministry of admonishing men to be good with Him
That God , in Christ , may make the world good to himself , and not return their transgressions to them , and that goodness may be entrusted to us .
Therefore we are the apostles of Christ , just as God persuaded you through us , and we ask for Christ goodness with God
God has made the innocent a sin for us , that we may be justified in him as God
&quot; For we who work together with God also exhort you to receive His grace from the ungodly .
For he said , &quot; In the time of grace I have given you my oath , and in the child of salvation I have rescued you . &quot; Behold , it is the time of grace , and it is the day of salvation
&quot; We do not hinder anyone in all things , lest this office be slandered
On the contrary , in all things they show that they are God &apos;s servants , as in many times of patience , suffering , poverty , and distress .
whipping , imprisonment , disturbance , hard work , watchfulness , not eating
Integrity , Knowledge , Patience , Mercy , Sensitivity of the Holy Spirit , Immaculate Love
True reason , the great power of God , the weapon of righteousness on the left .
Glory , shame , evil name , good name . It seems tempting , but it is true
It seems unknown to man , but it is known to man ; it seems to die , but it is alive ; it seems to be punished , but it is not dead
It seems sorrowful , but it is often happy . It seems poor , but it makes many rich . It seems nothing , but it is all
&quot; O you people of Corinth , we are open to you , and our hearts are generous .
&quot; You are narrower than we are , but your heart is narrower than yours
You will also respond to me with a generous heart , just as I said to my own children
You are not in harmony with the unbelievers , nor are you to be yoked with them . What is the connection between righteousness and wickedness , and what is the connection between light and darkness ?
What is the reconciliation between Christ and Pilate , the other name of Satan ? What is the reconciliation between the believers and the unbelievers ?
For we are the house of the everlasting God , just as God said , &quot; I will dwell among them , and I will come to them , and I will be their God , and they will be my children . &quot;
And said , &quot; You shall come out of among them separately from them , and do not touch unclean things , and I will receive you
&quot; I will be your father , and you will be my daughters , &quot; said the Almighty
Beloved brethren , having this promise , we are sanctified when we purify ourselves from all filth of the flesh and the soul , and when we fear God
&quot; You shall receive us with ease ; we have not lost , we have not defeated , we have not taken advantage of
&quot; I say this not to judge your sins , but as I have said in the past , you are always in our hearts , willing to live and die with you .
I am greatly daring to speak to you ; I am filled with comfort because of your exaggerations ; and we are separated in all our troubles .
&quot; When we have come to Macedonia , our bodies shall not be at rest ; there shall be trouble around them , there shall be wars outside , there shall be fear within .
But the God of those who comfort the depressed comforted us with Titus .
He has comforted us , not only through him , but also by the comfort he has received from you ; for he has told me your thoughts , your mourning , and your enthusiasm toward me , that I may rejoice more .
&quot; I wrote a letter to you before , and I regretted it later , but I do not regret it now , for I know that the letter is not temporary ,
&quot; Now I rejoice , not because of your sorrow , but because of your repentance which is born out of your sorrow , and because of the word of God you are sorrowful , and all things are not lost because of us .
For by the will of God the repentance of repentance without repentance is born , that we may be saved ; but the sorrow of the world is death .
&quot; Behold , what kind of diligence , complaint , hatred , fear , sorrow , longing , enthusiasm , and punishment has come from you , according to the will of God ? In all these things you have declared yourselves clean .
Even though I have written to you before , I am not for the loser , nor for the loser , but in the presence of God , to show you our zeal ,
&quot; Therefore we are comforted , and in comfort we rejoice even more , because your people rejoice with joy in the hearts of many .
I am not ashamed to praise Titus for what I have praised you ; for I have praised Titus for what I have praised you ; and as I have praised you , so have I praised you .
And Titus remembered the obedience of all your people , how he received him with fear and trembling , and the more he loved your hearts .
&quot; Now I am glad that I can reassure you in all things
Brothers , I have told you the grace which God has bestowed on the churches of Macedonia
It is in times of great tribulation that they are satisfied with joy , and in times of extreme poverty that the mercy of their grace is manifested
I can prove that they have contributed with force , and have also done so with force , with their own indulgence
Thirdly , ask us , that they may have a share in this grace which they have offered to the saints
And what they have done , not only according to our desire , but according to the will of God , they have first dedicated themselves to the Lord , and have attached themselves to us
Therefore I exhort Titus , that this mercy which is done among you should be done
Since you are exceedingly full in faith , in tongue , in knowledge , in enthusiasm , and in the love of our hearts , you are exceedingly satisfied in this mercy
&quot; I say this not by commandment , but by the passion of others , to test the truth of your love .
You know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ , who was rich for you , but became poor for you , that you might be rich for his poverty .
It is good for you that I have given you my opinion on this matter , for you have been working on it for a year
Now therefore do it , and do it with the will of your heart , and according to all that you do .
&quot; For if a man has a willing heart , he will be pleased with all that he has , and not with all that he has not .
I didn &apos;t want others to neglect ; you were tired
It is to be equal . It is to be equal that your abundance may now fill their shortcomings , and that their abundance may be filled their shortcomings , and that your abundance may be filled in the future
As it is recorded above , &apos; There is no more to be gained than what is gained , and there is no shortage of what is gained .
Thank God , who moved Titus &apos; heart , that he might be kind to you , as I am
He has certainly listened to my advice , but he is more enthusiastic and willing to go to you
We also sent a brother with him , who received the praise of the church in the gospel
Not only that , but he was also chosen by the churches , and accompanied us , and delivered this gift which was entrusted to us , to glorify the Lord , and to show our joyful heart .
&quot; This is so that no one will choose us because of the many gifts we have received
&quot; We keep the things of light , not only before the Lord , but also before men
And we sent a brother with us , whose zeal , which we have tested many times in many things , is increased in him because of your faith .
Concerning Titus , who is my companion , and who has worked together for you ; Concerning those two brothers , who are the messengers of the churches , and the glory of Christ ,
&quot; Therefore you must show before the churches the evidence of your love , and the evidence of your praise which I have given you
&quot; I will not write to you concerning the provision of the saints
For I know that your joyful heart often exalts you to the Macedonians , saying , &quot; A year has passed since the Achaeans were ready , and your zeal has stirred up many . &quot;
&quot; But I have sent the brethren to prepare for you according to my words , lest we should boast about your words in this matter .
&quot; If the Macedonians come with us and see that you have no preparation , then we will be ashamed of what we believe , and not to mention your shame .
&quot; Therefore I desire to ask the brethren to go to you first , and to prepare the pledges that were promised before , and to make it manifest that what you have given is for joy and not for restraint .
Less harvest , more harvest , more harvest . That &apos;s true
Let every man do according to his own heart , and do not be troubled , nor be weary ; for he who gives willingly is loved by God .
God will give you all kinds of grace , and more , and make all things sufficient for you , and do all kinds of good deeds
As it is written , &quot; He gives wealth and riches to relieve poverty . His mercy endures forever .
&quot; He who gives seed to those who sow , and gives food to those who eat , will add to the seed of your land , and to the fruit of your righteousness .
&quot; And thanks be to God for us , that you may be rich in all things and give more .
The work of this supply not only fills the lack of saints , but also makes many more grateful to God
&quot; They have obtained proof of this provision , knowing that you confessed the gospel of Christ , and obeyed him , and gave more money to them and to all , and glorified themselves before God .
And they remembered you , and prayed for you , because of the great grace of God , which was manifest in your hearts .
Thank God for His infinite grace
I , Paul , am humble when I see you , and brave to you when I am not with you ; and now I persuade you by the gentle peace of Christ ,
&quot; Some think that I am acting with blood , and that I must be brave in dealing with such people . Do not let me be so brave when I am with you .
For though we act with blood , yet we do not fight with blood
&quot; The weapons of our battle are not of blood , but of power in the sight of God , that they may overcome strong fortifications .
&quot; He has taken away every conceit , every obstruction of the knowledge of God , and has taken away all the hearts of men , that they may all be obedient to Christ
&quot; And I am well prepared to punish him who disobeys when you obey well .
If a man is confident that he belongs to Christ , let him think again how he belongs to Christ , and how we belong to Christ
&quot; The Lord gave them authority to build you , and not to destroy you ; and I exalt a little for this authority , and I am not ashamed
I say this lest you think that I am writing to intimidate you
For he who says to a man , &quot; His faith is heavy and profitable , &quot; and when he meets him , he is unworthy and speaks a rude word .
&quot; When we are not in it , how will the words of the letter be , and how will we act when we meet ? &quot;
For we dare not compare ourselves with those whom we have recommended ; for it is not possible for them to measure themselves by themselves , to compare themselves to themselves .
&quot; We do not want to exaggerate beyond the bounds which God has set for us , but to build them in your midst .
And we have not exceeded our own bounds , as if they were not built up among you : for we came to you early in the gospel of Christ .
We do not exaggerate on the basis of other people &apos;s labour , but when we expect your confidence to grow , the limits that are set for us can be increased by you .
to be able to preach the gospel to a place other than yourselves , and not within the boundaries of others , by exaggeration of what he has done
But the exaggeration refers to the exaggeration of the Lord
For he that is pleasing is not his own promise , but the promise of the Lord
&quot; But let it be foolish for you to tolerate me ; for you were tolerating me
My anger for you is as God &apos;s anger , for I have promised you a husband , and I have dedicated you to Christ as a virgin virgin .
&quot; I fear that your hearts , or that which is evil , will lose the pure heart which is with Christ , just as the serpent tempted Eve with deceit .
If any man cometh and preacheth another Jesus , which is not of us , or receiveth another spirit , which is not of you , or preacheth another gospel , which is not of you , let him alone
But I thought , I am not one of the greatest apostles
&quot; For though my words are profane , yet my knowledge is not profane ; and this is what we have revealed to you in all things .
&quot; Is it a sin for me that I have humbled myself by preaching to you the gospel of God in vain , and have exalted you ?
I have lost other churches , and I have paid their wages , and I have worked for you
&quot; I was not tired of you in the time that I lacked in you ; but the brethren who came from Macedonia have filled me with what I lacked ; and I kept all things , and I will keep them , and I will not be tired of you .
&quot; There was no man in the region of Achaia who could prevent me from boasting , because the truth of Christ was in me
Why ? Because I don &apos;t love you . God knows
I have done what I have done , and I will do it again , to cut off the opportunity of those who seek it , so that they may be as we are in the things which they boast
Those are false apostles , deceiving , and pretending to be the apostles of Christ
And this is no wonder : for for for Jonathan was also made an angel of light .
Therefore his servants , if they were to be seen as servants of righteousness , would not be surprised , and their end would certainly be according to their deeds .
And I say , &quot; No man shall regard me as foolish ; but let him accept me as foolish , that I may boast a little .
&quot; I speak not according to the commandment of the Lord , but as a fool boasts
&quot; There are many who boast of their blood , and I too will boast
&quot; For you are wise , and are able to endure fools .
&quot; If any man enslaves you , or enslaves you , or enslaves you , or repents of you , or strikes your faces , you will be able to bear him
I say this to shame myself , as though we had been weak before ; and yet when men are brave in anything , I am brave too
Are they Hebrews ? Me too . Are they Israelites ? Me too . Are they descendants of Abraham ? Me too
Are they the servants of Christ , and I am more than they ; I have suffered more , I have been imprisoned more , I have been beaten more , I have been put to death more and more times
The Jews were beaten five times , forty times each , to a lesser extent
Three times hit by a stick , three times hit by a stone , three times struck by a ship , one day and one night in the deep sea
The danger of the rivers , the danger of thieves , the danger of kinsmen , the danger of foreigners , the danger of cities , the danger of the wilderness , the danger of the sea , the danger of false brethren
Labour , hardship , many times not to sleep , hunger and thirst , many times not to eat , cold , bare body
Besides that which is outside , there is also that which concerns the congregation , which is pressed upon me daily
Who is weak , and I am not weak ? Who is fallen , and I am not anxious ?
If I must boast , it is easier to boast about my weaknesses
Knoweth that I lie not , O God the Father of the ever-blessed Lord Jesus
&quot; The governor under king Aida of Damascus , who is over Damascus , will seize me
And I was cast down from the window , and in the basket from the wall of the city , and was taken from his hand
For though I boast in vain , I am unable to do so . Now I shall speak of the Lord &apos;s revelation and revelation
I recognize a man in Christ who was mentioned to the third heaven forty-four years ago , whether in himself , I do not know , or outside himself , I do not know ; only God knows .
I do not know him , whether in me or outside of me ; only God knows .
He was mentioned in paradise , and heard secret words , which no man can speak .
&quot; I exalt for this man , but I do not exalt for myself , except for my weaknesses .
For I will be truthful , and I will not exaggerate , nor be mad ; but I will not say : for I am afraid that a man will look upon me high above what he sees and hears in me
&quot; I am afraid that I am too proud for the great revelation I have received . Therefore there is a man who has pierced my body , the servant of Satan , to attack me , lest I be too proud .
&quot; For this cause I have prayed three times to the Lord that he should cut me off
And he said unto me , My grace belongeth unto thee : for my power is perfect in the weakness of men ; therefore I prefer to exalt my weakness , that the power of Christ may cover me .
For the sake of Christ I rejoiced in weakness , humiliation , affliction , oppression , and distress ; for when I waited for weakness , I was strengthened
&quot; I have become a fool , and I have been compelled by you . I should have been promised , but I have done nothing , and there is not a thing under the greatest apostles .
&quot; I am among you with a great deal of patience , and with miracles and wonders , and with powers , and with the signs of the apostles ,
What is there with you besides that which I do not tire you of , and with the other churches ? It is unjust ; forgive me
&quot; Now I intend to go to you for the third time , and I will not tire of your gates ; for what I have asked is yours , not your property ; children should not accumulate for their parents , parents should accumulate for their children
I am also willing to spend money and effort on your souls.The more I love you , the less I will love you
&quot; Behold , I myself am not weary of you , but some of you say , &apos; I am a deceitful man , and I am a prisoner of your hearts .
&quot; Have I taken advantage of those whom I have sent to you by their own hand ?
&quot; I have persuaded Titus to go to you , and sent the brother with him . Did Titus take advantage of you , and what we do is different from a spirit , and different from a footprint ?
&quot; To this day you still think that we have appealed to you , and that we have spoken in Christ before God . Beloved brothers , all things are for your sakes .
I fear that when I come again , you will see me not as I desire , and you will see me not as you desire , and I fear that there will be divisions , jealousy , anger , partisanship , slander , speech , arrogance , and confusion .
Fearing my coming , my God made me ashamed before you , and I mourned for the sins of many , and for the wickedness of many , and for the wickedness of many , and for the wickedness of many , that they would not repent ;
&quot; This is the third time that I will come to you , and I will testify by the mouth of two or three men , and every word shall be confirmed .
&quot; I said before , &apos; I will not say again with you , as I said the second time I saw you , to those who have sinned and to the rest , &apos; If I come again , I will not tolerate&apos;
&quot; Because you seek the proof that Christ speaks in me , I will not tolerate ; for Christ is not weak in you , but mighty in you .
He was crucified because of his weakness , but he is still alive because of the power of God ; so we are weak with him , but we will live with him because of the power that God has revealed to you .
Do you not know that if you are not despisable , Jesus Christ is in your hearts ?
&quot; But I hope that you will know that we are not despisable
&quot; We ask God not to do any evil to you . This is not to show that we are pleasing , but to do righteousness , that people may see that we have been rejected
&quot; We are not able to oppose the truth , but to support it
Even though we were weak , and you were strong , we rejoiced ; and what we desired was that you were perfect men .
&quot; Therefore I will not write this word to you when I am with you , that I may see you , but I will not be harsh with you according to the commandment which the Lord has given me , which was made for men , and not for the wicked .
And lastly , let your brethren rejoice , and be perfect , and be comforted , and agree with one another , and be in harmony with one another ; and the God of such kindness and peace shall be with you all the time .
Have mercy on yourselves , and keep one another holy
All the saints ask you for peace .
May the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ , the mercy of God , and the touch of the Holy Spirit be with you all
Paul the Apostle , not by man , neither by man , but by Jesus Christ , the Father who raised him from the dead
and all the brethren that are with me , writing to the churches of Galatia
Grace and peace be with you from God the Father and our Lord Jesus Christ .
Christ , according to the will of our Father God , forgave himself for our sins , to save us from this generation of sin .
But glory belongs to God , straight to ever and ever .
&quot; I wonder how quickly you have departed from the calling of yourselves by the grace of Christ , to go to another gospel .
That is not the gospel , but some have disturbed you to change the gospel of Christ
But whoever of us is an apostle from heaven , if he preaches to you the gospel other than what we preach to you , he shall be cursed
&quot; We have said , and now we say , &apos; If a man who preaches to you the gospel is different from what you receive , he shall be cursed .
Am I now to receive the heart of men , or to receive the heart of God ? Am I to be liked by men ? If I were still liked by men , I would not be a servant of Christ
&quot; Brothers , I tell you that the gospel which I preached was not of men
For I am not taken from men , nor taught by men , but from the revelation of Jesus Christ
You have heard how I have exerted great pressure on the churches that oppress God , by what I have done before in Judaism
I am also more advanced in Judaism than many of my countrymen of the same age , and more enthusiastic for the inheritance of my country
&quot; But the God who separated me from my mother &apos;s womb and called me ,
&quot; Because I was pleased to enlighten his son in my heart , and to make him known among the Gentiles , I did not bargain with the people of the blood
Neither did he go up to Jerusalem to see those who were apostles before me , except to Abraham , and then to Damascus .
And it came to pass after three years , that he went up to Jerusalem to meet Elisha , and lived with him fifteen days
&quot; I saw no other apostles besides Jacob the brother of the Lord
&quot; What I have written to you is not a lie , but I have spoken it before God .
Then I went to Syria and to the country of Gilead
At that time the churches of the Jewish faith did not see my face
&quot; But I have heard that the one who oppressed us before is now preaching the truth of what he used to do .
For my sake they are glorified before God
Fourteen years later , I went up again to Jerusalem with Barnabas , and with Titus
&quot; I have come up with the revelation , preaching to my brethren the gospel that I preached among the Gentiles , but I spoke to the wise in the background , lest I should run away now or before .
But Titus , who was with me , though he was of the Philistines , was not forced to be circumcised
For there are false brethren who have stolen the liberty of us in Christ Jesus , and secretly seek to make us slaves .
&quot; We were a moment , and there was no way to obey them , and the truth of the gospel was still among you .
As for those who are well-known , they have nothing to do with me , no matter who He is . God does not take men by appearance . Those who are well-known have nothing to add to me
On the contrary , he saw that the Lord sent me the gospel to the uncircumcised , just as Peter sent the gospel to the circumcised
That moved Peter to be an apostle to the circumcised , and also moved me to be an apostle to the Gentiles
Knowing also the grace which was given to me , Jacob , and Caiaphas , and John , the so-called pillar of the Church , performed to me and Barnabas the intercession with their right hand , and commanded us to go to the Gentiles , and to the circumcised .
It &apos;s just that we want to remember the poor . That &apos;s what I wanted to do
Then came Gilead to Antiah , and I stood up against him because of his guilt
And he that came from Jacob came not unto Edom , but ate with the strangers ; and when they came , he departed from the strangers for fear of the circumcision
And the rest of the Jews were clothed with him , and even Barnabas was clothed with him .
But when I saw that what they did was unrighteous and contrary to the truth of the gospel , I said to Jacob in the presence of all the people , &quot; If you are a Jew and act with foreigners and do not act with them , how can you force foreigners to act with them ?
&quot; The Jews of our birth are not sinners of the Gentiles .
Knowing that men are justified not by the law , but by the faith of Jesus Christ , and that we also believe in Christ Jesus , that we may be justified by the faith of Christ , and not by the law ; for none is justified by the law for those who have blood
If we seek righteousness in Christ , and yet remain sinners , is Christ the one who calls men sinners ?
What I have destroyed , if it is rebuilt , it proves that I am a criminal
I died for the law , that I might live for God
I have been crucified with Christ ten times ; and he that is alive is no longer me ; but Christ is alive in me ; and I am alive in flesh , because of the Son of God , who loves me and forgives himself for me
I will not forsake the grace of God . If righteousness is obtained by the law , Christ is dead
&quot; O you ignorant Galatians , who has deceived you again , when Jesus Christ was crucified and painted before you in life ?
If I ask you this thing , you have received the Holy Spirit , because of the law , and because of the gospel .
Have you entered in by the Holy Spirit , and are you now perfected by your flesh ? Are you so ignorant ?
Is it futile for you to receive so much ? Is it really futile ?
He has given you the Holy Spirit , and works in your midst , because of your law , and because of your faith in the gospel .
It is as if Abraham believed in God , even if it was righteous for him .
Therefore you shall know that the man who believed was the son of Abraham .
And since the Scriptures were foretold that God would cause the Gentiles to be justified by faith , He had already preached the gospel to Abraham , saying , &quot; Blessed are all the nations because of You .
Blessed is he that believeth , and Abraham that trusteth
Every one who works according to the law is cursed , for it is written , &quot; He who does not always do all that is written in the law is cursed .
It is evident that no man is justified before God by the law , for it is written , &quot; The righteous shall live by faith . &quot;
The law was not faithful , but said , &apos; He who does these things shall live accordingly .
Christ , having been cursed for us , redeemed us from the curse of the law , for it is written , &quot; Everyone hanging on a tree is cursed .
&quot; This is Abraham &apos;s blessing , that Christ Jesus may come to the Gentiles , and that we may have faith in the promised Holy Spirit
&quot; Brothers , I say to you , according to the sayings of men , &apos; While the covenant of men is established , there is none that can be abolished or increased ,
The promise was made to Abraham and to his sons . God did not speak of many children , but of one man , and that one of your sons was Christ
&quot; I say thus , that the covenant of God which he foretold cannot be abolished from the law after forty and three years , that it may be returned to the void
For if it were lawful to possess the inheritance , it would not be lawful ; but God gave the inheritance to Abraham by law
Why then is the law , which was added to the sinful , waiting for the promised sons to come , and established by the hand of the angels ,
But the uprightness is not for one &apos;s own sake ; but God is one
Is the law thus contrary to God &apos;s promise ? Absolutely not . If a law had been preached that would bring life to man , righteousness would certainly have been according to the law
But the Bible encircles all men in sin , and returns the promised blessings to those who believe in Jesus Christ
But this is for the sake of salvation , and for the sake of the future , that we may be kept under the law , and that the true way of the future may be manifested .
Thus the law is the teacher whom they have been instructed to lead us to Christ , that we may be justified by faith
&quot; But this is the salvation of faith : since it has come , we have never been in the hands of the Master
Therefore , because you believe in Christ Jesus , you are all the sons of God
&quot; Those of you who were baptized into Christ are all clothed in Christ
&quot; You are not separated from the Jews , nor from the Hebrews , nor from the free , nor from the slaves , nor from the males , nor from the females ; for you are one in Christ Jesus .
&quot; You belong to Christ , and to Abraham &apos;s seed ; and you have received your inheritance according to the promise .
&quot; I say to him who bears the inheritance , even though he is the owner of all the inheritance , that in the days of a child he is not separated from a slave
He came under the master and the master &apos;s household , as soon as his father had appointed .
That is also the case when we were children under the yoke of the secular doctrine
And when it was fulfilled , God sent His Son , born for a woman , and born according to the law ,
&quot; Let us redeem those who are under the law , that we may be divided by the name of our sons .
&quot; For you are a son , and God has sent the Spirit of his son into your hearts , calling you , Father ,
Behold , from now on thou art not a servant , but a son : and being a son , thou shalt inherit God
But before you did not know God , you served those who were not of God .
Now that ye know God , or rather are known by God , how can ye return to that cowardly and useless elementary school , and wish to serve him again ?
Remember the days , the months , the seasons , the years
I fear for you , lest I waste my time on you
&quot; Brothers , I urge you to be like me , for I am like you , and you have nothing to do with me .
You know that the first time I preached the gospel to you was because of a disease of the body
You have been tested for my body , and have not despised me , nor abhorred me ; receive me instead , as the messenger of God , as Christ Jesus
And in it is the blessing which ye exalt in that day ; and if ye could do it , and cast forth your eyes unto me , then would ye also be willing , and I would bear witness unto you .
Now that I have told you the truth , have I become your enemy ?
It is not good for those who love you to leave you , that you should love them .
&quot; When I am with you , it is not only good to treat people with enthusiasm in good deeds
&quot; My little child , I have suffered again for you , until Christ is formed in your hearts
&quot; I cannot be present with you now to change my speech , for I have troubled your hearts .
&quot; Tell me , those of you who desire to be under the law , Did you not hear the law ?
For it is written in the law that Abraham had two sons , one to give birth to a woman , and the other to an independent woman
But he who gives birth to a woman is born by blood , and he who gives birth to a woman of her own accord is born by promise .
&quot; These are the likeness of the two women , two covenants , one from Mount Sinai , and the other from Shechem , who bore sons as slaves .
&quot; The name of Mount Sinai in this summer is like the name of Jerusalem , which is present in the land of Abraham , for Jerusalem and her children were enslaved
&quot; But Jerusalem above is independent , and she is our mother
For it is written in the Scriptures , &apos; You who are not pregnant and who are not brought forth shall rejoice ; and you who have not had trouble in giving birth , you shall sing with a loud voice , for there are more children than there are children without a husband .
&quot; Brothers , we are sons and daughters according to our oaths , just as Esau was
He who was born by blood and by spirit was compelled , and he who was born by the Holy Spirit is compelled , and so it is now
But what does the Scripture say ? It says , &quot; Drive out the prophet and his son , for the son of the prophet cannot bear the inheritance with the son of the free woman .
&quot; Brothers , it seems to me that we are not daughters of a woman , but daughters of a woman who is free .
Christ has delivered us , that we may be free , so that we may stand firm , and be no more bound by the yoke of slaves
&quot; I Paul tell you , Christ is of no use to you if you are circumcised
I also refer to that which is true of every circumcised , that he is a debtor of the law .
&quot; You who are justified by the law are separated from Christ , and have fallen from grace
By the Holy Spirit , by faith , we await the righteousness which we await
Blessed is he who was not baptized in Christ Jesus ; but faith in the love of life is effective
&quot; You used to run well . Who would stop you from obeying the truth ?
&quot; This counsel is not from your calling ,
A batch of yeast can make the whole mix up
&quot; I have confidence in the Lord that you will not have a different heart ; but whoever troubles you will bear his sins .
&quot; Brothers , if I continue to be circumcised , why am I being oppressed ? If so , the place where the cross is hated will be gone .
&quot; Do not despise those who stir up yourselves , and cut themselves off .
Brothers , you are called to liberty , but do not treat your liberty as an opportunity to indulge your desires , but always obey one another with love
For all the law is enclosed in the words of the love of one &apos;s own self
Be careful , and if you bite and swallow one another , be afraid of destroying one another .
&quot; I said , &apos; If you walk in the Spirit , you will not let the desire of the flesh go away .
For the Spirit and the desire are at odds , and the Spirit and the desire are at odds , so that you are not able to do what you will .
&quot; But if you are guided by the Spirit , you are not under the law .
All things of desire are evident , as adultery , filth , and wickedness
worship idols , evil deeds , hatred , strife , hatred , anger , partition , strife , discord
Jealousy , and drunkenness , and ravening , and the like ; I have told you before , and now I tell you again , that those who do such things will not be able to bear God
The fruit of the Holy Spirit is love , joy , peace , patience , mercy , goodness , faithfulness
There is no law forbidding such things
All who belong to Christ Jesus have been crucified by the flesh , and by the lusts of the flesh .
If we are born by the Spirit , then act by the Spirit
Don &apos;t be greedy of false names , angry of one another , jealous of one another
Brothers , if a man is overcome by chance , and you are of the Spirit , save him with a gentle heart , and be careful , lest he be tempted .
The burden of each one of you shall be on the other , and the law of Christ shall be perfected .
If a man has nothing , he is deceiving himself to have it
Let every man examine his own conduct , and that which he extols belongs to himself , and not to others .
For each man shall bear his own burden .
A man who is taught in the truth , and who supplies all that is needed
Do not deceive yourself , for God cannot be weak . What is the race , and what is the harvest ?
He that sows according to his will shall be taken away from his will , and he that sows according to the Spirit shall be taken away from the Spirit for evermore .
We do good and do not lose heart . If we do not despair , then when the time is come , we will receive it .
Therefore there is an opportunity to do good to all , and more so to a family of believers
Please see how great are the words which I have written to you by hand
&quot; All those who look like hypocrites are forcing you to be circumcised , for fear of being forcibly crucified for Christ .
Those who are circumcised do not keep the law , neither do they themselves ; they are willing to be circumcised of you , nor to exaggerate by your flesh .
But I reject no other exaggeration , but the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ : for it is for me that the world is crucified ; and it is for the world that I am crucified
Be baptized Be not baptized , it is not important , it is important to be a new man
May peace and mercy be upon them and upon the children of Israel of God
&quot; From now on no one will disturb me , for I have the seal of Jesus on me .
Brothers , may the grace of my Lord Jesus Christ be always in your hearts .
Paul , an apostle of Christ Jesus according to the will of God , wrote to the saints of Ephesus , who were faithful in Christ Jesus
Grace and peace be with you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ .
Blessed be the Father God of our Lord Jesus Christ , who in Christ has blessed all the spirits in our heavens
As God has chosen us in Christ from the foundation of the world , that we may be holy before Him without blemish
And because they loved us , they prepared us according to their own will , and divided us in the name of the Son by Jesus Christ .
to praise the grace of His glory , which He has given to us in the Son of love
&quot; We are redeemed by the blood of this beloved Son , and forgiveness is given to the transgressors by the grace of his abundance .
&quot; This is the grace which God has bestowed upon us with all wisdom and wisdom
&quot; All these are the good things which He has prepared for us , that we may know the secrets of His will .
to make all things in the heavens and on the earth one in Christ , according to the arrangement , at the fulfillment of the appointed time
&quot; In him we also have obtained the foundation . This is the One who does all things according to His will , as He has ordained .
The glory of him is praiseworthy from us , who are the first to hope in Christ .
You have heard the word of the truth , the gospel of salvation , and have believed in Christ ; and having believed in him , you have received the seal of the promised Spirit .
&quot; The Holy Spirit is the foundation of our inheritance , until the people of God are redeemed , that His glory may be glorified .
Therefore I have heard that you believe in the Lord Jesus , the beloved saints
For the grace of God that is not in your dwelling , and the time of prayer , is often called upon you .
Blessed be the God of our Lord Jesus Christ , the Father of glory , who rewards you with the Spirit of wisdom and revelation , that you may know Him
And lightened the eyes of your hearts , that you might know the hope of His calling , and the foundation of His glory among the saints ,
And know the greatness of the power which he revealed to those who believed in us
It was the great power which worked on him in Christ , that brought him to life from the dead , that he should sit on his right hand in heaven
He is far above all the ruling , the ruling , the mighty , the ruling , and all that are known ; but he is far above this world , and he is far above this world .
And all things will be obedient under his feet , and he will be the head of all things for the church
The church is his body , full of all things
&quot; You died in the midst of evil , and He brought you to life
&quot; In those days you were acting in them as leaders of the people , following the customs of this world , and obeying the rulers of the heavens . They are the evil spirits that are running in the hearts of the rebellious .
&quot; We have been in the midst of them before , suppressing the selfish desires of the flesh , and acting according to the flesh and the heart &apos;s desires , being children of anger , like other people .
But God has abundant mercy , because He loves us with great love
When we die in sin , we are called to live with Christ . It is gracious for you to save
He also raised us up together with Christ Jesus , and sat down together in heaven
to show to the later generations the riches of his grace , which he has bestowed on us in Christ Jesus
&quot; You shall be saved by grace and by faith . This is not from yourselves , but from God .
And not out of deeds , lest a man should boast
We were his work , which he made in Christ Jesus , that he might do good to us , which God had prepared for us
&quot; Therefore you should remember that you were an alien by flesh , and were called uncircumcised by those who were called circumcised by the hand of men by flesh .
&quot; In those days you were not related to Christ , but were aliens from the people of Israel in the promised covenants , and had no hope in the world , and no God
&quot; You who were far from God have come near in the blood of Christ Jesus ,
For he hath made us to be in harmony , and hath joined the two together to be one , and hath destroyed the wall that was between them .
And with his own flesh he blots out the iniquity , which is written in the law : that peace may be made , that he may take two sons , and make a new one out of himself .
&quot; He destroyed the iniquity on the cross , and with the cross he made the two seeds one , in harmony with God
and to preach the gospel of peace to those far off , and to those near
For both of us were able to enter into the Father through him by the touch of a Holy Spirit
&quot; Therefore you shall no longer be foreigners and travellers , but in the land of the saints , and in the house of God .
And on the foundation of the apostles and prophets was built Christ Jesus himself as a cornerstone of the house
And the houses were joined together by him , and they became the principal temples
And you have been built with him to dwell for God , borrowing the Spirit
&quot; Therefore I Paul pray for you , for your foreigners , as Christ Jesus was imprisoned
&quot; Forgive me , for you have heard God &apos;s grace upon me , and your duties will be entrusted to me
The mystery of the gospel is revealed to me by revelation , as I have written a little before
If you remember , you will know that I know the mystery of Christ .
For this mystery was not known in the ancients , as it is now in the saints and the prophets , who have been inspired by the Holy Spirit
This mystery is that the Gentiles , in Christ Jesus , through the gospel , are heirs , one body , and promised
I have been the minister of the gospel , according to the grace of God , which is given to me according to the great power which he exercises .
I was the least of the saints , and yet he gave me this grace , that I might pass on the inexhaustible riches of Christ to the Gentiles
and that they might know how the mystery of the God of creation , which is hidden throughout all generations , is arranged
For he who owes the church to rule over the heavens , and holds the throne , knoweth all the wisdom of God
This is the will of God , which was ordained in our Lord Jesus Christ from the beginning of the world
because we believed in Jesus , we came to God without fear in him , and without doubt in our faith
Therefore I ask you not to despair of the affliction which I have suffered for you , for that is your glory .
Therefore , I kneeled before my father
All the houses of the heavens and the earth are named after Him
Let him strengthen your hearts by the glory of his abundance , and by his Spirit ;
That Christ may dwell in your hearts because of your faith , and that your love may have roots
How wide and how deep is the love of Christ , that we may know it together with the saints
Knowing that this love is too great for man to measure , God fills you with all his fullness
And God did according to the power of our heart , and according to the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfilment of the fulfil
May he be glorified in the church , and in Christ Jesus , to the generations of the world , for ever and ever .
&quot; Behold , I , the Lord of the captives , exhort you , that when you are called , you should be commended for what you do for man .
Be humble , gentle , patient , and tolerant of one another with love
To communicate with one another in peace , and to work hard to keep the hearts united by the Holy Spirit
There is only one body , and only one Holy Spirit , and one hope , as you are called
One Lord , One Letter , One Wash
&quot; The One God , the Father of all , is above all , throughout all , and dwells in all
For all of us have been blessed , according to the measure of Christ
Therefore it is written , &quot; In the days of the high heavens he took away his enemies , and gave them all kinds of grace .
&quot; Have you not said , &apos; Go up , &apos; or &apos; Get down first underground ? &apos;
And that which descendeth is a far rise above the heavens , full of all things .
He has given to him apostles , prophets , evangelizers , priests and teachers .
To be all-holy , to do all their duties , and to establish the body of Christ
until all of us are joined together in the way of truth , knowing the Son of God , that we may grow to become mature , full of the measure of Christ
&quot; We shall no longer be little children , and we shall not be deceived by the deceit of men , nor by the deceitful deeds of the wicked ; but we shall be shaken by the winds of all the apostles , and we shall follow the winds of all the apostles .
Only with love speak the truth , that all things may prosper , and be joined to the Father Christ
The whole body is bound together by him , and the hundred sections according to their duties , according to the functions of the bodies , and they help one another , and the body grows and establishes itself in love .
&quot; Therefore I say , and it is true in the Lord , &apos; Do not act like the hypocritical hearts of the Gentiles ,
Their hearts are blind , and they are separated from the life which God has given them , because of their ignorance , and their hearts are stiff
Now that the conscience is exhausted , let go of selfish desires and corruption of all kinds
You have learned Christ , but not this way
If you have listened to his ways , and received his teachings , and learned his truths ,
Take away the old man from whom you have gone forth , and he shall become evil by the lusts of his own lusts .
And change your minds for a new one
and put on the new man , who is made in the image of God , and is righteous and holy in truth
&quot; Therefore give up lying , and tell the truth to your neighbors , for we are one another &apos;s bodies .
But life will not sin , nor will anger reach the sun .
Neither can the devil be left alone
&quot; Those who have stolen before shall not steal again ; but labour and righteousness shall be enough to give to those who lack it .
An unclean word cannot be uttered ; but it is good for a man to speak according to his doings , that he may hear .
Do not be afraid of the Holy Spirit of God , for the days of redemption have come , when you were sealed by Him .
Remove from among you all wickedness , and all bitterness , and all anger , and all wrath , and all slander , and all malice ,
Forgive one another with a merciful heart , just as God forgave you in Christ
Therefore obey God as merciful children
Act in love , just as Christ loved us , and gave himself for us as a sweet offering and a sacrifice to God
&quot; There is no question of obscenity , or of all filth , or of greed among you , in the body of the saints .
&quot; It is not good to say obscene words , deceitful words , and laughter , but to say thanksgiving words .
For indeed you know that in the land of Christ and God there is no distinction between obscene and profane and greedy , and those who are greedy are like idolaters .
Do not be deceived by falsehoods ; for these things the wrath of God will come upon the rebellious son .
So you don &apos;t want to be with them
&quot; You used to be dark , but now you are light in the Lord , and you act for man as children of light
The fruit of the light is all goodness , righteousness , and truth .
Always examine what is most pleasurable
