&quot; The Lord will deliver me from all evil , and will deliver me into His kingdom of heaven . May I return to Him , straight to ever and ever .
Ask of Baekhira , and of Ahira , and of the house of Anakim ,
And Elah dwelled in Corinth ; and when Trophim was sick , I left him in Millo
&quot; Come quickly to me before the winter ; for the friends of Bro , and of Budan , and of Livon , and of Gerodia , and of all the brethren , have asked you to be safe .
May the Lord be with your Spirit , and may mercy always be with you
Paul , the servant of God , the apostle of Jesus Christ , by the faith of God &apos;s chosen people , and by the knowledge of the pious truth
Hope in the God without lying , in the eternal life promised for ever and ever
By the time of the coming of the day , I have made his doctrine manifest through the time of preaching , which I am entrusted with by the commandment of God , our Savior .
&quot; I am writing to Titus , who is my true son according to our common faith : Grace and peace be to you from God our Father and Christ Jesus our Savior .
&quot; I have left you in Gilead , that you may do all that has not been done , and set up elders in the cities , as I have commanded you
And if there be a man who is blameless , and is the husband of only one woman , and his children are believers , and no man tells them that they are rebellious and disobedient , then it shall be established
Supervision is God &apos;s guardian ; it must be blameless , intransigent , not impatient , not drunken , not beaten , not corrupted
Pleasure to receive the distant , good , noble , fair , holy , self-reliant
He who holds fast to the truth that he teaches can persuade men to the truth , and he who disputes can defeat them .
For there are many who do not obey the commandment , and speak vain words , and deceive men ; even so are those who are circumcised .
The mouths of these men shall be shut , and they shall defeat the houses of the wicked , because of their corruption , and because of their unrighteousness .
One of the local prophets of Gilead said , &quot; The people of the land of Gilead often lie ; they are evil beasts , greedy and lazy .
&quot; This testimony is true ; therefore reproach them with severity , that they may be perfect in the way of truth .
&quot; Do not obey the words of the Jews , nor the commandments of those who deny the truth
Everything is clean in a clean man , and nothing is clean in a unbeliever who defiles . Even the heart and the heavens are defiled .
They say that they know God , and act against Him . This is abomination , and rebellion , and vanishable in all good deeds .
But what you say is always in accord with the truth .
Encourage the elderly to be discreet , noble , self-defensive , faithful , loving , and patient
and admonish the elderly women to act with respect , not to say words , not to give wine as a slave , and to teach by good doctrine
To teach young women , to love husbands , to love children
to be obedient , to be chaste , to do household chores , to be kind to others , to obey their husbands , and not to be deceived by the wisdom of God
And he urged the young men to keep their duty
Show yourselves the example of good deeds in all things , and be upright and noble in your teachings
&quot; The words are pure and blameless , and the opponents are ashamed , because there is no place to say what is not ours .
Persuade the servant to obey his master , and to love all things ; and do not overtake him .
&quot; You shall not take anything privately , but be faithful , that the way of God our Savior may be glorified in all things
For the grace of God for the salvation of all has been manifested
&quot; Learn us to keep ourselves safe in this world , to be righteous , and to observe the day of piety , apart from ungodly hearts and secular desires
Waiting for the blessing which we hope for , and for the great God , and for the glory of our Savior Jesus Christ to be manifested
&quot; For he has forgiven himself for us , to redeem us from all sin , and to purify us , and to be a son of his own , with a zeal for good .
These things thou shalt declare , and warn , and reproach with all authority ; and thou shalt not be taken lightly .
Wake up all the people , that they may obey the rulers , and the rulers , and follow his commandments , and prepare for every good thing
Don &apos;t slander , don &apos;t fight , always have peace , and be gentle to all people
We have been ignorant , rebellious , perplexed , obedient to all kinds of lusts and feasts , and possessed a heart of jealousy , hateful , and hating one another .
&quot; But it shall come to pass , when the mercy of God , our Savior , and the mercy which He hath shown unto man shall be manifested
He saved us , not by the righteousness of our own works , but by His mercy , by the renewal of the baptism and the renewal of the Holy Spirit .
The Holy Spirit , through Jesus Christ , our Savior , poured out upon us abundantly
That we may be called righteous because of His grace , and be heirs in the hope of everlasting life
&quot; This is a faithful saying , and I hope that you will make it clear in truth , that those who have believed in God may keep to the right path , which is good and beneficial to man .
Avoid foolish arguments , and the empty talk of the family , and divisions , and disputes arising out of the law ; for this is nothing but vanity .
And he that hath divided his gates and joined himself to a party shall forsake him once or twice
Knowing that they have transgressed and committed sins , knowing that they do not or do not
&quot; When I send you to Athens or to Tucque , you shall hurry to see me at Nicopolis , where I have made a plan to spend the winter .
Hurry and send the lawyers Sinai and Apollo , that they may have no shortage
and that our people may learn to do righteousness , and that they may prepare what is necessary , and that they may not bear fruit .
Have mercy on those who are with me , and on those who love us in faith . May mercy always be with you all .
Paul , the prisoner of Christ Jesus , and Timothy our brother , wrote to Philip , our beloved fellow worker
and Abijah our sister , and Ahab our soldier , and the church in your house ,
Grace and peace be with you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ .
&quot; When I pray to You , I always thank my God for You
For the love you have heard , and for the faith you have in the Lord Jesus and the saints
May your faith , which you share with men , be effective , and let men know that all your good works are for Christ
&quot; Brothers , I am greatly happy and comforted by your love , for the heart of the saints is refreshed from you
Even though I have the courage to command you according to the righteousness of Christ
&quot; However , Paul , who is as old as I am , who is now imprisoned for Christ Jesus , would rather seek you with love
I pray to you , for the name of the goodness , for the mother of Anice , my son , who was born in the bonds .
&quot; He was not profitable to you before , but now I am profitable to you
I now send him back to you in person . He is in my heart
&quot; I have purposed to leave him to serve you in the bonds of my gospel .
&quot; But if I do not know what you mean , I will not do it , that your good deeds may not be done by force , but by grace .
He will leave you temporarily , or you will always need him
For he is no longer a slave , but a higher than a slave , a beloved brother , in whom I am , and in whom you are , not by the flesh , but by the Lord
&quot; If you take me as your companion , receive him as you receive me .
&quot; If he loses to you or owes anything to you , it will be in my account
&quot; I will repay you , &quot; wrote Paul in writing , &quot; and I will not say to you that you are also a debtor to me
Brothers , I hope that you will make me happy in the Lord because of you , and that you will make my heart glad in Christ
&quot; I have written to you , and I am convinced that you will obey , that you will know what you are going to do , and that you will live up to what I have said
&quot; And you will also prepare for me a dwelling place , for I hope that by your prayers you will be blessed .
Blessed be Epaph , who is with me in prison for Christ Jesus
And Mark , and Aristarchus , and Demas , and Luke , who were with me , said unto thee , Peace be upon thee
May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be always in your heart .
God has spoken to his ancestors many times and in many ways , in the days of old
&quot; And in this last life He communicated to us through His Son , and He made Him to bear all things , and He created the worlds .
He is the glory of the glory of God , and the true image of God &apos;s body ; He keeps all things by His commandments , by His power ; He has cleansed the sins of men ; He sits on the right hand of the great and high .
The name which he has received is more precious than the name of the angel , and far above the angel
And God , the angel of all , said unto him , Thou art my son , and I have born thee this day ; and he said unto him , I will be his father , and he will be my son .
And again , when God brings the firstborn into the world , or when He brings the secondborn into the world , He says , &apos; To Him shall all the messengers of God be called .
And concerning the apostles , he said , &quot; God is an apostle by the wind , and a servant by the fire .
And he said unto the son , O God , thy throne is ever and ever far off , and thy kingdom is upright .
You love righteousness , and hate evil . Therefore God , your God , anoints you with joy , above your companions .
He said , &quot; Lord , you have laid the foundation of the earth , and the heavens have been created by your hand .
&quot; The heavens will perish , and you will live forever ; and the heavens will be as a garment that grows old
You will roll up the heavens like a garment , and the heavens will be changed ; but you will not change , and your years will not be exhausted .
And God , the angel of all , said unto that one , Sit thou on my right hand , and I will make thy enemy thy bench .
Are not angels ministering spirits , sent forth to minister to those who are to be saved ?
Therefore , when we exalt the truth that we have heard , we are afraid that we will be lost
&quot; The word of the angel is confirmed , and every one who does evil receives the recompense that he deserves .
How can we escape from sin if we neglect such a great salvation , which the Lord first spoke to us , and then confirmed to us by those who heard
God also bears witness with them by His will , by miracles and signs and by hundreds of powers and by the grace of the Holy Spirit
&quot; The world of the future , which we have said , was not given to angels
But it is written in the Scriptures , &quot; What is man , that thou carest for him , and what is the world , that thou carest for him
&quot; You shall make him a little less than an angel , and you shall give him glory and crowns of honour , and you shall give him control over all that your hands have created .
Let all things be subdued under his feet.If all things were subdued , there would be none to be subdued ; but now we have not seen all things subdued
&quot; Only he who is a little less than an angel sees Jesus , who is crowned with glory for the suffering of death , that by the grace of God he may taste death for man for man .
&quot; It is fitting that he who belongs to all things , who belongs to all things , should let many sons go to glory , to be their captain-in-in-chief , to be perfected in his sufferings .
He called them brethren , neither was he ashamed of them , because those who were sanctified were one and the same .
&quot; I will pass on your name to my brethren , and I will praise you in the congregation .
And said , I will rely on him . And said , Behold , I have given my children with God .
The Son of man is a flesh , and the Son of man is a flesh ; and the devil is the one who corrupts the power of death by means of death .
and to release those who have been enslaved for their lives for fear of death
He saved not the angels , but the seed of Abraham
Therefore he should be the same in all things as his brethren , that he might be a great priest of mercy and faith in the things of God , and redeem the sins of the people .
He himself , having suffered in trial , is able to save the tested
O you holy brethren , who are called by God , think of Jesus , whom we consider to be the Apostle , the high priest
He was faithful to the one who set him up , as Moses was faithful to the whole house of God
He is more glorious than Moses , and more honourable than the house that builds it
For every house shall be built by men ; but God is the builder of all things .
Moses was a servant , faithful in all the house of God , to prove the things that will be told in the future
But Christ is the Son , the house of God ; and if we endure to the end with exaltable hope and courage , it is his house .
The Holy Spirit said , &quot; If you listen to him today ,
How can he not be hardened , as he was in the wilderness , when he provoked him to anger , and tried him ?
&quot; Your ancestors have tried me there for forty years , and they have seen my deeds .
&quot; Therefore I am ashamed of those of that generation , saying , &apos; They are often confused in their hearts , and do not know what I am doing .
And I swore in anger , saying , They will not enter into my rest .
&quot; Brothers , be careful that you do not turn away from the eternal God from the wickedness of those who do not believe among you .
Let every one of you , while this day is still here , persuade one another every day , lest one of you be troubled by sin and become hardened in his heart
If we have faith from the beginning , and persevere to the end , then we are divided in Christ
It is written , &quot; If you listen to his words today , you will not be hardhearted , as in the days that provoke him to anger .
Then who , when he heard his words , provoked him to anger , was not he that followed Moses out of Egypt ?
&quot; Who is ashamed of God for forty years ? Are not the dead bodies of sinners in the wilderness ?
And to whom doth he swear that he will not allow them to enter into His rest ? Is it not to the faithless ?
It seemed that they could not enter into rest because of their disbelief .
&quot; When we have received the promise that we will enter into His rest , we fear that we will not be caught among us , or that some people will seem to escape us .
For the gospel is preached unto us , as it is to them : but the way which they hear is not profitable unto them , because they have no faith in the soundness of the way which they hear .
But those of us who have believed are able to enter that rest , just as God said , &quot; I have sworn in my anger that they will not enter my rest . &quot; His works have been perfected since the creation .
As for the seventh day , it is said , &quot; On the seventh day God shall rest all his work .
There is another saying : &apos; They refuse to enter my rest .
&quot; There is one who will enter into rest , and he who has heard the gospel before will not enter because he has not believed .
Then , after many years , in the book of David , he appointed a day , as it is said above , &quot; If you listen to his words today , you will not be hard of heart .
&quot; If Joshua had given them rest , God would not have another day
In this way there will be another day of rest for the children of God .
For he who enters into rest rest rests from his own work , as God rests from his own work .
&quot; Therefore we shall strive hard to enter into that rest , lest a man fall into the way of disobedience .
The way of God is vigorous and effective , faster than the sword of every two blades ; even the soul and the spirit , bones and marrow , can penetrate and cut apart , and discern thoughts and thoughts in the heart .
And there is not a thing that is not manifest before Him , which was made : for all things are open before the Lord , who is with us .
Since we have a great priest , Jesus , the Son of God , who has been raised up in the high places of glory , we have established the way that we have recognized
For the high priest of ours is not unable to bear our weaknesses ; he has been tested in all things , just as we are ; but he has not sinned .
&quot; Therefore we shall come unto the throne of grace without fear , to receive mercy and grace at all times .
&quot; The high priest who is chosen from among men is appointed to do the work of God for a gift and for a sin offering .
He is able to forgive the foolish and the lost , for he himself is weakened .
Therefore he is justified in offering a sacrifice for the people and for himself
The glory of this great priest was not taken for himself , but to be called by God , as Aaron was
Thus Christ is not the one who takes glory for himself as a great priest , but the one who says to him , Thou art my son , and I have born thee this day
As it is said in the Scriptures , &quot; You are the priest forever after Machiavelli .
When Christ was in the flesh , when he cried with a loud voice , and wept , and prayed for the Lord who would save him from death , he was justified by his piety
Though he was a son , yet he learned obedience by the sufferings he had suffered
He was perfected , and became a source of salvation for all who obeyed him for ever and ever .
And he called him a great priest , according to the number of the times of Machiavelli
Concerning Machiavelli , we have some good words , which are difficult to explain , because you do not listen in
&quot; Behold , you are masters in what you learn ! Who knows if someone will teach you from the beginning of the elementary school of the Holy Word and become a man who must eat milk and cannot eat dry bread ?
He who can only eat milk has no knowledge of righteousness , for he is a child .
Only those who grow up are able to eat the dried food , and their hearts are well-trained , and they are able to discern good and evil .
Therefore let us depart from the beginning of the doctrine of Christ , and work hard to the full ; and let us not be rooted again , as in repentance of death , and in faith in God
The various baptisms , the handshake , the resurrection of the dead , and the eternal judgment
&quot; If God permits us , we will do so
For those who have received the light , and have tasted the grace of God , have a share in the Holy Spirit
and have tasted the goodness of God , and have come to know the power of the world
But if they turn away from the truth , they will not be able to repent again , for they have crucified the Son of God , and they have clearly humiliated him .
Blessed is he that eateth the rain of many times , and groweth the fruit of the field , which is worthy of cultivation ;
&quot; If the thorns and the rhizomes grow long , they will be abolished . They will be near to the curse , and the end will be the burning .
Beloved brethren , although we say this , I am convinced that your deeds are more powerful and near to salvation
For God is not unrighteous , but forgets your works , and the love which you have shown for His name , which you used to serve the saints , and which you now serve .
May all of you show such diligence , that your hopes may be fulfilled forever and ever
And do not lay low , but do the will of those who endure the promises with faith and patience .
&quot; In the beginning , when God swore to Abraham , he swore to himself , because there was no one greater than himself ,
&quot; For blessing , I will give you great blessing ; and for children , I will multiply your children .
Thus Abraham endured and received what he had been promised
Every man swears greater than himself , and disputes all manner of things on the basis of his oath .
In this way God wills to bear witness to the promised one , and He has made His will unchanged .
God will never lie by these two things , which remain unchanged , that we may be greatly encouraged in our escape to the sanctuary , and in those whom he has set before us .
&quot; We have hope as an anchor of the Spirit , firm and firm and firm , and entered into the mantle
Jesus , who was a pioneer , and was a great priest for ever , like the likeness of Machiavelli , entered into the mantle for us
&quot; The priest of the most high God , King Zechariah , who was a long-term priest , greeted him , and blessed him , when he came back to destroy the kings .
And Abraham took one tenth of that which he had received , and the first name of him was translated , The king of righteousness , and the name of him was changed , The king of Samaria , the king of peace .
He has no father , no mother , no genealogy , no beginning of life , no end of life ; He is like the Son of God
&quot; What is this man worthy of , O Abraham the father of Israel , who took one tenth of all that he had taken captive ?
And the sons of Levi , who were appointed priests , commanded the people to take one tenth of the ordinance ; and the people were their brothers , even though they were born in Abraham &apos;s body , but they took one tenth of the ordinance
And it came to pass , that only Machiavelli , who was not with them in the book , took one tenth of Abraham , and blessed Abraham , who had been promised .
Blessed are those who give to those who give to those who give to those who give to those who give
&quot; Whoever receives here a tenth of it will die ; but whoever receives there a tenth of it will bear witness that he is alive .
And Levi , who received one tenth , also borrowed one tenth from Abraham
For at the time of his coming to Abraham , Levi was in the body of his fathers .
&quot; If the people had been under the law as priests in the Levites , and had been perfected by this office , why should another priest be appointed after the order of Machiavelli , and not after the order of Aaron ?
The priest &apos;s office has been changed , and the law must be changed
For there was not a man of the other tribes of the people to whom these words were spoken , to serve at the altar
&quot; Our Lord has revealed that he came out of Judah , but this tribe , Moses , was not called a priest
&quot; If another priest were to be raised in the likeness of Machiavelli , then my words would be more evident
He became a priest , not according to the ordinance of the flesh , but according to the great power of the infinite life
For those who testified to him said , &quot; You are a priest forever , as Machiavelli .
The previous regulations were repealed because they were weak and ineffective
And he brought forth a better hope , that we might come into the presence of God by it
Again , Jesus is a priest , and he has not sworn
As for the priests , who had not sworn , but Jesus sworn , because those who had sworn to him said to him , &quot; The Lord has sworn , and repent , and you will be priests forever . &quot;
As he had sworn , Jesus was the guardian of a better covenant
The number of those who became priests was exceedingly great , because death was inexhaustible
&quot; This man , who lives forever and ever , his priestly office will not be changed for ever
He saves all who come to God by him ; for he lives long and prays for them .
Thus is the great priest holy , without evil , without defilement , far from sinners , exalted above all the heavens , acceptable to us
&quot; He will not be like the great priests , who sacrifice for his own sins every day , and for the sins of the people ; for he has accomplished it only once .
The Law made the weak to be high priests ; but the word which I swore after the Law made the Son high priests , and it was fulfilled for ever .
And the first of the things which we speak concerns , that we have such a great priest , who has sat on the right hand of the great one in heaven
in the sanctuary , in the true tent , which is supported by the Lord , and not by man ;
All the high priests are appointed for the offerings and the offerings ; therefore the high priest must also offer something
&quot; If he is on the earth , he shall not be a priest , because he is a priest who has offered according to the law
The things that they serve are the forms and images of the things that are in heaven , just as Moses , when he was to build the tabernacle , warned him , saying , &quot; Be careful , and make all things according to the pattern that is shown to you in the mountains .
Now the office which Jesus received is more beautiful , just as he was the keeper of the better covenant , which was made by virtue of the better promise
&quot; If there is no defect in the former covenant , there is no place to seek after it
Therefore the Lord said to his people , &quot; The days are coming , and I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with all Judah
&quot; It is not like the covenant I made with their fathers when I drew them out of Egypt , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; because they kept not my covenant , neither did I obey them . &quot;
&quot; This is the covenant I made with the house of Israel in those days , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that I will put my law in their hearts , and write it in their hearts , and that I will be their God , and they will be my children .
They do not teach their neighbours and their brethren by themselves , saying , &quot; You should know the Lord ; for they will know Me from the least to the greatest . &quot;
I will forgive their iniquity , and remember no more their sins .
A new covenant is spoken , and it is about old ; but the old and the decreasing shall be brought to nothing
The former covenant contained the ordinance of worship , and the tabernacle of the world
For there is a tent prepared , and the first floor is called a sanctuary , and there are lampstands , tables , and tables , and tables for bread
And after the second mantle there was another layer of the tabernacle called to the sanctuary .
And there was a furnace of gold , and an ark of gold wrapped , and a pot of gold with which to store it , and a staff for Aaron to bear buds , and two tablets of the covenant .
There was a shadow of glory over the ark of the Lord &apos;s Seat . I can &apos;t elaborate on all these things now
And the priests went into the first tent of the tabernacle for the service of God , as these things were prepared
As for the second layer of the tent , only the high priest went in alone year after year , without blood , to offer it for his own sin and for the sin of the people
The way to the sanctuary has not yet been revealed while the first tabernacle remains
&quot; The first layer of the tabernacle is a model of what is now , that the gifts and the offerings which are offered are not perfect for those who worship by their conscience .
These things , including the diet and the manner of washing , are no more than the ordinance of the flesh , appointed for the time of revival
But now Christ has come , and is the great priest of the good things of the future , through the greater and greater tent , which is not made by man , nor belongs to the world .
And he entered into the sanctuary only once , not with the blood of a sheep or a calf , but with his own blood ; and it was an everlasting redemption
&quot; If the blood of the goats and the bulls , and the ashes of the lambs and the calves , is poured on the unclean person , he is sanctified and purified
Would not Christ , by the Spirit of everlasting life , give himself without blemish to God ? Would not his blood cleanse your hearts from your dead works , that you might serve the eternal God ?
And for this purpose he made a mediator in the new covenant , that , having been redeemed by death for the sins of men that were committed in the former covenant , he might give to the anointed the promised inheritance for ever .
&quot; Whoever has a will must wait until the man who leaves his will is dead .
For it is the will of the dead that is effective ; and if the will of the dead is still , will it be of any use ?
Therefore the former covenant is not without blood
&quot; Then he took red wool and oxen &apos;s knees , and sprinked the blood and water of the calves and the goats on the book , and sprinked it on all the people , because it was lawful for Moses to preach every commandment to all the people on that day ,
This blood is the testimony of the covenant of God with you .
And he sprinkled blood likewise upon the tabernacle and upon all the vessels
Almost everything is purified by blood according to the law ; and if there is no bleeding , sin shall not be forgiven
They must be used for the purification of the things that are made according to the pattern of the heavens ; but the things of that day are naturally purified by the better things .
For he has not entered into the sanctuary of the hands of men for Christ , but into heaven , which is now before God for us
Neither did he offer himself many times , as the great priest entered into the sanctuary every year with the blood of a sheep and a goat , which was not his own blood
If that were the case , he would have suffered many times since the beginning of the world ; but now , in this last world , he is revealed , offering himself as a sacrifice for the redemption of sin .
According to a decree , every soul has one death , after death , and a trial
Thus Christ , having been offered once , and bearing the sins of many , will appear to those who wait for him a second time , and not in sin , but for their salvation
For the law is the shadow of the good things of the future , and not the true image of the real things ; and it is not able to borrow an offering every year , that the former man may be perfected .
Had it not been for this , the sacrifices would have ceased beforehand , and the conscience of those who worship would not have been cleansed from sin .
But these sacrifices remind men of sin every year
For the blood of cattle and sheep it is not for atonement .
So when Christ came into the world , he said , &quot; God , you have prepared me a body for sacrifices and gifts which you do not want
&quot; You will not rejoice in the burnt offering and the sin offering .
Then I said , &quot; I have come , O God , to do your will ; and my affairs are written in the book . &quot;
&quot; The sacrifices and the gifts , the burnt offerings and the sin offerings , which you do not want , and which you do not rejoice in , are all according to the law
Then he said , &quot; I have come to do your will . Behold , he is the first to be removed , and the second to be established .
&quot; For by this will , and by Jesus Christ , we were sanctified only once , when we offered up his body
Every priest stands every day in the service of God , and offers an offering many times , which will never be able to absolve sin .
But when Christ had offered a perpetual sin offering , he sat down on the right hand of God
From this he waited for his enemy to become his bench
For he hath offered a sacrifice , that he that is sanctified may be perfect for ever .
The Holy Spirit also bears witness to us , because he has already said
&quot; This is the covenant I made with them after those days , &quot; says the Lord , &quot; that I will write my law in their hearts and put it in their hearts .
Then he said , &apos; I will no longer remember their sins and their transgressions .
These sins have been forgiven , and there is no need to offer any more sacrifices for them
Brothers , we have entered into the sanctuary openly because of the blood of Jesus
He has lent us a new and living way through the mantle , which is his body .
And another great priest ruled the house of God
And when the good deeds of our hearts have been poured out , and our bodies have been washed with water , then come we unto God with a good heart and with sufficient faith
And to keep the hope which we have acknowledged , and not to shake it ; for that which we have promised is true .
And to look after one another , to inspire love , to exhort to do good
You cannot cease from gathering as those who have ceased to be used to it , but to exhort one another , knowing that the day is near , even more so .
For after we have learned the truth , there will be no more atonement for sins committed intentionally
Only fear of war awaits judgment and the burning of the enemy .
&quot; If a man commits a crime against the law of Moses , he shall die by two or three witnesses , and shall not have mercy
&quot; How much more , then , do you think , that a man who tramples on the Son of God , and takes the blood of the covenant which made him holy as ordinary , and blasphemes the Holy Spirit ? How much more will his punishment be ?
For we know him who says , &quot; Repent on me , and I will recompense . &quot; And he says , &quot; Judge his people first . &quot;
How terrible it is to fall into the hands of the eternal God !
Remember the days when you endured all the hardships of the great battle under the light .
On the one hand he was slandered and afflicted , and made a spectacle to the people , and accompanied those who suffered so much
For you have suffered those who are bound , and your houses have been robbed ; and you are willing to endure , knowing that you have a more beautiful and enduring house .
Therefore do not forsake your brave hearts ; for such hearts will receive great reward
You must endure , that you may accomplish the will of God , and that you may receive what you have been promised
For there is still a little time , and that which is to come shall come , and not delay
Only the righteous will live by faith ; and if he turns away , I will not rejoice in him .
&quot; But we are not those who have gone back into desolation , but those who have faith that the soul may be saved .
Behold , the letter is the foundation of what is hoped , and the confirmation of what is not seen .
The ancients had good evidence in this letter
By faith we know that the worlds were created by the Word , and that what is seen is not of manifest things .
And because of the sacrifice he offered to God , which was more beautiful than the sacrifice of Cain , he received a righteous testimony , the testimony of God concerning his gift ; and though he was dead , yet he spoke of it
Noah was not brought to death by the faith , nor did any man seek him , for God had already brought him ; but he had been brought forth first , having received the proof that God was pleased with him .
If a man does not have faith , he cannot obtain the pleasure of God ; for he who comes before God must have faith .
And Noah , because of his faith , and because of the revelation of God that he had not seen , and because of the fear of God , prepared a ark that he might save his whole house , and because of the sins of that generation , and because of the righteousness that came from the faith ,
Abraham went out by faith and in the time of his calling , according to his commandments , to a place of service in the future , where he would not know when he would go .
By faith he served in the promised land as in a tent in a strange land , as Jacob , who had received the promise .
For he awaits the city of the foundations , which God has built .
By faith , even Sarah herself conceived , even though she was old enough to bear ; for he believed that what he had promised was faithful .
So from a dead man shall be born sons , as many as the stars of heaven , and as many as the sand of the sea .
All these are dead in faith , and have not received what they have been promised ; but they see from afar , and rejoice , and confess that they are travellers and dwellers in the world .
A man who says this is a sign that he wants to find a hometown
If they remember the hometown they left , they have a chance to go back
But they envy a better homeland , which is in heaven ; so God is called their God , and not with shame ; for He has prepared for them a city .
Abraham , in faith , when he was tested , offered up Isaac : this is the joyful man who was promised , who offered up his only son .
As for this son , it was said , &quot; You shall be called your seed from the son of Jesse .
He can also raise man from the dead for God &apos;s sake , and he seems to have returned his son from the dead
And it came to pass , when Isaac had believed , and had spoken of the things to come , that he blessed Jacob and Esau
And Jacob blessed the two sons of Joseph in the day of his death by the letter , and worshipped God with his staff on his head
Joseph wrote in his letter that in the time of the end the children of Israel would go out of Egypt and leave a remnant for their own bones
When Moses was born , and his parents saw that he was a handsome child , they hid him for three months by faith , and feared not the death of the king
Moses did not grow up to be called the son of Pharaoh &apos;s daughter , because he believed
He would rather suffer with the people of God , than enjoy the pleasure of sin for a while
He regarded the humiliation suffered by Christ as more precious than the riches of Egypt , for he desired the reward which he would have
He left Egypt because of his faith , and feared not the wrath of the king ; for he endured with endurance , as the Lord that cannot see .
By faith he kept the Passover , and the feast of the bloodshed , lest the Son of man should come near to Israel
By faith they passed over the Red Sea like dry land ; and the Egyptians were consumed when they tried to pass over .
And the children of Israel believed , and for seven days the walls of the city fell around Jericho
The prostitute Lalai , who had received the spies with peace in her letter , will not perish with the disobedient .
&quot; What else will I say ? The time will not come when I will speak one thing in detail concerning Gideon , Balak , Sanshur , Jephthah , David , Samuel , and the prophets
By faith they have subdued the enemy , they have done righteousness , they have received promises , they have shut the mouth of the lion
Destroy the fierceness of the fire , remove the sharp edge of the sword , turn weakness into strength , show bravery in battle , take away the whole army of the foreign lands
For there are women who shall raise up their dead , and there are men who endure severe punishment , and who refuse to be released , that they may have a better resurrection .
And there are some who endure scourges , whips , fetters , imprisonments , and so on
They are slain by stones , they are sawed by saws , they are tested , they are slain by swords , they run in all places covered with sheep and goats &apos; skins , they are afflicted , they are afflicted , they are afflicted
In the wilderness , in the mountains , in the caves , in the pits , the flow is uncertain . There is no one worthy of the world
All these have obtained good proof by faith , but they have not yet received what they were promised
For he has prepared for us better things for God , that they may not be perfect , if they have not received them with us
We have many witnesses , and as the clouds surround us , let us lay down all our burdens , let our sins be removed , let us persevere , let us go forth on the way before us .
Look to Jesus , who came to an end for our faith , and who will come to an end for the truth ; and for the joy that was before him , he humbled himself , and endured the torment of the cross , and sat on the right hand of the throne of God
&quot; Those who endure the stumbling of sinners , think , lest you be weary and despair .
&quot; You have fought against sin , and there is no way to prevent it from bleeding .
For you have forgotten that which you have been admonished as a child , saying , &quot; My son , you will not despise the commandment of the Lord , nor be disappointed when you are reproached by Him .
For he who loves the Lord will teach , and will whip up the sons whom he receives .
For what you endure is that God disciplines you , and treats you as a son . Why is there a son who is not disciplined by his father ?
&quot; The ministry was common to all the children ; and if you were not ministered , you would be private sons and not sons .
&quot; Are we not more to obey the Father of all spirits , who has taught us in the flesh , and whom we revere ?
The Father of life is teaching us by his own will ; but the Father of all spirits is teaching us for our benefit , that we may be divided in His holiness .
Then he did not rejoice in all that he taught , but was grieved ; and the fruit of peace came forth for him who had been trained , that is righteousness .
&quot; Therefore lift up your hands that are hanging down , and your legs that are aching .
And he shall straighten the way for his own feet , that the lame may not stumble , but be healed .
&quot; You shall seek harmony with all the people , and purity : for none can see the Lord without purity .
Be careful , lest a man lose God &apos;s grace ; lest a poisonous root be formed to disturb you , so that you may be defiled .
I fear that there is an obscene and greedy man , like Esau , who has sold his eldest son for a meal
&quot; But when he wanted to receive the blessings of his father , he was rejected , and when he cried out for them , he did not find the way to turn his father &apos;s heart , as you know .
&quot; You have not come to the mountains that can be touched , where there is fire , clouds , darkness , and wind .
The voice of the horns and the voice of speech . Those who heard it asked not to speak to them any more .
For when they did not speak what they had commanded , they said , &apos; Those who are near this mountain , even beasts , shall be put to death with stones .
What was seen was extremely frightening , and even Moses said , &apos; I am terrified .
&quot; You have come to Mount Zion , the city of the eternal God , Jerusalem in heaven , where there are thousands of angels
&quot; For there is a congregation in heaven , the congregation of the elders , a God who judges all , and a soul of righteousness who is perfected
and Jesus in the midst of the new covenant , and the blood that was poured out , which is more beautiful than that which was spoken of Beer-sheba .
Be careful , and do not forsake those who speak to you ; for those who forsake warn them on earth cannot escape sin ; and we are against those who warn us from heaven .
His voice at that time shook the earth . But now he should promise to say , &apos; I will shake not only the earth but also the heavens again .
&quot; This is yet another word , indicating that which is shaken , that which is created , is to be moved away , so that that which is not shaken remains .
&quot; Therefore we have obtained a land that cannot shake , and we serve God with gratitude , and with the joy of God , and with a heart of piety and fear .
For our God is the fire
You must always have a brotherly heart
Remember not to receive the journey with love ; for he who has received the journey has received the angel without knowledge .
Remember those who are bound , as if they were bound with them ; and those who are afflicted , as if they were in the flesh .
Marriage shall be respected , and the bed shall not be defiled ; for God must judge those who commit adultery .
Be careful not to be greedy of money , but to be worthy of all that you have ; for the Lord said , &quot; I will never leave you , neither will I leave you . &quot;
So let us be bold and say , &apos; The Lord is my helper ; I will not be afraid ; how will man treat me ? &apos;
guide you and preach to your people the way of God ; remember them , obey their faith , and be careful of the end of their affairs .
Jesus Christ , Yesterday and to this day , and forever , is the same
You will be drawn to all these strange teachings , for it is good that the heart be firm in grace , and not in food , which is devoted to food and never profits .
&quot; And we have an altar , and the offerings above shall not be eaten by those who serve in the tabernacle .
&quot; The blood of the beasts , which were brought into the sanctuary by the high priest for a sin offering , and the bodies of the beasts , were burned outside the camp
So Jesus suffered outside the gates of the city , to sanctify the people with his own blood
So we went out to the camp , and suffered the humiliation which he had suffered .
&quot; We have no permanent city here , but seek the city of the future .
&quot; We should rely on him , and offer him often as a sacrifice of praise to God . This is the fruit of the lips of those who confess the name of the Lord .
Only good deeds and sacrifices are to be remembered , for such sacrifices are acceptable to God .
Follow those who guide you , and obey them ; for they are watchful for your souls as those who pay the bills in the future ; and you will make them happy in the time of their payment , and not grieved ; and grief will be of no benefit to you .
Pray for us , that we may do all things according to the righteousness of our conscience
I ask you to pray for me , that I may return to you sooner
Blessed be the God of peace , the God of the resurrection from the dead , my Lord Jesus , the great shepherd of the flock , by the blood of the everlasting covenant .
Be all of you in all good deeds , that you may walk in His will , and do in your hearts the things which He pleases , in the name of Jesus Christ ; and glory be to Him , straight to ever and ever . Amen .
&quot; Brothers , I have written to you briefly , hoping that you will listen to my counsel .
&quot; You should know that our brother Timothy has been released . If he comes soon , I will see you with him
Ask them to guide your saints and your saints , and the men of righteousness also to ask you :
May mercy always be with you all . Amen
&quot; And Jacob , who is a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ , may he rest in the twelve tribes .
&quot; My brethren , be glad when you are in the midst of many trials
For it is known that your faith has been tested , and you are born to endure
But patience , when it is successful , will make you perfect , without any shortcomings
&quot; If there is a man among you who lacks wisdom , let him seek the God who is generous and does not reproach , and the Lord will give him .
If you ask with confidence , there is no doubt ; for he who doubts is like the waves of the sea blown by the wind .
For such a man will not seek anything from the Lord .
A man of two minds will not know in all that he does .
The humble brethren shall be exalted , and rejoice
And so should the rich humble himself ; for he needs to pass away like the flowers of the grass .
And the sun shall come forth , and the wind shall blow , and the grass shall dry up , and the flowers shall fade away , and the beauty shall fade away ; and so shall the rich man perish in that which he hath done .
Blessed is he that endureth trial : for after his trial he shall receive the crown of life , which the Lord hath promised unto those who love him .
A man is tested , and he cannot say , &quot; I am tested by God ; for God cannot be tested by evil , neither does he test men . &quot;
But every man is tempted by his own selfish desire
When selfishness conceives , it brings forth sin ; when sin grows , it brings forth death .
My beloved brethren , do not be mistaken
All the grace of good and good , and all the rewards of all things , are from above , and descended from the Father of light , in whom there is no change , nor shadow of change .
He created us by His will in the true way , that we might be like the first fruits of all things that He has created .
That is what you know , my beloved brethren ; but listen , every one of you , and be angry , and speak slowly .
For the wrath of men does not accomplish the righteousness of God
Therefore take away all filth , and the excess of evil , and receive the way that is planted with a gentle heart , which will save your souls .
&quot; But ye shall walk , and not listen , but deceive yourselves
For he that heareth , and walketh not , hath seen his own face in the mirror
When he saw it , and when he left , he immediately forgot his appearance
&quot; But he who observes in detail the law that sets him free , and often does so , will be blessed in that which he does , neither by hearing it , nor by forgetting it , but by doing it .
&quot; If a man sees himself to be pious , and does not hold his tongue , and deceives his own heart , then his piety is vain .
&quot; In the presence of God our Father , purity and devotion without defilement is for the orphan and widow in distress , and for keeping themselves from the worldly things .
My brethren , if you believe in the Lord Jesus Christ , our glory , you shall not walk in the way of appearance
&quot; When a man enters your synagogue with gold rings and fine clothes , and a poor man in filthy clothes enters ,
Then you looked at the man who was clothed in fine linen , and said , &quot; Sit in this good seat , &quot; and said to the poor man , &quot; Sit in it , or sit under my bench
&quot; Is it not that you preach to men , and judge them with malice ?
&quot; My beloved brethren , ask me , &quot; Has God not chosen the poor in the world , that they may be rich in the letter , and that they may bear the kingdom which He has promised to those who love Him ?
But you are ashamed of the poor , and the rich oppress you , and bring you to the synagogue .
Are they not blasphemers of the name which you worship
It is written , &quot; Love one as yourself , &quot; and it is good for you to keep this holy law
&quot; But if you treat men according to their appearance , it is a crime , and it is lawful to do so .
For he that keeps all the law falls only on one thing , and he is a transgressor of all things .
&quot; He who says , &apos; You must not commit adultery , &apos; says , &apos; You must not kill a man ; &apos; and you are still a transgressor who does not commit adultery but kills a man .
&quot; Now that you are to be judged according to the law of liberty , speak and do according to it
For those who do not have mercy will also be judged without mercy , for mercy is a triumph over judgment .
My brethren , what is the use of a man who says , &quot; If he has faith and does not act , will that faith save him ? &quot;
If brothers or sisters are naked and lack daily food
&quot; There are some among you who say to them , &apos; Go in peace . What good is it for you to be clothed and fed , but not to give them what they need ? &apos;
Thus , faith is dead without works
&quot; And some will say , &apos; You have faith , and I have deeds ; and you will show me the faith you did not do ; and I will borrow my deeds , and show you my faith .
There is only one God in whom you believe , and it is good that you believe ; and the devil believes , but he is terrified .
Wouldst thou , O man of vanity , know that faith without works is dead ?
&quot; Isn &apos;t it righteousness for our father Abraham to offer his son Isaac on the altar ?
It is evident that faith is in harmony with his deeds , and that faith is accomplished by doing
This is the test of what is said in the Scriptures : Abraham believed in God , and it was righteousness for him ; and he was called a friend of God
In this way , man is justified by his deeds , not by faith alone
&quot; Isn &apos;t the prostitute Lalai the one who receives the messengers and lets them go out on other roads ? Isn &apos;t she a worthy person for her deeds ?
The body without soul is dead , and faith without works is dead
My brethren , let no more men be masters , knowing that we shall be judged more severely
For in many things we have sinned ; and if there is one who has not sinned in speech , he is perfect , and able to hold his whole body
&quot; If we put the chewing ring in the mouth of the horse , and make him obey , we will move his whole body
Behold , the ship , though it be great , is driven by a great wind , and with a small rudder it moves according to the purpose of the rudder .
Thus is the tongue the smallest of a hundred , but it speaks a great word . Behold , the smallest fire can light the biggest forest .
The tongue is fire , and in the hundreds of our bodies the tongue is a world of sin , which defiles the whole body , and sets up the wheels of life , and is set up from hell .
All kinds of beasts , birds , insects and aquatic animals could have been subdued , and have been subdued by man
But the tongue is an abomination that cannot be contained , full of the poison of death .
&quot; We praise with our tongues the Father , and with our tongues those who are made in the image of God
Praise and curse come out of one mouth , My brethren , it is not right
Can the fountain spring two kinds of sweet and bitter water from one eye
My brethren , can an olive tree bear no fruit without its flowers , or a vine without its fruit without its flowers , and can no sweet water come out of salt water ?
Who among you has wisdom and understanding ? He shows his good deeds in the tenderness of wisdom .
&quot; If your hearts are filled with bitter jealousy and strife , you cannot boast , nor speak lies against the truth .
&quot; This wisdom is not from above , but from the earth , from the desire , from the devil .
Where there is jealousy and strife , there is trouble and all kinds of evil
Only wisdom from above , first clean , then peaceful , gentle , compassionate , fruitful , without prejudice , without hypocrisy
And that which brings peace is the fruit of peace planted .
&quot; Where did the fight between you come from ? Was it not from the desire to fight among your hundreds ?
You are lustful , or not ; you kill jealousy , or fight it , or not ; you are not lustful , because you do not ask
&quot; You will not be able to do what you ask for , for you will be wasted in your feasts .
&quot; You adulterers , do you not know that you are enemies of God , and that you are friends with the world ? Therefore whoever wants to be friends with the world is an enemy of God .
Do you think that what you say in the Scriptures is false ? Is it love as much as jealousy that God has given us the Spirit that lives in us ?
But He has given more grace , and it is written , &quot; God has hindered the proud , and He has given grace to the humble .
Therefore obey God , and resist the devil , and he will flee from you .
Close yourselves to God , and God will be close to you ; cleanse your hands , you sinners ; and cleanse your hearts , you who have two minds .
You shall mourn , you shall mourn , you shall weep , you shall make laughter to mourn , and joy to sorrow .
Be humble before the Lord , and the Lord will raise you up
Brothers , you cannot criticize one another . If a man criticizes a brother , he criticizes the law , he criticizes the law . If you criticize the law , it is not to obey the law , it is to judge .
&quot; There is only one who establishes the law and judges , and who can save and destroy . Who are you , that you dispute others ?
&quot; You said , &quot; Today and tomorrow we will go to a city where we will live for a year and sell and sell
You don &apos;t know what tomorrow will be like . What is your life ? You were a cloud and you didn &apos;t see it when it appeared
&quot; You say only , &apos; If the Lord wills , we can live , and do this thing or that thing
&quot; Now you exaggerate with madness , and all such exaggerations are evil
&quot; If a man knows to do good , but does not do it , that is his sin .
&quot; Woe to you , you rich men ! Cry and weep for the troubles that will come upon you
&quot; Your property is broken , and your clothes have been bitten by insects
&quot; Your silver and your gold will become rust , and it will prove that you are not , and it will eat your flesh like a fire . In the last days you will only accumulate money and wealth .
The workers harvest your crops , and you owe them for their wages ; and the wages cry out , and the wrath of the harvester has passed into the ears of the Lord of hosts .
Blessed are you in the world , having a good feast ; and the days of slaughter have nurtured your hearts
&quot; You have determined the sin of the righteous , and you have killed him ; and he will not stand in your way .
Brothers , endure , until the Lord comes ; behold , the farmers endure , waiting for the precious fruit in the land , until the autumn rain and spring rain come
For the days of the Lord are near .
Brothers , do not grieve one another , lest you be judged : behold , the Lord of judgment stands at the door
&quot; Brothers , you shall set the prophets who spoke before in the name of the Lord as an example of endurance and patience .
&quot; Blessed are those who have been patient in the past ; and you have heard the patience of Job , and know the end of the Lord &apos;s dealings with him ; for the Lord is compassionate and merciful .
Most important of all , my brethren , is not to swear , neither to swear by the heavens , nor to swear by the earth ; neither to swear by anything ; speak ye , and say ye , and say ye , and say ye not , lest ye fall under judgment .
For whoever among you suffers , let him pray ; and whoever rejoices , let him sing praises .
And if any of you be sick , he shall call the elders of the church , and they shall anoint him with oil in the name of the Lord , and pray for him .
The Lord will raise him up by faithful prayers to save the sick , and if he commits a sin , he will be forgiven
Therefore confess one another , and ask one another , that you may be healed . The power of the righteous in prayer is powerful .
Elijah was a man of one kind with us ; and he prayed earnestly that it should not rain , and that it should not rain on the earth for three and six months
And he prayed , and the heavens came down twice , and the earth gave birth to her inheritance
My brethren , if there be among you a man who is lost in the way of truth , he will be turned back
He who knows how to turn a sinner out of the abyss saves a soul from death , and covers up many sins .
Peter , the apostle of Jesus Christ , wrote to those who dwelled in the houses of Galatia , Cappadocia , Asia , and Pitus
Blessed are those who were chosen according to the Father &apos;s foreknowledge , and sanctified by the Holy Spirit , to obey Jesus Christ , and to be anointed with his blood . Grace be to you , and peace , and more .
Blessed be the Father God of our Lord Jesus Christ , who , through his great mercy , raised us from the dead , and gave us life again , that we might have hope .
Behold , it shall be a foundation for you in heaven , which shall not decay , nor defile , nor decay .
&quot; And those of you who keep yourselves in the power of God will receive the salvation which is prepared for the world to come .
Therefore , you are joyful , but now you are temporarily grieved in the trials of many
Let your faith be tested , that it may be more precious than the gold that is tested by fire , and that it may be praised , glorified , and exalted in the time of the manifestation of Jesus Christ
Though ye have not seen him , yet love ye him ; and though ye have not seen him now , yet by faith he speaketh not , and is full of joy and glory .
And the fruit of your faith is the salvation of the soul
And concerning this salvation , the prophets before you , who said that you would receive grace , searched for it in detail
To examine the Spirit of Christ in their hearts , and to prove first that Christ suffered , and then was glorified , which is the time and what is the time
They have been enlightened , and know that all that they preach is not for themselves , but for you ; and the one who preached the word of blessing to you by the Holy Spirit from heaven is present to report it to you ; and the angels are willing to see it in detail .
Therefore bind your hearts , and guard yourselves , and wait diligently for the grace which your Lord Jesus Christ will bring to you in the time of his manifestation .
&quot; You are children of righteousness , and you will not do what was done before in ignorance , which was a deceitful desire .
&quot; That which you have been called is holy , and you shall be holy in all that you do
For it is written , &quot; You shall be holy , for I am holy .
&quot; Behold , in a fearful heart , you shall measure the days of your dwelling in the world , even as you call the Lord , who is not a partisan , and judges according to every man .
Knowing that you have to redeem , and remove from your fathers the deceitful deeds , not by means of evil silver and gold ,
It is the precious blood of Christ , as the blood of a lamb without blemish without blemish .
Christ was known before the beginning of the world , and was revealed to you in the last world
because of him you believe in the God who raised him from the dead and glorified him , that your faith and hope may be in God
&quot; You have purified your hearts by obedience to the truth , so that there is no falseness in the love of your brothers , and you have truly loved one another in your hearts .
You are raised again , not because of the seed that can not be broken , but because of the seed that cannot be broken , by the way of God that lives and endures
For every bloodthirsty man is like the grass , and his glory is like the flowers of the grass ; and the grass will dry up , and the flowers will fade away .
Only the way of the Lord is eternal.This is the gospel which has been preached to you
Therefore you shall remove all the poison , and all the deceit , and all the false good , and all the jealousy , and all the blasphemy ,
Love the pure milk of the Spirit , like the milk of the newborn , that you may grow , and be saved .
&quot; If you have tasted the grace of the Lord , it will be so
The Lord is a living stone , which is forsaken , but which is precious by God &apos;s choosing
&quot; You have come before the Lord as living stones , and have been built as a sanctuary of the Spirit , as holy priests , and as a sacrifice of the Spirit acceptable to God through Jesus Christ
&apos;Behold , I have laid down in Zion the precious cornerstone of the house which I have chosen ; and those who believe in him will not be ashamed .
Therefore it is precious to him who believes in you , and to him who does not believe , that he said , &apos; The stone which the craftsman has left has become the headstone of the corner of the house .
And said , &quot; They have made a stone to stumble upon , a stone to fall upon , and they stumble on the basis of the law , both of disobedience and of disobedience ; and it is foretold that they shall stumble on the basis of the law . &quot;
Only you are a chosen nation , a noble priest , a holy nation , a son of God , to proclaim the virtue of calling you out of the darkness into the wonderful light .
Ye have not been children before , but ye are children of God ; and ye have not been pitied before , but ye are pitied
Beloved brethren , you are travellers and dwellers . I urge you to refrain from the selfish desire of the flesh , which fights with the soul .
&quot; You shall be righteous among the Gentiles , and those who blaspheme you shall be wicked ; and they shall be glorified in the days of reckoning , because they have seen your good deeds .
For the sake of your Lord , obey all the institutions of men , or the kings that are above you .
Or a king &apos;s servant who punishes evil and rewards good
For the will of God was that you should do good , and that you might shut up the mouth of the foolish .
&quot; While you are free , you cannot hide the evil from your freedom , but you must always be servants of God .
Respect all men , brothers in love , godfearing , kings .
&quot; You servants obey the master with a fearful heart in all things , and not only the kind and the gentle , but also the devious .
&quot; If a man endures the pain of wrong for the sake of his conscience , that he may dwell in God , it is a pleasant love
If you are reproached for your sins , and endure , what can be extolled ? But if you suffer for good deeds , and endure , it is acceptable in God &apos;s sight .
That is why you were called , because Christ also suffered for you , and gave you an example , that you might walk in His footsteps .
He has no sin , and no deceit in his mouth
He shall not be reproached , neither shall he be slandered ; but he shall entrust himself to the Lord who judgeth according to righteousness .
He is hanged on a tree , and bears our sins himself ; and since we are dead in our sins , we are able to live in righteousness ; and because of his whips you are healed .
You used to be a lost sheep ; but now your souls are overseen by a shepherd .
Be ye wives , and obey your own husbands ; and if there be a husband that believeth not in the truth , and they obey not , but are persuaded by the manner of his wife
&quot; This is because I have seen your holy works and your fearful hearts .
&quot; You shall not put on the outside braided hair , gold ornaments , fine clothes , and make-up
It is precious in the sight of God for a long and gentle and quiet heart to remain in it .
For the holy woman who relied on God in the ancient days was clothed with it , and obeyed her husband
&quot; Just as Sarah listened to Abraham and called him Lord ; and if you do good , and do not be afraid of fear , you are the daughter of Sarah
And ye that are husbands dwell with your wives according to your hearts ; and fear Him , because He is weaker than you , and He is a weak vessel with you , bearer of the grace of life ; that your prayers may not be hindered .
&quot; But all of you have to be compassionate , caring for one another , loving one another as brothers , and having a compassionate and humble heart
Blessed be ye not for evil and for reproach and for reproach , for ye are called for it , that ye may be blessed
For it is written in the Scriptures , &quot; If a man loves life and wishes to be blessed , let his tongue not speak evil words and his lips not speak deceitful words
and to do good from evil , and to seek harmony , and to pursue with one heart ;
For the eyes of the Lord look upon the righteous , and the ears of the Lord hear their prayers ; but the wicked are turned away from them .
&quot; Who will harm you if you are zealous for good
You are suffering for righteousness , and are blessed . Do not be afraid of the fear of men , nor be afraid of what they fear .
As long as the Lord Christ is holy in your hearts , and as long as someone asks the cause of your hope in your hearts , always be ready , and answer each one with a gentle heart of fear .
If you have a good conscience , that you may be deceived in what things , then the one who deceives you in what good works in Christ may be ashamed .
&quot; If the will of God were to make you suffer for good , it would be as strong as suffering for evil
For Christ also suffered once for sin , and was righteous in place of wickedness , to draw us to God , that he might be put to death according to the flesh , and that he might be raised up according to the spirit
He preached through this Spirit to those who were in prison
Those who had not believed in the time of God &apos;s patience , when he prepared the ark in Noah ; and when they entered into it , not many were saved by water , but eight .
The baptism which this water manifests is now in the resurrection of Jesus Christ , and will save you . This baptism is not for the removal of the filth of the flesh , but for the righteous conscience before God .
Jesus has entered into heaven on the right hand of God , and all the angels and all the powerful and competent have obeyed him
For Christ suffered in the flesh , and you have taken such a heart as a weapon : for he that suffered in the flesh has passed away from sin .
&quot; If you have such a heart , from now on , you will be able to avoid the desires of men , and only the will of God , and the shadow of the world .
For the time has come to follow the hearts of the Gentiles , to commit adultery , lusts , to drink wine , to feast , to drink in multitudes , and to worship idols .
&quot; When they see that you do not go along with them in the path of disobedience , they will reproach you .
They will pay the bill before the Lord who will judge the living and the dead .
For this reason the gospel of the dead was preached to them , that their flesh should be judged according to man , and that their spirit should live according to God
The end of all things is near ; therefore be careful of yourselves , and be watchful , and pray
The most important thing is to love one another in practice , for love can cover up many sins
You have to treat each other well , and not complain
Let every man serve one another according to the grace which he hath received , and be a good steward of God &apos;s abundance
Whosoever speaketh , let him speak according to the holy word of God ; and whosoever obeyeth , let him obey according to the power which God hath given him ; that God may be glorified in all things by the name of Jesus Christ : for to Him belongeth the glory and the power , even unto ever and ever .
Beloved brethren , the test of fire has come upon you , not as a strange thing , but as a great thing .
And rejoice , because you suffered with Christ , and rejoiced in his glory .
Blessed are you if you are reproached in the name of Christ , for the Spirit of glory is always with you
&quot; But there is no man among you who suffers for murder , for stealing , for evil , for good deeds ,
&quot; If you suffer as a Christian , don &apos;t be ashamed , but glorify God for this name
For the time is come , and judgment shall come from the house of God ; and what will be the end of those who do not believe in the gospel of God , if they first come from us ?
If only the righteous had been saved , where would the ungodly and sinners stand ?
Therefore he that suffereth according to the will of God , let his heart be good , and let his soul be given unto the Lord of true creation
I am an old man , a witness of the sufferings of Christ , and a man who persuades you among you to be with me in the glory that is to be revealed afterwards .
And shepherd the flock of God among you according to the will of God , not out of covetousness , but out of kindness , and not out of greed , but out of pleasure
&quot; It is not your trust in authority , but an example for sheep .
&quot; When the Lord comes , you will receive the crown of everlasting glory
&quot; You young men obey the old men ; and all of you obey one another in humility : for God has hindered the proud , and has given grace to the humble .
&quot; Therefore humble yourselves , and obey God &apos;s great power ; and He will raise you up at the time
&quot; You shall give away all your worries to God , because he cares for you .
Be watchful and watchful ; for your enemy , the devil , is as a roaring lion , traveling through the land seeking a man to eat .
Be strong in your faith , and stand against him , knowing that your brethren in the world have suffered as well .
&quot; The God who has blessed you , who has called you in Christ to his eternal glory , will be able to make you whole in himself , to strengthen you , and to give you strength after your trials .
To Him belongs the power of will , straight to ever and ever .
&quot; I have written this letter to you , that Silas , the brother whom I consider to be faithful , may pass it on to you , and encourage you , and prove that this grace is the true grace of God , and that you may stand firm on it .
Have mercy on you in Babylon , and on you in the Church of the anointed , and on you in my son Mark
Peace be to all of you who are in Christ , that you may say goodbye to one another with love
Simon Peter , a servant of Jesus Christ and an apostle , wrote to him who had the same precious confidence in the righteousness of our God and of the Savior Jesus Christ ,
Blessed be the peace , for you know God and our Lord Jesus , who has added much to you .
The God of God has given us all things concerning life and godliness , all because we know the Lord who calls us by His glory and virtue
Therefore he has given us a precious and great promise , that we may be separated from the evil of the world , and from the evil of the desires of God .
For this reason , you shall have an outward kindness , and faith , and good deeds , and knowledge
There is knowledge and there is restraint . There is restraint and there is patience . There is restraint and there is piety
For there is piety , and a heart that loves brothers , and a heart that loves brothers , and a heart that loves all
&quot; If you are full of these things , you will not be lazy nor fruitful in the knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ .
&quot; If a man has no such thing , he is blind , and sees nothing but the near , and forgets that his old sins have been cleansed
Therefore , brethren , be more earnest , that your calling and your election may be firm ; and if you do these things , you will never lose your feet .
&quot; This way you , rich and rich , will enter into the everlasting kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ
Even though you know these things , and are firm in the way which you have taken , I will often wake you up to them .
&quot; I will awaken you and excite you while I am still in this tent
For the time is near to know that I am departed from this tabernacle , as our Lord Jesus Christ commanded me .
&quot; And I will do my utmost to keep these things in remembrance when I die .
&quot; We have told you before of the great power of our Lord Jesus Christ , and of his coming , and not by falsehood , but by the glory of seeing him with our own eyes .
When he was glorified by the Father , a voice came out of great glory , saying to him , &quot; This is my beloved Son , whom I rejoice in .
And when we were with him in the mountain , we heard the voice from heaven in person
And We have a prophet with a more accurate prophecy , like a lamp in the darkness . It is better for you to bear witness to this prophecy until the morning stars appear in your hearts .
First and foremost , he should know that there is no private interpretation of all the prophecies in the Scriptures .
For the prophecy never came out of the mind of man , but the word of God spoken by the Holy Spirit .
&quot; There have been false prophets among the people , and there will be false teachers among you in the future . They will introduce their own mischief to the captives , and they will not even buy their lord , and they will not confess their own destruction .
&quot; Many will follow their wicked deeds , and will be called to the truth , and will be slandered for their sakes .
They profit from you with their greed , and with false words ; and their punishment has not delayed from the ancient times , and their destruction will come quickly .
For the angels have sinned , and God has not forgiven them ; He has cast them into hell , into the pit of darkness , waiting for judgment .
Neither did God tolerate the ancient generation ; He caused a flood to come upon the ungodly generation , but He protected eight of the house of Noah in the gospel .
Judging also Sodom and Moor , they overthrew the two cities and burned them to ashes , as a warning to the ungodly of the latter generations .
Only the righteous Rhodes , who is always troubled by the evildoers ,
For the righteous dwells among them , and his righteous heart hurts every day when he sees and hears what they do not do .
Knowing that the Lord delivers the pious from temptation , and keeps the wicked from punishment , and waits for the days of judgment
Even so are those who walk in flesh and in defiled desires , and are weak in the Lord &apos;s authority . They are bold , and do not know how to fear those who deny the honor .
&quot; The angels , even though their power is greater , do not speak blasphemies to them before the Lord
But they are as though they had no spirit ; they were created as beasts to be captured and slaughtered ; and they blaspheme what they do not know , and they will be destroyed in the time of the wicked .
&quot; The unrighteousness of their deeds will be their unrighteous wages ; and they will enjoy themselves with their own deceit , because they have been defiled , and defiled , and are sitting with you at the feast of the day .
Their eyes are full of prostitution , and they do not cease from committing sin ; and they are the kinds of cursed , who seduce those who are not strong in heart , who are accustomed to greed .
And they turned away from the right way , and followed the way of Balaam the son of Beer ; and Balaam was the prophet of the price of corruption and iniquity .
But he is reproached for his transgressions : the donkey that speaketh not , that with words hinders the foolishness of the prophet
These are the wells without water , the mist driven by the wind , and the darkness of the ink .
They speak lofty words of vanity , and with their fleshly desires and their wickedness they seduce those who have gone astray from deceit .
They have promised freedom to man , but they are themselves servants to the wicked : for whoever is subdued is his servant .
If , by the knowledge of the Lord and Savior Jesus Christ , they were able to get away from the filth of the world , and to be entangled therein again , their end would be worse than the former
For they know the way of righteousness , and have turned away from the Holy Ghost that is sent down to them , lest they know the wonders
There is no mistake in saying that what the dog spits he turns around and eats . The pig cleans up and rolls back into the mud . It is the same in their bodies
Beloved brethren , I am writing to you a second letter , both of which awaken you and excite your sincere hearts
Remember the words of the holy prophet , which he foretold , and the commandment of the Lord Savior , which the Apostles sent to you
First of all , let them know that in the last world there will be a good reproacher , who reproaches according to his own selfish desire
In that is the chief promise of the coming : for all things have been the same from the beginning of creation , since they slept with their fathers .
For they have deliberately forgotten that from ancient times there was a heaven by the life of God , and from water came out a land by water
Therefore , the world at that time was destroyed by the flood
But in the heavens that are , they will remain by that life , until the days when the ungodly are judged and destroyed and burned with fire .
Beloved , there is one thing that you must not forget : The Lord sees a day as a thousand years , and a thousand years as a day
The promise of the Lord has not yet been fulfilled , and some think that he is a delay ; but it is not a delay , but a mercy to you , that no man should perish , and that all men should repent .
&quot; But the day of the Lord will come like a thief , and the day will be overthrown with a great noise , and all that is visible will be destroyed by the fire , and the earth and all that is on it will be consumed .
How holy and how devout are you to men , since all these things are to be destroyed
The days of earnest reverence to God will come , and on that day they will be consumed by fire , and all that is in their form will be consumed by a fiery fire .
&quot; But we have hoped for a new heaven and a new land , according to His promise , and have lived in it righteously
Beloved brothers , while you wait for these things , be diligent , so that yourselves are not defiled , nor spotted , and that you may see the Lord in peace .
&quot; And as Paul , our beloved brother , wrote to you in the wisdom that was given to him , that you might be saved by the endurance of my Lord .
And in all his letters he speaks of these things , and there are things in them which are difficult to understand ; and a man who is ignorant and not strong , when he enjoins , as he enjoins in other scriptures , sins on his own .
Beloved brothers , since you have known this beforehand , beware , lest you fall from your firm footsteps by the false seduction of the wicked .
And ye shall prosper in the grace and knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ : glory be unto him from this day even unto the end . Amen .
For the way of life , which was from the beginning , is that which we have heard , seen , seen , seen , touched with our hands
&quot; This life has been revealed , and we have seen it and seen it , and are witnessing and bearing witness , that it may be revealed to you that it was with the Father , and that it may be with us forever .
&quot; We will convey to you what we have seen and heard , that you may be associated with us ; for we are associated with the Father and with His Son Jesus Christ
&quot; We have written these words to you , that your joy may be sufficient .
God is light , and in Him is no darkness : this is the word which we have heard from the Lord , and which He has revealed to you .
&quot; If we say that we associate ourselves with God , and yet walk in the darkness , we speak lies and do not the truth
If we walk in the light , as God walks in the light , we will intercede with one another , and the blood of His Son Jesus will cleanse all our sins .
&quot; If we say that we are innocent , we are deceiving ourselves ; and the truth is not in our hearts
If we confess our sins , God is faithful and righteous , and must forgive our sins and cleanse all our iniquities .
&quot; If we say that we have not sinned , we are lying to God , and His way is not in our hearts .
&quot; I have written these things to you , my little children , that you may not sin ; and if any man sins , then in the Father is one of us , the righteous , Jesus Christ .
He has redeemed us for our sins , not only for our sins , but also for all the nations
&quot; If we obey His commandments , we know that we know Him
&quot; If a man says , &apos; I know him , &apos; but does not obey his commandments , he is lying , and the truth is not in his heart .
&quot; From that time onward we know that we are in the Lord , and that the heart of those who keep the word and love God is perfect in him
&quot; If a man says that he lives in the Lord , let him walk according to what the Lord has done
Beloved brothers , what I have written to you is not a new commandment , but the old commandment which you received from the beginning , which is the word which you have heard .
Again , I have written to you a new commandment , which is true in the Lord , and true in you ; for the darkness has passed away , and the true light has shined .
&quot; If a man says he is in the light , and hates his brother , he is still in the darkness .
He who loves his brother lives in the light , and has no stumbling block in him
But he that hateth his brethren walketh in the darkness , and knoweth not to go therein ; for the darkness blindeth his eyes
I write to you , little children , for your sins have been forgiven in the name of the Lord
I write unto you , O fathers , because ye know that which was from the beginning ; and I write unto you , young men , because ye have overcome the wicked ; and I have written unto you , little children , because ye know the Father
I have written to you , O fathers , because you know what was from the beginning ; and I have written to you , young men , because you are strong , and the law of God is in your hearts ; and you have overcome the wicked .
Do not love the world and the things of the world . If a man loves the world , the heart of the Father is not in him
For all things in the world , like the desire of the flesh , the desire of the eyes , and the pride of this life , are not from the Father , but are from the world
This world and all the desires thereof shall pass away ; and only he that keepeth the will of God shall live forever .
Little children , now is the end , and you have heard that the coming of the enemy Christ has come , and that the coming of many enemies of Christ has come , and we know that now is the end .
They went out from among us , but they were not of us ; and if they were of us , they would still be with us ; and when they went out , they were clearly not of us .
&quot; You have been anointed by the Holy One , and know all these things .
&quot; I write to you not because you do not know the truth , but because you know , and know that no falsehood comes from the truth
Who is he who tells a lie , who does not recognize Jesus Christ ? Who does not recognize the Father and the Son , is the enemy of Christ
Whoever does not recognize a son has no father , and whoever recognizes a son has even a father .
&quot; As for you , let that which you have heard from the beginning be in your hearts ; and if that which you have heard from the beginning be in your hearts , you will live in the Son and in the Father
The Lord has promised us eternal life
&quot; I have written these words to you concerning the man who tempted you .
The anointing of the Lord is always in your hearts , and you do not teach it with men . The anointing of the Lord teaches you in all things , and it is true and not false ; and according to it you shall dwell in the Lord .
Little children , you shall dwell in the Lord ; so that when he comes , we may be without fear , and not be ashamed in his presence when he comes .
&quot; If you know that he is righteous , you will know that all the righteous are born of him
You see what kindness the Father has given us , that we may be called children of God ; and we are indeed His children ; therefore the world does not know us , but because it has not known Him
Beloved brethren , it is not yet clear what the future will be when we are children of God , but we know that if the Lord should appear , we must be like him , for we must see his true form .
&quot; Whoever has this hope in him , purify himself as he purified himself .
Whoever commits a crime is a transgressor of the law , and a transgressor of the law is a sin
You know that the Lord has appeared to remove the sins of men , and there is no sin in Him .
Whosoever dwelleth therein shall not sin ; and whosoever sinneth shall not see him , nor know him .
Little children , do not be tempted , but do righteousness , just as the Lord is righteous
The sin is of the devil , because he sinned for the devil from the beginning ; and the Son of God appeared for the purpose of destroying the devil .
He who is born of God does not sin ; for the Word of God is in his heart , and he cannot sin , for he is born of God .
From that time onward it shall be revealed who is the daughter of God , and who is the daughter of the devil ; and whosoever is not righteous , he is not of God ; and so is he who loveth not his brethren .
We shall love one another . This is the commandment which you have heard from the beginning
He belongs to the wicked one who killed his brother . Why did he kill him ? For his own deeds are evil , and the deeds of his brothers are good .
&quot; Brothers , if the world hates you , do not be ashamed
For we know , because we love our brethren , that we have come out of the dead into the living ; and those who have no love live in death
Whoever hates his brethren kills them ; and you know that whoever kills them does not live in them forever .
From this we know what love is , and we are also our brothers .
How can a heart that loves God exist in him who has all the riches of the world , and sees his brother in poverty , but has no mercy ?
Little children , let us love one another not only in words and tongues , but always in deeds and in truth .
From then on , we will know that we are of the truth , and that our hearts will be secure before God .
If our hearts reproach us , God is greater than our hearts , and knows not all things .
Beloved brethren , if our hearts do not reproach us , they will be open to God without fear
And all that we ask shall be obtained from Him , because we obey His commandments and do that which is pleasing to Him .
The commandment of God is that we should believe in the name of His Son Jesus Christ , and love one another according to the commandment which He has given us
He that keepeth the commandment of God dwelleth in him , and God dwelleth in him ; and we know that God dwelleth in us , because of the Holy Ghost which he hath given unto us
Beloved brethren , believe not all spirits , but test them whether they are of God , for many false prophets have passed through the world .
&quot; Everyone who recognizes Jesus Christ comes in the flesh and comes out of God . From then on you will recognize the Spirit of God .
&quot; Whoever does not recognize Jesus is not of God . He is the spirit of the enemy Christ . You have heard him come before , and now he is in the world .
Little children , you belong to God , and have overcome them ; for that which is in you is greater than that which is in the world .
They belong to the world ; therefore the world will listen to them concerning the things of the world
We belong to God , and those who know God obey us , and those who do not belong to God do not obey us , and from then on we shall know the Spirit of Truth and the Spirit of Falsehood .
Beloved brothers , let us love one another , for love is from God ; and whoever loves is born of God , and knows God
Whoever does not love does not know God , for love is for God
&quot; God has sent His only begotten Son into the world , and we have borrowed Him to live , and God loves our hearts .
&quot; Not because we love God , but because God loves us , the Son of God , who has redeemed us for our sins , that is love
Beloved brethren , God loves us , and we love one another
No man has ever seen God . If we love one another , God will dwell in us , and his love will be perfected in us .
God has given us His Spirit , and from that time on we know that we live in Him , and that He also lives in us
&quot; The Son of the Father is the Savior of the world . We have seen and witnessed this
&quot; Whoever recognizes Jesus as the Son of God , God lives in him , and he also lives in God
God loves our hearts , and we know and believe ; and God is love , and he who lives in love lives in God , and God lives in Him
Thus will love be perfected in us , and we will be openly fearless in the days of judgment ; for how he is , and how we are in this world
There is no fear in love . When love is perfect , it removes fear , for there is punishment for fear . Those who fear are not perfect in love
We love , because God loves us first .
&quot; If a man says , &apos; I love God , &apos; but hates his brothers , he is lying ; and if he does not love the brothers he sees , he will not love the God he does not see .
Beloved of God , beloved as brothers : this is our commandment from God
Whoever believes that Jesus is Christ , he is born of God ; and whoever loves the God of his birth , he also loves the Son of God
&quot; If we love God and obey His commandments , we will know our children who love God
We obey the commandments of God , and love Him ; and His commandments are not hard to keep .
For he that is born of God shall prevail over the world ; and our faith shall prevail over the world .
Who is greater than the world ? Is it not the faith that Jesus is the Son of God ?
This is Jesus Christ , who came by water and blood ; not by water alone , but by water and blood
And the Holy Spirit bears witness , for the Holy Spirit is the truth
And there were three witnesses : the Holy Spirit , and water , and blood : and they were all one
For we have received the witness of men , and more so the witness of God ; for the witness of God was made for his son .
He who believes in the Son of God has this testimony in his heart ; and he who does not believe in God is a liar , because he does not believe in the testimony of God for his son
&quot; This is the testimony that God gave to us for everlasting life , which is also in His Son
A man shall have a son of God , and a son without God shall have no life .
&quot; I have written these words to you who believe in the name of the Son of God , that you may know that you have eternal life .
&quot; Whatsoever we ask of Him , He hears us ; and this is our fearless heart toward Him .
Knowing that He hears all that we ask , we know that what we ask of Him is right
&quot; If a man sees a brother committing a sin that is not worthy of death , pray for him , and God will give him life ; and if there is a sin that is worthy of death , I say not that he should pray for it .
All that is unrighteous is a sin , and there is a sin that shall not perish
We know that whoever is born of God will not sin ; and whoever is born of God will keep himself ; and the wicked will not be able to harm him .
We know that we belong to God ; and the whole world is under the hand of the wicked .
We also know that the Son of God has come and has given us wisdom , that we may know the true One , and that we are in the true One , in His Son Jesus Christ , who is the true God and eternal
Little children , guard yourselves , and avoid idols .
As an elderly letter to the anointed wife , and to his children , which I love sincerely , and which I love not only , but also all those who know the truth .
Love is for the truth , which is in us , and will be with us forever
Grace , mercy , and peace , from God the Father and His Son , Jesus Christ , in truth and love , will always be with us
&quot; When I see your children , I rejoice that they do the truth as we are commanded by our Father
Madam , I am admonishing you , that we should all love one another . This is not a new commandment that I write to you , but one that we have received from the beginning
&quot; If we obey His commandments , this is love ; and this is the commandment which you heard from the beginning
For many wicked men have come out of the world , and they have not recognized Jesus Christ as a flesh : that is the wicked , the enemy of Christ
Be careful not to lose the work which you have done , but to receive a reward of satisfaction .
Whoever passes the lesson of Christ and does not keep it , there is no God ; and whoever keeps it , there is a father and a son .
&quot; If anyone comes to you , he will not be preached , nor will he be received at home , nor will he be asked for peace
For he who asks for his peace has a share in his evil deeds
I have many things to write to you , and I do not want to write them ink ; but I look forward to being with you , to speak to you in person , and to satisfy your joy .
Your chosen sisters and your daughters ask you for peace .
&quot; As for Judah , who wrote to his beloved for a long time , he is the beloved of my heart
I wish you , my beloved brother , to prosper in all things , as your soul prospers
Behold , there are brethren who testify to the truth which is in your heart , and I am glad that you do according to the truth
I have heard my children walk in the truth , and my joy is greater than this
Beloved brothers , all that you do to your fellow travellers is faithful
They have proved your love before the Church . If you are worthy of God to help them go forward , it is all right
For they are the name of the Lord , which is not taken away from the Gentiles .
Therefore we should receive such men , that we may work with them for the truth
I wrote briefly to the church , but Diocletian , the chief of the church , did not receive us
&quot; If therefore I go , it is necessary to say that what he has done is that he deceives us with evil words , and is not sufficient ; he does not receive the brethren himself , and there are those who are willing to receive him , and he forbids them , and he will drive out of the church those who receive them
Beloved brothers , do not do evil , but do good . The good belongs to God , and the evil has never seen God .
And there were witnesses to him , and there were witnesses to him of the truth ; and we also testified to him , and you know that our testimony is true .
I had many things to write to you , but I did not want to write to you in pencil
But we look forward to seeing you soon , and we shall speak in front of you
Peace be upon you . All your friends ask you for peace . Please ask for peace for me by your name .
The servant of Jesus Christ , the brother of Jacob , Judas , wrote to him who was called , and loved in the Father God , and kept him for Jesus Christ .
May mercy , peace , mercy , and abundance be added to you
Beloved brothers , I have written to you with all my heart , and I must write to you in a time of salvation , to persuade you to contend hard for the truth which was delivered to the saints from the first time .
For there are men who steal and come in , and have been condemned from ancient times , and have not been pious , and have turned the grace of our God into an opportunity for indulgence , and have not recognized the one who rules over us , our Lord Jesus Christ , or be with us .
&quot; The Lord saved His people from the land of Egypt and destroyed those who did not believe . You know all these things , but I will awaken you .
And there are angels who depart from their places of dwelling , and they are bound in chains by the Lord in darkness , waiting for the judgment of the great day
Like Sodom , Moor , and all the cities around them , they are punished with eternal fire for their sexual lusts , and for their desires to be rebellious .
&quot; These dreamers are like their defiled bodies , who are weak in the Lord &apos;s authority , who detest the glory .
&quot; But Michael , the chief angel , did not dare to blame Moses for the body and the devil in the time of the argument , but said , &quot; The Lord is blaming you
But they blasphemed that which they did not know , and in that they defeated themselves in that which they knew by nature , as the beasts that have no spirit .
Woe unto them ! for they have walked in the way of the hidden , and have strayed in the error of Leah unto Balaam , and have perished in the rebellion of Korah .
&quot; These are the rocks when they eat with you in your seats of love . They are shepherds , and know nothing but to feed themselves , and have no fear . There is no rain , and the wind is blown away . There is no fruitful tree in autumn , and it dies and dies , and its roots are cut out .
The waves of the sea pour out their own shameful drops . The stars are scattered , and darkness is black and black for ever .
The seventh son of Adam , Enoch , prophesied to these men , saying , &quot; Behold , the Lord comes with his thousands of saints
Judgment shall be done on the face of all the people , confirming that the most disobedient man has done all that is disobedient , and confirming the words of the disobedient sinner that are against him .
&quot; These hearts speak privately , they complain often , they act according to their own desires , they exaggerate in their mouths , they flatter others for their own gain
Beloved brothers , remember the words of the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ
&quot; They said to you , &apos; In the last days there will be a goodly reproacher who will do according to his own ungodly desires .
&quot; These are the ones who are drawn together in blood , and have no Holy Spirit .
Beloved brothers , make yourselves in the Holy Path , and pray in the Holy Spirit .
Keep yourselves always in the love of God , and look on the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ , straight to eternal life
&quot; Some have doubts , and you have pity for them .
Some of you will rescue them out of the fire ; some of you will have compassion on them in fear ; and even the garments that are stained with lust will be disliked .
that he may keep you from losing your feet , and that you may stand before His glory without blemish and with joy , the only God our Savior
Blessed be the glory , the might , the power , and the dominion , that they may return to Him , our Lord Jesus Christ , from the ancient times , even to the present , even to ever and ever . Amen .
The revelation of Jesus Christ , which God gave him , that he might direct all his servants to the things that are to be done soon ; and he sent messengers to speak to his servant John
John proved the word of God , and the testimony of Jesus Christ , all that he had seen
Blessed is he who remembers the prophecy of this book , and he who hears it , and keeps what is written therein ; for the day is near .
John wrote to the seven churches of Assyria : &quot; May the God who is from the ancients to the present , and who will live forever after them , and the seven Spirits before his throne ,
Blessed be He that beareth witness in truth , and is first raised from the dead , Jesus Christ , the head of the kingdoms of the world : and peace be unto you , because he hath loved us , and hath cleansed us from our sins with his own blood ;
And made us a nation , and a priest unto the God of his father ; and let the glory be given unto him , straight unto ever and ever . Amen .
Behold , he is come down in the clouds , and all the eyes shall see him , and all those who have struck him shall see him , and all the nations of the earth shall weep for him , for it is true .
&quot; I am Arafat , &quot; says the Lord God , &quot; and I am Omenkan , the Almighty , who has been in the past , and is in the present , and will be in the future
&quot; I John , your brother , share with you in the affliction , the kingdom , and the patience of Jesus , in the way of God , and in the testimony given to Jesus , on the island of the sea , which is called Bethlehem ,
And it came to pass on the Sabbath day , when I was moved by the Holy Spirit , that I heard a great voice speaking like a trumpet behind me
And what you have seen , when it is written in the book , the seven churches of Dan and Ephesus , and of Shechem , and of Becam , and of Thujah , and of Zedekiah , and of Phirah , and of Laodicea ,
&quot; I turned around to see who spoke to me . Then I turned around and saw seven golden lamps
And in the middle of the lampstand was a man like a child , clothed in a robe , hanging straight to his feet , and bound in his breast with a band of gold .
His head and his hair are white , like white wool , like snow , and his eyes like fire .
The feet are like brass in a furnace , and the voice is like the voice of waters .
His right hand had seven stars , and out of his mouth came a sword with two edges , and his face was as bright as a sunshine .
And when I heard it , I fell at his feet like a dead man , and he pressed his right hand upon me , saying , Fear not : I am the first , and I am the last .
I have died , and I am alive , and I live for ever and ever , and I hold the key to death and hell .
Therefore write down what you have seen , and what is present , and what will be done in the future
And concerning the seven stars which thou seest in my right hand , and the mystery of the seven golden lamps , which are the angels of the seven churches , and the seven lamps are the seven churches
&quot; You shall write to the apostles of the church of Ephesus , saying , &apos; The man with the right hand who walks among the seven golden lamps with seven stars ,
&quot; I know your works , your hard work , your patience ; and I know that you cannot tolerate the wicked ; and you have tested those who call themselves apostles , but are not apostles , and have seen that they are false .
&quot; You also have patience , and have labored for My name , and have not been weary .
&quot; But one thing I have to reproach thee is that thou hast forsaken the love of the beginning
&quot; Remember , therefore , where you fell , and repent of what you did in the beginning ; and if you do not repent , I will come to you and remove your lampstand from its place .
&quot; But there is another thing that is acceptable to you , which is that you hate the conduct of the party of Nicaragua , which I also hate .
&quot; He who has ears shall hear what the Holy Spirit has said to the churches ; and he who wins , I will give him the fruit of the tree of life in the Garden of God to eat
&quot; You shall write to the apostles of the church of Caesarea , saying , &apos; The first , the last , the dead and the living
I know thy affliction , thy poverty , and thy riches ; and I know the blasphemy of the Jews , which they claim to be ; for they are not Jews , but of the congregation of Satan .
Thou shalt have no fear of the affliction which thou shalt suffer ; and the devil shall put some of you in prison , that ye may be tested ; and ye shall suffer ten days ; and I will give the crown of life unto thee , that thou mayest be faithful unto death .
He who has ears shall hear what the Holy Spirit says to the churches ; and he who wins shall not suffer the second death .
&quot; You shall write to the apostles of the church of Beth Gama , saying ,
I know that thy dwelling place is the seat of Satan ; and thou hast kept my name , and not forsaken my way , when Antipas , a faithful witness among you , was killed in the place where Satan dwelled .
&quot; But there are certain things that I have to reproach you for , because there is a man who has obeyed the teachings of Balaam , who taught him that he would lay stones of stumbling block before the children of Israel , that they might eat of the idols and commit adultery
And there are also in your midst men who have obeyed the lesson of the party of Nicaragua
So when you repent , and if you do not repent , I will come to you with my sword in my mouth , and attack them
&quot; He who has ears shall hear what the Holy Spirit has said to the churches . If he wins , shall I give him that which is hidden , and give him a white stone , on which is written a new name , which no man knows except he who receives it
&quot; You shall write to the apostle of the church of the Torah , saying , &apos; The Son of God , whose eyes are like fire and whose feet like brass ,
I know your deeds , your love , your faith , your hard work , your patience , and the good things that you have done after the end , more than what you did at the beginning
&quot; But one thing I have to reproach thee is that thou hast allowed the prophetic woman , Jezebel , to lead my servants to adultery , and to eat idols
I gave him the opportunity to repent , but he refused to repent of his adultery
Behold , I will cause him to lay sick in bed ; and those who have committed adultery with him , if they do not repent of what they have done , I will cause them great tribulation .
&quot; And I will kill his party , that the church may know that I am the watcher of the hearts and the souls of men , and I will recompense every one of you according to your deeds .
&quot; The rest of you , Tuia and Tula , are all men who do not learn from that lesson , and do not know the depth of the wisdom of Satan , which they often speak . I tell you , I will not lay any other burden on you .
&quot; But as for you , you have passed through some of them , so hold fast , and wait until I come .
&quot; I will give him power to overthrow the nations , if he will prevail and keep My commandments to the end .
He will judge them with a rod of iron , and he will break them down like a pottery , like the power I received from my father .
I will give him the morning star again
&quot; Everyone who has ears should listen to what the Holy Spirit says to the churches
&quot; You shall write to the apostles of the church of Zedekiah , saying , &apos; The seven Spirits of God and the seven stars , I know your deeds , and by your name you are alive and indeed dead .
Be watchful , and stand firm , and the rest shall be weakened ; for I have seen your deeds in the sight of my God , and none of them is perfect .
Therefore remember how you received and heard , and observe and repent ; and if you do not watch , I will come to you as a thief ; and how long will I come , you will not know .
Yet there are some of you in Sadducee who have not defiled their own garments ; and they shall go with me in white , for they are well-dressed .
&quot; Whoever overcomes shall be clothed in white , and I will not blot out his name from the book of life ; and I will confess his name before my Father and before my father &apos;s apostles .
&quot; Everyone who has ears should listen to what the Holy Spirit says to the churches
&quot; You shall write to the apostles of the church of the Philistines , saying , &apos; The Holy One , the True One , who has the key of David , when he is opened , no one can turn it on ; when he is closed , no one can turn it on ;
I know your deeds , and you have a little strength , and have kept my ways , and have not forsaken my name . Behold , I have given you a door open before you , which no man can shut .
&quot; When the people of Satan , who claimed to be Jews , were not Jews , but lying , I will make them worship before your feet , and I will make them know that I have fallen in love with you
&quot; If you keep my patience , I will keep you from your trials in the time of trials in all the earth .
&quot; I will come quickly , and you will keep all that you have , lest someone take away your crown .
I will make him a pillar in the house of my God , and he will no longer go out of it ; and I will write on him the name of my God , and the name of my city , which is the new Jerusalem , which came down from heaven from my God , and my new name .
&quot; Everyone who has ears should listen to what the Holy Spirit says to the churches
&quot; You shall write to the apostles of the church of old Deca , saying , &apos; This is for the Lord , for the faithful and true witness , for the first of all that God has created ,
I know your deeds , and you are neither cold nor hot , and I fear you neither cold nor hot
&quot; Behold , you are as hot water , neither cold nor hot ; therefore I will spit you out of my mouth
&quot; You say , &apos; I am rich , and have been given abundance , and there is no lack of it ; but you do not know that you are the poor , the needy , the poor , the blind , the naked .
&quot; I urge you to buy me the gold of fire , so that you may be rich , and to put on white robes , so that your shame of your nakedness may not be revealed , and to buy your eyes to wash , so that you may see
&quot; I reproach him who loves me and teaches him ; therefore be thou filled with enthusiasm and repentance
&quot; Behold , I am standing outside the door knocking at the door ; and if anyone hears my voice , he will open the door , and I will enter into him , and I will sit with him , and he will sit with me
&quot; I will give him to sit with me in my throne , just as I have won and sat with him in my father &apos;s throne .
&quot; Everyone who has ears should listen to what the Holy Spirit says to the churches
Then I looked and saw that the heavens had opened , and I heard the sound of a trumpet for the first time , and said to me , &quot; Come up here , and I will tell you what will be done after you .
Immediately I was moved by the Spirit , and saw a throne placed in heaven , and another sitting on it
Behold , he who sits is like a jewel of blue and a stone of red ; and a rainbow surrounds the throne like a stone of green .
Around the altar were twenty-four seats , and upon them sat twenty-four elders in white robes , bearing golden crowns on their heads .
And lightning and sound and thunder came out of the throne , and seven lamps were set before the throne , seven of which were the seven Spirits of God .
There are four living creatures in the throne and around it , and they are full of eyes , both before and behind .
The first creature was like a lion , the second like a calf , the third like a man , and the fourth like an eagle
The four living creatures each have six wings , and they are full of eyes all over their bodies ; and those who do not dwell day and night say , &quot; Holy , holy , holy , Lord God , the Almighty , who is from the past to the present , and to come .
Every fourth living creature shall be given glory , honour , and thanksgiving to him who sits on the throne , and shall live to the time of the far off
Then the twenty-four elders bowed down before the throne , and worshipped the living forever and ever , and put their crowns before the throne ,
Blessed are You , our Lord , our God , who created all things , and all things were created by Your will .
And I saw in the right hand of the sitting throne a scroll , written in writing , sealed with seven seals ,
And I saw again a mighty angel proclaiming with a loud voice : Who is it that will open the book , and uncover the seven seals ?
There is no one in heaven , or on earth , or under the earth , who can open the book , or look at it .
&quot; I cried out for the book , because it had not been opened , because it had not been seen .
And one of the elders said unto me , Weep not : behold , the lion of the tribe of Judah , the root of David , hath won , and hath opened the book , and hath opened the seven seals .
And I saw in the throne , and in the four living creatures , and in the elders , a lamb standing , as though he had been slain , and seven horns and seven eyes , seven Spirits of God sent to the whole world .
&quot; The lamb came and took the scroll from the right hand of the throne
And he took the scrolls , and the four living creatures , and the twenty-four elders , and bowed down before the lambs , each with a harp , and a golden fire full of incense , which was the prayer of the saints
They sang a new song , saying , &quot; Take a book , and uncover seven seals ; for you have been slain , and bought people from every tribe and people and country with your blood , that they may return to God .
&quot; And that they may be a nation , and priests , and belong to God , and rule over the earth
And I saw again , and heard , and beside the throne and the living creatures and the ancients were many voices of angels , and their number was thousands and thousands and thousands
Saying with a loud voice , &quot; The Lamb who was slain is given power , riches , wisdom , power , honor , glory , and praise
&quot; And I heard again from all that is in heaven , and on earth , and under the earth , and in the sea , and in the heavens , and in all that is created , saying , &apos; Blessed be the seated and the Lamb , and the glory and the glory and the power , for ever and ever .
And the four beasts said , Amen ; and the elders bowed down and worshipped
When I saw the Lamb uncover the first of the seven seals , I heard the voice of one of the four living creatures sounding like a thunder , saying , Come
And I looked , and behold a white horse riding on the right hand with a bow , and a crown was given to him ; and he came out , and he won , and he would win .
When the second seal was opened , I heard the second creature say , &quot; Come
Then came forth another horse , a red one ; and he that had power over the horse , he could take it from the earth , and slay one another ; and he had given him a great sword .
And it came to pass , when the third seal was opened , that I heard the third creature say , Come , and I looked , and behold a black horse , riding in the hand of the horse , holding the balance
I heard in the four living creatures a voice saying , &quot; One silver for a litre of wheat , and one silver for three litres of barley , and oil and wine must not be wasted
When the fourth seal was opened , I heard the fourth creature say , &quot; Come
And I looked , and behold a gray horse , and he that rideth on it is called to death , and the valley is with him ; and he hath given them power to slay with the sword , and with the famine , and with the pestilence , and with the beasts , and to slay a quarter of the people of the earth .
&quot; When I opened the fifth seal , I saw under the altar the way of God and the soul of the slain as a witness
Saying with a loud voice , &quot; How long , O Lord , Holy and True , will you not judge the bloodshed of those who dwell on the earth ?
Then the white garments were given to each one of them , and words were spoken to them , saying , &quot; I will take a sabbath , and wait for the number of those who serve with me and their brothers , as they were slain . &quot;
When I opened the sixth seal , I saw again the great shaking of the earth : the sun turned black as a cloth , and the moon turned red as blood .
The morning of the stars in the sky falls upon the earth like a fruitless tree shaken by the wind , and a ripe fruit falling .
And the heavens were moved as if scrolls were rolled up , and the mountains and the islands were moved away from their places .
The kings of the earth , the princes , the generals , the rich , the mighty , and all that are slaves , and all that are free , are hidden in caves and rocky pits
&quot; Say to the mountains and to the rocks , &apos; Get down on us , and hide us from the face of those who sit on the throne , and from the wrath of the Lamb .
For the great day of their wrath is come ; who can stand ?
Then I saw four angels standing on the four corners of the earth , holding the wind on all sides of the earth , that the wind should not blow on the earth , on the sea , and on the trees
Then I saw another angel coming up from the land of the sun and bearing the seal of the eternal God , and he cried with a loud voice to the four angels who had power to harm the land and the sea ,
&quot; You shall not harm the earth and the sea , nor the trees , until we have sealed the face of our servants ,
And I heard the number of the children of Israel , and the number of the tribes that were sealed , was forty-four thousand .
Of the tribe of Judah were sealed twelve thousand ; of the tribe of Reuben twelve thousand ; of the tribe of Gad twelve thousand .
Of the tribe of Asheah were twelve thousand ; of the tribe of Naphtali were twelve thousand ; of the tribe of Manasseh were twelve thousand
Of the Simeonites , there were twelve thousand ; of the Levites , twelve thousand ; of the Issacharites , twelve thousand .
Of the tribe of West Branch were twelve thousand ; of the tribe of Joseph were twelve thousand ; of the tribe of Benjamin were twelve thousand sealed .
Then I looked , and behold , a great multitude came from every nation , from every tribe , and from every nation , standing before the throne and before the Lamb , clothed in white , with palm branches in their hands .
A loud voice cried out , &quot; May salvation be with the God who sits on the throne , and with the Lamb
And all the angels stood before the throne , and the elders , and the four living creatures , and bowed themselves to the ground , and worshipped God
Praise , glory , wisdom , thanksgiving , honor , power , and might belong to our God , straight to ever and ever .
Then one of the elders asked me , &quot; Who are these in white robes , and from where do they come
I said to him , &quot; You know , my Lord , &quot; and he said to me , &quot; These men have come out of great tribulation , and have washed their garments with the blood of lambs ,
So they served him in the presence of the throne of God , day and night , in his temple ; and those who sat on the throne shall cover them with a tent .
No more hunger , no more thirst ; neither will the sun and the heat harm them .
For the lambs of the throne shall feed them , and bring them to the fountain of life ; and God shall wash away all their tears .
And it came to pass at the time when the Lamb opened the seventh seal , that there was two hours of silence in heaven
I saw the seven angels who stood before God , and seven branches were given to them
And there stood by the altar an angel with a fire of gold , and many perfumes were given to him , to be offered together with the prayers of the saints on the altar before the throne
The smoke and the prayers of the saints were lifted up from the hands of the angels before God .
And the angel took a fireplace , and filled the altar with fire , and fell upon the earth ; and there was thunder , and loudness , and lightning , and earthquake .
And he prepared to blow with the seven angels of the seven branches
And the first angel blew , and hail and fire with blood fell upon the earth ; and a third of the earth and a third of the trees were burned , and all the grass was burned .
And the second angel blew , and there was cast into the sea a great mountain as if it were burning with fire , and a third of the sea became blood .
A third of the animals in the sea died and a third of the ships were destroyed
And the third angel blew , and there was a burning star , as if fire had fallen from heaven , and had fallen on a third of the rivers , and on the fountains of the waters of the people
And the name of the star was Rhine ; and a third of all the waters became Rhine ; and many people died because the waters became bitter
And the fourth angel blew a trumpet , and a third of the sun , and a third of the moon , and a third of the morning of the stars were struck , and a third of the stars of the day and the moon were darkened , and a third of the day and the day were lightless , and so was the night .
And I saw again an eagle flying in the air , and heard him say with a loud voice , &quot; Woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe , woe ! &quot;
Then the fifth angel blew , and I saw a star falling from heaven to the earth , and the key of a pitless pit was given to him .
He opened a pit without foundation , and smoke came up from the pit like the smoke of a great furnace , and the sun and the sky were darkened by it .
Then came locusts out of the smoke and flew to the earth ; and the power was given them as the power of a scorpion on the earth .
And they said unto them , Thou shalt not hurt the grass of the earth , and all the greenery , and all the trees , save those upon whom there is no sign of God .
But let not the locust kill them , but let them suffer for five months , as the scorpion stings a man .
In those days , people will seek to die , but they will not die ; and they will die , but they will be far from them .
The appearance of locusts is like the appearance of horses ready for war , and the crown of gold on their heads , and their faces like the faces of men .
Hair is like the hair of a woman , and teeth like the teeth of a lion
They have armor before their chests , like iron armor ; and the voice of their wings , like the voice of many chariots running forth .
There is a tail like a scorpion . A poison hook on the tail can hurt a person for five months
And there were messengers without a pit to be their kings : and the name of the Hebrews was Abiathar , and the name of the Hebrews was Abiaron ,
The first calamity is gone , and two more are to come
Then the sixth angel blew , and I heard a voice coming out of the four corners of the altar before God
And the sixth angel that blew the trumpet commanded him , saying , Release the four messengers that were bound by the River of Berlah .
And the four apostles were released ; and they were prepared to kill a third of the people by the time of a year or a month
There were twenty-one million horsemen . I heard their numbers
And I saw in the parable horses and riders , and in the breasts of the riders were armor like fire , and purple navy , and sulfur ; and the heads of the horses were like the heads of lions , and there was fire , and smoke , and sulfur , coming out of the mouths of the horses
Fire and smoke and sulfur from the mouth have killed one third of the people .
The power of the horse is in his mouth and in his tail ; for his tail is like a snake , and his head is for the slaughter of men .
Those who were not slain by these plagues still repent not of their own hands , but go to the devils , and to the idols of gold , silver , copper , wood , stone , which cannot see , hear , walk .
And not repent of their murders , and of their evil deeds , and of their adultery , and of their stealth
And I saw another mighty angel come down from heaven , clothed in clouds , and with rainbows on his head ; and his face was like the sun , and his feet like pillars of fire .
He had a small book in his hand and it was open . He walked on his right foot to the sea and on his left foot to the ground
And there was a great cry , as a lion crieth : and when the cry was finished , seven thunderbolts sounded
And it came to pass after the sound of the seven thunderbolts , when I was writing , that I heard a voice from heaven saying , &quot; You shall seal what the seven thunderbolts have said , and it shall not be written .
&quot; And the angel of the sea , whom I saw , lifted up his right hand to heaven ,
&quot; He who created the heavens and all that is on them , the earth and all that is on the earth , the sea and all that is in the sea , will live for ever and ever , and will swear that there will be no more delay .
But when the seventh angel blew his trumpet , the mystery of God was fulfilled , as God had spoken to all the prophets of His servants .
Then the voice which I had heard from heaven commanded me , saying , &quot; Go and take away the book which the angel of the sea had spread out in his hand .
Then I went to the angel , and said to him , &quot; Please give me the scroll , &quot; and he said to me , &quot; When you have eaten all that you have , it will make your belly and your hair weep , but it will be sweet in your mouth as honey
And I took the scroll out of the angel &apos;s hand , and I ate it all , and it was sweet as honey in my mouth ; and after I ate it , my belly was sore
And the angel said unto me , Thou shalt prophesy again concerning many people , and many nations , and many kings ;
A reed was given to me as a staff for measuring ; and it was said , &quot; Arise , and measure the house of God , and the altar , and all those who worship in it
&quot; It is only the courts outside the temple that will be left without measure ; for it was given to the foreigners , and they will trample the Holy City for forty-two months .
&quot; I will make my two witnesses to preach for a thousand two hundred and sixty days , clothed in linen
They are the two olive trees , the two lampstands , standing before the Lord of the world .
&quot; If any man seeks to harm them , fire shall come out of their mouths and devour their enemies ; and whoever seeks to harm them shall be killed in this manner .
These two have power to make the day not to rain in the days they preach , and to turn the waters into blood , and to attack the world with all kinds of calamity at any time
&quot; When they have finished bearing witness , the beast that comes up from the bottomless pit will fight with them , and he will prevail , and he will kill them
And their dead bodies fell in the streets of the great city , which was called by the Spirit Sodom , and Egypt , where their Lord was crucified .
&quot; For three and a half days there were people from all nations and tribes and countries looking at their bodies , and they were not allowed to be laid in graves .
Then the inhabitants of the earth rejoiced and gave gifts to each other , because the two prophets had caused the inhabitants of the earth to suffer
And after these three and a half days , when the spirit of God entered into them , they stood up , and behold , their people were afraid .
When the two prophets heard a loud voice coming up from heaven , they said to them , &quot; Come up here , &quot; and they rode on the clouds , and their enemies saw them .
At that time there was a great earthquake , and one tenth of the cities fell down . Seven thousand died because of the earthquake , and the rest feared and glorified the God of heaven .
The second scourge is gone . The third scourge is near
Then the seventh angel blew , and there was a loud voice in heaven , saying , &quot; The kingdom of the world has become the kingdom of my Lord and the Lord Christ , and he will reign for ever and ever .
And the twenty-four elders who sat upon their seats before God worshipped God on their faces ,
&quot; We thank You , O Lord Almighty , who is in the past and in the present , because You have taken over the kingdom with great power
The wrath of the nations has come , and your wrath has come , and the time has come to judge the dead , and the reward of your servants , and of your prophets , and of your saints , and of all those who fear your name , small and great , and the time has come to destroy those who have destroyed the world .
Then the house of God in heaven opened , and his ark appeared in his house ; and there followed lightning , and sound , and thunder , and earthquake , and hail .
And a great vision appeared in heaven , a woman clothed with the sun , and on her feet the moon , and on her head a crown of twelve stars .
He was pregnant , crying painfully in the hardships of production
And another vision appeared in heaven : a great dragon , with seven heads of ten horns , and seven crowns on seven heads .
And his tail dragged a third of the stars of heaven upon the earth , and the dragon stood before the woman that was to give birth , and ate his child after he had given birth .
A woman has a son in her life , who in the future will rule all the nations with a rod of iron . His son has been mentioned in the throne of God
And the woman fled to the wilderness , where God had prepared a place for her , and she bore him a thousand two hundred and sixty days
There was a battle in heaven . Michael fought with his angels against the dragon , and the dragon fought with his angels .
And there is no victory , and there is no place for them in heaven .
The dragon was the old serpent , the devil , and Satan , the one that troubled the whole earth ; and he was thrown down on the earth , and his messengers were thrown down with him
&quot; I heard a great voice in heaven say , &apos; The salvation , the power , the kingdom , and the power of my God , Christ , has come ; for those who accuse our brethren day and night before our God have been cast down .
The brethren are greater than he , because of the blood of the Lamb , and because of the way they witnessed : and they love not the life , though they die
&quot; Therefore rejoice in the heavens and in those who dwell therein ; but evil is the land and the sea ; for the devil is come down to you in wrath , because he has little time to know himself .
When the dragon saw that he was thrown to the ground , he pressed the woman who had the son
And there were two wings of the eagle given to the woman , that he might fly into the wilderness , to his own place , to hide himself from the snake , and there he would be kept alive for a load and a load and a half
And the serpent came after the woman , and poured out water out of her mouth , like a river , and slew her .
And the earth helped the woman , and opened her mouth , and swallowed up the water that came out of the mouth of the dragon .
And when the dragon was angry with the woman , he went out to fight with the rest of his daughters , which were witnesses to Jesus to keep the commandments of God , and stood on the sand of the sea .
And I saw another beast come up out of the sea , having ten horns and seven heads , and on the ten horns he had ten crowns , and on the seven heads a defiled name .
And the beast that I saw was like a leopard , and his feet like the feet of a bear , and his mouth like the mouth of a lion ; and the dragon gave him his power , and his seat , and his great power .
And I saw in the seven heads of the beast a man that seemed to have been injured , and was healed : and all the people of the land followed him .
And worship the dragon , because he has given his power to the beasts ; and worship the beasts , saying , Who can fight against him than this beast ?
And He gave him the tongue of blasphemy , and He gave him the power to do forty-two months at will .
And the beast opened his mouth unto God , and blasphemed the name of God , and His tabernacle , and those who dwell in heaven
And they entrusted him to fight with the saints , and they won ; and they gave him power , and overthrew nations , and peoples , and countries .
&quot; Everyone who lives on the earth , and whose name has not been written in the book of life of the slain Lamb since the beginning of the world , shall worship Him
Whoever has ears , let him hear .
Those who plunder shall be plundered , and those who kill with the sword shall be killed . Here is the patience and faith of the saints
Then I saw another beast come up from the earth , having two horns like lambs , and speaking like a dragon
And he will be before the first beast , and will do all the power of the first beast ; and he will call upon the land and the inhabitants of the earth to the first beast that is dead and healed .
And great wonders were done , even before men , that fire came down from heaven upon the earth
He troubled those who dwell on the earth , because he had given him power to do miracles in the presence of beasts , saying , &quot; Make a likeness to the beast that is still alive , that is wounded by the sword
and power was given to him to make the likeness of the beast angry , and to speak , and to kill all those who do not worship the likeness of the beast
And he made a sign upon all that were slaves , whether they were rich or poor , independent , in their right hand or on their foreheads .
&quot; No trade shall be made except that on which a seal is printed , the name of the beast is given , or the number of the names of the beast is given
There is wisdom in this place : and whosoever is wise , let him count the number of the beasts : for this is the number of man , and his number is six hundred sixty-six .
And I looked again , and behold , the Lamb stood on mount Zion , and with him were forty-four thousand men , all having his name and the name of his father written on their foreheads
I have heard a voice from heaven , like the sound of waters , and the sound of thunder ; and what I have heard is like the sound of a harp .
And they sang before the throne , and before the four living creatures , and before the elders , as if it were a new song : but none could learn it , save the forty-four thousand that were bought from the earth .
&quot; They had not touched women ; they were children ; and wherever the Lamb went , they followed him ; and they were bought of men for the first fruits to God and to the Lamb .
There is no lie in their mouths . They are without defects .
I also saw another angel flying in the air , and the gospel of a long way to be preached to those who dwell on the earth , nations and tribes and peoples
He cried out , &quot; You should fear God , and He will give you glory ; for the time of His judgment has come , and you should worship Him who created the heavens and the sea and the springs of all waters .
Then the second angel said , &quot; The great city of Babylon has fallen , the city of Babylon , which has caused all the people to drink the wine of great anger ,
Then came the third angel , and they spake with a loud voice , saying , &quot; If a man worships beasts and images of beasts , it will be marked on his forehead or on his hand
And he shall drink the wine of the wrath of God , pure in the cup of the wrath of God ; and he shall suffer in the presence of the angels and of the Lamb , in the midst of fire and sulfur .
And the smoke of his torment shall go up , and it shall go forth for ever and ever ; and those who worship beasts and beasts , and are inscribed in His name , shall not be at ease day and night .
Here is the patience of the saints , who keep the commandments of God and the truth of Jesus
&quot; I heard a voice from heaven say , &apos; Write , &apos; Blessed are those who die in the Lord from now on , &apos; and the Holy Spirit says , &apos; Yes , they have suffered their own labour , and the fruit of their labor is with them .
And I looked again , and behold a white cloud , and on it sat a man like a man , with a crown of gold on his head , and a sickle in his hand .
Then another angel came out of the temple , and cried out to him who sat on the cloud , saying , &quot; Stretch out your sickle to harvest ; for the time of harvest is come , and the crops of the earth are ripe .
And he who sits on the cloud casts down his sickle on the earth , and the crops of the earth are harvested .
And another angel came out of the temple of heaven , and he also had a sharp sickle
And another angel came out of the altar , having power over the fire , and cried with a loud voice to him who had a sharp sickle , and stretched out his sharp sickle to take the fruit of the vines of the earth , because the vines were ripe .
Then the angel cast down the sickle on the earth , and took the grapes of the earth , and cast them into the great winepress of the wrath of God
And when the winepress was thrown out of the city , blood came out of the winepress , high to the chewing ring of the horse , six hundred miles away .
And I saw again in heaven a vision , great and marvelous , of the seven final plagues , which the seven angels had ruled : for the wrath of God was consumed in them
And I saw as if there were a sea of glass , and fire was mixed therein ; and I saw the likeness of the beasts and of the beasts , and of men whose names were numbered , standing on the sea of glass , holding the harp of God .
Sing the song of Moses , the servant of God , and the song of the Lamb , saying , &quot; O Lord God , Almighty , how great is your work , O King of the worlds , and how righteous and true is your way !
Who will not fear thee , O LORD , and bring glory to thy name ? for thou art holy alone : and all the people shall come to worship before thee , because thy righteousness is manifested .
Then I saw the house of the ark opened in heaven
And the seven angels who were over the seven plagues came out of the temple , clothed in white and white linen , and bound in gold bands between their breasts .
One of the four living creatures gave the seven angels seven golden bowls full of the wrath of the God who lives forever and ever
For the glory and power of God filled the temple with smoke , and no man could enter it until the seven plagues which the seven angels had sent were finished .
I heard a loud voice coming out of the temple and saying to the seven angels , &quot; Go and lay down on the ground the seven bowls of the wrath of God
Then the first angel went and laid the bowl on the ground , and there was a wicked and toxic plague on those who had signs of beasts and worshipped beasts .
And the second angel cast the bowl into the sea , and the sea became blood , as the blood of the dead ; and all the living creatures of the sea were dead .
And the third angel cast the bowl into the fountain of the river and of the waters of the people , and the water became blood
&quot; I heard the angel who ruled the waters say , &apos; Your judgment , O Holy One who was and is , is righteous .
&quot; They have poured out the blood of the saints and the prophets , and now you drink their blood , and this is what they are to receive
Then I heard a voice in the altar saying , &quot; Yes , O Lord God Almighty , how righteous and how true is your judgment
And the fourth angel laid the bowl upon the head of the sun , that it might be baked with fire
&quot; He who is burned in the heat blasphemes the name of the God who has power over these evil things , and does not repent and return his glory to God
And the fifth angel laid the bowl upon the seat of the beast ; and the land of the beast was dark : and the man bit his tongue in pain .
And they blasphemed the God of heaven for the pain they had suffered , and for the wounds they had borne , and did not repent of their deeds
And the sixth angel laid the bowl upon the river , and the waters were dried up , to prepare the way for the kings that came out of the land of the sun
And I saw again three unclean spirits , like frogs , coming out of the mouth of the dragon and the mouth of the beast , and from the mouth of false prophets
They are the spirits of the devils , who do miracles , and go out to the kings of all the earth , to gather themselves together in battle on the great day of the Almighty .
&quot; Behold , I am come as a thief ; blessed is he who keeps his watch , and guards his garments , and walks without nakedness , and lets the people see his shame .
Then the three devils gathered the kings together in a place called in Hebrew Hamiddodon
Then the seventh angel cast the bowl into the air , and a loud voice came out of the throne of the temple , saying ,
There were flashes , sounds , thunderstorms , and great earthquakes , no earthquakes of such magnitude and such benefit since there were people on earth
And the great city was broken into three parts , and the cities of the nations fell down ; and God remembered the great city of Babylon , and brought to him the cup of his wrath .
The islands fled , and the mountains were not seen .
Then a great hail fell on a man from heaven , and he was joined to it by a weight of one yoke , and the hail was a great calamity , and he blasphemed God
And one of the seven angels who had the seven bowls came before me and said to me , &quot; Come here , and I will show you the punishment of the great prostitute who sits in the waters of the people .
The kings of the earth committed adultery with him ; and the inhabitants of the earth drunk of his lustful wine .
I was moved by the Spirit , and the angels took me to the wilderness , and I saw a woman riding on a beast of red , seven heads and ten horns , and a name defiled all over .
And the woman was clothed in purple and scarlet , and adorned herself with gold jewelry and pearls ; and she took a golden cup in her hand , and the cup was full of abominations : that is the filth of his prostitution .
And it was written on his forehead , O great Babylon , the prostitute of the world , and the mother of all abominations ,
And I saw the woman drinking the blood of the saints , and the blood of the witnesses to Jesus ; and when I saw him , I was greatly moved
Then said the angel to me , &quot; Why do you wonder ? I will tell you the secret of this woman and of the seven heads and ten horns of the beasts which she carried .
&quot; Behold , the beasts that you have seen were before , and are not ; they will come up from the bottomless pit , and will be brought to ruin ; and whoever lives on the earth whose name has not been written in the book of life since the beginning of the world will be astonished when he sees the beasts that were before , and are not , and the beasts that are after .
The heart of wisdom can think thereof ; and the seven heads are the seven mountains in which the woman sits .
And there are seven kings ; five have fallen , one is still , and one has not yet come ; and when he comes , he must remain for a while .
And the eighth beast , which was before , and which is not now , he was with the seven , and was in the abyss
&quot; The ten horns which you saw are the ten kings ; they have not yet obtained the kingdom ; but they shall have power as the beasts have power as the kings
They agreed with one accord , and gave their power to the beast
&quot; They will fight with the Lamb , and the Lamb will prevail over them ; for the Lamb is the Lord of all the Lord , the King of all the kings ; and he who is called with the Lamb , the faithful and chosen , will also prevail .
And the angel said unto me , Thou hast seen the multitude of the waters wherein the prostitute sat , many and many and many countries
And the ten horns which thou hast seen , and the beasts , shall hate the prostitute , and make him cold and naked , and eat his flesh , and burn him with fire .
For he made the kings to consent to God , to do his will , and to give his own kingdom to the beast , until the word of God was fulfilled
&quot; The woman whom you have seen is the great city of the kings of the land
Then I saw another angel with great power descending from heaven , and the earth was lighted for his glory .
And he cried with a loud voice , saying , The great city of Babylon is fallen down , and is fallen down , and becomes the dwelling place of the devils , and the nest of all the filthy spirits , and the nest of all the filthy fowls that hate .
For all the nations have been poured down by the wine of his wickedness , and the kings of the earth have prostituted themselves with him , and the merchants of the earth have multiplied their riches because of his luxury .
Then I heard a voice from heaven saying , &quot; My people , come out of that city , lest you sin with him , and suffer the punishment which he has suffered
For his wickedness is poured out , and his unrighteous God is remembered
As he behaves toward men , so shall he behave toward him ; and he shall be recompensed according to the doubling of what he has done ; and he shall drink a cup of his wine , a doubling of it .
For as he glorifies himself , and as he exalts himself , so shall he grieve , because he said in his heart , I am not a widow , neither am I grieved
Therefore in one day his affliction shall come together , death , sorrow , famine , and he shall be consumed by fire , for the Lord God is great in judgment .
The kings of the earth , who have been luxuriant with him in prostitution , will weep and mourn for him when they see his smoke burned .
For fear of his pain , he stood afar off , and said , &quot; Woe , woe , the great city of Babylon , the strong city ! Your punishment has come for a time
And the merchants of the earth wept for him , because no man had bought their goods any more .
The goods were gold , silver , jewels , pearls , fine linen , purple dye , silk , red dye , all kinds of fragrances , all kinds of ivory vessels , all kinds of precious wood , and all kinds of copper , iron , and Han white jade
and cinnamon , soybeans , spices , ointments , milk , wine , oil , fine flour , wheat , cattle , sheep , cars , horses , and slaves , and the people
&quot; O Babylon , the fruit of your lust has departed from you , and all your precious and beautiful things will be destroyed from among you , and will never be seen again .
&quot; The merchants who sold the goods , who borrowed money from him , stood far away crying and mourning for fear of his suffering ,
Woe , woe , O great city ! They wear fine linen , purple , and scarlet , and adorn themselves with gold , jewelry , and pearls
For in a time there will be no more such riches ; and all the captains of ships , and all that go in ships , and all the sailors , and all that work by the sea , shall stand afar off
And when they saw the smoke of his burning , they cried out , saying , What city can be greater than this ?
And they spread the dust upon their heads , crying and mourning , and crying , saying , Alas , Alas , Alas , O great city ! Whosoever has a ship in the sea , he is rich for his treasures ; and in a time he shall be a wilderness .
&quot; Rejoice in him , O God , O saints and apostles and prophets , because your iniquities have been stretched out on him for God &apos;s sake .
A mighty angel lifted up a stone like a great millstone , and cast it into the sea , saying , &quot; The great city of Babylon will be thrown down like this , and will never be seen again .
The voice of the violin , the music , the flute , the trumpet will never be heard among you ; the craftsmen will never meet among you ; the voice of the grinding will never be heard among you .
The light will never again shine in your midst ; the voice of the bride and the groom will never again be heard in your midst ; Your merchants were nobles on earth ; and the nations were perplexed by your evil deeds .
The prophet and the saints saw the blood of all the slain on the earth in this city
Then I heard the voice of a great multitude in heaven saying , &quot; Hallelujah , the salvation , the glory , and the power belong to our God
And his judgment is true and righteous : for he hath judged the great prostitute , which hath corrupted the world with prostitution ; and he hath rebuked them for the sins of the prostitute , which she hath shed with the blood of her servants .
Then he said , &quot; Halilouah , the smoke of the prostitute burns up and goes straight for ever and ever .
Then the twenty-four elders and the four living creatures bowed down and worshipped the God who sat on the throne , saying , &quot; Amen , Hallelujah
A voice came out of the throne , saying , &quot; O servants of God , whoever fears Him , let them praise our God , of whatever size they may be
I heard the voices of the multitude , the voices of the waters , the voices of the thunder , saying , &quot; Halilius , for he is our God , the Almighty , the King
&quot; We will rejoice and rejoice , and give him glory ; for the time of the Lamb &apos;s marriage has come , and the new woman has prepared herself
He will be blessed with a fine linen cloak of light and purity , which is the righteousness of the saints .
And the angel said unto me , Write , Blessed is he that is invited unto the Lamb &apos;s feast ; and he said unto me , This is the truth of God
And I fell down before his feet , and worshipped him ; and he said , Thou shalt not : for I am a servant unto thee , and unto thee , and unto thy brethren that bear witness unto Jesus ; and thou shalt worship God , because the Spirit of the prophecy beareth witness unto Jesus
When I looked , I saw the heavens opened , and there was a white horse , and he who rode on it was called faithful and true ; and he judged the battle according to righteousness .
His eyes were like fire , and many crowns were on his head ; and there were written names , but none knew them except himself .
He was clothed in blood , and his name was the way of God .
And the hosts of heaven , riding on white horses , clothed in fine linen , white and clean , followed him
And out of his mouth shall come a sword of strength , and he shall smite the nations ; and he shall rule over them with a rod of iron ; and he shall smite the winepress of the wrath of God .
In his garments and on his thighs is written , &quot; The King of the kings , the Lord of the kings ,
I saw again an angel standing in the sun , a bird flying in the sky , shouting , &quot; You are gathered together to the great feast of God
and the meat of kings and generals , and the meat of mighty men and horses and riders , and the meat of all that are freely enslaved , and the meat of people of all sizes ,
I saw the beast , and the kings of the earth , and all their hosts , gathered together to fight against the horse and his army
The beast was captured , and the one who did miracles in front of the beast , and was troubled by the mark of the beast , and by the false prophet of those who worshipped the like of the beast , was also captured with the beast ; and they were both thrown alive into the lake of fire , burning with sulfur .
The rest were slain with the sword that came out of the mouth of the horsemen , and the birds were fed with their flesh
And I saw again an angel come down from heaven , holding in his hand the key of a pit without foundation , and a great chain
He took the dragon , the old serpent , the devil , and Satan , and bound him for a thousand years
cast into the pit , and seal it with seals , so that he may no longer trouble the nations , until the thousand years have come to an end , and he shall be temporarily released .
And I saw the souls of those who were slain for the testimony of Jesus , and for the way of God , and of those who had not worshipped beasts and beasts , and had not received His seals on their foreheads and on their hands ; and they were all raised again , and were with Christ king for a thousand years
This is the first resurrection , and the rest of the dead have not yet been resurrected , as soon as the millennium is over
Blessed are they that are divided in the first resurrection , and holy , and the second death has no power over them ; and they shall be priests to God and to Christ , and shall be kings with Christ a thousand years
And when the thousand is accomplished , Satan shall be delivered out of prison
And it came to pass , that the nations that were on all sides of the earth were brought forth to trouble them , even Gog and Mark , to gather them together to battle ; and their number was as the number of the sea .
And they went up over all the land , and besieged the camps of the saints , and the city of the beloved : and fire came down from heaven , and consumed them
The place where the beasts and false prophets will be , and where their devils will be cast into the lake of fire of sulfur , they will be tormented day and night , and they will be gone forever and ever .
And I saw again a great white throne , and he that sat on it ; and the heavens and the earth fled from before him , and there was no more to be seen .
And I saw the dead , of all sizes , standing before the throne : and the book of life was opened , and another book was opened : and the dead were judged according to that which was written in the book of life , according to that which they did .
So the sea delivered the dead among them , and death and hell delivered the dead among them , and they were judged according to the works of every man .
Death and the shadow are thrown into the lake of fire , the second death .
If a man &apos;s name is not written in the book of life , he will be thrown into the lake of fire
I have seen a new heaven and a new land again ; for the former heavens have passed away , and the sea is no more .
&quot; And I saw the new Jerusalem , the holy city , which was prepared by God from heaven , as a newly dressed woman , waiting for her husband
And I heard a great voice from the throne saying , Behold , the tabernacle of God is in the midst of men , and he shall dwell with men , and they shall be his children , and God himself shall be with them , and he shall be their God
God will wipe away all their tears , and there will be no more death , no more sorrow , no more crying , no more pain , for the former things have passed away .
And he who sat on the throne said , &quot; Behold , I have renewed all things , and you shall write them down , because these words are faithful and true .
And he said unto me , All things are done : I am Arafat , and I am Omenkan , and I am the first , and I am the last ; and I will give the water of the fountain of life to drink to the thirsty man .
And the victor shall bear these things , and I shall be his God , and he shall be my son
Only the cowardly , the unbelieving , the hateful , the murderers , the adulterers , the evildoers , the idolaters , and all the liars will have their share in the lake of fire burning sulfur . This is the second death
And there came to me one of the seven angels of the seven aftermath of the seven plagues , bearing seven golden bowls , saying , Come here , and I will show you the new woman , the wife of the Lamb ,
I was moved by the Holy Spirit , and the angel took me to a high mountain , and directed me to the Holy City of Jerusalem , which God sent down from heaven .
The glory of God is in the city , and the glory of the city is as a precious stone , as a pearl , as a crystal .
And there was a high wall , and twelve gates , and twelve angels on the gates , and the names of the twelve tribes of Israel were written on the gates
There are three gates to the east , three gates to the north , three gates to the south , and three gates to the west .
The walls of the city had twelve foundations , and on the foundations were the names of the twelve Lambs
&quot; He who speaks to me shall take the golden reed as a scale to measure the city , and the walls of the gates of the city
&quot; The city is on all sides , and it is one and the same in length and breadth ; and the city is four thousand miles in length and breadth , and the height of it is one and the same in length .
And he measured the walls according to the measure of a man , the measure of an angel , one hundred forty-four cubits .
The walls are of purple , and the city of gold , as clear glass .
The foundations of the walls were decorated with various kinds of jewels : the first was a blue jewel , the second a blue jewel , the third a green marble , and the fourth a green jewel
The fifth was a red marble , the sixth a red stone , the seventh a yellow pearl , the eighth a watermelon , the ninth a red pearl , the tenth a jade , the eleventh a purple marble , the twelfth a purple crystal
The twelve gates are twelve pearls , and each gate is one pearl . The streets of the city are of gold , as clear glass .
I have not seen a house in the city for the house of the Lord God Almighty , and the Lamb
And there shall be no light of the sun nor of the moon in that city , because of the glory of God ; and there shall be a lamp for the city of the Lamb .
The nations shall walk in the light of the city ; and the kings of the earth shall return their glory to the city .
The gates of the city were never closed by day , and there was no night there
The glory of the nations shall be brought back to that city
&quot; Whoever is unclean , and does abominations and lies , shall not enter the city ; only those whose names are written in the Lamb &apos;s book of life shall enter it .
And the angel commanded me that in the streets of the city a river of water of life , bright as crystal , should flow out of the throne of God and of the Lamb
And there are trees of life on the one side of the river and on the other side of the river , bearing twelve kinds of fruit , and bearing fruit every month ; and the leaves of the tree are for the healing of the people .
There is no curse after him . There is God in the city , and the throne of the Lamb ; and all his servants serve him .
and his face shall be seen , and his name shall be written on their foreheads .
There shall be no darkness , neither shall they light the sun : for the LORD shall shine upon them , and he shall reign for ever and ever .
Then the angel said to me , &quot; These words are true . The Lord is the God of the prophets , the Spirit of the senses , who sent His messengers , and directed His servants to do what is necessary quickly .
Blessed is he who keeps the prophecy of this book , for I will come quickly
For these things I John heard and saw ; and when I had heard and seen , I bowed down before the feet of my angel to worship him
And he said unto me , Thou shalt not : I am a servant unto thee , and unto thy brethren , and unto the prophets , and unto those that keep the words of this book ; and thou shalt worship God .
And he said unto me , The prophecy which is in this book cannot be sealed , for the time is near .
The unjust shall be unjust ; the filthy shall be filthy ; the righteous shall be righteous ; the holy shall be holy .
Behold , I will come quickly , and I will recompense him according to all that men have done .
I am Arafat , I am Omekan , I am the first , I am the last , I am the first , I am the last
Blessed are they that wash their clothes , and have power to enter into the tree of life , and to enter into the city from the gate
Out of the city are dogs , evil-doers , adulterers , murderers , idolaters , and all those who like to tell lies and fabricate lies
&quot; I , Jesus , the messenger of my Lord , will prove these things to you in the congregation . I am the root of David , and his seed , and I am the bright star of the morning .
The Holy Spirit and the bride have spoken ; and the hearer shall speak ; and the thirsty shall come ; and whosoever willeth shall drink of the water of life .
&quot; I have heard the testimony of all the prophets in this book ; and if any man adds anything to it , God will add on him the evil that is written in it .
&quot; The prophecy in this book says , &apos; If a man removes anything , God will remove his portion from the tree of life and the holy city written in this book .
Saying , &quot; Yes , I will come quickly ; Amen , Lord Yahweh , I wish you would come
May the grace of the Lord Jesus always be with the saints . Amen
